ws that animals can protect each other.\",\"The ant’s bite scared the hunter, saving the pigeon.\",\"The pigeon used a leaf as a lifeboat for the ant.\",\"The hunter’s gunshot scared the pigeon, making it fly.\",\"The ant’s quick action saved both the ant and the pigeon.\",\"The story is simple and suitable for first‑class students.\",\"It can be read aloud with dialogue to practice speaking.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did the ant fall one day?\",\"options\":[\"In a pond\",\"On a tree\",\"In a nest\",\"On a leaf\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that one day, an ant fell into a pond.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who was sitting on a tree and saw the ant?\",\"options\":[\"A hunter\",\"A pigeon\",\"A bee\",\"A parrot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions a pigeon sitting on a tree saw the ant.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the pigeon throw into the pond?\",\"options\":[\"A stone\",\"A fruit\",\"A leaf\",\"A branch\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The pigeon threw a leaf into the pond to help the ant.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the ant come out of the pond safely?\",\"options\":[\"It swam to the side\",\"It climbed onto a leaf\",\"The hunter pulled it out\",\"It flew out\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the ant climbed onto the leaf and safely came out.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the hunter use to aim at the pigeon?\",\"options\":[\"A net\",\"A bow\",\"A gun\",\"A stone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the hunter aimed at the pigeon with a gun.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the ant bite the hunter?\",\"options\":[\"On his hand\",\"On his nose\",\"On his foot\",\"On his arm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The ant climbed up the hunter\'s foot and bit him.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened when the ant bit the hunter?\",\"options\":[\"The hunter laughed\",\"The hunter missed his aim\",\"The hunter caught the ant\",\"The hunter fell asleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Because the ant bit him, the hunter cried and missed his aim.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the pigeon fly away at the end?\",\"options\":[\"It saw the ant\",\"It was hungry\",\"It heard the gunshot\",\"It wanted to play\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The pigeon heard the gunshot and flew away to safety.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What did the ant do when it saw the hunter aiming at the pigeon?\",\"options\":[\"It ran away\",\"It climbed his foot and bit him\",\"It hid under a leaf\",\"It called for help\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ant took action to save the pigeon by biting the hunter.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which object helped the ant survive the pond?\",\"options\":[\"A gun\",\"A tree\",\"A leaf\",\"A foot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The leaf acted as a boat for the ant to come out of the water.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher motivate the children to use while telling the story?\",\"options\":[\"Dialogue\",\"Silence\",\"Only pictures\",\"Numbers\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly tells the teacher to motivate children to tell the story with dialogue.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In what language should the teacher accept responses?\",\"options\":[\"English only\",\"Mother tongue\",\"Foreign language\",\"Sign language only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the teacher should accept responses in their mother tongue.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the teacher supposed to motivate?\",\"options\":[\"The parents\",\"The principal\",\"The children\",\"The animals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instruction specifically mentions motivating the children.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main activity the children are being motivated to do?\",\"options\":[\"Draw a picture\",\"Tell the story\",\"Write a letter\",\"Sing a song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text focuses on motivating children to tell the story.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child speaks in their home language, what should the teacher do?\",\"options\":[\"Ask them to be quiet\",\"Accept the response\",\"Tell them it is wrong\",\"Ignore the child\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the teacher to accept responses in the mother tongue.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When a child says, \'The Ant said, Help me!\', which part of the instruction are they following?\",\"options\":[\"Telling the story with dialogue\",\"Drawing the story\",\"Writing in a notebook\",\"Playing a game\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Using words spoken by characters is telling the story with dialogue.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A teacher encourages a student to speak like the Pigeon in the story. This is an example of:\",\"options\":[\"Motivating dialogue\",\"Teaching math\",\"Accepting silence\",\"Giving homework\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Encouraging character speech is motivating the use of dialogue.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes the teacher\'s role according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To encourage and accept child participation\",\"To only speak in English\",\"To tell the story alone\",\"To correct every mistake\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Motivating dialogue and accepting mother tongue shows a role of encouragement and acceptance.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why should the teacher accept responses in the mother tongue?\",\"options\":[\"To help children express themselves\",\"To stop them from talking\",\"To make the class quiet\",\"To finish the lesson early\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Accepting the mother tongue allows children to respond freely as per the teacher\'s instructions.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which method of storytelling is specifically encouraged in the \'For the Teacher\' section?\",\"options\":[\"Storytelling with dialogue\",\"Reading silently\",\"Copying the text\",\"Memorizing dates\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifically highlights telling the story with dialogue.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21145,1,1,'English','en','Months of the Year','[\"There are 12 months in a year.\",\"January is the first month.\",\"February is the second month.\",\"March is the third month.\",\"April is the fourth month.\",\"May is the fifth month.\",\"June is the sixth month.\",\"July is the seventh month.\",\"August is the eighth month.\",\"September is the ninth month.\",\"October is the tenth month.\",\"November is the eleventh month.\",\"December is the twelfth month.\",\"The months are sung in order to remember them.\",\"Each month has a unique name and number.\",\"The year starts with January and ends with December.\",\"The months are used to keep track of time.\",\"They help us plan events and celebrations.\",\"The months are part of the calendar.\",\"They are important for school and holidays.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many months are there in a year according to the song?\",\"options\":[\"Ten\",\"Seven\",\"Twelve\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song states, \'Twelve months in a year\'.\",\"topic\":\"Complete the names of the months\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which month does the year start with?\",\"options\":[\"March\",\"January\",\"June\",\"December\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The year starts with January\'.\",\"topic\":\"Complete the names of the months\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which month does the year end with?\",\"options\":[\"November\",\"October\",\"August\",\"December\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'And ends with December\'.\",\"topic\":\"Complete the names of the months\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which month comes just after May in the list?\",\"options\":[\"June\",\"July\",\"April\",\"March\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the sequence provided, June follows May.\",\"topic\":\"Complete the names of the months\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which month comes just before August in the list?\",\"options\":[\"September\",\"July\",\"June\",\"October\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the sequence provided, July comes before August.\",\"topic\":\"Complete the names of the months\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the name of the month: M _ y.\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"e\",\"o\",\"u\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The correct spelling of the month is May.\",\"topic\":\"Complete the names of the months\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which letter is missing in the word \'Fe _ ruary\'?\",\"options\":[\"d\",\"b\",\"p\",\"t\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows \'Fe _ ruary\', and the missing letter is \'b\' to make \'February\'.\",\"topic\":\"Complete the names of the months\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"1\\/070_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which letter completes the name \'Sep _ ember\'?\",\"options\":[\"t\",\"d\",\"s\",\"p\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows \'Sep _ ember\', and the missing letter is \'t\' to make \'September\'.\",\"topic\":\"Complete the names of the months\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"1\\/070_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these months starts with the letter \'A\'?\",\"options\":[\"March\",\"May\",\"April\",\"June\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Among the options, only April starts with the letter \'A\'.\",\"topic\":\"Complete the names of the months\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which month name ends with the letters \'ber\'?\",\"options\":[\"January\",\"October\",\"March\",\"July\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"October, September, November, and December end with \'ber\'.\",\"topic\":\"Complete the names of the months\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21146,1,1,'English','en','Greetings','[\"- Greetings are words we say when we meet someone.\",\"- They show respect and friendliness.\",\"- Common greetings: \\\"Hello\\\", \\\"Good morning\\\", \\\"Good afternoon\\\", \\\"Good evening\\\".\",\"- We also say \\\"Happy Birthday\\\" when someone has a birthday.\",\"- \\\"Thank you\\\" is a polite way to show gratitude.\",\"- \\\"Merry Christmas\\\" is used during Christmas time.\",\"- \\\"Eid Mubarak\\\" is said during the Muslim festival of Eid.\",\"- \\\"Happy Diwali\\\" is used during the Hindu festival of Diwali.\",\"- \\\"Happy Independence Day\\\" is said on India\'s Independence Day (15th August).\",\"- \\\"Happy Republic Day\\\" is said on India\'s Republic Day (26th January).\",\"- \\\"All the best\\\" wishes someone good luck.\",\"- \\\"Congratulations\\\" is used when someone achieves something.\",\"- We can greet teachers with respect: \\\"Good morning, Teacher\\\".\",\"- Practice short conversations with these greetings.\",\"- Use appropriate greeting for the occasion and time of day.\",\"- Remember to smile when you greet someone.\",\"- Greetings help build good relationships.\",\"- They are an important part of everyday English.\",\"- Children should learn to use greetings politely.\",\"- Repeating greetings helps remember them.\",\"- Listening to others say greetings helps learn correct pronunciation.\",\"- Writing greetings can improve writing skills.\",\"- Use greetings in school, home, and with friends.\",\"- Practice greeting with classmates during recess.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What do we say to wish someone on Diwali?\",\"options\":[\"Happy Diwali\",\"Happy Birthday\",\"Eid-Mubarak\",\"Merry Christmas\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Happy Diwali !\' as a greeting.\",\"topic\":\"Festival Greetings\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which greeting is used for Eid?\",\"options\":[\"Happy New Year\",\"Eid-Mubarak\",\"All the Best\",\"Thank you\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'Eid-Mubarak !\' as a greeting.\",\"topic\":\"Festival Greetings\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used with \'Christmas\' in the greetings list?\",\"options\":[\"Happy\",\"Merry\",\"Eid\",\"Best\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the specific phrase \'Merry Christmas !\'.\",\"topic\":\"Festival Greetings\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do we say when someone is going on a trip?\",\"options\":[\"Happy Birthday\",\"Happy Journey\",\"Happy Diwali\",\"Congratulations\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A journey is a trip, and the text provides \'Happy Journey !\' as a greeting.\",\"topic\":\"Festival Greetings\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which greeting is used for the start of a new year?\",\"options\":[\"Happy New Year\",\"Happy Republic Day\",\"All the Best\",\"Thank you\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Happy New Year !\' as a greeting.\",\"topic\":\"Festival Greetings\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What do you say to a friend on the day they were born?\",\"options\":[\"Happy Birthday\",\"Happy Journey\",\"Eid-Mubarak\",\"Merry Christmas\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A birthday is the day one is born; the text lists \'Happy Birthday !\'.\",\"topic\":\"Festival Greetings\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If today is August 15th (Independence Day), what will you say to your teacher?\",\"options\":[\"Happy Republic Day\",\"Happy Independence Day\",\"Happy Diwali\",\"All the Best\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'Happy Independence Day !\' for this specific occasion.\",\"topic\":\"Festival Greetings\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which greeting do we use to wish someone good luck for a task?\",\"options\":[\"Thank you\",\"All the Best\",\"Happy Journey\",\"Eid-Mubarak\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text includes \'All the Best !\' as a way to wish someone well.\",\"topic\":\"Festival Greetings\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a greeting for a National Day mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Happy Republic Day\",\"Happy Birthday\",\"Happy Journey\",\"Merry Christmas\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Republic Day is a national festival mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Festival Greetings\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What do we say when we want to show we are happy for someone\'s success?\",\"options\":[\"Congratulations\",\"Happy New Year\",\"Happy Diwali\",\"Thank you\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Congratulations !\' as a greeting for success or achievement.\",\"topic\":\"Festival Greetings\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which greeting is mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Hello\",\"Congratulations\",\"Goodbye\",\"Sorry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'Congratulations !\' as one of the greetings.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is used to show gratitude in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Please\",\"Welcome\",\"Thank you\",\"Hi\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text includes \'Thank you !\' as a greeting to be practiced.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who should the teacher practice conversations with?\",\"options\":[\"Parents\",\"Children\",\"Other teachers\",\"Principals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the teacher to practice with the children.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of conversations does the text suggest?\",\"options\":[\"Long stories\",\"Short conversations\",\"Loud shouting\",\"Silent reading\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions practicing \'short conversations\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child wins a prize, what should the teacher say according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Thank you\",\"Congratulations\",\"Hello\",\"Goodbye\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Congratulations\' is the appropriate greeting from the text for an achievement.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a child helps the teacher, what greeting from the text should be used?\",\"options\":[\"Congratulations\",\"Thank you\",\"Welcome\",\"Hi\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Thank you\' is the greeting provided in the text for expressing thanks.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many specific greetings are listed in the \'For the Teacher\' section?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists two greetings: \'Congratulations !\' and \'Thank you !\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of using these greetings in class?\",\"options\":[\"To practice conversations\",\"To learn math\",\"To draw pictures\",\"To play sports\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says to use the greetings to \'Practise short conversations\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes the length of the conversations mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"Very long\",\"Short\",\"Difficult\",\"Noisy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the word \'short\' to describe the conversations.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a conversation using the text\'s greetings?\",\"options\":[\"Teacher: Hello! Student: Hi!\",\"Teacher: Congratulations! Student: Thank you!\",\"Teacher: Sit down. Student: Yes.\",\"Teacher: 1, 2, 3. Student: 4, 5, 6.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"This uses both greetings mentioned in the text to form a short conversation.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"create\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21147,1,1,'English','en','After My Bath','[\"After a bath you wash your body with soap and water.\",\"You use a bucket or a basin to hold water.\",\"A towel is used to dry yourself after washing.\",\"Hands, fingers, toes, legs and nose are washed and dried.\",\"You can use a toothbrush and toothpaste to clean your teeth.\",\"A shower or a tap provides running water for washing.\",\"A soap case keeps the soap handy in the bathroom.\",\"A toilet brush cleans the toilet after use.\",\"A stool helps you reach high places like the sink or shower.\",\"You can sing or recite a song while you wash to make it fun.\",\"Washing keeps you clean and healthy.\",\"Drying yourself after washing prevents cold.\",\"You can shake your body after a bath to get rid of water.\",\"You can ask friends to show items they have in their bathroom.\",\"Listening, repeating and showing are good ways to learn new words.\",\"Use simple words like wash, dry, soap, water, towel.\",\"Remember to wash your hands before eating.\",\"You can practice the words by singing a short song.\",\"Keep your bathroom tidy by putting items back in their places.\",\"Use a clean towel for each person to avoid germs.\",\"Wash your face, hair, body, and teeth every day.\"]','[{\"q\":\"After the bath, what does the child try to do?\",\"options\":[\"Stay wet\",\"Wipe himself dry\",\"Run away\",\"Sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'After my bath I try, try, try To wipe myself Till I\'m dry, dry, dry.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and show\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the body is described as \'shiny\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Hands\",\"Toes\",\"Nose\",\"Legs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions \'And a shiny nose.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and show\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Cat\",\"Dog\",\"Rabbit\",\"Elephant\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'If I were a dog...\'\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and show\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'nose\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Hands\",\"Toes\",\"Dry\",\"Shake\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the rhyming section, \'nose\' is paired with \'toes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and show\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many wet legs does the child mention?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'And two wet legs\'.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and show\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the child use to wipe himself according to the list of bathroom items?\",\"options\":[\"Soap\",\"Towel\",\"Brush\",\"Mug\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A towel is listed as a bathroom item and is used for wiping.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and show\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the color of the large bucket?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"Pink\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows a large pink bucket on the floor.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and show\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"1\\/073_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is kept inside the brown container next to the stool?\",\"options\":[\"Soap\",\"Toilet brush\",\"Toothpaste\",\"Handwash\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows a toilet brush kept in a brown container.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and show\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"1\\/073_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"From the list of items, which one is specifically used for washing hair?\",\"options\":[\"Handwash\",\"Cleaner\",\"Shampoo\",\"Toothpaste\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Shampoo is the item used for cleaning hair.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and show\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the child think a dog would take less time to dry?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is small\",\"Because it can shake itself\",\"Because it does not use a towel\",\"Because it likes water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says a dog could \'shake, shake, shake\' to dry quickly.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and show\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who does the text say should ask the question?\",\"options\":[\"The children\",\"The teacher\",\"The parents\",\"The principal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text starts with \'For the teacher\', indicating the teacher should ask the question.\",\"topic\":\"For the teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher ask the children about?\",\"options\":[\"Things in their school bag\",\"Things in their kitchen\",\"Things in their bathroom\",\"Things in their garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions asking about things in their bathrooms.\",\"topic\":\"For the teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is expected to answer the question about bathroom things?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher\",\"The children\",\"The neighbors\",\"The animals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instruction says to \'Ask the children\', so they are the ones who answer.\",\"topic\":\"For the teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where are the things located that the children need to identify?\",\"options\":[\"In the classroom\",\"In the bathroom\",\"In the playground\",\"In the market\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text focuses on things found in the bathroom.\",\"topic\":\"For the teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the teacher\'s role in this activity?\",\"options\":[\"To tell a story\",\"To ask a question\",\"To draw a picture\",\"To sing a song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the teacher to \'Ask the children\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child is answering the teacher, which item would they likely mention?\",\"options\":[\"A frying pan\",\"A bar of soap\",\"A school desk\",\"A swing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A bar of soap is a common item found in a bathroom.\",\"topic\":\"For the teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these items belongs to the category mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A bed\",\"A towel\",\"A gas stove\",\"A blackboard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A towel is a thing typically found in a bathroom.\",\"topic\":\"For the teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the teacher ask about \'bathrooms\' specifically in this chapter?\",\"options\":[\"Because the chapter is about eating\",\"Because the chapter is about bathing\",\"Because the chapter is about sleeping\",\"Because the chapter is about playing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The chapter title \'After My Bath\' relates directly to bathroom items.\",\"topic\":\"For the teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which item would NOT be a correct answer to the teacher\'s question?\",\"options\":[\"A bucket\",\"A mug\",\"A toothbrush\",\"A refrigerator\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"A refrigerator is usually in the kitchen, not the bathroom.\",\"topic\":\"For the teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the teacher\'s instruction, what would you name?\",\"options\":[\"A water tap\",\"A pencil box\",\"A lunch box\",\"A teddy bear\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A water tap is a thing found in a bathroom.\",\"topic\":\"For the teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21148,1,1,'English','en','Chit Chat (Unit 4)','[\"- A chat is a friendly conversation between people.\",\"- In the story, Aai (mother) and the child look for a bottle.\",\"- The child says ‘No, it is not here’ when the bottle is missing.\",\"- They look on the table, under the chair, and in the school bag.\",\"- The child says ‘Good! Keep your things properly’ to remind Aai to keep things tidy.\",\"- The child says ‘Thank you, Aai’ when the bottle is found.\",\"- We learn to use polite words like ‘Thank you’ and ‘Welcome’.\",\"- We practice listening and repeating sentences.\",\"- We learn to ask questions: ‘Where is my bottle?’\",\"- We learn to give directions: ‘Look on the table’ or ‘Check under the chair’.\",\"- We learn to give instructions: ‘May be in your school bag.’\",\"- We learn to use simple verbs: ‘look’, ‘check’, ‘keep’, ‘find’.\",\"- We learn to use the word ‘here’ to show a place.\",\"- We learn to use the word ‘not’ to say something is missing.\",\"- We learn to use the word ‘good’ to show approval.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the child asking for help in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Aai\",\"Baba\",\"Teacher\",\"Friend\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows the child calling out to \'Aai\' to ask where the bottle is.\",\"topic\":\"Words and Phrases\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What object is the child looking for?\",\"options\":[\"A bag\",\"A bottle\",\"A chair\",\"A table\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The child asks, \'Aai, where is my bottle?\'\",\"topic\":\"Words and Phrases\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Aai first tell the child to look?\",\"options\":[\"Under the chair\",\"In the school bag\",\"On the table\",\"In the kitchen\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aai first says, \'Look on the table.\'\",\"topic\":\"Words and Phrases\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Aai suggest checking after the table?\",\"options\":[\"Under the chair\",\"In the school bag\",\"On the bed\",\"Behind the door\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Aai says, \'Check under the chair\' after the child says it is not on the table.\",\"topic\":\"Words and Phrases\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the bottle finally found?\",\"options\":[\"On the table\",\"In the school bag\",\"Under the chair\",\"In the cupboard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The child finds it after Aai suggests it might be in the school bag.\",\"topic\":\"Words and Phrases\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What did the child say to Aai after finding the bottle?\",\"options\":[\"Sorry\",\"Hello\",\"Thank you, Aai\",\"Goodbye\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows the child saying \'Thank you, Aai\' once the bottle is found.\",\"topic\":\"Words and Phrases\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What advice did Aai give the child at the end?\",\"options\":[\"Keep your things properly\",\"Go to school now\",\"Drink your water\",\"Play with your toys\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Aai says, \'Good! Keep your things properly.\'\",\"topic\":\"Words and Phrases\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phrases is listed in the \'Listen and repeat\' table?\",\"options\":[\"Good morning\",\"Welcome\",\"Excuse me\",\"Please\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Welcome\' is one of the five phrases listed in the table in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Words and Phrases\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If someone says \'Thank you\', which word from the list is a polite response?\",\"options\":[\"Good\",\"Welcome\",\"May be\",\"Table\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Welcome\' is the standard polite response to \'Thank you\' provided in the list.\",\"topic\":\"Words and Phrases\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase from the text is used when you are not sure where something is?\",\"options\":[\"Good\",\"Thank you\",\"May be\",\"Welcome\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aai uses \'May be\' when suggesting the school bag because she isn\'t certain.\",\"topic\":\"Words and Phrases\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21149,1,1,'English','en','Lost and Found','[\"Lost and Found is a short story about birds looking for a whistle.\",\"The whistle is found by a bird and they ask other birds if it is theirs.\",\"The birds ask Sparrow, Crow, Owl, and Duck.\",\"Each bird says the whistle is not theirs.\",\"The whistle is finally found by Robin, who owns it.\",\"The story shows how to ask politely: \\\"Is this your whistle?\\\"\",\"The story also shows different feelings: happy, sad, scared, angry.\",\"The word pyramid shows how words can grow by adding letters: a, a big, a big sweet, etc.\",\"The story helps practice listening, speaking, and reading.\",\"It also introduces simple sentences with subject, verb, and object.\",\"It teaches the meaning of \\\"lost\\\" (not found) and \\\"found\\\" (found again).\",\"It shows how to use question words: \\\"Is this yours?\\\"\",\"It shows how to use negation: \\\"No, it’s not mine.\\\"\",\"It helps students practice repeating after the teacher.\",\"It helps students practice describing feelings with adjectives.\",\"It helps students practice matching words to pictures.\",\"It encourages students to act out the story in pairs.\",\"It encourages students to use polite language.\",\"It encourages students to use the word \\\"whistle\\\" in sentences.\",\"It encourages students to practice reading aloud.\",\"It encourages students to practice listening to the story.\",\"It encourages students to practice speaking in English.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What object did the birds find?\",\"options\":[\"A ball\",\"A whistle\",\"A ring\",\"A feather\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions finding a whistle and asking others if it belongs to them.\",\"topic\":\"Lost and Found\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the whistle found?\",\"options\":[\"In the river\",\"On the grass\",\"Under the mango tree\",\"Inside a nest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'I found it under the mango tree.\'\",\"topic\":\"Lost and Found\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who did the birds ask first about the whistle?\",\"options\":[\"The Crow\",\"The Owl\",\"The Sparrow\",\"The Duck\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story begins with the dialogue, \'Hi, Sparrow! I found this whistle. Is this yours?\'\",\"topic\":\"Lost and Found\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Robin looking sad?\",\"options\":[\"He was hungry\",\"He lost his whistle\",\"He wanted to fly away\",\"He was feeling cold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Robin says, \'I have lost my whistle\' when asked why he looks sad.\",\"topic\":\"Lost and Found\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which bird is carrying the pink whistle?\",\"options\":[\"The Crow\",\"The Sparrow\",\"The Parrot\",\"The Duck\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows a green parrot flying and holding the pink whistle.\",\"topic\":\"Lost and Found\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"1\\/076_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what does the bird in the water say when asked about the whistle?\",\"options\":[\"Yes\",\"No\",\"Maybe\",\"Thank you\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speech bubble for the Duck in the picture says \'No.\'\",\"topic\":\"Lost and Found\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"1\\/076_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which bird is sitting in the tree and asking \'Where did you find it?\'\",\"options\":[\"The Owl\",\"The Duck\",\"The Crow\",\"The Robin\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the Owl in the tree hollow asking the question.\",\"topic\":\"Lost and Found\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"1\\/077_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which bird suggested that the whistle must belong to Robin?\",\"options\":[\"The Sparrow\",\"The Crow\",\"The Owl\",\"The Duck\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"After being told where it was found, the Owl says, \'It must be Robin’s.\'\",\"topic\":\"Lost and Found\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Robin say when he got his whistle back?\",\"options\":[\"It is not mine\",\"Thank you so much\",\"Where was it?\",\"I am still sad\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text ends with Robin saying, \'Oh, yes! It’s mine. Thank you so much.\'\",\"topic\":\"Lost and Found\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a bird says \'No, it\'s not mine\', what does it mean?\",\"options\":[\"The bird wants to keep it\",\"The bird does not own the whistle\",\"The bird is angry\",\"The bird found the whistle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the context of the story, saying it is not mine means the object does not belong to that bird.\",\"topic\":\"Lost and Found\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What color is the rose flower in the Word Pyramid?\",\"options\":[\"red\",\"blue\",\"yellow\",\"pink\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'a red rose flower\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Pyramid\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these feelings is mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Hungry\",\"Sleepy\",\"Angry\",\"Thirsty\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Happy Sad Angry Scared\' as feelings.\",\"topic\":\"Word Pyramid\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is the home described in the Word Pyramid?\",\"options\":[\"a small home\",\"a big sweet home\",\"a red home\",\"a round home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The pyramid shows the progression to \'a big sweet home\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Pyramid\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What shape is the hat in the Word Pyramid?\",\"options\":[\"square\",\"triangle\",\"round\",\"flat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes \'a round hat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Pyramid\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The text asks you to enact the story as if you are which animal?\",\"options\":[\"cats\",\"dogs\",\"birds\",\"rabbits\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Enact the story as if you are the birds\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Pyramid\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the balloon pyramid, what color is the balloon?\",\"options\":[\"red\",\"blue\",\"green\",\"yellow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'a blue balloon\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Pyramid\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is added to \'a blue balloon\' to make the last step of the pyramid?\",\"options\":[\"big\",\"small\",\"sweet\",\"round\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The last step is \'a small blue balloon\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Pyramid\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many different feelings are listed to \'Look and act\'?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The feelings listed are Happy, Sad, Angry, and Scared (total 4).\",\"topic\":\"Word Pyramid\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'a red round hat\', which word tells us the color?\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"red\",\"round\",\"hat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Red is the color mentioned for the hat.\",\"topic\":\"Word Pyramid\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is found in every step of the flower pyramid?\",\"options\":[\"red\",\"rose\",\"flower\",\"big\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'flower\' appears in \'a flower\', \'a rose flower\', and \'a red rose flower\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Pyramid\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21150,1,1,'English','en','My Kitchen','[\"My Kitchen is a place where we cook food and make drinks.\",\"We use a mixer to mix ingredients.\",\"A ladle helps us pour soup or stew.\",\"The fridge keeps food cold and fresh.\",\"A gas stove is used for cooking on a flame.\",\"A saucer is a small dish for serving drinks.\",\"Dishes are plates or bowls for food.\",\"A lighter can start a fire for cooking.\",\"A pot is a deep container for boiling.\",\"A rolling pin is used to flatten dough.\",\"A pan is a shallow container for frying.\",\"A tap provides running water.\",\"A jug holds liquid for pouring.\",\"A glass is a small container for drinking.\",\"Sharbat is a sweet, cold drink made with water, lemon, sugar and salt.\",\"We add ingredients one by one and stir well.\",\"We pour the finished drink into glasses and serve it to friends.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these items is found in the kitchen?\",\"options\":[\"ladle\",\"pencil\",\"ball\",\"kite\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'ladle\' is listed as a kitchen item in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s make sharbat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What ingredient is needed to make sharbat?\",\"options\":[\"lemon\",\"book\",\"toy\",\"shoe\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'lemon\' as an item needed to make sharbat.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s make sharbat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which item in the kitchen is used to keep things cold?\",\"options\":[\"fridge\",\"pan\",\"tap\",\"pot\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A fridge is a kitchen appliance used for cooling.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s make sharbat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which item is used to get water in the kitchen?\",\"options\":[\"tap\",\"lighter\",\"saucer\",\"mixer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A tap is the source of water in a kitchen.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s make sharbat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which item do we use to cook food on?\",\"options\":[\"gas-stove\",\"rolling pin\",\"glass\",\"salt\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A gas-stove provides the heat needed for cooking.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s make sharbat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which item is used to drink the sharbat?\",\"options\":[\"glass\",\"lighter\",\"cooker\",\"tap\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A glass is used for drinking liquids like sharbat.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s make sharbat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to make your sharbat sweet, what should you add?\",\"options\":[\"sugar\",\"salt\",\"lemon\",\"pot\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Sugar is the ingredient listed that provides a sweet taste.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s make sharbat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which item from the list is used to mix ingredients together?\",\"options\":[\"mixer\",\"saucer\",\"rolling pin\",\"tap\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A mixer is used to blend or mix ingredients.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s make sharbat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT listed as an ingredient for sharbat?\",\"options\":[\"ladle\",\"lemon\",\"sugar\",\"salt\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A ladle is a kitchen tool, not an ingredient for sharbat.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s make sharbat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which item is used to hold a large amount of sharbat before pouring it into glasses?\",\"options\":[\"jug\",\"saucer\",\"lighter\",\"pan\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A jug is used to hold and pour large quantities of liquid.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s make sharbat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first thing to take in a jug?\",\"options\":[\"Milk\",\"Water\",\"Tea\",\"Oil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to take some water in a jug as the first step.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and act\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do we use to stir the sharbat?\",\"options\":[\"A fork\",\"A knife\",\"A spoon\",\"A plate\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 5 says to stir it with a spoon.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and act\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the drink being made in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Coffee\",\"Juice\",\"Sharbat\",\"Soup\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the word \'sharbat\' multiple times as the final drink.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and act\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how much salt should be added?\",\"options\":[\"One jug\",\"As per taste\",\"Five spoons\",\"A lot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 4 says to add salt as per taste.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and act\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is added to the water to make it sharbat?\",\"options\":[\"Lemon juice\",\"Rice\",\"Bread\",\"Butter\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Step 2 says to add some lemon juice in it.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and act\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where should you pour the sharbat when it is ready?\",\"options\":[\"In the jug\",\"In the glasses\",\"On the floor\",\"In the spoon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 7 says to pour the sharbat in the glasses.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and act\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do immediately after adding salt?\",\"options\":[\"Drink it\",\"Stir it with a spoon\",\"Serve it\",\"Take a jug\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 5 (stirring) follows Step 4 (adding salt).\",\"topic\":\"Listen and act\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which action word from the table means to give the drink to someone?\",\"options\":[\"Take\",\"Add\",\"Stir\",\"Serve\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Serve is the action used for giving the prepared drink to others.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and act\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which action word is NOT mentioned in the table provided?\",\"options\":[\"Pour\",\"Stir\",\"Eat\",\"Add\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table includes take, pour, add, stir, and serve; \'eat\' is not there.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and act\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very last step mentioned in the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Add sugar\",\"Stir with a spoon\",\"Serve the sharbat\",\"Drink and enjoy\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The final step (Step 9) is to drink the sharbat and enjoy.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and act\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21151,1,1,'English','en','Our Community Helpers','[\"Doctors help people when they are sick.\",\"Teachers teach children in school.\",\"Farmers grow food like wheat, rice and jowar.\",\"Soldiers protect the country and its borders.\",\"Police keep everyone safe and help when there is danger.\",\"Drivers move people and goods in cars, buses or trucks.\",\"A tailor makes and fixes clothes.\",\"Community helpers work together to make our life better.\",\"Doctors give medicines to make us feel better.\",\"Teachers read and write stories to us.\",\"Farmers plant seeds and water the crops.\",\"Soldiers wear uniforms and carry special tools.\",\"Police use whistles and radios to talk to each other.\",\"Drivers follow traffic rules and keep roads safe.\",\"Tailors use needles and thread to stitch clothes.\",\"Doctors check our heart, lungs and body parts.\",\"Teachers ask questions to help us think.\",\"Farmers use tractors to plant and harvest crops.\",\"Soldiers train every day to stay strong and brave.\",\"Police keep the streets clean and help people in trouble.\",\"Tailors help us wear new clothes when old ones break.\",\"Doctors use stethoscopes to listen to our hearts.\",\"Teachers use blackboards to write lessons.\",\"Farmers give us food to eat and grow our bodies.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who helps us to learn A, B, C?\",\"options\":[\"Doctor\",\"Teacher\",\"Farmer\",\"Soldier\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states that teachers help us to learn A, B, C.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do farmers grow according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Fruits and flowers\",\"Medicines\",\"Wheat, rice and jowar\",\"Shapes and colours\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Farmers grow wheat, rice and jowar\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When do doctors help us?\",\"options\":[\"When we want to learn\",\"When we are sick\",\"When we are safe\",\"When we are on borders\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Doctors help us when we’re sick\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where do soldiers fight?\",\"options\":[\"In the school\",\"On the farm\",\"On borders so far\",\"In the hospital\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Soldiers fight on borders so far\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What will \'do the trick\' to help us when we are sick?\",\"options\":[\"Wheat\",\"Medicines\",\"Shapes\",\"Jowar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states \'Medicines will do the trick!\' when we are sick.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to learn about shapes and colours, who should you go to?\",\"options\":[\"Police\",\"Farmer\",\"Teacher\",\"Driver\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says teachers help us learn shapes and colours.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main job of the police according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To grow rice\",\"To fight on borders\",\"To keep things safe\",\"To teach 1, 2, 3\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Police keep things safe for you\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which helper is mentioned in the \'Listen and repeat\' list but NOT in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Driver\",\"Doctor\",\"Farmer\",\"Soldier\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Driver is in the list at the bottom but not in the poem lines.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Besides A, B, C, what else does the teacher help us learn?\",\"options\":[\"How to fight\",\"1, 2, 3\",\"How to grow wheat\",\"How to drive\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says teachers help us learn \'1, 2, 3\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A person who grows wheat and rice is called a ________.\",\"options\":[\"Soldier\",\"Police\",\"Farmer\",\"Doctor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links growing wheat and rice to the farmer.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who says, \\\"I stitch clothes\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Doctor\",\"Tailor\",\"Farmer\",\"Driver\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the tailor stitches clothes.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact: Tailor\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does a doctor do?\",\"options\":[\"Drives a bus\",\"Grows crops\",\"Treats patients\",\"Stitches clothes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a doctor treats patients.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact: Tailor\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who helps students to learn?\",\"options\":[\"Teacher\",\"Soldier\",\"Tailor\",\"Farmer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the teacher helps students to learn.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact: Tailor\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A farmer\'s job is to:\",\"options\":[\"Drive a bus\",\"Grow crops\",\"Treat patients\",\"Serve the nation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a farmer grows crops.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact: Tailor\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The person who serves the nation is a:\",\"options\":[\"Driver\",\"Tailor\",\"Soldier\",\"Doctor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the soldier as the one who serves the nation.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact: Tailor\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does a driver do?\",\"options\":[\"Stitches clothes\",\"Drives the bus\",\"Helps students\",\"Grows crops\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I am a driver. I drive the bus.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact: Tailor\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you need a new shirt, who will stitch it for you?\",\"options\":[\"Farmer\",\"Doctor\",\"Tailor\",\"Soldier\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A tailor is the person who stitches clothes.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact: Tailor\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When you go to school, who helps you learn your lessons?\",\"options\":[\"Teacher\",\"Driver\",\"Tailor\",\"Farmer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher is the one who helps students learn.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact: Tailor\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which helper is most likely to be found working in a hospital?\",\"options\":[\"Farmer\",\"Doctor\",\"Driver\",\"Tailor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Doctors treat patients, which usually happens in a hospital.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact: Tailor\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who among these works in a field to produce food?\",\"options\":[\"Soldier\",\"Teacher\",\"Farmer\",\"Doctor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Growing crops is the work of a farmer.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact: Tailor\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21152,1,1,'English','en','The Magic Fish','[\"The magic fish can change colors.\",\"It can make any sea animal colorful.\",\"The sea animals start out white.\",\"The fish, crab, seahorse, starfish each want a different color.\",\"The fish shares the color with the animal.\",\"After sharing, all animals become colorful.\",\"The sea becomes happy when all animals are colorful.\",\"The fish says “Thank you” after sharing.\",\"The story shows sharing makes everyone happy.\",\"The fish is friendly and helpful.\",\"Colors mentioned: blue, orange, yellow, red.\",\"The fish can become colorful too.\",\"The fish can make you colorful like it.\",\"The sea is happy when it is colorful.\",\"Sharing is a kind act that brings joy.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where do the animals in this story live?\",\"options\":[\"In a small pond\",\"In a big sea\",\"In a river\",\"In a tank\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text starts by stating, \'It is a big sea.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Crab\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What color were all the sea animals at the beginning?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Orange\",\"White\",\"Colourful\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'All the sea animals are white.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Crab\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who comes to the sea and is very colourful?\",\"options\":[\"A dolphin\",\"A crab\",\"A magic fish\",\"A white fish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'There comes a colourful fish\' who identifies as a \'magic fish\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Crab\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What color does the crab want to be?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"White\",\"Orange\",\"Pink\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The crab wants orange.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Crab\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the magic fish do when an animal wants a color?\",\"options\":[\"It swims away\",\"It shares the color\",\"It says no\",\"It hides the color\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The magic fish shares it\' for both the dolphin and the crab.\",\"topic\":\"The Crab\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which animal has become orange?\",\"options\":[\"The dolphin\",\"The magic fish\",\"The crab\",\"The white fish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the crab is orange after the magic fish shares the color.\",\"topic\":\"The Crab\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"1\\/084_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what question does the crab ask the magic fish?\",\"options\":[\"Who are you?\",\"Can I have blue?\",\"Am I beautiful like you?\",\"Where is the sea?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The speech bubble from the crab in the figure says, \'Am I beautiful like you?\'\",\"topic\":\"The Crab\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"1\\/084_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How does the magic fish describe the crab after sharing the color?\",\"options\":[\"Very white\",\"Very big\",\"Very beautiful\",\"Very blue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The magic fish says, \'Yes, you are very beautiful.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Crab\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the dolphin got blue and the crab got orange, what is the magic fish doing for them?\",\"options\":[\"Playing a game\",\"Helping them become colourful\",\"Teaching them to swim\",\"Making them white\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The fish says, \'Sure, I can make you colourful\' and then shares colors with them.\",\"topic\":\"The Crab\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which color \'suits\' the dolphin well according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Orange\",\"White\",\"Blue\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Blue suits you well\' to the dolphin.\",\"topic\":\"The Crab\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What color does the seahorse want?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\",\"Red\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the seahorse wants yellow.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who shares the colors with the animals?\",\"options\":[\"The sea\",\"The magic fish\",\"The seahorse\",\"The teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the magic fish shares colors with the seahorse and starfish.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What color does the starfish want?\",\"options\":[\"Yellow\",\"Red\",\"Pink\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the starfish wants red.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the magic fish say to the seahorse after sharing yellow?\",\"options\":[\"You are so pretty\",\"You are so big\",\"You are so fast\",\"You are so sad\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says \'You are so pretty\' to the seahorse.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the sea happy at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is raining\",\"Because all the animals are colourful now\",\"Because the fish is magic\",\"Because the starfish is red\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the sea is happy because all the animals are colourful now.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How do the animals feel at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Sad\",\"Angry\",\"Very happy\",\"Tired\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The animals answer \'Yes, we are very happy\' at the end.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'For the Teacher\' section, what should the teacher ask the children?\",\"options\":[\"Math problems\",\"Brainstorming questions\",\"Their names\",\"To go home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the teacher to ask the children some brainstorming questions.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should children be encouraged to do with this story?\",\"options\":[\"Forget it\",\"Tell it to others\",\"Draw it\",\"Write it ten times\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to encourage the children to tell this story to others.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of the magic fish sharing its colors?\",\"options\":[\"The sea became dark\",\"All the animals became colourful\",\"The animals left the sea\",\"The magic fish became sad\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that all the animals are colourful now after sharing.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal said \'You made me so colourful\'?\",\"options\":[\"The seahorse\",\"The starfish\",\"The magic fish\",\"The sea\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text attributes the line \'You made me so colourful\' to the starfish section.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21153,1,1,'English','en','Thank You God','[\"Thank You God is a short poem that shows gratitude to God for many good things in life.\",\"The poem lists several blessings: a sweet world, food, singing birds, and everything else.\",\"It also mentions special moments like stories from grandparents, gifts from parents, help from others, and receiving gifts.\",\"After each blessing, the poem says \\\"Thank you\\\" to show thanks to God.\",\"The poem teaches children to say thank you for everyday blessings.\",\"It encourages gratitude and appreciation.\",\"The poem uses simple, repetitive language suitable for first‑class students.\",\"Each stanza ends with the same line: \\\"Thank you\\\".\",\"The poem can be sung or read aloud with pictures.\",\"It helps children remember to thank God for both big and small gifts.\",\"It also teaches the idea that gratitude is a way to show love and respect.\",\"The poem can be used in class to practice reading and speaking.\",\"It can be paired with a picture of a family, food, birds, and gifts.\",\"The poem is short enough for a quick classroom activity.\",\"It can be repeated daily to build a habit of gratitude.\",\"It helps develop listening and speaking skills in English.\",\"It can be used to teach rhyme and rhythm in simple English.\",\"It can be used as a basis for drawing or drawing activities.\",\"It can be used to practice the word \\\"thank you\\\" in conversation.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who are we thanking in this poem?\",\"options\":[\"God\",\"Friends\",\"Teachers\",\"Birds\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem repeatedly says \'Thank you God\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is described as \'so sweet\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"The food\",\"The birds\",\"The world\",\"The song\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Thank you God For the world so sweet\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do the birds do in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Fly high\",\"Sing\",\"Eat food\",\"Sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions \'the birds that sing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What do we do with the food mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"We cook it\",\"We buy it\",\"We eat it\",\"We give it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'For the food we eat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the line: \'Thank you God For _______.\'\",\"options\":[\"nothing\",\"everything\",\"someone\",\"everyone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The last line of the poem is \'Thank you God For everything\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are happy for the world, the food, and the birds, who should you thank according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"The birds\",\"The world\",\"God\",\"The food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem teaches us to thank God for all these things.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a sound mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"The world\",\"The food\",\"The birds singing\",\"The sweet taste\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Singing is a sound made by birds in the poem.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the poem, the word \'everything\' includes which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"Only the birds\",\"Only the food\",\"Only the world\",\"The world, food, and birds\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"\'Everything\' covers all the items mentioned in the previous lines.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why are we saying \'Thank you\' in this poem?\",\"options\":[\"To ask for more food\",\"To show we are happy for what we have\",\"To say goodbye to the birds\",\"To ask the world to be sweet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem is a prayer of gratitude for the things we have.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the world in this poem?\",\"options\":[\"Big\",\"Sweet\",\"Blue\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem specifically uses the adjective \'sweet\' for the world.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21154,2,1,'Marathi','mr','माझ्या या दारातून (कविता)','[\"माझ्या या दारातून कविता म्हणजे आपल्या घरात येणाऱ्या पाहुण्यांची ओळख करून देते.\",\"कवितेतील मुख्य पात्रे आहेत: मामा, मामी, काका, काकी, दादा, बहिनी, चणे फुटाणे घेऊन येणारे पाहुणे.\",\"मामा आणि मामी बाळाला गोड गोड खाऊ देऊन येतात.\",\"काका आणि काकी बाहुली घेऊन येतात.\",\"दादा आणि बहिनी चणे फुटाणे घेऊन येतात.\",\"गोड गोड पापी म्हणजे गोड गोड खाऊ घेऊन येणारी व्यक्ती.\",\"सणाच्या दिवशी घरात येणारे पाहुणे: काका, काकी, मामा, मामी, दादा, बहिनी इत्यादी.\",\"कवितेतील प्रत्येक ओळीत एक नवीन पाहुणा येतो हे दाखवते.\",\"कवितेतील शब्द \'दारातून\' म्हणजे घराचे दार.\",\"कवितेतील \'पाहुणे\' म्हणजे कुटुंबातील सदस्य किंवा नातेवाईक.\",\"कवितेचा सूर आनंदी आणि स्वागतशील आहे.\",\"कवितेतील प्रत्येक पाहुण्याने काहीतरी आणले आहे.\",\"कवितेतील \'गोड गोड पापी\' हे गोड खाऊ घेऊन येणाऱ्या पाहुण्याला म्हणतात.\",\"कवितेतील \'चणे फुटाणे\' म्हणजे चण्याचे तुकडे.\",\"कवितेतील \'बाहुली\' म्हणजे लहान मुलांना आवडणारी खेळणी.\",\"कवितेतील \'पापी\' म्हणजे गोड खाऊ घेऊन येणारी व्यक्ती.\",\"कवितेतील \'दारातून\' हे घराचे दार दाखवते.\",\"कवितेतील \'मामा\' आणि \'मामी\' हे नातेवाईक आहेत.\",\"कवितेतील \'काका\' आणि \'काकी\' हे नातेवाईक आहेत.\",\"कवितेतील \'दादा\' आणि \'बहिनी\' हे कुटुंबातील सदस्य आहेत.\"]','[{\"q\":\"मामासोबत दारातून कोण येते?\",\"options\":[\"मामी\",\"काकी\",\"वहिनी\",\"आजी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कवितेत \'मामा येतो नि मामी येते\' असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"सूचना\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"मामा आणि मामी काय देऊन जातात?\",\"options\":[\"खेळणी\",\"चणे फुटाणे\",\"गोड गोड खाऊ\",\"बाहुली\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मामा आणि मामी \'गोड गोड खाऊ\' देऊन जातात.\",\"topic\":\"सूचना\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"काका आणि काकी काय देऊन जातात?\",\"options\":[\"खाऊ\",\"छान छान बाहुली\",\"फुगे\",\"चणे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"काका आणि काकी \'छान छान बाहुली\' देऊन जातात.\",\"topic\":\"सूचना\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"दादा आणि वहिनी काय देऊन जातात?\",\"options\":[\"चणे फुटाणे\",\"गोड खाऊ\",\"बाहुली\",\"पापी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कवितेनुसार दादा आणि वहिनी \'चणे फुटाणे\' देऊन जातात.\",\"topic\":\"सूचना\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"बाबा आणि आई काय घेऊन जातात?\",\"options\":[\"खाऊ\",\"बाहुली\",\"गोड गोड पापी\",\"चणे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"कवितेच्या शेवटी बाबा आणि आई \'गोड गोड पापी\' घेऊन जातात असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"सूचना\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"ही कविता कोणाकडून तालासुरात व अभिनयासह सादर करून घ्यावी?\",\"options\":[\"पालकांकडून\",\"शिक्षकांकडून\",\"विद्यार्थ्यांकडून\",\"पाहुण्यांकडून\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"सूचनेनुसार, ही कविता विद्यार्थ्यांकडून तालासुरात व अभिनयासह सादर करून घ्यावी.\",\"topic\":\"सूचना\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"या कवितेच्या कवयित्री कोण आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"शांता शेळके\",\"अनुताई वाघ\",\"बहिणाबाई चौधरी\",\"सावित्रीबाई फुले\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेच्या शेवटी \'अनुताई वाघ\' हे नाव दिले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"सूचना\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"घरी पाहुणे आल्यावर तुला कसे वाटते, हे सांगण्यासाठी कोणाला प्रोत्साहन द्यावे?\",\"options\":[\"शिक्षकांना\",\"विद्यार्थ्यांना\",\"मामांना\",\"काकांना\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सूचनेनुसार, विद्यार्थ्यांना त्यांचे अनुभव सांगण्यासाठी प्रोत्साहन द्यावे.\",\"topic\":\"सूचना\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत आलेल्या जोड्यांपैकी \'बाहुली\' देणारी जोडी कोणती?\",\"options\":[\"मामा-मामी\",\"दादा-वहिनी\",\"काका-काकी\",\"बाबा-आई\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"काका आणि काकी बाहुली देऊन जातात.\",\"topic\":\"सूचना\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांना प्रश्न विचारण्याची संधी कशी द्यावी?\",\"options\":[\"एकट्याला बोलावून\",\"गट करून\",\"फक्त लिहून\",\"घरी जाऊन\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सूचनेनुसार, विद्यार्थ्यांचे गट करून त्यांना प्रश्न विचारण्याची संधी द्यावी.\",\"topic\":\"सूचना\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21155,2,1,'Marathi','mr','चित्रगप्पा','[\"चित्रगप्पा म्हणजे चित्रावरून बोलणे आणि विचार करणे\",\"चित्रात कुटुंब, प्राणी, निसर्ग इत्यादी दाखवले जाऊ शकते\",\"विद्यार्थ्यांना चित्र नीट पाहून काय दिसते ते सांगायला लावावे\",\"चित्रातील व्यक्तींची नावे आणि कामे ओळखायला शिकवावे\",\"प्रश्न विचारून विद्यार्थ्यांना उत्तर द्यायला प्रोत्साहित करावे\",\"उदाहरण: या चित्रात कोण आहेत?\",\"उदाहरण: कोण काय करत आहे?\",\"उदाहरण: तुम्हाला काय आवडले?\",\"कुटुंबाबद्दल बोलताना आपली मातृभाषा वापरावी\",\"चित्रावरून कथा तयार करणे मजेदार असते\",\"चित्रातील वस्तूंची क्रमवारी लक्षात ठेवावी\",\"चित्रात रंग, आकार, आकारमान ओळखायला शिकवावे\",\"चित्रातील वस्तूंचे परस्पर संबंध समजावून सांगावे\",\"चित्रावरून प्रश्न विचारल्याने लक्ष केंद्रित राहते\",\"चित्रगप्पा बोलणे आणि ऐकणे या दोन्ही कौशल्यांना वाढवते\",\"चित्रगप्पा करताना विद्यार्थ्यांना एकमेकांचे ऐकायला शिकवावे\",\"चित्रगप्पा मध्ये कल्पनाशक्तीला चालना मिळते\",\"चित्रगप्पा मध्ये शब्दसंग्रह वाढतो\",\"चित्रगप्पा मध्ये बोलण्याची प्रवाहीता वाढते\",\"चित्रगप्पा मध्ये समज आणि अभिव्यक्ती सुधारते\",\"चित्रगप्पा मध्ये सहकार्य आणि संवाद कौशल्ये विकसित होतात\"]','[{\"q\":\"चित्र पाहिल्यावर सुरुवातीला काय करणे आवश्यक आहे?\",\"options\":[\"चित्राचे बारकाईने निरीक्षण करणे\",\"चित्र फाडून टाकणे\",\"चित्र रंगवणे\",\"चित्र लपवून ठेवणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"पाठ्यपुस्तकानुसार विद्यार्थ्यांना चित्राचे बारकाईने निरीक्षण करण्यास सांगावे.\",\"topic\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांचे प्रकटीकरण\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"चित्राचे निरीक्षण करण्यासाठी विद्यार्थ्यांना काय दिले पाहिजे?\",\"options\":[\"खूप सारा गृहपाठ\",\"पुरेसा वेळ\",\"खाऊ\",\"शिक्षा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"निरीक्षणासाठी विद्यार्थ्यांना पुरेसा वेळ द्यावा असे सूचनेत म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांचे प्रकटीकरण\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"या पाठातील चित्रात प्रामुख्याने कोणाविषयी गप्पा मारायच्या आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"प्राण्यांविषयी\",\"कुटुंबाविषयी\",\"गाड्यांविषयी\",\"खेळण्यांविषयी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"चित्रातील कुटुंबाविषयी मुक्त गप्पा माराव्यात असे पाठ सांगतो.\",\"topic\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांचे प्रकटीकरण\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"शिक्षकांनी चित्रावर आधारित प्रश्न विचारल्यामुळे काय होईल?\",\"options\":[\"विद्यार्थी शांत बसतील\",\"विद्यार्थी रडतील\",\"विद्यार्थी अधिक बोलते होतील\",\"विद्यार्थी झोपून जातील\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"विविध चित्रे दाखवून आणि प्रश्न विचारून विद्यार्थ्यांना बोलते करणे हा उद्देश आहे.\",\"topic\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांचे प्रकटीकरण\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांनी कोणत्या विषयावर माहिती सांगावी यासाठी त्यांना प्रोत्साहन द्यावे?\",\"options\":[\"स्वतःच्या कुटुंबाविषयी\",\"जंगलातील वाघाविषयी\",\"बाजारातील गर्दीविषयी\",\"आकाशातील ताऱ्यांविषयी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांना स्वतःच्या कुटुंबाविषयी माहिती सांगण्यास प्रोत्साहन द्यावे.\",\"topic\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांचे प्रकटीकरण\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"माहिती सांगताना विद्यार्थ्यांच्या कोणत्या भाषेचा स्वीकार करावा?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ इंग्रजी\",\"मातृभाषा\",\"परकीय भाषा\",\"सांकेतिक भाषा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कुटुंबाविषयी माहिती सांगताना विद्यार्थ्यांच्या मातृभाषेचा स्वीकार करावा.\",\"topic\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांचे प्रकटीकरण\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"खालीलपैकी कोणता प्रश्न चित्रावर आधारित गप्पा मारण्यासाठी योग्य आहे?\",\"options\":[\"तुला जेवण मिळाले का?\",\"या कुटुंबात कोण कोण आहेत?\",\"बाहेर पाऊस पडतोय का?\",\"तुझे नाव काय आहे?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पाठ्यपुस्तकात \'या कुटुंबात कोण कोण आहेत?\' हा नमुना प्रश्न दिला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांचे प्रकटीकरण\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"चित्रातील व्यक्ती काय करत आहेत, हे विचारण्याचा हेतू काय आहे?\",\"options\":[\"विद्यार्थ्यांच्या कामाची तपासणी करणे\",\"विद्यार्थ्यांचे प्रकटीकरण तपासणे\",\"वेळ घालवणे\",\"चित्रातील चुका शोधणे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांनी चि