t is the correct way to write Ninety nine?\",\"options\":[\"Nine Tens Nine units\",\"Ten Tens Zero units\",\"Nine Tens Eight units\",\"Eight Tens Nine units\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines Ninety nine as Nine Tens Nine units.\",\"topic\":\"Introducing 100\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the number name for Ten Tens Zero units?\",\"options\":[\"Ninety\",\"Ninety nine\",\"Hundred\",\"Eighty\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Ten Tens Zero units is Hundred.\",\"topic\":\"Introducing 100\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many units are in Ninety four?\",\"options\":[\"Four units\",\"Nine units\",\"Zero units\",\"Ten units\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Ninety four is described as Nine Tens Four units.\",\"topic\":\"Introducing 100\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many units are there in the number Hundred according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Nine units\",\"Ten units\",\"Zero units\",\"One unit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes Hundred as Ten Tens Zero units.\",\"topic\":\"Introducing 100\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which number comes just after Ninety six?\",\"options\":[\"Ninety five\",\"Ninety seven\",\"Ninety eight\",\"Hundred\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Following the sequence in the text, Ninety seven (Nine Tens Seven units) follows Ninety six.\",\"topic\":\"Introducing 100\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the number sequence 95, __, __, __, 100, what number comes immediately after 98?\",\"options\":[\"97\",\"99\",\"96\",\"94\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the sequence leading to 100, 99 comes after 98 and before 100.\",\"topic\":\"Introducing 100\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which number has Ten Tens?\",\"options\":[\"Ninety\",\"Ninety nine\",\"Hundred\",\"Ninety one\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines Hundred as having Ten Tens.\",\"topic\":\"Introducing 100\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the sequence 95, 96, 97, 98, 99, 100, which number is missing if we write 95, 96, __, 98, 99, 100?\",\"options\":[\"94\",\"97\",\"100\",\"99\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"By comparing the sequence in the boxes, 97 is the number between 96 and 98.\",\"topic\":\"Introducing 100\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21217,3,1,'Maths','en','Number Song','[\"Numbers help us count objects around us.\",\"The number name for 1 is One.\",\"The number name for 2 is Two.\",\"The number name for 3 is Three.\",\"The number name for 4 is Four.\",\"The number name for 5 is Five.\",\"The number name for 6 is Six.\",\"The number name for 7 is Seven.\",\"The number name for 8 is Eight.\",\"The number name for 9 is Nine.\",\"The number name for 10 is Ten.\",\"A rainbow has seven colors.\",\"A butterfly has six legs.\",\"A human has five fingers on one hand.\",\"A human has ten toes on two feet.\",\"A kho-kho team has nine players.\",\"An umbrella has eight spokes.\",\"We use number names to write numbers in words.\",\"Counting helps us understand quantity.\",\"Always practice writing number names from one to ten.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many suns are in the sky according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first line of the poem states, \'In the sky there\'s One sun\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do five fingers make when they come together?\",\"options\":[\"A team\",\"A fist\",\"A fan\",\"A rainbow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Five fingers make fist together\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many legs does a butterfly have in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\",\"Seven\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'Six legs of the butterfly\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the umbrella have eight spokes in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"To look like a rainbow\",\"To give creamy milk\",\"To have no fear of getting wet\",\"To help us walk forward\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Eight spokes to umbrella all set No fear of getting wet\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are playing in a kho-kho team, how many friends will be there according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Seven\",\"Eight\",\"Nine\",\"Ten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says there are \'Nine friends in a kho-kho team\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, which of these has the most number of legs?\",\"options\":[\"Cow kapila\",\"The butterfly\",\"The sun\",\"The fan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The butterfly has six legs, while the cow has four legs.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what do we need ten toes for?\",\"options\":[\"To play kho-kho\",\"To make a fist\",\"To walk forward\",\"To see the world\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The last line says, \'Ten toes on two feet Walking forward all need\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the cow mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Kapila\",\"Butterfly\",\"Kho-kho\",\"Rainbow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem refers to the animal as \'Cow kapila\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many eyes are shown?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture clearly shows a pair of eyes, which equals two.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/072_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many blades are on the fan?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows a ceiling fan with three blades.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/072_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the number name for 1?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table shows that the number 1 is written as \'One\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the number name for 8?\",\"options\":[\"Seven\",\"Eight\",\"Nine\",\"Ten\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows that the number 8 is written as \'Eight\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the number name for 5?\",\"options\":[\"Four\",\"Six\",\"Five\",\"Seven\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows that the number 5 is written as \'Five\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which number matches the word \'Three\'?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'Three\' corresponds to the number 3 in the list.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which number matches the word \'Nine\'?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"7\",\"8\",\"9\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The word \'Nine\' corresponds to the number 9 in the list.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the number list, which name comes immediately after \'Six\'?\",\"options\":[\"Five\",\"Seven\",\"Eight\",\"Nine\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the sequence provided, Seven follows Six.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see the number 2, how should you write it in words?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The number 2 is written as \'Two\' according to the number names list.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word represents the number 4?\",\"options\":[\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\",\"Seven\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The number 4 is represented by the word \'Four\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the list, which number name comes just before \'Ten\'?\",\"options\":[\"Seven\",\"Eight\",\"Nine\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Looking at the sequence, Nine is the number name before Ten.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which number name starts with the letter \'S\' and represents the number 6?\",\"options\":[\"Seven\",\"Six\",\"Five\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both Six and Seven start with \'S\', but \'Six\' is the name for the number 6.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21218,3,1,'Maths','en','Pattern','[\"A pattern is a series of elements that repeat in a specific order.\",\"Patterns can be found in decorations, nature, and daily life.\",\"Observing patterns helps us predict what comes next.\",\"Patterns can be made using shapes, colors, or sizes.\",\"Numbers can also form patterns by following a rule.\",\"A \'step of two\' pattern means adding 2 to the previous number.\",\"Example of a step of two pattern: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10.\",\"Patterns can be created using objects like beads, shells, or pencils.\",\"Sound patterns can be created by clapping, snapping, or stamping.\",\"Movement patterns involve repeating actions like raising hands.\",\"Rangoli designs are often based on repeating patterns of dots.\",\"To extend a pattern, identify the repeating unit first.\",\"Patterns can be horizontal, vertical, or circular.\",\"You can create your own patterns using different materials.\",\"Patterns help in developing logical thinking and creativity.\"]','[{\"q\":\"On which festival did Anaya observe the decorations in her surroundings?\",\"options\":[\"Diwali\",\"Bailpola\",\"Holi\",\"Ganesh Chaturthi\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Anaya observed the decoration on the day of ‘Bailpola’.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Creating Patterns\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Anaya draw the patterns she saw?\",\"options\":[\"On the wall\",\"In her notebook\",\"On the ground\",\"On a slate\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she drew in her notebook some patterns from ‘Toran’ and ‘Zuli’.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Creating Patterns\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is a pattern?\",\"options\":[\"A collection of random drawings\",\"A series of elements that occur in a specific order\",\"A type of bull decoration\",\"A list of objects like groundnuts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a pattern as a series of elements that occur in a specific order.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Creating Patterns\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"From which two items of the bull did Anaya draw patterns?\",\"options\":[\"Horns and Tail\",\"Cart and Rope\",\"Toran and Zuli\",\"Bell and Food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies she drew patterns from the ‘Toran’ and ‘Zuli’ of the bull.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Creating Patterns\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should a student do after observing a decoration to finish a pattern?\",\"options\":[\"Erase the pattern\",\"Complete and extend the pattern\",\"Color the whole page\",\"Change the order of elements\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to complete and extend the pattern by observing the decoration.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Creating Patterns\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these objects is NOT mentioned in the text for creating patterns?\",\"options\":[\"Groundnuts\",\"Marbles\",\"Bangles\",\"Crayons\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Groundnuts, marbles, and bangles are listed, but crayons are not mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Creating Patterns\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Anaya makes a pattern using \'Pencil, Pen, Pencil, Pen\', what comes next to extend it?\",\"options\":[\"Lid\",\"Pencil\",\"Bangle\",\"Shell\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A pattern follows a specific order; since Pencil follows Pen, the next element is Pencil.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Creating Patterns\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Anaya wants to make a collage. Which group of objects can she use based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Beads, shells, and lids\",\"Leaves, flowers, and grass\",\"Paper, glue, and scissors\",\"Sand, water, and mud\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text encourages using objects like beads, shells, and lids to create collages.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Creating Patterns\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it important to observe the \'Toran\' decoration carefully?\",\"options\":[\"To see the colors only\",\"To understand the specific order of the elements\",\"To count how many bulls are there\",\"To learn how to draw a bull\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Careful observation is needed to identify the specific order that makes a pattern.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Creating Patterns\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a student creates a series using \'Groundnut, Shell, Groundnut, Shell\', what are they demonstrating?\",\"options\":[\"A collage of animals\",\"A pattern in a specific order\",\"A drawing of a Zuli\",\"A Bailpola celebration\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Creating a repeating series of objects in a specific order is the definition of a pattern.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Creating Patterns\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an action mentioned to create sound patterns?\",\"options\":[\"Running\",\"Clapping\",\"Sleeping\",\"Eating\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions clapping, snapping fingers, and stamping as actions for sound patterns.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, how many \'big steps\' did the monkey take to make a pattern?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Five\",\"Ten\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Two big steps long and clear\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is jumping high and playing a game in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"A lion\",\"A tiger\",\"A monkey\",\"An elephant\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem starts with \'From a jungle a monkey came\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which sequence of numbers makes the pattern \'very straight\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"1, 2, 3, 4\",\"5, 10, 15, 20\",\"2, 4, 6, 8\",\"1, 3, 5, 7\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem explicitly lists \'Two, Four, Six and Eight Making the pattern very straight\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Raising hands and moving hands forward are examples of what type of patterns?\",\"options\":[\"Sound patterns\",\"Movement patterns\",\"Color patterns\",\"Number patterns\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes raising and moving hands as \'movement patterns\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Stamping is used to create which kind of pattern?\",\"options\":[\"Sound pattern\",\"Drawing pattern\",\"Writing pattern\",\"Color pattern\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists stamping under \'sound patterns for actions\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you follow the monkey\'s pattern of \'Two, Four, Six, Eight\', what number would come next if he takes two more steps?\",\"options\":[\"Nine\",\"Ten\",\"Eleven\",\"Twelve\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The pattern increases by two each time, so 8 + 2 = 10.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student claps, then snaps fingers, then claps, then snaps fingers, what are they creating?\",\"options\":[\"A story\",\"A pattern\",\"A picture\",\"A number\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Repeating actions like clapping and snapping creates a sound pattern as per the activity.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the number pattern 2, 4, 6, 8, what is the rule for jumping?\",\"options\":[\"Skip one number\",\"Skip two numbers\",\"Skip three numbers\",\"Skip four numbers\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To get from 2 to 4, you skip 3; to get from 4 to 6, you skip 5, which is skipping one number (or adding two).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The monkey starts at 2 and takes \'two big steps\' to land on 4. If he is on 8 and takes two big steps, where will he be?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"9\",\"10\",\"12\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Following the \'two big steps\' rule, the next position after 8 is 10.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21219,3,1,'Maths','en','Measurement','[\"Measurement helps us understand the size, weight, and capacity of objects.\",\"A handspan is the distance from the tip of the thumb to the tip of the little finger when the hand is stretched.\",\"Fingers are used to measure smaller objects where a handspan is too large.\",\"Footsteps are used to measure long distances like the length of a room.\",\"Non-standard units like handspans and footsteps can vary from person to person.\",\"Heavier objects weigh more than lighter objects.\",\"Capacity is the amount of liquid a container can hold.\",\"We can measure capacity by counting how many smaller containers (like glasses or bowls) are needed to fill a larger one.\",\"A larger container usually holds more water than a smaller one.\",\"To compare weights, we can hold objects in our hands to feel which is heavier.\",\"Always use the same measuring tool to compare two things accurately.\",\"Estimation is a rough guess of a measurement before actually measuring it.\",\"The length of a book can be measured using handspans.\",\"The length of a classroom wall is best measured using footsteps.\",\"Measuring helps us describe the world around us precisely.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who measured the distance of the marble from the ditch?\",\"options\":[\"Rohit\",\"Namita\",\"Sanjay\",\"The teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Namita measured the distance of the marble from the ditch.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with handspan\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What game were Rohit, Namita, and Sanjay playing?\",\"options\":[\"Hide and seek\",\"Cricket\",\"Marbles\",\"Football\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first sentence mentions that Rohit, Namita, and Sanjay are playing marbles.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with handspan\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Namita use to measure the distance?\",\"options\":[\"A ruler\",\"Her handspan\",\"A string\",\"Her feet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says Namita measured the distance using her handspan.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with handspan\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Namita measured the distance of the marble from the ______.\",\"options\":[\"Wall\",\"Table\",\"Ditch\",\"Blackboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies the measurement was from the marble to the ditch.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with handspan\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to measure the length of your book like the children in the lesson, what will you use?\",\"options\":[\"Handspan\",\"Eraser\",\"Pencil\",\"Crayon\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text asks to use handspan to measure the length of a book.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with handspan\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To find the length of the blackboard in your classroom as mentioned in the text, you should use your ______.\",\"options\":[\"Steps\",\"Handspan\",\"Fingers\",\"Elbow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists the blackboard as an object to be measured using handspans.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with handspan\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these objects is NOT mentioned in the text to be measured using a handspan?\",\"options\":[\"Book\",\"Table\",\"Chair\",\"Blackboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions book, hand, table, and blackboard, but not a chair.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with handspan\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what can be measured using a handspan?\",\"options\":[\"The weight of a marble\",\"The length of a table\",\"The color of a book\",\"The number of friends\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'Length of table\' as an example for handspan measurement.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with handspan\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many children are mentioned by name in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The names Rohit, Namita, and Sanjay are mentioned, which makes three children.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with handspan\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Namita use her handspan while playing marbles?\",\"options\":[\"To clean the ditch\",\"To count the marbles\",\"To measure the distance\",\"To hold the book\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says she used her handspan to measure the distance of the marble.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with handspan\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What did Meena find more convenient than a handspan to measure a leaf?\",\"options\":[\"Footsteps\",\"Fingers\",\"A ruler\",\"A pencil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Meena found it more convenient to use fingers than handspan to measure the leaf.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with footsteps\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, we can measure length using handspan and ____.\",\"options\":[\"footsteps\",\"crayons\",\"strings\",\"scales\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that we can measure length using handspan and footsteps as well.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with footsteps\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do we call the number of steps we guess before measuring?\",\"options\":[\"Actual steps\",\"Total steps\",\"My estimation\",\"Wrong steps\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the text uses the term \'My estimation\' for the steps we guess.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with footsteps\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"For which of these objects are fingers more convenient to use for measurement than a handspan?\",\"options\":[\"A classroom wall\",\"A blackboard\",\"A leaf\",\"A staircase\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Meena\'s example shows that fingers are more convenient for measuring a small object like a leaf.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with footsteps\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which method is suggested to measure the distance between two opposite walls of a classroom?\",\"options\":[\"Using fingers\",\"Using handspan\",\"Using footsteps\",\"Using a leaf\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table lists the distance between opposite walls under the \'Count with footsteps\' activity.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with footsteps\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are measuring the length of your classroom wall, where should you write the final count of steps you took?\",\"options\":[\"In the \'My estimation\' column\",\"In the \'Actual steps\' column\",\"In the \'Length\\/Distance\' column\",\"On the blackboard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The actual count taken after walking is recorded in the \'Actual steps\' column.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with footsteps\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the girl using to measure the distance?\",\"options\":[\"Her hands\",\"Her fingers\",\"Her footsteps\",\"A measuring tape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The drawing shows a girl walking and counting her footsteps to measure distance.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with footsteps\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/079_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many different distances are listed to be measured in the table?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table lists four items: wall length, door to blackboard, door to staircase, and opposite walls.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with footsteps\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/079_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"To find the distance between the door and the staircase, what should a student do?\",\"options\":[\"Measure with their fingers\",\"Count their footsteps while walking\",\"Use a handspan on the floor\",\"Draw a circle around the door\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests counting footsteps to measure the distance between the door and the staircase.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with footsteps\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which is the best choice for measuring a very small object like a leaf?\",\"options\":[\"Footsteps\",\"Handspan\",\"Fingers\",\"Classroom wall\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that fingers are more convenient than handspan for measuring a leaf.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring with footsteps\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What did Atul help his mother to do with the things from the market?\",\"options\":[\"Play with them\",\"Place them in the house\",\"Eat them\",\"Wash them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Atul helped his mother to place the things she brought from the market.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do to the heavier objects according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Color them\",\"Cross them out\",\"Circle \'O\' them\",\"Underline them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says to \'Circle \'O\' the heavier objects.\'\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text suggest using to fill a small bucket completely?\",\"options\":[\"Glasses of water\",\"Spoons of sugar\",\"Handfuls of sand\",\"Pieces of paper\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions counting the number of glasses of water needed to fill the bucket completely.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which object is used in the activity to fill the water bottles?\",\"options\":[\"A plate\",\"A spoon\",\"A bowl\",\"A jug\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks \'How many bowls of water will completely fill your water bottle?\'\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When a bucket is \'filled completely\', what does it mean?\",\"options\":[\"It is empty\",\"It is half full\",\"It can hold no more water\",\"It is leaking\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Filling completely means the capacity is reached and it cannot hold more.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are comparing two bottles, how do you know which one holds more water?\",\"options\":[\"By its color\",\"By counting how many bowls of water fill it\",\"By its name\",\"By how heavy it is when empty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity uses the number of bowls to determine which bottle holds more water.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of the activity involving the bucket and glasses?\",\"options\":[\"To see how heavy the water is\",\"To see how many glasses it takes to fill the bucket\",\"To clean the bucket\",\"To drink the water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity focuses on measuring capacity by counting the units (glasses) needed to fill a container.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If your bottle takes 4 bowls to fill and your friend\'s bottle takes 6 bowls, whose bottle holds more?\",\"options\":[\"Mine\",\"Friend\'s\",\"Both are the same\",\"The bowl holds more\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A higher number of bowls indicates a larger capacity to hold water.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you use a small bowl to fill a bottle, and it takes 10 bowls, how many bowls were needed to fill it completely?\",\"options\":[\"5 bowls\",\"10 bowls\",\"2 bowls\",\"1 bowl\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The count of bowls used to reach the top is the measure of its capacity.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Between a small cup and a large bucket, which container will you circle as the one that holds more water?\",\"options\":[\"The small cup\",\"The large bucket\",\"Neither\",\"The one that is empty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A larger container like a bucket has more capacity than a small cup.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If Atul finds a feather and a stone, which one should he circle as \'lighter\'?\",\"options\":[\"The stone\",\"The feather\",\"Both\",\"Neither\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the instruction to identify lighter objects, a feather is lighter than a stone.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the teacher ask to use the \'same bowls\' when comparing two different bottles?\",\"options\":[\"Because there are no other bowls\",\"To make sure the comparison is fair\",\"To make the water change color\",\"To make the bottles look pretty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using the same unit of measurement (the same bowl) is necessary to accurately compare capacity.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21220,3,1,'Maths','en','Measurement of Time','[\"Time helps us understand the order of events.\",\"Words like \'before\' and \'after\' help us describe the sequence of actions.\",\"A daily routine is the set of activities we do every day in a specific order.\",\"We wake up in the morning and go to bed at night.\",\"Some activities take less time, while others take more time to complete.\",\"A week has 7 days: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, and Sunday.\",\"Sunday is often a holiday.\",\"The days of the week follow each other in a repeating cycle.\",\"Yesterday is the day that passed, today is the current day, and tomorrow is the day to come.\",\"A year is made up of 12 months.\",\"The months of the year are January, February, March, April, May, June, July, August, September, October, November, and December.\",\"A calendar helps us keep track of dates, days, and months.\",\"Some months have 30 days, some have 31, and February has 28 or 29 days.\",\"We use clocks to measure time during the day.\",\"Activities like brushing teeth take less time than cooking a meal.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the first step Aai mentions for making a Bhakari?\",\"options\":[\"Kneading the flour\",\"Patting the Bhakari\",\"Baking the Bhakari\",\"Eating the Bhakari\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the flour has to be kneaded first.\",\"topic\":\"Sequence of actions\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What must be done to the flour before it is patted?\",\"options\":[\"It must be baked\",\"It must be washed\",\"It must be kneaded\",\"It must be eaten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the dialogue, kneading happens before patting.\",\"topic\":\"Sequence of actions\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, who is Anay talking to about making a Bhakari?\",\"options\":[\"His teacher\",\"His Aai\",\"His sister\",\"His friend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text and the picture show Anay talking to his Aai (mother).\",\"topic\":\"Sequence of actions\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/082_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What action comes immediately after kneading the flour?\",\"options\":[\"Baking the Bhakari\",\"Washing hands\",\"Eating the Bhakari\",\"Patting the Bhakari\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Aai says, \'After kneading we have to pat the Bhakari.\'\",\"topic\":\"Sequence of actions\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When does Aai say the Bhakari should be baked?\",\"options\":[\"Before kneading\",\"After patting\",\"Before patting\",\"After eating\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'After patting it has to be baked.\'\",\"topic\":\"Sequence of actions\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Aai has just finished patting the Bhakari, what will she do next?\",\"options\":[\"Knead the flour\",\"Bake the Bhakari\",\"Wash her hands\",\"Eat the Bhakari\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The next step in the sequence after patting is baking.\",\"topic\":\"Sequence of actions\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Anay wants to eat the Bhakari. What is the very last thing he should do before eating?\",\"options\":[\"Pat the Bhakari\",\"Bake the Bhakari\",\"Wash his hands\",\"Knead the flour\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Anay says, \'Wash the hands before eating Bhakari,\' and Aai agrees.\",\"topic\":\"Sequence of actions\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these shows the correct sequence of making and eating a Bhakari?\",\"options\":[\"Bake -> Pat -> Knead\",\"Knead -> Pat -> Bake\",\"Pat -> Bake -> Knead\",\"Eat -> Wash -> Bake\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The correct order mentioned is kneading, then patting, then baking.\",\"topic\":\"Sequence of actions\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the white substance in the bowl that needs to be kneaded first?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Flour\",\"Milk\",\"Salt\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the flour has to be kneaded to make a Bhakari.\",\"topic\":\"Sequence of actions\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/082_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Is it correct to eat the Bhakari right after it is baked without washing hands?\",\"options\":[\"Yes, it is correct\",\"No, hands must be washed first\",\"Yes, if you are very hungry\",\"Aai did not say anything about it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aai confirms that hands should be washed before eating.\",\"topic\":\"Sequence of actions\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the girl who is telling us about her daily routine?\",\"options\":[\"Priya\",\"Riya\",\"Sita\",\"Geeta