\":\"In the given figure, which day is written on the sign held by the boy carrying a cricket bat and ball?\",\"options\":[\"Saturday\",\"Sunday\",\"Monday\",\"Tuesday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The boy with the cricket bat is holding the \'Sunday\' sign.\",\"topic\":\"Days of a week\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/087_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the monkeys are playing on the trees today, what day will it be tomorrow?\",\"options\":[\"Wednesday\",\"Thursday\",\"Friday\",\"Saturday\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Monkeys play on Thursday, so the next day (tomorrow) is Friday.\",\"topic\":\"Days of a week\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"On which day do the lambs lay under the tree?\",\"options\":[\"Sunday\",\"Saturday\",\"Friday\",\"Thursday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Today is Saturday Under the tree, the lambs lay\'.\",\"topic\":\"Days of a week\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is mentioned in the poem for Wednesday?\",\"options\":[\"Elephant\",\"Monkey\",\"Lamb\",\"Donkey\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem asks, \'Today is Wednesday How loud the donkeys bray?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Days of a week\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many months are there in one year?\",\"options\":[\"10 months\",\"11 months\",\"12 months\",\"7 months\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that a year has 12 months.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which is the first month of the year?\",\"options\":[\"December\",\"January\",\"March\",\"April\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that a year has months from January to December, starting with January.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which is the last month of the year?\",\"options\":[\"January\",\"June\",\"October\",\"December\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that a year has 12 months from January to December.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do we use to see the months and days of a year?\",\"options\":[\"A clock\",\"A calendar\",\"A ruler\",\"A scale\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs students to observe the calendar to see the months and days.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What specific days can we find by looking at a calendar?\",\"options\":[\"Cooking days\",\"Holidays and festivals\",\"Sleeping hours\",\"Playtime minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says we can discuss specific days such as holidays and festivals using a calendar.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides holidays, what other specific day is mentioned to be found in a calendar?\",\"options\":[\"Weekly market day\",\"Daily bath time\",\"Lunch time\",\"Bedtime\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions observing specific days like the weekly market day in the calendar.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to know when a festival is coming, what should you look at?\",\"options\":[\"A storybook\",\"A calendar\",\"A drawing\",\"A map\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A calendar is used to identify specific days like festivals.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a year has 12 months and you have finished the first month, how many months are left?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"11\",\"12\",\"9\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since there are 12 months total, if one is finished, 11 remain.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it important to observe a month in a calendar?\",\"options\":[\"To count the number of pages\",\"To find holidays and specific days\",\"To see the pictures of animals\",\"To learn how to draw\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"We observe the calendar to discuss and find specific days like holidays and festivals.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\