s as vertical arrangement.\",\"topic\":\"Lets play a game\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What objects are used in a string to add by counting forward?\",\"options\":[\"Sticks\",\"Beads\",\"Cards\",\"Lines\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions adding beads in the string by counting forward.\",\"topic\":\"Lets play a game\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the game, what must a student select from a stack?\",\"options\":[\"A number card\",\"A bead string\",\"A number strip\",\"A pencil\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The game instructions state a student will select a number card from a stack of cards.\",\"topic\":\"Lets play a game\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of the game mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"To draw the longest line\",\"To count beads as fast as possible\",\"To construct examples where the sum equals the number on the card\",\"To hide the number cards from other students\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says students construct examples such that the sum is equal to the number shown on the card.\",\"topic\":\"Lets play a game\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When using a number strip to add, in which direction do we count?\",\"options\":[\"Backward\",\"Forward\",\"Sideways\",\"Downwards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to addition by \'counting forward\' using the number strip.\",\"topic\":\"Lets play a game\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Using the number strip provided in the text, what is the sum of 8 + 6?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"13\",\"14\",\"15\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly provides the example 8 + 6 = 14 using the number strip.\",\"topic\":\"Lets play a game\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Using the number strip provided in the text, what is the sum of 16 + 2?\",\"options\":[\"18\",\"17\",\"16\",\"14\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly provides the example 16 + 2 = 18 using the number strip.\",\"topic\":\"Lets play a game\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the game, if a student shows a card with the number 10, which example correctly follows the rules?\",\"options\":[\"5 + 4\",\"6 + 4\",\"8 + 1\",\"7 + 2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sum must equal the card number (10), and 6 + 4 = 10.\",\"topic\":\"Lets play a game\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If the card shown in the game is 5, which of these is a correct construction for the game?\",\"options\":[\"1 + 2\",\"2 + 2\",\"3 + 2\",\"4 + 2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sum must equal the card number (5), and 3 + 2 = 5.\",\"topic\":\"Lets play a game\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who brought the bag of mangoes for Kajal and Deepak?\",\"options\":[\"Deepak\",\"Kajal\",\"Baba\",\"Aaji\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Kajal and Deepak saw the bag brought by Baba.\",\"topic\":\"Addition - Subtraction : Correlation\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many mangoes are there in the basket in total?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"4\",\"5\",\"2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure and text show there were 5 mangoes in the basket.\",\"topic\":\"Addition - Subtraction : Correlation\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/095_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Deepak took 2 mangoes from the basket of 5. How many mangoes are left?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"5\",\"3\",\"1\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Deepak says, \'I took 2 mangoes from the basket, so now 3 mangoes are left\'.\",\"topic\":\"Addition - Subtraction : Correlation\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many mangoes is the boy holding in his hands?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Deepak holding one mango in each hand, totaling 2 mangoes.\",\"topic\":\"Addition - Subtraction : Correlation\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/095_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Kajal says 3 mangoes left and 2 taken means how many mangoes were in the basket?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"2\",\"5\",\"6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Kajal explains that 3 + 2 = 5 mangoes were in the basket.\",\"topic\":\"Addition - Subtraction : Correlation\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the result shown for the subtraction 5 - 2?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"5\",\"0\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows the equation 5 - 2 = 3.\",\"topic\":\"Addition - Subtraction : Correlation\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/095_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If we subtract one number from the sum of two numbers, what do we get?\",\"options\":[\"Zero\",\"The other number\",\"The same number\",\"A bigger number\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes: \'from the sum of two numbers if we subtract any one of them, we get the other number.\'\",\"topic\":\"Addition - Subtraction : Correlation\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If 5 - 3 = 2, then what is the related addition sentence?\",\"options\":[\"5 + 3 = 8\",\"3 + 2 = 5\",\"5 + 2 = 7\",\"2 + 2 = 4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the correlation shown, if 5 - 3 = 2, then 3 + 2 = 5.\",\"topic\":\"Addition - Subtraction : Correlation\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Deepak had taken 3 mangoes from the basket of 5, how many would be left?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"5\",\"1\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Kajal says if he had taken 3 mangoes, then 5 - 3 = 2 mangoes would be left.\",\"topic\":\"Addition - Subtraction : Correlation\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to Deepak, what does 5 - 2 = 3 represent?\",\"options\":[\"Total mangoes\",\"Mangoes taken\",\"Mangoes left in the basket\",\"Mangoes in the bag\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Deepak says 5 - 2 = 3 means 3 mangoes are left in the basket.\",\"topic\":\"Addition - Subtraction : Correlation\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21222,3,1,'Maths','en','Coins and Currency Notes','[\"Money is used to buy things we need or want.\",\"Money comes in two forms: coins and currency notes.\",\"Common coins in India are of 1, 2, 5, and 10 rupees.\",\"Common currency notes are of 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 500, and 2000 rupees.\",\"A piggy bank is a container used to save money.\",\"We should always ask our parents before opening our piggy bank.\",\"Different combinations of coins and notes can make the same total amount.\",\"Example: 10 rupees can be made with two 5-rupee coins.\",\"Example: 10 rupees can be made with five 2-rupee coins.\",\"Example: 10 rupees can be made with ten 1-rupee coins.\",\"When buying items, we must pay the shopkeeper the correct price.\",\"If we have less money than the price, we need more money to complete the purchase.\",\"Addition is used to calculate the total cost of multiple items.\",\"Always check the value written on a note or coin before using it.\",\"Saving money helps us buy things we like in the future.\",\"Currency notes have different colors and sizes for easy identification.\",\"Coins are made of metal and are very durable.\",\"We should handle money carefully and keep it clean.\",\"Prices of toys or items are usually marked on them or on a price list.\",\"Practicing with play money helps us learn how to count and pay correctly.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where are Avani and Sachin going to go tomorrow?\",\"options\":[\"To the school\",\"To the fair\",\"To the garden\",\"To the market\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Avani and Sachin are going to the fair tomorrow.\",\"topic\":\"My Savings\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is another name for a saving box used in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Money bag\",\"Coin box\",\"Piggy bank\",\"Toy box\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses the term \'Piggy bank\' as another name for the saving box.\",\"topic\":\"My Savings\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Whose permission did the children take before opening their saving box?\",\"options\":[\"Their friends\",\"Their teacher\",\"Their parents\",\"Their neighbors\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they open their Piggy bank with their parents\' permission.\",\"topic\":\"My Savings\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Sachin decide to collect from the saving box?\",\"options\":[\"All the coins\",\"All the toys\",\"All the currency notes\",\"All the pencils\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sachin says, \'I will collect all the currency notes.\'\",\"topic\":\"My Savings\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Avani decide to collect from the saving box?\",\"options\":[\"All the coins\",\"All the currency notes\",\"All the crayons\",\"All the dolls\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Avani says, \'I will collect all the coins.\'\",\"topic\":\"My Savings\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Sachin wants to buy a flute and a ball, where will he get the money from according to the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"From his teacher\",\"From his saving box\",\"From the shopkeeper\",\"From a friend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sachin suggests using their saved money from the saving box to buy things at the fair.\",\"topic\":\"My Savings\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these items does Avani want to buy at the fair?\",\"options\":[\"A flute\",\"Coloured pencils\",\"A ball\",\"A doll\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Avani says she will buy a doll, crayons, and a balloon.\",\"topic\":\"My Savings\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what kind of saving box are the children using?\",\"options\":[\"A metal locker\",\"A clay piggy bank\",\"A plastic bottle\",\"A cloth bag\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows a broken clay pot used as a piggy bank.\",\"topic\":\"My Savings\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/097_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the girl doing with the money?\",\"options\":[\"She is sorting the coins\",\"She is counting the notes\",\"She is hiding the money\",\"She is buying a toy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the girl (Avani) touching and sorting the coins on the floor.\",\"topic\":\"My Savings\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/097_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the items Sachin wants to buy, which item is NOT on his list?\",\"options\":[\"Flute\",\"Coloured pencils\",\"Ball\",\"Crayons\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Sachin wants a flute, coloured pencils, and a ball; crayons are on Avani\'s list.\",\"topic\":\"My Savings\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these coins is mentioned by Sachin in the text?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 20\",\"₹ 50\",\"₹ 2\",\"₹ 100\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sachin mentions coins of ₹ 1, ₹ 2, ₹ 5, and ₹ 10.\",\"topic\":\"The Toy Seller\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Avani, which of these is a currency note?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 3\",\"₹ 20\",\"₹ 1\",\"₹ 2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Avani mentions currency notes of ₹ 5, ₹ 10, ₹ 20, ₹ 50, and ₹ 100.\",\"topic\":\"The Toy Seller\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What activity is suggested to be done with the help of elders?\",\"options\":[\"Buying all the toys\",\"Selling currency notes\",\"Making a saving bank box\",\"Counting coins alone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests making a saving bank box with elders\' help.\",\"topic\":\"The Toy Seller\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the price of one balloon?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 10\",\"₹ 15\",\"₹ 5\",\"₹ 20\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The price list shows the balloon is priced at ₹ 5.\",\"topic\":\"The Toy Seller\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/100_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the price of a doll is ₹ 15 and Avani has ₹ 10, how many more rupees does she need?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 5\",\"₹ 10\",\"₹ 15\",\"₹ 2\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"15 minus 10 equals 5, so she needs ₹ 5 more.\",\"topic\":\"The Toy Seller\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which two toys have the same price of ₹ 10?\",\"options\":[\"Ball and Car\",\"Flute and Bat\",\"Ball and Flute\",\"Balloon and Doll\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The price list shows both the ball and the flute cost ₹ 10.\",\"topic\":\"The Toy Seller\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/100_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which toy can be bought exactly for ₹ 20 according to the price list?\",\"options\":[\"Ball\",\"Car\",\"Elephant\",\"Balloon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The price list shows the elephant toy costs ₹ 20.\",\"topic\":\"The Toy Seller\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Sachin has a ₹ 20 note. Which toy can he buy with this exact amount?\",\"options\":[\"Two cars\",\"One elephant\",\"Two dolls\",\"One bat and one car\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The elephant costs ₹ 20, which matches Sachin\'s note.\",\"topic\":\"The Toy Seller\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT listed as a coin in the text?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 1\",\"₹ 5\",\"₹ 10\",\"₹ 20\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists ₹ 20 as a note, not a coin.\",\"topic\":\"The Toy Seller\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the price list, which toy is the most expensive?\",\"options\":[\"Bat\",\"Car\",\"Elephant\",\"Ball\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The elephant costs ₹ 20, which is the highest price on the list.\",\"topic\":\"The Toy Seller\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which amount does the text say can be made in different ways?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 5\",\"₹ 10\",\"₹ 20\",\"₹ 50\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'We can make the amount of ₹ 10 in different ways.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what can we use to make a certain amount?\",\"options\":[\"Only coins\",\"Only currency notes\",\"Combinations of coins and currency notes\",\"Only paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions making amounts using \'combinations of coins and currency notes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides ₹ 10, which other amount is mentioned to be made in the exercise?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 17\",\"₹ 15\",\"₹ 12\",\"₹ 7\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists ₹ 10 and ₹ 17 as amounts to be made.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Can the same amount of money be made in more than one way?\",\"options\":[\"No, only one way\",\"Yes, in different ways\",\"Only if we use notes\",\"Only if we use coins\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says we can make the amount in \'different ways\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the goal of the exercise for students?\",\"options\":[\"To draw coins\",\"To count to 100\",\"To experience making amounts in different ways\",\"To buy things from a shop\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states students should have experience to make a certain amount in different ways.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to make ₹ 10 using only ₹ 5 coins, how many coins do you need?\",\"options\":[\"1 coin\",\"2 coins\",\"5 coins\",\"10 coins\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Two ₹ 5 coins make ₹ 10, which is one of the \'different ways\' mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To make the amount of ₹ 17, which combination can be used?\",\"options\":[\"One ₹ 10 note and one ₹ 7 coin\",\"One ₹ 10 note, one ₹ 5 coin, and one ₹ 2 coin\",\"Three ₹ 5 coins\",\"One ₹ 10 note and one ₹ 5 coin\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"10 + 5 + 2 = 17, using standard coins and notes.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a way to make ₹ 10 using only ₹ 1 coins?\",\"options\":[\"Five ₹ 1 coins\",\"Two ₹ 1 coins\",\"Ten ₹ 1 coins\",\"One ₹ 1 coin\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ten ₹ 1 coins equal ₹ 10.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you have one ₹ 10 note and you need to make ₹ 17, how much more money do you need?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 5\",\"₹ 10\",\"₹ 7\",\"₹ 17\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"17 minus 10 equals 7, so ₹ 7 more is needed.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which combination makes exactly ₹ 10?\",\"options\":[\"Five ₹ 2 coins\",\"Three ₹ 2 coins\",\"One ₹ 5 coin and one ₹ 2 coin\",\"Two ₹ 10 notes\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Five ₹ 2 coins (2+2+2+2+2) make ₹ 10.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21223,3,1,'Maths','en','Multiplication: Preparation','[\"Multiplication is the process of repeated addition of the same number.\",\"The symbol \'x\' is used to represent multiplication.\",\"Adding 2 three times is the same as 2 multiplied by 3.\",\"2 + 2 + 2 = 6 can be written as 2 x 3 = 6.\",\"The expression 2 x 3 is read as \'Two multiplied by three\'.\",\"Multiplication helps us find the total number of objects in equal groups.\",\"If you have 2 groups of 2, it is 2 x 2 = 4.\",\"If you have 3 groups of 2, it is 2 x 3 = 6.\",\"If you have 4 groups of 2, it is 2 x 4 = 8.\",\"Repeated addition means adding the same number again and again.\",\"The result of multiplication is called the product.\",\"When we say \'2 times 3\', we mean 2 added 3 times.\",\"Counting objects in groups is the first step to understanding multiplication.\",\"Multiplication is a faster way to add equal numbers.\",\"Always check the number of items in each group before multiplying.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many hands does Dinu have?\",\"options\":[\"1 hand\",\"2 hands\",\"3 hands\",\"4 hands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text starts with Dinu saying \'My 2 hands\'.\",\"topic\":\"Count the objects\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many custard apples are in one dish?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'There are 2 custard apples in one dish.\'\",\"topic\":\"Count the objects\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the total of 2 + 2?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'total custard apples in two dishes are 2 + 2 = 4\'.\",\"topic\":\"Count the objects\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To find the total hands of Dinu and Rani, which addition do we use?\",\"options\":[\"1 + 1\",\"2 + 1\",\"2 + 2\",\"2 + 2 + 2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'My 2 hands, Rani\'s 2 hands\' as the first step for two people.\",\"topic\":\"Count the objects\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which number is being added repeatedly in all the examples?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In all examples (hands and apples), the number 2 is added repeatedly.\",\"topic\":\"Count the objects\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If there are three dishes of custard apples, how many times is the number 2 added?\",\"options\":[\"One time\",\"Two times\",\"Three times\",\"Four times\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"For three dishes, the text shows \'2 + 2 + 2\'.\",\"topic\":\"Count the objects\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many hands do Dinu, Rani, and Aman have in all?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"4\",\"6\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Three people have 2 + 2 + 2 = 6 hands.\",\"topic\":\"Count the objects\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the total number of custard apples in three dishes?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"4\",\"5\",\"6\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"For three dishes, the addition is 2 + 2 + 2, which equals 6.\",\"topic\":\"Count the objects\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If we write \'2 + 2 + 2 + 2\', how many people\'s hands are we counting?\",\"options\":[\"2 people\",\"3 people\",\"4 people\",\"5 people\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Each \'2\' represents one person\'s hands; four \'2s\' mean four people.\",\"topic\":\"Count the objects\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many hands do all four children (Dinu, Rani, Aman, and Maria) have together?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"6\",\"8\",\"10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Four children have 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 = 8 hands.\",\"topic\":\"Count the objects\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the sign \'×\' used for?\",\"options\":[\"Addition\",\"Subtraction\",\"Multiplication\",\"Division\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the sign \'×\' is used for multiplication.\",\"topic\":\"Try to understand\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How do we read \'2 × 3\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Two plus three\",\"Two minus three\",\"Two multiplied by three\",\"Two and three\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says we read it as \'Two multiplied by three\'.\",\"topic\":\"Try to understand\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If we add the number 2 three times, what is the sum?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"6\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'If we add the number 2 three times, we get the sum 6.\'\",\"topic\":\"Try to understand\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'2 flowers 3 times\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"2 + 3\",\"2 × 3\",\"3 + 3\",\"2 - 3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'2 flowers 3 times means 2 × 3\'.\",\"topic\":\"Try to understand\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"2 + 2 + 2 = 6 is the same as which multiplication?\",\"options\":[\"2 × 2 = 6\",\"2 × 3 = 6\",\"3 × 3 = 6\",\"2 + 3 = 6\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that 2+2+2=6 is the same as 2 × 3 = 6.\",\"topic\":\"Try to understand\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the addition 2 + 2 + 2 = 6, how many times is the number 2 added?\",\"options\":[\"One time\",\"Two times\",\"Three times\",\"Six times\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that we add the number 2 three times.\",\"topic\":\"Try to understand\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How do we read \'2 × 3 = 6\'?\",\"options\":[\"Two plus three is six\",\"Two multiplied by three is equal to six\",\"Two times three is three\",\"Two and three makes six\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says we read \'2 × 3 = 6\' as \'Two multiplied by three is equal to six\'.\",\"topic\":\"Try to understand\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does 2 × 3 mean in addition?\",\"options\":[\"Adding the number 2 three times\",\"Adding the number 3 two times\",\"Adding 2 and 3 together\",\"Subtracting 2 from 3\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explains that 2 × 3 means adding the number 2 three times.\",\"topic\":\"Try to understand\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If 2 × 3 = 6, then what is the result of 2 + 2 + 2?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"5\",\"6\",\"2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows that 2+2+2 is the same as 2 × 3, which equals 6.\",\"topic\":\"Try to understand\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which symbol is used to show \'multiplied by\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"+\",\"-\",\"×\",\"=\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies \'×\' as the sign used for multiplication.\",\"topic\":\"Try to understand\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which sign is used for multiplication?\",\"options\":[\"+\",\"-\",\"×\",\"=\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the sign \'×\' is used for multiplication.\",\"topic\":\"Activity for Teachers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is multiplication?\",\"options\":[\"Taking away numbers\",\"Repeated addition of the same number\",\"Adding different numbers\",\"Counting backwards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines multiplication as the repeated addition of the same number.\",\"topic\":\"Activity for Teachers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How do we read \'2 × 3 = 6\'?\",\"options\":[\"2 plus 3 is 6\",\"2 and 3 makes 6\",\"2 multiplied by 3 is equal to 6\",\"2 times 3 is more than 6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that 2 × 3 = 6 is read as \'2 multiplied by 3 is equal to 6\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activity for Teachers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the activity, what kind of addition is called multiplication?\",\"options\":[\"Addition of different numbers\",\"Addition of the same number\",\"Addition of zero\",\"Addition of large numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Multiplication is described as the repeated addition of the same number.\",\"topic\":\"Activity for Teachers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what groups of objects can a teacher show the students?\",\"options\":[\"Groups of 1 only\",\"Groups of 2, 3, or 4\",\"Groups of 10\",\"Groups of 100\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests showing students groups of 2, 3, or 4 objects each.\",\"topic\":\"Activity for Teachers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you add the same number again and again, which operation are you doing?\",\"options\":[\"Subtraction\",\"Division\",\"Multiplication\",\"Less than\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text brings to notice that multiplication is repeated addition of the same number.\",\"topic\":\"Activity for Teachers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What question helps us find the total number of objects in all groups?\",\"options\":[\"What is the color of the objects?\",\"What is the total number of objects in all the groups together?\",\"Which object is the biggest?\",\"How many groups are missing?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests asking \'what is the total number of objects in all the groups together?\' to understand multiplication.\",\"topic\":\"Activity for Teachers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If we have 2 multiplied by 3, what is the answer given in the text example?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"1\",\"6\",\"4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses the example 2 × 3 = 6.\",\"topic\":\"Activity for Teachers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To understand multiplication, what should we notice about the groups of objects?\",\"options\":[\"How many times a group of particular objects occurs\",\"The weight of the objects\",\"The shape of the objects\",\"The name of the objects\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text suggests discussing \'how many times a group of particular objects occurs\' to understand multiplication.\",\"topic\":\"Activity for Teachers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these represents \'repeated addition of the same number\' based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"2 + 3 + 4\",\"2 × 3\",\"6 - 2\",\"3 + 0\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links the concept of repeated addition of the same number to the multiplication sign and example 2 × 3.\",\"topic\":\"Activity for Teachers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21224,3,1,'Maths','en','Equal sharing, Equal groups','[\"Equal sharing means distributing objects equally among people.\",\"When we share equally, everyone gets the same number of items.\",\"If you have 6 pencils and share them between 2 people, each gets 3.\",\"Equal groups mean putting the same number of objects into each group.\",\"To make equal groups, count the total number of objects first.\",\"Decide how many objects should be in each group.\",\"If you have 6 guavas and make groups of 2, you get 3 groups.\",\"If you have 6 guavas and make groups of 3, you get 2 groups.\",\"Division is related to equal sharing and equal grouping.\",\"You can use real-life objects like pencils, chalks, or fruits to practice.\",\"Always count the total number of items before starting to share.\",\"Check if any items are left over after sharing equally.\",\"Equal sharing ensures fairness among everyone.\",\"Forming groups of twos means putting 2 items in each set.\",\"Forming groups of threes means putting 3 items in each set.\",\"The number of groups depends on the total items and the size of each group.\",\"Practice grouping with your friends in the classroom.\",\"Always count carefully to ensure groups are equal.\",\"Equal sharing helps in understanding basic division concepts.\",\"Mathematics is useful for solving daily life problems like distributing sweets.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many pencils did the teacher have at the very beginning?\",\"options\":[\"2 pencils\",\"4 pencils\",\"6 pencils\",\"3 pencils\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text starts with the teacher saying, \'I have 6 pencils.\'\",\"topic\":\"Equal Sharing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Between how many children were the pencils shared?\",\"options\":[\"1 child\",\"2 children\",\"3 children\",\"6 children\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher says she will share them between \'two of you\' (Sunny and Meena).\",\"topic\":\"Equal Sharing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the names of the two children in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Sunny and Teacher\",\"Meena and Teacher\",\"Sunny and Meena\",\"Sunny and Rahul\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Sunny and Meena as the two children receiving pencils.\",\"topic\":\"Equal Sharing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When the teacher gives 1 pencil to Sunny and 1 pencil to Meena, what is she doing?\",\"options\":[\"Keeping them\",\"Sharing them equally\",\"Losing them\",\"Taking them back\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher explicitly states, \'I will share them equally between two of you.\'\",\"topic\":\"Equal Sharing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"After the first time the teacher gave 1 pencil each to Sunny and Meena, how many pencils were left with the teacher?\",\"options\":[\"6 pencils\",\"5 pencils\",\"4 pencils\",\"2 pencils\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Sunny was given 1 pencil and Meena was given 1 pencil. Now, I have 4 pencils.\'\",\"topic\":\"Equal Sharing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many pencils did Sunny have at the very end?\",\"options\":[\"1 pencil\",\"2 pencils\",\"3 pencils\",\"6 pencils\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"At the end, Sunny says, \'I have 3 pencils.\'\",\"topic\":\"Equal Sharing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the teacher had 2 pencils left and gave 1 to Sunny and 1 to Meena, how many pencils does the teacher have now?\",\"options\":[\"0 pencils\",\"1 pencil\",\"2 pencils\",\"3 pencils\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"After giving the last 2 pencils away (1 to each child), the teacher has no pencils left.\",\"topic\":\"Equal Sharing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many times did the teacher give pencils to the children until they were all finished?\",\"options\":[\"1 time\",\"2 times\",\"3 times\",\"6 times\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher gave pencils three times: first when she had 6, then when she had 4, and finally when she had 2.\",\"topic\":\"Equal Sharing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If Sunny has 3 pencils and Meena has 3 pencils, what can we say about their shares?\",\"options\":[\"Sunny has more\",\"Meena has more\",\"They have unequal shares\",\"They have equal shares\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Since both have the same number (3), the sharing is equal.\",\"topic\":\"Equal Sharing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which number sentence shows the total pencils shared between Sunny and Meena?\",\"options\":[\"3 + 3 = 6\",\"1 + 1 = 2\",\"6 - 1 = 5\",\"4 - 1 = 3\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Sunny\'s 3 pencils plus Meena\'s 3 pencils equals the original 6 pencils.\",\"topic\":\"Equal Sharing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the table in the text, if there are 6 pencils and 2 people share them, how many pencils does each person get?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"6\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows that 6 pencils shared by 2 people results in 3 pencils each.\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Chintu ask the children to do while running?\",\"options\":[\"Form groups of twos\",\"Form groups of threes\",\"Form groups of fours\",\"Sit down in a circle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Chintu says, \'Run, run, run and while running form groups of twos.\'\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the game of making groups, Rani asks the children to form groups of how many?\",\"options\":[\"Twos\",\"Fours\",\"Threes\",\"Fives\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rani says, \'Run, run, run and while running form groups of threes.\'\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides pencils, which other object does the text ask you to count?\",\"options\":[\"Erasers\",\"Chalks\",\"Books\",\"Marbles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Count the chalks.\'\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the game, all the students who are playing will be divided into groups of ______ students.\",\"options\":[\"different\",\"equal\",\"many\",\"two\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that students will be divided into groups of equal students.\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When we share 6 pencils among 2 people and each gets 3, what does the number \'3\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"The total number of pencils\",\"The number of people sharing\",\"How many pencils each person got\",\"The number of groups\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the table, the column for \'3\' is titled \'How many pencils did each of you get?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a question that should be discussed after playing the game?\",\"options\":[\"Who ran the fastest?\",\"How many groups are formed?\",\"What color are the pencils?\",\"Where are the chalks?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'How many groups are formed?\' as a question for discussion.\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To have \'equal sharing\', what must be true about the number of objects each person gets?\",\"options\":[\"Everyone gets a different amount\",\"One person gets all the objects\",\"Everyone gets the same amount\",\"No one gets any objects\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Equal sharing means dividing objects so that every group or person has the same number.\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are playing the game and the instruction is to \'form groups of fours\', how many students should be in each group?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Forming groups of fours means putting 4 students in every group.\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If there are 6 children and they follow Chintu\'s instruction to form groups of twos, how many groups will they make?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"6\",\"1\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"6 children divided into groups of 2 results in 3 groups.\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many children are running around the circle before they form groups?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"6\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Counting the children running around the circle in the first part of the image shows there are 6 children.\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/107_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, when the children follow the instruction to form groups of threes, how many groups are created?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"2\",\"6\",\"1\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows 6 children forming 2 distinct groups of 3 children each.\",\"topic\":\"Game: Making Groups\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"3\\/107_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Who brought the first set of 6 guavas in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Meera\",\"Abdul\",\"Tai\",\"Baba\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states that Baba said, \'Meera, I have brought 6 guavas.\'\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many guavas did Tai bring for Abdul?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"6\",\"9\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tai says, \'Abdul, I have brought 6 guavas.\'\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Meera was asked to make groups of how many guavas?\",\"options\":[\"Twos\",\"Threes\",\"Fours\",\"Sixes\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Baba asked Meera to make groups of them in twos.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When Meera made groups of twos from 6 guavas, how many groups were formed?\",\"options\":[\"Two groups\",\"Three groups\",\"Six groups\",\"Four groups\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Meera says, \'There are three groups formed.\'\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who was asked to make groups of threes?\",\"options\":[\"Baba\",\"Meera\",\"Abdul\",\"Tai\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tai asked Abdul to make groups of threes.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many groups did Abdul form from 6 guavas when he made groups of threes?\",\"options\":[\"Two groups\",\"Three groups\",\"Six groups\",\"One group\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Abdul says, \'Two groups.\'\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the text, what fruit are the children grouping?\",\"options\":[\"Apples\",\"Mangoes\",\"Guavas\",\"Bananas\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions guavas throughout the conversation.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you have 6 guavas and put 3 in each group, how many guavas are in one group?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"6\",\"0\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Making groups of threes means there are 3 guavas in each group.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Meera get more groups (3) than Abdul (2) even though they both had 6 guavas?\",\"options\":[\"Meera had more guavas\",\"Abdul\'s groups were smaller\",\"Meera\'s groups were smaller (twos)\",\"Abdul had fewer guavas\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Smaller groups (twos) result in more groups than larger groups (threes) for the same total.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If Abdul wanted to have 3 groups like Meera, how many guavas should he put in each group?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"6\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"To get 3 groups from 6 guavas, they must be in groups of twos, as Meera did.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21225,3,1,'Maths','en','Mathematical Puzzles','[\"Mathematical puzzles help improve logical thinking and problem-solving skills.\",\"Addition is the process of putting numbers together to get a total.\",\"Subtraction is the process of taking one number away from another.\",\"A sum is the result of adding two or more numbers.\",\"A difference is the result of subtracting one number from another.\",\"When solving puzzles, always read the instructions carefully.\",\"In a grid puzzle, check if numbers can be repeated or used only once.\",\"Vertical lines go from top to bottom.\",\"Horizontal lines go from left to right.\",\"A shortest route is the path that covers the least distance.\",\"Increasing arrangement means writing numbers from smallest to largest.\",\"Number dots can be joined in sequence to form a picture.\",\"Puzzles often involve finding a missing number in a box or circle.\",\"Always check your work by re-calculat