ource of light in the sky?\",\"options\":[\"Sun\",\"Salt\",\"Six\",\"Socks\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The picture includes a drawing of the \'sun\', which is a source of light.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and learn (S-Z)\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/018_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What are you asked to prepare in the Project Work?\",\"options\":[\"Number cards\",\"Alphabet cards\",\"Story books\",\"Drawing sheets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly asks to \'Prepare your own alphabet cards\' for the project work.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should children observe and identify according to the teacher\'s note?\",\"options\":[\"Toys and games\",\"Colors and shapes\",\"Pictures, letters and words\",\"Animals and birds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions encouraging children to observe and identify pictures, letters and words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which book should the teacher show to the children to explain word order?\",\"options\":[\"A Math book\",\"A Dictionary\",\"A Story book\",\"A Coloring book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the teacher should \'Show a dictionary to the children\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What specific order of words does a dictionary help children understand?\",\"options\":[\"Numerical order\",\"Reverse order\",\"Alphabetical order\",\"Random order\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says a dictionary helps children understand the alphabetical order of different words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are making alphabet cards, which letter would you put on the first card?\",\"options\":[\"Z\",\"M\",\"A\",\"B\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Alphabetical order starts with the letter \'A\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The teacher encourages children to identify three things: pictures, letters, and what else?\",\"options\":[\"Numbers\",\"Words\",\"Symbols\",\"Sentences\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'pictures, letters and words\' as items to identify.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a dictionary, which word would likely come first based on alphabetical order?\",\"options\":[\"Cat\",\"Apple\",\"Dog\",\"Ball\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the alphabetical order mentioned in the text, \'Apple\' starts with \'A\' and comes first.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of showing a dictionary to children in this lesson?\",\"options\":[\"To teach them how to draw\",\"To help them identify pictures\",\"To understand the alphabetical order of words\",\"To count the number of pages\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links showing a dictionary to understanding alphabetical order.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When preparing \'your own alphabet cards\', what is the main subject you are working with?\",\"options\":[\"Numbers\",\"The Alphabet\",\"Shapes\",\"Plants\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The project work is specifically about \'alphabet cards\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To successfully complete the project work, what must a student create?\",\"options\":[\"A dictionary\",\"A set of cards with letters\",\"A list of pictures\",\"A new language\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The project requires creating \'alphabet cards\', which are cards featuring letters.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"create\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21259,5,2,'English','en','A Feast in the Forest','[\"- A Feast in the Forest is a story about animals and birds sharing food.\",\"- The story is about celebrating Forest Day with a big feast.\",\"- Foods mentioned: chapati, bhakari, dal, rice, curry, curd, salad, pickle, papad, carrots, tomatoes, brinjals, pulses, leafy vegetables, fruits, onions, cucumbers.\",\"- Foods are made into dishes like halwa, idli, sambar, soup, juice, salad, aamras, puranpoli.\",\"- Halwa is a sweet dish made from carrots.\",\"- Idli is a steamed rice cake made from rice and dal.\",\"- Sambar is a spicy lentil soup made from tomatoes, brinjals and pulses.\",\"- Soup is made from green leafy vegetables.\",\"- Juice is made from fruits.\",\"- Salad is made from onions and cucumbers.\",\"- Aamras is a sweet mango drink made from mangoes, dal and jaggery.\",\"- Puranpoli is a sweet pastry made from flour and jaggery.\",\"- The animals and birds enjoy the feast and find it tasty, sweet, salty, spicy, bitter and sour.\",\"- The teacher can ask children to repeat the food names and their tastes.\",\"- Children can act out the story and change characters or foods.\",\"- The story can be related to the Bal Anand Melava event.\",\"- The story teaches sharing, cooking, and tasting different flavors.\",\"- It also shows how nature provides food for all living beings.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which special day are the characters celebrating in the forest?\",\"options\":[\"School Day\",\"Forest Day\",\"Market Day\",\"Family Day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Today we are celebrating Forest Day\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Feast in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What will be made using the fruits brought for the feast?\",\"options\":[\"Soup\",\"Salad\",\"Juice\",\"Halwa\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'We have fruits to make juice\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Feast in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you have onions and cucumbers, what can you make for the feast?\",\"options\":[\"Soup\",\"Salad\",\"Idli\",\"Aamras\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'I have onions and cucumbers to make salad\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Feast in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these items is NOT needed to make \'sambar\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Tomatoes\",\"Brinjals\",\"Pulses\",\"Jaggery\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists tomatoes, brinjals, and pulses for sambar, but not jaggery.\",\"topic\":\"A Feast in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What ingredients are needed to make \'Aamras\' and \'Puranpoli\'?\",\"options\":[\"Rice and dal\",\"Onions and cucumbers\",\"Mangoes, dal, and jaggery\",\"Green leafy vegetables\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists mangoes, dal, and jaggery for making Aamras and Puranpoli.\",\"topic\":\"A Feast in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is being made using green leafy vegetables?\",\"options\":[\"Soup\",\"Juice\",\"Sambar\",\"Salad\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I have green leafy vegetables to make soup\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Feast in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To make \'Idli\', which two items should be brought?\",\"options\":[\"Carrots and fruits\",\"Rice and dal\",\"Tomatoes and brinjals\",\"Onions and cucumbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I have rice and dal to make Idli\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Feast in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why are all the animals bringing different food items together?\",\"options\":[\"To sell them in the forest\",\"To celebrate Forest Day with a feast\",\"To feed the forest trees\",\"To store them for winter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions bringing food items to celebrate \'Forest Day\' with a feast.\",\"topic\":\"A Feast in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which animal is shown holding the carrots?\",\"options\":[\"A monkey\",\"A rabbit\",\"A deer\",\"A bear\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows a rabbit holding a carrot and talking about making halwa.\",\"topic\":\"A Feast in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/020_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what does the character plan to make with the carrots?\",\"options\":[\"Soup\",\"Juice\",\"Halwa\",\"Salad\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The speech bubble in the figure says, \'I have carrots. Let us make halwa\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Feast in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/020_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Who enjoyed the great feast in the forest?\",\"options\":[\"Only the birds\",\"Only the animals\",\"All the animals and birds\",\"Only the forest guards\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'All the animals and birds enjoyed it.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of feast did the animals and birds have?\",\"options\":[\"A small feast\",\"A great feast\",\"A sad feast\",\"A quiet feast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first sentence of the text says, \'They had a great feast.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these food items is mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Pizza\",\"Puranpoli\",\"Burger\",\"Rice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Puranpoli is one of the specific food items listed at the end of the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how did the animals feel about the feast?\",\"options\":[\"They were bored\",\"They enjoyed it\",\"They did not like it\",\"They were scared\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says, \'All the animals and birds enjoyed it.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What word is used in the text to describe food that is very pleasing to eat?\",\"options\":[\"Salty\",\"Hot\",\"Tasty\",\"Little\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses the word \'tasty\' to describe the food animals liked.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which reaction is given for food that is \'little salty\'?\",\"options\":[\"Wow!\",\"Yummy!\",\"Oh no!\",\"Yaa!\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Oh no! It\'s little salty.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a bird is drinking something from the list, what could it be?\",\"options\":[\"Idli\",\"Puranpoli\",\"Juice\",\"Halwa\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Juice is the only liquid item in the list that is typically drunk.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which food item from the list is usually eaten with \'sambar\'?\",\"options\":[\"Aamras\",\"Idli\",\"Halwa\",\"Juice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the list provided, Idli and sambar are mentioned together as common food pairings.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text indicates that a food item might be too warm to eat immediately?\",\"options\":[\"Sweet\",\"Salty\",\"Hot\",\"Tasty\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'hot\' refers to the temperature of the food.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many specific food items are listed at the end of the text?\",\"options\":[\"Five\",\"Six\",\"Seven\",\"Eight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The list contains 7 items: halwa, Idli, sambar, Aamras, soup, Puranpoli, and juice.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21260,5,2,'English','en','Big \'A\'… Small \'a\'','[\"Big ‘A’ is a capital letter, small ‘a’ is a lowercase letter.\",\"Both look similar but the big one is taller.\",\"The big ‘A’ has a horizontal line in the middle, the small ‘a’ has a loop.\",\"In English, we use big letters at the start of sentences and names.\",\"The small ‘a’ is used in most words like ‘apple’ and ‘cat’.\",\"When you write a sentence, start with a big ‘A’ if the word begins with A.\",\"The shape of big ‘A’ is like a triangle with a cross‑bar.\",\"The shape of small ‘a’ looks like a circle with a line on the right side.\",\"In handwriting, keep the big ‘A’ straight and the small ‘a’ round.\",\"The alphabet has 26 letters, from A to Z (big) and a to z (small).\",\"You can read the alphabet by singing the song in class.\",\"Big letters are also called uppercase, small letters are lowercase.\",\"When writing, use the correct case to make words clear.\",\"Practice writing both big and small ‘A’ many times to remember the difference.\",\"The big ‘A’ is used in titles, like ‘A‑B‑C Song’.\",\"The small ‘a’ appears in words like ‘ball’, ‘hat’, ‘cat’.\",\"Remember: start a new sentence with a big letter.\",\"The alphabet is the building block of all English words.\",\"The big ‘A’ can be written with three strokes: left side, right side, and cross‑bar.\",\"The small ‘a’ can be written with two strokes: a loop and a tail.\",\"Use the alphabet chart to check if you are writing the right letter.\",\"Practice reading words that contain both big and small ‘A’ to improve spelling.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which small letter matches with the capital letter \'A\'?\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\",\"d\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the alphabet, the capital letter \'A\' corresponds to the small letter \'a\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which capital letter matches with the small letter \'b\'?\",\"options\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"C\",\"D\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The small letter \'b\' is the lowercase version of the capital letter \'B\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very first word of the rhyme?\",\"options\":[\"Big\",\"Small\",\"What\",\"See\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The rhyme begins with the phrase \'Big A, small a\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the last part of the rhyme, who is asked \'What do you see?\'\",\"options\":[\"Big A\",\"Small a\",\"Children\",\"The teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Children children, What do you see?\' in the final stanza.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the first three stanzas, the speaker says the object is looking at ____.\",\"options\":[\"me\",\"us\",\"you\",\"them\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states \'I see an looking at me\' in the first three parts.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the last stanza, the children say the objects are looking at ____.\",\"options\":[\"me\",\"us\",\"you\",\"them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The children respond with \'We see an and an and an looking at us.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the matching task, which small letter should be matched with the capital letter \'C\'?\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\",\"d\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The capital letter \'C\' matches with the small letter \'c\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the matching task, which small letter should be matched with the capital letter \'G\'?\",\"options\":[\"e\",\"f\",\"g\",\"a\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The capital letter \'G\' matches with the small letter \'g\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many times does the phrase \'Big A, small a\' appear in the rhyme?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'Big A, small a\' is repeated at the start of the first three stanzas.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the last stanza, how many items do the children see looking at them?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The children say \'We see an and an and an\', which indicates three items.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the codes, what number is given for the letter \'a\'?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"26\",\"10\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table shows that the letter \'a\' is matched with the number 1.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember the codes\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which letter is represented by the number 26?\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"m\",\"z\",\"n\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the code table, the number 26 is matched with the letter \'z\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember the codes\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, follow the arrow from number 13. Which number comes next?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"14\",\"15\",\"26\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The arrow in the figure shows the sequence moving from 13 down to 14.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember the codes\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/023_108.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If \'a\' is 1, what is the code for the letter \'b\'?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Following the alphabetical order in the table, \'b\' comes after \'a\' and is coded as 2.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember the codes\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How will you write the word \'cat\' using these codes?\",\"options\":[\"3 1 20\",\"1 3 20\",\"20 1 3\",\"3 20 1\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Using the table, c=3, a=1, and t=20, so \'cat\' is 3 1 20.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember the codes\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is made by the codes \'2 1 4\'?\",\"options\":[\"cab\",\"bad\",\"dad\",\"add\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the codes, 2 is \'b\', 1 is \'a\', and 4 is \'d\', which spells \'bad\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember the codes\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which letter is written directly below the letter \'b\'?\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"y\",\"z\",\"x\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Looking at the columns in the figure, the letter \'y\' is placed in the box below \'b\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember the codes\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/023_108.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these letters has a code number greater than 10?\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"e\",\"i\",\"k\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The codes are a=1, e=5, i=9, and k=11; only 11 is greater than 10.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember the codes\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If \'d\' is 4 and \'f\' is 6, which letter is 5?\",\"options\":[\"c\",\"e\",\"g\",\"h\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The letter \'e\' is between \'d\' and \'f\', and its code is 5.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember the codes\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the code for the letter \'m\'?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"13\",\"14\",\"26\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows the letter \'m\' is matched with the number 13.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember the codes\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21261,5,2,'English','en','Fruit Salad','[\"- Fruit salad is a tasty mix of different fruits.\",\"- First choose the fruits you like.\",\"- Wash the fruits well before using.\",\"- Peel the fruits and cut them into small pieces.\",\"- Put the cut pieces into a bowl.\",\"- If the fruits are dirty, wash them again.\",\"- If you want to make a fruit salad, mix the pieces together.\",\"- Mix the salad well so all pieces are coated.\",\"- Add a little sugar or salt to taste.\",\"- Serve the salad in a bowl and enjoy!\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the first step to make a fruit salad?\",\"options\":[\"Wash the fruits\",\"Take some fruits you like\",\"Cut the fruits\",\"Add sugar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the first step is to take some fruits you like.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do to the fruits properly before peeling them?\",\"options\":[\"Wash them\",\"Mix them\",\"Serve them\",\"Eat them\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states you must wash the fruits properly before peeling and cutting.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who should help you when you peel and cut the fruits?\",\"options\":[\"Your friends\",\"Your teacher\",\"Your parents\",\"No one\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions specify cutting the fruits with the help of your parents.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where should you put the fruit pieces after cutting them?\",\"options\":[\"In a bag\",\"In a bowl\",\"On a plate\",\"In a glass\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 4 says to put the pieces into a bowl.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What can you add to the fruit salad for taste?\",\"options\":[\"Water or milk\",\"Honey or jam\",\"Sugar or salt\",\"Oil or butter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 5 suggests adding some sugar or salt for taste.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What must you do after adding sugar or salt to the fruits?\",\"options\":[\"Wash it\",\"Peel it\",\"Mix it well\",\"Cut it again\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 6 instructs to mix it well after adding sugar or salt.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final step before you enjoy the salad?\",\"options\":[\"Peel the fruits\",\"Serve it\",\"Wash the bowl\",\"Buy more fruits\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 8 says \'Now serve it and enjoy.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the teacher encourage children to try such recipes?\",\"options\":[\"At the market\",\"At school\",\"At home\",\"At a restaurant\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The \'For the Teacher\' section says to encourage children to try recipes at home.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher give clear instructions about for different recipes?\",\"options\":[\"Mathematical operations\",\"Drawing fruits\",\"Buying fruits\",\"Cleaning the kitchen\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher instructions mention giving clear instructions about ‘mathematical operations’.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What are children encouraged to share with their friends?\",\"options\":[\"Their fruits\",\"Their experiences\",\"Their bowls\",\"Their sugar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher is told to encourage children to share their experiences with friends.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who is Kiran talking to in the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Aai\",\"Baba\",\"Teacher\",\"Friend\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the dialogue, Kiran addresses the person as \'Aai\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What dish is Aai making in the kitchen?\",\"options\":[\"Fruit Salad\",\"Misal-Pav\",\"Poha\",\"Upma\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aai explicitly states, \'I am making Misal-Pav.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does Aai ask Kiran to bring the tomatoes from?\",\"options\":[\"The fridge\",\"The bag\",\"The basket\",\"The table\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aai says, \'Bring two or three tomatoes from the basket.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many tomatoes does Aai ask Kiran to bring?\",\"options\":[\"One or two\",\"Two or three\",\"Three or four\",\"Only five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Aai asks for \'two or three tomatoes\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Kiran say after Aai asks for tomatoes?\",\"options\":[\"\\\"I am busy.\\\"\",\"\\\"No, I can\'t.\\\"\",\"\\\"Yes, here they are!\\\"\",\"\\\"Where are they?\\\"\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Kiran responds with \'Yes, here they are!\' when bringing the tomatoes.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'For the Teacher\' section, what should teachers give children exposure to?\",\"options\":[\"Cooking food\",\"Speaking and raising questions\",\"Buying vegetables\",\"Cleaning the basket\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher instructions state: \'Give exposure to the children to speak and raise questions.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher wants to follow the lesson instructions, what should they arrange in class?\",\"options\":[\"A cooking competition\",\"A drawing session\",\"Conversations on different situations\",\"A silent reading hour\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the teacher to \'Arrange conversations on different situations.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When Kiran says \'Wow! I like it\', what is Kiran feeling about the Misal-Pav?\",\"options\":[\"Kiran is sad\",\"Kiran is excited and happy\",\"Kiran is angry\",\"Kiran is bored\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The use of \'Wow!\' and \'I like it\' indicates excitement and a positive feeling.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Aai say \'No, thank you, dear\' at the end of the dialogue?\",\"options\":[\"She is finished cooking\",\"She does not like Kiran\'s help\",\"She does not need anything else\",\"She is too busy to talk\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"When Kiran asks \'Do you need anything else?\', Aai replies \'No\' because she has what she needs.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary purpose of the dialogue between Kiran and Aai for the students?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to make Misal-Pav\",\"To practice listening and speaking in a situation\",\"To learn the names of all vegetables\",\"To learn how to count tomatoes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Listen and practise\' heading and teacher notes suggest the goal is speaking and conversational practice.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21262,5,2,'English','en','Number Song','[\"- Numbers 1 to 10 are learned by singing a song with animals.\",\"- The song repeats after 10, so we can count again from 1.\",\"- Counting can be practiced with objects like apples, cats, toys, oranges, pens, bottles.\",\"- To make a noun plural, add \'s\' (cat → cats) or \'es\' (box → boxes). Some words stay the same (fish, sheep) or change differently (leaf → leaves).\",\"- Counting objects from left to right helps develop number sense.\",\"- Numbers 10, 20, 30… up to 100 are shown in a chart; each ten has a special name (ten, twenty, thirty).\",\"- Numbers 11 to 19 have unique names (eleven, twelve, thirteen…).\",\"- Counting can be linked to everyday items: balls, butterflies, stars, flowers, packets, bells, pencils, apples, carrots, whistles.\",\"- Practice matching words with pictures to reinforce counting and vocabulary.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what letter should be added to a word to make it \'many\'?\",\"options\":[\"s\",\"e\",\"t\",\"n\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to \'Add s to make one to many\'.\",\"topic\":\"One to many\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is mentioned first in the number song?\",\"options\":[\"Camels\",\"Monkeys\",\"Elephant\",\"Rabbits\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The song begins with the line \'Rabbits-rabbits one, two, three\'.\",\"topic\":\"One to many\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the names of the two friends who are counting their things?\",\"options\":[\"Rudra and Arya\",\"Ram and Arya\",\"Rudra and Amit\",\"Rudra and Arjun\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Rudra and Arya are very good friends\'.\",\"topic\":\"One to many\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the example \'cat - cats\', what does the word \'cats\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"One cat\",\"Many cats\",\"No cats\",\"Small cat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that adding \'s\' makes a word represent \'many\'.\",\"topic\":\"One to many\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the rule from the text: \'Add s to make ____ to many\'.\",\"options\":[\"two\",\"ten\",\"one\",\"all\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The textbook rule is \'Add s to make one to many\'.\",\"topic\":\"One to many\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Following the rule in the text, how should you write \'many\' for the word \'apple\'?\",\"options\":[\"apples\",\"applees\",\"aples\",\"apple\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"By adding \'s\' to \'apple\', we get \'apples\'.\",\"topic\":\"One to many\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Following the rule in the text, how should you write \'many\' for the word \'cap\'?\",\"options\":[\"capp\",\"caps\",\"capes\",\"capses\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"By adding \'s\' to \'cap\', we get \'caps\'.\",\"topic\":\"One to many\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you have one \'dog\', how do you write it to show you have \'many\'?\",\"options\":[\"doges\",\"dog\",\"dogs\",\"dogss\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The rule is to add \'s\' to the word \'dog\'.\",\"topic\":\"One to many\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the word \'Monkeys\' written with an \'s\' at the end in the song?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is a name\",\"Because it refers to more than one monkey\",\"Because the word ends with \'s\'\",\"Because it is at the start of the line\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'s\' indicates the \'many\' form as per the grammar rule provided.\",\"topic\":\"One to many\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal in the song is NOT written in the \'many\' form (without an \'s\')?\",\"options\":[\"Rabbits\",\"Camels\",\"Monkeys\",\"Elephant\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says \'The elephant says\', which is the \'one\' (singular) form.\",\"topic\":\"One to many\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what are there eleven of?\",\"options\":[\"balls\",\"pencils\",\"stars\",\"bells\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states \'eleven balls\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which number comes after \'nineteen\' in the first list?\",\"options\":[\"fifteen\",\"twenty\",\"eighteen\",\"seventeen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the list provided, \'twenty whistles\' follows \'nineteen carrots\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What object is paired with the number twelve?\",\"options\":[\"flowers\",\"carrots\",\"butterflies\",\"packets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'twelve butterflies\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word represents the number 14 in the text?\",\"options\":[\"thirteen\",\"fourteen\",\"fifteen\",\"sixteen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists the word \'fourteen\' followed by flowers.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see 19 items in the list, they are...\",\"options\":[\"apples\",\"carrots\",\"whistles\",\"pencils\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text associates the number nineteen with carrots.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the list of tens, which number comes right after \'thirty\'?\",\"options\":[\"twenty\",\"forty\",\"fifty\",\"sixty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sequence in the text is \'ten twenty thirty forty...\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct pair from the text?\",\"options\":[\"thirteen stars\",\"thirteen balls\",\"thirteen bells\",\"thirteen carrots\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifically pairs \'thirteen\' with \'stars\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which number is missing in this sequence from the text: sixty, seventy, ____, ninety?\",\"options\":[\"fifty\",\"eighty\",\"hundred\",\"forty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists the tens as \'sixty seventy eighty ninety\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many flowers are mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"twelve\",\"thirteen\",\"fourteen\",\"fifteen\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'fourteen flowers\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these numbers is the last and largest in the second list?\",\"options\":[\"ten\",\"fifty\",\"ninety\",\"hundred\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The list of tens ends with the word \'hundred\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21263,5,2,'English','en','Introduce Yourself','[\"Introduce yourself by saying your name and age.\",\"Use simple sentences like \\\"I am ___ years old.\\\"\",\"Mention where you live, e.g., \\\"I am from Mumbai.\\\"\",\"Say the name of your school: \\\"My school is ___.\\\"\",\"Use pronouns: I, We, You, He, She, It, They.\",\"Practice speaking about family members: \\\"She is my mother.\\\"\",\"Talk about friends: \\\"You are my friend Sanvi.\\\"\",\"Describe pets: \\\"It is my pet dog.\\\"\",\"Use present tense for everyday facts.\",\"Ask and answer simple questions about names and ages.\",\"Listen carefully to others when they introduce themselves.\",\"Repeat after the teacher to improve pronunciation.\",\"Use short sentences for clarity.\",\"Use the word wall to match pronouns with people.\",\"Keep sentences short and clear for Standard 2 level.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which grade is Sara studying?\",\"options\":[\"Grade One\",\"Grade Two\",\"Grade Three\",\"Grade Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'I am in Grade Two.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How old is Anuj?\",\"options\":[\"Seven years old\",\"Nine years old\",\"Eight years old\",\"Ten years old\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Anuj says, \'I am eight years old.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which city is referred to as the \'orange city\'?\",\"options\":[\"Mumbai\",\"Nagpur\",\"Pune\",\"Nashik\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sara says she is from \'orange city, Nagpur.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What role is Sara playing in the event?\",\"options\":[\"A teacher\",\"A little star\",\"Savitribai Phule\",\"An orange seller\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sara states, \'I am playing the role of Savitribai Phule.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is Anuj going to present?\",\"options\":[\"A song\",\"A dance\",\"A story\",\"Powada\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Anuj says, \'I am going to present Powada.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which city is described as the \'capital city\'?\",\"options\":[\"Nagpur\",\"Mumbai\",\"Delhi\",\"Nashik\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Anuj says, \'I come from capital city Mumbai.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student follows the teacher\'s hints, what should they talk about?\",\"options\":[\"Their favorite food\",\"Their likes and dislikes\",\"Their home address\",\"Their teacher\'s name\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s hints include speaking about \'likes and dislikes\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the teacher\'s instructions, where should children introduce themselves?\",\"options\":[\"At home\",\"In the playground\",\"In the classroom\",\"At the market\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Encourage the children to introduce themselves in the classroom.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the program mentioned at the beginning of the text?\",\"options\":[\"Little Stars Dance\",\"Rangotsav Little Stars\",\"Nagpur Stars\",\"School Stars\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The heading of the introduction text is \'Rangotsav Little Stars\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a hint provided for the teacher to help students talk?\",\"options\":[\"Speak about your friends\",\"Speak about your marks\",\"Speak about your clothes\",\"Speak about your toys\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s section suggests: \'Speak about your friends, your likes and dislikes, etc.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word does Sanika use to introduce her father?\",\"options\":[\"She\",\"It\",\"He\",\"They\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Sanika says, \'He is my father.\'\",\"topic\":\"Find and circle the words\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used for the mother in the text?\",\"options\":[\"He\",\"She\",\"We\",\"You\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'She is my mother.\'\",\"topic\":\"Find and circle the words\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What word does Sanika use to talk about her pet dog, Jimmy?\",\"options\":[\"He\",\"She\",\"It\",\"We\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'It is my pet dog, Jimmy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Find and circle the words\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used when Sanika talks about herself and her friend together?\",\"options\":[\"I\",\"We\",\"He\",\"She\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'We are friends.\'\",\"topic\":\"Find and circle the words\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'I am Sanika\', which word is found on the Word wall?\",\"options\":[\"am\",\"Sanika\",\"I\",\"girl\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'I\' is listed in the Word wall section of the text.\",\"topic\":\"Find and circle the words\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word does Sanika use to address her friend Sanvi directly?\",\"options\":[\"He\",\"She\",\"You\",\"It\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'You are my friend Sanvi.\'\",\"topic\":\"Find and circle the words\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used to describe the people who are doing homework?\",\"options\":[\"We\",\"They\",\"You\",\"I\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'They are doing homework.\'\",\"topic\":\"Find and circle the words\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used for the grandmother in the story?\",\"options\":[\"He\",\"She\",\"It\",\"They\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'She is my grandmother.\'\",\"topic\":\"Find and circle the words\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'He is my uncle\', which word is a pronoun from the Word wall?\",\"options\":[\"He\",\"uncle\",\"my\",\"is\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'He\' is the pronoun from the Word wall used to introduce the uncle.\",\"topic\":\"Find and circle the words\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used to introduce the aunt in the text?\",\"options\":[\"He\",\"She\",\"It\",\"We\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'She is my aunt.\'\",\"topic\":\"Find and circle the words\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the girl in the first sentence?\",\"options\":[\"Sanvi\",\"Sanika\",\"Sania\",\"Saru\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'I am Sanika\' in the first sentence.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are \'they\' doing in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Playing\",\"Eating\",\"Doing homework\",\"Sleeping\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sentence 2 states \'They are doing homework.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence: \'He is my ____.\'\",\"options\":[\"aunt\",\"mother\",\"uncle\",\"Sanvi\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sentence 3 says \'He is my uncle.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used to talk about the pet dog?\",\"options\":[\"She\",\"He\",\"It\",\"We\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sentence 7 uses \'It\' for the pet dog: \'It is my pet dog.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of family is mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Small family\",\"Big family\",\"Happy family\",\"Sad family\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sentence 10 says \'We are a happy family.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used for both the \'mother\' and the \'aunt\'?\",\"options\":[\"He\",\"She\",\"It\",\"They\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sentences 4 and 6 use \'She\' for aunt and mother.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are talking to your friend Sanvi, what should you say according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"I am Sanvi.\",\"She is my friend Sanvi.\",\"You are my friend Sanvi.\",\"He is my friend Sanvi.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sentence 9 provides the correct form: \'You are my friend Sanvi.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence should you use to introduce your brother?\",\"options\":[\"She is my brother.\",\"He is my brother.\",\"It is my brother.\",\"They are my brother.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sentence 8 shows the correct introduction: \'He is my brother.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence refers to more than one friend?\",\"options\":[\"You are my friend Sanvi.\",\"You are my friends.\",\"He is my uncle.\",\"I am Sanika.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sentence 5 uses the plural \'friends\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used to talk about a group that includes the speaker?\",\"options\":[\"They\",\"You\",\"We\",\"He\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sentence 10 uses \'We\' to describe the speaker\'s family.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21264,5,2,'English','en','Sounds - I','[\"- A *sound* is the way a letter or group of letters makes a word say something.\",\"- In English, each letter can have a *short* or *long* sound.\",\"- Vowels (a, e, i, o, u) are the most important for making sounds.\",\"- A *vowel family* is a group of words that have the same vowel sound but different consonants.\",\"- Example of a vowel family: *cat, bat, hat* all have the short ‘a’ sound.\",\"- Words that rhyme sound the same at the end, like *mat* and *bat*.\",\"- Rhyming words are useful for making poems and songs.\",\"- The letter ‘y’ can act as a vowel or a consonant depending on the word.\",\"- In this chapter we learn to read, write and recognise sounds of letters.\",\"- We practice by listening, matching, and making new words.\",\"- We can use bottle caps or flashcards to practise writing letters and forming words.\",\"- When a word is missing a letter, we listen to the sound and fill in the blank.\",\"- The alphabet has 26 letters, each with a name and a sound.\",\"- Knowing sounds helps us read new words easily.\",\"- Practice makes the sounds automatic and improves spelling.\",\"- Remember to say the sound clearly when you read aloud.\",\"- Use the same sound to find rhyming pairs in a list of words.\",\"- Vowel sounds can be short or long; short sounds are usually one syllable.\",\"- Long vowel sounds are often written with a silent ‘e’ at the end, e.g., *cake*.\",\"- Short vowel sounds are usually followed by two consonants, e.g., *cat*.\",\"- Learning sounds is the first step to becoming a good reader and writer.\",\"- Keep practising with simple words and then move to longer ones.\",\"- Ask the teacher to give you more words to make and rhyme.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these words belongs to the \'a\' family?\",\"options\":[\"mat\",\"hen\",\"pin\",\"dog\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the text, \'mat\' is listed under the \'a\' family.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word belongs to the \'e\' family?\",\"options\":[\"bat\",\"red\",\"tin\",\"log\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'red\' is explicitly listed under the \'e\' family in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The words \'pin\', \'win\', and \'tin\' belong to which vowel family?\",\"options\":[\"\'a\' family\",\"\'e\' family\",\"\'i\' family\",\"\'o\' family\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text groups \'pin\', \'win\', and \'tin\' under the \'i\' family.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The words \'dog\', \'log\', and \'mop\' belong to which vowel family?\",\"options\":[\"\'a\' family\",\"\'e\' family\",\"\'i\' family\",\"\'o\' family\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text groups \'dog\', \'log\', and \'mop\' under the \'o\' family.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'sun\' and \'fun\' are in the \'u\' family, which other word from the text also belongs there?\",\"options\":[\"fan\",\"net\",\"sit\",\"bun\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"\'bun\' is listed in the \'u\' family along with \'sun\' and \'fun\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words does NOT belong to the \'a\' family?\",\"options\":[\"rat\",\"bat\",\"van\",\"net\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"\'net\' belongs to the \'e\' family, while the others belong to the \'a\' family.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the words: hen, pen, ten. What is the common vowel letter used in this family?\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"e\",\"i\",\"o\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"These words are categorized under the \'e\' family because they contain the vowel \'e\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which set of words all belong to the \'o\' family?\",\"options\":[\"hop, top, got\",\"sun, fun, run\",\"mat, rat, bat\",\"pin, win, tin\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'hop\', \'top\', and \'got\' together under the \'o\' family.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The word \'mug\' belongs to which vowel family?\",\"options\":[\"\'a\' family\",\"\'e\' family\",\"\'i\' family\",\"\'u\' family\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'mug\' under the \'u\' family.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'i\' family is listed in the text?\",\"options\":[\"pig\",\"pan\",\"pen\",\"pot\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'pig\' is the only word from the options that is listed under the \'i\' family in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21265,5,2,'English','en','Open the Treasure (Unit 1)','[\"Open the Treasure is a fun activity to learn new words.\",\"The teacher opens a Word‑Bank with small cards or chits.\",\"Students read the words aloud with the teacher’s help.\",\"They work in pairs or groups to use the words.\",\"They can find words related to food, numbers, or family members.\",\"They can find rhyming words and add one more rhyming word.\",\"Rhyming words sound the same at the end, e.g., cat‑hat, dog‑log.\",\"Students say the rhyming words aloud to practise pronunciation.\",\"Copying the words into a notebook helps memory and spelling.\",\"The activity builds vocabulary and listening skills.\",\"It encourages teamwork and discussion among students.\",\"The teacher can create new activities from the Word‑Bank.\",\"Students can write sentences using the new words.\",\"The activity is suitable for Standard‑2 English learners.\",\"It helps students recognise word patterns and sounds.\",\"It supports phonics and early reading skills.\",\"Students learn to group words by meaning or sound.\",\"The activity can be repeated with different word sets.\",\"It makes learning enjoyable and interactive.\",\"Teachers can add pictures to the Word‑Bank for visual aid.\",\"Students can draw the words they learn for better recall.\",\"The activity can be used as a warm‑up or a closing exercise.\",\"It encourages confidence in speaking English.\",\"It helps students practise spelling and writing in a fun way.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the name of the \'Bank\' mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Money-Bank\",\"Word-Bank\",\"Toy-Bank\",\"Book-Bank\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions opening the \'Word-Bank\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who helps the children to read the words?\",\"options\":[\"The Principal\",\"The Parents\",\"The Teacher\",\"The Friends\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states children should read the words with the help of the teacher.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How should the words be read from the Word-Bank?\",\"options\":[\"Silently\",\"Aloud\",\"Very fast\",\"In a whisper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instruction says to \'Read the words aloud\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where are the words written according to the teacher\'s instructions?\",\"options\":[\"On the blackboard\",\"On the wall\",\"On the chits\",\"In the textbook\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions helping children to read the words from the chits.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which type of notebook should the children copy the words?\",\"options\":[\"Single line notebook\",\"Blank notebook\",\"Four line notebook\",\"Square line notebook\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions ask children to copy the words in a four line notebook.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to follow the activity, what is the very first thing they should do?\",\"options\":[\"Write in the notebook\",\"Ask the teacher a question\",\"Open the Word-Bank\",\"Read the words aloud\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first step listed in the activity is \'Open the Word-Bank\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main reason for conducting more activities based on the \'Word-Bank\'?\",\"options\":[\"To finish the class early\",\"To enrich children\'s vocabulary\",\"To practice drawing\",\"To clean the classroom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says activities are conducted to \'enrich their vocabulary\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student has opened the Word-Bank and read the words. What should they do next according to the teacher\'s guide?\",\"options\":[\"Close the book\",\"Go to play\",\"Copy the words in a notebook\",\"Draw a picture of the bank\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Following the sequence, children are asked to repeat and then copy the words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a specific task assigned to the teacher in this lesson?\",\"options\":[\"To give prizes to children\",\"To help children read from chits\",\"To write the words for the children\",\"To buy the notebooks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s section specifically lists \'Help the children to read the words from the chits\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the expected outcome for a child who completes all the Word-Bank activities?\",\"options\":[\"They will have a better vocabulary\",\"They will learn how to save money\",\"They will learn how to draw chits\",\"They will become a teacher\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The goal of enriching vocabulary implies the child will have a better word knowledge.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21266,5,2,'English','en','It\'s Raining…','[\"It’s raining is a sentence that tells us the weather is wet.\",\"When it rains, the sky is grey and drops of water fall.\",\"Birds sing, frogs hop, ducks quack and people play outside.\",\"The word ‘rain’ is pronounced with two syllables: ‘rain’ and ‘ing’.\",\"The word ‘sing’ has one syllable, ‘sing’.\",\"The word ‘play’ has one syllable, ‘play’.\",\"The word ‘beat’ has one syllable, ‘beat’.\",\"The word ‘nest’ has one syllable, ‘nest’.\",\"The word ‘day’ has one syllable, ‘day’.\",\"The word ‘feet’ has one syllable, ‘feet’.\",\"The word ‘best’ has one syllable, ‘best’.\",\"The word ‘everyone’ has three syllables: eve‑ry‑one.\",\"The word ‘rain‑ing’ has two syllables: rain‑ing.\",\"The word ‘sing‑ing’ has two syllables: sing‑ing.\",\"The word ‘rain‑ing’ is a rhyme with ‘sing‑ing’.\",\"Rhyme means the ending sounds are the same.\",\"When you read a poem, look for words that rhyme.\",\"A picture of rain can help you remember the words.\",\"Listening to the song helps you learn the words faster.\",\"Writing the words in your notebook helps you remember them better.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What kind of day is described in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"A rainy day\",\"A sunny day\",\"A windy day\",\"A snowy day\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem repeatedly says \'It\'s raining\' and mentions it is a rainy day.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where are the birds singing?\",\"options\":[\"In the sky\",\"In the nest\",\"On the ground\",\"In the water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Birds are singing in the nest\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the frogs doing in the rain?\",\"options\":[\"Running\",\"Swimming\",\"Hopping\",\"Sleeping\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Frogs are hopping at their best\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the speaker feel about going out in the rain?\",\"options\":[\"It is scary\",\"It is boring\",\"It is sad\",\"It is fun\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem starts by saying, \'What a fun to go out on a rainy day!\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The ducks are quacking to the _____.\",\"options\":[\"Music\",\"Beat\",\"Sound\",\"Water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Ducks are quacking to the beat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is out to play on the rainy day?\",\"options\":[\"Only the ducks\",\"Only the frogs\",\"Everyone\",\"No one\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Everyone is out to play\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is described as waddling on their feet?\",\"options\":[\"Birds\",\"Frogs\",\"Ducks\",\"Cats\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"After mentioning ducks quacking, the poem says \'Some are waddling on the feet\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, what is the main activity happening?\",\"options\":[\"It is raining\",\"It is snowing\",\"It is night time\",\"It is school time\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'It\'s raining\' is repeated throughout the entire poem.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs correctly matches the animal to its action in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Birds - Hopping\",\"Frogs - Quacking\",\"Ducks - Singing\",\"Frogs - Hopping\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem specifically links frogs with hopping.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The poem says frogs are hopping at their \'best\'. What does this tell us?\",\"options\":[\"They are tired\",\"They are enjoying the rain very much\",\"They are trying to hide\",\"They are very slow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Hopping at their \'best\' while everyone is out to play suggests they are enjoying the activity.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a weather condition mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"It\'s dark!\",\"It\'s hot!\",\"It\'s loud!\",\"It\'s fast!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'It\'s hot!\' as one of the weather conditions to repeat.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the children copy the rhyming words?\",\"options\":[\"On the blackboard\",\"In their notebooks\",\"On a piece of paper\",\"In the textbook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s instructions state to ask children to copy the rhyming words in their notebooks.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text say when there is a lot of sun in the sky?\",\"options\":[\"It\'s sunny!\",\"It\'s snowing!\",\"It\'s windy!\",\"It\'s cold!\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text uses the phrase \'It\'s sunny!\' to describe weather with sun.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used in the text when water is falling from the sky?\",\"options\":[\"Hot\",\"Windy\",\"Raining\",\"Sunny\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text includes \'It\'s raining!\' as a weather condition.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you need to wear a sweater because you feel chilly, which phrase from the text describes the weather?\",\"options\":[\"It\'s hot!\",\"It\'s cold!\",\"It\'s sunny!\",\"It\'s windy!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'cold\' describes the feeling of being chilly.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you see white snow falling outside, which phrase should you repeat according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"It\'s raining!\",\"It\'s snowing!\",\"It\'s hot!\",\"It\'s windy!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'It\'s snowing!\' as the phrase for snow.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these weather words is NOT mentioned in the list in section \'c\'?\",\"options\":[\"Windy\",\"Sunny\",\"Cloudy\",\"Hot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The words windy, sunny, and hot are listed, but cloudy is not in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The teacher is asked to ask questions about other ________.\",\"options\":[\"Animals\",\"Seasons\",\"Colors\",\"Toys\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s instructions specifically mention asking questions about other seasons.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"When the wind is blowing very hard, which phrase from the text is used?\",\"options\":[\"It\'s windy!\",\"It\'s sunny!\",\"It\'s cold!\",\"It\'s hot!\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'It\'s windy!\' to describe weather with wind.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many different weather phrases are listed for the children to repeat in section \'c\'?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"6\",\"7\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrases are: cold, hot, sunny, windy, raining, and snowing, which totals six.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21267,5,2,'English','en','What the Weather Says?','[\"Weather is the state of the atmosphere at a particular time and place.\",\"The weather can be sunny, rainy, cloudy, windy or snowy.\",\"When it rains, we see water droplets falling from clouds.\",\"A rainbow appears when sunlight shines through raindrops and the light is bent.\",\"Umbrellas, raincoats and boots help us stay dry during rain.\",\"In summer, the weather is hot and we wear light clothes.\",\"In winter, the weather is cold and we wear warm clothes like coats and gloves.\",\"Clouds are made of tiny water droplets or ice crystals that float in the air.\",\"Wind is the movement of air from high pressure to low pressure areas.\",\"The weather can change quickly, so it is good to listen to the weather forecast.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should you do carefully?\",\"options\":[\"Read a book\",\"Listen to your teacher\",\"Draw a picture\",\"Run in the circle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Listen carefully to your teacher.\'\",\"topic\":\"b. Listen and follow.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many flashcards should each child take?\",\"options\":[\"Two cards\",\"Three cards\",\"Any one card\",\"All the cards\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to \'Take any one flash card.\'\",\"topic\":\"b. Listen and follow.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In what shape should the children stand for the game?\",\"options\":[\"In a square\",\"In a line\",\"In a triangle\",\"In a circle\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Stand in a circle.\'\",\"topic\":\"b. Listen and follow.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should a child do after reading the word on their card?\",\"options\":[\"Sit down\",\"Respond to the teacher\",\"Give the card back\",\"Close their eyes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Read the word and respond to the teacher.\'\",\"topic\":\"b. Listen and follow.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the teacher says \'If it\'s rainy\', where should the children with rainy season cards go?\",\"options\":[\"Outside the classroom\",\"To their desks\",\"In the middle of the circle\",\"Behind the teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says children with related cards will \'come in the middle\'.\",\"topic\":\"b. Listen and follow.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the list is related to the rainy season?\",\"options\":[\"Sunglasses\",\"Puddle\",\"Bonfire\",\"Sweater\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A puddle is formed by rain, making it related to the rainy season.\",\"topic\":\"b. Listen and follow.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a child has a card that says \'sweater\', when should they come to the middle?\",\"options\":[\"When the teacher says \'If it\'s rainy\'\",\"When the teacher says \'If it\'s summer\'\",\"When the teacher says \'If it\'s winter\'\",\"When the teacher says \'If it\'s sunny\'\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A sweater is worn in winter, so the child responds to \'If it\'s winter\'.\",\"topic\":\"b. Listen and follow.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How should the children tell the word when they are in the middle?\",\"options\":[\"Softly\",\"Loudly\",\"In a whisper\",\"By writing it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they will \'tell the word loudly\'.\",\"topic\":\"b. Listen and follow.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which card would be correct to show if the teacher says \'If it\'s summer\'?\",\"options\":[\"Raincoat\",\"Gloves\",\"Sunglasses\",\"Rainbow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sunglasses are used in summer to protect eyes from the sun.\",\"topic\":\"b. Listen and follow.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which item from the list is used to stay warm during winter?\",\"options\":[\"Paper boat\",\"Bonfire\",\"Umbrella\",\"Puddle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A bonfire is used for warmth, which is related to the winter season.\",\"topic\":\"b. Listen and follow.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher ask the children to collect?\",\"options\":[\"Stamps from different countries\",\"Pictures about seasons\",\"Dried leaves and flowers\",\"Old storybooks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly asks the teacher to have children collect pictures about seasons.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity is mentioned as being related to the seasons?\",\"options\":[\"Playing football\",\"Writing an essay\",\"Mime act\",\"Planting trees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'mime act\' as an activity related to the seasons.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher give clear instructions for?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing pictures\",\"Mathematical operations\",\"Cleaning the classroom\",\"Singing songs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states to give clear instructions related to mathematical operations.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The activities like \'mime act\' and \'making paper boats\' are related to which topic?\",\"options\":[\"Numbers\",\"Seasons\",\"Animals\",\"Food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to conduct activities related to the seasons like mime act and making paper boats.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the intended audience for these specific instructions?\",\"options\":[\"The students\",\"The parents\",\"The teacher\",\"The principal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The heading of the text is \'For the Teacher\', indicating it is meant for them.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of boats are the children supposed to make?\",\"options\":[\"Wooden boats\",\"Plastic boats\",\"Paper boats\",\"Metal boats\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions \'making paper boats\' as an activity.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher wants to follow the text, what will they ask students to bring to class?\",\"options\":[\"Pictures of summer, winter, or rainy days\",\"Calculators for math class\",\"Costumes for a play\",\"Glue and scissors\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text asks to collect pictures about seasons, which includes summer, winter, and rainy days.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"During a rainy season activity mentioned in the text, what would a student likely create?\",\"options\":[\"A paper boat\",\"A math book\",\"A picture frame\",\"A mime mask\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Making paper boats is a season-related activity mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity from the text involves acting out a season without using words?\",\"options\":[\"Making paper boats\",\"Mime act\",\"Collecting pictures\",\"Mathematical operations\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A mime act involves acting without speaking, which is one of the activities listed.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Besides English and Science (Seasons), which other subject area is the teacher asked to include?\",\"options\":[\"History\",\"Geography\",\"Mathematics\",\"Physical Education\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions giving instructions for \'mathematical operations\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21268,5,2,'English','en','A Visit to a Farm','[\"- A farm is a place where animals and crops grow.\",\"- On a Sunday we visited a farm and saw many things.\",\"- Farmers work in the fields to grow crops like oats and vegetables.\",\"- A scarecrow is a tall figure made of old clothes to keep birds away.\",\"- Animals that live on a farm include cows, bulls, chickens, hens, and sometimes goats.\",\"- Cows and bulls are called bullocks when they pull carts.\",\"- Chickens and hens lay eggs and eat grains like oats.\",\"- Farmers use a bullock cart to carry goods to the market.\",\"- Fresh, cool water is important for animals and people on the farm.\",\"- The owner of the farm can give food like oats to visitors.\",\"- A hut is a small house where people stay on the farm.\",\"- The sun rises in the east and sets in the west.\",\"- The sun brings light to the world.\",\"- The sound “moo” comes from a cow.\",\"- Visiting a farm can be a fun learning experience.\"]','[{\"q\":\"On which day did the visitors go to the farm?\",\"options\":[\"Monday\",\"Saturday\",\"Sunday\",\"Friday\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'On one Sunday, we visited a farm.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was standing in the middle of the field?\",\"options\":[\"A hut\",\"A scarecrow\",\"A bullock cart\",\"A pot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'In the middle of the field, there was a scarecrow.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What were the farmers doing in the fields?\",\"options\":[\"Sleeping\",\"Working\",\"Playing\",\"Eating\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'we saw some farmers were working in the fields.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which animals were grazing in the field?\",\"options\":[\"Hens and chickens\",\"Dogs and cats\",\"Cows and goats\",\"Horses and sheep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Some cows and goats were grazing.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the visitors stop for some time?\",\"options\":[\"Near a hut\",\"In the market\",\"On the road\",\"Under a tree\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'There was a hut in a farm. We stopped there for some time.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What were the hens and chickens doing near the hut?\",\"options\":[\"Grazing\",\"Pecking\",\"Sleeping\",\"Running\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'The hens and chickens were pecking near the hut.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you were thirsty at this farm, where would you get water from according to the story?\",\"options\":[\"A bottle\",\"A tap\",\"A pot\",\"A well\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The visitors \'drank fresh, cool water from the pot.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What did the owner of the farm give to the visitors?\",\"options\":[\"Vegetables\",\"Water\",\"Berries\",\"Chickens\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The owner of the farm gave some berries to us.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How was the farmer carrying fresh vegetables to the market?\",\"options\":[\"In a truck\",\"In a bullock cart\",\"On a cycle\",\"In a basket\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'we saw a bullock cart. The farmer was carrying fresh vegetables to the market.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did the visitors feel about their trip to the farm?\",\"options\":[\"They were bored\",\"They were tired\",\"They enjoyed it\",\"They were sad\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes with, \'It was really a nice day. We enjoyed our visit to the farm.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, where does the sun rise?\",\"options\":[\"In the West\",\"In the North\",\"In the East\",\"In the South\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I rise in the East\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the sun set according to the riddle?\",\"options\":[\"In the East\",\"In the West\",\"In the North\",\"In the South\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I set in the West\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the sun bring to the world?\",\"options\":[\"Darkness\",\"Light\",\"Rain\",\"Cold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I bring light to the world\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal says \'moo\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A dog\",\"A cat\",\"A cow\",\"A goat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes an animal that says \'moo\' and gives milk, which is a cow.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the animal that says \'moo\' give us?\",\"options\":[\"Eggs\",\"Wool\",\"Milk\",\"Honey\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I say “moo”, and give milk\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see the sun rising in the East, what part of the day is it?\",\"options\":[\"Night\",\"Morning\",\"Evening\",\"Midnight\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Rising in the East happens at the start of the day, which is morning.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where would you likely be if you are visiting the animal that gives milk?\",\"options\":[\"At a school\",\"At a farm\",\"At a market\",\"At a park\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The chapter title is \'A Visit to a Farm\', where cows are typically found.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What are the children encouraged to share in this lesson?\",\"options\":[\"Their toys\",\"Their food\",\"Their experiences about a farm visit\",\"Their books\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Encourage the children to share their experiences about their visit to a farm\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which two things are described through riddles in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A tree and a flower\",\"The sun and a cow\",\"A bird and a fish\",\"A car and a bike\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'Who am I?\' riddles to describe the sun and the cow.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the teacher help the children with pictures?\",\"options\":[\"To help them learn to draw\",\"To help them learn the words\",\"To help them color\",\"To help them sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'help the children to learn the words using the pictures\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21269,5,2,'English','en','In the Park','[\"- The chapter is about a visit to the park.\",\"- Children talk about going to the park every day.\",\"- They decide to play on the swing first.\",\"- They wait for their turn before playing.\",\"- They see a ladder near the slide.\",\"- They decide to climb the ladder carefully.\",\"- The story teaches sharing and waiting.\",\"- It also teaches safety: climb carefully.\",\"- The park is a place for fun and play.\",\"- Children use polite words like \\\"please\\\" and \\\"thank you\\\".\",\"- They use simple present tense to describe actions.\",\"- The story shows friendship between Siya and Riya.\",\"- It encourages speaking in English about everyday activities.\",\"- It highlights the importance of keeping the park clean.\",\"- It reminds us to stay green and protect nature.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who are the two friends talking in the park?\",\"options\":[\"Siya and Riya\",\"Meena and Tina\",\"Rahul and Raj\",\"Siya and Meena\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text begins with a dialogue between Siya and Riya.\",\"topic\":\"Park Slogans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Riya say she likes?\",\"options\":[\"The school\",\"The park\",\"The house\",\"The shop\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Riya says, \'Yes! I like this park.\'\",\"topic\":\"Park Slogans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do the girls want to go on first?\",\"options\":[\"The slide\",\"The ladder\",\"The swing\",\"The bench\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Siya says, \'Let\'s go on the swing first.\'\",\"topic\":\"Park Slogans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should the girls do before using the swing?\",\"options\":[\"Run fast\",\"Shout loudly\",\"Wait for their turn\",\"Push others\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Riya says, \'Let\'s wait for our turn.\'\",\"topic\":\"Park Slogans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the ladder located according to Riya?\",\"options\":[\"Far away\",\"Near the slide\",\"On the swing\",\"Under the tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Riya says, \'Look, there is a ladder near the slide.\'\",\"topic\":\"Park Slogans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How must the girls climb the ladder?\",\"options\":[\"Quickly\",\"Carefully\",\"With eyes closed\",\"Running\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Riya says, \'But we must climb the ladder carefully.\'\",\"topic\":\"Park Slogans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which slogan tells us to keep the park beautiful and full of plants?\",\"options\":[\"Use me\",\"Wait for turn\",\"Keep clean, stay green\",\"Climb carefully\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The slogan \'Keep clean, stay green\' refers to maintaining the environment.\",\"topic\":\"Park Slogans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the slogan \'USE ME\' usually refer to in a park?\",\"options\":[\"A swing\",\"A dustbin\",\"A slide\",\"A flower\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'USE ME\' is a common slogan found on dustbins to encourage people to throw trash in them.\",\"topic\":\"Park Slogans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Riya say \'Let\'s wait for our turn\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because she is tired\",\"To follow good manners and safety\",\"Because she is scared\",\"To go home early\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Waiting for a turn is a way to be polite and safe in a public park.\",\"topic\":\"Park Slogans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a good rule to follow in the park based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Throw trash on the ground\",\"Climb ladders carelessly\",\"Keep the park clean\",\"Don\'t wait for your turn\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text includes the slogan \'Keep clean, stay green\' as a rule for the park.\",\"topic\":\"Park Slogans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the instruction in the text meant for?\",\"options\":[\"The children\",\"The teacher\",\"The parents\",\"The gardener\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text starts with the heading \'For the Teacher\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher give more exposure to?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing the picture\",\"Coloring the picture\",\"Conversing on the picture\",\"Buying the picture\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Give more exposure to converse on the above picture\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the text, what does the word \'converse\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"To run\",\"To sleep\",\"To talk\",\"To draw\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In this context, to converse means to talk or speak about the picture.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher encourage the children to do?\",\"options\":[\"To speak\",\"To play\",\"To shout\",\"To sit quietly\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Encourage the children to speak\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"On what kind of situations should the children speak?\",\"options\":[\"Different situations\",\"Similar situations\",\"Difficult situations\",\"Scary situations\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies to speak on \'similar situations\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher shows a picture of a park and asks children to talk about it, what are they providing?\",\"options\":[\"Homework\",\"Exposure to converse\",\"A test\",\"A drawing lesson\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Talking about the picture is giving exposure to converse.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When a child talks about their own visit to a park after seeing the picture, they are speaking on a:\",\"options\":[\"Similar situation\",\"New language\",\"Math problem\",\"Hidden picture\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A personal visit to a park is a similar situation to the \'In the Park\' picture.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal of the teacher\'s instruction in this text?\",\"options\":[\"To make children quiet\",\"To help children practice speaking\",\"To teach children how to paint\",\"To check the children\'s bags\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Encouraging children to converse and speak helps them practice speaking.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which action by the teacher follows the instruction in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Asking children to keep their books away\",\"Asking children to describe what they see in the picture\",\"Asking children to write a long essay\",\"Asking children to go home early\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Describing a picture is a way to converse on it.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, who is supposed to speak?\",\"options\":[\"Only the teacher\",\"The children\",\"The people in the picture\",\"No one\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Encourage the children to speak\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21270,5,2,'English','en','A Joyful Trip','[\"- A Joyful Trip is a story about Nitu and her helicopter.\",\"- Nitu’s Ajoba (grandfather) gave her a helicopter.\",\"- Nitu loves the helicopter and wishes to be a pilot.\",\"- She talks to the helicopter and keeps it with her when she sleeps.\",\"- The story mentions a zebra crossing and a traffic signal.\",\"- Nitu sees a dream about flying over trains and boats.\",\"- The teacher can ask students to retell the story and act it out.\",\"- Students can learn new words like helicopter, zebra, signal, dream, pilot.\",\"- The story encourages imagination and describing places.\",\"- Students can name places around their city such as bank, hospital, school, garden, zoo, etc.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who gave Nitu a helicopter?\",\"options\":[\"Ajoba\",\"The teacher\",\"The author\",\"Her friend\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that Nitu\'s Ajoba gave her a helicopter.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Nitu love to do with the helicopter?\",\"options\":[\"Give it away\",\"Play with it\",\"Draw it\",\"Break it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Nitu loved to play with the helicopter.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should children do after looking at the pictures in section \'a\'?\",\"options\":[\"Color them\",\"Talk about them\",\"Cut them\",\"Hide them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instruction says to look at the pictures and talk about them.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How should children retell the story according to the teacher\'s instructions?\",\"options\":[\"By reading it loudly\",\"Using their imagination\",\"By copying it\",\"By listening only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher is asked to let children retell the story using their imagination.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the teacher help children find the meanings of new words?\",\"options\":[\"In a notebook\",\"In the dictionary\",\"On a picture\",\"In a helicopter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to help children find new words and their meanings in the dictionary.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What are children asked to copy in their notebooks?\",\"options\":[\"Pictures\",\"Words\",\"Numbers\",\"Stories\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Section \'c\' asks children to listen and copy the words in their notebook.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When retelling the story, the child should act as if they are a\\/an...\",\"options\":[\"Teacher\",\"Author\",\"Ajoba\",\"Helicopter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests children retell the story as if they are an author.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very first thing children are asked to do in section \'a\'?\",\"options\":[\"Look at the pictures\",\"Write a story\",\"Find a dictionary\",\"Play with toys\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first instruction in section \'a\' is \'Look at the following pictures\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the teacher encourage the children to do with the story?\",\"options\":[\"Forget it\",\"Enact it\",\"Draw it\",\"Listen only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s instructions include encouraging children to enact the story.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to section \'c\', what must happen before copying the words?\",\"options\":[\"Talking\",\"Enacting\",\"Listening\",\"Playing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Section \'c\' says \'Listen and copy\', meaning listening comes first.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21271,5,2,'English','en','Music Store','[\"Music store is a place where you can buy musical instruments.\",\"Common instruments in a music store include piano, flute, drum, tabla, guitar, violin, harmonium, sitar, trumpet, and mridanga.\",\"A drum makes a sound like \\\"dhum-dhum-dhum\\\" when you hit it.\",\"A tabla makes a sound like \\\"dha-din-dha\\\" when you play it.\",\"A piano makes a sound like \\\"plink-plink-plink\\\" when you press the keys.\",\"A flute makes a sound like \\\"toodle-oodle-oo\\\" when you blow into it.\",\"A violin makes a sound like \\\"sha-la-la\\\" when you play it.\",\"You can sing and dance while listening to music from these instruments.\",\"When you visit a music store, you can see, listen, and even try the instruments.\",\"You can create your own poem using the sounds of different instruments.\",\"In Maharashtra, other instruments you may find are mridanga, harmonium, and sitar.\",\"The word \\\"taal\\\" means rhythm or beat in music.\",\"When you fill in the vowels in instrument names, you learn how to spell them correctly.\",\"You can discuss with friends where you have seen these instruments.\",\"Music is a fun way to learn about sounds and rhythm.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did the person in the song walk into?\",\"options\":[\"A toy shop\",\"A music store\",\"A school\",\"A garden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first line of the song states, \'I walked into a music store.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What word is used to describe the flute in the song?\",\"options\":[\"Big\",\"Heavy\",\"Little\",\"Long\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song says, \'I bought a flute, a little flute.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound does the little flute make according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Plink-plink-plink\",\"Toodle-oodle-oo\",\"Ding-dong-ding\",\"Boom-boom-boom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the flute\'s sound as \'Toodle-oodle-oo\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which instrument is described as \'big\' in the song?\",\"options\":[\"The flute\",\"The guitar\",\"The piano\",\"The drum\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song mentions, \'I bought a piano, a big piano.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What sound does the big piano make?\",\"options\":[\"Toodle-oodle-oo\",\"Sha-la-la\",\"Plink-plink-plink\",\"Sha-la-lee\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song describes the piano\'s sound as \'Plink-plink-plink\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what instrument is the man handing to the boy?\",\"options\":[\"A guitar\",\"A piano\",\"A flute\",\"A trumpet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the man handing a small flute to the boy.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/044_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many guitars are hanging on the wall?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"There are three guitars visible on the left side of the wall in the picture.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/044_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How does the song suggest we should sing and dance?\",\"options\":[\"Slowly\",\"Happily\",\"Quietly\",\"Sadly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The song says, \'Sing and dance so happily!\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the line from the song: \'Come and play along with ____!\'\",\"options\":[\"him\",\"them\",\"us\",\"me\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The song ends with the line, \'Come and play along with me!\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these instruments was NOT bought by the person?\",\"options\":[\"Flute\",\"Piano\",\"Guitar\",\"A little flute\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text only mentions buying a flute and a piano; it does not mention buying a guitar.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which sound does the drum make in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"ting-ting-ting\",\"dhum-dhum-dhum\",\"dha-din-dha\",\"trin-trin-trin\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the drum makes the sound \'dhum-dhum-dhum\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these instruments is mentioned in the list?\",\"options\":[\"Whistle\",\"Bell\",\"Flute\",\"Horn\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Flute is the first instrument mentioned in the \'Look, listen and repeat\' list.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which instrument starts with the letter \'V\' in the list?\",\"options\":[\"Violin\",\"Vase\",\"Van\",\"Vest\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Violin and Veena are listed as musical instruments in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound does the \'tabla\' make according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"dhum-dhum-dhum\",\"dha-din-dha\",\"pip-pip-pip\",\"boom-boom-boom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text associates the tabla with the sound \'dha-din-dha\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are the children asked to create using different musical instruments?\",\"options\":[\"A story\",\"A picture\",\"A poem\",\"A dance\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks to \'Create a poem by using different musical instruments\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a musical instrument from the list?\",\"options\":[\"Harmonium\",\"Hammer\",\"Helmet\",\"Handle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Harmonium is included in the list of instruments to look, listen, and repeat.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to sing a poem about a drum, what sound will you use?\",\"options\":[\"dha-din-dha\",\"dhum-dhum-dhum\",\"la-la-la\",\"ha-ha-ha\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the text, the sound for a drum is \'dhum-dhum-dhum\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How can you make a new poem according to the teacher\'s instructions?\",\"options\":[\"By drawing pictures\",\"By changing the colors\",\"By replacing the names of musical instruments\",\"By writing a story\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note says to sing the poem by replacing the names of musical instruments.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which instrument is paired with the sound \'dha-din-dha\'?\",\"options\":[\"Drum\",\"Tabla\",\"Guitar\",\"Piano\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'tabla - dha-din-dha\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT in the list of instruments to \'Look, listen and repeat\'?\",\"options\":[\"Mridanga\",\"Khanjiri\",\"Taal\",\"Radio\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Radio is not mentioned in the list of musical instruments provided in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21272,5,2,'English','en','The Story of the Flute','[\"- The story is about how a flute was made from bamboo.\",\"- Long ago, a bamboo forest had green and yellow bamboos.\",\"- Wind blew through the bamboo holes and produced music: Sa Re Ga Ma Pa Dha Ni Sa.\",\"- Bees and their friends made holes in the bamboo, creating more music.\",\"- Birds were amazed and thought the bamboos were singing like them.\",\"- Tribal people heard the music and cut bamboo to make a flute.\",\"- They blew into a big hole and made six small holes to play notes.\",\"- The first flute produced the same musical notes as the wind.\",\"- The flute became a popular instrument for everyone.\",\"- The story shows how nature and humans can create music together.\",\"- It teaches that even simple things can become beautiful when used creatively.\",\"- The story uses simple language suitable for Standard‑2 students.\",\"- Key words: bamboo, wind, music, flute, holes, notes, tribal people.\",\"- The story encourages imagination and listening skills.\",\"- It also introduces the musical scale: Sa Re Ga Ma Pa Dha Ni Sa.\",\"- The story highlights teamwork: bees, birds, and humans all contributed.\",\"- It shows that instruments can be made from natural materials.\",\"- The story ends with the flute singing for everyone.\",\"- The narrative is short, clear, and easy to retell.\",\"- It can be used to teach listening, imagination, and basic music concepts.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What were the colors of the bamboos in the forest?\",\"options\":[\"Red and blue\",\"Green and yellow\",\"Pink and white\",\"Brown and black\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states there were green and yellow bamboos in the forest.\",\"topic\":\"The Bumblebees\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How was the wind blowing in the bamboos?\",\"options\":[\"dho-dho\",\"ha-ha\",\"so-so\",\"la-la\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the wind was blowing \'so-so\' in the bamboos.\",\"topic\":\"The Bumblebees\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which bird was dancing happily in the bamboo forest?\",\"options\":[\"Sparrow\",\"Parrot\",\"Crow\",\"Peacock\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"According to the text, peacocks were dancing happily.\",\"topic\":\"The Bumblebees\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound was the rain making as it fell?\",\"options\":[\"so-so\",\"humming\",\"dho-dho\",\"singing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the rain falling as \'dho-dho\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Bumblebees\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the shiny bumblebee do when it came to the forest?\",\"options\":[\"It started dancing\",\"It came humming\",\"It started singing\",\"It blew like the wind\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says a shiny bumblebee came humming.\",\"topic\":\"The Bumblebees\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the bumblebee and its friends start making in the bamboo?\",\"options\":[\"Nests\",\"Holes\",\"Food\",\"Music\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that they began to make holes in the bamboo.\",\"topic\":\"The Bumblebees\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is one reason the bamboos could not tell anyone about their problem?\",\"options\":[\"They were too tall\",\"They were yellow\",\"They could not speak\",\"They were dancing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the bamboos could not even speak.\",\"topic\":\"The Bumblebees\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The text says the bamboos did not have hands or legs. What does this imply about them?\",\"options\":[\"They could run away\",\"They could not move or defend themselves\",\"They were very strong\",\"They liked the bumblebees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Having no hands or legs means they were helpless against the bumblebees making holes.\",\"topic\":\"The Bumblebees\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the author call them \'Poor bamboos!\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they had no money\",\"Because they were being hurt and could not do anything\",\"Because the forest was very old\",\"Because the birds were singing too loudly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The term \'poor\' is used here to show sympathy because they were being damaged and were helpless.\",\"topic\":\"The Bumblebees\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these things did the bamboos NOT have according to the story?\",\"options\":[\"Colors\",\"A forest\",\"Speech\",\"The wind\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the bamboos could not even speak.\",\"topic\":\"The Bumblebees\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the breeze dance into?\",\"options\":[\"The river\",\"The forest\",\"The village\",\"The mountains\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the breeze danced into the forest.\",\"topic\":\"The Tribal People\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the birds say the bamboos were doing?\",\"options\":[\"Dancing like us\",\"Sleeping like us\",\"Singing like us\",\"Flying like us\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The birds said, \'Look! The bamboos are singing like us...!\'\",\"topic\":\"The Tribal People\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why were the birds in the forest amazed?\",\"options\":[\"Because of the music\",\"Because of the rain\",\"Because of the tribal people\",\"Because of the dark forest\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the birds were amazed because of that music.\",\"topic\":\"The Tribal People\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the tribal people do after hearing the sweet music?\",\"options\":[\"They planted more bamboo\",\"They cut some bamboo\",\"They started dancing\",\"They went back home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they cut some bamboo after hearing the music.\",\"topic\":\"The Tribal People\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the story, how did the music come out of the bamboo?\",\"options\":[\"By hitting the bamboo\",\"By shaking the bamboo\",\"By blowing into the bamboo\",\"By washing the bamboo\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the tribal people \'blew into it\' and sweet tunes came out.\",\"topic\":\"The Tribal People\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did the tribal people feel after blowing into the bamboo?\",\"options\":[\"They were very happy\",\"They were scared\",\"They were still not happy\",\"They were very angry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that even though sweet tunes came out, \'still they were not happy.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Tribal People\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which musical notes are mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Do Re Mi Fa\",\"A B C D\",\"Sa Re Ga Ma\",\"1 2 3 4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists the notes \'Sa Re Ga Ma Pa Dha Ni Sa\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Tribal People\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the tribal people cut the bamboo?\",\"options\":[\"To make a fire\",\"To try and make music themselves\",\"To build a house\",\"To clear the forest path\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They liked the music they heard and cut the bamboo to blow into it and make tunes.\",\"topic\":\"The Tribal People\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the tribal people looking at?\",\"options\":[\"The clouds\",\"The bamboo stalks\",\"The birds\",\"The grass\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows the tribal people standing in front of and looking at the bamboo stalks.\",\"topic\":\"The Tribal People\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/047_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is visible on the bamboo stalks that the breeze enters?\",\"options\":[\"Holes\",\"Leaves\",\"Flowers\",\"Fruit\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The drawing shows black spots representing holes on the bamboo stalks.\",\"topic\":\"The Tribal People\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/047_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How many big holes were made to blow air into the flute?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Six\",\"Seven\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states they made one big hole to blow air in.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the purpose of the six small holes?\",\"options\":[\"To blow air in\",\"To hold the flute\",\"To play notes\",\"To clean the flute\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they made six small holes to play notes.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a note mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Do Re Mi\",\"Sa Re Ga Ma\",\"A B C D\",\"1 2 3 4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Sa Re Ga Ma Pa Dha Ni Sa\' as the notes.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the name of the musical instrument created in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Drum\",\"Flute\",\"Guitar\",\"Whistle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the object as the first flute.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who did the flute sing for after it was made?\",\"options\":[\"Only the makers\",\"Only the birds\",\"Everyone\",\"Nobody\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'from then on, the flute sang for everyone.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the author of this story?\",\"options\":[\"Dr. Sangita Barve\",\"A student\",\"A musician\",\"A teacher\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text attributes the story to Dr. Sangita Barve.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The story was originally written in which language?\",\"options\":[\"English\",\"Hindi\",\"Marathi\",\"Sanskrit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states it was adapted and translated from Marathi.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many small holes in total were made in the flute?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"4\",\"6\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states they made six small holes.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What must you do with the big hole to make the flute work?\",\"options\":[\"Cover it with a finger\",\"Blow air into it\",\"Pour water in it\",\"Look through it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the big hole is \'to blow air in\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what happened after the holes were made?\",\"options\":[\"The flute was broken\",\"The flute was hidden\",\"The first flute was created\",\"The flute stopped working\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says that after making the holes, \'This was the first flute.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21273,5,2,'English','en','Tring-Tring','[\"- Tring‑Tring is a short dialogue about a call between friends.\",\"- It shows how to greet and ask for permission to talk.\",\"- The conversation uses simple sentences and polite words like \\\"Namaste\\\" and \\\"please\\\".\",\"- It introduces the idea of Warli art and a friendly invitation.\",\"- Key phrases: \\\"Hello\\\", \\\"I am…\\\", \\\"Can I talk to…?\\\", \\\"Yes, wait a minute\\\", \\\"Did you finish your homework?\\\", \\\"Will you come to my house?\\\".\",\"- The dialogue also shows a phone call with a friend named John.\",\"- Students should practice speaking the dialogue aloud.\",\"- They can also ask each other similar questions in class.\",\"- The teacher can ask students to draw simple Warli pictures after the dialogue.\",\"- Warli art is a type of tribal art from Maharashtra.\",\"- The story ends with a friendly goodbye: \\\"Ok. Bye.\\\"\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is Amit?\",\"options\":[\"John\'s brother\",\"John\'s friend\",\"John\'s cousin\",\"John\'s teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Amit introduces himself to John\'s mother as \'John’s friend\'.\",\"topic\":\"Amit and John\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What greeting does Amit use when speaking to John\'s mother?\",\"options\":[\"Good morning\",\"Hi\",\"Namaste\",\"Good night\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Amit says \'Namaste Aunty\' to show respect to John\'s mother.\",\"topic\":\"Amit and John\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who answers the phone call first?\",\"options\":[\"John\",\"Amit\",\"John\'s mother\",\"John\'s father\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The dialogue shows Amit talking to John\'s mother before John comes to the phone.\",\"topic\":\"Amit and John\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Amit ask John about his school work?\",\"options\":[\"Did you go to school?\",\"Did you finish your homework?\",\"Do you have a pen?\",\"Is the school closed?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Amit specifically asks, \'Did you finish your homework?\'\",\"topic\":\"Amit and John\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What activity does Amit suggest they do together?\",\"options\":[\"Play football\",\"Draw Warli pictures\",\"Read a story\",\"Go to the park\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Amit says, \'We shall draw Warli pictures.\'\",\"topic\":\"Amit and John\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is Warli art?\",\"options\":[\"A type of tribal art\",\"A type of music\",\"A type of dance\",\"A type of food\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Amit explains to John that Warli pictures are a type of tribal art.\",\"topic\":\"Amit and John\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If John wants to draw the pictures with Amit, where must he go?\",\"options\":[\"To the school\",\"To the library\",\"To Amit\'s house\",\"To the market\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Amit asks, \'Will you come to my house?\' to draw the pictures.\",\"topic\":\"Amit and John\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What must John do before he can go to Amit\'s house?\",\"options\":[\"Finish his homework\",\"Eat his lunch\",\"Buy colors\",\"Call his teacher\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Amit asks about the homework first, and John confirms he has finished it before agreeing to come.\",\"topic\":\"Amit and John\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does John feel when he hears about Warli pictures?\",\"options\":[\"He is bored\",\"He is curious to know what they are\",\"He is scared\",\"He is angry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"John asks \'What are Warli pictures?\' showing he is interested in learning about them.\",\"topic\":\"Amit and John\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does John\'s mother say \'wait a minute\' to Amit?\",\"options\":[\"She is busy cooking\",\"She is looking for a pen\",\"She needs to call John to the phone\",\"She wants to hang up\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"She tells Amit to wait so she can tell John that his friend is on the call.\",\"topic\":\"Amit and John\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher give children more practice in?\",\"options\":[\"Singing songs\",\"Conversing likewise\",\"Running fast\",\"Writing stories\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to give children more practice to converse likewise.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which type of art is mentioned in the teacher\'s instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Modern art\",\"Warli art\",\"Oil painting\",\"Paper craft\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions helping children to draw basic shapes of Warli art.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What part of Warli art should the teacher help children draw?\",\"options\":[\"Complex portraits\",\"Basic shapes\",\"Large buildings\",\"Colorful flowers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies helping children draw the \'basic shapes\' of Warli art.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher encourage children to talk about?\",\"options\":[\"Other similar situations\",\"Their favorite food\",\"Mathematics problems\",\"School holidays\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The instructions tell the teacher to encourage children to talk on other similar situations.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'converse likewise\', what does \'converse\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"To draw\",\"To talk\",\"To run\",\"To sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, conversing refers to the practice of talking or having a conversation.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the teacher\'s role when children are drawing Warli art?\",\"options\":[\"To watch them only\",\"To draw for them\",\"To help them draw basic shapes\",\"To give them grades\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the teacher should \'Help the children to draw basic shapes\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher asks a student to talk about a phone call after reading the lesson, which instruction are they following?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing Warli art\",\"Giving practice to converse likewise\",\"Teaching new words\",\"Checking homework\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Talking in a similar way to the lesson content is \'conversing likewise\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A teacher asks a child to talk about meeting a friend at the park. This is an example of:\",\"options\":[\"Drawing basic shapes\",\"Talking on other similar situations\",\"Practicing spelling\",\"Learning Warli art\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Talking about a different but comparable event is talking on \'other similar situations\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity mentioned in the text combines verbal communication and practice?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing shapes\",\"Conversing likewise\",\"Looking at pictures\",\"Sitting quietly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Conversing involves verbal communication and the text suggests giving \'more practice\' for it.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the instructions, which of these is a creative task for the children?\",\"options\":[\"Listening to the teacher\",\"Drawing basic shapes of Warli art\",\"Reading the textbook silently\",\"Cleaning the classroom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Drawing shapes of Warli art is the creative activity mentioned in the teacher\'s notes.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21274,5,2,'English','en','Origami','[\"- Origami means folding paper to make shapes.\",\"- A square sheet of paper is used for a paper boat.\",\"- First fold the square in half, then fold it again in half.\",\"- Fold three corners of the paper to one side and the last corner to the other side to form a triangle.\",\"- Open the triangle from the middle to make a square shape again.\",\"- Pull the flaps outwards and press the folds to shape the boat.\",\"- The boat is ready when the folds are firm and the shape holds.\",\"- Origami helps develop hand‑eye coordination and fine motor skills.\",\"- It also encourages patience and concentration.\",\"- The teacher can appoint a leader to guide the class.\",\"- The leader should give clear, simple instructions.\",\"- The teacher should supervise and help if someone is stuck.\",\"- Origami can be used for other paper crafts too.\",\"- Always use a clean, flat surface to fold paper.\",\"- Keep the paper dry and free of tears for best results.\",\"- After making the boat, you can decorate it with markers or stickers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What shape of paper is needed to start making the boat?\",\"options\":[\"A circle paper\",\"A square paper\",\"A triangle paper\",\"A rectangle paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Take a square paper\' to begin the activity.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very first step mentioned in the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Fold it in half\",\"Pull the flaps\",\"Press the fold\",\"Open the triangle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first instruction after taking the paper is \'Fold it in half.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many times should the paper be folded in half at the beginning?\",\"options\":[\"One time\",\"Two times\",\"Three times\",\"Four times\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Fold it in half\' and then \'Fold it into half again\', which equals two times.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many parts of the paper are folded to one side to form a triangle?\",\"options\":[\"One part\",\"Two parts\",\"Three parts\",\"Four parts\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Fold three parts of the paper to one side.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What shape is ready after folding three parts to one side and the remaining one to the other?\",\"options\":[\"A square\",\"A circle\",\"A triangle\",\"A boat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'A triangle is ready\' after these specific folds.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"From where should you open the triangle to make the square?\",\"options\":[\"From the top\",\"From the corner\",\"From the middle\",\"From the side\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instruction is to \'Open the triangle from the middle to make the square.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final action to make the boat ready after pulling the flaps outwards?\",\"options\":[\"Press the fold\",\"Cut the paper\",\"Color the boat\",\"Fold it in half again\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Press the fold and your boat is ready.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who should the teacher appoint to conduct the activity?\",\"options\":[\"A monitor\",\"A leader\",\"A helper\",\"A guest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Appoint a leader and conduct the activity.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher guide the leader about?\",\"options\":[\"How to draw a boat\",\"How to clean the room\",\"How to give the instructions\",\"How to fold the paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Guide the leader about how to give the instructions.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of activity is being performed in this lesson?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing\",\"Origami\",\"Singing\",\"Dancing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Conduct other Origami activities\' at the end.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21275,5,2,'English','en','Sounds - II','[\"1. A sound is a vibration that travels through the air and can be heard by our ears.\",\"2. In English, words are made of letters that make sounds.\",\"3. Vowels are the letters A, E, I, O, U and sometimes Y.\",\"4. Consonants are all the other letters.\",\"5. Some letters together make one sound, e.g., \'sh\' sounds like the word \'shush\'.\",\"6. The same letter can make different sounds, e.g., \'a\' in \'cat\' and \'cake\'.\",\"7. Short vowel sounds are quick, like the \'a\' in \'cat\'.\",\"8. Long vowel sounds are pronounced as the letter name, like the \'a\' in \'cake\'.\",\"9. The letter \'y\' can be a vowel or a consonant; as a vowel it sounds like \'i\' or \'e\'.\",\"10. In words, the first letter often gives the main sound, but sometimes the last letter changes it.\",\"11. Words can be broken into syllables – each syllable usually has one vowel sound.\",\"12. Reading syllables helps us pronounce new words correctly.\",\"13. When we see a word with blanks, we fill in the missing letters to make a real word.\",\"14. A word list in a grid can hide many words; we look for patterns of letters.\",\"15. Practice makes our reading and listening skills stronger.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these words has the \'ee\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"book\",\"feet\",\"cook\",\"moon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'feet\' is listed under the \'ee\' sound group in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list has the \'oo\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"green\",\"sheep\",\"deep\",\"food\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The word \'food\' is listed under the \'oo\' sound group in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher\'s instructions, where should children find the meanings of words?\",\"options\":[\"In a dictionary\",\"On the moon\",\"In the food\",\"On their feet\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that teachers should help children find meanings in the dictionary.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'ee\' list is a color?\",\"options\":[\"seed\",\"green\",\"sheep\",\"deep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Green is a color found in the \'ee\' sound list.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'oo\' list is something you can read?\",\"options\":[\"book\",\"cook\",\"food\",\"cool\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A book is an object used for reading, found in the \'oo\' list.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'oo\' list is seen in the sky at night?\",\"options\":[\"food\",\"cool\",\"moon\",\"book\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The moon is an object in the sky, listed under the \'oo\' sound.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'feet\' has the \'ee\' sound, which other word has the same sound?\",\"options\":[\"cook\",\"sheep\",\"moon\",\"cool\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both \'feet\' and \'sheep\' belong to the \'ee\' sound group.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word has the same vowel sound as \'food\'?\",\"options\":[\"seed\",\"deep\",\"cool\",\"green\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Both \'food\' and \'cool\' are part of the \'oo\' sound group.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words does NOT belong to the \'ee\' sound group?\",\"options\":[\"seed\",\"green\",\"deep\",\"book\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Book belongs to the \'oo\' group, while the others belong to the \'ee\' group.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list rhymes with \'book\'?\",\"options\":[\"feet\",\"cook\",\"seed\",\"deep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the \'oo\' list, \'book\' and \'cook\' share the same ending sound.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21276,5,2,'English','en','Open the Treasure (Unit 2)','[\"1. The chapter is about opening a treasure of words.\",\"2. A Word‑Bank is a list of words that children can choose from.\",\"3. Children pick 3 to 4 words from the Word‑Bank.\",\"4. They read the chosen words aloud with the teacher’s help.\",\"5. Using those words, they make a short story or a poem.\",\"6. After the story or poem, the teacher asks questions about it.\",\"7. Questions help children think about the story’s characters and events.\",\"8. Example story: a frog did not go to school because it was raining.\",\"9. Example poem: a frog hops and dances in the rain.\",\"10. The main character in the example story is the frog.\",\"11. The animal mentioned is a frog.\",\"12. The frog did not go to school because it was raining heavily.\",\"13. The activity encourages creativity and speaking skills.\",\"14. It also improves listening and comprehension.\",\"15. Use simple sentences and clear pictures in the Word‑Bank.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the first step to start the activity mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Read a book\",\"Open the ‘Word-Bank’\",\"Draw a picture\",\"Go to school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to \'(1) Open the ‘Word-Bank’\' as the first step.\",\"topic\":\"Example: Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many words should you select from the Word-Bank?\",\"options\":[\"One word\",\"Ten words\",\"Three to four words\",\"Five to six words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions say to \'Select three to four words.\'\",\"topic\":\"Example: Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who should help you read the words aloud?\",\"options\":[\"Your friends\",\"Your teacher\",\"The frog\",\"Your parents\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Read the words aloud with the help of your teacher.\'\",\"topic\":\"Example: Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the example story, why did the frog not go to school?\",\"options\":[\"He was sleeping\",\"He was hungry\",\"It was raining heavily\",\"He was lost\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story states, \'One day, it was raining heavily. A frog did not go to school.\'\",\"topic\":\"Example: Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did 