ory instead\",\"Give them the words\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the teacher to help the children to compose.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Sonu is picking words for his story, who should be making the choice?\",\"options\":[\"His teacher\",\"His friend\",\"Sonu himself\",\"His parents\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says children should choose words \'on their own\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which two creative works are mentioned that involve composing?\",\"options\":[\"Words and Help\",\"Story and Poem\",\"Teacher and Children\",\"Own and Choose\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically lists a story and a poem as things to compose.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which action shows the children are working \'on their own\'?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher choosing the topic\",\"The children choosing the words\",\"The teacher writing the poem\",\"The children asking for the answer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Choosing words on their own is the specific independent action mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21277,5,2,'English','en','Where is it?','[\"- ‘Where is it?’ asks you to find the location of an object.\",\"- Use prepositions like on, in, under, near, behind, between, inside to describe positions.\",\"- ‘On’ means the object is on top of something.\",\"- ‘In’ means the object is inside something, like a box or a bag.\",\"- ‘Under’ means the object is below something, like a table or a shelf.\",\"- ‘Near’ means the object is close to something, but not touching it.\",\"- ‘Behind’ means the object is at the back of something.\",\"- ‘Between’ means the object is in the middle of two things.\",\"- ‘Inside’ is similar to ‘in’ but emphasises being inside a closed space.\",\"- When you hear a sentence like ‘The books are in the bag’, you can answer ‘in’.\",\"- When you see a picture, look for the object and the object it is near to, on, under, etc.\",\"- You can ask questions like ‘Where is the ball?’ to practice prepositions.\",\"- Listen to dialogues and find where each item is located.\",\"- Practice by making your own rhyme or poem about an object’s location.\",\"- Remember to use the correct preposition for each situation.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where are the notebooks kept according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"In the bag\",\"Under the table\",\"On the desk\",\"Near the house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The notebooks are on the desk.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the fox?\",\"options\":[\"On the rack\",\"In the box\",\"Under the table\",\"Near the house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Where is the fox? in the box, in the box.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the bottle located?\",\"options\":[\"On the desk\",\"In the bag\",\"Under the table\",\"Near the house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'A bottle is under the table.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the mouse in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Near the house\",\"In the box\",\"On the rack\",\"Under the table\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem asks, \'Where is the mouse? near the house, near the house.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to find the sack, where should you look?\",\"options\":[\"In the box\",\"Under the table\",\"On the rack\",\"Near the house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the sack is \'on the rack\'.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where should you put the books according to the first paragraph?\",\"options\":[\"On the desk\",\"In the bag\",\"Under the table\",\"Near the house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The books are in the bag.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these position words is NOT mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"On\",\"Under\",\"Behind\",\"Near\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'on, in, under, near\' but does not mention \'behind\'.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the pairs: Sack-Rack, Fox-Box. Which animal matches with \'House\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Bottle\",\"Mouse\",\"Bag\",\"Desk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem pairs \'mouse\' with \'house\'.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many times does the word \'near\' appear in the repeating line \'On, in, under, near, on, in, under, near\'?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'near\' is repeated twice in that specific line.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of this poem?\",\"options\":[\"To name different animals\",\"To tell us where things are\",\"To count the number of books\",\"To show how to clean a desk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem uses prepositions to describe the location of various objects and animals.\",\"topic\":\"Look, listen and recite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which word rhymes with \'fox\'?\",\"options\":[\"where\",\"table\",\"box\",\"under\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Fox\' and \'box\' as a rhyming pair.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Ronny finally find his pant?\",\"options\":[\"In the cupboard\",\"In the basket\",\"In the drawer\",\"Under the bed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Oh! It is here in the drawer\' regarding the pant.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where was Ronny\'s tie found?\",\"options\":[\"On the chair\",\"On the sofa\",\"On the table\",\"Under the shirt\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Oh! Here it is. It is on the table\' regarding the tie.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is Ronny sad in the story?\",\"options\":[\"He is hungry\",\"He is not getting his clothes\",\"He wants to go outside\",\"He lost his toy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'Ronny is sad. He is not getting his clothes.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'sack\' in the exercise?\",\"options\":[\"under\",\"house\",\"rack\",\"box\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'sack\' and \'rack\' as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the handkerchief hidden?\",\"options\":[\"Under the pillow\",\"Under the bed\",\"Under the shirt\",\"In the cupboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Oh! It is here under the shirt\' regarding the handkerchief.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Ronny plan to do after finding his shirt and handkerchief?\",\"options\":[\"Go to sleep\",\"Get ready\",\"Play with friends\",\"Clean the room\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Ronny says, \'Finally! Here is my shirt and handkerchief. Now I will get ready!\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If Ronny puts a ball between two boxes, which word describes the ball\'s position?\",\"options\":[\"on\",\"under\",\"between\",\"behind\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'between\' as one of the position words to describe where the ball is.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where is the monkey sitting?\",\"options\":[\"In the cupboard\",\"On the bed\",\"Under the bed\",\"Behind the curtain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the monkey (Ronny) sitting on top of the mattress\\/bed.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/054_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what can we see on the floor?\",\"options\":[\"Only a basket\",\"A neat carpet\",\"Scattered clothes and books\",\"A sleeping cat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows clothes, papers, and a book scattered on the floor, indicating the room is messy.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/054_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Ronny checked the chair and the sofa for his tie. Where else did he look for his clothes but NOT find them?\",\"options\":[\"The drawer\",\"The table\",\"The cupboard\",\"Under the shirt\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Not in the cupboard\' when he was looking for his pant.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the rhyming pair \'sack\' and \'rack\'. Which new word can be added to this group?\",\"options\":[\"back\",\"sock\",\"sick\",\"sun\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Back\' rhymes with \'sack\' and \'rack\', following the pattern in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"create\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21278,5,2,'English','en','Our Calendar','[\"Our calendar has 7 days in a week.\",\"Monday is the first day of the week.\",\"Tuesday is the second day, after Monday.\",\"Wednesday is the third day, before Thursday.\",\"Thursday is the fourth day, the middle day of the week.\",\"Friday is the fifth day, after Thursday.\",\"Saturday is the sixth day, before Sunday.\",\"Sunday is the seventh day, after Saturday and before Monday.\",\"Each week starts again with Monday.\",\"The days are named in order: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday.\",\"The calendar helps us know which day is today, tomorrow, yesterday, etc.\",\"If today is Friday, tomorrow is Saturday and the day after tomorrow is Sunday.\",\"Yesterday from Saturday is Friday, and the day before yesterday from Saturday is Thursday.\",\"The calendar repeats every 7 days.\",\"Knowing the days helps plan school activities and homework.\",\"The week is a cycle that never stops.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the first day of the week?\",\"options\":[\"Sunday\",\"Monday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Friday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Hello! I am the first day of the week\' referring to Monday.\",\"topic\":\"Our Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which day of the week is shown?\",\"options\":[\"Monday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Wednesday\",\"Thursday\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a girl holding a card that says \'Monday\'.\",\"topic\":\"Our Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/056_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text under the given figure, when does this day come?\",\"options\":[\"Before Monday\",\"After Monday\",\"Before Saturday\",\"After Sunday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text for the second day (Tuesday) says, \'I come after Monday\'.\",\"topic\":\"Our Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/056_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which day comes after Saturday but before Monday?\",\"options\":[\"Friday\",\"Sunday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Wednesday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I am the seventh day. I come after Saturday but before Monday.\'\",\"topic\":\"Our Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which day is known as the \'middle one\' of the week?\",\"options\":[\"Second day\",\"Third day\",\"Fourth day\",\"Fifth day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I am the fourth day, I am the middle one.\'\",\"topic\":\"Our Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If today is the third day of the week, which day comes next (Thursday)?\",\"options\":[\"Monday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Wednesday\",\"Thursday\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the third day comes before Thursday, making Thursday the next day.\",\"topic\":\"Our Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many days come before the middle day of the week?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says about the middle day, \'Three days come before me\'.\",\"topic\":\"Our Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which day comes before Sunday?\",\"options\":[\"Fourth day\",\"Fifth day\",\"Sixth day\",\"Seventh day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I am the sixth day, I come before Sunday.\'\",\"topic\":\"Our Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are the fifth day, which day do you come after?\",\"options\":[\"Monday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Wednesday\",\"Thursday\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I am the fifth day, I come after Thursday.\'\",\"topic\":\"Our Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, how many days are there in a full week if Sunday is the seventh day?\",\"options\":[\"5 days\",\"6 days\",\"7 days\",\"8 days\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the days up to the \'seventh day\', which is the last one mentioned before the cycle repeats.\",\"topic\":\"Our Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the ordinal name for the number 3?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Third\",\"Second\",\"Fourth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Third\' as the ordinal word for the number 3.\",\"topic\":\"Look and answer\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the text, what day is it today?\",\"options\":[\"Thursday\",\"Saturday\",\"Friday\",\"Sunday\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'Today is Friday.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look and answer\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If today is Friday, what day was yesterday according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Wednesday\",\"Thursday\",\"Saturday\",\"Monday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Yesterday was Thursday.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look and answer\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What day comes after Friday in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Sunday\",\"Monday\",\"Saturday\",\"Thursday\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'What day is tomorrow? Tomorrow is Saturday.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look and answer\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the day after tomorrow?\",\"options\":[\"Sunday\",\"Saturday\",\"Monday\",\"Friday\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The day after tomorrow is Sunday.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look and answer\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the day before yesterday according to the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Tuesday\",\"Wednesday\",\"Thursday\",\"Friday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The day before yesterday was Wednesday.\'\",\"topic\":\"Look and answer\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the list of numbers, which word comes immediately after \'Ninth\'?\",\"options\":[\"Eight\",\"Ten\",\"Tenth\",\"Seventh\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the sequence provided, \'Tenth\' follows \'Ninth\'.\",\"topic\":\"Look and answer\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the ordinal word for the number 8?\",\"options\":[\"Eight\",\"Eighth\",\"Seventh\",\"Ninth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the text shows \'Eighth\' corresponds to the number 8.\",\"topic\":\"Look and answer\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which year is shown on the calendar?\",\"options\":[\"2024\",\"2025\",\"2026\",\"2027\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The calendar image clearly displays the year \'2026\' at the top right.\",\"topic\":\"Look and answer\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/057_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what day of the week is the 25th of December?\",\"options\":[\"Sunday\",\"Monday\",\"Thursday\",\"Friday\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Looking at the calendar, the number 25 falls under the column for \'FRIDAY\'.\",\"topic\":\"Look and answer\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/057_101.jpg\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21279,5,2,'English','en','Treasure Hunt','[\"Shapes are objects that have a fixed form, like a triangle, square, rectangle, and cylinder.\",\"A triangle has three sides and three corners.\",\"A square has four equal sides and four right angles.\",\"A rectangle has four sides, opposite sides are equal, and all angles are right angles.\",\"A cylinder is a 3‑dimensional shape with two parallel circular bases and a curved side.\",\"In the treasure hunt game, each shape is placed in a corner of the classroom labelled A, B, C, and D.\",\"Students pick a card with a letter and then go to the corner that matches the letter.\",\"They find the object of the shape in that corner and say “Bingo!” to show they found it.\",\"The game helps children recognise shapes and remember their names.\",\"It also encourages listening, following directions, and teamwork.\",\"During the game, the teacher sings a song to keep the children moving and engaged.\",\"After finding the object, children show it to the whole class and name it.\",\"The game can be repeated with different shapes or letters to keep it fun.\",\"The treasure hunt is a fun way to learn shapes and practice listening skills.\",\"It also helps children learn to stop when told to stop and to wait for their turn.\",\"The activity is suitable for a small classroom or outdoor ground.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these shapes is mentioned in the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Triangle\",\"Circle\",\"Star\",\"Oval\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'triangle\' as one of the shapes to collect.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher - Instructions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the teacher place the objects of different shapes?\",\"options\":[\"In the middle of the room\",\"In four corners of the classroom\",\"Outside the school gate\",\"On the teacher\'s table\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to place the objects in four corners of the classroom or ground.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher - Instructions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher do to the corners after placing the objects?\",\"options\":[\"Paint them\",\"Label them\",\"Hide them\",\"Clean them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Label the corners\' after placing the objects.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher - Instructions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of cards should the teacher prepare?\",\"options\":[\"Number cards\",\"Color cards\",\"Letter cards\",\"Picture cards\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically instructs to \'Prepare the cards of the letters\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher - Instructions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the letter cards be placed?\",\"options\":[\"In the corners\",\"In the middle of the classroom\",\"In the teacher\'s pocket\",\"Under the chairs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to put the cards \'in the middle of the classroom\\/ground\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher - Instructions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When should the children pick a card?\",\"options\":[\"When they start running\",\"When they are asked to stop\",\"Before the game begins\",\"After the game is over\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs children to pick a card \'when they are asked to stop\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher - Instructions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many corners are used to place the objects of different shapes?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies placing objects in \'four corners\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher - Instructions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a shape listed in the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Cylinder\",\"Cone\",\"Sphere\",\"Cube\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'triangle, square, rectangle, cylinder\' as examples of shapes.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher - Instructions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which card is a child allowed to pick?\",\"options\":[\"Only the first card\",\"The card the teacher chooses\",\"A card which they want or like\",\"The smallest card\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to instruct children to \'pick a card which they want or like\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher - Instructions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of these instructions for the teacher?\",\"options\":[\"To clean the classroom\",\"To conduct a game\",\"To teach drawing\",\"To count the children\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The final sentence says to \'Conduct the following game by using different shapes and objects\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher - Instructions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where should you stand at the beginning of the activity?\",\"options\":[\"At the back of the classroom\",\"At the center of the classroom\",\"Outside the classroom\",\"Near the teacher\'s desk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to come forward and stand at the center of the classroom.\",\"topic\":\"Playing the Treasure Hunt\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which song are the students asked to sing?\",\"options\":[\"Twinkle Twinkle Little Star\",\"Rain Rain Go Away\",\"Ringa Ringa Roses\",\"Old MacDonald Had a Farm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions singing \'Ringa Ringa Roses\'.\",\"topic\":\"Playing the Treasure Hunt\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do while singing the song?\",\"options\":[\"Sit in a chair\",\"Run in the circle\",\"Jump up and down\",\"Clap your hands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to sing the song and run in the circle.\",\"topic\":\"Playing the Treasure Hunt\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first thing you do after the teacher says \'Stop!\'?\",\"options\":[\"Select a card from \'Find the corners\'\",\"Go back to your seat\",\"Start singing again\",\"Find an object\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"After the command \'Stop!\', the next instruction is to select any card from \'Find the corners\'.\",\"topic\":\"Playing the Treasure Hunt\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What word should you say when you find the object of a shape?\",\"options\":[\"Found!\",\"Hurray!\",\"Bingo!\",\"Yes!\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs students to say \'Bingo!\' once they find the object.\",\"topic\":\"Playing the Treasure Hunt\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What two things must you do after saying \'Bingo!\'?\",\"options\":[\"Hide the object and sit down\",\"Show the object to the class and name it\",\"Give the object to the teacher and sing\",\"Put the object back and run\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to show the object to the whole class and name it.\",\"topic\":\"Playing the Treasure Hunt\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"After showing the object to the class, what is the next step?\",\"options\":[\"Go home\",\"Sing a new song\",\"Join your groups again\",\"Find a new card\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to join your groups again and continue the game.\",\"topic\":\"Playing the Treasure Hunt\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what determines which group you join?\",\"options\":[\"The color of your shirt\",\"The card you selected\",\"The friend you like most\",\"The size of the classroom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to select a card and \'join the respective group\', meaning the group matching the card.\",\"topic\":\"Playing the Treasure Hunt\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What specific type of object are you looking for during the game?\",\"options\":[\"A heavy object\",\"A red object\",\"An object of a shape\",\"A wooden object\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Run and find the object of a shape\'.\",\"topic\":\"Playing the Treasure Hunt\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct order of actions in the game?\",\"options\":[\"Sing -> Stop -> Select card -> Find object\",\"Find object -> Sing -> Stop -> Select card\",\"Select card -> Find object -> Sing -> Stop\",\"Stop -> Find object -> Sing -> Select card\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text follows the sequence: Sing \'Ringa Ringa Roses\', Stop, Select a card, and then Find the object.\",\"topic\":\"Playing the Treasure Hunt\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21280,5,2,'English','en','India','[\"India is a country in South Asia.\",\"It has many rivers, mountains, fields and forests.\",\"People in India are called Indians.\",\"India is known for its diversity of languages and cultures.\",\"The national flag of India is called the Tiranga (tricolor).\",\"The flag has saffron, white and green colours with a blue wheel in the centre.\",\"The national bird of India is the Peacock.\",\"The national flower of India is the Lotus.\",\"The national fruit of India is Mango.\",\"The national tree of India is the Banyan tree.\",\"The national animal of India is the Tiger.\",\"The national emblem of India is a Lion Capital of Ashoka.\",\"The national anthem of India is called Jana Gana Mana.\",\"India is a democratic republic with a President as the head of state.\",\"India is the seventh largest country in the world by area.\",\"India has a population of over 1.4 billion people.\",\"India is known for its many religions including Hinduism, Islam, Christianity, Sikhism and Buddhism.\",\"The official language of India is Hindi, but many other languages are spoken.\",\"India has a rich history of art, music, dance and literature.\",\"India is famous for its spices, sweets and diverse cuisine.\",\"India has a growing economy and many technology companies.\",\"India celebrates many festivals such as Diwali, Holi, Eid and Christmas.\",\"India has many famous monuments like the Taj Mahal, Qutub Minar and Red Fort.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the name of the country mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"India\",\"America\",\"Japan\",\"China\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem explicitly states \'I love my country, India\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what are found in India along with mountains?\",\"options\":[\"Oceans\",\"Rivers\",\"Deserts\",\"Cities\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Rivers and mountains are in India\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the poet feel about India?\",\"options\":[\"Sad\",\"Proud\",\"Angry\",\"Scared\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'I am proud of India\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who does the poet love in addition to the country?\",\"options\":[\"Only friends\",\"Brothers and sisters\",\"Only teachers\",\"Strangers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'I love my brothers and sisters\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these are mentioned in India along with forests?\",\"options\":[\"Buildings\",\"Fields\",\"Cars\",\"Roads\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states \'Fields and forests are in India\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, which word describes India?\",\"options\":[\"Small\",\"Beautiful\",\"Ugly\",\"Dark\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Beautiful country is India\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen an