,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions the \'Mango tree\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which sport is included in the list?\",\"options\":[\"Cricket\",\"Football\",\"Kabaddi\",\"Hockey\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text includes \'Kabaddi\' in the list of items to learn.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should you do with the map?\",\"options\":[\"Color the map\",\"Name the state it belongs to\",\"Draw a new map\",\"Fold the map\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Question (2) in the text asks to \'Name the state to which the map belongs?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are you asked to identify in the given map?\",\"options\":[\"The colors\",\"The numbers\",\"The pictures\",\"The names of cities\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Question (3) in the text asks to \'Identify the pictures in the given map.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see a picture of a Mango tree on the map, which instruction are you following?\",\"options\":[\"Look, listen and learn\",\"Name the state\",\"Identify the pictures in the given map\",\"Read the words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Finding the Mango tree picture on the map corresponds to the instruction to \'Identify the pictures\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a game that you might find in the pictures mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"Shekru\",\"Hariyal\",\"Kabaddi\",\"Mango tree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Kabaddi is the only sport\\/game listed among the four items.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the list, which item belongs to the category of \'Plants\'?\",\"options\":[\"Shekru\",\"Hariyal\",\"Kabaddi\",\"Mango tree\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The Mango tree is a plant, while the others are animals, birds, or sports.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first instruction given in the exercise section \'e\'?\",\"options\":[\"Write and read\",\"Look, listen and learn\",\"Draw and color\",\"Run and play\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The section starts with the instruction \'Look, listen and learn.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21281,5,2,'English','en','Clock and Me','[\"Clock shows the time.\",\"The word \\\"o’clock\\\" means the hour exactly.\",\"If the hour hand points to 3, it is 3 o’clock.\",\"If the minute hand points to 12, it is the start of the hour.\",\"The big hand is the hour hand.\",\"The small hand is the minute hand.\",\"When the minute hand is at 12, the minute is 0.\",\"When the minute hand is at 6, the minute is 30.\",\"The clock is round and has numbers 1 to 12.\",\"The hour hand moves slowly, the minute hand moves fast.\",\"If the hour hand is between 2 and 3, it is after 2 o’clock.\",\"The clock can be a wall clock or a pocket clock.\",\"We use clocks to know when to eat, sleep, go to school.\",\"We can ask, \\\"What’s the time?\\\" to find the time.\",\"The clock shows the same time for everyone in the same place.\",\"When the minute hand is at 3, it is 15 minutes past the hour.\",\"When the minute hand is at 9, it is 45 minutes past the hour.\",\"The clock helps us keep a daily routine.\",\"We can say, \\\"It’s 6 o’clock.\\\" when the hour hand is at 6.\",\"We can say, \\\"It’s 10 o’clock.\\\" when the hour hand is at 10.\",\"The clock is a useful tool for learning time.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the first time mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"It\'s 5 o\'clock.\",\"It\'s 6 o\'clock.\",\"It\'s 7 o\'clock.\",\"It\'s 10 o\'clock.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text starts the list with \'It\'s 6 o\'clock.\'\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the third action you should do after you \'Look\' and \'Listen\'?\",\"options\":[\"Write\",\"Draw\",\"Repeat\",\"Sleep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instruction says \'Look, listen and repeat.\'\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific time is mentioned after 7 o\'clock in the text?\",\"options\":[\"8 o\'clock\",\"9 o\'clock\",\"10 o\'clock\",\"11 o\'clock\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'It\'s 7 o\'clock. It\'s 10 o\'clock.\'\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What concept is the teacher supposed to introduce to the children?\",\"options\":[\"The \'o\'clock\' concept\",\"The \'minutes\' concept\",\"The \'seconds\' concept\",\"The \'calendar\' concept\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note explicitly says to \'Introduce the o\'clock concept\'.\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How should the children ask questions to each other?\",\"options\":[\"Alone\",\"In groups\",\"With parents\",\"In the library\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note says to \'Tell them to ask the questions to each other in groups.\'\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the clock shows the number 7, how should a student say the time based on the examples?\",\"options\":[\"7 time\",\"It\'s 7 o\'clock\",\"7 hours\",\"It\'s 7\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the format \'It\'s [number] o\'clock\' for all examples.\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What two things are children encouraged to do with the story?\",\"options\":[\"Read and write\",\"Enact and retell\",\"Sing and dance\",\"Paint and draw\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note says to \'Encourage them to enact and retell the story.\'\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should children observe to help discuss the story?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher\",\"The clock on the wall\",\"The pictures\",\"The blackboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Section \'b\' says \'Observe the pictures and discuss the story\'.\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Besides pictures, what else helps the children discuss the story?\",\"options\":[\"Given questions\",\"A dictionary\",\"A ruler\",\"Music\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Section \'b\' says \'discuss the story with the help of given questions.\'\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct way to complete the phrase \'It\'s 10...\' according to the text pattern?\",\"options\":[\"o\'clock\",\"minutes\",\"hours\",\"morning\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text consistently uses \'o\'clock\' after the number to tell the time.\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how should children discuss the pictures?\",\"options\":[\"In groups\",\"By themselves\",\"Silently\",\"With the principal\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions motivating children to discuss pictures in groups.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher ask the children about?\",\"options\":[\"Their lunch boxes\",\"Their likes and dislikes\",\"Their home address\",\"Their favorite color\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the teacher should ask them about their likes and dislikes.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the two things children are encouraged to do with the story?\",\"options\":[\"Read and write\",\"Enact and retell\",\"Draw and color\",\"Listen and sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages children to enact and retell the story.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'retell the story\' mean in this lesson?\",\"options\":[\"To tell the story again\",\"To change the story\",\"To forget the story\",\"To read the story silently\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Retelling involves telling the story again to demonstrate understanding.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When the teacher asks about \'similar occasions\', what should the children talk about?\",\"options\":[\"Things that are completely different\",\"Other times like the one in the story\",\"What they will eat for dinner\",\"How to draw a clock\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Similar occasions refer to other times or events that are like the one described in the story.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is acting out a part of the story, which activity are they doing?\",\"options\":[\"Discussing\",\"Enacting\",\"Retelling\",\"Listing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Enacting means to perform or act out the story.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are talking to three friends about a picture in the book, you are working in a ________.\",\"options\":[\"Group\",\"Library\",\"Solo\",\"Secret\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Discussing with friends constitutes working in a group as suggested by the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity helps the teacher know what a child enjoys or does not enjoy?\",\"options\":[\"Discussing pictures\",\"Asking about likes and dislikes\",\"Retelling the story\",\"Speaking about other occasions\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Likes and dislikes directly relate to what a child enjoys or does not enjoy.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the teacher encourage children to speak about \'other similar occasions\'?\",\"options\":[\"To help them connect the story to their own lives\",\"To make them finish the work faster\",\"To teach them how to draw\",\"To check if they have their textbooks\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Speaking about similar occasions helps children relate the story to their personal experiences.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT an activity mentioned for the children in the teacher\'s instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Discussing pictures\",\"Enacting the story\",\"Writing a 100-page book\",\"Speaking about similar occasions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Writing a 100-page book is not mentioned in the text; the others are.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21282,5,2,'English','en','Birthday Celebration','[\"Birthday is a special day when we celebrate our birth.\",\"We say “Happy Birthday” to the person who is having a birthday.\",\"People usually have a party or celebration on their birthday.\",\"Friends and family come to the birthday party to wish good wishes.\",\"A birthday party can be held at home or at a special place.\",\"We can give gifts or cake at a birthday party.\",\"During a birthday celebration we sing songs and play games.\",\"We can invite many friends to join the celebration.\",\"It is common to say “Happy Birthday” and give a hug or a kiss.\",\"Birthday celebrations are a way to show love and friendship.\",\"We can write a birthday card with warm wishes.\",\"The birthday person may have a special meal or cake at the party.\",\"We can decorate the house with balloons and streamers for a party.\",\"Birthday parties are fun and make the birthday person feel special.\",\"Celebrating birthdays helps us remember the joy of growing older.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Whose birthday is it today in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Garima\",\"Govind\",\"Jayraj\",\"Pari\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Garima says, \'It\'s my birthday today.\'\",\"topic\":\"Friends Joining\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"At what time is the birthday celebration?\",\"options\":[\"5 o\'clock in the morning\",\"6 o\'clock in the evening\",\"7 o\'clock in the evening\",\"6 o\'clock in the morning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Garima mentions the celebration is at 6 o\'clock in the evening.\",\"topic\":\"Friends Joining\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the birthday celebration going to be held?\",\"options\":[\"At school\",\"In a park\",\"At Garima\'s house\",\"At Govind\'s house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Garima tells Govind, \'do come to my house.\'\",\"topic\":\"Friends Joining\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Govind say when he hears it is Garima\'s birthday?\",\"options\":[\"Good morning\",\"Wow! Happy Birthday, Garima!\",\"I am busy\",\"Thank you\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Govind reacts with excitement and wishes her \'Happy Birthday\'.\",\"topic\":\"Friends Joining\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Govind mean when he says \'I will come on time\'?\",\"options\":[\"He will be late\",\"He will not come\",\"He will arrive at 6 o\'clock\",\"He will come the next day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Coming on time means arriving at the specific time mentioned, which is 6 o\'clock.\",\"topic\":\"Friends Joining\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these friends is NOT mentioned as joining the party?\",\"options\":[\"Tanmay\",\"Sanvi\",\"Rahul\",\"Navjyot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rahul is not in the list of friends provided by Garima.\",\"topic\":\"Friends Joining\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If Garima is inviting friends at 6 o\'clock in the evening, what should they see outside?\",\"options\":[\"The sun rising\",\"The sun setting or getting dark\",\"The hot midday sun\",\"Breakfast time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"6 o\'clock in the evening is the time when the day ends and it starts to get dark.\",\"topic\":\"Friends Joining\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many friends are listed in the group including Jayraj, Meher, Tanmay, Sanvi, Navjyot, Pari and Sam?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"6\",\"7\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Counting the names: 1. Jayraj, 2. Meher, 3. Tanmay, 4. Sanvi, 5. Navjyot, 6. Pari, 7. Sam.\",\"topic\":\"Friends Joining\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the relationship between Garima and Govind based on their conversation?\",\"options\":[\"They are enemies\",\"They are strangers\",\"They are friends\",\"They are teachers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"They greet each other warmly and Garima invites him to her birthday, showing they are friends.\",\"topic\":\"Friends Joining\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is Govind\'s opinion about the upcoming celebration?\",\"options\":[\"He thinks it will be boring\",\"He thinks they will have a great time\",\"He thinks it is too early\",\"He thinks Garima is lying\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Govind says, \'We will have a great time.\'\",\"topic\":\"Friends Joining\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher ask the children to do with the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Read it silently\",\"Enact it in the classroom\",\"Write it in their notebooks\",\"Memorize it at home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly tells the teacher to ask children to enact the conversation in the classroom.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the enactment of the conversation take place?\",\"options\":[\"In the playground\",\"In the classroom\",\"In the library\",\"At the school gate\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that the enactment should happen \'in the classroom\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who should participate in the conversation according to the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Only the teacher\",\"Only a few students\",\"Each child\",\"Only the students who like birthdays\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the teacher should \'Ensure that each child participates\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher motivate the children to speak about?\",\"options\":[\"Their favorite colors\",\"Other similar occasions\",\"Their school subjects\",\"The weather today\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the teacher to motivate children to speak about \'other similar occasions\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the teacher need to \'ensure\' during the activity?\",\"options\":[\"That the room is quiet\",\"That each child participates\",\"That the children draw pictures\",\"That the children finish their lunch\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instruction specifically says to \'Ensure that each child participates in the conversation\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child is in the classroom, what action are they expected to do with the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Paint it\",\"Enact it\",\"Sing it\",\"Ignore it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks for the conversation to be enacted.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these would be a \'similar occasion\' for a child to speak about?\",\"options\":[\"A festival celebration\",\"Doing homework\",\"Sharpening a pencil\",\"Sleeping at night\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A festival celebration is a social occasion similar to a birthday celebration.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the teacher\'s role regarding children who might not speak up?\",\"options\":[\"To let them stay quiet\",\"To motivate them to speak\",\"To give them extra homework\",\"To ask them to leave the room\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Motivate the children to speak\' and ensure everyone participates.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text say \'each child\' instead of \'some children\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the classroom is