:\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What shape is used to make the eyes of the robot?\",\"options\":[\"Circles\",\"Squares\",\"Triangles\",\"Lines\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Use circles for eyes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hands and legs of the robot\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, the head of the robot is a:\",\"options\":[\"Rectangle\",\"Square\",\"Triangle\",\"Circle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Head of the robot : Draw a square\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hands and legs of the robot\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are used to join the head and the trunk of the robot?\",\"options\":[\"Circles\",\"Squares\",\"Lines for neck\",\"Triangles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Join head and trunk with lines for neck\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hands and legs of the robot\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are drawing the mouth of the robot, which shape will you use?\",\"options\":[\"Square\",\"Triangle\",\"Circle\",\"Rectangle\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Use rectangle and make mouth\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hands and legs of the robot\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To make the ears of the robot, you need to sketch:\",\"options\":[\"Rectangles\",\"Triangles\",\"Circles\",\"Squares\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Sketch rectangles for ears\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hands and legs of the robot\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should you use to make the hands and legs of the robot?\",\"options\":[\"Only circles\",\"Only triangles\",\"The help of given shapes\",\"Only lines\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Make hands and legs with the help of given shapes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hands and legs of the robot\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the robot is joined to the head using lines?\",\"options\":[\"The nose\",\"The trunk\",\"The ears\",\"The eyes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions joining the head and trunk with lines.\",\"topic\":\"Hands and legs of the robot\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very first thing (a) you must do with the shapes?\",\"options\":[\"Colour them\",\"Identify and name them\",\"Cut them out\",\"Erase them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step \'a\' says \'Identify and name the following shapes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hands and legs of the robot\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"After drawing the robot using shapes, what is the final instruction in step \'b\'?\",\"options\":[\"Erase it\",\"Name it\",\"Colour it\",\"Cut it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step \'b\' says \'Draw a robot using the above shapes and colour it\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hands and legs of the robot\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does activity number 4 ask the children to do to the robot?\",\"options\":[\"Break the robot\",\"Colour the robot\",\"Hide the robot\",\"Sell the robot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Activity 4 explicitly states \'Colour the robot\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should children use to design their own robot in activity 5?\",\"options\":[\"A ruler\",\"Their own ideas\",\"A picture from a book\",\"A toy from a shop\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Activity 5 tells children to \'Design your own robot with your own ideas\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What materials are suggested for the Project Work to make a robot?\",\"options\":[\"New plastic\",\"Expensive metal\",\"Waste materials\",\"Clay and mud\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Project Work section says to \'Make your own robot with waste materials\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who should the teacher appoint to conduct the activity?\",\"options\":[\"A robot\",\"A leader\",\"A parent\",\"A visitor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text for the teacher says to \'Appoint a leader and conduct the activity\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the teacher\'s role when children are drawing the robot?\",\"options\":[\"To draw it for them\",\"To help the children\",\"To tell them not to draw\",\"To watch from outside\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions state \'Help the children to draw a robot as above\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What specific guidance should the teacher give to the leader?\",\"options\":[\"How to draw a circle\",\"How to give the instructions\",\"How to clean the classroom\",\"How to use waste materials\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Guide the leader about how to give the instructions\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the main goal of the Project Work?\",\"options\":[\"Make your own robot\",\"Read about robots\",\"Colour a robot\",\"Buy a robot\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The Project Work section title is \'Make your own robot with waste materials\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is using old boxes and bottles to build a robot, which part of the lesson are they doing?\",\"options\":[\"Activity 4\",\"Activity 5\",\"Project Work\",\"For the Teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Using waste materials like old boxes is part of the \'Project Work\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who is responsible for giving instructions during the activity under the teacher\'s guidance?\",\"options\":[\"The leader\",\"The robot\",\"The principal\",\"The artist\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions guiding the leader on how to give instructions.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'For the Teacher\' section, what is the sequence of the teacher\'s tasks?\",\"options\":[\"Help draw, appoint a leader, guide the leader\",\"Colour the robot, then design a new one\",\"Find waste materials, then draw\",\"Give instructions, then appoint a leader\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists helping to draw, appointing a leader, and guiding the leader in that order.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21284,5,2,'English','en','Genia Vs. Mr. Germ','[\"Genia is a healthy girl who likes to keep clean.\",\"Mr. Germ is a bad character who wants to make people sick.\",\"We use soap, handwash, toothpaste, towel and water to stay clean.\",\"Hands should be washed before eating and after using the toilet.\",\"Wash hands with water and handwash, rub palms, back of hands, fingers and nails.\",\"After washing, dry hands with a towel or air dry.\",\"To clean teeth, use toothpaste and brush them twice a day.\",\"Germs can stay on food, so wash fruits and vegetables before eating.\",\"If you do not wash your hands, germs can make you sick.\",\"Keeping clean helps you stay healthy and happy.\",\"Use a rhythmic song to remember the steps of washing hands.\",\"Wash both thumbs and fingertips carefully.\",\"Wash and dry hands after washing to remove germs.\",\"Germs are tiny and cannot be seen, but they can make you ill.\",\"Cleaning yourself keeps you and others safe from sickness.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is described as a very healthy and happy girl in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Mr. Germ\",\"Genia\",\"The shopkeeper\",\"The doctor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Genia is a very healthy and happy girl.\",\"topic\":\"Genia Vs. Mr. Germ\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Mr. Germ always want to do to Genia and her friends?\",\"options\":[\"Help them\",\"Play with them\",\"Harm them\",\"Give them fruits\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says Mr. Germ always wants to harm Genia and her friends.\",\"topic\":\"Genia Vs. Mr. Germ\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Genia and her friend go one day?\",\"options\":[\"To a school\",\"To a bazaar\",\"To a garden\",\"To a hospital\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Genia and her friend went to the bazaar.\",\"topic\":\"Genia Vs. Mr. Germ\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the girl in the purple dress carrying in her hand?\",\"options\":[\"A towel\",\"A piece of soap\",\"A bag\",\"A bottle of water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the girl in the purple dress carrying a white bag.\",\"topic\":\"Genia Vs. Mr. Germ\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/065_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what items are being sold at the stall?\",\"options\":[\"Toys and books\",\"Fruits and vegetables\",\"Soap and toothpaste\",\"Clothes and shoes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text and the picture show them buying fruits and vegetables at the bazaar.\",\"topic\":\"Genia Vs. Mr. Germ\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/065_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Genia tell her friend not to eat the fruit immediately?\",\"options\":[\"Because it was too expensive\",\"Because it was not ripe\",\"Because it needed to be washed first\",\"Because she wanted to eat it herself\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Genia says, \'We have to wash it before eating. There may be germs on it.\'\",\"topic\":\"Genia Vs. Mr. Germ\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the list of things in the text, which one is used to clean our teeth?\",\"options\":[\"Soap\",\"Towel\",\"Handwash\",\"Toothpaste\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Toothpaste is listed as a thing we use, and its purpose is for cleaning teeth.\",\"topic\":\"Genia Vs. Mr. Germ\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to stay healthy like Genia, what should you do after buying vegetables from the market?\",\"options\":[\"Eat them right away\",\"Wash them with water\",\"Keep them in the bag forever\",\"Give them to Mr. Germ\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Genia teaches that we must wash items from the bazaar to remove germs.\",\"topic\":\"Genia Vs. Mr. Germ\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to people when germs are successful in their plan?\",\"options\":[\"They become happy\",\"They become healthy\",\"They become sick\",\"They become strong\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that germs say, \'We will make her sick.\'\",\"topic\":\"Genia Vs. Mr. Germ\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Mr. Germ say, \'Oh, No! We missed the chance\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the bazaar was closed\",\"Because Genia decided to wash the fruit\",\"Because the fruit fell on the ground\",\"Because Genia\'s friend forgot to buy the fruit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Mr. Germ lost the chance to make them sick because Genia insisted on washing the fruit.\",\"topic\":\"Genia Vs. Mr. Germ\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very first step to wash your hands?\",\"options\":[\"Wet your hands\",\"Apply handwash\",\"Rub your palms\",\"Dry your hands\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Step 1 in the text is \'Wet your hands\'.\",\"topic\":\"Steps to wash hands\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you apply to your hands in Step 2?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Handwash\",\"Oil\",\"Cream\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 2 in the text says \'Apply handwash\'.\",\"topic\":\"Steps to wash hands\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Step 3, what should you rub together?\",\"options\":[\"Fingers\",\"Wrists\",\"Both the palms\",\"Thumbs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 3 says to \'Rub both the palms together\'.\",\"topic\":\"Steps to wash hands\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should you clean in Step 5?\",\"options\":[\"Back of hands\",\"Between fingers\",\"Wrists\",\"Nails\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 5 specifically says \'Clean between fingers\'.\",\"topic\":\"Steps to wash hands\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"After rubbing the back of each hand (Step 4), what is the next thing to do?\",\"options\":[\"Wash thumbs\",\"Clean between fingers\",\"Rub nails\",\"Dry hands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 5 follows Step 4, which is to clean between fingers.\",\"topic\":\"Steps to wash hands\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which step tells you to rub your fingertips and nails?\",\"options\":[\"Step 2\",\"Step 5\",\"Step 8\",\"Step 10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 8 in the text is \'Rub fingertips and nails\'.\",\"topic\":\"Steps to wash hands\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What part of the hand is cleaned in Step 9?\",\"options\":[\"Palms\",\"Fingers\",\"Around both the wrists\",\"Thumbs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 9 says \'Wash around both the wrists\'.\",\"topic\":\"Steps to wash hands\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In Step 6, which part of the fingers are you supposed to rub?\",\"options\":[\"The tips\",\"The front\",\"The back of fingers\",\"The nails\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 6 says \'Rub the back of fingers\'.\",\"topic\":\"Steps to wash hands\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very last thing you should do in Step 10?\",\"options\":[\"Apply handwash\",\"Rub palms\",\"Wash and dry\",\"Clean between fingers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The final step, Step 10, is \'Wash and dry\'.\",\"topic\":\"Steps to wash hands\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which step mentions washing the thumbs?\",\"options\":[\"Step 1\",\"Step 4\",\"Step 7\",\"Step 9\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 7 in the text is \'Wash both the thumbs\'.\",\"topic\":\"Steps to wash hands\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21285,5,2,'English','en','Talking Marks','[\"- A full stop (.) ends a statement.\",\"- A question mark (?) ends a question.\",\"- A comma (,) gives a short pause between words.\",\"- Inverted commas (‘ ’) or quotation marks are used to show spoken words.\",\"- Punctuation marks help readers understand the meaning of sentences.\",\"- Always put a full stop or question mark at the end of a sentence.\",\"- Use commas to separate items in a list.\",\"- Inverted commas are also called quotation marks.\",\"- Punctuation marks are small symbols that give clues to the reader.\",\"- Knowing punctuation makes writing clear and easy to read.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is another name for Inverted Commas?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Comma\",\"Quotation Marks\",\"Question Mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Inverted Commas are also called Quotation Marks.\",\"topic\":\"Inverted Commas\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which punctuation mark looks like a dot?\",\"options\":[\"Comma\",\"Full Stop\",\"Inverted Commas\",\"Question Mark\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'My name is Full Stop. I look like a dot.\'\",\"topic\":\"Inverted Commas\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does a Full Stop come in a sentence?\",\"options\":[\"At the beginning\",\"Between words\",\"At the end\",\"Before a question\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the Full Stop comes at the end of the sentence.\",\"topic\":\"Inverted Commas\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a Comma used between words in a sentence?\",\"options\":[\"To end the sentence\",\"For a short rest\",\"To ask a question\",\"To look like a dot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Comma comes between words for a short rest.\",\"topic\":\"Inverted Commas\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which mark is used to quote sentences?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Question Mark\",\"Comma\",\"Inverted Commas\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says Inverted Commas are used to quote sentences.\",\"topic\":\"Inverted Commas\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which mark comes at the end of every question?\",\"options\":[\"Question Mark\",\"Full Stop\",\"Comma\",\"Inverted Commas\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Question Mark comes at the end of every question.\",\"topic\":\"Inverted Commas\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the symbol for Inverted Commas from the text.\",\"options\":[\".\",\"?\",\",\",\"“...”\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'“...”\' as the symbol for Inverted Commas.\",\"topic\":\"Inverted Commas\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the function of Quotation Marks?\",\"options\":[\"To give a short rest\",\"To end a sentence\",\"To quote sentences\",\"To look like a dot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that Quotation Marks (Inverted Commas) are used to quote sentences.\",\"topic\":\"Inverted Commas\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which mark is correctly matched with its description?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop - short rest\",\"Comma - end of question\",\"Inverted Commas - quote sentences\",\"Question Mark - looks like a dot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Inverted Commas are used to quote sentences.\",\"topic\":\"Inverted Commas\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a mark is placed between words for a rest, which symbol is it?\",\"options\":[\".\",\",\",\"?\",\"“ ”\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the Comma (,) as coming between words for a short rest.\",\"topic\":\"Inverted Commas\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher ask the children to find out?\",\"options\":[\"New words\",\"Different punctuation marks\",\"Pictures of animals\",\"Page numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly tells the teacher to ask children to find out different punctuation marks.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of activity should the teacher conduct according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A drawing activity\",\"A singing activity\",\"A role play activity\",\"A running activity\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the teacher to \'Conduct a role play activity.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How should the teacher give exposure to using punctuation marks?\",\"options\":[\"By giving examples\",\"By giving homework\",\"By giving prizes\",\"By giving tests\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states to \'Give exposure to use these punctuation marks by giving examples.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is responsible for finding the punctuation marks in the classroom activity?\",\"options\":[\"The parents\",\"The children\",\"The principal\",\"The gardener\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Ask the children to find out\' the marks.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher wants to follow the instructions, what would they show the students?\",\"options\":[\"How to use punctuation marks\",\"How to sharpen a pencil\",\"How to tie shoelaces\",\"How to plant a tree\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The instructions focus on giving exposure to using punctuation marks.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A teacher is showing the class how to use a question mark and a full stop. What is the teacher doing?\",\"options\":[\"Conducting a race\",\"Giving exposure by giving examples\",\"Cleaning the classroom\",\"Checking the attendance\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Showing how to use marks is part of giving exposure through examples as mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is a task for the teacher?\",\"options\":[\"Buying new books\",\"Asking children to find punctuation marks\",\"Cooking lunch for children\",\"Fixing the school gate\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Ask the children to find out different punctuation marks\' as a task for the teacher.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main topic the teacher is helping the children with?\",\"options\":[\"Numbers\",\"Punctuation marks\",\"Colors\",\"Shapes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The entire \'For the Teacher\' section is focused on punctuation marks.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity involves students acting out parts to learn about punctuation?\",\"options\":[\"Finding marks\",\"Giving examples\",\"Role play activity\",\"Reading silently\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Role play is the specific activity mentioned for students to participate in.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned as a teacher\'s task in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Conducting a role play\",\"Giving examples of marks\",\"Asking children to find marks\",\"Drawing pictures of birds\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Drawing pictures of birds is not mentioned in the provided text instructions.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21286,5,2,'English','en','Sounds - III','[\"- Sounds are the basic units of speech.\",\"- Each sound is called a phoneme.\",\"- In English, letters combine to make sounds.\",\"- The same letter can make different sounds (e.g., \'a\' in \'cat\' vs \'cake\').\",\"- Vowels are sounds made with an open vocal tract.\",\"- Consonants are sounds made with some obstruction in the mouth.\",\"- Words are made of one or more sounds.\",\"- We can read, write and pronounce words by knowing their sounds.\",\"- In this chapter we practice reading words that start with the same sound.\",\"- Words that start with \'br\' sound: broom, branch, brain, brush, etc.\",\"- Words that start with \'cl\' sound: cloth, clean, clue, etc.\",\"- Words that start with \'sl\' sound: slide, sleep, slow, etc.\",\"- Words that start with \'cr\' sound: crayon, crack, crawl, etc.\",\"- Words that start with \'dr\' sound: drink, drum, drop, etc.\",\"- Matching sounds with words helps improve spelling.\",\"- Practising missing letters helps remember word patterns.\",\"- The teacher can use a dictionary to find meanings of new words.\",\"- Repeating words aloud helps remember their sounds.\",\"- Listening to words and identifying sounds is a useful skill.\",\"- Practice makes the sounds easier to recognise and use.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these words starts with the letters \'gl\'?\",\"options\":[\"glad\",\"from\",\"space\",\"shell\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'glad\' under the \'gl\' category.\",\"topic\":\"Read, form and write the words\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which letters are added to \'esh\' to form the word \'fresh\'?\",\"options\":[\"gl\",\"fr\",\"sp\",\"sh\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'fr\' combined with \'esh\' to form \'fresh\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read, form and write the words\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you join \'st\' with \'one\', which word is formed?\",\"options\":[\"stone\",\"stove\",\"stool\",\"stall\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'st\' combined with \'one\' forms \'stone\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read, form and write the words\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is formed by joining \'tr\' and \'ee\'?\",\"options\":[\"trap\",\"trip\",\"tree\",\"true\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'tree\' as a word formed with \'tr\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read, form and write the words\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the word: \'sp\' + \'ider\' = ?\",\"options\":[\"sport\",\"space\",\"spider\",\"speed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'sp\' combined with \'ider\' results in \'spider\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read, form and write the words\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word can be formed using the letters \'sc\'?\",\"options\":[\"scarf\",\"shell\",\"stone\",\"ship\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'scarf\' as a word starting with \'sc\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read, form and write the words\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word is formed by joining the center letters with \'ow\'?\",\"options\":[\"glow\",\"glad\",\"globe\",\"glue\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows \'gl\' in the center and \'ow\' in one of the segments, forming \'glow\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read, form and write the words\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/068_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many different words can be formed using the center letters \'gl\'?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure has four segments (ad, obe, ow, ue) to join with \'gl\', making 4 words.\",\"topic\":\"Read, form and write the words\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/068_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which word ending is used for both \'fl\' and \'tr\' groups in the text?\",\"options\":[\"ad\",\"ap\",\"obe\",\"ow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'flap\' for \'fl\' and \'trap\' for \'tr\', both ending in \'ap\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read, form and write the words\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word starts with the sound \'sh\'?\",\"options\":[\"ship\",\"scan\",\"stool\",\"trap\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'ship\' under the \'sh\' category.\",\"topic\":\"Read, form and write the words\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word starts with the sound \'cl\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"clock\",\"brick\",\"smoke\",\"shark\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'clock\' and \'cloth\' under the sound \'cl\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with sounds\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound do the words \'thumb\' and \'thorn\' start with?\",\"options\":[\"tr\",\"th\",\"sh\",\"ch\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text groups \'thumb\' and \'thorn\' under the sound \'th\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with sounds\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the text, which word starts with the \'sn\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"smile\",\"snail\",\"swan\",\"star\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'snow\' and \'snail\' for the \'sn\' sound.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with sounds\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which pair of words starts with the same sound in the textbook list?\",\"options\":[\"brick and broom\",\"brick and clock\",\"broom and smoke\",\"clock and shark\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Both \'brick\' and \'broom\' are listed under the \'br\' sound group.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with sounds\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list has the sound \'lt\' at the end?\",\"options\":[\"salt\",\"star\",\"slide\",\"swan\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'salt\' and \'belt\' for the sound \'lt\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with sounds\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'frog\' starts with \'fr\', which other word from the list starts with \'fr\'?\",\"options\":[\"fruit\",\"flower\",\"flute\",\"glass\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'frog\' and \'fruit\' under the \'fr\' sound.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with sounds\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which sound is shown with the pictures of a \'crab\' and \'crayon\'?\",\"options\":[\"br\",\"cr\",\"dr\",\"tr\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows \'crab\' and \'crayon\' under the \'cr\' label.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with sounds\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/069_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which two objects are shown for the sound \'tr\'?\",\"options\":[\"tree and trumpet\",\"frog and fruit\",\"brick and broom\",\"drink and drum\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure displays a tree and a trumpet next to the \'tr\' sound label.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with sounds\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/069_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which sound from the list is found at the end of the word \'belt\'?\",\"options\":[\"bl\",\"lt\",\"st\",\"sl\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies \'lt\' as the sound for \'salt\' and \'belt\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with sounds\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the pattern: \'tw\' is to \'twelve\' as \'sw\' is to ____.\",\"options\":[\"swan\",\"snail\",\"star\",\"spoon\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'sw\' with \'swan\' and \'swim\', just as \'tw\' is paired with \'twelve\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with sounds\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21287,5,2,'English','en','Open the Treasure (Unit 3)','[\"- The chapter is about reading and speaking words with syllables.\",\"- A syllable is a part of a word that has one vowel sound.\",\"- Children should clap each syllable when they read a word.\",\"- Example: banana = ba‑na‑na (3 syllables).\",\"- Example: elephant = el‑e‑phant (3 syllables).\",\"- Example: today = to‑day (2 syllables).\",\"- Example: umbrella = um‑brel‑la (3 syllables).\",\"- Example: tomato = to‑ma‑to (3 syllables).\",\"- Example: computer = com‑pue‑ter (3 syllables).\",\"- Students should practice reading words aloud and writing them.\",\"- They can create short stories using given characters.\",\"- A story can have a beginning, a problem, and an ending.\",\"- The teacher can use a word‑bank to help students choose words.\",\"- Students should read the words aloud with the teacher’s help.\",\"- Group work helps children practice speaking and listening.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What should the children open first according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The Story-Book\",\"The Word-Bank\",\"The Toy-Box\",\"The Drawing-Book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to \'Open the Word-Bank\'.\",\"topic\":\"Teacher\'s Notes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who helps the children read the words aloud?\",\"options\":[\"The parents\",\"The friends\",\"The teacher\",\"The neighbors\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to read the words aloud with the help of the teacher.\",\"topic\":\"Teacher\'s Notes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How should children work to complete the activities?\",\"options\":[\"Alone\",\"In pairs or in a group\",\"Only with the principal\",\"Outside the school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to work in pairs or in a group to complete activities.\",\"topic\":\"Teacher\'s Notes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should children do to words to help read them properly?\",\"options\":[\"Color the words\",\"Erase the words\",\"Break them down into syllables\",\"Hide the words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s notes suggest helping children break down words into syllables.\",\"topic\":\"Teacher\'s Notes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are children encouraged to make using different characters?\",\"options\":[\"Their own stories\",\"Paper dolls\",\"New alphabets\",\"Wall paintings\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions encouraging children to make their own stories with different characters.\",\"topic\":\"Teacher\'s Notes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Children are encouraged to read and write words with how many syllables?\",\"options\":[\"One or two\",\"Three to four\",\"Seven to eight\",\"Ten to twelve\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies encouraging children to read and write three to four syllable words.\",\"topic\":\"Teacher\'s Notes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In what way should the words from the Word-Bank be read?\",\"options\":[\"Silently\",\"Aloud\",\"In a whisper\",\"Very fast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states to \'Read the words aloud\'.\",\"topic\":\"Teacher\'s Notes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the teacher help children break down words?\",\"options\":[\"To help them read properly\",\"To make the words shorter\",\"To change the meaning\",\"To count the letters\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Breaking down words into syllables is a method to help children read the words properly.\",\"topic\":\"Teacher\'s Notes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity involves both reading and writing according to the notes?\",\"options\":[\"Opening the Word-Bank\",\"Working in pairs\",\"Working with three to four syllable words\",\"Reading words aloud\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The notes specifically mention encouraging children to \'read and write\' three to four syllable words.\",\"topic\":\"Teacher\'s Notes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the activities mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"To play games\",\"To learn and use words properly\",\"To draw characters\",\"To sit quietly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activities focus on reading, writing, and understanding words and stories.\",\"topic\":\"Teacher\'s Notes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21288,5,2,'English','en','Read a Book','[\"Read a book helps you learn new words and ideas.\",\"When you read, you see pictures, stories, and facts about people and places.\",\"A book can be a story, a poem, a picture book, or a newspaper.\",\"Reading a book is fun when you read with a friend or family.\",\"You can read aloud, listen to someone read, or read silently.\",\"Books have a cover page, a back page, and many pages inside.\",\"A newspaper tells you what happened today in your city and the world.\",\"Reading newspapers helps you know about news, sports, and events.\",\"You can read a book or a newspaper in a quiet place or while listening to music.\",\"Reading a book or newspaper improves your vocabulary and imagination.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what should you read today?\",\"options\":[\"A newspaper\",\"A book\",\"A letter\",\"A map\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem starts with the line \'Read a book today!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Discuss with your friends\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What can you learn about by reading a book, according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Places far away\",\"How to cook\",\"How to run\",\"New games\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Learn about, learn about Places far away!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Discuss with your friends\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, why should we read a book?\",\"options\":[\"To sleep\",\"To know about things\",\"To eat food\",\"To draw pictures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Read a book to know!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Discuss with your friends\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who does the poem suggest you read a book with?\",\"options\":[\"A toy\",\"A pet\",\"A friend\",\"A bird\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Read it with a friend!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Discuss with your friends\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How should you read the book, according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Word by word\",\"Page by page\",\"Line by line\",\"Letter by letter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Page by page, page by page\'.\",\"topic\":\"Discuss with your friends\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to know about people who lived long ago, what should you do?\",\"options\":[\"Go to sleep\",\"Read a book\",\"Play a game\",\"Watch TV\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says to read a book to \'Know about... People long ago!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Discuss with your friends\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When should you stop reading the book according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"When you are tired\",\"When you reach the end\",\"When you see a picture\",\"When you start the book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says to read \'Until you reach the end!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Discuss with your friends\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The section \'Discuss with your friends\' asks you to talk about which of these?\",\"options\":[\"Your favorite food\",\"Which line of the poem you like the most\",\"Your favorite toy\",\"Your school bag\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The discussion section asks \'Which line of the above poem do you like the most?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Discuss with your friends\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poem say we can \'know about\'?\",\"options\":[\"People long ago\",\"Future cars\",\"Space ships\",\"Cooking food\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions to \'Know about, know about People long ago!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Discuss with your friends\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the discussion section, what are you asked about your feelings toward the poem?\",\"options\":[\"If you want to write a poem\",\"If you enjoyed singing the poem\",\"If the poem is too long\",\"If the poem is hard to read\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Question 2 in the discussion section asks \'Did you enjoy singing this poem?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Discuss with your friends\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who are busy reading a newspaper in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Bina and Hardika\",\"Sanchit and Hardika\",\"Sanchit and Bina\",\"The Teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Sanchit and Hardika are busy in reading a newspaper.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are Sanchit and Hardika busy doing?\",\"options\":[\"Playing a game\",\"Writing a story\",\"Reading a newspaper\",\"Drawing a picture\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they are busy reading a newspaper.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence from the text: \'Bina brings a big blue .....\'\",\"options\":[\"book\",\"bag\",\"balloon\",\"box\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the completion exercise in section e, the correct word is \'book\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence from the text: \'Greedy goats grab green .....\'\",\"options\":[\"grass\",\"grapes\",\"grain\",\"ground\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the completion exercise in section e, the correct word is \'grapes\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher bring to the class according to the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Storybooks\",\"Various newspapers\",\"Coloring books\",\"Picture cards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'For the Teacher\' section explicitly asks to bring various newspapers in the class.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should children know about the newspapers brought to class?\",\"options\":[\"The cost of the paper\",\"The name of the printer\",\"Different things in the newspapers\",\"The weight of the paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to let the children know different things in the newspapers.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What activity should the teacher encourage the children to do?\",\"options\":[\"Write a newspaper\",\"Sell newspapers\",\"Read newspapers\",\"Cut newspapers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher is instructed to encourage the children to read newspapers.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'Greedy goats grab green grapes\', what color are the grapes?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the grapes as \'green\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the \'For the Teacher\' section, what is the purpose of bringing newspapers to class?\",\"options\":[\"To teach children how to fold paper\",\"To help children identify different things in them and encourage reading\",\"To clean the classroom desks\",\"To show children how to draw pictures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions focus on letting children know different things in them and encouraging reading.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a question asked in the text to help children think about newspapers?\",\"options\":[\"Where can you buy a newspaper?\",\"How much does a newspaper cost?\",\"Why should we read a newspaper?\",\"Who writes the newspaper?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Question (3) in section d specifically asks \'Why should we read a newspaper?\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21289,5,2,'English','en','In the Market','[\"- The market is a place where people buy and sell goods.\",\"- Goods are items like apples, bananas, clothes, etc.\",\"- Prices tell how much money you need to buy a good.\",\"- Prices can be given per kilogram, per dozen, per piece, etc.\",\"- A kilogram (kg) is a unit of weight.\",\"- A dozen means 12 items.\",\"- In the story, apples cost 100 rupees per kilogram.\",\"- Bananas cost 40 rupees per dozen.\",\"- To find total cost, multiply price by quantity.\",\"- Example: 1 dozen bananas × 40 rupees = 40 rupees.\",\"- Example: 1 kilogram apples × 100 rupees = 100 rupees.\",\"- When buying, you ask the shopkeeper the price.\",\"- The shopkeeper tells you the price per unit.\",\"- You can ask for different quantities (e.g., 1 kg, 2 kg).\",\"- You pay the shopkeeper the total amount after buying.\",\"- The shopkeeper may give you a receipt or say the total in words.\",\"- Children can practice by pretending to buy items in a market.\",\"- Listening to the conversation helps learn how to ask and answer about prices.\",\"- Repeating the dialogue helps remember the words and numbers.\",\"- Understanding units (kg, dozen) helps in real life shopping.\",\"- The market teaches about money, counting, and communication.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who says that the apples look fresh?\",\"options\":[\"The Shopkeeper\",\"Nikita\",\"Nikita\'s Mother\",\"A fruit seller\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the text, Nikita says, \'Mom, these apples look fresh.\'\",\"topic\":\"Buying Bananas\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the cost of apples per kilogram?\",\"options\":[\"40 rupees\",\"50 rupees\",\"100 rupees\",\"80 rupees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The shopkeeper states that the apples are 100 rupees per kilogram.\",\"topic\":\"Buying Bananas\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many kilograms of apples does Nikita\'s mother buy?\",\"options\":[\"Two kilograms\",\"Half a kilogram\",\"One kilogram\",\"Five kilograms\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Nikita\'s mother says, \'Give me one kilogram, please.\'\",\"topic\":\"Buying Bananas\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which fruit is sold by the dozen in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Apples\",\"Mangoes\",\"Bananas\",\"Oranges\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Nikita\'s mother asks for the price of bananas per dozen.\",\"topic\":\"Buying Bananas\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the shopkeeper ask after giving the apples?\",\"options\":[\"Where is the money?\",\"Do you want bananas?\",\"Sure, anything else?\",\"Are the apples fresh?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The shopkeeper asks, \'Sure, anything else?\' after the mother asks for apples.\",\"topic\":\"Buying Bananas\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How much does one dozen bananas cost?\",\"options\":[\"100 rupees\",\"40 rupees\",\"20 rupees\",\"60 rupees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The shopkeeper says, \'Bananas are for 40 rupees per dozen.\'\",\"topic\":\"Buying Bananas\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Nikita\'s mother buys one dozen bananas, how much money should she pay for them?\",\"options\":[\"100 rupees\",\"140 rupees\",\"40 rupees\",\"60 rupees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since one dozen costs 40 rupees, she pays 40 rupees for one dozen.\",\"topic\":\"Buying Bananas\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the shopkeeper gives 1 kg of apples, how much money does he charge for it?\",\"options\":[\"40 rupees\",\"100 rupees\",\"140 rupees\",\"200 rupees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The price for one kilogram of apples is 100 rupees.\",\"topic\":\"Buying Bananas\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where are Nikita and her mother in this conversation?\",\"options\":[\"At home\",\"At school\",\"In the market\",\"In a garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The title of the topic is \'In the Market\' and they are talking to a shopkeeper.\",\"topic\":\"Buying Bananas\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Nikita want to buy the apples?\",\"options\":[\"Because they were cheap\",\"Because they looked fresh\",\"Because she was hungry\",\"Because the shopkeeper asked her\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Nikita mentions the apples look fresh as the reason to buy them.\",\"topic\":\"Buying Bananas\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who is paying the money in the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"The Shopkeeper\",\"Nikita\'s Mother\",\"The Teacher\",\"A student\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows Nikita\'s Mother saying \'Here it is\' after the shopkeeper asks for money.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the total amount mentioned by the shopkeeper?\",\"options\":[\"100 rupees\",\"40 rupees\",\"140 rupees\",\"114 rupees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The shopkeeper says, \'That will be 140 rupees in total.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher give children more exposure to do?\",\"options\":[\"To sleep in class\",\"To speak and raise questions\",\"To draw pictures\",\"To write long essays\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s instructions state to give exposure to speak and raise questions.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instructions, who should participate in the discussion?\",\"options\":[\"Only the teacher\",\"Only one child\",\"Each child\",\"Only the shopkeeper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Make sure that each child participates in the discussion.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher follows the instructions, what will the students do in class?\",\"options\":[\"Sit silently\",\"Ask questions on similar topics\",\"Read the book without talking\",\"Listen only to the teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions encourage children to speak and raise questions.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which two people are talking in the market scene?\",\"options\":[\"A teacher and a student\",\"Nikita and her friend\",\"A shopkeeper and Nikita\'s Mother\",\"Two shopkeepers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The dialogue is between the Shopkeeper and Nikita\'s Mother.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What phrase does the shopkeeper use when giving the items?\",\"options\":[\"Take it now\",\"Here it is\",\"Give me money\",\"Thank you\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The shopkeeper starts his sentence with \'Here it is.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The instruction \'Make sure each child participates\' means the teacher should:\",\"options\":[\"Let everyone have a turn to talk\",\"Only talk to the smartest child\",\"Tell the children to be quiet\",\"Ask the children to go home\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Participation means every child gets involved in the activity.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which activity is happening in the market?\",\"options\":[\"Playing a game\",\"A transaction of goods and money\",\"A singing competition\",\"Cleaning the street\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The mention of a shopkeeper and rupees indicates a transaction.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the teacher need to give \'more exposure\' to children?\",\"options\":[\"To help them learn how to communicate\",\"To make the classroom noisy\",\"To finish the lesson faster\",\"To help the shopkeeper sell things\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Giving exposure to speak helps children learn to communicate and ask questions.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21290,5,2,'English','en','Good Habits','[\"Good habits are actions that keep us healthy and happy.\",\"Bad habits are actions that can make us sick or unhappy.\",\"Rohan is a good example: he washes his hands before eating and follows his parents’ rules.\",\"Sohan is a bad example: he does not brush his teeth and eats junk food.\",\"A stomach ache can happen if we do not keep good habits.\",\"Doctors advise us to wash hands, brush teeth, and eat clean food to stay healthy.\",\"Good habits include drinking clean water, brushing teeth twice a day, bathing daily, wearing clean clothes, washing hands before meals, washing hands with soap after using the toilet, and avoiding uncovered food.\",\"Bad habits are the opposite of these good habits.\",\"If we follow good habits, we feel better and stay healthy.\",\"If we do not follow good habits, we can get sick or feel bad.\",\"It is important to listen to doctors and parents about good habits.\",\"Good habits help us grow strong and smart.\",\"Bad habits can make us feel tired or sick.\",\"We should practice good habits every day.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Rohan and Sohan are ______.\",\"options\":[\"friends\",\"brothers\",\"cousins\",\"neighbors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Rohan and Sohan are brothers.\",\"topic\":\"Rohan and Sohan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of food does Rohan eat?\",\"options\":[\"Junk food\",\"Fresh and healthy food\",\"Only sweets\",\"Spicy food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Rohan eats fresh and healthy food.\",\"topic\":\"Rohan and Sohan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the boy doing at the washbasin?\",\"options\":[\"Brushing his teeth\",\"Washing his hands\",\"Drinking water\",\"Playing with soap\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the boy washing his hands under a tap at the basin.\",\"topic\":\"Rohan and Sohan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/074_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How is Rohan described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Naughty and messy\",\"Neat and tidy\",\"Lazy and tired\",\"Sad and angry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly describes Rohan as neat and tidy.\",\"topic\":\"Rohan and Sohan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Sohan get a stomach ache?\",\"options\":[\"Because he played too much\",\"Because he followed good habits\",\"Because he ate junk food and never washed his hands\",\"Because he brushed his teeth every day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sohan\'s poor hygiene and eating habits led to his stomach ache.\",\"topic\":\"Rohan and Sohan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which activity helps the boy keep his teeth clean?\",\"options\":[\"Washing hands\",\"Eating rice\",\"Brushing teeth\",\"Sitting at the table\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the boy using a toothbrush and toothpaste to clean his teeth.\",\"topic\":\"Rohan and Sohan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/074_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a good habit followed by Rohan?\",\"options\":[\"Teasing others\",\"Eating junk food\",\"Washing hands before eating\",\"Not brushing teeth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Washing hands before eating is listed as one of Rohan\'s good habits.\",\"topic\":\"Rohan and Sohan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to be like Sohan, what would you do?\",\"options\":[\"Obey your parents\",\"Tease others\",\"Eat healthy food\",\"Keep yourself tidy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes Sohan as a naughty boy who teases others.\",\"topic\":\"Rohan and Sohan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main difference between Rohan and Sohan\'s habits?\",\"options\":[\"Rohan is naughty, but Sohan is neat\",\"Rohan washes his hands, but Sohan never does\",\"Rohan eats junk food, but Sohan eats fresh food\",\"Rohan teases others, but Sohan obeys parents\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text contrasts Rohan\'s cleanliness with Sohan\'s lack of hygiene.\",\"topic\":\"Rohan and Sohan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why is Sohan called a \'naughty boy\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because he obeys his parents\",\"Because he teases others and has bad habits\",\"Because he has a stomach ache\",\"Because he is Rohan\'s brother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sohan is called naughty because he teases others and does not follow good hygiene.\",\"topic\":\"Rohan and Sohan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who takes Sohan to the doctor?\",\"options\":[\"His father\",\"His mother\",\"His sister\",\"His friend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'His mother takes him to the doctor.\'\",\"topic\":\"Doctor\'s Advice\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the doctor\'s advice, how many times a day should you brush your teeth?\",\"options\":[\"Once a day\",\"Twice a day\",\"Three times a day\",\"Once a week\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The doctor\'s instruction is to \'Brush your teeth twice a day.\'\",\"topic\":\"Doctor\'s Advice\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the doctor use to treat Sohan?\",\"options\":[\"Sweets\",\"Fruits\",\"Medicines\",\"Toys\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the doctor \'treats with some medicines.\'\",\"topic\":\"Doctor\'s Advice\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of water does the doctor advise Sohan to drink?\",\"options\":[\"Cold water\",\"Sweet water\",\"Pure and clean water\",\"River water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The doctor\'s instruction is to \'Drink pure and clean water.\'\",\"topic\":\"Doctor\'s Advice\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Sohan is about to eat his lunch, what should he do first according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Brush his teeth\",\"Wash his hands\",\"Have a bath\",\"Wear new shoes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text advises to \'Wash your hands before eating.\'\",\"topic\":\"Doctor\'s Advice\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should be used to wash hands after using the toilet?\",\"options\":[\"Only water\",\"A towel\",\"Soap\",\"Oil\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Wash your hands with soap after using the toilet.\'\",\"topic\":\"Doctor\'s Advice\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a \'good habit\' mentioned by the doctor to keep the body clean every day?\",\"options\":[\"Have a bath everyday\",\"Avoid drinking water\",\"Wear dirty clothes\",\"Eat uncovered food\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The doctor instructs to \'Have a bath everyday.\'\",\"topic\":\"Doctor\'s Advice\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the doctor\'s advice, what should we do with uncovered food?\",\"options\":[\"Eat it quickly\",\"Avoid it\",\"Share it with friends\",\"Buy it from the market\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says to \'Avoid uncovered food.\'\",\"topic\":\"Doctor\'s Advice\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what instrument is the doctor wearing around his neck?\",\"options\":[\"A tie\",\"A stethoscope\",\"A whistle\",\"A necklace\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a doctor with a stethoscope around his neck.\",\"topic\":\"Doctor\'s Advice\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/075_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the doctor doing while giving advice?\",\"options\":[\"He is sleeping\",\"He is washing his hands\",\"He is pointing his finger up to instruct\",\"He is drinking water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The image shows the doctor with one finger raised, indicating he is giving instructions or advice.\",\"topic\":\"Doctor\'s Advice\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/075_101.jpg\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21291,5,2,'English','en','Five Senses','[\"The five senses are the ways our body learns about the world.\",\"1. Sight – the eyes help us see colours, shapes and distance.\",\"2. Hearing – the ears help us hear sounds like music, speech and noise.\",\"3. Smell – the nose helps us smell food, flowers and other scents.\",\"4. Taste – the tongue helps us taste sweet, salty, sour and bitter foods.\",\"5. Touch – the skin helps us feel hot, cold, rough or smooth.\",\"The senses work together to help us understand our surroundings.\",\"We can use words like ‘see’, ‘hear’, ‘smell’, ‘taste’ and ‘touch’ to describe what we feel.\",\"Our eyes are the most important sense for reading and writing.\",\"The ears help us listen to our teachers and friends.\",\"The nose helps us know when food is fresh or spoiled.\",\"The tongue helps us decide if food is yummy or not.\",\"The skin helps us feel safe by protecting our body.\",\"We can practice our senses by looking, listening, smelling, tasting and touching things around us.\",\"We can use ‘this’, ‘that’, ‘these’, ‘those’ to talk about objects near or far.\",\"We can sing a poem about our senses to remember them easily.\",\"We should be careful not to touch hot or sharp objects.\",\"We can use our senses to learn new words and ideas.\",\"Our senses help us stay safe and healthy.\",\"We can share what we feel with friends and family.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what do the eyes help us do?\",\"options\":[\"Hear\",\"See\",\"Smell\",\"Taste\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The eyes that I have, help to see\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which body part helps us to hear everything?\",\"options\":[\"Hands\",\"Nose\",\"Ears\",\"Tongue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The ears that I have help to hear\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the use of the nose according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To touch\",\"To see\",\"To taste\",\"To smell\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The nose that I have helps to smell\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do the hands help us to do?\",\"options\":[\"Touch everything\",\"Hear everything\",\"See everything\",\"Taste everything\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The hands that I have help to touch... Touch everything!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, which part of the body is used to taste?\",\"options\":[\"Nose\",\"Tongue\",\"Hands\",\"Ears\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The tongue that I have help to taste\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The poem says we use our senses to sense \'everything\'. Which word is repeated for every sense?\",\"options\":[\"Nothing\",\"Something\",\"Everything\",\"Anything\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem uses the phrase \'everything\' for seeing, hearing, smelling, touching, and tasting.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to know if a flower has a nice scent, which body part from the poem will you use?\",\"options\":[\"Eyes\",\"Ears\",\"Nose\",\"Hands\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The nose is used to smell scents.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are holding a soft toy, which action from the poem are you doing with your hands?\",\"options\":[\"Seeing\",\"Hearing\",\"Tasting\",\"Touching\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The hands are used to touch and feel objects.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which body part is shown?\",\"options\":[\"Eyes\",\"Ears\",\"Nose\",\"Tongue\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a pair of eyes.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/076_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the main function of these parts as described in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"To hear sounds\",\"To smell flowers\",\"To see everything\",\"To taste food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows eyes, and the poem says eyes are used to see everything.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/076_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which organ is used to smell according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Ear\",\"Nose\",\"Skin\",\"Tongue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly links \'nose\' with \'smell\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sense is associated with the skin?\",\"options\":[\"Hear\",\"See\",\"Touch\",\"Taste\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'skin touch\' as one of the sense pairs.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these body parts is suggested to create a new poem?\",\"options\":[\"Hair\",\"Legs\",\"Back\",\"Shoulder\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'legs, teeth, fingers\' as examples for creating a poem.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When talking about one nose that is far away, which word is used in the text?\",\"options\":[\"This\",\"These\",\"That\",\"Those\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'That is your nose\' to refer to a nose that is not \'my nose\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is the correct pair for the ears?\",\"options\":[\"Ear - See\",\"Ear - Taste\",\"Ear - Smell\",\"Ear - Hear\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'ear\' with the action \'hear\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used for many objects (plural) that are near you?\",\"options\":[\"This\",\"That\",\"Those\",\"These\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'These are my ears\' to show plural objects near the speaker.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are pointing to your own two eyes, how should you start the sentence based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"This is my eyes\",\"These are my eyes\",\"That is my eyes\",\"Those are my eyes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'These\' for plural body parts belonging to \'me\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Besides body parts, what else can be used to practice \'this\\/that\' and \'these\\/those\'?\",\"options\":[\"Only the teacher\",\"Objects in the surrounding\",\"Only the poem\",\"Only the textbook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests practicing with \'various objects in the surrounding\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text mention \'legs, teeth, fingers\'?\",\"options\":[\"To show how to walk\",\"To list all body parts\",\"To give examples for a new poem\",\"To explain how to taste\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides these as examples for creating and singing the poem using other body parts.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final activity encouraged for children regarding sentences?\",\"options\":[\"Only read them\",\"Make and write them\",\"Only listen to them\",\"Draw them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages children to \'make and write the sentences\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21292,5,2,'English','en','Magic Words','[\"Magic words are polite words that help us ask for help or give permission.\",\"Excuse me – used to get someone\'s attention politely.\",\"May I…? – used to ask for permission to do something.\",\"You may – a polite answer meaning ‘yes, you can’.\",\"I am sorry – used to apologize when we make a mistake.\",\"Please – used to make a request more polite.\",\"Thank you – used to show gratitude.\",\"You can do it – encouraging words to give confidence.\",\"I can’t do this – honest statement when we cannot do something.\",\"Help – asking for assistance.\",\"Use magic words in everyday conversations to be polite and friendly.\",\"Remember to say ‘Excuse me’ before speaking to a teacher or a friend.\",\"When you spill something, say ‘I am sorry’ and ask ‘May I help you?’\",\"Use ‘Please’ when you ask for something like an eraser or water.\",\"After someone helps you, say ‘Thank you’ and ‘You’re welcome’.\",\"Magic words help keep the classroom friendly and respectful.\",\"Practice speaking with a friend or family member using these words.\",\"Use magic words in both speaking and writing to improve manners.\",\"Listening to others use magic words can help you learn them faster.\",\"Always use a calm tone when speaking magic words.\",\"Magic words are also called polite words or manners.\",\"They help build good relationships at school and home.\",\"Use them every day to become a polite and kind person.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What should you say before asking the teacher for permission to drink water?\",\"options\":[\"Hello\",\"Excuse me\",\"Goodbye\",\"Sorry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows the student starting the conversation with \'Excuse me, Teacher.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used in the text to politely ask for water?\",\"options\":[\"Now\",\"Give\",\"Please\",\"Water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The student asks, \'May I drink water, please?\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the student say after spilling water?\",\"options\":[\"I am sorry!\",\"Thank you!\",\"Excuse me!\",\"Wow!\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the text, the student says \'I am sorry!\' after spilling water.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What instruction does the teacher give after the water is spilled?\",\"options\":[\"Don\'t drink water.\",\"Go out.\",\"Be careful, next time.\",\"Clean it now.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher responds to the spill by saying, \'Be careful, next time.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to borrow an eraser, which \'magic word\' should you use according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Sorry\",\"Please\",\"Excuse me\",\"Great\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the sentence \'Please, give me your eraser.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should you say after someone gives you their eraser?\",\"options\":[\"Take it.\",\"I am sorry.\",\"Thank you.\",\"Excuse me.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The conversation shows the student saying \'Thank you\' after receiving the eraser.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text suggest saying when you see someone who cannot do a task?\",\"options\":[\"I am sorry.\",\"Can I help you to do it?\",\"Excuse me.\",\"Take it.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"When a student says \'I can not do this\', the other responds with \'Can I help you to do it?\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What specific object is mentioned in the conversation about borrowing?\",\"options\":[\"Pencil\",\"Book\",\"Eraser\",\"Water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions borrowing an \'eraser\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the text, how does the other person react when someone offers to help?\",\"options\":[\"No, thank you.\",\"I am sorry.\",\"Yes, please.\",\"Excuse me.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text ends the help conversation with the response \'Yes, please.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used to express excitement or praise before offering help?\",\"options\":[\"Oh!\",\"Wow!\",\"Please\",\"Sorry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'Wow! That\'s great!\' before the offer to help.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21293,5,2,'English','en','Rahi : The Girl Who Never Gives up!','[\"Rahi is a girl from a small town in Maharashtra who loves shooting.\",\"She practiced shooting every day even when people said it was not a sport for girls.\",\"She slipped and hurt her elbow, doctors said she might never shoot again.\",\"Rahi did not give up, she worked hard and became stronger.\",\"She returned to shooting and won a gold medal at the Asian Games for India.\",\"She is the first Indian woman to win a gold medal in shooting.\",\"The story teaches us to be brave and never give up.\",\"Key words: shooter, medal, slip, elbow, Asian Games, gold medal.\",\"Dictionary words: shooter – a person who shoots; medal – a small metal award; slip – to slide or fall; elbow – part of the arm; Asian Games – a sports event for Asian countries.\",\"Syllable clapping: badminton → bad‑min‑ton, volleyball → vol‑ley‑ball.\",\"Games mentioned: Chess, Carrom, Badminton, Ludo, Table tennis, Snakes and Ladders, Cricket, Kabaddi, Hockey, Football, Volleyball, Kho‑kho.\",\"Fill in the blanks: \\\"______ is my favourite game.\\\" \\\"It is ______ game.\\\" \\\"There are ______ players in this game.\\\" \\\"I ______ this game.\\\"\",\"Remember to use a dictionary to find meanings of new words.\",\"Be brave like Rahi and never give up on your dreams.\",\"Practice regularly to improve your skills.\",\"Celebrate small successes on the way to big goals.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which state of India is Rahi\'s small town located?\",\"options\":[\"Gujarat\",\"Maharashtra\",\"Goa\",\"Punjab\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Rahi is a girl from a small town in Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"Rahi\'s Comeback and Success\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sport did Rahi love to practise every day?\",\"options\":[\"Running\",\"Wrestling\",\"Shooting\",\"Swimming\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Rahi loved to practise shooting every day.\",\"topic\":\"Rahi\'s Comeback and Success\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did people say to Rahi about shooting?\",\"options\":[\"It is a very easy sport\",\"That’s not a sport for girls!\",\"You should practise more\",\"It is a sport for everyone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, people said, \'That’s not a sport for girls!\'\",\"topic\":\"Rahi\'s Comeback and Success\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of her body did Rahi hurt when she slipped?\",\"options\":[\"Her knee\",\"Her wrist\",\"Her elbow\",\"Her shoulder\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that one day she slipped and hurt her elbow badly.\",\"topic\":\"Rahi\'s Comeback and Success\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the doctors\' opinion about Rahi after her injury?\",\"options\":[\"She would be fine in two days\",\"She might never shoot again\",\"She should change her sport\",\"She should stop walking\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says doctors said that she might never shoot again.\",\"topic\":\"Rahi\'s Comeback and Success\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, how did Rahi manage to come back to the game?\",\"options\":[\"She waited for a miracle\",\"She stopped practising\",\"She worked hard and became stronger\",\"She found a new doctor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rahi didn\'t give up, worked hard, and became stronger to come back.\",\"topic\":\"Rahi\'s Comeback and Success\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the result of Rahi\'s hard work after her injury?\",\"options\":[\"She became stronger and came back\",\"She decided to leave Maharashtra\",\"She started a new hobby\",\"She became a doctor\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explains that after working hard, she became stronger and came back to the game.\",\"topic\":\"Rahi\'s Comeback and Success\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which medal did Rahi win at the Asian Games?\",\"options\":[\"Silver medal\",\"Gold medal\",\"Bronze medal\",\"Participation medal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states she went to the Asian games and won a gold medal.\",\"topic\":\"Rahi\'s Comeback and Success\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is special about Rahi\'s achievement at the Asian Games?\",\"options\":[\"She was the youngest player\",\"She was the only one from Maharashtra\",\"She is the first Indian woman to win gold in shooting there\",\"She won the medal without any practice\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she is the first Indian woman to win a gold medal in shooting for India at the Asian Games.\",\"topic\":\"Rahi\'s Comeback and Success\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the title \'The Girl Who Never Gives up!\' suitable for Rahi?\",\"options\":[\"Because she lived in a small town\",\"Because she listened to what people said\",\"Because she came back to win even after a bad injury\",\"Because she liked to travel for games\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story shows Rahi\'s determination to return and win despite a serious injury and negative comments.\",\"topic\":\"Rahi\'s Comeback and Success\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main lesson we learn from Rahi’s story?\",\"options\":[\"Be brave and never give up\",\"Always be quiet in class\",\"Give up when things are hard\",\"Only play indoor games\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that Rahi’s story teaches us to be brave and never give up.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the story, what should you \'never\' do?\",\"options\":[\"Never play games\",\"Never give up\",\"Never read books\",\"Never talk to teachers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text teaches the lesson to \'never give up\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should children collect information about, according to the teacher\'s instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Famous players\",\"Famous toys\",\"Famous movies\",\"Famous animals\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note encourages children to collect information about famous players.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which tool should children use to find the meanings of words?\",\"options\":[\"A notebook\",\"A dictionary\",\"A drawing board\",\"A map\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions helping children find words and their meanings from a dictionary.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of games should the teacher discuss with the children?\",\"options\":[\"Only video games\",\"Local and regional games\",\"Games that are not fun\",\"Only games played in other countries\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher is instructed to discuss local and regional games with the children.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a student finds a difficult word in the story, what should they do based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Look for the meaning in a dictionary\",\"Stop reading the story\",\"Skip the word entirely\",\"Draw a picture of the word\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using a dictionary to find words and their meanings.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher motivate the children to do?\",\"options\":[\"Play different games\",\"Stay inside all day\",\"Stop playing games\",\"Only play one game\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note says to motivate children to play different games.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are making a scrap-book about sports, who does the text suggest you look for?\",\"options\":[\"Famous players\",\"Famous doctors\",\"Famous singers\",\"Famous dancers\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text encourages collecting information about famous players.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the attitude Rahi’s story wants us to have?\",\"options\":[\"Brave\",\"Scared\",\"Angry\",\"Lazy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says \'Be brave\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The teacher discusses games that are \'local\'. What does this imply about the games?\",\"options\":[\"They are played in the nearby area\",\"They are played in space\",\"They are played on computers only\",\"They are not real games\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Local games refer to games played in the children\'s own region or area.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21294,5,2,'English','en','Mother Duck','[\"Mother duck and her ducklings live near a lake.\",\"They swim in the cool water of the lake.\",\"One day a fox appears and scares them.\",\"Mother duck is worried because the ducklings cannot fly.\",\"She tells them to run to the lake and then runs away to lead the fox away.\",\"The fox follows her but she takes it far from the lake.\",\"The ducklings jump into the water and stay safe.\",\"After the danger is gone, mother duck returns to her ducklings.\",\"The ducklings are happy and swim again.\",\"The fox goes away sadly.\",\"The story shows how a mother protects her children.\",\"It teaches courage and quick thinking.\",\"It also shows that animals can be friendly or scary.\",\"The story is simple and suitable for young readers.\",\"It encourages retelling and discussion about feelings and actions.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did the mother duck and her ducklings live?\",\"options\":[\"In a forest\",\"Near a lake\",\"In a farm\",\"On a tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states they lived happily near a lake.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox Appears\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is the lake described in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Small\",\"Dirty\",\"Beautiful\",\"Hot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'It was a beautiful lake.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Fox Appears\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the ducklings love to do in the water?\",\"options\":[\"Sleep\",\"Swim\",\"Fly\",\"Dance\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they loved to swim in the cool water.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox Appears\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How was the water of the lake?\",\"options\":[\"Warm\",\"Cool\",\"Salty\",\"Deep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the water as \'cool water\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox Appears\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How often did the mother duck take her ducklings to the lake?\",\"options\":[\"Once a week\",\"Every day\",\"Only on Sundays\",\"Never\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Mother duck took her ducklings every day to the lake.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Fox Appears\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What were they doing near the lake one morning?\",\"options\":[\"Eating\",\"Sleeping\",\"Playing\",\"Running\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'One morning, they were playing near the lake.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Fox Appears\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Whose cry did they hear suddenly?\",\"options\":[\"A lion\",\"A dog\",\"A fox\",\"A wolf\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Suddenly, they heard the cry of a fox.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Fox Appears\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the mother duck tell the ducklings to do when she heard the fox?\",\"options\":[\"To jump in the lake\",\"To run away\",\"To hide in the grass\",\"To start swimming\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Mother duck said, \'Come, let’s run away.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Fox Appears\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the mother duck want to run away?\",\"options\":[\"She was tired of playing\",\"The water was too cold\",\"A fox was nearby\",\"It was time for lunch\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"She wanted to run away because she heard the cry of a fox.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox Appears\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, how did the ducks feel about the lake?\",\"options\":[\"They were afraid of it\",\"They lived happily there\",\"They did not like the water\",\"They wanted to leave it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they lived happily near the lake and loved to swim in it.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox Appears\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Mother duck worried?\",\"options\":[\"Her ducklings could not swim\",\"Her ducklings could not fly\",\"The lake was very far\",\"She was feeling hungry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Mother duck was worried because her ducklings couldn\'t fly.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox is Fooled\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Mother duck tell her ducklings to rush?\",\"options\":[\"To the forest\",\"To the lake\",\"To the nest\",\"To the fox\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Mother duck said to the ducklings, \'Quick! Rush to the lake at once.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Fox is Fooled\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Mother duck do to pretend she was hurt?\",\"options\":[\"She sat on the ground\",\"She closed her eyes\",\"She dragged her wings\",\"She started crying\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she dragged her wings as if she was hurt to trick the fox.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox is Fooled\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Mother duck walk very fast away from the lake?\",\"options\":[\"To find some food\",\"To teach the ducklings to run\",\"To take the fox far away from the lake\",\"To reach the other side of the forest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"She walked fast to lead the fox away so the ducklings could safely reach the water.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox is Fooled\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does the story describe the fox?\",\"options\":[\"Clever\",\"Foolish\",\"Kind\",\"Strong\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically uses the word \'foolish\' to describe the fox.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox is Fooled\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the ducklings do when the fox followed Mother duck?\",\"options\":[\"They followed the fox\",\"They hid in the grass\",\"They rushed into the water\",\"They tried to fly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the ducklings rushed into the water while the fox was busy following Mother duck.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox is Fooled\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the fox doing while Mother duck drags her wings?\",\"options\":[\"He is sleeping\",\"He is following Mother duck\",\"He is swimming in the lake\",\"He is catching a duckling\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the fox walking behind Mother duck as she leads him away.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox is Fooled\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/082_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where are the ducklings while Mother duck is away?\",\"options\":[\"They are in the water\",\"They are under a tree\",\"They are flying in the sky\",\"They are behind the fox\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the ducklings have successfully reached and entered the water.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox is Fooled\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/083_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Mother duck is a ________ mother because she saved her ducklings from the fox.\",\"options\":[\"Lazy\",\"Wise\",\"Scared\",\"Mean\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"By thinking of a plan to fool the fox, Mother duck showed she is wise.\",\"topic\":\"The Fox is Fooled\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What were the exact words Mother duck said to her ducklings?\",\"options\":[\"Go away now!\",\"Hide in the bushes.\",\"Quick! Rush to the lake at once.\",\"Follow the fox.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the direct quote: \'Quick! Rush to the lake at once.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Fox is Fooled\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who returned to the ducklings?\",\"options\":[\"The fox\",\"Mother duck\",\"A hunter\",\"A fish\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that mother duck flew away and returned to her ducklings.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the ducklings swim again?\",\"options\":[\"In the sea\",\"In a river\",\"In the lake\",\"In a pond\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says they swam in the lake again.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the ducklings feel when they saw mother duck?\",\"options\":[\"Sad\",\"Angry\",\"Scared\",\"Happy\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the ducklings were happy to see her.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the fox go away?\",\"options\":[\"Happily\",\"Sadly\",\"Quickly\",\"Noisily\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the fox went away sadly.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did mother duck do to reach her ducklings?\",\"options\":[\"She walked back\",\"She swam back\",\"She flew away and returned\",\"She jumped back\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says mother duck flew away and returned to her ducklings.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why were the ducklings happy?\",\"options\":[\"Because the fox was coming\",\"Because they saw mother duck\",\"Because they were sleeping\",\"Because they were eating\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links their happiness to seeing mother duck.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the ducklings after mother duck returned?\",\"options\":[\"They were safe\",\"They were lost\",\"They were cold\",\"They were hungry\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states \'They were safe.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'They swam in the lake again\', who does \'They\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"The fox\",\"The mother duck and ducklings\",\"The trees\",\"The hunters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Contextually, \'They\' refers to the mother duck and her ducklings who were together at the lake.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the final action the ducks did in the text?\",\"options\":[\"They flew away\",\"They went to the fox\",\"They swam in the lake\",\"They hid in the grass\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text ends with the ducks swimming in the lake again.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which character did NOT have a happy ending in this story?\",\"options\":[\"Mother duck\",\"The ducklings\",\"The fox\",\"The lake\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the fox went away sadly, unlike the happy ducklings.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21295,5,2,'English','en','Story Time','[\"- Dice can be used to start a story.\",\"- Each group rolls the dice and looks at the picture and word that matches the number.\",\"- After reading, the group discusses and writes a short story.\",\"- The story should have a title, a beginning, middle and end.\",\"- Groups present their stories to the class.\",\"- Use simple sentences and clear ideas.\",\"- The dice helps choose random elements like people, places, times and events.\",\"- Remember to use the words you see on the dice in your story.\",\"- Practice speaking and listening while presenting.\",\"- Have fun and be creative!\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many students should sit together in a group?\",\"options\":[\"One or two\",\"Three or four\",\"Five or six\",\"Ten or twelve\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states to sit in groups of three or four.\",\"topic\":\"Story Creation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What object is used to get a number for the story?\",\"options\":[\"A ball\",\"A pencil\",\"A dice\",\"A ruler\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to roll the dice and look at the number.\",\"topic\":\"Story Creation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you look at after rolling the dice?\",\"options\":[\"The ceiling\",\"The number on the dice\",\"The floor\",\"The clock\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 3 says to look at the number on the dice.\",\"topic\":\"Story Creation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What must you do with the words for your number?\",\"options\":[\"Erase them\",\"Read them\",\"Color them\",\"Hide them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 4 says to read the words for that number.\",\"topic\":\"Story Creation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the group go to discuss the story?\",\"options\":[\"To the playground\",\"To the teacher\'s desk\",\"Back to their place\",\"Outside the classroom\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 5 instructs the group to go back to their place to discuss.\",\"topic\":\"Story Creation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of story should the group make?\",\"options\":[\"A very long story\",\"A short story\",\"A scary story\",\"A poem\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies to make a short story.\",\"topic\":\"Story Creation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides the story, what else must the group decide?\",\"options\":[\"A title for the story\",\"A price for the story\",\"A song for the story\",\"A dance for the story\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Step 5 says to decide a title for your story.\",\"topic\":\"Story Creation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happens after one group finishes rolling the dice and goes back?\",\"options\":[\"The class ends\",\"The other groups do the same\",\"Everyone goes to sleep\",\"The teacher rolls the dice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 6 says the other groups will do the same.\",\"topic\":\"Story Creation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very first step in this activity?\",\"options\":[\"Roll the dice\",\"Read the words\",\"Sit in groups\",\"Decide a title\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first instruction is to sit in groups of three or four.\",\"topic\":\"Story Creation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of looking at the pictures and reading the words?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to draw\",\"To create a story\",\"To win a race\",\"To count the pictures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity is titled \'Story Creation\' and the pictures\\/words help make the story.\",\"topic\":\"Story Creation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the girl in the example story live?\",\"options\":[\"In the village\",\"In the city\",\"In the forest\",\"In the school\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states \'There was a girl in the village.\'\",\"topic\":\"Example Story\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When did the girl see her brother playing football?\",\"options\":[\"In the evening\",\"In the morning\",\"At night\",\"In the afternoon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The example story says, \'In the morning, she saw her brother playing football.\'\",\"topic\":\"Example Story\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who did the girl live with in her house?\",\"options\":[\"Her friends\",\"Her grandmother\",\"Her mother and father\",\"Her teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she lived with her mother and father.\",\"topic\":\"Example Story\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the prompts, where was the dog in the afternoon?\",\"options\":[\"In the field\",\"On the road\",\"In the market\",\"At the square\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The prompt list links \'dog\', \'road\', and \'afternoon\' together.\",\"topic\":\"Example Story\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the fox at the grape farm?\",\"options\":[\"He slept\",\"He ran away\",\"He jumped\",\"He ate grapes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The prompt for the fox at the grape farm says \'jumped\'.\",\"topic\":\"Example Story\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"At what time did the accident happen near the policeman?\",\"options\":[\"1 o\'clock\",\"2 o\'clock\",\"Midday\",\"Morning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The prompt list states \'policeman square 2 o\'clock accident\'.\",\"topic\":\"Example Story\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"On which day was the old woman in the market?\",\"options\":[\"Monday\",\"Saturday\",\"Friday\",\"Sunday\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'old woman in a market Sunday crowd\'.\",\"topic\":\"Example Story\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the brother doing in the morning?\",\"options\":[\"Reading a book\",\"Playing football\",\"Eating breakfast\",\"Sleeping\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The example story says she saw her brother playing football.\",\"topic\":\"Example Story\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the farmer on a rainy day?\",\"options\":[\"In the house\",\"In the field\",\"In the market\",\"On the road\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The prompt list associates the farmer with the field.\",\"topic\":\"Example Story\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the dog on the road in the afternoon?\",\"options\":[\"He was hungry\",\"He was thirsty\",\"He was playing\",\"He was lost\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The prompt for the dog on the road includes the word \'thirsty\'.\",\"topic\":\"Example Story\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21296,5,2,'English','en','Grow a Little Plant','[\"- A plant grows from a seed when it gets water, soil and sunlight.\",\"- Seeds are tiny and can be found in many places like gardens, farms and even in your kitchen.\",\"- To grow a plant you need a pot, soil, water and a sunny spot.\",\"- First put the pot in a sunny place so the seed can grow strong.\",\"- Fill the pot half full with soil, then make a small hole in the middle.\",\"- Drop the seed into the hole and cover it gently with more soil.\",\"- Water the soil lightly, just enough to keep it moist.\",\"- Water the plant every day, but not too much, otherwise the seed may rot.\",\"- After a few days a little sprout will appear; keep it in the sun and water it daily.\",\"- When the plant is big enough you can take it outside or keep it indoors.\",\"- Seeds can be stored at home in a dry place until you want to plant them.\",\"- You can also make seed balls by mixing seed, soil and water and rolling them into balls.\",\"- A seed ball is a small ball that can be planted in the garden and will grow a plant.\",\"- Growing a plant teaches responsibility and patience.\",\"- Remember: Sunlight, soil, water and care are the four important things for a plant to grow.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the first step to grow a little plant according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Take a pot\",\"Pour water\",\"Keep in sun\",\"Fill with soil\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first step in the instructions is \'Take a pot\'.\",\"topic\":\"Project Work\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How much soil should you fill in the pot at the beginning?\",\"options\":[\"Fill it to the top\",\"Fill it half\",\"Fill it very little\",\"Do not use soil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 2 says to fill the pot half with soil.\",\"topic\":\"Project Work\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should you make in the soil before putting the seeds?\",\"options\":[\"A big mountain\",\"A small hole\",\"A long line\",\"A deep well\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 3 says to \'Make a small hole in the soil\'.\",\"topic\":\"Project Work\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What must you do immediately after putting the seeds into the holes?\",\"options\":[\"Pour all the water\",\"Cover them with soil\",\"Keep them in the dark\",\"Take them out\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 5 instructs to \'Cover them with soil\' after putting the seeds in.\",\"topic\":\"Project Work\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the pot be kept to help the plant grow?\",\"options\":[\"Inside a cupboard\",\"Under the bed\",\"In the sunlight\",\"In a dark room\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 7 says to \'Keep the pot in the sunlight\'.\",\"topic\":\"Project Work\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How often should you water the pot?\",\"options\":[\"Once a week\",\"Every day\",\"Only on Sundays\",\"Never water it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 8 says to \'Water the pot every day\'.\",\"topic\":\"Project Work\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What can you make with the different types of seeds you collect?\",\"options\":[\"Seed balls\",\"Seed toys\",\"Seed boxes\",\"Seed food\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'You can make seed balls\' from collected seeds.\",\"topic\":\"Project Work\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which action comes right after pouring a little water?\",\"options\":[\"Fill the pot half\",\"Make a hole\",\"Keep the pot in the sunlight\",\"Collect seeds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 6 is pouring water, and Step 7 is keeping it in the sunlight.\",\"topic\":\"Project Work\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where should you store the seeds you collect?\",\"options\":[\"At the park\",\"At your home\",\"At the shop\",\"In the school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Store them at your home\'.\",\"topic\":\"Project Work\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you have just covered the seeds with soil, what is your next task?\",\"options\":[\"Pour little water\",\"Take a pot\",\"Make a hole\",\"Store seeds at home\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Step 5 is covering with soil, and the next step (Step 6) is to pour little water.\",\"topic\":\"Project Work\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the children practice the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"In the playground\",\"In the classroom\",\"At home\",\"In the garden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states to help children practice the instructions in the classroom.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the children asked to collect?\",\"options\":[\"Flowers\",\"Leaves\",\"Seeds\",\"Stones\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks children to collect seeds.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When were the seeds that need to be collected sown?\",\"options\":[\"During the summer season\",\"During the winter season\",\"During the rainy season\",\"During the spring season\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions seeds sown during the rainy season.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should be arranged using the seeds collected by the children?\",\"options\":[\"A party\",\"An exhibition\",\"A race\",\"A game\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to arrange an exhibition of the seeds collected by the children.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student finds a seed sown in the rainy season, what should they do according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Throw it away\",\"Eat it\",\"Collect it\",\"Paint it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions ask children to collect the seeds sown during the rainy season.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where would a teacher help children practice their classroom instructions?\",\"options\":[\"In the market\",\"In the classroom\",\"In the library\",\"In the bus\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that the practice happens in the classroom.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who is responsible for collecting the seeds for the exhibition?\",\"options\":[\"The teachers\",\"The children\",\"The parents\",\"The principal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks the children to collect the seeds.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The exhibition mentioned in the text is specifically for which items?\",\"options\":[\"Books\",\"Toys\",\"Seeds\",\"Drawings\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the exhibition is of the seeds collected by the children.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the final goal of collecting the seeds?\",\"options\":[\"To cook them\",\"To sell them\",\"To arrange an exhibition\",\"To play with them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying an exhibition should be arranged with the collected seeds.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What are the children asked to practice in the classroom?\",\"options\":[\"Singing\",\"Instructions\",\"Dancing\",\"Running\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins by saying to help children practice the instructions.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21297,5,2,'English','en','Alphabet Train','[\"Alphabetical order means arranging words from A to Z.\",\"The alphabet has 26 letters, from A to Z.\",\"Each letter has a capital (uppercase) and a small (lowercase) form.\",\"To find the order, look at the first letter of each word.\",\"If two words start with the same letter, look at the second letter.\",\"If the second letters are the same, look at the third, and so on.\",\"A word that starts with A comes before a word that starts with B.\",\"The word “apple” comes before “banana” because A < B.\",\"The word “cat” comes after “banana” because C > B.\",\"The word “dog” comes after “cat” because D > C.\",\"The alphabet can be written on a line or on cards.\",\"You can use flash cards to practice sorting words.\",\"A picture dictionary is a list of pictures with their names in alphabetical order.\",\"When you write a word, write the capital letter first and then the small letters.\",\"If you see a word that is not in the right place, move it to the correct spot.\",\"Practice with different sets of words to improve speed.\",\"Use the alphabet chart to check your order.\",\"You can write the alphabet on a piece of paper and colour each letter.\",\"The alphabet is the same in English and in many other languages.\",\"Knowing the alphabet helps you read and write better.\",\"Practice every day for a few minutes.\",\"Ask a teacher or parent to help you if you are unsure.\",\"Keep your alphabet cards tidy so you can find them easily.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word starts with the letter \'A\' in the picture dictionary?\",\"options\":[\"ant\",\"ball\",\"cap\",\"doll\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the words for \'A\' are ant, apple, and arrow.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is listed under the letter \'M\' in the dictionary?\",\"options\":[\"monkey\",\"lizard\",\"kite\",\"joker\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'man, medicine, monkey\' under the letter M.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word starts with the letter \'G\' in the dictionary?\",\"options\":[\"gate\",\"hat\",\"iron\",\"jug\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'gate, gift, grapes\' for the letter G.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'E\' section, which word comes after \'elephant\'?\",\"options\":[\"eye\",\"ear\",\"egg\",\"eagle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The sequence for E is \'ear, elephant, eye\'.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of words all start with the letter \'B\' in the dictionary?\",\"options\":[\"ball, banana, bird\",\"ant, apple, arrow\",\"cap, calendar, camel\",\"fan, fish, flower\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text groups ball, banana, and bird under the letter B.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct alphabetical order for: dog, cat, banana, apple?\",\"options\":[\"apple, banana, cat, dog\",\"dog, cat, banana, apple\",\"cat, dog, apple, banana\",\"banana, apple, dog, cat\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The example in the text shows the alphabetical order as apple, banana, cat, dog.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are looking for the word \'lizard\', which letter section should you check?\",\"options\":[\"L\",\"K\",\"M\",\"J\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'lizard\' is listed under the letter L in the dictionary.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Arrange these words from the text in alphabetical order: camel, banana, ant.\",\"options\":[\"ant, banana, camel\",\"camel, banana, ant\",\"banana, ant, camel\",\"ant, camel, banana\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Following alphabetical order (A, B, C), the order is ant, banana, camel.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is listed first in the \'F\' section of the dictionary?\",\"options\":[\"fan\",\"fish\",\"flower\",\"fruit\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists the \'F\' words in the order: fan, fish, flower.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which letter section contains the words \'kettle\', \'king\', and \'kite\'?\",\"options\":[\"K\",\"J\",\"L\",\"I\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"These words are grouped under the letter K in the dictionary list.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT listed in the \'D\' section of \'My Picture Dictionary\'?\",\"options\":[\"dog\",\"doll\",\"deer\",\"duck\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"While \'dog\' is in the alphabetical order example, the \'D\' section of the dictionary only lists doll, deer, and duck.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'apple\' placed before \'banana\' in the dictionary?\",\"options\":[\"Because A comes before B in the alphabet\",\"Because A comes after B in the alphabet\",\"Because apple is a fruit\",\"Because banana is yellow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Alphabetical order is determined by the sequence of letters in the alphabet.\",\"topic\":\"My Picture Dictionary (A-M)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words starts with the letter \'N\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"nest\",\"oil\",\"pot\",\"rat\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'nest\' as a word starting with the letter \'N\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word starts with the letter \'Z\'?\",\"options\":[\"yak\",\"zebra\",\"van\",\"sun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'zebra\' under the letter \'Z\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the word that starts with the letter \'Q\' from the list.\",\"options\":[\"queen\",\"rabbit\",\"star\",\"tree\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'queen\' as an example for the letter \'Q\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The words \'table\', \'tree\', and \'tiger\' all start with which letter?\",\"options\":[\"S\",\"T\",\"U\",\"V\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the text, table, tree, and tiger are grouped under the letter \'T\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word belongs to the letter \'X\' group in the Alphabet Train?\",\"options\":[\"x-ray\",\"yellow\",\"watch\",\"vase\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'x-ray\' as a word for the letter \'X\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a word starting with the letter \'U\'?\",\"options\":[\"umbrella\",\"violin\",\"wheel\",\"yacht\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'umbrella\' as a word starting with the letter \'U\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to find the word \'van\', which letter section should you look in?\",\"options\":[\"U\",\"V\",\"W\",\"X\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'van\' is listed under the letter \'V\' in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word starts with the same letter as \'rabbit\'?\",\"options\":[\"red\",\"sun\",\"table\",\"van\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Both \'rabbit\' and \'red\' are listed under the letter \'R\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of words all start with the letter \'O\'?\",\"options\":[\"oil, onion, ostrich\",\"nest, nine, newspaper\",\"papaya, pencil, pot\",\"sun, shirt, star\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text groups oil, onion, and ostrich under the letter \'O\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the list for the letter \'Y\', which word describes a color?\",\"options\":[\"yak\",\"yellow\",\"yacht\",\"zip\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Yellow is a color and is listed under the letter \'Y\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21298,5,2,'English','en','Open the Treasure (Unit 4)','[\"Open the Treasure is a game where you use a Word‑Bank to make a chain of words.\",\"You start with any word, e.g. tree.\",\"The next word must begin with the last letter of the previous word.\",\"You keep adding words to make a long chain.\",\"You can choose words from food, fruits, vegetables, animals, school, etc.\",\"You can also find words that have four syllables.\",\"During the game you talk about the words with your friends.\",\"You can ask questions about the words, e.g. about tomatoes.\",\"You can ask what colour a fruit is, how much it costs, where to buy it, and if it is a vegetable.\",\"The teacher helps students play the game and ask questions.\",\"The game helps students learn new words and practice speaking.\",\"It also helps them remember the order of letters in words.\",\"You can use the Word‑Bank to find words that start with the last letter of the previous word.\",\"You can make the chain as long as you want.\",\"The game is fun and helps build vocabulary.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the first step in the \'Word-Bank\' activity?\",\"options\":[\"Close the book\",\"Open the Word-Bank\",\"Draw a picture\",\"Go home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the first step is to open the \'Word-Bank\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Chain\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a word chain, which letter of the previous word is used to start the next word?\",\"options\":[\"The first letter\",\"The middle letter\",\"The last letter\",\"The second letter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to find a new word that starts with the last letter of the previous word.\",\"topic\":\"Word Chain\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the example chain, what word comes after \'tree\'?\",\"options\":[\"goat\",\"apple\",\"egg\",\"tomato\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The example chain provided in the text is tree -> egg.\",\"topic\":\"Word Chain\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a question asked about tomatoes in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Do you like tomatoes?\",\"Are tomatoes blue?\",\"Can you jump on a tomato?\",\"Is a tomato a fruit?\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Do you like tomatoes?\' as one of the questions.\",\"topic\":\"Word Chain\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the word is \'egg\', what is the last letter used to start the next word?\",\"options\":[\"e\",\"g\",\"a\",\"t\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The last letter of \'egg\' is \'g\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Chain\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the last letter of the word \'goat\' in the example chain?\",\"options\":[\"g\",\"o\",\"a\",\"t\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The word \'goat\' ends with the letter \'t\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Chain\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are continuing the chain \'tree -> egg -> goat\', what letter must the next word start with?\",\"options\":[\"e\",\"g\",\"t\",\"r\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since \'goat\' is the last word and ends in \'t\', the next word must start with \'t\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Chain\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word can correctly follow \'goat\' in a word chain?\",\"options\":[\"apple\",\"tiger\",\"ball\",\"sun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tiger starts with \'t\', which is the last letter of \'goat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Chain\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The text asks: \'What is the _____ of tomato?\'\",\"options\":[\"size\",\"shape\",\"colour\",\"name\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The specific question in the text is \'What is the colour of tomato?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Chain\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Look at this chain: tree -> egg -> goat. Which word would correctly fit next?\",\"options\":[\"table\",\"elephant\",\"orange\",\"dog\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Table starts with \'t\', matching the last letter of \'goat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Chain\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where should children find words related to food items and animals?\",\"options\":[\"From a storybook\",\"From the \'Word-Bank\'\",\"From the playground\",\"From the kitchen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks students to find words related to various categories from the \'Word-Bank\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do after finding words from the Word-Bank?\",\"options\":[\"Keep them a secret\",\"Talk about those words with your friends\",\"Draw a picture of the Word-Bank\",\"Forget the words\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to talk about those words with your friends.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many syllabic words are children asked to find and write down?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Activity \'d\' specifically asks to find and write down four syllabic words.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is responsible for assisting children to execute the activities properly?\",\"options\":[\"The Teacher\",\"The Monitor\",\"The Principal\",\"The Parents\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The \'For the Teacher\' section states the teacher should assist the children.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you find the word \'Tiger\' in the Word-Bank, which category does it belong to?\",\"options\":[\"Food items\",\"School\",\"Animals\",\"Vegetables\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tiger is an animal, which is one of the categories mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you find the word \'Chalk\' in the Word-Bank, which category is most suitable?\",\"options\":[\"Fruits\",\"School\",\"Vegetables\",\"Animals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Chalk is a word related to the \'school\' category mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher help children to raise?\",\"options\":[\"Their hands in class\",\"Questions on different topics\",\"Their desks and chairs\",\"Plants in the garden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s role is to help children raise questions on different topics or situations.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a category mentioned to find words for?\",\"options\":[\"Fruits\",\"Vegetables\",\"Space\",\"School\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists food items, fruits, vegetables, animals, and school, but not space.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal of the \'For the Teacher\' instructions?\",\"options\":[\"To tell the teacher to go home\",\"To guide the teacher on how to help students with activities\",\"To ask the teacher to write in the Word-Bank\",\"To make the teacher talk to their own friends\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions provide guidance for the teacher to assist and help students.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the teacher need to assist the children according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To help them finish their lunch\",\"To execute the activities properly\",\"To help them run fast\",\"To make them draw pictures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the teacher should assist children to execute these activities properly.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the national 24-hour toll-free emergency number for children in distress?\",\"options\":[\"100\",\"101\",\"1098\",\"108\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Childline 1098 is a national 24-hour toll-free emergency phone service for children.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you feel uneasy about someone touching you, you should tell someone you ____.\",\"options\":[\"fear\",\"trust\",\"do not know\",\"met just now\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text advises children to \'Tell someone whom you trust\' if they feel uneasy about a touch.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which Ministry supports the CHILDLINE India Foundation?\",\"options\":[\"Ministry of Education\",\"Ministry of Health\",\"Ministry of Women & Child Development\",\"Ministry of Sports\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Childline is supported by the Ministry of Women & Child Development.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How might a child feel when they receive an unsafe touch?\",\"options\":[\"Happy and excited\",\"Strong and brave\",\"Confused and helpless\",\"Sleepy and tired\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that when you get an unsafe touch, you may feel bad, confused, and helpless.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why should a child not feel \'bad\' after an unsafe touch?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is a secret\",\"Because it is not the child\'s fault\",\"Because it happens to everyone\",\"Because it is a game\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says you need not feel \'bad\' because it\'s not your fault.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should you NOT do if someone touches you inappropriately?\",\"options\":[\"Tell a trusted person\",\"Keep quiet\",\"Call 1098\",\"Inform NCPCR\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states: \'you should not keep quiet.\'\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you know another child who is in distress, what should you do?\",\"options\":[\"Keep it a secret\",\"Call 1098\",\"Do nothing\",\"Blame the child\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to call 1098 if you know some other child who is troubled or in distress.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first thing you should do regarding yourself if you face an inappropriate touch?\",\"options\":[\"Blame yourself\",\"Not blame yourself\",\"Hide in a room\",\"Forget about it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first point listed in the text is \'Not blame yourself.\'\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The 1098 service is available for children below which age?\",\"options\":[\"10 years\",\"12 years\",\"15 years\",\"18 years\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the service is for those \'below 18 years of age.\'\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the POCSO e-box used for?\",\"options\":[\"Playing games\",\"Online classes\",\"Informing NCPCR about unsafe touch\",\"Watching cartoons\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says you can inform the National Commission for Protection of Child Rights through the POCSO e-box.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the name of the button that the children are pointing to?\",\"options\":[\"Start Button\",\"POCSO e-box\",\"Help Menu\",\"Game Box\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows a large red button labeled \'e-box\' with \'POCSO\' written above it.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/091_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what message is given to children who feel bad after an unsafe touch?\",\"options\":[\"It is your fault\",\"You should feel bad\",\"It is not your fault\",\"You should keep quiet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text in the figure clearly states: \'You need not feel \\\"bad\\\" because it’s not your fault.\'\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"5\\/091_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the name of the national animal mentioned in the word bank?\",\"options\":[\"Lion\",\"Tiger\",\"Elephant\",\"Leopard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Tiger is the national animal of India, which is a common item in primary word banks.\",\"topic\":\"Word-Bank Items\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'nest\'?\",\"options\":[\"Next\",\"Best\",\"Near\",\"Nose\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Best\' rhymes with \'nest\' as they share the same ending sound.\",\"topic\":\"Word-Bank Items\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words starts with the letter \'e\'?\",\"options\":[\"Apple\",\"Ball\",\"Egg\",\"Cat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'Egg\' starts with the letter \'e\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word-Bank Items\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word contains the \'oo\' sound like in the word \'Moon\'?\",\"options\":[\"Boat\",\"Book\",\"Bark\",\"Beak\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Book\' contains the \'oo\' sound mentioned in the word bank.\",\"topic\":\"Word-Bank Items\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a 5-letter word?\",\"options\":[\"Table\",\"Pen\",\"It\",\"School\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'Table\' has exactly 5 letters (T-a-b-l-e).\",\"topic\":\"Word-Bank Items\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is one of the five musical instruments?\",\"options\":[\"Pencil\",\"Flute\",\"Bottle\",\"Eraser\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A flute is a musical instrument.\",\"topic\":\"Word-Bank Items\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word starts with the \'cl\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"Cry\",\"Clap\",\"Car\",\"Cup\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Clap\' starts with the \'cl\' consonant blend.\",\"topic\":\"Word-Bank Items\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a day of the week?\",\"options\":[\"January\",\"Monday\",\"Morning\",\"Spring\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Monday is one of the seven days of the week.\",\"topic\":\"Word-Bank Items\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word ends with the \'t\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"Bat\",\"Bag\",\"Bad\",\"Ban\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'Bat\' ends with the letter \'t\' and its sound.\",\"topic\":\"Word-Bank Items\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a 2-letter word?\",\"options\":[\"The\",\"In\",\"And\",\"Dog\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'In\' consists of only 2 letters.\",\"topic\":\"Word-Bank Items\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21299,6,2,'Marathi','mr','अजाण आम्ही तुझी लेकरे (प्रार्थना)','[\"अजाण आम्ही तुझी लेकरे ही प्रार्थना आपल्याला देवाच्या गुणांची आठवण करून देते.\",\"प्रार्थनेत देवाला पिता, सर्वांचा पिता म्हणून ओळखले जाते.\",\"देवाला सूर्य, चंद्र, पाणी, डोंगर, फळे, फुले, पक्षी अशा सर्व गोष्टींचे स्वामी मानले जाते.\",\"देवाची सर्व दिशांना उपस्थिती आहे, तो सर्वत्र वसतो.\",\"प्रार्थनेत देवाची माया सर्वांवर पसरलेली आहे असे सांगितले आहे.\",\"देवाला प्रेम, काम, शिकणे, हौस या सर्व गोष्टींची मागणी आहे.\",\"शिक्षकांनी विद्यार्थ्यांना प्रार्थना तालासुरात घेण्यास सांगितले आहे.\",\"प्रार्थनेतील नवीन शब्दांचे अर्थ समजावून सांगणे महत्त्वाचे आहे.\",\"चित्रांमध्ये खेळ, मुलांची नावे, रंग इत्यादी निरीक्षण करणे शिकवले आहे.\",\"चित्रातील मुलांच्या पोशाखाचे रंग ओळखून नावे लिहिणे हे एक सराव आहे.\",\"वाक्यांमध्ये योग्य पर्याय निवडून उत्तर देणे हे व्याकरणाचे सराव आहे.\",\"चित्रातील झाडावर बसलेल्या रेवाबद्दल विचार करणे निरीक्षण कौशल्य वाढवते.\",\"“भोवरा” या खेळासाठी आवश्यक साहित्य विचारणे खेळांच्या ज्ञानाला चालना देते.\",\"शिक्षकांनी विद्यार्थ्यांना विविध खेळांची नावे सांगून त्यांच्या आवडीबद्दल चर्चा करायला सांगितले आहे.\",\"प्रार्थनेत देवाला सर्व गोष्टींचा स्वामी मानून आभार मानणे हे मुख्य उद्दिष्ट आहे.\"]','[{\"q\":\"कवितेत सर्वांचा \'पिता\' कोणाला म्हटले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"सूर्याला\",\"देवाला\",\"डोंगराला\",\"सागराला\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेच्या पहिल्या कडव्यात देवाला सर्वांचा पिता म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"मुले देवाला काय गाऊन दाखवत आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"गाणी\",\"गोष्टी\",\"गुणांच्या कथा\",\"कविता\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मुले देवाच्या गुणांच्या कथा गात आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेनुसार देवाची माया सगळ्यांवर कशी असते?\",\"options\":[\"कमी\",\"जास्त\",\"सारखीच\",\"वेगवेगळी\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"देव सगळ्यांवर सारखीच माया करतो असे कवितेत म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"देवाची घरे किती दिशांना आहेत असे कवितेत सांगितले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"चार\",\"दहा\",\"दोन\",\"आठ\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेत \'दहा दिशांना घर\' असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"मुलांनी मनात काय धरावे असे कवितेत म्हटले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"राग\",\"लोभ\",\"प्रेम\",\"भिती\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मुलांनी मनात प्रेम धरावे अशी मागणी केली आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात मुले देवाला नमन करण्यासाठी काय करत आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"हात जोडत आहेत\",\"धावत आहेत\",\"खेळत आहेत\",\"झोपले आहेत\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"चित्रात मुले हात जोडून प्रार्थना (नमन) करत आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"6\\/011_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात शेतात कोण काम करताना दिसत आहे?\",\"options\":[\"मुलगा\",\"मुलगी\",\"शेतकरी आणि बैल\",\"पक्षी\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"चित्रात एक शेतकरी बैलांच्या मदतीने शेतात काम करताना दिसत आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"6\\/011_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत \'अजाण\' हा शब्द कोणासाठी वापरला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"देवांसाठी\",\"लेकरांसाठी (मुलांसाठी)\",\"प्राण्यांसाठी\",\"फुलांसाठी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मुले स्वतःला \'अजाण लेकरे\' म्हणत आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"मुलांनी देवाला कोणती मुख्य मागणी घातली आहे?\",\"options\":[\"खूप खेळावे\",\"खूप शिकावे व काम करावे\",\"खूप फिरावे\",\"खूप खावे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"खूप शिकावे आणि काम करावे ही मुलांची मागणी आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"खालीलपैकी कोणती गोष्ट देवाची आहे असे कवितेत आले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त सूर्य\",\"फक्त चंद्र\",\"सूर्य, चंद्र, डोंगर, सागर सर्व\",\"काहीच नाही\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"निसर्गातील सर्व गोष्टी देवाच्या आहेत असे कवितेत सांगितले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"\'अजाण आम्ही तुझी लेकरे\' या कवितेच्या कवयित्री कोण आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"संजीवनी मराठे\",\"बहिणाबाई चौधरी\",\"शांता शेळके\",\"पद्मा गोळे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मजकुराच्या सुरुवातीला कवयित्रीचे नाव \'संजीवनी मराठे\' असे दिले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"विद्यार्थ्यांनी प्रार्थना कशी म्हणावी असे मजकुरात सांगितले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"खूप मोठ्या आवाजात\",\"तालासुरात\",\"हळू आवाजात\",\"रडत रडत\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात प्रार्थना \'तालासुरात\' म्हणून घ्यावी असे स्पष्ट म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"शाळेत कोणत्या वेळी विविध प्रार्थना ऐकवाव्यात?\",\"options\":[\"खेळाच्या तासाला\",\"जेवणाच्या सुट्टीत\",\"परिपाठाच्या वेळी\",\"शाळा सुटल्यावर\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात \'शाळेत परिपाठाच्या वेळी\' प्रार्थना ऐकवण्यास सांगितले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"शिक्षकांनी विद्यार्थ्यांना कशाचे अर्थ समजावून सांगावेत?\",\"options\":[\"नवीन शब्दांचे\",\"फक्त नावांचे\",\"कवितेच्या ओळींचे\",\"चित्रांचे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात \'विद्यार्थ्यांत प्रार्थनेतील नवीन शब्दांचे अर्थ समजावून सांगावेत\' असे दिले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"प्रार्थना म्हणण्याच्या कोणत्या दोन पद्धती मजकुरात दिल्या आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ बसून व उभे राहून\",\"वैयक्तिक व सामूहिकरीत्या\",\"केवळ मोठ्याने व मनातल्या मनात\",\"केवळ शिक्षकांसोबत\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात \'वैयक्तिक व सामूहिकरीत्या\' प्रार्थना म्हणून घ्यावी असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"विविध प्रार्थना ऐकवण्यासाठी कशाचे साहाय्य घेण्यास सांगितले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"पुस्तकाचे\",\"रेडिओचे\",\"संकलनाचे\",\"दूरदर्शनचे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात \'संकलनाच्या साहाय्याने विविध प्रार्थना ऐकवाव्यात\' असे नमूद केले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"जर शिक्षकांना वर्गात प्रार्थना घ्यायची असेल, तर त्यांनी ती कशी घ्यावी?\",\"options\":[\"विद्यार्थ्यांकडून तालासुरात म्हणून घ्यावी\",\"फक्त स्वतः म्हणून दाखवावी\",\"विद्यार्थ्यांना लिहायला सांगावी\",\"विद्यार्थ्यांना पाठांतर करायला सांगावे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मजकुरातील सूचनेनुसार शिक्षकांनी विद्यार्थ्यांकडून प्रार्थना तालासुरात म्हणून घेणे अपेक्षित आहे.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"\'तालासुरात\' या शब्दाचा योग्य वापर खालीलपैकी कोणत्या क्रियेसाठी केला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"चित्र काढण्यासाठी\",\"प्रार्थना म्हणण्यासाठी\",\"शब्द लिहिण्यासाठी\",\"गप्प बसण्यासाठी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात प्रार्थना \'तालासुरात\' म्हणण्याबाबत सूचना दिली आहे.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"मजकुरातील \'ऐकू या. गाऊ या. म्हणू या.\' या ओळीवरून कोणती कृती अपेक्षित नाही?\",\"options\":[\"प्रार्थना ऐकणे\",\"प्रार्थना गाणे\",\"प्रार्थना म्हणणे\",\"प्रार्थना लिहिणे\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात ऐकणे, गाणे आणि म्हणणे या क्रिया दिल्या आहेत, पण लिहिणे ही क्रिया दिलेली नाही.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी दिलेल्या या सूचनांचा मुख्य उद्देश काय आहे?\",\"options\":[\"विद्यार्थ्यांना खेळायला लावणे\",\"प्रार्थना प्रभावीपणे शिकवणे व ऐकवणे\",\"विद्यार्थ्यांना शिक्षा करणे\",\"फक्त नवीन शब्द पाठ करणे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"या सर्व सूचना प्रार्थना योग्य प्रकारे म्हणण्यासाठी आणि समजून घेण्यासाठी दिल्या आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gem