\":\"गीतात \'अस्मानाच्या सुलतानीला जवाब देती जिभा\' असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"कशा प्रकारची मनगटे जीवघेणी खेळ खेळतात?\",\"options\":[\"सोनेरी\",\"पोलादी\",\"नाजूक\",\"मोठी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"गीतात \'पोलादी मनगटे खेळती, खेळ जीवघेणी\' असे वर्णन आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"महाराष्ट्र कशाने भिजला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"पावसाने\",\"नदीच्या पाण्याने\",\"निढळाच्या घामाने\",\"समुद्राने\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"गीतात \'निढळाच्या घामाने भिजला\' असे कष्टकऱ्यांचे वर्णन केले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"महाराष्ट्र कोणाचे तख्त राखतो?\",\"options\":[\"मुंबईचे\",\"पुण्याचे\",\"दिल्लीचे\",\"नागपूरचे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"गीतात \'दिल्लीचेही तख्त राखितो, महाराष्ट्र माझा\' असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"महाराष्ट्राचा नाद कोठून गुंजला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त शहरातून\",\"दरीदरीतून\",\"आकाशातून\",\"घराघरातून\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"गीतात \'दरीदरीतून नाद गुंजला महाराष्ट्र माझा\' असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"हा देश कशासाठी झिजला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"पैशासाठी\",\"देश गौरवासाठी\",\"स्वतःसाठी\",\"खेळासाठी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"गीतात \'देश गौरवासाठी झिजला\' असे स्पष्ट म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21327,7,2,'Maths','en','Let\'s Understand Geometrical Shapes - Part 1','[\"Geometrical shapes are objects that have a fixed form.\",\"A shape can be flat (like a square) or curved (like a circle).\",\"A cube has 6 flat faces, 12 edges and 8 corners.\",\"A cuboid (rectangular box) also has 6 faces, 12 edges and 8 corners but the faces can be different sizes.\",\"A cylinder has 2 flat circular faces and 1 curved side surface.\",\"A cone has 1 flat circular base and 1 curved side surface.\",\"A sphere has no flat faces – it is completely round.\",\"Surfaces are the flat or curved outer parts of a shape.\",\"Edges are the lines where two surfaces meet.\",\"Corners (vertices) are the points where edges meet.\",\"A shape can have many surfaces, edges and corners – count them to learn geometry.\",\"Curved surfaces are smooth and round, flat surfaces are straight and even.\",\"When you draw a shape, you can label its surfaces, edges and corners to practice counting.\",\"Shapes can be found everywhere – in toys, buildings, food and nature.\",\"Knowing the names and counts of surfaces, edges and corners helps in math and science.\",\"Practice by looking at objects around you and naming their shapes.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does Poonam stick on each surface of the box?\",\"options\":[\"Stars\",\"Beads\",\"Lace\",\"Buttons\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Poonam sticks a star on each surface of the box.\",\"topic\":\"Saving box decorated by Poonam\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What shape is the box that Poonam is decorating?\",\"options\":[\"Sphere\",\"Cone\",\"Cylinder\",\"Cuboid\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states to \'Take a cuboid shaped box\' for the activity.\",\"topic\":\"Saving box decorated by Poonam\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Poonam stick on each corner of the box?\",\"options\":[\"Stars\",\"Lace\",\"Beads\",\"Paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Stick beads on each corner of the box\'.\",\"topic\":\"Saving box decorated by Poonam\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"On which part of the box is the slit made?\",\"options\":[\"Lower face\",\"Upper face\",\"Side face\",\"Corner\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructions say to \'Make a slit on the upper face of the box\'.\",\"topic\":\"Saving box decorated by Poonam\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many edges does a cuboid shaped box have in total?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"8\",\"10\",\"12\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"A cuboid has 12 edges, so Poonam needs 12 pieces of lace.\",\"topic\":\"Saving box decorated by Poonam\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is used to decorate the edges of the box?\",\"options\":[\"Stars\",\"Beads\",\"Lace\",\"Slits\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions sticking pieces of lace on each edge of the box.\",\"topic\":\"Saving box decorated by Poonam\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Poonam sticks one star on each surface, how many stars will she stick in total?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"6\",\"8\",\"12\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A cuboid has 6 surfaces, so sticking one star on each results in 6 stars.\",\"topic\":\"Saving box decorated by Poonam\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Poonam wants to stick a bead on every corner. How many beads does she need in total?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"8\",\"10\",\"12\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A cuboid has 8 corners, so 8 beads are needed.\",\"topic\":\"Saving box decorated by Poonam\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Poonam sticking on the corners of the box?\",\"options\":[\"Stars\",\"Lace\",\"Beads\",\"Slits\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration in the last row shows beads being placed on the corners.\",\"topic\":\"Saving box decorated by Poonam\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/015_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which part of the box is being decorated with pieces of lace?\",\"options\":[\"Surfaces\",\"Edges\",\"Corners\",\"Slit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The middle row of the figure shows lace being applied along the edges of the box.\",\"topic\":\"Saving box decorated by Poonam\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/015_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the shape of the saving box that Ramesh decorated?\",\"options\":[\"Sphere\",\"Cylinder\",\"Cuboid\",\"Cone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states Ramesh took a cuboid shaped box to decorate.\",\"topic\":\"Handling Geometrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Ramesh stick on each surface of the box?\",\"options\":[\"Beads\",\"Stars\",\"Lace\",\"Flowers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Ramesh stuck a star on each surface of the box.\",\"topic\":\"Handling Geometrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Ramesh stick the beads on the box?\",\"options\":[\"On each surface\",\"On each edge\",\"On each corner\",\"Inside the box\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Ramesh stuck beads on each corner of the box.\",\"topic\":\"Handling Geometrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many stars did Ramesh stick on the cuboid box in total?\",\"options\":[\"4 stars\",\"6 stars\",\"8 stars\",\"12 stars\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A cuboid has 6 surfaces, so Ramesh stuck 6 stars.\",\"topic\":\"Handling Geometrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many beads did Ramesh need for all the corners of the cuboid box?\",\"options\":[\"6 beads\",\"12 beads\",\"8 beads\",\"4 beads\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A cuboid has 8 corners, so Ramesh used 8 beads.\",\"topic\":\"Handling Geometrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Ramesh use to decorate the edges of the box?\",\"options\":[\"Pieces of lace\",\"Small stars\",\"Round beads\",\"Color pens\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says Ramesh stuck pieces of lace on each edge of the box.\",\"topic\":\"Handling Geometrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these shapes is mentioned in the text for children to handle?\",\"options\":[\"Triangle\",\"Circle\",\"Cylinder\",\"Square\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists cuboid, cube, cone, cylinder, and sphere as shapes to handle.\",\"topic\":\"Handling Geometrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you handle a sphere, what type of surface will you find based on the concepts mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"Flat surface\",\"Curved surface\",\"Square surface\",\"Cornered surface\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks to clarify the concept of curved and flat surfaces for shapes like the sphere.\",\"topic\":\"Handling Geometrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Ramesh used 12 pieces of lace for the edges, how many edges does a cuboid have?\",\"options\":[\"6 edges\",\"8 edges\",\"10 edges\",\"12 edges\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Since Ramesh stuck lace on each edge and used 12 pieces, a cuboid has 12 edges.\",\"topic\":\"Handling Geometrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which three things are children asked to count when handling the geometrical shapes?\",\"options\":[\"Weight, height, and width\",\"Color, size, and name\",\"Surfaces, edges, and corners\",\"Stars, lace, and beads\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks children to count the number of surfaces, edges, and corners.\",\"topic\":\"Handling Geometrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21328,7,2,'Maths','en','Number and Number Names','[\"Number names are the word forms of numbers.\",\"We write numbers in words to avoid confusion in transactions.\",\"From 1 to 20, each number has a unique name.\",\"Numbers from 21 to 99 are formed by combining tens and ones (e.g., twenty-one).\",\"The word \'hundred\' is used for 100.\",\"Spelling of number names must be correct (e.g., Thirteen, not \'Thirteen\' with extra letters).\",\"When writing amounts in banks, both figures and words are used.\",\"The number name for 13 is \'Thirteen\'.\",\"The number name for 20 is \'Twenty\'.\",\"The number name for 100 is \'One hundred\'.\",\"Number names help in reading and writing amounts correctly.\",\"We do not use hyphens in number names for 21-99 in Indian English (e.g., twenty one).\",\"Zero is written as \'Zero\'.\",\"Number names are used in cheques, deposit slips, and official documents.\",\"Always double-check spelling when writing number names.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How much money (in figures) does Jayesh want to deposit into the bank?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 10\",\"₹ 13\",\"₹ 24\",\"₹ 18\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Jayesh wants to deposit ₹ 13.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the account holder mentioned on the deposit slip?\",\"options\":[\"Tanvi\",\"Jayesh\",\"School\",\"Cashier\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The deposit slip lists Jayesh as the name of the account holder.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the deposit slip, how is the number 13 written in words?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Thirty\",\"Thirteen\",\"Ten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The amount in words is written as \'Rupees Thirteen only\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the account number (A\\/c.No.) written on Jayesh\'s deposit slip?\",\"options\":[\"13\",\"1812\",\"0024\",\"2025\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows the account number as A\\/c.No. 0024.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the amount in words is \'Rupees Thirteen only\', how should it be written in the \'Amount (in figures)\' box?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 31\\/-\",\"₹ 13\\/-\",\"₹ 3\\/-\",\"₹ 10\\/-\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure representation of thirteen is 13.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"On what date did Jayesh fill the deposit slip for the bank?\",\"options\":[\"18\\/12\\/2025\",\"12\\/18\\/2025\",\"01\\/01\\/2025\",\"13\\/12\\/2025\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The date mentioned on the deposit slip is 18\\/12\\/2025.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the person that signed the slip as the \'Depositor\'?\",\"options\":[\"Tanvi\",\"The Teacher\",\"Jayesh\",\"The Principa