it is in the units place.\",\"- The tens place can be empty (zero) if the number is less than 10.\",\"- Practice by drawing beads or dots to represent numbers and identify tens and units.\",\"- Use the table of beads to learn how many strings of tens and loose beads are needed for a given number.\",\"- Remember: 10 = 1 ten, 20 = 2 tens, 30 = 3 tens, etc.\",\"- The face value of 7 is 7, but its place value in 73 is 70.\",\"- The face value of 3 is 3, but its place value in 73 is 3.\",\"- When adding groups of ten, count each group as one ten.\",\"- For numbers like 82, 8 is in the tens place (80) and 2 is in the units place (2).\",\"- The total number of beads is the sum of beads in ten‑groups and loose beads.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many beads are there in one string to make it one ten?\",\"options\":[\"5 beads\",\"10 beads\",\"1 bead\",\"20 beads\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, there are 10 beads in the string to make one ten.\",\"topic\":\"Write the appropriate number\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a string of 10 beads called?\",\"options\":[\"One unit\",\"One ten\",\"Two tens\",\"Ten tens\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a string of 10 beads is one ten.\",\"topic\":\"Write the appropriate number\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If we take less than 10 beads, do we get one ten?\",\"options\":[\"Yes\",\"No\",\"Sometimes\",\"Always\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly asks this and implies the answer is no.\",\"topic\":\"Write the appropriate number\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What do we get if we untie a string of one-ten?\",\"options\":[\"One bead\",\"Ten-unit beads\",\"Two strings\",\"Five units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that untying a string results in ten-unit beads.\",\"topic\":\"Write the appropriate number\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Sanika has one string of ten. How many beads does she have?\",\"options\":[\"1 bead\",\"10 beads\",\"100 beads\",\"0 beads\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"One string of ten is equal to 10 beads.\",\"topic\":\"Write the appropriate number\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Mayuresh has one string of ten and eight-unit beads. How many beads does he have in total?\",\"options\":[\"8 beads\",\"10 beads\",\"18 beads\",\"81 beads\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"One ten (10) plus eight units (8) equals 18 beads.\",\"topic\":\"Write the appropriate number\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Neeta has two strings of tens and nine-unit beads. How many beads does she have?\",\"options\":[\"2 beads\",\"9 beads\",\"19 beads\",\"29 beads\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Two strings of tens (20) plus nine units (9) equals 29 beads.\",\"topic\":\"Write the appropriate number\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happens if we tie ten beads together?\",\"options\":[\"We get one unit\",\"We get a string of one-ten\",\"We get two strings\",\"We get zero beads\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that tying ten beads together results in a string of one-ten.\",\"topic\":\"Write the appropriate number\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If you have 10 unit beads, how many strings of one-ten can you make?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Ten\",\"Zero\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"10 beads make exactly one string of one-ten.\",\"topic\":\"Write the appropriate number\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To have \'one ten\', which of the following is necessary?\",\"options\":[\"Having exactly 5 beads\",\"Having less than 10 beads\",\"Having exactly 10 beads\",\"Having 9 beads\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines one ten as having exactly 10 beads in a string.\",\"topic\":\"Write the appropriate number\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the table, what is another name for loose beads?\",\"options\":[\"Tens\",\"Units\",\"Strings\",\"Numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table header explicitly states \'Loose beads means units\'.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing strings and beads\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many strings of tens are drawn for Manish?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"36\",\"3\",\"10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows 3 strings of tens next to Manish\'s name.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing strings and beads\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/021_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many loose beads (units) are drawn for Manish?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"30\",\"6\",\"1\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows 6 small circles representing loose beads for Manish.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing strings and beads\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/021_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Ria has 43 beads. How many strings of tens should she take?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"4\",\"43\",\"7\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the number 43, the digit in the tens place is 4, so she needs 4 strings of tens.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing strings and beads\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Soham has 54 beads. How many loose beads (units) does he have?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"54\",\"4\",\"9\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the number 54, the digit in the units place is 4, representing 4 loose beads.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing strings and beads\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"John wants 77 beads. How many strings of tens and how many loose beads should he take?\",\"options\":[\"7 strings of tens and 0 loose beads\",\"70 strings of tens and 7 loose beads\",\"7 strings of tens and 7 loose beads\",\"77 strings of tens and 77 loose beads\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The number 77 is made of 7 tens and 7 units.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing strings and beads\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Isha has 82 beads. How many strings of tens does she need to draw?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"8\",\"80\",\"10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The digit 8 in 82 represents 8 tens, which means 8 strings.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing strings and beads\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the table, which friend has the same number for both strings of tens and loose beads?\",\"options\":[\"Manish\",\"Ria\",\"John\",\"Isha\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"John has 77 beads, which means 7 strings of tens and 7 loose beads.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing strings and beads\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a friend takes 5 strings of tens and 4 loose beads, which name from the table matches this amount?\",\"options\":[\"Ria\",\"Soham\",\"John\",\"Manish\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"5 strings of tens and 4 loose beads make the number 54, which belongs to Soham.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing strings and beads\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does a \'string of tens\' represent in this activity?\",\"options\":[\"1 bead\",\"10 beads\",\"100 beads\",\"0 beads\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A string of tens represents a group of 10 beads.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing strings and beads\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is another name for the \'ones\' place mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Tens place\",\"Units place\",\"Digits place\",\"Box place\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the ones place is also called the units place.\",\"topic\":\"Identifying digits in places\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 36, which digit is in the tens place?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"36\",\"3\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that in the number 36, the digit 3 is in the tens place.\",\"topic\":\"Identifying digits in places\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 63, which digit is in the units place?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"3\",\"63\",\"9\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, in the number 63, the digit 3 is in the units place.\",\"topic\":\"Identifying digits in places\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 43, which digit is at the tens pla