er\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Numbers formed by Sachin 3, 6 33 66\'.\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Sachin and Salma, how do they decide which number is greatest or smallest?\",\"options\":[\"By adding the digits\",\"By looking at the colors of the cards\",\"From the digits in the tens and units place\",\"By counting the number of digits\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sachin and Salma state they decide \'From the digits in the tens and units place.\'\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Among the numbers 36, 63, 33, and 66, which one is the smallest?\",\"options\":[\"36\",\"63\",\"33\",\"66\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sachin states that the \'Smallest number is 33\'.\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you use the digits 3 and 6, which number is formed by putting 3 in the tens place and 6 in the units place?\",\"options\":[\"63\",\"33\",\"66\",\"36\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"A number with 3 tens and 6 units is 36.\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the first example of the text, if the smallest number is 13 and the greatest number is 26, which number is smaller?\",\"options\":[\"26\",\"13\",\"31\",\"62\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states \'smallest number is 13\'.\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is 63 considered greater than 36 based on the tens place?\",\"options\":[\"Because 3 tens is more than 6 tens\",\"Because 6 tens is more than 3 tens\",\"Because 3 units is more than 6 units\",\"Because they both have the same tens\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Comparing the tens place, 6 tens (in 63) is greater than 3 tens (in 36).\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many different two-digit numbers were formed in total using the digits 3 and 6 in the teacher\'s example?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The numbers formed were 36, 63, 33, and 66, which are 4 different numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many numbers did John form using the digits 3 and 6?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The diagram shows John formed four numbers: 36, 63, 33, and 66.\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/030_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which digit is shown in the units place for the number 36?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"6\",\"9\",\"0\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows that for the number 36, the digit in the Units column is 6.\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/030_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the greatest number mentioned in the very first example of the text?\",\"options\":[\"13\",\"26\",\"34\",\"66\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'greatest number is 34\' in the first example provided.\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Salma suggest doing to help decide which number is greatest?\",\"options\":[\"Write the numbers in tens and units form\",\"Color the numbers\",\"Add the numbers together\",\"Use 0 to 9 digit cards\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Salma says, \'Let\'s write these numbers in tens and units form.\'\",\"topic\":\"Forming two-digit numbers\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21332,7,2,'Maths','en','Ascending and Descending Order of three Numbers','[\"Ascending order means arranging numbers from smallest to largest.\",\"Descending order means arranging numbers from largest to smallest.\",\"To compare two-digit numbers, first check the tens digit.\",\"If tens digits are equal, compare the units digit.\",\"The number with the greater tens digit is larger.\",\"The number with the smaller tens digit is smaller.\",\"On a 1 to 100 chart, numbers increase left to right and top to bottom.\",\"Moving right increases the number by 1 (units digit changes).\",\"Moving down increases the number by 10 (tens digit changes).\",\"To find ascending order using the chart, locate numbers and see which comes first when reading left to right, top to bottom.\",\"To find descending order, reverse the ascending order.\",\"The middle number is the one that is neither the smallest nor the largest.\",\"Example: For 63, 28, 71 → tens: 6, 2, 7 → smallest tens is 2 → 28 is smallest; greatest tens is 7 → 71 is greatest; remaining 63 is in between.\",\"Example: Ascending order of 13, 35, 27 is 13, 27, 35 (13 < 27 < 35).\",\"Practice by comparing tens first, then units if tens are same.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Among the numbers 13, 34, and 24, which one is the smallest number?\",\"options\":[\"34\",\"24\",\"13\",\"43\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, 13 has the smallest tens and is therefore the smallest number.\",\"topic\":\"Ascending order of three numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which number is the \'Greatest number\' in the group 13, 34, and 24?\",\"options\":[\"13\",\"24\",\"34\",\"31\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 34 has the greatest tens, making it the greatest number.\",\"topic\":\"Ascending order of three numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where is the \'Number in between\' placed on the arrow?\",\"options\":[\"At the bottom\",\"In the middle\",\"At the very top\",\"Outside the arrow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The diagram shows the \'Number in between\' positioned between the smallest and greatest numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Ascending order of three numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/031_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, a number is the smallest if it has the ________ tens.\",\"options\":[\"greatest\",\"middle\",\"smallest\",\"most\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the smallest number as the one with the smallest tens.\",\"topic\":\"Ascending order of three numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct ascending order for the numbers 13, 34, and 24?\",\"options\":[\"34, 24, 13\",\"13, 24, 34\",\"24, 13, 34\",\"13, 34, 24\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Ascending order starts from the smallest (13), then the middle (24), to the greatest (34).\",\"topic\":\"Ascending order of three numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many units does the number 34 have?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"4\",\"1\",\"2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows that the number 34 has 4 units.\",\"topic\":\"Ascending order of three numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/031_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which number is placed at the highest point of the arrow to show ascending order?\",\"options\":[\"13\",\"24\",\"34\",\"43\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows 34 at the top of the arrow as the greatest number.\",\"topic\":\"Ascending order of three numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/031_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If 13 is the smallest and 34 is the greatest, which number is the \'number in between\'?\",\"options\":[\"13\",\"34\",\"24\",\"42\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies 24 as the number in between 13 and 34.\",\"topic\":\"Ascending order of three numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is 34 called the \'Greatest number\' in the comparison of 13, 34, and 24?\",\"options\":[\"It has the smallest tens\",\"It has the greatest tens\",\"It has the smallest units\",\"It has 2 tens\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that the greatest tens (3) makes 34 the greatest number.\",\"topic\":\"Ascending order of three numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How many tens does the number 13 have according to the table?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"1\",\"4\",\"2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows that the number 13 has 1 ten.\",\"topic\":\"Ascending order of three numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the smallest number among 63, 28, and 71?\",\"options\":[\"63\",\"28\",\"71\",\"10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, 28 is the smallest number because it has the fewest tens.\",\"topic\":\"Using chart of 1 to 100\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the 1 to 100 chart, how are the numbers arranged?\",\"options\":[\"In descending order\",\"In ascending order\",\"In random order\",\"From biggest to smallest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that in the 1 to 100 chart, the numbers are in ascending order.\",\"topic\":\"Using chart of 1 to 100\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which number is the greatest among 63, 28, and 71?\",\"options\":[\"28\",\"63\",\"71\",\"36\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies 71 as the greatest number among the three.\",\"topic\":\"Using chart of 1 to 100\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the set of numbers 63, 28, and 71, which number is \'in between\' the others?\",\"options\":[\"71\",\"28\",\"63\",\"100\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 63 is the number in between the greatest (71) and the smallest (28).\",\"topic\":\"Using chart of 1 to 100\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many tens are there in the number 28 according to the table?\",\"options\":[\"8\",\"2\",\"28\",\"10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the text shows that the number 28 has 2 tens.\",\"topic\":\"Using chart of 1 to 100\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct ascending order for the numbers 13, 35, and 27 using the chart?\",\"options\":[\"35, 27, 13\",\"13, 35, 27\",\