r\":2,\"explain\":\"The greatest number is 71, and the table shows it has 7 tens.\",\"topic\":\"Using chart of 1 to 100\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'descending order\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Arranging from smallest to biggest\",\"Arranging from biggest to smallest\",\"Arranging in any random order\",\"Arranging only even numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Descending order means starting with the greatest number and moving to the smallest.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which set of numbers is mentioned in the text for the activity?\",\"options\":[\"1, 2, 3\",\"9, 46, 25\",\"10, 20, 30\",\"100, 50, 0\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks to write the numbers 9, 46, and 25 in order.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which tool does the text suggest using to help arrange the numbers?\",\"options\":[\"A ruler\",\"A clock\",\"A 1 to 100 chart\",\"A weighing scale\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks if you can write the numbers using a 1 to 100 chart.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Among the numbers 9, 46, and 25, which number is the biggest?\",\"options\":[\"9\",\"25\",\"46\",\"100\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"On a 1 to 100 chart, 46 comes after 9 and 25, making it the greatest.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct descending order for the numbers 9, 46, and 25?\",\"options\":[\"9, 25, 46\",\"46, 25, 9\",\"25, 9, 46\",\"46, 9, 25\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In descending order, we write the biggest number (46) first, then 25, then the smallest (9).\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you look at a 1 to 100 chart, which of these three numbers (9, 46, 25) appears first?\",\"options\":[\"46\",\"25\",\"9\",\"1\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The number 9 is the smallest and appears earliest in the 1 to 100 chart.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To write 9, 46, and 25 in descending order, which number must come first?\",\"options\":[\"The smallest number\",\"The middle number\",\"The biggest number\",\"The number 1\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Descending order always starts with the biggest (greatest) number.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which number will be in the middle when 9, 46, and 25 are arranged in descending order?\",\"options\":[\"25\",\"46\",\"9\",\"100\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Arranged as 46, 25, 9, the number 25 is in the middle.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many numbers are given in the text to be arranged?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists three numbers: 9, 46, and 25.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is 46 placed before 25 in descending order?\",\"options\":[\"Because 46 is smaller than 25\",\"Because 46 is greater than 25\",\"Because 46 comes first in the chart\",\"Because 46 has only one digit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In descending order, greater numbers are placed before smaller numbers.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21333,7,2,'Maths','en','Counting in Steps','[\"Counting in steps means adding the same number again and again.\",\"It is like jumping forward on a number line by equal steps.\",\"For example, counting in steps of 2: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10...\",\"We can use number strips to count in steps.\",\"Tens and ones help us add numbers easily.\",\"25 means 2 tens and 5 ones.\",\"When adding, add ones to ones and tens to tens.\",\"If ones make 10 or more, carry over to tens.\",\"Vertical arrangement helps in adding two-digit numbers neatly.\",\"Horizontal arrangement writes numbers side by side with plus sign.\",\"Addition gives the total when we combine two or more numbers.\",\"Word problems describe real-life situations needing addition.\",\"We read the problem, find numbers, add them, and write the answer.\",\"Always check if the answer makes sense.\",\"Practice with beads, blocks, or strips makes addition clear.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is another name for \'counting in steps\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Fast counting\",\"Skip counting\",\"Big counting\",\"Number counting\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that counting in steps can also be called skip counting.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What can \'steps of 10\' be called as per the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Jump of tens\",\"Jump of ones\",\"Step of five\",\"Skip by ones\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text clarifies that steps of 10 can be called jump of tens or skip by tens.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When we take steps of 10, which digit in the number changes?\",\"options\":[\"Units digit\",\"Hundreds digit\",\"Tens digit\",\"No digit changes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text advises drawing attention to how the tens digit changes during steps of 10.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who noted the numbers on which Paresh and Rani landed?\",\"options\":[\"Paresh\",\"Rani\",\"Ritika\",\"The teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Ritika noted the steps on which Paresh and Rani landed.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, from which number did Paresh start jumping?\",\"options\":[\"0\",\"1\",\"2\",\"3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The number strip shows the first jump starting from the number 1.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/034_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, from which number did Rani start jumping?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The number strip shows the first jump starting from the number 2.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/034_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you are counting in steps of 2 and you are at number 5, what is the next number you will land on?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"7\",\"8\",\"9\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Adding a step of 2 to the number 5 results in 7.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of \'skip by tens\'?\",\"options\":[\"Taking steps of 2\",\"Taking steps of 5\",\"Taking steps of 10\",\"Taking steps of 1\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text clarifies that skip by tens is the same as steps of 10.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if you start from number 2 and take a jump of 3, which number will you land on?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"4\",\"5\",\"6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Starting at 2 and jumping 3 steps forward (3, 4, 5) lands you on 5.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/035_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you start at number 10 and take a \'jump of tens\', which number will you reach next?\",\"options\":[\"11\",\"15\",\"20\",\"30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A jump of tens from 10 means adding 10, which equals 20.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Look at this sequence: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10. What is the size of the steps being used?\",\"options\":[\"Steps of 1\",\"Steps of 2\",\"Steps of 3\",\"Steps of 10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The difference between each consecutive number in the sequence is 2.\",\"topic\":\"Counting in Steps\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If Rani jumps in steps of 2 starting from number 2, which of these numbers will she land on?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"5\",\"6\",\"7\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Starting from 2, the steps of 2