 subtraction are opposite operations.\",\"You can check subtraction by adding the answer to the subtracted number.\",\"You can check addition by subtracting one number from the sum.\",\"If 5 + 3 = 8, then 8 - 3 = 5 and 8 - 5 = 3.\",\"The numbers used in addition are called addends.\",\"The result of addition is called the sum.\",\"The result of subtraction is called the difference.\",\"Adding zero to a number gives the same number.\",\"Subtracting zero from a number gives the same number.\",\"Subtracting a number from itself gives zero.\",\"Addition can be done in any order (commutative property).\",\"Subtraction is not commutative; changing order changes the result.\",\"Use pictures or objects to understand addition and subtraction better.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many note-books did father bring for Mahesh?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"14\",\"26\",\"10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states father brought 14 note-books for Mahesh.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction from the sum\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many note-books did father bring for Neeta?\",\"options\":[\"14\",\"26\",\"12\",\"2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states father brought 12 note-books for Neeta.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction from the sum\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who asked their father to bring note-books?\",\"options\":[\"Only Mahesh\",\"Only Neeta\",\"Mahesh and Neeta\",\"The teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text begins by saying Mahesh and Neeta asked their father to bring note-books.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction from the sum\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the total number of note-books father brought?\",\"options\":[\"14\",\"12\",\"26\",\"2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"14 + 12 = 26, which is the total number of note-books.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction from the sum\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which addition sentence shows the total number of note-books?\",\"options\":[\"14 + 12 = 26\",\"26 - 14 = 12\",\"26 - 12 = 