.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If 14 + 12 = 26, then what is 26 - 14?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"12\",\"14\",\"26\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, if 14 + 12 = 26, then 26 - 14 = 12.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"From the sum, if we subtract one of the two numbers, what do we get?\",\"options\":[\"The same number\",\"A bigger number\",\"The other number\",\"Zero\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that subtracting one of the two numbers from the sum gives the other number.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the example 14 + 12 = 26, which number is the \'sum\'?\",\"options\":[\"14\",\"12\",\"26\",\"2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sum is the result of adding the two numbers, which is 26.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If 14 + 12 = 26, then 26 - 12 = ?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"14\",\"26\",\"38\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the correlation shown in the text, 26 - 12 = 14.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If 10 + 5 = 15, which subtraction fact can be found using the correlation rule?\",\"options\":[\"15 - 5 = 10\",\"10 - 5 = 5\",\"15 + 5 = 20\",\"10 + 15 = 25\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Subtracting one of the numbers (5) from the sum (15) gives the other number (10).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the sum of two numbers is 20 and one number is 8, how do we find the other number?\",\"options\":[\"By adding 20 and 8\",\"By subtracting 8 from 20\",\"By adding 8 and 8\",\"By subtracting 20 from 20\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says from the sum, if we subtract one number, we get the other.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many subtraction facts are shown in the text for the addition 14 + 12 = 26?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides two facts: 26 - 14 = 12 and 26 - 12 = 14.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which addition fact is related to the subtraction 26 - 14 = 12?\",\"options\":[\"26 + 14 = 40\",\"12 + 12 = 24\",\"14 + 12 = 26\",\"26 + 12 = 38\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links 26 - 14 = 12 directly to the addition fact 14 + 12 = 26.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence: \'By adding two numbers, we can find their ____.\'\",\"options\":[\"Difference\",\"Total\",\"Sum\",\"Answer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically uses the word \'sum\' for the result of addition.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21337,7,2,'Maths','en','Multiplication','[\"Multiplication is repeated addition.\",\"To multiply 2 × 3, add 2 three times: 2+2+2 = 6.\",\"The multiplication table for 2 shows 2×1=2, 2×2=4, … up to 2×10=20.\",\"Similarly, the table for 3 starts with 3×1=3 and ends with 3×10=30.\",\"The table for 4 starts with 4×1=4 and ends with 4×10=40.\",\"The table for 5 starts with 5×1=5 and ends with 5×10=50.\",\"Each row of a table is called a “multiplication row.”\",\"The first number in a row is called the “multiplicand.”\",\"The second number is called the “multiplier.”\",\"The product is the result of multiplication.\",\"Multiplication tables help us solve many problems quickly.\",\"If you know the table of 2, you can find 2×7 by counting 7 twos.\",\"The same idea works for any number from 1 to 10.\",\"Multiplication is commutative: a×b = b×a.\",\"You can use a table to check if a number is a multiple of another.\",\"Multiplication tables are a foundation for division and fractions.\",\"Practice tables up to 5 first, then 6, 7, 8, and 10.\",\"Use flashcards, songs, or games to remember the tables.\",\"When you can multiply quickly, you can solve bigger problems faster.\",\"Multiplication is a building block for all higher math.\",\"Keep practicing and you will become confident with tables.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many chalks are there in all?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"6\",\"5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'There are 6 chalks in all.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In what groups were the chalks counted in the example?\",\"options\":[\"Groups of three\'s\",\"Groups of two\'s\",\"Groups of four\'s\",\"Groups of five\'s\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I counted them in groups of two\'s.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What word does the text use to mean \'three times\'?\",\"options\":[\"Twice\",\"Thrice\",\"Double\",\"Triple\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'number 2 is taken three times(thrice)\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'2 multiplied by 3\' mean according to the chalk example?\",\"options\":[\"Number 2 is taken three times and added\",\"Number 3 is taken two times and subtracted\",\"Number 2 is added to number 3\",\"Number 6 is divided by 2\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that 2 multiplied by 3 means number 2 is taken three times and added.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To find the \'Total flowers\', we multiply \'Flowers in one flowerpot\' by what?\",\"options\":[\"Number of garlands\",\"Number of leaves\",\"Number of flowerpots\",\"Number of chalks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The formula provided is \'Total flowers = × Flowers in one flowerpot Number of flowerpots\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are the chalks, flowers, and leaves being used for in the text?\",\"options\":[\"For decoration\",\"For a meal\",\"For a game\",\"For cleaning\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text begins with \'Material for decoration.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If there are three pairs of 2 chalks, how is this written as an addition sentence?\",\"options\":[\"2 + 3\",\"2 + 2\",\"2 + 2 + 2\",\"3 + 3 + 3\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows the addition as 2 + 2 + 2 for three pairs of 2.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which formula correctly shows how to find the total number of leaves?\",\"options\":[\"Leaves in one garland + Number of garlands\",\"Leaves in one garland × Number of garlands\",\"Leaves in one garland - Number of garlands\",\"Total flowers × Total leaves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines Total leaves as \'× Leaves in one garland Number of garlands\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the number 2 is taken three times and added, what is the result?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"5\",\"6\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states 2 + 2 + 2 = 6.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How is the addition \'2 + 2 + 2\' written using the multiplication symbol?\",\"options\":[\"2 + 3\",\"2 × 3\",\"3 × 3\",\"2 × 2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows the equality 2 + 2 + 2 = 2 × 3.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the multiplication \'2 × 3\', what does the number 3 represent in the context of the chalks?\",\"options\":[\"The total number of chalks\",\"The number of chalks in each pair\",\"The number of times the group of 2 is taken\",\"The number of flowerpots\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that number 2 is taken three times, represented by the 3 in the multiplication.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s count flowers and leaves\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{