rty\', what is its Multiplication Form?\",\"options\":[\"5 × 5\",\"6 × 6\",\"5 × 6\",\"5 × 30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows that \'Five sixes are thirty\' corresponds to the Multiplication Form 5 × 6.\",\"topic\":\"Table of 5\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which Multiplication Form represents the addition \'5 + 5 + 5\'?\",\"options\":[\"5 × 2\",\"5 × 3\",\"5 × 5\",\"3 × 3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Adding 5 three times (5 + 5 + 5) is written as 5 × 3 in Multiplication Form.\",\"topic\":\"Table of 5\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the Table of 5, what number comes after 5, 10, 15, 20?\",\"options\":[\"21\",\"25\",\"30\",\"35\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sequence in the Table of 5 column shows 5, 10, 15, 20, followed by 25.\",\"topic\":\"Table of 5\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If one hand has 5 fingers, how many fingers do 5 hands have altogether according to the table?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"20\",\"25\",\"30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Using the table, 5 fives (5 × 5) equals 25.\",\"topic\":\"Table of 5\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A box contains 5 pencils. How many pencils are there in 8 such boxes?\",\"options\":[\"35\",\"40\",\"45\",\"50\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the table, 5 eights (5 × 8) is 40.\",\"topic\":\"Table of 5\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, look at the second row. What number should be filled in the empty box under the \'Table of 5\' column?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"10\",\"15\",\"20\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The second row shows 5 + 5 and 5 × 2; the result in the Table of 5 is 10.\",\"topic\":\"Table of 5\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/055_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, look at the row for \'Five eights are forty\'. What number is missing in the pink box under the \'Multiplication Form\' column?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"8\",\"9\",\"10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"For \'Five eights are forty\', the multiplication form is 5 × 8, so the missing number is 8.\",\"topic\":\"Table of 5\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/055_101.jpg\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21338,7,2,'Maths','en','Measurements','[\"Length can be measured using non-standard units like hand-span or pencil.\",\"Different people may get different measurements when using hand-span because hand-spans vary in size.\",\"When the same unit (like a pencil) is used by different people, the measurement remains the same.\",\"Capacity refers to how much a container can hold.\",\"A bucket that holds more water has greater capacity; one that holds less has smaller capacity.\",\"We can compare capacities by counting how many glasses of water each container holds.\",\"Ascending order means arranging from smallest to largest capacity.\",\"Descending order means arranging from largest to smallest capacity.\",\"Heavy and light can be compared using a weighing scale.\",\"The side with the heavier object goes down on a weighing scale.\",\"Fruits like watermelon are heavier than fruits like guava or ber.\",\"Shapes like square, rectangle, triangle, and circle are used in drawings.\",\"Lines can be vertical, horizontal, slanting, or curved.\",\"Rangoli patterns are made using dots and coloured powders.\",\"We can create our own weighing scales using materials like paper cups, string, and straws.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which festival are Avani and Anshuman celebrating in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Diwali\",\"Dussehra\",\"Holi\",\"Christmas\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Today is Dussehra\'.\",\"topic\":\"Toran (Garland)\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a \'toran\' as described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A wooden door\",\"A hand-span\",\"A flower garland\",\"A measuring tape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a toran as a \'flower garland\'.\",\"topic\":\"Toran (Garland)\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Anshuman using to measure the length of the door?\",\"options\":[\"A ruler\",\"A string\",\"His hand-span\",\"A pencil\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Anshuman using the width of his hand to measure, which the text calls a \'hand-span\'.\",\"topic\":\"Toran (Garland)\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/057_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to Anshuman\'s measurement, how long is the door?\",\"options\":[\"5 hand-spans\",\"6 hand-spans\",\"7 hand-spans\",\"8 hand-spans\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Anshuman says, \'The door is 7 hand-spans long.\'\",\"topic\":\"Toran (Garland)\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many hand-spans long is the toran that Anshuman is measuring?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"6\",\"7\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the figure, the speech bubble shows Anshuman counting \'1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6.\'\",\"topic\":\"Toran (Garland)\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/058_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Where do Avani and Anshuman want to hang the toran?\",\"options\":[\"On the wall\",\"Over the door\",\"On the window\",\"On the floor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they are making a toran \'to hang over the door\'.\",\"topic\":\"Toran (Garland)\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many hand-spans long is the toran that Avani has made?\",\"options\":[\"6 hand-spans\",\"7 hand-spans\",\"8 hand-spans\",\"9 hand-spans\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the figure, Avani counts \'1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7\' and says it is 7 hand-spans long.\",\"topic\":\"Toran (Garland)\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/058_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Anshuman measure the door with his hand-span?\",\"options\":[\"To see if the door is clean\",\"To decide how long the toran should be\",\"To count the flowers\",\"To play a game\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they measured because they were \'unable to decide how long the toran should be\'.\",\"topic\":\"Toran (Garland)\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the door is 7 hand-spans long, which toran will fit the door exactly?\",\"options\":[\"A toran that is 6 hand-spans long\",\"A toran that is 7 hand-spans long\",\"A toran that is 5 hand-spans long\",\"A toran that is 4 hand-spans long\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"To fit a 7 hand-span door, the toran must also be 7 hand-spans long.\",\"topic\":\"Toran (Garland)\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What did Avani say to her brother (Dada) after the measurement was done?\",\"options\":[\"I am making a toran that is 6 hand-spans long.\",\"I am making a toran that is 7 hand-spans long.\",\"The door is too big.\",\"I don\'t want to make a toran.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Avani says, \'Dada, I’m making a toran that is 7 hand-spans long.\'\",\"topic\":\"Toran (Garland)\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which two children were measuring the length of the first-aid box?\",\"options\":[\"Ravina and Sunil\",\"Rama and Suresh\",\"Rina and Sumit\",\"Radha and Sunil\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that Ravina and Sunil were measuring the length of the first-aid box.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the first measurement, what was Ravina given to use?\",\"options\":[\"An ice cream stick\",\"A stick from a matchbox\",\"A hand-span\",\"A piece of string\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Ravina was given a stick from a matchbox.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To avoid confusion while measuring an object, what should be done?\",\"options\":[\"Use different units\",\"Use the same unit\",\"Use any unit\",\"Use no unit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that if the same unit is used for measurement, there will be no confusion.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens if the same object is measured with a hand-span and then with another unit?\",\"options\":[\"The length stays exactly the same\",\"The measurement changes\",\"The object breaks\",\"The measurement is always 4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text implies that using different units leads to different measurements and confusion.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you and your friend measure the same table using your own hand-spans, why might you get different numbers?\",\"options\":[\"Because your hands are different sizes\",\"Because the table is growing\",\"Because you are using the same unit\",\"Because the table is too long\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Hand-spans vary between people, so using them as units leads to inconsistent results.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, why does the girl count 9 sticks while the boy counts 4 sticks for the same box?\",\"options\":[\"The girl is measuring a different box\",\"They are using different measuring tools\",\"The boy is measuring the height\",\"The girl is counting wrong\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the girl using small matchbox sticks and the boy using longer ice cream sticks.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/059_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What was Sunil given to measure the box in the first attempt?\",\"options\":[\"A matchbox stick\",\"An ice cream stick\",\"A hand-span\",\"A toran\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Sunil was given an ice cream stick.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text say will happen if the same unit is used for measurement?\",\"options\":[\"There will be confusion\",\"There will be no confusion\",\"The object will grow\",\"The measurement will be wrong\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if the same unit is used, then there will be no confusion.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, why do both children now get the same measurement of 4 sticks?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are using different tools\",\"Because they are using the same measuring tool\",\"Because the box became smaller\",\"Because they are guessing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows both children using ice cream sticks, which leads to a consistent result.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/059_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"To make sure everyone in a class gets the same measurement for a cupboard, what should the teacher do?\",\"options\":[\"Ask them to use their own hand-spans\",\"Give everyone the same measuring unit\",\"Let them use any stick they find\",\"Tell them to guess the length\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using equal measuring tools gives consistent results for everyone.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If two different people measure the same toran with their own hand-spans, why might the results be different?\",\"options\":[\"Hand-spans can be different sizes\",\"The toran changes its length\",\"Hand-spans are always the same\",\"Hand-spans cannot be used for torans\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Since hand-spans are not equal units, they result in different measurements for the same object.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s measure the length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what unit is used to measure objects along with a hand-span?\",\"options\":[\"A ruler\",\"A full pencil\",\"A piece of string\",\"An eraser\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions measuring the length of objects with a full pencil.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Measuring Length\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when different people measure the same object using unequal units like a hand-span?\",\"options\":[\"The measurements remain the same\",\"The measurements differ\",\"The object becomes longer\",\"The object becomes shorter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when using unequal units like a hand-span, the measurements of the length of that object differ.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Measuring Length\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which is the first object shown in the classroom list for measurement?\",\"options\":[\"A table\",\"A bench\",\"A book\",\"A blackboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first image in the \'Objects in the classroom\' column of the table is a book.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Measuring Length\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/060_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why do measurements differ when different people use their hand-spans?\",\"options\":[\"Because hand-spans are unequal units\",\"Because the object changes size\",\"Because the pencil is too long\",\"Because the classroom is big\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explains that measurements differ when people use unequal units like a hand-span.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Measuring Length\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you and your teacher measure the same object using the same unit, like a pencil, what will be the result?\",\"options\":[\"The measurements will be different\",\"The measurements will remain the same\",\"The teacher\'s measurement will be more\",\"The student\'s measurement will be more\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if different people measure with the same unit like a pencil, the measurement remains the same.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Measuring Length\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is considered an \'unequal unit\' for measurement?\",\"options\":[\"A full pencil\",\"A hand-span\",\"A standard scale\",\"A new crayon\"],\"