that has heavy fruits?\",\"options\":[\"It goes up\",\"It stays in the middle\",\"It goes down\",\"It breaks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The scale-pan with heavy fruits will go down.\'\",\"topic\":\"Heavy and Light\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the scale-pan with Guava went down when compared to a Mango, what does it mean?\",\"options\":[\"Guava is lighter than Mango\",\"Guava is heavier than Mango\",\"Mango is heavier than Guava\",\"Both are equal in weight\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that if the Guava pan goes down, Guava is heavier than the Mango.\",\"topic\":\"Heavy and Light\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the conversation, which of these fruits is lighter than the Mango?\",\"options\":[\"Watermelon\",\"Papaya\",\"Jamun\",\"Guava\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Mango says that Ber Fruit and Jamun are lighter than it.\",\"topic\":\"Heavy and Light\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Mango, which fruit is heavier than it?\",\"options\":[\"Ber Fruit\",\"Jamun\",\"Watermelon\",\"Small seeds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Mango specifically mentions that Watermelon is heavier than it.\",\"topic\":\"Heavy and Light\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Guava is heavier than Mango, then what is the relation of Mango to Guava?\",\"options\":[\"Mango is heavier than Guava\",\"Mango is lighter than Guava\",\"Mango is the same as Guava\",\"Mango is bigger than Guava\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that if Guava is heavier than Mango, it means Mango is lighter than Guava.\",\"topic\":\"Heavy and Light\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who is addressed as the \'King of Fruits\' in the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Watermelon\",\"Guava\",\"Mango\",\"Papaya\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The monkey addresses the Mango as \'Oh King of Fruits!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Heavy and Light\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a fruit is \'light\', what will happen to its side of the weighing scale compared to a heavy fruit?\",\"options\":[\"It will go down\",\"It will stay higher\",\"It will spin\",\"It will disappear\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since the heavy side goes down, the lighter side must stay higher or go up.\",\"topic\":\"Heavy and Light\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which fruit is shown asking the question, \'Am I heavier or lighter than you?\'\",\"options\":[\"Watermelon\",\"Guava\",\"Papaya\",\"Jamun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows the Guava asking this specific question in a purple speech bubble.\",\"topic\":\"Heavy and Light\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/061_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which two fruits are pictured in the top-right bubble as being lighter than the Mango?\",\"options\":[\"Watermelon and Papaya\",\"Guava and Jamun\",\"Ber Fruit and Jamun\",\"Mango and Watermelon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The top-right bubble shows pictures of a Ber fruit and a Jamun next to the text \'are lighter than me\'.\",\"topic\":\"Heavy and Light\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/061_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the term used for the amount of water a bucket can hold?\",\"options\":[\"Weight\",\"Height\",\"Capacity\",\"Length\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that if a bucket holds water, that amount is its capacity.\",\"topic\":\"Do it yourself\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a bucket holds more water, what can we say about its capacity?\",\"options\":[\"Its capacity is less\",\"Its capacity is more\",\"Its capacity is zero\",\"Its capacity is the same\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, if a bucket holds more water, then its capacity is more.\",\"topic\":\"Do it yourself\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the children bring buckets of water to the school garden?\",\"options\":[\"To wash their hands\",\"To water the trees\",\"To play with water\",\"To clean the classroom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the trees in the school garden need to be watered.\",\"topic\":\"Do it yourself\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the activity, how should the four vessels of different sizes be arranged?\",\"options\":[\"In descending order of size\",\"In ascending order of size\",\"In random order\",\"From heaviest to lightest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity instructions say to arrange the vessels in ascending order of size.\",\"topic\":\"Do it yourself\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To compare the capacity of different vessels fairly, what should be used to fill them?\",\"options\":[\"Different sized mugs\",\"The same glass\",\"A large pipe\",\"Small spoons\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to fill all four vessels completely using the same glass.\",\"topic\":\"Do it yourself\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a bucket holds less water, its capacity is ______.\",\"options\":[\"more\",\"less\",\"large\",\"full\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if a bucket holds less water, then its capacity is less.\",\"topic\":\"Do it yourself\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you have a small bowl and a big pot, which one has more capacity?\",\"options\":[\"The small bowl\",\"The big pot\",\"Both have same capacity\",\"Neither has capacity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Capacity is more if the vessel holds more water, which a bigger pot does.\",\"topic\":\"Do it yourself\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When vessels are arranged in ascending order of size, what happens to the number of glasses of water they hold?\",\"options\":[\"The number of glasses decreases\",\"The number of glasses stays the same\",\"The number of glasses also increases\",\"The number of glasses becomes zero\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks to verify if the number of glasses increases according to the size of the vessel.\",\"topic\":\"Do it yourself\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides water, which other liquid is mentioned for measuring capacity in the discussion?\",\"options\":[\"Juice\",\"Petrol\",\"Oil\",\"Honey\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests discussing measuring capacity using milk or oil.\",\"topic\":\"Do it yourself\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If we have four vessels (1, 2, 3, 4) in ascending order of size, which vessel will hold the most water?\",\"options\":[\"Vessel 1\",\"Vessel 2\",\"Vessel 3\",\"Vessel 4\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"In ascending order, the last vessel (4) is the largest and will hold the most water.\",\"topic\":\"Do it yourself\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21339,7,2,'Maths','en','Let\'s Understand Geometrical Shapes - Part 2','[\"A rectangle has 4 sides, 4 corners, and 2 pairs of equal opposite sides.\",\"A square is a special rectangle with all 4 sides equal.\",\"A triangle has 3 sides and 3 corners.\",\"Shapes can be identified by tracing the edges of objects on paper.\",\"Corners are points where two sides meet.\",\"Edges are the straight lines that form the boundary of a shape.\",\"Greeting cards are often made from rectangular paper.\",\"A rectangle has 4 edges and 4 corners.\",\"A square has 4 edges and 4 corners, all sides equal.\",\"A triangle has 3 edges and 3 corners.\",\"We can make shapes using sticks by joining their ends.\",\"Four equal sticks can make a square.\",\"Six equal sticks can make a rectangle (e.g., 2 sticks for length, 2 for breadth, 2 for height — but in 2D, we consider outline).\",\"To make a rectangle with sticks, opposite sides must be equal.\",\"To make a triangle with sticks, the sum of any two sides must be greater than the third.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the name of the art style Neeta Tai used to draw the picture?\",\"options\":[\"Modern Art\",\"Warli Art\",\"Folk Art\",\"Oil Painting\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the picture is of Warli Art.\",\"topic\":\"Picture Exhibition\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these shapes is mentioned by Neeta Tai in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Oval\",\"Star\",\"Triangle\",\"Diamond\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Neeta Tai mentions triangle, rectangle, square, and circle.\",\"topic\":\"Picture Exhibition\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Neeta Tai use besides shapes to draw the picture?\",\"options\":[\"Colors\",\"Lines\",\"Stickers\",\"Paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Neeta Tai says, \'I also used some lines while drawing.\'\",\"topic\":\"Picture Exhibition\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which type of line is described as \'|\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Horizontal line\",\"Slanting line\",\"Curved line\",\"Vertical line\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the \'|\' symbol as a vertical line.\",\"topic\":\"Picture Exhibition\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name for the \'—\' line used in the drawing?\",\"options\":[\"Horizontal line\",\"Vertical line\",\"Slanting line\",\"Curved line\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the \'—\' symbol as a horizontal line.\",\"topic\":\"Picture Exhibition\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which lines are represented by the symbols \'\\\\ \\/\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Vertical lines\",\"Slanting lines\",\"Horizontal lines\",\"Curved lines\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'\\\\ \\/\' are slanting lines.\",\"topic\":\"Picture Exhibition\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of lines are represented by the symbols \'~ ~\'?\",\"options\":[\"Straight lines\",\"Vertical lines\",\"Curved lines\",\"Slanting lines\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'~ ~\' are curved lines.\",\"topic\":\"Picture Exhibition\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\