opic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the first subtraction example given in the text?\",\"options\":[\"46 - 17\",\"46 - 7\",\"100 - 46\",\"17 - 7\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first example listed in the text is 46 - 7.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the number chart, what does the word \'jump\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"Physical exercise\",\"Moving across numbers on the chart\",\"Skipping a page in the book\",\"Drawing a circle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the number chart method, a jump refers to moving from one number to another to perform calculation.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21342,7,2,'Maths','en','Let\'s Understand the Information','[]','[{\"q\":\"Which shape of wall-clock is mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Triangle\",\"Square\",\"Star\",\"Heart\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks for the number of square-shaped wall-clocks.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand the Information\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What part of the wrist-watch are we looking at to check the color?\",\"options\":[\"The dial\",\"The hands\",\"The straps\",\"The numbers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks about wrist-watches having black or pink straps.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand the Information\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What part of the sun-glasses is being checked for its shape?\",\"options\":[\"The frame\",\"The lenses\",\"The arms\",\"The case\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks about sun-glasses with square lenses or round lenses.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand the Information\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides square, what other shape is mentioned for wall-clocks and sun-glasses?\",\"options\":[\"Oval\",\"Round\",\"Rectangle\",\"Diamond\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions both square-shaped and round-shaped items.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand the Information\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What two colors of straps are mentioned for the wrist-watches?\",\"options\":[\"Red and Blue\",\"Black and Pink\",\"Green and Yellow\",\"White and Brown\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to wrist-watches with black straps and pink straps.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand the Information\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To answer \'How many sun-glasses are more than wrist-watches?\', what must we do?\",\"options\":[\"Add the numbers together\",\"Compare the number of each item\",\"Count only the sun-glasses\",\"Count only the wrist-watches\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Comparing the counts helps us find out which item is \'more\' or \'less\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand the Information\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If there are 4 square sun-glasses and 2 round sun-glasses, how many sun-glasses are there in all?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"4\",\"6\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Adding the two types of sun-glasses (4 + 2) gives the total count of 6.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand the Information\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If there are 10 sun-glasses and 7 wall-clocks, how many wall-clocks are less than sun-glasses?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"7\",\"10\",\"17\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Subtracting the number of wall-clocks from sun-glasses (10 - 7) gives the difference of 3.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand the Information\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Question 7 in the text asks to compare sun-glasses with which other item?\",\"options\":[\"Wall-clocks\",\"Wrist-watches\",\"Lenses\",\"Straps\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Question 7 asks how many sun-glasses are more than wrist-watches.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand the Information\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal of asking all these questions about the objects?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to draw\",\"To understand the information provided\",\"To learn how to tell time\",\"To buy new glasses\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The chapter title and the questions focus on understanding information through counting and comparing.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand the Information\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a daily life object mentioned in the text to practice asking questions?\",\"options\":[\"Leaves\",\"Cars\",\"Buildings\",\"Stars\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions leaves, flowers, and household items as examples of objects from daily life.\",\"topic\":\"Project\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which grades should you visit in your school for the project?\",\"options\":[\"Grade 5 to Grade 8\",\"Grade 1 to Grade 4\",\"Only Grade 2\",\"Grade 1 to Grade 10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks to visit classes from Grade 1 to Grade 4.\",\"topic\":\"Project\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is suggested to help you when you visit different classes in school?\",\"options\":[\"The Principal\",\"Your Teacher\",\"The Peon\",\"Your Friend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to visit the classes \'With the help of your teacher\'.\",\"topic\":\"Project\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When visiting families to collect information, whose help should you get?\",\"options\":[\"Your Teacher\",\"Your Neighbors\",\"Your Parents\",\"The Shopkeeper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Get the help of your parents\' when visiting families.\",\"topic\":\"Project\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you find 5 women and 4 men in a family, what will be the \'Total Members in the Family\'?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"5\",\"4\",\"9\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The total is found by adding the number of women (5) and men (4), which equals 9.\",\"topic\":\"Project\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Standard 2 has 12 boys and 13 girls, what is the total number of students in that class?\",\"options\":[\"25\",\"12\",\"13\",\"1\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The total students is the sum of boys and girls: 12 + 13 = 25.\",\"topic\":\"Project\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which column is used to record the number of female students?\",\"options\":[\"Standard\",\"Boys\",\"Girls\",\"Total Students in the class\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The column labeled \'Girls\' is where the number of female students is recorded.\",\"topic\":\"Project\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/089_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many rows are provided under the \'Standard\' column to fill in data?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table shows four rows numbered 1, 2, 3, and 4 for the different standards.\",\"topic\":\"Project\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/089_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How many families are you supposed to visit for the second project?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says to \'visit five families\'.\",\"topic\":\"Project\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What specific information are you asked to collect about the classes you visit?\",\"options\":[\"Number of books\",\"Number of boys and girls\",\"Number of desks\",\"Number of windows\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The project asks to \'Find the number of boys and girls in each class\'.\",\"topic\":\"Project\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21343,7,2,'Maths','en','Patterns','[\"Patterns are arrangements that repeat in a regular way.\",\"We can use letters like A, B, C to show repeating patterns.\",\"Example: A B A B A B is a pattern where A and B repeat.\",\"Patterns can be made with shapes, colours, numbers, or letters.\",\"To complete a pattern, look at what comes before and guess what comes next.\",\"Mehendi designs often use repeating patterns on hands.\",\"Stamping with leaves, potatoes, or okra can create fun patterns.\",\"The Gregorian calendar has 12 months in a year.\",\"January has 31 days, February has 28 or 29 days.\",\"Months with 31 days: Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Aug, Oct, Dec (7 months).\",\"Months with 30 days: Apr, Jun, Sep, Nov (4 months).\",\"February has 28 days normally, 29 in a leap year.\",\"A leap year has 366 days and comes every 4 years.\",\"Seasons: Summer (Mar–Jun), Winter (Oct–Feb), each about 3–4 months.\",\"Indian Solar Year starts with Chaitra and ends with Phalgun.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the description of an arrangement called according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A style\",\"A drawing\",\"A game\",\"A flower\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that this type of description of an arrangement is called a style.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Style\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many different objects are used in the style described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that \'Two different objects are used\' in this style.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Style\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the first object in Asha\'s arrangement?\",\"options\":[\"A flower\",\"A leaf\",\"The letter A\",\"The letter B\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Looking at the picture, Asha\'s arrangement starts with a leaf.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Style\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/090_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what letters did Vivek use for his arrangement?\",\"options\":[\"X and Y\",\"C and D\",\"A and B\",\"P and Q\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows Vivek has arranged the letters A and B.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Style\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/090_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What did Asha use for her arrangement?\",\"options\":[\"A and B\",\"One leaf and one flower\",\"Stones and sticks\",\"Two different flowers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says Asha has arranged one leaf and one flower alternately.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Style\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does it mean when objects are placed \'alternately\'?\",\"options\":[\"Placing all same objects together\",\"Placing two different objects one after the other\",\"Placing objects in a pile\",\"Using only one kind of object\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains the style as two different objects placed one after the other alternately.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Style\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If we use a circle and a square to make the same style, what will the arrangement look like?\",\"options\":[\"Circle Circle Square Square\",\"Circle Square Circle Square\",\"Circle Circle Circle Circle\",\"Square Square Square Square\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Following the alternate style, the objects must be placed one after the other.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Style\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the style of Asha\'s and Vivek\'s arrangements said to be the same?\",\"options\":[\"Because they used the same objects\",\"Because they used two objects alternately\",\"Because they are both in the same room\",\"Because they used the same colors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains the style is the same because two different objects are placed one after the other alternately in both cases.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Style\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If Vivek places two \'A\' letters together (AA), is he following the style described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Yes, because he is using letters\",\"No, because the objects must be placed one after the other alternately\",\"Yes, because A is a letter\",\"No, because he must use flowers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The style requires objects to be placed alternately, not two of the same kind together.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Style\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"To make a new arrangement with the same style as Asha, which pair of objects could you use?\",\"options\":[\"Only green leaves\",\"Only red flowers\",\"A bat and a ball alternately\",\"Three different colored pencils\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Using two different objects (bat and ball) alternately follows the style described.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Style\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"create\"},{\"q\":\"What is a particular repeated way of doing things called?\",\"options\":[\"A drawing\",\"A pattern\",\"A number\",\"A letter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that things done in a particular repeated way are called a pattern.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which letters can be used to show patterns according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only X and Y\",\"Only numbers 1 and 2\",\"Letters like A, B, C etc.\",\"Only symbols like stars\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that patterns can be shown using the letters A, B, C etc.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If we call a leaf \'A\' and a flower \'B\', what are we identifying?\",\"options\":[\"The color of objects\",\"The weight of objects\",\"The style of the pattern\",\"The size of the objects\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Assigning letters to objects helps identify if patterns follow the same style.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When two different arrangements use the same letter sequence, they are considered to be:\",\"options\":[\"Exactly the same style\",\"Completely different\",\"Wrong patterns\",\"Only for flowers\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says if arrangements follow the same letter sequence, they become exactly the same style.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a pattern is Leaf-Flower-Leaf-Flower, and Leaf is \'A\' and Flower is \'B\', what is the pattern style?\",\"options\":[\"ABC\",\"AABB\",\"ABAB\",\"BAAA\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Repeating A (leaf) and B (flower) alternately creates an ABAB style.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a pattern is shown as A-B-C, A-B-C, how many different types of items are being repeated?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Each different letter (A, B, and C) represents a different type of item in the pattern.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what happens to two arrangements if they follow the same letter sequence?\",\"options\":[\"They become different\",\"They become exactly the same style\",\"They stop being patterns\",\"They become letters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if arrangements follow the same letters, they become exactly the same style.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If we have a pattern of \'Sun-Moon-Sun-Moon\', which letter style does it follow?\",\"options\":[\"AABB\",\"ABC\",\"ABAB\",\"AAAA\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since two items repeat alternately, it follows the ABAB style mentioned in the text examples.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the letter \'A\' represent when we describe a pattern style?\",\"options\":[\"The first item in the repeated sequence\",\"The word \'Apple\'\",\"The end of a pattern\",\"A random drawing\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Letters like A are used to represent specific items to show the pattern\'s structure.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a pattern is \'Leaf-Leaf-Flower-Leaf-Leaf-Flower\', and Leaf is \'A\' and Flower is \'B\', what is the style?\",\"options\":[\"ABB\",\"AAB\",\"ABC\",\"AAA\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Two leaves (AA) followed by one flower (B) creates an AAB pattern style.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21344,7,2,'Maths','en','Measuring Time','[\"A day has 24 hours.\",\"A week has 7 days: Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday.\",\"A month has 4 or 5 weeks.\",\"The calendar shows dates and days of the week.\",\"The first day of a month can be any day of the week.\",\"To find hours between two times, subtract the start time from the end time.\",\"From 6 o’clock to 10 o’clock is 4 hours.\",\"From 4 o’clock to 7 o’clock is 3 hours.\",\"From 8 o’clock to 9 o’clock is 1 hour.\",\"If today is Monday, then after 24 hours it will be Monday again.\",\"24 hours make one day.\",\"The first Sunday of a month can be on the 1st, 2nd, 3rd, or later.\",\"The last day of a month depends on the number of days in that month.\",\"February can have 28 or 29 days.\",\"January always has 31 days.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which is the first month of the Gregorian year?\",\"options\":[\"December\",\"January\",\"February\",\"March\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Gregorian year starts from January.\",\"topic\":\"Months of Gregorian Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many months are there in a year?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"10\",\"12\",\"31\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, there are 12 months in a year.\",\"topic\":\"Months of Gregorian Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which month comes just after May?\",\"options\":[\"April\",\"June\",\"July\",\"August\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks \'Which month is just after May?\' and the sequence shows June follows May.\",\"topic\":\"Months of Gregorian Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which is the last month of the year?\",\"options\":[\"November\",\"January\",\"December\",\"October\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Gregorian year ends with December.\",\"topic\":\"Months of Gregorian Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many days are there in the month of February?\",\"options\":[\"30 or 31 days\",\"28 or 29 days\",\"Exactly 30 days\",\"Exactly 31 days\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure and text indicate February has 28 or 29 days.\",\"topic\":\"Months of Gregorian Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens after the month of December ends?\",\"options\":[\"The year stops\",\"A new month called February starts\",\"A new year begins with January\",\"The months go backwards\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that after December ends, a new year again begins with January.\",\"topic\":\"Months of Gregorian Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many months are shown to have exactly 30 days?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"4\",\"12\",\"5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"By looking at the figure, April, June, September, and November have 30 days, totaling 4 months.\",\"topic\":\"Months of Gregorian Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/094_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, count the months starting from January and ending at July. How many months are there?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"7\",\"8\",\"5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Counting from January (1) to July (7) in the figure gives a total of 7 months.\",\"topic\":\"Months of Gregorian Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/094_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which two consecutive months (one after the other) both have 31 days?\",\"options\":[\"June and July\",\"July and August\",\"August and September\",\"April and May\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows that July has 31 days and the next month, August, also has 31 days.\",\"topic\":\"Months of Gregorian Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"By checking the number of days for every month in the figure, how many months in one year have 31 days?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"6\",\"7\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Counting the months with 31 days (Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Aug, Oct, Dec) results in 7 months.\",\"topic\":\"Months of Gregorian Calendar\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many days are there in one English year?\",\"options\":[\"360 days\",\"365 days\",\"366 days\",\"300 days\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that in one English year there are 365 days.\",\"topic\":\"Season Wheel\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a year called when it has 366 days?\",\"options\":[\"Full Year\",\"English Year\",\"Leap Year\",\"Season Year\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A year that has 366 days is called a Leap Year.\",\"topic\":\"Season Wheel\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a Leap Year, how many days does the month of February have?\",\"options\":[\"28 days\",\"29 days\",\"30 days\",\"31 days\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that in a Leap Year, February has 29 days.\",\"topic\":\"Season Wheel\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Generally, how many months are there in one season?\",\"options\":[\"2 months\",\"3 months\",\"4 months\",\"6 months\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the season wheel logic in the text, there are generally 4 months in one season.\",\"topic\":\"Season Wheel\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the season wheel, which month does the winter season begin from?\",\"options\":[\"June\",\"October\",\"February\",\"August\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the Maharashtra State Board season cycle, the winter season begins from the month of October.\",\"topic\":\"Season Wheel\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The month of August belongs to which season?\",\"options\":[\"Summer\",\"Winter\",\"Rainy\",\"Spring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the season wheel for Std 2, August is part of the rainy season.\",\"topic\":\"Season Wheel\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"