ch two toys give the highest total when sold together.\",\"We use real or dummy money to practice counting.\",\"Notes have numbers and pictures on them.\",\"We observe notes to learn about symbols and monuments.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who sold fruits and vegetables at the Children Fun Fair?\",\"options\":[\"Parveen Kaur\",\"Rohan\",\"The Shopkeeper\",\"The Teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Rohan sold fruits and vegetables at the Children Fun Fair.\",\"topic\":\"Currency Notes and Coins\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was Parveen Kaur given by the shopkeeper in exchange for her ₹ 50 note?\",\"options\":[\"Fruits\",\"Vegetables\",\"Change\",\"A toy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Parveen Kaur got change of ₹ 50 from the shopkeeper.\",\"topic\":\"Currency Notes and Coins\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which note has the highest value among those shown?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 10\",\"₹ 100\",\"₹ 200\",\"₹ 500\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The figure shows notes of ₹ 10, ₹ 100, ₹ 200, and ₹ 500; ₹ 500 is the highest.\",\"topic\":\"Currency Notes and Coins\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/105_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many ₹ 2 coins did Parveen Kaur receive in her change?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows two ₹ 2 coins being given as part of the change for ₹ 50.\",\"topic\":\"Currency Notes and Coins\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"7\\/105_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What was the value of the note Parveen Kaur had before she got change?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 10\",\"₹ 20\",\"₹ 50\",\"₹ 100\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Parveen Kaur had a ₹ 50 note.\",\"topic\":\"Currency Notes and Coins\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is Rohan handling?\",\"options\":[\"Only fruits\",\"Only vegetables\",\"Coins and notes of different deno