\/033_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many men are there?\",\"options\":[\"Five\",\"Ten\",\"Two\",\"Seven\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text repeatedly mentions \'ten men\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where are the ten men and a hen?\",\"options\":[\"In a pen\",\"In a den\",\"On a bus\",\"In a box\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'ten men and a hen in a den\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What color is the bed mentioned in the reading exercise?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"Red\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the bed as \'a red bed\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is on the red bed in the first instance mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"A cat\",\"A dog\",\"A hen\",\"A man\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'a hen on a red bed\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text belongs to the same \'word family\' as \'den\' and \'men\'?\",\"options\":[\"Bed\",\"Red\",\"Ten\",\"Hens\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ten, den, and men all belong to the \'-en\' word family.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you follow the pattern of \'bed\' and \'red\', which new word could you make?\",\"options\":[\"Fed\",\"Fan\",\"Fin\",\"Fun\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Fed\' follows the \'-ed\' word family pattern used in \'bed\' and \'red\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'ten hens on a red bed\', how many hens are mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Ten\",\"Two\",\"None\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The phrase explicitly states \'ten hens\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which two things are found together in a den?\",\"options\":[\"Ten men and a bed\",\"A red bed and a hen\",\"Ten men and a hen\",\"Ten hens and a bed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'ten men and a hen in a den\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What example is given in section \'g\' for making new words?\",\"options\":[\"hen\",\"ten\",\"bed\",\"den\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Section \'g\' says \'For example - bed\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words does NOT rhyme with \'hen\'?\",\"options\":[\"men\",\"ten\",\"den\",\"red\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"\'Red\' ends in \'-ed\', while the others end in \'-en\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21394,11,3,'English','en','Coconut Tree','[\"Coconut tree is a tall, green tree that grows near the sea.\",\"Its leaves are long and dance in the wind.\",\"The tree bears green coconuts that hang from its branches.\",\"Coconut fruit has a hard shell, a brown husk, and a white, sweet milk inside.\",\"The tree gives us coconut oil, which is used for cooking and hair care.\",\"The husk of the coconut can be used as a mat or a bowl.\",\"The tree is called the \\\"Tree of Life\\\" because it provides food, water and shade.\",\"Coconut trees grow in warm, tropical places and need plenty of sunlight and water.\",\"The tree is very useful – nothing is wasted: shell, husk, oil and milk.\",\"Coconut trees are also used in poems and songs because they are beautiful and helpful.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where does the poem say the coconut tree is located?\",\"options\":[\"In the middle of a desert\",\"Near home and near school\",\"On top of a high mountain\",\"Inside a big building\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states the tree is \'Near my home, near my school\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What color is the coconut milk as described in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Green\",\"Yellow\",\"White\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'milk so white\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the coconut husk used for according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Making bowls\",\"Making mats\",\"Making oil\",\"Making laddoos\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'husk for mat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the coconut tree called the \'Tree of Life\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is very tall\",\"Because it grows near the sea\",\"Because nothing from the tree is wasted\",\"Because it has green coconuts\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem calls it the Tree of Life after explaining that nothing is wasted.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the coconut tree give us that is \'sweet and cool\'?\",\"options\":[\"Oil\",\"Milk\",\"Water\",\"Shells\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says the tree \'Gives us water, sweet and cool\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How are the leaves of the coconut tree described?\",\"options\":[\"Short and stiff\",\"Long and dancing free\",\"Small and round\",\"Dry and brown\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the leaves as \'long, dancing free\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person wants to make a bowl from a coconut, which part should they use?\",\"options\":[\"The leaves\",\"The shell\",\"The oil\",\"The husk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem suggests using the \'Shell for bowls\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these food items mentioned in the text is a drink?\",\"options\":[\"Modaks\",\"Laddoos\",\"Barfies\",\"Solkadhi\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Solkadhi is a traditional coconut-based drink mentioned in the food list.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When the poem says the leaves are \'waving hands\', what does it mean?\",\"options\":[\"The tree is literally human\",\"The leaves are moving in the breeze\",\"The tree is trying to catch the clouds\",\"The leaves are falling off the tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Waving hands is a metaphor for the movement of the long leaves in the wind.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main reason the poet calls the coconut tree \'Nature\'s gift beyond compare\'?\",\"options\":[\"It is the only tree that grows near the sea\",\"It is taller than all other trees\",\"It provides many useful things like food, water, and materials\",\"It is the only tree with green fruit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem lists many uses (water, oil, milk, shell, husk), showing its immense value.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first instruction given to the learners in the \'For the Teacher\' section?\",\"options\":[\"Read and write\",\"Listen and repeat\",\"Draw and color\",\"Speak and sing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins with the instruction \'Listen and repeat\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of trees and plants should learners be promoted to collect pictures of?\",\"options\":[\"Fruit trees\",\"Tall trees\",\"Medicinal trees and plants\",\"Wild plants\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions promoting learners to collect pictures of medicinal trees and plants.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What length of sentences should learners be encouraged to write?\",\"options\":[\"Long sentences\",\"Short sentences\",\"Very long paragraphs\",\"Single words only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically says to encourage learners to \'write in short sentences\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides speaking, what else should learners do regarding \'food items\'?\",\"options\":[\"Draw them\",\"Eat them\",\"Write poems on them\",\"Buy them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests motivating learners to write poems on different food items.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher encourage learners to identify in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Hard words\",\"Important ideas\",\"Rhyming words\",\"The number of lines\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'Encourage them to identify important ideas in the poem.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are learners encouraged to speak about?\",\"options\":[\"Their friends\",\"Food items\",\"The weather\",\"School games\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Encourage learners to speak about food items\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher asks a student to talk about \'Rice and Dal\', which instruction is being followed?\",\"options\":[\"Collect pictures of plants\",\"Identify ideas in a poem\",\"Speak about food items\",\"Listen and repeat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rice and Dal are food items, so this follows the instruction to speak about food items.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student brings a picture of a Tulsi plant to class. This activity matches which instruction?\",\"options\":[\"Write in short sentences\",\"Collect pictures of medicinal trees and plants\",\"Identify important ideas\",\"Listen and repeat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tulsi is a medicinal plant, so this fits the instruction to collect pictures of medicinal trees and plants.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which two activities are specifically linked to \'food items\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Speaking and writing poems\",\"Listening and repeating\",\"Collecting pictures and writing sentences\",\"Identifying ideas and speaking\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions speaking about food items and writing poems on different food items.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity helps a student understand the meaning of the poem better according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Collecting pictures\",\"Writing short sentences\",\"Identifying important ideas in the poem\",\"Repeating after the teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Identifying important ideas is the activity directly related to analyzing the content of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21395,11,3,'English','en','Narali Pournima','[\"Narali Pournima is a festival celebrated in Maharashtra on the full moon day of the month of Chaitra.\",\"It is also called Narali Pournima because people eat a special sweet called Narali Bhat made from coconut.\",\"Families visit the sea shore and offer a coconut to the sea as a prayer for safety and prosperity.\",\"People decorate their houses with coconut shells and make doormats from brown husk of coconut.\",\"Children enjoy sweets like coconut laddoos, barfi and other coconut based sweets.\",\"The festival is celebrated with family and friends, and people share stories and songs.\",\"It is a time to thank the sea for its bounty and to wish for good health and harmony.\",\"During Narali Pournima, people also celebrate Rakshabandhan, a festival of brother-sister love.\",\"The story of Mukta and Raghav shows how families come together to celebrate this festival.\",\"The mother prepares coconut sweets and a special drink called solkadhi made from coconut flesh.\",\"The father is a fisherman, and the family lives near the sea, which is important for the festival.\",\"The whole day is spent with relatives, sharing food and enjoying the sea view.\",\"The story emphasizes the importance of family, tradition, and respect for nature.\",\"Children learn to recognize key characters and main ideas in the story.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where do Mukta and Raghav live?\",\"options\":[\"In a big city\",\"In a small village near Alibaug\",\"In a forest\",\"In a desert\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Mukta and Raghav live in a small village near Alibaug.\",\"topic\":\"Narali Pournima: Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is Alibaug famous for besides its long seashore?\",\"options\":[\"Mango trees\",\"Apple trees\",\"Coconut trees\",\"Banyan trees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Alibaug is famous for its long seashore and coconut trees.\",\"topic\":\"Narali Pournima: Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the relationship between Mukta and Raghav?\",\"options\":[\"Friends\",\"Siblings\",\"Cousins\",\"Neighbors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Mukta and Raghav are siblings.\",\"topic\":\"Narali Pournima: Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the occupation of Mukta and Raghav\'s father?\",\"options\":[\"Farmer\",\"Teacher\",\"Fisherman\",\"Doctor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that their father is a fisherman.\",\"topic\":\"Narali Pournima: Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the coconut does the mother use to make solkadhi?\",\"options\":[\"Brown husk\",\"Coconut shell\",\"Coconut flesh\",\"Coconut leaves\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the mother makes solkadhi by using coconut flesh.\",\"topic\":\"Narali Pournima: Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What do Mukta and Raghav\'s family make from the brown husk of the coconut?\",\"options\":[\"Sweets\",\"Doormats\",\"Solkadhi\",\"Decorations\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states they make doormats from brown husk.\",\"topic\":\"Narali Pournima: Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Mukta wants to decorate her house, what will she use according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Coconut shells\",\"Brown husk\",\"Coconut flesh\",\"Fish nets\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they use coconut shells to decorate their house.\",\"topic\":\"Narali Pournima: Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what objects are shown lying on the ground in the bottom left corner?\",\"options\":[\"Fish\",\"Doormats\",\"Coconut shells\",\"Sweets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows two empty coconut shells in the bottom left corner.\",\"topic\":\"Narali Pournima: Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/037_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the mother carrying on her head?\",\"options\":[\"A basket of fish\",\"A decorated coconut in a pot\",\"A bundle of brown husk\",\"A tray of sweets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the mother carrying a decorated coconut (Naral) on her head for the festival.\",\"topic\":\"Narali Pournima: Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/037_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these items is described as \'tasty\'?\",\"options\":[\"Coconut shells\",\"Brown husk\",\"Coconut sweets\",\"Doormats\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that their mother makes \'tasty coconut sweets\'.\",\"topic\":\"Narali Pournima: Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What did Mukta do early in the morning?\",\"options\":[\"She went to the market\",\"She woke up early\",\"She cooked breakfast\",\"She went to the seashore\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Today, Mukta woke up early.\'\",\"topic\":\"Celebration at the Seashore\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two festivals are mentioned by Mukta?\",\"options\":[\"Diwali and Holi\",\"Ganesh Chaturthi and Eid\",\"Narali Pournima and Rakshabandhan\",\"Christmas and Pongal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mukta says, \'Today is Narali Pournima and Rakshabandhan.\'\",\"topic\":\"Celebration at the Seashore\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What special dish did the family have for breakfast?\",\"options\":[\"Puran Poli\",\"Narali Bhat\",\"Sabudana Khichdi\",\"Poha\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions their mother called them to have \'Narali Bhat\' for breakfast.\",\"topic\":\"Celebration at the Seashore\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who asked Mukta why the day was special?\",\"options\":[\"Her mother\",\"Her father\",\"Raghav\",\"The sea\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Raghav asked \'What’s special Mukta?\' after she said it was a special day.\",\"topic\":\"Celebration at the Seashore\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"At what time of the day did the family go to the seashore?\",\"options\":[\"In the morning\",\"At noon\",\"In the evening\",\"Late at night\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'In the evening, whole family reached the seashore.\'\",\"topic\":\"Celebration at the Seashore\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the mother prepare a pooja thali?\",\"options\":[\"To serve breakfast\",\"To worship the sea\",\"To give a gift to Raghav\",\"To carry the Narali Bhat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Her mother prepared a pooja thali to worship the sea.\'\",\"topic\":\"Celebration at the Seashore\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you were celebrating Narali Pournima like Mukta\'s family, what would you offer to the sea at the end of the pooja?\",\"options\":[\"A plate of rice\",\"A coconut\",\"A flower garland\",\"A sweet box\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'At the end they offered a coconut to the sea.\'\",\"topic\":\"Celebration at the Seashore\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, which item is necessary for the evening celebration at the seashore?\",\"options\":[\"A pooja thali\",\"A school bag\",\"A breakfast table\",\"An alarm clock\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The mother prepared a pooja thali specifically for the seashore worship.\",\"topic\":\"Celebration at the Seashore\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Mukta smile when Raghav asked her what was special?\",\"options\":[\"She was laughing at a joke\",\"She was happy about the festivals\",\"She was still feeling sleepy\",\"She wanted to go back to bed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Mukta smiled because it was a special day of celebration (Narali Pournima and Rakshabandhan).\",\"topic\":\"Celebration at the Seashore\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does the family show their respect to the sea during Narali Pournima?\",\"options\":[\"By swimming in the water\",\"By eating breakfast on the sand\",\"By worshipping the sea with a pooja thali and a coconut\",\"By waking up early in the morning\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The family shows respect by reaching the seashore, worshipping with a pooja thali, and offering a coconut.\",\"topic\":\"Celebration at the Seashore\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who did the people in the story spend the whole day with?\",\"options\":[\"Their friends\",\"Their relatives\",\"Their teachers\",\"Their neighbors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that they spent the whole day with their relatives.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sweets is specifically mentioned as something they enjoyed?\",\"options\":[\"Puran Poli\",\"Gulab Jamun\",\"Narali Bhat\",\"Jalebi\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists Narali Bhat, coconut laddoos, and barfi as the sweets they enjoyed.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What can you make from the shell mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Food items\",\"Different craft articles\",\"Clothes\",\"Sweets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'You can make different craft articles from my shell.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should teachers encourage learners to express their views about?\",\"options\":[\"Their favorite toys\",\"Narali Pournima\",\"School holidays\",\"Cooking food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'For the Teacher\' section says to encourage learners to express views about Narali Pournima.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is looking for the \'main characters\', where should they look according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"In the dictionary\",\"At the back of the book\",\"In the context of the story\",\"In the title only\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests encouraging learners to identify main characters from the context.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When a teacher asks a student to find the \'central idea\', what is the student trying to find?\",\"options\":[\"The longest word in the story\",\"The main point or message of the story\",\"The number of pages in the story\",\"The names of all the sweets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Identifying the central idea means understanding the main theme or point of the text.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What type of stories should teachers motivate learners to read?\",\"options\":[\"Stories about space\",\"Stories about Indian festivals\",\"Stories about animals\",\"Stories about sports\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions motivating them to read stories about Indian festivals.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Besides the central idea, what other part of the story should learners identify?\",\"options\":[\"Key aspects\",\"Page numbers\",\"Spelling errors\",\"Price of the book\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions identifying the central idea and the key aspects of the story.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is one specific skill the teacher should motivate students to practice regarding the text structure?\",\"options\":[\"Recognizing different sentences\",\"Counting the number of letters\",\"Drawing the relatives\",\"Eating the sweets\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The \'For the Teacher\' section says to motivate them to recognize different sentences.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a coconut-based sweet mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Coconut laddoos\",\"Chocolate cake\",\"Fruit salad\",\"Bread butter\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions coconut laddoos as one of the sweets enjoyed.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21396,11,3,'English','en','Word Family - III','[\"Word family is a group of words that share the same base letters and meaning.\",\"In this chapter we learn the word family that starts with the letters B, I, G, P, and F.\",\"The base word is the simplest form, e.g. ‘bin’ or ‘pig’.\",\"Add the letters ‘b’, ‘i’, ‘g’, ‘p’, or ‘f’ to the base to make new words.\",\"Examples: ‘bin’ → ‘big’, ‘pig’ → ‘fig’ (by changing the middle letter).\",\"The words in a family have similar sounds and meanings.\",\"Use the word family to build new words when you read or write.\",\"Remember the pattern: base word + one of the letters B, I, G, P, F.\",\"Practice by making sentences with the new words.\",\"The word family helps you understand how words are formed.\",\"It also helps you remember spelling of new words.\",\"Keep the base word in mind when you see a new word in a sentence.\",\"The base word is the ‘root’ of the family.\",\"The family can be used in stories, poems, and everyday conversation.\",\"Knowing word families makes reading easier and faster.\",\"The more families you know, the better your vocabulary becomes.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these words is included in the \'Word Family - III\' revision list?\",\"options\":[\"cat\",\"pig\",\"dog\",\"sun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'pig\' is explicitly listed in the revision section of the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What color is the fig described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"green\",\"yellow\",\"red\",\"blue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'a fig, a red fig\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the kid wearing in the story?\",\"options\":[\"a hat\",\"a cap\",\"a bag\",\"a pin\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'a kid, a kid with a cap\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does the bin have?\",\"options\":[\"a lid\",\"a zip\",\"a pin\",\"a fig\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text describes \'a bin, a bin with a lid\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who hit the big pig in the story?\",\"options\":[\"the fig\",\"the bin\",\"the kid\",\"the lid\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'The kid hit the big pig\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the revision list rhymes with \'win\'?\",\"options\":[\"sit\",\"big\",\"pin\",\"did\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Both \'win\' and \'pin\' are in the list and belong to the same word family.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence based on the text: \'The big pig hit the ____.\'\",\"options\":[\"kid\",\"bin\",\"fig\",\"lid\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text follows the sequence: \'The big pig hit the bin.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If \'pig\' is described as \'big\', how is the \'fig\' described in the phrases?\",\"options\":[\"big\",\"red\",\"kid\",\"zip\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'a big pig\' and \'a red fig\' as descriptive phrases.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happened immediately after the big pig hit the bin?\",\"options\":[\"The kid ran.\",\"The bin hit the fig.\",\"The pig hit the kid.\",\"The fig hit the bin.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows a chain reaction: \'The big pig hit the bin. The bin hit the fig.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which action happened first in the sequence of events?\",\"options\":[\"The pig hit the bin.\",\"The bin hit the fig.\",\"The kid ran.\",\"The kid hit the pig.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story sequence starts with \'The kid ran.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21397,11,3,'English','en','I am Growing Up','[\"I am growing up every day.\",\"I learn new things and play.\",\"I can do more by myself.\",\"I still need some help sometimes.\",\"I feel big and strong at times.\",\"I feel small and wrong at times.\",\"I feel happy and proud at times.\",\"I feel sad and loud at times.\",\"Growing up is not easy.\",\"Sometimes it makes me dizzy.\",\"I love growing up anyway.\",\"I can listen and sing to help me learn.\",\"I can write rhyming words to practice spelling.\",\"I can read and copy new words like learn, grow, make, help.\",\"I can use a dictionary to find meanings of words like grow, wrong, strong, proud, dizzy.\",\"I can express my feelings when I win or when a friend claps.\",\"I can talk about my feelings such as happy, sleepy, proud, sad, scared, shy, tired, angry, surprised.\",\"I can create posters with pictures of emotions.\",\"I can talk about emojis and what they mean.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, how often is the child growing up?\",\"options\":[\"Every week\",\"Every day\",\"Every month\",\"Every year\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first line of the poem states, \'I’m growing up every day.\'\",\"topic\":\"Growing up is not easy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What two things does the child do while growing up?\",\"options\":[\"Eat and sleep\",\"Run and jump\",\"Learn new things and play\",\"Read and write\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'I learn new things and I play.\'\",\"topic\":\"Growing up is not easy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The child says, \'I can do more by ____.\'\",\"options\":[\"my friends\",\"my teacher\",\"my parents\",\"myself\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem contains the line, \'I can do more by myself.\'\",\"topic\":\"Growing up is not easy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Even though the child can do more alone, what do they still need?\",\"options\":[\"New toys\",\"Some help\",\"More time\",\"New clothes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'But I still need some help.\'\",\"topic\":\"Growing up is not easy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does the child feel when they are not feeling \'big and strong\'?\",\"options\":[\"Small and wrong\",\"Happy and proud\",\"Fast and quick\",\"Tall and thin\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem pairs \'big and strong\' with the opposite feeling \'small and wrong\'.\",\"topic\":\"Growing up is not easy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is \'not easy\'?\",\"options\":[\"Playing games\",\"Learning to read\",\"Growing up\",\"Helping others\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem explicitly says, \'Growing up is not easy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Growing up is not easy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the poem rhymes with \'day\' and \'play\'?\",\"options\":[\"Help\",\"Strong\",\"Anyway\",\"Easy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the final stanza, \'anyway\' rhymes with \'day\'.\",\"topic\":\"Growing up is not easy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a child feels \'dizzy\' because of growing up, what is the reason given in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"They are spinning around\",\"Growing up is not easy\",\"They are very hungry\",\"They are playing too hard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem links feeling dizzy to the fact that growing up is not easy.\",\"topic\":\"Growing up is not easy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which pair of emotions is mentioned together in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Happy and loud\",\"Sad and proud\",\"Happy and proud\",\"Small and strong\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Sometimes, I feel happy and proud.\'\",\"topic\":\"Growing up is not easy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the child\'s final attitude toward growing up at the end of the poem?\",\"options\":[\"They want to stop growing\",\"They love it anyway\",\"They are afraid of it\",\"They think it is boring\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The last line of the poem is, \'And I love it anyway!\'\",\"topic\":\"Growing up is not easy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners discuss according to the teacher\'s instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Different games\",\"Different emotions\",\"Different colors\",\"Different animals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to encourage learners to discuss different emotions.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are learners encouraged to create using pictures?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing books\",\"Posters\",\"Storybooks\",\"Greeting cards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions promoting learners to create posters using pictures of emotions.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What specific items are learners motivated to talk about?\",\"options\":[\"Emojis they see\",\"Letters they write\",\"Numbers they count\",\"Songs they sing\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says to motivate them to talk about different emojis they see.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of pictures should be used to make the posters?\",\"options\":[\"Pictures of nature\",\"Pictures of food\",\"Pictures of emotions\",\"Pictures of vehicles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies using pictures of emotions for the posters.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the teacher\'s role regarding emojis?\",\"options\":[\"To draw emojis for students\",\"To motivate learners to talk about them\",\"To tell students to stop using them\",\"To test students on emoji names\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the teacher should motivate learners to talk about different emojis they see.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity involves learners sharing their thoughts with each other?\",\"options\":[\"Creating posters alone\",\"Discussing different emotions\",\"Looking at pictures silently\",\"Drawing emojis\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Discussing emotions involves learners talking and sharing thoughts.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student finds a picture of a happy face, what activity from the text can they use it for?\",\"options\":[\"Solving a math problem\",\"Creating a poster\",\"Writing a spelling list\",\"Playing a sport\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests creating posters using pictures of emotions (like a happy face).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher wants to follow the instructions in the text, what should they ask the students to do?\",\"options\":[\"Talk about the emojis they see on a phone or screen\",\"Memorize the names of all emotions\",\"Paint a landscape\",\"Read a story about animals\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Talking about emojis they see is a direct instruction provided for the teacher.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these activities mentioned in the text combines both art and the study of feelings?\",\"options\":[\"Discussing emotions\",\"Creating posters using pictures of emotions\",\"Talking about emojis\",\"Listening to the teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Creating posters is an art activity, and using pictures of emotions relates to feelings.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main theme of all three instructions given to the teacher?\",\"options\":[\"Learning how to draw\",\"Understanding and expressing emotions\",\"Using technology in class\",\"Improving reading skills\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"All three points (discussing emotions, posters of emotions, talking about emojis) focus on emotions.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21398,11,3,'English','en','My Friend, the Clock','[\"- A clock tells the time using numbers and two hands.\",\"- The big hand (short hand) shows the hour.\",\"- The small hand (long hand) shows the minutes.\",\"- Clocks make a tick‑tick sound when they move.\",\"- We can use a clock to know when to wake up, go to school, study, play, eat dinner and go to bed.\",\"- A clock is a helpful friend that helps us stay on schedule.\",\"- The word ‘clock’ comes from the Latin word ‘clocca’ meaning bell.\",\"- Clocks can be wall clocks, desk clocks, or wrist watches.\",\"- The hands of a clock move round and round in a circle.\",\"- The time shown on a clock is called the ‘time of day’.\",\"- We read the time by looking at where the hands point on the numbers.\",\"- The hour hand moves slowly, the minute hand moves faster.\",\"- A clock can also have a second hand that ticks every second.\",\"- We can set a clock by turning the knob or pressing buttons.\",\"- Clocks help us keep our daily routine and stay healthy and active.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What sound did the child hear from the clock?\",\"options\":[\"ding-dong, ding-dong\",\"tick-tick, tick-tick\",\"ring-ring, ring-ring\",\"tock-tock, tock-tock\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the clock made a sound again and again, \'tick-tick, tick-tick.\'\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the child see the clock when they were very small?\",\"options\":[\"On the table\",\"On the floor\",\"On the wall\",\"In the garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the child looked at the clock on the wall.\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the child think the clock was doing at first?\",\"options\":[\"Telling a story\",\"Only making noise\",\"Singing a song\",\"Sleeping\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'At that time, I thought the clock was only making noise.\'\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What parts of the clock did the child notice as they grew older?\",\"options\":[\"The glass and the frame\",\"The battery and the wires\",\"The numbers and hands\",\"The bells and the pendulum\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that as the child grew older, they began to notice its numbers and hands.\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the \'special language\' of the clock?\",\"options\":[\"Showing the time\",\"Making loud noises\",\"Changing colors\",\"Moving on the wall\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explains that the child understood the clock had a special language because it always showed the time.\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When does the clock remind the child to eat dinner?\",\"options\":[\"When the Sun rises\",\"When it is noon\",\"When the Sun sets\",\"When it is morning\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'When the Sun sets, the clock reminds me to eat my dinner.\'\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity does the clock help the child with in the morning?\",\"options\":[\"Going to bed\",\"Getting up\",\"Eating dinner\",\"Playing with friends\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'it tells me when to get up in the morning.\'\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does the clock help the child stay healthy and active?\",\"options\":[\"By playing music\",\"By showing pictures\",\"By helping the child follow a daily routine\",\"By running around the room\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the clock helps every day with tasks like waking up, school, and dinner, which keeps the child healthy and active.\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What are the two types of hands mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The fast hand and the slow hand\",\"The big hand and the small hand\",\"The red hand and the black hand\",\"The long hand and the short hand\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically names \'The big hand and the small hand.\'\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the child call the clock a \'good friend\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it talks to the child\",\"Because it plays games\",\"Because it helps and reminds the child of important times\",\"Because it looks like a person\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The clock is a friend because it reminds the child when to study, play, eat, and sleep.\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the child looking at while sitting on the floor?\",\"options\":[\"A window\",\"A clock on the wall\",\"A toy on the ground\",\"A picture book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a small child looking up at a round clock hanging on the wall.\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/041_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the clock helping the child to do at night?\",\"options\":[\"Go to school\",\"Play with friends\",\"Go to bed\",\"Eat breakfast\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the child sleeping in bed at night, which the text says the clock reminds them to do.\",\"topic\":\"My Friend, the Clock\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/042_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, at what time does the person wake up?\",\"options\":[\"7 a.m.\",\"8 a.m.\",\"9 a.m.\",\"6 p.m.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'I wake up at 7 a.m.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list means to make someone think of something again?\",\"options\":[\"often\",\"reminds\",\"healthy\",\"moved\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'reminds\' means to cause someone to remember something.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which time follows 7 a.m. in the sequence provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"8 a.m.\",\"9 a.m.\",\"7.15 a.m.\",\"6 p.m.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists 7.15 a.m. immediately after the 7 a.m. activity.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to the way people speak or write to each other?\",\"options\":[\"noise\",\"language\",\"clock\",\"moved\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Language is the method of human communication using words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the person wakes up at 7 a.m., which time is mentioned for later in the evening?\",\"options\":[\"7.15 a.m.\",\"8 a.m.\",\"9 a.m.\",\"6 p.m.\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"In the list of times, 6 p.m. is the only time indicating the evening.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to the object that tells us the time?\",\"options\":[\"clock\",\"noise\",\"active\",\"showed\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A clock is a device used to measure and show time.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the word from the list that refers to a meal usually eaten at the end of the day.\",\"options\":[\"often\",\"notice\",\"dinner\",\"moved\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Dinner is the word in the list that refers to a meal.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the time difference between the first two times mentioned (7 a.m. and 7.15 a.m.)?\",\"options\":[\"5 minutes\",\"10 minutes\",\"15 minutes\",\"20 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The difference between 7:00 and 7:15 is 15 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list describes being busy and full of energy?\",\"options\":[\"active\",\"healthy\",\"often\",\"dinner\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Being active means engaging in physical activity or being energetic.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list means to have become aware of or seen something?\",\"options\":[\"notice\",\"noise\",\"language\",\"clock\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To notice something means to observe or become aware of it.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21399,11,3,'English','en','Library','[\"A library is a quiet place where many books are kept.\",\"Books in a library include story books, poetry books, newspapers and magazines.\",\"You can read books in the library or borrow them to take home.\",\"A librarian helps you find the books you want.\",\"Libraries encourage children to read more and become good readers.\",\"When using a library, keep it clean: no folding corners, no tearing pages.\",\"Always return books on time so others can use them.\",\"Use a bookmark instead of folding the corners of a page.\",\"Keep your bags outside the library to keep the place tidy.\",\"Speak quietly in the library – it is a place of silence.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what kind of place is a library?\",\"options\":[\"A noisy and dark place\",\"A quiet and happy place\",\"A place to play games\",\"A place to buy food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that a library is a quiet and happy place.\",\"topic\":\"About the Library\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the library called on the other hand?\",\"options\":[\"A house of toys\",\"A house of books\",\"A house of music\",\"A house of flowers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the library as a \'house of books\'.\",\"topic\":\"About the Library\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these items is NOT mentioned as being in the library?\",\"options\":[\"Story books\",\"Poetry books\",\"Video games\",\"Newspapers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions story books, poetry books, newspapers, and magazines, but not video games.\",\"topic\":\"About the Library\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text say we can do with books besides reading them there?\",\"options\":[\"We can sell them\",\"We can borrow them\",\"We can draw in them\",\"We can keep them forever\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that we can also borrow books and take them home for some days.\",\"topic\":\"About the Library\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you cannot find a book you want, who does the text say will help you?\",\"options\":[\"A friend\",\"A librarian\",\"A driver\",\"A shopkeeper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that a librarian helps us to find the books.\",\"topic\":\"About the Library\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the girl in the blue dress doing at the bookshelf?\",\"options\":[\"Cleaning the shelf\",\"Reaching for a book\",\"Painting the shelf\",\"Closing the door\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows the girl reaching out to touch or take a book from the shelf.\",\"topic\":\"About the Library\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/043_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where are the children sitting to read their books?\",\"options\":[\"On the floor\",\"On top of the bookshelves\",\"At a large table\",\"Under the chairs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows several children sitting around a large table reading books.\",\"topic\":\"About the Library\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/043_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How does the library help a child who loves reading?\",\"options\":[\"It helps them sleep better\",\"It helps them be a good reader\",\"It helps them run faster\",\"It helps them sing songs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying the library helps us to be a good reader.\",\"topic\":\"About the Library\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why would a child want to borrow a book?\",\"options\":[\"To give it to a stranger\",\"To take it home for some days to read\",\"To hide it from the librarian\",\"To use it as a pillow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that we borrow books to take them home for some days.\",\"topic\":\"About the Library\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of a library according to the passage?\",\"options\":[\"To provide a place to talk loudly\",\"To motivate us to read more\",\"To sell magazines and newspapers\",\"To store toys for children\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the library motivates us to read more.\",\"topic\":\"About the Library\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"On which day is the Book Festival event scheduled?\",\"options\":[\"Friday\",\"Saturday\",\"Monday\",\"Sunday\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Arnav says the Book Festival is on Friday.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"At what time does the Book Festival start in the morning?\",\"options\":[\"9.30 a.m.\",\"10.00 a.m.\",\"11.30 a.m.\",\"12.00 noon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the event starts at 10 O\' clock in the morning.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to the person who works in a library?\",\"options\":[\"Reader\",\"Librarian\",\"Teacher\",\"Student\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'librarian\' is included in the vocabulary list for the library topic.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the library rules, what should you use instead of folding the corners of pages?\",\"options\":[\"A pencil\",\"A piece of tape\",\"A bookmark\",\"A ruler\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text advises to \'Use a bookmark instead of folding corners\'.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where should students keep their bags when they enter the library?\",\"options\":[\"On the reading table\",\"Under the chair\",\"Outside the library\",\"In the cupboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"One of the library rules mentioned is \'Keep your bags outside\'.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct way to handle library books according to the rules?\",\"options\":[\"Fold the pages to remember where you stopped\",\"Handle books carefully and do not tear pages\",\"Keep the books for as long as you want\",\"Eat while reading the books\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The rules state to \'Handle books carefully\' and \'Do not tear or fold pages\'.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Purvi wants to reach school on time as suggested by Arnav, when should she arrive?\",\"options\":[\"10.00 a.m.\",\"9.30 a.m.\",\"11.30 a.m.\",\"12.00 noon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Arnav mentions that they should reach school by 9.30 a.m.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student only wants to attend the prize distribution, what time should they be ready?\",\"options\":[\"10.00 a.m.\",\"9.30 a.m.\",\"11.30 a.m.\",\"12.00 noon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the prize distribution will start at 11.30 a.m.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the start and end times mentioned, how many hours will the Book Festival last?\",\"options\":[\"1 hour\",\"2 hours\",\"3 hours\",\"4 hours\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The event starts at 10 a.m. and lasts till 12 noon, which is a duration of 2 hours.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these events happens last during the Book Festival day?\",\"options\":[\"Reaching school\",\"The event starts\",\"Prize distribution starts\",\"The event ends\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The event ends at 12 noon, which is after the start (10 a.m.) and prize distribution (11.30 a.m.).\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the name of the boy who is wearing glasses?\",\"options\":[\"Arnav\",\"Purvi\",\"Librarian\",\"Reader\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the figure, the girl greets the boy by saying \'Hi Arnav!\', identifying him as Arnav.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/045_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the two children doing?\",\"options\":[\"Reading books silently\",\"Having a conversation\",\"Folding book corners\",\"Putting bags outside\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows speech bubbles indicating that Purvi and Arnav are talking to each other.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation: Book Festival\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/045_101.jpg\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21400,11,3,'English','en','Punctuation Friends','[\"Full Stop (.) ends a sentence.\",\"Capital Letter starts a sentence.\",\"Comma (,) gives a small pause.\",\"Question Mark (?) ends a question.\",\"Use punctuation correctly to make meaning clear.\",\"Write sentences with a capital letter at the start.\",\"Add a full stop at the end of a statement.\",\"Add a question mark at the end of a question.\",\"Use commas to separate items in a list.\",\"Punctuation helps readers understand the text.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does a Capital Letter do in a sentence?\",\"options\":[\"It ends the sentence\",\"It starts the sentence\",\"It asks a question\",\"It takes a tiny pause\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states that a Capital Letter starts the sentence.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which punctuation mark takes a \'tiny pause\'?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Question Mark\",\"Comma\",\"Capital Letter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the poem, a Comma takes a tiny pause.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does a Full Stop say at the end of a sentence?\",\"options\":[\"“Now we end”\",\"“Who? What? Why?”\",\"“Stand up tall”\",\"“Take a breath”\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions that a Full Stop says, \'Now we end\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which mark is described as \'bending its head\'?\",\"options\":[\"Comma\",\"Full Stop\",\"Capital Letter\",\"Question Mark\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem says a Question Mark bends its head to ask questions.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to ask \'Why?\', which punctuation mark should you use?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Comma\",\"Question Mark\",\"Capital Letter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Question Mark is used for asking \'Who? What? Why?\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does a Comma help us while reading?\",\"options\":[\"It helps the clause and rests our breath\",\"It makes the words very big\",\"It finishes the whole story\",\"It stands up very tall\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says the Comma rests our breath and helps the clause.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the \'finish\' of a sentence marked?\",\"options\":[\"At the start with a Capital Letter\",\"In the middle with a Comma\",\"At the end with a Full Stop\",\"Everywhere with a Question Mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Full Stop is described as the \'finish\' in the poem.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of all these punctuation marks working together?\",\"options\":[\"They make reading bright\",\"They make the sentence long\",\"They make the words quiet\",\"They hide the meaning\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem states that together they make reading bright.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, how do punctuation marks help words?\",\"options\":[\"They help words to sound just right\",\"They help words to stay small\",\"They help words to run away\",\"They help words to look dark\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says they help words to sound just right.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which punctuation mark is described as \'standing up tall\'?\",\"options\":[\"Comma\",\"Full Stop\",\"Capital Letter\",\"Question Mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem begins by saying a Capital Letter stands up tall.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many groups should the teacher divide the class into?\",\"options\":[\"Two groups\",\"Three groups\",\"Four groups\",\"Five groups\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher instructions state to divide the class into four groups.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which couplet should all the groups sing together?\",\"options\":[\"The first couplet\",\"The second couplet\",\"The middle couplet\",\"The last couplet\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says to ask all the groups to sing the last couplet together.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who guides each group to sing the first couplet?\",\"options\":[\"The students\",\"The teacher\",\"The principal\",\"The monitor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions state the teacher should guide each group to sing the first couplet.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first task students are asked to do in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Sing a song\",\"Write a story\",\"Read and identify punctuation marks\",\"Draw a ball\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first instruction in the text is \'Read and identify the punctuation marks\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'The sun is shining\', what kind of punctuation mark is missing at the end?\",\"options\":[\"Comma\",\"Question mark\",\"Full stop\",\"Exclamation mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A statement like \'The sun is shining\' requires a full stop at the end.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The sentence \'Where is my ball\' is asking something. Which mark should be placed at the end?\",\"options\":[\"Full stop (.)\",\"Comma (,)\",\"Question mark (?)\",\"Hyphen (-)\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sentences that ask a question, like \'Where is my ball\', end with a question mark.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'I like apples oranges and bananas\', where should a comma be placed to separate the items?\",\"options\":[\"After \'I\'\",\"After \'apples\'\",\"After \'bananas\'\",\"Before \'like\'\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Commas are used to separate items in a list, so one is needed after \'apples\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sentences from the text would correctly end with a question mark?\",\"options\":[\"The sun is shining\",\"I like apples oranges and bananas\",\"Where is my ball\",\"Divide the class\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Where is my ball\' is the only sentence in the list that asks a question.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the sentence \'I like apples oranges and bananas\' need punctuation marks between the words?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is a question\",\"Because it lists different fruits\",\"Because it is a very loud sentence\",\"Because it is the start of a song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Punctuation like commas are needed to separate multiple items in a list.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the sentence \'The sun is shining\'. Why is a question mark NOT suitable for this sentence?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is not asking a question\",\"Because the sun is too hot\",\"Because it is a short sentence\",\"Because it has the word \'sun\'\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A question mark is only used for questions; \'The sun is shining\' is a statement of fact.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21401,11,3,'English','en','Hide and Seek','[\"Hide and Seek is a game where one person hides and the others try to find them.\",\"The seeker counts to a number (like ten) before looking for the hidden person.\",\"In the story, the characters are animals: Hen, Crow, Rabbit, Squirrel, Cat, Fox, Calf, etc.\",\"The seeker asks questions like “Where is she?” or “Can you see a pair of feet?” to help find the hidden one.\",\"The story shows how the seeker talks to different animals to find the Hen.\",\"The sentences in the story are simple and use short phrases and questions.\",\"The characters can be renamed with human friends’ names to practice speaking.\",\"The story can be acted out to make learning fun and interactive.\",\"Students should practice writing short sentences with punctuation marks like commas and question marks.\",\"They can also retell the story using different names to show understanding.\",\"The game helps develop listening, speaking, and observation skills.\",\"It also teaches counting and following instructions.\",\"Students can draw pictures of the game or the animals to show what they learned.\",\"The teacher can ask students to write a short story about a game they play.\",\"The story should have a clear beginning, middle, and end.\",\"Students should use simple words and correct punctuation.\",\"They can also discuss the story in small groups to practice speaking.\",\"They can present the story orally to the class.\",\"These activities help build language and social skills.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who suggested playing the game of \'Hide and Seek\'?\",\"options\":[\"Calf\",\"Hen\",\"Crow\",\"Rabbit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'“Let’s play hide and seek,” says Hen.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Up to what number did the Calf say he would count?\",\"options\":[\"Five\",\"Seven\",\"Ten\",\"Twelve\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Calf says, \'I’ll count to ten.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What clue did the Calf see that made him find the Crow?\",\"options\":[\"A red comb\",\"A black beak\",\"Long ears\",\"A furry tail\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Calf asks, \'Oh! A black beak?\' before finding the Crow.\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which two animals are shown talking to each other at the beginning of the story?\",\"options\":[\"A Hen and a Calf\",\"A Crow and a Rabbit\",\"A Cat and a Fox\",\"A Squirrel and a Hen\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first figure shows the Hen and the Calf interacting as they start the game.\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/048_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the Calf look when he saw \'long brown ears\'?\",\"options\":[\"Behind a basket\",\"In a rose garden\",\"Inside a tent\",\"Under a sheet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Look! A tent! Is Hen in the tent? Can you see long brown ears?\'\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal was found under the \'stripy sheet\'?\",\"options\":[\"Rabbit\",\"Cat\",\"Squirrel\",\"Fox\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Calf has found a stripy sheet... It’s a Squirrel.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which animal is shown with a large, bushy tail standing near the Crow and the Calf?\",\"options\":[\"Cat\",\"Fox\",\"Rabbit\",\"Squirrel\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The second figure shows the Squirrel with its distinct bushy tail alongside the other animals.\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/049_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What did the Calf see behind the basket?\",\"options\":[\"A pair of feet\",\"A furry tail\",\"A stripy nose\",\"A black beak\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks, \'May be Hen is behind this basket. Can you see a furry tail?\'\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal was hiding behind the rose garden?\",\"options\":[\"Fox\",\"Cat\",\"Rabbit\",\"Crow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text asks, \'Who’s behind this rose garden?\' and then mentions the Fox.\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see a \'stripy nose\' behind the rose garden, which animal have you found according to the story?\",\"options\":[\"The Hen\",\"The Fox\",\"The Cat\",\"The Squirrel\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text associates the \'stripy nose\' behind the rose garden with the Fox.\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the ending of the text, what is the result of the Calf\'s search?\",\"options\":[\"He finds the Hen in the tent.\",\"He finds the Hen behind the basket.\",\"He still cannot find where the Hen went.\",\"The Hen was hiding in the rose garden.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text ends with \'Still no Hen! Where did she go? Calf can’t guess.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal offers to lead the group to a picnic spot?\",\"options\":[\"Squirrel\",\"Fox\",\"Rabbit\",\"Crow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Fox says, \'I’ll lead you to our picnic spot.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hide and Seek\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the young one of a cow called?\",\"options\":[\"calf\",\"chick\",\"cub\",\"puppy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that cow - calf.\",\"topic\":\"Animals and their young ones\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A young one of a dog is called a _____.\",\"options\":[\"kid\",\"foal\",\"puppy\",\"bunny\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that dog - puppy.\",\"topic\":\"Animals and their young ones\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these animals has a young one called a \'kid\'?\",\"options\":[\"horse\",\"goat\",\"squirrel\",\"fox\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text matches goat with kid.\",\"topic\":\"Animals and their young ones\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which two animals have young ones both called \'chick\'?\",\"options\":[\"cow and hen\",\"hen and crow\",\"fox and squirrel\",\"rabbit and dog\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists both hen - chick and crow - chick.\",\"topic\":\"Animals and their young ones\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see a \'foal\' in a field, which adult animal is its parent?\",\"options\":[\"rabbit\",\"horse\",\"cow\",\"goat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that a foal is the young one of a horse.\",\"topic\":\"Animals and their young ones\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A small \'kit\' is playing in a tree. Which animal is it?\",\"options\":[\"squirrel\",\"fox\",\"crow\",\"dog\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that squirrel - kit.\",\"topic\":\"Animals and their young ones\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the pairs: fox-cub and rabbit-bunny. Which animal\'s young one is a \'cub\'?\",\"options\":[\"rabbit\",\"fox\",\"squirrel\",\"goat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly pairs fox with cub.\",\"topic\":\"Animals and their young ones\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the young one of a rabbit called?\",\"options\":[\"kit\",\"foal\",\"bunny\",\"calf\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that rabbit - bunny.\",\"topic\":\"Animals and their young ones\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word correctly matches the animal \'fox\'?\",\"options\":[\"chick\",\"cub\",\"kid\",\"puppy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text matches fox with cub.\",\"topic\":\"Animals and their young ones\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the list, which pair is correctly matched?\",\"options\":[\"squirrel - foal\",\"crow - chick\",\"cow - kid\",\"goat - bunny\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text confirms that crow - chick is the correct pair.\",\"topic\":\"Animals and their young ones\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21402,11,3,'English','en','Word Family - IV','[\"Word family means words that share the same base sound or spelling.\",\"In this chapter we learn the word family that starts with the letters L, D, and T.\",\"All words in this family have the same short vowel sound \\/ɒ\\/ like in \\\"hot\\\" or \\\"pot\\\".\",\"Common words: dog, fog, jog, log, hot, pot, not, cot, got, dot, top, hop, rod, box, fox, job, boy, joy, toy, lot.\",\"You can make new words by adding a letter at the start or end of the base word.\",\"Example: add ‘b’ to ‘ox’ to get ‘box’ or add ‘t’ to ‘op’ to get ‘top’.\",\"The words are usually written in the same order in the book: dog, fog, jog, log, hot, pot, not, cot, got, dot, top, hop, rod, box, fox, job, boy, joy, toy, lot.\",\"When you read them aloud, keep the short vowel sound the same in each word.\",\"If you see a picture, match the picture with the correct word from the family.\",\"Practice by saying each word and thinking of a sentence that uses it.\",\"Remember: the word family helps you learn many words at once.\",\"Use flashcards: write the word on one side and a picture on the other.\",\"Try to find other words that fit the same family in your own books.\",\"Ask the teacher to check your pronunciation of each word.\",\"Keep repeating the words until you can say them quickly and correctly.\",\"Doing this will help you read and write better in English.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where is the big red box placed?\",\"options\":[\"On the floor\",\"On the cot\",\"In the bag\",\"Under the bed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'a big red box on the cot\'.\",\"topic\":\"What is in the big red box?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who got the big red box?\",\"options\":[\"A girl\",\"A dog\",\"A boy\",\"A fox\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'a boy got the big red box\'.\",\"topic\":\"What is in the big red box?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What color is the box mentioned in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text repeatedly describes it as a \'big red box\'.\",\"topic\":\"What is in the big red box?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these animals was NOT guessed to be in the box?\",\"options\":[\"A dog\",\"A fox\",\"A cat\",\"A pot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks about a dog, a fox, and a pot, but never mentions a cat.\",\"topic\":\"What is in the big red box?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is actually inside the big red box?\",\"options\":[\"A pot\",\"A dog\",\"A toy\",\"A fox\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes with \'There is a toy in the big red box\'.\",\"topic\":\"What is in the big red box?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"From the \'Word Family\' list, which word rhymes with \'hot\'?\",\"options\":[\"dog\",\"pot\",\"box\",\"boy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the list, \'hot\' and \'pot\' belong to the same rhyming group.\",\"topic\":\"What is in the big red box?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list rhymes with \'toy\'?\",\"options\":[\"top\",\"joy\",\"log\",\"rod\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the list, \'boy\', \'joy\', and \'toy\' are grouped together as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"What is in the big red box?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the reading section, what was the very first guess made about what is in the box?\",\"options\":[\"A fox\",\"A pot\",\"A toy\",\"A dog\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The first question asked after \'What is in the big red box?\' is \'A dog?\'.\",\"topic\":\"What is in the big red box?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The text says \'a big red box\'. What does the word \'big\' tell us about the box?\",\"options\":[\"Its color\",\"Its size\",\"Its weight\",\"Its name\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Big is an adjective used to describe the size of the box.\",\"topic\":\"What is in the big red box?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Word Family\' list has the same ending sound as \'box\'?\",\"options\":[\"fox\",\"boy\",\"log\",\"dot\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the list, \'box\' and \'fox\' are grouped together because they share the same ending sound.\",\"topic\":\"What is in the big red box?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is paired with \'log\' in the first list?\",\"options\":[\"boy\",\"dog\",\"fox\",\"pot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'log dog\' as a pair.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is paired with \'box\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"fox\",\"top\",\"rod\",\"joy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'fox box\' as a pair.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'For the Teacher\' section, how should learners read the words?\",\"options\":[\"Very fast\",\"Silently\",\"With proper stress patterns\",\"Only once\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note specifically mentions using proper stress patterns.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher encourage learners to do?\",\"options\":[\"Write the words ten times\",\"Read aloud words and phrases\",\"Draw pictures of a dog\",\"Memorize the spellings only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states to encourage learners to read aloud words and phrases.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are reading \'top hop\', which vowel sound are you practicing?\",\"options\":[\"The \'a\' sound\",\"The \'e\' sound\",\"The \'o\' sound\",\"The \'u\' sound\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Both \'top\' and \'hop\' contain the \'o\' vowel sound common in this word family.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list rhymes with \'toy\'?\",\"options\":[\"boy\",\"box\",\"fog\",\"rod\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'boy\' and \'joy\' and \'top\' and \'toy\', showing \'boy\' and \'toy\' belong to the same sound group.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the pair \'cop cot\'. What is the same at the beginning of both words?\",\"options\":[\"They end with \'t\'\",\"They start with the letter \'c\'\",\"They rhyme perfectly\",\"They have no \'o\' sound\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both \'cop\' and \'cot\' begin with the letter \'c\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs from the text rhymes?\",\"options\":[\"fog fox\",\"rod rob\",\"top hop\",\"cop cot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the list \'top hop\', both words end with the same \'-op\' sound.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is paired with \'rod\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"rob\",\"cot\",\"pot\",\"dog\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'rod rob\' as a pair.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'proper stress patterns\', what does the teacher want the students to focus on?\",\"options\":[\"Writing neatly\",\"Speaking correctly with the right emphasis\",\"Drawing lines between words\",\"Counting the number of letters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Stress patterns refer to the emphasis placed on sounds while speaking.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21403,11,3,'English','en','Diwali, the Festival of Lights','[\"Diwali is known as the Festival of Lights.\",\"It celebrates the victory of good over evil.\",\"People light lamps and candles to remove darkness.\",\"Children enjoy sparklers and fireworks during Diwali.\",\"Families exchange gifts and sweets with love.\",\"The festival brings happiness and removes sorrow.\",\"Rangoli designs are made at the entrance of homes.\",\"Diwali is a time for family gatherings and prayers.\",\"Clay forts are sometimes made as part of Diwali activities.\",\"Health care during Diwali includes avoiding loud noise and fire hazards.\",\"Making greeting cards is a common Diwali activity.\",\"Listening to poems and songs helps understand the festival better.\",\"The festival teaches values like sharing, kindness, and joy.\",\"Diwali is celebrated by people of all ages with enthusiasm.\",\"It is one of the most important festivals in India.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what is Diwali known as?\",\"options\":[\"The festival of colors\",\"The festival of lights\",\"The festival of flowers\",\"The festival of sounds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem explicitly states, \'The festival of lights Diwali has come.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do the children have in their hands while they are out?\",\"options\":[\"Gifts\",\"Sweets\",\"Sparklers\",\"Lamps\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Children are out with sparklers in hands.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who wrote the poem \'Diwali, the Festival of Lights\'?\",\"options\":[\"A. C. Sharma\",\"R. K. Narayan\",\"Balbharati\",\"J. K. Rowling\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The author\'s name, A. C. Sharma, is mentioned at the end of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The poem says the fireworks sound like which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"Thunder in the sky\",\"Musical bands\",\"Loud drums\",\"Cracking sticks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'The fireworks sound like musical bands.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the festival of Diwali show a victory of?\",\"options\":[\"Rich over poor\",\"New over old\",\"Good over evil\",\"Strength over weakness\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Victory of good over evil it shows.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the elders exchanging with each other?\",\"options\":[\"Sparklers and lamps\",\"Gifts and sweets\",\"Books and pens\",\"Flowers and fruits\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows adults handing over gift boxes and a plate of sweets (ladoos) to one another.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/052_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the food items listed in the 