lustration shows four children (two boys and two girls) building and decorating the fort.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s listen and talk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/054_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and read\' list is the opposite of \'happiness\'?\",\"options\":[\"Delight\",\"Victory\",\"Sorrow\",\"Festival\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sorrow is the opposite of happiness in the provided vocabulary list.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s listen and talk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Zara wants to make the fort look \'attractive\', what should she do based on the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Leave it plain and brown\",\"Use only cardboard\",\"Decorate it with flags, diyas, and plants\",\"Only use water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The conversation suggests that decorations and plants make the fort look attractive.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s listen and talk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text refers to things that people light up during Diwali?\",\"options\":[\"Streets\",\"History\",\"Fireworks\",\"Tools\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Fireworks are mentioned in the vocabulary list and are items lit during festivals.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s listen and talk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of using cardboard in this activity?\",\"options\":[\"To sow seeds in it\",\"To use as a material for the fort structure\",\"To paint the flags\",\"To light up the fort\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Cardboard is listed as a material needed to build the fort.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s listen and talk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is a school subject listed in the text?\",\"options\":[\"nature\",\"Mathematics\",\"seashore\",\"husk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Mathematics is listed as a subject in the House of Words.\",\"topic\":\"House of Words - 2\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a young cow called in the word list?\",\"option