sure?\",\"options\":[\"delight\",\"angry\",\"scared\",\"powerful\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Delight is a feeling of great pleasure or happiness.\",\"topic\":\"House of Words - 2\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes the shape of a circle or a ball?\",\"options\":[\"hanging\",\"round\",\"easy\",\"active\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Round is the word used to describe a circular shape.\",\"topic\":\"House of Words - 2\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of our national flag as mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Tiranga\",\"Rainbow\",\"Saffron\",\"Ashoka Chakra\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem starts by saying \'Our Tiranga is flying high and high\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tiranga\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which color in the flag stands for \'courage, bold and bright\'?\",\"options\":[\"White\",\"Green\",\"Saffron\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Saffron for courage, bold and bright\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tiranga\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what does the color white represent?\",\"options\":[\"Growth and nature\",\"Peace and truth\",\"Courage and boldness\",\"Love and pride\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'White for peace and truth so right\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tiranga\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where is the Ashoka Chakra placed on the flag?\",\"options\":[\"On the saffron band\",\"On the green band\",\"In the middle of the white band\",\"At the top of the pole\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the Ashoka Chakra in the center of the white strip.\",\"topic\":\"Tiranga\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/056_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what action are the children performing to show respect?\",\"options\":[\"Running\",\"Saluting\",\"Sitting\",\"Sleeping\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows children with their hands raised in a salute to the flag.\",\"topic\":\"Tiranga\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/056_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to show \'growth and nature\'s way\' in a drawing of the flag, which color should they use?\",\"options\":[\"Saffron\",\"White\",\"Green\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions \'Green for growth and nature\'s way\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tiranga\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, which of these is NOT one of the three main colors of the Tiranga?\",\"options\":[\"Saffron\",\"White\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem lists Saffron, white, and green as the colors of the flag.\",\"topic\":\"Tiranga\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What do we sing every day with love and pride?\",\"options\":[\"A story\",\"Our anthem\",\"A lullaby\",\"A prayer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states \'We sing our anthem every day, With love and pride\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tiranga\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the wheel mentioned in the poem that flows with the flag?\",\"options\":[\"Dharma Chakra\",\"Ashoka Chakra\",\"Time Wheel\",\"Sun Wheel\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions \'With Ashoka Chakra as it flows\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tiranga\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the poet describe the sky where the Tiranga is flying?\",\"options\":[\"Dark and cloudy\",\"Bright and sunny\",\"Lovely sky\",\"Rainy sky\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says the flag is flying \'in a lovely sky!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tiranga\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is listed in the \'Listen and repeat\' section?\",\"options\":[\"sky\",\"saffron\",\"flows\",\"bright\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'saffron\' is explicitly listed in the \'Listen and repeat\' section of the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very first word mentioned in the \'Listen and repeat\' list?\",\"options\":[\"courage\",\"truth\",\"Tiranga\",\"anthem\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text begins the list with the word \'Tiranga\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'Read and enjoy\' section, which word rhymes with \'sky\'?\",\"options\":[\"high\",\"bright\",\"way\",\"shows\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'high-sky\' as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'flows\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"day\",\"right\",\"shows\",\"bold\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'shows-flows\' together in the rhyming section.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'way\' rhymes with \'day\', which other word from the text also rhymes with them?\",\"options\":[\"sky\",\"say\",\"bold\",\"peace\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'way-day-say\' as a group of rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list is NOT a quality or an action like \'courage\' or \'salute\'?\",\"options\":[\"truth\",\"peace\",\"bold\",\"Tiranga\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Tiranga is the name of the flag, while the others are qualities or actions mentioned in the list.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'right\' in the \'Read and enjoy\' section?\",\"options\":[\"bright\",\"high\",\"flows\",\"truth\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides the pair \'bright-right\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words belongs to the \'Read and enjoy\' section rather than the \'Listen and repeat\' section?\",\"options\":[\"anthem\",\"saffron\",\"sky\",\"salute\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Sky\' is part of the rhyming words in section c, while the others are in section b.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the rhyming patterns in the text, how many words are grouped to rhyme with \'way\'?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text groups two words (day, say) to rhyme with \'way\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list describes a feeling of being brave?\",\"options\":[\"courage\",\"anthem\",\"saffron\",\"truth\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Courage is the word in the list that represents bravery.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21404,11,3,'English','en','Word Family - V','[\"Word family V words have the same vowel sound and end with the letter \'u\' or \'n\' or \'b\' etc.\",\"Examples: cup, cut, fun, gun, gum, mud, hut, tub, nut, pup, run, rub, rug, jug, sun, sum.\",\"All words in this family rhyme with each other.\",\"Students should read aloud to hear the common sound.\",\"Use picture clues to guess the word (e.g., a cup picture → cup).\",\"Write the word after the picture to practice spelling.\",\"Make a word family chart: write the base word and add different endings (e.g., run, ran, running).\",\"Use the words in simple sentences: “I have a cup.” “The sun is hot.”\",\"Play matching games: match picture to word on the board.\",\"Ask students to think of another word that fits the family (e.g., “funny” is not in this family).\",\"Encourage students to use the words in their own sentences.\",\"Use flashcards with the word on one side and picture on the other.\",\"Repeat the words daily to build memory.\",\"Teach that word families help in learning new words quickly.\",\"Use the family to build a story: “Raju ran to the sun.”\",\"Review the words at the end of the week to reinforce learning.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is excited to celebrate her birthday according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Sophia\",\"Mini\",\"Kavya\",\"Susan\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Kavya is excited to celebrate her birthday.\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What ceremony does Nawaz want to invite his friends to?\",\"options\":[\"Birthday party\",\"Christmas party\",\"Housewarming ceremony\",\"Wedding ceremony\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Nawaz wants to invite his friends to his housewarming ceremony because he has a new house.\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the story \'Read aloud\', who did not run?\",\"options\":[\"Raju\",\"Mini\",\"Shantanu\",\"Chetana\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says, \'Mini did not run.\'\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Raju do with the bun after he got it?\",\"options\":[\"He threw it\",\"He cut it\",\"He hid it\",\"He lost it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Raju cut the bun.\'\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Sophia decide to invite her friends for a party?\",\"options\":[\"She has a new house\",\"It is her birthday\",\"Christmas is coming soon\",\"She wants to run a race\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says Sophia invites them because Christmas is coming soon.\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does Nawaz feel about having a new house?\",\"options\":[\"He is sad\",\"He is very happy\",\"He is angry\",\"He is tired\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'Nawaz has a new house. He is very happy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Word Family\' list correctly completes this sentence: \'The ___ is very hot in the afternoon.\'?\",\"options\":[\"mud\",\"sun\",\"tub\",\"pup\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Among the word family list, \'sun\' is the object that is hot.\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used at the end of the invitation cards to show who sent them?\",\"options\":[\"Dear\",\"Please\",\"From\",\"Come\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In all three invitation examples, the sender\'s name follows the word \'From\'.\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, who is the invitation card addressed to?\",\"options\":[\"Kavya\",\"Shantanu\",\"Nawaz\",\"Chetana\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The card in the figure starts with \'Dear Shantanu\', meaning it is for him.\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/059_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the main reason for the invitation?\",\"options\":[\"A Christmas party\",\"A housewarming ceremony\",\"A birthday party\",\"A school trip\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text in the figure says, \'It is my birthday. I am having a birthday party.\'\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/059_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the story, what was the result of Raju cutting the bun?\",\"options\":[\"Only Raju got a bun\",\"Mini did not get a bun\",\"Both Raju and Mini got a bun\",\"The bun was lost\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"After Raju cut the bun, the text says \'Raju got a bun. Mini got a bun.\', meaning they both received one.\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the common purpose of the messages written by Kavya, Nawaz, and Sophia?\",\"options\":[\"To tell a story about a bun\",\"To invite their friends to join them\",\"To practice their writing\",\"To ask for birthday gifts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"All three characters are writing invitation cards to ask their friends to come to their respective celebrations.\",\"topic\":\"Invitation Cards\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where was Radha going when she met the man who had lost his eyesight?\",\"options\":[\"To the market\",\"To the school\",\"To the playground\",\"To the hospital\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Radha came across the man on her way to the school.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the man tapping on the road to help himself?\",\"options\":[\"His foot\",\"A stone\",\"His stick\",\"An umbrella\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the man kept tapping his stick on the road.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was it difficult for the man to cross the road?\",\"options\":[\"The road was too long\",\"He could not see\",\"He was in a hurry\",\"It was raining heavily\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he lost his eyesight and Radha realized crossing was difficult for a man who could not see.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how is Radha helping the man?\",\"options\":[\"She is giving him a stick\",\"She is holding his hand and helping him cross\",\"She is calling for a bus\",\"She is showing him the way to the school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Radha holding the man\'s arm\\/hand to guide him across the zebra crossing.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/060_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How did the man feel after Radha helped him cross the road?\",\"options\":[\"He felt scared\",\"He felt angry\",\"He felt very happy\",\"He felt tired\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the man thanked her and felt very happy.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who was watching Radha while she was helping the man?\",\"options\":[\"Her mother\",\"Her friends\",\"Her headmistress\",\"A shopkeeper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Radha\'s headmistress was watching this.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is happening to Radha in school?\",\"options\":[\"She is being punished\",\"She is being rewarded and praised\",\"She is writing an exam\",\"She is cleaning the classroom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Radha receiving a reward while others clap and praise her.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/060_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What reward did the headmistress give to Radha?\",\"options\":[\"A new bag\",\"A story book\",\"A gold medal\",\"A box of chocolates\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the headmistress gave her a story book as a reward.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The headmistress was proud of Radha for being helpful to a ______ person.\",\"options\":[\"Rich\",\"Divyang\",\"Young\",\"Strong\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the specific term \'Divyang person\' to describe the man Radha helped.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the story best describes Radha\'s action of helping the man?\",\"options\":[\"Kind gesture\",\"Fast running\",\"Loud talking\",\"Hard work\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text refers to Radha\'s help as a \'kind gesture\'.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Radha\'s teachers and friends praise her?\",\"options\":[\"Because she won a race\",\"Because she was helpful and kind\",\"Because she reached school early\",\"Because she finished her homework\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They praised her because of her kind gesture and helpfulness towards the blind man.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If you see someone struggling to walk, based on Radha\'s story, what should you do?\",\"options\":[\"Watch them and laugh\",\"Walk away quickly\",\"Rush towards them and help\",\"Tell them to be careful\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Radha rushed towards the man and helped him, which is the positive behavior taught in the story.\",\"topic\":\"Kind Radha\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does Diya say when she feels thirsty?\",\"options\":[\"I am thirsty.\",\"I want food.\",\"The tap is low.\",\"I am happy.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Diya explicitly states \'I am thirsty\' at the beginning of the conversation.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Diya need help to get water?\",\"options\":[\"The tap is broken.\",\"The tap is high above.\",\"She is afraid.\",\"She has no glass.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Diya mentions that \'The tap is high above\', which is why she needs help.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is Jason\'s response when Diya says \'Thank you so much\'?\",\"options\":[\"Hello!\",\"You are welcome!\",\"Please help.\",\"I am thirsty.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Jason politely replies \'You are welcome!\' after being thanked.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the conversation completion, why is Manav\'s bag difficult to carry?\",\"options\":[\"It is very heavy.\",\"It is very small.\",\"It is very light.\",\"It is very colorful.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Manav states \'My bag is very heavy\' because he is carrying many books.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word should Anushka use to offer help to Manav?\",\"options\":[\"Can I help you?\",\"Why I help you?\",\"Where I help you?\",\"Am I help you?\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The key words provided include \'Can\' and \'help\' to form the question \'Can I help you?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does Manav say to Anushka after she offers to carry some books?\",\"options\":[\"You are very kind. Thank you.\",\"You are very kind. Hi.\",\"You are very kind. Hello.\",\"You are very kind. Heavy.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"After receiving help, the appropriate response from the key words is \'Thank you\'.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to Manav, how does helping others make us feel?\",\"options\":[\"Sad\",\"Angry\",\"Happy\",\"Tired\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Manav says, \'Yes, Helping others makes us happy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is NOT in the \'Listen and repeat\' list provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Headmistress\",\"Gesture\",\"Thirsty\",\"Realised\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Thirsty\' appears in the dialogue, but it is not in the specific \'Listen and repeat\' word list.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Anushka think about helping others?\",\"options\":[\"It is a difficult task.\",\"It is good to help others.\",\"It is a reward.\",\"It is a gesture.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Anushka says, \'It is good to help others.\'\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list refers to a movement of the body to express an idea?\",\"options\":[\"Gesture\",\"Sight\",\"Task\",\"Reward\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A gesture is a movement of the body, usually the head or hands, to express a meaning.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which pair of words are used as greetings in the conversation completion?\",\"options\":[\"Please and Thank you\",\"Hello and Hi\",\"Can and Help\",\"Heavy and Kind\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Anushka and Manav greet each other using \'Hello\' and \'Hi\'.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the central idea of both conversations in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Reading many books\",\"Drinking water\",\"Helping people\",\"Going to school\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text focuses on Jason helping Diya and Anushka helping Manav.\",\"topic\":\"Conversation Completion\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Where has the butterfly been according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"To the garden\",\"To the forest\",\"To the house\",\"To the school\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'I have been to the garden\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the butterfly see in the garden?\",\"options\":[\"Green leaves\",\"Bright blossom\",\"Small stones\",\"Tall trees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The butterfly says, \'I saw bright blossom\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used in the poem to describe the \'scene\'?\",\"options\":[\"Bright\",\"Lovely\",\"Smiling\",\"Dear\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem describes it as \'such a lovely scene\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What were the blossoms doing when the butterfly saw them?\",\"options\":[\"Crying at me\",\"Hiding from me\",\"Smiling at me\",\"Sleeping near me\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I saw bright blossom, Smiling at me.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the butterfly do with the flowers?\",\"options\":[\"It ate them\",\"It played with them\",\"It picked them\",\"It watered them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The butterfly says, \'I played with flowers\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list rhymes with \'been\'?\",\"options\":[\"Lovely\",\"Blossom\",\"Scene\",\"Swinging\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the poem, \'been\' and \'scene\' are used as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, what was swinging with the air?\",\"options\":[\"The rain\",\"The garden\",\"The flowers\",\"The sun\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'I played with flowers Swinging with air.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When does the butterfly say it will see the person again?\",\"options\":[\"Before sunset\",\"After rain\",\"During lunch\",\"Tomorrow morning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The butterfly says, \'See you after rain.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is NOT in the \'Listen and repeat\' list at the end of the text?\",\"options\":[\"Butterfly\",\"Blossom\",\"Swinging\",\"Garden\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The list includes butterfly, lovely, scene, blossom, and swinging; garden is not in that specific list.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list refers to the insect mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Blossom\",\"Butterfly\",\"Lovely\",\"Scene\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The butterfly is the main subject and an insect.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and repeat\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two colors of butterflies are mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Red and Green\",\"Red and Blue\",\"Blue and Yellow\",\"Black and Red\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions \'Red, red butterfly\' and \'Blue, blue butterfly\'.\",\"topic\":\"Do you know?\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step in making a paper butterfly?\",\"options\":[\"Cut a curve\",\"Roll a strip\",\"Fold a square paper in half\",\"Stick it on the wall\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 1 in the instructions is to fold a square paper in half.\",\"topic\":\"Do you know?\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the riddle, what does the tiny, black and red creature love?\",\"options\":[\"Ice-cream\",\"Sugar\",\"Flowers\",\"Paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The riddle states, \'I am tiny, black and red. I love sugar.\'\",\"topic\":\"Do you know?\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do with the small strip of paper to make the body?\",\"options\":[\"Fold it\",\"Cut it\",\"Roll it\",\"Stick it on the wall\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 3 says to \'Roll a small strip for the body.\'\",\"topic\":\"Do you know?\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which season is described as having \'long bright days\' and \'ice-cream\'?\",\"options\":[\"Winter\",\"Rainy\",\"Summer\",\"Spring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Hot sun, ice-cream, and long bright days are characteristics of the summer season.\",\"topic\":\"Do you know?\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"After you cut a curve and open the paper, what part of the butterfly have you made?\",\"options\":[\"The body\",\"The wings\",\"The head\",\"The legs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 2 says to \'Cut a curve and open it to make wings.\'\",\"topic\":\"Do you know?\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very last step mentioned in the butterfly craft instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Decorate your butterfly\",\"Stick it on the wall\",\"Roll a strip\",\"Cut a curve\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 6, the final instruction, is to \'Stick it on the wall.\'\",\"topic\":\"Do you know?\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you have just finished sticking the body on the wings, what is the next step?\",\"options\":[\"Fold the paper\",\"Cut a curve\",\"Decorate your butterfly\",\"Roll a strip\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 4 is sticking the body, and Step 5 is decorating the butterfly.\",\"topic\":\"Do you know?\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What specific shape of paper is required to start making the butterfly?\",\"options\":[\"Circle\",\"Triangle\",\"Rectangle\",\"Square\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Step 1 specifically mentions using a \'square paper\'.\",\"topic\":\"Do you know?\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the description \'tiny, black and red\' and \'loves sugar\', who is the speaker?\",\"options\":[\"A butterfly\",\"An ant\",\"A bee\",\"A spider\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"An ant is tiny, can be black or red, and is known for loving sugar.\",\"topic\":\"Do you know?\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the sun like on the summer day described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Cold\",\"Hot\",\"Dim\",\"Hidden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'It was a summer day. The sun was hot.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the ant carrying?\",\"options\":[\"A leaf\",\"A flower\",\"A grain of rice\",\"A paper boat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'The ant was carrying a grain of rice.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the grasshopper sit?\",\"options\":[\"On a branch\",\"On a leaf\",\"On a stone\",\"In a puddle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'A grasshopper sat on a leaf.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the grasshopper feel on the summer day?\",\"options\":[\"He was sad and quiet\",\"He was happy and sang loudly\",\"He was tired and slept\",\"He was angry and jumped\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'He was happy. He sang loudly.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the ant tired?\",\"options\":[\"Because she was singing\",\"Because the grain was heavy\",\"Because it was raining\",\"Because she was jumping from leaf to leaf\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains, \'The grain was heavy. The ant was tired...\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the ant do even though she was tired?\",\"options\":[\"She sat on a leaf\",\"She started singing\",\"She did not stop\",\"She went to sleep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The ant was tired, but she did not stop.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the list of season items, which of these is used in the Summer season?\",\"options\":[\"Ear muff\",\"Sweater\",\"Sunglasses\",\"Rainbow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sunglasses are listed under the Summer season items in the text.\",\"topic\":\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you were out on the hot summer day described, which item from the list would protect your head?\",\"options\":[\"Scarf\",\"Puddles\",\"Hat\\/cap\",\"Paper boat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A hat\\/cap is listed as a summer item used for protection from the sun.\",\"topic\":\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the ant doing while the grasshopper is sitting?\",\"options\":[\"Sleeping in the grass\",\"Carrying a grain on its head\",\"Swimming in a puddle\",\"Eating mangoes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the ant carrying a large grain while the grasshopper sits on a leaf.\",\"topic\":\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/065_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what indicates that the weather is hot as described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The presence of a rainbow\",\"The grasshopper wearing a sweater\",\"The bright sun in the sky\",\"The ant playing with a paper boat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a bright sun, which matches the text \'The sun was hot.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant and the Grasshopper\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/065_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What was the weather like when the Grasshopper first spoke to the Ant?\",\"options\":[\"It was raining heavily\",\"It was a sunny day\",\"It was a cold night\",\"It was very cloudy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the Grasshopper asks why the Ant is working on \'such a sunny day\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Rainy Season\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound did the rain make when the rainy season arrived?\",\"options\":[\"Ding-dong\",\"Tick-tock\",\"Pitter-patter\",\"Boom-boom\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the sound of the rain as \'Pitter-patter, pitter-patter\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Rainy Season\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the sky full of when the rainy season came?\",\"options\":[\"Bright stars\",\"White birds\",\"Dark clouds\",\"The hot sun\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The sky was full of dark clouds\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Rainy Season\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the Ant say she could not play with the Grasshopper?\",\"options\":[\"She was feeling very sleepy\",\"She had to collect food for the rainy days\",\"She did not like the Grasshopper\",\"She wanted to go for a walk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Ant says, \'I must collect food. Soon the rainy season will come.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Rainy Season\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the Grasshopper want the Ant to do?\",\"options\":[\"Help him carry food\",\"Go to sleep in the grass\",\"Sing and play with him\",\"Build a house for the rain\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Grasshopper says, \'Come and sing with me. Come and play with me!\'\",\"topic\":\"The Rainy Season\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the Grasshopper think about the rainy season at the start?\",\"options\":[\"He thought it was far away\",\"He thought it would never come\",\"He was very scared of it\",\"He was already prepared for it\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The Grasshopper replied, \'The rainy season is far away.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Rainy Season\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the Ant\'s actions, what is the best way to prepare for the future?\",\"options\":[\"By playing all day in the sun\",\"By laughing at others who work\",\"By working hard and saving what is needed\",\"By waiting for the clouds to appear\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Ant prepares for the rainy season by working hard to collect food in advance.\",\"topic\":\"The Rainy Season\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the Ant had followed the Grasshopper\'s advice, what would she be doing on the sunny day?\",\"options\":[\"Collecting more food\",\"Singing and playing\",\"Building a new home\",\"Shaking her head\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Grasshopper invited the Ant to sing and play instead of working.\",\"topic\":\"The Rainy Season\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did the Ant respond when the Grasshopper told her she was worrying too much?\",\"options\":[\"She stopped working and played\",\"She started laughing with him\",\"She shook her head and kept on working\",\"She went home to sleep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The ant shook her head and kept on working.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Rainy Season\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the Ant\'s character in this story?\",\"options\":[\"Lazy\",\"Responsible\",\"Playful\",\"Careless\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Ant is responsible because she works hard to prepare for the coming rainy season.\",\"topic\":\"The Rainy Season\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What was the condition of the ground according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The ground was dry.\",\"The ground was wet.\",\"The ground was hot.\",\"The ground was hard.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'The ground was wet.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Grasshopper\'s Plea\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What were the fields full of?\",\"options\":[\"Flowers\",\"Grass\",\"Water\",\"Seeds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The fields were full of water.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Grasshopper\'s Plea\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the grasshopper feel?\",\"options\":[\"Happy and full\",\"Cold and hungry\",\"Angry and tired\",\"Sleepy and warm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The grasshopper felt cold and hungry.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Grasshopper\'s Plea\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why could the grasshopper not jump and fly?\",\"options\":[\"He was too tired.\",\"He was too lazy.\",\"His wings were wet.\",\"He did not want to.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains, \'His wings were wet. He could not jump and fly.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Grasshopper\'s Plea\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was one thing the grasshopper could NOT do because he was wet?\",\"options\":[\"Sleep\",\"Eat\",\"Sing\",\"Think\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'He could not sing.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Grasshopper\'s Plea\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Whose house did the grasshopper go to for help?\",\"options\":[\"The bee\'s house\",\"The ant\'s house\",\"The bird\'s house\",\"The beetle\'s house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'He went to the ant’s house.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Grasshopper\'s Plea\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What action did the grasshopper take when he reached the door?\",\"options\":[\"He kicked the door.\",\"He opened the door.\",\"He knocked at the door.\",\"He painted the door.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states he \'knocked at the door.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Grasshopper\'s Plea\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What did the grasshopper ask the ant to give him?\",\"options\":[\"A dry coat\",\"Some food\",\"A new song\",\"A map\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The grasshopper says, \'Please give me some food.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Grasshopper\'s Plea\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why did the grasshopper need help?\",\"options\":[\"He wanted to play a game.\",\"He had no food and no dry place to stay.\",\"He wanted to teach the ant how to fly.\",\"He was looking for his lost wings.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows he was cold, hungry, had no food, and no dry place to stay.\",\"topic\":\"The Grasshopper\'s Plea\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the main cause of the grasshopper\'s problems in this story?\",\"options\":[\"The wet environment and lack of food\",\"The ant being mean to him\",\"His inability to find his way home\",\"The fact that he forgot how to sing\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The wet ground and fields caused him to be cold and prevented him from flying or finding food.\",\"topic\":\"The Grasshopper\'s Plea\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who opened the door in the story?\",\"options\":[\"The grasshopper\",\"The ant\",\"A bird\",\"A bee\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The ant opened the door.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant\'s Advice\",\"part\":25,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the grasshopper do during the summer?\",\"options\":[\"He worked hard\",\"He carried food every day\",\"He sang, danced, and played\",\"He built a house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The grasshopper answered that he sang, danced, and played in summer.\",\"topic\":\"The Ant\'s Advice\",\"part\":25,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How often did the ant carry food in the summer?\",\"options\":[\"Once a week\",\"Every day\",\"Only when it rained\",\"Never\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ant said, \'I carried food every day.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant\'s Advice\",\"part\":25,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the grasshopper feel when he talked to the ant?\",\"options\":[\"He felt happy\",\"He felt angry\",\"He felt sorry\",\"He felt proud\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'The grasshopper felt sorry and answered.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant\'s Advice\",\"part\":25,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the ant have enough food for the rainy season?\",\"options\":[\"Because she found it on the ground\",\"Because she worked hard in summer\",\"Because the grasshopper gave it to her\",\"Because she bought it from a shop\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ant explains that she worked hard and carried food every day to have enough for the rainy season.\",\"topic\":\"The Ant\'s Advice\",\"part\":25,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the ant allow the grasshopper to do?\",\"options\":[\"Sing a new song\",\"Share her food\",\"Stay outside in the rain\",\"Go back to the field\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ant says, \'Come inside, Grasshopper. You may share my food.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant\'s Advice\",\"part\":25,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the ant\'s advice, when must one work to avoid suffering in the rain?\",\"options\":[\"In the winter\",\"In the rainy season\",\"In the summer\",\"At night\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The ant advises, \'in summer, you must work. Then you will not suffer in the rain.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Ant\'s Advice\",\"part\":25,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to be prepared like the ant, what should they do?\",\"options\":[\"Play all day and wait for help\",\"Work hard before the difficult time comes\",\"Only dance and sing\",\"Ask others for food every day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ant\'s behavior shows that working hard in advance prevents suffering later.\",\"topic\":\"The Ant\'s Advice\",\"part\":25,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the main difference between the ant\'s summer and the grasshopper\'s summer?\",\"options\":[\"The ant played while the grasshopper worked\",\"The ant worked hard while the grasshopper did not work\",\"The ant sang while the grasshopper carried food\",\"Both of them worked very hard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows the ant worked daily while the grasshopper only sang, danced, and played.\",\"topic\":\"The Ant\'s Advice\",\"part\":25,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the lesson or \'advice\' given by the ant at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"It is better to dance than to work\",\"Always stay outside during the rain\",\"Work in the right season so you do not have problems later\",\"Never share food with friends\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The ant\'s advice is to work in summer so that one does not suffer in the rain.\",\"topic\":\"The Ant\'s Advice\",\"part\":25,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What did the grasshopper do when he said, \'Yes, you are right\'?\",\"options\":[\"He jumped\",\"He nodded\",\"He ran away\",\"He laughed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The grasshopper nodded.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":29,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who shared the food together?\",\"options\":[\"The two friends\",\"The ant and the bee\",\"The grasshopper and the bird\",\"The ant and the spider\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'The two friends shared the food together.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":29,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list is the opposite of \'light\'?\",\"options\":[\"bright\",\"heavy\",\"hungry\",\"sang\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the list provided, \'heavy\' is the word that describes weight, which is the opposite of light.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":29,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did the ant feel about helping the grasshopper?\",\"options\":[\"The ant was angry\",\"The ant was sad\",\"The ant was happy to help\",\"The ant was tired\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'the ant was happy to help.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":29,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When does the grasshopper say he will work?\",\"options\":[\"When it is time to play\",\"When it is time to work\",\"Only at night\",\"Never\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The grasshopper says, \'I will work when it is time to work.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":29,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the grasshopper feel after sharing the food?\",\"options\":[\"He was thankful\",\"He was greedy\",\"He was sleepy\",\"He was scared\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The grasshopper was thankful.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":29,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list describes a feeling of needing food?\",\"options\":[\"remember\",\"bright\",\"hungry\",\"heavy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'hungry\' describes the need for food.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":29,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is NOT in the \'Listen and repeat\' list?\",\"options\":[\"grasshopper\",\"remember\",\"sang\",\"friend\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The words grasshopper, remember, and sang are in the list, but \'friend\' is not.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":29,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What lesson did the grasshopper learn about time?\",\"options\":[\"He should only play\",\"He should only work\",\"There is a time to work and a time to play\",\"He should sleep all day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The grasshopper says he will work when it is time to work and play when it is time to play.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":29,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what kind of relationship did the ant and the grasshopper have at the end?\",\"options\":[\"They were enemies\",\"They were friends\",\"They did not know each other\",\"They were fighting\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to them as \'The two friends\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":29,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21405,11,3,'English','en','Word Family - VI','[\"Word family means words that share the same root or base word.\",\"In this chapter we learn words that start with the letters **b**, **c**, **h**, **l**, **m**, **p**, **t**, **w** and end with **oo** or **ook**.\",\"Examples: book, cook, hook, look, took, wood, wool, good, tool, foot, shook, stood.\",\"The root word is the part that stays the same in all words of the family.\",\"Changing the first letter or adding a few letters gives new words but the meaning stays related.\",\"The words in this chapter help you read and write better because they look similar.\",\"Practice by reading the sentences and repeating the words aloud.\",\"Remember: all words in a family have the same sound in the middle, like **oo** in *book* and *look*.\",\"Use the pictures to match the words with their meanings.\",\"When you see a new word, try to find its family word to remember it easier.\",\"Keep a list of word families in your notebook and add new words as you learn them.\",\"Ask your teacher to show you more pictures of the same family.\",\"Try to make your own sentences using the new words.\",\"Listen carefully when the teacher reads the words aloud.\",\"Repeat after the teacher to improve pronunciation.\",\"Write the words in bold to see the common part clearly.\",\"Review the word families every week to keep them fresh in your mind.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these words is included in the \'Word Family - VI\' list?\",\"options\":[\"back\",\"book\",\"bake\",\"bike\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'book\' is the first word listed in the word family text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Pooja have in the story?\",\"options\":[\"A tool\",\"A hook\",\"A book\",\"A foot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Pooja has a book.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the wood located?\",\"options\":[\"Inside the hut\",\"On top of the hut\",\"Near the hut\",\"Far from the hut\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'There is wood near the hut.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what kind of cook is Pooja?\",\"options\":[\"A fast cook\",\"A good cook\",\"A new cook\",\"A bad cook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'Pooja is a good cook.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How is the word \'holiday\' divided into parts in the exercise?\",\"options\":[\"hol-i-day\",\"ho-lid-ay\",\"ho-li-day\",\"h-o-l-i-day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'holiday\' divided as \'ho\', \'li\', \'day\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list rhymes with \'stood\'?\",\"options\":[\"wool\",\"wood\",\"tool\",\"cook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the word family list, \'wood\' and \'stood\' share the same \'ood\' ending sound.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What action did Pooja perform with the wool?\",\"options\":[\"She cooked the wool\",\"She put it on the wood\",\"She put it in the book\",\"She gave it to the elephant\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'She took some wool and put it on the wood.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the exercise, the word \'computer\' is broken into how many parts?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'computer\' divided into three parts: \'com\', \'pu\', and \'ter\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Pooja stand?\",\"options\":[\"Near the wood\",\"Near the elephant\",\"Inside the hut\",\"On the tool\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Pooja stood near the wood.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, how does Pooja cook?\",\"options\":[\"She cooks slowly\",\"She cooks well\",\"She cooks poorly\",\"She does not cook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'She cooks well.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21406,11,3,'English','en','Kind Race','[\"Technology means using tools and machines to make work easier.\",\"Examples of technology: tablet, app, robot, phone, computer.\",\"Technology helps us learn, play, and do tasks faster.\",\"Robots can help in homes, hospitals, and factories.\",\"A tablet is a flat screen device we can touch to watch videos or play games.\",\"An app is a program on a phone or tablet that does a specific job.\",\"Robots can help doctors do surgeries safely.\",\"Using technology, we can see planets and stars through videos.\",\"Technology helps us learn and enjoy at the same time.\",\"We should use technology wisely and for good purposes.\",\"Studying hard helps us use technology to make the future better.\",\"Science and technology together help us understand the world.\",\"Listening and repeating words improves pronunciation and vocabulary.\",\"Guessing games like \'Who am I?\' help us think and learn new things.\",\"Technology is all around us in daily life.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is a tablet used for?\",\"options\":[\"Making phone calls only\",\"Watching videos and playing games\",\"Cooking food\",\"Washing clothes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A tablet is a flat screen device used to watch videos, play games, and learn.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is an example of technology?\",\"options\":[\"Pencil\",\"Book\",\"Robot\",\"Stone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A robot is a machine that uses technology to do work.\"},{\"q\":\"What helps us see planets and stars according to the dialogue?\",\"options\":[\"Microscope\",\"Telescope\",\"Video on an app\",\"Magnifying glass\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Shyam says he is watching a video about space on an app to see planets and stars.\"},{\"q\":\"What can robots help doctors do?\",\"options\":[\"Teach students\",\"Do surgeries\",\"Fly airplanes\",\"Bake cakes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Robots can help doctors do surgeries safely and precisely.\"},{\"q\":\"What does Mina use to listen to stories?\",\"options\":[\"Father\'s phone\",\"Mother\'s phone\",\"Tablet\",\"Radio\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Mina says she uses her mother’s phone to listen to stories.\"},{\"q\":\"What do Shyam and Mina want to do to make the future bright?\",\"options\":[\"Play games\",\"Study hard\",\"Watch TV\",\"Sleep more\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They say, \'Let’s study hard and make the future bright with technology.\'\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \'causing wonder or surprise\'?\",\"options\":[\"Boring\",\"Amazing\",\"Tired\",\"Quiet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Amazing means causing great wonder or surprise.\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'app\' stand for?\",\"options\":[\"Application\",\"Apple\",\"April\",\"Arrow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"App is short for application, a type of software program.\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence is true about technology?\",\"options\":[\"It only helps in offices.\",\"It helps us learn and enjoy at the same time.\",\"It is not useful for children.\",\"It makes work harder.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Shyam says technology helps us learn and enjoy at the same time.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main idea of the chapter \'Kind Race\'?\",\"options\":[\"To avoid using machines\",\"To race with friends\",\"To learn how technology helps us in daily life\",\"To build a rocket\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The chapter shows how technology like tablets, apps, and robots helps us learn, work, and enjoy.\"}]','nvidia/nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21407,11,3,'English','en','Butterfly and the Grasshopper','[\"The poem \'Butterfly and the Grasshopper\' is about two insects talking about their lives.\",\"The butterfly is proud of its beautiful wings and colorful appearance.\",\"The grasshopper is happy with its strong legs and ability to jump high.\",\"The butterfly says it flies from flower to flower to sip nectar.\",\"The grasshopper says it sings and jumps in the grass all day long.\",\"Both insects are content with what they can do and who they are.\",\"The poem teaches us to appreciate our own unique qualities.\",\"It shows that everyone has special talents and should be proud of them.\",\"The butterfly and grasshopper do not envy each other’s abilities.\",\"The language of the poem is simple and rhythmic, suitable for young learners.\",\"Rhyming words in the poem make it fun to read and remember.\",\"The poem encourages self-confidence and self-acceptance.\",\"It helps children understand that differences make us special.\",\"The tone of the poem is cheerful and positive.\",\"Students learn to respect different ways of living and being.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the first riddle, what takes pictures with just one click?\",\"options\":[\"A book\",\"A camera\",\"A drone\",\"A key\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the object takes pictures with just one click.\",\"topic\":\"Riddle 4\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which object is described as opening like a book and having keys to type?\",\"options\":[\"A camera\",\"A drone\",\"A laptop or computer\",\"A storage file\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The second riddle describes an object that opens like a book and has keys to type.\",\"topic\":\"Riddle 4\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the drone do according to the third riddle?\",\"options\":[\"It types words\",\"It stores games\",\"It takes photos from the sky\",\"It opens like a book\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the object flies high and takes photos from the sky.\",\"topic\":\"Riddle 4\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the object in the fourth riddle?\",\"options\":[\"To fly without a crew\",\"To store files, pictures, and games\",\"To click pictures in a blink\",\"To show words and pictures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The fourth riddle states it keeps files and stores pictures and games.\",\"topic\":\"Riddle 4\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'capture memories in a blink\' mean in the first riddle?\",\"options\":[\"Closing your eyes\",\"Taking a photo very quickly\",\"Sleeping for a short time\",\"Drawing a picture\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Capturing memories in a blink refers to the speed of taking a photograph.\",\"topic\":\"Riddle 4\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the second riddle, how does the object help you?\",\"options\":[\"By flying high in the sky\",\"By taking photos from above\",\"By helping you learn and write\",\"By clicking pictures\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the object helps you to learn and write.\",\"topic\":\"Riddle 4\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to take a photo of a mountain from high up without being in a plane, which object would you use?\",\"options\":[\"The object that has keys to type\",\"The object that flies without a crew\",\"The object that opens like a book\",\"The object that stores files\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The drone is described as flying high without a crew to take photos.\",\"topic\":\"Riddle 4\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student needs to save a very large game, which object from the riddles is best suited for this?\",\"options\":[\"The one that takes pictures in a blink\",\"The one that flies high\",\"The one that keeps files big and small\",\"The one that has keys to type\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The fourth riddle describes an object that keeps files big and small and stores games.\",\"topic\":\"Riddle 4\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the difference between the object in the first riddle and the object in the third riddle?\",\"options\":[\"One stores games, the other types words\",\"One takes photos on the ground, the other takes them from the sky\",\"One has keys, the other opens like a book\",\"One is big, the other is small\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first is a camera (one click) and the third is a drone (photos from the sky).\",\"topic\":\"Riddle 4\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which two objects mentioned in the riddles are capable of taking photos?\",\"options\":[\"The one with keys and the one that stores files\",\"The one that opens like a book and the one that stores games\",\"The one that clicks in a blink and the one that flies without a crew\",\"The one that helps you write and the one that keeps files\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Both the camera (riddle 1) and the drone (riddle 3) are described as taking pictures\\/photos.\",\"topic\":\"Riddle 4\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners find from the conversation according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Important ideas\",\"New characters\",\"Funny jokes\",\"Long sentences\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly tells the teacher to encourage learners to find important ideas from the conversation.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is mentioned as a source to find words?\",\"options\":[\"A storybook\",\"A dictionary\",\"A notebook\",\"A drawing book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'dictionary\' as one of the sources for finding words.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides a dictionary, what other specific source is mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Newspaper\",\"Encyclopaedia\",\"Magazine\",\"Atlas\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'dictionary, encyclopaedia, etc.\' as sources.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of words should the learners enlist?\",\"options\":[\"Words related to nature\",\"Words related to technology\",\"Words related to food\",\"Words related to sports\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that learners should enlist words related to technology.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is looking for information in an encyclopaedia, what are they doing according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Finding important ideas from a conversation\",\"Finding sources to enlist technology words\",\"Drawing a picture of a butterfly\",\"Writing a letter to the teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using an encyclopaedia as a source to enlist words related to technology.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the target audience for these specific instructions?\",\"options\":[\"The students\",\"The parents\",\"The teacher\",\"The principal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The heading of the text is \'For the Teacher\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal of using different sources like a dictionary?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to draw\",\"To find and list technology-related words\",\"To read a story aloud\",\"To count the number of pages\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links using sources to the task of enlisting words related to technology.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student finds the word \'Internet\' in a dictionary, which category does it fit into based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Conversation ideas\",\"Technology words\",\"Dictionary definitions\",\"Encyclopaedia facts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages enlisting words related to technology from sources like a dictionary.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text suggest using \'various sources\'?\",\"options\":[\"To make the bag heavy\",\"To find words related to technology from different places\",\"To finish the homework quickly\",\"To learn how to talk to friends\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages finding \'various sources\' specifically to enlist words related to technology.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the teacher\'s role regarding the conversation in the lesson?\",\"options\":[\"To read it alone\",\"To encourage learners to find important ideas in it\",\"To tell the students to ignore it\",\"To ask students to memorize every word\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the teacher should encourage learners to find important ideas from the conversation.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21408,11,3,'English','en','The Ant','[\"Sant Gora Kumbhar was a kind saint from Maharashtra.\",\"He lived long ago in the village ‘Ter’ in Dharashiv district.\",\"He worked as a potter and made pots with his hands.\",\"He believed in hard work and honesty.\",\"He taught people to work sincerely and be kind.\",\"People respected him and lovingly called him ‘Kaka’.\",\"He sang Abhangas and performed Kirtanas to spread goodness.\",\"He lived at the same time as Sant Namdev and Sant Dnyaneshwar.\",\"His life teaches us the values of honesty, kindness, and dedication to work.\",\"He is remembered as a saint who combined work with devotion.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What was the weather like during the summer according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The sun was cold\",\"The sun was hot\",\"It was raining\",\"It was snowing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that in summer, the sun was hot.\",\"topic\":\"Correct or Wrong\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the ant doing in the summer?\",\"options\":[\"Playing all day\",\"Sleeping in the sun\",\"Collecting food\",\"Dancing in the rain\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that in summer, the ant was collecting food.\",\"topic\":\"Correct or Wrong\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sentences about the grasshopper is WRONG?\",\"options\":[\"The grasshopper felt cold when it rained\",\"The grasshopper felt hungry when it rained\",\"The grasshopper worked hard in summer\",\"The grasshopper did not collect food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text implies the grasshopper did not work hard, making the statement \'The grasshopper worked hard in summer\' wrong.\",\"topic\":\"Correct or Wrong\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the ground when it rained?\",\"options\":[\"It became dry\",\"It became hot\",\"It became wet\",\"It became hard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that when it rained, the ground became wet.\",\"topic\":\"Correct or Wrong\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the grasshopper feel when the rain started?\",\"options\":[\"Happy and excited\",\"Cold and hungry\",\"Hot and thirsty\",\"Strong and busy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, when it rained, the grasshopper felt cold and hungry.\",\"topic\":\"Correct or Wrong\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Is the statement \'The ant did not share food with the grasshopper\' correct or wrong?\",\"options\":[\"It is correct\",\"It is wrong\",\"It is partially correct\",\"The text does not say\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks \'What did the ant give him?\', implying the ant shared food, so saying the ant did not share is wrong.\",\"topic\":\"Correct or Wrong\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If it is time to work, what should a person do according to the lesson?\",\"options\":[\"They should play\",\"They should sleep\",\"They should work\",\"They should wait for rain\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Work when it is time to work\'.\",\"topic\":\"Correct or Wrong\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why did the ant gather food in the summer?\",\"options\":[\"Because the sun was hot\",\"To prepare for when it rains and food is scarce\",\"Because the grasshopper told him to\",\"To make the ground wet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ant collects food in summer so that it has food when it rains and the grasshopper is hungry.\",\"topic\":\"Correct or Wrong\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct thing to do when it is time to play?\",\"options\":[\"Collect food\",\"Work hard\",\"Play\",\"Feel hungry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'play when it is time to play\'.\",\"topic\":\"Correct or Wrong\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which character followed the rule \'Work when it is time to work\' during the summer?\",\"options\":[\"The grasshopper\",\"The ant\",\"The rain\",\"The sun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ant worked by collecting food in the summer, while the grasshopper did not.\",\"topic\":\"Correct or Wrong\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word matches with \'cloud\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"cloudy\",\"rainy\",\"sunny\",\"windy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'cloud\' with \'cloudy\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many times should a learner clap when they hear the word \'grasshopper\'?\",\"options\":[\"Zero times\",\"Once\",\"Twice\",\"Three times\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher instructions state to clap once for the word \'grasshopper\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many times should a learner clap when they hear the word \'ant\'?\",\"options\":[\"Once\",\"Twice\",\"Three times\",\"Four times\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher instructions state to clap twice for the word \'ant\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners identify besides the main characters of the story?\",\"options\":[\"The names of all insects\",\"The importance of working on time\",\"The color of the grasshopper\",\"The number of pages in the book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to identify the importance of working on time.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"From whom can learners express the storylines they have heard?\",\"options\":[\"Only from the teacher\",\"Only from the textbook\",\"Granny, Grandpa, and friends\",\"Strangers on the street\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions expressing storylines heard by Granny, Grandpa, friends, etc.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are learners encouraged to do with the words like \'rain-rainy\' and \'sun-sunny\'?\",\"options\":[\"Draw them\",\"Copy them in their notebook\",\"Sing them as a song\",\"Paint them on the wall\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'read and copy the words in your notebook\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the weather has \'fog\', which word describes it according to the list?\",\"options\":[\"Foggy\",\"Sunny\",\"Rainy\",\"Windy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides the pair \'fog-foggy\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the weather has \'snow\', what is the correct word to use based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Snowy\",\"Rainy\",\"Cloudy\",\"Foggy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides the pair \'snow-snowy\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the recommended way for learners to read age-appropriate stories?\",\"options\":[\"As fast as possible\",\"Without any stops\",\"With proper pauses\",\"By skipping difficult words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to read with proper pauses.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these word pairs is correctly matched based on the vocabulary list?\",\"options\":[\"sun-rainy\",\"wind-windy\",\"cloud-foggy\",\"snow-sunny\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'wind-windy\' as a correct pair.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21409,11,3,'English','en','Technology Around Us','[\"Technology means tools and machines that help us do work easily.\",\"Examples of technology: computers, phones, TVs, washing machines, and cars.\",\"Technology saves time and effort in daily tasks.\",\"We use technology at home, school, and in offices.\",\"Electricity is needed for many technologies to work.\",\"Simple machines like levers and pulleys are early forms of technology.\",\"Technology helps in communication, like phones and emails.\",\"Transport technology includes buses, trains, and bicycles.\",\"Medical technology helps doctors check and treat illnesses.\",\"We should use technology safely and responsibly.\",\"Too much screen time can harm our eyes and health.\",\"Turning off devices when not in use saves electricity.\",\"Technology keeps improving with new inventions.\",\"Robots and AI are modern examples of advanced technology.\",\"Learning to use technology helps us in studies and future jobs.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What device is Shyam using to watch a video?\",\"options\":[\"A laptop\",\"A tablet\",\"A television\",\"A radio\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Shyam is using a tablet to watch a video about space.\",\"topic\":\"Robots and the Future\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the subject of the video Shyam is watching on the app?\",\"options\":[\"Animals\",\"Plants\",\"Space\",\"History\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Shyam mentions he is watching a video about \'space\' on an app.\",\"topic\":\"Robots and the Future\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the conversation, what does technology help us see in the sky?\",\"options\":[\"Clouds and rain\",\"Planets and stars\",\"Birds and planes\",\"Kites and balloons\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Shyam says, \'Technology helps us see planets and stars!\'\",\"topic\":\"Robots and the Future\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Mina use her mother\'s phone for?\",\"options\":[\"To play games\",\"To take photos\",\"To listen to stories\",\"To call her friends\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mina says, \'I use my mother\'s phone to listen to the stories.\'\",\"topic\":\"Robots and the Futur