ar the \'sh\' sound according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only in the car\",\"Only in the bathroom\",\"Wherever you are\",\"Only in a shop\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'You’ll hear the sound wherever you are\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sh... Sh... Sh...\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the text starts with the \'sh\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"Fish\",\"Brush\",\"Shell\",\"Dish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'shell\' as a word starting with \'sh\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sh... Sh... Sh...\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the text ends with the \'sh\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"Shut\",\"Shop\",\"She\",\"Wish\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'wish\' as a word ending with the \'sh\' sound.\",\"topic\":\"Sh... Sh... Sh...\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the first list refers to a place where people live?\",\"options\":[\"Saint\",\"Village\",\"Potter\",\"Honest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A village is a place where people live, and it is in the first list of words.\",\"topic\":\"Sh... Sh... Sh...\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the list \'she, shut, shell, shop\', what is common among all the words?\",\"options\":[\"They all end with \'sh\'\",\"They all start with \'sh\'\",\"They all have three letters\",\"They all mean the same thing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"All these words provided in the text start with the letters \'sh\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sh... Sh... Sh...\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'sh\' list refers to a place where you buy things?\",\"options\":[\"Shell\",\"Shut\",\"Shop\",\"Dish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A shop is a place for buying things, mentioned in the \'sh\' word list.\",\"topic\":\"Sh... Sh... Sh...\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text rhymes with \'fish\'?\",\"options\":[\"Shut\",\"Dish\",\"Shell\",\"Shop\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Fish and dish both end with the \'ish\' sound and are listed together in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Sh... Sh... Sh...\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21411,11,3,'English','en','Sant Gadge Baba','[\"Tarabai Modak was a social worker and teacher.\",\"She was born on 19th April 1892 in Maharashtra.\",\"She loved children and wanted every child to go to school.\",\"She worked for children in villages who did not attend school.\",\"She started schools in villages to help children learn.\",\"She worked for tribal children in Maharashtra.\",\"She received the Padmabhushan award for her work.\",\"She passed away on 31st August 1973.\",\"She is known as the Mother of Pre-school Education in India.\",\"She started the first balwadi in Bordi village, Thane.\",\"She made learning easy and fun using toys, songs, and games.\",\"She believed children learn best by playing.\",\"She trained teachers to teach in fun and playful ways.\",\"We should learn to help others from her example.\",\"Her work helped improve early childhood education in India.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who was Tarabai Modak according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A famous singer\",\"A great social worker and teacher\",\"A village doctor\",\"A police officer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Tarabai Modak was a great social worker and teacher.\",\"topic\":\"Work in Villages\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When was Tarabai Modak born?\",\"options\":[\"15th August 1947\",\"26th January 1950\",\"19th April 1892\",\"2nd October 1869\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she was born on 19th April 1892.\",\"topic\":\"Work in Villages\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which state was Tarabai Modak born?\",\"options\":[\"Gujarat\",\"Maharashtra\",\"Karnataka\",\"Goa\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions she was born in Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"Work in Villages\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Tarabai Modak want for every child?\",\"options\":[\"To go to school\",\"To stay at home\",\"To work in the fields\",\"To play all day\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says she wanted every child to go to school.\",\"topic\":\"Work in Villages\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Tarabai Modak start schools in villages?\",\"options\":[\"Because she wanted to live in a village\",\"Because many children from villages did not go to school\",\"Because she wanted to build big buildings\",\"Because the text says she was a doctor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that many village children did not go to school, so she started schools for them.\",\"topic\":\"Work in Villages\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did Tarabai Modak feel about children?\",\"options\":[\"She was afraid of them\",\"She ignored them\",\"She loved them very much\",\"She thought they were noisy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that she loved children very much.\",\"topic\":\"Work in Villages\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a village child in the past was not going to school, what would Tarabai Modak most likely do?\",\"options\":[\"Give the child money\",\"Start a school in that village\",\"Tell the child to stay home\",\"Buy the child new clothes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on her actions in the text, she started schools in villages for children who didn\'t go to school.\",\"topic\":\"Work in Villages\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which action shows that Tarabai Modak was a social worker?\",\"options\":[\"She worked hard for the children in villages\",\"She traveled to different states\",\"She celebrated her birthday\",\"She lived in Maharashtra\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Working hard for the benefit of village children\'s education is an example of social work.\",\"topic\":\"Work in Villages\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the main problem Tarabai Modak tried to solve in \'those days\'?\",\"options\":[\"Children having too many toys\",\"Children not having enough food\",\"Village children not going to school\",\"Schools being too crowded\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text highlights that many children from villages did not go to school in those days.\",\"topic\":\"Work in Villages\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text best describes the effort Tarabai Modak put in for the children?\",\"options\":[\"Lazy\",\"Hard work\",\"Easy\",\"Careless\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically says \'Tarabai Modak worked hard for them\'.\",\"topic\":\"Work in Villages\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Tarabai Modak start the first balwadi?\",\"options\":[\"Bordi village\",\"Mumbai city\",\"Pune district\",\"Nashik village\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that Tarabai Modak started the first balwadi in Bordi village in Thane.\",\"topic\":\"Achievements and Legacy\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which prestigious award did Tarabai Modak receive?\",\"options\":[\"Bharat Ratna\",\"Padmabhushan\",\"Padma Shri\",\"Arjuna Award\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that she received the Padmabhushan award.\",\"topic\":\"Achievements and Legacy\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Tarabai Modak, how do children learn best?\",\"options\":[\"By sitting quietly\",\"By reading big books\",\"By playing\",\"By writing all day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says she believed children learn best by playing.\",\"topic\":\"Achievements and Legacy\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"On which date did Tarabai Modak pass away?\",\"options\":[\"15th August 1947\",\"31st August 1973\",\"1st May 1960\",\"26th January 1950\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text records that Tarabai Modak passed away on 31st August 1973.\",\"topic\":\"Achievements and Legacy\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What title is Tarabai Modak known by in India?\",\"options\":[\"Mother of Science\",\"Mother of Pre-school Education\",\"Mother of Sports\",\"Mother of Music\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states she is known as the Mother of Pre-school Education in India.\",\"topic\":\"Achievements and Legacy\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher wants to follow Tarabai Modak\'s method, what should they use to teach?\",\"options\":[\"Only blackboards\",\"Toys, songs and games\",\"Strict punishments\",\"Silent reading only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says she used toys, songs, and games to make learning easy and fun.\",\"topic\":\"Achievements and Legacy\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of children in Maharashtra did Tarabai Modak specifically work for?\",\"options\":[\"City children\",\"Tribal children\",\"Foreign children\",\"High school children\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions she worked for tribal children in Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"Achievements and Legacy\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What important value should we learn from Tarabai Modak\'s life?\",\"options\":[\"To earn a lot of money\",\"To help others\",\"To travel to different countries\",\"To win many games\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying we should learn to help others from her.\",\"topic\":\"Achievements and Legacy\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Tarabai Modak train other teachers?\",\"options\":[\"To help them find new villages\",\"To teach them how to sing better\",\"To teach in fun ways\",\"To make them work in factories\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states she trained teachers to teach in fun ways.\",\"topic\":\"Achievements and Legacy\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is Tarabai Modak\'s work in Bordi village considered a major achievement?\",\"options\":[\"It was the location of the first balwadi\",\"It was the largest village in Thane\",\"She built a big hospital there\",\"She taught children how to farm\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Starting the first balwadi in Bordi was a significant milestone in pre-school education.\",\"topic\":\"Achievements and Legacy\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21412,11,3,'English','en','Shri Sai Modak','[\"Tarabai Modak was born on 19 April 1892 in Maharashtra.\",\"She loved children and wanted every child to go to school.\",\"In the early 1900s many children in villages did not attend school.\",\"She started the first balwadi (pre‑school) in Bordi village, Thane.\",\"A balwadi is a small school where children learn through play, songs and games.\",\"She used toys, songs and games to make learning fun and easy.\",\"She trained children to become teachers who teach in fun ways.\",\"She worked especially for tribal children in Maharashtra.\",\"She received the Padma Bhushan award for her social work.\",\"She passed away on 31 August 1973.\",\"She is called the Mother of Pre‑school Education in India.\",\"Her work shows that children learn best by playing.\",\"She believed that learning should be enjoyable and interactive.\",\"She encouraged teachers to use games and songs in lessons.\",\"Her life teaches us to help others and make learning fun.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the \'For the Teacher\' section, who is the first lady professional to be discussed?\",\"options\":[\"The first lady pilot of India\",\"The first lady doctor of India\",\"The first lady engineer of India\",\"The first lady scientist of India\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions discussing \'The first lady doctor of India\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific type of officer should the teacher discuss with the learners?\",\"options\":[\"I.A.S. officer\",\"Army officer\",\"I.P.S. officer\",\"Forest officer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'The first lady I.P.S. officer in India\' as a topic for discussion.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where should learners go to find more information about Indian women freedom fighters?\",\"options\":[\"To the playground\",\"To the market\",\"To the library\",\"To the laboratory\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to \'make use of library books\' for information on freedom fighters.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners note down about the social workers of Maharashtra?\",\"options\":[\"Their favorite colors\",\"Important events in their life\",\"Their home addresses\",\"Their school names\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text motivates learners to \'note down important events in the life of social workers\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list refers to a group of people living in a specific traditional way?\",\"options\":[\"award\",\"tribal\",\"trained\",\"started\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'tribal\' is included in the list of words to repeat.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to learn about Sarojini Naidu (a freedom fighter), what does the text suggest they use?\",\"options\":[\"Television\",\"Library books\",\"Radio\",\"Newspapers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using library books to get information about Indian women freedom fighters.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which state\'s social workers are specifically mentioned for discussion?\",\"options\":[\"Gujarat\",\"Maharashtra\",\"Goa\",\"Delhi\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions social workers of Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'Listen and repeat\' section, which word is related to the process of learning and schooling?\",\"options\":[\"games\",\"worked\",\"education\",\"believed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Education\' is the word in the list that refers to learning and schooling.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the teacher\'s role regarding the information about women freedom fighters?\",\"options\":[\"To tell the learners to stop reading\",\"To encourage learners to use library books\",\"To write the books for the learners\",\"To hide the library books\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'Encourage learners to make use of library books to get more information\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the purpose of the \'Listen and repeat\' section?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to draw\",\"To practice saying specific words like \'received\' and \'trained\'\",\"To learn how to cook\",\"To play outdoor games\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Listen and repeat\' section provides a list of words for pronunciation practice.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which unit are the words in this \'House of Words\' from?\",\"options\":[\"Unit 1\",\"Unit 2\",\"Unit 3\",\"Unit 4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states these are the words covered in Unit 3.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners prepare to help them with these words?\",\"options\":[\"Toys and dolls\",\"Flashcards and charts\",\"Food and water\",\"Bags and shoes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to prepare flashcards\\/charts for these words.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the title of this section in the textbook?\",\"options\":[\"House of Words - 1\",\"House of Words - 2\",\"House of Words - 3\",\"House of Words - 4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The title at the top of the text is \'House of Words - 3\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the text suggest these words may be revised?\",\"options\":[\"Through tests\",\"Through games\",\"Through homework\",\"Through singing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says these words may be revised through games.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What tool should learners be encouraged to use for these words?\",\"options\":[\"A calculator\",\"A map\",\"A dictionary\",\"A ruler\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to use a dictionary.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides flashcards, what else should learners be encouraged to prepare?\",\"options\":[\"Charts\",\"Paintings\",\"Models\",\"Stories\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions preparing flashcards\\/charts.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher wants students to say the words correctly, what should they practice?\",\"options\":[\"Running and jumping\",\"Stress and pronunciations\",\"Writing and drawing\",\"Singing and dancing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that stress and pronunciations should be thoroughly practised.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student does not know the meaning of a word in Unit 3, which resource mentioned in the text should they use?\",\"options\":[\"A dictionary\",\"A notebook\",\"A drawing book\",\"A storybook\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifically encourages the use of a dictionary for these words.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the primary audience for these specific instructions?\",\"options\":[\"The Student\",\"The Teacher\",\"The Parent\",\"The Principal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The section is explicitly titled \'For the Teacher\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what two specific aspects of speaking must be \'thoroughly practised\'?\",\"options\":[\"Stress and pronunciations\",\"Speed and volume\",\"Games and charts\",\"Reading and writing\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text highlights that stress and pronunciations should be thoroughly practised.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28');
INSERT INTO `ep_topic_packs` VALUES (21413,11,3,'English','en','Colour Song','[\"Red is the colour of an apple, cherries and strawberries.\",\"Blue is the colour of the sky, baby things and my sister’s eyes.\",\"Yellow is the colour of the sun, lemonade and a baby chick.\",\"Green is the colour of leaves, green peas and a watermelon.\",\"Orange is the colour of oranges, carrots and a pumpkin.\",\"Purple is the colour of grapes, grape juice and a brinjal (eggplant).\",\"The rainbow has seven colours: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo (purple) and violet (purple).\",\"A rainbow appears after rain and looks like a bow.\",\"Colours are used to describe objects in our world.\",\"The song helps children remember which colour goes with which object.\",\"Rearranging letters can help find colour names.\",\"Matching colours with objects helps learning vocabulary.\",\"Rhyming words make learning fun and memorable.\",\"The poem encourages children to sing about colours.\",\"Teachers can ask students to create picture dictionaries for new words.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many colours does the \'bow\' mentioned in the poem have?\",\"options\":[\"Five\",\"Six\",\"Seven\",\"Eight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem starts by asking \'Do you know? I have seven colours\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When does the \'bow\' appear according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Before the rain\",\"During the rain\",\"After the rain\",\"At night\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I appear after rain\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these fruits is described as red in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Orange\",\"Strawberry\",\"Grapes\",\"Watermelon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Red is the colour for strawberries\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What colour are the sister\'s eyes in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Black\",\"Brown\",\"Green\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Blue is the colour for my sister’s eyes\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what is yellow besides the sun?\",\"options\":[\"A pumpkin\",\"A baby chick\",\"A carrot\",\"Green peas\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'Yellow is the colour of a baby chick\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is associated with leaves on the trees?\",\"options\":[\"Yellow\",\"Orange\",\"Green\",\"Purple\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Green is the colour for the leaves on the trees\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are drawing a picture of a pumpkin based on this poem, which colour should you use?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Yellow\",\"Orange\",\"Purple\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Orange is the colour of a pumpkin\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which vegetable is mentioned as being purple in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Carrot\",\"Green peas\",\"Brinjal\",\"Pumpkin\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Purple is the colour for a brinjal\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these items is NOT listed as being red in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Apple\",\"Cherries\",\"Strawberries\",\"Lemonade\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Lemonade is listed under yellow, while the others are listed under red.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the description \'I have seven colours, I look like a bow, I appear after rain\', what is the speaker?\",\"options\":[\"A cloud\",\"A rainbow\",\"The sun\",\"An umbrella\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The description of seven colours and a bow shape after rain identifies a rainbow.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is used for both a fruit (orange) and a vegetable (carrot) in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Orange\",\"Purple\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem groups oranges and carrots under the colour orange.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is mentioned as being for \'baby things\'?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Yellow\",\"Green\",\"Purple\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Blue is the colour for baby things, too\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to instruction \'a\', what is the first thing you should do with the song?\",\"options\":[\"Listen\",\"Write\",\"Draw\",\"Read\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states \'a. Listen and sing.\'\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are learners asked to create for unfamiliar words?\",\"options\":[\"A story book\",\"A picture dictionary\",\"A math chart\",\"A list of names\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note suggests learners create their own picture dictionary.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"From where should the unfamiliar words be found?\",\"options\":[\"From the newspaper\",\"From each unit\",\"From the library\",\"From the playground\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Find unfamiliar words from each unit\'.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners identify from the poem?\",\"options\":[\"The number of pages\",\"Important ideas\",\"The teacher\'s name\",\"The date\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to \'identify important ideas from the poem\'.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the specific note about finding unfamiliar words written for?\",\"options\":[\"The Teacher\",\"The Shopkeeper\",\"The Doctor\",\"The Driver\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly labels the section \'For the Teacher\'.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main topic of the song based on the title?\",\"options\":[\"Animals\",\"Colours\",\"Numbers\",\"Fruits\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The title of the topic is \'Colour Song\'.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student finds a new word like \'Indigo\' in a unit, what should they do according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Skip the word\",\"Add it to their picture dictionary\",\"Erase the word\",\"Write it on the wall\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests creating a picture dictionary for unfamiliar words found in the units.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student draws a small red apple next to the word \'Red\'. What are they making?\",\"options\":[\"A picture dictionary\",\"A science project\",\"A greeting card\",\"A math table\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Creating a dictionary with pictures for words is a \'picture dictionary\' as mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the instruction say to \'Listen\' before \'Sing\'?\",\"options\":[\"To learn the words and tune first\",\"To take a rest\",\"To wait for the bell\",\"To stop the class\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Listening is the first step to understanding how to sing the song correctly.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it useful for a student to identify \'important ideas\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"To understand the meaning of the poem\",\"To count how many words there are\",\"To check if the spelling is wrong\",\"To make the book look colorful\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Identifying important ideas helps a learner grasp the core message or theme of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21414,11,3,'English','en','Source of Energy','[\"Solar energy is produced by the Sun and is clean and renewable.\",\"Solar panels are special devices that change sunlight into electricity.\",\"They work even when the main electricity supply is off.\",\"Solar power does not create pollution or smoke.\",\"Wind can also produce electricity, but the text says it cannot, which is incorrect; however, for this class we focus on solar energy.\",\"Food gives us energy for our bodies, not electricity for lights.\",\"Solar panels give light, warmth and electricity to homes.\",\"Using solar panels helps save money and keeps Earth green.\",\"The Sun is the main source of power for our planet.\",\"Solar panels are placed on roofs to capture sunlight.\",\"When the Sun is high, panels produce more electricity.\",\"Solar energy is safe for the environment.\",\"Solar panels help reduce dependence on fossil fuels.\",\"Solar power can be used for lights, fans, and TVs.\",\"Solar energy is a clean source of power for homes and schools.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does Anil use to keep his lights on when the electricity goes off in his area?\",\"options\":[\"Candles\",\"Solar panels\",\"Batteries\",\"Gas lamps\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Anil explains to Manu that his lights are on because they use solar panels.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where are the special solar panels placed at Anil\'s house?\",\"options\":[\"In the kitchen\",\"In the garden\",\"On the roof\",\"Under the windows\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Anil mentions that the special panels are on their roof.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what do solar panels do with sunlight?\",\"options\":[\"They turn sunlight into water\",\"They block the sunlight\",\"They convert sunlight into electricity\",\"They change sunlight into wind\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that solar panels convert sunlight into electricity.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Anil say solar energy is good for the Earth?\",\"options\":[\"It makes the Earth hotter\",\"It doesn\'t make pollution\",\"It makes the Earth blue\",\"It is very loud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Anil says it is good for the Earth because it doesn\'t make pollution.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the blue rectangular objects placed on the roofs of the different types of houses?\",\"options\":[\"Glass windows\",\"Solar panels\",\"Blue paint\",\"Water heaters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows solar panels installed on the roofs of all the houses in the village.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/080_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these appliances does Manu specifically ask about when checking if solar power works?\",\"options\":[\"Washing machine\",\"Computer\",\"TV\",\"Iron\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Manu asks if it works for lights, fans, and even the TV.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are Manu and Anil doing while standing in front of the houses?\",\"options\":[\"They are playing a game\",\"They are fixing a roof\",\"They are having a conversation\",\"They are planting trees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The image shows the two characters enacting the dialogue about solar panels.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/081_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does Anil say solar energy helps to do for nature?\",\"options\":[\"Conserve the nature\",\"Change the nature\",\"Hide the nature\",\"Remove the nature\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Anil mentions that solar energy helps to conserve the nature.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides light and warmth, what else does the Sun give us according to Anil?\",\"options\":[\"Food\",\"Rain\",\"Electricity\",\"Oxygen\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Anil says the Sun gives us light, warmth, and now electricity too.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Manu\'s parents want to save money and help the Earth, what should they do based on Anil\'s advice?\",\"options\":[\"Buy more lights\",\"Get solar panels\",\"Keep the TV off\",\"Move to a new area\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Anil says solar energy saves money and helps nature, so Manu decides to tell his parents to get them.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main source of power mentioned by Manu in the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"The Moon\",\"The Wind\",\"The Sun\",\"The Water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Manu states, \'The Sun is our source of power.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final goal shared by both Manu and Anil at the end of their talk?\",\"options\":[\"To build bigger houses\",\"To use solar power and keep Earth bright and green\",\"To turn off all the fans\",\"To stay inside Anil\'s house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both say, \'Let\'s use solar power and keep our Earth bright and green!\'\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Solar Panels\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is listed in the \'Listen and repeat\' section?\",\"options\":[\"water\",\"electricity\",\"moon\",\"cold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'electricity\' is the first word in the provided list.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"At what times should learners observe the Sun\'s position according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"morning and night\",\"morning, noon and evening\",\"only at noon\",\"evening and midnight\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs teachers to encourage learners to observe the Sun in the morning, noon, and evening.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher encourage learners to identify from the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"the main characters\",\"the spelling of words\",\"the price of solar panels\",\"the number of pages\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks to identify the main characters from the conversation.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the topic of the short oral presentations mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"the weather\",\"energy sources\",\"the moon\",\"pollution\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text motivates learners to make presentations on energy sources.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is talking about \'solar panels\' in class, which activity from the \'For the Teacher\' section are they likely doing?\",\"options\":[\"observing the sun\'s position\",\"identifying characters\",\"making an oral presentation on energy sources\",\"listening to smoke\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Solar panels are an energy source, and the text suggests making presentations on that topic.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list describes the feeling of heat?\",\"options\":[\"smoke\",\"warmth\",\"surprised\",\"electricity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Warmth\' is the word in the list that refers to the sensation of heat.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list refers to something that makes the environment dirty?\",\"options\":[\"bright\",\"smoke\",\"pollution\",\"energy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Pollution is the term used for environmental contamination.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher\'s instructions, what specific detail about the Sun should be observed?\",\"options\":[\"its position\",\"its color\",\"its size\",\"its temperature\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions observing the Sun\'s \'position\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list describes a feeling of being amazed?\",\"options\":[\"bright\",\"energy\",\"surprised\",\"warmth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Surprised\' is the word in the list that describes a feeling of amazement.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is included in the \'Listen and repeat\' list?\",\"options\":[\"pollution\",\"nature\",\"forest\",\"animal\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Pollution\' is one of the eight words provided in the list.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21415,11,3,'English','en','Word Family - VII','[\"• Words with the sound ‘ee’ are called a word family.\",\"• In this family the letters ‘ee’ stay the same in all words.\",\"• Examples: bee, see, jeep, keep, meet, deep, feet, peel, knee, fee, need, peep, week, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep\",\"• When you read a word, listen for the ‘ee’ sound like in ‘see’ or ‘deep’.\",\"• You can make new words by adding a prefix or suffix to a word in this family, e.g., ‘kept’, ‘keeps’, ‘keening’.\",\"• Practice by writing sentences with words that have ‘ee’.\",\"• The teacher can ask students to name objects around the school that have ‘ee’ in their name.\",\"• Repetition and singing the words helps memory.\",\"• Use flashcards with pictures to show the words.\",\"• Encourage students to read aloud to hear the ‘ee’ sound.\",\"• Ask students to find other words that have ‘ee’ but are not in the list.\",\"• Write the words in a notebook and colour them to remember.\",\"• The word family helps build spelling and vocabulary skills.\",\"• Keep practicing by adding new words to the list each week.\",\"• Review the list regularly to reinforce learning.\",\"• Use the words in simple sentences like “The bee is in the tree.”\",\"• The ‘ee’ sound is short, like in ‘see’ and ‘deep’.\",\"• The ‘ee’ sound is long, like in ‘bee’ and ‘meet’.\",\"• Both short and long ‘ee’ sounds belong to the same word family.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word from the list rhymes with \'seed\'?\",\"options\":[\"feel\",\"need\",\"week\",\"beep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the word list, \'seed\' and \'need\' share the same ending sound.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound does the vehicle in the story make?\",\"options\":[\"Vroom\",\"Honk\",\"Beep\",\"Ring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text starts with \'Beep! Beep! Beep!\' to describe the sound.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is the jeep described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A small jeep\",\"A big jeep\",\"A red jeep\",\"A fast jeep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'A big jeep.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are the characters told to keep in the jeep?\",\"options\":[\"A book\",\"A toy\",\"A bag\",\"A seed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Let us keep this bag in the jeep.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who are the characters going to meet?\",\"options\":[\"A bee\",\"Bheem\",\"A teacher\",\"A friend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Let us go to meet Bheem.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to a part of the body?\",\"options\":[\"heel\",\"peel\",\"feel\",\"fee\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Among the options, \'heel\' is a part of the human foot.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what action should the characters take after sitting in the jeep?\",\"options\":[\"Eat a seed\",\"Keep a bag\",\"Meet Bheem\",\"Peel a fruit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"After sitting and keeping the bag, the next action mentioned is to go meet Bheem.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher\'s note, what should learners speak about?\",\"options\":[\"Animals in the forest\",\"Objects in their school surrounding\",\"Different types of cars\",\"Their family members\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note says to encourage learners to speak on objects in their school surrounding.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list is an insect that makes honey?\",\"options\":[\"fee\",\"bee\",\"see\",\"wee\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A \'bee\' is a common insect mentioned in the word family list.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence from the text: \'Let us ____ in the jeep.\'\",\"options\":[\"run\",\"jump\",\"sit\",\"sleep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Let us sit in the jeep.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21416,11,3,'English','en','A Trip to the Moon','[\"- The moon is a natural satellite of Earth.\",\"- It is round and appears bright at night.\",\"- A full moon is when the whole face of the moon is lit.\",\"- The moon has less gravity than Earth, so things can jump higher.\",\"- Astronauts wear special suits to stay safe in space.\",\"- The moon is a place where we can dream of exploring.\",\"- Gravity is the force that pulls objects toward the center of the Earth.\",\"- An astronaut is a person who travels in space.\",\"- On the moon, you can bounce like a ball because of low gravity.\",\"- The moon is waiting for future explorers.\",\"- We can make a paper rocket to learn about space travel.\",\"- We can write sentences using words like moon, bounce, dream, safe, less.\",\"- The moon is a big, beautiful object in the sky.\",\"- Space travel requires learning and dreaming.\",\"- The moon is a place for adventure and learning.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What kind of moon does Komal say it is tonight?\",\"options\":[\"A new moon\",\"A half moon\",\"A full moon\",\"A crescent moon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Komal explicitly states, \'It\'s a full moon, isn\'t it beautiful?\'\",\"topic\":\"A Trip to the Moon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do astronauts wear to stay safe on the moon?\",\"options\":[\"Heavy coats\",\"Special suits\",\"Oxygen masks\",\"Raincoats\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that astronauts wear special suits to stay safe.\",\"topic\":\"A Trip to the Moon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why would someone rise really high when jumping on the moon?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is very dark\",\"Because there is less gravity\",\"Because the moon is big\",\"Because it is very cold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Komal explains that if you jump, you rise high because there\'s less gravity.\",\"topic\":\"A Trip to the Moon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Sujal say he would bounce like on the moon?\",\"options\":[\"A bird\",\"A rabbit\",\"A ball\",\"A spring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sujal says, \'Wow! I\'d bounce like a ball.\'\",\"topic\":\"A Trip to the Moon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to Komal, what should Sujal keep doing to reach the moon one day?\",\"options\":[\"Running and jumping\",\"Dreaming and learning\",\"Playing and sleeping\",\"Eating and growing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Komal tells Sujal to \'keep dreaming and learning\' to reach his goal.\",\"topic\":\"A Trip to the Moon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a person jumps on Earth and then jumps on the Moon, how will the jump on the Moon be different?\",\"options\":[\"They will not be able to jump at all\",\"They will jump lower than on Earth\",\"They will rise really high\",\"They will fall down immediately\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that on the Moon, you would rise really high due to less gravity.\",\"topic\":\"A Trip to the Moon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the dialogue, who seems to know more facts about the moon?\",\"options\":[\"Sujal\",\"Komal\",\"The Astronaut\",\"The Moon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Komal provides the information about gravity and what astronauts wear.\",\"topic\":\"A Trip to the Moon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does Sujal\'s final sentence, \'One small step for us, one big dream for the future!\' suggest?\",\"options\":[\"He is afraid of the moon\",\"He is tired of learning\",\"He is hopeful about going to the moon\",\"He wants to stay on Earth forever\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase shows Sujal\'s excitement and ambition for the future trip to the moon.\",\"topic\":\"A Trip to the Moon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is shown inside the thought bubble?\",\"options\":[\"A telescope\",\"A rocket\",\"A star\",\"A mountain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a rocket launching, representing the dream of a trip to the moon.\",\"topic\":\"A Trip to the Moon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/083_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the thought bubble represents a dream. Based on the text, whose dream is this most likely to be?\",\"options\":[\"Komal\'s dream\",\"Sujal\'s dream\",\"An astronaut\'s dream\",\"A scientist\'s dream\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sujal expresses his wish to go to the moon and play, making it his dream.\",\"topic\":\"A Trip to the Moon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/083_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the force that attracts things to the center of the earth?\",\"options\":[\"Wind\",\"Gravity\",\"Light\",\"Sound\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines gravity as the force that attracts things to the center of the earth.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A person who travels in space is called an ____.\",\"options\":[\"Pilot\",\"Sailor\",\"Driver\",\"Astronaut\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text defines an astronaut as a person who travels in space.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does an astronaut travel?\",\"options\":[\"In the ocean\",\"In space\",\"In a forest\",\"Under the ground\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the definition, an astronaut travels in space.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Gravity attracts things towards which part of the earth?\",\"options\":[\"The top\",\"The surface\",\"The center\",\"The clouds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that gravity attracts things to the center of the earth.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does gravity do to things on the surface of the earth?\",\"options\":[\"Pushes them away\",\"Attracts them\",\"Makes them disappear\",\"Makes them hot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The definition says gravity is a force that attracts things on the surface.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is defined as a \'force\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Astronaut\",\"Space\",\"Gravity\",\"Earth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines gravity as a force.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If an apple falls from a tree to the ground, which force mentioned in the text is working?\",\"options\":[\"Astronaut\",\"Gravity\",\"Space\",\"Surface\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Gravity is the force that attracts things towards the earth.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a girl named Meena goes on a trip to the moon, what would she be called?\",\"options\":[\"Astronaut\",\"Gravity\",\"Center\",\"Surface\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A person traveling in space (like to the moon) is an astronaut.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is a person and not a force?\",\"options\":[\"Gravity\",\"Center\",\"Astronaut\",\"Surface\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"An astronaut is defined as a person, while gravity is defined as a force.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement is true according to the definitions provided?\",\"options\":[\"Gravity pushes things into space.\",\"Astronauts stay only on the earth\'s surface.\",\"Gravity attracts things to the earth\'s center.\",\"Astronauts are a type of force.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states gravity attracts things to the center of the earth.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21417,11,3,'English','en','Cloud','[\"Clouds are fluffy white things that float in the sky.\",\"They are made of tiny water droplets or ice crystals.\",\"Clouds can bring rain, snow, or sunshine.\",\"When it rains, clouds release water as drops.\",\"Snow comes from clouds when it is very cold.\",\"A rainbow appears when sunlight shines through rain droplets.\",\"Clouds can be seen when the sky is blue or grey.\",\"Clouds move with the wind.\",\"Clouds are important for the water cycle.\",\"They help keep the Earth cool by reflecting sunlight.\",\"Clouds can be described as cotton, smoke, or clouds of milk.\",\"Clouds can be high, low, or middle in the sky.\",\"Clouds can be thick (stormy) or thin (clear).\",\"Clouds are part of the atmosphere.\",\"Clouds help plants grow by providing water.\",\"Clouds can be seen in many shapes and sizes.\",\"Clouds can be white, gray, or sometimes colorful.\",\"Clouds are made of water vapor that condenses.\",\"Clouds can be seen in pictures and poems.\",\"Clouds are a natural part of weather.\",\"Clouds can be fun to watch and to learn about.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What color is the cloud described as in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"White\",\"Grey\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem describes the cloud as \'fluffy white\'.\",\"topic\":\"4.5 Cloud\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the cloud look like in the sky according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"A pile of cotton\",\"A piece of paper\",\"A white bird\",\"A tall tree\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem asks what is \'Like a pile of cotton in the sky?\'.\",\"topic\":\"4.5 Cloud\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who are the authors of the poem \'Cloud\'?\",\"options\":[\"William Wordsworth\",\"Jackie Silberg and Pam Schiller\",\"Robert Frost\",\"Enid Blyton\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text attributes the poem to Jackie Silberg\\/Pam Schiller.\",\"topic\":\"4.5 Cloud\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the cloud when the wind blows hard and strong?\",\"options\":[\"It disappears immediately\",\"It turns into a dark color\",\"It very gently floats along\",\"It falls down to the ground\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'And when the wind blows hard and strong, What very gently floats along?\'.\",\"topic\":\"4.5 Cloud\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the cloud floating according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"On the ocean water\",\"In the high blue sky\",\"Under the green trees\",\"On the mountain top\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions looking up in the \'high blue sky\' to see it float by.\",\"topic\":\"4.5 Cloud\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What two things does the cloud bring down to us?\",\"options\":[\"Cotton and wool\",\"Wind and air\",\"Rain and snow\",\"Sunlight and heat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem asks, \'What brings the rain? What brings the snow?\'.\",\"topic\":\"4.5 Cloud\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see something \'showering down on us below\' during winter, what is the cloud bringing?\",\"options\":[\"Cotton\",\"Wind\",\"Snow\",\"Blue sky\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions that the cloud brings snow which showers down on us.\",\"topic\":\"4.5 Cloud\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the poem describes how the cloud moves even when the wind is strong?\",\"options\":[\"Quickly\",\"Gently\",\"Roughly\",\"Noisily\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem uses the word \'gently\' to describe how it floats along.\",\"topic\":\"4.5 Cloud\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet compare the cloud to a \'pile of cotton\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is heavy and hard\",\"Because it is fluffy and white\",\"Because it is used to make clothes\",\"Because it grows on plants in the sky\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Clouds are compared to cotton because they are both \'fluffy white\'.\",\"topic\":\"4.5 Cloud\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, which of these is a main function of the cloud?\",\"options\":[\"To block the blue sky\",\"To bring rain and snow\",\"To stop the wind from blowing\",\"To stay still in the sky\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem highlights that the cloud \'brings the rain\' and \'brings the snow\'.\",\"topic\":\"4.5 Cloud\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following words is listed in the exercise to find a rhyming word for?\",\"options\":[\"Cloud\",\"Strong\",\"Rain\",\"Wiggle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The exercise specifically lists \'strong\' as one of the words to find a rhyme for.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'Listen and do\' section, what should you do with your fingers?\",\"options\":[\"Snap them\",\"Clap them\",\"Wiggle them upward\",\"Hide them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly instructs to \'Wiggle your fingers upward\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which topic is suggested for writing a short and simple poem in section \'e\'?\",\"options\":[\"Sun\",\"Rainbow\",\"Wind\",\"Storm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Section \'e\' lists \'Rain\', \'Cloud\', and \'Rainbow\' as topics for writing a poem.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct way to open your hands as per the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Palm up\",\"Palm down\",\"In a fist\",\"Behind your back\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instruction says to \'Open your hands palm down\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In section \'e\', what kind of poem are you asked to write?\",\"options\":[\"Long and complex\",\"Short and simple\",\"Funny and loud\",\"A rhyming story\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies writing a \'short and simple\' poem.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list is a rhyming word task for \'sky\'?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"High\",\"Fly\",\"Sky\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'sky\' as one of the words needing a completion for its rhyme.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the \'Listen and do\' instructions, in which direction should your fingers move?\",\"options\":[\"Downward\",\"Sideways\",\"Upward\",\"Circular\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instruction states to wiggle fingers \'upward\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you choose to write about the weather based on section \'e\', which topic would you pick?\",\"options\":[\"Rain\",\"Summer\",\"Winter\",\"Spring\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Rain\' is one of the three specific topics provided in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a word provided in the rhyming table in section \'b\'?\",\"options\":[\"high\",\"strong\",\"sky\",\"rain\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table in section \'b\' only contains \'high\', \'strong\', and \'sky\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the common purpose of the topics \'Rain\', \'Cloud\', and \'Rainbow\' in this exercise?\",\"options\":[\"They are words to rhyme\",\"They are actions to do\",\"They are topics for writing a poem\",\"They are words to wiggle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Section \'e\' groups these three words as topics for writing a short and simple poem.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21418,11,3,'English','en','Tej, The Tiger','[\"Tej is a tiger, a wild animal.\",\"Tigers have orange bodies with black stripes.\",\"Their eyes are bright and teeth are sharp.\",\"Tigers have strong legs and can run fast.\",\"They live in forests with tall trees, rivers and grass.\",\"Their home is called a den where they rest during the day.\",\"They hunt deer and other animals by stalking quietly.\",\"A stalking walk is called a stalk.\",\"Tigers can roar loudly to communicate with other tigers.\",\"A tiger’s roar can be heard far away.\",\"Tigers are meat‑eaters and hunt when hungry.\",\"A baby tiger is called a cub.\",\"Tigers can swim well to cross rivers.\",\"India’s national animal is the tiger.\",\"Protecting tigers helps keep the jungle healthy.\"]','[{\"q\":\"On which date is International Tiger Day celebrated?\",\"options\":[\"29th June\",\"29th July\",\"15th August\",\"26th January\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that International Tiger Day is celebrated on 29th July.\",\"topic\":\"Tej, the Tiger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the tiger in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Sheru\",\"Raja\",\"Tej\",\"Bagheera\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The tiger introduces himself by saying, \'Hello! I am Tej.\'\",\"topic\":\"Tej, the Tiger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of animal is Tej?\",\"options\":[\"A pet animal\",\"A farm animal\",\"A wild animal\",\"A domestic animal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tej says, \'I am a tiger, a wild animal.\'\",\"topic\":\"Tej, the Tiger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what are Tej\'s teeth like?\",\"options\":[\"Small\",\"Sharp\",\"Soft\",\"Weak\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes Tej\'s teeth as \'sharp\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tej, the Tiger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where does Tej rest during the day?\",\"options\":[\"Under a tree\",\"In a river\",\"In a den\",\"On the grass\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'My home is called a den. I rest there during the day.\'\",\"topic\":\"Tej, the Tiger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these does Tej like to have in his forest home?\",\"options\":[\"Hot deserts\",\"Cool rivers\",\"Dry sand\",\"Big cities\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tej mentions he likes places with \'cool rivers\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tej, the Tiger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what pattern can you see on the tiger\'s orange body that matches the text?\",\"options\":[\"White spots\",\"Black stripes\",\"Brown circles\",\"Blue lines\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says his body is orange with black stripes, which is clearly visible in the drawing.\",\"topic\":\"Tej, the Tiger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/085_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where is the tiger sitting?\",\"options\":[\"Inside the water\",\"On top of a tree\",\"Outside his den near the water\",\"In a wooden cage\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the tiger sitting near a rocky opening (den) and a river.\",\"topic\":\"Tej, the Tiger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/085_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If Tej has strong legs and bright eyes, which word from the text best describes his character?\",\"options\":[\"Scared\",\"Brave\",\"Lazy\",\"Tiny\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tej says, \'I look beautiful and brave, don\'t I?\'\",\"topic\":\"Tej, the Tiger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the description of his home, why does Tej live in the forest?\",\"options\":[\"Because he likes tall green trees and soft grass\",\"Because he likes to live with people\",\"Because he wants to play in the city\",\"Because he likes to sleep in a bed\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Tej lives in the forest because he likes places with tall green trees and soft grass.\",\"topic\":\"Tej, the Tiger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"When does the tiger hunt for food?\",\"options\":[\"When it wants to play\",\"When it feels hungry\",\"When it is sleeping\",\"When it is raining\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I hunt when I feel hungry.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hunting and Habits\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the quiet and slow walk of a tiger called?\",\"options\":[\"A run\",\"A jump\",\"A stalk\",\"A crawl\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the quiet walk as a \'stalk\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hunting and Habits\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of eater is the tiger?\",\"options\":[\"A grass-eater\",\"A fruit-eater\",\"A meat-eater\",\"A leaf-eater\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The tiger says, \'I am a meat-eater.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hunting and Habits\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the tiger make a loud roar?\",\"options\":[\"To go to sleep\",\"To talk to other tigers\",\"To find water\",\"To hide from others\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the roar helps the tiger talk to other tigers.\",\"topic\":\"Hunting and Habits\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does the tiger move when it is hunting?\",\"options\":[\"Noisily and fast\",\"Quietly and slowly\",\"By jumping high\",\"By shouting loudly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I move quietly and slowly when I hunt.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hunting and Habits\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the tiger\'s roar show to other animals?\",\"options\":[\"That it is tired\",\"That it is lost\",\"That this is its home\",\"That it is cold\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The roar shows \'that this is my home\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hunting and Habits\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a tiger needs to get to the other side of a river, what will it do?\",\"options\":[\"It will fly over\",\"It will swim across\",\"It will call for help\",\"It will wait for a boat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I can also swim well when I need to cross a river.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hunting and Habits\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the tiger do the moment it sees its prey?\",\"options\":[\"It starts to sleep\",\"It runs very fast to catch it\",\"It walks away slowly\",\"It makes a quiet sound\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'When I see my prey, I can run very fast to catch it.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hunting and Habits\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the \'stalk\' important for the tiger while hunting?\",\"options\":[\"It helps the tiger move without being heard\",\"It helps the tiger sleep better\",\"It makes the tiger look beautiful\",\"It helps the tiger cross the river\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A stalk is a quiet walk, which helps the tiger approach prey without making noise.\",\"topic\":\"Hunting and Habits\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these animals would a tiger hunt?\",\"options\":[\"A butterfly\",\"A deer\",\"A small bird\",\"A fish\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions, \'I hunt deer and other animals.\'\",\"topic\":\"Hunting and Habits\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is a baby tiger called according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A kitten\",\"A calf\",\"A cub\",\"A puppy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'It\'s called a cub!\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who took care of the tiger when it was a baby?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher\",\"Its mother\",\"The jungle\",\"Its father\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'When I was a cub, my mother took care of me.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these did the mother tiger NOT teach the cub?\",\"options\":[\"How to walk\",\"How to run\",\"How to hunt\",\"How to fly\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions walking, running, and hunting, but not flying.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The tiger is the national animal of which country?\",\"options\":[\"Africa\",\"India\",\"America\",\"Japan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The tiger says, \'I am India\'s national animal.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the tiger live now that it is grown up?\",\"options\":[\"It lives with its mother\",\"It lives in a group\",\"It lives alone\",\"It lives with the teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Now I live alone.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'For the Teacher\' section, what should learners identify from the story?\",\"options\":[\"The tiger\'s weight\",\"Main characters and important ideas\",\"The names of the trees\",\"How to draw a tiger\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note says to \'Encourage learners to identify main characters and important ideas from the story.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What topics should the teacher encourage students to read and discuss?\",\"options\":[\"National birds and animals\",\"Different types of cars\",\"How to cook food\",\"Planets and stars\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text suggests encouraging them to \'read and discuss about national birds and animals.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the tiger ask people to protect tigers?\",\"options\":[\"So they can learn to hunt\",\"So they can live happily\",\"So they can find their mother\",\"So they can live in a house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Please protect tigers like me, so that we can live happily.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the tiger say it loves to live?\",\"options\":[\"In a cage\",\"In a city\",\"In the jungle\",\"In a zoo\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The tiger says, \'I love my jungle.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is an important message the tiger gives to the readers?\",\"options\":[\"Tigers should be hunted\",\"Tigers should be protected\",\"Tigers should live in schools\",\"Tigers should not run\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The tiger asks readers to \'Please protect tigers like me\', which is a main idea of the text.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21419,11,3,'English','en','My Profile','[\"- A profile is a short description about yourself.\",\"- It usually includes your name, age, family members, school, hobbies and favourite things.\",\"- Write in simple sentences: \\\"I am ___ years old.\\\"\",\"- Mention where you live and what you like to do.\",\"- Include your favourite colour, food, animal, fruit and subject.\",\"- End with a wish: \\\"I wish to be ___ when I grow up.\\\"\",\"- Use capital letters at the start of each sentence.\",\"- Keep sentences short and clear for Standard‑3 students.\",\"- Practice writing your own profile to improve writing skills.\",\"- Check spelling of common words like mother, father, colour, favourite, animal, fruit, subject.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the name of Bela’s mother?\",\"options\":[\"Prakash\",\"Vinita\",\"Shahapur\",\"Chakli\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'My mother’s name is Vinita.\'\",\"topic\":\"Bela\'s Profile\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How old is Bela?\",\"options\":[\"Seven years old\",\"Eight years old\",\"Nine years old\",\"Ten years old\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Bela says, \'I am nine years old.\'\",\"topic\":\"Bela\'s Profile\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which grade does Bela study?\",\"options\":[\"Grade one\",\"Grade two\",\"Grade three\",\"Grade four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Bela mentions, \'I study in grade three.\'\",\"topic\":\"Bela\'s Profile\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Bela want to become when she grows up?\",\"options\":[\"A teacher\",\"An artist\",\"A doctor\",\"A pilot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Bela says, \'I wish to be an artist when I grow up.\'\",\"topic\":\"Bela\'s Profile\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Bela wants to eat her favorite fruit, which one should she choose?\",\"options\":[\"Apple\",\"Banana\",\"Mango\",\"Orange\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Bela\'s favorite fruit is mango.\",\"topic\":\"Bela\'s Profile\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Bela is going to color a picture with her favorite color. Which crayon will she use?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Bela states, \'My favourite colour is yellow.\'\",\"topic\":\"Bela\'s Profile\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs shows Bela\'s favorite foods?\",\"options\":[\"Puranpoli and Laddu\",\"Chakli and Puranpoli\",\"Mango and Chakli\",\"Puranpoli and Apple\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Puranpoli and Chakli\' as her favorite foods.\",\"topic\":\"Bela\'s Profile\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If Bela is asked to choose between a cat and a dog, why would she choose the cat?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is small\",\"Because it is her favorite animal\",\"Because it drinks milk\",\"Because it catches mice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that her favorite animal is the cat.\",\"topic\":\"Bela\'s Profile\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the girl wearing in her hair?\",\"options\":[\"Red ribbons\",\"White bows\",\"Blue caps\",\"Yellow clips\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The drawing shows Bela with two white bows in her hair.\",\"topic\":\"Bela\'s Profile\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/088_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are you supposed to put in the empty box?\",\"options\":[\"A drawing of a cat\",\"Your photo\",\"A picture of a mango\",\"Bela\'s name\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The box in the figure is labeled \'Your Photo\'.\",\"topic\":\"Bela\'s Profile\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/088_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the profile template, what grade does the student study in?\",\"options\":[\"Grade one\",\"Grade two\",\"Grade three\",\"Grade four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'I study in grade three.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these topics is specifically suggested \'For the Teacher\' to encourage learners to write about?\",\"options\":[\"My school\",\"My favourite food\",\"My pet\",\"My village\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'For the Teacher\' section lists \'My favourite food\' as one of the three suggested topics.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should a student place in the box at the very beginning of the profile?\",\"options\":[\"A drawing of a flower\",\"Their father\'s signature\",\"Their own photo\",\"A picture of their school\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text begins with the instruction \'Your Photo\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the profile, what information comes immediately after the mother\'s name?\",\"options\":[\"The father\'s name\",\"The favorite colour\",\"The place where I live\",\"The age\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The template follows the order: \'My mother’s name is ..... My father’s name is .....\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to write about their best friend, which suggested topic from the teacher\'s note should they use?\",\"options\":[\"My family\",\"My favourite food\",\"My friend\",\"My profile\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note suggests \'My friend\' as a specific topic for writing.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where should a student write the name of their town or city in the profile?\",\"options\":[\"I study in...\",\"I live in...\",\"I wish to be...\",\"I like to...\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'I live in\' is used to indicate a person\'s place of residence.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the profile asks the student to think about their future career or dreams?\",\"options\":[\"I like to...\",\"My favorite colour is...\",\"I wish to be ..... when I grow up\",\"I am .... years old\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sentence \'I wish to be... when I grow up\' refers to future aspirations.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many specific extra topics are listed in the \'For the Teacher\' section?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The section lists three topics: My family, My favourite food, and My friend.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of information is missing in the sentence \'I am ____ years old\'?\",\"options\":[\"A name\",\"A number\",\"A colour\",\"A place\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Age is expressed as a number of years.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a personal preference asked for in the main profile template but NOT in the teacher\'s extra list?\",\"options\":[\"Favorite colour\",\"Favorite food\",\"Family members\",\"Friends\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'My favorite colour\' is in the main template, while the others are in the teacher\'s list.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21420,11,3,'English','en','Money cannot Buy Everything','[\"Money means money but it cannot buy everything.\",\"Aman is 8 years old.\",\"His father earns about Rs.500 per hour.\",\"Aman has saved about Rs.1,500 in his piggy bank.\",\"Aman wants his father to spend time with him, play and have dinner together.\",\"The story shows that time and love are more valuable than money.\",\"The moral: Money cannot buy love and time.\",\"Aman’s father is busy and forgets to spend time with his son.\",\"Aman asks how much his father earns to understand the value of money.\",\"Aman’s father is surprised by his son’s question.\",\"The father embraces his son after learning his wish.\",\"The story encourages children to ask questions and value relationships.\",\"Teachers can ask students to visit a shop and note prices.\",\"Teachers can ask students to read stories and identify characters.\",\"Teachers can ask students to find simple sentences and questions in a story.\",\"The story is about a child who wants to spend time with his father.\",\"The father’s earnings are about Rs.500 per hour, not per day.\",\"The piggy bank holds Rs.1,500, which is 3 times the hourly wage.\",\"The story teaches that money cannot buy time, love or happiness.\",\"The father’s love is priceless and cannot be bought with money.\",\"The story is suitable for Standard‑3 students to learn values.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How old was Aman in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Six years old\",\"Seven years old\",\"Eight years old\",\"Nine years old\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Aman was eight years old.\'\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Aman was the ________ child of his parents.\",\"options\":[\"first\",\"second\",\"only\",\"youngest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'He was the only child of his parents.\'\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"On which day did Aman stay awake until his father came home?\",\"options\":[\"Saturday\",\"Sunday\",\"Monday\",\"Friday\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'On Saturday evening, Aman kept awake till his father came.\'\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How much money did Aman have saved in his piggy bank?\",\"options\":[\"Rs. 500\",\"Rs. 1,000\",\"Rs. 1,500\",\"Rs. 2,000\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aman says, \'I have saved around Rs. 1,500 in my piggy bank.\'\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Aman rarely see his father in the morning?\",\"options\":[\"His father left before Aman woke up\",\"His father was still asleep when Aman left for school\",\"His father worked in another city\",\"Aman went to school very early\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'He remained asleep by the time Aman left for school.\'\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Aman\'s father confused when Aman spoke to him?\",\"options\":[\"Because Aman was still awake\",\"Because Aman asked how much he earns in a day\",\"Because Aman was crying\",\"Because Aman wanted to go outside\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Aman’s father was confused and asked, “My dear son, why are you asking this question?”\' after Aman asked about his earnings.\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'embraced\' mean in the last sentence of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Scolded\",\"Hugged\",\"Ignored\",\"Called out\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'embraced\' means to hold someone closely in one\'s arms as a sign of affection.\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the main reason Aman wanted his father\'s money information?\",\"options\":[\"He wanted to buy a new toy\",\"He wanted to know if they were rich\",\"He wanted to pay for his father\'s time\",\"He wanted to give it to his mother\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aman used the information to offer his savings in exchange for three hours of his father\'s time.\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Aman\'s father earns Rs. 500 in one hour, how many hours of time did Aman try to \'buy\' with his Rs. 1,500?\",\"options\":[\"1 hour\",\"2 hours\",\"3 hours\",\"5 hours\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rs. 1,500 divided by Rs. 500 per hour equals 3 hours.\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What specific activities did Aman want to do with his father during the three hours?\",\"options\":[\"Go to the office and work\",\"Play and have dinner\",\"Watch a movie and sleep\",\"Go to school and study\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aman says, \'I want you to be with me, play with me and have dinner with me.\'\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Aman\'s father doing when Aman approaches him with the piggy bank?\",\"options\":[\"He is sleeping on the sofa\",\"He is working on a laptop\",\"He is eating his dinner\",\"He is reading a newspaper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows the father sitting on a sofa with a laptop on his lap.\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/089_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the color and shape of the object Aman is holding?\",\"options\":[\"A blue square box\",\"A pink pig-shaped bank\",\"A yellow round ball\",\"A green rectangular book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows Aman holding a pink piggy bank shaped like a pig.\",\"topic\":\"Money cannot Buy Everything\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"11\\/089_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should learners note down when they visit a store?\",\"options\":[\"The name of the shopkeeper\",\"The color of the walls\",\"The price of different objects\",\"The number of people in the store\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to visit the store and note down the price of different objects.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list means to hold someone closely in one\'s arms?\",\"options\":[\"Confused\",\"Embraced\",\"Amount\",\"Remain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Embraced\' is one of the words listed in the \'Listen and repeat\' section.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should students be motivated to do after reading stories from the library?\",\"options\":[\"Express about the stories read\",\"Return the books immediately\",\"Draw the cover page\",\"Count the number of pages\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states teachers should motivate learners to express about the stories they have read from the library.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What helps learners find simple sentences and questions in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The price of the book\",\"The library teacher\",\"Punctuation marks\",\"The color of the ink\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions finding simple sentences and questions with the help of punctuation marks.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is looking for a \'?\' in a story, what are they trying to identify?\",\"options\":[\"A character\",\"A price tag\",\"A question\",\"A storyline\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using punctuation marks to find questions.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these objects is specifically mentioned for students to guess the price of?\",\"options\":[\"A school bag\",\"A cricket bat\",\"A water bottle\",\"A lunch box\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A cricket bat is listed under section \'c\' for guessing the price.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When a teacher asks a student to identify \'who\' is in the story, which activity are they doing?\",\"options\":[\"Identifying different characters\",\"Guessing the price\",\"Finding punctuation marks\",\"Visiting a store\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Identifying characters involves recognizing the people or figures in a story.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How should learners be encouraged to express the storyline?\",\"options\":[\"By reading it exactly as written\",\"In their own words\",\"By writing it in a different language\",\"By only using punctuation marks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s instructions state to motivate learners to express the storyline in their own words.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If a student visits a store and sees a notebook, what action does the text suggest they take?\",\"options\":[\"Buy the notebook\",\"Note down its price\",\"Read it in the store\",\"Give it to the teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to visit the store and note down the price of objects like notebooks.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT an activity mentioned for the teacher to encourage?\",\"options\":[\"Identifying characters\",\"Expressing storylines in own words\",\"Calculating the total profit of the store\",\"Finding simple sentences using punctuation\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Calculating store profit is not mentioned; the text focuses on prices, stories, characters, and punctuation.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21421,11,3,'English','en','Stay Calm and Smile','[\"Stay calm and smile means to keep your cool when you feel angry.\",\"Anger is a normal feeling but it must be controlled so it does not hurt others.\",\"You can control anger by talking to someone you trust, like parents or friends.\",\"Sharing your feelings helps you feel better.\",\"Doing something you enjoy, like playing, drawing, or listening to music, can calm you.\",\"Taking deep breaths and counting from 100 to 1 helps you relax.\",\"Walking or running in a park can also reduce anger.\",\"When you feel angry, try to stay quiet for a moment before reacting.\",\"Smile and think of something happy to change your mood.\",\"If you feel angry, ask a teacher or a friend to help you calm down.\",\"It is okay to feel angry, but it is important to manage it.\",\"You can use simple techniques like breathing, counting, or talking to control anger.\",\"Being calm and smiling shows you are in control of your feelings.\",\"Practice these techniques so you can stay calm in any situation.\",\"Remember: Anger is natural, but calmness is powerful.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who says that everyone feels angry because things do not always happen the way we want?\",\"options\":[\"A teacher\",\"A grandmother\",\"A friend\",\"A brother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text starts with the speaker saying, \'My grandmother says...\'\",\"topic\":\"Techniques to control anger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How should you count in your mind to help control your anger?\",\"options\":[\"1 to 10\",\"10 to 100\",\"100 to 1\",\"1 to 100\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests to \'count numbers 100 to 1 in your mind\'.\",\"topic\":\"Techniques to control anger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where can you go for a walk or run to feel better?\",\"options\":[\"In the classroom\",\"In the kitchen\",\"In the park\",\"On the road\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions you can \'go for walk\\/ run in the park\'.\",\"topic\":\"Techniques to control anger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why do people feel angry?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are tired\",\"Because things do not always happen the way they want\",\"Because they want to sleep\",\"Because they are hungry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The grandmother explains that anger happens because things don\'t always go the way we want.\",\"topic\":\"Techniques to control anger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the grandmother say about the feeling of anger?\",\"options\":[\"It is bad to feel angry\",\"It is okay to feel angry\",\"You should never feel angry\",\"Anger is always funny\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'It\'s okay to feel angry but it is important to manage it.\'\",\"topic\":\"Techniques to control anger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When does the speaker in the text feel very angry?\",\"options\":[\"When they have to go to school\",\"When people do not listen to them\",\"When they have to eat vegetables\",\"When they lose a toy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speaker says, \'I feel very angry when my family, my friends and other people do not listen to me.\'\",\"topic\":\"Techniques to control anger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are feeling angry, what should you do with your breathing?\",\"options\":[\"Hold your breath\",\"Breathe very fast\",\"Take deep breaths\",\"Stop breathing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"One of the techniques mentioned is to \'take deep breath\'.\",\"topic\":\"Techniques to control anger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to share your feelings to feel better, who should you talk to?\",\"options\":[\"Strangers on the street\",\"Your parents or friends\",\"Only yourself\",\"No one\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests, \'You can talk with your parents or friends and share your feelings.\'\",\"topic\":\"Techniques to control anger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a creative activity mentioned in the text to help you feel better?\",\"options\":[\"Shouting\",\"Drawing\",\"Fighting\",\"Running\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Play, draw or listen to music to feel better.\'\",\"topic\":\"Techniques to control anger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What should you share besides your feelings when you talk to others about your anger?\",\"options\":[\"Your toys\",\"Your food\",\"Your opinions about things that make you angry\",\"Your homework\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'You can also share your opinions about things that make you angry.\'\",\"topic\":\"Techniques to control anger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do along with being calm according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Cry\",\"Smile\",\"Shout\",\"Run\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Be calm and smile.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the speaker say they can manage now?\",\"options\":[\"Their homework\",\"Their toys\",\"Their anger\",\"Their food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Now I can manage my anger.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is the first word in the \'Read aloud\' list?\",\"options\":[\"calm\",\"manage\",\"feel\",\"control\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The \'Read aloud\' list starts with the word \'feel\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main advice given in the text to handle anger?\",\"options\":[\"Be calm and smile\",\"Read aloud quickly\",\"Feel techniques\",\"Say yeah loudly\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text suggests to \'Be calm and smile\' to manage anger.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list means to handle or deal with something effectively?\",\"options\":[\"feel\",\"techniques\",\"manage\",\"calm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To manage something means to handle or deal with it.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the result of saying \'Yeah! So true\'?\",\"options\":[\"Being angry\",\"Managing anger\",\"Reading aloud\",\"Feeling techniques\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speaker agrees it is true and then says they can now manage their anger.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are using different ways to stay quiet, which word from the list describes these \'ways\'?\",\"options\":[\"feel\",\"techniques\",\"control\",\"manage\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Techniques are specific ways or methods of doing something.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When you are trying not to let your anger take over, which word from the list are you practicing?\",\"options\":[\"feel\",\"techniques\",\"control\",\"smile\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Control means to have power over something, like one\'s anger.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Read aloud\' list describes a sensation or emotion?\",\"options\":[\"techniques\",\"control\",\"manage\",\"feel\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"To \'feel\' is to experience an emotion or sensation.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the list \'feel techniques control manage calm\', which word is a synonym for \'manage\' in the context of handling anger?\",\"options\":[\"feel\",\"techniques\",\"control\",\"calm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the context of anger, to control it is similar to managing it.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21422,11,3,'English','en','Word Family - VIII','[\"Word family means a group of words that share the same root word, like bake, baker, baking.\",\"In a word family, you can change the ending to make new words: bake → baker, baking, baked.\",\"The book shows words that have the same ending, such as -ate, -ate, -ate, etc.\",\"You can find many words that start with the same letters, for example: bake, baker, baking, baked.\",\"The word family helps you learn new words faster because you already know the base word.\",\"A word family can have many words: bake, baker, baking, baked, bakery, etc.\",\"When you read a new word, try to see if it belongs to a word family you already know.\",\"The book lists words that have ‘tr’ in them, like ‘control’ or ‘rocket’ – these are special groups to remember.\",\"Words that end with ‘ing’ are action words, like ‘running’, ‘jumping’ – they show an action is happening.\",\"The longest word in the list is ‘immediately’ – it has 11 letters.\",\"Words related to space include ‘astronaut’, ‘rocket’, ‘space’, ‘gravity’ and ‘sunlight’.\",\"Words related to the forest are ‘forest’, ‘wild’, ‘cub’ and ‘hunting’ – they describe nature.\",\"Opposites of some words: spend ↔ earn, pet ↔ let, downward ↔ upward, ugly ↔ beautiful.\",\"Words that end with ‘y’ in the list: ‘beautiful’, ‘colour’, ‘energy’, ‘different’, ‘learning’, ‘protect’, ‘suit’.\",\"The book also shows words that have nine letters, like ‘question’, ‘puzzle’, ‘colour’ and ‘future’.\",\"Use flash cards or word games to practice these word families and remember them better.\",\"Remember to read each word carefully and find its meaning and use in a sentence.\",\"When you see a new word, try to guess its meaning from the root word and the ending.\",\"Practice writing the words in sentences to improve your vocabulary.\",\"Keep a small notebook of new words and their families to review every week.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these words is found in the first list of \'Read aloud\'?\",\"options\":[\"cake\",\"book\",\"look\",\"cook\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'cake\' is explicitly listed in the third line of the \'Read aloud\' section.\",\"topic\":\"Word Grid Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text suggest we do with a cake?\",\"options\":[\"Eat it\",\"Bake it\",\"Buy it\",\"Sell it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sentence in the text says, \'Let us bake a cake.\'\",\"topic\":\"Word Grid Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the sentences, where shall we go?\",\"options\":[\"To the park\",\"To the school\",\"To the lake\",\"To the shop\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'We shall go to the lake.\'\",\"topic\":\"Word Grid Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'gate\' and \'rate\' in the word list?\",\"options\":[\"face\",\"late\",\"cage\",\"same\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the first list, \'gate\', \'rate\', \'date\', and \'late\' are grouped together as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Word Grid Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence from the text: \'Open the ____.\'\",\"options\":[\"door\",\"book\",\"gate\",\"box\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text contains the specific instruction: \'Open the gate.\'\",\"topic\":\"Word Grid Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list ends with the same sound as \'race\' and \'lace\'?\",\"options\":[\"page\",\"gave\",\"face\",\"lake\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Face\' belongs to the same word family group as \'lace\' and \'race\' in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Word Grid Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the first row of the grid: | h | t | a | k | e | b | c | g | w | h |. Which word is hidden here?\",\"options\":[\"take\",\"bake\",\