\"तलवारी\",\"जिभा\",\"हात\",\"डोळे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेत \'अस्मानाच्या सुलतानीला जबाब देती जिभा\' असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"महाराष्ट्राची मनगटे कशी आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"लोखंडी\",\"पोलादी\",\"दगडी\",\"कठोर\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेत \'पोलादी मनगटे खेळती, खेळ जीवघेणी\' असा उल्लेख आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"महाराष्ट्र कशाच्या घामाने भिजला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"पावसाच्या\",\"नदीच्या\",\"निढळाच्या (कपाळाच्या)\",\"समुद्राच्या\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"कवितेत \'निढळाच्या घामाने भिजला\' असे म्हटले आहे, ज्याचा अर्थ कष्टाचा घाम असा होतो.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"महाराष्ट्र कशासाठी झिजला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"स्वतःच्या सुखासाठी\",\"देश गौरवासाठी\",\"पैशासाठी\",\"लेणी कोरण्यासाठी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेत \'देश गौरवासाठी झिजला\' असे स्पष्टपणे सांगितले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"\'दरी दरीतून नाद गुंजला\' या ओळीचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"दरीमध्ये पाणी वाहत आहे\",\"दरीमध्ये पक्षी ओरडत आहेत\",\"महाराष्ट्राचा जयजयकार सगळीकडे घुमत आहे\",\"दरीमध्ये वारा सुटला आहे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"नाद गुंजणे म्हणजे महाराष्ट्राच्या नावाचा आवाज सर्वत्र पसरणे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"महाराष्ट्र कशाच्या उन्हात शिजला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"कडक उन्हात\",\"दारिद्र्याच्या उन्हात\",\"दुखाच्या उन्हात\",\"आगीच्या उन्हात\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेत \'दारिद्र्याच्या उन्हात शिजला\' असा शब्दप्रयोग केला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"\'खेळ जीवघेणी\' यातून महाराष्ट्राचा कोणता गुण दिसून येतो?\",\"options\":[\"भीती\",\"आळस\",\"शौर्य आणि धाडस\",\"शांतता\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"जीवघेणे खेळ खेळणे हे शौर्याचे आणि धाडसाचे लक्षण आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"या कवितेत महाराष्ट्राचा जयजयकार करण्यासाठी कोणता शब्द वापरला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"रडा\",\"गर्जा\",\"बसा\",\"पळा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेच्या सुरुवातीलाच \'गर्जा महाराष्ट्र माझा\' असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"राज्यगीत\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21449,13,3,'Maths','en','Find Shapes Around Us','[\"Shapes are all around us in everyday objects.\",\"Three-dimensional shapes have length, width, and height.\",\"Common 3D shapes: cube, cuboid, cylinder, cone, sphere.\",\"A cube has 6 square faces, 12 edges, and 8 corners.\",\"A cuboid has 6 rectangular faces, 12 edges, and 8 corners.\",\"A cylinder has 2 flat circular faces and 1 curved surface.\",\"A cone has 1 flat circular face and 1 curved surface meeting at a point.\",\"A sphere has no faces, edges, or corners; it is completely round.\",\"The net of a 3D shape is a flat pattern that can be folded to make the shape.\",\"Nets help us understand how 3D shapes are formed from 2D surfaces.\",\"Objects like dice, boxes, cans, and balls are examples of 3D shapes.\",\"We can identify shapes by observing their faces, edges, and corners.\",\"Shapes in nature include spheres (fruits), cylinders (tree trunks), and cones (mountains).\",\"Playing with blocks and clay helps us learn about 3D shapes.\",\"Activities like unfolding boxes show us the nets of shapes.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the name of the geometric shape similar to the gift box?\",\"options\":[\"Cube\",\"Cuboid\",\"Cone\",\"Sphere\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the text explicitly labels the shape similar to the gift box as a Cuboid.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the shape: \'I have no corners and no edges. I have only one curved surface.\'\",\"options\":[\"Cylinder\",\"Cone\",\"Sphere\",\"Cuboid\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes a shape with no corners, no edges, and only one curved surface as the third \'Identify who am I\' item, which is a sphere.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which shape is described as having one corner, one curved surface, and one flat surface?\",\"options\":[\"Sphere\",\"Cylinder\",\"Cuboid\",\"Cone\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text defines a shape with one corner, one curved surface, and one flat surface in the second \'Identify who am I\' riddle.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many corners does a cylinder have?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"One\",\"Zero\",\"Three\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that a shape with two curved edges and one curved surface (a cylinder) has \'no corners\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are looking at a shape with two curved edges and one curved surface, what is it called?\",\"options\":[\"Cylinder\",\"Cone\",\"Sphere\",\"Cube\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first riddle in the text describes the cylinder as having two curved edges and one curved surface.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these objects from the text would be similar to a cone?\",\"options\":[\"A ball\",\"A gift box\",\"A party hat\",\"A cake\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the table, the party hat is paired with a cone shape.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which object is shown directly above the cake?\",\"options\":[\"A gift box\",\"A colorful cube\",\"A party hat\",\"A ball\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Looking at the \'Object\' column in the figure, the colorful Rubik\'s cube is placed in the second row, directly above the cake.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/013_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the geometric shape shown for the last object (the ball)?\",\"options\":[\"Circle\",\"Sphere\",\"Cylinder\",\"Oval\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The geometri