n a number depend on?\",\"options\":[\"Its position\",\"Its face value\",\"The total number of digits\",\"The color of the digit\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the place value of a digit in a number depends on its position.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If zero is at any place in a number, what is its place value?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"1\",\"Depends on the position\",\"0\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states that if zero is at any place, its face value and place value both are zero.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 809, what is the face value of the digit 8?\",\"options\":[\"800\",\"80\",\"8\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The face value of a digit is always the digit itself, regardless of its position.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 809, what is the place value of the digit 0?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"0\",\"100\",\"9\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the place value of 0 is always 0.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 524, which digit has the same face value and place value?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"2\",\"4\",\"None of them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the units place, the face value (4) and place value (4) are the same.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If the digit 5 is in the hundreds place, what is its place value?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"50\",\"500\",\"5000\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"5 hundreds is equal to 500.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 809, what is the place value of the digit 8?\",\"options\":[\"8\",\"80\",\"800\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The digit 8 is in the hundreds place, so its place value is 800.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is true for the digit 0 in any position in a number?\",\"options\":[\"Face value is 0 but place value is 10\",\"Face value and place value both are zero\",\"Face value is 10 but place value is 0\",\"Place value depends on the H, T or U column\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that for zero, both face value and place value are zero.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If we move a digit from the units place to the tens place, what happens to its values?\",\"options\":[\"Its face value changes\",\"Its place value changes\",\"Both values change\",\"Neither value changes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Place value depends on position, while face value remains the same as the digit.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the place value shown for the digit 2?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"20\",\"200\",\"22\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows 2 in the \'T\' (tens) column with a place value of 20.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/026_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the face value of the digit 5?\",\"options\":[\"500\",\"50\",\"5\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure explicitly states \'Face value of 5 is 5\'.\",\"topic\":\"Face value and Place value\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/026_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the expanded form of a number?\",\"options\":[\"The sum of the digits in that number\",\"The sum of the place values of the digits in that number\",\"The number written in words only\",\"The number written backwards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the expanded form of a number is the sum of the place values of the digits in that number.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 824, what does the letter \'H\' stand for?\",\"options\":[\"Heavy\",\"Higher\",\"Hundreds\",\"Half\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the H T U notation used in the text, H stands for Hundreds.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the expanded form of 824?\",\"options\":[\"8 + 2 + 4\",\"80 + 20 + 4\",\"800 + 2 + 4\",\"800 + 20 + 4\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly shows 824 = 800 + 20 + 4.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is the number 705 written using H, T, and U notation?\",\"options\":[\"7 H + 0 T + 5 U\",\"70 H + 0 T + 5 U\",\"7 H + 5 T + 0 U\",\"700 H + 0 T + 5 U\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows 705 = 7 H + 0 T + 5 U.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the expanded form 700 + 0 + 5, what does the \'0\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"The Hundreds place\",\"The Tens place\",\"The Units place\",\"The total sum\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In 705, the 0 is in the middle position, which corresponds to the Tens (T) place.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When using the folding strip for the number 735, which parts get hidden after folding?\",\"options\":[\"The digits 7, 3, and 5\",\"The letters H, T, and U\",\"The \'00 +\' and \'0 +\' parts\",\"The whole number\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The activity states that after folding, ‘00 +’ and ‘0 +’ get hidden.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the expanded form of the number 735 as shown in the activity?\",\"options\":[\"70 + 30 + 5\",\"700 + 30 + 5\",\"700 + 3 + 5\",\"7 + 3 + 5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Following the pattern of 824 and 705, the expanded form of 735 is 700 + 30 + 5.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the expanded form of a number is 800 + 20 + 4, what number is seen on the folded strip?\",\"options\":[\"824\",\"800204\",\"86\",\"8204\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows that 800 + 20 + 4 is the expanded form of the number 824.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"On the folding strip activity, what is seen when the strip is opened?\",\"options\":[\"Only the number 735\",\"Only the digit 7\",\"The expanded form of the number\",\"A blank piece of paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'on the opened strip, its expanded form is seen.\'\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct way to break down 705 into its place value components?\",\"options\":[\"7 Hundreds, 5 Tens, 0 Units\",\"7 Hundreds, 0 Tens, 5 Units\",\"0 Hundreds, 7 Tens, 5 Units\",\"70 Hundreds, 0 Tens, 5 Units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines 705 as 7 H + 0 T + 5 U, which means 7 Hundreds, 0 Tens, and 5 Units.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If 735 = 700 + ___ + 5, what value is missing to complete the expanded form?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"300\",\"30\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the number 735, the digit 3 is in the Tens place, so its place value is 30.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which statement is true about the number 824?\",\"options\":[\"It is made of 800, 20, and 4\",\"It is made of 8, 20, and 400\",\"It is made of 80, 20, and 4\",\"It is made of 800, 2, and 4\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The expanded form 800 + 20 + 4 shows the values that make up the number.\",\"topic\":\"Expanded form of number\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21451,13,3,'Maths','en','Addition and Subtraction','[\"Addition is combining two or more numbers to get a total.\",\"Subtraction is finding the difference between two numbers.\",\"When adding, start from the units place and move left.\",\"If the sum of digits in a place is 10 or more, carry over to the next place.\",\"When subtracting, if the top digit is smaller, borrow from the next left place.\",\"Borrowing means taking 1 from the next place, which equals 10 in the current place.\",\"Addition and subtraction are inverse operations.\",\"Word problems can be solved by identifying the operation needed.\",\"To frame a word problem, use real-life situations like buying, giving, or collecting.\",\"Check your answer by using the reverse operation.\",\"Addition is commutative: changing order does not change the sum.\",\"Subtraction is not commutative: changing order changes the result.\",\"Adding zero to a number gives the same number.\",\"Subtracting zero from a number gives the same number.\",\"Subtracting a number from itself gives zero.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, which of these is used to help with the addition of the fruit costs?\",\"options\":[\"Blocks of hundreds, tens rods and unit cubes\",\"Measuring tapes and rulers\",\"Only a number line\",\"Calculators and computers\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to use blocks of hundreds, tens rods, and unit cubes to do the addition.\",\"topic\":\"Addition\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many different methods of arrangement for addition are mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions three methods: horizontal arrangement, vertical arrangement, and addition using a number line.\",\"topic\":\"Addition\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal Gauri wants to achieve after selecting her fruits?\",\"options\":[\"To find the weight of the apples\",\"To find the total cost of fruits purchased\",\"To count the number of chikoos\",\"To see which fruit is heavier\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks \'Then what is the total cost of fruits purchased?\' as the problem to solve.\",\"topic\":\"Addition\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which addition method described in the text involves drawing a line with numbers?\",\"options\":[\"Vertical arrangement\",\"Horizontal arrangement\",\"Addition using number line\",\"Addition using blocks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Addition using number line\' as one of the ways to perform the calculation.\",\"topic\":\"Addition\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you use the horizontal arrangement to add the components of the total cost mentioned in the text, which equation is correct?\",\"options\":[\"200 + 9 + 5 = 214\",\"20 + 90 + 5 = 115\",\"200 + 90 + 5 = 295\",\"2 + 9 + 5 = 16\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text and figures show the total 295 is made of 200, 90, and 5.\",\"topic\":\"Addition\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Gauri buys 1 kilo of apples for Rs. 160 and the total cost is Rs. 295, what is the cost of 1 kilo of chikoo?\",\"options\":[\"Rs. 135\",\"Rs. 295\",\"Rs. 160\",\"Rs. 85\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Subtracting the apple cost (160) from the total (295) gives the chikoo cost (135).\",\"topic\":\"Addition\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many \'tens rods\' are shown in the final total cost at the bottom?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"9\",\"2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The bottom section of the figure shows 9 yellow tens rods representing the number 90.\",\"topic\":\"Addition\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/038_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the price per kg for bananas?\",\"options\":[\"Rs. 160\",\"Rs. 225\",\"Rs. 60\",\"Rs. 50\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The price tag next to the bananas in the shop drawing clearly states \'Rs. 60 per kg\'.\",\"topic\":\"Addition\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/037_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What wa