text says if any object or shape is divided into four equal parts, each part is called a quarter.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If an object is divided into four equal parts, what is each part called?\",\"options\":[\"A half\",\"A whole\",\"A quarter\",\"A piece\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that each part is a quarter of the whole when divided into four equal parts.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What do two quarters make when put together?\",\"options\":[\"A whole\",\"A half\",\"Three quarters\",\"A small part\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Two quarters together make a half.\'\",\"topic\":\"Quarter\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you have a sheet of paper and you want to make quarters, how should you divide it?\",\"options\":[\"Into two equal parts\",\"Into four unequal parts\",\"Into four equal parts\",\"Into three equal parts\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The definition of a quarter requires the object to be divided into four equal parts.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Meghana has 4 equal parts of a bhakari. If she gives you only one part, what fraction did she give you?\",\"options\":[\"A quarter\",\"A half\",\"A whole\",\"Two quarters\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Each of the four equal parts is called a quarter.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To get a quarter, the parts of a shape must be:\",\"options\":[\"Different sizes\",\"Big and small\",\"Equal\",\"Only round\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text emphasizes that the four parts must be \'equal\' to be called quarters.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these can be divided into quarters?\",\"options\":[\"Only food items\",\"Only bhakari\",\"Any object or shape\",\"Only paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'If any object or shape is divided into four equal parts, each part is called a quarter.\'\",\"topic\":\"Quarter\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement is true based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"A quarter is bigger than a half\",\"Four quarters make a half\",\"A quarter is half of a half\",\"Two quarters make a whole\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text directly defines a quarter as \'Half of a half\'.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the activity, what part of the balloons should be coloured yellow?\",\"options\":[\"Half\",\"One quarter\",\"Three quarters\",\"Whole\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states to colour one quarter of the balloons yellow.\",\"topic\":\"Half, quarter and three quarters\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you colour half of a collection red and the remaining half black, how many equal parts have you divided the collection into?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Dividing into halves means splitting the collection into two equal parts.\",\"topic\":\"Half, quarter and three quarters\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given picture, how many beads should be coloured red to show half of the necklace?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"6\",\"8\",\"12\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"There are 12 beads in the necklace, and half of 12 is 6.\",\"topic\":\"Half, quarter and three quarters\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/053_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given picture, if one quarter of the balloons are coloured yellow, how many balloons will remain uncoloured?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"4\",\"6\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"There are 8 balloons. One quarter is 2 balloons. So, 8 minus 2 equals 6 uncoloured balloons.\",\"topic\":\"Half, quarter and three quarters\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/053_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given picture, how many marbles must be coloured blue to show three quarters of the collection?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"6\",\"9\",\"12\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"There are 12 marbles. One quarter is 3, so three quarters (3 times 3) is 9.\",\"topic\":\"Half, quarter and three quarters\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/053_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the necklace activity, what colour should be used for the remaining half of the beads?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Yellow\",\"Blue\",\"Black\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text specifies to colour the remaining half black.\",\"topic\":\"Half, quarter and three quarters\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which fraction of marbles is suggested to be coloured blue in the activity?\",\"options\":[\"Half\",\"One quarter\",\"Three quarters\",\"Remaining half\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions colouring three quarters of the marbles blue.\",\"topic\":\"Half, quarter and three quarters\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these collections is used to show the activity for \'one quarter\'?\",\"options\":[\"Beads\",\"Balloons\",\"Marbles\",\"Necklace\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity for one quarter is specifically linked to the balloons.\",\"topic\":\"Half, quarter and three quarters\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are asked to colour three quarters of a collection, you are colouring:\",\"options\":[\"Less than half\",\"Exactly half\",\"More than half\",\"The whole collection\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Three quarters is more than half of a collection.\",\"topic\":\"Half, quarter and three quarters\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a collection has 4 items, how many items represent one quarter?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"One quarter of 4 is 1.\",\"topic\":\"Half, quarter and three quarters\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Into how many equal parts must a collection be divided to get a \'half\'?\",\"options\":[\"2 equal parts\",\"3 equal part