 parts\",\"Parts considered\",\"The whole object\",\"The number two\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the numerator as the \'parts considered\' or \'shaded parts\'.\",\"topic\":\"Numerator and Denominator\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a whole is divided into 5 equal parts and 4 parts are shaded, what is the denominator?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"1\",\"5\",\"9\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The denominator represents the total equal parts, which is 5 in this case.\",\"topic\":\"Numerator and Denominator\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How do we write \'quarter\' in numbers?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/2\",\"1\\/4\",\"3\\/4\",\"4\\/1\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that 1\\/4 is how we write \'quarter\' in numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Numerator and Denominator\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which number is shown as the \'Parts considered\'?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"1\",\"1\\/2\",\"0\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure explicitly labels the \'Parts considered (numerator)\' as 1.\",\"topic\":\"Numerator and Denominator\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/055_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the denominator for the fraction \'half\'?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows that for the fraction 1\\/2, the denominator (total equal parts) is 2.\",\"topic\":\"Numerator and Denominator\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/055_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a fraction is read as \'three parts out of four\', what is the numerator?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"1\",\"7\",\"3\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text explains that \'three parts out of four\' means the numerator is 3.\",\"topic\":\"Numerator and Denominator\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To write the fraction \'four upon five\', which number must be the numerator?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"4\",\"9\",\"1\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the fraction 4\\/5 (four upon five), the top number 4 is the numerator.\",\"topic\":\"Numerator and Denominator\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the fraction for \'1 quarter\'?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/2\",\"1\\/4\",\"3\\/4\",\"4\\/4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that 1 quarter is written as 1\\/4.\",\"topic\":\"Unit Fraction\",\"part\":15,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the fraction \'2\\/4\' called in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Quarter\",\"Three quarters\",\"Half\",\"One whole\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines 2 quarters as \'Half\' (2\\/4).\",\"topic\":\"Unit Fraction\",\"part\":15,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When the numerator is equal to the denominator, what does the fraction become?\",\"options\":[\"A quarter\",\"A half\",\"Three quarters\",\"One whole\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states that when the numerator is equal to the denominator, it becomes one whole.\",\"topic\":\"Unit Fraction\",\"part\":15,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In fractions like \'half\' and \'quarter\', how does the numerator compare to the denominator?\",\"options\":[\"The numerator is always smaller\",\"The numerator is always larger\",\"The numerator is always equal\",\"The numerator is always zero\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says that in fractions like half and quarter, the numerator is always smaller than the denominator.\",\"topic\":\"Unit Fraction\",\"part\":15,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a flower has 5 petals and 2 of them are coloured, what fraction represents the coloured part?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/5\",\"2\\/5\",\"5\\/2\",\"5\\/5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the example that if 2 out of 5 petals are coloured, the fraction is 2\\/5.\",\"topic\":\"Unit Fraction\",\"part\":15,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is 1\\/4 called a \'unit fraction\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is smaller than a half\",\"Because it has 4 as a deno