 and Proper Fraction\",\"part\":16,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is a fraction called when the denominator is greater than the numerator?\",\"options\":[\"Proper fraction\",\"Improper fraction\",\"Unit fraction\",\"Whole fraction\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that fractions in which the denominator is greater than the numerator are proper fractions.\",\"topic\":\"Definitions of Fractions\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a fraction called when the numerator is greater than the denominator?\",\"options\":[\"Proper fraction\",\"Improper fraction\",\"Unit fraction\",\"Small fraction\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines improper fractions as those where the numerator is greater than the denominator.\",\"topic\":\"Definitions of Fractions\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of a proper fraction according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"7\\/2\",\"6\\/5\",\"5\\/9\",\"13\\/9\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In 5\\/9, the denominator (9) is greater than the numerator (5), making it a proper fraction.\",\"topic\":\"Definitions of Fractions\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of an improper fraction?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/2\",\"3\\/4\",\"11\\/14\",\"19\\/11\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"In 19\\/11, the numerator (19) is greater than the denominator (11), which is the definition of an improper fraction.\",\"topic\":\"Definitions of Fractions\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you take the unit fraction 1\\/4 three times, what fraction do you get?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/4\",\"2\\/4\",\"3\\/4\",\"4\\/4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that 3 times 1\\/4 is 3\\/4.\",\"topic\":\"Definitions of Fractions\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If we take 1\\/4 seven times, we get 7\\/4. What kind of fraction is 7\\/4?\",\"options\":[\"Proper fraction\",\"Improper fraction\",\"Unit fraction\",\"Half fraction\"],\