},{\"q\":\"If a teacher follows the instructions, what will they provide to the students for practice?\",\"options\":[\"Only a textbook\",\"Materials from the mathematics kit\",\"A calculator\",\"A storybook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs teachers to use \'materials from the mathematics kit\'.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the examples provided, what does the symbol \'[ ]\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"A subtraction sign\",\"A multiplication sign\",\"A space to be filled to form a fraction\",\"The end of a sentence\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The empty boxes [ ] are used within fraction structures like [ ]\\/17 to show where numbers should be placed.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the example \'[ ]\\/17\', which part of the fraction is represented by the empty box?\",\"options\":[\"The upper part\",\"The lower part\",\"The side part\",\"The middle part\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Visually, in \'[ ]\\/17\', the box is placed above the line, which is the upper part of the fraction.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the examples \'37\\/[ ]\' and \'59\\/[ ]\', where is the empty box located?\",\"options\":[\"In the upper part\",\"In the lower part\",\"Before the number\",\"After the number\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In these examples, the box is placed below the fraction line, which is the lower part.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21453,13,3,'Maths','en','Length and Weight','[\"Length is measured using metre, centimetre, etc.\",\"1 metre = 100 centimetres.\",\"For longer distances, metre is used; for shorter lengths, centimetre is used.\",\"Weight is measured using weighing balance and standard weights.\",\"Standard unit of weight is kilogram (kg).\",\"1 kilogram = 1000 grams.\",\"Heavier objects tilt the weighing balance down on their side.\",\"Same object weighs the same regardless of who measures it using same weights.\",\"To measure length, we can use a rope marked at 1 m, ½ m, and ¼ m.\",\"Half metre rope is made by folding a one-metre rope into two equal parts.\",\"Quarter metre rope is made by folding a half-metre rope into two equal parts.\",\"We estimate length as less than, more than, or equal to a given measure.\",\"Actual measurement verifies estimation.\",\"Marbles of different size\\/material give different counts for same object weight.\",\"Standard weights give consistent measurement regardless of person or tool.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is measuring the length of the side of the window in the discussion?\",\"options\":[\"Anuj\",\"Shyam\",\"Rina\",\"Arnav\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Shyam is the one measuring the side of the window.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Length\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What object are Anuj and Rina measuring together?\",\"options\":[\"A window\",\"A board\",\"A table\",\"A door\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks what Anuj and Rina are using to measure the length of the table.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Length\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is responsible for measuring the length of the board?\",\"options\":[\"Tanushree\",\"Shyam\",\"Arnav\",\"Anuj\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Arnav is measuring the length of the board.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Length\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why might the length of the table measured by Anuj and Rina be different?\",\"options\":[\"Because the table changes size\",\"Because they are measuring different tables\",\"Because hand-spans or foot-spans differ from person to person\",\"Because they are using the same measuring tape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Measurements like hand-spans vary between individuals, leading to different results.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Length\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these tools will give the same measurement of length, no matter who uses it?\",\"options\":[\"Hand-span\",\"Foot-span\",\"Measuring tape\",\"A stick\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A measuring tape is a standard tool that provides the same result regardless of the person measuring.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Length\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides a measuring tape, which other tool mentioned gives a consistent measurement regardless of the person?\",\"options\":[\"Pencil\",\"Measuring rope\",\"Hand-span\",\"Foot-span\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists measuring rope as a tool that gives the same measurement regardless of who measures it.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Length\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Tanushree wants to measure the door so that the measurement is exactly the same for everyone, what should she use?\",\"options\":[\"Her hand-span\",\"A pencil\",\"A measuring tape\",\"Her foot-span\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To get a measurement that is the same for everyone, a standard tool like a measuring tape is required.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Length\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Arnav is measuring the board. If he uses his hand-span and then his friend uses their hand-span, what will likely happen?\",\"options\":[\"The measurements will be exactly the same\",\"The measurements will be different\",\"The board will get longer\",\"The hand-spans will become the same length\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since hand-spans vary by person, the measurements will likely be different.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Length\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of measuring methods are \'non-standard\' because they change based on the person measuring?\",\"options\":[\"Measuring tape and measuring rope\",\"Hand-span and foot-span\",\"Measuring tape and hand-span\",\"Measuring rope and foot-span\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Hand-spans and foot-spans are body-based and vary, unlike standard tapes or ropes.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Length\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main difference between using a \'pencil\' and a \'measuring tape\' to measure a table?\",\"options\":[\"A pencil is longer than a measuring tape\",\"A measuring tape is only for windows\",\"A measuring tape gives a standard result that everyone agrees on\",\"A pencil gives the same result even if different pencils are used\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text implies that standard tools like measuring tapes provide universal measurements.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Length\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the standard unit for measuring length according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Centimetre\",\"Metre\",\"Kilometre\",\"Gram\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a metre is a standard unit for measuring length.\",\"topic\":\"Measurement using a metre scale\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many equal parts is 1 metre divided into to get centimetres?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"50\",\"100\",\"1000\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that if 1 metre is divided into 100 equal parts, each part is 1 centimetre.\",\"topic\":\"Measurement using a metre scale\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of scale is used in a cloth shop to ensure the measurement is the same no matter who measures it?\",\"options\":[\"A short plastic scale\",\"A long metal scale\",\"A wooden stick\",\"A piece of string\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that a long metal scale is used to measure cloth in a cloth shop.\",\"topic\":\"Measurement using a metre scale\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a standard metre scale used to measure cloth in shops?\",\"options\":[\"To make the cloth look beautiful\",\"So that the cloth measures the same no matter who measures it\",\"To make the cloth easy to fold\",\"Because metal scales are very cheap\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that a sheet of cloth must measure the same no matter who measures it, which is why a standard scale is used.\",\"topic\":\"Measurement using a metre scale\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the length of an object is less than one metre, which unit is used to measure it?\",\"options\":[\"Metre\",\"Kilometre\",\"Centimetre\",\"Litre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that if the length is less than one metre, then it is measured in centimetres.\",\"topic\":\"Measurement using a metre scale\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the length of a metre scale?\",\"options\":[\"One centimetre\",\"One metre\",\"Three metres\",\"100 metres\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the length of a metre scale is one metre.\",\"topic\":\"Measurement using a metre scale\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If 1 metre is equal to 100 centimetres, how many centimetres make up 2 metres?\",\"options\":[\"50 centimetres\",\"100 centimetres\",\"200 centimetres\",\"300 centimetres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since 1 metre = 100 cm, then 2 metres = 100 + 100 = 200 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Measurement using a metre scale\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A shopkeeper needs to measure 3 metres of cloth using a one-metre scale. How many times must he apply the scale to the cloth?\",\"options\":[\"One time\",\"Two times\",\"Three times\",\"Four times\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To get 3 metres using a 1-metre scale, the shopkeeper must measure the length three times.\",\"topic\":\"Measurement using a metre scale\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the highest number marked on the scale shown at the bottom?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"50\",\"90\",\"100\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The scale at the bottom of the image shows markings from 0 up to 100.\",\"topic\":\"Measurement using a metre scale\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/060_101.jpg\"},{\"q\"