:\"After marking the quarter metre and opening the rope again, how many marks can you see?\",\"options\":[\"1 mark\",\"2 marks\",\"3 marks\",\"4 marks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Open the rope again. Now you can see 3 marks.\'\",\"topic\":\"Quarter, Half, Three-fourth of One metre\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first thing you should do before verifying the length by actual measurement?\",\"options\":[\"Cut the rope\",\"Estimate the length\",\"Buy a new rope\",\"Paint the object\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'Estimated length\' must be filled before \'Verify by actual measurement\'.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter, Half, Three-fourth of One metre\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To get a quarter-metre length, how many times must you fold the 1-metre rope in total?\",\"options\":[\"Once\",\"Twice\",\"Three times\",\"Four times\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The rope is folded once to get half, and that half is folded again (twice) to get a quarter.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter, Half, Three-fourth of One metre\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of the table provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"To list the prices of objects\",\"To compare estimated length with actual measurement\",\"To count the number of chairs\",\"To draw the window\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table columns are for \'Estimated length\' and \'Verify by actual measurement\'.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter, Half, Three-fourth of One metre\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which measurement is marked immediately after making the half-metre rope?\",\"options\":[\"Quarter metre\",\"Half metre\",\"One metre\",\"Three-fourth metre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Now a rope of half metre length is ready. Mark half metre.\'\",\"topic\":\"Quarter, Half, Three-fourth of One metre\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the three marks on the rope represent quarter, half, and three-quarters, which mark was made last during the folding process?\",\"options\":[\"The half metre mark\",\"The one metre mark\",\"The quarter metre mark\",\"The zero mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes marking the half metre first, then folding again to mark the quarter metre.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter, Half, Three-fourth of One metre\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these lengths are marked on the ropes used in the activity?\",\"options\":[\"One metre, two metres, three metres\",\"One metre, half metre, quarter metre\",\"Half metre, quarter metre, eighth metre\",\"One metre, two metres, half metre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions using ropes marked as one metre, half metre, and quarter metre.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What tool is used in this activity to determine the length of different objects?\",\"options\":[\"A wooden ruler\",\"A measuring tape\",\"Marked ropes\",\"A compass box\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The activity specifically instructs to use ropes marked with different lengths.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the activity, what should you do in the correct box after comparing lengths?\",\"options\":[\"Write the name of the object\",\"Put a tick\",\"Write the measurement in numbers\",\"Draw a line\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Put a tick in the correct box\'.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If an object is longer than the one-metre rope, it is said to be ______.\",\"options\":[\"Less than one metre\",\"More than one metre\",\"Exactly one metre\",\"Half of one metre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity uses the categories \'Less\' and \'More\' for comparison.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the smallest length marker used for comparison in the activity?\",\"options\":[\"One metre\",\"Half metre\",\"Quarter metre\",\"Two metres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Quarter metre is the smallest of the three markers (1, 1\\/2, 1\\/4) mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many different standard lengths are used to compare each object in the table?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Objects are compared to quarter metre, half metre, and one metre.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a pencil is shorter than the quarter-metre rope, where should you tick in the \'Compared to quarter metre\' column?\",\"options\":[\"More\",\"Less\",\"One metre\",\"Half metre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Shorter length corresponds to the \'Less\' box in the comparison table.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A table is longer than the half-metre rope but shorter than the one-metre rope. Which box is correct for the \'Compared to half metre\' column?\",\"options\":[\"Less\",\"More\",\"Quarter\",\"One metre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Being longer than the rope means it belongs in the \'More\' category for that length.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If an object is marked as \'Less than quarter metre\', what must also be true about its length?\",\"options\":[\"It is more than one metre\",\"It is more than half metre\",\"It is less than half metre\",\"It is exactly one metre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"If something is smaller than a quarter, it is naturally smaller than a half.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If an object is marked as \'More than one metre\', which other box will definitely have a tick in the \'More\' column?\",\"options\":[\"Compared to half metre\",\"Compared to two metres\",\"Compared to three metres\",\"None of these\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"If an object is longer than one metre, it is also longer than half a metre.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which unit is used to measure longer distances?\",\"options\":[\"Centimetre\",\"Metre\",\"Kilogram\",\"Litre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that to measure longer distances, metre is used.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Distance\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which unit is used for measuring shorter lengths as mentioned in the topic?\",\"options\":[\"Metre\",\"Centimetre\",\"Metre rope\",\"Scale\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that for shorter lengths, centimetre is used.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Distance\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the exact distance between the two trees when measured using both a scale and a rope?\",\"options\":[\"5 metres\",\"40 centimetres\",\"5 metres 40 centimetres\",\"More than 5 metres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states the distance between the two trees is 5 metres 40 centimetres.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Distance\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When the distance was first measured using a metre rope, what was the result?\",\"options\":[\"It was exactly 5 metres\",\"It was less than 5 metres\",\"It was more than 5 metres\",\"It was 40 centimetres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the distance measured using a metre rope is more than 5 metres.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Distance\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why was a measuring scale used after the metre rope?\",\"options\":[\"To measure the height of the trees\",\"To measure the remaining distance in centimetres\",\"Because the rope was broken\",\"To measure the distance to the school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions measuring the remaining distance using a measuring scale in centimetres.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Distance\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the two children measuring