he pen\",\"The textbook\",\"Both are equal\",\"The pen is heavier than the book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In a comparison between a textbook and a pen, the textbook is the heavier object.\",\"topic\":\"I Understood\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the weight of an object when different people measure it using the same standard weights?\",\"options\":[\"It changes every time\",\"It depends on who is measuring\",\"It remains the same\",\"It becomes lighter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the weight of an object remains the same no matter who measures it using the same weights.\",\"topic\":\"I Understood\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a shopkeeper gives you 1 kilogram of sugar, how many grams of sugar are you getting?\",\"options\":[\"100 grams\",\"1000 grams\",\"10 grams\",\"500 grams\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since 1 kilogram = 1000 grams, 1 kilogram of sugar is 1000 grams.\",\"topic\":\"I Understood\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where are standard measures and instruments for weight used according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only in schools\",\"In daily life\",\"Only in textbooks\",\"Nowhere\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that in daily life, these measures are used to measure the weight of objects.\",\"topic\":\"I Understood\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Comparing a pen and a textbook, which statement is true based on the \'Heavy or Light\' activity?\",\"options\":[\"The pen is lighter than the textbook\",\"The textbook is lighter than the pen\",\"The pen is heavier than the textbook\",\"They both have the same weight\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Since the textbook is heavier, the pen is the lighter object.\",\"topic\":\"I Understood\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why do we use standard units and standard weights for measuring?\",\"options\":[\"To make the object heavier\",\"To make the object lighter\",\"To ensure the weight remains the same no matter who measures it\",\"To change the weight of the object\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Standard units ensure consistency in measurement regardless of the person measuring.\",\"topic\":\"I Understood\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the children using to measure objects like the blackboard and the window?\",\"options\":[\"Standard weights\",\"Measuring tape and hand spans\",\"Kilogram stones\",\"Clocks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows children using a measuring tape on the blackboard and hand spans\\/fingers on other surfaces.\",\"topic\":\"I Understood\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/059_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many different types of instruments for measuring weight are shown?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure displays five distinct weighing instruments, including a balance, digital scales, and a spring balance.\",\"topic\":\"I Understood\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/064_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What are used to measure the weight of objects in a standard way?\",\"options\":[\"Standard units and standard weights\",\"Only hand spans\",\"Only fingers\",\"Strings\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that for measuring weight, standard units and standard weights are used.\",\"topic\":\"I Understood\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If your friend measures a bag and says it is 1 kilogram, and you measure the same bag with the same weight, what will your result be?\",\"options\":[\"2 kilograms\",\"1 kilogram\",\"500 grams\",\"0 kilograms\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The weight remains the same no matter who measures it using the same weights.\",\"topic\":\"I Understood\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these was a unit used to measure weight in ancient times?\",\"options\":[\"Meter\",\"Man\",\"Liter\",\"Centimeter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Man\' as one of the units used in ancient times to measure weights.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the ancient unit of weight mentioned in the text.\",\"options\":[\"Kilogram\",\"Gram\",\"Tola\",\"Milligram\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tola is explicitly listed in the text as an ancient unit of weight.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which ancient unit is mentioned along with Man, Sher, and Tola?\",\"options\":[\"Gunj\",\"Rupee\",\"Handspan\",\"Kilometer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists Man, Sher, Tola, and Gunj as ancient units for measuring weight.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the text suggest you experience the weight of 1 kilogram?\",\"options\":[\"By looking at a picture\",\"By lifting the object by hand\",\"By measuring its length\",\"By counting the objects\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text advises students to experience the weight by lifting objects by hand.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where should you look to find the words \'1 kilogram\' written on objects?\",\"options\":[\"In your daily life\",\"In ancient history books\",\"Only in the classroom\",\"On the playground\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text asks to write names of objects from daily life that have \'1 kilogram\' written on them.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do after experiencing the weight of a 1 kilogram object?\",\"options\":[\"Estimate other objects of the same weight\",\"Throw the object away\",\"Measure the object with a ruler\",\"Draw a picture of the object\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text suggests estimating which other objects have a weight of 1 kilogram after experiencing it.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you find an old weight labeled \'Sher\', what was it used for according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To measure length\",\"To measure time\",\"To measure weight\",\"To measure distance\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sher is listed as a unit used in ancient times to measure weights.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you lift a bag of sugar and it feels the same as a known 1 kilogram weight, what are you doing?\",\"options\":[\"Calculating the price\",\"Estimating the weight\",\"Measuring the height\",\"Ancient counting\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Lifting objects to find others of similar weight is the process of estimation described in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following units does NOT belong to the group of ancient units mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Man\",\"Sher\",\"Kilogram\",\"Gunj\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Kilogram is the modern unit mentioned, while Man, Sher, and Gunj are ancient units.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the purpose of lifting a 1 kilogram object by hand?\",\"options\":[\"To exercise your muscles\",\"To help you estimate the weight of other objects\",\"To learn how to write the word \'kilogram\'\",\"To compare it with ancient units like Tola\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity is designed to help the student estimate other objects of the same weight through experience.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21454,13,3,'Maths','en','Data Handling','[\"Data handling means collecting, organizing, and showing information in a clear way.\",\"We use tables to arrange data in rows and columns for easy reading.\",\"Tally marks are used to count things quickly, with every fifth mark drawn across the previous four.\",\"A table helps us compare numbers, like how many students like different fruits.\",\"The title of a table tells us what the data is about.\",\"Rows and columns in a table help us find specific information.\",\"We can answer questions like \'most\', \'least\', \'more than\', \'less than\' using data from tables.\",\"Symbols like © in the text are not part of the question and should be ignored.\",\"Fill-in-the-blank questions need words like \'more\', \'less\', or \'equal\' to complete the sentence correctly.\",\"Always check the table carefully before answering questions based on it.\",\"Data from real-life situations like fruit choices or transport modes can be shown in tables.\",\"We use data handling to understand patterns, like which fruit is most popular.\",\"Reading a table means looking at the headers and matching them with the numbers.\",\"When comparing two values, we use words like \'more than\', \'less than\', or \'equal to\'.\",\"Tally marks help in recording data as it is collected, especially in surveys or observations.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who recorded the colours of the dresses for the Fun Fair?\",\"options\":[\"Manisha, Neeraj, and Salma\",\"The teachers and students\",\"The parents and guests\",\"The principal and clerks\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that Manisha, Neeraj, and Salma recorded the colours.\",\"topic\":\"6. Data Handling\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"For which event did the children come to school in coloured dresses?\",\"options\":[\"Prize Distribution\",\"Fun Fair\",\"Independence Day\",\"Teacher\'s Day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that children came in coloured dresses for the Fun Fair.\",\"topic\":\"6. Data Handling\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To record the data, what kind of line is drawn for each colour?\",\"options\":[\"Horizontal line\",\"Vertical line\",\"Zigzag line\",\"Dotted line\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'we will draw a vertical line for each colour.\'\",\"topic\":\"6. Data Handling\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of recording the colours in a table?\",\"options\":[\"To find out who likes which colour\",\"To see who is the tallest child\",\"To count the number of trees\",\"To check the school building\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text asks, \'can we find out who likes which colour?\' and suggests recording data to do this.\",\"topic\":\"6. Data Handling\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If there are 3 children wearing red dresses, how many vertical lines will be drawn for the red colour in the table?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states a vertical line is drawn for each colour (each occurrence).\",\"topic\":\"6. Data Handling\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In what format is the record of dress colours kept according to the activity?\",\"options\":[\"A paragraph\",\"A table\",\"A map\",\"A drawing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions recording the colours of the dresses in a table.\",\"topic\":\"6. Data Handling\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the colour of the dress worn by the lady in the foreground holding a plate?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Blue\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The lady in the foreground holding a plate is wearing a yellow saree.\",\"topic\":\"6. Data Handling\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/066_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many children are standing on the stage?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"There are two girls performing on the stage in the picture.\",\"topic\":\"6. Data Handling\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/066_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how does everybody look in their different coloured dresses?\",\"options\":[\"Very nice\",\"Very funny\",\"Very strange\",\"Very tall\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Everybody looks very nice in their different coloured dresses.\'\",\"topic\":\"6. Data Handling\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first thing suggested to find out who likes which colour?\",\"options\":[\"Asking the teacher\",\"Looking at the pictures\",\"Writing names\",\"Buying new dresses\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks, \'By looking at the pictures, can we find out who likes which colour?\'\",\"topic\":\"6. Data Handling\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are the vertical lines used to classify information in the table called?\",\"options\":[\"Number marks\",\"Tally marks\",\"Color marks\",\"Student marks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher explicitly states that these lines are called tally marks.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many children in total were observed by Manisha, Salma, and Neeraj?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"20\",\"28\",\"6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Manisha mentions that in all there are 28 children in total.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which color dress was worn by the highest number of children?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Manisha states that the number of children wearing blue-coloured dresses is the highest, which is 10.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which color dress was worn by the least number of children?\",\"options\":[\"Yellow\",\"Blue\",\"Red\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Salma states that the number of children wearing yellow-coloured dresses is the least, which is 4.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the table, what does one vertical line represent?\",\"options\":[\"One color\",\"One child\",\"One group\",\"One school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Salma explains that for each child, they used one vertical line.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many children are wearing green-coloured dresses according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"4\",\"10\",\"8\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Manisha says green is 2 more than red (6), so 6 + 2 = 8.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What method did the children use to collect the information?\",\"options\":[\"Reading a book\",\"Asking the teacher\",\"Observing the colours of dresses\",\"Drawing pictures\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Salma says they prepared the table by observing the colours of dresses of 28 children.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the tally marks for Blue are \'||||| |||||\', what is the number of students?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"10\",\"15\",\"20\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Manisha confirms that the number of children wearing blue is 10.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a new child wearing a red dress joins, how many tally marks will there be for Red?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"6\",\"7\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Red currently has 6 marks; adding one more child adds one more mark, making it 7.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the tally marks for Yellow are \'||||\', what number should be written in the \'Number of Students\' column for Yellow?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Each vertical line represents one child, so four lines represent 4 students.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the table and text, which color has 2 more students than Red (6)?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Yellow\",\"Green\",\"None\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the number of children wearing green is 2 more than those wearing red.\",\"topic\":\"What are Tally Marks?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which set of tally marks r