hich shape has been used to represent the clown\'s hat?\",\"options\":[\"Cuboid\",\"Sphere\",\"Cone\",\"Cube\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Based on the 3D shapes mentioned in the text, the pointed hat of the clown represents a cone.\",\"topic\":\"3D Shapes and Views\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/076_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, look at the first section with blue blocks. What does the observer see from their current position?\",\"options\":[\"A large 4x5 grid of squares\",\"A thin 1x5 strip of squares\",\"A small 2x2 square\",\"A long 4x2 rectangle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The observer is standing directly in front of the wide side of the blue block wall, so they see the 4x5 grid.\",\"topic\":\"3D Shapes and Views\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/076_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"When we look at an object from directly above, which view are we observing?\",\"options\":[\"Side view\",\"Front view\",\"Top view\",\"Bottom view\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Looking at an object from the top provides the \'top view\' as mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"3D Shapes and Views\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which shape is mentioned in the \'For Teachers\' section as an example of a 3D shape to provide to students?\",\"options\":[\"Rectangle\",\"Sphere\",\"Oval\",\"Point\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note specifically mentions providing students with shapes like cube, cuboid, and sphere.\",\"topic\":\"3D Shapes and Views\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you use a mathematical kit to build a \'bus\', which shape from the text would be most suitable for the main body?\",\"options\":[\"Cone\",\"Sphere\",\"Cuboid\",\"Triangle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A cuboid is the most appropriate 3D shape mentioned in the text for the body of a bus.\",\"topic\":\"3D Shapes and Views\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of drawing pictures showing side, top, and front views of a built object?\",\"options\":[\"To make the drawing colorful\",\"To show how the 3D object looks from different directions\",\"To count how many blocks were used\",\"To change the shape of the object\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Views are drawn to represent the appearance of a 3D object from different perspectives.\",\"topic\":\"3D Shapes and Views\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these objects can be made using 3D shapes from a mathematical kit?\",\"options\":[\"A bridge\",\"A cloud\",\"A river\",\"A sun\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists bus, house, table, truck, and bridge as objects that can be made.\",\"topic\":\"3D Shapes and Views\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If an observer changes their position around a stack of blocks, what happens to the \'view\' they see?\",\"options\":[\"The view stays exactly the same\",\"The color of the blocks changes\",\"The shape visible to the observer changes\",\"The blocks become two-dimensional\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"As seen in the block diagrams, changing the observer\'s position changes which side or view is visible.\",\"topic\":\"3D Shapes and Views\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a 3D shape mentioned in the lesson text?\",\"options\":[\"Cube\",\"Cone\",\"Cylinder\",\"Circle\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Circle is a 2D shape; the text focuses on 3D shapes like cube, cone, and cylinder.\",\"topic\":\"3D Shapes and Views\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21456,13,3,'Maths','en','Multiplication','[\"Multiplication is repeated addition.\",\"The symbol for multiplication is \'×\'.\",\"The result of multiplication is called the product.\",\"The number being multiplied is the multiplicand.\",\"The number by which we multiply is the multiplier.\",\"Multiplicand × Multiplier = Product.\",\"Any number multiplied by 1 gives the same number.\",\"Any number multiplied by 0 gives 0.\",\"The order of numbers in multiplication does not change the product (commutative property).\",\"Multiplication tables help in quick calculation.\",\"To multiply by 10, add a zero to the right of the number.\",\"To multiply by 20, multiply by 2 and then add a zero.\",\"Lattice method is a grid-based way to multiply numbers.\",\"Vertical arrangement is the standard column method of multiplication.\",\"Word problems in multiplication describe real-life situations like total cost, total items, etc.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who helped their parents to fill the boxes with oranges during the holiday?\",\"options\":[\"Only Ramesh\",\"Only Surekha\",\"Ramesh and Surekha\",\"The neighbors\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that both Ramesh and Surekha helped their parents fill the boxes.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication Concept\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many oranges did Surekha put in each box?\",\"options\":[\"5 oranges\",\"6 oranges\",\"30 oranges\",\"11 oranges\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Surekha filled boxes with 6 oranges in each box.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication Concept\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many boxes did Surekha fill in total?\",\"options\":[\"6 boxes\",\"30 boxes\",\"5 boxes\",\"11 boxes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Surekha filled 5 boxes.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication Concept\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the total number of oranges Surekha filled in the boxes?\",\"options\":[\"11\",\"25\",\"30\",\"36\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The calculation 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 equals 30.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication Concept\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does \'five times six\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Adding 5 and 6\",\"Adding 6 five times\",\"Subtracting 5 from 6\",\"Multiplying 5 by 5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 means five times six.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication Concept\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How is the phrase \'six five times equals thirty\' written using mathematical symbols?\",\"options\":[\"6 + 5 = 30\",\"6 - 5 = 30\",\"6 × 5 = 30\",\"5 × 5 = 30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'six five times equals thirty\' is written as 6 × 5 = 30.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication Concept\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Surekha had filled 6 boxes with 6 oranges in each, how would the addition be written?\",\"options\":[\"6 + 6 + 6 + 6 + 6\",\"6 + 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 + 6\",\"5 + 5 + 5 + 5 + 5 + 5\",\"6 + 5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Adding 6 oranges for each of the 6 boxes results in adding 6 six times.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication Concept\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If there were only 4 boxes with 6 oranges in each, what would be the total number of oranges?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"18\",\"24\",\"30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Following the concept, 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 (four times six) equals 24.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication Concept\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the multiplication 6 × 5 = 30, what does the number 5 represent in the story?\",\"options\":[\"The number of oranges in one box\",\"The total number of oranges\",\"The number of boxes filled\",\"The number of children\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the context of the text, 5 represents the 5 boxes Surekha filled.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication Concept\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these mathematical expressions represents the same concept as 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 + 6?\",\"options\":[\"Five times six\",\"Six times six\",\"Five plus six\",\"Thirty times five\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 means five times six.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication Concept\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the result of 6 × 7?\",\"options\":[\"36\",\"42\",\"48\",\"49\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows 6 × 7 = 42.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The text states that 6 × 7 is equal to which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"6 + 7\",\"7 + 6\",\"7 × 6\",\"6 × 6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states 6 × 7 = 7 × 6.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many cakes are mentioned in the first part of the example?\",\"options\":[\"5 cakes\",\"6 cakes\",\"8 cakes\",\"9 cakes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins with \'Here 6 cakes...\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'six times 7\' mean in terms of the total number of cupcakes?\",\"options\":[\"There are 13 cupcakes\",\"There are 42 cupcakes\",\"There are 76 cupcakes\",\"There are 67 cupcakes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'six times 7 means that there are a total of 42 cupcakes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you have 7 cakes taken 6 times, how many cakes do you have in total?\",\"options\":[\"13\",\"42\",\"48\",\"36\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the text, 7 cakes times 6 equals 42.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the equation 6 × 7 = 7 × 6, what can we conclude about multiplication?\",\"options\":[\"Changing the order of numbers changes the total\",\"The total is always 42 regardless of the numbers\",\"Changing the order of numbers does not change the total\",\"Multiplication is the same as addition\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The equality 6 × 7 = 7 × 6 shows that the order of factors does not change the product.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Besides 6 cakes, what is the other number of cakes mentioned in the \'times\' phrasing?\",\"options\":[\"4 cakes\",\"5 cakes\",\"7 cakes\",\"10 cakes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'7 cakes.....times\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is another way to say \'seven times 6\' according to the text structure?\",\"options\":[\"7 + 6\",\"7 - 6\",\"7 × 6\",\"7 ÷ 6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links \'seven times\' to the multiplication expression 7 × 6.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student calculates 7 × 6, what total should they reach based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"42\",\"36\",\"49\",\"13\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows 7 × 6 = 42.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'6 times 7 means that there are a total of .... cupcakes\', what number completes the total?\",\"options\":[\"13\",\"42\",\"7\",\"6\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The product of 6 and 7 is 42, which represents the total cupcakes.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21457,13,3,'Maths','en','Division','[\"Division means sharing equally or making equal groups.\",\"Dividend is the total number to be divided.\",\"Divisor is the number of groups or number in each group.\",\"Quotient is the result of division (number in each group or number of groups).\",\"Remainder is what is left after equal sharing.\",\"Dividend = Divisor × Quotient + Remainder.\",\"Remainder is always less than the divisor.\",\"Division is repeated subtraction.\",\"Division is the opposite of multiplication.\",\"When a number is divided by itself, quotient is 1 and remainder is 0.\",\"When a number is divided by 1, quotient is the number itself and remainder is 0.\",\"Zero divided by any number (except 0) is 0.\",\"We can use multiplication tables to divide.\",\"Long division helps divide bigger numbers step by step.\",\"Check division: Multiply divisor and quotient, add remainder to get dividend.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what are multiplication tables?\",\"options\":[\"A game of jumping\",\"Multiplication done in order\",\"Adding numbers randomly\",\"A way to count flowers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that multiplication tables are simply multiplication done in order.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the table of 7, how is \'7 x 5\' read?\",\"options\":[\"Seven fives are twenty five\",\"Seven fives are thirty\",\"Seven fives are thirty five\",\"Seven fives are forty\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table of 7 explicitly lists \'Seven fives are thirty five\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If Sadu starts from zero and jumps in steps of 9, what is the 4th number he reaches (9 x 4)?\",\"options\":[\"32\",\"36\",\"45\",\"27\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Following the sequence 9, 18, 27, the next number (9 x 4) is 36.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Pooja\'s recorded numbers are 32, 40, 48, 56. What is the size of her jump step?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"7\",\"8\",\"9\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The difference between 40 and 32, or 48 and 40, is 8.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the next three numbers in the sequence: 20, 40, 60, ...\",\"options\":[\"70, 80, 90\",\"80, 100, 120\",\"80, 90, 100\",\"100, 120, 140\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"This is a sequence of 20s; 60 + 20 = 80, 80 + 20 = 100, 100 + 20 = 120.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the next three numbers in the sequence: 6, 12, 18, ...\",\"options\":[\"20, 24, 28\",\"24, 30, 36\",\"21, 24, 27\",\"24, 28, 32\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"This is the table of 6; the next numbers are 24, 30, and 36.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To reach a flower on number 18 in the \'least number of jumps\', which jump size should you choose?\",\"options\":[\"Steps of 2\",\"Steps of 3\",\"Steps of 6\",\"Steps of 9\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Steps of 9 reach 18 in 2 jumps, which is fewer than steps of 2, 3, or 6.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Gopal recorded Pooja\'s numbers as ..., ..., ..., 32, 40. What are the first three missing numbers?\",\"options\":[\"7, 14, 21\",\"10, 20, 30\",\"8, 16, 24\",\"6, 12, 18\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since the sequence is the table of 8 (32, 40), the preceding numbers are 8, 16, and 24.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of 9 x 6 according to the provided tables?\",\"options\":[\"45\",\"54\",\"63\",\"72\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Table of 9 shows 9 x 6 = 54.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is \'7 x 9\' read in the multiplication table?\",\"options\":[\"Seven nines are sixty\",\"Seven nines are sixty three\",\"Seven nines are seventy\",\"Seven nines are fifty six\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Seven nines are sixty three\' for 7 x 9.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the \'Addition form\' for 7 x 3 as shown in the text?\",\"options\":[\"7 + 7\",\"7 + 7 + 7\",\"7 + 7 + 7 + 7\",\"3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table of 7 shows the addition form of 7 x 3 is 7 + 7 + 7.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the multiplication form shown for the row containing 4 leaf pictures?\",\"options\":[\"7 x 1\",\"7 x 2\",\"7 x 3\",\"7 x 4\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"In the table of 7, the row with 4 leaf pictures corresponds to 7 x 4.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/080_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the value of 6 multiplied by 7?\",\"options\":[\"36\",\"42\",\"48\",\"54\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Table of 6 clearly shows 6 x 7 = 42.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/081_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the result of 