re distributed among 5 people and each gets 3, how many karanjis are left over?\",\"options\":[\"0\",\"1\",\"2\",\"3\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text and table show that when 17 karanjis are distributed among 5 people, 2 karanjis are left.\",\"topic\":\"Division by distribution equally\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the table, how many karanjis were distributed in total before any were left over?\",\"options\":[\"17\",\"5\",\"3\",\"15\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table shows that out of 17 karanjis, 15 were distributed (3 each to 5 people).\",\"topic\":\"Division by distribution equally\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why were there 2 karanjis left over when distributing 17 among 5 cousins?\",\"options\":[\"Because 17 cannot be divided into 5 equal groups without a remainder\",\"Because the cousins did not want the last two\",\"Because only 3 cousins were present\",\"Because the uncle took two lamps back\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Equal distribution of 17 among 5 results in 3 each with a remainder of 2.\",\"topic\":\"Division by distribution equally\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many people are shown to be receiving the distributed lamps?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"15\",\"5\",\"1\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows 5 distinct people (Me and four cousins) receiving the lamps.\",\"topic\":\"Division by distribution equally\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/092_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the process of subtracting the same number again and again called?\",\"options\":[\"Addition\",\"Multiplication\",\"Division\",\"Grouping\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that subtracting the same number of items again and again is division.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'I Understood\' section, what does making equal groups of items mean?\",\"options\":[\"Subtraction\",\"Division\",\"Addition\",\"Counting\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines making equal groups of items as division.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the Giant wheel example, how many children were allowed to sit in one carriage at a time?\",\"options\":[\"20 children\",\"5 children\",\"10 children\",\"4 children\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that only 4 children could sit in 1 carriage at a time.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When 20 children were divided into groups of 4 for the Giant wheel carriages, what was the remainder?\",\"options\":[\"Zero\",\"Four\",\"Five\",\"One\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that if 4 children sat in each cradle, there were 5 groups and the remainder is \'zero\'.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Suman had 24 chikoos and made groups of 4 each. How many total groups did she make?\",\"options\":[\"4 groups\",\"24 groups\",\"6 groups\",\"12 groups\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states: Total chikoos = 24, chikoos in each group = 4, Total groups = 6.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the division 20 ÷ 4 = 5, what does the number 5 represent in the Giant wheel story?\",\"options\":[\"Total number of children\",\"Number of children in one carriage\",\"Number of carriages used\",\"Number of children left in line\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that 20 children sat in 5 carriages, so 5 is the number of groups\\/carriages.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many times is 4 subtracted from 20 to reach the remainder zero?\",\"options\":[\"4 times\",\"5 times\",\"20 times\",\"0 times\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the subtraction of 4 repeated 5 times until it reaches 0.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/093_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if the total number of chikoos is 24 and 3 chikoos are distributed to each, how many groups are formed?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"6\",\"8\",\"3\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows that for 24 chikoos, if 3 are distributed, there are 8 groups.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/094_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, when 35 items are put into groups of 4, what is the number of remaining items?\",\"options\":[\"0\",\"5\",\"3\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows that for 35 items with 4 in each group, the remaining items are 3.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/094_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is another meaning of division besides equal grouping and repeated subtraction?\",\"options\":[\"Equal distribution of items\",\"Adding items repeatedly\",\"Multiplying groups\",\"Increasing the total number\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The \'I Understood\' section states that equal distribution of items is division.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If we have 20 children and we put 4 in the first carriage, how many children are left in the queue?\",\"options\":[\"20\",\"16\",\"12\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows 20 - 4 = 16 left in the line\\/queue.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Using the logic from the table for 35 items, if there are 5 items in each group, how many groups will be formed with zero remainder?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"6\",\"7\",\"10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Based on the table logic, 35 items divided into groups of 5 results in 7 groups (35 ÷ 5 = 7).\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the repeated subtraction method shown in the text, what does each subtraction of 4 represent?\",\"options\":[\"One child leaving the line\",\"One carriage being filled\",\"The total number of children\",\"The number of wheels\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Each time 4 is subtracted, it represents one group of 4 children sitting in a carriage.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'Equal distribution\' table, when 24 chikoos are distributed by 7, how many chikoos are left over?\",\"options\":[\"0\",\"3\",\"4\",\"7\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows that when 7 chikoos are distributed from a total of 24, 4 chikoos remain.\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many total children were standing in line to sit in the Giant wheel?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"20\",\"24\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'There were 20 children in the line to sit in the Giant wheel.\'\",\"topic\":\"Division by subtracting and grouping\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21458,13,3,'Maths','en','Fun with Shapes (Two-dimensional)','[\"A closed shape has no open ends.\",\"A polygon is a closed shape made of straight line segments.\",\"A triangle has 3 sides and 3 corners.\",\"A square has 4 equal sides and 4 right angles.\",\"A rectangle has opposite sides equal and all angles are right angles.\",\"A pentagon has 5 sides and 5 corners.\",\"A hexagon has 6 sides and 6 corners.\",\"An octagon has 8 sides and 8 corners.\",\"A vertex is a point where two sides meet.\",\"A side is a line segment that forms part of a shape.\",\"Angles are formed when two lines meet at a point.\",\"Shapes can be made using sticks, straws, or paper folding.\",\"Folding a square corner can create new shapes like pentagons.\",\"Geoboards help in creating shapes by connecting dots with rubber bands.\",\"Shapes like triangle, square, rectangle are found in surroundings.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the first step mentioned in the activity for each three-dimensional shape?\",\"options\":[\"Break the shape\",\"Colour or paste a paper on one face\",\"Throw the shape away\",\"Count the corners\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Colour or paste a paper on one face of each three-dimensional shapes.\'\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which three-dimensional shape is specifically mentioned by name in the table?\",\"options\":[\"Sphere\",\"Cylinder\",\"Cube\",\"Cone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'Cube\' under the name of the three-dimensional shape column.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the activity table, what two types of faces are we asked to observe?\",\"options\":[\"Big and small faces\",\"Red and blue faces\",\"Flat and curved faces\",\"Rough and smooth faces\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table headers are \'Number of flat face\' and \'Number of curved face\'.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What do we do after coloring or pasting paper on a face?\",\"options\":[\"Observe and complete the table\",\"Draw a new shape\",\"Close the book\",\"Measure the paper with a ruler\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text directs: \'Observe and complete the table below.\'\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are completing the table for a Cube, how many curved faces will you find?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"0\",\"6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A cube is made of flat squares and has zero curved faces.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many faces should you colour or paste paper on for each shape?\",\"options\":[\"All faces\",\"Any one face\",\"Two faces\",\"No faces\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I will colour any one face\' and \'paste coloured paper... on any one face.\'\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a cube has 6 flat faces, which column in the table will you write \'6\' in?\",\"options\":[\"Number of curved face\",\"Name of the shape\",\"Number of flat face\",\"Three dimensional shape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since the faces of a cube are flat, the count goes under \'Number of flat face\'.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of pasting a paper of the same size on a face?\",\"options\":[\"To hide the shape\",\"To identify the 2D shape of that face\",\"To make the shape heavier\",\"To clean the shape\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Pasting paper on a face helps a student see the two-dimensional shape (like a square or circle) that makes up the 3D object.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a column heading in the activity table?\",\"options\":[\"Three dimensional shape\",\"Number of flat face\",\"Colour of the shape\",\"Number of curved face\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table includes shape name, flat faces, and curved faces, but not the color of the shape.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the activity, if a shape has only curved faces and no flat faces, it is likely to be a:\",\"options\":[\"Cube\",\"Sphere (like a ball)\",\"Box\",\"Die\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A cube, box, and die have flat faces; a sphere is the only one with only a curved face.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many sticks are used to make a triangle?\",\"options\":[\"Two sticks\",\"Three sticks\",\"Four sticks\",\"Five sticks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":