,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states: \'Opposite sides of a rectangle are of equal length.\'\",\"topic\":\"Rectangle and Square\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When you fold a rectangular paper in half to connect the opposite sides, what happens to the corners?\",\"options\":[\"They stay apart\",\"They also match\",\"They become round\",\"They disappear\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that when folding the paper, the longer side matches exactly and \'corners also matches\'.\",\"topic\":\"Rectangle and Square\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many sides of a square are of equal length?\",\"options\":[\"Only two sides\",\"Only three sides\",\"All four sides\",\"No sides\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'That means all four sides of a square are of equal length.\'\",\"topic\":\"Rectangle and Square\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what shape of paper is being folded to check its sides?\",\"options\":[\"A rectangle\",\"A circle\",\"A square\",\"A triangle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text accompanying the figure says \'Observe the square paper as shown above.\'\",\"topic\":\"Rectangle and Square\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/107_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the longer side of a rectangle is 6 cm, what will be the length of the side opposite to it?\",\"options\":[\"3 cm\",\"12 cm\",\"6 cm\",\"0 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since opposite sides of a rectangle are of equal length, the opposite side must also be 6 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Rectangle and Square\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the dotted lines show the paper being folded horizontally, vertically, and diagonally. What does this folding process prove about the square?\",\"options\":[\"It has only two equal sides\",\"All four sides are of equal length\",\"It has no corners\",\"It is longer than it is wide\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure and text show that folding a square in these ways demonstrates that all four sides match and are equal.\",\"topic\":\"Rectangle and Square\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/107_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when the shorter sides of a rectangle are folded to meet each other?\",\"options\":[\"They match exactly with the opposite side\",\"They do not reach the other side\",\"They form a circle\",\"They become longer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'Similarly, the shorter sides also exactly matches with the opposite side.\'\",\"topic\":\"Rectangle and Square\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If one side of a square paper is 5 cm long, what can you say about the other three sides?\",\"options\":[\"They are all 10 cm long\",\"They are all 5 cm long\",\"They are all different lengths\",\"Only one other side is 5 cm long\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Because all four sides of a square are of equal length, if one is 5 cm, all must be 5 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Rectangle and Square\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To see if the opposite sides of a square match, in which directions should you fold the paper?\",\"options\":[\"Only diagonally\",\"Horizontally and vertically\",\"Only in a circle\",\"It cannot be folded\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says: \'Fold the paper horizontally and vertically and see if the opposite sides match.\'\",\"topic\":\"Rectangle and Square\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you fold a piece of paper and find that only the opposite sides match but all four sides are not the same, what shape is it?\",\"options\":[\"A square\",\"A rectangle\",\"A triangle\",\"A circle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A rectangle has opposite sides of equal length, whereas a square must have all four sides equal.\",\"topic\":\"Rectangle and Square\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many sides does a triangle have?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Th