s a shape into two identical halves is called the axis of symmetry.\",\"A shape is symmetric if one half is the mirror image of the other half.\",\"Folding a paper along the axis of symmetry makes both sides overlap perfectly.\",\"Symmetry can be seen in leaves, butterflies, rangoli, and festival decorations.\",\"Not all shapes have symmetry; some are asymmetrical and do not match when folded.\",\"Symmetry helps in creating balanced and beautiful designs in art and rangoli.\",\"Rotating a symmetric shape does not change its appearance.\",\"Symmetry is used in masks, greeting cards, and paper crafts for festivals.\",\"Symmetry is found in nature, architecture, and cultural patterns like kolam and alipana.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What do we call a figure that can be divided by a line into two identical halves?\",\"options\":[\"A rectangular figure\",\"A symmetrical figure\",\"A folded figure\",\"A Diwali figure\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a figure that can be divided into two identical halves is a symmetrical figure.\",\"topic\":\"Axis of Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the line that divides a figure into two identical halves?\",\"options\":[\"Middle line\",\"Folding line\",\"Axis of symmetry\",\"Identical line\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the line that divides a figure into two identical halves as the axis of symmetry.\",\"topic\":\"Axis of Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the text, what shape of paper did the children fold to make a lantern?\",\"options\":[\"Circular\",\"Triangular\",\"Square\",\"Rectangular\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the children used rectangular pieces of paper to fold.\",\"topic\":\"Axis of Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a piece of paper is folded and the two halves match exactly, what can we say about the figure?\",\"options\":[\"It is a lantern\",\"It is symmetrical\",\"It is a colored paper\",\"It is a broken shape\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if both halves match exactly, the figure is symmetrical with respect to the line.\",\"topic\":\"Axis of Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the two parts of a symmetrical figure when it is folded along the axis of symmetry?\",\"options\":[\"They become different shapes\",\"They match exactly\",\"They become two different sizes\",\"They do not touch each other\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that in a symmetrical figure, both halves match exactly when folded.\",\"topic\":\"Axis of Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, a figure is symmetrical only if the line divides it into how many identical halves?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Two\",\"One\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a symmetrical figure as one that can be divided into two identical halves.\",\"topic\":\"Axis of Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you fold a paper shape and the two parts do NOT match exactly, what does this tell you about the fold line?\",\"options\":[\"It is an axis of symmetry\",\"It is not an axis of symmetry\",\"The paper is rectangular\",\"The paper is colored\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since an axis of symmetry must result in identical halves that match exactly, a line that doesn\'t do this is not an axis of symmetry.\",\"topic\":\"Axis of Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To check if a new shape you made is symmetrical, what action should you perform based on the lesson?\",\"options\":[\"Color the paper\",\"Cut the paper into four pieces\",\"Fold the shape to see if the halves match\",\"Measure the length of the paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The lesson uses folding to demonstrate how to find if halves match exactly for symmetry.\",\"topic\":\"Axis of Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the line of a fold in the rectangular paper called the \'axis of symmetry\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it makes the paper colorful\",\"Because it divides the figure into two identical halves\",\"Because it is used for Diwali lanterns\",\"Because it makes the paper smaller\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains the line is the axis of symmetry because it divides the figure into two identical halves.\",\"topic\":\"Axis of Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which condition must be met for a figure to be considered symmetrical according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"It must be made of colored paper\",\"It must be used for a lantern\",\"It must be divided into two identical halves by a line\",\"It must be a rectangular shape only\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that being divided into two identical halves is the requirement for a symmetrical figure.\",\"topic\":\"Axis of Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What are shapes called if they do not give identical halves when folded?\",\"options\":[\"Perfect shapes\",\"Not symmetrical\",\"Trace-paper shapes\",\"Coloured shapes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that shapes which do not give identical halves after folding are not symmetrical.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should be drawn at the right place on a greeting card to make it symmetrical?\",\"options\":[\"A circle\",\"A border\",\"An axis\",\"A name\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to draw an axis at the right place to make greeting card shapes symmetrical.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"On which occasion does the text mention getting greeting cards of various shapes?\",\"options\":[\"Birthdays\",\"Diwali\",\"New Year\",\"Christmas\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions receiving greeting cards on the occasion of New Year.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do with the axis of symmetry found in leaves?\",\"options\":[\"Cut it out\",\"Trace it with a pen or pencil\",\"Erase it\",\"Colour it green\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks to find the axis of symmetry in leaves and trace it with a pen\\/pencil.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When a shape is folded to find its symmetry, what are the two resulting parts called?\",\"options\":[\"Different pieces\",\"Identical halves\",\"Uneven sides\",\"Opposite corners\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to the two matching parts of a symmetrical shape as identical halves.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which objects from the surroundings are mentioned to help find symmetry?\",\"options\":[\"Stones\",\"Leaves of trees\",\"Clouds\",\"Buildings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests observing the leaves of trees in the surroundings to find symmetry.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step mentioned to find the symmetry of a shape drawn on paper?\",\"options\":[\"Colour the shape\",\"Fold the paper first\",\"Cut it along the sides\",\"Stick it in a book\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to draw the shape and then cut it along the sides before folding.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which property is used when making masks from coloured paper as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"Property of thickness\",\"Property of symmetry\",\"Property of stickiness\",\"Property of weight\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says to use the property of symmetry to make masks.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What tool is mentioned to help copy shapes before cutting them to find symmetry?\",\"options\":[\"Graph paper\",\"Trace-paper\",\"Newspaper\",\"Cardboard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to trace the shapes using trace-paper.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you fold a shape and the parts do not match exactly, what can you conclude?\",\"options\":[\"The shape is symmetrical\",\"The shape is not symmetrical\",\"The paper is too thick\",\"The axis is correct\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, shapes that do not give identical halves are not symmetrical.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher\'s note, why is symmetry useful for decorations?\",\"options\":[\"To make them stronger\",\"To make them cheaper\",\"To make them aesthetically appealing\",\"To make them easier to carry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states symmetry is useful in decorating to make things aesthetically appealing.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What two types of shapes does the teacher want students to experience the difference between?\",\"options\":[\"Big and small shapes\",\"Coloured and plain shapes\",\"Symmetrical and asymmetrical shapes\",\"Round and square shapes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note encourages students to experience the difference between symmetrical and asymmetrical shapes.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the art form practiced in Tamilnadu called?\",\"options\":[\"Rangoli\",\"Kolam\",\"Alipana\",\"Mehendi\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that in Tamilnadu, the art is practiced in the form of Kolam.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which type of paper is used to draw symmetrical figures as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Graph paper\",\"Plain paper\",\"Dot paper\",\"Lined paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text begins by instructing to draw symmetrical figures using dot paper.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Rotating the hands of a clock in the opposite direction is called ______.\",\"options\":[\"Clockwise\",\"Straight\",\"Anti-clockwise\",\"Circular\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines rotating in the opposite direction of clock hands as anti-clockwise.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In Bengal, the art of decoration is known by which name?\",\"options\":[\"Rangoli\",\"Kolam\",\"Alipana\",\"Painting\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that in Bengal, this art is practiced under the name of Alipana.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, for what purpose is art like Rangoli used in mathematics?\",\"options\":[\"To study addition\",\"To study patterns and symmetry\",\"To study subtraction\",\"To study division\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that it is used to study patterns, sequences, combinations, and symmetry.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, in which direction are the colorful arrows moving?\",\"options\":[\"Clockwise\",\"Anti-clockwise\",\"Upwards\",\"Downwards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure label and the direction of arrows show the anti-clockwise direction.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/118_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the movement shown is the opposite of how a clock\'s hands usually move. This is called ______.\",\"options\":[\"Clockwise direction\",\"Anti-clockwise direction\",\"Vertical direction\",\"Horizontal direction\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure illustrates the anti-clockwise direction, which is opposite to the normal movement of clock hands.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/118_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Amazing symmetry can be seen in the carvings of which famous structure mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Gateway of India\",\"Taj Mahal\",\"Red Fort\",\"Qutub Minar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions amazing symmetry in the carvings of the Taj Mahal and Ellora-Elephanta.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What must be done to a diagram so that a given line becomes an axis of symmetry?\",\"options\":[\"Erase the diagram\",\"Complete the diagram\",\"Rotate the diagram\",\"Color the diagram\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Complete the diagram so that the given line becomes an axis of symmetry\'.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student rotates a symmetrical shape in the same direction as the hands of a clock, they are rotating it ______.\",\"options\":[\"Anti-clockwise\",\"Clockwise\",\"Backwards\",\"Upwards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to the direction of clock hands as the clockwise direction.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text mention that ancient artworks were found in temples, mosques, and churches?\",\"options\":[\"To show that this art existed thousands of years ago\",\"To teach history only\",\"To show how to build them\",\"To teach about religions\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that from these artworks, students should be made aware that this art existed thousands of years ago.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher\'s note, what should we do while preserving our own culture?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore other cultures\",\"Respect the culture of others\",\"Only study one\'s own art\",\"Avoid ancient structures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'while preserving our culture we should respect the culture of others\'.\",\"topic\":\"Rotation of Symmetrical Shapes\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the shape of a symmetrical object when it is rotated?\",\"options\":[\"It changes into a new shape\",\"It becomes smaller\",\"It does not change its shape\",\"It becomes bigger\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that rotating a symmetrical shape does not change its shape.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you turn a symmetrical shape clockwise, what stays the same?\",\"options\":[\"Its color only\",\"Its shape\",\"Its weight\",\"Its size only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the rule, clockwise rotation does not change the shape of a symmetrical object.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student rotates a symmetrical square anticlockwise. What will the square look like after the rotation?\",\"options\":[\"A triangle\",\"A circle\",\"The same square shape\",\"A rectangle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rotating a symmetrical shape anticlockwise does not change its shape.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these actions will NOT change the shape of a symmetrical object according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Cutting it in half\",\"Rotating it clockwise\",\"Stretching it\",\"Tearing it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions that rotation (clockwise or anticlockwise) does not change the shape.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In which directions can you rotate a symmetrical shape without changing its shape?\",\"options\":[\"Only clockwise\",\"Only anticlockwise\",\"Both clockwise and anticlockwise\",\"Only upwards\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions both clockwise and anticlockwise rotation.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text say about rotating a symmetrical shape anticlockwise?\",\"options\":[\"It makes the shape disappear\",\"It does not change its shape\",\"It makes the shape crooked\",\"It only works for circles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that anticlockwise rotation does not change the shape.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a symmetrical star is turned anticlockwise, its shape:\",\"options\":[\"Disappears\",\"Changes into a moon\",\"Remains the same\",\"Becomes a straight line\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since a star is a symmetrical shape, rotation does not change its shape.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what kind of shape does not change when rotated?\",\"options\":[\"Any irregular shape\",\"Only very large shapes\",\"A symmetrical shape\",\"Only shapes made of paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The rule specifically applies to a \'symmetrical shape\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a shape is symmetrical, rotating it clockwise:\",\"options\":[\"Changes its basic form\",\"Keeps its shape the same\",\"Makes it look like a different object\",\"Makes it asymmetrical\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text confirms that rotation does not change the shape of a symmetrical object.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why does a symmetrical shape look the same after a clockwise rotation?\",\"options\":[\"Because rotation does not change its shape\",\"Because it is painted with bright colors\",\"Because it is a very small shape\",\"Because it is moving very fast\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides the fact that rotating a symmetrical shape does not change its shape.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21460,13,3,'Maths','en','Volume and Capacity','[\"Volume is the amount of space a substance occupies.\",\"Capacity is the amount a container can hold when full.\",\"Both volume and capacity are measured in litres (L) or millilitres (mL).\",\"1 litre = 1000 millilitres.\",\"A litre is a standard unit for measuring liquids like water, milk, juice.\",\"Containers like bottles, jugs, buckets, and mugs have different capacities.\",\"To find capacity, fill the container completely with water using a litre measure.\",\"If 2 litres of water fill a jug, its capacity is 2 litres.\",\"Half litre = 500 mL, quarter litre = 250 mL, three-quarter litre = 750 mL.\",\"We can estimate capacity before measuring to develop sense of size.\",\"Real-life examples: milk packets, water bottles, cold drink cans show litres.\",\"Capacity does not change with the shape of the container.\",\"Volume of liquid remains same even if poured into different containers.\",\"We use measuring jars or marked bottles to measure liquid accurately.\",\"Activities like pouring water from one container to another help understand capacity.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many bowls of water of the same size did Ramesh pour to fill the vessel completely?\",\"options\":[\"4 bowls\",\"6 bowls\",\"8 bowls\",\"10 bowls\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states that Ramesh poured 10 bowls of water of the same size to fill the vessel.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe and Discuss\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many pots of water did Anagha pour to fill the same vessel completely?\",\"options\":[\"2 pots\",\"4 pots\",\"10 pots\",\"12 pots\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when Anagha poured 4 pots of water, the vessel was completely filled.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe and Discuss\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the measurement of water to fill the vessel not the same for Ramesh and Anagha?\",\"options\":[\"Because the water was different\",\"Because different measuring objects were used\",\"Because the vessel changed its size\",\"Because they filled it at different times\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains the measurement is not the same because different measuring objects (bowls and pots) were used.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe and Discuss\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which vessel will hold the most water when filled completely?\",\"options\":[\"The glass\",\"The bowl\",\"The bucket\",\"The bottle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"By observing the sizes in the figure, the bucket is the largest vessel and will hold the most water.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe and Discuss\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/119_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the capacity of the vessel in terms of the small bowls Ramesh is using?\",\"options\":[\"4 bowls\",\"10 bowls\",\"2 bowls\",\"8 bowls\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text and figure show that Ramesh fills the vessel using 10 bowls of water.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe and Discuss\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/119_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the capacity of the vessel mentioned in the text in terms of mugs?\",\"options\":[\"10 mugs\",\"4 mugs\",\"1 mug\",\"6 mugs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the vessel has a capacity of 10 bowls or 4 mugs.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe and Discuss\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to fill the vessel using fewer turns of pouring, which utensil from the text should you choose?\",\"options\":[\"The bowl\",\"The pot\",\"A spoon\",\"A small cup\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since it takes only 4 pots compared to 10 bowls to fill the same vessel, the pot is larger and requires fewer turns.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe and Discuss\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Ramesh used 10 units and Anagha used 4 units to fill the same vessel. What does this tell us about the size of their measuring units?\",\"options\":[\"Ramesh\'s bowl is bigger than Anagha\'s pot\",\"Anagha\'s pot is bigger than Ramesh\'s bowl\",\"Both units are exactly the same size\",\"The bowl holds more water than the pot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since fewer pots (4) are needed than bowls (10) to fill the same space, the pot must be larger.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe and Discuss\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what were used to fill the same vessel?\",\"options\":[\"Different colors of water\",\"Different utensils\",\"The same size of mugs only\",\"Only one type of bowl\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that to fill the same vessel, different utensils (measurements) were used.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe and Discuss\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the result when Ramesh poured 10 bowls of water into the vessel?\",\"options\":[\"The vessel was half full\",\"The vessel was completely filled\",\"The vessel remained empty\",\"The water overflowed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when Ramesh poured 10 bowls, the vessel was completely filled.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe and Discuss\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the standard unit of measurement for liquids?\",\"options\":[\"Meter\",\"Litre\",\"Gram\",\"Kilogram\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a litre is a standard unit of measurement for liquids.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the example given in the text, what unit was used to measure the capacity of the pans?\",\"options\":[\"Glass bottles\",\"Copper pots\",\"Plastic buckets\",\"Steel spoons\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the capacity of both the pans is 4 copper pots.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If two people use the same unit to measure the capacity of a container, what will happen to the measurement?\",\"options\":[\"It will be different\",\"It will be the same\",\"It will be wrong\",\"It will change every time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says that if anyone uses the same unit to measure the capacity, the measurement will be the same.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why are standard units used to measure the volume of a container?\",\"options\":[\"To make the container look bigger\",\"To ensure the volume remains the same regardless of who fills it\",\"To change the amount of water in the container\",\"To use different objects every time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Standard units ensure that the volume remains the same, no matter who performs the measurement.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text say is important for ensuring a measurement remains the same no matter what makes it?\",\"options\":[\"Using different units\",\"Using standardized units\",\"Using larger containers\",\"Using different people\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states it is important to use standardized units so that the measurement remains the same.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a pan has a capacity of 4 copper pots, and you use the same copper pots to measure another pan of the exact same size, what will the measurement be?\",\"options\":[\"2 copper pots\",\"4 copper pots\",\"6 copper pots\",\"8 copper pots\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since the unit (copper pots) and the container size are the same, the measurement remains 4 copper pots.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a shopkeeper and a customer both measure 1 litre of milk using a standard litre measure, what can we conclude?\",\"options\":[\"The shopkeeper will have more milk\",\"The customer will have more milk\",\"The measurement will be the same for both\",\"The measurement will change\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Using a standard unit like a litre ensures the measurement remains the same regardless of who fills it.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of using the same unit (like copper pots) to measure two identical pans?\",\"options\":[\"The capacity will be different for each pan\",\"The capacity will be the same because the unit is the same\",\"The capacity cannot be measured\",\"The unit will change\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that because the unit is the same, the measurement will be the same.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Analyze this: If we do NOT use standard units, what might happen to the measurement of a container\'s volume?\",\"options\":[\"It might change depending on who measures it\",\"It will always stay the same\",\"It will always be measured in litres\",\"It will become more accurate\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Standard units are used specifically to prevent measurements from changing based on who is measuring.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a \'litre\' better for measuring milk than using a \'small bowl\' from your kitchen?\",\"options\":[\"A litre is a standard unit that gives the same measurement for everyone\",\"A bowl is easier to carry\",\"A bowl holds more milk than a litre\",\"A litre changes its size every day\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A litre is a standard unit, which ensures consistency, unlike non-standard objects like bowls.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What does the milkman use to give milk to Gauri?\",\"options\":[\"A measuring jar\",\"A small spoon\",\"A large plate\",\"A plastic bag\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that Gauri watches the milkman uncle giving milk using a measuring jar.\",\"topic\":\"Volume\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the capacity of the water bottle Gauri has?\",\"options\":[\"10 litres\",\"5 litres\",\"1 litre\",\"2 litres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Gauri says, \'I have a one-litre water bottle.\'\",\"topic\":\"Volume\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If there was 10 litres of milk in the kettle, what is the volume of milk in that kettle?\",\"options\":[\"1 litre\",\"10 litres\",\"5 litres\",\"20 litres\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if there was 10 litres of milk in the kettle, the volume is 10 litres.\",\"topic\":\"Volume\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Gauri do with the water from her bottle?\",\"options\":[\"She drinks it all\",\"She pours it into a mug\",\"She washes the kettle\",\"She gives it to the milkman\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Gauri says, \'I pour the water from it into a mug.\'\",\"topic\":\"Volume\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If 1 litre of milk is poured from a kettle into a bottle, what is the volume of milk in the bottle?\",\"options\":[\"10 litres\",\"1 litre\",\"9 litres\",\"0 litres\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that when 1 litre is poured into the bottle, the volume of milk in the bottle is 1 litre.\",\"topic\":\"Volume\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Gauri fills the mug \'to the brim\'. What does this mean?\",\"options\":[\"The mug is half full\",\"The mug is empty\",\"The mug is filled to the very top\",\"The mug is leaking\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Filling to the brim means filling a container completely to its top edge.\",\"topic\":\"Volume\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the milkman doing with the measuring jar?\",\"options\":[\"Drinking milk from it\",\"Pouring milk into a bottle\",\"Washing the jar in the kettle\",\"Putting the jar in his pocket\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the milkman using the jar to pour milk into a bottle held by Gauri.\",\"topic\":\"Volume\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/120_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Gauri looking at on the table in the right-side drawing?\",\"options\":[\"A large milk kettle\",\"A mug and her water bottle\",\"A measuring jar\",\"A plate of food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The right side of the image shows Gauri with her water bottle and a mug on the table.\",\"topic\":\"Volume\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/120_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How much milk was originally in the milk kettle mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"1 litre\",\"2 litres\",\"10 litres\",\"5 litres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'There was 10 litres of milk in the milk kettle.\'\",\"topic\":\"Volume\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If Gauri\'s one-litre bottle is used to fill a mug completely to the brim, what can we say about the mug\'s capacity?\",\"options\":[\"It is exactly 10 litres\",\"It is exactly 1 litre\",\"It is more than 10 litres\",\"It is less than half a litre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since the water from a one-litre bottle fills the mug to the brim, the mug holds 1 litre.\",\"topic\":\"Volume\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is commonly found on sealed packets, cans, or bottles of liquids to show their measure?\",\"options\":[\"Metre\",\"Litre\",\"Kilogram\",\"Rupee\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions finding the word \'litre\' on sealed packets, cans, and bottles.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss and Guess\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the discussion in the text, which of these items is measured in litres?\",\"options\":[\"A piece of ribbon\",\"A sack of grain\",\"A bottle of oil\",\"A bundle of sticks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Liquids in bottles, like oil, are measured in litres as per the topic.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss and Guess\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A glass of water will approximately hold ____ than 1 litre of water.\",\"options\":[\"more\",\"less\",\"exactly\",\"double\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A standard glass has a capacity that is less than 1 litre.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss and Guess\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A bucket will approximately hold ____ than 1 litre of water.\",\"options\":[\"less\",\"exactly\",\"more\",\"half\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A bucket is a large container that holds more than 1 litre of water.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss and Guess\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, where can you find the word \'litre\' written?\",\"options\":[\"On a school blackboard\",\"On a sealed packet of milk\",\"On a wooden table\",\"On a pair of shoes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests looking for the word \'litre\' on sealed packets, cans, and bottles.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss and Guess\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A mug will approximately hold ____ 1 litre of water.\",\"options\":[\"more than\",\"exactly\",\"less than\",\"ten times\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A mug is smaller than a 1-litre bottle, so it holds less than 1 litre.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss and Guess\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you have a can of juice, which unit of measurement are you likely to see on it?\",\"options\":[\"Centimetre\",\"Gram\",\"Litre\",\"Metre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that cans of liquid items have the word \'litre\' on them.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss and Guess\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Compare a glass and a bucket. Which statement is correct based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"The glass holds more than the bucket.\",\"The bucket holds less than 1 litre.\",\"The bucket holds more than 1 litre.\",\"The glass holds exactly 1 litre.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks to identify that a bucket holds more than 1 litre.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss and Guess\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these containers is specifically mentioned in the text to check for the word \'litre\'?\",\"options\":[\"Cans\",\"Boxes\",\"Envelopes\",\"Bags\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions sealed packets, cans, and bottles.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss and Guess\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is the most likely observation about a mug\'s capacity?\",\"options\":[\"It holds more than a bucket.\",\"It holds less than 1 litre.\",\"It holds exactly 5 litres.\",\"It holds more than 1 litre.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the size of a mug compared to a 1-litre measure, it holds less than 1 litre.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss and Guess\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which two containers are mentioned as examples in the text for the activity?\",\"options\":[\"A bucket and a mug\",\"A small bowl and a glass\",\"A spoon and a plate\",\"A jar and a cup\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions a small bowl and a glass as examples of containers of different sizes.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the capacity of the bottle that needs to be filled in this activity?\",\"options\":[\"5 litres\",\"500 ml\",\"1 litre\",\"2 litres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks how many bowls or glasses are needed to pour into a 1 litre bottle.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should you do before actually pouring the water into the bottle?\",\"options\":[\"Measure the bowl\",\"First estimate\",\"Clean the bottle\",\"Drink the water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'First estimate and then actually pour the water\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which two pots are shown in the first column for the experiment?\",\"options\":[\"A bottle and a jug\",\"A bowl and a glass\",\"A cup and a saucer\",\"A bucket and a spoon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Pots\' column in the figure shows a blue bowl and a transparent glass.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/121_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what information is recorded in the \'Actual\' column?\",\"options\":[\"The weight of the water\",\"The color of the pots\",\"The number of pots needed to fill the bottle completely\",\"The time taken to fill the bottle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The \'Actual\' column is under the heading \'Fill completely with water\', indicating the real count of pots used.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/121_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the unit of measurement used for the bottle in this topic?\",\"options\":[\"Kilogram\",\"Metre\",\"Litre\",\"Centimetre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text refers to the bottle as a \'1 litre bottle\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the activity suggest using two containers of different sizes?\",\"options\":[\"To see if they have the same color\",\"To compare how many of each are needed to fill 1 litre\",\"To see which one is heavier\",\"To check if they are made of glass\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity asks to compare how many small bowls versus how many glasses are needed for the same volume.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How can you check whether your estimate is correct according to the activity?\",\"options\":[\"By asking a teacher\",\"By looking at the picture\",\"By actually pouring the water and checking\",\"By weighing the bottle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'actually pour the water and check whether your estimate is correct\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you use a small bowl and a glass to fill the same 1 litre bottle, what are you measuring?\",\"options\":[\"The height of the bottle\",\"The capacity of the bottle using different units\",\"The temperature of the water\",\"The weight of the bowl\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity uses different sized pots to measure the volume\\/capacity of the 1 litre bottle.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final task mentioned at the end of the text?\",\"options\":[\"Draw the pots\",\"List vessels that can store more than 1 litre of water\",\"Empty the bottle\",\"Wash the glass\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The final sentence of the text is \'List the vessels that can store more than 1 litre of water.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the capacity of a vessel like a jug or a bucket?\",\"options\":[\"The weight of the vessel\",\"The amount of water it holds to fill it completely\",\"The height of the vessel\",\"The color of the vessel\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines capacity as the amount of water a vessel holds to fill it completely.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If 2 litres of water is needed to fill a vessel completely, what is its capacity?\",\"options\":[\"1 litre\",\"2 litres\",\"4 litres\",\"Half litre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, if 2 litres fill a vessel completely, its capacity is 2 litres.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A vehicle whose tank holds the most diesel is said to have the:\",\"options\":[\"Lowest tank capacity\",\"Highest tank capacity\",\"Smallest tank\",\"Empty tank\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the vehicle whose tank holds the most diesel has the highest tank capacity.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many parts of kokum syrup are in a bottle that is \'One Litre\' full?\",\"options\":[\"One part\",\"Two parts\",\"Three parts\",\"Four parts\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that a one litre bottle is filled with four parts.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When two parts out of four parts are filled in a bottle, what is the amount of syrup?\",\"options\":[\"Quarter litre\",\"Half litre\",\"Three quarter litre\",\"One litre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that two parts out of four parts being filled means there is half a litre.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the amount of kokum syrup shown in the bottle?\",\"options\":[\"One litre\",\"Half litre\",\"Quarter litre\",\"Three quarter litre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows one part out of four filled, which is a quarter litre.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/121_107.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many parts out of four are filled with kokum syrup?\",\"options\":[\"One part\",\"Two parts\",\"Three parts\",\"Four parts\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure represents three quarters of a litre, which consists of three parts.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/121_108.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What do we call the amount when only one part out of four parts is filled?\",\"options\":[\"Half litre\",\"One litre\",\"Quarter litre\",\"Three quarter litre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines one part out of four as a quarter litre.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a bottle is filled with three out of four parts, how much syrup does it have?\",\"options\":[\"Quarter litre\",\"Half litre\",\"Three quarters of a litre\",\"One litre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that three out of four parts is three quarters of a litre.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you have a half litre of syrup, how many more parts are needed to make it one full litre?\",\"options\":[\"One part\",\"Two parts\",\"Three parts\",\"Four parts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since half litre is 2 parts and one litre is 4 parts, 2 more parts are needed.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these amounts is the smallest?\",\"options\":[\"One litre\",\"Half litre\",\"Quarter litre\",\"Three quarter litre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A quarter litre is 1 part, while the others are 2, 3, or 4 parts.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"To have a \'Three quarter litre\', how many parts must be empty in a four-part bottle?\",\"options\":[\"One part\",\"Two parts\",\"Three parts\",\"Four parts\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"If 3 parts are filled for a three quarter litre, then 1 part (4 minus 3) must be empty.\",\"topic\":\"Tell me\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What do you get if you take a quarter litre of water twice?\",\"options\":[\"One litre\",\"Half a litre\",\"Three quarters of a litre\",\"Two litres\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, taking a quarter litre twice gives you half a litre.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of putting a quarter litre and a half litre together?\",\"options\":[\"One litre\",\"Half a litre\",\"Three quarters of a litre\",\"A quarter litre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that a quarter litre and a half litre together make three quarters of a litre.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the capacity of the bottle used to make the marks in the activity?\",\"options\":[\"Half a litre\",\"One litre\",\"Three quarters of a litre\",\"Two litres\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity instructions specify to take a bottle of one litre capacity.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these marks should be made on the bottle with the teacher\'s help?\",\"options\":[\"Full, Empty, Half\",\"One, Two, Three\",\"Quarter, Half, Three quarter\",\"Small, Medium, Large\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions making marks like \'Quarter\', \'Half\', and \'Three quarter\' on the bottle.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step you should do before filling a vessel with water to find its capacity?\",\"options\":[\"Mark the vessel\",\"Estimate the capacity\",\"Call the teacher\",\"Empty the 1 litre bottle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions say to \'First estimate and then fill it with water\'.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are using a marked 1-litre bottle to fill an empty vessel, what are you trying to find?\",\"options\":[\"The weight of the vessel\",\"The height of the vessel\",\"The capacity of the vessel\",\"The color of the water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The activity is designed to find the capacity of different vessels.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many quarter litres are needed to make half a litre?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says taking a quarter litre twice (two times) gives half a litre.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a vessel is filled exactly to the \'Three quarter\' mark on the 1-litre bottle, it contains:\",\"options\":[\"Less than a half litre\",\"Exactly a quarter litre\",\"A quarter litre and a half litre combined\",\"Two full litres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines three quarters as a quarter litre and a half litre together.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it important to use a marked 1-litre bottle when measuring different vessels?\",\"options\":[\"To make the water cleaner\",\"To accurately find the capacity of the vessels\",\"To make the vessel look beautiful\",\"To change the shape of the vessel\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using a marked bottle allows you to measure the exact capacity of other vessels.\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should you do after finding the capacity of one vessel?\",\"options\":[\"Stop the activity\",\"Break the bottle\",\"Do the same procedure for different vessels\",\"Drink the water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Do the same procedure to find the capacity of different vessels.\'\",\"topic\":\"Do The Activity\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific measures should students use to practice measuring water according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"1 litre and half litre measures\",\"2 litre and 5 litre measures\",\"10 litre and 20 litre measures\",\"100 ml and 200 ml measures\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that students should practice measuring water using 1 litre and half litre measures.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should students do after measuring water with different containers?\",\"options\":[\"Empty the containers immediately\",\"Discuss the findings\",\"Draw the containers in their books\",\"Measure the weight of the containers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that students should be given the opportunity to measure water and discuss the findings.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which two concepts are mentioned for students to learn in this topic?\",\"options\":[\"Length and Breadth\",\"Volume and Capacity\",\"Weight and Mass\",\"Height and Width\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that students should learn the concepts of volume and capacity.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides learning the concepts themselves, what else should students learn about volume and capacity?\",\"options\":[\"How to spell the words\",\"The difference between volume and capacity\",\"The history of these measurements\",\"How to draw the measuring tools\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that students should learn the difference between volume and capacity.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is following the activity in the text, which tool would they most likely use to measure water?\",\"options\":[\"A weighing scale\",\"A ruler\",\"A 1 litre measure\",\"A thermometer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests practicing measurement using a 1 litre measure.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student wants to measure a smaller amount of water using the measures mentioned in the text. Which one should they use?\",\"options\":[\"A 10 litre bucket\",\"A half litre measure\",\"A 5 litre jar\",\"A 2 litre bottle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions using a half litre measure as one of the standard tools for practice.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text suggest using \'different containers\' to measure water?\",\"options\":[\"To make the classroom look colorful\",\"To compare findings and understand volume\\/capacity\",\"To see which container is the heaviest\",\"To practice cleaning different shapes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Measuring with different containers allows students to discuss findings and learn the concepts of volume and capacity.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary activity students should be given the opportunity to do?\",\"options\":[\"Measure water using different containers\",\"Measure the length of the classroom\",\"Count the number of water bottles\",\"Calculate the price of water\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text begins by saying students should be given the opportunity to measure water using different containers.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is one of the main goals of practicing with 1 litre and half litre measures?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to pour water without spilling\",\"To learn the concept of volume\",\"To learn about different types of liquids\",\"To learn how to wash containers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links practicing with these measures to learning the concept of volume.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When students discuss their findings after measuring, what are they evaluating?\",\"options\":[\"The cost of the water\",\"The volume and capacity of the containers used\",\"The temperature of the water\",\"The material the containers are made of\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The discussion is intended to help them learn the concepts of volume and capacity based on their measurements.\",\"topic\":\"For teachers\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28');
INSERT INTO `ep_topic_packs` VALUES (21461,13,3,'Maths','en','Measurement of Time','[\"Time is measured in hours, minutes, and seconds.\",\"There are 60 minutes in 1 hour.\",\"There are 60 seconds in 1 minute.\",\"Quarter past means 15 minutes after the hour.\",\"Half past means 30 minutes after the hour.\",\"Quarter to means 15 minutes before the next hour.\",\"When the minute hand is at 3, it is quarter past.\",\"When the minute hand is at 6, it is half past.\",\"When the minute hand is at 9, it is quarter to.\",\"The hour hand moves slowly as time passes.\",\"At quarter past, the hour hand is just after the hour number.\",\"At half past, the hour hand is halfway between two numbers.\",\"At quarter to, the hour hand is just before the next hour number.\",\"A day has 24 hours.\",\"A week has 7 days.\",\"A month has about 30 or 31 days, except February.\",\"February has 28 days, or 29 in a leap year.\",\"A year has 12 months.\",\"Clocks have two main hands: hour hand (short) and minute hand (long).\",\"Digital time shows hours and minutes like 3:45.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the name of the big hand on the clock?\",\"options\":[\"Second hand\",\"Hour hand\",\"Minute hand\",\"Small hand\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I am the big hand. My name is minute hand\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many minutes are there in one hour?\",\"options\":[\"12 minutes\",\"60 minutes\",\"5 minutes\",\"24 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text clearly says, \'There are 60 minutes in an hour.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the given figure, what does the small hand show on the clock?\",\"options\":[\"Seconds\",\"Minutes\",\"Numbers\",\"Hours\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The figure states, \'I show hours on the clock\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/123_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What are the units used for time measurement?\",\"options\":[\"Numbers and hands\",\"Big and small\",\"Hours and minutes\",\"Clocks and watches\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Hours and minutes are the units of time measurement.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, how much time does the big hand take to move from one number to the next number?\",\"options\":[\"1 hour\",\"5 minutes\",\"60 minutes\",\"12 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure states, \'It takes me 5 minutes to move from one number to the next number.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/123_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the hour hand is at 7 and the minute hand is at 12, what time is it?\",\"options\":[\"12 O\'clock\",\"5 O\'clock\",\"7 O\'clock\",\"60 O\'clock\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Based on the example in the text, if the hour hand is at a number and the minute hand is at 12, it is that number O\'clock.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How much time does the hour hand take to move from the number 4 to the number 5?\",\"options\":[\"5 minutes\",\"12 minutes\",\"60 hours\",\"1 hour\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'It takes me 1 hour to move from one number to the next number\' for the hour hand.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When the minute hand moves all the way from 12 back to 12, how many hours have passed?\",\"options\":[\"12 hours\",\"1 hour\",\"5 hours\",\"60 hours\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when the minute hand moves from 12 to 12, it makes 60 minutes, which is 1 hour.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which hand takes a longer time to move from one number to the next number?\",\"options\":[\"The minute hand\",\"The big hand\",\"The hour hand\",\"Both take the same time\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The minute hand takes 5 minutes, while the hour hand takes 1 hour (60 minutes) to move between numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If the minute hand moves from number 12 to number 1, and then to number 2, how many total minutes have passed?\",\"options\":[\"2 minutes\",\"5 minutes\",\"10 minutes\",\"60 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"It takes 5 minutes to move from one number to the next; moving two gaps (12 to 1 and 1 to 2) takes 5 + 5 = 10 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the gap of minutes between each of the two adjacent numbers on a clock?\",\"options\":[\"1 minute\",\"5 minutes\",\"10 minutes\",\"12 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states there is a gap of 5 minutes between each of the two adjacent numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Clock reading\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the hour hand has moved forward from 2, what does it mean?\",\"options\":[\"It is exactly 2 o\'clock\",\"It is before 2 o\'clock\",\"It is past 2 o\'clock\",\"It is 5 o\'clock\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the hour hand moving forward from 2 means it is past 2 o\'clock.\",\"topic\":\"Clock reading\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To find the minutes, which table should you multiply the number at the minute hand by?\",\"options\":[\"Table of 2\",\"Table of 4\",\"Table of 5\",\"Table of 10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to multiply the number where the minute hand is by the table of 5.\",\"topic\":\"Clock reading\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the minute hand is at 4, how many minutes have passed?\",\"options\":[\"4 minutes\",\"10 minutes\",\"20 minutes\",\"40 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Using the table of 5, 5 x 4 = 20 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Clock reading\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the hour hand is past 3 and the minute hand is at 2, what is the time?\",\"options\":[\"3 hours 2 minutes\",\"3 hours 10 minutes\",\"2 hours 3 minutes\",\"3 hours 5 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The hour is past 3, and for the minute hand at 2, we calculate 5 x 2 = 10 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Clock reading\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the clock shows 2 hours 20 minutes, where is the minute hand pointing?\",\"options\":[\"At 2\",\"At 4\",\"At 5\",\"At 20\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since 5 x 4 = 20, the minute hand must be at 4 to show 20 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Clock reading\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If the minute hand is at 7, how many minutes does it show?\",\"options\":[\"7 minutes\",\"35 minutes\",\"12 minutes\",\"5 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Following the rule in the text, 5 x 7 = 35 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Clock reading\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What determines the minutes on a clock according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The number the hour hand is on\",\"The number the minute hand is on multiplied by 5\",\"The gap between 12 and 1\",\"The table of 2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that minutes are found by multiplying the minute hand\'s number by 5.\",\"topic\":\"Clock reading\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the hour hand is past 12 and the minute hand is at 1, what is the time?\",\"options\":[\"12 hours 1 minute\",\"12 hours 5 minutes\",\"1 hour 12 minutes\",\"12 hours 10 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The hour is 12 and the minute hand at 1 means 5 x 1 = 5 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Clock reading\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Why do we multiply the minute hand number by 5 to find the minutes?\",\"options\":[\"Because there are 5 hands on a clock\",\"Because there is a gap of 5 minutes between each adjacent number\",\"Because the hour hand is always at 5\",\"Because the table of 5 is the only one used in math\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states we multiply by 5 because there is a gap of 5 minutes between each of the two adjacent numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Clock reading\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many minutes are there in one hour?\",\"options\":[\"30 minutes\",\"45 minutes\",\"60 minutes\",\"15 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, 1 hour = 60 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many minutes make a quarter of an hour?\",\"options\":[\"15 minutes\",\"30 minutes\",\"45 minutes\",\"60 minutes\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that a quarter of an hour = 15 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many minutes are there in 3 quarters of an hour?\",\"options\":[\"15 minutes\",\"30 minutes\",\"60 minutes\",\"45 minutes\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text defines 3 quarters of an hour as 45 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is 30 minutes past an hour called?\",\"options\":[\"Quarter past\",\"Half past\",\"Quarter to\",\"Full hour\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that half an hour is 30 minutes, and 3:30 is called \'half past three\'.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When the minute hand is at 3, it is called _____.\",\"options\":[\"Half past\",\"Quarter to\",\"Quarter past\",\"O\'clock\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says when the minute hand is at 3, it is called \'quarter past\'.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'quarter to two\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"15 minutes past 2\",\"15 minutes before 2\",\"30 minutes past 2\",\"15 minutes past 12\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'quarter to two\' means it is 15 minutes before 2.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which hand is pointing exactly at the number 3?\",\"options\":[\"The hour hand\",\"The minute hand\",\"The second hand\",\"Both hands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the figure for \'Quarter Past\', the longer hand (minute hand) is pointing at 3.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/126_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the time is 15 minutes past 10, how do we say it in words?\",\"options\":[\"Half past ten\",\"Quarter to ten\",\"Quarter past ten\",\"Quarter past eleven\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Following the pattern \'15 minutes past 1 = Quarter past one\', 15 minutes past 10 is Quarter past ten.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the time is 9:45, how is it expressed using the \'quarter\' term?\",\"options\":[\"Quarter past nine\",\"Quarter to nine\",\"Quarter to ten\",\"Half past nine\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Based on the example 3:45 = Quarter to four, 9:45 would be Quarter to ten.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the time shown?\",\"options\":[\"Quarter past one\",\"Quarter to one\",\"Half past one\",\"Quarter past two\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the hour hand between 1 and 2 and the minute hand at 3, which is quarter past one.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/126_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the hour hand is between 3 and 4 and the minute hand is on 6, what is the time?\",\"options\":[\"3:15\",\"4:30\",\"3:30\",\"3:45\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that when the hour hand is between 3 and 4 and the minute hand is on 6, the time is 3:30.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a clock shows \'quarter to two\', how many minutes have passed since 1 o\'clock?\",\"options\":[\"15 minutes\",\"30 minutes\",\"45 minutes\",\"60 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'quarter to two\' means it is 45 minutes past 1.\",\"topic\":\"Quarter past, Half, Quarter to\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should students prepare for the current year?\",\"options\":[\"A 1-month calendar\",\"A 6-month calendar\",\"A 12-month calendar\",\"A weekly calendar\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher instructions state that students should prepare a 12-month calendar for the current year.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which day of the week is highlighted in a different color at the top of the list?\",\"options\":[\"Mon\",\"Sun\",\"Sat\",\"Fri\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the figure, the box for \'Sun\' (Sunday) is highlighted in an orange\\/red color.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/128_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a type of festival that students are asked to list in their 1-year table?\",\"options\":[\"School festivals\",\"National festivals\",\"Sports festivals\",\"Music festivals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that learners should complete a table of national festivals and Indian festivals.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who are the students advised to take help from when necessary?\",\"options\":[\"Only teachers\",\"Friends and parents\",\"Only neighbors\",\"Strangers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that learners should be advised to take help from friends and parents where necessary.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what two pieces of information are required to be filled at the very top of the calendar grid?\",\"options\":[\"Name and Roll Number\",\"Day and Date\",\"Month and Year\",\"Season and Time\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The top of the figure shows \'Month ...... Year ......\' to be filled in.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/128_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to find out how many Fridays there are in a specific month, which tool mentioned in the text should you look at?\",\"options\":[\"A clock\",\"A ruler\",\"A calendar\",\"A compass\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks to \'Look at the calendar\' to answer questions like how many Fridays are in the month.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What information should be included in the 1-year table of festivals besides the name of the festival?\",\"options\":[\"Dates and time\",\"Pictures and colors\",\"Names of friends\",\"Weather and temperature\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says learners should complete a table of festivals with \'dates and time\'.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the 1st day of a month is a Sunday, what will be the date of the next Sunday?\",\"options\":[\"7th\",\"8th\",\"2nd\",\"9th\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since a week has 7 days, adding 7 to the 1st gives the 8th as the next Sunday.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If your birthday falls on the 10th of the month and it is a Wednesday, what day will the 17th of that same month be?\",\"options\":[\"Tuesday\",\"Thursday\",\"Wednesday\",\"Friday\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Adding 7 days to the 10th (Wednesday) results in the 17th, which will be the same day (Wednesday).\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the 15th day of the month is a Monday, which of these dates will also fall on a Monday?\",\"options\":[\"22nd\",\"20th\",\"16th\",\"25th\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Dates falling on the same day occur every 7 days; 15 + 7 = 22.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it important for students to look at the calendar according to the teacher\'s note?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to draw boxes\",\"To get information about the days of the month and week\",\"To practice their handwriting\",\"To count how many friends they have\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states students should be motivated to look at the calendar to get information about the days of the month and week.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To complete a 1-year table of festivals as instructed, how many monthly calendars must be prepared first?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"7\",\"12\",\"30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A full year consists of 12 months, so a 12-month calendar is needed for a 1-year table.\",\"topic\":\"Calendar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Whom should you discuss with to find out and write your exact age in the box?\",\"options\":[\"Friends\",\"Parents\",\"Neighbors\",\"Classmates\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly asks to \'Discuss with your parents and write the exact age\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these family members\' present age is NOT asked to be written in the boxes according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Mother\",\"Father\",\"Grandmother\",\"Brother\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists mother, father, grandmother, and grandfather, but not brother.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Whose date of birth is mentioned to be written in the table along with family members?\",\"options\":[\"Teacher\'s date of birth\",\"My friend\'s date of birth\",\"Grandfather\'s date of birth\",\"Grandmother\'s date of birth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table completion section specifically includes \'My friend\'s date of birth\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the term \'present age\' mean in the context of this topic?\",\"options\":[\"Age at the time of birth\",\"Age 3 years ago\",\"Age today\",\"Age after 7 years\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Present age refers to the current age or \'age today\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which box is used to show the age of the boy at the current moment?\",\"options\":[\"The first box (3 years ago)\",\"The middle box (My age today)\",\"The last box (After 7 years)\",\"The box for date of birth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The middle box in the figure is labeled \'My age today is\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/129_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to find your age 3 years ago, what calculation should you do?\",\"options\":[\"Add 3 to your age today\",\"Subtract 3 from your age today\",\"Multiply your age today by 3\",\"Divide your age today by 3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"To find an age in the past, we subtract the number of years from the current age.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child\'s age today is 9 years, what was their age 3 years ago?\",\"options\":[\"12 years\",\"6 years\",\"3 years\",\"9 years\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"9 minus 3 equals 6.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a child\'s age today is 8 years, what will be their age after 7 years?\",\"options\":[\"1 year\",\"15 years\",\"7 years\",\"8 years\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"8 plus 7 equals 15.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if the boy writes \'10\' in the middle box (My age today), what number should he write in the last box (after 7 years)?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"7\",\"17\",\"13\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"If today is 10, then after 7 years it will be 10 + 7 = 17.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/129_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If your grandmother\'s present age is 70 years and she was 62 years old when you were born, how old are you today?\",\"options\":[\"8 years\",\"70 years\",\"62 years\",\"10 years\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The difference between her current age and her age at your birth (70 - 62) gives your current age.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If your father\'s date of birth is in the year 1980 and your date of birth is in 2015, what does the difference between these years represent?\",\"options\":[\"Your father\'s present age\",\"Your father\'s age when you were born\",\"Your age today\",\"Your friend\'s age\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The difference between the parent\'s birth year and the child\'s birth year is the parent\'s age at the time of the child\'s birth.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which information is required to calculate \'My grandmother\'s age at the time of my birth\'?\",\"options\":[\"Only my grandmother\'s present age\",\"Only my date of birth\",\"My grandmother\'s present age and my present age\",\"My friend\'s date of birth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Subtracting the child\'s current age from the grandmother\'s current age gives her age at the child\'s birth.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Age\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should we read on packed items like food, drinks, and medicines?\",\"options\":[\"The color of the packet\",\"The printed information\",\"The name of the shopkeeper\",\"The delivery address\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states we should read the printed information on packed items used in daily life.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the \'Manufacturing date\' of an item tell us?\",\"options\":[\"The date the item was sold\",\"The date the item was made\",\"The price of the item\",\"The weight of the item\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Manufacturing date refers to the date when the item was produced or made.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"While purchasing a packed item, which two dates are important to check according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Today\'s date and Yesterday\'s date\",\"Manufacturing date and Expiry date\",\"Price and Weight\",\"Sr. No and Name of the item\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions discussing the manufacturing date and the date up to which the item can be used (expiry date) while purchasing.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The \'Expiry date\' on a medicine bottle indicates the date _______.\",\"options\":[\"the item was first packed\",\"the item was bought from the shop\",\"up to which that item can be used\",\"the item was delivered to the house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the expiry information as the date up to which that item can be used.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher\'s note, which tool should be used to find information about festivals, moonrise, and constellations?\",\"options\":[\"A clock\",\"A ruler\",\"A calendar\",\"A weighing scale\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using the calendar to give information about festivals, celebrations, moonrise, constellations, etc.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides dates and price, what other information is listed in the activity table for packed items?\",\"options\":[\"Shop address\",\"Weight\\/Capacity\",\"Weather report\",\"School name\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table headers include Weight\\/Capacity as one of the details to be recorded.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which column is meant for recording the name of the food or drink item?\",\"options\":[\"Sr. No\",\"Name of the item\",\"Price\",\"Weight\\/Capacity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The second column in the table is specifically titled \'Name of the item\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/130_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many total columns are provided in the table to record information about an item?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"6\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table has 6 columns: Sr. No, Name of the item, Manufacturing date, Expiry date, Price, and Weight\\/Capacity.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/130_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it necessary to complete the table shown in the text when studying packed items?\",\"options\":[\"To practice drawing straight lines\",\"To organize and compare important safety and cost information\",\"To calculate the total number of items in the shop\",\"To list the names of all the students in the class\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Completing the table helps students organize information like expiry dates and price for better understanding.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If a milk packet shows an \'Expiry date\' that has already passed, what should a student conclude?\",\"options\":[\"The milk is very fresh\",\"The milk is now cheaper\",\"The milk should not be used\",\"The milk was made today\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since the expiry date is the date up to which an item can be used, a passed date means it is no longer safe to use.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21462,13,3,'Maths','en','Patterns','[\"Patterns repeat in a regular way using shapes, numbers, or colours.\",\"ABC pattern means three different items repeating in order.\",\"AAB pattern means first two items same, third different.\",\"ABB pattern means first item different, next two same.\",\"Number patterns increase or decrease by a fixed amount.\",\"Shape patterns can be made using circles, triangles, squares.\",\"Tiling means covering a surface with shapes without gaps or overlaps.\",\"Folding and cutting paper can create symmetrical patterns.\",\"Patterns in tables show regular changes in digits, like units place.\",\"Selecting two items from three gives three possible pairs (order doesn’t matter).\",\"Arranging three different items in a line gives six possible orders.\",\"Passwords using three different digits once each have 3×2×1 = 6 possibilities.\",\"Combination is selection where order does not matter.\",\"Permutation is arrangement where order matters.\",\"Observe patterns in daily life like floors, sarees, tiles, and calendars.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the pattern of digits in the units place in the table of 5?\",\"options\":[\"5, 0, 5, 0...\",\"1, 2, 3, 4...\",\"5, 5, 5, 5...\",\"0, 0, 0, 0...\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows the units place pattern for the table of 5 as 5, 0, 5, 0...\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where are students encouraged to observe the use of tiling in their daily life?\",\"options\":[\"On the windows\",\"On the ceilings\",\"On the floors\",\"On the doors\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note mentions observing tiling on floors at home and in school premises.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the pattern of the table of 5, which digit follows 0 in the units place?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"5\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The pattern alternates between 5 and 0, so 5 follows 0.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which group of three numbers is highlighted in a horizontal box?\",\"options\":[\"(10, 11, 12)\",\"(4, 11, 18)\",\"(5, 11, 17)\",\"(6, 13, 20)\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the numbers 4, 11, and 18 enclosed in a horizontal rectangle.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/135_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the sum of the numbers in the groups (5, 11, 17) and (10, 11, 12) as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"22\",\"30\",\"33\",\"40\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that adding these numbers horizontally, vertically, and diagonally gives the answer 33.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you continue the units place pattern 5, 0, 5, 0, what will be the next two digits?\",\"options\":[\"5, 5\",\"0, 0\",\"5, 0\",\"0, 5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The pattern repeats the sequence 5 then 0.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is used to help draw the different shapes like squares and triangles?\",\"options\":[\"Lines only\",\"Dots\",\"Numbers\",\"Colors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows shapes being completed using a grid of dots.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/135_104.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, in which directions can a pattern be formed in the calendar to get the same sum?\",\"options\":[\"Only horizontally\",\"Only vertically\",\"Only diagonally\",\"Horizontally, vertically, and diagonally\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions patterns formed by adding numbers horizontally, vertically, and diagonally.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of numbers from the calendar example has the same sum as (4, 11, 18)?\",\"options\":[\"(1, 8, 15)\",\"(5, 11, 17)\",\"(7, 14, 21)\",\"(2, 9, 16)\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies (5, 11, 17), (4, 11, 18), and (10, 11, 12) as groups having the same sum of 33.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the common number present in all three groups (5, 11, 17), (4, 11, 18), and (10, 11, 12)?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"18\",\"11\",\"12\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"By looking at the sets provided in the text, the number 11 appears in every group.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Besides calendars, what does the teacher suggest using to encourage students to make patterns?\",\"options\":[\"Stones\",\"Dots\",\"Leaves\",\"Books\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note suggests using dots and calendars to encourage making patterns.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a pattern is formed by adding numbers in a group of three and the sum is always 33, what does this represent?\",\"options\":[\"A multiplication table\",\"A pattern of groups with the same sum\",\"A subtraction rule\",\"A list of random numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes this as finding a pattern of groups of three numbers that have the same sum.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s do it\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many different types of fruits were in the basket when Ramesh came home?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions three fruits: guava, apple, and chikoo.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these fruits was NOT mentioned in the basket?\",\"options\":[\"Guava\",\"Apple\",\"Mango\",\"Chikoo\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The basket contained guava, apple, and chikoo; mango is not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many fruits did Ramesh\'s mother ask him to choose?\",\"options\":[\"Any one fruit\",\"Any two fruits\",\"All three fruits\",\"None of the fruits\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"His mother asked Ramesh to choose any two fruits.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Ramesh chooses a pair of fruits, how many fruits will he have in his hand?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A pair consists of two fruits as requested by his mother.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a valid pair Ramesh could choose according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Apple and Orange\",\"Guava and Banana\",\"Guava and Chikoo\",\"Chikoo and Papaya\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Guava and Chikoo are both listed as fruits available in the basket.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many different combinations of two fruits are listed in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists three combinations: Apple-Guava, Apple-Chikoo, and Guava-Chikoo.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to instruction (4), what should you do after completing the design?\",\"options\":[\"Erase it\",\"Give it to Ramesh\",\"Colour it with your choice of colours\",\"Draw a fruit next to it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Instruction (4) says to \'Colour it with the colours of your choice.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If Ramesh has already picked an Apple, which other fruit can he pick to complete a pair?\",\"options\":[\"Only Guava\",\"Only Chikoo\",\"Either Guava or Chikoo\",\"Only another Apple\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ramesh can pair the Apple with either of the other two fruits: Guava or Chikoo.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why are \'Apple Guava\' and \'Guava Apple\' considered the same combination in this context?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are the same two fruits\",\"Because Ramesh is not hungry\",\"Because there are only three fruits\",\"Because the mother said so\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In combinations of pairs, the order does not change the set of fruits chosen.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal of instruction (5) in the text?\",\"options\":[\"To eat the fruits\",\"To name the fruits\",\"To create different patterns using given colours\",\"To count the number of baskets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Instruction (5) explicitly asks to \'Create different patterns using the given colours\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Observe\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the concept called where the \'selection\' matters and not the \'order\'?\",\"options\":[\"Addition\",\"Combination\",\"Multiplication\",\"Subtraction\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when selection matters and not the order, the concept is known as \'Combination\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, we have already seen how to obtain various patterns using which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"Numbers\",\"Shapes\",\"Letters\",\"Colors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins by mentioning, \'We have seen how to obtain various patterns using shapes.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the concept of \'Combination\', which of these is NOT important?\",\"options\":[\"The selection\",\"The games chosen\",\"The order\",\"The conditions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note explains that in combination, the \'selection\' matters and not the \'order\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many total games are available for the students to choose from?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows three games: Badminton, Cycling, and Cricket.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/136_104.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many different pairs of games have been formed from the three options?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows three distinct pairs: Badminton-Cricket, Cycling-Cricket, and Badminton-Cycling.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"13\\/136_105.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a student chooses \'Cycling and Cricket\', which other choice is considered the same combination?\",\"options\":[\"Badminton and Cycling\",\"Cricket and Cycling\",\"Badminton and Cricket\",\"Cricket and Kabaddi\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since order does not matter in a combination, \'Cycling and Cricket\' is the same as \'Cricket and Cycling\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which new game does the text suggest adding to the list to practice finding pairs?\",\"options\":[\"Football\",\"Hockey\",\"Kabaddi\",\"Tennis\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks, \'If Kabaddi had been included... in how many ways can two games be selected?\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When creating patterns as per the text, what determines the order of the pattern?\",\"options\":[\"The size of shapes\",\"Determining order or given conditions\",\"The color of the games\",\"The number of students\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions creating patterns by \'determining their order or according to given conditions\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If there are 4 games (Badminton, Cycling, Cricket, and Kabaddi), in how many ways can two games be selected?\",\"options\":[\"4 ways\",\"5 ways\",\"6 ways\",\"8 ways\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"With 4 items, the pairs are (1,2), (1,3), (1,4), (2,3), (2,4), and (3,4), totaling 6 ways.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If you must register for \'any two games\' out of the three shown, which of these is a correct selection?\",\"options\":[\"Badminton only\",\"All three games\",\"Badminton and Cycling\",\"Cycling only\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instruction is to register for \'any two games\', so selecting two like Badminton and Cycling is correct.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the pair \'Badminton and Cycling\' the same as \'Cycling and Badminton\' in this lesson?\",\"options\":[\"Because the order matters\",\"Because the selection of games is the same\",\"Because they are both played outdoors\",\"Because they start with the same letter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In a combination, the selection is what matters, not the order in which they are picked.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many games is a student required to select from the options provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text and figure explicitly say \'Register for any two games\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Understand: Combination\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the concept called where the order of objects is important?\",\"options\":[\"Addition\",\"Permutation\",\"Subtraction\",\"Multiplication\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the concept where order is important is known as \'Permutation\'.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is formed if the sequence in which objects are arranged is altered?\",\"options\":[\"A distinct arrangement\",\"The same design\",\"A pair of objects\",\"A single shape\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says if the sequence is altered, a distinct arrangement or configuration is formed.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how are objects arranged in a permutation?\",\"options\":[\"In any random way\",\"Without any sequence\",\"In a specific order\",\"Only in pairs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions exploring how objects can be arranged in a specific order.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What have we observed before learning about how objects are arranged in a specific order?\",\"options\":[\"How shapes are colored\",\"How pairs are formed\",\"How numbers are added\",\"How lines are drawn\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins by stating we have observed how pairs are formed by selecting from given objects.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of making a toran, what does \'altering the sequence\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Changing the color of shapes\",\"Using the same shape twice\",\"Changing the order of the shapes\",\"Removing all the shapes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Altering the sequence refers to changing the order in which the objects are placed.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you use three distinct shapes, is it possible to make different designs?\",\"options\":[\"No, only one design is possible\",\"Yes, by changing their order\",\"No, shapes cannot be moved\",\"Yes, but only if we add more shapes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests thinking about making different designs using three distinct shapes by changing the sequence.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'distinct\' mean when talking about shapes in a toran?\",\"options\":[\"Different types\",\"Exactly the same\",\"Very small\",\"Circular\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Distinct shapes refer to different or unique types of shapes used in the arrangement.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the \'order\' considered important in a permutation?\",\"options\":[\"Because it makes the shapes bigger\",\"Because it changes the number of shapes\",\"Because changing it creates a new configuration\",\"Because it is easier to count\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that if the sequence is altered, a distinct configuration is formed, making order important.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you have a triangle, a circle, and a square, and you change their positions, what are you creating?\",\"options\":[\"A new pair\",\"A permutation\",\"A single shape\",\"A subtraction\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Changing the sequence of objects to form a new arrangement is the concept of permutation.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student makes a toran with a star, then a moon, and then a sun, how can they make a \'distinct arrangement\'?\",\"options\":[\"By using the exact same order\",\"By changing the order to moon, sun, then star\",\"By keeping the star in the first place only\",\"By not changing anything\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Altering the sequence (changing the order) creates a distinct arrangement.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main difference between just \'selecting pairs\' and \'permutation\'?\",\"options\":[\"Permutation uses no objects\",\"Permutation requires a specific order\",\"Selecting pairs is always decorative\",\"There is no difference\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text contrasts selecting pairs with arranging objects in a specific order (permutation).\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If the sequence of shapes in a decorative toran is NOT altered, what happens to the arrangement?\",\"options\":[\"It becomes a new permutation\",\"It stays the same configuration\",\"It becomes a distinct design\",\"It becomes a pair\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since a distinct arrangement is formed only if the sequence is altered, it stays the same if the sequence is not changed.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Discuss\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21463,14,3,'Maths','mr','सभोवताली शोधू आकार','[\"तीन अंकी संख्येतील शतक, दशक, एकक स्थानांची किंमत ओळखा.\",\"शतकस्थानाचे अंक 100 गुना, दशकस्थानाचे अंक 10 गुना, एककस्थानाचे अंक 1 गुना वाढवते.\",\"संख्येचे विस्तारित रूप म्हणजे प्रत्येक अंकाची स्थानिक किंमत जोडणे.\",\"उदा: ४७५ = ४०० + ७० + ५.\",\"दर्शनी किंमत म्हणजे अंकाची स्वयंची किंमत (जसे ४७५ मध्ये ७ ची दर्शनी किंमत ७).\",\"स्थानिक किंमत म्हणजे अंकाची ठिकाणी आधारित किंमत (जसे ४७५ मध्ये ७ ची स्थानिक किंमत ७०).\",\"शून्यची दर्शनी किंमत व स्थानिक किंमत सदैव शून्य असते.\",\"तीन अंकी संख्यांची तुलना करण्यास शतकपहिले पाहावे, नंतर दशक, नंतर एकक.\",\"शतक समान असल्यास दशक तुलना करा, दशक समान असल्यास एकक तुलना करा.\",\"वृद्धी क्रम म्हणजे लहानपासून मोठ्यापर्यंत, घटते क्रम म्हणजे मोठ्यापासून लहानपर्यंत.\",\"तीन अंकी सर्व लहान संख्या १००, सर्व मोठी संख्या ९९९.\",\"तीन अंकी संख्या तयार करताना अंक दोन वेळा वापरता येत नाही.\",\"एकांक, दहा, शंभर यांचे प्रतीक क्रमशः ए, द, श असतात.\",\"अंकी रूप व अक्षरी रूपांत रूपांतरण करा (उदा: २३५ = दोनशे पन्नास).\",\"विस्तारित रूपात संख्या लिहताना शून्य ठेवणे आवश्यक नाही.\"]','[{\"q\":\"मला एकही कोपरा नाही आणि एकही कडा नाही. फक्त एक वक्र पृष्ठ आहे. मी कोण?\",\"options\":[\"इष्टिकाचिती\",\"शंकू\",\"गोल\",\"दंडगोल\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"गोलाला कोपरा आणि कडा नसते, फक्त एक वक्र पृष्ठ असते.\",\"topic\":\"आठवा व ओळखा\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"ज्या आकाराला एक कोपरा, एक वक्र पृष्ठ आणि एक सपाट पृष्ठ असते, त्या आकाराला काय म्हणतात?\",\"options\":[\"शंकू\",\"गोल\",\"इष्टिकाचिती\",\"दंडगोल\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"शंकूला एक कोपरा आणि एक सपाट पृष्ठ असते.\",\"topic\":\"आठवा व ओळखा\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"मला दोन वक्र कडा आणि एक वक्र पृष्ठ आहे, पण एकही कोपरा नाही. मी कोण?\",\"options\":[\"गोल\",\"दंडगोल\",\"शंकू\",\"इष्टिकाचिती\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"दंडगोलाला दोन वक्र कडा असतात आणि कोपरा नसतो.\",\"topic\":\"आठवा व ओळखा\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या सारणीनुसार, पहिल्या चित्रातील भेटवस्तूच्या (Gift box) आकाराचे नाव काय आहे?\",\"options\":[\"शंकू\",\"गोल\",\"इष्टिकाचिती\",\"दंडगोल\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"सारणीत भेटवस्तूच्या आकाराचे नाव इष्टिकाचिती दिले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"आठवा व ओळखा\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"14\\/013_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"वाढदिवसाच्या टोपीचा आकार खालीलपैकी कोणत्या भौमितिक आकाराशी जुळतो?\",\"options\":[\"इष्टिकाचिती\",\"दंडगोल\",\"गोल\",\"शंकू\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"वाढदिवसाची टोपी शंकूच्या आकाराची असते.\",\"topic\":\"आठवा व ओळखा\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात, टेबलावर असलेल्या केकचा आकार कोणता आहे?\",\"options\":[\"दंडगोल\",\"शंकू\",\"गोल\",\"इष्टिकाचिती\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"चित्रातील केकचा आकार दंडगोलाकार आहे.\",\"topic\":\"आठवा व ओळखा\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"14\\/013_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"चेंडूचा आकार कोणत्या भौमितिक आकाराचे उदाहरण आहे?\",\"options\":[\"दंडगोल\",\"गोल\",\"शंकू\",\"इष्टिकाचिती\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"चेंडू हा गोल आकाराचा असतो.\",\"topic\":\"आठवा व ओळखा\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या सारणीत, रंगीत ठोकळ्याच्या (Rubik\'s cube) समोर रिकाम्या जागी कोणता आकार येईल?\",\"options\":[\"इष्टिकाचिती\",\"घन\",\"शंकू\",\"गोल\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"रंगीत ठोकळा हा घन आकाराचा असतो.\",\"topic\":\"आठवा व ओळखा\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"14\\/013_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"जर एखाद्या वस्तूचे पृष्ठभाग पूर्णपणे वक्र असेल आणि तिला एकही कडा नसेल, तर ती वस्तू खालीलपैकी कोणती असू शकते?\",\"options\":[\"विटा\",\"आईस्क्रीमचा कोन\",\"चेंडू\",\"पाण्याचा पिंप\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"चेंडू (गोल) याला कडा नसते आणि पृष्ठभाग वक्र असतो.\",\"topic\":\"आठवा व ओळखा\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"इष्टिकाचिती आणि दंडगोल यांमध्ये कोणता मुख्य फरक आहे?\",\"options\":[\"इष्टिकाचितीला कोपरे असतात, दंडगोलाला नसतात\",\"दंडगोलाला कोपरे असतात, इष्टिकाचितीला नसतात\",\"दोघांनाही कोपरे नसतात\",\"दोघांनाही वक्र कडा असतात\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"इष्टिकाचितीला कोपरे असतात, तर दंडगोलाला एकही कोपरा नसतो.\",\"topic\":\"आठवा व ओळखा\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"इष्टिकाचिती आकाराच्या खोक्याला किती कडा असतात?\",\"options\":[\"६\",\"८\",\"१०\",\"१२\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"पाठ्यपुस्तकातील मजकुरानुसार, इष्टिकाचिती आकाराच्या खोक्याला १२ कडा असतात.\",\"topic\":\"इष्टिकाचिती व घडणी\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"इष्टिकाचिती आकाराच्या खोक्याला किती कोपरे असतात?\",\"options\":[\"४\",\"६\",\"८\",\"१२\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"पाठ्यपुस्तकात नमूद केल्याप्रमाणे इष्टिकाचितीला ८ कोपरे असतात.\",\"topic\":\"इष्टिकाचिती व घडणी\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"इष्टिकाचिती आकाराच्या खोक्याला किती पृष्ठे दिसतात?\",\"options\":[\"६\",\"८\",\"१०\",\"१२\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"इष्टिकाचिती आकाराच्या खोक्याला ६ पृष्ठे असतात.\",\"topic\":\"इष्टिकाचिती व घडणी\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"ज्या आकारापासून खोका तयार होतो, त्या आकाराला काय म्हणतात?\",\"options\":[\"कडा\",\"कोपरा\",\"घडणी\",\"पृष्ठ\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"ज्या आकारापासून खोका तयार होतो, त्या आकाराला खोक्याची घडणी म्हणतात.\",\"topic\":\"इष्टिकाचिती व घडणी\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"खोका उलगडून पाहिल्यामुळे आपल्याला कोणती गोष्ट समजते?\",\"options\":[\"खोका कसा तयार झाला\",\"खोक्याचे वजन किती आहे\",\"खोक्याची किंमत किती आहे\",\"खोक्याचा रंग कोणता आहे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"खोका उलगडून पाहिल्यामुळे तो कसा तयार झाला हे आपल्याला कळते.\",\"topic\":\"इष्टिकाचिती व घडणी\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"इष्टिकाचितीची घडणी वापरून आपण खालीलपैकी काय तयार करू शकतो?\",\"options\":[\"चेंडू\",\"खोका\",\"टोपी\",\"केक\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"घडणीचा वापर करून आपण त्या आकाराचा खोका तयार करू शकतो.\",\"topic\":\"इष्टिकाचिती व घडणी\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"एका इष्टिकाचितीच्या कडा (१२) आणि पृष्ठे (६) यांची एकूण बेरीज किती होईल?\",\"options\":[\"१४\",\"१८\",\"२०\",\"२६\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"१२ कडा + ६ पृष्ठे = १८.\",\"topic\":\"इष्टिकाचिती व घडणी\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात मुलगा जो भेटवस्तूचा खोका उघडत आहे, त्याचा आकार कोणता आहे?\",\"options\":[\"गोल\",\"त्रिकोण\",\"इष्टिकाचिती\",\"शंकू\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"चित्रातील भेटवस्तूचा खोका इष्टिकाचिती आकाराचा आहे.\",\"topic\":\"इष्टिकाचिती व घडणी\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"14\\/014_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रातील टेबलावर ठेवलेल्या लहान गुलाबी रंगाच्या भेटवस्तूच्या खोक्याला किती कोपरे आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"६\",\"८\",\"१०\",\"१२\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"गुलाबी खोका इष्टिकाचिती आकाराचा असल्याने त्याला ८ कोपरे आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"इष्टिकाचिती व घडणी\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"14\\/014_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"एखादा इष्टिकाचिती आकाराचा खोका पूर्णपणे उलगडल्यास आपल्याला काय मिळते?\",\"options\":[\"खोक्याची घडणी\",\"एक गोल चेंडू\",\"एक लांब काठी\",\"एक त्रिकोणी टोपी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"खोका उलगडल्यावर मिळणाऱ्या आकाराला त्याची घडणी म्हणतात.\",\"topic\":\"इष्टिकाचिती व घडणी\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"पाठ्यपुस्तकातील माहितीनुसार, झाडाचा बुंधा हा कोणत्या आकाराचे उदाहरण आहे?\",\"options\":[\"इष्टिकाचिती\",\"शंकू\",\"घन\",\"दंडगोल\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी दिलेल्या टीपमध्ये झाडाचा बुंधा हे दंडगोल आकाराचे उदाहरण म्हणून दिले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"त्रिमितीय आकार व घडणी\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"त्रिमितीय आकारांची खोकी उलगडून दाखवल्यावर काय तयार होते?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त चौरस\",\"घडणी\",\"वर्तुळ\",\"त्रिकोण\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"खोकी उलगडून दाखवल्यावर त्यांच्या घडणी कशा असतात हे समजते.\",\"topic\":\"त्रिमितीय आकार व घडणी\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रातील घडणीचा उपयोग करून कोणता त्रिमितीय आकार बनवला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"शंकू\",\"दंडगोल\",\"इष्टिकाचिती\",\"घन\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"चित्रात दाखवलेली घडणी इष्टिकाचिती तयार करण्यासाठी वापरली जाते.\",\"topic\":\"त्रिमितीय आकार व घडणी\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"14\\/015_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"सूर्यमालेतील ग्रह हे कोणत्या प्रकारचे आकार आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"द्विमितीय आकार\",\"त्रिमितीय आकार\",\"सरळ रेषा\",\"कोन\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पाठ्यपुस्तकानुसार सूर्यमालेतील ग्रह हे परिसरात आढळणारे त्रिमितीय आकार आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"त्रिमितीय आकार व घडणी\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},