":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"जिंजीचा किल्ला सध्या भारताच्या कोणत्या राज्यात आहे?\",\"options\":[\"महाराष्ट्र\",\"तमिळनाडू\",\"कर्नाटक\",\"आंध्र प्रदेश\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात स्पष्ट दिले आहे की जिंजीचा किल्ला सध्याच्या तमिळनाडू राज्यात आहे.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"स्वराज्यातील आंबे आणि फणस यांसारखी झाडे तोडण्यास महाराजांनी का मनाई केली?\",\"options\":[\"ती झाडे खूप उंच असतात म्हणून\",\"त्या झाडांचे लाकूड कमकुवत असते म्हणून\",\"ती झाडे प्रजेने लेकरांसारखी जतन करून वाढवलेली असतात म्हणून\",\"त्या झाडांपासून सावली मिळत नाही म्हणून\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"ही झाडे रयतेने लेकरांसारखी बहुत काल जतन करून वाढविलेली असतात, म्हणून त्यांना तोडू नये असे महाराजांचे धोरण होते.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"जर एखादे झाड खूप जीर्ण झाले असेल आणि ते तोडणे आवश्यक असेल, तर काय करावे असे आज्ञापत्रात म्हटले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"मालकास राजी करून व द्रव्य देऊन तोडून न्यावे\",\"मालकाला न सांगता गुपचूप तोडावे\",\"सरकारी आदेश काढून जबरदस्तीने तोडावे\",\"ते झाड तसेच वाळून जाईपर्यंत थांबावे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"जीर्ण झाड तोडताना त्याच्या धन्यास राजी करून आणि द्रव्य (पैसे) देऊन त्याच्या संतोषाने तोडावे, असा नियम होता.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"आरमारासाठी लाकूड हवे असल्यास आणि ते स्वराज्यात उपलब्ध नसल्यास कोणता मार्ग अवलंबण्यास सांगितले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"आंबे-फणसाची झाडे तोडावीत\",\"शेतातील झाडे तोडावीत\",\"जंगलात आग लावून लाकूड मिळवावे\",\"परमुल्कीहून (दुसऱ्या देशातून) खरेदी करून आणावे\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"स्वराज्यातील फळझाडांना हात न लावता, आवश्यक लाकूड परमुल्कीहून खरेदी करून आणण्यास सांगितले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"राजाराम महाराज मुघलांच्या वेढ्यात असूनही जिंजीच्या किल्ल्यावर सात वर्षे सुरक्षित राहू शकले, याचे मुख्य कारण काय?\",\"options\":[\"मुघलांकडे सैन्य कमी होते\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दूरदृष्टी ठेवून किल्ला अधिक मजबूत केला होता\",\"किल्ल्यावर खूप पाऊस पडत होता\",\"मुघलांना किल्ल्याचा रस्ता माहित नव्हता\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"महाराजांनी दूरदृष्टीने किल्ल्याचे तट व बुरुज बांधून तो मजबूत केल्यामुळेच राजाराम महाराज तिथे सुरक्षित राहिले.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"किल्ले दुर्गम कसे बनवावेत, याचे शिक्षण शिवाजी महाराजांना कोणाकडून मिळाले होते?\",\"options\":[\"रामचंद्रपंत अमात्य\",\"राजाराम महाराज\",\"शहाजीराजे\",\"बाजीप्रभू देशपांडे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात उल्लेख आहे की किल्ले दुर्गम कसे बनवावेत, याचे शिक्षण शहाजीराजांनी महाराजांना लहानपणीच दिले होते.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"राजाराम महाराजांनी मुघलांच्या वेढ्यात असताना जिंजीचा किल्ला किती काळ लढवला?\",\"options\":[\"सुमारे सात वर्षे\",\"दोन वर्षे\",\"दहा वर्षे\",\"पाच महिने\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मजकुराप्रमाणे राजाराम महाराजांनी वेढ्यात अडकूनही सुमारे सात वर्षांपर्यंत किल्ला लढवला.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"\'आज्ञापत्र\' या ग्रंथातून शिवाजी महाराजांचा कोणता दृष्टिकोन प्रामुख्याने स्पष्ट होतो?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ युद्धनीतीचा\",\"पर्यावरणासंबंधीचा\",\"केवळ व्यापाराचा\",\"केवळ शेतीचा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"दिलेल्या उताऱ्यातून महाराजांचा पर्यावरणासंबंधीचा आणि वृक्षसंवर्धनाचा दृष्टिकोन स्पष्ट होतो.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"प्रजेला दुःख देऊन केलेले कार्य केल्यास काय परिणाम होतो, असे आज्ञापत्रात म्हटले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"ते कार्य खूप यशस्वी होते\",\"ते कार्य करणाऱ्यास बक्षीस मिळते\",\"ते कार्य करणाऱ्यासह अल्पकाळातच नष्ट होते\",\"त्यामुळे राज्याची प्रगती होते\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"एकास दुःख देऊन केलेले कार्य करणाऱ्यासहित स्वत्कालचेच (लवकरच) बुडीन नाहीसेच होते, असे उताऱ्यात म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"स्वराज्यातील अरण्यात प्रामुख्याने कोणती झाडे असल्याचे उताऱ्यात म्हटले आहे, जी आरमारासाठी वापरता येतात?\",\"options\":[\"सागवानादि वृक्ष\",\"नारळाची झाडे\",\"वड आणि पिंपळ\",\"बाभळीची झाडे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"उताऱ्यात नमूद केले आहे की स्वराज्यात अरण्यात सागवानादि वृक्ष आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"झाडे तोडल्यामुळे धन्याच्या पदरी कोणता दोष पडतो?\",\"options\":[\"चोरीचा दोष\",\"आळसाचा दोष\",\"खोटेपणाचा दोष\",\"प्रजापीडणाचा दोष\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"वृक्ष तोडल्यामुळे प्रजेला दुःख होते आणि धन्याच्या पदरी प्रजापीडणाचा (प्रजेला त्रास देण्याचा) दोष पडतो.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात कोणता ऐतिहासिक किल्ला दाखवला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"किल्ले प्रतापगड\",\"किल्ले राजगड\",\"किल्ले रायगड\",\"किल्ले पन्हाळा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"चित्र क्र. १ (F1) वर स्पष्टपणे \'किल्ले राजगड\' असे नाव लिहिलेले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"18\\/089_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात जिंजी किल्ल्याचा कोणता महत्त्वाचा भाग दर्शविला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"किल्ल्याचा मुख्य दरवाजा\",\"किल्ल्याची बाजारपेठ\",\"जिंजी किल्ल्याचा बालेकिल्ला\",\"किल्ल्याचा हत्तीखाना\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"चित्र क्र. २ (F2) च्या शीर्षकात \'जिंजी किल्ल्याचा बालेकिल्ला\' असे स्पष्ट नमूद केले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"18\\/089_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"महाराजांनी झाडांची तुलना कोणाशी केली आहे?\",\"options\":[\"लेकरांशी\",\"शत्रूंशी\",\"दगडांशी\",\"केवळ लाकडाशी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"महाराजांनी झाडे ही लेकरांसारखी बहुत काल जतन करून वाढविलेली असतात, असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"आज्ञापत्रातील पर्यावरण रक्षण व जिंजी\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21508,19,4,'English','en','Back to School','[\"- Back to School is a poem about the excitement of the first day of school.\",\"- The poem talks about new clothes, books, friends and the teacher’s smile.\",\"- It mentions learning, singing, playing and having fun.\",\"- The teacher encourages us to read, write and enjoy school activities.\",\"- The poem ends with a question: \\\"How about you?\\\" to share feelings with classmates.\",\"- The chapter also includes activities like listening, repeating, naming pictures and solving riddles.\",\"- Riddles describe common school items: a bookcase, a clock, a chair and a globe.\",\"- Students are encouraged to make lists of things they receive on the first day.\",\"- The teacher’s role is to create a friendly, bright learning environment.\",\"- The poem and activities help students practice listening, speaking, reading and writing skills.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does the child cheer when the day is finally here?\",\"options\":[\"Hello!\",\"Hurray!\",\"Goodbye!\",\"Welcome!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem explicitly states, \'The day is here, I cheer, “Hurray!”\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these items is NOT mentioned as \'new\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Dress\",\"Shoes\",\"Pencil box\",\"Books\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions new dress, shoes, bag, and books, but not a pencil box.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the name of the school written on the building?\",\"options\":[\"Primary School\",\"Z. P. SCHOOL\",\"City School\",\"Model School\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sign on the building in the picture clearly says \'Z. P. SCHOOL\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/011_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How does everyone look on this brand new day according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Tired and sleepy\",\"Sad and lonely\",\"Happy and joyful\",\"Angry and loud\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Happy and joyful, Everyone looks!\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How is the teacher\'s smile described in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Cold and scary\",\"Warm and bright\",\"Sad and dark\",\"Funny and loud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'My teacher’s smile, Feels warm and bright\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the children carrying that shows they are going to school?\",\"options\":[\"Lunch boxes and water bottles\",\"School bags and books\",\"Toys and games\",\"Umbrellas and raincoats\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows children wearing school bags and two of them are holding books.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/011_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, which pair of activities will the children do together?\",\"options\":[\"Sleep and dream\",\"Read and write\",\"Cook and eat\",\"Fight and shout\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'We’ll read and write, We’ll sing and play.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, how will the children learn new things?\",\"options\":[\"In boring ways\",\"In fun-filled ways\",\"In difficult ways\",\"In quiet ways\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'We’ll learn new things, In fun-filled ways!\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The poem says \'Old friends to meet, And new ones too.\' What does this imply about the first day of school?\",\"options\":[\"The child is leaving all their friends.\",\"The child will see both familiar and new people.\",\"The child is moving to a new city.\",\"The child has no friends at all.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Meeting old and new friends implies a mix of familiar faces and new acquaintances.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the child say \'I am feeling great!\' in the context of the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is a holiday.\",\"Because they are excited to go back to school.\",\"Because they are going to the market.\",\"Because they are going to sleep.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The entire poem expresses excitement about the new school day, new things, and meeting friends.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list \'together, delight, hurray, warm, bright, cheer\' is used to express excitement?\",\"options\":[\"together\",\"delight\",\"hurray\",\"bright\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'hurray\' is an exclamation used to express joy or excitement.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What activity are you asked to do regarding the first day of school?\",\"options\":[\"Sing a song\",\"Make a list of things you get\",\"Draw a picture of the school\",\"Play a game with friends\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks students to \'Make a list of things you get on the first day of school.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if you want to measure a straight line, which circled word would you use?\",\"options\":[\"Pencil\",\"Ruler\",\"Sharpener\",\"Pen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'ruler\' is circled in the last column of the grid and is used for measuring.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/012_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list \'together, delight, hurray, warm, bright, cheer\' means \'shining\'?\",\"options\":[\"warm\",\"bright\",\"cheer\",\"together\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'bright\' is a synonym for shining or full of light.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list \'together, delight, hurray, warm, bright, cheer\' has the most letters?\",\"options\":[\"delight\",\"hurray\",\"together\",\"bright\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'together\' has 8 letters, which is more than the other words in the list.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which action is shown in the fourth picture of the first row?\",\"options\":[\"Eating\",\"Drawing\",\"Singing\",\"Crying\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The fourth picture in the first row shows a boy wearing headphones and holding a microphone to sing.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/012_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these items found in the grid is used to sharpen a pencil?\",\"options\":[\"Ruler\",\"Eraser\",\"Sharpener\",\"Chart\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'sharpener\' is found in the last row of the grid and is used to sharpen pencils.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list \'together, delight, hurray, warm, bright, cheer\' is a synonym for \'joy\'?\",\"options\":[\"warm\",\"bright\",\"delight\",\"together\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Delight\' means a high degree of pleasure or joy.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is found in the very last row of the grid?\",\"options\":[\"pencil\",\"chart\",\"ruler\",\"sharpener\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The last row of the grid contains the letters s-h-a-r-p-e-n-e-r.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to section \'e\', what should you do after looking at the pictures?\",\"options\":[\"Color them\",\"Name the actions\",\"Cut them out\",\"Count them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instruction in section \'e\' is \'Look at the pictures and name the actions.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is big and flat, hangs on the wall, and is used by the teacher to write for everyone?\",\"options\":[\"A calendar\",\"A clock\",\"A blackboard\",\"A globe\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the object that is big, flat, hangs on the wall, and is written on by the teacher is the blackboard.\",\"topic\":\"Riddles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how does the calendar help a student?\",\"options\":[\"It helps you to sit down\",\"It helps you to plan in many ways\",\"It helps you to draw oceans\",\"It helps you to write lessons\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the calendar helps you to plan in many ways by showing months and days.\",\"topic\":\"Riddles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which object has four legs but cannot run and is used for sitting?\",\"options\":[\"A desk\",\"A clock\",\"A chair\",\"A blackboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the chair as having four legs but not running, and being used to sit on when lessons begin.\",\"topic\":\"Riddles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to see the countries and oceans of the Earth, which object should you look at?\",\"options\":[\"A calendar\",\"A globe\",\"A clock\",\"A blackboard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the globe is round like a ball and shows Earth\'s countries and oceans.\",\"topic\":\"Riddles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What sound does the clock make all day long according to the riddle?\",\"options\":[\"Ding-dong\",\"Tick-tock\",\"Ring-ring\",\"Click-clack\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions the clock goes \'tick-tock\' the whole day long.\",\"topic\":\"Riddles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The riddle says the clock has two hands but never does what?\",\"options\":[\"Wave\",\"Write\",\"Clap\",\"Hold books\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the clock has two hands but never claps.\",\"topic\":\"Riddles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which object is described as standing on four legs and holding books?\",\"options\":[\"A chair\",\"A desk\",\"A globe\",\"A calendar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions an object that stands on four legs and holds the books, which refers to a desk.\",\"topic\":\"Riddles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what must you do to the calendar to see the dates?\",\"options\":[\"Write on it\",\"Hang it up\",\"Flip its pages\",\"Spin it around\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Flip my pages, date by date\' to see what is early or late.\",\"topic\":\"Riddles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main difference between the shape of the blackboard and the globe as described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The blackboard is round and the globe is flat\",\"The blackboard is flat and the globe is round like a ball\",\"The blackboard has legs and the globe hangs on the wall\",\"The blackboard shows oceans and the globe shows dates\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the blackboard as flat and the globe as round like a ball.\",\"topic\":\"Riddles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the riddles, which two objects are mentioned to have \'legs\'?\",\"options\":[\"The clock and the globe\",\"The blackboard and the calendar\",\"The chair and the desk\",\"The teacher and the student\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the chair has four legs and the desk stands on four legs.\",\"topic\":\"Riddles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21509,19,4,'English','en','Conversation Starters','[\"- Conversation starters are simple questions that help people start talking.\",\"- They can be about festivals, weather, games, colours, birthdays, vacations, and more.\",\"- Good starters are short, clear, and invite a reply.\",\"- Use friendly words like \\\"What\\\", \\\"How\\\", \\\"Which\\\", \\\"Do you\\\".\",\"- Practice by asking a friend or family member.\",\"- You can also make statements that invite answers, e.g. \\\"I like the colour blue.\\\"\",\"- Use transitional words (next, finally, because) to connect ideas.\",\"- Remember to listen carefully to the other person’s answer.\",\"- Repeat what you heard to show you understand.\",\"- Conversation starters help build confidence in speaking English.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these is the first topic suggested for a conversation in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Weather\",\"Birthdays\",\"Vacation\",\"Games\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text begins with the topic \'Let’s talk about weather!\'\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Under which topic should you talk about the \'best gift\' you have received?\",\"options\":[\"Festivals\",\"Birthdays\",\"Vacation\",\"Colours\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The question about the best gift is listed under the \'Let’s talk about birthdays!\' section.\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What specific object are you asked to talk about under the topic of \'Colours\'?\",\"options\":[\"A rainbow\",\"A painting\",\"Our national flag\",\"Your school uniform\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly asks to \'Talk about our national flag\' under the colours topic.\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which topic includes a discussion about \'indoor and outdoor\' activities?\",\"options\":[\"Weather\",\"Vacation\",\"Games\",\"Festivals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests talking about \'indoor and outdoor games of your liking\' under the games topic.\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are describing the current state of the sky and temperature, which question are you answering?\",\"options\":[\"Which weather do you like most?\",\"How is the weather today?\",\"When is your birthday?\",\"Where would you like to go?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'How is the weather today?\' refers to the current state of the weather.\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The text asks about \'National festivals\' specifically under which heading?\",\"options\":[\"Games\",\"Colours\",\"Vacation\",\"Festivals\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The instruction to talk about National festivals is found under \'Let’s talk about festival\'.\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text ask \'Where would you like to go on the next vacation?\'\",\"options\":[\"To talk about a place you already visited\",\"To talk about future plans or wishes\",\"To talk about your school\",\"To talk about birthday gifts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'next\' indicates a future plan or desire for a vacation.\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are talking about the color of a mango or an apple, which conversation starter are you following?\",\"options\":[\"Let\'s talk about weather\",\"Let\'s talk about colours\",\"Let\'s talk about games\",\"Let\'s talk about birthdays\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Talking about the \'colour of your favourite fruit\' is part of the colours topic.\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these questions from the text requires you to give a reason (\'Why\') for your answer?\",\"options\":[\"When is your birthday?\",\"Which weather do you like most?\",\"Which games do you like to play?\",\"What is the colour of your favourite fruit?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically adds \'Why?\' after the question \'Which games do you like to play?\'.\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If you discuss playing Ludo at home or Cricket on the ground, which category does this fit into?\",\"options\":[\"Vacation places\",\"Indoor and outdoor games\",\"National festivals\",\"Weather preferences\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Ludo and Cricket are examples of indoor and outdoor games mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should you talk about regarding festivals in addition to your personal favorites?\",\"options\":[\"The food you eat\",\"The clothes you wear\",\"National festivals celebrated in our country\",\"The gifts you get\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks to \'Talk about National festivals celebrated in our country\' under the festival topic.\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which topic asks you to think about both a place you have already been to and a place you want to go?\",\"options\":[\"Weather\",\"Vacation\",\"Colours\",\"Birthdays\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The vacation topic asks \'Which place did you visit?\' (past) and \'Where would you like to go?\' (future).\",\"topic\":\"1.2 Conversation Starters\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which sentence is used to tell someone which class you are in?\",\"options\":[\"I am .....\",\"I am in Grade .....\",\"The name of my school is .....\",\"I like to .....\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sentence \'I am in Grade .....\' is specifically used to mention one\'s class or grade level.\",\"topic\":\"d. Read and complete\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence helps you talk about the people you live with at home?\",\"options\":[\"I am in Grade .....\",\".....and .....are my friends.\",\"In my family, there are .....members.\",\"I like to .....\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sentence about family members describes the people living in one\'s household.\",\"topic\":\"d. Read and complete\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If your name is Amit, how would you complete the first sentence in the list?\",\"options\":[\"I am Amit.\",\"I am in Grade Amit.\",\"The name of my school is Amit.\",\"Amit and Amit are my friends.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The starter \'I am .....\' is used to introduce one\'s name.\",\"topic\":\"d. Read and complete\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'.....and .....are my friends\', how many blanks are provided for names?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows two blanks separated by \'and\' for the names of friends.\",\"topic\":\"d. Read and complete\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of information should you fill in the blank for \'The name of my school is .....\'?\",\"options\":[\"Your friend\'s name\",\"Your favorite game\",\"The place where you study\",\"The number of your family members\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"This sentence requires the specific name of the educational institution you attend.\",\"topic\":\"d. Read and complete\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you enjoy drawing, which conversation starter would you use to share this interest?\",\"options\":[\"I am .....\",\"I am in Grade .....\",\"In my family, there are .....members.\",\"I like to .....\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'I like to .....\' is used to express personal interests or hobbies like drawing.\",\"topic\":\"d. Read and complete\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'In my family, there are .....members\', what type of word is most suitable for the blank?\",\"options\":[\"A color\",\"A number\",\"A city name\",\"An action word\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The blank refers to the count of people in a family, which requires a number.\",\"topic\":\"d. Read and complete\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the section \'d. Read and complete\'?\",\"options\":[\"To solve math problems\",\"To practice introducing yourself\",\"To draw a picture of a school\",\"To list all the teachers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sentences provided are starters for a student to give information about themselves.\",\"topic\":\"d. Read and complete\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a \'Conversation Starter\' mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Where do you live?\",\"I am in Grade .....\",\"What is your name?\",\"Goodbye, friend.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'I am in Grade .....\' is one of the specific starters listed under section d.\",\"topic\":\"d. Read and complete\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the sentence \'.....and .....are my friends.\' What must you provide to make this sentence complete?\",\"options\":[\"One name and one hobby\",\"Two names of people\",\"The name of a school and a grade\",\"A number and a name\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The structure \'X and Y are my friends\' requires two names to identify the friends.\",\"topic\":\"d. Read and complete\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a topic mentioned in section \'e\' for preparing a conversation?\",\"options\":[\"At the Hospital\",\"At the Picnic\",\"At the Market\",\"At the Zoo\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Section \'e\' lists \'At the Picnic\' as one of the four topics for conversation.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many transitional phrases should the teacher encourage learners to use while speaking?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Five\",\"Ten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The \'For the Teacher\' section explicitly mentions encouraging students to use five transitional phrases.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners participate in and create, according to the \'For the Teacher\' section?\",\"options\":[\"Textbooks\",\"Conversation bites\",\"School buildings\",\"Bus stands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states teachers should motivate learners to participate and create their own conversation bites.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of the words like \'next\', \'then\', and \'finally\' listed in section \'f\'?\",\"options\":[\"They are names of places\",\"They are transitional phrases\",\"They are names of school functions\",\"They are drawing tools\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note refers to these as transitional phrases to be used while speaking.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is following the teacher\'s guidance to prepare a poster, what should the poster be based on?\",\"options\":[\"A movie\",\"School functions\",\"A grocery list\",\"A map of the world\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text guides the teacher to help students prepare posters based on school functions.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the list in section \'f\' helps to show the beginning of a sequence?\",\"options\":[\"Because\",\"First\",\"Both\",\"Too\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'First\' is included in the list of transitional phrases in section \'f\' to indicate the start of a sequence.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a topic suggested for group presentation in section \'e\'?\",\"options\":[\"Lunch Time\",\"Drawing Competition\",\"At the Bus Stand\",\"At the Library\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Section \'e\' lists Picnic, Drawing Competition, Lunch Time, and Bus Stand; it does not mention \'At the Library\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the list of transitional phrases, which word is used to show a reason for something?\",\"options\":[\"Because\",\"Next\",\"Also\",\"Finally\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Because\' is a transitional phrase listed in section \'f\' that indicates a reason.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What activity should learners do in groups according to section \'e\'?\",\"options\":[\"Write a poem\",\"Prepare and present a simple conversation\",\"Draw a map\",\"Run a race\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Section \'e\' instructs learners to prepare a simple conversation and present them in groups.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the teacher\'s role regarding transitional phrases?\",\"options\":[\"Encourage students to use five while speaking\",\"Tell students to ignore them\",\"Ask students to draw them\",\"Make students memorize them silently\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says the teacher should encourage students to read and use five transitional phrases while speaking.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21510,19,4,'English','en','The Clever Answer','[\"- The story is about Emperor Akbar asking Birbal how many crows are in his kingdom.\",\"- Birbal gives a very large number, 50,000,349 crows.\",\"- Akbar wonders if the number could change if more crows come or some leave.\",\"- Birbal says the number can change because crows from other kingdoms may visit or some may leave for vacation.\",\"- The story shows Birbal’s cleverness and quick thinking.\",\"- Key idea: Numbers can change when new people (or crows) join or leave.\",\"- The moral: A clever answer can solve a problem quickly.\",\"- The story is a short dialogue between Akbar and Birbal.\",\"- It teaches listening, speaking, and understanding simple conversations.\",\"- It also encourages students to think about how numbers can change in real life.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who was the wise minister in Emperor Akbar\'s court?\",\"options\":[\"Akbar\",\"Birbal\",\"A guard\",\"A crow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Birbal as the wise minister of Emperor Akbar.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was Emperor Akbar\'s mood one morning in the royal court?\",\"options\":[\"Angry\",\"Sad\",\"Playful\",\"Sleepy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Emperor Akbar was in a playful mood.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many crows did Birbal say were in the kingdom?\",\"options\":[\"Fifty thousand\",\"Fifty thousand three hundred and forty-nine\",\"Fifty thousand three hundred\",\"Fifty thousand four hundred and thirty-nine\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Birbal gave the specific number fifty thousand three hundred and forty-nine.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where is the scene taking place?\",\"options\":[\"In a dense forest\",\"In the royal court\",\"In a local market\",\"In a school classroom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text and the image show the setting as the royal court.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/016_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does Birbal mean when he addresses Akbar as \'Your Majesty\'?\",\"options\":[\"He is calling him a friend.\",\"It is a respectful way to address a king.\",\"He is talking to a crow.\",\"He is calling him by his first name.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Your Majesty is a formal title used for monarchs like Emperor Akbar.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to Birbal, why might there be more crows than his count?\",\"options\":[\"Because crows are born every day.\",\"Because some crows are hiding.\",\"Because crows from neighboring kingdoms might be visiting friends.\",\"Because the men counted incorrectly.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Birbal explained that extra crows might be visitors from other kingdoms.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Akbar\'s men found fewer crows than Birbal\'s number, where did Birbal say the missing crows went?\",\"options\":[\"They went to sleep.\",\"They went to a different city.\",\"They went on vacation to other kingdoms.\",\"They flew away forever.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Birbal said that if there are fewer, some crows have gone on vacation to other kingdoms.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Birbal\'s logic, if 10 extra crows were found, who would they be?\",\"options\":[\"New babies\",\"Friends and relatives from neighboring kingdoms\",\"Crows that were hiding in the palace\",\"Crows that returned from vacation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Birbal applied the logic that extra crows are visitors from neighboring kingdoms.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Akbar sent his men to count the crows and they found exactly the number Birbal said, what would Birbal\'s reaction likely be?\",\"options\":[\"He would be surprised.\",\"He would be calm because he already gave that answer.\",\"He would be angry at the men.\",\"He would change his answer.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Birbal is depicted as calm and always having an answer, so he would remain composed.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how can you distinguish Emperor Akbar from Birbal?\",\"options\":[\"Akbar is standing while Birbal is sitting.\",\"Akbar is sitting on a throne while Birbal is standing and gesturing.\",\"Akbar is wearing a green robe.\",\"Birbal is the one wearing the largest crown.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows the Emperor seated on a throne and Birbal standing before him.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/016_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Akbar burst out laughing at the end of the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Birbal told a joke about a crow.\",\"He realized Birbal had a clever answer for every situation.\",\"He saw a crow fly into the court.\",\"Birbal forgot the number of crows.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Akbar laughed because Birbal was witty enough to handle any challenge to his answer.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes Birbal\'s character in this story?\",\"options\":[\"Forgetful\",\"Clever\",\"Fearful\",\"Dishonest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The title and Birbal\'s quick, logical responses show he is clever.\",\"topic\":\"The Clever Answer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is spelled correctly according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"emparor\",\"emperor\",\"emperer\",\"empror\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists the correct spelling as \'emperor\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'royal\' usually refer to?\",\"options\":[\"Something belonging to a king or queen\",\"Something very old\",\"A type of food\",\"A common person\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'royal\' describes things related to a monarch or their family.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to a person who rules an empire?\",\"options\":[\"royal\",\"kingdom\",\"emperor\",\"neighbouring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"An emperor is a male ruler of an empire.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes the land or country that a king rules?\",\"options\":[\"neighbouring\",\"royal\",\"emperor\",\"kingdom\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"A kingdom is the territory or country ruled by a king or queen.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a country is \'neighbouring\', where is it located?\",\"options\":[\"Very far away\",\"Across the ocean\",\"Right next to another place\",\"Inside a palace\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Neighbouring means situated next to or very near something.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Fill in the blank: The prince lived in a ____ palace.\",\"options\":[\"kingdom\",\"royal\",\"emperor\",\"neighbouring\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Royal\' is the adjective used to describe things belonging to royalty, like a palace.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list is an adjective used to describe a nearby place?\",\"options\":[\"neighbouring\",\"emperor\",\"kingdom\",\"royal\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Neighbouring\' is used to describe places that are close by.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Out of the four words, which one refers to a person rather than a place or a quality?\",\"options\":[\"kingdom\",\"royal\",\"neighbouring\",\"emperor\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"\'Emperor\' is a noun referring to a person; the others refer to places or qualities.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word contains the root word \'neighbour\'?\",\"options\":[\"kingdom\",\"neighbouring\",\"emperor\",\"royal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Neighbouring\' is derived from the word \'neighbour\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are talking about the \'royal kingdom\', which word describes the location?\",\"options\":[\"royal\",\"kingdom\",\"emperor\",\"neighbouring\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Kingdom\' is the noun that represents the physical location or territory.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21511,19,4,'English','en','Dhanraj Pillay','[\"- Dhanraj Pillay is a famous Indian hockey player.\",\"- He was born in Pune and played for the Indian national team.\",\"- He never gave up even when his best player was absent.\",\"- He led his team to win matches by staying positive.\",\"- Dhanraj teaches teamwork, leadership and perseverance.\",\"- Hockey is India’s national game.\",\"- Key words: scored, cheering, lesson, among, whistle, teamwork, leadership.\",\"- A good player helps the team and does not give up.\",\"- The story shows that practice and confidence help in sports.\",\"- Dhanraj’s life is an example for young students to follow.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which city was the school located where the hockey match was about to begin?\",\"options\":[\"Pune\",\"Mumbai\",\"Nashik\",\"Nagpur\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the match was about to begin one morning in a school in Pune.\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What game were the children going to play?\",\"options\":[\"Cricket\",\"Football\",\"Hockey\",\"Kabaddi\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The passage explicitly mentions that a hockey match was about to begin.\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the name of the young boy mentioned in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Dhanraj Pillay\",\"Sunil Chhetri\",\"Dhyan Chand\",\"Sachin Tendulkar\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the young boy among the children as Dhanraj Pillay.\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Dhanraj\'s team feeling worried before the match?\",\"options\":[\"They did not have a hockey stick\",\"Their best player was absent\",\"The ground was too small\",\"It was raining heavily\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the team felt worried because their best player was absent.\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did Dhanraj respond when the teacher asked him to lead the team?\",\"options\":[\"He said he was too tired\",\"He started crying\",\"He smiled and nodded\",\"He asked someone else to do it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, when the teacher asked him to lead, Dhanraj smiled and nodded.\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What signal indicated that the match had started?\",\"options\":[\"The whistle blew\",\"The teacher shouted\",\"The children clapped\",\"A bell rang\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The passage states, \'The whistle blew and the match started.\'\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which action by Dhanraj showed he accepted the responsibility of being the captain?\",\"options\":[\"He clapped his hands\",\"He nodded to the teacher\",\"He ran to the ground\",\"He cheered for the other team\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Nodding in response to the teacher\'s request to lead shows his acceptance of the role.\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happened first after the match started?\",\"options\":[\"Dhanraj scored a goal\",\"The other team scored the first goal\",\"Dhanraj\'s team won\",\"The match was cancelled\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The other team was strong and scored first goal.\'\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did some players in Dhanraj\'s team feel like giving up?\",\"options\":[\"Because they were hungry\",\"Because the other team was strong and scored first\",\"Because the teacher was angry\",\"Because the match was too long\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links the feeling of giving up to the other team being strong and scoring the first goal.\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How did Dhanraj show leadership when his team felt discouraged?\",\"options\":[\"He scolded the players\",\"He clapped his hands and encouraged them to play together\",\"He walked off the field\",\"He told the teacher he wanted to stop\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Dhanraj clapped his hands and said, \'Don\'t worry! Let us play together and try again.\'\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Dhanraj\'s words, what was his strategy for the team?\",\"options\":[\"To play individually\",\"To play together and try again\",\"To let the other team win\",\"To stop playing hockey\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He specifically tells his team, \'Let us play together and try again.\'\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"At what time of the day did these events take place?\",\"options\":[\"In the evening\",\"At night\",\"One morning\",\"In the afternoon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The very first sentence of the passage mentions \'One morning in school in Pune\'.\",\"topic\":\"The School Match\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Dhanraj do right before he scored a goal?\",\"options\":[\"He passed the ball and ran fast\",\"He sat down on the ground\",\"He left the hockey field\",\"He stopped playing the match\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states he passed the ball, ran fast, and cheered everyone before scoring.\",\"topic\":\"A Great Hockey Player\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When did Dhanraj\'s team score the goal that won them the match?\",\"options\":[\"In the first minute\",\"At half-time\",\"In the last minute\",\"After the match ended\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the team scored again and won the match in the last minute.\",\"topic\":\"A Great Hockey Player\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the children react when Dhanraj scored a goal?\",\"options\":[\"They were very quiet\",\"They cheered loudly\",\"They went back home\",\"They started crying\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the children cheered loudly when Dhanraj scored.\",\"topic\":\"A Great Hockey Player\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What important lesson did Dhanraj learn on the day of the match?\",\"options\":[\"To play only for himself\",\"To never give up and help the team\",\"To run slowly on the field\",\"To score goals without passing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says he learned that a good player never gives up but helps the team.\",\"topic\":\"A Great Hockey Player\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which sport did Dhanraj Pillay become a great player of?\",\"options\":[\"Cricket\",\"Football\",\"Hockey\",\"Tennis\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies Dhanraj Pillay as a great hockey player of India.\",\"topic\":\"A Great Hockey Player\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a player is in a difficult situation during a game, what would Dhanraj\'s life suggest they do?\",\"options\":[\"Stop playing immediately\",\"Wait for others to do the work\",\"Never give up and work with the team\",\"Leave the field and go home\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Dhanraj\'s life teaches teamwork and to never give up.\",\"topic\":\"A Great Hockey Player\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which country did Dhanraj Pillay lead in many matches?\",\"options\":[\"India\",\"England\",\"America\",\"Japan\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states he led India in many matches.\",\"topic\":\"A Great Hockey Player\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did everyone feel after the team won the match?\",\"options\":[\"Tired and angry\",\"Happy and proud\",\"Sad and lonely\",\"Bored and sleepy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says everyone was happy and feeling proud after the win.\",\"topic\":\"A Great Hockey Player\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which quality is essential for a captain who leads a team?\",\"options\":[\"Running away from the ball\",\"Leadership\",\"Playing alone\",\"Scoring only one goal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions his life teaches us teamwork and leadership.\",\"topic\":\"A Great Hockey Player\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the passage, what defines a \'good player\'?\",\"options\":[\"Someone who plays only for themselves\",\"Someone who gives up easily\",\"Someone who helps the team and never gives up\",\"Someone who only cheers but does not play\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states a good player never gives up but helps the team.\",\"topic\":\"A Great Hockey Player\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21512,19,4,'English','en','Honesty Builds Trust','[\"Honesty means telling the truth and doing the right thing.\",\"When you find something lost, the best thing is to return it to its owner.\",\"If you keep a lost coin, you are being dishonest and it can hurt others.\",\"Being honest can make you feel proud and happy, even if you lose something you wanted.\",\"Aai (mother) taught Pawan that keeping the coin would be wrong.\",\"Pawan announced loudly that a coin was found so the owner could come back.\",\"The owner was a poor man who thanked Pawan and Aai with tears.\",\"Truth and honesty bring real happiness, not just temporary joy.\",\"Children should practice honesty by returning lost items and admitting mistakes.\",\"Honesty builds trust between people, making relationships stronger.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where was young Pawan walking when he found the coin?\",\"options\":[\"In a big city market\",\"Along the road near his village\",\"Inside his school playground\",\"In a thick forest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Pawan was walking along the road near his village.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Pawan first think of doing with the coin he found?\",\"options\":[\"Buying new clothes\",\"Giving it to a beggar\",\"Buying sweets\",\"Saving it in a bank\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Pawan thought he could buy sweets with the coin he found.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Pawan doing near the village?\",\"options\":[\"He is running happily with the coin he found\",\"He is looking for his lost school bag\",\"He is chasing a butterfly in the garden\",\"He is crying because he fell down\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Pawan running happily, and the text mentions he was happy after finding the coin.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/020_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What was Aai\'s reaction when Pawan showed her the coin?\",\"options\":[\"She was very happy and asked for sweets\",\"She became serious but spoke lovingly\",\"She got angry and punished Pawan\",\"She told him to hide the coin\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says Aai became serious but spoke lovingly when she saw the coin.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Pawan doing while talking to Aai?\",\"options\":[\"He is eating the sweets he bought\",\"He is showing the coin to his Aai\",\"He is hiding the coin behind his back\",\"He is playing with a toy car\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Pawan standing in front of Aai and showing her the coin in his hand.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/020_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Aai say that keeping the coin would be wrong?\",\"options\":[\"Because the coin was dirty\",\"Because the coin was not theirs\",\"Because the coin was made of plastic\",\"Because Pawan already had many coins\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aai explained that the coin did not belong to them, so keeping it would be wrong.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to Aai, what is more important than being happy for a moment?\",\"options\":[\"Being rich\",\"Being honest\",\"Buying sweets\",\"Playing games\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aai told Pawan that being honest is more important than being happy just for a moment.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Aai ask Pawan to do to find the owner of the coin?\",\"options\":[\"Put up a poster on a tree\",\"Go to the police station\",\"Announce loudly that a coin had been found\",\"Keep the coin until someone asked for it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aai asked Pawan to announce loudly that a coin had been found.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What did Aai do before returning the coin to the poor man?\",\"options\":[\"She asked him to pay some money\",\"She asked him a few questions\",\"She told him to come back the next day\",\"She gave him some sweets first\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Aai asked the man a few questions before returning the coin.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how can you tell the man is very thankful?\",\"options\":[\"He is dancing with joy\",\"He has tears in his eyes and hands joined in thanks\",\"He is giving Pawan a gift\",\"He is laughing loudly at Pawan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the man with a tear and his hands joined in a \'Namaste\' gesture to thank them.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/021_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How did Pawan feel at the end of the day despite not getting sweets?\",\"options\":[\"He felt angry and sad\",\"He felt proud and happy\",\"He felt hungry and tired\",\"He felt like he made a mistake\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that though he did not get sweets, he felt proud and happy.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What lesson did Pawan learn from this incident?\",\"options\":[\"Finding coins makes you rich\",\"Sweets are the most important thing\",\"Truth and honesty bring real happiness\",\"It is better to hide things from Aai\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Pawan understood that day that truth and honesty bring real happiness.\",\"topic\":\"Read and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is included in the \'Listen and repeat\' list?\",\"options\":[\"happiness\",\"notebook\",\"honesty\",\"assembly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'honesty\' as one of the words to listen and repeat.\",\"topic\":\"Collect good thoughts\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where should you write the \'good thoughts\' you collect?\",\"options\":[\"On the blackboard\",\"In your notebook\",\"On a piece of paper\",\"In a textbook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically instructs to write the collected thoughts in your notebook.\",\"topic\":\"Collect good thoughts\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what brings \'real happiness\'?\",\"options\":[\"Money and toys\",\"Truth and honesty\",\"Writing and reading\",\"Listening and repeating\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Truth and honesty bring real happiness.\'\",\"topic\":\"Collect good thoughts\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you find a \'good thought\', what is the first action you should take according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Forget it immediately\",\"Write it in your notebook\",\"Tell only one friend\",\"Keep it a secret\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to collect good thoughts and write them in your notebook.\",\"topic\":\"Collect good thoughts\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where are you supposed to \'present\' the good thoughts you have collected?\",\"options\":[\"In the playground\",\"At home\",\"In your school assembly\",\"In the market\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to present the thoughts in your school assembly.\",\"topic\":\"Collect good thoughts\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is NOT in the \'Listen and repeat\' list provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"moment\",\"announce\",\"felt\",\"happiness\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"\'Happiness\' is part of the good thought, but not in the \'Listen and repeat\' list which contains felt, important, moment, announce, and honesty.\",\"topic\":\"Collect good thoughts\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message of the \'good thought\' provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Honesty makes you sad\",\"Truth is not important\",\"Truth and honesty lead to happiness\",\"Only writing brings happiness\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the thought that truth and honesty bring real happiness.\",\"topic\":\"Collect good thoughts\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are preparing for a school assembly based on these instructions, what should you do?\",\"options\":[\"Play a game\",\"Present good thoughts\",\"Draw a picture\",\"Listen to music\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests presenting collected good thoughts in the school assembly.\",\"topic\":\"Collect good thoughts\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'Truth and honesty bring real happiness\', what are the two keys to happiness?\",\"options\":[\"Truth and honesty\",\"Collecting and writing\",\"Announcing and repeating\",\"Notebooks and assemblies\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text identifies truth and honesty as the factors that bring real happiness.\",\"topic\":\"Collect good thoughts\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of collecting good thoughts according to the activity?\",\"options\":[\"To fill up the notebook pages\",\"To share them with others at the school assembly\",\"To practice handwriting only\",\"To announce a specific moment\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity involves collecting, writing, and then presenting them to others in the assembly.\",\"topic\":\"Collect good thoughts\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21513,19,4,'English','en','Fun With Actions','[\"- Actions are things we do with our body like waving, jumping, standing still, etc.\",\"- In this chapter we learn how to listen to a poem and act out the actions described.\",\"- The poem gives us a list of actions: wave, jump, stop, shake knees, turn around, etc.\",\"- We can practice by doing the actions while reading the words aloud.\",\"- Opposite words help us understand meaning: fast ↔ slow, high ↔ low, stop ↔ go, up ↔ down.\",\"- Repeating actions helps us remember the words and improves our listening skills.\",\"- We can write our own funny actions and instructions and act them out with friends.\",\"- Acting out the poem helps us learn new vocabulary and pronunciation.\",\"- When we need a break, we can sit down, raise our hand, run fast, or wave our hand to relax.\",\"- Practising actions in a group makes learning fun and interactive.\",\"- Listening and acting together builds teamwork and confidence.\",\"- The poem encourages us to think, freeze, and then move again, showing the cycle of action.\",\"- By acting out the poem, we learn to follow directions and understand instructions.\",\"- The chapter teaches us that actions can be described, repeated, and enjoyed together.\",\"- Remember to act safely: keep space around you when jumping or running.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, where should you wave your hands?\",\"options\":[\"Up in the air\",\"Behind your back\",\"On your knees\",\"In your pockets\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says \'Wave your hands up in the air\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and act\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poem tell you NOT to do when you \'freeze\'?\",\"options\":[\"Think\",\"Blink\",\"Stand still\",\"Smile\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Stop and freeze, don\'t even blink\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and act\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you touch after you shake your knees?\",\"options\":[\"Your nose\",\"Your elbows\",\"Your toes\",\"Your head\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem follows the sequence: \'Shake your knees, touch your toes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and act\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'land with ease\' most likely mean in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Land softly and safely\",\"Fall down hard\",\"Land with a loud noise\",\"Do not land at all\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the context of jumping, landing with ease implies a smooth and soft landing.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and act\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which action should be done with \'joyful cheer\'?\",\"options\":[\"Running fast\",\"Clapping hands\",\"Turning around\",\"Counting to ten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states \'Turn around with joyful cheer\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and act\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what action is the boy at the very top performing?\",\"options\":[\"Jumping up high\",\"Sitting down\",\"Counting to ten\",\"Touching his toes\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The boy at the top is shown in mid-air with his arms up, representing \'Jump up high\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and act\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/022_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the poem\'s instructions, what do you do immediately after wiggling your fingers?\",\"options\":[\"Turn around\",\"Strike a pose\",\"Jump up high\",\"Clap your hands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Wiggle fingers, strike a pose\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and act\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very last thing you do before the poem says \'let\'s play again\'?\",\"options\":[\"Smile bright\",\"Count to ten\",\"Bend your knees\",\"Land with ease\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Smile bright and count to ten, Ready, set-let\'s play again!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and act\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which two actions are mentioned together in the same line involving hands and legs?\",\"options\":[\"Wave hands and run fast\",\"Clap hands and bend knees\",\"Shake knees and wiggle fingers\",\"Touch toes and jump high\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem contains the line \'Clap your hands and bend your knees\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and act\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, look at the girl in the middle. Which action from the poem is she doing?\",\"options\":[\"Waving hands\",\"Shaking her knees\",\"Running fast\",\"Blinking her eyes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The girl in the middle is shown slightly bent with motion lines near her knees, indicating \'Shake your knees\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, sing and act\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/022_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'air\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"here\",\"there\",\"hair\",\"fair\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly pairs \'air\' with \'there\' as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the rhyming word for \'blink\' in the given list?\",\"options\":[\"think\",\"pink\",\"drink\",\"sink\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'blink - think\' as a rhyming pair.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'ten\' in the exercise?\",\"options\":[\"pen\",\"hen\",\"again\",\"men\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the pair \'ten - again\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should you do with your hands?\",\"options\":[\"Shake them\",\"Clap them\",\"Wave them\",\"Fold them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text gives the instruction: \'Wave your hands.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which body part are you instructed to \'shake\'?\",\"options\":[\"Hands\",\"Knees\",\"Head\",\"Toes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Shake your knees.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the instruction: \'Jump up ____.\'\",\"options\":[\"high\",\"now\",\"fast\",\"low\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifically says \'Jump up high.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\