t for the teacher and classmates.\",\"Good manners create a friendly learning environment.\",\"Practice good manners daily to become a respectful student.\"]','[{\"q\":\"On which day of the week did the teacher announce \'A Day without Rules\'?\",\"options\":[\"Sunday\",\"Monday\",\"Friday\",\"Saturday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'It was Monday morning\' when the events took place.\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which grade did the children run into when the bell rang?\",\"options\":[\"Grade One\",\"Grade Two\",\"Grade Three\",\"Grade Four\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that all the children ran into Grade Four.\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why were the students very excited during the first period?\",\"options\":[\"Because they were going on a picnic\",\"Because it was a holiday\",\"Because the teacher announced \'A Day without Rules\'\",\"Because they had a new teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The students were excited because the teacher said they would have \'A Day without Rules\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what did Ayush do when there were no rules?\",\"options\":[\"He jumped on the chair\",\"He threw paper balls in the air\",\"He talked loudly to his friend\",\"He broke the chalks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically states, \'Ayush threw paper balls in the air.\'\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the chalks in the classroom when there were no rules?\",\"options\":[\"They were used to draw beautiful pictures\",\"They were kept safely in the box\",\"They broke into small pieces\",\"They were lost\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that \'chalks broke into small pieces\' during the chaos.\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the boy standing on the chair doing?\",\"options\":[\"He is cleaning the fan\",\"He is jumping in excitement\",\"He is trying to reach the board\",\"He is looking for his book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Swaraj jumping on the chair because he is excited about having no rules.\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/023_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what can be seen on the table and floor that shows the room is untidy?\",\"options\":[\"Only water bottles\",\"Flowers and ribbons\",\"Books and broken pieces of chalk\",\"Lunch boxes and spoons\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows books lying open and scattered, along with small white pieces representing broken chalk.\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/023_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What was the teacher\'s reaction while the classroom was becoming noisy and messy?\",\"options\":[\"She shouted at the children\",\"She watched quietly\",\"She left the classroom\",\"She started scribbling on the board\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Teacher just watched quietly.\'\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What did the students do when the headmaster opened the door and looked inside?\",\"options\":[\"They continued shouting\",\"They ran out of the room\",\"Everyone froze\",\"They started cleaning the room\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'He opened the door and looked inside. Everyone froze!\'\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student follows the example of Avantika from the text, what would they be doing?\",\"options\":[\"Jumping on furniture\",\"Talking loudly to a friend\",\"Scribbling on the board\",\"Throwing paper balls\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Avantika was talking loudly to her friend.\'\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the events in the classroom, what is a likely result of not having any rules?\",\"options\":[\"The classroom becomes a better place to study\",\"Students become very disciplined\",\"The room becomes untidy and noisy\",\"The teacher becomes very happy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes how the lack of rules led to noise, broken chalk, and an untidy room.\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the headmaster laugh and say, \'Let’s see how long you can manage without rules\'?\",\"options\":[\"He thought the children were doing a great job\",\"He wanted to see if the children would eventually realize that rules are necessary\",\"He liked the scribbles on the board\",\"He was happy that the room was untidy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The headmaster\'s comment suggests he wants the students to experience the consequences of having no rules.\",\"topic\":\"A Day without Rules\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What could Swaraj not find after some time?\",\"options\":[\"His notebook\",\"His pencil\",\"His eraser\",\"His bag\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Swaraj could not find his pencil.\'\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who slipped on a paper that was lying on the floor?\",\"options\":[\"Avantika\",\"Ayush\",\"Bhakti\",\"Swaraj\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that \'Bhakti slipped on a paper on the floor.\'\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to Ayush’s notebook during the day without rules?\",\"options\":[\"It was lost\",\"It was wet\",\"It was stolen\",\"It was torn\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Ayush’s notebook was torn.\'\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What word did the teacher write on the board to describe classroom rules?\",\"options\":[\"Discipline\",\"Etiquettes\",\"Manners\",\"Behaviors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher wrote \'Classroom etiquettes\' on the board.\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the children feel when there were no rules in the class?\",\"options\":[\"Excited and energetic\",\"Tired and sad\",\"Happy and playful\",\"Angry and loud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Everyone looked tired and sad.\'\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Avantika unable to hear anything?\",\"options\":[\"Because the music was loud\",\"Because she was far away\",\"Because of the noise in the class\",\"Because the teacher was whispering\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Avantika said, \'I can’t hear anything in this noise!\'\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the children do together after remembering the rules?\",\"options\":[\"They went home\",\"They cleaned the room\",\"They started shouting\",\"They played a game\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Then the children cleaned the room together.\'\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Headmaster, which class became the best in the school?\",\"options\":[\"Grade Three\",\"Grade Five\",\"Grade Four\",\"Grade Two\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Headmaster said Grade Four is the best class, and it became the neatest and happiest.\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the second rule written on the blackboard?\",\"options\":[\"Listen carefully when others speak\",\"Keep your desk and class clean\",\"Be kind and helpful\",\"Raise your hand before talking\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Rule number 2 in the image is \'Raise your hand before talking.\'\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/024_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which polite word is listed as an example of classroom etiquette?\",\"options\":[\"Hello\",\"Sorry\",\"Welcome\",\"Excuse me\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Rule 5 in the image lists \'please, sorry, thank you\' as polite words.\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/024_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the children describe their day without rules as \'terrible\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they had no homework\",\"Because the teacher was not there\",\"Because things were messy, broken, and noisy\",\"Because they wanted to go to the playground\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows that without rules, items were lost, torn, and the room was noisy and messy.\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the final result of the children promising to follow classroom etiquettes?\",\"options\":[\"The class became very quiet and boring\",\"The class became the neatest and happiest\",\"The children got new pencils and notebooks\",\"The teacher stopped giving them rules\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that Grade Four became the most neat and happiest class in the school.\",\"topic\":\"Learning the Lesson\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'untidy\'?\",\"options\":[\"Clean and neat\",\"Very loud\",\"Not neat or clean\",\"Writing carefully\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Untidy means something that is messy or not organized.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word refers to the set of rules for polite behavior?\",\"options\":[\"Scribbles\",\"Etiquettes\",\"Noisy\",\"Froze\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Etiquettes are the social rules for good behavior.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does it mean to be \'polite\'?\",\"options\":[\"To be rude to others\",\"To have good manners\",\"To make a lot of noise\",\"To draw on walls\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Being polite means showing good manners and respect.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a classroom is full of loud sounds, which word describes it best?\",\"options\":[\"Polite\",\"Noisy\",\"Untidy\",\"Rules\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Noisy describes a place or person making a lot of sound.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are you doing if you write or draw something very carelessly?\",\"options\":[\"Making rules\",\"Following etiquettes\",\"Making scribbles\",\"Being polite\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Scribbles are careless marks or drawings.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of \'Good Manners\', what are \'rules\'?\",\"options\":[\"Things we must follow to behave well\",\"Messy drawings in a book\",\"Loud shouting in the park\",\"Ice that does not melt\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Rules are instructions that tell us what is allowed and what is not.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Rohan told his teacher he would complete his work. This means he ____ to do it.\",\"options\":[\"Froze\",\"Scribbled\",\"Promised\",\"Noisy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To promise means to give your word that you will do something.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to show \'Good Manners\', how should you speak to your elders?\",\"options\":[\"In an untidy way\",\"In a polite way\",\"In a noisy way\",\"By making scribbles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Speaking politely is a key part of having good manners.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a person suddenly stops moving and becomes very still, which word describes this?\",\"options\":[\"Promised\",\"Froze\",\"Rules\",\"Etiquettes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Froze means to become suddenly still or unable to move.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these actions shows a lack of \'etiquettes\' in a library?\",\"options\":[\"Being polite\",\"Following rules\",\"Being noisy\",\"Keeping books tidy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Being noisy in a library is against the rules of polite behavior (etiquettes).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21515,19,4,'English','en','The Honey Village','[\"Patgaon is a small village in Kolhapur district known as the Honey Village.\",\"Bees are the makers of honey; they collect nectar from flowers.\",\"Nectar is a sweet liquid that bees bring back to the hive.\",\"Honey is made by bees from nectar and is stored in honeycombs.\",\"Honey is very important for our health; it gives us energy and strength.\",\"It is used as a natural medicine to cure cough, cold and aid digestion.\",\"Warm water with honey helps digestion and keeps us healthy and active.\",\"People in Patgaon keep honeybees and collect pure natural honey.\",\"The project in Patgaon helps villagers earn money and protects nature.\",\"Honey can be used every day in milk, tea, sweets and home remedies.\",\"Bees fly around flowers, spreading joy and love.\",\"The village is surrounded by green hills, forests and many flowers.\",\"Bees collect nectar from flowers, not from fruits.\",\"Honey keeps us healthy and active.\",\"The project was started by experts and nature-loving people.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which district is the village of Patgaon located?\",\"options\":[\"Pune district\",\"Kolhapur district\",\"Satara district\",\"Nashik district\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Patgaon is a small village in Kolhapur district.\",\"topic\":\"Patgaon: The Honey Village\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is Patgaon famous as?\",\"options\":[\"The Flower Village\",\"The Forest Village\",\"The Honey Village\",\"The Green Village\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Patgaon is known as the Honey Village.\",\"topic\":\"Patgaon: The Honey Village\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of honey do the people in Patgaon collect?\",\"options\":[\"Artificial honey\",\"Pure and natural honey\",\"Sweet syrup\",\"Flavored honey\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that people in Patgaon collect pure and natural honey.\",\"topic\":\"Patgaon: The Honey Village\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who developed the Honey Village project?\",\"options\":[\"Only the villagers\",\"Experts and nature loving people\",\"Factory owners\",\"Foreign tourists\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states this project was developed by experts and nature loving people.\",\"topic\":\"Patgaon: The Honey Village\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What were the two main goals of starting the Honey Village project?\",\"options\":[\"To build houses and roads\",\"To plant trees and sell wood\",\"To help villagers earn money and protect nature\",\"To catch bees and sell them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The project was started to help villagers earn money and protect nature.\",\"topic\":\"Patgaon: The Honey Village\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what do bees use to make honey?\",\"options\":[\"Water from hills\",\"Nectar from flowers\",\"Leaves from forests\",\"Soil from the village\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that bees collect nectar from flowers and make honey.\",\"topic\":\"Patgaon: The Honey Village\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person wants to see a village surrounded by green hills and forests, where should they go?\",\"options\":[\"A big city\",\"Patgaon\",\"A desert\",\"A factory area\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes Patgaon as being surrounded by green hills, forests, and many flowers.\",\"topic\":\"Patgaon: The Honey Village\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"