the flowers, bees do fly\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sweet Honey\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, honey is used as a ________.\",\"options\":[\"Toy\",\"Medicine\",\"Vegetable\",\"Stone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that honey is used as medicine.\",\"topic\":\"Sweet Honey\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the benefit of drinking warm water with honey?\",\"options\":[\"It is good for digestion\",\"It makes us sleepy\",\"It hurts our throat\",\"It makes us cold\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that warm water with honey is good for digestion.\",\"topic\":\"Sweet Honey\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does honey affect our daily activity?\",\"options\":[\"It makes us lazy\",\"It keeps us healthy and active\",\"It makes us slow\",\"It makes us bored\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says honey keeps us healthy and active.\",\"topic\":\"Sweet Honey\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child has a cough, what does the text suggest might help?\",\"options\":[\"Drinking cold juice\",\"Using honey\",\"Eating spicy food\",\"Playing in the rain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that honey helps to cure cough and cold.\",\"topic\":\"Sweet Honey\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In which of these drinks can honey be used every day according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Salt water\",\"Tea\",\"Oil\",\"Vinegar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists milk, tea, sweets, and home remedies as daily uses for honey.\",\"topic\":\"Sweet Honey\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poem describe honey as \'Golden food we love to bite\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is made of metal\",\"Because of its bright color and sweet taste\",\"Because it is very heavy\",\"Because it is hard like a rock\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem calls it \'sweet and bright\' and \'golden\', indicating its appearance and taste.\",\"topic\":\"Sweet Honey\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why is honey considered important in our life?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is only for bees\",\"Because it has many health benefits and uses\",\"Because it is very expensive\",\"Because it is hard to find\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists multiple benefits like energy, health, and its use in medicine and food.\",\"topic\":\"Sweet Honey\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What sound does the bee make in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Moo, moo\",\"Buzz, buzz\",\"Quack, quack\",\"Chirp, chirp\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem starts with the words \'Buzz, buzz\', which is the sound the bee makes.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the bee making in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Milk\",\"Sugar\",\"Honey\",\"Jam\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states the bee is \'Making honey\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, who is the honey being made for?\",\"options\":[\"The flowers\",\"The forest\",\"Me\",\"The birds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says the bee is \'Making honey just for me\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used to describe the bee in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Lazy\",\"Busy\",\"Sleepy\",\"Angry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem refers to the bee as a \'busy bee\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the bee flying?\",\"options\":[\"Far from the trees\",\"Near the flowers fair\",\"Inside a house\",\"High in the clouds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions the bee is \'Flying near the flowers fair\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the bee spread everywhere?\",\"options\":[\"Dust and dirt\",\"Water and seeds\",\"Joy and love\",\"Honey and wax\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The last line of the poem says the bee is \'Spreading joy and love everywhere\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the poem, which word rhymes with \'bee\'?\",\"options\":[\"fair\",\"me\",\"love\",\"busy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the first two lines, \'bee\' and \'me\' end with the same sound, making them rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'fair\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"everywhere\",\"honey\",\"buzz\",\"joy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the last two lines, \'fair\' and \'everywhere\' rhyme with each other.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the bee\'s main action while it is near the flowers?\",\"options\":[\"Sleeping\",\"Running\",\"Flying\",\"Swimming\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem describes the bee as \'Flying near the flowers fair\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, how does the bee make the world feel?\",\"options\":[\"Sad and lonely\",\"Scary and dark\",\"Full of joy and love\",\"Quiet and still\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The bee is described as spreading joy and love, which makes the world feel happy.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21516,19,4,'English','en','Sant Gadge Maharaj','[\"Sant Gadge Maharaj was born on 23 February 1876 in Shendgaon village, Amravati district, Maharashtra.\",\"His birth name was Debuji Zhingraji Janorkar.\",\"He was a saint and a social reformer who worked for the poor and for equality.\",\"He opposed blind faith, superstitions and caste discrimination.\",\"He believed in simple living, cleanliness and education for children.\",\"He cleaned villages, temples and public places to show how clean life is peaceful.\",\"He helped build schools, hostels and shelters for poor people.\",\"He never kept money for himself; he lived only to serve others.\",\"People from all religions and castes respected him.\",\"He died on 20 December 1956 but is still remembered for his teachings and social work.\",\"Key values he taught: honesty, kindness, helping others, cleanliness and education.\",\"He used songs and speeches to spread good values.\",\"He encouraged children to go to school and helped them with infrastructure.\",\"He believed that cleanliness makes body and mind peaceful.\",\"He was known for his simple life and high thinking.\",\"He was a great saint of Maharashtra.\",\"He worked for social reform and equality.\",\"He taught that kindness and honesty are important.\",\"He believed in serving people and not keeping money for himself.\",\"He was respected by people of all castes and religions.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What was the real name of Sant Gadge Maharaj?\",\"options\":[\"Debuji Zhingraji Janorkar\",\"Zhingraji Debuji Janorkar\",\"Sant Tukaram Maharaj\",\"Amravati Janorkar\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states his name was Debuji Zhingraji Janorkar.\",\"topic\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"On which date was Sant Gadge Maharaj born?\",\"options\":[\"23 January 1876\",\"23 February 1876\",\"23 March 1886\",\"23 February 1976\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, he was born on 23 February 1876.\",\"topic\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which village was Sant Gadge Maharaj born?\",\"options\":[\"Amravati\",\"Maharashtra\",\"Shendgaon\",\"Janorkar\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he was born at Shendgaon village.\",\"topic\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj is recognized as a great saint and a ______.\",\"options\":[\"Freedom fighter\",\"Social reformer\",\"Scientist\",\"Rich merchant\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes him as a great saint and social reformer.\",\"topic\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on his beliefs, how did Sant Gadge Maharaj treat other people?\",\"options\":[\"With caste discrimination\",\"With equality and kindness\",\"By ignoring poor people\",\"With blind faith\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says he believed in equality and kindness.\",\"topic\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these did Sant Gadge Maharaj speak against?\",\"options\":[\"Cleanliness and health\",\"Education and schools\",\"Blind faith and superstitions\",\"Helping poor people\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states he spoke against blind faith, superstitions, and caste discrimination.\",\"topic\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Sant Gadge Maharaj ask people to give up bad social practices?\",\"options\":[\"To become a king\",\"To collect money\",\"To reform society and help people\",\"To travel to different districts\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"As a social reformer, he wanted people to improve their lives by leaving bad practices.\",\"topic\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If Sant Gadge Maharaj saw someone being treated unfairly because of their caste, what action would he take based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"He would support the discrimination.\",\"He would speak against the discrimination.\",\"He would ignore the situation.\",\"He would encourage blind faith.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says he spoke against caste discrimination.\",\"topic\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Sant Gadge Maharaj holding in his hand that represents his work for cleanliness?\",\"options\":[\"A walking stick\",\"A broom\",\"A sword\",\"A flag\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows him holding a broom, which is a symbol of his cleanliness mission.\",\"topic\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/027_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what activity are the people in the background performing?\",\"options\":[\"They are planting trees.\",\"They are sweeping and cleaning.\",\"They are building a house.\",\"They are fighting with each other.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The background of the image shows people sweeping, reflecting the topic of cleanliness.\",\"topic\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/027_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of life did Sant Gadge Maharaj live?\",\"options\":[\"A luxurious life\",\"A very simple life\",\"A secret life\",\"A life of comfort\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Sant Gadge Maharaj lived a very simple life.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"On which date did Sant Gadge Maharaj pass away?\",\"options\":[\"15 August, 1947\",\"26 January, 1950\",\"20 December, 1956\",\"2 October, 1869\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Sant Gadge Maharaj died on 20 December, 1956.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phrases describes Sant Gadge Maharaj\'s belief?\",\"options\":[\"High living and simple thinking\",\"Simple living and high thinking\",\"Rich living and no thinking\",\"Fast living and simple thinking\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions he believed in simple living and high thinking.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did Sant Gadge Maharaj spread good values among the people?\",\"options\":[\"Through books and newspapers\",\"Through songs and speeches\",\"Through television and radio\",\"Through letters and emails\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states he imbibed good values through songs and speeches.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to Sant Gadge Maharaj, what is the benefit of cleanliness?\",\"options\":[\"It makes us rich\",\"It makes us famous\",\"It makes our body and mind peaceful\",\"It helps us sleep longer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says he believed cleanliness makes our body and mind peaceful.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Sant Gadge Maharaj clean villages and public places himself?\",\"options\":[\"To earn money\",\"To set an example for others\",\"Because it was his job\",\"To pass his time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says he cleaned these places himself to set an example.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to follow Sant Gadge Maharaj\'s advice on education, what should they do?\",\"options\":[\"Stay at home and play\",\"Go to school regularly\",\"Only clean the house\",\"Keep all their money\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that he encouraged children to go to school.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you see a dirty temple, what action would Sant Gadge Maharaj likely suggest?\",\"options\":[\"Wait for someone else to clean it\",\"Complain to the authorities\",\"Clean it yourself to help others\",\"Leave the place immediately\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"He himself cleaned villages and temples to show people the importance of cleanliness.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did people from all religions and castes respect Sant Gadge Maharaj?\",\"options\":[\"Because he was a very wealthy man\",\"Because he lived only to serve people\",\"Because he only helped people of his own caste\",\"Because he was a powerful politician\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes he did not keep money for himself and lived only to serve people, earning him respect from all.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the purpose of building hostels and schools according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To provide places for poor people and students\",\"To store the money he collected\",\"To live in a big house himself\",\"To start a business\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says he helped build schools, hostels, and places for poor people to stay.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which quality of Sant Gadge Maharaj is shown by the fact that he \'did not keep money for himself\'?\",\"options\":[\"Selfishness\",\"Selflessness\",\"Greed\",\"Carelessness\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Living only to serve others without keeping money shows the quality of selflessness.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the most important lesson Sant Gadge Maharaj gave to society?\",\"options\":[\"One should only focus on their own family\",\"Cleanliness and social work are essential for a peaceful life\",\"Collecting money is the goal of life\",\"Songs are only for entertainment\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text emphasizes his work in cleanliness, education, and serving the poor as his main teachings.\",\"topic\":\"Cleanliness and Social Work\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"create\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is one of the four key words mentioned at the beginning of the text?\",\"options\":[\"Honesty\",\"Equality\",\"Bravery\",\"Friendship\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'equality\' as one of the four key words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are learners encouraged to collect information about?\",\"options\":[\"Different kings of India\",\"Different cities in Maharashtra\",\"Different saints from Maharashtra\",\"Different types of trees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to collect information about different saints from Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should learners read to learn more?\",\"options\":[\"Newspapers\",\"Books about saints\",\"Comic books\",\"Science journals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically encourages learners to read books about saints.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners talk about after reading the lesson?\",\"options\":[\"Their favorite food\",\"Key elements, events, and ideas\",\"The weather in Maharashtra\",\"How to draw a picture\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to talk about the key elements\\/events and ideas from the lesson.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text refers to treating everyone as the same and giving them the same rights?\",\"options\":[\"Superstition\",\"Discrimination\",\"Equality\",\"Humanity\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Equality is the state of being equal, especially in status, rights, or opportunities.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is looking for a biography of Sant Tukaram, which instruction from the text are they following?\",\"options\":[\"Talking about events\",\"Collecting information of different saints\",\"Avoiding discrimination\",\"Studying humanity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Finding a biography is a way to collect information about a saint, as suggested in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list describes the quality of being kind and showing concern for all people?\",\"options\":[\"Humanity\",\"Superstition\",\"Discrimination\",\"Events\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Humanity refers to the quality of being human and showing benevolence or kindness.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student shares a story about a specific miracle performed by a saint. This is an example of talking about what?\",\"options\":[\"Discrimination\",\"Key events\",\"Superstition\",\"Equality\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sharing a story about a specific occurrence is talking about an \'event\' from the saint\'s life.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following words from the text represents an unfair practice that saints likely fought against?\",\"options\":[\"Humanity\",\"Equality\",\"Discrimination\",\"Information\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Discrimination is the unjust treatment of different categories of people, which is a negative practice.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text refers to beliefs that are not based on reason or scientific knowledge?\",\"options\":[\"Humanity\",\"Superstition\",\"Equality\",\"Ideas\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Superstition is a belief or practice resulting from ignorance or fear of the unknown.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21517,19,4,'English','en','My Word Family (Unit 1)','[\"- A word family is a group of words that share the same root word.\",\"- The root word is the main part that gives the meaning of the word.\",\"- Adding prefixes or suffixes to the root changes the meaning but keeps the root the same.\",\"- Syllables are parts of a word that are spoken together; you can split a word into syllables by listening to its sounds.\",\"- Example: \'kingdom\' has two syllables: king – dom.\",\"- Example: \'competition\' has four syllables: com – pe – ti – tion.\",\"- Words in a word family can be nouns, verbs, adjectives, or adverbs.\",\"- Sorting words into boxes helps you see which words are actions, qualities, or objects.\",\"- Writing sentences with words from a word family helps you use the words correctly.\",\"- Remember to use the root word correctly when making new words (e.g., \'freeze\' is a verb, \'frozen\' is an adjective).\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many syllables are there in the word \'kingdom\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states kingdom → king – dom (2).\",\"topic\":\"Sort words into boxes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Into which box should the word \'pebble\' be sorted?\",\"options\":[\"Action words\",\"Words denoting quality\",\"Objects\",\"Syllables\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'pebble\' under the \'Objects\' box.\",\"topic\":\"Sort words into boxes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of an \'Action word\' provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"honest\",\"pebble\",\"freeze\",\"kingdom\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text categorizes \'freeze\' as an action word.\",\"topic\":\"Sort words into boxes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many syllables are identified in the word \'competition\'?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows competition → com – pe – ti – tion (4).\",\"topic\":\"Sort words into boxes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What type of word is \'honest\' according to the word family boxes?\",\"options\":[\"Action word\",\"Word denoting quality\",\"Object\",\"Syllable\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text places \'honest\' in the \'Words denoting quality\' box.\",\"topic\":\"Sort words into boxes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you hear the word \'freeze\' and then \'sneeze\', what is the instruction given in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Write the word\",\"Sort the word\",\"Act accordingly\",\"Count syllables\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Task 2 says \'Listen to the word and act accordingly\' using freeze and sneeze as examples.\",\"topic\":\"Sort words into boxes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the syllable breakdown \'king – dom\', what does the number 2 represent?\",\"options\":[\"The number of letters\",\"The number of words\",\"The number of syllables\",\"The number of boxes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses the number to identify the count of syllables in the word.\",\"topic\":\"Sort words into boxes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which category would best describe words like \'brave\' or \'kind\' if they follow the same pattern as \'honest\'?\",\"options\":[\"Action words\",\"Words denoting quality\",\"Objects\",\"Syllables\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since \'honest\' is a quality, similar words would fit in the \'Words denoting quality\' box.\",\"topic\":\"Sort words into boxes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step mentioned in the text for identifying syllables?\",\"options\":[\"Read the word family\",\"Listen carefully\",\"Sort into boxes\",\"Act accordingly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Task 1 begins with the instruction \'Listen carefully\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sort words into boxes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the syllable breakdown of \'competition\', which part is the third syllable?\",\"options\":[\"com\",\"pe\",\"ti\",\"tion\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The breakdown provided is com (1) – pe (2) – ti (3) – tion (4).\",\"topic\":\"Sort words into boxes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21518,19,4,'English','en','Catch a Little Rhyme','[\"- A rhyme is a short poem that has words that sound the same at the end.\",\"- In this poem the rhyme keeps changing into different things.\",\"- The poem shows how a rhyme can be playful and imaginative.\",\"- Key words: rhyme, caught, floor, bicycle, icicle, hat, cat, tail, whale, boat, goat, tin, paper, skyscraper, kite, sight.\",\"- The poem ends with the rhyme flying away, showing freedom.\",\"- Rhyming pairs in the poem: rhyme\\/​time, floor\\/​door, bicycle\\/​icicle, hat\\/cat, tail\\/​whale, boat\\/goat, tin\\/paper, skyscraper\\/kite, sight\\/out.\",\"- The poem encourages listening, repeating and singing.\",\"- Students should identify rhyming words and think of their own rhymes.\",\"- Opposite words: in – out, tall – short, melt – freeze, little – big.\",\"- Fill‑in‑the‑blanks help practice word order and meaning.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the poet of the poem \'Catch a Little Rhyme\'?\",\"options\":[\"Robert Frost\",\"Eve Merriam\",\"William Wordsworth\",\"Ruskin Bond\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem is written by Eve Merriam as mentioned at the end of the text.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the speaker first set the little rhyme?\",\"options\":[\"On the table\",\"On the chair\",\"On the floor\",\"In a box\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'I set it on the floor\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the rhyme when the speaker chased it on a bicycle?\",\"options\":[\"It turned into a cat\",\"It ran out the door\",\"It melted to an icicle\",\"It grew into a kite\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'I chased it on my bicycle but it melted to an icicle\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what did the rhyme turn into after being scooped up in a hat?\",\"options\":[\"A goat\",\"A whale\",\"A cat\",\"A skyscraper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'I scooped it up in my hat but it turned into a cat\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what animal is shown sitting inside a pink bowl-like hat held by the girl?\",\"options\":[\"A dog\",\"A cat\",\"A rabbit\",\"A mouse\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a cat inside the hat being held by the girl.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/030_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the rhyme stretched into a whale, how did the speaker catch it?\",\"options\":[\"By the tail\",\"In a boat\",\"With a net\",\"By the fin\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'I caught it by the tail but it stretched into a whale\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What did the speaker follow in a boat?\",\"options\":[\"A whale\",\"A goat\",\"A cat\",\"An icicle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The speaker followed the rhyme (which was a whale) in a boat before it changed into a goat.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what object is shown flying at the top left corner with a blue face and yellow edges?\",\"options\":[\"A bird\",\"A kite\",\"A balloon\",\"A plane\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a kite at the top left corner, which matches the end of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/030_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What two things did the speaker feed the rhyme to make it a skyscraper?\",\"options\":[\"Milk and bread\",\"Tin and paper\",\"Grass and water\",\"Fruit and rice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'When I fed it tin and paper it became a tall skyscraper\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the very last thing the rhyme grew into before flying away?\",\"options\":[\"A skyscraper\",\"A goat\",\"A whale\",\"A kite\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The final lines say, \'Then it grew into a kite and flew far out of sight\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is included in the \'Listen and repeat\' list?\",\"options\":[\"Circle\",\"Icicle\",\"Bicycle\",\"Cycle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'icicle\' is the first word listed in the \'Listen and repeat\' section of the text.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher guide learners to collect?\",\"options\":[\"Toys and games\",\"Rhymes, songs and poems\",\"Pens and pencils\",\"Pictures and drawings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that teachers should guide learners to collect rhymes, songs, and poems.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides intonation, what should learners use while practicing singing?\",\"options\":[\"Proper stress\",\"Loud shouting\",\"Fast speed\",\"Hand gestures\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that teachers should give practice to singing with \'proper stress and intonation\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the teacher encourage learners to recognize and explain about a poem?\",\"options\":[\"The number of pages\",\"The central idea\",\"The name of the printer\",\"The color of the ink\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that learners should be encouraged to recognize and explain the central idea of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list refers to a very tall building?\",\"options\":[\"Icicle\",\"Scooped\",\"Skyscraper\",\"Sight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A skyscraper is a technical term for a very tall building, found in the provided vocabulary list.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal of the \'For the Teacher\' section regarding singing?\",\"options\":[\"To make students sing as fast as possible\",\"To improve singing through proper stress and intonation\",\"To make students memorize the whole book\",\"To teach students how to play instruments\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions focus on giving practice to singing with proper stress and intonation for better expression.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher asks a student to find a new song in the library, which instruction is being followed?\",\"options\":[\"Listen and repeat\",\"Practice singing\",\"Collect rhymes, songs and poems\",\"Explain the central idea\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Finding a new song in a library is a way of \'collecting\' rhymes, songs, and poems as suggested in the text.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When a student changes their voice tone to show feeling while singing, they are practicing:\",\"options\":[\"Intonation\",\"Collecting poems\",\"Spelling icicle\",\"Stretching\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Intonation refers to the rise and fall of the voice in speaking or singing, which is a focus area in the teacher\'s notes.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'proper stress\' important when singing a poem according to the teacher\'s guide?\",\"options\":[\"To make the poem longer\",\"To help in collecting rhymes\",\"To improve the way the poem is expressed and sung\",\"To learn how to spell skyscraper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Proper stress helps in the rhythmic and meaningful delivery of the poem during singing practice.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these activities best follows all the \'For the Teacher\' instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Just reading the words once silently\",\"Singing a collected poem with stress and explaining its main meaning\",\"Only writing the word \'scooped\' ten times\",\"Drawing a picture of an icicle without reading the poem\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"This option combines collecting, singing with stress\\/intonation, and explaining the central idea.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21519,19,4,'English','en','Talking to Raghu Kaka','[\"- Raghu Kaka delivers fresh milk from his farm to houses in the town.\",\"- Milk can be used to make curd, butter, ghee, ice cream and masala buttermilk.\",\"- Cows and buffaloes give milk every day.\",\"- A simple masala buttermilk recipe: 1 cup curd, 1 cup water, salt, cumin powder, grated ginger, chopped coriander leaves, stir well.\",\"- Milk is good for health: keeps you strong and healthy.\",\"- Conversation shows how to ask about daily activities and show gratitude.\",\"- Key words: milk, curd, butter, ghee, ice cream, masala buttermilk, farm, cows, buffaloes, cans, deliver, fresh.\",\"- Remember to say “Good morning” and “Thank you” politely.\",\"- Use polite questions: “How are you?” “Did you bring fresh milk?”\",\"- The teacher encourages learners to identify main ideas and talk with community helpers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who delivers fresh milk to Riya and Aarav every morning?\",\"options\":[\"Aarav\'s father\",\"Raghu Kaka\",\"The shopkeeper\",\"Riya\'s mother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Raghu Kaka brings fresh milk every morning from his farm.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does Raghu Kaka get the milk from?\",\"options\":[\"A dairy shop\",\"The town market\",\"His farm\",\"A factory\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Raghu Kaka mentions he brings fresh milk every morning from his farm.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which animals does Raghu Kaka have on his farm to provide milk?\",\"options\":[\"Only cows\",\"Only buffaloes\",\"Both cows and buffaloes\",\"Goats and cows\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Raghu Kaka confirms he has both cows and buffaloes on his farm.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Raghu Kaka do immediately after milking the animals?\",\"options\":[\"He makes ice cream\",\"He pours the milk into cans\",\"He boils the milk\",\"He drinks the milk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Raghu Kaka says, \'I pour the milk into cans and deliver it to houses\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the conversation, what does Aarav\'s mother use milk for?\",\"options\":[\"To make ghee\",\"To make ice cream\",\"To make curd and tea\",\"To make butter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aarav mentions his mother makes curd and adds milk to tea.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to Raghu Kaka, why should children drink milk every day?\",\"options\":[\"To stay strong and healthy\",\"To make the tea tasty\",\"To help him deliver cans\",\"To learn how to milk cows\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Raghu Kaka advises Riya to drink milk every day to stay strong and healthy.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these items is NOT mentioned by Raghu Kaka as a product made from milk?\",\"options\":[\"Butter\",\"Ghee\",\"Ice cream\",\"Cheese\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Raghu Kaka mentions butter, ghee, and ice cream, but not cheese.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is Riya\'s favorite milk product?\",\"options\":[\"Curd\",\"Ice cream\",\"Tea\",\"Butter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Riya explicitly says, \'I love ice cream! It\'s my favourite milk product.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does Raghu Kaka feel when Riya says she loves ice cream?\",\"options\":[\"He is angry\",\"He is sad\",\"He is smiling\",\"He is surprised\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that Raghu Kaka is \'(smiling)\' when he responds to Riya.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What greeting does Riya use when she first sees Raghu Kaka?\",\"options\":[\"Goodbye\",\"Thank you\",\"Good morning\",\"Welcome\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The dialogue begins with Riya saying, \'Good morning, Raghu Kaka!\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what vehicle is Raghu Kaka using to carry the milk cans to the houses?\",\"options\":[\"A motorcycle\",\"A bicycle\",\"A bullock cart\",\"A van\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows Raghu Kaka standing next to a bicycle with milk cans attached to it.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/032_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Raghu Kaka doing for the little girl?\",\"options\":[\"Selling her a bicycle\",\"Feeding a cow\",\"Pouring milk into her vessel\",\"Making ice cream\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The drawing shows Raghu Kaka pouring milk from a small measure into the bowl held by the girl.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and enact.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/032_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first ingredient you need to take in a bowl?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Salt\",\"Curd\",\"Ginger\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to step 1, you must take one cup of curd in a bowl.\",\"topic\":\"Making Masala buttermilk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How much water should be added to one cup of curd?\",\"options\":[\"Two cups\",\"Half a cup\",\"One cup\",\"Three cups\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 2 states to add one cup of water to the curd.\",\"topic\":\"Making Masala buttermilk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In what form should the ginger be added to the buttermilk?\",\"options\":[\"Boiled\",\"Grated\",\"Fried\",\"Sliced\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 5 specifies adding grated ginger to the mixture.\",\"topic\":\"Making Masala buttermilk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which words are used in the text to describe Masala Buttermilk?\",\"options\":[\"Hot and spicy\",\"Bitter and sour\",\"Tasty, cool and healthy\",\"Salty and oily\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying the buttermilk is tasty, cool and healthy.\",\"topic\":\"Making Masala buttermilk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you have just added salt and cumin powder, what is the next ingredient to add?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Grated ginger\",\"Chopped coriander\",\"Curd\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 4 is adding salt and cumin, and Step 5 is adding grated ginger.\",\"topic\":\"Making Masala buttermilk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What must be done to the coriander leaves before adding them to the bowl?\",\"options\":[\"They must be dried\",\"They must be boiled\",\"They must be chopped\",\"They must be ground into powder\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 6 mentions adding chopped coriander leaves.\",\"topic\":\"Making Masala buttermilk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these ingredients is added in a \'powder\' form according to the recipe?\",\"options\":[\"Ginger\",\"Cumin\",\"Coriander\",\"Water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The list of ingredients mentions \'cumin powder\'.\",\"topic\":\"Making Masala buttermilk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final step to perform before the Masala Buttermilk is ready?\",\"options\":[\"Mix it well\",\"Add water\",\"Stir it\",\"Add salt\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 7, the last step, is to stir the mixture.\",\"topic\":\"Making Masala buttermilk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the list of ingredients, which of these is NOT needed to make this recipe?\",\"options\":[\"Sugar\",\"Salt\",\"Water\",\"Curd\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The recipe lists curd, water, salt, coriander, ginger, and cumin, but not sugar.\",\"topic\":\"Making Masala buttermilk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In which step do you add the grated ginger?\",\"options\":[\"Step 2\",\"Step 4\",\"Step 5\",\"Step 7\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists adding grated ginger as the 5th step.\",\"topic\":\"Making Masala buttermilk\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21520,19,4,'English','en','Maharashtra Day','[\"Maharashtra Day is celebrated on 1st May every year.\",\"The state of Maharashtra was established on 1st May 1960.\",\"Maharashtra Day is also called Kamgar Din (Labour Day).\",\"On Labour Day we thank all workers like factory workers, drivers, cleaners, etc.\",\"The flag of Maharashtra (Tiranga) is unfurled on Maharashtra Day.\",\"The state song of Maharashtra is called Rajyageet.\",\"Maharashtra is known for its rich culture, heritage, delicious food, and folk songs.\",\"Mumbai is the capital city of Maharashtra and is called the Financial Capital of India.\",\"Neighbouring states of Maharashtra are Gujarat, Karnataka, Telangana, and Goa.\",\"The national flag (Tiranga) is also unfurled in schools on Maharashtra Day.\",\"Maharashtra Day is a day of pride and joy for people of the state.\",\"The day reminds us of the dignity of labour and the importance of workers.\",\"Children’s Day is celebrated on 1st November.\",\"Teachers’ Day is celebrated on 5th September.\",\"Republic Day is celebrated on 26th January.\",\"Independence Day is celebrated on 15th August.\",\"Science Day is celebrated on 28th February.\",\"The flag of India is also unfurled on Republic Day.\",\"Maharashtra Day is a public holiday in the state.\",\"People write slogans and poems to celebrate Maharashtra Day.\",\"Students can write about their favourite food, sportsperson, festival, and science topics.\"]','[{\"q\":\"On which date is Maharashtra Day celebrated every year?\",\"options\":[\"15th August\",\"26th January\",\"1st May\",\"2nd October\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Maharashtra day is celebrated on 1st May.\",\"topic\":\"Maharashtra Day\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which year was the state of Maharashtra established?\",\"options\":[\"1947\",\"1950\",\"1960\",\"1966\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Maharashtra state was established in 1960.\",\"topic\":\"Maharashtra Day\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the national flag of India called in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Rajyageet\",\"Tiranga\",\"Saffron\",\"Mudra\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the national flag as (Tiranga).\",\"topic\":\"Maharashtra Day\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why is 1st May a special day for the people of Maharashtra?\",\"options\":[\"It is a day for brainstorming.\",\"The state was established on this day.\",\"It is the day to learn new languages.\",\"It is the day to visit neighbouring states.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that Maharashtra state was established on this day.\",\"topic\":\"Maharashtra Day\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the national flag unfurled on Maharashtra Day?\",\"options\":[\"Only in houses\",\"Only in markets\",\"In schools and state government offices\",\"In neighbouring states\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the flag is unfurled in schools and state government offices.\",\"topic\":\"Maharashtra Day\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which song is sung specifically on the occasion of Maharashtra Day?\",\"options\":[\"The National Anthem\",\"A brainstorming song\",\"The Rajyageet of Maharashtra\",\"A song about neighbouring states\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that on this occasion, we sing the Rajyageet of Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"Maharashtra Day\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is at school on 1st May, what activity from the text are they most likely to see?\",\"options\":[\"A brainstorming competition\",\"Unfurling of the Tiranga\",\"Learning a new language\",\"Visiting a government office\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the Tiranga is unfurled in schools on this day.\",\"topic\":\"Maharashtra Day\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which state\'s map is shown with various cultural symbols?\",\"options\":[\"Gujarat\",\"Maharashtra\",\"Goa\",\"Madhya Pradesh\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the map of Maharashtra state as mentioned in the topic.\",\"topic\":\"Maharashtra Day\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/034_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which historical symbol is placed in the center of the map?\",\"options\":[\"The Gateway of India\",\"A person playing a musical instrument\",\"The Royal Seal (Rajmudra)\",\"A saint sitting down\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The image shows the Rajmudra (Royal Seal) positioned in the center of the state map.\",\"topic\":\"Maharashtra Day\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/034_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what two feelings do people express while celebrating Maharashtra Day?\",\"options\":[\"Fear and sadness\",\"Joy and pride\",\"Anger and pride\",\"Joy and surprise\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says people celebrate this day with joy and pride.\",\"topic\":\"Maharashtra Day\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"On which date is Kamgar Din celebrated in Maharashtra?\",\"options\":[\"15th August\",\"26th January\",\"1st May\",\"2nd October\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 1st May is celebrated as Kamgar Din.\",\"topic\":\"Kamgar Din\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which city is known as the \'Financial Capital of India\'?\",\"options\":[\"Pune\",\"Nagpur\",\"Nashik\",\"Mumbai\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Mumbai is called the Financial Capital of India.\",\"topic\":\"Kamgar Din\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the English name for \'Kamgar Din\'?\",\"options\":[\"Independence Day\",\"Labour Day\",\"Republic Day\",\"Children\'s Day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Kamgar Din is also celebrated as Labour Day.\",\"topic\":\"Kamgar Din\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why do we celebrate Kamgar Din?\",\"options\":[\"To visit new forts\",\"To thank all workers\",\"To eat delicious food\",\"To sing folk songs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says that on this day, we thank all workers such as factory workers, drivers, and cleaners.\",\"topic\":\"Kamgar Din\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the celebration of Kamgar Din signify?\",\"options\":[\"The wealth of the capital\",\"The history of forts\",\"The dignity of labour\",\"The flow of rivers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the celebration of this day signifies the dignity of labour.\",\"topic\":\"Kamgar Din\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned as something Maharashtra is famous for?\",\"options\":[\"Rich culture\",\"Delicious food\",\"Snowy mountains\",\"Heritage history\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions culture, food, and history, but does not mention snowy mountains.\",\"topic\":\"Kamgar Din\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to thank a \'cleaner\' for their hard work on 1st May, which day are you observing?\",\"options\":[\"Heritage Day\",\"Kamgar Din\",\"Mumbai Day\",\"Food Festival Day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies cleaners as workers we thank on Kamgar Din.\",\"topic\":\"Kamgar Din\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which group of people are specifically honored on May 1st?\",\"options\":[\"Only factory workers\",\"Only drivers and cleaners\",\"All workers including factory workers, drivers, and cleaners\",\"Only people living in the dream city\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions thanking \'all workers\' and lists factory workers, drivers, and cleaners as examples.\",\"topic\":\"Kamgar Din\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does the text describe the relationship between Mumbai and Maharashtra?\",\"options\":[\"Mumbai is a river in Maharashtra\",\"Mumbai is the capital of Maharashtra\",\"Mumbai is a folk song of Maharashtra\",\"Mumbai is a fort in Maharashtra\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that Mumbai is the capital of Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"Kamgar Din\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text best describes the respect given to the work done by labourers?\",\"options\":[\"Financial\",\"Dignity\",\"Heritage\",\"Famous\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the phrase \'dignity of labour\' to signify the importance of the day.\",\"topic\":\"Kamgar Din\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21521,19,4,'English','en','Teddy at the Bus Stop','[\"- Teddy is a soft toy that can be lost and found.\",\"- A little girl and her father waited for a bus at the bus stop.\",\"- The girl forgot her teddy on the bench when she boarded the bus.\",\"- A kind lady saw the teddy and put it on a book so it was visible.\",\"- Three naughty boys played with the teddy and its arm came off.\",\"- The boys sewed the arm back on the teddy.\",\"- A lady with two children came, asked to take the teddy, but the lady said it belonged to someone else.\",\"- The children left a small candy for the teddy.\",\"- Many people saw the teddy waiting all day.\",\"- The next morning the teddy was gone, but a note was left on the bench.\",\"- The note thanked everyone for their kindness and said the teddy’s arm felt better.\",\"- The story teaches kindness, caring for others’ belongings, and the importance of returning lost items.\",\"- Key vocabulary: bus stop, teddy bear, kind, owner, sewed, candy, lost, found, note.\",\"- The sequence of events: waiting → forgetting → lady finds → boys play → arm breaks → boys sew → lady with children → candy → waiting all day → teddy gone → note left.\",\"- The story shows that people can help each other even if they don’t know the owner.\",\"- The note is a way to thank those who helped.\",\"- The teddy’s arm was fixed by sewing, showing how small acts help.\",\"- The story can be used to practice reading, writing, and speaking skills.\",\"- It also helps students learn about empathy and responsibility.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where were the little girl and her father waiting in the morning?\",\"options\":[\"At the railway station\",\"At the bus stop\",\"At the school gate\",\"In the park\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states they were waiting for the bus at the bus stop.\",\"topic\":\"A kind lady finds Teddy\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the little girl holding while waiting?\",\"options\":[\"A school bag\",\"A water bottle\",\"A soft teddy bear\",\"A story book\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the girl was holding her soft teddy bear.\",\"topic\":\"A kind lady finds Teddy\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the girl forget her Teddy at the bus stop?\",\"options\":[\"She did not like the toy anymore\",\"She gave it to her father\",\"She boarded the bus quickly\",\"She fell asleep on the bench\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says she boarded quickly, but she forgot her Teddy on the bench.\",\"topic\":\"A kind lady finds Teddy\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where exactly was the Teddy left behind?\",\"options\":[\"On the bus\",\"On the road\",\"On the bench\",\"Under a tree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states she forgot her Teddy on the bench at the bus stop.\",\"topic\":\"A kind lady finds Teddy\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who arrived at the bus stop after the girl had left?\",\"options\":[\"A little boy\",\"A kind lady\",\"A bus driver\",\"A policeman\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that after a while, a kind lady came to the bus stop.\",\"topic\":\"A kind lady finds Teddy\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the lady say when she saw the Teddy?\",\"options\":[\"\\\"Oh! poor Teddy\\\"\",\"\\\"What a dirty toy\\\"\",\"\\\"I will take this home\\\"\",\"\\\"Who lost this bag?\\\"\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The lady expressed sympathy by saying, \'Oh! poor Teddy\'.\",\"topic\":\"A kind lady finds Teddy\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the lady use to prop up the Teddy on the bench?\",\"options\":[\"A bag\",\"A chair\",\"A book\",\"A box\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says she put Teddy on a book and placed it on the bench.\",\"topic\":\"A kind lady finds Teddy\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the lady place the Teddy \'properly\' on the bench?\",\"options\":[\"So she could play with it\",\"So it could be seen easily\",\"To keep it away from the rain\",\"To hide it from others\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states she placed it properly so that it could be seen easily.\",\"topic\":\"A kind lady finds Teddy\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What did the lady believe the owner would do?\",\"options\":[\"Buy a new toy\",\"Never come back\",\"Forget about the Teddy\",\"Surely come back soon\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The lady said, \'Your owner must be looking for you and will surely come back soon.\'\",\"topic\":\"A kind lady finds Teddy\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text best describes the lady\'s character?\",\"options\":[\"Quick\",\"Kind\",\"Forgetful\",\"Little\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly refers to her as a \'kind lady\'.\",\"topic\":\"A kind lady finds Teddy\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How many boys reached the spot mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'three naughty boys reached there\'.\",\"topic\":\"Three naughty boys arrive\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What word is used to describe the boys in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Quiet\",\"Helpful\",\"Naughty\",\"Kind\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly describes them as \'naughty boys\'.\",\"topic\":\"Three naughty boys arrive\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did one of the boys shout when he saw the Teddy?\",\"options\":[\"\\\"Hey, look! A Teddy!\\\"\",\"\\\"Where is the bus?\\\"\",\"\\\"Let\'s go home!\\\"\",\"\\\"I am hungry!\\\"\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text records the shout as \'Hey, look! A Teddy!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Three naughty boys arrive\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What action did one of the boys take when he saw the Teddy?\",\"options\":[\"He whispered\",\"He shouted\",\"He cried\",\"He ran away\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'one of them shouted\'.\",\"topic\":\"Three naughty boys arrive\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'Soon, three naughty boys reached there\', what does \'reached\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Left a place\",\"Arrived at a place\",\"Ran away from\",\"Looked at\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Reached means to arrive at a specific destination.\",\"topic\":\"Three naughty boys arrive\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the text suggests that the boys arrived shortly after something else happened?\",\"options\":[\"Naughty\",\"Shouted\",\"Soon\",\"Look\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'Soon\' indicates that not much time had passed.\",\"topic\":\"Three naughty boys arrive\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If there were two groups of the same number of naughty boys, how many boys would there be in total?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Six\",\"Nine\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"There were 3 boys; two groups of 3 equals 6 (3 + 3 = 6).\",\"topic\":\"Three naughty boys arrive\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which punctuation mark in the boy\'s speech shows that he was excited?\",\"options\":[\"Comma\",\"Full stop\",\"Exclamation mark\",\"Question mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The exclamation marks in \'Hey, look! A Teddy!\' show excitement.\",\"topic\":\"Three naughty boys arrive\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the boy use the words \'Hey, look!\'?\",\"options\":[\"To tell a secret\",\"To get the attention of the other boys\",\"To talk to the Teddy\",\"To ask a question\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The phrase is used to draw others\' attention to something seen.\",\"topic\":\"Three naughty boys arrive\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, how did the boys feel when they saw the Teddy?\",\"options\":[\"Surprised or excited\",\"Bored and tired\",\"Sad and lonely\",\"Angry and mean\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Shouting \'Hey, look!\' indicates a feeling of surprise or excitement.\",\"topic\":\"Three naughty boys arrive\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21522,19,4,'English','en','From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold','[\"- Sugarcane is a tall plant grown in fields.\",\"- Farmers cut sugarcane when it is ready for harvest.\",\"- The cut cane is taken to a jaggery‑making place called Gurhal.\",\"- In Gurhal a big machine crushes the cane to get sweet juice.\",\"- The juice is poured into a big iron pan and heated over fire.\",\"- While heating, the juice thickens and turns brown, becoming jaggery.\",\"- Workers stir the juice to help it cook evenly.\",\"- The thickened jaggery is poured into small moulds to set.\",\"- After cooling, jaggery blocks are ready for use.\",\"- Jaggery is a natural sweetener used in many Indian dishes.\",\"- The process shows how a plant becomes a sweet food.\",\"- The story of Rajveer shows how children learn by watching.\",\"- Jaggery is famous in Maharashtra and is used in tea and sweets.\",\"- The process involves crushing, heating, stirring, and moulding.\",\"- Understanding the steps helps students see science in everyday life.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did Rajveer live according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Pune\",\"Karveer near Kolhapur\",\"Mumbai\",\"Nagpur\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Rajveer lived in Karveer near Kolhapur in Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the \'Gurhal\' mentioned in the story?\",\"options\":[\"A place to grow sugarcane\",\"A place to sell tea\",\"A jaggery-making place\",\"A school for Grade Four students\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines Gurhal as a jaggery-making place.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what crop is the man standing next to in the field?\",\"options\":[\"Wheat\",\"Rice\",\"Sugarcane\",\"Cotton\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the tall sugarcane crop that Rajveer saw in the field.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/039_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Rajveer find it difficult to cut the sugarcane?\",\"options\":[\"The cane was too soft\",\"He was too small to do it\",\"He did not have a knife\",\"The wind was too strong\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"His father told him he was too small to cut the cane after he found it difficult.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how are the sugarcane canes being transported to the Gurhal?\",\"options\":[\"On a tractor\",\"On a bullock-cart\",\"In a truck\",\"By hand\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows sugarcane loaded onto a cart pulled by two bullocks.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/039_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What happens immediately after the sugarcane is crushed in the big machine?\",\"options\":[\"It turns into brown blocks\",\"It is poured into moulds\",\"Sweet juice flows out\",\"Steam comes out\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says a big machine crushed the sugarcane and sweet juice flowed out.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, what is the correct order of the jaggery-making process?\",\"options\":[\"Boiling -> Crushing -> Moulding -> Cutting\",\"Cutting -> Crushing -> Boiling -> Moulding\",\"Moulding -> Boiling -> Crushing -> Cutting\",\"Crushing -> Cutting -> Moulding -> Boiling\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The process starts with cutting the canes, then crushing for juice, boiling the juice, and finally pouring into moulds.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the workers doing with the juice in the big iron pan?\",\"options\":[\"Drinking the juice\",\"Washing the sugarcane\",\"Stirring the juice over a fire\",\"Planting new seeds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows workers stirring the juice in a large pan over a fire to make it thick.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/039_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Prakash uncle tell Rajveer to be careful near the iron pan?\",\"options\":[\"The juice was too sweet\",\"The pan was made of iron\",\"Fire can hurt people\",\"The wooden sticks were heavy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Prakash uncle warned him because fire helps but can also hurt.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What tool did the workers use to make the juice thick and brown?\",\"options\":[\"Iron spoons\",\"Long wooden sticks\",\"Plastic pipes\",\"Bullock-carts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions workers stirred the juice with long wooden sticks.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If Rajveer wants to help make the jaggery solid and shaped, what should he use?\",\"options\":[\"The crushing machine\",\"The bullock-cart\",\"Small moulds\",\"The iron pan\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says juice is poured into small moulds to make jaggery blocks.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these ingredients did Rajveer\'s grandmother use to make tea in the evening?\",\"options\":[\"Candy\",\"Sugarcane juice\",\"Jaggery\",\"Puranpoli\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the grandmother made tea using jaggery.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Rajveer feel proud at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"He learned how to drive a tractor\",\"Kolhapuri jaggery is famous across Maharashtra\",\"He cut all the sugarcane by himself\",\"He made tea for his grandmother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He felt proud because of the fame of his village\'s jaggery and his culture.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What did the workers remove from the juice while stirring it?\",\"options\":[\"The sweet taste\",\"All the stuff (impurities)\",\"The brown color\",\"The wooden sticks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says workers removed all the stuff from the juice to clean it.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which vehicle was NOT mentioned as a way to transport sugarcane in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Tractors\",\"Trucks\",\"Bicycles\",\"Bullock-carts\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions bullock-carts, tractors, and trucks, but not bicycles.\",\"topic\":\"From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to Teddy\'s arm when the children picked it up to play?\",\"options\":[\"It got dirty\",\"It came off\",\"It changed color\",\"It became longer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when they picked it up, suddenly Teddy’s arm came off.\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the lady tell her children that they could not take the Teddy?\",\"options\":[\"Because it was broken\",\"Because it was too old\",\"Because it belongs to someone else\",\"Because it was dirty\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The lady said, \'No, it belongs to someone else. Let’s leave it here for its owner.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the children leave for Teddy before they left?\",\"options\":[\"A small candy\",\"A new ribbon\",\"A toy car\",\"A piece of bread\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the children agreed and even left a small candy for Teddy.\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the lady\'s actions, what is the right thing to do if you find a lost toy in a public place?\",\"options\":[\"Take it home for yourself\",\"Throw it in the dustbin\",\"Leave it safely for its owner to find\",\"Give it to a stranger\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The lady demonstrates kindness and honesty by leaving the toy for its rightful owner.\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What did the people wonder about when they saw Teddy sitting on the bench in the evening?\",\"options\":[\"If Teddy was hungry\",\"If Teddy was cold\",\"If its owner would return\",\"If Teddy could talk\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says that at evening, people wondered if its owner would return.\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the note found the next morning?\",\"options\":[\"In Teddy\'s hand\",\"On the bench\",\"Under the candy\",\"On the ground\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states there was a short note on the bench.\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the note, who does Teddy refer to as his \'buddy\'?\",\"options\":[\"The lady\",\"The two children\",\"His owner\",\"The person who fixed his arm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Teddy thanks them for keeping him safe for his \'buddy\', which refers to his owner.\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the note, what was the most important thing Teddy thanked the friends for?\",\"options\":[\"Fixing his arm\",\"Giving him candy\",\"Keeping him safe for his buddy\",\"Sitting on the bench\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The note says, \'But most of all, thank you for keeping me safe for my buddy.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How did the person fix Teddy\'s arm after it came off?\",\"options\":[\"By using glue\",\"By tying it with a string\",\"By carefully sewing it\",\"By using sticky tape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'He carefully sewed the arm and put Teddy nicely on the bench again.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The note says \'My arm feels better now\'. What does this tell us about the person who fixed it?\",\"options\":[\"They were in a hurry\",\"They were very helpful and kind\",\"They did not know how to sew\",\"They wanted to keep the toy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Fixing the arm carefully shows the person was helpful and kind to the lost toy.\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what tools can be seen in the box that are being used to help Teddy?\",\"options\":[\"Pencils and paper\",\"Needle, thread, and scissors\",\"Hammer and nails\",\"Spoons and forks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a sewing kit with scissors and thread being used to fix the toy.\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/037_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the boy on the left doing while his friend fixes the arm?\",\"options\":[\"He is eating the candy\",\"He is holding Teddy steady to help his friend\",\"He is writing the thank you note\",\"He is running away with the toy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows one boy holding the bear while the other sews, showing teamwork.\",\"topic\":\"The Story of Teddy\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/037_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'sewed\' from the list?\",\"options\":[\"Stitched with a needle and thread\",\"Cut with a pair of scissors\",\"Painted with a brush\",\"Washed with water\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'sewed\' refers to the action of stitching cloth or materials together.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to a sweet treat?\",\"options\":[\"waited\",\"candy\",\"boarded\",\"belongs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Candy is a common term for a sweet or sugar-based treat.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'boarded\' mean when talking about a bus or a train?\",\"options\":[\"Jumped off\",\"Cleaned the windows\",\"Got onto the vehicle\",\"Waited at the station\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To board a vehicle means to get onto it to start a journey.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you feel relaxed and at ease in a chair, the chair is ______.\",\"options\":[\"wondered\",\"comfortable\",\"picked\",\"sewed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Comfortable describes a state of physical ease or relaxation.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes the action of staying in one place until something happens?\",\"options\":[\"waited\",\"boarded\",\"belongs\",\"candy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Waiting means staying in a place or delaying action until a particular time or event.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When you think about something because you are curious, you have ______.\",\"options\":[\"picked\",\"sewed\",\"wondered\",\"boarded\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To wonder means to think about something with curiosity or doubt.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence: \'This blue bag ______ to my sister.\'\",\"options\":[\"waited\",\"belongs\",\"comfortable\",\"picked\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Belongs\' is used to show ownership or that something is the property of someone.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word correctly completes this sentence: \'The girl ______ a flower from the garden.\'\",\"options\":[\"picked\",\"sewed\",\"candy\",\"comfortable\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Picked\' is the correct past tense verb for choosing or collecting a flower.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the list of words. Which of these words does NOT end in \'-ed\'?\",\"options\":[\"waited\",\"boarded\",\"belongs\",\"wondered\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Waited, boarded, and wondered are past tense verbs ending in -ed, while belongs ends in -s.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list is used to describe how a person feels rather than an action they did?\",\"options\":[\"comfortable\",\"sewed\",\"picked\",\"boarded\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Comfortable is an adjective describing a state of being, while the others are action verbs.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21523,19,4,'English','en','We Say, Thank You','[\"• ‘Thank you’ is said when someone gives or helps you.\",\"• ‘Please’ is used when you want something politely.\",\"• ‘Excuse me’ is said before you interrupt or when you sneeze.\",\"• ‘Sorry’ is said when you hurt someone or make a mistake.\",\"• Saying these words shows good manners and kindness.\",\"• We use ‘Thank you’ after receiving help or a gift.\",\"• We use ‘Please’ before asking for something.\",\"• ‘Excuse me’ can mean ‘Sorry’ or ‘Pardon me’ when we bump into someone.\",\"• ‘Sorry’ is used when we do something wrong.\",\"• Good manners make friends and keep peace.\",\"• When you help a friend tie shoelaces, you show kindness.\",\"• A small help can make someone’s day better.\",\"• Listening kindly and speaking politely keeps relationships strong.\",\"• Polite words are called ‘magic words’ because they make people happy.\",\"• We can pair a word with a picture to remember its meaning.\",\"• We can create short poems or posters to practice polite words.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, when should we say \'Excuse me\'?\",\"options\":[\"When we eat\",\"When we sneeze\",\"When we sleep\",\"When we run\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'And “Excuse me,” When we sneeze.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet say we should do with our toys?\",\"options\":[\"Hide them\",\"Break them\",\"Share them\",\"Keep them alone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'We share our toys, We don’t fight.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the children have their hands joined together. Which line from the poem does this action show?\",\"options\":[\"We open doors\",\"We greet our friends\",\"We say “Please”\",\"We share our toys\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Joining hands is a way to greet, matching the line \'We greet our friends\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/041_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the expression on the children\'s faces as they greet each other?\",\"options\":[\"They are crying\",\"They look angry\",\"They are smiling\",\"They look scared\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the children with happy, smiling faces, matching the line \'We smile each day\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/041_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to ask someone for help, which \'magic word\' mentioned in the poem should you use?\",\"options\":[\"Sorry\",\"Excuse me\",\"Please\",\"Thank you\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'Please\' is used when making a request or asking for something politely.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does the poet describe the way we should listen to others?\",\"options\":[\"Listen loudly\",\"Listen kindly\",\"Listen quickly\",\"Do not listen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'We listen kindly, To what they say.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the poem rhymes with the word \'sneeze\'?\",\"options\":[\"Toys\",\"Right\",\"Please\",\"Friends\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the poem, \'Please\' and \'sneeze\' are rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet call \'magic\' in the last part of the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Toys\",\"Manners\",\"Friends\",\"Doors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem concludes with \'Manners are magic, For me and you!\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned as a good manner in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Opening doors\",\"Sharing toys\",\"Fighting with others\",\"Saying Sorry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem explicitly says \'We don’t fight\', so fighting is not a good manner.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message the poet Sanjay Ahluwalia wants to give through this poem?\",\"options\":[\"Toys are very expensive\",\"We should only talk to friends\",\"Manners make life better for everyone\",\"Sneezing is bad for health\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem emphasizes that manners are \'magic\' for everyone, implying they improve our interactions.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who was struggling to tie his shoelaces in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Rudra\",\"Dhruv\",\"A teacher\",\"A group of friends\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Dhruv was struggling to tie his shoelaces.\",\"topic\":\"Helping Hands\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was Rudra doing before he noticed his classmate?\",\"options\":[\"He was studying in class.\",\"He was eating his lunch.\",\"He was playing with his friends.\",\"He was sleeping.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story begins by saying Rudra was playing with his friends when he noticed Dhruv.\",\"topic\":\"Helping Hands\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did Dhruv\'s face look when Rudra went to help him?\",\"options\":[\"It was sad.\",\"It lit up with joy.\",\"It looked angry.\",\"It looked tired.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Dhruv\'s face lit up with joy when Rudra went to help him.\",\"topic\":\"Helping Hands\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Rudra do to help Dhruv besides tying the laces?\",\"options\":[\"He gave him new shoes.\",\"He called a teacher.\",\"He explained how to tie shoelaces properly.\",\"He tied his own laces instead.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says Rudra bent down and explained how to tie shoelaces properly.\",\"topic\":\"Helping Hands\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the result of Rudra\'s help and Dhruv saying thank you?\",\"options\":[\"They both became friends.\",\"They stopped playing.\",\"They went to the classroom.\",\"They started a race.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that after the help and the thanks, they both became friends.\",\"topic\":\"Helping Hands\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given picture, what action is the boy in the yellow shirt performing?\",\"options\":[\"He is running away.\",\"He is helping his classmate tie his shoelaces.\",\"He is taking off his own shoes.\",\"He is pointing at the school building.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the boy in the yellow shirt (Rudra) kneeling to help the other boy with his laces.\",\"topic\":\"Helping Hands\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/042_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you see a friend who cannot open their water bottle, what should you do based on the lesson from this story?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore them and keep playing.\",\"Laugh at them for not being able to open it.\",\"Offer to help them open the bottle.\",\"Tell them to buy a new bottle.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story teaches that a small help can bring joy to someone else\'s life.\",\"topic\":\"Helping Hands\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text describes the act of being helpful and nice to others?\",\"options\":[\"Struggling\",\"Kindness\",\"Properly\",\"Noticed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying \'Kindness can make someone’s day better.\'\",\"topic\":\"Helping Hands\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given picture and the text, which boy is likely to be Dhruv?\",\"options\":[\"The boy in the yellow shirt who is kneeling.\",\"The boy in the orange shirt who is sitting and receiving help.\",\"The boy standing near the house in the background.\",\"The boy who is running in the field.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says Dhruv was struggling with laces and Rudra went to help him; the picture shows the boy in orange receiving help.\",\"topic\":\"Helping Hands\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/042_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message the author wants to convey through Rudra and Dhruv\'s story?\",\"options\":[\"Tying shoelaces is the most important skill.\",\"You should only play with your best friends.\",\"Small acts of help and kindness bring joy and build friendships.\",\"Always wear shoes when playing outside.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that small help brings joy and kindness makes days better.\",\"topic\":\"Helping Hands\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How should the learners read the poem according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Silently by themselves\",\"Aloud together as a class\",\"Only in their minds\",\"By writing it down\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to encourage learners to read the poem aloud together as a class.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Into how many groups should the students be divided for the singing activity?\",\"options\":[\"Three groups\",\"Four groups\",\"Two groups\",\"Five groups\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to divide students into two groups.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the poem does the first group sing?\",\"options\":[\"The whole poem\",\"The last four lines\",\"The first four lines\",\"Only the polite words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the first group sings the first four lines.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the poem does the other group sing?\",\"options\":[\"The first four lines\",\"The last four lines\",\"The middle lines\",\"The entire poem\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that the other group will sing the last four lines.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is told to do an action for the word \'please\', what should they do?\",\"options\":[\"Join their hands\",\"Jump up high\",\"Bow\",\"Clap their hands\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text gives the example of \'bow\' for the word \'please\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What action is suggested for the words \'thank you\'?\",\"options\":[\"Bow\",\"Join your hands\",\"Wave your hand\",\"Close your eyes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text gives the example of \'join your hands\' for \'thank you\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the students motivated to do for each polite word?\",\"options\":[\"Write them down\",\"Do the actions\",\"Draw a picture\",\"Repeat them ten times\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to motivate them to do the actions for each polite word.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, \'please\' and \'thank you\' are examples of what?\",\"options\":[\"Action words\",\"Polite words\",\"Singing words\",\"Group names\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to \'please\' and \'thank you\' as polite words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If there are 8 lines in the poem, which lines will the second group sing?\",\"options\":[\"Lines 1 to 4\",\"Lines 5 to 8\",\"Lines 1 to 8\",\"Lines 2 to 6\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the other group sings the last four lines, which would be 5 to 8 in an 8-line poem.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of dividing the class into two groups for this activity?\",\"options\":[\"To make the class noisy\",\"To sing different parts of the poem\",\"To see who sings louder\",\"To draw different pictures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The division is used so one group sings the first four lines and the other sings the last four.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21524,19,4,'English','en','The Giant Panda','[\"The giant panda is a very rare animal found only in the mountains of Western China and Tibet.\",\"It lives in bamboo forests at high altitudes.\",\"Its favourite food is bamboo – about 99 % of its diet.\",\"A panda can eat 12–38 kilograms of bamboo each day.\",\"Pandas have strong jaws and teeth to crush bamboo stalks.\",\"Adult pandas weigh 70–100 kilograms, sometimes more.\",\"A baby panda is called a cub and weighs about 100 grams at birth.\",\"Pandas are slow‑moving, peaceful and friendly animals.\",\"They are a symbol of peace and friendship in China.\",\"Pandas spend most of their day eating and resting.\",\"Only a few pandas remain in the world, so we must protect forests for them and other animals.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where is the giant panda found according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Mountains of Western China and Tibet\",\"Jungles of India and Sri Lanka\",\"Deserts of Africa\",\"Forests of Australia\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the giant panda is found in the mountains of Western China and Tibet.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the giant panda\'s favorite food?\",\"options\":[\"Sugarcane\",\"Bamboo\",\"Small insects\",\"Fruits\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that their favourite food is bamboo.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What makes the giant panda special among other animals?\",\"options\":[\"It is the fastest animal in the world\",\"It is one of the rarest animals in the world\",\"It is the only animal that lives in China\",\"It is the heaviest animal on land\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks if you knew that the giant panda is one of the rarest animals in the world.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In which specific environment do pandas live?\",\"options\":[\"Lowland swamps\",\"Dry sandy deserts\",\"Bamboo forests at high altitudes\",\"Coastal beaches\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that pandas live in bamboo forests at high altitudes.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a panda eats a meal, what percentage of it is likely to be bamboo?\",\"options\":[\"12%\",\"38%\",\"70%\",\"99%\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says bamboo makes up 99% of their diet.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the introductory activity, which letter would you assign to a giant panda?\",\"options\":[\"\'p\' because it is a pet\",\"\'w\' because it is a wild animal\",\"\'b\' because it lives in bamboo\",\"\'c\' because it is from China\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity asks to write \'w\' for wild animals and \'p\' for pets; since pandas live in mountain forests, they are wild animals.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a panda has eaten 15 kilograms of bamboo today, is it within its normal daily range?\",\"options\":[\"No, it is too much\",\"No, it is too little\",\"Yes, because it eats between 12–38 kilograms\",\"Yes, because it eats exactly 15 kilograms every day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states a panda can eat up to 12–38 kilograms of bamboo every day.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does a panda have strong jaws and teeth?\",\"options\":[\"To fight other wild animals\",\"To climb high altitude mountains\",\"To crush bamboo stalks\",\"To carry its heavy body weight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that pandas have strong jaws and teeth to crush bamboo stalks.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the typical weight range for an adult panda?\",\"options\":[\"12 to 38 kilograms\",\"70 to 100 kilograms\",\"99 to 100 kilograms\",\"Over 200 kilograms\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states adult pandas usually weigh between 70 to 100 kilograms.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these weights would be considered normal for a fully grown panda?\",\"options\":[\"25 kilograms\",\"50 kilograms\",\"85 kilograms\",\"150 kilograms\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"85 kilograms falls within the 70 to 100 kilograms range mentioned for adult pandas.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and learn\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is a baby panda called?\",\"options\":[\"A calf\",\"A cub\",\"A kitten\",\"A pup\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that a baby panda is called a cub.\",\"topic\":\"Life and Conservation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How much does a baby panda weigh when it is born?\",\"options\":[\"About 100 grams\",\"About 500 grams\",\"About 1 kilogram\",\"About 10 grams\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a baby panda weighs only about 100 grams at birth.\",\"topic\":\"Life and Conservation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In China, the panda is considered a symbol of which two things?\",\"options\":[\"Strength and power\",\"Speed and hunting\",\"Peace and friendship\",\"Wealth and luck\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that pandas are considered a symbol of peace and friendship in China.\",\"topic\":\"Life and Conservation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the two main activities pandas do during the day?\",\"options\":[\"Running and jumping\",\"Eating and resting\",\"Hunting and climbing\",\"Playing and swimming\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states they spend most of their day eating and resting.\",\"topic\":\"Life and Conservation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes how a panda moves?\",\"options\":[\"Fast-moving\",\"Slow-moving\",\"Quickly\",\"Rapidly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the panda as a slow-moving animal.\",\"topic\":\"Life and Conservation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the giant panda loved all over the world?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is very fast\",\"Because it is a kind animal\",\"Because it lives in China\",\"Because it eats bamboo\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the giant panda is loved all over the world as a kind animal.\",\"topic\":\"Life and Conservation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If we want to help pandas and other animals live safely, what action should we take?\",\"options\":[\"Build more houses\",\"Keep them in cages\",\"Protect forests\",\"Feed them 100 grams of food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests we should protect forests so pandas and other animals can live safely.\",\"topic\":\"Life and Conservation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the description of a panda as \'peaceful\', how would it likely behave around other animals?\",\"options\":[\"It would try to fight them\",\"It would move away quietly and not cause trouble\",\"It would run very fast to catch them\",\"It would make a lot of noise\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Being peaceful and slow-moving implies a calm behavior rather than aggression or speed.\",\"topic\":\"Life and Conservation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text imply about the current population of pandas?\",\"options\":[\"There are too many pandas\",\"Pandas are found everywhere\",\"Their numbers are very low\",\"They are increasing every day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'There are only few pandas left in the world,\' implying a low population.\",\"topic\":\"Life and Conservation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main reason provided for protecting forests?\",\"options\":[\"To make the world look green\",\"So that pandas and other animals can live safely\",\"To help pandas grow to 100 grams\",\"To make pandas move faster\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links protecting forests directly to the safety of pandas and other animals.\",\"topic\":\"Life and Conservation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is speaking in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A tiger\",\"A panda\",\"A lion\",\"A bear\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'Hi! I am a panda.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the very first instruction given in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Read and write\",\"Look and tell\",\"Listen and repeat\",\"Complete the profile\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text begins with the instruction \'Listen and repeat.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the panda want the reader to complete?\",\"options\":[\"A drawing\",\"A story\",\"A profile\",\"A poem\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The panda says, \'Complete my profile.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What greeting does the panda use to address the reader?\",\"options\":[\"Hello!\",\"Hi!\",\"Good morning!\",\"Welcome!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The panda starts its introduction with the word \'Hi!\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the instruction \'Listen and repeat\' mean for a student?\",\"options\":[\"Hear the words and say them again\",\"Write the words in a notebook\",\"Draw a picture of the panda\",\"Read the text silently\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To repeat means to say or do something again after hearing it.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'I am a panda\', what is the speaker doing?\",\"options\":[\"Asking a question\",\"Giving an order\",\"Introducing itself\",\"Telling a secret\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"By saying \'I am a panda\', the speaker is telling the reader who it is.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you follow the panda\'s request, what action will you take?\",\"options\":[\"You will ignore the panda\",\"You will fill in information about the panda\",\"You will draw a bamboo forest\",\"You will listen to a song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Completing a profile involves filling in specific details or information.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instructions, which action should be done immediately after listening?\",\"options\":[\"Writing\",\"Sleeping\",\"Repeating\",\"Coloring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instruction \'Listen and repeat\' places repeating directly after listening.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'Complete my profile\', who does the word \'my\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher\",\"The student\",\"The panda\",\"The textbook\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The panda is the one speaking (\'I am a panda\'), so \'my\' refers to the panda.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the text indicates that this is an interactive activity for the student?\",\"options\":[\"Panda\",\"Complete\",\"Hi\",\"Am\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Complete\' is a command that requires the student to perform a task.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21525,19,4,'English','en','True Friends','[\"True friends are people who help each other without asking for anything in return.\",\"A best friend is someone you trust, share secrets with, and spend time together.\",\"Honesty means telling the truth and being fair to others.\",\"Friendship is shown by sharing, caring, and being honest.\",\"In the story, Gopi and Krishna were good friends and neighbours.\",\"Krishna’s crops were ruined by heavy rains, showing how nature can hurt farmers.\",\"Gopi lent land to Krishna so he could grow crops, showing kindness.\",\"Krishna found a golden statue while tilling the land.\",\"The king listened to the friends and decided to buy the statue.\",\"Tenali Raman suggested using the money to help poor farmers.\",\"A monument can remember a good friendship for everyone.\",\"The moral of the story is that honesty and friendship are very important.\",\"When friends face problems, they should help each other and be honest.\",\"A good friend is always ready to share his land, time, or money if needed.\",\"True friends respect each other’s property and do not keep it for themselves.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What was the statue that the two men brought to the court made of?\",\"options\":[\"Silver\",\"Bronze\",\"Gold\",\"Stone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions a \'beautiful statue of a golden swan\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who actually found the statue while tilling the land?\",\"options\":[\"Gopi\",\"Krishna\",\"Tenali Raman\",\"The King\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Gopi states that \'Krishna got this precious statue\' while tilling the land.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Gopi lend his land to Krishna?\",\"options\":[\"Because Krishna was his brother\",\"Because Krishna\'s crops were ruined by heavy rains\",\"Because Krishna wanted to find a statue\",\"Because Gopi had too much land\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Gopi lent the land because Krishna\'s crops were ruined by natural disaster (heavy rains).\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to Gopi, why did he refuse to take the statue from Krishna?\",\"options\":[\"He thought the statue was unlucky\",\"He believed it belonged to the king\",\"He believed it belonged to the finder, Krishna\",\"He did not like the golden swan\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Gopi said he could not take it as it belongs to the finder, which is Krishna.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a farmer\'s crops are destroyed by a flood today, which part of Tenali Raman\'s suggestion would help him?\",\"options\":[\"Erecting a stone pillar\",\"Buying a golden statue\",\"Using a fund maintained for peasants\",\"Visiting the royal court\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tenali suggested a fund for peasants who face troubles due to natural disasters.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the King and the courtiers admire Gopi and Krishna?\",\"options\":[\"For their wealth and land\",\"For their friendship and honesty\",\"For their skill in farming\",\"For finding a golden statue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states they admired their friendship and honesty.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the purpose of erecting a pillar as a monument?\",\"options\":[\"To mark the boundary of the land\",\"To show the King\'s power\",\"To be an inspiration of selfless friendship to people\",\"To help farmers grow more crops\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Raman suggested the monument could be an inspiration to people regarding selfless friendship.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who did the King look at to find a solution to the farmers\' problem?\",\"options\":[\"Gopi\",\"Krishna\",\"Tenali Raman\",\"The Queen\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The king looked at Tenali Raman for a solution.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'unearthed\' mean in the sentence \'He unearthed it and wanted to hand it over to me\'?\",\"options\":[\"To bury something deep\",\"To dig something up out of the ground\",\"To break something into pieces\",\"To hide something from others\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the context of tilling land and finding a statue, unearthed means to dig it up.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which quality best describes the friendship between Gopi and Krishna based on their actions?\",\"options\":[\"Selfish\",\"Selfless\",\"Greedy\",\"Jealous\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tenali Raman refers to it as \'selfless friendship\' because they both thought of the other person first.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, who is shown sitting on the royal throne?\",\"options\":[\"Tenali Raman\",\"Gopi\",\"Raja Krishnadevaraya\",\"Krishna\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the King (Raja Krishnadevaraya) seated on the throne.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/046_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the person with the bald head and a ponytail (Tenali Raman) doing?\",\"options\":[\"He is tilling the land\",\"He is arguing with the farmers\",\"He is speaking and gesturing to provide a solution\",\"He is carrying a golden swan\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows Tenali Raman gesturing with his hand as he addresses the King and the farmers.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and express.\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/046_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is included in the list provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"statue\",\"palace\",\"kingdom\",\"soldier\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'statue\' is the first word listed in the vocabulary section of the text.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are learners encouraged to narrate in their own words?\",\"options\":[\"A poem\",\"A story\",\"A song\",\"A letter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to encourage learners to narrate a story in their own words.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to a person who works on a farm?\",\"options\":[\"statue\",\"treasure\",\"peasant\",\"honest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A peasant is a traditional term for a small farmer or agricultural laborer.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should learners discuss about a story?\",\"options\":[\"The spelling of words\",\"The number of pages\",\"Its theme\",\"The price of the book\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests encouraging learners to discuss the theme of the story.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes someone who always tells the truth?\",\"options\":[\"tilling\",\"honest\",\"treasure\",\"peasant\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Honest is the word used to describe a person who is truthful and sincere.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of stories should learners be encouraged to write based on their experiences?\",\"options\":[\"True news reports\",\"Imaginary stories\",\"History textbooks\",\"Dictionary entries\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions encouraging learners to write imaginary stories based on experiences.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a farmer is preparing the land for crops, which word from the list describes this action?\",\"options\":[\"tilling\",\"treasure\",\"statue\",\"honest\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Tilling is the process of preparing land for growing crops.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is talking about why they like or dislike a person in a story, what are they doing according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Finding treasure\",\"Tilling the soil\",\"Expressing views on a character\",\"Writing a dictionary\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to express their views on any character.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to a collection of very valuable objects like gold or jewels?\",\"options\":[\"peasant\",\"statue\",\"treasure\",\"tilling\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Treasure refers to a store of precious metals, jewels, or other valuable objects.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these activities involves using one\'s own imagination according to the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Copying the word \'statue\'\",\"Writing imaginary stories\",\"Reading the word \'peasant\'\",\"Listing the word \'honest\'\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Writing imaginary stories requires the use of imagination as suggested in the teacher\'s instructions.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21526,19,4,'English','en','Eat Healthy, Stay Better!','[\"- Eating healthy food keeps the body strong and happy.\",\"- Fruits and vegetables are full of vitamins that help you grow and stay fit.\",\"- Milk is good for bones and teeth and gives energy for play.\",\"- Eating too many sweets can upset the stomach and make you feel tired.\",\"- Water is essential; drink enough every day to stay active.\",\"- Resting well helps the body recover and keeps the mind sharp.\",\"- Healthy foods include carrots, tomatoes, apples, bananas, sprouts, lentils, rice, roti, eggs, fish, and milk.\",\"- A balanced meal should have at least two servings of grains and vegetables.\",\"- Avoid eating too many chocolates or sugary snacks.\",\"- If you feel a tummyache, ask a parent or a doctor for help.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did Aman want to eat for breakfast, lunch, and dinner?\",\"options\":[\"Fruits and vegetables\",\"Milk and bread\",\"Chocolates\",\"Healthy food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Aman liked to eat chocolates a lot and wanted to eat them all the time for every meal.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did Aman feel when he woke up with a tummyache?\",\"options\":[\"Strong and happy\",\"Weak and tired\",\"Hungry and excited\",\"Angry and loud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the story, when Aman woke up with a tummyache, he felt weak and tired.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Aman\'s stomach upset according to the doctor?\",\"options\":[\"He drank too much milk\",\"He ate too many sweets\",\"He did not sleep enough\",\"He played too much\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The doctor told Aman his stomach was upset because he ate too many sweets.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the doctor give Aman to help him learn about better food choices?\",\"options\":[\"A box of chocolates\",\"A new toy\",\"A small chart showing healthy food items\",\"A picture book about doctors\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The doctor gave Aman medicines and a small chart showing healthy food items.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, whom should you consult if you have a stomachache?\",\"options\":[\"A teacher\",\"A friend\",\"A doctor\",\"A shopkeeper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks \'If you have a stomachache, whom should you consult?\' and then shows Aman\'s mother taking him to a doctor.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the doctor\'s advice to Aman regarding his diet?\",\"options\":[\"He must eat only chocolates\",\"He must eat healthy food too\",\"He should stop eating breakfast\",\"He should only eat at night\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The doctor explicitly told Aman, \'You must eat healthy food too.\'\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happened just after Aman\'s eyes slowly closed while reading on his bed?\",\"options\":[\"His mother took the chart away\",\"He woke up feeling better\",\"Something strange happened with the chart\",\"He finished his medicines\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that as his eyes closed, something strange happened where items on the chart began to pop out.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What did the fruits and vegetables do after popping out from the paper?\",\"options\":[\"They ran away\",\"They started singing for Aman\",\"They went back into the chart\",\"They talked to Aman\'s mother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the fruits, vegetables, and other foods started singing for Aman.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which order did the events happen in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Aman ate healthy food, then got a tummyache, then saw a doctor\",\"Aman saw a doctor, then ate chocolates, then got a tummyache\",\"Aman ate many chocolates, got a tummyache, then saw a doctor\",\"Aman read a chart, then got a tummyache, then ate chocolates\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story follows Aman eating chocolates, getting a tummyache, and then visiting the doctor.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where was Aman when the food items started popping out of the chart?\",\"options\":[\"In the kitchen\",\"At the doctor\'s clinic\",\"On his bed\",\"In the school\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says Aman was reading the chart on his bed when his eyes closed and the strange event happened.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Aman doing with the food on the plate?\",\"options\":[\"He is pushing it away\",\"He is happily eating the sweets\",\"He is sharing it with his mother\",\"He is counting the items\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Aman with a wide smile, actively putting a piece of food in his mouth.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/048_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what kind of food is shown on the plate in front of Aman?\",\"options\":[\"Green leafy vegetables\",\"Fresh fruits like apples\",\"Square-shaped chocolates or sweets\",\"Healthy bowls of soup\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The drawing shows Aman eating brown, square-shaped pieces which represent the chocolates he likes.\",\"topic\":\"Aman\'s Story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/048_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What color is the tomato described as in the song?\",\"options\":[\"Green and small\",\"Red and bright\",\"Yellow and round\",\"Purple and long\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I am tomato, red and bright.\'\",\"topic\":\"Healthy Food Song\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which food is described as \'long and red\'?\",\"options\":[\"Tomato\",\"Banana\",\"Carrot\",\"Rice\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'This is carrot, long and red.\'\",\"topic\":\"Healthy Food Song\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many times should you have sprouts, dal, roti, and rice?\",\"options\":[\"Once a week\",\"Only once\",\"At least twice\",\"Never\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Sprouts, dal, roti and rice... You should have at least twice.\'\",\"topic\":\"Healthy Food Song\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why is the tomato helpful for us?\",\"options\":[\"It makes us sleep\",\"It is rich with vitamins to fight\",\"It helps us jump ahead\",\"It is a tasty dish\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the tomato is \'Rich with vitamins, strong to fight.\'\",\"topic\":\"Healthy Food Song\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the benefit of eating apples and bananas day by day?\",\"options\":[\"You will stay fit and fine\",\"You will run fast\",\"You will get enough rest\",\"You will jump ahead\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Apples and bananas, day by day… Fit and fine you will stay.\'\",\"topic\":\"Healthy Food Song\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When does the song suggest having a cup of milk?\",\"options\":[\"After you sleep\",\"Before you work or play\",\"Only at night\",\"Once a month\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'A cup of milk, before you work or play.\'\",\"topic\":\"Healthy Food Song\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To keep your body and brain active, what should you do along with drinking water?\",\"options\":[\"Eat only fish\",\"Rest enough\",\"Run all day\",\"Eat only rice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Rest enough for active body and brain.\'\",\"topic\":\"Healthy Food Song\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to \'run in a better way\', what does the text suggest they drink?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Dal\",\"A cup of milk\",\"Fish soup\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states milk \'Will make you run in a better way.\'\",\"topic\":\"Healthy Food Song\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these foods are specifically described as being \'Full of energy\'?\",\"options\":[\"Tomato and carrot\",\"Egg and fish\",\"Roti and rice\",\"Apple and banana\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Sometimes egg… sometimes fish… Full of energy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Healthy Food Song\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the overall goal of following the advice in this song?\",\"options\":[\"To eat only once a day\",\"To play all the time\",\"To eat healthy and stay better\",\"To drink water only once\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The final line concludes, \'Eat healthy and stay better.\'\",\"topic\":\"Healthy Food Song\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How did Aman feel when he woke up the next morning?\",\"options\":[\"Tired\",\"Fresh\",\"Strange\",\"Sick\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when Aman woke up the next morning, he felt fresh.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Aman look at before deciding to eat healthy food?\",\"options\":[\"A mirror\",\"A book\",\"The chart\",\"The clock\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Aman looked at the chart again before making his decision.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was Aman\'s new resolution from that day onwards?\",\"options\":[\"To wake up early\",\"To eat healthy food only\",\"To take medicines twice\",\"To look at charts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aman said, \'From today, I will eat healthy food only.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did Mother react when Aman decided to eat healthy food?\",\"options\":[\"She gave him medicines\",\"She told him to sleep\",\"She smiled and hugged him tightly\",\"She asked him to repeat the words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Mother smiled and hugged him tightly after his statement.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the \'Listen and repeat\' list refers to a type of food?\",\"options\":[\"Tummyache\",\"Sprouts\",\"Medicines\",\"Strange\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sprouts is the only item in the list that is a food item.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'For the Teacher\' section, what should students be encouraged to identify?\",\"options\":[\"The names of different medicines\",\"The difference between sentence structures\",\"The number of vitamins in food\",\"How to cure a tummyache\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text guides teachers to encourage learners to identify the difference between sentence structures.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What topic should the learners use to prepare a poster?\",\"options\":[\"Personal Hygiene\",\"Medicines and Vitamins\",\"Healthy Food\",\"Tired and Fresh\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher is guided to help learners prepare a poster on \'Healthy Food.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text means \'two times\'?\",\"options\":[\"Enough\",\"Strange\",\"Twice\",\"Fresh\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'twice\' in the list means two times.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides healthy food, what else should teachers make learners aware of?\",\"options\":[\"Their personal hygiene\",\"How to wake up fresh\",\"How to hug tightly\",\"How to read charts\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The \'For the Teacher\' section explicitly mentions making learners aware about their personal hygiene.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list describes a feeling of needing rest?\",\"options\":[\"Tired\",\"Strange\",\"Enough\",\"Fresh\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'tired\' describes the physical state of needing rest or sleep.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21527,19,4,'English','en','My Word Family (Unit 2)','[\"- A word family is a group of words that share the same root or base word.\",\"- Words in a word family can be nouns, verbs, adjectives, etc.\",\"- Example: the root word \\\"giant\\\" can lead to \\\"giant\\\" (noun), \\\"gigantic\\\" (adj).\",\"- Some words in the list are action words (verbs) like chase, stretch, melt, deliver, hug, pour, sew, crush.\",\"- Some words describe nature: sugarcane, ginger, jaggery, mountain.\",\"- One-syllable words are short and easy to remember: chase, stretch, melt, hug, pour, sew, crush, giant, rare, jaw, peace, symbol, capital, pride, brave, celebrate, vitamin.\",\"- Opposites help you understand meaning: brave ↔ fearful, giant ↔ tiny, rare ↔ common, peace ↔ war, excite ↔ calm.\",\"- Practice by making lists, finding odd ones out, and circling one-syllable words.\",\"- Remember: a word family helps you learn many words from one root.\",\"- Use the word family to improve reading, writing, and speaking skills.\",\"- Keep a notebook of new word families and review them regularly.\",\"- Try to use new words in sentences to remember them better.\",\"- The word \\\"sugarcane\\\" is a plant, \\\"ginger\\\" is a spice, \\\"jaggery\\\" is a sweetener.\",\"- \\\"Mould\\\" and \\\"mold\\\" are the same word spelled differently in UK and US.\",\"- \\\"Specimen\\\" is a sample, \\\"extinct\\\" means no longer existing.\",\"- \\\"Capital\\\" can mean a city or money, but here it means city.\",\"- \\\"Symbol\\\" represents an idea, like a peace sign.\",\"- \\\"Vitamin\\\" is a nutrient that keeps you healthy.\",\"- \\\"Celebrate\\\" means to honor or enjoy a special day.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the word family table, what is the meaning of the word \'giant\'?\",\"options\":[\"Very small\",\"Very big\",\"Very fast\",\"Very cold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'giant\' as \'very big\'.\",\"topic\":\"Odd One Out\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is the odd one out in the list: ginger, jaggery, sugarcane, giant?\",\"options\":[\"ginger\",\"jaggery\",\"sugarcane\",\"giant\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"In this list, giant is the odd one out because the others are related to food\\/plants.\",\"topic\":\"Odd One Out\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'It is a giant mountain\', which word describes the mountain?\",\"options\":[\"It\",\"is\",\"giant\",\"a\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'giant\' as an adjective to describe the mountain in the short sentence.\",\"topic\":\"Odd One Out\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the text is related to nature?\",\"options\":[\"sew\",\"sugarcane\",\"deliver\",\"symbol\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists sugarcane under \'Words related to nature\'.\",\"topic\":\"Odd One Out\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the list \'pour, sew, crush, hug, mountain\', why is \'mountain\' the odd one out?\",\"options\":[\"It is an action word\",\"It is a naming word (noun) while others are actions\",\"It is a very small thing\",\"It is a type of food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Pour, sew, crush, and hug are actions, whereas mountain is a place\\/thing.\",\"topic\":\"Odd One Out\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Find the odd one out from this list: chase, stretch, melt, deliver, ginger.\",\"options\":[\"chase\",\"stretch\",\"melt\",\"ginger\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Ginger is a plant\\/food item, while the others are action words.\",\"topic\":\"Odd One Out\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word appears in both the \'nature\' list and the \'odd one out\' lists?\",\"options\":[\"mountain\",\"ginger\",\"vitamin\",\"sew\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Ginger is listed as a nature word and appears in multiple odd-one-out sets.\",\"topic\":\"Odd One Out\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the list \'ginger, jaggery, sugarcane, vitamin, symbol\', which word is the odd one out?\",\"options\":[\"ginger\",\"jaggery\",\"sugarcane\",\"symbol\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Symbol is the odd one out as the others are related to food or health.\",\"topic\":\"Odd One Out\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is NOT listed in the text provided?\",\"options\":[\"crush\",\"deliver\",\"forest\",\"stretch\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'forest\' does not appear in the provided textbook text.\",\"topic\":\"Odd One Out\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the first \'Odd One Out\' list, why is \'giant\' different from ginger, jaggery, and sugarcane?\",\"options\":[\"It describes a quality (size) rather than a specific food item\",\"It is a word for a plant\",\"It is something you can eat\",\"It is a word related to nature\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Giant is an adjective for size, while the others are specific food-related nouns.\",\"topic\":\"Odd One Out\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to exercise 4, what kind of words are you asked to list?\",\"options\":[\"Action words\",\"Naming words\",\"Color words\",\"Number words\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Exercise 4 specifically instructs to \'Make a list of action words\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do to the words that have only one syllable in exercise 5?\",\"options\":[\"Underline them\",\"Circle them\",\"Cross them out\",\"Highlight them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Exercise 5 asks the student to \'circle the words that have only one syllable\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific text are you asked to read in exercise 5?\",\"options\":[\"My Action Words\",\"My Syllables\",\"My Word Family\",\"My List\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Exercise 5 begins with the instruction to \'Read My Word Family\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal of exercise 4?\",\"options\":[\"To count syllables\",\"To identify words that show movement or doing\",\"To find rhyming words\",\"To draw pictures of family members\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Action words are words that describe doing something or movement.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When exercise 5 mentions \'one syllable\', what is it referring to?\",\"options\":[\"The number of letters in a word\",\"The number of vowel sounds in a word\",\"The number of capital letters\",\"The number of sentences\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A syllable is a single unit of pronunciation or a beat in a word.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words would fit in the list for exercise 4?\",\"options\":[\"Table\",\"Green\",\"Jump\",\"Happy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Jump\' is an action word, whereas the others are objects, colors, or feelings.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the instruction in exercise 5, which word should you circle?\",\"options\":[\"Cat\",\"Elephant\",\"Banana\",\"Computer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Cat\' has only one syllable, while the others have three.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does an \'action word\' help us understand in a sentence?\",\"options\":[\"What color something is\",\"Where someone is going\",\"What someone is doing\",\"How many things there are\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Action words describe the activity or what is being done.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word would NOT be circled in exercise 5 because it has more than one syllable?\",\"options\":[\"Dog\",\"Sun\",\"Tiger\",\"Bat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Tiger\' (Ti-ger) has two syllables, so it does not meet the \'only one syllable\' rule.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the list \'Run, Eat, Sleep\', what is the common feature based on exercise 4?\",\"options\":[\"They are all names of animals\",\"They are all action words\",\"They all have three syllables\",\"They all start with the same letter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Run, Eat, and Sleep are all words that describe actions.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21528,19,4,'English','en','Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow','[\"Wheat, jowar and bajra are crops grown on farms.\",\"Seeds are sown in long, narrow rows.\",\"Farmers water the seeds and pull out weeds.\",\"They protect the crops from birds by standing all day.\",\"When the crops are ready, the farmer cuts them and blows a horn.\",\"The poem describes the whole process of growing these crops.\",\"Chapati is made from wheat flour, while jowar roti is made from jowar flour.\",\"Both roti types are cooked on a hot griddle.\",\"Farmers use simple tools like a foot stamp and a hand clap to show their work.\",\"The poem mentions the farmer’s pride in his land.\",\"Harvest time is a festive occasion for many people.\",\"Farming involves planting, watering, weeding, protecting, and harvesting.\",\"The farmer’s work is celebrated in songs and poems.\",\"Learning about farming helps us understand food production.\",\"Being a farmer requires hard work, patience, and care for the land.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does the farmer sow first in the field?\",\"options\":[\"Fruits\",\"Flowers\",\"Seeds\",\"Trees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'First the seeds the farmer sows\'.\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In what way does the farmer sow the seeds?\",\"options\":[\"In big circles\",\"In long and narrow rows\",\"In square blocks\",\"Randomly everywhere\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the seeds are sown \'In long, long and narrow rows.\'\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the farmer is looking at his land. What has he just finished doing in these long, narrow rows?\",\"options\":[\"Cutting the corn\",\"Sowing the seeds\",\"Scaring the birds\",\"Calling the bands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the empty rows where the farmer \'First the seeds the farmer sows\'.\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/053_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the farmer stand in the field all day after the seedlings appear?\",\"options\":[\"To watch the rain\",\"To sleep in the sun\",\"To scare the naughty birds away\",\"To talk to his friends\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Next the farmer stands all day, To scare the naughty birds away.\'\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the farmer do while he waters the seeds?\",\"options\":[\"He cuts the corn\",\"He pulls out the weeds\",\"He plants trees\",\"He calls the bands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Next the farmer waters the seeds, Bends down to pull out the weeds.\'\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, which of these crops is used to make Jowar roti?\",\"options\":[\"Wheat\",\"Bajra\",\"Jowar\",\"Rice\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Jowar roti is made using Jowar, which is one of the crops mentioned in the poem.\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What action is repeated in the poem whenever the farmer \'turns around to see his lands\'?\",\"options\":[\"He jumps high\",\"He stamps his foot and claps his hands\",\"He sits down and rests\",\"He starts to cry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"This specific physical action is repeated throughout the poem as the farmer checks his land.\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, what is the correct order of growth on the farm?\",\"options\":[\"Seedlings -> Seeds -> Crops\",\"Seeds -> Seedlings -> Crops\",\"Crops -> Seeds -> Seedlings\",\"Seedlings -> Crops -> Seeds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem follows the sequence of sowing seeds, then seedlings appearing, and finally crops swaying.\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the farmer do at the very last stage when the corn is ready?\",\"options\":[\"He sows more seeds\",\"He pulls out weeds\",\"He cuts the corn and blows the horn\",\"He stands all day to scare birds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'At last the farmer cuts the corn, Stands erect and blows the horn.\'\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'merrymaking on the farm\' suggest about the farmer\'s feelings?\",\"options\":[\"He is very sad\",\"He is angry with the birds\",\"He is happy and celebrating\",\"He is tired and wants to go home\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Merrymaking indicates joy and celebration after the harvest is complete.\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If a farmer is \'bending down\' after watering, what is he most likely doing according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Sowing seeds\",\"Pulling out weeds\",\"Scaring birds\",\"Blowing a horn\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem links the action of bending down specifically to pulling out weeds.\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, people are seen with musical instruments. Which stage of farming does this represent?\",\"options\":[\"Sowing the seeds\",\"Watering the seeds\",\"Merrymaking after cutting the corn\",\"Pulling out the weeds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the \'bands\' and celebration described in the final part of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"Wheat, Jowar and Bajra Grow\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/054_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which word rhymes with \'grow\'?\",\"options\":[\"know\",\"seeds\",\"sows\",\"day\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'grow\' with \'know\' as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is paired with \'seeds\' in the list?\",\"options\":[\"weeds\",\"rows\",\"lands\",\"horn\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'seeds weeds\' together as a rhyming pair.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'sows\' based on the text provided?\",\"options\":[\"rows\",\"know\",\"away\",\"arm\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'sows rows\' as a rhyming pair.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the rhyming word for \'corn\' in the given text?\",\"options\":[\"horn\",\"farm\",\"bands\",\"seeds\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifically pairs \'corn\' with \'horn\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are looking for a word that rhymes with \'lands\', which word should you choose from the text?\",\"options\":[\"hands\",\"grow\",\"day\",\"arm\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'hands lands\' as a rhyming pair.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list rhymes with \'day\'?\",\"options\":[\"away\",\"know\",\"weeds\",\"rows\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'day\' with \'away\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'farm\' in the provided text?\",\"options\":[\"arm\",\"horn\",\"bands\",\"lands\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'farm arm\' as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which word rhymes with \'bands\'?\",\"options\":[\"hands\",\"farm\",\"day\",\"corn\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'hands bands\' at the end of the sequence.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the list \'seeds weeds sows rows\', which word rhymes with \'weeds\'?\",\"options\":[\"seeds\",\"sows\",\"grow\",\"arm\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows that \'seeds\' and \'weeds\' rhyme with each other.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text can rhyme with both \'lands\' and \'bands\'?\",\"options\":[\"hands\",\"sows\",\"rows\",\"day\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'hands\' appears twice in the text, paired with \'lands\' and then with \'bands\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21529,19,4,'English','en','Our Flying Friends','[\"- Birds have three kinds of feathers: down (warmth), body (cover), flight (help flying).\",\"- All birds are warm‑blooded and have two feet.\",\"- Birds have wings; most can fly, but penguins and ostriches cannot.\",\"- A bird’s body is light and shaped like an aeroplane, with strong muscles and light bones.\",\"- Beaks are used to cut, open, tear, and crush food; they have no teeth.\",\"- Birds have three toes forward and one toe backward, used for walking, holding, balancing, climbing, swimming, and wading.\",\"- Birds build nests in trees, walls, or on the ground; the female sits on eggs to keep them warm.\",\"- After hatching, baby birds are blind and featherless; parents feed and care for them.\",\"- Migration is the yearly journey to warmer places to find food and then return to build nests.\",\"- Penguins live in cold places, swim well, and walk\\/slide on ice.\",\"- Ostriches live in hot places, are the heaviest and largest birds, and run fast on land.\",\"- Claws are used for different purposes: ducks swim, eagles catch prey, cranes walk in water, hens scratch ground, woodpeckers climb trees.\",\"- An Arctic Tern can travel about 35,000 km in a year, almost around the Earth.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many feet do all birds have?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'All birds have two feet.\'\",\"topic\":\"General Characteristics of Birds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a feature that only birds have?\",\"options\":[\"Wings\",\"Two feet\",\"Feathers\",\"Eyes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Birds are the only living creatures that have feathers.\'\",\"topic\":\"General Characteristics of Birds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is another special thing about birds besides having feathers?\",\"options\":[\"They have wings\",\"They have four legs\",\"They have fur\",\"They live underwater\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that \'Another special thing about birds is that they have wings\'.\",\"topic\":\"General Characteristics of Birds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Does the text say that every single bird can fly?\",\"options\":[\"Yes, all birds fly\",\"No, only one bird flies\",\"Most of them can fly\",\"None of them can fly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that \'most of them can fly\', implying not all.\",\"topic\":\"General Characteristics of Birds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you find a creature that has feathers, what kind of living creature is it?\",\"options\":[\"An insect\",\"A bird\",\"A mammal\",\"A fish\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since birds are the only creatures with feathers, any feathered creature must be a bird.\",\"topic\":\"General Characteristics of Birds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which two specific birds are listed in the \'Read and repeat\' section?\",\"options\":[\"Crow and Sparrow\",\"Penguin and Ostrich\",\"Parrot and Eagle\",\"Woodpecker and Duck\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Penguin\' and \'Ostrich\' under the \'Read and repeat\' section.\",\"topic\":\"General Characteristics of Birds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text describes the sharp parts on a bird\'s feet?\",\"options\":[\"Beak\",\"Claws\",\"Feathers\",\"Muscles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'claws\' is listed as a bird characteristic in the text.\",\"topic\":\"General Characteristics of Birds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does a bird do when it comes out of its egg?\",\"options\":[\"Glide\",\"Hatch\",\"Perch\",\"Wading\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'hatch\' is included in the vocabulary list related to birds.\",\"topic\":\"General Characteristics of Birds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the vocabulary list, which of these is a type of bird?\",\"options\":[\"Migration\",\"Woodpecker\",\"Glide\",\"Perch\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Woodpecker is the only specific bird species mentioned in the first vocabulary list.\",\"topic\":\"General Characteristics of Birds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a bird is moving through the air smoothly without flapping its wings, which word from the text describes this?\",\"options\":[\"Wading\",\"Perch\",\"Glide\",\"Hatch\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'glide\' is listed in the text as a way birds fly.\",\"topic\":\"General Characteristics of Birds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which bird is described as the heaviest and largest bird in the world?\",\"options\":[\"Penguin\",\"Ostrich\",\"Sparrow\",\"Eagle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Ostrich is the heaviest and largest bird in the world.\",\"topic\":\"Kinds of Feathers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In what kind of environment do Penguins live?\",\"options\":[\"Hot deserts\",\"Grasslands\",\"Cold places\",\"Tropical forests\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Penguins live in cold places.\",\"topic\":\"Kinds of Feathers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the colors of a Penguin as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Grey and white\",\"Black and white\",\"Brown and black\",\"Blue and white\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Penguins are black and white in colour.\",\"topic\":\"Kinds of Feathers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific purpose of \'Down feathers\'?\",\"options\":[\"To help the bird fly\",\"To cover the bird\'s body\",\"To keep the bird warm\",\"To help the bird swim\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines down feathers as those that keep the bird warm.\",\"topic\":\"Kinds of Feathers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which type of feathers covers the bird\'s body?\",\"options\":[\"Flight feathers\",\"Down feathers\",\"Body feathers\",\"Tail feathers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that body feathers cover the bird\'s body.\",\"topic\":\"Kinds of Feathers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a bird is soaring high in the sky, which feathers are primarily helping it?\",\"options\":[\"Down feathers\",\"Body feathers\",\"Flight feathers\",\"Soft feathers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Flight feathers are specifically mentioned as the ones that help the bird to fly.\",\"topic\":\"Kinds of Feathers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A bird living in a very chilly, snowy region would rely most on which feathers to stay cozy?\",\"options\":[\"Flight feathers\",\"Down feathers\",\"Wing feathers\",\"Tail feathers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Down feathers keep the bird warm, which is essential in cold regions.\",\"topic\":\"Kinds of Feathers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How do Penguins move when they are on ice?\",\"options\":[\"They fly and hop\",\"They run and jump\",\"They walk and slide\",\"They crawl and swim\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says that Penguins walk and slide on ice.\",\"topic\":\"Kinds of Feathers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is a common characteristic shared by both the Penguin and the Ostrich?\",\"options\":[\"They both live in hot places\",\"They both are good swimmers\",\"They both cannot fly\",\"They both are the fastest runners\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text begins by stating that the Penguin and the Ostrich are two birds that cannot fly.\",\"topic\":\"Kinds of Feathers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what makes the Ostrich unique among land birds?\",\"options\":[\"It is the only bird with body feathers\",\"It is the fastest running bird on land\",\"It is the only bird that lives in grasslands\",\"It is the only bird that cannot swim\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the Ostrich as the fastest running bird on land.\",\"topic\":\"Kinds of Feathers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Like humans, birds are described as being ________.\",\"options\":[\"Cold-blooded\",\"Warm-blooded\",\"Fast-blooded\",\"Cool-blooded\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that birds are warm-blooded, just like humans.\",\"topic\":\"Migration\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to a bird\'s body temperature?\",\"options\":[\"It changes every hour\",\"It gets colder in winter\",\"It gets hotter in summer\",\"It stays almost the same\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a bird\'s body temperature stays almost the same.\",\"topic\":\"Migration\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A bird\'s body is shaped like which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"A boat\",\"An aeroplane\",\"A car\",\"A bicycle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that birds\' bodies are shaped like aeroplanes.\",\"topic\":\"Migration\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two features help birds flap their wings easily?\",\"options\":[\"Heavy bones and weak muscles\",\"Small wings and large bodies\",\"Strong muscles and light bones\",\"Aeroplane shape and warm blood\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that strong muscles and light bones help birds flap their wings easily.\",\"topic\":\"Migration\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the journey called when birds travel to warmer places every year?\",\"options\":[\"Vacation\",\"Migration\",\"Rotation\",\"Flapping\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the journey to warmer places to find food as migration.\",\"topic\":\"Migration\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do birds travel to warmer places every year?\",\"options\":[\"To find food\",\"To learn to fly\",\"To meet other birds\",\"To build new nests\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states birds travel to warmer places to find food.\",\"topic\":\"Migration\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a bird is already high up in the air, how does it move?\",\"options\":[\"It must flap its wings constantly\",\"It falls down quickly\",\"It moves gently and easily\",\"It stops moving completely\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says that when birds are up in the air, they move gently and easily.\",\"topic\":\"Migration\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, how are birds and aeroplanes similar?\",\"options\":[\"Both have the same body shape\",\"Both are warm-blooded\",\"Both have strong muscles\",\"Both travel to find food\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly compares the shape of a bird\'s body to an aeroplane.\",\"topic\":\"Migration\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"A bird does not need to flap its wings all the time when it is ________.\",\"options\":[\"Up in the air\",\"Finding food\",\"On the ground\",\"Starting its journey\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that birds do not need to flap their wings all the time when they are up in the air.\",\"topic\":\"Migration\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a reason why birds are able to fly easily?\",\"options\":[\"They have very light bodies\",\"They have heavy bones\",\"They are cold-blooded\",\"They stay in one place\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that most birds are very light, which helps them fly.\",\"topic\":\"Migration\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where do birds build their nests according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only in tall trees\",\"In trees, on walls, or on the ground\",\"Only inside houses\",\"Under the water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states birds build nests in many places like in trees, on walls, or even on the ground.\",\"topic\":\"Nests and Life Cycle\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When does the female bird lay her eggs?\",\"options\":[\"Before building the nest\",\"While flying to a new home\",\"When the nest is ready\",\"After the baby birds hatch\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that when the nest is ready, the female bird lays eggs.\",\"topic\":\"Nests and Life Cycle\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the female bird sit on the eggs?\",\"options\":[\"To hide them from the sun\",\"To keep the eggs warm\",\"To help her feathers grow\",\"To protect the nest from rain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the eggs must be kept warm, so the female bird sits on them.\",\"topic\":\"Nests and Life Cycle\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is a common characteristic of newly hatched baby birds?\",\"options\":[\"They have colorful feathers\",\"They can fly immediately\",\"They are usually blind and have no feathers\",\"They start building their own nests\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes baby birds as usually blind and having no feathers when they hatch.\",\"topic\":\"Nests and Life Cycle\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is responsible for feeding and taking care of the baby birds?\",\"options\":[\"The baby birds themselves\",\"Other animals in the forest\",\"The adult birds\",\"No one takes care of them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the adult birds feed and take care of the baby birds.\",\"topic\":\"Nests and Life Cycle\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a bird finds a safe spot on a wall, what will it likely do first before laying eggs?\",\"options\":[\"Wait for the eggs to hatch\",\"Build a nest\",\"Find feathers for the babies\",\"Teach the babies to fly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the life cycle described, birds return to their homes to build nests before laying eggs.\",\"topic\":\"Nests and Life Cycle\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct order of events in a bird\'s life cycle based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Hatch -> Lay eggs -> Build nest\",\"Build nest -> Lay eggs -> Hatch\",\"Lay eggs -> Build nest -> Hatch\",\"Feed babies -> Lay eggs -> Build nest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text follows the sequence: building a nest, laying eggs, and then the eggs hatching.\",\"topic\":\"Nests and Life Cycle\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What must happen for the baby birds to come out of the eggs?\",\"options\":[\"The eggs must be kept cold\",\"The adult birds must leave the nest\",\"The eggs must hatch after being kept warm\",\"The baby birds must grow feathers first\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that eggs are kept warm and then, after some time, they hatch.\",\"topic\":\"Nests and Life Cycle\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student finds a nest on the ground. Based on the text, is this normal behavior for birds?\",\"options\":[\"Yes, because birds build nests in many places including the ground\",\"No, birds only build nests in trees\",\"Yes, but only if there are no walls nearby\",\"No, the nest must have fallen from a tree\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that birds build nests in many places, including on the ground.\",\"topic\":\"Nests and Life Cycle\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the adult bird\'s presence important after the eggs hatch?\",\"options\":[\"To help the female bird lay more eggs\",\"To build a second nest for the babies\",\"To feed and take care of the featherless babies\",\"To teach the babies how to sit on eggs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says baby birds have no feathers and are blind, so adult birds must feed and care for them.\",\"topic\":\"Nests and Life Cycle\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How many toes do birds usually have in the front?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that birds have three toes in front.\",\"topic\":\"Feet and Claws\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the single toe located on a bird\'s foot?\",\"options\":[\"In the front\",\"At the back\",\"On the side\",\"Under the foot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions birds have one toe at the back.\",\"topic\":\"Feet and Claws\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which bird is mentioned as having strong, sharp claws?\",\"options\":[\"Sparrow\",\"Duck\",\"Eagle\",\"Parrot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses eagles as an example of birds with strong, sharp claws.\",\"topic\":\"Feet and Claws\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do flesh-eating birds use their claws for?\",\"options\":[\"To swim in water\",\"To catch and hold live animals\",\"To build nests\",\"To clean their feathers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states flesh-eating birds use claws to catch and hold live animals.\",\"topic\":\"Feet and Claws\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What can some birds do while they are sitting on branches?\",\"options\":[\"Fly\",\"Swim\",\"Sleep\",\"Run\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says some birds can even sleep while sitting on branches.\",\"topic\":\"Feet and Claws\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why do birds have different shaped feet and claws?\",\"options\":[\"To look beautiful\",\"To use their toes in many ways\",\"To help them sing better\",\"To stay warm in winter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that birds use their toes in many ways, which relates to their different shapes.\",\"topic\":\"Feet and Claws\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see a bird moving through shallow water, which activity is it doing according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Climbing\",\"Perching\",\"Wading\",\"Holding\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists wading in water as one of the uses for a bird\'s toes.\",\"topic\":\"Feet and Claws\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A bird needs to stay steady on a thin branch. Which function of the toes is it using?\",\"options\":[\"Swimming\",\"Balancing\",\"Wading\",\"Catching animals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Balancing is one of the specific uses of toes mentioned in the text for birds.\",\"topic\":\"Feet and Claws\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned in the text as a use for a bird\'s toes?\",\"options\":[\"Walking\",\"Swimming\",\"Flying\",\"Climbing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists walking, swimming, and climbing, but does not mention toes are used for flying.\",\"topic\":\"Feet and Claws\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the relationship between a bird\'s diet and its claws?\",\"options\":[\"All birds have the same claws regardless of what they eat.\",\"Flesh-eating birds have specific claws to help them catch prey.\",\"Birds only use their claws for walking, not for eating.\",\"Only birds that sleep on branches have sharp claws.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links flesh-eating birds specifically to strong, sharp claws for catching animals.\",\"topic\":\"Feet and Claws\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What do birds use instead of teeth to handle their food?\",\"options\":[\"Their wings\",\"Their beaks\",\"Their claws\",\"Their feathers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that birds do not have teeth and use their beaks to cut, open, tear and crush.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, do birds have teeth?\",\"options\":[\"Yes, they have sharp teeth\",\"No, they do not have teeth\",\"Only some birds have teeth\",\"They have teeth only when they are young\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'They do not have teeth.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a function of a bird\'s beak mentioned in the passage?\",\"options\":[\"To chew food\",\"To taste food\",\"To crush food\",\"To swallow food whole\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that birds use their beaks to \'crush\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do birds have different shaped beaks?\",\"options\":[\"To help them fly higher\",\"To perform different tasks like cutting and tearing\",\"To make different sounds\",\"To change their color\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links the different shapes of beaks to their uses: to cut, open, tear, and crush.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text tell us about the appearance of bird beaks?\",\"options\":[\"All birds have the same beak\",\"Beaks are always the same size\",\"Birds have different shaped beaks\",\"Beaks are only used for opening things\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first sentence of the text is \'Birds have different shaped beaks.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the text describes how a bird might use its beak to get into a sealed nut or shell?\",\"options\":[\"Cut\",\"Open\",\"Tear\",\"Crush\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'open\' describes the action of getting into something that is closed.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a bird needs to break a hard seed into small pieces, which action from the text is it performing?\",\"options\":[\"Tearing\",\"Cutting\",\"Crushing\",\"Opening\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Crushing is the action used to break something hard into smaller pieces.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A bird is pulling a piece of meat apart into smaller bits. Which beak function is it using?\",\"options\":[\"Crushing\",\"Tearing\",\"Opening\",\"Flying\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tearing is the action of pulling something apart, which is one of the functions mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which statement is true about how birds eat?\",\"options\":[\"They use teeth to grind food\",\"Their beaks are multi-purpose tools for food\",\"All birds use their beaks in the exact same way\",\"Beaks are only for show and not for eating\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows beaks have multiple functions (cut, open, tear, crush) because birds lack teeth.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If we know a bird has a beak, what can we conclude about its mouth based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"It definitely has teeth inside\",\"It uses its beak to chew like humans\",\"It does not have teeth to help it eat\",\"It only uses its beak to drink water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states birds use beaks because they do not have teeth.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21530,19,4,'English','en','I am Indian First','[\"- India is a country in South Asia.\",\"- It is called the land of sages and has a rich culture.\",\"- The poem talks about snowy peaks and the sea at its feet.\",\"- India invented the number zero, a very important idea.\",\"- Soldiers protect the country and are called heroes.\",\"- The poem celebrates being Indian first, not Hindu or Muslim.\",\"- Republic Day is celebrated on 26th January to honor the Constitution.\",\"- Students can make posters and poems about India.\",\"- Maps help us see where each state is located.\",\"- The word ‘crowned’ means having a crown or being the best.\",\"- ‘Prostrate’ means lying down or showing respect.\",\"- ‘Heights’ refers to high places like mountains.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, the land is a land of which people?\",\"options\":[\"Sages\",\"Kings\",\"Farmers\",\"Sailors\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first line of the poem states, \'I come from land of sages\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is at the \'feet\' of the land according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Snowy peaks\",\"The sea\",\"Golden Sparrow\",\"Soldiers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Sea prostrates at its feet\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which mathematical value is mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Value of One\",\"Value of Infinity\",\"Value of Zero\",\"Value of Ten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'I know value of Zero\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'crowned with snowy peaks\' describe?\",\"options\":[\"The sea\",\"The soldiers\",\"The mountains at the top of the land\",\"The Golden Sparrow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A crown is worn on the head (top), and snowy peaks refer to high mountains.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who are described as the \'Hero\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"The sages\",\"The martyrs\",\"The soldiers\",\"The Golden Sparrow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem explicitly states, \'My soldiers are my Hero\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What has been \'rich from ages\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The sea\",\"The culture\",\"The snowy peaks\",\"The birds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'With culture rich from ages\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person follows the message of the last stanza, how would they identify themselves first?\",\"options\":[\"As a Hindu\",\"As a Muslim\",\"As an Indian\",\"As a Golden Sparrow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem concludes with \'Not Hindu, nor Muslim, I am Indian first\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The speaker wants to take the country to \'new heights\' using the flight of which symbol?\",\"options\":[\"A White Pigeon\",\"The Golden Sparrow\",\"A Brave Soldier\",\"A Wise Sage\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'With Golden Sparrow’s flights, I’ll take it to new heights\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the line \'The martyrs paid the cost\' suggest about the country\'s freedom and safety?\",\"options\":[\"It was bought with money\",\"It was achieved through the sacrifices of lives\",\"It was given by the sea\",\"It was found in the snowy peaks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Martyrs are those who die for a cause, implying sacrifice is the \'cost\' paid.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes the speaker\'s attitude toward their country?\",\"options\":[\"They are afraid of the sea\",\"They only care about the past\",\"They love and take pride in their national identity\",\"They want to be a sage\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem expresses love, pride in culture, heroes, and a primary identity as an Indian.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the \'Look and say\' list refers to a person who belongs to India?\",\"options\":[\"Region\",\"Indian\",\"Nation\",\"Language\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'Indian\' describes a person belonging to the country of India.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list starts with the letter \'N\' and means a country?\",\"options\":[\"Nature\",\"Nation\",\"Native\",\"Night\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'Nation\' is included in the list and refers to a country.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list means a system of faith or worship?\",\"options\":[\"Creed\",\"Region\",\"Religion\",\"Unity\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Religion is the term used for a particular system of faith and worship.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list describes the state of being joined together as one?\",\"options\":[\"Diversity\",\"Unity\",\"Nation\",\"Caste\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Unity means being together or in agreement as a single whole.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are talking about Marathi, Hindi, or English, which word from the list are you referring to?\",\"options\":[\"Religion\",\"Region\",\"Language\",\"Creed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Marathi, Hindi, and English are examples of languages.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list refers to a specific area or part of a country?\",\"options\":[\"Region\",\"Religion\",\"Nation\",\"Creed\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A region is a specific area or part of a larger country or world.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list describes having many different types of people, cultures, and beliefs?\",\"options\":[\"Unity\",\"Diversity\",\"Caste\",\"Indian\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Diversity refers to the variety of different things or people within a group.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the chapter title \'I am Indian First\', how does \'unity\' relate to \'diversity\'?\",\"options\":[\"They are exactly the same\",\"They are opposites that cannot exist together\",\"They show how different people stay together as one\",\"They are not related to the topic\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Unity in diversity is a core concept of being Indian, where different people are united.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list starts with the letter \'C\' and refers to a social group one is born into?\",\"options\":[\"Caste\",\"Region\",\"Nation\",\"Unity\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Caste is a social category mentioned in the \'Look and say\' list.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the \'Look and say\' list has exactly four letters?\",\"options\":[\"First\",\"Last\",\"Caste\",\"Unity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'Last\' consists of four letters: L-A-S-T.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21531,19,4,'English','en','The Smart Traveller','[\"- The story is about a smart traveller named Ramdas and a thief named Hari.\",\"- Ramdas is a merchant who travels to Royal Parks.\",\"- Hari joins him on the journey and pretends to be a merchant.\",\"- While Ramdas sleeps at an inn, Hari searches for money but finds none.\",\"- Ramdas hides his money in Hari’s own bag for safekeeping.\",\"- Hari discovers the trick and admits he was outsmarted.\",\"- Key words: traveller, merchant, inn, belongings, profession, identity, outsmarted.\",\"- Important ideas: honesty, cleverness, safety of money, travel etiquette.\",\"- Remember: a traveller should keep money in a safe place, like a bag that is hard to find.\",\"- The story shows that being clever can protect you from thieves.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What was Ramdas\'s profession according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A thief\",\"A cloth merchant\",\"An innkeeper\",\"A soldier\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'I am a cloth merchant,\' said Ramdas.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where was Ramdas travelling to?\",\"options\":[\"A nearby village\",\"Royal Parks\",\"A big market\",\"His home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first sentence mentions Ramdas was on a journey to Royal Parks.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are both the men carrying on their shoulders as they talk?\",\"options\":[\"Bundles of cloth\",\"Bags\",\"Walking sticks\",\"Water pots\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows both Ramdas and Hari with bags slung over their shoulders.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/061_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What did Hari lie about when he met Ramdas?\",\"options\":[\"His name\",\"His destination\",\"His profession\",\"His family\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Hari, who was a thief, lied and said, \'I am a merchant too.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Hari disappointed at the inn?\",\"options\":[\"He could not find any money in Ramdas\'s belongings\",\"The inn was not comfortable\",\"Ramdas did not talk to him\",\"He lost his own bag\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says Hari searched for money but found nothing and was very disappointed.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the man in the yellow shirt doing while the other man is asleep?\",\"options\":[\"He is sleeping too\",\"He is eating food\",\"He is searching through a bag\",\"He is looking out of the window\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows Hari (in yellow) kneeling and searching a bag while Ramdas sleeps.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/061_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'resumed their journey\' mean in the story?\",\"options\":[\"They finished their travel\",\"They started travelling again\",\"They went back home\",\"They stayed at the inn longer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"To resume means to begin again after a pause, which they did the next morning.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Ramdas actually keep his money during the night?\",\"options\":[\"Under his pillow\",\"In his own bag\",\"In Hari\'s bag\",\"With the innkeeper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ramdas replied that he kept the money in the safest place—Hari\'s bag.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Hari had searched his own bag at the inn, what would he have found?\",\"options\":[\"Only his clothes\",\"Ramdas\'s money\",\"Nothing at all\",\"A map to Royal Parks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since Ramdas hid the money in Hari\'s bag, Hari would have found it there.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Ramdas choose Hari\'s bag to hide his money?\",\"options\":[\"Because Hari\'s bag was bigger\",\"Because he knew a thief would not look for stolen money in his own bag\",\"Because his own bag was torn\",\"Because he wanted to give the money to Hari\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It was a smart move because Hari was busy searching Ramdas\'s belongings, not his own.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'outsmarted\' mean in the context of the story?\",\"options\":[\"To be taller than someone\",\"To run faster than someone\",\"To be cleverer than someone and defeat their plan\",\"To travel to a further place\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ramdas was cleverer than the thief, which is why Hari admitted he was outsmarted.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What can we conclude about Ramdas from his reaction when Hari revealed his identity?\",\"options\":[\"He was very scared\",\"He was surprised and shocked\",\"He was observant and had already suspected Hari\",\"He was angry and started a fight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ramdas smiled and said \'I knew it,\' showing he was already aware of the truth.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to a person who buys and sells goods?\",\"options\":[\"traveller\",\"merchant\",\"inn\",\"identity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A merchant is a person involved in trade or commerce.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a small hotel or a place for travellers to stay called?\",\"options\":[\"business\",\"profession\",\"inn\",\"belongings\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"An inn is a place providing accommodation, food, and drink, especially for travellers.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is cleverer than someone else and defeats them, they have ____ them.\",\"options\":[\"revealed\",\"belongings\",\"outsmarted\",\"identity\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To outsmart means to defeat or get the better of someone by being clever.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word refers to the things that a person owns?\",\"options\":[\"belongings\",\"business\",\"profession\",\"merchant\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Belongings are the things that one owns.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A person who is on a journey or visiting different places is a ____.\",\"options\":[\"merchant\",\"traveller\",\"inn\",\"business\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A traveller is a person who is travelling or who often travels.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes the work or job that a person does to earn money?\",\"options\":[\"identity\",\"revealed\",\"profession\",\"outsmarted\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A profession is a type of job that requires special training or skill.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When a secret is made known to others, it is said to be ____.\",\"options\":[\"revealed\",\"outsmarted\",\"belongings\",\"business\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To reveal means to make something known that was previously secret or unknown.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes who a person is, such as their name or details?\",\"options\":[\"merchant\",\"identity\",\"inn\",\"profession\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Identity is the fact of being who or what a person or thing is.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A merchant usually runs a ____ to earn a living.\",\"options\":[\"belongings\",\"identity\",\"business\",\"outsmarted\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Business refers to the activity of making, buying, and selling goods or services.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is most likely to be used when talking about a person\'s suitcase and clothes?\",\"options\":[\"belongings\",\"revealed\",\"inn\",\"merchant\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Suitcases and clothes are examples of a person\'s belongings.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21532,19,4,'English','en','Yoga','[\"Yoga is a set of exercises that keeps the body fit and the mind calm.\",\"Doing yoga every day helps you stay active and happy.\",\"Yoga helps you develop healthy habits like regular breathing and stretching.\",\"It improves flexibility, balance and concentration.\",\"Yoga can be practiced at home or in school after playtime.\",\"You can make a chart of healthy habits and paste it at home to remember them.\",\"Yoga is good for all ages and can be done in a quiet space.\",\"It encourages a calm and peaceful mind.\",\"Doing yoga regularly can help you sleep better and feel energetic.\",\"Yoga is a simple way to stay healthy and happy every day.\"]','[{\"q\":\"On which day does the conversation between Papa and Sunny take place?\",\"options\":[\"Monday\",\"Friday\",\"Sunday\",\"Saturday\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sunny says, \'Papa, it is Sunday\' when he is asked to wake up.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, repeat and enact\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Papa, what keeps the body fit?\",\"options\":[\"Sleeping late\",\"Daily Yogasana\",\"Only playing at school\",\"Eating breakfast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Papa states that \'Daily Yogasana keeps the body fit\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, repeat and enact\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Papa want Sunny to develop?\",\"options\":[\"Healthy habits\",\"Sleeping habits\",\"Drawing habits\",\"Sunday habits\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Papa tells Sunny, \'You should develop healthy habits.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen, repeat and enact\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does Yogasana affect the mind according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"It makes the mind tired\",\"It makes the mind busy\",\"It keeps the mind calm\",\"It makes the mind sleepy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Papa says Yogasana keeps the \'mind calm\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, repeat and enact\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Sunny wants to stay active and happy, what activity should he do?\",\"options\":[\"Sleep all day\",\"Yogasana\",\"Skip school\",\"Only play on Sundays\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Papa mentions that \'Yogasana helps us to stay active and happy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen, repeat and enact\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Papa say Yoga is needed even if Sunny plays at school?\",\"options\":[\"Because playing is not good\",\"Because school is closed on Sunday\",\"Because everyday you need to do Yoga in addition to play\",\"Because Sunny is lazy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Papa says play time is required, but \'everyday you need to do Yoga\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, repeat and enact\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who says the line, \'Please, let me sleep\'?\",\"options\":[\"Papa\",\"Sunny\",\"The Teacher\",\"The Narrator\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows Sunny responding to Papa with \'Please, let me sleep.\'\",\"topic\":\"Listen, repeat and enact\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main topic of the conversation between Papa and Sunny?\",\"options\":[\"School subjects\",\"Sunday breakfast\",\"The importance of Yoga\",\"How to play games\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The entire dialogue focuses on why Sunny should wake up to do Yoga.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, repeat and enact\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the conversation, what will Sunny do every day from now on?\",\"options\":[\"Sleep late\",\"Go to school early\",\"Do Yoga\",\"Only play\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sunny agrees to Papa\'s question by saying, \'Yes, Papa. I will\' regarding doing Yoga every day.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, repeat and enact\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What can we conclude about Sunny\'s final attitude toward Yoga?\",\"options\":[\"He is still confused\",\"He disagrees with his father\",\"He understands its importance and agrees to do it\",\"He wants to sleep instead\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sunny says \'Oh! I understood now\' and promises to do Yoga.\",\"topic\":\"Listen, repeat and enact\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list is the past tense of \'sleep\'?\",\"options\":[\"matter\",\"slept\",\"active\",\"hope\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'slept\' is the past tense form of the verb \'sleep\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word refers to the physical world, including plants, animals, and the landscape?\",\"options\":[\"nature\",\"exercise\",\"understood\",\"matter\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Nature refers to the physical world and everything in it that is not made by people.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the past tense of the word \'understand\' as given in the text?\",\"options\":[\"understands\",\"understanding\",\"understood\",\"under\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'understood\' is the past tense of \'understand\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is energetic and busy doing things, which word describes them best?\",\"options\":[\"slept\",\"hope\",\"active\",\"matter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Being \'active\' means engaging in physical movement or being energetic.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes physical activity done to keep the body strong and healthy?\",\"options\":[\"nature\",\"exercise\",\"understood\",\"hope\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Exercise is physical activity performed to improve health and fitness.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word represents a feeling of wanting something to happen and thinking that it could happen?\",\"options\":[\"hope\",\"matter\",\"active\",\"slept\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Hope is a feeling of expectation and desire for a particular thing to happen.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence using a word from the list: \'It does not ____ how slow you go, as long as you do not stop.\'\",\"options\":[\"nature\",\"active\",\"matter\",\"slept\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'matter\' means to be important or significant.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Choose the correct word to complete this sentence: \'After doing yoga, the tired boy ____ soundly at night.\'\",\"options\":[\"active\",\"slept\",\"nature\",\"hope\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Slept\' is the correct past tense verb to describe the boy\'s action at night.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list is the opposite (antonym) of being \'lazy\' or \'still\'?\",\"options\":[\"matter\",\"understood\",\"active\",\"nature\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Active\' is the opposite of being lazy or inactive.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the state of a student who has successfully grasped a new yoga lesson?\",\"options\":[\"understood\",\"slept\",\"matter\",\"nature\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Understood\' indicates that the student has comprehended or learned the lesson.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21533,19,4,'English','en','Let\'s Fly in an Aeroplane','[\"Let’s Fly in an Aeroplane is about a trip from Mumbai to Goa by plane.\",\"The story starts at the airport where we check in, show tickets and ID, and get boarding passes.\",\"At the security check, bags go on a conveyor belt and pass through a machine that makes a whir‑whir sound.\",\"We walk through a gate that beeps and then wait at the gate for our turn to board.\",\"The flight number 302 to Goa is announced and we board through a long tunnel called the aerobridge.\",\"The air hostess greets us at the door and we find our seats and fasten seat belts with a click sound.\",\"The plane starts to move slowly, then faster, and the wings stretch wide while the engines roar and the plane takes off.\",\"During flight we see tiny houses, moving cars, twisting roads, fluffy clouds, green trees and an endless blue sky.\",\"The pilot speaks from the speaker, saying the weather is clear and sunny and that we are flying high above the clouds.\",\"When we reach Goa the pilot announces we are ready to land, the plane slows down, touches the ground and we land safely.\",\"The whole experience is full of sounds like whir‑whir, beep‑beep, vroom‑vroom, whoosh, and sights like cotton candy clouds and a green carpet of trees.\",\"The story teaches us about airport procedures, safety, and what we can see from a plane’s window.\",\"It also includes activities such as matching dialogues, arranging events in order, and making a paper aeroplane.\",\"The chapter encourages listening, repeating, and describing what we see and feel.\",\"It introduces simple transitional words like “first”, “then”, “after that”, “finally”.\",\"It helps students practice vocabulary related to travel, such as aeroplane, airport, ticket, boarding, seat belt, engine, pilot, passengers, and flight.\",\"The exercises involve fill‑in‑the‑blank, matching, true\\/false, and descriptive questions.\",\"Students can also create new words from given letters and match sound words to actions.\",\"The chapter ends with a hands‑on activity to fold a paper aeroplane.\"]','[{\"q\":\"From which city are the travelers starting their trip?\",\"options\":[\"Pune\",\"Mumbai\",\"Goa\",\"Delhi\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'We are going on a trip from Mumbai to Goa!\'\",\"topic\":\"At the Airport\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do the big boards at the airport show?\",\"options\":[\"The names of the pilots\",\"The price of food\",\"Where the flights are going\",\"The weather in Goa\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'big boards showing where the flights are going.\'\",\"topic\":\"At the Airport\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where do the travelers go to show their tickets and ID-cards?\",\"options\":[\"To the security gate\",\"To the check-in counter\",\"To the airplane door\",\"To the baggage area\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'We go to the check-in counter. The officer smiles and says, “Please show me your tickets and ID-cards.”\'\",\"topic\":\"At the Airport\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What do the travelers receive after handing over their tickets and ID-cards?\",\"options\":[\"A map of Goa\",\"Their luggage\",\"Boarding passes\",\"New passports\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'We hand them over and get our boarding passes.\'\",\"topic\":\"At the Airport\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the actions in the text, what would you be doing with your bags as you enter the airport?\",\"options\":[\"Carrying them on your head\",\"Leaving them at the door\",\"Pulling them as you walk\",\"Putting them on a bus\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Let\'s pull our bags and walk into the big airport.\'\",\"topic\":\"At the Airport\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Imagine you are at the check-in counter. Based on the text, what information will you find on the pass the officer gives you?\",\"options\":[\"The color of the plane\",\"Your seat number\",\"The weight of your bag\",\"The name of the airport\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Now we know our seat numbers\' after getting the boarding passes.\",\"topic\":\"At the Airport\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the travelers say \'Hurray!\' after receiving their boarding passes?\",\"options\":[\"Because they were leaving the airport\",\"Because they were happy to know their seat numbers and move forward with the trip\",\"Because they found their lost bags\",\"Because the officer gave them a gift\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The exclamation \'Hurray!\' shows excitement about getting the passes and knowing their seat numbers.\",\"topic\":\"At the Airport\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these details from the text best describes the atmosphere inside the airport?\",\"options\":[\"Quiet and empty\",\"Dark and scary\",\"Busy with many people, lights, and boards\",\"Small and crowded with trees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the airport as having \'so many people, lights and big boards\'.\",\"topic\":\"At the Airport\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the aeroplane doing?\",\"options\":[\"Landing on a short road\",\"Flying in the sky above houses and trees\",\"Parking inside a large garage\",\"Floating on a river\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the aeroplane in the sky with clouds around it, above the ground level.\",\"topic\":\"At the Airport\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/066_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the given figure, what objects are shown on the ground below the clouds?\",\"options\":[\"Only a large airport building\",\"A road, houses, and trees\",\"A beach with sand and umbrellas\",\"A mountain covered in snow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration clearly shows a winding road, two houses, and several green trees on the ground.\",\"topic\":\"At the Airport\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/066_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What sound does the big machine make when the bags go inside?\",\"options\":[\"whirr-whirr-whirr\",\"beep-beep\",\"tick-tock\",\"zoom-zoom\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the big machine goes \'whirr-whirr-whirr\' when the bags go inside.\",\"topic\":\"Security and Boarding\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the number of the flight mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Flight No. 203\",\"Flight No. 302\",\"Flight No. 501\",\"Flight No. 100\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Flight No. 302 to Goa\' in the boarding announcement.\",\"topic\":\"Security and Boarding\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the long tunnel used to reach the aeroplane?\",\"options\":[\"aerobridge\",\"skywalk\",\"security gate\",\"conveyor belt\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text describes the long tunnel as an \'aerobridge\'.\",\"topic\":\"Security and Boarding\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when you walk through the security gate?\",\"options\":[\"It says \'Welcome\'\",\"It makes a beep-beep sound\",\"It starts to whirr\",\"It turns into a tunnel\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'We walk through a gate that makes a beep-beep sound.\'\",\"topic\":\"Security and Boarding\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who greets the passengers at the door of the aeroplane?\",\"options\":[\"The security officer\",\"The pilot\",\"The air hostess\",\"The gate agent\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the air hostess at the door greets them with a smile.\",\"topic\":\"Security and Boarding\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How is the aeroplane described when seen from the aerobridge?\",\"options\":[\"Small and white\",\"Big and shiny\",\"Fast and loud\",\"Old and grey\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The aeroplane looks so big and shiny.\'\",\"topic\":\"Security and Boarding\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what should you do immediately after the security officer says \'All clear\'?\",\"options\":[\"Board the plane\",\"Put bags on the belt\",\"Walk to the gate and wait\",\"Listen to the air hostess\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says after the officer says \'All clear\', the next step is to walk to the gate and wait for the turn to board.\",\"topic\":\"Security and Boarding\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you hear the announcement \'Flight No. 302 to Goa is ready for boarding\', what is about to happen?\",\"options\":[\"The security check is starting\",\"The passengers are going to enter the plane\",\"The bags are being put on the belt\",\"The plane is landing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Boarding means the process where passengers get onto the aeroplane to start their journey.\",\"topic\":\"Security and Boarding\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why do the passengers\' hearts \'jump with joy\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the machine made a loud noise\",\"Because they are excited that their flight is ready\",\"Because they like walking through tunnels\",\"Because the security officer smiled at them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links the feeling of joy to the announcement that the flight is ready for boarding.\",\"topic\":\"Security and Boarding\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct order of events described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Boarding -> Security Check -> Aerobridge\",\"Aerobridge -> Security Check -> Boarding\",\"Security Check -> Waiting at Gate -> Aerobridge\",\"Waiting at Gate -> Security Check -> Aerobridge\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text follows the sequence: security check first, then waiting at the gate, then walking through the aerobridge.\",\"topic\":\"Security and Boarding\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How do the things inside the aeroplane look to the passengers?\",\"options\":[\"Old and dusty\",\"New\",\"Broken\",\"Dark\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'everything looks new\' inside the aeroplane.\",\"topic\":\"Take-off\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound is heard when the seat belts are fastened?\",\"options\":[\"Vroooom!\",\"Zoom!\",\"Click!\",\"Rumble!\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'fasten our seat belts—click!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Take-off\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the small windows in the aeroplane used for?\",\"options\":[\"To let in the rain\",\"To talk to the pilot\",\"To look outside\",\"To throw things out\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'there are small windows to look outside\'.\",\"topic\":\"Take-off\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the first thing the aeroplane does when it starts to move?\",\"options\":[\"It flies up high\",\"It moves slowly\",\"It stops suddenly\",\"It moves backwards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'The aeroplane starts to move slowly\'.\",\"topic\":\"Take-off\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you hear the sound \'rumble-rumble-rumble\', what is the aeroplane doing?\",\"options\":[\"Flying in the sky\",\"Moving slowly on the ground\",\"Fastening the seat belts\",\"Stretching its wings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text associates the \'rumble-rumble-rumble\' sound with moving slowly.\",\"topic\":\"Take-off\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which sound indicates that the aeroplane is moving faster?\",\"options\":[\"Click!\",\"Soft\",\"Vroooom!\",\"Wide\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'then faster—vroooom!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Take-off\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the wings during the take-off process?\",\"options\":[\"They flap like a bird\",\"They stretch wide\",\"They fold inside\",\"They make a click sound\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'The wings stretch wide\'.\",\"topic\":\"Take-off\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the correct order of events?\",\"options\":[\"Fasten belts, move slowly, engines roar\",\"Engines roar, fasten belts, move slowly\",\"Move slowly, fasten belts, up in the sky\",\"Up in the sky, move faster, fasten belts\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text follows the sequence: fastening belts, moving slowly, then engines roaring for take-off.\",\"topic\":\"Take-off\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the aeroplane is described as making a \'roar\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"The seats\",\"The windows\",\"The engines\",\"The seat belts\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'the engines roar—zoom! zoom!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Take-off\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final result of the engines roaring and the wings stretching?\",\"options\":[\"The seats become soft\",\"The windows get smaller\",\"The plane moves slowly\",\"The plane goes up in the sky\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that after the engines roar, \'suddenly, we are up in the sky!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Take-off\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what do the houses look like from the aeroplane window?\",\"options\":[\"Moving dots\",\"Toy blocks\",\"Twisted ribbons\",\"Cotton candy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the houses look tiny like toy blocks.\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which city is the aeroplane about to reach?\",\"options\":[\"Mumbai\",\"Delhi\",\"Goa\",\"Pune\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions, \'Look! We are about to reach Goa.\'\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound is heard when the aeroplane\'s wheels touch the ground?\",\"options\":[\"Whooosh\",\"Swoosh\",\"Thud\",\"Rumble\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the wheels touching the ground with a \'thud!\' sound.\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the pilot\'s voice come from?\",\"options\":[\"The window\",\"The engine\",\"The speaker\",\"The clouds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The pilot’s voice comes from the speaker.\'\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'big green carpet\' refer to in the passage?\",\"options\":[\"The sky\",\"The clouds\",\"The trees\",\"The roads\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The trees look like a big green carpet!\'\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does the world below change as the aeroplane slowly goes down for landing?\",\"options\":[\"It appears smaller\",\"It appears bigger\",\"It turns white\",\"It disappears\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that as the plane goes down, \'The world below appears bigger.\'\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the weather like according to the pilot\'s announcement?\",\"options\":[\"Rainy and cold\",\"Cloudy and dark\",\"Clear and sunny\",\"Windy and stormy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The pilot states, \'The weather is clear and sunny.\'\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the author compare the roads to \'ribbons\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are colorful\",\"Because they twist and turn\",\"Because they are made of cloth\",\"Because they are very wide\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'The roads twist like ribbons,\' implying a comparison based on their shape.\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are sitting in the plane and hear \'screech... rumble...\', what part of the journey are you in?\",\"options\":[\"Taking off from the ground\",\"Flying high above the clouds\",\"Rolling along the runway after landing\",\"Waiting at the airport\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text associates \'screech... rumble\' with rolling along the runway after the wheels touch the ground.\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sounds best describes the aeroplane flying smoothly through the sky?\",\"options\":[\"Thud\",\"Screech\",\"Whooosh... swoosh...\",\"Rumble\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'whooosh... swoosh...\' to describe the plane flying smoothly.\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the descriptions in the text, which color is most associated with the trees?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"White\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text compares trees to a \'green carpet\', identifying their color as green.\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the aeroplane\'s wings as it rolls along the runway?\",\"options\":[\"They fall off\",\"They flap slightly\",\"They turn into ribbons\",\"They stop moving completely\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'the wings flap slightly as we roll along the runway.\'\",\"topic\":\"In the Air and Landing\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the person who flies the aeroplane?\",\"options\":[\"Officer\",\"Pilot\",\"Passenger\",\"Air hostess\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A pilot is the person trained to fly and operate an aircraft.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where do aeroplanes take off from and land?\",\"options\":[\"Tunnel\",\"Station\",\"Airport\",\"Engine\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"An airport is a specialized place where aircraft take off and land.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the woman called who looks after the people on a plane?\",\"options\":[\"Pilot\",\"Officer\",\"Air hostess\",\"Passenger\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"An air hostess is responsible for the comfort and safety of people on a flight.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the process of getting onto the aeroplane called?\",\"options\":[\"Fastening\",\"Checking\",\"Flight\",\"Boarding\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Boarding is the act of passengers entering the aircraft.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Before the plane takes off, what must you do to your seatbelt?\",\"options\":[\"Fasten\",\"Check\",\"Board\",\"Flight\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To fasten means to close or join the ends of the seatbelt securely.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are already inside the plane, you are said to be ______.\",\"options\":[\"Aboard\",\"Tunnel\",\"Engine\",\"Officer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Aboard means being on or inside a vehicle like an aeroplane.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the aeroplane provides the power to fly?\",\"options\":[\"Tunnel\",\"Engine\",\"Airport\",\"Boarding\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The engine is the machine that provides the necessary power for the flight.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"A person who travels in the plane but does not fly it is a ______.\",\"options\":[\"Pilot\",\"Officer\",\"Passenger\",\"Air hostess\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A passenger is a person traveling in a vehicle who is not the driver or crew.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The journey made by an aeroplane through the air is called a ______.\",\"options\":[\"Boarding\",\"Flight\",\"Tunnel\",\"Engine\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Flight refers to the action or process of flying through the air.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When the staff looks at your tickets or bags to verify them, they ______ them.\",\"options\":[\"Fasten\",\"Flight\",\"Check\",\"Aboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To check means to examine something to ensure it is correct or safe.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21534,19,4,'English','en','The Warli Art and Culture','[\"Warli people live in Maharashtra, near green forests and hills of Palghar and Thane.\",\"They are one of the oldest tribes in India.\",\"They live in small mud houses with thatched roofs.\",\"They decorate their houses with beautiful white Warli art.\",\"Warli painting is a special kind of art made by the Warli people.\",\"It is done on mud walls using white paint made from rice flour paste.\",\"They use simple shapes like circles, triangles, and squares in their paintings.\",\"Shapes represent people, animals, trees, huts and the sun.\",\"Warli paintings tell stories about farming, hunting, dancing, fishing and celebrations.\",\"Every picture shows how they love and respect nature.\",\"Tarpa dance is a famous Warli dance where men and women hold hands and move in a circle.\",\"A Tarpa is a musical instrument made from bamboo and a dried gourd.\",\"Warli art is not just decoration; it is a way to share life, joy and love for nature.\",\"The art helps the Warli people express their daily life and feelings.\",\"Warli artists use bright white paint on dark mud walls.\",\"They often paint scenes of their village life and nature.\",\"The art style is simple but powerful and symbolic.\",\"Warli art has gained national and international recognition.\",\"Warli people value community, nature and harmony.\",\"They celebrate festivals with dances and music.\",\"Their art is passed down from generation to generation.\",\"Warli culture is an important part of Maharashtra’s heritage.\",\"Warli art is a living tradition that continues to thrive today.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which districts of Maharashtra do the Warli people live?\",\"options\":[\"Palghar and Thane\",\"Mumbai and Pune\",\"Nashik and Nagpur\",\"Satara and Sangli\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that Warli people live near the green forests and hills of Palghar and Thane.\",\"topic\":\"Warli Painting\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the white paint used in Warli art made from?\",\"options\":[\"White chalk powder\",\"Rice flour paste\",\"Milk and water\",\"White oil paint\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, they use white paint made from rice flour paste.\",\"topic\":\"Warli Painting\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of roofs do the mud houses of Warli people have?\",\"options\":[\"Tiled roofs\",\"Concrete roofs\",\"Thatched roofs\",\"Tin roofs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Warli people live in small mud houses with thatched roofs.\",\"topic\":\"Warli Painting\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these shapes is NOT mentioned as being used in Warli paintings?\",\"options\":[\"Circles\",\"Triangles\",\"Squares\",\"Stars\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists circles, triangles, and squares as the simple shapes used in their art.\",\"topic\":\"Warli Painting\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a Warli artist wants to draw a sun or a person, what would they use?\",\"options\":[\"Complex 3D models\",\"Simple shapes like circles and triangles\",\"Bright oil colors\",\"Photographs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they use simple shapes like circles, triangles, and squares to show people, animals, and the sun.\",\"topic\":\"Warli Painting\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What do Warli paintings tell stories about?\",\"options\":[\"City life and traffic\",\"Farming, hunting, and dancing\",\"Space travel and stars\",\"Kings and queens in palaces\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states their paintings tell stories about farming, hunting, dancing, fishing and celebrations.\",\"topic\":\"Warli Painting\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Warli people are described as one of the ______ tribes in India.\",\"options\":[\"Newest\",\"Oldest\",\"Richest\",\"Largest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions they are one of the oldest tribes in India.\",\"topic\":\"Warli Painting\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the Warli art specifically painted on the houses?\",\"options\":[\"On the wooden doors\",\"On the mud walls\",\"On the thatched roofs\",\"On the stone floors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they do the painting on mud walls.\",\"topic\":\"Warli Painting\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does every Warli picture show about their relationship with the environment?\",\"options\":[\"How they want to cut down trees\",\"How they love and respect nature\",\"How they build big factories\",\"How they ignore the animals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying every picture shows how they love and respect nature.\",\"topic\":\"Warli Painting\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which activity would most likely be the subject of a Warli painting?\",\"options\":[\"A celebration in the village\",\"A car race on a highway\",\"A computer class\",\"A flight to the moon\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions celebrations as one of the themes in their paintings.\",\"topic\":\"Warli Painting\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the famous Warli dance mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Ghoomar dance\",\"Tarpa dance\",\"Bhangra dance\",\"Kathak dance\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that one famous Warli dance is the Tarpa dance.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which materials are used to make the Tarpa musical instrument?\",\"options\":[\"Plastic and metal\",\"Wood and iron\",\"Bamboo and a dried gourd\",\"Clay and paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the Tarpa is made from bamboo and a dried gourd.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How do men and women move during the Tarpa dance?\",\"options\":[\"They stand in two separate lines\",\"They sit down and clap\",\"They hold hands and move in a circle\",\"They dance individually without touching\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes that in this dance, men and women hold hands and move in a circle.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, Warli art is not just decoration. What else does it share?\",\"options\":[\"Their wealth and power\",\"Their life, joy and love for nature\",\"Their history of wars\",\"Their knowledge of science\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says their art is a way to share their life, joy and love for nature.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a Warli man is playing a \'Tarpa\', what is he doing?\",\"options\":[\"He is cooking food\",\"He is painting a wall\",\"He is playing a musical instrument\",\"He is building a house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the Tarpa as a musical instrument.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text means \'a thing used for playing music\'?\",\"options\":[\"Famous\",\"Instrument\",\"Decoration\",\"Nature\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'instrument\' is used in the text to describe the Tarpa used for music.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what can we say about the participation in the Tarpa dance?\",\"options\":[\"Only men are allowed to dance\",\"Only women are allowed to dance\",\"Both men and women participate together\",\"Children are not allowed to watch\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'men and women hold hands\', implying joint participation.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why would a Warli artist create a painting according to the passage?\",\"options\":[\"To earn a lot of money\",\"To show their love for nature and life\",\"To hide the cracks in the wall\",\"To compete with other tribes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains their art is a way to share their life, joy, and love for nature.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT the primary purpose of Warli art as stated in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Just decoration\",\"Sharing joy\",\"Sharing life\",\"Love for nature\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says their art is \'not just decoration\', implying decoration is not the only or primary purpose.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the use of bamboo and dried gourd for an instrument suggest about the Warli people?\",\"options\":[\"They use natural materials from their environment\",\"They prefer to buy expensive instruments\",\"They do not know how to use wood\",\"They only use plastic items\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Bamboo and gourds are natural items, reflecting their \'love for nature\' mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21535,19,4,'English','en','The Kite','[\"- A kite is a light toy that flies in the wind.\",\"- Kites are usually made of paper, cloth or plastic on a lightweight frame.\",\"- The string is tied to the kite and pulled to keep it aloft.\",\"- Kites fly because the wind pushes against their wings, giving lift.\",\"- Colours of kites are bright and many people choose their favourite colour.\",\"- In Maharashtra, people celebrate Makar Sankranti by flying kites and eating Tilgul.\",\"- To make a paper kite, you need paper, a stick, string, and glue.\",\"- The kite’s shape is like a triangle or diamond to catch the wind.\",\"- Opposites: up ↔ down, light ↔ heavy, small ↔ big, above ↔ below, wild ↔ tame, town ↔ forest.\",\"- Kites are fun because they let us see the sky from a new height.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In the poem, the kites are compared to which of these?\",\"options\":[\"Coloured birds\",\"Small airplanes\",\"Floating clouds\",\"Paper boats\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Like coloured birds \\/ In the wind-whipped sky.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Kite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where are the kites flying in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"In the park\",\"Up in the air\",\"Over the sea\",\"Near the rooftops\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem begins with \'Up in the air \\/ See the kites fly\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Kite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is the sky described in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Blue and clear\",\"Dark and rainy\",\"Wind-whipped\",\"Bright and sunny\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem uses the phrase \'In the wind-whipped sky.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Kite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the speaker wish to be like so they can climb on a kite?\",\"options\":[\"Fast and strong\",\"Small and light as air\",\"Big and heavy\",\"Thin and tall\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speaker says, \'I wish I were small \\/ and light as air\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Kite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the speaker were on a kite, what would they drift upon?\",\"options\":[\"Cotton clouds\",\"Soft feathers\",\"Paper wings\",\"Silk strings\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'Then I’d drift upon \\/ The paper wings\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Kite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the wild wind do in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"It blows the trees\",\"It sings songs\",\"It makes the speaker cold\",\"It tears the paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says the speaker would \'hear the songs \\/ That the wild wind sings.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Kite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which two places would the speaker look down upon from the kite?\",\"options\":[\"The forest and the river\",\"The school and the playground\",\"The park and the rooftops\",\"The beach and the mountains\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Over the park \\/ And the rooftops of town.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Kite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What would the people below do when they see the speaker high in the air?\",\"options\":[\"Run and hide\",\"Shout and wave\",\"Stand and stare\",\"Sit and sleep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'The people below \\/ Would stand and stare\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Kite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what would the people below wish for?\",\"options\":[\"They would wish to be the speaker\",\"They would wish for a new kite\",\"They would wish for the wind to stop\",\"They would wish to go to the park\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says the people would \'wish they were me \\/ High, high in the air.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Kite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What material are the kite\'s wings made of, as mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Cloth\",\"Plastic\",\"Paper\",\"Leaves\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem specifically mentions \'The paper wings\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Kite\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'fly\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"sky\",\"wings\",\"town\",\"air\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'fly\' and \'sky\' together as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with \'wings\' in the given list?\",\"options\":[\"sky\",\"sings\",\"down\",\"there\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'wings\' with \'sings\' as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the word that rhymes with \'town\'.\",\"options\":[\"down\",\"stare\",\"fly\",\"wings\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'town\' and \'down\' as a rhyming pair.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words rhymes with \'air\'?\",\"options\":[\"sings\",\"sky\",\"there\",\"town\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'air\', \'there\', and \'stare\' as rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of three words rhyme together in the text?\",\"options\":[\"fly, sky, wings\",\"air, there, stare\",\"town, down, air\",\"wings, sings, sky\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text groups \'air\', \'there\', and \'stare\' together as a set of rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides a kite, what is another \'paper thing\' the text suggests making?\",\"options\":[\"A bird\",\"A boat\",\"A house\",\"A car\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s notes suggest motivating students to prepare other paper things like a boat.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"For which festival should students create invitation cards?\",\"options\":[\"Diwali\",\"Holi\",\"Makar Sankranti\",\"Eid\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions creating invitation cards for Makar Sankranti.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the common feature between the words \'air\', \'there\', and \'stare\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"They all start with the letter \'a\'\",\"They are all names of colors\",\"They rhyme with each other\",\"They are names of birds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"These words are grouped together because they have similar ending sounds (rhymes).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a \'paper thing\' mentioned in the teacher\'s notes for preparation?\",\"options\":[\"A cap\",\"A pen\",\"A table\",\"A tree\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'cap\' as an example of a paper thing students can prepare.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners share their experience about, according to the teacher\'s notes?\",\"options\":[\"Making a boat\",\"Kite making\",\"Making a cap\",\"Making a card\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The notes state to encourage learners to share their experience regarding kite making.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21536,19,4,'English','en','A Windy Discovery','[\"- Windmills or wind turbines use the wind to make electricity.\",\"- When wind blows, it pushes the long blades of a windmill, making them spin.\",\"- The spinning blades turn a rod that is connected to a generator.\",\"- A generator is a machine that turns the movement of the wind wheel into electrical power.\",\"- Wind energy is renewable, meaning it never runs out and it does not produce dirty smoke like factories.\",\"- Windmills are clean, green and smart helpers for our homes.\",\"- A simple model of a windmill can be made with paper, a pin and a straw or pencil.\",\"- The model has 7 coloured sections that spin when blown or moved by wind.\",\"- The windmill’s blades are like a giant fan that turns electricity.\",\"- Wind energy is a type of renewable energy that helps keep the earth clean.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did Dhiraj think the giant white fans were used for when he first saw them?\",\"options\":[\"To make the wind blow faster\",\"To keep the earth cool\",\"To help birds fly\",\"To clean the clouds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Dhiraj asks his dad if the giant fans are used to keep the earth cool.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is another name for the giant white fans?\",\"options\":[\"Air Coolers\",\"Wind Turbines\",\"Electric Poles\",\"Hill Fans\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Dhiraj\'s father explains that they are called Windmills or Wind Turbines.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What causes the long blades of the windmill to spin round and round?\",\"options\":[\"The generator\",\"Electricity from the house\",\"The blowing wind\",\"A motor inside the box\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that when the wind blows, it pushes the long blades and makes them spin.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the \'magic box\' machine that turns movement into power?\",\"options\":[\"A battery\",\"A transformer\",\"A generator\",\"An engine\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The father describes the machine connected to the rod as a generator.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Under what condition will the windmill stop making electricity?\",\"options\":[\"When it gets too hot\",\"Only if the wind stops blowing\",\"When the sun goes down\",\"When the house lights are turned off\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The father says it only stops if the wind stops blowing.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the term \'Renewable Energy\' mean in this lesson?\",\"options\":[\"Energy that is very expensive\",\"Energy that makes the air dirty\",\"Energy that never runs out\",\"Energy that comes from factories\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines Renewable Energy as meaning it never runs out.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the box containing the rod and generator located on the windmill?\",\"options\":[\"At the bottom of the hill\",\"Inside the car\",\"At the top of the windmill\",\"Underground\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions there is a box inside placed at the top.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is wind energy considered better than energy from factories?\",\"options\":[\"It is much louder\",\"It doesn\'t make the air dirty like smoke does\",\"It only works during the day\",\"It uses giant fans to cool the air\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states wind energy doesn\'t make the air dirty like smoke from factories does.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a town wants to use \'clean and green\' energy, which source should they choose based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Smoke from factories\",\"Wind energy\",\"Burning wood\",\"Coal power\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The father describes wind energy as clean, green, and smart.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the conversation, which sequence correctly shows how electricity is made?\",\"options\":[\"Electricity -> Wind -> Blades\",\"Generator -> Rod -> Wind\",\"Wind -> Spinning Blades -> Rod -> Generator\",\"Blades -> Wind -> House -> Generator\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains wind pushes blades, blades turn a rod, and the rod turns the generator.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is shown inside the cutaway section of the box at the top?\",\"options\":[\"A large cooling fan\",\"A rod connected to a machine with gears\",\"A battery for the car\",\"A bucket of water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the internal parts including the rod and the generator machine.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/077_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many long blades are attached to the hub of the wind turbine?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration clearly shows three blades on the wind turbine.\",\"topic\":\"A Windy Discovery\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/077_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step in making the windmill model according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Cut the paper neatly\",\"Draw a large round circle on the paper\",\"Color the sections with rainbow colors\",\"Attach a pin to a straw\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 1 clearly states to draw a large round circle on the paper using a compass or plate.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Into how many equal sections should the circle be divided?\",\"options\":[\"5 sections\",\"6 sections\",\"7 sections\",\"8 sections\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 3 specifies to divide the circle into 7 equal sections like pizza slices.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these materials is NOT mentioned in the \'Materials Needed\' list?\",\"options\":[\"Compass or round object\",\"Sketch pens or crayons\",\"Glue or tape\",\"Pin or paper fastener\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists compass, sketch pens, and pins, but does not mention glue or tape.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct order of rainbow colors to be used for the sections?\",\"options\":[\"Red, Orange, Yellow, Green, Blue, Indigo, Violet\",\"Violet, Indigo, Blue, Green, Yellow, Orange, Red\",\"Green, Yellow, Blue, Red, Violet, Indigo, Orange\",\"Blue, Green, Red, Yellow, Orange, Indigo, Violet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 5 lists the colors in order: Violet, Indigo, Blue, Green, Yellow, Orange, Red.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When making the straight cuts from the edge, where should you stop?\",\"options\":[\"At the very center of the circle\",\"1 cm from the edge\",\"2–3 cm before the centre\",\"Halfway through the slice\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 7 instructs to stop at 2–3 cm before the centre and not to cut fully.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In which direction should you twist each cut section?\",\"options\":[\"Anti-clockwise\",\"Clockwise\",\"Upwards\",\"Downwards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 8 states to slightly twist each cut section in the same direction (clockwise).\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the seven colors when the windmill spins?\",\"options\":[\"They turn into a dark black color\",\"They appear almost like one color\",\"They start to fade away\",\"They change their order\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 12 explains that when you watch them spin, the colors appear almost like one.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why must you ensure the pin attached to the straw or pencil \'rotates freely\'?\",\"options\":[\"So the pin does not fall off\",\"So the paper stays flat\",\"So the windmill can spin when you blow on it\",\"So the colors look brighter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rotation is necessary for the windmill to function as a model that spins with wind or breath.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What shape is the paper after you complete Step 2?\",\"options\":[\"A square sheet\",\"A round disc\",\"A long strip\",\"A triangle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 2 says to cut the circle neatly to get a round disc.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Listen and repeat\' list refers to energy that does not run out?\",\"options\":[\"Generator\",\"Renewable\",\"Turbines\",\"Exactly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Renewable energy refers to sources like wind that are not depleted when used.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of the pin or paper fastener in Step 9?\",\"options\":[\"To poke holes in the straw\",\"To fix all twisted tips at the centre\",\"To color the middle of the circle\",\"To measure the 2-3 cm distance\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 9 says to use a pin or paper fastener to fix all twisted tips at the centre.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the instructions, how can you make the windmill model move?\",\"options\":[\"By shaking the pencil\",\"By spinning it with your finger\",\"By blowing gently or taking it outdoors\",\"By pulling the pin out\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 11 suggests blowing gently or taking it outdoors to make it move.\",\"topic\":\"Let’s make a model of windmill\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21537,19,4,'English','en','My Word Family (Unit 3)','[\"- A word family is a group of words that share the same root or meaning.\",\"- Opposite words are called antonyms. Example: essential – unnecessary.\",\"- Hidden words are smaller words inside a longer word. Example: downtrodden contains down, odd, den.\",\"- Double letters appear when a letter is repeated, e.g., “cluck” has double ‘c’ sound but only one letter; a better example is “fluffy” with double ‘f’ sound.\",\"- Words ending with the letter ‘e’ are called e‑words. Example: essential, equality, justice.\",\"- Alphabetical order means arranging words from A to Z.\",\"- Syllables are the beats in a word. Example: hu-ma-ni-ty has three syllables.\",\"- A poem can use many words from the word family to make it interesting.\",\"- Dictionaries give the meaning of words and help you learn new ones.\",\"- Practice makes you better at spotting hidden words, antonyms, and syllables.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word from the list starts with \'e\' and means \'absolutely necessary\' or \'very important\'?\",\"options\":[\"essential\",\"entire\",\"equality\",\"evils\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'essential\' means something that is absolutely necessary.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list represents the sound made by a hen?\",\"options\":[\"stamp\",\"cluck\",\"fasten\",\"outward\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Cluck\' is the specific word in the list that describes the sound of a hen.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words refers to a person who collects and reports news?\",\"options\":[\"merchant\",\"reporter\",\"citizen\",\"humanity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A \'reporter\' is a person whose job is to discover information about news events and describe them.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list describes something soft and airy, like a cloud or wool?\",\"options\":[\"heavy\",\"narrow\",\"fluffy\",\"bottom\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Fluffy\' is the adjective used to describe something soft and light.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are told to secure your seatbelt, which word from the list means \'to close or join securely\'?\",\"options\":[\"fasten\",\"aligned\",\"boarding\",\"inspire\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Fasten\' means to close or join the two parts of something together.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list is the opposite of \'inward\'?\",\"options\":[\"entire\",\"outward\",\"previous\",\"narrow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Outward\' is the directional opposite of \'inward\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the word from the list that refers to a person who buys and sells goods in large quantities.\",\"options\":[\"citizen\",\"merchant\",\"reporter\",\"humanity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A \'merchant\' is a person involved in trade or commerce.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the final list of words, which word describes something that is not complex or is easy to understand?\",\"options\":[\"purity\",\"simplicity\",\"aligned\",\"narrow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Simplicity\' is the quality of being simple or easy to understand.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to waste material or trash?\",\"options\":[\"substance\",\"garbage\",\"tunnel\",\"bottom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Garbage\' is another word for waste or rubbish.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list means \'the state of being equal\', especially in status, rights, or opportunities?\",\"options\":[\"equality\",\"justice\",\"purity\",\"humanity\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Equality\' is the noun form representing the state of being equal.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21538,19,4,'English','en','Our Smart Village','[\"Solar energy is light from the Sun that can be used to make electricity or heat.\",\"Solar lights are small lamps that work all day and night by using solar panels.\",\"E‑library is a digital library where we can read books on a computer or phone.\",\"Maps help us find places and directions like North, South, East and West.\",\"Farmers can use phones to check weather and learn how to grow crops better.\",\"In a smart village, technology like solar power and e‑libraries make life easier.\",\"Solar panels absorb sunlight and convert it into electricity for lights and gadgets.\",\"Reading books in an e‑library is free and can be done anywhere in the village.\",\"Maps are useful for planning routes, finding schools, markets and farms.\",\"Using solar energy reduces the need for electricity from the grid.\",\"E‑libraries help children learn new words and stories without travelling.\",\"Smart villages use technology to improve health, education and farming.\",\"Solar lights keep streets bright after sunset, making it safer to walk.\",\"E‑libraries and maps are examples of digital tools that help villagers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what shines both day and night in the smart village?\",\"options\":[\"The moon\",\"Solar lights\",\"The stars\",\"Flashlights\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Solar lights shine day and night\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What device do farmers use to help them grow grain?\",\"options\":[\"Radio\",\"Television\",\"Phone\",\"Computer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Farmers use phone to grow the grain\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where are the \'wonders\' found in the E-Library?\",\"options\":[\"On the street\",\"In hidden nooks\",\"In the grain\",\"Under the sun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions the E-Library is \'Full of wonders in hidden nooks\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why do farmers watch the weather, Sun, and rain on their phones?\",\"options\":[\"To read maps\",\"To visit the library\",\"To grow the grain\",\"To charge solar lights\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links using the phone to watch weather with growing grain.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is installed on the roofs of the houses to collect energy from the Sun?\",\"options\":[\"Water tanks\",\"Solar panels\",\"Chimneys\",\"Satellite dishes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows blue solar panels on the roofs of the houses in the smart village.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/080_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which modern tool mentioned in the poem is the farmer using while standing near his crops?\",\"options\":[\"A drone\",\"A robot\",\"A mobile phone\",\"A map\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the farmer holding and talking into a mobile phone, as described in the poem.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/080_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What activity does the poem describe as \'just the best\'?\",\"options\":[\"Growing grain\",\"Reading maps\",\"Watching rain\",\"Shining lights\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The last line of the poem states, \'Reading maps is just the best\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poem say the E-Library is full of?\",\"options\":[\"Grain\",\"Books\",\"Phones\",\"Maps\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Our E-Library is full of books\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to find your way from North to South, which tool mentioned in the poem should you use?\",\"options\":[\"A phone\",\"A map\",\"Solar lights\",\"A book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem associates directions like North and South with reading maps.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, how do the solar lights change the appearance of the street?\",\"options\":[\"They make it wet and rainy\",\"They make it warm and bright\",\"They make it full of grain\",\"They make it hidden and dark\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says solar lights make the street \'so warm and bright\'.\",\"topic\":\"Listen and sing\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a topic listed for discussion in the exercise?\",\"options\":[\"Cooking food\",\"Map finding\",\"Playing cricket\",\"Watching TV\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'Map finding\' as one of the topics to talk about.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the teacher encouraged to help learners create?\",\"options\":[\"A wooden boat\",\"A paper plane\",\"A model of \'Solar house\'\",\"A clay pot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note suggests helping learners create a model of a \'Solar house\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is listed in the exercise to find a rhyming word for?\",\"options\":[\"Day\",\"Night\",\"Sun\",\"Moon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Night\' is the first word listed in the rhyming words exercise section.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are looking for a rhyming word for \'books\' from the list, which word fits best?\",\"options\":[\"Hooks\",\"Bags\",\"Pens\",\"Paper\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Hooks\' rhymes with \'books\', which is a word listed in the rhyming exercise.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The exercise asks students to talk about the use of which type of energy?\",\"options\":[\"Wind energy\",\"Solar energy\",\"Electrical energy\",\"Muscle energy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Use of Solar energy\' as a discussion topic.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity mentioned in the text involves using technology for reading and study?\",\"options\":[\"Map finding\",\"Use of e-library\",\"Solar energy\",\"Finding rhymes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"An e-library is a digital resource for reading, mentioned as a discussion topic.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The exercise asks to find a rhyming word for \'west\'. Which of these is a rhyming word for it?\",\"options\":[\"East\",\"Best\",\"North\",\"South\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Best\' rhymes with \'west\', which is one of the words provided in the exercise.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is making a \'Solar house\' model, whose suggestion are they following?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher\'s suggestion\",\"The librarian\'s suggestion\",\"The map maker\'s suggestion\",\"The farmer\'s suggestion\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states \'For the Teacher: Help them to create a model of Solar house.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners share their experience about, according to the teacher\'s note?\",\"options\":[\"City life\",\"School life\",\"Village life\",\"Forest life\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note encourages learners to share their experience about village life.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the exercise list rhymes with the word \'rain\'?\",\"options\":[\"Books\",\"West\",\"Grain\",\"Night\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Grain\' is listed in the exercise and it rhymes with \'rain\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21539,19,4,'English','en','The Giant Radish','[\"- A radish is a root vegetable that grows underground.\",\"- Ramu Kaka planted radish seeds in his garden.\",\"- He dug holes, sowed seeds, covered them with soil, watered and pulled weeds.\",\"- Most radishes grew small, but one grew very big – a giant radish.\",\"- Ramu Kaka, his wife, daughter, son, dog, cat, and hen all tried to pull the giant radish.\",\"- The hen helped by scratching the soil around the radish, loosening it.\",\"- After the soil was loose, the radish came out easily.\",\"- The story shows teamwork and that even a small hen can help a big task.\",\"- Key words: radish, soil, leaves, giant, curry, pull, heave‑ho, scratch, peck, loose, easier, harder.\",\"- The story also teaches listening to sounds and matching them with actions.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did Ramu Kaka plant in his garden one morning?\",\"options\":[\"Tomato seeds\",\"Radish seeds\",\"Carrot seeds\",\"Pumpkin seeds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that one morning Ramu Kaka went to his garden to plant radish seeds.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound did Ramu Kaka make while sowing the seeds?\",\"options\":[\"Scritch, scratch\",\"Pat, pat, pat\",\"Plink, plink, plink\",\"Splish, splash\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, he sowed the seeds in - plink, plink, plink!\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what part of the plant is Ramu Kaka holding to pull the radish?\",\"options\":[\"The root\",\"The stem\",\"The leaves\",\"The flowers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text and image show Ramu Kaka held the leaves and pulled.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/083_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Unscramble the vegetable name: \'ractors\'\",\"options\":[\"Radishes\",\"Carrots\",\"Onions\",\"Tomatoes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'ractors\' unscrambles to \'carrots\', which is in the list of vegetables.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Ramu Kaka call his wife, Renu?\",\"options\":[\"To cook dinner\",\"To water the plants\",\"To help him pull the radish\",\"To bring him water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ramu Kaka called Renu saying, \'Please help me pull the radish!\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who held onto the dog, Raju, while pulling the radish?\",\"options\":[\"Ravi\",\"Radha\",\"Rani the cat\",\"The hen\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Rani held Raju. Ra