Narrating a fantasy story\",\"Reading a textbook\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Telling a story about a talking mountain (fantasy) aligns with \'narrate any fantasy stories\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the common theme between a \'Giant Tomato\' and a \'Man with Giant Head\'?\",\"options\":[\"They are both real things\",\"They are both fantasy things\",\"They are both characters in the story\",\"They are both found in a garden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text groups these examples under the category of \'fantasy things\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity combines both identifying story elements and artistic expression?\",\"options\":[\"Reading other fantasy stories\",\"Narrating a story\",\"Listing characters and drawing your favorite one\",\"Creating a poster of a Giant Tomato\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Listing characters identifies elements, and drawing the favorite one is artistic expression.\",\"topic\":\"For the Teacher\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21540,19,4,'English','en','Animal Fair','[\"- An animal fair is a place where many animals are sold.\",\"- Raju and his father went to the fair to buy animals for their farm.\",\"- They bought five cows and twenty hens.\",\"- The farm already had a horse, a bullock and two dogs.\",\"- Cows give milk, which can be used to make butter and cheese.\",\"- Hens give eggs, which can be used to make cakes and other foods.\",\"- Animals need a clean home: a shed for cows, a coop for hens, a stable for the horse, kennels for dogs.\",\"- If animals get sick, a veterinary doctor gives them medicine.\",\"- Animals make different sounds: cows moo, ducks quack, hens squawk, dogs bark, goats bleat, donkeys bray, snakes hiss.\",\"- Children should learn to care for animals and keep them healthy.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which animals were already on Raju\'s farm before they went to the fair?\",\"options\":[\"A horse, a bullock and two dogs\",\"Cows, ducks and hens\",\"Goats and buffaloes\",\"Only a horse and a cow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states Raju\'s farm had \'Just a horse, a bullock and two dogs.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Baba say they would go to buy more animals?\",\"options\":[\"To the city\",\"To the forest\",\"To the animal fair\",\"To another farm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Baba said, \'We will go to the animal fair and buy some animals.\'\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where were the animals kept at the fair?\",\"options\":[\"In small cages\",\"In big pens\",\"In wooden boxes\",\"In the open fields\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions there were many animals kept in \'big pens\' at the fair.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what sound did the ducks make?\",\"options\":[\"Mooed\",\"Squawked\",\"Barked\",\"Quacked\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists sounds made by animals, including \'quacked\' for ducks.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Raju and his father go to the animal fair?\",\"options\":[\"To sell their horse\",\"To buy some animals\",\"To see the big pens\",\"To feed the cows\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Baba suggested going to the fair to buy some animals because they only had a few on their farm.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Raju wants to see an animal that \'mooed\', which animal should he look for at the fair?\",\"options\":[\"Ducks\",\"Hens\",\"Cows\",\"Dogs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text associates the sound \'mooed\' with the animals listed, where cows are the primary animal that moos.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which o