c\":\"Complete the following\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is listed in the first column (Subject) of the table?\",\"options\":[\"They\",\"She\",\"It\",\"Them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first column of the table includes \'I\', \'He\', \'She\', \'We\', and \'You\'.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare sentences\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which action word (verb) is found in the third column of the table?\",\"options\":[\"Sing\",\"Praise\",\"Write\",\"Play\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The third column lists \'do\', \'work\', \'read\', \'help\', and \'praise\'.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare sentences\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the situational prompts, where might you see your friend crying?\",\"options\":[\"On the playground\",\"In the classroom\",\"At the library\",\"In the garden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the situation: \'When you see your friend is crying in the classroom.\'\",\"topic\":\"Prepare sentences\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used in the second column for every sentence prepared from the table?\",\"options\":[\"can\",\"shall\",\"will\",\"must\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The second column of the table contains only the word \'will\'.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare sentences\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase completes the last column of the table?\",\"options\":[\"in your task\",\"in the book\",\"very fast\",\"the lesson\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The last column includes \'the poem\', \'my best\', \'my work\', \'hard\', and \'in your task\'.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare sentences\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific subject mentioned in the situation involving a Maths problem?\",\"options\":[\"Science\",\"English\",\"History\",\"Maths\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the situation: \'You do not understand a Maths problem.\'\",\"topic\":\"Prepare sentences\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Using the table, which of these is a correctly formed sentence?\",\"options\":[\"I will help hard.\",\"We will do the poem.\",\"She will praise my best.\",\"He will read my work.\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"By combining words from each column, \'He\' (Col 1) + \'will\' (Col 2) + \'read\' (Col 3) + \'my work\' (Col 4) forms a valid sentence.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare sentences\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence using words from the table: \'We will ____ hard.\'\",\"options\":[\"do\",\"work\",\"praise\",\"read\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the table, \'work\' is the verb that logically pairs with the complement \'hard\'.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare sentences\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are not selected for the quiz competition, which sentence from the table best shows a positive mindset?\",\"options\":[\"I will do my best.\",\"You will read the poem.\",\"She will help hard.\",\"He will praise in your task.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Doing one\'s best is a constructive response to not being selected, using words available in the table.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare sentences\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which situation from the text involves a competition?\",\"options\":[\"Not understanding a problem\",\"Seeing a friend cry\",\"Not being selected for the quiz\",\"Reading a poem\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'You are not selected for the quiz competition\' as a situation.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare sentences\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main task mentioned in the textbook text?\",\"options\":[\"Write a story\",\"Prepare a poster\",\"Sing a song\",\"Draw a map\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly asks the student to \'Prepare a poster\'.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare a poster\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you use to prepare the poster?\",\"options\":[\"Only colors\",\"Your own ideas\",\"A textbook picture\",\"A friend\'s drawing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to prepare the poster \'by using your own ideas\'.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare a poster\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase from the text is used to talk about your abilities?\",\"options\":[\"I am\",\"I can\",\"I have\",\"I was\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'I can\' is the prompt used to express what a person is able to do.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare a poster\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase is used to describe your qualities or identity?\",\"options\":[\"I can\",\"I am\",\"I will\",\"I do\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'I am\' is the prompt used for self-description or qualities.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare a poster\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The phrase \'I can overcome .....\' is meant for talking about:\",\"options\":[\"Food you like\",\"Games you play\",\"Difficulties or challenges\",\"Your name\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To \'overcome\' means to succeed in dealing with a problem or difficulty.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare a poster\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to write about your skill in \'drawing\' on the poster, which prompt is best?\",\"options\":[\"I am\",\"I can\",\"I overcome\",\"I was\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Skills and actions are best expressed using the \'I can\' prompt.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare a poster\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to describe yourself as \'brave\', which prompt should you use?\",\"options\":[\"I can\",\"I am\",\"I overcome\",\"I will\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Personal qualities like being brave are expressed using \'I am\'.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare a poster\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phrases is NOT one of the three prompts listed in the text?\",\"options\":[\"I can\",\"I am\",\"I can overcome\",\"I want to\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"\'I want to\' is not mentioned in the provided textbook text.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare a poster\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of using these specific prompts on a \'Mindset\' poster?\",\"options\":[\"To practice handwriting\",\"To show a positive and confident mindset\",\"To list grocery items\",\"To write a letter to a friend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Prompts like \'I can\' and \'I can overcome\' help build self-confidence and a positive mindset.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare a poster\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best completes the prompt \'I can overcome _____\' based on the meaning of the word?\",\"options\":[\"my fears\",\"a sandwich\",\"a blue pen\",\"the sun\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"One overcomes challenges or fears, not objects like pens or food.\",\"topic\":\"Prepare a poster\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21542,19,4,'English','en','We are One - The Rainbow Story','[\"A rainbow is a beautiful arc of colours seen after rain when sunlight passes through water droplets.\",\"The rainbow has seven colours: Red, Orange, Yellow, Green, Blue, Indigo, Violet.\",\"Red is the colour of fire and bravery.\",\"Orange is full of energy and joy.\",\"Yellow makes everyone smile and is bright like the sun.\",\"Green gives life to plants and trees.\",\"Blue is calm like the sky and deep like the sea.\",\"Indigo is magical and mysterious.\",\"Violet is royal and graceful.\",\"All colours together make a rainbow and they are all friends.\",\"White light is made of all the rainbow colours mixed together.\",\"When white light passes through a prism, it splits into the seven rainbow colours.\",\"Unity in diversity means that even though colours are different, they are all part of one whole.\",\"The story teaches that fighting is wrong and cooperation makes the world bright.\",\"The main lesson is that we should respect differences and work together.\",\"The colours in the story were fighting because each thought it was the greatest.\",\"White colour explained that they all come from white light and become white again when together.\",\"If two colours disappear, the rainbow will be incomplete and less bright.\",\"The rainbow appears in the sky after rain when sunlight shines through water droplets.\",\"The story encourages children to be kind, respectful and to celebrate differences.\",\"The rainbow is a natural phenomenon that shows the spectrum of visible light.\",\"The colours of the rainbow are always in the same order: Red, Orange, Yellow, Green, Blue, Indigo, Violet.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is Red the colour of?\",\"options\":[\"Peace and quiet\",\"Fire and bravery\",\"Energy and joy\",\"Plants and trees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Red states, \'I am the colour of fire and bravery!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour says it is \'bright like the sun\'?\",\"options\":[\"Orange\",\"Red\",\"Yellow\",\"Violet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Yellow says, \'I am bright like the sun!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Blue says it is calm like the sky and deep like the ______.\",\"options\":[\"River\",\"Lake\",\"Sea\",\"Well\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Blue says, \'I am calm like the sky and deep like the sea!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour claims to be \'royal and graceful\'?\",\"options\":[\"Indigo\",\"Violet\",\"Blue\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Violet says, \'I am royal and graceful.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Green think there would be no world without it?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is the strongest\",\"Because it is the most beautiful\",\"Because it gives life to plants and trees\",\"Because it is magical and mysterious\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Green says, \'I give life to plants and trees. Without me, there is no world!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What qualities does Orange claim to have?\",\"options\":[\"Energy and joy\",\"Bravery and strength\",\"Calmness and depth\",\"Mystery and magic\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Orange says, \'I am full of energy and joy!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What makes Indigo feel \'special\' according to the scene?\",\"options\":[\"It is the brightest\",\"It is magical and mysterious\",\"It makes everyone smile\",\"It is the strongest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Indigo says, \'I am magical and mysterious. I am special!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are all the colours doing at the end of Scene 2?\",\"options\":[\"Singing a song together\",\"Helping each other\",\"Arguing loudly\",\"Sleeping in the sky\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'(All colours speak together, arguing loudly.)\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a soldier wanted to wear a colour that represents \'bravery\' based on this story, which colour should he choose?\",\"options\":[\"Green\",\"Blue\",\"Red\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Red claims to be the colour of bravery.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to create a painting that feels \'calm\', which colour from the story would be most suitable?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Orange\",\"Blue\",\"Indigo\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Blue describes itself as \'calm like the sky\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main reason the colours are fighting in this scene?\",\"options\":[\"They are hungry\",\"They want to leave the sky\",\"Each colour thinks it is the greatest\",\"They do not like the sun\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The narrator explains that each thought, \'I am the greatest!\', leading to the argument.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes the attitude of all the colours in Scene 2?\",\"options\":[\"Humble and kind\",\"Proud and boastful\",\"Scared and worried\",\"Quiet and shy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Each colour is boasting about why they are the best or greatest.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 2 : The Colours Start Fighting\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What appeared suddenly when the sky became noisy and the colours were angry?\",\"options\":[\"A dark cloud\",\"A bright light\",\"A loud thunder\",\"Raindrops\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that suddenly a bright light appeared when the sky became noisy.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 5 : The Big Truth\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the colours forget when they were fighting?\",\"options\":[\"Their names\",\"Their way home\",\"Their friendship\",\"Their beauty\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the narrator in Scene 3, the colours were angry and forgot their friendship.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 5 : The Big Truth\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why were the colours fighting according to Red?\",\"options\":[\"They wanted to play\",\"They wanted to prove who is the greatest\",\"They were hungry\",\"They did not like the sky\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Red explains to White that they are fighting because they want to prove who is the greatest.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 5 : The Big Truth\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where does White say all the colours live?\",\"options\":[\"Inside the sun\",\"Inside the prism\",\"Inside White\",\"In the clouds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"White tells the colours, \'You all live inside me.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 5 : The Big Truth\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What object is mentioned that helps White turn into seven different colours?\",\"options\":[\"A mirror\",\"A lens\",\"A prism\",\"A glass of water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"White explains that when light passes through a prism, it becomes the seven colours.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 5 : The Big Truth\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when all the colours come together again?\",\"options\":[\"They become black\",\"They become white\",\"They disappear\",\"They become a rainbow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"White states that when all the colours come together, they become white again.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 5 : The Big Truth\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these colours is NOT listed in the text as one of the seven colours?\",\"options\":[\"Indigo\",\"Violet\",\"Pink\",\"Orange\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists Red, Orange, Yellow, Green, Blue, Indigo, and Violet; Pink is not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 5 : The Big Truth\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the \'Big Truth\' revealed by White in Scene 5?\",\"options\":[\"That the sky is blue\",\"That all colours are born from White\",\"That Red is the strongest\",\"That the prism is magic\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Big Truth\' is that all colours are born from White and are part of White.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 5 : The Big Truth\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why is it unnecessary for the colours to fight about who is greatest?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are all actually part of one (White)\",\"Because the sky is too big\",\"Because they are all the same colour\",\"Because White is the only great one\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows they are all born from and live inside White, meaning they are all one.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 5 : The Big Truth\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How do the colours react when White tells them they are born from him?\",\"options\":[\"They get angrier\",\"They start crying\",\"They ask \'Really?\' in surprise\",\"They run away\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows the colours saying \'Really?\' together after White shares the secret.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 5 : The Big Truth\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In Scene 6, what does Green say the colors are?\",\"options\":[\"Enemies\",\"Friends\",\"Strangers\",\"Rivals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In Scene 6, Green explicitly states, \'We are friends!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 8 : Ending Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Blue, the colors are not just friends, but a ________.\",\"options\":[\"Team\",\"Group\",\"Family\",\"Crowd\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Blue says, \'We are a family!\' in Scene 6.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 8 : Ending Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do the colors make when they are together, according to Violet?\",\"options\":[\"A painting\",\"A rainbow\",\"A circle\",\"A shadow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Violet says, \'Together we make a rainbow!\' in Scene 6.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 8 : Ending Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the message in Scene 7, what happens when the colors are \'Together\'?\",\"options\":[\"They shine\",\"They hide\",\"They glow\",\"They cry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Different we shine, Together we glow!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 8 : Ending Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does White say makes us \'strong and beautiful\'?\",\"options\":[\"Fighting\",\"Unity\",\"Being the same\",\"Shining alone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"White says, \'Unity makes us strong and beautiful.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 8 : Ending Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a group of students from different states works together happily, which lesson from the text are they applying?\",\"options\":[\"Unity in diversity\",\"Being different is bad\",\"Only one color is best\",\"Friends are enemies\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The narrator mentions that \'Unity in diversity makes the world bright and beautiful.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 8 : Ending Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What important lesson did the colors learn at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Diversity is not good\",\"Unity in diversity makes the world bright and beautiful\",\"Colors should not mix\",\"The world is dark\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The narrator states the lesson learned is \'Unity in diversity makes the world bright and beautiful.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 8 : Ending Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final line spoken by all the characters together?\",\"options\":[\"We are many colours, but we are ONE!\",\"We are all the same color!\",\"We are enemies no more!\",\"The rainbow is finished!\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The very last line of the text is \'We are many colours, but we are ONE!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 8 : Ending Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on White\'s message, how should we view people who look different from us?\",\"options\":[\"We are not the same\",\"We are one despite looking different\",\"We should stay away\",\"We are enemies\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"White says, \'We may look different, but we are one.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene 8 : Ending Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the relationship between the colors by the end of Scene 8?\",\"options\":[\"Division\",\"Unity\",\"Confusion\",\"Disagreement\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The entire ending focuses on the theme of Unity.\",\"topic\":\"Scene 8 : Ending Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21543,19,4,'English','en','The Encyclopaedia','[\"An encyclopaedia is a large book that contains information about many subjects like animals, planets, famous people and volcanoes.\",\"It used to be a big book kept in libraries, but now it is available online on computers and phones.\",\"You can learn about Science, Technology, Geography and Space with just a few clicks.\",\"An encyclopaedia is like a friend that helps us find answers and learn more about the world.\",\"It is a useful reference book that contains facts, definitions and explanations.\",\"You can read an encyclopaedia to learn new words and ideas.\",\"Encyclopaedias are organized in alphabetical order so you can find information quickly.\",\"They are written by many experts who research and write about different topics.\",\"You can use an encyclopaedia to study for school, do homework or satisfy curiosity.\",\"The book is a collection of articles, each about a specific topic.\",\"It is a reliable source of information because it is checked by experts.\",\"Encyclopaedias are available in many languages.\",\"You can use online encyclopaedias like Wikipedia or Britannica.\",\"Reading an encyclopaedia helps improve vocabulary and reading skills.\",\"Encyclopaedias can be used for research, writing reports and learning new facts.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is an encyclopaedia compared to in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A small notebook\",\"A big magic book\",\"A comic book\",\"A story book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'An encyclopaedia is like a big magic book.\'\",\"topic\":\"What is an Encyclopaedia?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where were encyclopaedias kept a long time ago?\",\"options\":[\"In schools\",\"In markets\",\"In libraries\",\"In parks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that a long time ago, encyclopaedias were large books kept in libraries.\",\"topic\":\"What is an Encyclopaedia?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how can we access encyclopaedias today?\",\"options\":[\"Only by going to a library\",\"Through online platforms\",\"By buying toys\",\"By watching television\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that today, encyclopaedias are available through online platforms like computers and mobile phones.\",\"topic\":\"What is an Encyclopaedia?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is an encyclopaedia called a \'friend\' for all of us?\",\"options\":[\"Because it helps us to find answers\",\"Because it plays games with us\",\"Because it tells us jokes\",\"Because it goes to school with us\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says it is like a friend because it helps us to find answers and learn more about the world.\",\"topic\":\"What is an Encyclopaedia?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to learn about \'Space\' quickly today, what should you use according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A drawing book\",\"A physical map\",\"A storybook\",\"A few clicks on a computer\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that with just a few clicks on online platforms, we can learn about subjects like Space.\",\"topic\":\"What is an Encyclopaedia?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these subjects is NOT mentioned in the text as something we can learn from an encyclopaedia?\",\"options\":[\"Science and Technology\",\"Geography\",\"Cooking recipes\",\"Space\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Science, Geography, and Space are listed in the text, but cooking recipes are not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"What is an Encyclopaedia?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how is the \'Encyclopaedia\' shown to make it look like a \'friend\'?\",\"options\":[\"As a heavy stone\",\"As a character with a face and hands\",\"As a closed box\",\"As a piece of paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the book with eyes, a mouth, and arms to personify it as a friend.\",\"topic\":\"What is an Encyclopaedia?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/097_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, which of these can you see coming out of the \'magic book\'?\",\"options\":[\"A car and a bus\",\"A volcano and animals\",\"A house and a tree\",\"A pen and a pencil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a volcano, a lion, a giraffe, and an elephant emerging from the open book.\",\"topic\":\"What is an Encyclopaedia?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/097_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the two children doing?\",\"options\":[\"Playing football\",\"Looking at an encyclopaedia\",\"Sleeping\",\"Eating food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows two children focused on reading or looking at a book labeled \'Encyclopaedia\'.\",\"topic\":\"What is an Encyclopaedia?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/097_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a student needs to know about \'famous people\', why would they open an encyclopaedia?\",\"options\":[\"To draw a picture\",\"To learn new things about them\",\"To write a letter\",\"To hide a secret\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when you open an encyclopaedia, you learn new things about famous people.\",\"topic\":\"What is an Encyclopaedia?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many syllables are shown for the word \'planet\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'planet | .....| .....|\', which indicates two syllables (plan-et).\",\"topic\":\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is responsible for answering questions in the \'Encyclopaedia Detective Game\'?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher\",\"The whole class\",\"The Encyclopaedia Detective\",\"The librarian\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the detective will answer by using the Encyclopaedia.\",\"topic\":\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the example of \'volcano\', how many syllables does the word \'animal\' have?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides three spaces for \'animal\', which are an-i-mal.\",\"topic\":\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What tool must the detective use to answer the questions during the game?\",\"options\":[\"A dictionary\",\"The Encyclopaedia\",\"A textbook\",\"The internet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The guidelines state the detective will answer by using the Encyclopaedia.\",\"topic\":\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should happen when the topic of the game changes?\",\"options\":[\"The game ends\",\"The teacher takes over\",\"The role of the detective is changed\",\"The same detective continues\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says to \'Change the role of detective for each topic.\'\",\"topic\":\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the syllable pattern for \'library\', how many parts will you write?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides three spaces for \'library\' (li-brar-y).\",\"topic\":\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is chosen as the \'Encyclopaedia Detective\', what is their primary task when other learners ask questions?\",\"options\":[\"To write the questions on the board\",\"To find the answers in the Encyclopaedia\",\"To count the syllables in the questions\",\"To select the next topic\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The detective\'s role is to answer questions using the Encyclopaedia.\",\"topic\":\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Following the example \'volcano | vol | ca | no |\', which is the correct way to divide \'planet\'?\",\"options\":[\"planet | p | lanet |\",\"planet | pla | net |\",\"planet | plan | et |\",\"planet | plane | t |\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'planet\' is divided into two syllables: plan and et.\",\"topic\":\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Counting the spaces provided in the text, how many syllables does the word \'encyclopaedia\' have?\",\"options\":[\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\",\"Seven\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides six spaces for the word \'encyclopaedia\' (en-cy-clo-pae-di-a).\",\"topic\":\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the classroom game, what is the relationship between the \'other learners\' and the \'detective\'?\",\"options\":[\"The detective asks and the learners answer\",\"The learners ask and the detective answers\",\"The teacher asks both of them\",\"They all look for answers at the same time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Other learners will ask questions to Encyclopaedia Detective\' and the detective will answer.\",\"topic\":\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21544,19,4,'English','en','Civic Sense','[\"Civic sense is the habit of being a good citizen by following rules and keeping the surroundings clean.\",\"It means not littering and putting garbage in the bin.\",\"It includes respecting public property like benches and walls.\",\"Waiting for your turn in a line shows respect for others.\",\"Helping friends cross the street safely is a civic act.\",\"Small actions together make the city safer and happier.\",\"Civic sense is taught by Parry the Civic sense parrot in the story.\",\"The story shows how children can practice civic sense in a park.\",\"Civic sense is about responsibility and caring for the community.\",\"When you throw garbage in a bin, you are following civic sense.\",\"Public property should never be damaged or defaced.\",\"Civic sense helps keep the city clean, safe and pleasant.\",\"Children can promise to practice civic sense every day.\",\"Civic sense is a promise to follow rules and respect others.\",\"Civic sense is a way to keep our city beautiful and friendly.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is Parry in the story?\",\"options\":[\"A child in the park\",\"A civic sense parrot\",\"A park security guard\",\"Yasmeen\'s pet bird\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text introduces Parry as \'Parry the Civic sense parrot\'.\",\"topic\":\"What is Civic Sense?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where are Yasmeen and Sam when they notice the garbage?\",\"options\":[\"At school\",\"In their house\",\"In the park\",\"On the street\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Yasmeen asks why there is so much garbage in \'our park\' today.\",\"topic\":\"What is Civic Sense?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Parry, what is the definition of civic sense?\",\"options\":[\"Playing games with friends\",\"Feeding birds in the park\",\"Following rules and keeping surroundings clean\",\"Talking to parrots\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Parry defines civic sense as following rules, keeping surroundings clean, and being responsible.\",\"topic\":\"What is Civic Sense?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of civic sense mentioned by Parry?\",\"options\":[\"Throwing garbage in the park\",\"Waiting for your turn in lines\",\"Breaking public property\",\"Leaving the park dirty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Parry mentions \'waiting for your turn in lines\' as an example of civic sense.\",\"topic\":\"What is Civic Sense?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see a bench in a public park, what does civic sense teach you to do?\",\"options\":[\"Draw pictures on it\",\"Break the legs of the bench\",\"Take care of it as public property\",\"Move it to your own house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Parry states that taking care of public property is part of civic sense.\",\"topic\":\"What is Civic Sense?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should a responsible citizen do when they have trash in their hand?\",\"options\":[\"Throw it on the park grass\",\"Avoid littering and keep the place clean\",\"Hide it under a park bench\",\"Wait for someone else to pick it up\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Parry agrees that \'not littering\' is exactly what civic sense is about.\",\"topic\":\"What is Civic Sense?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the specific problem Yasmeen and Sam noticed at the beginning of the talk?\",\"options\":[\"The park was too crowded\",\"There was too much garbage\",\"The parrot was lost\",\"The rules were too hard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Yasmeen asks why there is \'so much garbage\' in the park.\",\"topic\":\"What is Civic Sense?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Parry the Parrot talk to the children?\",\"options\":[\"To ask them for food\",\"To teach them how to keep their place clean and safe\",\"To tell them to go home\",\"To complain about the noise\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Parry says, \'I teach everyone how to keep our place clean and safe.\'\",\"topic\":\"What is Civic Sense?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the dialogue, what is the relationship between \'not littering\' and \'civic sense\'?\",\"options\":[\"Not littering is one way to show civic sense\",\"Not littering has nothing to do with civic sense\",\"Civic sense means you must litter\",\"Only parrots need to avoid littering\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"When Sam asks if civic sense is like not littering, Parry says \'Exactly!\'.\",\"topic\":\"What is Civic Sense?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which action would Parry the Parrot most likely approve of?\",\"options\":[\"Cutting in front of a line\",\"Helping an elderly person cross the road\",\"Leaving chocolate wrappers on the ground\",\"Writing your name on a park fence\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Parry mentions \'helping others\' as a part of civic sense.\",\"topic\":\"What is Civic Sense?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Where does Yasmeen say she should throw garbage to show civic sense?\",\"options\":[\"On the street\",\"In a bin\",\"In the garden\",\"Under the seat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Yasmeen mentions that throwing garbage in a bin is a sign of using civic sense.\",\"topic\":\"Making a Difference\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Sam promise to do if he sees trash lying around?\",\"options\":[\"He will ignore it\",\"He will tell his teacher\",\"He will pick it up\",\"He will walk away\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sam explicitly states, \'I will pick up trash if I see it lying around.\'\",\"topic\":\"Making a Difference\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Parry, what kind of actions make our city better?\",\"options\":[\"Only big actions\",\"Only expensive actions\",\"Small actions\",\"No actions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Parry says that even small actions make our city better and safe for everyone.\",\"topic\":\"Making a Difference\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What will Yasmeen remind her friends to do?\",\"options\":[\"To play more\",\"To follow rules\",\"To buy toys\",\"To run fast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Yasmeen says, \'And I will remind my friends to follow rules.\'\",\"topic\":\"Making a Difference\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are waiting for a bus, what action shows civic sense according to Yasmeen?\",\"options\":[\"Pushing to get in first\",\"Waiting for your turn\",\"Shouting at others\",\"Leaving the line\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Yasmeen mentions that waiting for her turn is part of using civic sense.\",\"topic\":\"Making a Difference\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"You see a plastic wrapper on the floor. Based on the text, what is the best way to show civic sense?\",\"options\":[\"Kick it under a desk\",\"Wait for someone else to see it\",\"Pick it up and put it in a bin\",\"Tell your friends to look at it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests picking up trash and putting garbage in a bin are acts of civic sense.\",\"topic\":\"Making a Difference\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which three words does Parry use to describe a city where people have good civic sense?\",\"options\":[\"Big, loud, and busy\",\"Clean, safe, and happy\",\"Old, dark, and quiet\",\"New, rich, and fast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Parry states that good civic sense makes our city \'clean, safe and happy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Making a Difference\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it important to follow civic sense every day according to the children?\",\"options\":[\"To make the city better for everyone\",\"To get a reward from the teacher\",\"To finish their work quickly\",\"To make the city bigger\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explains that these actions make the city better, safe, and happy for everyone.\",\"topic\":\"Making a Difference\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How often do Yasmeen and Sam promise to follow civic sense?\",\"options\":[\"Only on weekends\",\"Every day\",\"Once a month\",\"Only at school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both children say, \'We promise to follow civic sense every day!\'\",\"topic\":\"Making a Difference\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message of the conversation between Yasmeen, Parry, and Sam?\",\"options\":[\"Only adults should clean the city\",\"Rules are not important for children\",\"Small individual actions help the whole city\",\"Picking up trash is Sam\'s job only\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The dialogue emphasizes that individual actions like throwing garbage in bins and following rules make the city better.\",\"topic\":\"Making a Difference\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, who is the primary person being given instructions?\",\"options\":[\"The student\",\"The teacher\",\"The parent\",\"The principal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text starts with \'For the Teacher\', indicating the instructions are for them.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should the teacher encourage learners to write?\",\"options\":[\"Common etiquettes\",\"Short stories\",\"Math tables\",\"Science facts\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to encourage learners to write common etiquettes to be followed.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When should learners follow the etiquettes they learn?\",\"options\":[\"Only during school hours\",\"Only when the teacher is looking\",\"In their daily life\",\"Only on special occasions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions motivating learners to follow etiquettes in their daily life.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the teacher\'s role regarding \'actions of civic senses\'?\",\"options\":[\"To list them alone\",\"To help learners list more actions\",\"To tell learners to stop listing them\",\"To ignore the list\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Help them to list more actions of civic senses\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text suggest about the number of civic sense actions learners should know?\",\"options\":[\"They should only know one\",\"They should not list any\",\"They should be helped to list more than they already know\",\"They should only read them from a book\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'list more actions\' implies expanding their current knowledge.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the text means to give someone a reason or incentive to do something?\",\"options\":[\"Encourage\",\"Motivate\",\"Follow\",\"List\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Motivate means to provide a reason for someone to act in a certain way.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher asks a student to write down \'saying thank you\', which instruction are they following?\",\"options\":[\"Motivating them to play\",\"Encouraging learners to write common etiquettes\",\"Helping them to draw\",\"Listing names of students\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Saying thank you\' is a common etiquette, and the teacher is having them write it.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student uses polite words at home. This is an example of following etiquettes in:\",\"options\":[\"A textbook\",\"Daily life\",\"A list\",\"A classroom only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using etiquettes outside of specific school tasks constitutes \'daily life\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the teacher\'s instructions, what is the ultimate goal for the learners?\",\"options\":[\"To memorize the textbook\",\"To write a long essay\",\"To practice civic sense and etiquettes daily\",\"To become a teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions focus on writing, listing, and most importantly, using etiquettes in daily life.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity combines both writing and thinking about civic sense as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"Reading a story aloud\",\"Listing more actions of civic senses\",\"Drawing a picture of the school\",\"Cleaning the classroom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Listing involves both the mental act of identifying actions and the physical act of writing.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21545,19,4,'English','en','Rose','[\"Roses are beautiful flowers with many colours like pink, white, red.\",\"They have soft petals that feel like velvet.\",\"The centre of a rose is called the heart and it is sweet and fragrant.\",\"Roses grow on bushes or hedges and can be seen in gardens or parks.\",\"The word ‘rose’ can mean both the flower and the colour red.\",\"Roses are often used in poems and songs because of their beauty and smell.\",\"The petals of a rose are arranged in layers around the heart.\",\"Roses can be described as ‘dainty’, ‘shy’, or ‘beautiful’ depending on how they look.\",\"Roses have a strong fragrance that can be felt from a distance.\",\"The word ‘rose’ is also used as a verb meaning to become red or pink.\",\"Roses are often given as gifts on special occasions like birthdays and anniversaries.\",\"The stem of a rose is long and can be used to hold the flower in a vase.\",\"Roses can be used to make perfumes, jams, and teas.\",\"The word ‘rose’ can also mean a past tense of ‘rise’ in English.\",\"Roses are a symbol of love, friendship, and respect in many cultures.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, which colors can roses be?\",\"options\":[\"Blue, yellow, or pink\",\"Pink, white, or red\",\"Red, orange, or white\",\"Purple, red, or pink\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions \'Be it pink, or white, or red\' when describing the colors of roses.\",\"topic\":\"Dog roses\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the poet describe the way a rose holds its head?\",\"options\":[\"Shyly\",\"Proudly\",\"Sadly\",\"Quickly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that each lovely coloured head \'Is always held so proudly\'.\",\"topic\":\"Dog roses\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are the petals of the roses compared to in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Silk\",\"Cotton\",\"Velvet\",\"Soft grass\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Their petals are like velvet\'.\",\"topic\":\"Dog roses\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is hidden inside the rose that nestles closely?\",\"options\":[\"A sweet and fragrant heart\",\"A tiny green seed\",\"A drop of morning dew\",\"A small honey bee\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the petals nestle closely \'holding a sweet and fragrant heart\'.\",\"topic\":\"Dog roses\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the poet see the dog roses growing?\",\"options\":[\"In a garden pot\",\"On a hazel hedge\",\"Near a river bank\",\"Under a tall tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says the dog roses were \'Clambering on a hazel hedge\'.\",\"topic\":\"Dog roses\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which words are used to describe the appearance of dog roses?\",\"options\":[\"Proud and tall\",\"Dainty and shy\",\"Big and bright\",\"Strong and wild\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poet describes dog roses as \'So dainty and so shy\'.\",\"topic\":\"Dog roses\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see a flower \'clambering\' on a hedge, what is it doing?\",\"options\":[\"Falling down\",\"Climbing or growing over it\",\"Hiding under the leaves\",\"Turning into a hedge\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Clambering implies the roses are climbing or spreading over the hazel hedge.\",\"topic\":\"Dog roses\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What specific color were the dog roses that the poet saw?\",\"options\":[\"Pure white\",\"Bright red\",\"Rose-pink\",\"Dark green\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes them as \'Rosepink against the green\'.\",\"topic\":\"Dog roses\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poet\'s reaction, how did they feel about the dog roses?\",\"options\":[\"They thought they were common\",\"They thought they were the loveliest they had seen\",\"They thought they were too small\",\"They did not like their color\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poet says, \'I\'m sure they were the loveliest roses, I had ever seen!\'\",\"topic\":\"Dog roses\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet mention \'against the green\' when talking about the dog roses?\",\"options\":[\"To show that the roses were turning green\",\"To describe the contrast of the pink flowers on the green hedge\",\"To say the roses were hidden by the leaves\",\"To explain that the roses were not yet ripe\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The phrase describes the visual contrast of the \'Rosepink\' flowers against the \'green\' of the hazel hedge.\",\"topic\":\"Dog roses\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21546,19,4,'English','en','Saying \'No\' to Strangers','[\"- A stranger is someone you do not know.\",\"- Children should never talk to strangers.\",\"- If a stranger offers gifts, say ‘NO’ loudly.\",\"- Stay together with parents or teachers.\",\"- Call for help if you feel unsafe.\",\"- Saying ‘NO’ is a safe action.\",\"- Do not accept chocolates or toys from strangers.\",\"- Keep your distance from unknown people.\",\"- Always stay in a group when outside school.\",\"- Report any suspicious person to a teacher or adult.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where are the children standing at the beginning of the scene?\",\"options\":[\"Inside the classroom\",\"At the playground\",\"Outside the school\",\"At the bus station\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the scene is \'Outside the school, after school is over.\'\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is coming to pick up Kabir?\",\"options\":[\"His father\",\"His mother\",\"His teacher\",\"His brother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Kabir says, \'My mother will come to pick me up.\'\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the stranger offer to give the children?\",\"options\":[\"Books and pens\",\"Chocolates and toys\",\"Money and bags\",\"Fruit and water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The stranger says, \'I have chocolates and toys.\'\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Neha look worried during the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"She lost her school bag\",\"She is very hungry\",\"She does not know the stranger\",\"She missed her bus\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Neha looks worried and says, \'We do not know you.\'\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, who are the only people the children go home with?\",\"options\":[\"Friends or neighbors\",\"Strangers who are good people\",\"Anyone who knows their school\",\"Parents or teachers\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Neha says, \'Yes. We only go with our parents or teachers.\'\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What action does Divya take when the stranger first approaches and says hello?\",\"options\":[\"She runs away\",\"She steps back\",\"She shakes his hand\",\"She gives him a toy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes: \'Divya : Hello! (steps back)\'.\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the children\'s behavior, what should you do if a stranger asks you to \'come fast\' because they are in a hurry?\",\"options\":[\"Follow them quickly\",\"Ask them where they are going\",\"Tell them to go away and stay with your group\",\"Help them because they are in a hurry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Kabir says \'No! Please go away\' and the children stand together when the stranger tries to rush them.\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what items is the man holding out to the girl?\",\"options\":[\"A book and a pencil\",\"A lollipop and a teddy bear\",\"A bag and a bottle\",\"A ball and a bat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the stranger offering a lollipop and a pink teddy bear.\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/103_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what does the large red circle with a diagonal line represent?\",\"options\":[\"The school zone sign\",\"A sign to cross the road\",\"A warning to say \'No\' to strangers\",\"A target for a game\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The red \'prohibited\' symbol over the stranger and the girl indicates the lesson\'s theme: Saying \'No\' to strangers.\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/103_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why do the children stand together at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"To play a game\",\"Because they feel unsafe\",\"To wait for the bus more easily\",\"To look at the stranger\'s toys\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'(Children stand together.) Divya : We feel unsafe.\'\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What reason does the stranger give to try and convince the children he is safe?\",\"options\":[\"He is a teacher\",\"He is a good person\",\"He is their neighbor\",\"He is Kabir\'s uncle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The stranger says, \'Why? I am a good person.\'\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which child reminds the stranger that their parents forbade talking to people they don\'t know?\",\"options\":[\"Divya\",\"Aman\",\"Neha\",\"Kabir\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aman says, \'Our parents told us not to talk with strangers.\'\",\"topic\":\"Encounter with a Stranger\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Kabir shout to get attention and help?\",\"options\":[\"Go away!\",\"Help! Help!\",\"Teacher! Teacher!\",\"No! No!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Kabir shouted \'Help! Help!\' to get attention.\",\"topic\":\"Responding to the Stranger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who used a loud voice to tell the stranger to go away?\",\"options\":[\"Aman\",\"Divya\",\"Neha\",\"Kabir\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Neha used a loud voice to say \'Please go away!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Responding to the Stranger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the stranger feel when the children started shouting?\",\"options\":[\"He felt happy.\",\"He felt angry.\",\"He got scared.\",\"He felt brave.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'(Stranger gets scared.)\' after the children shout.\",\"topic\":\"Responding to the Stranger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Divya say the children refused to take from the stranger?\",\"options\":[\"Toys\",\"Chocolates\",\"Money\",\"Books\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Divya says, \'We did not take chocolates.\'\",\"topic\":\"Responding to the Stranger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Kabir, what was one important thing the children did together?\",\"options\":[\"They ran in different directions.\",\"They stayed together.\",\"They hid behind a tree.\",\"They ignored the stranger.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Kabir points out their safety strategy by saying, \'We stayed together.\'\",\"topic\":\"Responding to the Stranger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Aman say the children did NOT do with the stranger?\",\"options\":[\"They did not talk to the teacher.\",\"They did not stay together.\",\"They did not go with the stranger.\",\"They did not shout for help.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aman confirms their safety by saying, \'We did not go with a stranger.\'\",\"topic\":\"Responding to the Stranger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a stranger approaches you, which action from the text shows the best way to refuse?\",\"options\":[\"Taking a gift and walking away\",\"Saying \'NO\' clearly\",\"Going with them to find a teacher\",\"Whispering quietly to them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Neha highlights their successful action by saying, \'We said ‘NO’ clearly.\'\",\"topic\":\"Responding to the Stranger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Aman\'s first suggestion, who is a safe adult to call for help in this situation?\",\"options\":[\"A different stranger\",\"The teacher\",\"A younger child\",\"No one\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aman suggests, \'We will call our teacher,\' identifying the teacher as a safe person to help.\",\"topic\":\"Responding to the Stranger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Neha say \'I feel safe now\' at the end of the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Because the stranger left and the teacher is coming.\",\"Because she received chocolates.\",\"Because she is going to play a game.\",\"Because the stranger was just joking.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Neha feels safe because the stranger left after they stood their ground and the teacher is now arriving.\",\"topic\":\"Responding to the Stranger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these actions by the children directly caused the stranger to leave?\",\"options\":[\"They gave him their bags.\",\"They shouted for help and told him to go away.\",\"They followed him to his car.\",\"They stayed quiet and did nothing.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The stranger leaves only after Neha shouts \'Go away!\' and Kabir shouts \'Help!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Responding to the Stranger\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to Aman, what did the children say to the stranger?\",\"options\":[\"Hello\",\"NO!\",\"Yes\",\"Please\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aman specifically mentions that they said \'NO!\' to the stranger.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Rules to Remember\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Neha do when the stranger talked to them?\",\"options\":[\"She ran away\",\"She took a gift\",\"She called for help\",\"She stayed quiet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Neha states in the text, \'We called for help.\'\",\"topic\":\"Safety Rules to Remember\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the teacher call the children after hearing their story?\",\"options\":[\"Smart children\",\"Naughty children\",\"Scared children\",\"Quiet children\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher praises them by saying, \'Very good! You are smart children.\'\",\"topic\":\"Safety Rules to Remember\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a safety rule mentioned by the teacher?\",\"options\":[\"Talk to everyone you meet\",\"Do not take gifts\",\"Stay alone in the park\",\"Say \'NO\' softly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"One of the teacher\'s rules is \'Do not take gifts.\'\",\"topic\":\"Safety Rules to Remember\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher, how should children say \'NO\' to a stranger?\",\"options\":[\"Quietly\",\"Slowly\",\"Loudly\",\"Softly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher advises the children to \'Say ‘NO’ loudly.\'\",\"topic\":\"Safety Rules to Remember\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal of saying \'NO\' to strangers according to the learners?\",\"options\":[\"To get gifts\",\"To stay safe\",\"To be rude\",\"To play games\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The learners say together, \'Say ‘NO’ to strangers and stay safe.\'\",\"topic\":\"Safety Rules to Remember\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a stranger offers you a chocolate while you are playing, which rule from the text should you follow?\",\"options\":[\"Do not take gifts\",\"Say \'Yes\' politely\",\"Talk to the stranger\",\"Run away alone\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly tells children not to take gifts from strangers.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Rules to Remember\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a stranger tries to talk to a group of friends, what should they do based on Kabir\'s action?\",\"options\":[\"Stay together\",\"Run in different directions\",\"Hide behind a tree\",\"Wait for the stranger to leave\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Kabir mentions \'We stayed together,\' which is a key safety action.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Rules to Remember\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the boy in the middle doing with his arms to show he is following the safety rules?\",\"options\":[\"Waving at someone\",\"Crossing them to show \'No\'\",\"Clapping his hands\",\"Putting them in his pockets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The boy in the middle has his arms crossed in an \'X\' shape, a gesture for \'No\' or \'Stop\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Rules to Remember\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/104_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what word is written on the sign held by the boy on the right?\",\"options\":[\"YES\",\"STOP\",\"NO\",\"HELP\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The boy on the right is holding a sign that clearly says \'NO\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Rules to Remember\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/104_101.jpg\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21547,19,4,'English','en','My Word Family (Unit 4)','[\"- A word family is a group of words that share the same root or base word.\",\"- Words in a family are connected by meaning or sound.\",\"- In this chapter we learn words like *grassland*, *desert*, *turbine* and *elephant*.\",\"- A word chain is a sequence where each word is linked to the next by a common theme.\",\"- Riddles help us think about words in a fun way.\",\"- Anagrams are words made by rearranging letters of another word.\",\"- Dictionary is a useful tool to find meanings of new words.\",\"- *Windmills* are machines that turn with the wind to make electricity.\",\"- *Volcano* is a mountain that erupts lava and ash.\",\"- *Planet* is a large body that orbits a star.\",\"- *Adult* means a grown-up person.\",\"- *Tear* can mean a drop of liquid from the eye or a rip in paper.\",\"- *Nectar* is sweet liquid from flowers that bees collect.\",\"- *Exact* means precise or correct.\",\"- *Turbine* is a device that turns when air or water flows through it.\",\"- *Journey* is a long travel from one place to another.\",\"- *Knowledge* is information and understanding you have.\",\"- *Muscles* are body parts that help you move.\",\"- *Migration* is the movement of animals from one place to another.\",\"- *Discovery* is finding something new.\",\"- *Flour* (likely *flesh* in OCR) is the body part of animals.\",\"- *Bones* are the hard parts inside the body.\",\"- *Warmer* can mean a device that makes heat.\",\"- *Windmills* and *turbines* both use wind to produce power.\",\"- Understanding word families helps improve reading and writing skills.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What should you do if you feel uneasy about someone touching you inappropriately?\",\"options\":[\"Keep quiet about it\",\"Blame yourself for it\",\"You should not keep quiet\",\"Hide in your room\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that if you feel uneasy about an inappropriate touch, you should not keep quiet.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - POCSO\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, whose fault is it when a child receives an unsafe touch?\",\"options\":[\"The child\'s fault\",\"It is not the child\'s fault\",\"The parents\' fault\",\"The teacher\'s fault\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text reassures children that they need not feel bad because an unsafe touch is not their fault.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - POCSO\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the e-box mentioned for reporting child rights protection?\",\"options\":[\"Safety e-box\",\"POCSO e-box\",\"Child e-box\",\"NCPCR e-box\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions informing the National Commission for Protection of Child Rights through the POCSO e-box.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - POCSO\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How might a child feel after experiencing an unsafe touch?\",\"options\":[\"Happy and excited\",\"Bad, confused and helpless\",\"Angry and loud\",\"Sleepy and tired\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when you get an unsafe touch, you may feel bad, confused, and helpless.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - POCSO\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child feels uncomfortable with a touch, who is the best person to talk to?\",\"options\":[\"A stranger on the street\",\"Someone whom they trust\",\"A younger sibling\",\"Nobody at all\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text advises children to tell someone whom they trust if they feel uneasy.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - POCSO\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text advise children not to blame themselves for an unsafe touch?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are too young to understand\",\"Because it is not their fault\",\"Because it is a secret\",\"Because they should keep quiet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that children need not feel bad or blame themselves because it is not their fault.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - POCSO\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the official email address provided to access the POCSO e-box?\",\"options\":[\"help@ncpcr.in\",\"pocso@gov.in\",\"ncpcr@gov.in\",\"safety@ncpcr.gov.in\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that the POCSO e-box is available at ncpcr@gov.in.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - POCSO\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which organization can be informed through the POCSO e-box?\",\"options\":[\"The Local Police Station\",\"National Commission for Protection of Child Rights\",\"The State Education Board\",\"The Health Department\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states you can inform the National Commission for Protection of Child Rights through the POCSO e-box.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - POCSO\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the color of the circular button that contains the word \'e-box\'?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"Red\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a red circular button with \'e-box\' written in the center.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - POCSO\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/107_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which two specific labels are written in yellow text around the central red button?\",\"options\":[\"POCSO and NCPCR\",\"HELP and SAFE\",\"BOY and GIRL\",\"STOP and TELL\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The image shows the words \'POCSO\' at the top and \'NCPCR\' at the bottom of the circle in yellow text.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - POCSO\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"19\\/107_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the emergency phone number for children in distress mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"100\",\"101\",\"1098\",\"108\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to \'Call 1098\' for children in distress.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Childline\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who can use the CHILDLINE service according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only adults over 21\",\"Children below 18 years of age\",\"Only teachers and parents\",\"Only police officers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins by addressing those \'below 18 years of age\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Childline\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"For how many hours a day is the CHILDLINE service available?\",\"options\":[\"8 hours\",\"12 hours\",\"24 hours\",\"Only during school hours\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes it as a \'national 24 hours toll free emergency phone service\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Childline\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text mean by saying the service is \'toll free\'?\",\"options\":[\"It costs a lot of money\",\"It is a free phone service\",\"It is only for people living near tolls\",\"You must pay after the call\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Toll-free indicates that the caller does not have to pay for the phone call.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Childline\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child knows another child who is being abused, what should they do?\",\"options\":[\"Keep it a secret\",\"Call 1098\",\"Do nothing\",\"Wait until they are 18\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to call 1098 if you \'know some other child who is\' troubled or abused.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Childline\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which organization is CHILDLINE 1098 an initiative of?\",\"options\":[\"CHILDLINE India Foundation\",\"The Local Police\",\"The School Board\",\"The Health Department\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states it is \'an initiative of CHILDLINE India Foundation\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Childline\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which Ministry supports the CHILDLINE India Foundation?\",\"options\":[\"Ministry of Finance\",\"Ministry of Education\",\"Ministry of Women & Child Development\",\"Ministry of Home Affairs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the foundation is \'supported by Ministry of Women & Child Development\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Childline\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text say \'some numbers are good\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are easy to remember\",\"Because they change lives\",\"Because they are short\",\"Because they are lucky\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'some numbers are good! They change lives!!!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Childline\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In which of these situations should a child call 1098?\",\"options\":[\"When they want to play a game\",\"When they are hungry for snacks\",\"When they are troubled, confused, or in distress\",\"When they want to talk to a friend\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists being \'troubled or confused or abused or in distress\' as reasons to call.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Childline\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the primary purpose of CHILDLINE 1098?\",\"options\":[\"To provide entertainment for kids\",\"To offer emergency help to children in distress\",\"To help children with their homework\",\"To sell mobile phones to children\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines it as an \'emergency phone service for children in distress\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Childline\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main topic of the guidance mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Good touch and bad touch\",\"Playing outdoor games\",\"Learning new languages\",\"Eating healthy food\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions providing guidance on recognizing and understanding good touch and bad touch.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Guidelines\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it important for students to understand good touch and bad touch?\",\"options\":[\"To get higher marks in exams\",\"To ensure their physical and emotional well-being\",\"To learn how to draw better\",\"To become a famous athlete\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that this guidance ensures the students\' physical and emotional well-being.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Guidelines\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The phrase \'Towards a new dawn\' is translated from which Hindi phrase in the text?\",\"options\":[\"नए दिन की शुरुआत\",\"नया सवेरा\",\"नए समाज की ओर\",\"अच्छी शिक्षा\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'नए समाज की ओर\' as the Hindi equivalent for \'Towards a new dawn\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Guidelines\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of guidance should be provided to students according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Age-appropriate guidance\",\"Difficult and complex guidance\",\"Guidance only for adults\",\"Guidance about history\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that students should be provided with age-appropriate guidance.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Guidelines\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of safety, what does \'recognizing\' a touch mean?\",\"options\":[\"Ignoring the touch completely\",\"Identifying if a touch is good or bad\",\"Drawing a picture of the touch\",\"Counting how many times someone touched you\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Recognizing in this context refers to the ability to identify and understand the nature of the touch for safety.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Guidelines\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student follows the safety guidelines, which two aspects of their health are protected?\",\"options\":[\"Physical and financial\",\"Physical and emotional\",\"Emotional and social\",\"Mental and spiritual\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions ensuring \'physical and emotional well-being\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Guidelines\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"A student learns to say \'no\' to an uncomfortable touch. This is an example of applying guidance on:\",\"options\":[\"Bad touch\",\"Good touch\",\"New dawn\",\"Age-appropriate games\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Recognizing and reacting to an uncomfortable touch is part of understanding \'bad touch\'.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Guidelines\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the ultimate goal of teaching students about touch safety?\",\"options\":[\"To make them afraid of everyone\",\"To help them stay safe and well\",\"To teach them how to run fast\",\"To help them memorize Hindi phrases\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The goal is to ensure their well-being by helping them understand safety boundaries.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Guidelines\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the text describes the state of being healthy and happy?\",\"options\":[\"Guidance\",\"Recognizing\",\"Well-being\",\"Dawn\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Well-being refers to the state of being comfortable, healthy, or happy.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Guidelines\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The text suggests that providing safety awareness is a step towards:\",\"options\":[\"An old society\",\"A new dawn\",\"A dark night\",\"A small village\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text opens with the phrase \'Towards a new dawn\', indicating progress through awareness.\",\"topic\":\"Safety Awareness - Guidelines\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21548,20,4,'Marathi','mr','हीच अमुची प्रार्थना (प्रार्थना)','[\"हीच अमुची प्रार्थना म्हणजे आपल्याला एकमेकांशी चांगले वागायला शिकवणारी प्रार्थना आहे.\",\"प्रार्थनेत सर्व धर्म, जाती, प्रांत, भाषा यांना एकत्र आणून एक निष्ठा, एक आशा, एक रंगी रंगू दे अशी भावना व्यक्त केली आहे.\",\"माणसाने माणसाशी वागणे हे मुख्य विषय आहे.\",\"प्रार्थनेत अंधार, दुःख आणि सूर्य सत्य यांचा उल्लेख करून आशा आणि खात्री दाखवली आहे.\",\"प्रार्थनेच्या शेवटी ‘माणसाने माणसाशी वागणे’ हे वाक्य तीन वेळा पुनरावृत्ती केले आहे.\",\"प्रार्थना शाळेच्या परिपाठात समाविष्ट करून विद्यार्थ्यांना प्रार्थनात्मक अनुभव द्यावा.\",\"प्रार्थनेत ‘काजव्यांचे जागणे’ आणि ‘सूर्य सत्याचा उद्या’ यांचा उल्लेख आहे ज्यातून आशा आणि उजेडाची कल्पना येते.\",\"प्रार्थनेत ‘धर्म, जाती, प्रांत, भाषा’ यांना एकत्र आणून ‘सर्व काही एकत्र येईल’ असा संदेश दिला आहे.\",\"प्रार्थनेत ‘लाभले आयुष्य जितके ते जगावे चांगले’ या वाक्याने आयुष्याचा सदुपयोग करण्याचा सल्ला दिला आहे.\",\"प्रार्थना लिहिताना ‘माणसाने माणसाशी’ हे शब्द वापरून सर्वांना एकमेकांशी मैत्रीपूर्ण राहण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले आहे.\",\"प्रार्थना शिकवताना शिक्षकांनी विद्यार्थ्यांना ‘साभिनय’ आणि ‘तालासुर’ मध्ये वाचायला सांगावे.\",\"प्रार्थनेत ‘काजव्यांचे जागणे’ हे शब्द वापरून निसर्गातील प्रकाशाचे प्रतीक दाखवले आहे.\",\"प्रार्थनेत ‘सूर्य सत्याचा उद्या’ हे वाक्य आशेचे प्रतीक आहे.\",\"प्रार्थना शिकवताना ‘विविध प्रश्‍न विचारावेत’ आणि ‘अनुभव व्यक्त करण्याची संधी द्यावी’ हे निर्देश दिले आहेत.\",\"प्रार्थना लिहिताना ‘माणसाने माणसाशी’ हे वाक्य पुनरावृत्ती करून एकता आणि सहानुभूतीचा संदेश दिला आहे.\"]','[{\"q\":\"\\\"हीच अमुची प्रार्थना\\\" या कवितेचे कवी कोण आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"वसंत बापट\",\"समीर सामंत\",\"कुसुमाग्रज\",\"बालकवी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेच्या शेवटी कवीचे नाव \'समीर सामंत\' असे दिले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत कशाचा सूर्य उद्या उगवेल अशी खात्री कवीला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"चंद्राचा\",\"प्रकाशाचा\",\"सत्याचा\",\"सुखाचा\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"कवितेत \'सूर्य सत्याचा उद्या उगवेल आहे खात्री\' अशी ओळ आली आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"\\\"माणसाने माणसाशी माणसासम वागणे\\\" या प्रार्थनेचा मुख्य अर्थ काय आहे?\",\"options\":[\"माणसाने प्राण्यांसारखे वागावे\",\"माणसाने एकमेकांशी माणुसकीने वागावे\",\"माणसाने फक्त स्वतःचा विचार करावा\",\"माणसाने रागाने वागावे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"माणसाने माणसासारखे वागणे म्हणजे एकमेकांशी माणुसकीने आणि आदराने वागणे होय.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेनुसार मनावर कशाचे चांदणे पुन्हा पसरावे असे म्हटले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"शुद्धतेचे\",\"पांढरे\",\"शीतल\",\"प्रकाशाचे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कवितेत \'शुद्धतेचे चांदणे\' मनावर पसरावे असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"\\\"जे थांबले ते संपले\\\" या ओळीतून कवीला कोणता संदेश द्यायचा आहे?\",\"options\":[\"विश्रांती घ्यावी\",\"सतत प्रगती करत पुढे जात राहावे\",\"काम सोडून द्यावे\",\"एकाच जागी स्थिर राहावे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"प्रगतीसाठी सतत चालत राहणे किंवा प्रयत्न करणे आवश्यक आहे, थांबणे म्हणजे प्रगती खुंटणे होय.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"आपल्याला लाभलेले आयुष्य कसे जगावे असे कवी सांगतो?\",\"options\":[\"खूप श्रीमंतीत जगावे\",\"दुसऱ्यांवर अवलंबून जगावे\",\"चांगले आणि सत्कार्याने जगावे\",\"फक्त स्वतःसाठी जगावे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"कवितेत \'लाभले आयुष्य जितके ते जगावे चांगले\' असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"अंधार दुःखाचा असताना कवीने कशाचे \'जागणे\' मागितले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"सूर्याचे\",\"काजव्याचे\",\"विजेचे\",\"दिव्याचे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"दुःखाच्या अंधारात थोडासा आशेचा किरण म्हणून \'काजव्याचे जागणे\' मागितले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत कोणत्या गोष्टींचा द्वेष संपायला हवा असे सुचवले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ पैशांचा\",\"केवळ अभ्यासाचा\",\"धर्म, जाती, प्रांत आणि भाषा यांचा\",\"केवळ खेळाचा\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"कवितेत धर्म, जाती, प्रांत आणि भाषा यांमुळे निर्माण होणारा द्वेष संपवण्याबद्दल सांगितले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात मुले कोणती कृती करताना दिसत आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"मैदानावर खेळताना\",\"वर्गात अभ्यास करताना\",\"हात जोडून प्रार्थना करताना\",\"बागेत फिरताना\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"चित्रात सर्व मुले आणि शिक्षक डोळे मिटून हात जोडून प्रार्थनेच्या स्थितीत उभे आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"20\\/011_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रावरून शाळेतील वातावरणाबद्दल काय सांगता येईल?\",\"options\":[\"शाळेत गोंधळ सुरू आहे\",\"शाळेत शिस्त आणि प्रार्थनेचे वातावरण आहे\",\"शाळेत सुट्टी जाहीर झाली आहे\",\"शाळेत फक्त मुलेच उपस्थित आहेत\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"चित्रात मुले आणि शिक्षक रांगेत उभे राहून प्रार्थना करत आहेत, जे शिस्तीचे प्रतीक आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"20\\/011_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"चित्रकथेच्या सुरुवातीला अमेयला काय आले होते?\",\"options\":[\"ताप\",\"कंटाळा\",\"झोप\",\"भूक\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पाठात अमेय म्हणतो, \'आजीऽऽ खूप कंटाळा आलाय.\'\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"आजीने अमेयला कोणता गमतीदार खेळ खेळायला सांगितला?\",\"options\":[\"मैदानात धावण्याचा\",\"कागदापासून वेगवेगळे आकार करण्याचा\",\"लपाछपी खेळण्याचा\",\"गोष्टी वाचण्याचा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"आजी म्हणते, \'चल, कागदापासून वेगवेगळे आकार करण्याचा गमतीदार खेळ खेळू या.\'\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"अमेयने कागदापासून सर्वात आधी काय तयार केले?\",\"options\":[\"होडी\",\"पतंग\",\"विमान\",\"फिरफीर\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"अमेय म्हणतो, \'मी कागदी विमान तयार केलंय.\'\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"अमेयने तयार केलेले विमान कसे होते?\",\"options\":[\"ते फाटलेले होते\",\"ते खूप मोठे होते\",\"ते खरंच उडत होते\",\"ते रंगीत नव्हते\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"चित्रातील मुलगी म्हणते, \'हो अमेय, तुझं विमान तर खरंच उडतंय!\'\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात मुलगा आकाशात काय उडताना दाखवत आहे?\",\"options\":[\"पक्षी\",\"कागदी विमान\",\"फुगा\",\"पतंग\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"चित्रात मुलगा बोटाने वर उडणाऱ्या कागदी विमानाकडे निर्देश करत आहे.\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"20\\/013_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात एकूण किती मुले कागदी विमानाचा आनंद घेताना दिसत आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"दोन\",\"चार\",\"पाच\",\"तीन\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"चित्रात दोन मुले आणि एक मुलगी असे एकूण तीन मुले दिसत आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"20\\/013_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"मुलीने कागदापासून काय तयार केले होते?\",\"options\":[\"फिरफीर\",\"चेंडू\",\"टोपी\",\"फूल\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मुलगी म्हणते, \'हे बघ माझं फिरफीर.\'\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"शेवटी मुलांनी कोणत्या वस्तूचा उल्लेख केला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"गाडी\",\"पतंग\",\"घर\",\"प्राणी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"शेवटी संवाद आहे, \'हा बघ माझा पतंग.\'\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"जर तुम्हाला अमेयसारखा कंटाळा आला असेल, तर या पाठानुसार तुम्ही काय करू शकता?\",\"options\":[\"टीव्ही पाहू शकता\",\"कागदापासून नवीन वस्तू बनवू शकता\",\"झोपून राहू शकता\",\"बाहेर फिरायला जाऊ शकता\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पाठात कंटाळा घालवण्यासाठी कागदापासून आकार बनवण्याचा पर्याय दिला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"कागदापासून विमान आणि फिरफीर बनवल्यानंतर मुलांची मनस्थिती कशी झाली?\",\"options\":[\"मुले रडू लागली\",\"मुले अजून कंटाळली\",\"मुलांना खूप मजा आली\",\"मुले घाबरली\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"पाठाच्या शेवटी \'आज खूप मजा आली\' असे म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"या चित्रकथेतून आपल्याला कोणता संदेश मिळतो?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त अभ्यास करावा\",\"हस्तकलतेतून आनंद मिळवता येतो\",\"कागद वाया घालवावा\",\"नेहमी रुसून बसावे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कागदापासून वस्तू बनवून मुले आनंदी झाली, यावरून हस्तकलेचा आनंद समजतो.\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"खालीलपैकी कोणती वस्तू बनवण्यासाठी कागदाचा वापर केला गेला नाही?\",\"options\":[\"विमान\",\"फिरफीर\",\"पतंग\",\"बॅट\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"पाठामध्ये विमान, फिरफीर आणि पतंग कागदापासून बनवल्याचा उल्लेख आहे, बॅटचा नाही.\",\"topic\":\"माझा पतंग (चित्रकथा)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"\'सरावण\' या शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"श्रावण\",\"सावण\",\"सरवण\",\"सराव\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"दिलेल्या मजकुरानुसार \'सरावण\' म्हणजे \'श्रावण\' असा अर्थ होतो.\",\"topic\":\"नवीन शब्द शिकू या\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"\'लांडोर\' म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"मोराचा नर\",\"मोराची मादी\",\"लांडगा\",\"चिमणी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पाठातील शब्दार्थांनुसार \'लांडोर\' म्हणजे \'मोराची मादी\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"नवीन शब्द शिकू या\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"\'धाकधुक\' या शब्दाचा अर्थ खालीलपैकी कोणता?\",\"options\":[\"आनंद\",\"भीती\",\"राग\",\"उत्साह\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात \'धाकधुक\' या शब्दाचा अर्थ \'भीती\' असा दिला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"नवीन शब्द शिकू या\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"\'ईजा\' या शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"विजा\",\"इजा\",\"राजा\",\"मजा\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"दिलेल्या नवीन शब्दांच्या यादीत \'ईजा\' म्हणजे \'विजा\' असा अर्थ दिला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"नवीन शब्द शिकू या\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"\'भुरुक भुरुक\' या शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"मुसळधार पाऊस\",\"रिमझिम पाऊस\",\"वादळ\",\"ऊन\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुरानुसार \'भुरुक भुरुक\' म्हणजे \'रिमझिम पाऊस\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"नवीन शब्द शिकू या\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"बेडकाच्या आवाजासाठी कोणता शब्द वापरला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"भुरुक भुरुक\",\"डुरुक डुरुक\",\"