{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what specific instruction does the teacher give the students regarding the flowers?\",\"options\":[\"Put them in groups of five\",\"Put them in groups of two each\",\"Give them all to Sudhir\",\"Count them one by one\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher in the figure says, \'Put these flowers in groups of two each.\'\",\"topic\":\"Even numbers and Odd numbers\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/027_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the same as distributing a number of objects into 2 equal groups?\",\"options\":[\"Adding 2 to the number\",\"Multiplying the number by 2\",\"Dividing the number by 2\",\"Subtracting 2 from the number\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that distributing objects into 2 equal groups is the same as dividing the number by 2.\",\"topic\":\"Even numbers and Odd numbers\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Using the rule for units places, which of these numbers is an even number?\",\"options\":[\"11\",\"24\",\"35\",\"47\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"24 has a 4 in the units place, which makes it an even number according to the text.\",\"topic\":\"Even numbers and Odd numbers\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a number is divided by 2 and the remainder is 0, what can we conclude?\",\"options\":[\"The number is odd\",\"The number is even\",\"The number is 10\",\"The number is small\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says numbers that do not leave any remainder when divided by two are even numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Even numbers and Odd numbers\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'Fun with Maths\' game, what does the first digit of the final two-digit number tell you?\",\"options\":[\"Number of sisters\",\"Total siblings\",\"Number of brothers\",\"The number 25\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 9 of the game states the first digit is the number of brothers.\",\"topic\":\"Even numbers and Odd numbers\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{