r\"},{\"q\":\"According to the grid game instructions, where should the bottle be drawn?\",\"options\":[\"Top left corner\",\"Centre of the grid\",\"Right corner at the bottom\",\"Top right corner\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to draw a picture of a bottle in the right corner at the bottom.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity: Pathfinding\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Seema\'s instructions, in which row and column should the apple be drawn?\",\"options\":[\"Row-1, Column-1\",\"Row-2, Column-2\",\"Row-3, Column-3\",\"Row-1, Column-3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Seema instructs to draw an apple at the centre of row-2, second column.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity: Pathfinding\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if you enter through the Entrance and take the first turn to the left, which department will you reach?\",\"options\":[\"Registration Dept.\",\"Pharmacy Dept.\",\"Emergency Dept.\",\"Eye Dept.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sketch map shows the Emergency Dept. is the first department on the left after entering.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity: Pathfinding\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/077_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which department is located between the Dental Dept. and the Surgery Dept.?\",\"options\":[\"ENT Dept.\",\"Paediatrics Dept.\",\"Eye Dept.\",\"Pharmacy Dept.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The top row of the sketch map shows the Paediatrics Dept. situated between the Dental and Surgery departments.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity: Pathfinding\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/077_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If Seema tells you to draw an eraser in the top left corner of Row-3, what is she helping you do?\",\"options\":[\"Measuring the grid\",\"Filling in the adjacent grid\",\"Calculating steps\",\"Drawing a hospital\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'To fill in the adjacent grid, do as Seema instructed\', followed by the eraser instruction.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity: Pathfinding\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are at \'Start\' and the ball is 3 boxes away horizontally and 2 boxes away vertically, how many steps are needed (no slanting)?\",\"options\":[\"3 steps\",\"2 steps\",\"5 steps\",\"6 steps\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since 1 box = 1 step and slanting is not allowed, you add the horizontal and vertical boxes (3 + 2 = 5).\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity: Pathfinding\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To reach the mango tree from \'Start\' using the grid game rules, what must you provide?\",\"options\":[\"A drawing of the tree\",\"Instructions to reach it\",\"A slanting line\",\"A picture of a bottle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks to \'Instruct to reach the mango tree from the Start\'.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity: Pathfinding\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When comparing the routes from \'Start\' to the \'ball\', what is the main goal of counting the steps for each route?\",\"options\":[\"To find the longest way\",\"To see how many different paths exist and their lengths\",\"To draw more pictures\",\"To change the scale\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity asks to show all routes and count steps, which helps analyze path efficiency and variety.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity: Pathfinding\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of John drawing a sketch map instead of a full map during his field visit?\",\"options\":[\"To show the exact distance in kilometers\",\"To provide a quick visual layout of the hospital departments\",\"To play a grid game\",\"To count the number of steps to the hospital\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A sketch map provides a quick visual representation of locations, as shown by the department labels in the figure.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity: Pathfinding\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who drew the sketch map of the rural hospital mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"John\",\"The Doctor\",\"The Teacher\",\"A student named Ram\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'John has drawn a sketch map of the rural hospital.\'\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What type of hospital is represented in John\'s sketch map?\",\"options\":[\"City hospital\",\"Private hospital\",\"Rural hospital\",\"Veterinary hospital\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the map as a \'sketch map of the rural hospital.\'\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To find the ENT department, what is the first direction one must follow?\",\"options\":[\"Turn left immediately\",\"Go straight\",\"Turn right\",\"Go backwards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The location instructions for the ENT department begin with \'After going straight\'.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which turn leads to the ENT department after going straight?\",\"options\":[\"The first left\",\"The first right\",\"The second left\",\"The second right\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The location is described as \'After going straight, second left.\'\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these departments is NOT mentioned as a question in the hospital map exercise?\",\"options\":[\"ENT department\",\"Eye department\",\"Dental department\",\"X-ray department\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions ENT, Eye, and Dental departments, but not X-ray.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a visitor follows the instruction \'second left\', how many left turns would they have passed in total to reach the destination?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"None\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'second left\' implies passing the first left turn and taking the next one.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of drawing a map showing different sections of a school?\",\"options\":[\"To show the colors of the building\",\"To represent the location of various school areas\",\"To list the names of all students\",\"To calculate the school fees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Maps are used to show the layout and locations of different sections or departments.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'After going straight, second left\', what does the word \'second\' help to determine?\",\"options\":[\"The speed of walking\",\"The time of day\",\"The specific sequence of the turn\",\"The number of doctors present\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'second\' indicates the order or sequence of the turns to be taken.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the exercise, what is the most appropriate way to describe the location of a department in a building?\",\"options\":[\"By its room number only\",\"By providing directions relative to a path\",\"By naming the doctor in charge\",\"By describing the furniture inside\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses relative directions like \'after going straight, second left\' to state locations.\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If you are asked to follow the final instruction in the text, what would be the result of your work?\",\"options\":[\"A map of school sections\",\"A map of the hospital\",\"A drawing of a doctor\",\"A list of hospital departments\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The final instruction is \'Draw a map showing the different sections of your school.\'\",\"topic\":\"स्वाध्याय\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"create\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21578,21,4,'Maths','en','Multiplication','[\"Multiplication is repeated addition.\",\"The result of multiplication is called the product.\",\"Multiplying any number by 0 gives 0.\",\"Multiplying any number by 1 gives the same number.\",\"Multiplication is commutative: a × b = b × a.\",\"Multiplication is associative: (a × b) × c = a × (b × c).\",\"To multiply by 10, add a zero at the end.\",\"To multiply by 100, add two zeros at the end.\",\"Use the vertical method for multiplying two-digit numbers.\",\"Use the lattice method for visual multiplication.\",\"Carry over when the product in a place is 10 or more.\",\"Check multiplication by using division.\",\"Word problems require identifying what to multiply.\",\"Units must be the same before multiplying.\",\"Estimate products by rounding numbers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the product of 8 and 7 as mentioned in the multiplication exercises?\",\"options\":[\"54\",\"56\",\"64\",\"48\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to basic multiplication tables, 8 multiplied by 7 equals 56.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'Fun with Maths\' activity, what is the difference between the product of the middle number by itself and the product of the first and third consecutive numbers?\",\"options\":[\"0\",\"1\",\"2\",\"3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that 8 x 8 = 64 and 7 x 9 = 63, and 64 - 63 = 1.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If one kilogram of sugar costs ₹ 45, what is the price for 9 kilograms of sugar?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 365\",\"₹ 405\",\"₹ 450\",\"₹ 395\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"To find the total price, multiply 45 by 9, which equals 405.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"An auditorium has 24 chairs in each row. How many chairs would be there in 18 such rows?\",\"options\":[\"432\",\"422\",\"332\",\"442\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Multiplying 24 chairs by 18 rows gives a total of 432 chairs.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you choose the consecutive numbers 4, 5, and 6, what is the product of the middle number by itself?\",\"options\":[\"16\",\"20\",\"25\",\"30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The middle number is 5, and 5 multiplied by itself (5 x 5) is 25.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the product of the three numbers in the first row?\",\"options\":[\"31\",\"216\",\"120\",\"180\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The numbers in the first row are 1, 12, and 18. Multiplying them (1 x 12 x 18) equals 216.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/080_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, is the product of all 3 numbers in every row and column the same?\",\"options\":[\"No, they are different\",\"Yes, they are all the same\",\"Only the rows are the same\",\"Only the columns are the same\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Calculating the product for every row and column in the grid results in 216 for each.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/080_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If 105 boxes of mangoes are kept in each tempo, how many boxes are kept in 6 tempos in all?\",\"options\":[\"600\",\"630\",\"650\",\"730\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Multiplying 105 boxes by 6 tempos equals 630 boxes.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the example of consecutive numbers 7, 8, and 9, what is the product of the first and third number?\",\"options\":[\"63\",\"64\",\"72\",\"56\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first number is 7 and the third is 9; their product is 7 x 9 = 63.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of multiplying 135 by 6?\",\"options\":[\"810\",\"710\",\"610\",\"910\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"135 multiplied by 6 equals 810.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the Lattice Method, how is the number 46 expanded for multiplication?\",\"options\":[\"4 + 6\",\"40 + 6\",\"400 + 6\",\"40 + 60\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, 46 is expanded as 40 + 6 for the Lattice Method.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a two-digit number\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the Lattice Method for 46 × 32, what is the result of multiplying 40 by 30?\",\"options\":[\"120\",\"70\",\"1200\",\"430\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows that 40 × 30 = 1200 in the lattice grid.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a two-digit number\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the method that uses a grid to multiply 46 × 32?\",\"options\":[\"Vertical Method\",\"Lattice Method\",\"Addition Method\",\"Carry over Method\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly introduces the grid-based calculation as the Lattice Method.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a two-digit number\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When using the Vertical Method, what should a student practice keeping in mind?\",\"options\":[\"The multiplication table of 100\",\"The lattice grid\",\"The carry over\",\"The expansion of numbers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text advises to \'Practice keeping carry over in mind\' when using the Vertical Method.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a two-digit number\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the Lattice Method table for 46 × 32, which multiplication results in 180?\",\"options\":[\"40 × 30\",\"6 × 30\",\"40 × 2\",\"6 × 2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The lattice grid shows that 6 × 30 = 180.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a two-digit number\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are multiplying 39 × 43 using the Lattice Method, how should you expand 43?\",\"options\":[\"4 + 3\",\"30 + 9\",\"40 + 3\",\"40 + 30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Following the example of 32 = 30 + 2, the number 43 would be expanded as 40 + 3.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a two-digit number\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Vertical Method steps, which multiplication is performed first?\",\"options\":[\"Multiplying by tens\",\"Multiplying by units\",\"Adding the carry over of tens\",\"Multiplying the two tens digits\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'multiplying by units\' before \'multiplying by tens\' in the Vertical Method sequence.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a two-digit number\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the Lattice Method for 46 × 32, what is the product of the units digits (6 and 2)?\",\"options\":[\"8\",\"12\",\"62\",\"26\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The lattice grid shows the calculation 6 × 2 = 12.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a two-digit number\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the Vertical Method, when does the text mention handling the \'carry over\'?\",\"options\":[\"Only before multiplying\",\"Only after multiplying by units\",\"After multiplying by units and after multiplying by tens\",\"Only at the very end of the sum\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions carry over occurs \'after multiplying by units\' and \'after multiplying by tens\'.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a two-digit number\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To complete the multiplication 39 × 43 using the Vertical Method, what is the first multiplier used for the number 39?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"40\",\"3\",\"30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the Vertical Method, we start by multiplying by the units digit, which in 43 is 3.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a two-digit number\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"When the cost of one item is given and we need to find the total cost of many such items, which mathematical operation do we use?\",\"options\":[\"Subtraction\",\"Addition\",\"Multiplication\",\"Division\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that to find the total cost of many items from the cost of one, we need to multiply.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the restaurant example, what is the cost of a single chair bought by Mama?\",\"options\":[\"₹25\",\"₹375\",\"₹9375\",\"₹1875\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that each chair costs ₹375.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the multiplication of 375 by 25, what does the number 7500 represent?\",\"options\":[\"375 multiplied by 5 units\",\"375 multiplied by 2 units\",\"375 multiplied by 2 tens\",\"375 multiplied by 5 tens\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"As shown in the table, 7500 is the result of multiplying 375 by 2 tens.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the carry-over numbers written in the top-most blue row when multiplying 375 by 2 tens?\",\"options\":[\"3 and 2\",\"1 and 1\",\"7 and 5\",\"9 and 3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the carry-overs for multiplying by tens (2) are 1 and 1.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/082_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the final product obtained after multiplying 199 by 32?\",\"options\":[\"398\",\"5970\",\"6368\",\"6386\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The bottom row of the table in the figure shows the total cost as 6368.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/083_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a \'0\' placed in the units place before multiplying by the tens digit in these examples?\",\"options\":[\"Because the units digit is always zero\",\"Because we are multiplying by a number of tens\",\"To make the addition easier\",\"Because the carry-over is zero\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Multiplying by a tens digit means multiplying by a multiple of 10, which results in a zero in the units place.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Anagha buys 15 kg of apples at ₹185 per kg. What is the total amount she spends?\",\"options\":[\"₹1850\",\"₹925\",\"₹2775\",\"₹2875\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"185 × 15 = (185 × 5) + (185 × 10) = 925 + 1850 = 2775.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A class of 47 students each paid ₹175 for an English Dictionary. How much total money did the teacher collect?\",\"options\":[\"₹8225\",\"₹7000\",\"1225\",\"₹8125\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"175 × 47 = (175 × 7) + (175 × 40) = 1225 + 7000 = 8225.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the problem 199 × 32, what is the result of multiplying 199 by 2 units?\",\"options\":[\"199\",\"398\",\"597\",\"636\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The textbook calculation shows 199 × 2 = 398.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many chairs did Mama buy for his restaurant?\",\"options\":[\"375\",\"9375\",\"25\",\"32\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text starts by stating Mama bought 25 chairs.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the rate of apples per kg that Anagha bought?\",\"options\":[\"₹15\",\"₹185\",\"₹2775\",\"₹175\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the rate of apples is ₹185 per kg.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To solve the dictionary problem, the teacher needs to multiply 175 by which number?\",\"options\":[\"15\",\"32\",\"25\",\"47\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions 47 students paid for the dictionary, so we multiply by 47.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the cost of one shirt is ₹199, what would be the cost of 10 such shirts?\",\"options\":[\"₹199\",\"₹1990\",\"₹19900\",\"₹1900\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Multiplying 199 by 10 (1 ten) results in 1990.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the multiplication 375 × 25, which step is performed first in the vertical method shown?\",\"options\":[\"Multiplying 375 by 2 tens\",\"Adding 1875 and 7500\",\"Multiplying 375 by 5 units\",\"Carrying over the thousands\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows the first partial product is obtained by multiplying 375 by 5 units.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Anagha spent ₹2775 on apples at a rate of ₹185 per kg, how many kilograms did she buy?\",\"options\":[\"10 kg\",\"15 kg\",\"25 kg\",\"47 kg\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states she buys 15 kg apples to get the total expense.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication of a three-digit number\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How much total money did Omkar earn by selling Bhel at the Fun Fair?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 2585\",\"₹ 2855\",\"₹ 2850\",\"₹ 2558\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Omkar earned ₹ 2855 by selling Bhel.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does Omkar need to deposit the money he earned?\",\"options\":[\"In a grocery shop\",\"In the School Savings Bank\",\"In a post office\",\"In his piggy bank at home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, he needs to deposit the amount in the School Savings Bank.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is mentioned as a coin denomination in the activity?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 10\",\"₹ 20\",\"₹ 5\",\"₹ 50\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists ₹ 1, ₹ 2, and ₹ 5 as the denominations of coins.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which document must Omkar fill to deposit his money in the bank?\",\"options\":[\"A cheque book\",\"A withdrawal slip\",\"A Deposit Slip\",\"A school report card\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he has to fill the \'Deposit Slip\' to deposit the amount.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following note denominations is NOT mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 200\",\"₹ 2000\",\"₹ 500\",\"₹ 100\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists notes of ₹ 10, ₹ 20, ₹ 50, ₹ 100, ₹ 200, and ₹ 500; ₹ 2000 is not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Omkar has five notes of ₹ 500, what is the total value of these notes?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 2000\",\"₹ 2500\",\"₹ 1500\",\"₹ 5000\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using multiplication, 500 x 5 = 2500.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Omkar needs to make ₹ 20 using only ₹ 2 coins. How many coins will he need?\",\"options\":[\"5 coins\",\"2 coins\",\"10 coins\",\"20 coins\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To get ₹ 20 using ₹ 2 coins, we divide 20 by 2, which is 10.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Omkar has four ₹ 500 notes and four ₹ 200 notes, how much more does he need to reach his total of ₹ 2855?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 55\",\"₹ 855\",\"₹ 2800\",\"₹ 155\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"(4 x 500) + (4 x 200) = 2000 + 800 = 2800. 2855 - 2800 = 55.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To have a total amount ending in \'5\' (₹ 2855), which combination of coins is most likely?\",\"options\":[\"Two ₹ 2 coins\",\"One ₹ 5 coin\",\"Ten ₹ 1 coins\",\"Three ₹ 2 coins\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A single ₹ 5 coin results in a total ending in 5, whereas the other options result in even numbers or 0.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary purpose of the \'Deposit Slip\' in this activity?\",\"options\":[\"To calculate the profit from selling Bhel\",\"To record the number of notes and coins being put into the bank\",\"To invite students to the Fun Fair\",\"To list the ingredients used in Bhel\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A deposit slip is used to estimate and record the number of coins\\/notes of each denomination being deposited.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which Indian mathematician\'s method of multiplication is mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Aryabhata\",\"Ganesh Daivadnya\",\"Bhaskara\",\"Varahamihira\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions Ganesh Daivadnya\'s Kapaatsandhi method.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the Kapaatsandhi method, the product is written as if ________ of a cupboard are opened.\",\"options\":[\"the shelves\",\"the drawers\",\"two doors\",\"the locks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the product is written as if two doors of a cupboard are opened.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The Kapaatsandhi method of multiplication is done in the same manner as which other method?\",\"options\":[\"Vertical method\",\"Lattice method\",\"Horizontal method\",\"Division method\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the multiplication is done in the same manner as the lattice method.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do if the digits in a diagonal section add up to 10 or more?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore the extra digit\",\"Write both digits in the same section\",\"Carry over and add the digit to the next diagonal section\",\"Subtract the digit from the next section\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to carry over and add the digit to the numbers in the next diagonal section if the sum is 10 or more.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"An auditorium has 18 rows of chairs with 15 chairs in each row. How many chairs does it have in all?\",\"options\":[\"250\",\"270\",\"280\",\"300\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"18 rows multiplied by 15 chairs per row equals 270 chairs.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To solve 357 × 42 using the Kapaatsandhi method, where are the digits 4 and 2 written?\",\"options\":[\"On the top of the columns\",\"On the left side of the grid\",\"On the right side of the grid\",\"Below the grid\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states to write the digits 4 and 2 on the right of the grid.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the Kapaatsandhi method, what is the purpose of the diagonal lines drawn in each box?\",\"options\":[\"To decorate the grid\",\"To separate the digits of the product into two parts\",\"To show where to write the multiplier\",\"To count the number of rows\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The diagonal lines divide each box into two parts to write the product digits separately.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many columns are prepared to multiply the number 357?\",\"options\":[\"One column\",\"Two columns\",\"Three columns\",\"Four columns\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows three columns, one for each digit of the number 357.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/086_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what do the dashed lines inside the rectangular boxes represent?\",\"options\":[\"The outer boundary of the grid\",\"The rows of the auditorium\",\"Diagonal lines to divide each box into two parts\",\"The numbers to be added\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The dashed lines are the diagonals used to divide each box in the Kapaatsandhi method.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/086_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the example in the text, what is the result of 357 × 42?\",\"options\":[\"14994\",\"15994\",\"14884\",\"13994\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly provides the answer 357 × 42 = 14994.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it necessary to add the digits separated by the extended diagonal lines at the end of the process?\",\"options\":[\"To find the number of rows\",\"To calculate the final product of the multiplication\",\"To check if the grid is drawn correctly\",\"To identify the mathematician\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Adding the digits in the diagonal sections is the final step to obtain the total product.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"When multiplying 7 by 4 in the Kapaatsandhi method, where is the digit 2 of the product 28 written?\",\"options\":[\"Below the diagonal line\",\"Above the diagonal line\",\"Outside the grid\",\"On top of the number 7\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that for 7 x 4 = 28, 2 is written above the diagonal line.\",\"topic\":\"Indian Knowledge System\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21579,21,4,'Maths','en','Division','[\"Division means splitting a number into equal parts.\",\"The number being divided is the dividend.\",\"The number we divide by is the divisor.\",\"The result of division is the quotient.\",\"If division is not exact, the leftover is the remainder.\",\"Remainder is always less than the divisor.\",\"Dividend = Divisor × Quotient + Remainder.\",\"Division is the inverse operation of multiplication.\",\"From one multiplication fact, we can get two division facts.\",\"To check division, multiply divisor and quotient and add remainder.\",\"If remainder is zero, we say the dividend is completely divisible.\",\"We use division to find how many groups or how many in each group.\",\"When dividing money, we divide the total amount equally.\",\"Division helps in real-life situations like packing, sharing, arranging.\",\"We can divide step by step using long division method.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many division statements can be obtained from one multiplication statement?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that from one multiplication statement, two division statements can be obtained.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication and Division\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what specific item does Didi ask Swara and Yogesh to pack in the boxes?\",\"options\":[\"Mango juice bottles\",\"Kokam sharbat bottles\",\"Orange squash bottles\",\"Water bottles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the speech bubble, Didi specifically mentions packing \'bottles of Kokam sharbat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication and Division\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/087_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if the girl packed 48 bottles in six boxes, how many bottles are in each box?\",\"options\":[\"6 bottles\",\"8 bottles\",\"48 bottles\",\"12 bottles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the text, 48 ÷ 6 = 8, meaning there are 8 bottles in each box.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication and Division\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/087_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If 6 × 8 = 48, which of the following is a correct division statement derived from it?\",\"options\":[\"48 ÷ 6 = 8\",\"48 ÷ 2 = 24\",\"6 ÷ 8 = 48\",\"48 - 6 = 42\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows that if 6 × 8 = 48, then 48 ÷ 6 = 8.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication and Division\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If 5 × 7 = 35, what is the value of 35 ÷ 7?\",\"options\":[\"35\",\"7\",\"5\",\"12\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"From the multiplication 5 × 7 = 35, the division statement 35 ÷ 7 gives the result 5.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication and Division\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Yogesh packed 48 bottles using 8 boxes. How many bottles did he pack in each box?\",\"options\":[\"8 bottles\",\"48 bottles\",\"6 bottles\",\"40 bottles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Yogesh used 8 boxes for 48 bottles, so 48 ÷ 8 = 6 bottles per box.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication and Division\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what must be remembered while packing the bottles in boxes?\",\"options\":[\"Place a different number of bottles in each box\",\"Place an equal number of bottles in each box\",\"Pack only two boxes\",\"Pack 10 bottles in every box\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Didi tells them to remember to place an equal number of bottles in each box.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication and Division\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If 9 × 8 = 72, which number fills the box in the statement 72 ÷ [ ] = 9?\",\"options\":[\"72\",\"9\",\"8\",\"1\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Based on the correlation shown in the text, if 9 × 8 = 72, then 72 ÷ 8 = 9.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication and Division\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If we have 35 bottles and we put 5 bottles in each box, how many boxes are needed based on the multiplication 5 × 7 = 35?\",\"options\":[\"5 boxes\",\"7 boxes\",\"35 boxes\",\"30 boxes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since 35 ÷ 5 = 7, we need 7 boxes.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication and Division\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs of division statements is correctly obtained from 8 × 6 = 48?\",\"options\":[\"48 ÷ 8 = 6 and 48 ÷ 6 = 8\",\"48 ÷ 4 = 12 and 48 ÷ 2 = 24\",\"8 ÷ 6 = 48 and 6 ÷ 8 = 48\",\"48 - 8 = 40 and 48 - 6 = 42\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text demonstrates that 48 ÷ 8 = 6 and 48 ÷ 6 = 8 are the two statements from the multiplication of 8 and 6.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplication and Division\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the vertical arrangement of 42 ÷ 8, what is the number 42 called?\",\"options\":[\"Divisor\",\"Dividend\",\"Quotient\",\"Remainder\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly labels 42 as the Dividend in the vertical arrangement example.\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the division 42 ÷ 8, what is the number 8 called?\",\"options\":[\"Dividend\",\"Remainder\",\"Divisor\",\"Quotient\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the number 8 as the Divisor in the \'Let\'s Recall\' section.\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result \'5\' called in the division of Isma\'s bottles?\",\"options\":[\"Quotient\",\"Dividend\",\"Divisor\",\"Remainder\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text labels the result 5 as the Quotient in the vertical arrangement diagram.\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the number of bottles left unpacked called in the division 42 ÷ 8?\",\"options\":[\"Divisor\",\"Quotient\",\"Dividend\",\"Remainder\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text labels the 2 bottles left over as the Remainder.\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'Let\'s Remember\' section, the remainder is always ____ than the divisor.\",\"options\":[\"Bigger\",\"Smaller\",\"Equal\",\"Double\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the remainder is always smaller than the divisor.\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which mathematical operation is used to find the number of autorickshaws from a total number of wheels?\",\"options\":[\"Addition\",\"Multiplication\",\"Subtraction\",\"Division\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says \'To get the number of autorickshaws we need to use division.\'\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If each autorickshaw needs 3 wheels, how many autorickshaws can be made from 78 wheels?\",\"options\":[\"26\",\"78\",\"3\",\"18\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows the calculation 78 ÷ 3 results in 26 autorickshaws.\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Isma has 42 bottles and packs 8 in each box. How many full boxes does she pack?\",\"options\":[\"8\",\"42\",\"5\",\"2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states she could pack 5 such boxes from 42 bottles.\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the vertical arrangement of 78 ÷ 3, the text shows the calculation (10+10+6 = 26). What does this sum represent?\",\"options\":[\"The Dividend\",\"The Quotient\",\"The Divisor\",\"The Remainder\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sum 10+10+6 represents the total quotient obtained through the steps of division.\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the quotient for 42 ÷ 8 equal to 5 and not 6?\",\"options\":[\"Because 8 times 6 is 48, which is more than 42\",\"Because 8 times 5 is exactly 42\",\"Because 5 is a lucky number\",\"Because the remainder must be 0\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The divisor is subtracted as many times as possible without exceeding the dividend; 8 fits into 42 only 5 times.\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a student divides a number by 8 and gets a remainder of 9, which rule from the text is being broken?\",\"options\":[\"The dividend must be smaller than the divisor\",\"The quotient must be 0\",\"The remainder is always smaller than the divisor\",\"The divisor must be subtracted only once\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the remainder must always be smaller than the divisor; 9 is not smaller than 8.\",\"topic\":\"Division and Vertical Arrangement\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"While dividing, what is subtracted from the dividend as many times as possible?\",\"options\":[\"The remainder\",\"The quotient\",\"The divisor\",\"The autor