e has infinite axes of symmetry.\",\"Folding a paper along the axis of symmetry makes both halves match exactly.\",\"Mirror images are formed due to reflection.\",\"In a mirror, left and right appear swapped, but top and bottom remain the same.\",\"Water reflection also produces a mirror-like image, with the axis of symmetry being horizontal.\",\"Some letters and numbers look the same in mirror image (e.g., A, H, I, M, O, T, U, V, W, X, Y, 0, 1, 8).\",\"Ambulances write \'AMBULANCE\' in reverse so it reads correctly in a rear-view mirror.\",\"Not all mirror images are symmetrical to the original object; it depends on the object\'s symmetry.\",\"Symmetry is observed in nature, such as in butterflies, leaves, and flowers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the fold on the paper called in a symmetrical figure?\",\"options\":[\"Axis of symmetry\",\"Ink drop\",\"Equal part\",\"Blank paper\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the fold on the paper is the axis of symmetry.\",\"topic\":\"Reflective Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When a blank white paper is folded in the middle, how many equal parts are seen?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when the paper is folded in the middle, two equal parts are seen.\",\"topic\":\"Reflective Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of figure is obtained after unfolding the paper with the ink drop experiment?\",\"options\":[\"A circular figure\",\"A symmetrical figure\",\"A blank figure\",\"A square figure\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the complete figure obtained after unfolding the paper is a symmetrical figure.\",\"topic\":\"Reflective Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what can be drawn in two-dimensional shapes?\",\"options\":[\"Only circles\",\"Number of axes\",\"Only ink drops\",\"Three parts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to the number of axes that can be drawn in two-dimensional shapes.\",\"topic\":\"Reflective Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the ink drop activity, which part of the paper represents the axis of symmetry?\",\"options\":[\"The drop of paint\",\"The edge of the paper\",\"The fold in the middle\",\"The white color\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the fold on the paper as the axis of symmetry.\",\"topic\":\"Reflective Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when you place one part of the folded paper on top of the other and press slightly?\",\"options\":[\"The paper tears\",\"The paint disappears\",\"The paint transfers to create a symmetrical figure\",\"The paper becomes three-dimensional\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Pressing the parts together transfers the ink to create a complete symmetrical figure upon unfolding.\",\"topic\":\"Reflective Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To create a symmetrical figure using the method in the text, what should you do immediately after putting a drop of ink?\",\"options\":[\"Cut the paper\",\"Place the other part on top and press slightly\",\"Wash the paper\",\"Draw a line with a ruler\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity instructions say to place the other part on top and press slightly after putting the ink drop.\",\"topic\":\"Reflective Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the paper be folded to ensure two equal parts are seen?\",\"options\":[\"At the corner\",\"In the middle\",\"At the bottom\",\"Only on the left side\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies to fold the paper in the middle to see two equal parts.\",\"topic\":\"Reflective Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the figure obtained after unfolding the paper called a symmetrical figure?\",\"options\":[\"Because it has ink on it\",\"Because it was made on white paper\",\"Because the fold creates two equal, matching parts\",\"Because it is a two-dimensional shape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A figure is symmetrical when the fold (axis) divides it into two equal parts that match.\",\"topic\":\"Reflective Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step mentioned in the activity to create a symmetrical figure?\",\"options\":[\"Put a drop of ink\",\"Take a blank white paper\",\"Press the paper slightly\",\"Unfold the paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity starts with the instruction: \'Take a blank white paper.\'\",\"topic\":\"Reflective Symmetry\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the girl mentioned in the text who looks into the mirror once she is ready for school?\",\"options\":[\"Radhika\",\"Savita\",\"Meena\",\"Anita\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions Radhika looks into the mirror once ready for school.\",\"topic\":\"Mirror Image\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What term does the text use to describe the image seen in the mirror?\",\"options\":[\"Shadow\",\"Reflected image\",\"Duplicate copy\",\"Dark image\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to the mirror image as the \'reflected image of the original object\'.\",\"topic\":\"Mirror Image\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if the mirror is placed vertically next to the letter \'N\', what will be shown on the right side?\",\"options\":[\"The same letter \'N\'\",\"A mirror image of \'N\'\",\"The number 63\",\"A picture of Radhika\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the \'Original image\' on the left and labels the space on the right for the \'Mirror image\'.\",\"topic\":\"Mirror Image\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/101_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the girl doing to observe her reflection?\",\"options\":[\"Looking into a mirror\",\"Drawing a picture\",\"Looking through a window\",\"Brushing her hair\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Radhika looking into a round mirror to see her reflected image.\",\"topic\":\"Mirror Image\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/100_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should you observe when the mirror is placed at different positions?\",\"options\":[\"If the mirror breaks\",\"If the mirror image looks different from the original object\",\"If the color of the object changes\",\"If the object disappears\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks to observe why some mirror images look different from the original objects at different positions.\",\"topic\":\"Mirror Image\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific number does the text ask the reader to draw the mirror image of?\",\"options\":[\"36\",\"63\",\"88\",\"10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text ends with the instruction: \'Now draw the mirror image of the number 63.\'\",\"topic\":\"Mirror Image\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you follow the text\'s instruction to draw the mirror image of \'63\', which digit will appear reversed and on the left side of the reflection?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"3\",\"9\",\"0\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In a mirror image, the right side of the original (the digit 3) appears on the left side of the reflection.\",\"topic\":\"Mirror Image\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text suggest to \'Take experience actually\'?\",\"options\":[\"To check if the image looks like the person\",\"To learn how to clean a mirror\",\"To see if the mirror is expensive\",\"To practice drawing circles\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text asks \'Does her image look like her?\' and then suggests taking the experience actually to verify.\",\"topic\":\"Mirror Image\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"The text mentions that a mirror image is a reflection of the ________ object.\",\"options\":[\"imaginary\",\"hidden\",\"original\",\"fake\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the mirror image as the \'reflected image of the original object\'.\",\"topic\":\"Mirror Image\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"At what time of the day is Radhika looking into the mirror in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Before going to bed\",\"Once ready for school\",\"After coming back from play\",\"During lunch time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text starts by saying \'Once ready for school, Radhika looks into the mirror.\'\",\"topic\":\"Mirror Image\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When an object\'s image is reflected in the water, what is the position of the axis of symmetry?\",\"options\":[\"Vertical\",\"Horizontal\",\"Slanting\",\"Circular\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when an object\'s image is reflected in the water, the axis of symmetry is horizontal.\",\"topic\":\"Water Reflection\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, where can an object\'s image be seen besides water?\",\"options\":[\"In a mirror\",\"In a book\",\"In the sky\",\"On a wall\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that an object\'s image can be seen in the mirror.\",\"topic\":\"Water Reflection\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what specific object is shown creating a reflection in a small puddle of water?\",\"options\":[\"A cricket bat\",\"A cricket ball\",\"Cricket stumps\",\"A football\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the reflection of three cricket stumps in a water puddle.\",\"topic\":\"Water Reflection\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/101_105.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure of the tree by the river, where is the reflection of the tree\'s leaves positioned relative to the real tree?\",\"options\":[\"Above the tree\",\"To the right of the tree\",\"Directly below the tree in the water\",\"Behind the tree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Water reflection appears below the object, as seen in the figure of the tree and the river.\",\"topic\":\"Water Reflection\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/101_106.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the dog carrying that can also be seen in its water reflection?\",\"options\":[\"A bone\",\"A piece of bread\",\"A toy\",\"A stone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a dog with a piece of bread in its mouth and its reflection in the water.\",\"topic\":\"Water Reflection\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/101_107.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"The text suggests observing water reflections in which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"Only in drawings\",\"Only in mirrors\",\"In nature\",\"In the dark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says to \'Observe the water reflection in nature.\'\",\"topic\":\"Water Reflection\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are looking at the water reflection of a word, what kind of axis of symmetry are you observing?\",\"options\":[\"A vertical axis\",\"A horizontal axis\",\"A diagonal axis\",\"No axis at all\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that for water reflections, the axis of symmetry is horizontal.\",\"topic\":\"Water Reflection\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these can have a water reflection?\",\"options\":[\"Only letters\",\"Only words\",\"Only objects in nature\",\"Letters, words, and objects in nature\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions looking at reflections of letters, words, and nature in water.\",\"topic\":\"Water Reflection\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the term used in the text to describe the image of an object seen in water?\",\"options\":[\"Shadow\",\"Water reflection\",\"Painting\",\"Sketch\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to an object\'s image in water as \'water reflection\'.\",\"topic\":\"Water Reflection\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"By comparing the real object and its water reflection in the figures, we can conclude that the reflection is:\",\"options\":[\"A side-by-side copy\",\"An upside-down image across a horizontal line\",\"A larger version of the object\",\"A different color than the object\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The horizontal axis of symmetry mentioned in the text results in an upside-down reflection relative to the object.\",\"topic\":\"Water Reflection\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the Std 4 Maths textbook, the word AMBULANCE is used to explain which concept?\",\"options\":[\"Addition\",\"Symmetry\",\"Multiplication\",\"Measurement\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The textbook uses the example of an ambulance to illustrate the concept of reflection symmetry.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why are the letters of the word AMBULANCE written in a special reversed manner on the front of the vehicle?\",\"options\":[\"To make the vehicle look beautiful\",\"So it can be read correctly in a rearview mirror\",\"Because the painter made a mistake\",\"To save space on the vehicle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Mirror images are reversed, so writing it reversed on the vehicle makes it appear correct in a mirror.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you hold a mirror in front of the reversed word \'AMBULANCE\' as seen on the vehicle, how will it appear in the mirror?\",\"options\":[\"It will still look reversed\",\"It will appear upside down\",\"It will appear correctly readable\",\"It will be invisible\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A mirror reflects the reversed image back into a readable format.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these letters from the word \'AMBULANCE\' looks exactly the same when seen in a mirror?\",\"options\":[\"B\",\"L\",\"A\",\"E\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The letter \'A\' has vertical symmetry, so its mirror image looks identical to the original.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The special way \'AMBULANCE\' is written is an example of which type of symmetry?\",\"options\":[\"Rotational symmetry\",\"Reflection symmetry\",\"Quarter turn symmetry\",\"Half turn symmetry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The way mirrors show images is called reflection symmetry.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When a driver in front looks in their mirror, what happens to the \'left\' and \'right\' sides of the image they see?\",\"options\":[\"They stay the same\",\"They are swapped\",\"They turn upside down\",\"They disappear\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In a mirror reflection, the left and right sides are interchanged.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the word \'AMBULANCE\' was written normally (not reversed) on the front of the van, how would a driver in front see it in their mirror?\",\"options\":[\"Normally\",\"In reverse\",\"Upside down\",\"Vertically\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A normal word appears reversed in a mirror reflection.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which other letter in the word \'AMBULANCE\' (besides A) would look the same in a mirror?\",\"options\":[\"M\",\"N\",\"C\",\"E\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The letter \'M\' has vertical symmetry and looks the same in a mirror reflection.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it important for the driver in front to be able to read the word \'AMBULANCE\' correctly in their mirror?\",\"options\":[\"To check the spelling\",\"To know it is an emergency vehicle and give way\",\"To see the color of the letters\",\"To practice reading backwards\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Quick identification of an ambulance allows drivers to clear the path for the emergency.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"The textbook asks \'Why are the letters written in this manner?\' to prompt students to think about:\",\"options\":[\"Speed of the vehicle\",\"Mirror images and symmetry\",\"The number of letters\",\"The cost of the paint\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The question is designed to introduce the concept of mirror reflections in the Symmetry chapter.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21581,21,4,'Maths','en','Perimeter and Area','[\"Perimeter is the total length of all sides of a closed figure.\",\"To find perimeter, add the lengths of all sides.\",\"Perimeter of a rectangle = 2 × (length + breadth).\",\"Perimeter of a square = 4 × side.\",\"Area is the space covered by a surface.\",\"Area of a rectangle = length × breadth.\",\"Area of a square = side × side.\",\"Standard unit for area is square unit (e.g., sq cm, sq m).\",\"Same perimeter can have different areas and vice versa.\",\"To compare areas, use same-sized square units.\",\"Counting squares gives area when each square is 1 unit by 1 unit.\",\"Garland length needed equals perimeter of the blackboard.\",\"Wire mesh needed equals perimeter of the field.\",\"Lace needed equals perimeter of the handkerchief.\",\"Area helps to know how much space a surface covers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the sum of the lengths of all edges of a board called?\",\"options\":[\"Area\",\"Perimeter\",\"Volume\",\"Length\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the sum of lengths of all edges of the board is the perimeter of the board.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Rohan, what tool should be used to measure the length of the edges of the board?\",\"options\":[\"A compass\",\"A measuring tape\",\"A divider\",\"A protractor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Rohan suggests that the edges of the board need to be measured using measuring tape.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Radhika holding in her hands to put on the edges of the blackboard?\",\"options\":[\"A measuring tape\",\"A piece of chalk\",\"A flower garland\",\"A wooden ruler\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure and text show Radhika holding a flower garland to put on the edges of the blackboard.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/104_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which object\'s edges are the children measuring to find the perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"A table\",\"A window\",\"A blackboard\",\"A door\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows children standing in front of a blackboard discussing its edges.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/104_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"The total length of the garland required for the board is equal to which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"The length of one edge\",\"The perimeter of the board\",\"The height of the board\",\"The thickness of the board\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the total length of the garland is equal to the perimeter of the board.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the lengths of the four edges of a board are 100 cm, 50 cm, 100 cm, and 50 cm, what is the perimeter of the board?\",\"options\":[\"150 cm\",\"200 cm\",\"300 cm\",\"250 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Perimeter is the sum of all edges: 100 + 50 + 100 + 50 = 300 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To find the perimeter of any object in the classroom, what must we do?\",\"options\":[\"Measure only the longest edge\",\"Measure and add the lengths of all its edges\",\"Measure the weight of the object\",\"Measure the distance from the floor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The concept of perimeter involves measuring and summing the lengths of all edges of an object.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'sum\' mean when calculating the perimeter of the board?\",\"options\":[\"Subtracting the lengths\",\"Multiplying the lengths\",\"Adding the lengths together\",\"Dividing the lengths\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'sum\' to describe adding the lengths of all edges (.....cm + .....cm + .....cm + .....cm).\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Radhika need to know the perimeter of the blackboard?\",\"options\":[\"To find the weight of the board\",\"To know the length of the garland she needs\",\"To see if the board is clean\",\"To measure the height of the wall\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Radhika asks about the length of the garland, which the text explains is equal to the perimeter.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a student only measures three edges of a four-sided blackboard, will they find the correct perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"Yes, three edges are enough\",\"No, because perimeter is the sum of all edges\",\"Yes, if the edges are the same\",\"No, because they need to measure the middle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Perimeter is defined as the sum of lengths of all edges; missing one edge would result in an incorrect total.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Where exactly does Radhika want to put the flower garlands?\",\"options\":[\"In the middle of the board\",\"On the edges of the board\",\"Behind the board\",\"On the floor below the board\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Radhika explicitly says, \'I want to put flower garlands on the edges of the blackboard.\'\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes the perimeter of a classroom object?\",\"options\":[\"The total length of its boundary\",\"The space inside the object\",\"The color of the object\",\"The number of corners it has\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Perimeter is the sum of the lengths of all edges, which forms the total boundary length.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Perimeter\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the perimeter of a closed figure?\",\"options\":[\"The length of the longest side\",\"The sum of the measures of all sides\",\"The space inside the figure\",\"The number of corners in the figure\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the sum of the measures of all sides of a closed figure is its perimeter.\",\"topic\":\"The Concept of Perimeter\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the farmer need to buy to protect his field from animals?\",\"options\":[\"Wooden sticks\",\"Stone walls\",\"Wire mesh\",\"Plastic sheets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the farmer wants to build a fence using wire mesh.\",\"topic\":\"The Concept of Perimeter\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To find the length of the wire mesh needed for the fence, what should the farmer do?\",\"options\":[\"Measure only one side\",\"Multiply the sides\",\"Add up the lengths of all the sides\",\"Subtract the shortest side from the longest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Add up the lengths of all the sides of the farmer\'s field\' to find the length of the wire mesh.\",\"topic\":\"The Concept of Perimeter\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a field has four sides, how many measurements must be added to find the perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"Two measurements\",\"Four measurements\",\"One measurement\",\"Three measurements\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows an addition of four values (....m + ....m +.... m +.... m) for a four-sided field.\",\"topic\":\"The Concept of Perimeter\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the farmer\'s field, what does the total \'....metre\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"The area of the field\",\"The height of the fence\",\"The perimeter of the field\",\"The number of animals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sum of all sides indicates the perimeter of the figure.\",\"topic\":\"The Concept of Perimeter\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a farmer\'s field has sides of 2m, 3m, 2m, and 3m, what is the length of the wire mesh needed?\",\"options\":[\"5 metres\",\"6 metres\",\"10 metres\",\"12 metres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Perimeter is the sum of all sides: 2 + 3 + 2 + 3 = 10 metres.\",\"topic\":\"The Concept of Perimeter\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A square field has four sides, each measuring 5 metres. What is its perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"10 metres\",\"15 metres\",\"20 metres\",\"25 metres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Adding all four sides: 5 + 5 + 5 + 5 = 20 metres.\",\"topic\":\"The Concept of Perimeter\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a requirement for a figure to have a perimeter calculated by adding its sides as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"It must be a closed figure\",\"It must be an open figure\",\"It must be a very large figure\",\"It must be a circular figure\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The definition specifies that the rule applies to a \'closed figure\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Concept of Perimeter\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a farmer knows the perimeter of his field is 40 metres, what does this tell him about the wire mesh?\",\"options\":[\"He needs 40 metres of wire mesh to go around the field\",\"He needs to buy 40 different pieces of wire\",\"The field is 40 metres wide\",\"The wire mesh will cost 40 rupees\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The perimeter is the total length of the wire mesh needed to fence the field.\",\"topic\":\"The Concept of Perimeter\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it necessary to add \'all\' sides to find the perimeter rather than just some sides?\",\"options\":[\"Because the wire mesh must cover the entire boundary of the closed figure\",\"Because adding only some sides makes the calculation too easy\",\"Because the farmer has extra wire mesh\",\"Because animals only enter from the longest side\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To protect the field, the fence must cover the whole boundary, which is the sum of all sides.\",\"topic\":\"The Concept of Perimeter\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher, what does \'measurement of the surface of the floor\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Perimeter of the floor\",\"Area of the floor\",\"Height of the floor\",\"Length of the floor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that measurement of the surface of the floor means area of the floor.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Area\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why were the tiles brought to the classroom?\",\"options\":[\"To be stacked in a corner\",\"To be placed on the classroom floor\",\"To be given to the students\",\"To be used for a wall\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher explains that the tiles are to be placed on the classroom floor.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Area\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What question did the student ask about the tiles?\",\"options\":[\"What is the color of these tiles?\",\"How much do these tiles cost?\",\"Will these many tiles be enough to cover the floor?\",\"Where were these tiles made?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The student specifically asks if the tiles will be enough to cover the classroom floor.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Area\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What do we need to measure to decide if the tiles are enough for the classroom?\",\"options\":[\"The surface of the classroom floor\",\"The weight of the tiles\",\"The height of the classroom walls\",\"The number of windows in the room\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher says we need to measure the surface of the classroom floor to decide if the tiles are enough.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Area\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to find the area of a table top, what should you measure based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"The weight of the table\",\"The height of the table legs\",\"The surface of the table top\",\"The price of the table\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Measurement of a surface is defined as area in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Area\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the conversation, which concept helps us understand how much space a floor covers?\",\"options\":[\"Volume\",\"Perimeter\",\"Area\",\"Thickness\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links the measurement of the floor\'s surface to the concept of area.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Area\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of measuring the floor\'s surface in this lesson?\",\"options\":[\"To see if the floor is clean\",\"To determine if the tiles will cover the floor\",\"To find the distance around the floor\",\"To count the number of students\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The measurement is done to decide if the tiles brought are enough to cover the floor.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Area\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used in the text to describe the flat top part of the floor?\",\"options\":[\"Boundary\",\"Surface\",\"Corner\",\"Edge\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the word \'surface\' when referring to the floor and its measurement.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Area\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A student wants to cover a small box with paper. What does the student need to find to know how much paper is needed?\",\"options\":[\"The area of the box surface\",\"The weight of the box\",\"The age of the box\",\"The sound the box makes\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Covering a surface involves measuring the area, as implied by the tile example.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Area\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'Area\' the correct measurement to use when placing tiles on a floor?\",\"options\":[\"Because tiles cover the surface of the floor\",\"Because tiles are very heavy\",\"Because tiles are only placed on the edges\",\"Because tiles are used to measure height\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Area is the measurement of a surface, and tiles are used to cover that surface.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Area\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the measurement of the space covered by the surface of any figure called?\",\"options\":[\"Perimeter\",\"Length\",\"Area\",\"Volume\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines area as the measurement of the space covered by the surface of any figure.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the activity table, which tool is used to measure the surface of a table top?\",\"options\":[\"Compass box\",\"Notebook\",\"Textbook\",\"Scale\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'notebook\' as the measuring tool for the surface of a table top.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which surface is measured using a compass box in the textbook activity?\",\"options\":[\"Surface of a book\",\"Surface of a table top\",\"Surface of an iron trunk\",\"Surface of the classroom floor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists the \'surface of an iron trunk\' to be measured with a \'compass box\'.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when we measure the same surface using different measuring tools?\",\"options\":[\"We get the same answer every time\",\"We get different answers of measurement\",\"The surface area changes\",\"The tool size stays the same\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Every time we get different answers of measurement\' when using different tools.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text suggest that a standard unit to measure area needs to be decided?\",\"options\":[\"Because notebooks are too heavy\",\"Because different tools give different answers for the same surface\",\"Because length is more important than area\",\"Because compass boxes are too small\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes that different tools yield different results, leading to the need for a standard unit.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you measure a classroom table using textbooks, the area will be expressed as the number of:\",\"options\":[\"Notebooks\",\"Compass boxes\",\"Textbooks\",\"Iron trunks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The activity table shows that if the tool is a textbook, the area is measured in \'textbooks\'.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is mentioned as a standard unit that has already been decided?\",\"options\":[\"Standard unit for measuring area\",\"Standard unit for measuring length\",\"Standard unit for measuring notebooks\",\"Standard unit for measuring tables\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'Just as the standard unit for measuring length is decided...\'\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of using a \'notebook\' or \'compass box\' in these activities?\",\"options\":[\"To use them as standard units\",\"To use them as measuring tools for area\",\"To store them inside the iron trunk\",\"To measure the length of the table only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes these items as \'measuring tools\' used to measure various surfaces.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the activity, what does the \'Actual number\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"The weight of the tools\",\"The number of tools that cover up the surface\",\"The length of the table\",\"The price of the notebook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table column is titled \'Actual number of such tools that cover up the surface\'.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student measures a table with a notebook and then with a compass box, which statement is true based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"The number of notebooks will be the same as the number of compass boxes\",\"The measurement results will likely be different\",\"The table\'s surface will grow larger with the compass box\",\"Only the notebook is a correct tool\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that using different tools results in different measurement answers.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the lesson, which of these is a \'surface\' to be measured rather than a \'tool\'?\",\"options\":[\"Notebook\",\"Textbook\",\"Compass box\",\"Iron trunk\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the \'iron trunk\' as a \'Name of Surface\' and the others as \'Measuring tools\'.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main conclusion drawn from measuring the classroom table with notebooks, textbooks, and compass boxes?\",\"options\":[\"Area cannot be measured\",\"A standard unit for area is necessary for consistency\",\"Textbooks are the best tools for all surfaces\",\"The classroom table has no area\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that because different tools give different answers, a standard unit for area needs to be decided.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Area with Tools\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the standard unit used to measure surface area?\",\"options\":[\"A circle unit\",\"A square unit\",\"A triangle unit\",\"A line unit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the square unit is the standard unit used to measure surface area.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Anil and Aditi get different measurements for the same table at first?\",\"options\":[\"They measured different tables\",\"They used squares of different sizes\",\"They counted the squares incorrectly\",\"The table size changed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states they got different measurements because they covered the surface with squares of different sizes.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To ensure everyone\'s measurement of area is the same, a square with a side of how many units is used?\",\"options\":[\"1 unit\",\"2 units\",\"5 units\",\"10 units\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a square with a side of 1 unit is used as a standard unit.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT mentioned in the text as a side length for measuring area?\",\"options\":[\"1 cm\",\"1 metre\",\"1 litre\",\"1 kilometre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions cm, metre, kilometre, and foot, but does not mention litre, which is a unit of volume.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Anil and Aditi measure the same table using the same sized squares, what will be the result?\",\"options\":[\"They will get different measurements\",\"They will get the same surface area\",\"The area will become double\",\"The area cannot be measured\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when they used the same sized squares, both of them got the same surface area.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why is a standard unit necessary for measuring area?\",\"options\":[\"To make the table look better\",\"To make the measurement process faster\",\"To ensure everyone\'s measurement of area is the same\",\"To use fewer squares\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that a standard unit is used to ensure that everyone\'s measurement of area of any figure is the same.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which shape did the teacher ask Anil and Aditi to use to cover the surface of the table?\",\"options\":[\"Rectangle\",\"Triangle\",\"Circle\",\"Square\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The teacher asked them to cover the surface of the table with squares.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are measuring a very small surface, which standard side length mentioned in the text would be most suitable?\",\"options\":[\"1 kilometre\",\"1 metre\",\"1 foot\",\"1 cm\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Among the units mentioned (cm, metre, kilometre, foot), 1 cm is the smallest unit suitable for small surfaces.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many squares did Anil use to cover the surface of the table?\",\"options\":[\"4 squares\",\"6 squares\",\"8 squares\",\"10 squares\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Counting the squares in the figure shows 2 rows of 4 squares each, totaling 8 squares.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/109_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what does the total number of squares represent?\",\"options\":[\"The weight of the table\",\"The length of the table only\",\"The area obtained by Anil\",\"The height of the table\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The caption of the figure states it is the \'Area obtained after covering the surface of the table with squares used by Anil\'.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/109_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the measurement of the area of a figure if the size of the unit square is changed?\",\"options\":[\"The measurement stays the same\",\"The measurement becomes different\",\"The measurement becomes zero\",\"The measurement cannot be calculated\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that when Anil and Aditi used squares of different sizes, they got different measurements.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a standard unit for measuring area as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"1 foot square\",\"1 gram square\",\"1 second square\",\"1 degree square\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions measuring area using squares with sides of 1 foot.\",\"topic\":\"Standard Unit for Measuring Area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the text, what was used to measure the spaces allotted for the rangoli competition?\",\"options\":[\"Long sticks\",\"Squares of the same size\",\"Round beads\",\"Measuring tapes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher suggests measuring the spaces using squares of the same size to count them.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher, if the length and breadth of a surface are given in cm, how is the area expressed?\",\"options\":[\"In cm\",\"In square cm\",\"In meters\",\"In square units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if dimensions are in cm, the area is expressed in square cm.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many squares were needed to cover the space allotted to Neeta?\",\"options\":[\"10 squares\",\"14 squares\",\"12 squares\",\"7 squares\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that the area of the spaces allotted to each of them is 12 square units.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Sayali notice after counting the squares for both allotted spaces?\",\"options\":[\"Neeta had more squares\",\"Sayali had more squares\",\"The number of squares was the same for both\",\"The squares were of different sizes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sayali observes that the number of squares used to cover the spaces allotted to both is the same.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When the text says the area is \'12 square units\', what does \'12\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"The number of students\",\"The number of squares covering the space\",\"The length of the boundary\",\"The number of rangoli colors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The area is determined by the number of squares used to cover the space.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the teacher insist on using squares of the \'same size\' to measure the spaces?\",\"options\":[\"To make the rangoli look better\",\"To ensure a fair comparison of the two areas\",\"Because the school only had one size of square\",\"To make the counting faster\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using the same unit (squares of the same size) allows for an accurate comparison of the two spaces.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many small squares make up the top rectangle that has a length of 4 units and a breadth of 3 units?\",\"options\":[\"7 squares\",\"10 squares\",\"12 squares\",\"16 squares\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Counting the grid in the figure shows 4 columns and 3 rows, totaling 12 squares.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/110_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a student measures a surface and finds it is covered exactly by 12 squares of 1 cm each, what is the area of that surface?\",\"options\":[\"12 cm\",\"12 square cm\",\"24 cm\",\"12 units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the teacher\'s note, if dimensions are in cm, the area is in square cm.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how does the area of the top rectangle compare to the area of the bottom rectangle?\",\"options\":[\"The top rectangle has a larger area\",\"The bottom rectangle has a larger area\",\"Both rectangles have the same area\",\"The areas cannot be compared\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Both rectangles in the figure are made of 12 squares, meaning their areas are equal.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/110_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Neeta initially thought her space was less than Sayali\'s. What evidence proved that the spaces were actually equal?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher said so without measuring\",\"They both drew the same rangoli\",\"Both spaces were covered by the same number of squares\",\"They used different sized squares\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Counting the squares showed that both spaces were covered by 12 squares, proving the areas were equal.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific unit of area mentioned for the rangoli spaces in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Centimeters\",\"Square units\",\"Squares\",\"Units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states the area is \'12 square units\'.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To compare the area of two different shapes accurately, what must be true about the squares used to cover them?\",\"options\":[\"They must be different colors\",\"They must be squares of the same size\",\"They must be very small\",\"They must be made of paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher specifies using \'squares of same size\' to measure and compare the spaces.\",\"topic\":\"Comparing Areas of Figures\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21582,21,4,'Maths','en','Volume and Capacity','[\"Volume is the amount of space a 3D object occupies.\",\"Volume is measured in cubic units (like cubic cm).\",\"A cube with side 1 unit has volume 1 cubic unit.\",\"To find volume, count how many 1-unit cubes fit inside the object.\",\"Capacity is the amount of liquid a container can hold.\",\"Capacity is measured in litres and millilitres.\",\"1 litre = 1000 millilitres.\",\"To convert litres to millilitres, multiply by 1000.\",\"To convert millilitres to litres, divide by 1000.\",\"Half litre = 500 ml, quarter litre = 250 ml, three-quarter litre = 750 ml.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the volume of a cube where each side is 1 unit?\",\"options\":[\"1 square unit\",\"1 cubic unit\",\"1 unit\",\"2 cubic units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the volume of a cube with each side of 1 unit is 1 cubic unit.\",\"topic\":\"Volume: Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a cube, which of these measurements are the same?\",\"options\":[\"Only length and width\",\"Only width and height\",\"Length, width, and height\",\"Only length and height\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that for a cube, the length, width, and height are the same.\",\"topic\":\"Volume: Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a block is made of 8 cubes, each having a volume of 1 cubic unit, what is the volume of the block?\",\"options\":[\"1 cubic unit\",\"4 cubic units\",\"8 cubic units\",\"16 cubic units\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 8 cubes of volume 1 cubic unit each result in a block of 8 cubic units.\",\"topic\":\"Volume: Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What unit is used to measure the volume of a solid?\",\"options\":[\"Square units\",\"Cubic units\",\"Linear units\",\"Metre units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the volume of a solid is measured in cubic units.\",\"topic\":\"Volume: Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the volume of any 3D shape mean?\",\"options\":[\"The number of sides it has\",\"The number of cubes of measure 1 unit it holds\",\"The length of its longest side\",\"The area of its base\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines volume as the number of cubes of measure 1 unit that a 3D shape holds.\",\"topic\":\"Volume: Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you have 27 cubes of volume 1 cubic unit each, what is the volume of the resulting block?\",\"options\":[\"9 cubic units\",\"27 cubic units\",\"54 cubic units\",\"3 cubic units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that 27 cubes of volume 1 cubic unit each make a block of 27 cubic units.\",\"topic\":\"Volume: Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a block has a volume of 10 cubic units, how many cubes of 1 cubic unit each were used to make it?\",\"options\":[\"1 cube\",\"5 cubes\",\"10 cubes\",\"20 cubes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows that a block of 10 cubic units is made from 10 cubes of volume 1 cubic unit each.\",\"topic\":\"Volume: Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many units is each side of the basic cube mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"1 unit\",\"2 units\",\"3 units\",\"4 units\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text starts by stating that each side of the cube is 1 unit.\",\"topic\":\"Volume: Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which shape is specifically described as having the same length, width, and height?\",\"options\":[\"Rectangle\",\"Sphere\",\"Cube\",\"Triangle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses the cube as the example where length, width, and height are the same.\",\"topic\":\"Volume: Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definition in the text, what is the volume of a shape that holds 15 cubes of 1 unit measure?\",\"options\":[\"1 cubic unit\",\"10 cubic units\",\"15 cubic units\",\"30 cubic units\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since volume is the number of 1-unit cubes a shape holds, 15 cubes equals 15 cubic units.\",\"topic\":\"Volume: Let\'s Understand\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the amount of water needed to fill a container up to the brim called?\",\"options\":[\"Weight of the container\",\"Capacity of the container\",\"Length of the container\",\"Height of the container\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines capacity as the amount of water needed to fill a container up to the brim.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity: Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these units are used to measure capacity?\",\"options\":[\"Metres and centimetres\",\"Grams and kilograms\",\"Litres and millilitres\",\"Hours and minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the units used to measure capacity are litres and millilitres.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity: Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the short form used to write \'millilitres\'?\",\"options\":[\"(m)\",\"(l)\",\"(g)\",\"(ml)\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states that in short, millilitres is written as (ml).\",\"topic\":\"Capacity: Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If water from a bottle fills a vessel exactly to the brim, what can we say about the vessel?\",\"options\":[\"It has the same volume as the bottle\",\"It is bigger than the bottle\",\"It is smaller than the bottle\",\"It has no capacity\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that whichever vessel fills to the brim has the same volume as that of the bottle.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity: Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In what unit is the volume of liquids measured?\",\"options\":[\"Kilograms\",\"Litres\",\"Metres\",\"Centimetres\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically states that the volume of liquids is measured in litres.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity: Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When is a container considered to be at its full capacity?\",\"options\":[\"When it is empty\",\"When it is half full\",\"When it is filled to the brim\",\"When it is leaking\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Capacity is defined as the amount needed to fill a container up to the brim.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity: Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A tank has a capacity of 1000 litres. If 200 litres of water is poured into the empty tank, what is the volume of water in the tank?\",\"options\":[\"1000 litres\",\"800 litres\",\"200 litres\",\"1200 litres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides this exact example: if 200 litres is poured into an empty tank, the volume of water is 200 litres.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity: Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How would you write \'10 litres\' using the short form mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"10 ml\",\"10 l\",\"10 g\",\"10 m\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that litres is written in short as (l).\",\"topic\":\"Capacity: Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the difference between the capacity of a tank and the volume of water in it?\",\"options\":[\"They are always the same number\",\"Capacity is the maximum it can hold, volume is what it actually contains\",\"Capacity is measured in grams, volume is measured in litres\",\"There is no difference between them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that a tank can have a capacity of 1000 litres but a volume of 200 litres if only that much is poured in.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity: Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a tank with a capacity of 1000 litres already contains 200 litres of water, how much more water is needed to reach its capacity?\",\"options\":[\"200 litres\",\"1000 litres\",\"800 litres\",\"1200 litres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since capacity is the amount needed to fill to the brim (1000) and it has 200, it needs 800 more to reach the brim.\",\"topic\":\"Capacity: Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How many millilitres (ml) are equal to 1 litre?\",\"options\":[\"500 ml\",\"750 ml\",\"1000 ml\",\"1250 ml\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 1000 ml is equal to 1 litre.\",\"topic\":\"Conversion of Units of Measurement\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is 250 ml called in terms of a litre?\",\"options\":[\"Half litre\",\"Quarter litre\",\"Three quarters litre\",\"One litre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines 250 ml as a quarter litre.\",\"topic\":\"Conversion of Units of Measurement\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the measurement for a \'half litre\'?\",\"options\":[\"100 ml\",\"250 ml\",\"500 ml\",\"750 ml\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 500 ml is equal to 1\\/2 (half litre).\",\"topic\":\"Conversion of Units of Measurement\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which measurement is referred to as \'three quarters\' of a litre?\",\"options\":[\"250 ml\",\"500 ml\",\"750 ml\",\"1000 ml\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 750 ml is equal to 3\\/4 (3 quarters) litre.\",\"topic\":\"Conversion of Units of Measurement\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many bottles of 500 ml are required to fill a 1 litre bottle completely?\",\"options\":[\"1 bottle\",\"2 bottles\",\"3 bottles\",\"4 bottles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since 500 ml + 500 ml = 1 litre, two bottles are needed.\",\"topic\":\"Conversion of Units of Measurement\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many bottles of 250 ml are needed to fill a 1 litre bottle completely?\",\"options\":[\"2 bottles\",\"3 bottles\",\"4 bottles\",\"5 bottles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows that four 250 ml bottles added together equal 1 litre.\",\"topic\":\"Conversion of Units of Measurement\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To fill a 1 litre bottle, how many bottles of 100 ml must be used?\",\"options\":[\"5 bottles\",\"10 