ain\":\"The textbook states that 1 litre = 1000 millilitres.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If 1 litre is 1000 ml, then 3 litres is equal to 3 × 1000 ml, which is ______ ml.\",\"options\":[\"30 ml\",\"300 ml\",\"3000 ml\",\"30000 ml\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Following the pattern 3 × 1000 ml = 3000 ml.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To convert 4 litres into millilitres, we should multiply 4 by which number?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"100\",\"1000\",\"500\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows 4 litres = 4 × 1000 ml.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If we have 5000 ml of water, how many litres is that?\",\"options\":[\"50 litres\",\"5 litres\",\"500 litres\",\"1 litre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states 5000 ml = 5 litres.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How can 3450 ml be written in litres and millilitres?\",\"options\":[\"3 litres + 450 ml\",\"34 litres + 50 ml\",\"300 litres + 450 ml\",\"345 litres + 0 ml\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows 3450 ml = 3000 ml + 450 ml = 3 litres + 450 ml.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If 1000 ml = 1 litre, then how many millilitres are there in 8 litres?\",\"options\":[\"80 ml\",\"800 ml\",\"8000 ml\",\"80000 ml\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Based on the text, 8 litres is equivalent to 8000 ml.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the volume of a liquid when it is poured from a glass tray into a glass jar?\",\"options\":[\"The volume increases\",\"The volume decreases\",\"The volume does not change\",\"The volume becomes zero\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the volume of the liquid does not change even if the container is changed.\",\"topic\":\"Do the Activity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If water in a 