s the honeycomb as an example to help understand patterns found in three-dimensional shapes.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main shift in learning described in this \'Let\'s Remember\' section?\",\"options\":[\"Moving from 3D shapes to 2D shapes\",\"Moving from 2D shapes to 3D shapes\",\"Moving from numbers to shapes\",\"Moving from nature to machines\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text indicates a transition from studying 2D shapes in previous standards to 3D shapes now.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text mention the pineapple, honeycomb, and lantern together?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are all found in a house\",\"Because they all show specific styles of repeating patterns\",\"Because they are all the same shape\",\"Because they are all two-dimensional\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text groups these items because they \'all have some specific styles in which repeating patterns are seen.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Remember\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is an attractive pattern made using various regular and irregular shapes called?\",\"options\":[\"A line\",\"A design\",\"A number\",\"A circle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a design as an attractive pattern made using various regular and irregular shapes.\",\"topic\":\"Creating designs using shapes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, where can designs of leaves and flowers be found?\",\"options\":[\"On the floor\",\"On the pallu of a mother\'s saree\",\"On a car\",\"On a book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions designs of leaves and flowers on the pallu of a mother\'s saree and on the walls of the house.\",\"topic\":\"Creating designs using shapes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which vegetable is used in the activity to make beautiful designs on paper?\",\"options\":[\"Potato\",\"Carrot\",\"Lady\'s finger