s using shapes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which geometric shape is used to form the repeating border at the top and bottom?\",\"options\":[\"Circles\",\"Squares\",\"Triangles\",\"Rectangles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The image shows a border made of repeating small triangles.\",\"topic\":\"Creating designs using shapes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/124_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the shape of the yellow motifs repeated throughout the pattern?\",\"options\":[\"Hexagons\",\"Octagons\",\"Pentagons\",\"Circles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The yellow shapes in the pattern have eight sides, making them octagons.\",\"topic\":\"Creating designs using shapes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/124_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text suggest looking for motifs in your surroundings?\",\"options\":[\"To count them\",\"To make similar designs\",\"To clean them\",\"To ignore them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages looking for motifs to make similar designs.\",\"topic\":\"Creating designs using shapes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What should be used to create a pattern in the frame as per the text instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Geometric shapes\",\"Only black ink\",\"Numbers\",\"Letters\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to create a pattern using geometric shapes in the given frame.\",\"topic\":\"Creating designs using shapes\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"create\"},{\"q\":\"What should not be left between tiles when they are arranged in a tiling pattern?\",\"options\":[\"Colors\",\"Gaps or empty spaces\",\"Lines\",\"Shapes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that tiles are arranged so that there are no gaps or empty spaces left between them.\",\"topic\":\"Tiling\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a tiling pattern, how are the pieces of tiles arranged?\",\"options\":[\"One on top of another\",\"Far away 