, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 18, 20 are 2, 4, 6, 8, 0 repeating.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher\'s note, how should the concept of patterns in odd-even numbers be explained?\",\"options\":[\"By memorizing the tables\",\"By writing numbers in a notebook\",\"By pairing objects, pictures, or dots\",\"By counting backwards from 100\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that odd-even concepts should be explained by pairing objects, pictures, or dots.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, look at the \'Pattern of Counting Numbers\'. If the pattern continues, how many dots will be in the next group?\",\"options\":[\"4 dots\",\"5 dots\",\"6 dots\",\"8 dots\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The counting number pattern increases by one dot each time (1, 2, 3, 4), so the next is 5.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/127_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many dots are used to form the fourth number in the \'Pattern of Triangular Numbers\'?\",\"options\":[\"6 dots\",\"8 dots\",\"10 dots\",\"12 dots\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Counting the dots in the fourth triangle shown in the figure reveals there are 10 dots.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/127_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the pattern of digits in the units place for the 4 times table (4, 8, 12, 16, 20...)?\",\"options\":[\"4, 8, 0, 4, 8\",\"4, 8, 2, 6, 0\",\"4, 6, 8, 0, 2\",\"2, 4, 6, 8, 0\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The units digits of 4, 8, 12, 16, 20 are 4, 8, 2, 6, 0.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you write the 8 times table in your notebook as instructed, what is the pattern of digits in the unit\'s place?\",\"options\":[\"8, 6, 4, 2, 0\",\"8, 0, 8, 0, 8\",\"8, 7, 6, 5, 4\",\"2, 4, 6, 8, 0\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The 8 times table (8, 16, 24, 32, 40) has units digits 8, 6, 4, 2, 0.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Following the instruction to write the 3 times table, what digit appears in the unit\'s place for the number 21?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"2\",\"1\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the number 21 (which is 3 x 7), the digit in the unit\'s place is 1.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following sequences represents the \'Pattern of Even Numbers\' mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"1, 3, 5, 7, 9\",\"2, 4, 6, 8, 10\",\"1, 2, 3, 4, 5\",\"1, 3, 6, 10, 15\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 as the first example of a times table pattern which are even numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which pattern is formed by the numbers 1, 3, 5, and 7 as shown in the dot diagrams?\",\"options\":[\"Pattern of Even Numbers\",\"Pattern of Triangular Numbers\",\"Pattern of Counting Numbers\",\"Pattern of Odd Numbers\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text and figure label the sequence 1, 3, 5, 7 as the \'Pattern of Odd Numbers\'.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When writing the 7 times table to find a pattern, what is the unit\'s digit of the fifth number (7 x 5)?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"4\",\"1\",\"5\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"7 x 5 = 35; the digit in the unit\'s place is 5.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT one of the four specific dot patterns mentioned in the \'Complete the pattern\' section?\",\"options\":[\"Pattern of Counting Numbers\",\"Pattern of Square Numbers\",\"Pattern of Even Numbers\",\"Pattern of Triangular Numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists Counting, Triangular, Even, and Odd numbers; Square numbers are not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Number Patterns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"e