's Think\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the series 10, 22, 34, 46, 58, 70, 82, 94, what is the difference between any two consecutive numbers?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"12\",\"2\",\"20\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Subtracting 10 from 22 gives 12, and 22 from 34 gives 12.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Think\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the common digit in the units place for the series 3, 13, 23, 33, 43, 53, 63, 73?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Every number in this specific series ends with the digit 3.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Think\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'For Teachers\' note, what should one child do while the other identifies the number?\",\"options\":[\"Write a number\",\"Call out a number\",\"Draw a pattern\",\"Hide a number\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'One child can call out a number and other can identify the number as odd or even.\'\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Think\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the series: 10, 22, 34, 46, 58, 70, 82, 94. Are these numbers odd or even?\",\"options\":[\"They are all odd numbers\",\"They are all even numbers\",\"They alternate between odd and even\",\"They are neither odd nor even\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"All numbers in this series end in 0, 2, 4, 6, or 8, making them even.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Think\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these series from the text consists entirely of odd numbers?\",\"options\":[\"4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32\",\"10, 22, 34, 46, 58, 70, 82, 94\",\"3, 13, 23, 33, 43, 53, 63, 73\",\"None of the above\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The series 3, 13, 23... ends in 3, which makes all the numbers odd.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Think\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what color should be used to fill the boxes with even numbers in a grid from 301 to 400?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"Red\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\