 been replaced by numbers\",\"The shapes have been removed\",\"The shapes have stayed in the exact same order\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"DEFG and HGED use different letters to represent a change in the order of the items in the pattern.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Solve\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What type of number positions are 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, and 15?\",\"options\":[\"Even positions\",\"Odd positions\",\"Multiples of 10\",\"Multiples of 4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"These numbers are not divisible by 2, making them odd positions.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Solve\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'For Teachers\' section, what should be used to explain the concept of pattern formation?\",\"options\":[\"Geometric shapes in the Maths Kit\",\"Only numbers from 1 to 100\",\"Pictures of animals\",\"Stories from the English book\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s note suggests using geometric shapes in the Maths Kit for pattern formation.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Solve\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the pattern style \'ABB\', what does the repetition of the letter \'B\' signify?\",\"options\":[\"The first shape is used twice\",\"Three different shapes are used\",\"The second shape is repeated twice\",\"No shapes are repeated\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In ABB, \'A\' is the first item and \'B\' is the second item which appears twice.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Solve\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many small rectangular boxes are there in one horizontal row?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"8\",\"10\",\"12\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"By counting the boxes across the top row of the grid, there are 10 boxes.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Solve\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/129_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if you start writing numbers from 301 in the first box, what color should the second box be according to the text instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"White\",\"Red\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The second box would contain the number 302, which is an even number, and even numbers must be green.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s Solve\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/129_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How many different colours of curtains did Mother want to buy from the shopkeeper?\",\"options\":[\"One colour\",\"Two colours\",\"Three colours\",\"Four colours\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that she wants to buy curtains of two colours.\",\"topic\":\"Permutations\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what items is the shopkeeper showing to the mother and the boy?\",\"options\":[\"Bangles\",\"Dumbbells\",\"Curtains\",\"Prizes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a shopkeeper displaying patterned cloths, which the text identifies as curtains.\",\"topic\":\"Permutations\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/132_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which two colours did Mother choose for the four curtains she bought for the large window?\",\"options\":[\"Red and Green\",\"Yellow and Green\",\"Red and Yellow\",\"Blue and Red\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Mother bought two red and two yellow curtains.\",\"topic\":\"Permutations\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which three specific items are being used by the students for their school drill?\",\"options\":[\"Bangles, curtains and rings\",\"Dumbbells, lezim and rings\",\"Prizes, dots and walls\",\"Red, yellow and green colours\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure labels show students performing a drill with dumbbells, lezim, and rings.\",\"topic\":\"Permutations\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/133_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How many bangles of each colour does the girl want to wear on one hand?\",\"options\":[\"1 red and 1 green\",\"2 red and 2 green\",\"3 red and 3 green\",\"2 red and 2 yellow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\