part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To find all the \'other different ways\' to paint the wall as mentioned in the text, what must we change?\",\"options\":[\"The size of the wall\",\"The number of colours used\",\"The order of the three colours\",\"The type of paint used\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Permutations involve changing the order or sequence of the items (colours) to create new arrangements.\",\"topic\":\"Permutations\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many curtains did Mother buy in total to hang on the large window?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mother bought two red and two yellow curtains, which equals four curtains.\",\"topic\":\"Permutations\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Into how many groups (Pools) is the \'Asia Hockey Cup\' organised according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the \'Asia Hockey Cup\' is organised into two groups (Pools) \'A\' and \'B\'.\",\"topic\":\"Combinations\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these countries is part of Pool \'A\' in the Asia Hockey Cup?\",\"options\":[\"Pakistan\",\"Sri Lanka\",\"Kazakhstan\",\"Malaysia\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists India, China, Japan, and Kazakhstan as the countries in Pool \'A\'.\",\"topic\":\"Combinations\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the list provided, how many total matches will be played in Pool \'A\' to reach the semi-finals?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"6\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists 6 specific match combinations for Pool \'A\'.\",\"topic\":\"Combinations\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which country\'s name appears first in the list for Pool \'A\'?\",\"options\":[\"China\",\"India\",\"Japan\",\"Kazakhstan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows \'India\' at the top of the list under Pool \'A\'.\",\"topic\":\"Combinations\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/136_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the given figure, how many countries are participating in Pool \'A\'?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure lists four countries: India, China, Japan, and Kazakhstan.\",\"topic\":\"Combinations\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/136_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If we look at the match list, how many matches is India scheduled to play in Pool \'A\'?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"India plays against China, Japan, and Kazakhstan, totaling 3 matches.\",\"topic\":\"Combinations\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a new country, \'Singapore\', joined Pool \'A\', which of the following would be a new match combination?\",\"options\":[\"India vs China\",\"Japan vs Kazakhstan\",\"China vs Singapore\",\"China vs Japan\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A match with Singapore would be a new combination not already in the list of six.\",\"topic\":\"Combinations\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'China vs India\' not listed as a separate match in the list of 6 matches?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are in different pools\",\"Because \'India vs China\' is already counted as one match between them\",\"Because China is not playing in the semi-finals\",\"Because India plays only against Japan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In combinations, the order does not matter; a match between India and China is the same as China vs India.\",\"topic\":\"Combinations\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which country plays the very last match listed in the Pool \'A\' combinations?\",\"options\":[\"India\",\"China\",\"Japan\",\"Kazakhstan\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The 6th match listed is \'Japan Kazakhstan\', so Kazakhstan (and Japan) are in the last match.\",\"topic\":\"Combinations\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the match list, if every country plays every other country exactly once, how many matches does each individual country play?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"6\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Each country (like India) appears in exactly 3 match pairings.\",\"topic\":\"Combinations\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which path must you take from the start to reach the end?\",\"options\":[\"A straight path\",\"A diagonal path\",\"A reverse path\",\"A zig-zag path\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that to reach the end, you need to go by the straight path.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many guests are mentioned in the handshake activity on the dais?\",\"options\":[\"Three guests\",\"Four guests\",\"Five guests\",\"Six guests\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that there are five guests on a dais.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If five guests greet each other by shaking hands exactly once, how many handshakes occur in total?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"10\",\"15\",\"25\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"For 5 people, the number of handshakes is 4+3+2+1 = 10.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which four notes of music are used to create different combinations in the activity?\",\"options\":[\"Sa, Re, Ga, Ma\",\"Pa, Dha, Ni, Sa\",\"Sa, Ga, Pa, Ni\",\"Re, Ga, Ma, Pa\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifies using the four notes of music: Sa, Re, Ga, Ma.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the path activity, which of the following movements is strictly NOT allowed?\",\"options\":[\"Going forward\",\"Following a diagonal path\",\"Moving to the next circle\",\"Going straight\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the condition that you cannot follow a diagonal path.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the rule regarding the circles when moving from start to end?\",\"options\":[\"Skip every other circle\",\"No circle should be skipped\",\"Skip the first two circles\",\"Only touch the even circles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text clearly states \'No circle should be skipped\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many total circles are shown in the grid between the Start and Finish arrows?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"12\",\"14\",\"16\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Counting the circles in the figure: 2 in the top row and 4 in each of the other three rows equals 14.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/138_110.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the number that will fill the blank in the bottom right corner?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"13\",\"14\",\"15\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The pattern is the sum of the top two numbers in each column (7+8=15, 6+4=10, so 9+5=14).\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/138_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if the sum of each row and column is 15, what number should fill the blank box in the top row between 2 and 6?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"3\",\"9\",\"1\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To make the top row sum to 15 (2 + ? + 6 = 15), the missing number must be 7.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/138_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How many times can each music note be used in a single combination according to the activity?\",\"options\":[\"Only once\",\"Twice\",\"As many times as you like\",\"Not more than three times\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says to use the four notes of music \'only once\' in each combination.\",\"topic\":\"Fun with Maths\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the national 24-hour toll-free emergency phone service number for children in distress?\",\"options\":[\"100\",\"101\",\"1098\",\"1091\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that CHILDLINE 1098 is a national 24-hour toll-free emergency phone service for children.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Message\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Up to what age is the CHILDLINE service available for children who are troubled or abused?\",\"options\":[\"Below 10 years\",\"Below 15 years\",\"Below 18 years\",\"Below 21 years\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the service is for those who are \'below 18 years of age\'.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Message\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a child feels uneasy about someone touching them inappropriately, what should they NOT do?\",\"options\":[\"Tell someone they trust\",\"Not blame themselves\",\"Keep quiet\",\"Inform the NCPCR\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'If you feel uneasy about someone touching you inappropriately, you should not keep quiet.\'\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Message\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text say a child need not feel \'bad\' after an unsafe touch?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is a secret\",\"Because it is not their fault\",\"Because they are young\",\"Because they are quiet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says: \'You need not feel “bad” because it’s not your fault.\'\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Message\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A child wants to inform the National Commission for Protection of Child Rights about an unsafe touch. Which tool should they use?\",\"options\":[\"A letter\",\"A text message\",\"The POCSO e-box\",\"A newspaper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions informing the National Commission for Protection of Child Rights through the POCSO e-box.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Message\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which foundation is the CHILDLINE service an initiative of?\",\"options\":[\"NCPCR Foundation\",\"POCSO Foundation\",\"CHILDLINE India Foundation\",\"Ministry Foundation\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that CHILDLINE 1098 is an initiative of CHILDLINE India Foundation.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Message\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the name of the electronic box shown in the center?\",\"options\":[\"POCSO e-box\",\"NCPCR Box\",\"Child Box\",\"Safety Box\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The image clearly labels the central red button as \'POCSO e-box\'.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Message\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/139_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the phone number shown for CHILDLINE?\",\"options\":[\"100\",\"1098\",\"101\",\"1091\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image displays the number \'1098\' in large red digits.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Message\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"21\\/139_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the email address provided in the text for the POCSO e-box?\",\"options\":[\"ncpcr@gov.in\",\"childline@gov.in\",\"pocso@gov.in\",\"help@gov.in\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides the email address ncpcr@gov.in for the POCSO e-box.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Message\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do if you know another child who is being abused or is in distress?\",\"options\":[\"Keep it a secret\",\"Call 1098\",\"Blame the child\",\"Do nothing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text advises calling 1098 if you \'know some other child who is\' troubled, confused, or abused.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Message\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child is in distress at 2 o\'clock in the morning, can they call CHILDLINE for help?\",\"options\":[\"No, only in the morning\",\"No, only in the evening\",\"Yes, it is a 24-hour service\",\"Yes, but only on weekends\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes CHILDLINE as a \'national 24 hours toll free emergency phone service\'.\