चीन नागरी संस्कृतीत कोणत्या शास्त्रांचा विकास झाला होता?\",\"options\":[\"संगणक आणि अणुऊर्जा\",\"गणित, खगोलशास्त्र आणि वैद्यक\",\"विमानविद्या आणि रोबोटिक्स\",\"केवळ चित्रकला आणि संगीत\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पाठ्यपुस्तकातील १० व्या मुद्द्यानुसार गणित, खगोलशास्त्र आणि वैद्यक यांसारख्या शास्त्रांचा विकास झाला होता.\",\"topic\":\"प्राचीन नागरी संस्कृतीची वैशिष्ट्ये\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"प्राचीन नगरातील रस्त्यांचे वैशिष्ट्य काय होते?\",\"options\":[\"रस्ते अरुंद आणि कच्चे होते\",\"रस्ते फलाटबंद होते\",\"रस्ते केवळ मातीचे होते\",\"रस्ते नव्हतेच\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सुव्यवस्थित नगररचनेमध्ये फलाटबंद रस्ते हे एक महत्त्वाचे वैशिष्ट्य होते.\",\"topic\":\"प्राचीन नागरी संस्कृतीची वैशिष्ट्ये\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"शेतीसाठी कोणत्या प्रकारच्या पद्धतीचा विकास प्राचीन नागरी संस्कृतीत झाला होता?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ पावसावर आधारित शेती\",\"विकसित सिंचनपद्धती\",\"स्थलांतरित शेती\",\"केवळ बागायती शेती\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पायाभूत वास्तूंसोबतच विकसित सिंचनपद्धती हे या संस्कृतीचे वैशिष्ट्य होते.\",\"topic\":\"प्राचीन नागरी संस्कृतीची वैशिष्ट्ये\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"नगरांच्या संरक्षणासाठी कोणती महत्त्वाची वास्तू बांधली जात असे?\",\"options\":[\"मोठी बागेची भिंत\",\"संरक्षक तटबंदी\",\"लाकडी कुंपण\",\"केवळ पाण्याचे हौद\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"नगराच्या संरक्षणासाठी संरक्षक तटबंदी बांधणे हे सुव्यवस्थित नगररचनेचे वैशिष्ट्य होते.\",\"topic\":\"प्राचीन नागरी संस्कृतीची वैशिष्ट्ये\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21634,27,5,'English','en','Songs and Greetings','[\"The chapter includes simple English songs and greetings for young learners.\",\"Songs help in learning rhythm, pronunciation, and basic vocabulary.\",\"Greetings like \'Good morning\' are used to start the day politely.\",\"Repeating phrases in songs aids memory and language practice.\",\"Actions with songs improve understanding and engagement.\",\"The song \'Good morning\' teaches daily routine expressions.\",\"The song \'The more we get together\' promotes friendship and unity.\",\"Actions like clapping or waving can be done while singing.\",\"Listening to songs improves listening skills in English.\",\"Singing builds confidence in speaking English aloud.\",\"Simple sentence structures in songs are easy to imitate.\",\"Songs introduce common words like \'you\', \'we\', \'together\', \'happy\'.\",\"Rhyming words in songs make learning enjoyable.\",\"Teachers use songs to create a joyful classroom atmosphere.\",\"Students learn to greet others through song practice.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What greeting is used at the start of Song 1?\",\"options\":[\"Good morning\",\"Good night\",\"Good afternoon\",\"Good evening\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Song 1 begins with the words \'Good morning, good morning\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Song 2, what will happen if we get together more?\",\"options\":[\"We will be sad\",\"We will be angry\",\"We will be happier\",\"We will be sleepy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Song 2 states, \'The more we get together, the happier we’ll be.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Song 1, the poet hopes the person is feeling ______.\",\"options\":[\"sick\",\"fine\",\"tired\",\"sad\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I hope you are feeling fine\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In Song 2, whose friends are being talked about?\",\"options\":[\"Only my friends\",\"Only your friends\",\"Your friends and my friends\",\"No friends at all\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song mentions \'For your friends and my friends \\/ And my friends and your friends.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to wish someone the \'best\' in the morning as per Song 1, what is the correct phrase?\",\"options\":[\"The best to you this morning!\",\"Goodbye for now!\",\"How are you today?\",\"I am feeling fine!\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Song 1 contains the line \'The best to you this morning!\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message of Song 2?\",\"options\":[\"Being alone is better\",\"Friends make us unhappy\",\"Togetherness brings happiness\",\"We should not talk to friends\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song emphasizes that being together makes people happier.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from Song 1 rhymes with the word \'fine\'?\",\"options\":[\"Morning\",\"Best\",\"Time\",\"Hope\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In Song 1, \'fine\' and \'time\' are rhyming words at the end of the lines.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what greeting are the two children using in their speech bubbles?\",\"options\":[\"Hello!\",\"Hi!\",\"Good morning!\",\"Goodbye!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speech bubbles in the image clearly show the word \'Hi!\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/011_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the given figure, what are the two boys doing?\",\"options\":[\"They are fighting over a toy\",\"They are sleeping in class\",\"They are greeting each other happily\",\"They are crying because they are sad\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The image shows two smiling boys saying \'Hi!\' to each other.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/011_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In Song 1, when does the poet hope the person is happy?\",\"options\":[\"Only in the morning\",\"All the time\",\"Only when they are alone\",\"Never\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The last line of Song 1 says, \'And happy all the time!\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who is introduced as Riya\'s friend in the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Minu\",\"Sonali\",\"Riya\",\"Teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the text, Riya says, \'And this is my friend, Sonali.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is an action word mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Run\",\"Jump\",\"Sway\",\"Sleep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'sing, dance, play, sway\' as actions.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct response to the question \'How are you?\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"I am happy.\",\"I’m fine, thank you.\",\"I am singing.\",\"Hello, Minu.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly provides the response: \'I’m fine, thank you.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which unit does this revision topic belong to?\",\"options\":[\"Unit Two\",\"Unit Five\",\"Unit One\",\"Unit Ten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Unit One : Revision\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Riya say to Minu when she first introduces herself?\",\"options\":[\"Hi, I am Sonali.\",\"Hello, Minu. I’m Riya.\",\"How are you, Minu?\",\"Goodbye, Minu.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows Riya saying, \'Hello, Minu. I’m Riya.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instructions, how should the songs be sung?\",\"options\":[\"Very loudly\",\"Without looking\",\"With actions\",\"While sitting down\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instruction says \'Listen, learn and sing with actions.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the textbook\'s conversation, what would you say immediately after someone says \'How are you?\'\",\"options\":[\"Hello.\",\"I’m fine, thank you.\",\"This is my friend.\",\"Hi!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text follows \'How are you?\' with \'I’m fine, thank you.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which greeting is used by the characters in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Good morning\",\"Good night\",\"Hello\",\"Welcome\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The characters use \'Hi!\' and \'Hello\' to greet each other.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is NOT one of the four specific actions listed for the songs?\",\"options\":[\"Dance\",\"Sing\",\"Play\",\"Read\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The four actions listed are sing, dance, play, and sway; \'read\' is not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the relationship between Riya and Sonali as described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"They are sisters.\",\"They are friends.\",\"They are teachers.\",\"They are neighbors.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Riya introduces Sonali by saying, \'this is my friend, Sonali.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21635,27,5,'English','en','\'A\' to \'Z\' / We Speak English','[\"The English alphabet has 26 letters from A to Z.\",\"Capital letters are also called uppercase letters.\",\"Small letters are also called lowercase letters.\",\"We write capital letters at the beginning of sentences and for proper nouns.\",\"Small letters are used for most words in a sentence.\",\"Letters can be written in different sizes: big, small, very big, very tiny.\",\"Letters can be written in different styles: plain, fancy shapes.\",\"Writing letters helps improve handwriting and letter recognition.\",\"Practise writing both capital and small letters regularly.\",\"Observe the shape of each letter carefully while writing.\",\"Use plain paper or notebook to practise letter writing.\",\"Say the letter sound as you write it to remember better.\",\"Capital A looks like a triangle with a line in the middle.\",\"Small a is written as a circle with a line on the right.\",\"Practise writing letters in sequence from A to Z and a to z.\"]','[