els\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Write all the small letters in fancy shapes\' as a task.\",\"topic\":\"Writing Small Letters\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the list of example words in the text, which letter\'s example is \'owl\'?\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"e\",\"o\",\"u\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'owl\' as one of the example words for the letters.\",\"topic\":\"Writing Small Letters\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many letters are shown in the bottom-most row?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"6\",\"5\",\"8\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The last row in the image contains 6 letters: u, v, w, x, y, and z.\",\"topic\":\"Writing Small Letters\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/013_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT mentioned as an example in the first paragraph of the text?\",\"options\":[\"apple\",\"elephant\",\"umbrella\",\"orange\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions apple, elephant, ice-cream, owl, and umbrella, but not orange.\",\"topic\":\"Writing Small Letters\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal of the tasks described in section 2 of the text?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to spell \'elephant\'\",\"To improve the skill of writing small letters in various ways\",\"To count the number of letters in the alphabet\",\"To draw pictures of owls and apples\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The tasks focus on different ways to write small letters to build proficiency.\",\"topic\":\"Writing Small Letters\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which type of letters should be written on a single line?\",\"options\":[\"Small letters\",\"Capital letters\",\"Cursive letters\",\"Numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to \'Write all the capital letters on a single line.\'\",\"topic\":\"We Speak English: Dialogues\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"On what kind of paper should the capital letters be written?\",\"options\":[\"Lined paper\",\"Graph paper\",\"Plain paper\",\"Rough paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to \'Write all the capital letters on plain paper.\'\",\"topic\":\"We Speak English: Dialogues\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sizes are suggested for writing the capital letters?\",\"options\":[\"Only medium size\",\"Very big and very tiny\",\"Only very big\",\"Only very tiny\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to write them in different sizes – \'very big and very tiny\'.\",\"topic\":\"We Speak English: Dialogues\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides sizes, in what other way can the capital letters be shaped?\",\"options\":[\"Fancy shapes\",\"Square shapes\",\"Circular shapes\",\"Broken shapes\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text suggests writing all the capital letters in \'fancy shapes\'.\",\"topic\":\"We Speak English: Dialogues\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step mentioned in instruction number 1?\",\"options\":[\"Listen\",\"Read\",\"Look\",\"Dialogue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instruction starts with \'Look, listen, read with me.\'\",\"topic\":\"We Speak English: Dialogues\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"After finding the correct picture for a dialogue, what should you do to the picture?\",\"options\":[\"Color it\",\"Give it the proper number\",\"Draw it again\",\"Cut it out\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'find the proper picture for it and give it the proper number.\'\",\"topic\":\"We Speak English: Dialogues\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student writes the letter \'A\' as a very large letter and the letter \'B\' as a very small letter, which instruction are they following?\",\"options\":[\"Writing on a single line\",\"Writing in fancy shapes\",\"Writing in different sizes\",\"Writing on plain paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Writing very big and very tiny letters refers to the instruction about different sizes.\",\"topic\":\"We Speak English: Dialogues\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which action is NOT part of the first set of three actions in instruction 1?\",\"options\":[\"Look\",\"Listen\",\"Read\",\"Write\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The sequence is \'Look, listen, read\'; \'Write\' is not part of this specific sequence in instruction 1.\",\"topic\":\"We Speak English: Dialogues\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many different ways to write capital letters are listed in the bullet points?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"There are four bullet points: single line, plain paper, different sizes, and fancy shapes.\",\"topic\":\"We Speak English: Dialogues\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the purpose of the activity \'Can you? Yes, you can!\'?\",\"options\":[\"To practice writing capital letters in various ways\",\"To learn how to draw pictures\",\"To count the number of letters\",\"To listen to stories\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The instructions under this heading all relate to different methods of writing capital letters.\",\"topic\":\"We Speak English: Dialogues\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the dialogue, which class is Subhash in?\",\"options\":[\"Class Four\",\"Class Five\",\"Class Six\",\"Class Seven\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Subhash explicitly states, \'I\'m in Class Five.\'\",\"topic\":\"Practise Dialogues\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the nickname of the boy named Shubham?\",\"options\":[\"Subhash\",\"Bunty\",\"Uncle\",\"Aunty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Shubham says, \'You can call me Bunty.\'\",\"topic\":\"Practise Dialogues\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What time is mentioned in the dialogues?\",\"options\":[\"One o\'clock\",\"Two o\'clock\",\"Three o\'clock\",\"Four o\'clock\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'It\'s two o\'clock.\'\",\"topic\":\"Practise Dialogues\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When someone says \'Thank you so much for this lovely gift\', what is the polite response given in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Never mind.\",\"Sure.\",\"You are welcome!\",\"Please wait for me.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the dialogue, the response to the gift thanks is \'You are welcome!\'\",\"topic\":\"Practise Dialogues\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the teacher say when a student asks to come in?\",\"options\":[\"Never mind.\",\"Sure.\",\"Yes. Please come in.\",\"Thank you so much.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher responds with \'Yes. Please come in.\'\",\"topic\":\"Practise Dialogues\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct response to \'I\'m sorry I broke the cup\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"You are welcome!\",\"Never mind.\",\"Sure.\",\"Excuse me.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that when someone apologizes for breaking a cup, the reply is \'Never mind.\'\",\"topic\":\"Practise Dialogues\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to ask an elder for help finding a location, which phrase from the text should you use?\",\"options\":[\"Excuse me, Aunty. Can you please help me find this address?\",\"Excuse me, Uncle. Is this yours?\",\"Where are you going?\",\"Would you like to come with us?\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides this specific dialogue for asking help with an address.\",\"topic\":\"Practise Dialogues\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you accidentally bump into someone and want to be polite like the characters in the text, which word is most appropriate to start your sentence?\",\"options\":[\"Hello\",\"Excuse me\",\"Welcome\",\"Sure\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'Excuse me\' as a polite way to get someone\'s attention.\",\"topic\":\"Practise Dialogues\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where are the characters going when they invite someone to join them?\",\"options\":[\"To the classroom\",\"To the playground\",\"To a birthday party\",\"To find an address\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The dialogue states, \'We are going to the playground.\'\",\"topic\":\"Practise Dialogues\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the introductions, what is the age relationship between Subhash and Shubham?\",\"options\":[\"Subhash is older than Shubham.\",\"They are in the same class.\",\"Shubham is in a higher class than Subhash.\",\"Subhash is in Class Seven.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Subhash is in Class Five and Shubham is in Class Seven, making Shubham the student in the higher class.\",\"topic\":\"Practise Dialogues\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is used to greet someone?\",\"options\":[\"Hello\",\"Excuse me\",\"Please\",\"Thank you\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Hello\' is the standard greeting mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When you receive help from someone, what should you say according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"I am sorry\",\"Thank you\",\"Excuse me\",\"Never mind\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Thank you\' is the polite expression for showing gratitude.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to get someone\'s attention politely, which phrase should you use?\",\"options\":[\"Hello\",\"Please\",\"Excuse me\",\"Never mind\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Excuse me\' is used to politely interrupt or get attention.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct response when someone says \'I am sorry\' for a small mistake?\",\"options\":[\"Please\",\"Thank you\",\"Never mind\",\"Hello\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Never mind\' is used to tell someone not to worry about a mistake.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used to make a request polite?\",\"options\":[\"Please\",\"Hello\",\"Excuse me\",\"I am sorry\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Please\' is the standard word for making polite requests.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you accidentally step on someone\'s foot, what is the best thing to say?\",\"options\":[\"Thank you\",\"I am sorry\",\"Never mind\",\"Excuse me\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'I am sorry\' is used to apologize for a mistake or accident.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a common way to start a conversation with a friend?\",\"options\":[\"Thank you\",\"Hello\",\"Never mind\",\"I am sorry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Hello\' is used to begin a conversation.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When you want to move past someone in a crowded place, you should say:\",\"options\":[\"Please\",\"Thank you\",\"Excuse me\",\"Never mind\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Excuse me\' is the polite way to ask someone to let you pass.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which phrase is most likely used to dismiss a small concern?\",\"options\":[\"Hello\",\"Thank you\",\"Never mind\",\"Please\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Never mind\' indicates that something is not important or shouldn\'t be worried about.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase from the text is used to show appreciation?\",\"options\":[\"Excuse me\",\"Thank you\",\"Hello\",\"I am sorry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Thank you\' expresses appreciation for something done.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21636,27,5,'English','en','Number Work / B-I-N-G-O','[\"Numbers can be written in words or digits.\",\"Place value helps us understand the value of each digit in a number.\",\"In a two-digit number, the left digit is the tens place and the right digit is the ones place.\",\"Example: In 24, 2 is in the tens place (value 20) and 4 is in the ones place (value 4).\",\"We can compare numbers using greater than (>), less than (<), or equal to (=).\",\"To add numbers, we add the ones place first, then the tens place.\",\"Example: 23 + 15 = (20+10) + (3+5) = 30 + 8 = 38.\",\"Subtraction is done similarly: subtract ones from ones, tens from tens.\",\"Example: 42 - 17 = (40-10) + (2-7) = 30 + (-5) = 25 (after borrowing).\",\"Borrowing is used when the top digit in a place is smaller than the bottom digit.\",\"We can estimate sums and differences by rounding numbers to the nearest ten.\",\"Patterns in numbers help us predict what comes next in a sequence.\",\"Even numbers end with 0, 2, 4, 6, or 8; odd numbers end with 1, 3, 5, 7, or 9.\",\"Zero is an even number and is neither positive nor negative.\",\"Number lines help us visualize addition, subtraction, and number order.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did the Queen find while taking a walk in her garden?\",\"options\":[\"A necklace of pearls\",\"Three big diamonds\",\"A big, beautiful golden feather\",\"Ninety-nine gold coins\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Queen found a big, beautiful golden feather in her garden.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who was the first person the Queen met after finding the feather?\",\"options\":[\"A little man\",\"An old woman\",\"The King\",\"The little prince\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the story, after finding the feather, she first met a little man.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the little man offer the Queen in exchange for the feather?\",\"options\":[\"Twenty-one pearls\",\"Three big diamonds\",\"Ninety-nine gold coins\",\"A bright crown\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The little man said he would give the Queen three big diamonds for the feather.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many pearls were in the necklace offered by the old woman?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"12\",\"21\",\"99\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The old woman offered a necklace of twenty-one pearls.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the Queen had accepted the King\'s offer, how many gold coins would she have received?\",\"options\":[\"9\",\"19\",\"90\",\"99\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The King offered ninety-nine gold coins for the feather.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which number mentioned in the story is the largest?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Twenty-one\",\"Ninety-nine\",\"One\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The numbers mentioned are 1, 3, 21, and 99; 99 is the largest.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the Queen say \'Sorry!\' to the little man, the old woman, and the King?\",\"options\":[\"She did not like their gifts\",\"She wanted to keep the feather for the prince\",\"She had lost the feather\",\"She was in a hurry to go home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Queen refused all valuable offers but immediately gave the feather to the prince, showing she valued his happiness more.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To whom did the Queen finally give the golden feather?\",\"options\":[\"The little man\",\"The old woman\",\"The King\",\"The little prince\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The Queen gave the feather to the little prince and told him to keep it safe.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What adjective did the little prince use to describe the feather that the others did not use?\",\"options\":[\"Golden\",\"Beautiful\",\"Bright\",\"Big\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The little prince exclaimed, \'What a bright beautiful feather!\'\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the Queen when she found the golden feather?\",\"options\":[\"In the palace\",\"In her garden\",\"In the market\",\"In the forest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the Queen was taking a walk in her garden.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the Queen doing when she finds the feather?\",\"options\":[\"She is running away\",\"She is bending down to look at the feather\",\"She is talking to the King\",\"She is wearing a necklace\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the Queen bending down towards the golden feather on the grass.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/016_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, which of these best describes the feather\'s appearance on the ground?\",\"options\":[\"It is dull and brown\",\"It is small and hidden\",\"It is glowing or shining\",\"It is broken into pieces\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The drawing shows lines around the feather indicating it is shining or glowing.\",\"topic\":\"The Golden Feather\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/016_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the table, what is the word for the number 11?\",\"options\":[\"ten\",\"eleven\",\"twelve\",\"thirteen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table explicitly lists \'eleven\' as the word for the number 11.\",\"topic\":\"Numbers 1 to 100\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many days are there in a week according to the example sentences?\",\"options\":[\"six\",\"seven\",\"eight\",\"nine\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'There are seven days in a week.\'\",\"topic\":\"Numbers 1 to 100\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the word for the number 100 in the table?\",\"options\":[\"ninety\",\"ten\",\"thousand\",\"hundred\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The last cell in the table lists the 