n each successive line.\",\"topic\":\"Vanishing Sentences\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the teacher use the sentence about the fox and the dog for this specific activity?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is about animals.\",\"Because it is easy to draw.\",\"Because it contains every letter of the alphabet for practice.\",\"Because it is a very short sentence.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text highlights that this sentence contains all English letters, making it a comprehensive tool for reading practice.\",\"topic\":\"Vanishing Sentences\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the sequence: \'The quick brown fox jumps\', \'The quick brown fox\', \'The quick brown\', what will the next line be?\",\"options\":[\"The quick\",\"The quick brown fox\",\"The quick brown fox jumps over\",\"The\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Following the pattern of erasing the last word, \'brown\' would be removed next, leaving \'The quick\'.\",\"topic\":\"Vanishing Sentences\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21637,27,5,'English','en','Talking about Things','[\"1. Numbers 1 to 100 can be written in words, e.g., 21 is \\\"twenty one\\\".\",\"2. A sentence about a number can describe its size, e.g., \\\"Twenty five is a small number.\\\"\",\"3. There are seven days in a week and thirty days in a month like January.\",\"4. A year has 365 days, a leap year has 366 days.\",\"5. A spider has eight legs, a dog has four legs.\",\"6. The quick brown fox jumps over a lazy dog is a pangram that uses every letter of the alphabet.\",\"7. Numbers can be grouped: 100, 200, 300, etc., and we can talk about hundreds, thousands, millions.\",\"8. Sentences can use adjectives to describe objects: big, small, red, shiny, etc.\",\"9. We can form sentences like \\\"My mother bought a table for five thousand rupees.\\\"\",\"10. A table of numbers from 1 to 100 helps us see patterns in tens and ones.\",\"11. We can make sentences about larger numbers: \\\"There are three hundred and sixty‑five days in a year.\\\"\",\"12. We can use adjectives to describe people: young, old, strong, weak.\",\"13. We can use adjectives to describe food: sweet, sour, salty, crunchy, juicy.\",\"14. We can use adjectives to describe objects: shiny, dull, bright, dark.\",\"15. We can use adjectives to describe feelings: happy, sad, angry, excited.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the \'Useful Words\' list describes a color?\",\"options\":[\"tall\",\"violet\",\"thick\",\"ripe\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'violet\' is listed among the colors in the textbook text.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Words\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list is used to describe the taste of something?\",\"options\":[\"shiny\",\"sweet\",\"dark\",\"new\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'sweet\' is a taste descriptor included in the useful words list.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Words\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the list describes the size of an object?\",\"options\":[\"small\",\"pink\",\"raw\",\"soft\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Small\' is a word used to describe the size of a thing.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Words\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the example \'a big red sweet apple\', which word describes the color of the apple?\",\"options\":[\"big\",\"red\",\"sweet\",\"apple\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the phrase, \'red\' is the word that tells us the color of the apple.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Words\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list would you use to describe a fruit that is ready to be eaten?\",\"options\":[\"raw\",\"ripe\",\"hard\",\"new\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'ripe\' describes a fruit that is fully developed and ready to eat.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Words\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list is the opposite of \'old\' when describing a person?\",\"options\":[\"new\",\"young\",\"short\",\"thin\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'young\' is used for people, while \'new\' is usually used for objects.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Words\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to describe a clean mirror that reflects light well, which word from the list is most suitable?\",\"options\":[\"dirty\",\"shiny\",\"raw\",\"fat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Shiny\' describes something that reflects light or is very clean and bright.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Words\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To describe an orange that has a lot of liquid inside, which word from the list should you use?\",\"options\":[\"crunchy\",\"juicy\",\"hard\",\"thick\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Juicy\' is the correct word to describe something full of juice.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Words\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Look at the words: \'pink, yellow, golden, blue\'. What category do all these words belong to?\",\"options\":[\"Size\",\"Taste\",\"Colors\",\"Shapes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"All these words are names of colors provided in the useful words list.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Words\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the example phrase \'a big red sweet apple\', how many describing words (adjectives) are used before the name of the object?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The three describing words used are \'big\', \'red\', and \'sweet\'.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Words\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what kind of tree is mentioned in the sample phrases?\",\"options\":[\"a short tree\",\"a tall tree\",\"a green tree\",\"a big tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'a tall tree\' as a sample phrase.\",\"topic\":\"Sample Phrases\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used to describe the fish in the examples provided?\",\"options\":[\"thin\",\"small\",\"fat\",\"blue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses the phrase \'a fat fish\' as an example.\",\"topic\":\"Sample Phrases\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phrases from the text uses the word \'an\' correctly?\",\"options\":[\"an tall tree\",\"an fat fish\",\"an old man\",\"an shiny star\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically provides \'an old man\' as the correct example using \'an\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sample Phrases\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'a shiny star\', which word is being described?\",\"options\":[\"tree\",\"man\",\"fish\",\"star\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The word \'shiny\' is used as a descriptor for the noun \'star\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sample Phrases\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the game mentioned in the text, if Student A says \'Umbrella\', what does Student B say?\",\"options\":[\"Dry\",\"Wet\",\"Red\",\"Big\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the example \'A : Umbrella. B : Wet.\' for the game.\",\"topic\":\"Sample Phrases\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the teacher\'s instructions, which of these is a correct phrase to say in class?\",\"options\":[\"a old man\",\"an tall tree\",\"a shiny star\",\"an fat fish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'a shiny star\' as a correct sample phrase.\",\"topic\":\"Sample Phrases\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the teacher instructed to check when children are saying phrases?\",\"options\":[\"If they are speaking loudly\",\"If they use a\\/an correctly\",\"If they know the spelling\",\"If they can draw the pictures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher\'s instructions state to see if children use \'a\\/an\' correctly while saying phrases.\",\"topic\":\"Sample Phrases\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the game example, if \'Umbrella\' is the name of the picture, what does the word \'Wet\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"The name of another picture\",\"A word about the picture\",\"A question about the picture\",\"A greeting to the teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions say one student names the picture and the other says a word about it.\",\"topic\":\"Sample Phrases\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used to describe the man in the text?\",\"options\":[\"young\",\"old\",\"tall\",\"fat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the phrase \'an old man\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sample Phrases\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific descriptor is paired with \'star\' in the sample list?\",\"options\":[\"bright\",\"shiny\",\"twinkling\",\"night\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'a shiny star\' as one of the four sample phrases.\",\"topic\":\"Sample Phrases\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21638,27,5,'English','en','Sentence Race / Action Time','[\"Sentences can be statements, questions, commands, or exclamations.\",\"A sentence must have a subject and a predicate to be complete.\",\"Subject tells who or what the sentence is about.\",\"Predicate tells what the subject does or is.\",\"Use capital letter at the beginning and a full stop, question mark, or exclamation mark at the end.\",\"Questions often begin with words like who, what, where, when, why, how, or auxiliary verbs like is, am, are, do, does.\",\"To form a question, we often invert the subject and verb (e.g., \'She is\' → \'Is she?\').\",\"Fill-in-the-blank questions test understanding of sentence structure and vocabulary.\",\"Meaningful sentences make clear sense and follow grammar rules.\",\"Practicing sentence formation helps improve speaking and writing skills.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many race tracks are provided in the \'Sentence Race\' activity?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'Three race tracks are given below.\'\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Race\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the time limit given to complete a set of sentences in each track?\",\"options\":[\"One hour\",\"One minute\",\"Ten minutes\",\"Five minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions say to try to complete the set \'within one minute\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Race\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the rules, what must you use in every sentence you write?\",\"options\":[\"The same word\",\"A new word or words\",\"Only numbers\",\"No words\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'You have to use a new word\\/words in each sentence.\'\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Race\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who is declared the winner of the Sentence Race?\",\"options\":[\"The one who writes the longest sentence\",\"The first one to complete a set correctly\",\"The one who uses the most difficult words\",\"The one who draws the best picture\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The first one to complete a set correctly is the winner.\'\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Race\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which track requires you to use the words \'have\' and \'has\'?\",\"options\":[\"The first track\",\"The second track\",\"The third track\",\"All tracks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The third track listed in the text contains starters like \'I have\', \'He has\', etc.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Race\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the second track, which word follows the pronoun \'She\'?\",\"options\":[\"like\",\"likes\",\"liking\",\"liked\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text for the second track lists \'She likes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Race\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are completing the first track, which word is already provided to follow the pronoun \'They\'?\",\"options\":[\"is\",\"am\",\"are\",\"was\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first track ends with the starter \'They are\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Race\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific word is used with \'He\', \'She\', and \'It\' in the third track?\",\"options\":[\"have\",\"has\",\"am\",\"are\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'He has\', \'She has\', and \'It has\' for the third track.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Race\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many sentence starters are listed in each individual track?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"6\",\"7\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Counting the bullet points in any track in the figure (I, You, We, He, She, It, They) gives a total of 7.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Race\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/020_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which pronoun is used to start the very first sentence of every track?\",\"options\":[\"You\",\"We\",\"I\",\"They\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Looking at the top of all three tracks in the figure, each one begins with the pronoun \'I\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Race\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/020_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what kind of hair does the sister have?\",\"options\":[\"Straight hair\",\"Curly hair\",\"Short hair\",\"Black hair\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'She has curly hair.\'\",\"topic\":\"Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which action is associated with \'It\' in the provided examples?\",\"options\":[\"Singing\",\"Running\",\"Hopping\",\"Eating\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses the example \'It is hopping.\'\",\"topic\":\"Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the person doing in the example \'I am...\'?\",\"options\":[\"Dancing\",\"Singing\",\"Playing\",\"Reading\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the example \'I am singing.\'\",\"topic\":\"Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of completing the sentences in each box?\",\"options\":[\"To make meaningful questions\",\"To write a long story\",\"To draw pictures\",\"To memorize words\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Complete the sentences in each box to make meaningful questions.\'\",\"topic\":\"Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sentences from the text describes the weather?\",\"options\":[\"I am happy.\",\"It is big.\",\"It is raining.\",\"She has curly hair.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'It is raining\' is the sentence that refers to weather conditions.\",\"topic\":\"Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used in the text to describe a feeling or state of mind?\",\"options\":[\"Big\",\"Happy\",\"Hopping\",\"Singing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'I am happy\' to show a state of being or feeling.\",\"topic\":\"Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you follow instruction (b) in the text, what will you do with the words in each set?\",\"options\":[\"Write them down\",\"Read them aloud\",\"Translate them\",\"Color them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Instruction (b) says, \'Read aloud the words in each set.\'\",\"topic\":\"Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which word correctly completes the sentence: \'She ___ curly hair\'?\",\"options\":[\"is\",\"am\",\"have\",\"has\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text uses the specific phrase \'She has curly hair.\'\",\"topic\":\"Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'It is big\', what does the word \'big\' describe?\",\"options\":[\"An action\",\"A person\'s name\",\"The size of \'It\'\",\"A question\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the context of \'It is big\', \'big\' is an adjective describing size.\",\"topic\":\"Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instructions, what is the very first thing you should do with this game?\",\"options\":[\"Play\",\"Practise\",\"Learn\",\"Read aloud\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sequence given in the text is \'Learn, practise and play this game.\'\",\"topic\":\"Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is listed under the category of \'birds\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"squirrel\",\"crane\",\"cat\",\"kite\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'crane\' as one of the birds.\",\"topic\":\"Question Frames\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which of these is a vehicle?\",\"options\":[\"aeroplane\",\"balloon\",\"tricycle\",\"sparrow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text categorizes \'aeroplane\' under vehicles.\",\"topic\":\"Question Frames\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the question frames provided, which word follows \'Has\'?\",\"options\":[\"I\",\"we\",\"she\",\"they\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Has she got?\' as a correct question frame.\",\"topic\":\"Question Frames\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which helping verb is used with \'it\' in the \'Do\\/Does\' question frames?\",\"options\":[\"Do\",\"Does\",\"Am\",\"Have\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'Does it\' as the correct frame for the subject \'it\'.\",\"topic\":\"Question Frames\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are pretending to be a parrot, which question frame would you use to ask about your color?\",\"options\":[\"Do I green?\",\"Am I green?\",\"Have I green?\",\"Has I green?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'Am I (green)?\' as the standard question frame for self-description.\",\"topic\":\"Question Frames\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To ask if a motorcar has wheels using the frames, which is correct?\",\"options\":[\"Has it got (wheels)?\",\"Have it got (wheels)?\",\"Do it (wheels)?\",\"Is it got (wheels)?\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Has it got?\' as the correct frame for a singular object like a motorcar.\",\"topic\":\"Question Frames\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In which category does the text place the \'tricycle\'?\",\"options\":[\"vehicles\",\"birds\",\"toys\",\"animals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically lists \'tricycle\' under the \'toys\' category.\",\"topic\":\"Question Frames\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the question frames, which pair is grammatically matched?\",\"options\":[\"Do - she\",\"Does - they\",\"Do - you\",\"Does - I\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Do you?\' as a correct question frame.\",\"topic\":\"Question Frames\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a correct question frame for the subject \'they\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Has they got?\",\"Are they?\",\"Does they?\",\"Is they?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'Are they?\' as a valid question frame.\",\"topic\":\"Question Frames\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT listed in the \'animals\' category?\",\"options\":[\"mouse\",\"elephant\",\"owl\",\"dog\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The owl is listed under \'birds\', not \'animals\', in the text provided.\",\"topic\":\"Question Frames\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21639,27,5,'English','en','Words We Know / Say \'Yes\' or \'No\'!','[\"Prepositions show the position of a person or thing: in, on, under, near, in front of, behind.\",\"\'In\' means inside something.\",\"\'On\' means on top of something.\",\"\'Under\' means below something.\",\"\'Near\' means close to something.\",\"\'In front of\' means before something.\",\"\'Behind\' means at the back of something.\",\"Commands are words that tell someone to do something: Sit, Stand, Walk, Run, etc.\",\"Adverbs tell how an action is done: quickly, slowly, loudly, softly.\",\"Direction words show where to go: left, right, around, up, down.\",\"Action words (verbs) show what someone does: laugh, speak, clap, tap, look, point.\",\"We can make sentences using prepositions: The mouse is in the hat.\",\"We can make sentences using commands: Stand up. Sit down.\",\"We can make sentences using adverbs: He runs fast. She speaks softly.\",\"We can name objects and say what we can do with them: An apple – we can eat it, wash it, peel it.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, where is the mouse located?\",\"options\":[\"On the hat\",\"Under the hat\",\"In the hat\",\"Near the hat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'There is a mouse in the hat.\'\",\"topic\":\"Talking about Things – 2\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is NOT mentioned in the list of position words in the text?\",\"options\":[\"under\",\"between\",\"behind\",\"near\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'in, on, under, near, in front of, behind\'; it does not mention \'between\'.\",\"topic\":\"Talking about Things – 2\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many sentences is a student expected to frame for each position word?\",\"options\":[\"At least one\",\"At least two\",\"At least three\",\"Exactly five\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'frame at least three sentences for each of these words.\'\",\"topic\":\"Talking about Things – 2\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the correct phrase to describe the position of the apples?\",\"options\":[\"Apples on the basket\",\"Apples in the basket\",\"Apples under the basket\",\"Apples behind the basket\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The apples are placed inside the container shown in the picture.\",\"topic\":\"Talking about Things – 2\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/022_108.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where is the cow resting?\",\"options\":[\"On the tree\",\"In the tree\",\"Under the tree\",\"Behind the tree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The drawing shows the cow sitting on the ground beneath the branches of the tree.\",\"topic\":\"Talking about Things – 2\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/022_109.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word best describes the position of the sun relative to the mountains?\",\"options\":[\"in front of\",\"under\",\"on\",\"behind\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The sun is partially hidden by the mountains, indicating it is at the back.\",\"topic\":\"Talking about Things – 2\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/022_109.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a student says \'a cow under the tree\' instead of a full sentence, what does the teacher\'s note suggest?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher should correct the grammar immediately.\",\"The teacher should accept it if it is correct.\",\"The teacher should ask the student to sit down.\",\"The teacher should tell the student it is wrong.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Marathi note states that if children say phrases, they should be accepted if they are correct.\",\"topic\":\"Talking about Things – 2\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which preposition from the text would you use to describe a fish\'s position in the \'fish tank\' mentioned in the activity?\",\"options\":[\"on\",\"under\",\"in\",\"behind\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Fish live inside the water of a tank, so \'in\' is the appropriate preposition.\",\"topic\":\"Talking about Things – 2\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The text mentions \'spectacles\'. Which word from the list best describes their position when worn on the face?\",\"options\":[\"under\",\"on\",\"behind\",\"in\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Spectacles are worn \'on\' the nose\\/eyes.\",\"topic\":\"Talking about Things – 2\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the activity described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to draw animals\",\"To practice using words that describe position\",\"To count the number of objects in a hat\",\"To learn the names of different vegetables\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity focuses on framing sentences using position words like \'in\', \'on\', and \'under\'.\",\"topic\":\"Talking about Things – 2\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is found in list \'A\'?\",\"options\":[\"up\",\"fast\",\"Smile\",\"slowly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Smile is one of the action words listed in group A.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from list \'B\' tells us about a direction?\",\"options\":[\"right\",\"Run\",\"Walk\",\"Sing\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Right\' is a direction word found in list B.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instructions, what should the students do after the leaders give a command?\",\"options\":[\"Write the words\",\"Act according to the command\",\"Draw a picture\",\"Close their eyes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Listen carefully to the leaders... and act\'.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a meaningful command formed by joining a word from \'A\' and \'B\'?\",\"options\":[\"Speak loudly\",\"Sit fast\",\"Sing your feet\",\"Laugh to the board\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Speak\' (from A) and \'loudly\' (from B) make a meaningful command.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want someone to move their body towards the ground, which command from the lists would you use?\",\"options\":[\"Stand up\",\"Bend down\",\"Walk around\",\"Look in\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Bend\' is in list A and \'down\' is in list B, forming a logical command for moving towards the ground.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase from list \'B\' can be correctly used with the action \'Clap\' from list \'A\'?\",\"options\":[\"your feet\",\"to the board\",\"your hands\",\"around\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Clap your hands\' is a common and meaningful command using words from both lists.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the pair of opposite words found in list \'B\'.\",\"options\":[\"fast and loudly\",\"left and around\",\"in and out\",\"softly and your feet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'In\' and \'out\' are opposites both present in list B.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which action from list \'A\' involves using your eyes to see something?\",\"options\":[\"Tap\",\"Look\",\"Speak\",\"Clap\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Look\' is the action word in list A that refers to using one\'s sight.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word is written to the right of \'Walk\'?\",\"options\":[\"Run\",\"Stand\",\"Turn\",\"Sing\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the table for list A, \'Run\' is placed to the right of \'Walk\'.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/023_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which phrase is located in the bottom right corner?\",\"options\":[\"to the board\",\"your hands\",\"at the door\",\"around\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the table for list B, \'at the door\' is the last phrase in the bottom right corner.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/023_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these commands CANNOT be made using only the words provided in lists \'A\' and \'B\'?\",\"options\":[\"Sit down\",\"Walk slowly\",\"Jump quickly\",\"Stand up\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'Jump\' is not present in list A.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How many total action words are listed in table \'A\'?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"14\",\"16\",\"18\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"There are 4 rows and 4 columns of words in table A, totaling 16 words.\",\"topic\":\"Action Time\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following objects is mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A pencil\",\"A bottle\",\"A table\",\"A bag\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'a bottle\' as one of the objects.\",\"topic\":\"Words We Know\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what can we do with an apple?\",\"options\":[\"Read it\",\"Write it\",\"Peel it\",\"Sleep it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Peel it\' as one of the actions we can do with an apple.\",\"topic\":\"Words We Know\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many objects are listed at the beginning of the text to name and talk about?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists five objects: an apple, a bottle, cloth, a sheet of paper, and flowers.\",\"topic\":\"Words We Know\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to divide an apple into thin pieces, which action from the text should you use?\",\"options\":[\"Slice it\",\"Buy it\",\"Catch it\",\"Wash it\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Slice it\' is the specific action mentioned for dividing the apple into pieces.\",\"topic\":\"Words We Know\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which action mentioned in the text involves getting an apple from a shop by giving money?\",\"options\":[\"Sell it\",\"Buy it\",\"Throw it\",\"Drop it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Buy it\' is the action of acquiring the apple, as listed in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Words We Know\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the word from the sight word table that is used to ask about a place.\",\"options\":[\"who\",\"where\",\"what\",\"when\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Where\' is in the table and is the word used to ask about location.\",\"topic\":\"Words We Know\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is NOT found in the sight word table provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"without\",\"every\",\"always\",\"their\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Always\' is not present in the provided table of words.\",\"topic\":\"Words We Know\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are preparing a meal with an apple, which action from the text would you perform?\",\"options\":[\"Cook it\",\"Catch it\",\"Throw it\",\"Drop it\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Cook it\' is the action related to food preparation mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Words We Know\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sight word table, which word starts with the letter \'u\'?\",\"options\":[\"up\",\"us\",\"under\",\"until\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Us\' is the only word in the table starting with \'u\'.\",\"topic\":\"Words We Know\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The text mentions \'a sheet of\' which material?\",\"options\":[\"cloth\",\"paper\",\"glass\",\"wood\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions \'a sheet of paper\'.\",\"topic\":\"Words We Know\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21640,27,5,'English','en','Cuckoo','[\"The poem \'Cuckoo\' describes what the cuckoo bird does each month from April to August.\",\"In April, the cuckoo poem, the bird opens its bill in April.\",\"In May, the cuckoo sings all day.\",\"In June, the cuckoo changes its tune.\",\"In July, the cuckoo flies away.\",\"In August, the cuckoo says \'Go, go I must\'.\",\"The poem uses simple rhyming words to make it musical and easy to remember.\",\"Rhyming words in the poem include: do-you, bill-May, tune-June, fly-July, must-August (approximate rhymes).\",\"The poem helps students learn the names of months and seasonal activities.\",\"Students are asked to find rhyming words in the poem as an exercise.\",\"Students are asked to tick the months mentioned in the poem from a list.\",\"Students are asked to copy the month names and write them in Marathi.\",\"The Little Red Hen story teaches the value of hard work and helping others.\",\"The Little Red Hen finds wheat grains and asks others to help sow, cut, and thresh the wheat.\",\"The duck, cat, and dog all refuse to help at each stage.\",\"The Little Red Hen does all the work herself: sowing, cutting, and threshing the wheat.\",\"The story shows that those who do not work should not expect to enjoy the results.\",\"The story is used to teach moral lessons about responsibility and teamwork.\",\"Students practice reading aloud and listening carefully in the Little Red Hen lesson.\",\"Key vocabulary includes: sow, cut, thresh, wheat, grains, farm, hen, duck, cat, dog.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which month does the cuckoo open its bill?\",\"options\":[\"April\",\"May\",\"June\",\"July\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'In April I open my bill\'.\",\"topic\":\"Months in the poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the cuckoo do throughout the day in May?\",\"options\":[\"Flies away\",\"Changes tune\",\"Sings all day\",\"Goes away\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'In May I sing all day\'.\",\"topic\":\"Months in the poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what happens in the month of June?\",\"options\":[\"The cuckoo opens its bill\",\"The cuckoo changes its tune\",\"The cuckoo flies away\",\"The cuckoo sings all day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'In June I change my tune\'.\",\"topic\":\"Months in the poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which month does the cuckoo fly away?\",\"options\":[\"April\",\"June\",\"July\",\"August\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'In July Away I fly\'.\",\"topic\":\"Months in the poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word rhymes with the month \'July\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Day\",\"Tune\",\"Fly\",\"Must\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the poem, \'July\' rhymes with \'fly\'.\",\"topic\":\"Months in the poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a cuckoo is changing its tune, which month is it most likely to be according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"May\",\"June\",\"July\",\"August\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links the action of changing the tune specifically to the month of June.\",\"topic\":\"Months in the poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these months is NOT mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"April\",\"May\",\"June\",\"September\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem only mentions April, May, June, July, and August.\",\"topic\":\"Months in the poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final month mentioned in the poem before the cuckoo says it \'must go\'?\",\"options\":[\"June\",\"July\",\"August\",\"May\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"August is the last month mentioned in the sequence of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"Months in the poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, which month represents the time the cuckoo spends the most time singing?\",\"options\":[\"April\",\"May\",\"June\",\"July\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'In May I sing all day\', implying continuous singing.\",\"topic\":\"Months in the poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'bill\' refer to in the context of the cuckoo in April?\",\"options\":[\"A piece of paper\",\"The bird\'s beak\",\"Money to pay\",\"A type of song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the context of a bird \'opening\' it to sing or act, \'bill\' refers to its beak.\",\"topic\":\"Months in the poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21641,27,5,'English','en','The Little Red Hen','[\"The Little Red Hen is a story about hard work and responsibility.\",\"The hen finds wheat seeds and decides to plant them.\",\"She asks the duck, cat, and dog for help, but they all refuse.\",\"She does all the work herself: planting, cutting, threshing, grinding, and baking.\",\"When the bread is ready, the duck, cat, and dog want to eat it.\",\"The hen refuses to share because they did not help.\",\"She eats the bread with her chicks instead.\",\"The story teaches that those who do not work should not expect to enjoy the results.\",\"It highlights the values of self-reliance and perseverance.\",\"The hen’s chicks benefit from her hard work.\",\"The animals who refused to work learn a lesson about fairness.\",\"The story is often used to teach moral lessons in early education.\",\"Key characters: Little Red Hen, duck, cat, dog, and her chicks.\",\"Sequence of events: planting → growing → harvesting → threshing → grinding → baking → eating.\",\"The hen says \'I will\' each time others say \'Not I\'.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did the Little Red Hen live according to the story?\",\"options\":[\"In a forest\",\"On a farm\",\"In a house\",\"Near a river\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'A little red hen lived on a farm...\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which animals lived with the Little Red Hen?\",\"options\":[\"A cat, a dog and a duck\",\"A cow, a goat and a pig\",\"A cat, a dog and a horse\",\"A duck, a chick and a cat\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she lived with a cat, a dog and a duck.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the cat doing while the hen looks at the grains of wheat?\",\"options\":[\"Helping the hen\",\"Sleeping on the grass\",\"Relaxing in a chair with a drink\",\"Chasing the duck\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the cat sitting in a blue chair, holding a glass with a straw.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/026_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What did the Little Red Hen find one day?\",\"options\":[\"A loaf of bread\",\"A few grains of wheat\",\"A bag of flour\",\"Some tall wheat plants\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'One day, she found a few grains of wheat.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the first task the hen asked for help with?\",\"options\":[\"Cutting the wheat\",\"Grinding the wheat\",\"Sowing the wheat\",\"Baking the bread\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first question she asked was, \'Who will sow the wheat?\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the wheat after it was sowed?\",\"options\":[\"It turned into flour\",\"It was eaten by the duck\",\"It grew tall with ears full of grain\",\"It was baked into bread\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'After some time, the wheat grew tall with ears full of grain.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the hen using to turn the wheat into flour?\",\"options\":[\"A large oven\",\"A grinding stone\",\"A sharp knife\",\"A wooden spoon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the hen using a traditional manual grinding stone to grind the wheat.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/027_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct order of the work done by the hen?\",\"options\":[\"Sow, Cut, Thresh, Grind, Bake\",\"Bake, Grind, Thresh, Cut, Sow\",\"Sow, Thresh, Grind, Cut, Bake\",\"Cut, Sow, Grind, Bake, Thresh\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The story follows the sequence: sow, cut, thresh, grind, and then bake.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What did the wheat become after it was ground?\",\"options\":[\"Dough\",\"Bread\",\"Flour\",\"Grains\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'When the wheat was ground into flour...\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what has the hen just taken out of the oven?\",\"options\":[\"A bowl of grains\",\"A bag of flour\",\"A lovely loaf of bread\",\"A plate of seeds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the hen holding a steaming loaf of bread on a spatula near an oven.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/027_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the duck, cat, and dog say \'Oh! I will\' at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"They wanted to help bake\",\"They wanted to eat the bread\",\"They wanted to sow more wheat\",\"They wanted to play with the chicks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They only offered to help when the hen asked \'Who will eat the bread?\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who did the Little Red Hen share the bread with?\",\"options\":[\"The duck and the cat\",\"The dog and the duck\",\"Her chicks\",\"No one\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'she called her chicks and they all ate up the lovely loaf of bread.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the character of the Little Red Hen?\",\"options\":[\"Lazy\",\"Hardworking\",\"Selfish\",\"Angry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The hen did all the work of sowing, cutting, threshing, grinding, and baking by herself.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'Not I\' repeated by the animals show about them?\",\"options\":[\"They were very busy\",\"They did not know how to work\",\"They were unwilling to help\",\"They were afraid of the hen\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Every time the hen asked for help with a chore, they refused by saying \'Not I\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, what is the result of not helping with the work?\",\"options\":[\"You get to eat the bread later\",\"The hen does the work for you and shares\",\"You do not get to share the final reward\",\"The work never gets finished\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Because the animals did not help, the hen said \'Oh, no, you won’t!\' when they wanted to eat.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Red Hen\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does Mr Clean dislike?\",\"options\":[\"The color of the bucket\",\"The scribbling on the wall\",\"The birds in the sky\",\"Entering the house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that Mr Clean does not like the scribbling on the wall.\",\"topic\":\"What will happen?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Mr Clean holding in his hand to fix the problem on the wall?\",\"options\":[\"A paintbrush\",\"A piece of chalk\",\"A wet cloth\",\"A hammer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows Mr Clean holding a cloth and a bucket to clean the scribbles.\",\"topic\":\"What will happen?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/028_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the most likely action the man will take to enter the house?\",\"options\":[\"He will ring the bell or knock on the door\",\"He will climb through the window\",\"He will water the plant\",\"He will open his briefcase and wait\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Based on his name \'Mr Knocker\' and the situation, he will likely knock or use the bell shown on the wall.\",\"topic\":\"What will happen?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/028_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what does Manisha\'s expression and posture suggest she will do next?\",\"options\":[\"She will go to the playground to run\",\"She will look for something to eat\",\"She will start doing her homework\",\"She will put on her school bag\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says she is hungry and the picture shows her holding her stomach, implying she needs food.\",\"topic\":\"What will happen?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/028_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the person that wants to enter the house?\",\"options\":[\"Mr Clean\",\"Sheru\",\"Mr Knocker\",\"Dolly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Mr Knocker wants to enter this house.\'\",\"topic\":\"What will happen?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If Manisha is thirsty, what is the most appropriate action for her to take?\",\"options\":[\"She will eat a sandwich\",\"She will drink some water\",\"She will go to sleep\",\"She will play with her friends\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Thirst is satisfied by drinking liquids like water.\",\"topic\":\"What will happen?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Dolly falls and hurts her knee. What is the kindest thing her friends will do?\",\"options\":[\"They will continue playing without her\",\"They will help her and take care of her\",\"They will run away from the spot\",\"They will start laughing at her\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Helping a friend who is hurt is the logical and expected social response.\",\"topic\":\"What will happen?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the status of Mr and Mrs Engineer while Sheru wants to play?\",\"options\":[\"They are sleeping\",\"They are busy\",\"They are playing with Sheru\",\"They are out of the house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Mr and Mrs Engineer are busy.\'\",\"topic\":\"What will happen?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why might Sheru not be able to play with the Engineers right now?\",\"options\":[\"Because he is too tired to move\",\"Because they have work to finish\",\"Because the wall is dirty\",\"Because Manisha is hungry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since they are described as \'busy\', it implies they have work or tasks to complete.\",\"topic\":\"What will happen?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the descriptions provided, which character is most concerned with cleanliness?\",\"options\":[\"Mr Knocker\",\"Manisha\",\"Mr Clean\",\"Sheru\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mr Clean\'s name and his dislike for scribbling on walls show he values cleanliness.\",\"topic\":\"What will happen?\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What did the person find in the song \'Just now!\'?\",\"options\":[\"A mango\",\"A peanut\",\"A coin\",\"A seed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The song explicitly states \'Found a peanut just now\'.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is getting ready for school in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Daji\",\"Vanitakaku\",\"Sunil\",\"Sundara\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Sunil is getting ready for school\'.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is Sundara doing according to the passage?\",\"options\":[\"Watering the plants\",\"Grazing\",\"Drying clothes\",\"Going to school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Sundara is grazing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the weather a concern for Vanitakaku?\",\"options\":[\"She wants to go to school\",\"She is hungry for peanuts\",\"She has put clothes on the clothes-line to dry\",\"She needs to water the plants\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says it is about to rain and she has clothes on the line, which would get wet.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If it starts raining immediately, what should Daji likely do regarding his task?\",\"options\":[\"Water the plants more\",\"Stop watering the plants\",\"Find a peanut\",\"Go to school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since rain provides water, Daji would not need to continue watering the plants manually.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the very first thing the person did with the peanut after finding it?\",\"options\":[\"Ate it\",\"Called the doctor\",\"Cracked it open\",\"Had an operation\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the song sequence, \'Cracked it open\' follows \'Found a peanut\'.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Vanitakaku put the clothes to dry?\",\"options\":[\"In the washing machine\",\"On the clothes-line\",\"On the grass\",\"In the school bag\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Vanitakaku has put the clothes on the clothes-line to dry\'.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happened immediately after the person ate the peanut?\",\"options\":[\"They found another peanut\",\"They went to school\",\"They got a stomach ache\",\"They watered the plants\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song says \'Ate the peanut... Got a stomach ache\'.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the song, which action requires a doctor\'s help?\",\"options\":[\"Cracking the peanut\",\"Grazing in the field\",\"Getting a stomach ache\",\"Putting clothes on the line\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song links \'Got a stomach ache\' to \'Call the doctor\'.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct order of events in the song?\",\"options\":[\"Ate -> Found -> Cracked\",\"Found -> Cracked -> Ate\",\"Cracked -> Ate -> Found\",\"Found -> Ate -> Cracked\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The song follows the logical sequence of finding, opening, and then eating the peanut.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final medical step mentioned in the song before asking \'How are you feeling?\'\",\"options\":[\"Taking medicine\",\"Calling the doctor\",\"Operation\",\"Cracking a peanut\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The last action mentioned before the final question is \'Operation\'.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who is going to water the plants?\",\"options\":[\"Sunil\",\"Daji\",\"Sundara\",\"Vanitakaku\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Daji is going to water the plants\'.\",\"topic\":\"Just now!\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21642,27,5,'English','en','Just now!','[\"The poem \'Just now!\' describes a sequence of events happening immediately one after another.\",\"Each action is repeated with the phrase \'just now\' to emphasize immediacy.\",\"The actions include: finding a peanut, cracking it open, eating it, getting a stomach ache, calling the doctor, and undergoing an operation.\",\"The poem uses simple past tense to describe completed actions.\",\"Repetition of lines creates rhythm and musicality, making it suitable for singing and enacting.\",\"The poem helps students understand time sequence and cause-effect (eating peanut → stomach ache → doctor → operation).\",\"Words like \'found\', \'cracked\', \'ate\', \'got\', \'call\', \'operation\' are action verbs in past tense.\",\"The structure follows a pattern: action line, repetition with \'Just now, I...\', then repeated action line.\",\"The poem is meant to be listened to, repeated, sung, and enacted as per the initial instruction.\",\"It builds vocabulary related to daily actions and health situations.\",\"The tone is narrative and cumulative, building a short story in verse form.\",\"Students learn to recognize and use the phrase \'just now\' to indicate recent past actions.\",\"The poem supports listening and speaking skills through repetition and rhythm.\",\"It introduces the idea of consequences in a simple, relatable context.\",\"The language is simple, repetitive, and easy to memorize for young learners.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the example given in the text, what ailment does the boy have?\",\"options\":[\"A headache\",\"A fever\",\"A stomach ache\",\"A cough and cold\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states in the example: \'This boy has a stomach ache.\'\",\"topic\":\"Dialogue Expressions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the person being addressed with \'Bye-bye\' in the song?\",\"options\":[\"The Teacher\",\"The Doctor\",\"A Friend\",\"The Parent\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The song repeats the phrase \'Bye-bye Doctor\' several times.\",\"topic\":\"Dialogue Expressions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT listed as an ailment in the topic text?\",\"options\":[\"fever\",\"headache\",\"cough and cold\",\"back pain\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists stomach ache, headache, cough and cold, and fever; back pain is not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Dialogue Expressions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'Feeling better\' imply in the context of the poem?\",\"options\":[\"The person is becoming more sick\",\"The person is recovering from being unwell\",\"The person is feeling very hungry\",\"The person is going to sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Feeling better indicates a transition from being unwell to health, as shown by saying goodbye to the doctor.\",\"topic\":\"Dialogue Expressions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which question from the text is used to ask someone about their health condition?\",\"options\":[\"Can I help?\",\"What\'s the matter?\",\"Go home?\",\"Aren\'t you happy?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'What\'s the matter?\' as a dialogue expression to inquire about someone\'s health.\",\"topic\":\"Dialogue Expressions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the dialogue, why does a person say \'Oh! I\'m so sorry!\'?\",\"options\":[\"They made a mistake\",\"They are feeling sick themselves\",\"They feel bad that the other person is unwell\",\"They forgot to bring medicine\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"It is an expression of sympathy used when someone else says they are not feeling well.\",\"topic\":\"Dialogue Expressions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student tells you they have a fever, which response is suggested by the text?\",\"options\":[\"You must see a doctor.\",\"Bye-bye Doctor.\",\"I don\'t know.\",\"No, it\'s all right.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The dialogue expressions include \'You must see a doctor\' as a response to someone being unwell.\",\"topic\":\"Dialogue Expressions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the dialogue based on the text: \'Can I help?\' \'____, it\'s all right.\'\",\"options\":[\"Yes\",\"No\",\"Maybe\",\"Please\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the specific dialogue pair: \'Can I help? No, it\'s all right.\'\",\"topic\":\"Dialogue Expressions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the dialogue, what is the first suggested action when a student is not feeling well at school?\",\"options\":[\"Go home immediately\",\"We must tell the teacher\",\"Say bye-bye to the doctor\",\"Take a rest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests \'We must tell the teacher\' as a necessary step when someone isn\'t feeling well.\",\"topic\":\"Dialogue Expressions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the logical sequence of events described by the combined song and dialogue?\",\"options\":[\"Feeling better -> Seeing a doctor -> Having a headache\",\"Having a headache -> Seeing a doctor -> Feeling better\",\"Bye-bye doctor -> Having a fever -> Telling the teacher\",\"Taking rest -> Telling the teacher -> Feeling sick\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The dialogue moves from identifying a problem (headache) to advice (see a doctor) to the result (feeling better).\",\"topic\":\"Dialogue Expressions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21643,27,5,'English','en','True Friends','[\"The poem \'Feeling better\' shows how a child feels after being sick.\",\"Repeating phrases like \'Feeling better just now\' show happiness and relief.\",\"Saying \'Bye-bye Doctor\' means the child is healthy again and doesn’t need the doctor.\",\"The poem uses simple words and rhythm to express joy.\",\"It teaches that rest and care help us feel better when we are unwell.\",\"We should tell elders or teachers when we feel sick.\",\"Seeing a doctor and taking rest are good habits when ill.\",\"Helping others who are unwell is a kind act.\",\"The poem has a cheerful and hopeful tone.\",\"Words like \'Oh! I’m so sorry!\' and \'Can I help?\' show empathy and care.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did Aman study?\",\"options\":[\"In a school\",\"In a college\",\"In a library\",\"At home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Aman was in college.\'\",\"topic\":\"Aman Falls Ill\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who was Aman\'s best friend?\",\"options\":[\"Munna\",\"A classmate\",\"Ronak\",\"A teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says, \'his best friend was Ronak.\'\",\"topic\":\"Aman Falls Ill\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did Ronak offer to take Aman home?\",\"options\":[\"On his bicycle\",\"In his car\",\"By walking\",\"On a bus\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Ronak says, \'Let\'s go home in my car.\'\",\"topic\":\"Aman Falls Ill\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the relationship between Munna, Aman, and Ronak?\",\"options\":[\"They were brothers\",\"They were in the same class\",\"They were neighbors\",\"They were cousins\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'Munna was in the same class.\'\",\"topic\":\"Aman Falls Ill\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Munna wonder how Aman and Ronak could be friends?\",\"options\":[\"Because they lived far away\",\"Because they studied different subjects\",\"Because Ronak is rich and Aman is poor\",\"Because they never talked to each other\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Munna thinks, \'Ronak is so rich and Aman is poor. How can they be friends?\'\",\"topic\":\"Aman Falls Ill\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"For how many days did Aman miss college when he fell ill?\",\"options\":[\"Two days\",\"Three days\",\"Five days\",\"One week\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'He didn\'t go to college for three days.\'\",\"topic\":\"Aman Falls Ill\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Aman stop going to college for a short period?\",\"options\":[\"He went on a vacation\",\"He had to work\",\"He fell ill\",\"He was angry with Ronak\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Aman fell ill.\'\",\"topic\":\"Aman Falls Ill\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the friends say to Aman when they visited him?\",\"options\":[\"Where is Ronak?\",\"Get well soon\",\"Come to college now\",\"Why are you poor?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The friends said, \'How are you, Aman? Get well soon.\'\",\"topic\":\"Aman Falls Ill\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which friend was NOT present when the group came to see Aman?\",\"options\":[\"Munna\",\"Ronak\",\"The other classmates\",\"Aman\'s brother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A friend remarks, \'I don\'t see Ronak,\' implying he was not there.\",\"topic\":\"Aman Falls Ill\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the main difference Munna sees between Aman and Ronak?\",\"options\":[\"Their age\",\"Their intelligence\",\"Their wealth\",\"Their height\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Munna compares them by saying one is rich and the other is poor.\",\"topic\":\"Aman Falls Ill\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who was ill according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Ronak\",\"Munna\",\"Aman\",\"The teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that Aman is ill when Ronak is asked about him.\",\"topic\":\"Munna Visits Aman\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Munna not visit Aman on the first day?\",\"options\":[\"He was also ill\",\"He was busy\",\"He was angry with Aman\",\"He did not know where Aman lived\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Munna tells his friends, \'I was busy,\' as the reason for not visiting Aman.\",\"topic\":\"Munna Visits Aman\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What reason did the other friend give to suggest that Munna and Aman were not good friends?\",\"options\":[\"Aman was very angry\",\"Munna did not like Aman\",\"Aman didn\'t even ask about Munna\",\"Ronak was a better friend than Munna\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The friend says they cannot be good friends because \'Aman didn\'t even ask us about you.\'\",\"topic\":\"Munna Visits Aman\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When did Munna finally go to visit Aman at his house?\",\"options\":[\"The same evening\",\"The next day\",\"A week later\",\"He never went\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The next day, Munna went to Aman\'s house.\'\",\"topic\":\"Munna Visits Aman\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, if a friend is ill and you are busy, when is a good time to visit them?\",\"options\":[\"Never visit them\",\"Wait for them to get well first\",\"Visit them as soon as you are free, like the next day\",\"Wait for them to call you\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Munna shows that even if you are busy one day, you should visit the next day.\",\"topic\":\"Munna Visits Aman\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Munna question Ronak\'s friendship while talking to Aman?\",\"options\":[\"Because Ronak is also ill\",\"Because Ronak doesn\'t come to see Aman at all\",\"Because Ronak is too busy to play\",\"Because Ronak told lies about Aman\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Munna asks \'What sort of a friend is this Ronak?\' because he believes Ronak hasn\'t visited Aman.\",\"topic\":\"Munna Visits Aman\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does Aman describe Ronak despite Munna\'s doubts?\",\"options\":[\"A busy person\",\"A forgetful friend\",\"The best of friends\",\"A bad friend\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aman defends Ronak by saying, \'Oh, but he\'s the best of friends.\'\",\"topic\":\"Munna Visits Aman\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, who is the boy saying, \'Thank you for coming, Munna\'?\",\"options\":[\"Ronak\",\"Munna\",\"Aman\",\"Aman\'s father\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the illustration, the boy in the green shirt (Aman) thanks Munna for visiting him.\",\"topic\":\"Munna Visits Aman\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/033_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what object is placed on the cupboard behind Munna?\",\"options\":[\"A mirror\",\"A bottle\",\"A book\",\"A toy car\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a blue bottle sitting on the wooden cupboard behind Munna.\",\"topic\":\"Munna Visits Aman\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/033_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If Aman says \'I\'m much better now\', what does it imply about his health?\",\"options\":[\"He is getting sicker\",\"His health has improved since yesterday\",\"He is perfectly healthy and was never ill\",\"He needs to go to the hospital immediately\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'much better\' indicates that his condition has improved from being ill.\",\"topic\":\"Munna Visits Aman\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the shop located according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Near Ronak\'s house\",\"Near Aman\'s house\",\"In the city center\",\"Near Munna\'s school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states they walk to a shop near Aman\'s house.\",\"topic\":\"Ronak\'s Secret\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who was working in the shop when Munna and Aman arrived?\",\"options\":[\"Aman\",\"Munna\",\"Ronak\",\"The shopkeeper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Munna is surprised to see Ronak working in the shop.\",\"topic\":\"Ronak\'s Secret\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"At what time of day does Aman usually work in the shop?\",\"options\":[\"In the morning\",\"In the afternoon\",\"In the evening\",\"Late at night\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aman says, \'I work in this shop in the evening.\'\",\"topic\":\"Ronak\'s Secret\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Ronak working in the shop instead of Aman?\",\"options\":[\"Aman was on holiday\",\"Aman fell ill\",\"Ronak wanted to earn money\",\"Aman left the job\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aman explains that Ronak is doing his job because he fell ill.\",\"topic\":\"Ronak\'s Secret\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the shopkeeper threaten to do if Aman did not come to work?\",\"options\":[\"Close the shop\",\"Reduce Aman\'s salary\",\"Give the job to another boy\",\"Call Aman\'s parents\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The shopkeeper said, \'If you don\'t come to work I\'ll give your job to some other boy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Ronak\'s Secret\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Munna surprised to see Ronak working in the shop?\",\"options\":[\"Because Ronak is a rich boy\",\"Because Ronak is very young\",\"Because Ronak is lazy\",\"Because Ronak does not like Aman\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Munna exclaims, \'A rich boy like Ronak, working in a shop!\'\",\"topic\":\"Ronak\'s Secret\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what was Ronak\'s \'secret\'?\",\"options\":[\"He was planning a party\",\"He was doing Aman\'s job to help him\",\"He was buying the shop\",\"He was hiding from Munna\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The context shows Ronak was secretly working Aman\'s shift to save Aman\'s job.\",\"topic\":\"Ronak\'s Secret\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Ronak had not worked in the shop, what would have most likely happened to Aman?\",\"options\":[\"He would have stayed rich\",\"He would have lost his job\",\"He would have moved to a new house\",\"He would have become the shopkeeper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The shopkeeper stated he would give the job to someone else if Aman didn\'t show up.\",\"topic\":\"Ronak\'s Secret\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does Ronak\'s decision to work in the shop reveal about his character?\",\"options\":[\"He is greedy for money\",\"He is a true and supportive friend\",\"He wants to show off his skills\",\"He dislikes going to school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Working a job for a sick friend to ensure they don\'t lose it shows true friendship.\",\"topic\":\"Ronak\'s Secret\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement best describes the situation in the passage?\",\"options\":[\"Aman is teaching Ronak how to work in a shop.\",\"The shopkeeper is Ronak\'s father.\",\"Ronak is helping Aman during a difficult time.\",\"Munna is angry at Ronak for working.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The passage describes Ronak stepping in to work because Aman is ill and might lose his job.\",\"topic\":\"Ronak\'s Secret\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28');
INSERT INTO `ep_topic_packs` VALUES (21644,27,5,'English','en','Keeping Quiet','[\"The poem \'Keeping Quiet\' is about taking a moment of silence to reflect.\",\"It encourages people to stop their busy activities and think about peace.\",\"The poet suggests counting to twelve and staying still.\",\"Silence helps us understand ourselves and others better.\",\"It promotes unity and brotherhood among all people.\",\"The poem warns against harmful actions like wars and violence.\",\"It asks us to protect nature and not harm the environment.\",\"Even in silence, life continues — like the earth that seems dead but is alive.\",\"The message is to pause, reflect, and act with kindness.\",\"Keeping quiet does not mean sleeping or being inactive — it means being aware.\",\"The poet believes silence can bring about inner change.\",\"This change can lead to a more peaceful and harmonious world.\",\"The poem is written by Pablo Neruda, a famous Chilean poet.\",\"It is part of Unit Two in the English textbook.\",\"The theme is mindfulness, peace, and self-awareness.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the speaker talking to in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Mitali\",\"Shama\",\"Namita\",\"The Teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text begins with \'Hello, Namita\', identifying the person being addressed.\",\"topic\":\"2. Say what Namita might say\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the speaker ask Namita to do together?\",\"options\":[\"Go out to play\",\"Go to the office\",\"Find a pen\",\"Talk to Shama\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The speaker asks, \'Shall we go out to play?\'\",\"topic\":\"2. Say what Namita might say\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the chapter title \'Keeping Quiet\', why is the speaker asking \'What\'s wrong with you?\'\",\"options\":[\"Because Namita is shouting\",\"Because Namita is not speaking\",\"Because Namita is crying\",\"Because Namita is running\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The title \'Keeping Quiet\' implies Namita is silent, which makes the speaker wonder what is wrong.\",\"topic\":\"2. Say what Namita might say\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What object is the speaker looking for when they ask \'Where is it?\'\",\"options\":[\"A ball\",\"A book\",\"A pen\",\"A bag\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The question \'Where is it?\' follows the request \'Can I take your pen?\'\",\"topic\":\"2. Say what Namita might say\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If Namita is keeping quiet, how might she answer the question \'Are you busy?\'\",\"options\":[\"By shouting \'No\'\",\"By nodding or shaking her head\",\"By singing a song\",\"By writing a long letter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A person keeping quiet would use gestures like nodding instead of speaking.\",\"topic\":\"2. Say what Namita might say\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which two locations does the speaker mention as possible places for Shama?\",\"options\":[\"Classroom and Library\",\"Garden and Canteen\",\"Playground and Office\",\"Home and School\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks \'On the playground? In the office?\' regarding Shama.\",\"topic\":\"2. Say what Namita might say\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the speaker assume when Namita does not answer their questions?\",\"options\":[\"Namita is happy\",\"Namita might be angry\",\"Namita is sleeping\",\"Namita is at home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speaker asks, \'Are you angry with me?\' because Namita is not responding.\",\"topic\":\"2. Say what Namita might say\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Namita wants to show the speaker where her pen is without talking, what should she do?\",\"options\":[\"Close her eyes\",\"Point towards the pen\",\"Walk away\",\"Start playing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Pointing is a non-verbal way to indicate a location while keeping quiet.\",\"topic\":\"2. Say what Namita might say\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the speaker finally say, \'Then I think I\'ll go to her\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because Namita told them to leave\",\"Because Namita is not responding to the questions\",\"Because the speaker is scared of Namita\",\"Because the office is closed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speaker decides to find someone else (Mitali or Shama) because Namita remains silent.\",\"topic\":\"2. Say what Namita might say\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which names are mentioned as other friends Namita might know the location of?\",\"options\":[\"Mitali and Shama\",\"Namita and Mitali\",\"Shama and Namita\",\"The speaker and Shama\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The speaker asks \'Where\'s Mitali? Where\'s Shama?\'\",\"topic\":\"2. Say what Namita might say\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who offered to do Aman\'s work when he was not feeling well?\",\"options\":[\"Munna\",\"Ronak\",\"The shopkeeper\",\"Aman\'s brother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Ronak says, \'Don\'t worry, Aman. I\'ll do your work for you.\'\",\"topic\":\"Don\'t worry, Aman\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the name of the shop Ronak comes out of?\",\"options\":[\"AMAN STORES\",\"MUNNA SHOP\",\"VIVIDH\",\"FRIENDSHIP\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sign on the shop in the illustration clearly says \'VIVIDH\'.\",\"topic\":\"Don\'t worry, Aman\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/034_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Ronak tell Aman to go home and rest?\",\"options\":[\"Because Aman was lazy\",\"Because the shop was closed\",\"Because Aman was not well\",\"Because Ronak wanted to work alone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ronak tells Aman he can go back to work when he is \'better\', implying he is currently unwell.\",\"topic\":\"Don\'t worry, Aman\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Ronak give to Aman after coming out of the shop?\",\"options\":[\"A gift\",\"Medicine\",\"Food\",\"Money\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Here\'s your money, Aman.\'\",\"topic\":\"Don\'t worry, Aman\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Ronak\'s actions, what is the best way to help a sick friend?\",\"options\":[\"Ask them to work harder\",\"Help them by doing their tasks so they can rest\",\"Take their money for yourself\",\"Tell them to stay away from the shop\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Ronak demonstrates true friendship by doing Aman\'s work so Aman can recover.\",\"topic\":\"Don\'t worry, Aman\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Aman say, \'But you did the work, Ronak\'?\",\"options\":[\"He was angry with Ronak\",\"He didn\'t want Ronak to work\",\"He felt Ronak deserved the money because Ronak did the labor\",\"He forgot that Ronak was his friend\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aman hesitates to take the money because he recognizes that Ronak performed the actual work.\",\"topic\":\"Don\'t worry, Aman\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What lesson does this story teach about friendship?\",\"options\":[\"Friends should only work for money\",\"True friends help each other in times of need\",\"It is better to work alone than with friends\",\"Friends should not go to shops together\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aman says, \'You\'ve shown me what true friendship is,\' after Ronak helps him without keeping the money.\",\"topic\":\"Don\'t worry, Aman\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"When does Aman plan to return to work?\",\"options\":[\"Today\",\"Tomorrow\",\"Next week\",\"Never\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aman says, \'I\'ll go back to work tomorrow.\'\",\"topic\":\"Don\'t worry, Aman\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Aman doing while Ronak is shown working in the shop?\",\"options\":[\"He is playing with Munna\",\"He is resting in bed with a cloth on his head\",\"He is buying things from the shop\",\"He is helping Ronak pack boxes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The thought bubble in the illustration shows Aman lying in bed while Ronak works.\",\"topic\":\"Don\'t worry, Aman\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/034_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which character is mentioned as being present when Ronak brings the money, besides Aman and Ronak?\",\"options\":[\"The Shopkeeper\",\"Aman\'s mother\",\"Munna\",\"The Doctor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ronak says \'Hello, Munna\' when he arrives to give Aman the money.\",\"topic\":\"Don\'t worry, Aman\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'my car\', which word shows who the car belongs to?\",\"options\":[\"car\",\"my\",\"the\",\"a\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'my\' is a possessive adjective showing ownership.\",\"topic\":\"3. Make and write phrases\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase from the text shows something belonging to a girl?\",\"options\":[\"his money\",\"her book\",\"their team\",\"its tail\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Her\' is used to show possession for a female.\",\"topic\":\"3. Make and write phrases\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'our school\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"School belonging to me\",\"School belonging to you\",\"School belonging to us\",\"School belonging to them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Our\' refers to something belonging to a group that includes the speaker.\",\"topic\":\"3. Make and write phrases\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'Aman\'s house\', what does the \'s indicate?\",\"options\":[\"There are many Amans\",\"The house belongs to Aman\",\"Aman is a house\",\"Aman is going to the house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The apostrophe \'s\' is used to show that the house belongs to Aman.\",\"topic\":\"3. Make and write phrases\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phrases follows the same pattern as \'his money\'?\",\"options\":[\"he money\",\"him money\",\"his pen\",\"he\'s money\"],