According to the grammar rules in the text, \'We\' is followed by \'don\'t\'.\",\"topic\":\"8. Complete the sentences\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase correctly completes the sentence starting with \'It\'?\",\"options\":[\"It don\'t grow tall\",\"It doesn\'t grow tall\",\"It don\'t grows tall\",\"It doesn\'t grows tall\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'It doesn\'t\' with options like \'grow tall\'.\",\"topic\":\"8. Complete the sentences\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Choose the correct completion for the sentence: \'You ____ jump high.\'\",\"options\":[\"doesn\'t\",\"don\'t\",\"does\",\"not\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'You don\'t\' as the correct structure.\",\"topic\":\"8. Complete the sentences\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to say that a boy is not working in a specific place, which sentence is correct?\",\"options\":[\"He don\'t work here.\",\"He doesn\'t work here.\",\"He not work here.\",\"He doesn\'t works here.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'He doesn\'t\' and the verb phrase \'work here\'.\",\"topic\":\"8. Complete the sentences\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the correct sentence regarding a group of people and their food habits.\",\"options\":[\"They doesn\'t eat vegetables.\",\"They don\'t eat vegetables.\",\"They don\'t eats vegetables.\",\"They not eat vegetables.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'They don\'t\' with \'eat vegetables\'.\",\"topic\":\"8. Complete the sentences\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sentences follows the pattern provided in the textbook?\",\"options\":[\"She doesn\'t have a sister.\",\"She don\'t have a sister.\",\"She doesn\'t has a sister.\",\"She don\'t has a sister.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'She doesn\'t\' and the phrase \'have a sister\'.\",\"topic\":\"8. Complete the sentences\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Analyze the following and pick the grammatically correct sentence based on the list.\",\"options\":[\"It don\'t fall ill.\",\"He don\'t get angry.\",\"He doesn\'t get angry.\",\"They doesn\'t jump high.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Third-person singular subjects (He\\/She\\/It) take \'doesn\'t\' while others take \'don\'t\'.\",\"topic\":\"8. Complete the sentences\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which pairing of subject and auxiliary is WRONG according to the exercise?\",\"options\":[\"I don\'t\",\"They don\'t\",\"She doesn\'t\",\"We doesn\'t\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'We don\'t\', so \'We doesn\'t\' is incorrect.\",\"topic\":\"8. Complete the sentences\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the first word in all the example questions?\",\"options\":[\"What\'s\",\"Where\'s\",\"Who\'s\",\"How\'s\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides four examples, all starting with \'Where\'s\'.\",\"topic\":\"9. Listen and complete the question\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How should this activity or game be conducted according to the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Very slowly\",\"Over a long period\",\"Quickly\",\"In writing only\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'हा खेळ\\/स्वाध्याय शक्यतो भरभर घ्यावा\', which means the activity should be done quickly.\",\"topic\":\"9. Listen and complete the question\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should a student do when the teacher points to them and starts a question?\",\"options\":[\"Wait for the teacher to finish\",\"Complete the question at once\",\"Repeat what the teacher said\",\"Ask a different question\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instruction says \'Listen to my question and complete it at once\'.\",\"topic\":\"9. Listen and complete the question\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the instruction \'त्याच त्याच कल्पना पुन्हा वापरल्या जाऊ नयेत\' mean for the students?\",\"options\":[\"They should repeat the same words\",\"They should not use the same ideas again\",\"They should only use the examples in the book\",\"They should not answer the question\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"This instruction tells students to be creative and avoid repeating ideas already mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"9. Listen and complete the question\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the teacher says \'Where\'s your...?\', which of these is a correct way for a student to complete it?\",\"options\":[\"is it?\",\"pencil?\",\"going?\",\"are you?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The student must complete the question \'Where\'s your...?\' with a noun like \'pencil\' to make a valid question.\",\"topic\":\"9. Listen and complete the question\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT one of the starting phrases provided in the textbook?\",\"options\":[\"Where\'s my ?\",\"Where\'s our ?\",\"Where\'s their ?\",\"Where\'s your ?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Where\'s their\' is not listed in the four bulleted examples in the text.\",\"topic\":\"9. Listen and complete the question\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The instruction \'स्वतःच्या मनाने प्रश्न पूर्ण करावा\' suggests that the student should:\",\"options\":[\"Use their own imagination\",\"Read the answer from the book\",\"Ask the teacher for the answer\",\"Copy the previous student\'s answer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"This phrase means the student should complete the question using their own mind\\/ideas.\",\"topic\":\"9. Listen and complete the question\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to complete the prompt \'Where\'s...?\', which of these follows the activity rules?\",\"options\":[\"Where\'s the cat?\",\"Where\'s is the cat?\",\"Where\'s my my pen?\",\"Where\'s go home?\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Where\'s the cat?\' is a grammatically correct completion of the prompt \'Where\'s...?\'\",\"topic\":\"9. Listen and complete the question\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does the teacher indicate which student should complete the question?\",\"options\":[\"By calling out a roll number\",\"By pointing at a student\",\"By throwing a ball\",\"By writing a name on the board\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'शिक्षकांनी कोणत्याही विद्यार्थ्याकडे निर्देश करून\', which means pointing towards a student.\",\"topic\":\"9. Listen and complete the question\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If the teacher says \'Where\'s our...?\', which completion uses a new idea as requested?\",\"options\":[\"Where\'s our school?\",\"Where\'s our Where\'s our?\",\"Where\'s our is big?\",\"Where\'s our quickly?\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'School\' is a valid noun that completes the question meaningfully.\",\"topic\":\"9. Listen and complete the question\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21645,27,5,'English','en','Interviews','[\"An interview is a conversation where one person asks questions and another answers.\",\"The person asking questions is called the interviewer.\",\"The person answering questions is called the interviewee.\",\"Interviews help us know more about a person\'s life, work, or feelings.\",\"Good interviews need polite and clear questions.\",\"Listening carefully is important during an interview.\",\"We can take interviews of friends, family, or community helpers.\",\"Interviews can be done in person, over phone, or in writing.\",\"Answers in an interview should be honest and to the point.\",\"Body language like eye contact and nodding shows respect in an interview.\",\"Interviews help improve speaking and listening skills.\",\"We should thank the person after taking their interview.\",\"Notes can be taken during an interview to remember important points.\",\"Interviews are used in newspapers, TV, and school projects.\",\"Always ask permission before interviewing someone.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the first question you should ask your partner according to the interview list?\",\"options\":[\"What\'s your full name?\",\"Where do you live?\",\"What\'s your hobby?\",\"What subjects do you like?\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'What\'s your full name?\' as the first question for the interview.\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is mentioned as a game in the topic text?\",\"options\":[\"Cricket\",\"Kho-kho\",\"Football\",\"Chess\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Kho-kho is specifically listed under the question \'What games do you play?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the examples in the text, what is something a student might want to learn?\",\"options\":[\"Cooking\",\"Karate\",\"Driving\",\"Painting\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the example \'I want to learn karate\' under things about yourself.\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are students instructed to do first for this activity?\",\"options\":[\"Read a story\",\"Form pairs\",\"Draw a picture\",\"Write a poem\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first instruction in the text is \'Form pairs and interview your partner\'.\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase is used in the text to show interest or react to an answer?\",\"options\":[\"Goodbye\",\"Oh, I see!\",\"No thanks\",\"Please wait\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Oh, I see!\', \'Is that so?\', and \'How nice\' as reactive phrases.\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of answers should the friend give during the interview?\",\"options\":[\"Answers from the textbook\",\"His\\/her own answers\",\"Only \'Yes\' or \'No\' answers\",\"Answers provided by the teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Your friend will give his\\/her own answers.\'\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to know where your friend stays, which question from the text will you ask?\",\"options\":[\"What\'s your hobby?\",\"Where do you live?\",\"What games do you play?\",\"What\'s your full name?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The question \'Where do you live?\' is used to find out a person\'s address or location.\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Under which category does the text place \'climbing hills\'?\",\"options\":[\"Subjects\",\"Games\",\"Hobby\",\"Address\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the text, \'climbing hills\' is listed as an example under \'What\'s your hobby?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which question requires the partner to talk about their current abilities and future goals?\",\"options\":[\"What\'s your full name?\",\"Tell me a few things about yourself\",\"What\'s your favourite dish?\",\"Where do you live?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"This question asks for what you can do, what you like to do, and what you want to learn.\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is NOT listed as a specific hobby?\",\"options\":[\"Whistling\",\"Sleeping\",\"Eating\",\"Cooking\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Whistling, sleeping, and eating are all listed as hobbies in the text, but cooking is not.\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the boy holding in his hands to record the interview answers?\",\"options\":[\"A mobile phone\",\"A slate\",\"A notepad and a pen\",\"A large textbook\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the boy holding a notepad and a pen while interviewing the girl.\",\"topic\":\"Interviews\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/038_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which question bubble provides the longest list of example choices for the student to pick from?\