\"options\":[\"Let\'s play cricket.\",\"Let\'s work quickly.\",\"Let me go home.\",\"Let\'s wash the plants.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'Example : Let\'s work quickly.\' right after the instructions for Activity 1.\",\"topic\":\"Friendly Plans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main goal of the \'Friendly Plans\' activity?\",\"options\":[\"To draw pictures of fruits\",\"To make as many meaningful sentences as possible\",\"To count the number of boxes\",\"To translate words into another language\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the goal is to \'Make as many meaningful sentences as you can\'.\",\"topic\":\"Friendly Plans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In Activity 3, which phrase should be used at the beginning instead of \'Let\'s\'?\",\"options\":[\"Let you\",\"Let us\",\"Let me\",\"Let them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Activity 3 states: \'Instead of Let\'s, use Let me at the beginning\'.\",\"topic\":\"Friendly Plans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text mean by \'neighbouring boxes\'?\",\"options\":[\"Boxes that are far apart\",\"Boxes that are empty\",\"Boxes that are next to each other\",\"Boxes that have the same color\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In this context, neighbouring boxes refers to words located near the starting point to form a sequence.\",\"topic\":\"Friendly Plans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Using the words from the text, which word correctly completes the sentence: \'Let\'s wash ____\'?\",\"options\":[\"the plants\",\"slowly\",\"well\",\"hard\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'the plants\' is a valid object for the action \'wash\' found in the text boxes.\",\"topic\":\"Friendly Plans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you change \'Let\'s play cricket\' using the rule in Activity 3, what does it become?\",\"options\":[\"Let me play cricket.\",\"Let\'s play home.\",\"Let me go home.\",\"Let\'s play well.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Activity 3 asks to replace \'Let\'s\' with \'Let me\' at the beginning of the sentence.\",\"topic\":\"Friendly Plans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a meaningful sentence that can be made using only the words in the boxes?\",\"options\":[\"Let\'s drink the books.\",\"Let\'s study every day.\",\"Let\'s eat the plants.\",\"Let\'s wash quickly away.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The words \'Let\'s\', \'study\', and \'every day\' are all present in the text and form a meaningful sentence.\",\"topic\":\"Friendly Plans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following words from the text is an action (verb)?\",\"options\":[\"biscuits\",\"cricket\",\"drink\",\"the fruits\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Drink\' is an action word provided in the boxes to form sentences.\",\"topic\":\"Friendly Plans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The words \'slowly\', \'quickly\', and \'carefully\' in the text are used to describe:\",\"options\":[\"Names of people\",\"Types of food\",\"How an action is done\",\"Places to go\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"These words are adverbs used in the grid to modify actions like \'work\' or \'wash\'.\",\"topic\":\"Friendly Plans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text would best complete the sentence \'Let\'s colour ____\'?\",\"options\":[\"the books\",\"it\",\"the fruits\",\"all of the above\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"While \'it\' could work, \'the books\' is a specific noun provided in the text that can be coloured.\",\"topic\":\"Friendly Plans\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21646,27,5,'English','en','Friendly Plans','[\"Friendship means caring for each other and helping in times of need.\",\"A true friend supports you when you are sad or unwell.\",\"Sharing and kindness strengthen friendships.\",\"Helping a friend without expecting anything in return is a sign of good friendship.\",\"Friends feel happy when they see each other well and safe.\",\"We should speak kindly and listen to our friends.\",\"Writing or telling a story in your own words helps you understand it better.\",\"Using your own ideas to create sentences shows creativity and understanding.\",\"Phrases like \'my car\', \'his money\', \'our school\' show possession using apostrophes or possessive words.\",\"Possessive forms tell us who something belongs to.\",\"We can make similar phrases for friends, books, teams, houses, etc.\",\"Enacting a story helps us remember the events and feelings in it.\",\"Retelling a story in short improves memory and language skills.\",\"Working together and helping each other makes tasks easier and happier.\",\"Friendship brings joy, trust, and a sense of belonging.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did Ronak do for Aman when he was unwell?\",\"options\":[\"Took his money\",\"Did his work\",\"Wrote a story\",\"Gave him a book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Ronak did Aman\'s work so he could rest and get better.\"},{\"q\":\"How did Aman feel after Ronak helped him?\",\"options\":[\"Angry\",\"Thankful\",\"Jealous\",\"Tired\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aman thanked Ronak and said he learned what true friendship is.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following shows possession correctly?\",\"options\":[\"her book\",\"she book\",\"book her\",\"book of her\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Her book\' is the correct possessive form showing the book belongs to her.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do to retell a story in your mother tongue?\",\"options\":[\"Write it in English\",\"Speak and write it in your mother tongue\",\"Draw pictures only\",\"Sing it as a song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instruction says to tell the story short in your mother tongue and write it down.\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase is NOT like \'my car\', \'his money\', \'our school\'?\",\"options\":[\"your friend\",\"her book\",\"their team\",\"go to park\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"\'Go to park\' does not show possession like the others.\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'Aman’s house\' tell us?\",\"options\":[\"Aman built the house\",\"The house belongs to Aman\",\"Aman sold the house\",\"The house is near Aman\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The apostrophe s (\'s) shows possession — the house belongs to Aman.\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it good to help a friend without being asked?\",\"options\":[\"It makes you famous\",\"It shows true friendship\",\"You get money\",\"You avoid work\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Helping selflessly is a sign of true friendship, as shown by Ronak.\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity helps you understand a story better?\",\"options\":[\"Ignoring it\",\"Enacting the story\",\"Tearing the page\",\"Leaving it unread\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Enacting the story helps you remember and understand the events and feelings.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct possessive form for \'the book of the girl\'?\",\"options\":[\"girl book\",\"girls book\",\"girl\'s book\",\"book girl\'s\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Girl\'s book\' is the correct possessive form.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Aman say he would do after feeling better?\",\"options\":[\"Stop working\",\"Go on vacation\",\"Go back to work tomorrow\",\"Give Ronak money\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aman said, \'Now I\'m better. I\'ll go back to work tomorrow.\'\"}]','nvidia/nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21647,27,5,'English','en','Words','[\"Words can show comparison: good, better, best.\",\"Words can show opposite meanings: good vs bad, big vs small.\",\"Some words change form to show comparison: bad, worse, worst.\",\"We use \'good\', \'better\', \'best\' to compare two or more things.\",\"We use \'bad\', \'worse\', \'worst\' to compare two or more things in a negative way.\",\"Fill in the blanks with the correct form of the word based on the sentence.\",\"Underline the correct word in a sentence from the given list.\",\"Find the opposite of a given word from the text.\",\"Complete sentences using suitable words from the options given.\",\"Translate sentences into your mother tongue.\",\"Listen and complete the sentence immediately.\",\"Answer questions based on pictures or situations.\",\"Form meaningful dialogues using given sentence starters.\",\"Match actions with their correct meanings or speech.\",\"Work in pairs or groups to practice speaking and listening.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many seconds are allowed to say \'a\' to \'z\'?\",\"options\":[\"5 seconds\",\"10 seconds\",\"15 seconds\",\"20 seconds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states \'Say a to z in 10 seconds\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Lists I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many words beginning with \'th\' are you asked to tell?\",\"options\":[\"3 words\",\"4 words\",\"5 words\",\"6 words\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks to \'Tell 4 words that begin with th\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Lists I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words satisfies the task \'Tell 5 words that end with e\'?\",\"options\":[\"Egg\",\"Elephant\",\"Apple\",\"Eat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Apple ends with the letter \'e\', which is one of the tasks mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Word Lists I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides \'What\' and \'Who\', which other word are you asked to use to frame a question?\",\"options\":[\"Where\",\"When\",\"How\",\"Why\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks to frame questions beginning with \'What\', \'Who\', and \'How\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Lists I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of words all begin with the letter \'b\' as requested in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Bat, Ball, Boy, Box, Big\",\"Cat, Cup, Can, Cake, Car\",\"Ant, Axe, Arm, Any, All\",\"Net, New, Nil, Not, Now\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first option contains 5 words all starting with \'b\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Lists I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a word that ends with \'r\' as mentioned in the word list tasks?\",\"options\":[\"Road\",\"Star\",\"Rain\",\"Red\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Star ends with \'r\', which matches the task \'Tell 5 words that end with r\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Lists I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which two activities in the text share the exact same time limit of 10 seconds?\",\"options\":[\"Telling words with \'a\' and \'e\'\",\"Saying \'a\' to \'z\' and numbers 1 to 20\",\"Singing a song and framing a question\",\"Telling words with \'n\' and \'b\'\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both \'Say a to z\' and \'Say 1 to 20\' are assigned a 10-second limit.\",\"topic\":\"Word Lists I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"For which of the following letters are you asked to find words that \'end\' with that letter?\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"n\",\"p\",\"b\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks for words that end with \'e\', \'r\', \'t\', and \'p\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Lists I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a student says \'Top, Map, Cup, Hop, Tap\', which task are they completing?\",\"options\":[\"Tell 5 words that begin with t\",\"Tell 5 words that end with p\",\"Tell 5 words that begin with b\",\"Tell 5 words that end with t\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"All the words provided (Top, Map, Cup, Hop, Tap) end with the letter \'p\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Lists I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a correct example of the task \'Frame a question that begins with Who\'?\",\"options\":[\"Who is your best friend?\",\"What is your name?\",\"How are you today?\",\"I like to sing songs.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first option is a question starting with \'Who\', as requested in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Word Lists I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many words ending with the letter \'k\' should you tell?\",\"options\":[\"3 words\",\"4 words\",\"5 words\",\"6 words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text e