fast.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text asks to \'Make a sentence that has and\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Look at this list: \'Sun, Ten, Pen, Bin, Fan\'. Which instruction does this list satisfy?\",\"options\":[\"Tell 5 words that begin with \'p\'\",\"Tell 5 words that end with \'n\'\",\"Tell 5 words that begin with \'t\'\",\"Tell 5 words that end with \'k\'\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"All words in the list end with the letter \'n\', which is one of the tasks.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a student says \'Dog, Doll, Desk, Door, Duck\', which task have they completed?\",\"options\":[\"Words beginning with \'d\'\",\"Words beginning with \'t\'\",\"Words beginning with \'p\'\",\"Words beginning with \'m\'\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"All these words start with \'d\', fulfilling the instruction \'Tell 5 words that begin with d\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main difference between the instruction for \'and\' and the instruction for \'p\'?\",\"options\":[\"One requires a sentence, the other requires a list of words.\",\"One requires 10 seconds, the other requires 5 words.\",\"One is about the letter \'k\', the other is about \'p\'.\",\"There is no difference.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The \'and\' task requires making a sentence, while the \'p\' task requires telling 5 words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21648,27,5,'English','en','Trains','[\"Trains run on tracks and carry people and goods.\",\"Trains can go over mountains, plains, and rivers.\",\"Trains carry passengers, mail, and freight.\",\"Freight cars are used to transport goods.\",\"Trains run through day and night, in all weather.\",\"Trains help connect different places.\",\"The poem \'Over the mountains\' describes a train\'s journey.\",\"James S. Tippett wrote the poem about trains.\",\"Trains do not stop easily; they keep going \'without fail\'.\",\"Trains are an important means of transport.\",\"Trains can carry heavy loads over long distances.\",\"Trains run on rails laid on the ground.\",\"Trains are faster than bullock carts and bicycles.\",\"Trains help in carrying mail to faraway places.\",\"Trains run from dawn to dusk and beyond.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the word meanings provided, what does the word \'mail\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"A type of train\",\"Letters and packages (टपाल)\",\"A mountain path\",\"A fast river\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The textbook defines \'mail\' as \'टपाल\', which refers to letters or packages.\",\"topic\":\"Word Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the poem means \'valuable\' or \'बहुमोल\'?\",\"options\":[\"Precious\",\"Freight\",\"Plain\",\"Fail\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'precious\' is defined in the text as \'किमती\' or \'बहुमोल\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are \'freight cars\' as described in the topic?\",\"options\":[\"Cars that carry passengers\",\"Cars that fly over mountains\",\"Wagons used for carrying goods (मालगाड्या)\",\"Small boats on the river\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'freight cars\' as \'मालगाड्या\', which are used to carry goods.\",\"topic\":\"Word Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When does \'dawn\' (डॉन्) occur?\",\"options\":[\"Late at night\",\"In the afternoon\",\"At sunset\",\"Early morning or sunrise (पहाट)\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'dawn\' as \'पहाट\' or \'उपःकाल\', which is early morning.\",\"topic\":\"Word Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'without fail\' tell us about the trains?\",\"options\":[\"They often get lost\",\"They arrive regularly without missing (न चुकता)\",\"They only travel in the day\",\"They stop at every river\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'without fail\' as \'न विसरता\' or \'न चुकता\', meaning they arrive certainly.\",\"topic\":\"Word Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes the time of evening just before it gets dark?\",\"options\":[\"Dawn\",\"Dusk\",\"Mail\",\"Freight\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'dusk\' as \'सायंकाळ\' or \'दिवसागणिकची वेळ\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a train is carrying \'precious loads\', what is it most likely carrying?\",\"options\":[\"Empty boxes\",\"Valuable items like mail and passengers\",\"Only water from the rivers\",\"Rocks from the mountains\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since \'precious\' means \'valuable\', the load consists of important things like passengers and mail mentioned in the poem.\",\"topic\":\"Word Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The poem mentions trains rushing through \'dusk and dawn\'. This means they travel during:\",\"options\":[\"Only the daytime\",\"Only the nighttime\",\"Both early morning and early evening\",\"Only when it rains\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Dusk is evening and dawn is morning; traveling through both implies they travel at these specific times of transition.\",\"topic\":\"Word Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the correct pair of opposites based on the time of day mentioned in the text.\",\"options\":[\"Mountain and Plain\",\"River and Train\",\"Dusk and Dawn\",\"Mail and Freight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Dusk (evening) and Dawn (morning) are times of the day that represent opposite ends of daylight.\",\"topic\":\"Word Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet use the word \'thousands\' to describe freight cars?\",\"options\":[\"To show there are very few trains\",\"To show that the railway carries a very large amount of goods\",\"To show that trains are very slow\",\"To show that trains only carry mail\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'thousands\' emphasizes the large scale and volume of goods (freight) being moved.\",\"topic\":\"Word Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the phrase \'without fail\'?\",\"options\":[\"Sometimes happening\",\"Regularly and every time\",\"Failing to do something\",\"Happening only once\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'without fail\' means that something happens regularly without missing any time.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'day and night\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Only during the afternoon\",\"Only when it is dark\",\"All the time, continuously\",\"For one hour daily\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Day and night\' refers to something that happens all the time, both during the day and the night.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase means \'from sunrise to sunset\'?\",\"options\":[\"Without fail\",\"Day and night\",\"From dawn to dusk\",\"Every morning\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'From dawn to dusk\' specifically refers to the period from sunrise (dawn) to sunset (dusk).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a train arrives at the station \'without fail\', it means the train is ______.\",\"options\":[\"Always late\",\"Always on time\",\"Never coming\",\"Sometimes missing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Arriving \'without fail\' implies the action is consistent and reliable.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase best describes a machine that runs all 24 hours of a day?\",\"options\":[\"Without fail\",\"Day and night\",\"From dawn to dusk\",\"Once a week\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Day and night\' covers the entire 24-hour cycle.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When a farmer works \'from dawn to dusk\', he is working ______.\",\"options\":[\"Only at night\",\"All day long until sunset\",\"For a few minutes\",\"After the sun goes down\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Working from dawn to dusk means working throughout the daylight hours.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Choose the correct phrase: \'I promise to complete my homework every day ______.\'\",\"options\":[\"from dawn to dusk\",\"day and night\",\"without fail\",\"only once\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Without fail\' is used here to show a commitment to doing something regularly.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a park is open \'from dawn to dusk\', at what time will it close?\",\"options\":[\"At sunrise\",\"At sunset\",\"At midnight\",\"At noon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Dusk\' is the time when the sun sets, so the park closes at sunset.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phrases describes an action that happens during both light and dark hours?\",\"options\":[\"Without fail\",\"Day and night\",\"From dawn to dusk\",\"Every morning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Day and night\' includes both the daylight (day) and the darkness (night).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase would you use to describe a person who never forgets to do their duty?\",\"options\":[\"Day and night\",\"From dawn to dusk\",\"Without fail\",\"Sometimes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Without fail\' emphasizes the reliability and consistency of the person\'s actions.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21649,27,5,'English','en','The Little Babul Tree','[\"The little babul tree was unhappy because it had small leaves and sharp thorns.\",\"It wished for big leaves like the mango trees and got them the next day.\",\"A goat ate all the big leaves, making the tree sad again.\",\"Then it wished for gold leaves, which it got, but a thief stole them.\",\"Next, it wished for glass leaves, which it got, but a strong wind broke them.\",\"Finally, it wished for its original thorns and small leaves back.\",\"When it got its thorns and small leaves again, it felt truly happy.\",\"The story teaches that being happy with what you have is important.\",\"Goats do not eat thorns, thieves do not steal thorns, and wind does not harm small leaves.\",\"The little babul tree learned to accept itself and found real happiness.\",\"The story shows how wishes can bring temporary joy but not lasting happiness.\",\"Natural features like thorns and small leaves have their own usefulness.\",\"The tree’s journey reflects the value of contentment and self-acceptance.\",\"Each wish was fulfilled but led to a new problem, showing that greed brings trouble.\",\"The ending emphasizes inner happiness over external appearance.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where was the little babul tree located at the beginning of the story?\",\"options\":[\"In a forest of pine trees\",\"In a grove of mango trees\",\"In a garden of roses\",\"On a high mountain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'In a grove of mango trees, there was one little babul tree.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why did the little babul tree think children did not like it?\",\"options\":[\"Because it was too tall\",\"Because it had no flowers\",\"Because its thorns were sharp and stiff\",\"Because it had no fruit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The tree says, \'My thorns are sharp and stiff. Children do not like me.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how does the little tree in the center differ from the trees surrounding it?\",\"options\":[\"It is smaller and has different leaves\",\"It is much taller than the others\",\"It is covered in bright red flowers\",\"It has no branches at all\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a small babul tree with thin branches among larger, fuller mango trees.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/042_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the tree\'s big leaves that were \'just like the mango trees\'?\",\"options\":[\"They were stolen by a thief\",\"They were broken by the wind\",\"A goat came along and ate them\",\"They dried up in the sun\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'But a goat came along and ate up all the big leaves.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the babul tree wanted to prevent someone from stealing its leaves, which type of leaves should it NOT have chosen?\",\"options\":[\"Glass leaves\",\"Big green leaves\",\"Gold leaves\",\"Small thorny leaves\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that a thief came along and stole all the gold leaves.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the sun doing to the tree\'s new leaves?\",\"options\":[\"Burning the leaves\",\"Making the leaves shine\",\"Turning the leaves green\",\"Hiding behind the leaves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows rays coming off the glass leaves, and the text says \'See my leaves shine in the sun.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/043_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What sound did the strong wind make when it blew against the glass leaves?\",\"options\":[\"Whish-sh!\",\"Woo-oo!\",\"Rustle-rustle!\",\"Bang-bang!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions, \'“Woo-oo!” said the wind.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what has happened to the tree\'s glass leaves because of the wind?\",\"options\":[\"They turned into gold\",\"They grew into big green leaves\",\"They broke and fell to the ground\",\"They flew away into the sky\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the glass leaves shattered on the ground around the bare tree.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/043_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the babul tree eventually decide that its original thorns and small leaves were best?\",\"options\":[\"Because goats do not eat them and the wind does not harm them\",\"Because they were the prettiest leaves in the grove\",\"Because children finally started to like the thorns\",\"Because the mango trees told it to change back\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The tree realizes, \'Goats do not eat them all up... The wind will do them no harm.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, which material would be the most \'sturdy\' or \'safe\' for the babul tree\'s survival against all threats?\",\"options\":[\"Glass\",\"Gold\",\"Big soft leaves\",\"Small leaves and thorns\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The story shows that big leaves are eaten, gold is stolen, and glass is broken, while thorns remain safe.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'stiff\' as used to describe the tree\'s thorns?\",\"options\":[\"Soft and bendable\",\"Firm and difficult to bend\",\"Bright and colorful\",\"Very long and thin\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the context of thorns, \'stiff\' means they are rigid and firm.\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"At the very end of the story, how does the babul tree feel about its natural appearance?\",\"options\":[\"It is still unhappy and wants new leaves\",\"It is sad because it has no gold\",\"It is happier than it has ever been\",\"It is jealous of the mango trees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The final sentence is, \'“Oh, I never was so happy!” said the little babul tree.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Little Babul Tree\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'grove\'?\",\"options\":[\"A large city\",\"A small forest or wood\",\"A high mountain\",\"A deep river\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a grove as a small forest or wood.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the plural form of the word \'leaf\'?\",\"options\":[\"leafs\",\"leafes\",\"leaves\",\"leafing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the \'Read and remember\' section, one leaf becomes many leaves.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \'took away secretly\'?\",\"options\":[\"grove\",\"thorns\",\"stole\",\"sprang up\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'stole\' means to take something secretly (चोरले).\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the pair: one shelf – many _______.\",\"options\":[\"shelfs\",\"shelves\",\"shelvs\",\"shelfes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists the plural of shelf as shelves.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are \'thorns\' called in Marathi as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"पाने\",\"फुले\",\"काटे\",\"मुळे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the Marathi meaning of thorns as \'काटे\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct plural for \'knife\'?\",\"options\":[\"knifes\",\"knive\",\"knives\",\"knivs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows that the plural of knife is knives.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see many \'thieves\', how many are there if you see only \'one\'?\",\"options\":[\"thieve\",\"thief\",\"thiefs\",\"thiefes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The singular form of thieves is thief.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the pattern in the text, what is the plural of \'wolf\'?\",\"options\":[\"wolfs\",\"wolfes\",\"wolves\",\"wolvs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'one wolf – many wolves\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word follows the same plural pattern (changing \'f\' or \'fe\' to \'ves\') as \'life\'?\",\"options\":[\"grove\",\"thorns\",\"leaf\",\"stole\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Leaf changes to leaves, just as life changes to lives.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the correct singular-plural pair from the list provided in the text.\",\"options\":[\"one life – many lifes\",\"one thief – many thieves\",\"one shelf – many shelfs\",\"one knife – many knifes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'one thief – many thieves\' as a correct pair.\",\"topic\":\"Read and remember\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21650,27,5,'English','en','Lots of Things','[\"Phrases like \'a bundle of clothes\' and \'a bunch of flowers\' are used to group things together.\",\"A bundle means things tied or wrapped together, like sticks or clothes.\",\"A bunch means things growing or held together, like flowers, grapes, or keys.\",\"These phrases help us describe groups of objects in a simple way.\",\"We use \'a\' before singular bundle\\/bunch: a bundle, a bunch.\",\"Do not use \'bundles of\' or \'bunches of\' with these fixed phrases in this context.\",\"Examples: a bundle of sticks, a bunch of grapes, a chain of flowers.\",\"These are called collective phrases or grouping expressions.\",\"They make sentences more vivid and specific.\",\"Practice reading and copying such phrases to improve vocabulary.\",\"Use them in speaking and writing to describe what you see.\",\"They are common in English to talk about collections of similar items.\",\"Notice the pattern: article + noun (bundle\\/bunch) + of + plural noun.\",\"These help avoid saying \'many\' or \'several\' every time.\",\"Learn to recognize and use them correctly in sentences.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is a group of bees called?\",\"options\":[\"a pack of bees\",\"a swarm of bees\",\"a flock of bees\",\"a colony of bees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states \'a swarm of bees\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phrases - Set 4\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used to describe a group of cattle?\",\"options\":[\"herd\",\"flock\",\"grove\",\"team\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'a herd of cattle\' as the correct phrase.\",\"topic\":\"Phrases - Set 4\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which two animals can be called a \'flock\'?\",\"options\":[\"birds and bees\",\"geese and sheep\",\"dogs and ants\",\"cattle and birds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'a flock of geese\' and \'a flock of sheep\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phrases - Set 4\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used for both \'clothes\' and \'sticks\' in the phrases provided?\",\"options\":[\"bunch\",\"group\",\"bundle\",\"row\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'a bundle of clothes\' and \'a bundle of sticks\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phrases - Set 4\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see a group of ants working together, what phrase should you use?\",\"options\":[\"a swarm of ants\",\"a colony of ants\",\"a pack of ants\",\"a flight of ants\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies a group of ants as \'a colony of ants\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phrases - Set 4\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A group of players playing a match is called a ____.\",\"options\":[\"team\",\"crowd\",\"group\",\"list\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides the phrase \'a team of players\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phrases - Set 4\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these items can be described using the word \'bunch\'?\",\"options\":[\"bees, keys, and sticks\",\"flowers, keys, and grapes\",\"birds, geese, and sheep\",\"children, ants, and dogs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists a bunch of flowers, a bunch of keys, and a bunch of grapes.\",\"topic\":\"Phrases - Set 4\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific collective noun used for a group of trees?\",\"options\":[\"bundle\",\"grove\",\"row\",\"chain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the phrase \'a grove of trees\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phrases - Set 4\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase correctly describes a large number of people gathered together?\",\"options\":[\"a group of people\",\"a pack of people\",\"a crowd of people\",\"a team of people\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically uses \'a crowd of people\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phrases - Set 4\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is a group of birds called in the textbook list?\",\"options\":[\"a flock of birds\",\"a flight of birds\",\"a swarm of birds\",\"a pack of birds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins with the phrase \'a flight of birds\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phrases - Set 4\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21651,27,5,'English','en','Know your Body','[\"Our body has many parts, each with a special function.\",\"The heart keeps working even when we are sleeping.\",\"Babies are born with around 300 bones.\",\"As we grow, some bones fuse together.\",\"Adults have 206 bones in their body.\",\"Bones can grow back and repair themselves when broken.\",\"Doctors use a plaster-cast to help a broken bone heal properly.\",\"When we cough, air travels at about 9 kilometres per hour.\",\"A sound mind in a sound body means good health comes from both mental and physical well-being.\",\"Keeping our body and hair clean is part of good hygiene.\",\"Writing health messages and holding exhibitions helps spread awareness about hygiene.\",\"Exercise, rest, and cleanliness are important for maintaining good health.\",\"The skeletal system supports the body and protects internal organs.\",\"Bones are hard but living tissues that can repair themselves.\",\"Hygiene habits like washing hands and bathing prevent illness.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many bones do babies have in their body?\",\"options\":[\"206\",\"Around 300\",\"50,000\",\"Millions\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that babies have around 300 bones in their body.\",\"topic\":\"Senses and Bones\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many bones are there in the body of a grown-up?\",\"options\":[\"300\",\"50,000\",\"206\",\"Millions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, there are 206 bones in your body (referring to grown-ups).\",\"topic\":\"Senses and Bones\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the body keeps working even when you are sleeping?\",\"options\":[\"Eyes\",\"Bones\",\"Brain\",\"Nose\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the brain keeps working even when you are sleeping.\",\"topic\":\"Senses and Bones\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to a baby\'s bones as they grow up?\",\"options\":[\"They break apart\",\"They fuse together\",\"They stay the same\",\"They disappear\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that as babies grow up, the bones fuse together.\",\"topic\":\"Senses and Bones\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Even though we have two eyes, how many pictures do we see?\",\"options\":[\"Two pictures\",\"One picture\",\"Millions of pictures\",\"No picture\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that we have two eyes but we see one picture.\",\"topic\":\"Senses and Bones\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is true about the millions of bacteria on our skin?\",\"options\":[\"They are all harmful\",\"Most of them are harmless\",\"They only live on babies\",\"They help us see pictures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says there are millions of bacteria on our skin but most of them are harmless.\",\"topic\":\"Senses and Bones\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is identifying 50,000 different smells, which organ are they using?\",\"options\":[\"Skin\",\"Brain\",\"Eyes\",\"Nose\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states our nose can remember 50,000 different scents\\/smells.\",\"topic\":\"Senses and Bones\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A grown-up has fewer bones than a baby. Based on the text, why is this?\",\"options\":[\"Grown-ups lose bones as they age\",\"Bones fuse together as babies grow up\",\"Babies have 206 bones\",\"Grown-ups have 300 bones\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that bones fuse together as babies grow, resulting in fewer bones in grown-ups.\",\"topic\":\"Senses and Bones\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Compare the number of bones in a baby and a grown-up. Which statement is correct?\",\"options\":[\"Babies have more bones than grown-ups\",\"Grown-ups have more bones than babies\",\"Both have exactly 206 bones\",\"Both have exactly 300 bones\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Babies have around 300 bones while grown-ups have 206, so babies have more.\",\"topic\":\"Senses and Bones\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these facts from the text proves that our body parts are \'special\'?\",\"options\":[\"The brain stops working during sleep\",\"The nose can only remember ten smells\",\"We see one picture despite having two eyes\",\"All bacteria on the skin are dangerous\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'seeing one picture with two eyes\' as a special fact about our body.\",\"topic\":\"Senses and Bones\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the speed of air from a sneeze?\",\"options\":[\"95 kilometres per hour\",\"120 kilometres per hour\",\"160 kilometres per hour\",\"200 kilometres per hour\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that air from our sneeze can travel at a speed of about 160 kilometres per hour.\",\"topic\":\"Sneeze and Cough\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the speed of air when we cough?\",\"options\":[\"About 95 kilometres per hour\",\"About 160 kilometres per hour\",\"About 50 kilometres per hour\",\"About 10 kilometres per hour\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that air from a cough travels at about 95 kilometres per hour.\",\"topic\":\"Sneeze and Cough\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the blood a little while after the skin is cut?\",\"options\":[\"It stops flowing and dries up\",\"It clots\",\"It turns into new skin immediately\",\"It flows faster\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says that after a little while, the blood clots.\",\"topic\":\"Sneeze and Cough\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What forms on a cut before the new skin appears?\",\"options\":[\"A plaster-cast\",\"A bone\",\"A scab\",\"A bruise\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that a scab forms on the cut, and after it falls off, there is new skin under it.\",\"topic\":\"Sneeze and Cough\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child breaks a leg bone, what will a doctor use to help it grow properly?\",\"options\":[\"A bandage\",\"A scab\",\"A plaster-cast\",\"New skin\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that doctors use a plaster-cast to help a broken bone grow properly.\",\"topic\":\"Sneeze and Cough\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Comparing a sneeze and a cough, which one has air traveling at a higher speed?\",\"options\":[\"A cough\",\"A sneeze\",\"Both have the same speed\",\"Neither has a measurable speed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A sneeze (160 km\\/h) is faster than a cough (95 km\\/h).\",\"topic\":\"Sneeze and Cough\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the scab after a few days?\",\"options\":[\"It turns into a bone\",\"It becomes a plaster-cast\",\"It falls off\",\"It starts bleeding\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that after a few days, the scab falls off.\",\"topic\":\"Sneeze and Cough\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is found directly under a scab when it falls off?\",\"options\":[\"A broken bone\",\"New skin\",\"Flowing blood\",\"A plaster-cast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'There is new skin under the scab!\'\",\"topic\":\"Sneeze and Cough\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a car is driving at 100 kilometres per hour, which bodily action is faster than the car?\",\"options\":[\"A cough\",\"A sneeze\",\"Blood flowing\",\"A bone growing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A sneeze travels at 160 km\\/h, which is faster than 100 km\\/h, while a cough is only 95 km\\/h.\",\"topic\":\"Sneeze and Cough\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement best describes how the body handles a broken bone?\",\"options\":[\"The body cannot fix bones\",\"The bone stays broken forever\",\"The bone grows again and repairs itself\",\"The bone turns into a scab\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'A broken bone grows again and repairs itself.\'\",\"topic\":\"Sneeze and Cough\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should we eat along with vegetables?\",\"options\":[\"Junk food\",\"Fruits\",\"Sweets\",\"Spices\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that we should eat fruits and vegetables.\",\"topic\":\"Taking Care of Our Body\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How often should we wear clean clothes?\",\"options\":[\"Once a week\",\"Every day\",\"Every two days\",\"Only on holidays\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions we should wear clean clothes every day.\",\"topic\":\"Taking Care of Our Body\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific saying mentioned at the beginning of the text?\",\"options\":[\"A fast mind in a fast body\",\"A sound mind in a sound body\",\"A clean mind in a clean body\",\"A strong mind in a strong body\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins with the proverb \'A sound mind in a sound body.\'\",\"topic\":\"Taking Care of Our Body\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text suggest about the timing of our meals?\",\"options\":[\"We should eat only when we are very hungry\",\"We should eat only at night\",\"We should eat well at regular times\",\"We should eat once a day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says we should eat well at regular times.\",\"topic\":\"Taking Care of Our Body\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should we do to our nails to take care of our body?\",\"options\":[\"Paint them\",\"Grow them long\",\"Cut them regularly\",\"Bite them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states we should cut our nails regularly.\",\"topic\":\"Taking Care of Our Body\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides water and exercise, what else does the text say we need \'enough\' of?\",\"options\":[\"Sleep\",\"Toys\",\"Money\",\"Games\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions we should get enough sleep, water, and exercise.\",\"topic\":\"Taking Care of Our Body\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Rahul is coughing, what action should he take according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Run away from others\",\"Cover his mouth\",\"Close his eyes\",\"Drink cold water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text advises to cover our mouth when we cough or sneeze.\",\"topic\":\"Taking Care of Our Body\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To maintain personal hygiene for the head, what does the text tell us to keep clean?\",\"options\":[\"Hair\",\"Hats\",\"Ears\",\"Face\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifically says we should keep our body and hair clean.\",\"topic\":\"Taking Care of Our Body\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs are mentioned together as things we must keep clean?\",\"options\":[\"Hands and feet\",\"Body and hair\",\"Books and bags\",\"Shoes and socks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text groups \'body and hair\' together regarding cleanliness.\",\"topic\":\"Taking Care of Our Body\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does the author describe our body in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Small\",\"Difficult\",\"Wonderful\",\"Heavy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states \'Our body is so wonderful.\'\",\"topic\":\"Taking Care of Our Body\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21652,27,5,'English','en','Alyonushka','[\"Alyonushka is a girl who lives with her parents and baby brother Ivanushka.\",\"Her parents go to work and ask her to look after Ivanushka.\",\"Alyonushka forgets her duty and plays with friends, leaving Ivanushka alone.\",\"Birds take Ivanushka away while Alyonushka is distracted.\",\"Alyonushka feels sad and decides to bring her brother back.\",\"She chases the birds and meets an oven, apple tree, and milk river.\",\"Each asks her to eat something first before helping: oven wants wheat bread, apple tree wants a wild apple, milk river wants milk.\",\"At home, Alyonushka’s family does not eat wheat cakes, garden apples, or cream, so she hesitates.\",\"She overcomes her hesitation, eats what is offered, and each helps her find the way.\",\"She reaches Baba Yaga’s hut on hen’s feet, where the witch has Ivanushka.\",\"Baba Yaga calls geese to chase Alyonushka and Ivanushka.\",\"The milk river, apple tree, and oven hide the children from the geese when asked.\",\"Alyonushka bravely takes her brother and runs home.\",\"The story teaches responsibility, courage, and kindness.\",\"Helping others and saying sorry can lead to support in difficult times.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who did Alyonushka live with according to the story?\",\"options\":[\"Only her baby brother\",\"Her father, mother, and baby brother\",\"Her friends and her brother\",\"Her grandmother and grandfather\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Alyonushka lived with her father, mother, and baby brother Ivanushka.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the name of Alyonushka\'s baby brother?\",\"options\":[\"Alyonushka\",\"Ivanushka\",\"Geese\",\"Ivan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the baby brother\'s name is Ivanushka.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Alyonushka\'s parents leave the house?\",\"options\":[\"To go to the market\",\"To play with friends\",\"To go out to work\",\"To catch some geese\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mother said, \'Daughter, we are going out to work.\'\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Alyonushka seat her baby brother before she went to play?\",\"options\":[\"On a chair\",\"In the house\",\"On the grass\",\"Under a tree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says she seated her baby brother on the grass.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'clean forgot\' mean in the context of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Forgot after cleaning the house\",\"Completely and totally forgot\",\"Remembered only a little bit\",\"Forgot to wash her hands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'clean forgot\' means she completely forgot her mother\'s instructions.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of birds swooped down and took the baby?\",\"options\":[\"A flock of crows\",\"A flock of ducks\",\"A flock of geese\",\"A flock of eagles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the birds as a flock of geese.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Alyonushka unable to catch the birds?\",\"options\":[\"She was too tired to run\",\"The birds flew faster and faster\",\"Her friends stopped her from running\",\"She did not know which way they went\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the birds flew faster and faster and were soon out of sight.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, what was Alyonushka\'s main mistake?\",\"options\":[\"She did not like her brother\",\"She left the house without permission\",\"She failed to look after her brother as told\",\"She invited the geese to the garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Alyonushka forgot her mother\'s instruction to look after her baby brother and went to play instead.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Alyonushka call the birds \'wicked\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they were flying too fast\",\"Because they were making a lot of noise\",\"Because they took her baby brother away\",\"Because they were black in color\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"She calls them wicked because they swooped down and kidnapped her brother.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If Alyonushka had been a \'good girl\' as her mother asked, what would she have done?\",\"options\":[\"Played with her friends all day\",\"Stayed and watched over Ivanushka\",\"Gone to work with her parents\",\"Fed the flock of geese\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Being a \'good girl\' in this context meant following the instruction to look after her baby brother.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many geese are shown flying in the sky?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows exactly four geese flying.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/048_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the baby doing as he is being carried away?\",\"options\":[\"He is sleeping soundly\",\"He is laughing at the birds\",\"He is crying with his mouth open\",\"He is trying to fly like a bird\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the baby with tears and an open mouth, indicating he is crying.\",\"topic\":\"Alyonushka\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/048_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What did Alyonushka do immediately after she stopped weeping and got up?\",\"options\":[\"She went back home to sleep.\",\"She decided to bring back her baby brother.\",\"She started eating wheat cakes.\",\"She asked the birds for help.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that after sobbing and weeping, she got up and said, \'I must bring back my baby brother.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Oven\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What condition did the oven set before telling Alyonushka where the geese had flown?\",\"options\":[\"She had to bring some wood.\",\"She had to clean the oven.\",\"She had to eat a slice of its wheat bread.\",\"She had to sing a song.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The oven said, \'Eat a slice of my wheat bread first\' when asked for directions.\",\"topic\":\"The Oven\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the oven keep quiet when Alyonushka first asked for help?\",\"options\":[\"The oven was broken and could not speak.\",\"The oven did not know where the geese went.\",\"Alyonushka refused to eat the wheat bread and spoke rudely about it.\",\"The oven was waiting for the birds to return.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"After Alyonushka rudely compared the oven\'s bread to what they eat at home, the oven kept quiet.\",\"topic\":\"The Oven\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Alyonushka\'s decision to turn back and apologize show about her character?\",\"options\":[\"She was hungry and wanted a free meal.\",\"She realized her mistake and was determined to find her brother.\",\"She was afraid of the oven.\",\"She wanted to show off her manners.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Her apology shows she realized that being polite and following the oven\'s request was necessary to get help for her brother.\",\"topic\":\"The Oven\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what do Alyonushka\'s family members \'not eat even\' at home?\",\"options\":[\"Wheat bread\",\"Wheat cakes\",\"Rye bread\",\"Corn cakes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Alyonushka says, \'At home, we don’t eat even wheat cakes.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Oven\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happened after Alyonushka finally ate the slice of wheat bread?\",\"options\":[\"The oven fell asleep.\",\"The oven showed her the way.\",\"The oven gave her more bread for the journey.\",\"The geese flew back to her.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Alyonushka ate a slice of the wheat bread and the oven showed her the way.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Oven\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Alyonushka had continued to run without apologizing to the oven, what would most likely have been the result based on the story?\",\"options\":[\"She would have found the geese immediately.\",\"The oven would have chased her.\",\"She would not have received the directions she needed from the oven.\",\"The birds would have come back to help her.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The oven only helped her after she apologized and ate the bread; without it, she lacked the necessary guidance.\",\"topic\":\"The Oven\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the oven holding inside its opening that it wants Alyonushka to eat?\",\"options\":[\"A bowl of porridge\",\"A slice of wheat bread\",\"A whole wheat cake\",\"A small bird\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a piece of bread inside the oven, which corresponds to the \'slice of wheat bread\' mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"The Oven\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/049_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, how is the oven depicted as a character rather than just an object?\",\"options\":[\"It has a chimney with smoke.\",\"It has eyes and a mouth-like opening.\",\"It is painted in bright colors.\",\"It is standing on two legs.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the oven with eyes and a mouth, giving it a human-like appearance to show it can talk.\",\"topic\":\"The Oven\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/049_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes Alyonushka\'s feeling when she says, \'I must bring back my baby brother\'?\",\"options\":[\"Careless\",\"Determined\",\"Angry\",\"Fearful\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'I must\' indicates a strong sense of duty and determination to fix the situation.\",\"topic\":\"The Oven\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What did Alyonushka ask the apple tree?\",\"options\":[\"Where the geese have flown\",\"Where her brother was hiding\",\"How to grow garden apples\",\"If she could have some water\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states Alyonushka asked, \'Apple Tree, Apple Tree, tell me where the geese have flown.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Apple Tree\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of apples did the tree offer Alyonushka?\",\"options\":[\"Garden apples\",\"Sweet apples\",\"Wild apples\",\"Red apples\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The apple tree specifically asked her to \'Eat one of my wild apples first.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Apple Tree\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the apple tree keep quiet at first?\",\"options\":[\"It was sleeping\",\"Alyonushka refused to eat its apple\",\"It did not know where the geese were\",\"It was afraid of the geese\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The tree kept quiet because Alyonushka initially refused to eat the wild apple, comparing it poorly to garden apples.\",\"topic\":\"The Apple Tree\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to Alyonushka, what is the eating habit at her home?\",\"options\":[\"They only eat wild apples\",\"They don\'t eat even garden apples\",\"They eat apples every day\",\"They prefer wild apples over garden ones\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Alyonushka says, \'At home, we don’t