 realized she must not refuse if she wanted the river to help her find the way.\",\"topic\":\"The Milk River\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what happened after Alyonushka had some milk?\",\"options\":[\"The river gave her some cream\",\"The geese flew back to her\",\"The milk river showed her the way\",\"She fell asleep by the river\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'So she had some milk and the milk river showed her the way.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Milk River\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the color of the river which represents what it is made of?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"White\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The river is shown in white to represent that it is a \'milk river\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Milk River\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/049_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Alyonushka doing as she stands by the river?\",\"options\":[\"She is drinking milk with a glass\",\"She is looking at the river and speaking\",\"She is swimming in the milk\",\"She is running away from the river\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The drawing shows Alyonushka looking down at the river with her mouth open as if she is talking to it.\",\"topic\":\"The Milk River\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/049_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does Alyonushka\'s action of thanking the river and running on suggest about her situation?\",\"options\":[\"She is in a hurry to find the geese\",\"She wants to stay and play by the river\",\"She is tired and wants to go home\",\"She is looking for more milk\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Her thanking the river and immediately running on shows she is focused and urgent about her mission.\",\"topic\":\"The Milk River\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If Alyonushka had been rude to the milk river, what is the most likely outcome based on the story\'s logic?\",\"options\":[\"The river would have given her cream instead\",\"The river would not have helped her find the geese\",\"The geese would have appeared automatically\",\"She would have reached home faster\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The river only helped her after she followed its request, implying cooperation was necessary.\",\"topic\":\"The Milk River\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Alyonushka find the hut?\",\"options\":[\"In the middle of a field\",\"At the edge of a wood\",\"Near a wide river\",\"Inside a deep cave\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states she saw a hut at the edge of a wood.\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the hut standing on?\",\"options\":[\"Wooden poles\",\"Large wheels\",\"Hen\'s feet\",\"Stone pillars\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the hut as being \'on hen’s feet\'.\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who was sitting inside the hut?\",\"options\":[\"Alyonushka\'s father\",\"A little bird\",\"Ivanushka\",\"Baba Yaga, the witch\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that \'Inside the hut sat Baba Yaga, the witch.\'\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was Ivanushka doing when Alyonushka saw him?\",\"options\":[\"Eating an apple\",\"Sleeping in a corner\",\"Playing with a toy\",\"Crying loudly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says Alyonushka saw Ivanushka \'sleeping in a corner\'.\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the hut doing when Alyonushka first saw it?\",\"options\":[\"It was flying away\",\"It was turning round and round\",\"It was growing taller\",\"It was making a loud noise\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the hut as \'turning round and round\'.\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Alyonushka go inside the hut even though she was frightened?\",\"options\":[\"To hide from the witch\",\"To find some food\",\"To take her baby brother\",\"To rest for a while\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Alyonushka tells Baba Yaga, \'I have come to take my baby brother.\'\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did Baba Yaga react when Alyonushka said she came for her brother?\",\"options\":[\"She started crying\",\"She helped her carry him\",\"She laughed at her\",\"She fell asleep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says Baba Yaga laughed \'He-he-he!\' when Alyonushka spoke.\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Alyonushka do immediately after picking up Ivanushka?\",\"options\":[\"She hid under the bed\",\"She jumped out of the hut and ran\",\"She started to cook dinner\",\"She asked the witch for directions\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states she picked him up, jumped out, and began to run home.\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, which word best describes Alyonushka\'s decision to enter the witch\'s hut?\",\"options\":[\"Lazy\",\"Brave\",\"Careless\",\"Greedy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Entering a witch\'s hut while frightened to save a brother shows bravery.\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what part of the hut is shown that allows it to move as described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The pointed roof\",\"The small window\",\"The hen\'s feet\",\"The wooden door\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the hut standing on hen\'s feet, which the text says allows it to turn.\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/050_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where is the hut located?\",\"options\":[\"In a clearing surrounded by trees\",\"On a beach by the sea\",\"In the middle of a village\",\"On top of a snowy mountain\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the hut in an open space with many trees behind it, matching the \'edge of a wood\' description.\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/050_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the turning of the hut important for Alyonushka?\",\"options\":[\"It made her feel dizzy\",\"It allowed her to see Ivanushka inside\",\"It helped her find the path home\",\"It scared the witch away\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'as the hut turned, Alyonushka saw Ivanushka\'.\",\"topic\":\"Baba Yaga\'s Hut\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who called up the geese to bring the children back?\",\"options\":[\"The Milk River\",\"Baba Yaga the witch\",\"The Apple Tree\",\"Father and Mother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Baba Yaga the witch called up the geese.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the children hide first when Alyonushka ran away?\",\"options\":[\"In the oven\",\"Under the apple tree\",\"In the milk river\",\"Inside their home\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Alyonushka first came to the milk river and asked it to hide them.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where specifically did the apple tree hide the children?\",\"options\":[\"Under its roots\",\"Behind its trunk\",\"In its branches\",\"Under its leaves\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Quickly, the apple tree hid the children in its branches.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the geese turn back the first time they chased the children?\",\"options\":[\"They were tired of flying\",\"They couldn\'t find the children\",\"Baba Yaga called them back\",\"It started to rain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the geese turned back because they couldn\'t find the children in the milk river.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was Alyonushka doing while she was running away from the geese?\",\"options\":[\"Carrying a basket of apples\",\"Singing a song\",\"Holding her brother\",\"Looking for her parents\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Holding her brother, Alyonushka ran and ran\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the geese do when they reached the oven?\",\"options\":[\"They flew round and round and up and down\",\"They sat on top of the oven\",\"They went inside the oven\",\"They flew straight back to the witch\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says the geese \'flew round and round and up and down\' near the oven.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which action word describes how Alyonushka moved out of the oven?\",\"options\":[\"Jumped\",\"Walked\",\"Crawled\",\"Ran\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically uses the word \'crawled\' to describe her leaving the oven.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, where did the children go immediately after leaving the oven?\",\"options\":[\"Back to the apple tree\",\"To the milk river\",\"To find Baba Yaga\",\"Home\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says she crawled out of the oven and \'ran home with him\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct sequence of objects that helped Alyonushka hide?\",\"options\":[\"Apple Tree -> Milk River -> Oven\",\"Milk River -> Apple Tree -> Oven\",\"Oven -> Apple Tree -> Milk River\",\"Milk River -> Oven -> Apple Tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The story follows the sequence: Milk River first, then Apple Tree, and finally the Oven.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the geese finally fly back to Baba Yaga at the end of the search?\",\"options\":[\"Because the sun was setting\",\"Because they saw the parents coming\",\"Because it was no use searching anymore\",\"Because the children reached home\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'it was no use\' and \'At last, they turned and flew back to Baba Yaga.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who arrived at the house shortly after Alyonushka and her brother got back?\",\"options\":[\"Baba Yaga\",\"The Geese\",\"Father and Mother\",\"The Milk River\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text ends by saying \'before long, Father and Mother came home too.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which character shows the most responsibility for the baby brother\'s safety?\",\"options\":[\"The Geese\",\"Alyonushka\",\"Baba Yaga\",\"The Oven\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Alyonushka is the one who carries her brother and asks for help to hide him from the witch\'s geese.\",\"topic\":\"The Escape\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21653,27,5,'English','en','One Thing at a Time','[\"The poem \'One Thing at a Time\' teaches focus and concentration.\",\"It advises doing one task fully before starting another.\",\"The poem uses simple rhymes to make the message easy to remember.\",\"Key idea: Avoid distractions while working, studying, playing, or eating.\",\"Rhyming words help in learning pronunciation and memory.\",\"The poem is from the English curriculum for Standard 5.\",\"Students are encouraged to recite the poem aloud.\",\"It promotes discipline and mindfulness in daily activities.\",\"The tone is gentle and advisory, not commanding.\",\"Repetition of \'one thing at a time\' reinforces the central message.\",\"The poem links focus to better outcomes in tasks.\",\"It is part of Unit Three in the textbook.\",\"Students are asked to find rhyming word pairs from the poem.\",\"They are also asked to recall lines from earlier English books.\",\"The poem supports language development through rhythm and repetition.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the author of the poem \'One Thing at a Time\'?\",\"options\":[\"R. L. Stevenson\",\"M. A. Stodart\",\"William Wordsworth\",\"Anonymous\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions M. A. Stodart at the end of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing at a Time\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is described as a \'very good rule\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Working and playing together\",\"Doing many things at once\",\"One thing at a time\",\"Playing all day long\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'One thing at a time... Is a very good rule\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing at a Time\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what should you do while you play?\",\"options\":[\"Think about work\",\"Play\",\"Rest\",\"Do things by halves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Play while you play\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing at a Time\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet say about \'things done by halves\'?\",\"options\":[\"They are done quickly\",\"They are always useful\",\"They are never done right\",\"They are done with might\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Things done by halves are never done right\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing at a Time\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of working while you work and playing while you play?\",\"options\":[\"Being useful and happy\",\"Being tired and sad\",\"Being rich and famous\",\"Being busy and worried\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'To be useful and happy, That is the way.\'\",\"topic\":\"One Thing at a Time\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'Do with your might\' mean in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Do it slowly\",\"Do it with all your strength and effort\",\"Do it only if you want to\",\"Do it with someone\'s help\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'might\' refers to using one\'s full power or effort to complete a task.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing at a Time\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is eating lunch and trying to solve a math problem at the same time, which advice from the poem are they ignoring?\",\"options\":[\"Do with your might\",\"Play while you play\",\"One thing at a time\",\"Moments should never be trifled away\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Doing two different tasks at once goes against the rule of \'One thing at a time\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing at a Time\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A girl is cleaning her room but stops every two minutes to look out the window. How would the poet describe her work?\",\"options\":[\"Done with might\",\"Done by halves\",\"Done well\",\"Useful and happy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Stopping frequently means the task is not being done with full focus, which is doing it \'by halves\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing at a Time\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet say \'Moments should never be trifled away\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because time is not important\",\"Because we should always be playing\",\"To emphasize that every moment should be used properly for the task at hand\",\"To show that work is better than play\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Trifling away moments means wasting time; the poet wants us to focus on the current activity.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing at a Time\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message regarding how tasks should be completed to ensure they are \'done right\'?\",\"options\":[\"They should be done quickly\",\"They should be done with full effort and one at a time\",\"They should be done while playing\",\"They should be done by many people\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem combines the ideas of doing things with \'might\' and \'one thing at a time\' to do them \'well\' and \'right\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing at a Time\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many words are listed in Exercise 2 for which you need to find rhyming words?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"6\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists six words: play, might, well, you, one, and should.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Exercise 3, in which book did you previously learn four lines of this poem?\",\"options\":[\"My English Book Three\",\"My English Book Four\",\"My English Book Five\",\"Marathi Sulabhbharati\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Exercise 3 specifically mentions \'My English Book Four\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first word listed in the rhyming activity in Exercise 2?\",\"options\":[\"might\",\"well\",\"play\",\"you\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The list of words in Exercise 2 starts with the word \'play\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the Marathi instruction \'शब्द लक्षपूर्वक ऐका\' mean in English?\",\"options\":[\"Write the words carefully\",\"Find the words quickly\",\"Listen to the word carefully\",\"Read the words aloud\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the English translation \'Listen to the word carefully\' for the Marathi instruction.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"After finding the rhyming words, what is the final step mentioned in Exercise 2?\",\"options\":[\"Draw a picture\",\"Write down the pairs of rhyming words\",\"Recite the poem\",\"Find the meaning of the words\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Write down these pairs of rhyming words.\'\",\"topic\":\"Reference Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is NOT included in the list of words to find rhymes for in Exercise 2?\",\"options\":[\"might\",\"should\",\"one\",\"time\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The words listed are play, might, well, you, one, and should. \'Time\' is not in that specific list.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the instructions in Exercise 3, how many lines are you looking for in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Four\",\"Six\",\"Ten\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Exercise 3 asks to find \'four of these lines\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem \'One Thing at a Time\', which word from the list rhymes with \'tell\'?\",\"options\":[\"play\",\"well\",\"might\",\"one\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the poem, \'well\' rhymes with \'tell\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the Marathi translation for the instruction \'Find them\' as used in Exercise 3?\",\"options\":[\"त्या लिहा\",\"त्या वाचा\",\"त्या शोधा\",\"त्या ऐका\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'त्या शोधा\' as the Marathi equivalent for \'Find them\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list in Exercise 2 rhymes with \'right\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"might\",\"well\",\"should\",\"you\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the poem, \'might\' rhymes with \'right\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Activity\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21654,27,5,'English','en','Pen-friends','[\"Pen-friends are friends who write letters to each other regularly.\",\"Pen-friends usually write in English to practice the language.\",\"You can find a pen-friend in another class or school.\",\"Start a letter with a greeting like \'Hello\' or \'Excuse me\'.\",\"Introduce yourself by name, class, and section.\",\"Share personal details like name, address, and birthday.\",\"Talk about your favourite things: colour, game, subject, teacher, book, movie, TV show, dish.\",\"Mention your best friend in school.\",\"Share your hobbies and what you enjoy the most.\",\"Tell about the people in your family.\",\"Be polite and avoid starting quarrels in letters.\",\"Writing letters helps improve English writing and communication skills.\",\"Always end a letter with a closing like \'Thanks a lot\' or \'Never mind\'.\",\"Pen-friendship builds friendship and cultural understanding.\",\"Regular letter writing helps develop a habit of expressing thoughts in writing.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what do \'pen-friends\' do regularly?\",\"options\":[\"Play games together\",\"Write letters to each other\",\"Study in the same class\",\"Go to the same school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'pen-friends\' as friends who write letters to each other regularly.\",\"topic\":\"Step 1 : Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which language must the pen-friends write their letters?\",\"options\":[\"Marathi\",\"Hindi\",\"English\",\"Sanskrit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically states, \'We have to write letters in English.\'\",\"topic\":\"Step 1 : Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the instructions in the text, which standard should your pen-friend be from?\",\"options\":[\"Std IV or Std V\",\"Std V or Std VI\",\"Std VI or Std VII\",\"Std VII or Std VIII\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks to find a pen-friend studying in Std VI or Std VII.\",\"topic\":\"Step 1 : Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct way to introduce your class according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"I am in fifth \'A\'.\",\"I am fifth standard.\",\"My standard is five.\",\"I study in five class.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides the example phrase: \'I am in fifth \'A\'.\' or \'I am in the fifth standard.\'\",\"topic\":\"Step 1 : Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a polite way to start a conversation with a potential pen-friend?\",\"options\":[\"Give me a letter.\",\"Excuse me.\",\"Who are you?\",\"Write to me.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests starting the introduction with \'Excuse me\' or \'Hello\'.\",\"topic\":\"Step 1 : Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should you say if someone says \'No, I\'m sorry!\' to your request to be pen-friends?\",\"options\":[\"That\'s great!\",\"Thanks a lot.\",\"Never mind.\",\"Oh, yes.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests saying \'All right! \\/ Never mind.\' if the person refuses.\",\"topic\":\"Step 1 : Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student agrees to be your pen-friend by saying \'Oh, yes\', what is an appropriate response to show your joy?\",\"options\":[\"I\'m sorry!\",\"Never mind.\",\"That\'s great!\",\"Excuse me.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'That\'s great! Thanks a lot.\' as the response to an acceptance.\",\"topic\":\"Step 1 : Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which phrase is used to ask someone to be your pen-friend?\",\"options\":[\"Are you my friend?\",\"Do you like letters?\",\"Would you like to be my \'pen-friend\'?\",\"Can you write in English?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly uses the question: \'Would you like to be my \'pen-friend\'?\'\",\"topic\":\"Step 1 : Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the girl on the left doing?\",\"options\":[\"Agreeing to be a pen-friend\",\"Declining the request politely\",\"Asking for a pen\",\"Writing a letter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The girl on the left says \'No, I\'m sorry!\', which is a polite way to decline.\",\"topic\":\"Step 1 : Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/054_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which phrase is used by the girl in the center to respond to the girl on the right?\",\"options\":[\"All right!\",\"Never mind.\",\"That\'s great!\",\"I\'m sorry!\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The speech bubble pointing towards the girl who said \'Oh, yes\' contains the phrase \'That\'s great! Thanks a lot.\'\",\"topic\":\"Step 1 : Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/054_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first piece of information requested in \'Step 2: Exchanging information\'?\",\"options\":[\"Name and address\",\"Favorite color\",\"Hobby\",\"Birthday\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text begins by asking for the person\'s name and address.\",\"topic\":\"Step 2 : Exchanging information\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT listed as a \'Favourite thing\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Favourite book\",\"Favourite movie\",\"Favourite animal\",\"Favourite dish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists book, movie, and dish, but does not mention \'favourite animal\'.\",\"topic\":\"Step 2 : Exchanging information\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What specific school-related person are you asked to name in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The Principal\",\"Your best friend in school\",\"The school peon\",\"The librarian\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly asks, \'Who is your best friend in school?\'\",\"topic\":\"Step 2 : Exchanging information\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should you tell your pen-friend about your home life?\",\"options\":[\"The size of your house\",\"The number of rooms\",\"The people in your family\",\"Your neighbor\'s name\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks to \'Tell me about the people in your family.\'\",\"topic\":\"Step 2 : Exchanging information\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What information is requested regarding the day you were born?\",\"options\":[\"Place of birth\",\"Time of birth\",\"When is your birthday?\",\"Your current age\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks, \'When is your birthday?\'\",\"topic\":\"Step 2 : Exchanging information\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to talk about your leisure activities or interests, which question from the text should you answer?\",\"options\":[\"What is your hobby?\",\"What is your favorite subject?\",\"Who is your best friend?\",\"What is your name?\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A hobby refers to activities done for pleasure during leisure time.\",\"topic\":\"Step 2 : Exchanging information\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a pen-friend asks you about your \'favourite dish\', what information are they looking for?\",\"options\":[\"Your favorite plate\",\"Your favorite type of food\",\"Your favorite game\",\"Your favorite TV show\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'dish\' refers to a specific type of prepared food.\",\"topic\":\"Step 2 : Exchanging information\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What advice does the text give regarding quarrels or fights?\",\"options\":[\"Never talk to anyone\",\"Be the first to start a quarrel\",\"Be the last one to start a quarrel\",\"Always win every quarrel\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes with the advice: \'Be the last one to start a quarrel.\'\",\"topic\":\"Step 2 : Exchanging information\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these categories is mentioned for \'Favourite things\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Favourite song\",\"Favourite TV programme\",\"Favourite clothes\",\"Favourite fruit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically lists \'Favourite TV programme\' as one of the items.\",\"topic\":\"Step 2 : Exchanging information\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is a personal detail you are encouraged to share to build a friendship?\",\"options\":[\"Your bank balance\",\"Your name and address\",\"Your secret password\",\"Your phone\'s brand name\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text starts by asking for name and address as basic information for pen-friends.\",\"topic\":\"Step 2 : Exchanging information\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the third step (Step 3) men