laughed\' after being thrown in the river, how was he feeling?\",\"options\":[\"Scared\",\"Sad\",\"Happy\",\"Angry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Laughing indicates that the turtle was happy or amused because his plan worked.\",\"topic\":\"चतुर कासव\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these punishments did the turtle NOT mention as an alternative to the river?\",\"options\":[\"Hanging him\",\"Whipping him\",\"Burning him\",\"Drowning him\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The turtle mentioned hanging, whipping, burning, and pushing from a cliff, but not drowning.\",\"topic\":\"चतुर कासव\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the turtle described as \'clever\' in the title of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Because he was faster than the villagers\",\"Because he escaped by tricking the chief into doing exactly what he wanted\",\"Because he lived in a field instead of a river\",\"Because he could speak the villagers\' language\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"His cleverness is shown through his ability to manipulate the chief to gain his freedom.\",\"topic\":\"चतुर कासव\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word is already provided in the third section of the puzzle?\",\"options\":[\"he\",\"top\",\"busy\",\"turtle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The third section of the puzzle image shows the word \'busy\'.\",\"topic\":\"चतुर कासव\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/061_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, looking at the first section, how many letters are required for the word in the step immediately following \'he\'?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The step after \'he\' shows three empty circles, indicating a three-letter word is needed.\",\"topic\":\"चतुर कासव\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/061_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What was the final outcome for the turtle after the chief\'s order?\",\"options\":[\"He was punished by the villagers\",\"He was cooked by the chief\",\"He swam away merrily\",\"He was pushed from a cliff\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text ends by saying the turtle laughed and swam away merrily.\",\"topic\":\"चतुर कासव\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the author of the poem about the grizzly bear?\",\"options\":[\"Mary Hunter Austin\",\"Ramanujan\",\"The CM\",\"New Zealand\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'- Mary Hunter Austin\' at the end of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"बातम्या\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what must you never ask a grizzly bear?\",\"options\":[\"What his name is\",\"Where he is going\",\"If he wants to play\",\"How he moves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states: \'You must never, never, never ask him where He is going\'.\",\"topic\":\"बातम्या\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet say will happen if you dare to stop a grizzly bear?\",\"options\":[\"He will take you to a science fair\",\"He will give you a prize\",\"You will never meet another grizzly bear\",\"He will tell you where he is going\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem warns: \'For if you ever, ever dare To stop a grizzly bear, You will never meet another grizzly bear.\'\",\"topic\":\"बातम्या\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the CM visit the Science Fair?\",\"options\":[\"Chakan\",\"Lohgaon\",\"Nagar\",\"Scotland\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The headline reads: \'CM VISITS SCIENCE FAIR AT NAGAR\'.\",\"topic\":\"बातम्या\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many people were injured in the road accident near Chakan?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"None\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The headline states: \'TWO INJURED IN ROAD ACCIDENT NEAR CHAKAN\'.\",\"topic\":\"बातम्या\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which student bagged the Ramanujan Prize?\",\"options\":[\"A student from Nagar\",\"A student from Chakan\",\"A student from Lohgaon\",\"A student from Scotland\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The headline says: \'LOHGAON STUDENT BAGS RAMANUJAN PRIZE\'.\",\"topic\":\"बातम्या\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the World Cup 2015 news, which team beat Scotland?\",\"options\":[\"New Zealand\",\"Lohgaon\",\"Nagar\",\"Chakan\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The headline states: \'New Zealand beat Scotland by 3 wickets\'.\",\"topic\":\"बातम्या\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"By how many wickets did New Zealand win the match?\",\"options\":[\"2 wickets\",\"3 wickets\",\"5 wickets\",\"10 wickets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the win was \'by 3 wickets\'.\",\"topic\":\"बातम्या\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these headlines is related to a sports event?\",\"options\":[\"CM VISITS SCIENCE FAIR AT NAGAR\",\"TWO INJURED IN ROAD ACCIDENT NEAR CHAKAN\",\"LOHGAON STUDENT BAGS RAMANUJAN PRIZE\",\"World Cup 2015 : New Zealand beat Scotland by 3 wickets\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The mention of \'World Cup\' and \'wickets\' indicates a sports (cricket) news item.\",\"topic\":\"बातम्या\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which headline reports a positive achievement by an individual student?\",\"options\":[\"CM VISITS SCIENCE FAIR AT NAGAR\",\"TWO INJURED IN ROAD ACCIDENT NEAR CHAKAN\",\"LOHGAON STUDENT BAGS RAMANUJAN PRIZE\",\"World Cup 2015 : New Zealand beat Scotland by 3 wickets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Winning a prize (Ramanujan Prize) is a personal achievement for the student.\",\"topic\":\"बातम्या\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21656,27,5,'English','en','Location Games / Texts','[\"Location games involve finding places using clues or maps.\",\"Direction words like north, south, east, west help describe where things are.\",\"A map is a drawing that shows the position of places.\",\"Symbols on a map represent real things like rivers, roads, or buildings.\",\"A legend or key explains what the symbols on a map mean.\",\"Grids on maps use rows and columns to locate exact positions.\",\"Coordinates like (A, 3) or (2, B) help find a specific square on a grid.\",\"Left, right, forward, and backward are used to give simple directions.\",\"Landmarks are special places like schools or parks that help us find our way.\",\"Scale on a map shows how much smaller the map is than the real area.\",\"We use maps to find our way in new places or to plan a route.\",\"Playing location games improves observation and thinking skills.\",\"Following directions step by step helps reach the correct place.\",\"Maps can be of a classroom, school, neighborhood, or city.\",\"In location games, one person gives clues and others guess the place.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the specimen letter, what is the writer thanking the person for?\",\"options\":[\"For a birthday gift\",\"For being a pen-friend\",\"For visiting their house\",\"For lending a book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'Thank you so much for being my pen-friend.\'\",\"topic\":\"Specimen Letter 1\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of this specimen letter?\",\"options\":[\"To ask for money\",\"To invite a friend to a party\",\"To tell a friend about a superb movie\",\"To complain about school\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The writer says, \'I want to tell you about a superb movie.\'\",\"topic\":\"Specimen Letter 1\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When did the writer see the movie mentioned in the letter?\",\"options\":[\"Yesterday\",\"Last month\",\"Last week\",\"Today\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I saw it last week.\'\",\"topic\":\"Specimen Letter 1\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the layout in the given figure, where is the \'Date\' supposed to be written?\",\"options\":[\"At the bottom left\",\"In the middle of the page\",\"At the top right corner\",\"After the signature\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the placeholder for \'Date :\' at the top right of the letter.\",\"topic\":\"Specimen Letter 1\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/056_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which specific word is highlighted in a blue box to show emphasis?\",\"options\":[\"hope\",\"see\",\"fine\",\"tell\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows the word \'see\' inside a blue highlighted box.\",\"topic\":\"Specimen Letter 1\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/056_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does the writer ask the friend to give to their parents?\",\"options\":[\"A gift\",\"Regards\",\"A letter\",\"Money\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The letter ends with, \'Give my regards to your parents.\'\",\"topic\":\"Specimen Letter 1\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to use this specimen to write to your own friend, which closing phrase should you use according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Yours faithfully,\",\"With love,\",\"Your friend,\",\"Goodbye,\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The specimen letter uses \'Your friend,\' as the closing phrase.\",\"topic\":\"Specimen Letter 1\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the writer say \'You must SEE it\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the movie is boring\",\"Because the writer is sure the friend will like it\",\"Because it is a school requirement\",\"Because the friend is a director\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The writer recommends it because they found it superb and are sure the friend will like it.\",\"topic\":\"Specimen Letter 1\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the writer\'s opinion of the movie they saw?\",\"options\":[\"It was okay\",\"It was superb\",\"It was too long\",\"It was scary\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The writer describes the movie as \'a superb movie\'.\",\"topic\":\"Specimen Letter 1\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which question does the writer ask to show interest in the friend\'s life?\",\"options\":[\"What is the date?\",\"How is everyone in your family?\",\"What movie did you see?\",\"Where do you live?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The letter includes the question, \'How is everyone in your family?\'\",\"topic\":\"Specimen Letter 1\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which competition is originally mentioned in the letter template?\",\"options\":[\"Story Telling Competition\",\"Recitation Competition\",\"‘Jokes’ Telling Competition\",\"Movie Review Competition\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions a ‘Jokes’ Telling Competition in the second paragraph.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Substitutions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the letter, who should the receiver give regards to besides their parents?\",\"options\":[\"Their sister\",\"Their brother\",\"Their teacher\",\"Their friend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The letter ends with \'Regards to your parents and to your brother.\'\",\"topic\":\"Useful Substitutions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which substitution is provided for the word \'movie\' if you are talking about a poem?\",\"options\":[\"a very good programme\",\"a wonderful book\",\"a lovely poem\",\"an interesting story\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The list of substitutions includes \'a lovely poem\' as an alternative to \'movie\'.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Substitutions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the writer changes the competition to a \'Recitation Competition\', what should they ask their friend to suggest?\",\"options\":[\"a joke\",\"a story\",\"a poem\",\"a book\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the substitutions, \'Recitation Competition\' is paired with \'poem\'.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Substitutions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which verb is suggested as a substitution when talking about a book?\",\"options\":[\"watch\",\"read\",\"write\",\"tell\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The list of substitutions includes \'read\' as an action related to a book.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Substitutions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What adjective is used to describe the \'story\' in the list of substitutions?\",\"options\":[\"wonderful\",\"lovely\",\"interesting\",\"good\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'an interesting story\' as a substitution.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Substitutions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to write about a \'programme\' instead of a \'movie\', which phrase should they use?\",\"options\":[\"a wonderful programme\",\"a very good programme\",\"an interesting programme\",\"a lovely programme\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The specific phrase provided in the substitutions is \'a very good programme\'.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Substitutions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of the list of words provided at the end of the letter?\",\"options\":[\"To correct spelling mistakes in the letter\",\"To provide alternative options to change the letter\'s topic\",\"To list the names of the sender\'s brothers\",\"To show the answers to the competition\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The substitutions allow the writer to change the subject of the letter (e.g., from movie to book).\",\"topic\":\"Useful Substitutions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the substitution list, which competition is grouped with the word \'story\'?\",\"options\":[\"Jokes Telling Competition\",\"Recitation Competition\",\"Story Telling Competition\",\"Reading Competition\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Story Telling Competition\' as a substitution option.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Substitutions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If the writer uses the substitution \'watch\', which item from the list are they most likely referring to?\",\"options\":[\"a poem\",\"a book\",\"a programme\",\"a joke\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"One \'watches\' a programme or movie, whereas one \'reads\' a book or poem.\",\"topic\":\"Useful Substitutions\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a closing expression mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Hello there\",\"Yours sincerely\",\"Good morning\",\"How are you?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Yours sincerely\' as a useful expression for closing a letter.\",\"topic\":\"Some useful expressions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, to whom should you give your \'regards\'?\",\"options\":[\"Little sister\",\"Little brother\",\"Parents or elders\",\"Pets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests giving regards to parents or the elders in the family.\",\"topic\":\"Some useful expressions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What expression is used for a little sister or brother?\",\"options\":[\"Give my regards\",\"Give my love\",\"Yours truly\",\"Please come over\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically uses \'Give my love\' for a little sister or brother.\",\"topic\":\"Some useful expressions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which expression is used to invite someone to your home?\",\"options\":[\"See you soon\",\"With regards\",\"Please come over to my house on Sunday\",\"Yours lovingly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Please come over to my house on Sunday\' as an invitation expression.\",\"topic\":\"Some useful expressions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word completes the expression \'Yours ______\' to show affection?\",\"options\":[\"Regards\",\"Sincerely\",\"Lovingly\",\"Soon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text includes \'Yours lovingly\' as a useful expression.\",\"topic\":\"Some useful expressions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to tell someone you will meet them in the near future, which expression should you use?\",\"options\":[\"Give my regards\",\"See you soon\",\"Yours truly\",\"With lots of love\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'See you soon\' is the expression used when planning to meet again shortly.\",\"topic\":\"Some useful expressions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are writing to a teacher or an official, which formal closing from the text is most appropriate?\",\"options\":[\"Love\",\"With lots of love\",\"Yours sincerely\",\"See you soon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Yours sincerely\' is a standard formal expression listed in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Some useful expressions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which expression would you use if you were writing a letter to your best friend?\",\"options\":[\"Give my regards to the elders\",\"Yours truly\",\"With lots of love\",\"Please come over to my house on Sunday\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'With lots of love\' is a friendly and affectionate expression suitable for a friend.\",\"topic\":\"Some useful expressions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the difference between giving \'love\' and giving \'regards\'?\",\"options\":[\"Love is for elders, regards is for children\",\"Love is for younger siblings, regards is for parents\\/elders\",\"They are exactly the same\",\"Regards is for Sunday only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text differentiates by using \'love\' for little siblings and \'regards\' for parents\\/elders.\",\"topic\":\"Some useful expressions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these expressions is the shortest way to end a friendly note according to the list?\",\"options\":[\"Yours sincerely\",\"With regards\",\"Love\",\"Yours lovingly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Love\' is the shortest single-word closing expression provided in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Some useful expressions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21657,27,5,'English','en','Shapes and Maps','[\"Shapes are the forms or outlines of objects, like circle, square, triangle, rectangle.\",\"Maps are drawings that show places and help us find directions.\",\"A map uses symbols to represent real things like rivers, roads, and buildings.\",\"A key or legend on a map explains what the symbols mean.\",\"Directions on a map are north, south, east, and west.\",\"Scale on a map shows how much smaller the drawing is compared to real life.\",\"Grid lines on a map help locate places using rows and columns.\",\"A compass rose shows the four main directions on a map.\",\"Maps can be of a room, school, village, city, or country.\",\"We use maps to find our way, plan trips, and understand locations.\",\"Shapes help us describe and draw objects correctly.\",\"Recognizing shapes helps in drawing maps and reading pictures.\",\"Flat shapes are 2D; solid shapes are 3D (like cube, sphere).\",\"We can fold paper to make shapes and understand their sides and corners.\",\"Maps do not show everything; they show only important details.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of the following is listed as a \'shape\' in the textbook text?\",\"options\":[\"fountain\",\"square\",\"lawn\",\"canteen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'square\' under the names of shapes in exercise 1.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which item is included in the \'Map of a Garden\' index?\",\"options\":[\"arrow\",\"star\",\"fountain\",\"triangle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The \'Map of a Garden\' index includes \'fountain\' as one of the garden features.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words refers to a geometric shape rather than a garden feature?\",\"options\":[\"bushes\",\"rectangle\",\"slides\",\"toilets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Rectangle is listed among the shapes, while the others are part of the garden index.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the garden index, where would you go if you wanted to buy something to eat?\",\"options\":[\"canteen\",\"rocket\",\"point\",\"line\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A canteen is a place where food is sold, and it is listed in the garden index.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are looking for a place to sit under a specific tree mentioned in the index, which one should you find?\",\"options\":[\"bushes\",\"banyan tree and platform\",\"lawn\",\"star\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The index specifically mentions a \'banyan tree and platform\', which provides a place to sit.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which shape from the list is most suitable to indicate the direction to the entrance on a map?\",\"options\":[\"circle\",\"square\",\"arrow\",\"point\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"An arrow is the standard shape used to show direction.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following groups contains ONLY items found in the garden map index?\",\"options\":[\"fountain, bushes, star\",\"slides, swings, rectangle\",\"lawn, canteen, toilets\",\"arrow, point, line\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Lawn, canteen, and toilets are all listed in the garden index; the other options include shapes.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which item in the garden index is intended for keeping the garden clean?\",\"options\":[\"fountain\",\"garbage bin\",\"stalls\",\"rocket\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A garbage bin is used to dispose of waste to keep the area clean.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many different names of shapes are listed in the first exercise?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"7\",\"8\",\"9\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The shapes listed are: arrow, point, square, rectangle, triangle, circle, star, and line (total 8).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the \'Map of a Garden\', what is the purpose of the \'Index\'?\",\"options\":[\"To list the names of people in the garden\",\"To list the items and features shown on the map\",\"To provide the history of the garden\",\"To list the shapes used in geometry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The index provides a list of all the features (like trees, slides, and canteen) that appear on the map.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:28'),(21658,27,5,'English','en','Tock Tock Tong Tong','[\"The poem \'Tock Tock Tong Tong\' uses sound\' describes different sounds made by objects and actions.\",\"It uses onomatopoeic words like \'tock\', \'tong\', \'click\', \'clack\' to represent sounds.\",\"The poem helps students identify sounds in their surroundings.\",\"Rhythm and repetition are used to make the poem musical and engaging.\",\"Words like \'tick-tock\' show time-related sounds, often from clocks.\",\"Sounds can be soft, loud, sharp, or dull depending on the source.\",\"The poem encourages listening carefully to everyday noises.\",\"It connects sounds to actions like walking, hammering, or raining.\",\"Students learn to associate specific sounds with objects or events.\",\"The poem builds vocabulary related to auditory sensations.\",\"It supports language development through sound imitation and pattern recognition.\",\"Repeated sounds create a beat, helping in memorization and recitation.\",\"The poem is meant to be read aloud to enjoy its musical quality.\",\"It teaches that sounds are produced by vibrations and movement.\",\"Students are encouraged to create their own sound words for familiar things.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which faraway land did the minister live?\",\"options\":[\"India\",\"Korea\",\"Japan\",\"China\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the story takes place in the faraway land of Korea.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who lived on the left side of the minister\'s house?\",\"options\":[\"A blacksmith\",\"A soldier\",\"A carpenter\",\"A farmer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the carpenter lived on the left of the minister\'s house.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound did the blacksmith make while beating the iron?\",\"options\":[\"Tock, tock, tock\",\"Tong, tong, tong\",\"Krrr, krrr, krrr\",\"Ding, dong, ding\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the blacksmith made the sound \'Tong, tong, tong\' by beating iron.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which tool did the carpenter use to make the \'krrr - krrr - krrr\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"A big hammer\",\"A small hammer\",\"A saw\",\"An iron rod\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the carpenter used his saw to cut the wood, making the \'krrr\' sound.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you hear the sound \'Tock, tock, tock\', which tool is being used?\",\"options\":[\"The blacksmith\'s big hammer\",\"The carpenter\'s small hammer\",\"The carpenter\'s saw\",\"The minister\'s bell\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text associates \'Tock, tock, tock\' with the carpenter\'s small hammer.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the minister think he must do something about his neighbors?\",\"options\":[\"They were very poor\",\"They were his friends\",\"Their noise disturbed him\",\"They did not work enough\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that all the noise made by the blacksmith and carpenter disturbed the minister.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"When did the blacksmith and the carpenter start their work every day?\",\"options\":[\"Late in the evening\",\"At noon\",\"Early in the morning\",\"In the middle of the night\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says they began their work early in the morning.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What material was the blacksmith working with?\",\"options\":[\"Wood\",\"Iron\",\"Gold\",\"Stone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the blacksmith beat the iron with his big hammer.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which character is shown standing in the center wearing a purple robe?\",\"options\":[\"The blacksmith\",\"The carpenter\",\"The minister\",\"A neighbor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The central figure in the illustration represents the minister described in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/063_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which sound is written in the top left corner near the roof of the house?\",\"options\":[\"tong tong\",\"tock tock\",\"krrr krrr\",\"ding dong\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows \'tock tock\' written near the house on the left side.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/063_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the carpenter needs to cut wood, which sound will be heard according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Tong, tong, tong\",\"Tock, tock, tock\",\"Krrr, krrr, krrr\",\"Bang, bang, bang\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Krrr - krrr - krrr\' is the sound made when using the saw to cut wood.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what was the main cause of the minister\'s problem?\",\"options\":[\"The distance of the land\",\"The size of the hammers\",\"The constant noise day and night\",\"The location of the houses\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that they worked day and night and made a lot of noise, which disturbed him.\",\"topic\":\"Tock, Tock, Tong, Tong\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who did the minister call first to give the order?\",\"options\":[\"The carpenter\",\"The blacksmith\",\"The king\",\"The cook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that one day, the minister called the blacksmith first.\",\"topic\":\"The Minister\'s Order\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What specific order did the minister give to both the blacksmith and the carpenter?\",\"options\":[\"To build a new palace\",\"To shift their house somewhere else\",\"To make new tools\",\"To stay for dinner\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The minister ordered the blacksmith and the carpenter to shift their houses somewhere else.\",\"topic\":\"The Minister\'s Order\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When did the blacksmith say he would move his house?\",\"options\":[\"Today\",\"Next week\",\"Tomorrow\",\"In a few days\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The blacksmith told the minister, \'I\'m moving my house tomorrow.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Minister\'s Order\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the minister feel when the carpenter said he was also moving?\",\"options\":[\"Angry\",\"Sad\",\"Overjoyed\",\"Worried\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that the minister was \'overjoyed\' when the carpenter spoke.\",\"topic\":\"The Minister\'s Order\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the minister offer his neighbors for lunch?\",\"options\":[\"Only water and bread\",\"Tasty dishes, sweets and fruits\",\"Vegetables and rice\",\"Tea and biscuits\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the minister offered many tasty dishes, sweets and fruits.\",\"topic\":\"The Minister\'s Order\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the minister call the blacksmith a \'good man\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because he was a hard worker\",\"Because he agreed to move his house\",\"Because he brought gifts\",\"Because he was a relative\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The minister called him a good man because he agreed to the order of moving his house.\",\"topic\":\"The Minister\'s Order\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the minister says \'You are too kind!\', what is he doing?\",\"options\":[\"Complaining about the neighbors\",\"Praising the neighbors for their cooperation\",\"Asking for a favor\",\"Warning the neighbors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The minister uses these words to show appreciation for their willingness to move.\",\"topic\":\"The Minister\'s Order\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what was the minister\'s main goal in this passage?\",\"options\":[\"To host a big party\",\"To get the blacksmith and carpenter to move\",\"To learn how to build houses\",\"To sell fruits and sweets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The entire passage focuses on the minister ordering and ensuring the neighbors move their houses.\",\"topic\":\"The Minister\'s Order\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'gave him the same order\', what does \'the same order\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"The order to cook lunch\",\"The order to shift his house somewhere else\",\"The order to buy fruits\",\"The order to stay for lunch\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The minister gave the carpenter the same instruction he gave the blacksmith: to move his house.\",\"topic\":\"The Minister\'s Order\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What can we conclude about the minister\'s reaction to the neighbors moving?\",\"options\":[\"He was relieved and happy to see them go\",\"He was upset that they were leaving\",\"He was indifferent and did not care\",\"He wanted them to stay longer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"His happiness, joy, and the treat of lunch indicate he was very pleased that they were moving.\",\"topic\":\"The Minister\'s Order\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What sound did the minister expect to hear when he woke up the next morning?\",\"options\":[\"Sweet sounds of birds\",\"Tong, tong, tong\",\"Tock, tock, tock\",\"Krrr, krrr, krrr\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states the minister thought he would listen to the sweet sounds of birds the next morning.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the minister call his servants in the morning?\",\"options\":[\"To ask for his breakfast\",\"To find out who was making all that noise\",\"To help him move to a new house\",\"To feed the birds in the garden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The minister got annoyed by the noise and told his servants to go and see who was making it.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does the phrase \'got annoyed\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Became very happy\",\"Felt very sleepy\",\"Became troubled or irritated\",\"Felt very hungry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the meaning in Marathi as \'trasla\' or \'vaitagla\', which translates to troubled or irritated.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the \'news\' that the servants brought to the minister?\",\"options\":[\"The craftsmen had stopped their work\",\"The craftsmen had left the town forever\",\"The craftsmen had simply swapped their houses\",\"The craftsmen were now making sweet music\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The servants reported that the blacksmith moved to the carpenter\'s house and vice versa.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what action is the man in the center performing to show he is annoyed?\",\"options\":[\"He is clapping his hands loudly\",\"He is covering his ears with his hands\",\"He is pointing at the roof of the house\",\"He is sleeping peacefully\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the minister covering his ears to block out the loud \'tock\' and \'krrr\' sounds.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure and the text, what are the words \'tock\' and \'krrr\' representing?\",\"options\":[\"The names of the servants\",\"The names of the houses\",\"The loud noises made by the craftsmen\",\"The songs of the birds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows these words floating in the air, representing the noise that is annoying the minister.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the carpenter move to?\",\"options\":[\"To the minister\'s palace\",\"To the blacksmith\'s house\",\"To a house in the forest\",\"To the servants\' quarters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the carpenter had moved to the blacksmith\'s house.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When did the blacksmith and the carpenter carry on their work?\",\"options\":[\"Only during the day\",\"Only during the night\",\"Day and night\",\"Only in the evening\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they carried on their work in their houses day and night.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The minister thought he would have peace because he expected the craftsmen to move. Why was he still annoyed the next morning?\",\"options\":[\"Because the birds were too loud\",\"Because the servants woke him up early\",\"Because the craftsmen were still nearby, just in different houses\",\"Because he forgot to go to sleep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The noise continued because the craftsmen only swapped houses and continued working.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"At what time did the minister think, \'Ah! At last I will have some peace\'?\",\"options\":[\"When he was eating breakfast\",\"When he went to bed the night before\",\"When he heard the blacksmith working\",\"When the servants came back with news\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'The next day, when the minister went to bed, he thought...\'\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes the craftsmen\'s \'surprise\' for the minister?\",\"options\":[\"They followed his wish to move but stayed close enough to keep him annoyed\",\"They gave him a gift of sweet-singing birds\",\"They decided to become servants for the minister\",\"They stopped making noise to please the minister\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The surprise was that they moved houses as requested, but since they swapped with each other, the noise stayed the same.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who moved into the carpenter\'s house?\",\"options\":[\"The minister\",\"The blacksmith\",\"The servants\",\"The birds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'the blacksmith had moved to the carpenter\'s house\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Surprise\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21659,27,5,'English','en','On the Time-line','[\"Prepositions of place tell us where something or someone is located.\",\"Common prepositions of place: in, on, under, behind, in front of, near, between, next to, above, below.\",\"\'In\' is used for inside a space or enclosed area (e.g., in the room, in the box).\",\"\'On\' is used for a surface or top of something (e.g., on the table, on the wall).\",\"\'Under\' means below or beneath something (e.g., under the chair, under the bed).\",\"\'Behind\' means at the back of something or someone (e.g., behind the door, behind you).\",\"\'In front of\' means at the front side of something or someone (e.g., in front of the class, in front of the house).\",\"\'Near\' means close to or not far from (e.g., near the window, near the school).\",\"\'Between\' is used when something is in the middle of two things or people (e.g., between the chairs, between Rita and Sita).\",\"\'Next to\' means beside or at the side of (e.g., next to the bench, next to me).\",\"We use these words to answer questions like \'Where is...?\' or \'Where are...?\'.\",\"The answer to \'Where are you?\' can be a short sentence using a preposition of place (e.g., I am on the bench).\",\"Prepositions help us describe position clearly in speaking and writing.\",\"Practice using prepositions by describing where things are in your classroom.\",\"Always choose the correct preposition based on the actual position of the object or person.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, when did dinosaurs live on the earth?\",\"options\":[\"Thousands of years from now\",\"Millions of years ago\",\"A few years ago\",\"Last week\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that dinosaurs lived on the earth millions of years ago.\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase is used in the example sentence about a king?\",\"options\":[\"Once upon a time\",\"Long, long ago\",\"In the future\",\"Yesterday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The example sentence provided is \'Long, long ago, there lived a king.\'\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phrases refers to the day before today?\",\"options\":[\"Day after tomorrow\",\"Yesterday\",\"Last week\",\"Day before yesterday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Yesterday is the standard term for the day before the current day.\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What phrase is used in the example sentence \'I gave you a book ____\'?\",\"options\":[\"tomorrow\",\"next week\",\"a little while ago\",\"in future\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses the example: \'I gave you a book a little while ago.\'\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phrases refers to the \'present\' time?\",\"options\":[\"At present\",\"After a while\",\"Last year\",\"Next year\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'At present\' indicates the current time or now.\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are talking about the time that is happening right now, which phrase from the list would you use?\",\"options\":[\"Later\",\"Just now\",\"Tomorrow\",\"In the past\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Just now\' or \'now\' refers to the current moment.\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase describes a time that will come after today?\",\"options\":[\"Yesterday\",\"Tomorrow\",\"Last week\",\"Some time ago\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tomorrow is the day that follows today in the future.\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'after a while\' mean in the context of the time-line?\",\"options\":[\"In the past\",\"At this moment\",\"Later in the future\",\"Millions of years ago\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text groups \'after a while\' with \'later\', indicating a future time.\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence meaningfully: \'We will go for a picnic ____.\'\",\"options\":[\"yesterday\",\"next week\",\"long long ago\",\"a little while ago\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Next week\' is a future phrase suitable for the future tense \'will go\'.\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase would best complete a sentence about something that happened very recently in the past?\",\"options\":[\"Thousands of years from now\",\"Some time ago\",\"Next year\",\"In future\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Some time ago\' or \'a little while ago\' refers to a recent past event.\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phrases represents the furthest point in the future mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Next year\",\"After a few years\",\"Thousands of years from now\",\"Day after tomorrow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Thousands of years from now\' is the longest future duration listed.\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase refers to a time that is further back in the past than \'yesterday\'?\",\"options\":[\"Today\",\"Day before yesterday\",\"Now\",\"Tonight\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Day before yesterday\' occurs before \'yesterday\' on the time-line.\",\"topic\":\"Time-line Phrases\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sentences refers to a time that has already passed?\",\"options\":[\"I am busy\",\"I was in Std I\",\"School starts\",\"They will go home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'was\' indicates a past state or time.\",\"topic\":\"Sentences for Practice\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the sentence that describes a future event.\",\"options\":[\"We visited the zoo\",\"She needs water\",\"People will land on Mars\",\"There lived a king\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'will land\' indicates an action that is yet to happen.\",\"topic\":\"Sentences for Practice\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence mentions a specific planet?\",\"options\":[\"There were dinosaurs on the earth\",\"People will land on Mars\",\"We visited the zoo\",\"School starts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'Mars\' in the context of future travel.\",\"topic\":\"Sentences for Practice\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The sentence \'I am drawing a picture\' tells us the action is happening when?\",\"options\":[\"In the past\",\"In the future\",\"Right now (Present)\",\"Long ago\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'I am drawing\' indicates a continuous action in the present time.\",\"topic\":\"Sentences for Practice\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What time-line category does the sentence \'There lived a king\' belong to?\",\"options\":[\"Past\",\"Present\",\"Future\",\"Every day\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'lived\' is the past tense form, indicating a time gone by.\",\"topic\":\"Sentences for Practice\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'She needs water\', what is the current state of the person?\",\"options\":[\"She needed water yesterday\",\"She will need water tomorrow\",\"She needs water at this moment\",\"She never needs water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Needs\' is a present tense verb showing a current requirement.\",\"topic\":\"Sentences for Practice\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to promise to return a borrowed item later, which sentence from the text would you use?\",\"options\":[\"I gave you a book\",\"I will give it back to you\",\"I want something to read\",\"He is going to play cricket\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'I will give it back\' is a future-oriented sentence used for promises.\",\"topic\":\"Sentences for Practice\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence would be most appropriate for a student currently sitting in a classroom?\",\"options\":[\"We will be in college\",\"I was in Std I\",\"School starts\",\"There were dinosaurs on the earth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'School starts\' is a present tense statement suitable for a current school scenario.\",\"topic\":\"Sentences for Practice\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Compare the sentences \'I was in Std I\' and \'We will be in college\'. What is the main difference?\",\"options\":[\"The first is about the past, the second is about the future\",\"The first is about the future, the second is about the past\",\"Both are about the present\",\"Both are about the past\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Was\' indicates the past (Std I), while \'will be\' indicates the future (college).\",\"topic\":\"Sentences for Practice\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which sentence refers to a time before humans existed or a very ancient time?\",\"options\":[\"We visited the zoo\",\"There were dinosaurs on the earth\",\"We will grow old\",\"They will go home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Dinosaurs represent a prehistoric time on the past time-line.\",\"topic\":\"Sentences for Practice\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which proverb is mentioned at the beginning of the text?\",\"options\":[\"Time and tide wait for none\",\"There\'s no time like the present\",\"A stitch in time saves nine\",\"Time is a great healer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly starts with the proverb \'There\'s no time like the present.\'\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the proverbs in the text, when does \'tomorrow\' come?\",\"options\":[\"Every day\",\"Soon\",\"Never\",\"After the present\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Tomorrow never comes.\'\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first thing students should do with the word groups on the time-line?\",\"options\":[\"Write them down\",\"Read them\",\"Translate them\",\"Draw them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'कालरेषेवरील शब्दगट मुलांकडून वाचून घ्यावे\' (Have students read the word groups on the time-line).\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What must the teacher ensure after students read the word groups?\",\"options\":[\"That they can spell the words\",\"That they have memorized the words\",\"That they understand the meaning of the word groups\",\"That they can write in cursive\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'मुलांना त्यांचा अर्थ समजत असल्याची खात्री करून घ्यावी\' (Ensure that they understand their meaning).\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"On which page number are the sentences located that need to be completed?\",\"options\":[\"Page 56\",\"Page 58\",\"Page 57\",\"Page 55\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'पान 57 वरील प्रत्येक वाक्यात\' (In every sentence on page 57).\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the goal of putting word groups into the sentences on page 57?\",\"options\":[\"To make the sentences longer\",\"To create meaningful sentences\",\"To finish the homework quickly\",\"To learn new Marathi words\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions creating \'अर्थपूर्ण वाक्ये\' (meaningful sentences).\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides using given sentences, what else should students be encouraged to do?\",\"options\":[\"Copy the proverbs five times\",\"Create their own sentences\",\"Read the next chapter\",\"Draw a time-line\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'स्वतःच्या मनाने वाक्ये तयार करण्यासही मुलांना उत्तेजन द्यावे\' (Encourage children to prepare sentences on their own).\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How often should this activity be conducted according to the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Only once\",\"Every single day\",\"Occasionally from time to time\",\"Only during exams\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'ही कृती नंतरही अधूनमधून घ्यावी\' (This activity should be taken occasionally later as well).\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the teacher need to do to help students make \'meaningful connections\'?\",\"options\":[\"Give them the answers directly\",\"Get them to talk about which word groups fit in which sentences\",\"Ask them to keep quiet and read\",\"Tell them to ignore the time-line\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'मुलांना बोलते करून विविध जोडण्या करू द्याव्या\' (Make the children talk and let them make various connections).\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the teacher\'s instructions, which skill is being developed when students create their own sentences?\",\"options\":[\"Handwriting skills\",\"Independent sentence construction\",\"Translation skills\",\"Listening skills\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Encouraging students to make sentences \'स्वतःच्या मनाने\' (on their own) develops independent construction.\",\"topic\":\"शिक्षकांसाठी\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21660,27,5,'English','en','I speak, I say, I talk','[\"Speaking means using your voice to say words.\",\"Saying is expressing something with words.\",\"Talking is having a conversation with someone.\",\"We speak to share our thoughts and feelings.\",\"We say things to give information or answer questions.\",\"We talk to communicate and build relationships.\",\"Speaking, saying, and talking are all forms of oral communication.\",\"Good speaking includes clear voice and correct words.\",\"Listening is important when someone is talking to you.\",\"We use polite words like \'please\', \'thank you\', \'sorry\' while speaking.\",\"Your tone of voice shows your feelings while speaking.\",\"Practice speaking in English to improve fluency.\",\"Speak slowly and clearly so others can understand you.\",\"Use full sentences when speaking in class or presentations.\",\"Confidence grows when you practice speaking regularly.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what sound does a lion make?\",\"options\":[\"purr\",\"roar\",\"hoot\",\"snore\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states \'Lions roar.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is described as making a \'squeak\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"Sheep\",\"Crickets\",\"Mice\",\"Bears\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions \'Mice squeak.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the first stanza, what action does the human perform while animals like cats and lions make their sounds?\",\"options\":[\"squeak\",\"chatter\",\"speak\",\"hum\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first stanza ends with the line \'But I speak!\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these animals makes a \'cluck\' sound according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Horses\",\"Chickens\",\"Pigs\",\"Pigeons\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states \'Chickens cluck.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you hear a \'buzz\' near a flower, which insect mentioned in the poem is likely making that sound?\",\"options\":[\"Flies\",\"Bees\",\"Crickets\",\"Bats\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem associates \'buzz\' with \'Bees\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a dog is angry or warning someone, which sound from the poem would it most likely make?\",\"options\":[\"howl\",\"growl\",\"screech\",\"croak\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem identifies the sound of dogs as \'growl\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, how does the sound of a wolf differ from the sound of a frog?\",\"options\":[\"Wolf howls and frog croaks\",\"Wolf hums and frog buzzes\",\"Wolf screeches and frog squawks\",\"Wolf neighs and frog moos\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Wolves howl\' and \'Frogs croak\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the pattern of the poem, which word does the human use to describe their communication at the very end of the third stanza?\",\"options\":[\"speak\",\"say\",\"talk\",\"chatter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The final line of the third stanza is \'But I talk!\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which animal is shown standing upright and making a \'snore\' sound?\",\"options\":[\"Lion\",\"Bear\",\"Monkey\",\"Dog\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a bear standing and the text next to it says \'Bears snore.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/068_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which bird is shown at the top with a red beak and green feathers making a sound?\",\"options\":[\"Owl\",\"Pigeon\",\"Chicken\",\"Parrot\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a green parrot with a red beak near the text \'Parrots squawk.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/068_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the first instruction, what should you suit your actions to?\",\"options\":[\"Your thoughts\",\"Your words\",\"Your friends\",\"Your sounds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states: \'Suit your actions to your words.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the creature who wants honey say?\",\"options\":[\"I am so happy\",\"I want lots of honey\",\"Where are you?\",\"Now I can fly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'I want lots of honey\' as one of the things the animals say.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When does the creature in the last sentence say it can fly?\",\"options\":[\"In the morning\",\"In the afternoon\",\"At night\",\"During the day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says: \'It is night. Now I can fly.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What feeling is paired with being \'warm\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Sadness\",\"Happiness\",\"Anger\",\"Fear\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says: \'I am so warm. I am so happy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the final step mentioned in the first instruction?\",\"options\":[\"Listen\",\"Repeat\",\"Learn\",\"Recite\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The instruction sequence is: \'Listen, repeat, learn and recite.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the creature searching for when it asks \'Where are you?\'\",\"options\":[\"Honey\",\"A friend\",\"Food\",\"A home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says: \'Where are you, my friend?\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the instructions to act out the poem, what should you do while speaking?\",\"options\":[\"Close your eyes tightly\",\"Suit your actions to your words\",\"Sit perfectly still\",\"Read the text silently\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the student to \'Suit your actions to your words.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence from the text shows that a creature is looking for social connection?\",\"options\":[\"I am so warm.\",\"I want lots of honey.\",\"Where are you, my friend?\",\"It is night.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Asking for a friend indicates a search for social connection.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to pretend to be a hungry bear based on the text, which line should they use?\",\"options\":[\"I am so happy\",\"I want lots of honey\",\"Where are you?\",\"It is night\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Bears are known for liking honey, and the text provides the line \'I want lots of honey.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the specific condition that allows the last creature to fly?\",\"options\":[\"It must be warm\",\"It must be happy\",\"It must be night time\",\"It must find honey\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links the ability to fly to the time: \'It is night. Now I can fly.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21661,27,5,'English','en','Science Funfair','[\"A science funfair is an event where students display science projects and experiments.\",\"It helps students learn science by doing hands-on activities.\",\"Projects can include models, charts, and simple experiments.\",\"Students explain their work to visitors and judges.\",\"Teamwork and creativity are important in preparing for a funfair.\",\"Safety rules must be followed while doing experiments.\",\"Recycled materials can be used to make eco-friendly projects.\",\"Judges look for originality, effort, and scientific thinking.\",\"Funfairs encourage curiosity and interest in science.\",\"Presenting clearly helps others understand your project.\",\"Participating builds confidence and communication skills.\",\"Teachers guide students in choosing and developing projects.\",\"Science funfairs are often held in schools or community centers.\",\"They provide a platform to share ideas and learn from others.\",\"Every project should have a clear aim and observation.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, where does the girl rub the balloon first?\",\"options\":[\"On the wall\",\"On her head\",\"On her hand\",\"On the floor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'first I rub it on my head.\'\",\"topic\":\"Static Electricity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What object is being used to demonstrate the experiment in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A magnet\",\"A piece of paper\",\"A balloon\",\"A bottle of glue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes an experiment showing how a balloon sticks to the wall.\",\"topic\":\"Static Electricity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main reason the balloon sticks to the wall without glue?\",\"options\":[\"Magic\",\"Gravity\",\"Electricity\",\"Air pressure\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains, \'This happens due to electricity.\'\",\"topic\":\"Static Electricity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the girl is demonstrating that the balloon can stay on the wall without using ______.\",\"options\":[\"Air\",\"Glue\",\"Color\",\"Hands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The caption for the first figure says the balloon sticks to the wall \'without glue\'.\",\"topic\":\"Static Electricity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/070_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"The speaker says \'There is no trick in this.\' What does this tell us about the experiment?\",\"options\":[\"It is a magic show\",\"It is based on science, not a trick\",\"It is a secret\",\"It is not real\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"By saying there is no trick, the speaker emphasizes that the result is due to a scientific cause (electricity).\",\"topic\":\"Static Electricity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to present this experiment at a Science Funfair, in which language should you learn to present it?\",\"options\":[\"Marathi\",\"Hindi\",\"English\",\"Sanskrit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to \'Learn to do it yourself and present it in English.\'\",\"topic\":\"Static Electricity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do immediately after rubbing the balloon on your head to make it stick?\",\"options\":[\"Wash the balloon\",\"Stick it to the wall\",\"Pop the balloon\",\"Rub it on the floor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'first I rub it on my head. Then I stick it to the wall.\'\",\"topic\":\"Static Electricity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what object is the boy holding to show something that \'looks like magic\'?\",\"options\":[\"A balloon\",\"A magnet\",\"A bowl\",\"A piece of paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The second figure shows a boy holding a U-shaped magnet over a table.\",\"topic\":\"Static Electricity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/071_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the speaker rub the balloon on their head?\",\"options\":[\"To clean the hair\",\"To make the balloon stick using electricity\",\"To make the balloon change color\",\"To make the balloon bigger\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Rubbing the balloon on the head is the action that causes the electricity mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Static Electricity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the speaker ask the audience to do at the very beginning of the presentation?\",\"options\":[\"Read the book\",\"Listen carefully and watch\",\"Start rubbing balloons\",\"Go to the wall\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins with the instruction \'Listen carefully and watch the experiment.\'\",\"topic\":\"Static Electricity\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What material are the bowls in the experiment made of?\",\"options\":[\"Plastic\",\"Metal\",\"Glass\",\"Ceramic\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'These are all glass bowls.\'\",\"topic\":\"Musical Glass Bowls\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the speaker use to tap the bowls?\",\"options\":[\"A pencil\",\"A spoon\",\"A glass rod\",\"A finger\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speaker says, \'Now I\'ll tap each bowl gently with this spoon.\'\",\"topic\":\"Musical Glass Bowls\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which bowl contains \'very little water\'?\",\"options\":[\"The first bowl\",\"The middle bowl\",\"The last bowl\",\"Every bowl\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'This last bowl has very little water in it.\'\",\"topic\":\"Musical Glass Bowls\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is the water level arranged in the bowls from left to right?\",\"options\":[\"Each bowl has less water than the one on its left.\",\"Each bowl has the same amount of water.\",\"Each bowl has more water than the bowl on the left.\",\"The water levels are random.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Each bowl has more water than the bowl on the left.\'\",\"topic\":\"Musical Glass Bowls\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of sound is produced when the bowls are tapped?\",\"options\":[\"A loud noise\",\"A musical sound\",\"A cracking sound\",\"No sound at all\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speaker exclaims, \'What a musical sound!\'\",\"topic\":\"Musical Glass Bowls\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What greeting does the speaker use to start the presentation?\",\"options\":[\"Hello\",\"Good morning\",\"Namaste\",\"Welcome\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text begins with the word \'Namaste.\'\",\"topic\":\"Musical Glass Bowls\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the speaker\'s instructions, how should you tap the bowls?\",\"options\":[\"Gently\",\"Hard\",\"Quickly\",\"With both hands\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The speaker says, \'Now I\'ll tap each bowl gently...\'\",\"topic\":\"Musical Glass Bowls\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the last bowl has very little water, which bowl is likely \'full of water\' based on the arrangement described?\",\"options\":[\"The second bowl\",\"The last bowl\",\"The first bowl\",\"The middle bowl\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since each bowl has more water than the one on its left, the leftmost (first) bowl would be the fullest if the sequence ends with \'very little\'.\",\"topic\":\"Musical Glass Bowls\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the speaker say \'Please be careful\' when inviting others to try?\",\"options\":[\"Because the water is hot\",\"Because glass bowls can break easily\",\"Because the spoon is sharp\",\"Because the music is too loud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Glass is a fragile material, so tapping it with a spoon requires care to avoid breaking it.\",\"topic\":\"Musical Glass Bowls\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of this demonstration?\",\"options\":[\"To show how to wash glass bowls\",\"To show how to pour water\",\"To show a simple musical instrument\",\"To show how to use a spoon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The speaker starts by saying, \'I want to show you a simple musical instrument.\'\",\"topic\":\"Musical Glass Bowls\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What liquid is kept inside the bottle for the experiment?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Vinegar\",\"Oil\",\"Juice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'This bottle holds vinegar.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Blowing Balloon\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the gas that forms when soda and vinegar are mixed?\",\"options\":[\"Oxygen\",\"Nitrogen\",\"Carbon dioxide\",\"Helium\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'a gas known as carbon dioxide forms.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Blowing Balloon\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why does the balloon blow up?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is filled with water\",\"Because of the gas formed\",\"Because the boy blew air into it\",\"Because the bottle is hot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The balloon blows up because of the gas.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Blowing Balloon\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the balloon hold before it is attached to the bottle?\",\"options\":[\"Baking soda\",\"Vinegar\",\"Air\",\"Water\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'This balloon holds baking soda.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Blowing Balloon\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where is the balloon fitted?\",\"options\":[\"On the boy\'s hand\",\"On the table\",\"On the mouth of the bottle\",\"On the soda jar\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the balloon attached to the top opening of the bottle.\",\"topic\":\"The Blowing Balloon\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/071_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what indicates that the gas has already formed inside the bottle?\",\"options\":[\"The boy is smiling\",\"The table is brown\",\"The jar is closed\",\"The balloon is blown up\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The inflated state of the balloon in the drawing shows that the gas has filled it.\",\"topic\":\"The Blowing Balloon\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/071_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What happens immediately after the soda falls into the bottle?\",\"options\":[\"The balloon blows up\",\"The bottle breaks\",\"The balloon shrinks\",\"The liquid turns blue\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text sequence is: soda falls in the bottle... then the balloon blows up.\",\"topic\":\"The Blowing Balloon\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To make the soda fall into the bottle, what action must the speaker take?\",\"options\":[\"Shake the bottle\",\"Lift the balloon\",\"Open the window\",\"Stir the liquid\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Now I will lift the balloon. Then the soda will fall in the bottle.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Blowing Balloon\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to repeat this experiment, which two substances must they mix?\",\"options\":[\"Soda and water\",\"Oil and vinegar\",\"Vinegar and soda\",\"Soda and juice\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The experiment is based on mixing soda and vinegar to form gas.\",\"topic\":\"The Blowing Balloon\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the speaker\'s main purpose in this passage?\",\"options\":[\"To sell balloons\",\"To teach how to cook\",\"To clean a bottle\",\"To present a science experiment\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The speaker starts by saying, \'I\'m going to present an experiment.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Blowing Balloon\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what material is attracted to a magnet?\",\"options\":[\"Plastic\",\"Iron\",\"Wood\",\"Glass\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a magnet attracts everything that is made of iron.\",\"topic\":\"Magic with Magnets\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the speaker use to demonstrate the magnet\'s power?\",\"options\":[\"Iron nails\",\"Paper clips\",\"Iron clips\",\"Steel pins\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions using \'clips\' which are made of iron.\",\"topic\":\"Magic with Magnets\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Through which of these does the magnet draw the clips first in the demonstration?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Glass\",\"Air\",\"Paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Just watch. It draws the clips through air\' before mentioning glass or water.\",\"topic\":\"Magic with Magnets\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'attracts\' mean in the sentence \'It attracts towards itself\'?\",\"options\":[\"Pushes away\",\"Draws or pulls towards\",\"Breaks into pieces\",\"Changes the color of\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the context of magnets, attraction means pulling objects towards itself.\",\"topic\":\"Magic with Magnets\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the speaker say the demonstration is \'not magic\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is science\",\"Because it is a trick\",\"Because it is boring\",\"Because the clips are heavy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The speaker explicitly states, \'But it\'s not magic. It is science.\'\",\"topic\":\"Magic with Magnets\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the \'Magic with Magnets\' demonstration?\",\"options\":[\"To show how to fill a bowl with water\",\"To show that magnets attract iron through different materials\",\"To show how to make iron clips\",\"To teach how to clean glass bowls\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The demonstration shows attraction through air, glass, and water to explain how magnets work.\",\"topic\":\"Magic with Magnets\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you put iron clips inside a glass bowl filled with water, how can you move them without touching the water?\",\"options\":[\"By blowing air on the glass\",\"By using a magnet outside the glass\",\"By shaking the bowl\",\"By using a piece of paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that a magnet draws clips through both glass and water.\",\"topic\":\"Magic with Magnets\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the speaker\'s suggestion at the end, how would you test the magnet further?\",\"options\":[\"By putting the magnet in the fire\",\"By trying to attract clips through paper\",\"By breaking the glass bowl\",\"By drinking the water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speaker ends by saying, \'Do you want to try it? Try it with paper.\'\",\"topic\":\"Magic with Magnets\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What can we conclude about the force of a magnet from this text?\",\"options\":[\"It only works in empty space\",\"It is blocked by water\",\"It can act through certain solid and liquid barriers\",\"It only works on things made of glass\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The demonstration proves the magnetic force passes through air (gas), glass (solid), and water (liquid).\",\"topic\":\"Magic with Magnets\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which sequence correctly shows the materials the magnet worked through in the demonstration?\",\"options\":[\"Air -> Glass -> Water\",\"Water -> Air -> Glass\",\"Paper -> Glass -> Air\",\"Glass -> Paper -> Water\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text follows the order: air, then glass bowl, then water inside the glass.\",\"topic\":\"Magic with Magnets\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What should be collected before starting the Science Funfair activity?\",\"options\":[\"Money\",\"Required materials\",\"Textbooks\",\"Prizes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that materials required for the activity should be collected beforehand.\",\"topic\":\"Instructions for Teachers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which language should the students practice presenting their experiments?\",\"options\":[\"Marathi\",\"Hindi\",\"English\",\"Sanskrit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions specify that students should practice presenting their experiments in English.\",\"topic\":\"Instructions for Teachers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What must the teacher do before the students try the experiments?\",\"options\":[\"Ask students to buy materials\",\"Try all experiments personally first\",\"Call the parents\",\"Write the results on the board\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the teacher to try all experiments themselves first.\",\"topic\":\"Instructions for Teachers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How should the children choose their experiments?\",\"options\":[\"By lottery\",\"As assigned by the teacher\",\"According to their own interest\",\"Alphabetically by name\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions state that children should be allowed to choose experiments according to their liking\\/interest.\",\"topic\":\"Instructions for Teachers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"For the \'pairs\' experiment, what specific tool is recommended to be of good quality?\",\"options\":[\"Battery\",\"Magnet\",\"Glass tube\",\"Copper wire\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions using a good magnet (loha-chumbak) for the pairs experiment.\",\"topic\":\"Instructions for Teachers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many students should be given the chance to present their experiments daily?\",\"options\":[\"The whole class\",\"Only one student\",\"Two to four students\",\"Ten students\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests giving two to four children the opportunity to present every day.\",\"topic\":\"Instructions for Teachers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the ultimate goal that can be achieved by adding more experiments to these?\",\"options\":[\"A school picnic\",\"A real science fair in school\",\"A class test\",\"A drawing competition\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that by adding more experiments, a real science fair can be organized in the school.\",\"topic\":\"Instructions for Teachers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of magnet is suggested for the specific experiment mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"A weak magnet\",\"A broken magnet\",\"A good magnet\",\"A large magnet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Marathi text uses the word \'changla\' (good) for the magnet to be used.\",\"topic\":\"Instructions for Teachers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides presenting in English, what else should the students practice regarding the experiment?\",\"options\":[\"Doing it quickly\",\"Doing it carefully\",\"Doing it silently\",\"Doing it without materials\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions emphasize practicing the experiment carefully (\'kalajipurvak\').\",\"topic\":\"Instructions for Teachers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the instructions, what is the teacher\'s first responsibility regarding the experiment materials?\",\"options\":[\"To sell them to students\",\"To collect them in advance\",\"To hide them until the fair\",\"To ask students to find them at home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The very first instruction is to collect the necessary materials beforehand.\",\"topic\":\"Instructions for Teachers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21662,27,5,'English','en','The Wind','[\"Wind is moving air.\",\"Wind can be felt but not seen.\",\"Wind helps in flying kites and sailing boats.\",\"Wind can be gentle (breeze) or strong (storm).\",\"Wind helps in scattering seeds and pollination.\",\"Windmills use wind to generate electricity.\",\"Wind direction can be found using a wind vane.\",\"Anemometer measures the speed of wind.\",\"Hot air rises, cool air sinks, creating wind.\",\"Wind can cause erosion and shape landscapes.\",\"We feel wind on our face when we run or ride a bicycle.\",\"Wind carries sound and smells over distances.\",\"In winter, cold winds make us feel colder.\",\"In summer, breeze gives relief from heat.\",\"Wind plays a role in the water cycle by moving clouds.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does the wind do to the kites according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"It tears them apart\",\"It tosses them on high\",\"It brings them down\",\"It makes them colorful\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I saw you toss the kites on high\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Wind - Stanza 2\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the wind blow the birds?\",\"options\":[\"Into their nests\",\"Under the trees\",\"About the sky\",\"Across the grass\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'And blow the birds about the sky\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Wind - Stanza 2\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sound does the wind make as it passes across the grass?\",\"options\":[\"Like a loud whistle\",\"Like ladies\' skirts\",\"Like a bird\'s song\",\"Like falling rain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poet compares the sound to \'ladies\' skirts across the grass\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Wind - Stanza 2\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How long does the wind blow for?\",\"options\":[\"Only at night\",\"For an hour\",\"All day long\",\"Only in the morning\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'O wind, a-blowing all day long\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Wind - Stanza 2\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of song does the wind sing?\",\"options\":[\"A soft song\",\"A loud song\",\"A sad song\",\"A quiet song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes it as a \'wind, that sings so loud a song!\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Wind - Stanza 2\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the second stanza, what is always true about the wind\'s appearance?\",\"options\":[\"It is very colorful\",\"It looks like a bird\",\"It hides itself\",\"It looks like a lady\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'But always you yourself you hid\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Wind - Stanza 2\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you were standing outside, what physical action of the wind might you feel according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A pull\",\"A push\",\"A tickle\",\"A scratch\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poet mentions, \'I felt you push\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Wind - Stanza 2\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these actions does the poet perform to experience the wind?\",\"options\":[\"He tastes the wind\",\"He smells the wind\",\"He hears the wind call\",\"He sees the wind\'s face\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poet says, \'I heard you call\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Wind - Stanza 2\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main mystery about the wind described in the second stanza?\",\"options\":[\"Why it sings so loudly\",\"Where it goes at night\",\"That it does things but cannot be seen\",\"Why it tosses kites so high\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The stanza emphasizes that the poet saw the things the wind did but \'could not see yourself at all\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Wind - Stanza 2\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which line suggests that the wind is a very active force?\",\"options\":[\"I could not see yourself at all\",\"I saw the different things you did\",\"Like ladies\' skirts across the grass\",\"But always you yourself you hid\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'different things you did\' implies the wind is constantly active and performing various tasks.\",\"topic\":\"The Wind - Stanza 2\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the poet of the poem \'The Wind\'?\",\"options\":[\"William Wordsworth\",\"Robert Louis Stevenson\",\"Rudyard Kipling\",\"Rabindranath Tagore\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem is written by Robert Louis Stevenson as mentioned at the end of the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two words are used to describe the wind in the first line?\",\"options\":[\"Hot and weak\",\"Soft and warm\",\"Strong and cold\",\"Fast and loud\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first line explicitly states, \'O you that are so strong and cold\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the wind do all day long according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Sleeps quietly\",\"Blows all day long\",\"Hides in the trees\",\"Plays with the children\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'O wind, a-blowing all day long\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The poet asks the wind if it is a \'beast\' of which two places?\",\"options\":[\"Mountain and river\",\"Sky and sea\",\"Field and tree\",\"House and garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem asks, \'Are you a beast of field and tree?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the poem, what kind of song does the wind sing?\",\"options\":[\"A soft song\",\"A loud song\",\"A sad song\",\"A sweet song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The last line mentions, \'O wind, that sings so loud a song!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the poem rhymes with \'cold\'?\",\"options\":[\"Tree\",\"Long\",\"Old\",\"Song\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the first two lines, \'cold\' rhymes with \'old\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does the poet compare his own strength to the wind\'s strength?\",\"options\":[\"The poet is stronger than the wind\",\"The wind is a stronger child than the poet\",\"They both have equal strength\",\"The poet is a beast and the wind is a child\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poet asks if the wind is \'just a stronger child than me?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the rhyming pair for the word \'long\' used in the poem.\",\"options\":[\"Strong\",\"Song\",\"Young\",\"Cold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The last two lines end with \'long\' and \'song\', which are rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When the poet calls the wind a \'blower\', what is he referring to?\",\"options\":[\"The wind\'s age\",\"The wind\'s song\",\"The wind\'s action of blowing\",\"The wind\'s coldness\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A \'blower\' is someone or something that blows, describing the wind\'s primary activity.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the poet mainly doing in the first four lines of the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Telling the wind to stop\",\"Asking the wind questions about its identity\",\"Singing a song with the wind\",\"Complaining about the cold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poet asks if the wind is young or old, a beast, or a stronger child.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21663,27,5,'English','en','\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'','[\"The story is set in ancient Korea.\",\"A minister lived between a blacksmith and a carpenter.\",\"The blacksmith made loud noises with his hammer: \'Tong, tong, tong\'.\",\"The carpenter worked with a small hammer and a saw: \'Tock, tock, tock\' and \'Krrr—krrr—krrr\'.\",\"Both workers made noise day and night.\",\"The noise disturbed the minister\'s peace.\",\"The minister decided he must do something about the noise.\",\"The story teaches about noise pollution and its effects.\",\"It shows how different occupations create different sounds.\",\"The words \'Go!\' and \'Come!\' in the title are commands used to direct action.\",\"Listening carefully helps us understand sounds around us.\",\"Onomatopoeic words like \'tong\', \'tock\', \'krrr\' imitate real sounds.\",\"Living in harmony means respecting others\' need for quiet.\",\"We should be aware of how our actions affect others.\",\"Stories from other cultures teach us universal values.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did the little boy live according to the story?\",\"options\":[\"In a pretty little cottage\",\"In a big stone castle\",\"In a small city apartment\",\"In a hut in the forest\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the little boy lived in a pretty little cottage.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What two things did the boy\'s strict uncle believe in?\",\"options\":[\"Hard work and discipline\",\"Playing and singing\",\"Sleeping and resting\",\"Eating and drinking\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the uncle believed in hard work and discipline.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these tasks was NOT mentioned as work to be done in the garden?\",\"options\":[\"Water the plants\",\"Give manure\",\"Paint the cottage\",\"Weed the garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists watering, manuring, pruning, weeding, and cleaning, but not painting.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'his eyes welled up\' suggest about the boy?\",\"options\":[\"He was very sleepy\",\"He was about to cry\",\"He was looking into a well\",\"He was very angry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Welled up eyes indicate that he was sad and tears were forming.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the boy feel that his uncle was \'unfair\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the uncle took his toys\",\"Because the uncle ordered him to work when he didn\'t feel like it\",\"Because the uncle didn\'t give him food\",\"Because the uncle was leaving the house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The boy felt sad and thought it was unfair because he was ordered to weed while he wanted to play.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, when should plants be cut and pruned?\",\"options\":[\"Every day\",\"At the right time\",\"From time to time\",\"Only when it rains\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'cut and prune the plants at the right time\'.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the boy doing when his uncle told him to weed the garden?\",\"options\":[\"He was sleeping\",\"He was playing in the house\",\"He was eating his lunch\",\"He was reading a book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'One day the boy was playing in the house\' when the uncle spoke to him.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the mother react when she heard about the weeding task?\",\"options\":[\"She got angry at the uncle\",\"She told the boy to go back to sleep\",\"She said it would be fun and offered to help\",\"She told the boy to finish his homework first\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The mother said, \'What fun that will be!\' and asked if she could help.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a gardener is \'weeding\', what is he actually doing?\",\"options\":[\"Planting new seeds\",\"Removing unwanted plants\",\"Picking flowers for a vase\",\"Building a fence\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Weeding refers to the process of removing weeds (unwanted plants) from a garden.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main difference between the uncle\'s approach and the mother\'s approach?\",\"options\":[\"The uncle was lazy, but the mother was hardworking\",\"The uncle gave an order (\'Go!\'), while the mother offered to join (\'Come!\')\",\"The uncle wanted to play, but the mother wanted to work\",\"There was no difference in how they spoke\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The uncle ordered the boy to \'Go!\', while the mother invited him to work together by saying \'Come!\'.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text describes someone who is \'mischievous\' or \'badly behaved\'?\",\"options\":[\"Strict\",\"Naughty\",\"Unfair\",\"Lovely\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'naughty\' to describe the boy when the uncle tells him not to be so.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the author of the story from which this text is adapted?\",\"options\":[\"Laura E. Richards\",\"William Wordsworth\",\"Robert Louis Stevenson\",\"Enid Blyton\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text credits \'Adapted from ‘Go!’ and ‘Come!’ by Laura E. Richards\'.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story\'s ending, why did the boy have a \'good time\' weeding?\",\"options\":[\"Because he finished the work very quickly\",\"Because he got a reward from his uncle\",\"Because he worked, chatted, and laughed with his mother\",\"Because he found a treasure in the garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says they had a good time \'working and chatting and laughing\' together.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the most prominent feature surrounding the cottage?\",\"options\":[\"A tall brick wall\",\"A lovely garden with plants and flowers\",\"A large swimming pool\",\"A busy city street\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The picture shows a cottage surrounded by a lush garden with many plants and flowers.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/073_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the boy\'s mood as he goes to work in the garden?\",\"options\":[\"He looks very angry and is shouting\",\"He looks happy and is smiling\",\"He is crying and looking at the ground\",\"He looks scared and is running away\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the boy smiling and looking happy while holding a gardening tool.\",\"topic\":\"\'Go!\' and \'Come!\'\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/074_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'unhappy\' as used in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Very glad\",\"Sad or not happy\",\"Extremely angry\",\"Feeling sleepy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'unhappy\' is the opposite of happy, meaning sad.\",\"topic\":\"Read and Guess Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list refers to a small, simple house?\",\"options\":[\"Matter\",\"Cottage\",\"Different\",\"Wobble\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A cottage is a small, simple house, typically in the country.\",\"topic\":\"Read and Guess Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'His chin began to wobble\', what does the word \'wobble\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"To stay perfectly still\",\"To turn blue\",\"To shake or tremble unsteadily\",\"To grow hair\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Wobble means to move unsteadily from side to side, often when someone is about to cry.\",\"topic\":\"Read and Guess Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the phrase \'His eyes welled up\'?\",\"options\":[\"He closed his eyes tightly\",\"His eyes filled with tears\",\"He looked at a deep well\",\"He put on glasses\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"To \'well up\' means that liquid (tears) rises to the surface of the eyes.\",\"topic\":\"Read and Guess Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is a synonym for \'pretty\'?\",\"options\":[\"Ugly\",\"Beautiful\",\"Dirty\",\"Large\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Pretty and beautiful have similar meanings regarding appearance.\",\"topic\":\"Read and Guess Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If two friends are \'chatting\', what are they doing?\",\"options\":[\"Running a race\",\"Eating lunch\",\"Talking in a friendly way\",\"Drawing pictures\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Chatting means talking in a light, informal, or friendly manner.\",\"topic\":\"Read and Guess Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'Uncle is so unfair\', what does the word \'unfair\' suggest about the Uncle\'s behavior?\",\"options\":[\"He is being very kind\",\"He is not treating someone justly or rightly\",\"He is very tall\",\"He is moving very fast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Unfair means not based on what is right or proper.\",\"topic\":\"Read and Guess Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text describes things that are not the same as each other?\",\"options\":[\"Little\",\"Different\",\"Matter\",\"Pretty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Different means not the same as another or each other.\",\"topic\":\"Read and Guess Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the sentences \'His chin began to wobble\' and \'His eyes welled up\', how is the person most likely feeling?\",\"options\":[\"Excited and joyful\",\"Upset and about to cry\",\"Brave and strong\",\"Hungry and thirsty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A wobbling chin and eyes filling with tears are physical signs of being upset or sad.\",\"topic\":\"Read and Guess Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list can be used to ask about a problem, as in \'What is the ___?\'\",\"options\":[\"Wobble\",\"Matter\",\"Cottage\",\"Chatting\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'matter\' refers to a subject or situation under consideration, often a problem.\",\"topic\":\"Read and Guess Meanings\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the opposite of the word \'go\'?\",\"options\":[\"come\",\"run\",\"stay\",\"walk\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'go × come\' as a pair of opposite action words.\",\"topic\":\"Collection of ‘opposite’ words\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word is listed as the opposite of \'different\'?\",\"options\":[\"new\",\"same\",\"small\",\"bad\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows the pair \'different × same\' under describing words for objects.\",\"topic\":\"Collection of ‘opposite’ words\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/075_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Under which category are the words \'little\' and \'big\' placed in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Action words\",\"Describing words for objects, people, etc.\",\"Describing words for actions\",\"Naming words\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'little × big\' under the heading \'Describing words for objects, people, etc.\'\",\"topic\":\"Collection of ‘opposite’ words\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The words \'now\' and \'then\' are examples of which type of describing words?\",\"options\":[\"Describing words for people\",\"Describing words for objects\",\"Describing words for actions\",\"Describing words for places\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text categorizes \'now × then\' as describing words for actions.\",\"topic\":\"Collection of ‘opposite’ words\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the category of \'Action words\', what would be a suitable opposite for \'push\'?\",\"options\":[\"pull\",\"throw\",\"give\",\"ask\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"While the text leaves the opposite of \'push\' blank, \'pull\' is the logical opposite action word.\",\"topic\":\"Collection of ‘opposite’ words\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are adding to the list of \'Describing words for actions\', what is the most likely opposite for the word \'up\'?\",\"options\":[\"down\",\"out\",\"left\",\"fast\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'up\' under describing words for actions; \'down\' is its common opposite.\",\"topic\":\"Collection of ‘opposite’ words\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the text is classified as an \'Action word\'?\",\"options\":[\"slowly\",\"clean\",\"throw\",\"sad\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'throw\' under the \'Action words\' category.\",\"topic\":\"Collection of ‘opposite’ words\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs belongs to the \'Describing words for objects, people, etc.\' category?\",\"options\":[\"go × come\",\"now × then\",\"good × bad\",\"up × down\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'good\' under describing words for objects\\/people; \'bad\' is its natural opposite.\",\"topic\":\"Collection of ‘opposite’ words\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many more pairs are we instructed to add to the \'Action words\' collection?\",\"options\":[\"At least 10\",\"At least 15\",\"At least 20\",\"At least 5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure explicitly states \'(Add at least 20 more pairs.)\' at the bottom of the Action words column.\",\"topic\":\"Collection of ‘opposite’ words\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/075_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the opposite of \'slowly\' according to the category \'Describing words for actions\'?\",\"options\":[\"fast\",\"quickly\",\"hurriedly\",\"rapidly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"While \'fast\' is common, \'quickly\' is the standard grammatical opposite for the adverb \'slowly\' in this context.\",\"topic\":\"Collection of ‘opposite’ words\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instructions for Activity 7, how many minutes are given to write related words?\",\"options\":[\"1 minute\",\"2 minutes\",\"3 minutes\",\"5 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states to write as many related words as you can within 3 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Word Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Activity 8, what is the minimum number of words you must add to the chain before returning to the first word?\",\"options\":[\"At least 2 words\",\"At least 3 words\",\"At least 5 words\",\"At least 10 words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions for the Word Chain activity specify to add at least 5 words to the chain.\",\"topic\":\"Word Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word is written on the flower at the very top of the \'mother\' vase?\",\"options\":[\"son\",\"father\",\"love\",\"family\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the drawing of the \'mother\' vase, the word \'father\' is written on the highest flower.\",\"topic\":\"Word Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/075_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main rule for choosing the next word in a \'Word Chain\'?\",\"options\":[\"It must start with the last letter of the previous word.\",\"It must rhyme with the previous word.\",\"It must be related to the previous word.\",\"It must have more letters than the previous word.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Write a word related to a given word. Then write a word that is related to the second word.\'\",\"topic\":\"Word Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the instruction \'come back to the first word\' mean in the context of the Word Chain activity?\",\"options\":[\"Restart the activity from the beginning.\",\"The last word added should be related to the very first word.\",\"Erase all words and write the first word again.\",\"Write the first word after every new word.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A word chain forms a loop where the final word relates back to the starting word.\",\"topic\":\"Word Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes the purpose of the \'Word Activities\' described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"To practice spelling difficult words.\",\"To learn how to draw vases and chains.\",\"To explore connections between different words.\",\"To memorize the names of family members.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Both activities focus on finding and linking \'related\' words, which explores word connections.\",\"topic\":\"Word Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are writing related words for a vase labeled \'School\', which word would be most appropriate to write on a flower?\",\"options\":[\"Teacher\",\"Forest\",\"Ocean\",\"Mountain\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A teacher is directly related to a school, whereas the other options are not.\",\"topic\":\"Word Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word from the list would be the most suitable related word for \'house\' in a word chain?\",\"options\":[\"eyes\",\"time\",\"naughty\",\"cottage\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"A cottage is a type of house, making it a related word.\",\"topic\":\"Word Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/075_104.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word is used to link \'doctor\' back to \'garden\' to complete the loop?\",\"options\":[\"medicine\",\"gardener\",\"water\",\"ice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the chain shown, \'doctor\' leads to \'gardener\', which then leads back to \'garden\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/075_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the example chain \'water -> ice -> cold -> cough\', why is \'cough\' a valid next step after \'cold\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they both start with the letter \'c\'.\",\"Because having a cold often causes a cough.\",\"Because they are both four-letter words.\",\"Because they are both things you can drink.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity requires words to be related; a cough is a symptom related to having a cold.\",\"topic\":\"Word Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21664,27,5,'English','en','The Golden Touch','[\"The story \'The Golden Touch\' is about a king named Midas who loves gold more than anything.\",\"Midas wished that everything he touched would turn into gold.\",\"The wish was granted by a magical being, often a god or fairy.\",\"At first, Midas was happy as he turned stones, roses, and food into gold.\",\"Soon, he realized his food turned to gold when he tried to eat, so he could not eat.\",\"Even his daughter turned into a golden statue when he hugged her.\",\"Midas became sad and realized that gold cannot bring happiness.\",\"He begged the magical being to take back the wish.\",\"The wish was taken away, and everything returned to normal.\",\"The moral of the story is: greed for wealth can lead to loss of what truly matters.\",\"True happiness comes from love, family, and simple joys, not from material riches.\",\"We should be content with what we have and not always want more.\",\"The story teaches us to value relationships over possessions.\",\"It warns against the dangers of excessive desire for wealth.\",\"The tale is a classic myth that teaches a timeless lesson about contentment.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where is King Midas sitting at the beginning of the scene?\",\"options\":[\"In a dark cellar\",\"In a beautiful garden\",\"On a golden throne\",\"In a locked bedroom\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'King Midas is sitting in a dark cellar.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is King Midas doing when the Stranger enters?\",\"options\":[\"Sleeping soundly\",\"Counting his gold\",\"Planting flowers\",\"Eating his breakfast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'He is counting his gold.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the Stranger enter the cellar?\",\"options\":[\"He uses a golden key\",\"The servant lets him in\",\"Locked doors cannot keep him out\",\"He climbs through a window\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Stranger says, \'Locked doors cannot keep me out.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Stranger, what is far more beautiful than gold?\",\"options\":[\"Jewels and diamonds\",\"Dark cellars\",\"Flowers and golden sunshine\",\"Locked doors\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Stranger says, \'In your garden are flowers and golden sunshine. They are far more beautiful.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How long has it taken King Midas to collect all his gold?\",\"options\":[\"A few days\",\"Many years\",\"One week\",\"Since sunrise\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"King Midas says, \'It has taken me many years to get all this gold.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is King Midas\'s specific wish?\",\"options\":[\"To have a garden of gold\",\"To be the strongest king\",\"That everything he touched would turn to gold\",\"To never have to sit in a cellar again\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Midas says, \'I wish that everything I touched would turn to gold.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When will King Midas receive the \'Golden Touch\'?\",\"options\":[\"Immediately\",\"At sunset today\",\"Tomorrow morning, at sunrise\",\"In many years\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Stranger says, \'Tomorrow morning, at sunrise, you shall have the Golden Touch.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why does King Midas want to be richer?\",\"options\":[\"To buy more flowers\",\"Because he believes gold makes you rich and everyone loves it\",\"To help the Stranger\",\"To unlock his cellar doors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Midas says, \'Why, everyone loves gold. It makes you rich.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If King Midas touches a flower in his garden after sunrise tomorrow, what will happen?\",\"options\":[\"It will wilt and die\",\"It will turn into real gold\",\"It will grow bigger\",\"Nothing will happen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since his wish is that everything he touches turns to gold, the flower would become gold.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the Stranger mean when he says, \'Perhaps you will be sorry\'?\",\"options\":[\"He is apologizing for being late\",\"He thinks the wish might lead to unhappiness\",\"He is sad that he is not rich\",\"He wants Midas to give him the gold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Stranger warns Midas that his wish might not bring the happiness he expects.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which character is NOT present in the dialogue of Scene I?\",\"options\":[\"King Midas\",\"The Stranger\",\"Marygold\",\"The King\'s shadow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Although Marygold is listed in the characters, she does not speak or act in this specific scene text.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How would you describe King Midas\'s attitude toward his wish at the end of the scene?\",\"options\":[\"He is fearful and worried\",\"He is angry at the Stranger\",\"He is extremely happy and excited\",\"He is bored and wants to sleep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Midas says, \'Oh, no! It\'s a dream come true!\' showing his excitement.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the King when Marygold was looking for him at the start of the scene?\",\"options\":[\"In his bedroom\",\"In the breakfast-room\",\"In the rose garden\",\"By the stream\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The servant tells Marygold that the King is in the rose garden.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Marygold notice about the King\'s bedroom?\",\"options\":[\"It was full of flowers\",\"Everything was turned to gold\",\"The servant was cleaning it\",\"The King was sleeping there\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Marygold mentions that everything in the King\'s bedroom is turned to gold.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Marygold cry when she smelled the rose the King gave her?\",\"options\":[\"She did not like the color yellow\",\"It had a very strong smell\",\"It had no smell and the hard petals pricked her nose\",\"She wanted a real golden rose instead\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Marygold cries because the golden rose has no smell and its hard petals pricked her nose.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which two food items are mentioned as turning to gold when the King tries to eat breakfast?\",\"options\":[\"Bread and butter\",\"Fish and an egg\",\"Apple and milk\",\"Meat and wine\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the fish and then an egg turning to gold.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the King\'s main problem during breakfast?\",\"options\":[\"The food is too hot\",\"He is not hungry\",\"Everything he touches turns to gold, so he cannot eat\",\"The servant forgot to bring his breakfast\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The King realizes he will never be able to eat because everything he touches turns to gold.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to Marygold when she rushes forward to help her father?\",\"options\":[\"She trips and falls\",\"She turns into a statue of gold\",\"She starts laughing\",\"She runs to the garden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"When the King touches her, Marygold turns into a statue of gold.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what has happened to the girl the King is touching?\",\"options\":[\"She is wearing a new yellow dress\",\"She has turned into a golden statue\",\"She is playing a game of hide and seek\",\"She is glowing because she is happy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Marygold as a solid yellow (golden) figure, representing the statue described in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/078_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what does the King\'s expression and posture suggest?\",\"options\":[\"He is very proud of his gold\",\"He is angry at the servant\",\"He is full of sorrow and regret\",\"He is excited to show off his daughter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The King is kneeling and looks distressed, matching his dialogue \'I am the unhappiest man in the world.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/078_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does the King compare Marygold to before she became a \'golden doll\'?\",\"options\":[\"A beautiful rose\",\"A ray of sunshine\",\"A sparkling diamond\",\"A piece of fruit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The King says she was \'So full of life! Like a ray of sunshine!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the King tell the Stranger he is the \'unhappiest man in the world\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because he lost his crown\",\"Because he has no gold left\",\"Because he cannot eat and his daughter is a statue\",\"Because the Stranger is his enemy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Despite having gold, the King is unhappy because he lost his daughter and cannot eat.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the King want to have in his garden instead of golden roses?\",\"options\":[\"Statues of himself\",\"Real flowers\",\"A bigger stream\",\"More fruit trees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The King tells the Stranger, \'I want real flowers in my garden.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first thing the Stranger tells the King to do to lose the Golden Touch?\",\"options\":[\"Drink a pitcher of water\",\"Bathe in the stream in the garden\",\"Give all his gold to the poor\",\"Touch the roses again\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Stranger tells him to \'go and bathe in the stream that flows through your garden.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What must the King use to sprinkle water on things he wants to change back?\",\"options\":[\"A golden cup\",\"His bare hands\",\"A pitcher\",\"A rose petal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Stranger instructs him to \'bring back a pitcher of water and sprinkle it.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why did the King say \'I hate it\' regarding the Golden Touch?\",\"options\":[\"It made him too famous\",\"It took away the things he truly loved and needed\",\"The gold was not shiny enough\",\"The Stranger forced him to keep it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The King hates the touch because it prevents him from eating and turned his daughter into a doll.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What name does the Stranger use to address the King?\",\"options\":[\"King Gold\",\"Friend Midas\",\"Master Midas\",\"Your Majesty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Stranger says, \'Well, friend Midas, what do you say now?\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"At the start of Scene III, what is Marygold described as?\",\"options\":[\"A little girl playing\",\"A golden statue\",\"A sleeping princess\",\"A flower in the garden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Marygold is still a statue\' at the beginning of the scene.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the King first sprinkle water?\",\"options\":[\"On the roses\",\"On the garden floor\",\"Over Marygold\'s head\",\"On his own hands\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The King says, \'First I will sprinkle some water over my dear little Marygold.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to Marygold after the King sprinkles water on her?\",\"options\":[\"She turns into a rose\",\"She comes alive\",\"She falls asleep\",\"She turns into solid gold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The stage direction in the text notes \'(Comes alive)\' after the water is sprinkled.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is Marygold\'s first question to her father when she wakes up?\",\"options\":[\"Where are the roses?\",\"Can we go to the garden?\",\"What are you doing, father?\",\"Why is everything gold?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Marygold\'s first line is \'What are you doing, father?\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does Marygold notice about her clothes?\",\"options\":[\"They are made of gold\",\"They are torn\",\"They are very dirty\",\"Water has been sprinkled on her frock\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Marygold says, \'You have sprinkled water on my frock.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what must the King do to the other things he touched?\",\"options\":[\"He must hide them\",\"He must sprinkle water on them\",\"He must sell them\",\"He must polish them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The King says, \'I have to sprinkle this on everything that I touched.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the King suggest they go?\",\"options\":[\"Into the palace\",\"To the market\",\"Into the garden\",\"To the river\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The King says, \'Let us go into the garden, Marygold.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does the King describe the roses they will get?\",\"options\":[\"Hard and shiny roses\",\"Golden roses with no smell\",\"Beautiful roses with a lovely smell\",\"Yellow roses from the palace\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The King mentions \'Beautiful roses with a lovely smell!\' at the end of the scene.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the King\'s attitude toward Marygold in this scene?\",\"options\":[\"Greedy\",\"Caring\",\"Angry\",\"Forgetful\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The King calls her \'dear little Marygold\' and focuses on bringing her back to life and taking her to the garden.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If the King finds a golden chair he touched earlier, what will he likely do next based on his dialogue?\",\"options\":[\"Sprinkle water on it\",\"Throw it away\",\"Keep it as a statue\",\"Give it to Marygold\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The King states he must sprinkle water on \'everything\' he touched to restore it.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21665,27,5,'English','en','Where Go the Boats?','[\"The chapter \'Where Go the Boats?\' is a poem by Robert Louis Stevenson about a child watching toy boats float away.\",\"The poem describes boats sailing down a river, passing under bridges and disappearing into the distance.\",\"It reflects on the journey of the boats and the child\'s imagination about where they might go.\",\"The tone is thoughtful and dreamy, focusing on observation and wonder.\",\"Key images include the river, boats, bridges, and the flowing water carrying the boats away.\",\"The poem uses simple language and rhythm suitable for young readers.\",\"It encourages children to think about movement, travel, and the unknown destination of things that float away.\",\"The boats are symbolic of dreams, thoughts, or things that leave our sight but continue onward.\",\"The child stands on the bank and watches, feeling both curiosity and a sense of loss.\",\"The poem does not have a fixed answer — it invites personal imagination about where the boats go.\",\"Repetition of \'Where go the boats?\' emphasizes the central question and mood of wondering.\",\"The river represents the passage of time or life\'s journey.\",\"The poem is part of Stevenson\'s collection \'A Child\'s Garden of Verses\'.\",\"It helps develop listening skills, imagination, and appreciation for nature and simple journeys.\",\"Students are encouraged to visualize the scene and express their thoughts in words or drawings.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the first stanza of the poem, what color is the river?\",\"options\":[\"Golden\",\"Dark brown\",\"Green\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states \'Dark brown is the river\' in the very first line.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is described as \'golden\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"The river\",\"The foam\",\"The sand\",\"The leaves\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The second line of the poem says \'Golden is the sand.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet mean by the phrase \'With trees on either hand\'?\",\"options\":[\"Trees are growing inside the river\",\"Trees are on both sides of the river\",\"The poet is holding trees in his hands\",\"There are no trees near the river\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'On either hand\' is a poetic way of saying on both sides.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are the \'castles\' mentioned in the second stanza made of?\",\"options\":[\"Sand\",\"Wood\",\"Foam\",\"Stone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions \'Castles of the foam\' floating on the water.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the child doing at the riverbank?\",\"options\":[\"Building a mill\",\"Setting paper boats afloat\",\"Planting green leaves\",\"Digging for golden sand\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a child crouched by the water placing paper boats into the river.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/080_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the third stanza, which of these does the river flow past?\",\"options\":[\"A castle\",\"A mill\",\"A bridge\",\"A forest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states \'And out past the mill\' in the third stanza.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the river go after passing the mill?\",\"options\":[\"Up the hill and into the sand\",\"Away down the valley and down the hill\",\"Back to the child\'s home\",\"Into a dark brown forest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem describes the path as \'Away down the valley, Away down the hill.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the boats after they travel a hundred miles or more?\",\"options\":[\"They sink in the dark brown river\",\"They turn into castles of foam\",\"Other little children bring them ashore\",\"They float back to the mill\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The final stanza says \'Other little children Shall bring my boats ashore.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what objects are shown floating on the water surface besides the boats?\",\"options\":[\"Large stones and fish\",\"Green leaves and white foam\",\"Golden sand and trees\",\"A mill and a valley\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration depicts green leaves and white bubbly foam floating alongside the paper boats.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/080_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, why does the poet ask \'Where will all come home?\'\",\"options\":[\"He is lost and wants to find his way back\",\"He is curious about the final destination of his boats\",\"He is worried about the trees on either hand\",\"He wants to know where the mill is located\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The question reflects the poet\'s wonder about where the river will eventually take his boats.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the author of the poem \'Where Go the Boats?\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"R. L. Stevenson\",\"William Wordsworth\",\"Rudyard Kipling\",\"Robert Frost\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions R. L. Stevenson as the author.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the English meaning of the Marathi word \'फेस\'?\",\"options\":[\"Floating\",\"Foam\",\"Ashore\",\"Castles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'foam\' as \'फेस\' (foam).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'a-floating\' mean in English?\",\"options\":[\"Sinking\",\"Flying\",\"Floating\",\"Running\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text translates \'a-floating\' to the Marathi word \'तरंगणारी\', which means floating.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a boat reaches the land near the water, it is said to be ______.\",\"options\":[\"a-floating\",\"foam\",\"ashore\",\"castles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'ashore\' as \'किनाऱ्यावर\', which means on the shore.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text refers to \'forts\' or \'palaces\'?\",\"options\":[\"Foam\",\"Castles\",\"Ashore\",\"a-floating\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'castles\' as \'किल्ले\' (forts) or \'राजवाडे\' (palaces).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words describes something that is staying on top of the water?\",\"options\":[\"Ashore\",\"Castles\",\"a-floating\",\"Foam\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'a-floating\' (तरंगणारी) describes the state of staying on the water surface.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the Marathi meaning of the word \'ashore\'?\",\"options\":[\"तरंगणारी\",\"किनाऱ्यावर\",\"किल्ले\",\"फेस\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'ashore\' with the Marathi meaning \'किनाऱ्यावर\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you see white bubbles on the river water, which word from the text best describes it?\",\"options\":[\"Castles\",\"Ashore\",\"Foam\",\"a-floating\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Foam (फेस) refers to the bubbles or froth seen on water.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Choose the correct pair of English word and its Marathi meaning based on the text.\",\"options\":[\"Foam - किल्ले\",\"Ashore - तरंगणारी\",\"Castles - किल्ले\",\"a-floating - फेस\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text correctly pairs \'castles\' with \'किल्ले\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the list is used to describe a location rather than an object or action?\",\"options\":[\"a-floating\",\"foam\",\"ashore\",\"castles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Ashore\' refers to a location (on the shore), while the others are actions or objects.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21666,27,5,'English','en','Our Solar System','[\"The Solar System consists of the Sun and all objects that orbit it.\",\"There are eight planets in the Solar System: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune.\",\"Planets are divided into inner (rocky) and outer (gas giant) planets.\",\"Mercury is the closest planet to the Sun and the smallest planet.\",\"Venus is the hottest planet due to its thick atmosphere and greenhouse effect.\",\"Earth is the only known planet to support life.\",\"Mars is called the Red Planet because of iron oxide (rust) on its surface.\",\"Jupiter is the largest planet and has a Great Red Spot, a giant storm.\",\"Saturn is known for its prominent ring system made of ice and rock.\",\"Uranus rotates on its side, with an axial tilt of about 98 degrees.\",\"Neptune is the farthest known planet from the Sun and has strong winds.\",\"Pluto was reclassified as a dwarf planet in 2006 by the IAU.\",\"Asteroids are rocky objects mostly found in the asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter.\",\"Comets are icy bodies that develop glowing tails when they approach the Sun.\",\"A moon is a natural satellite that orbits a planet; Earth has one moon.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, in which direction does the Sun rise?\",\"options\":[\"West\",\"North\",\"East\",\"South\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'You say that I rise in the east\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Sun\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the Sun say it actually is?\",\"options\":[\"A planet\",\"A star\",\"A moon\",\"A cloud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Actually, I am a star like other stars you see at night.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Sun\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the Sun look so big and bright compared to other stars?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is the only star\",\"Because it is close to the earth\",\"Because it rises in the east\",\"Because it goes round the earth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains, \'But I am close to the earth. That is why, I look so big and bright.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Sun\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What two things does the Sun provide to the earth?\",\"options\":[\"Water and air\",\"Food and shelter\",\"Heat and light\",\"Rocks and soil\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I give the earth heat and light.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Sun\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these statements is true about the movement of the Sun and Earth?\",\"options\":[\"The Sun goes round the earth\",\"The earth goes round the Sun\",\"The stars go round the Sun\",\"The Sun does not move at all\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text clarifies, \'I don\'t go round the earth. The earth goes round me.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Sun\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a pupil is watching the Sun set, which direction are they looking towards?\",\"options\":[\"East\",\"West\",\"North\",\"South\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the Sun sets in the west.\",\"topic\":\"The Sun\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main difference mentioned between the Sun and the stars seen at night?\",\"options\":[\"The Sun is a star but the others are not\",\"The Sun is close to earth while others are far\",\"The Sun gives light but others do not\",\"The Sun stays in the sky but others do not\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes the Sun is a star like others, but it is close to the earth.\",\"topic\":\"The Sun\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"When does the text say you see the Sun in the sky?\",\"options\":[\"Every day\",\"Only at night\",\"Every week\",\"Only in the west\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text begins with, \'You see me in the sky every day.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Sun\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which celestial body is depicted with a face?\",\"options\":[\"The Moon\",\"The Earth\",\"The Sun\",\"A Planet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a bright, orange-yellow sphere which the text identifies as the Sun.\",\"topic\":\"The Sun\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/082_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure and the text, what is the primary function of the object shown for the Earth?\",\"options\":[\"To make the Earth go round it\",\"To provide heat and light\",\"To rise in the west\",\"To look small and dim\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the Sun (shown in the figure) gives the earth heat and light.\",\"topic\":\"The Sun\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/082_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which planet is the Earth from the sun?\",\"options\":[\"First\",\"Second\",\"Third\",\"Fourth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I am the third planet from the sun.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Earth\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How much time does the Earth take to go round the sun?\",\"options\":[\"One day\",\"One week\",\"One month\",\"One year\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'I take one year to go round the sun.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Earth\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do some people call the Earth the \'blue planet\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is very cold\",\"Because much of its surface is covered with water\",\"Because it is the third planet\",\"Because it has an envelope of air\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that much of the surface is covered with water, making it appear blue from space.\",\"topic\":\"The Earth\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is present around the Earth like an envelope?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Air\",\"Space\",\"Sunlight\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'There is an envelope of air around me.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Earth\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a scientist travels to space and looks back, what color will the Earth appear?\",\"options\":[\"Green\",\"Blue\",\"Brown\",\"White\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'If you look at me from space, I appear blue in colour.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Earth\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who makes their home on the Earth today according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only humans\",\"Only plants and animals\",\"Plants, animals, and human beings\",\"Only birds and fish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions it is the only home of plants, animals, and human beings.\",\"topic\":\"The Earth\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which two actions does the Earth perform at the same time?\",\"options\":[\"Spins around itself and goes round the sun\",\"Stops spinning and goes round the sun\",\"Goes round the moon and the sun\",\"Spins around the sun and goes round itself\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I spin around myself all the time. At the same time, I go round the sun.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Earth\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is special about the Earth \'today\' compared to other places?\",\"options\":[\"It is the only planet with water\",\"It is the only home of plants, animals, and human beings\",\"It is the only planet that spins\",\"It is the only planet in the solar system\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text highlights that today, Earth is the only home for these living beings.\",\"topic\":\"The Earth\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which planet is shown introducing itself?\",\"options\":[\"Mars\",\"Jupiter\",\"Earth\",\"Venus\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a cartoon of the Earth, which corresponds to the text \'I am the earth.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Earth\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/082_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the planet appears mostly blue. According to the text, what covers much of its surface to make it look this way?\",\"options\":[\"Air\",\"Land\",\"Water\",\"Ice\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The blue color in the drawing represents the water that the text says covers much of the surface.\",\"topic\":\"The Earth\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/082_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the Earth\'s closest neighbour according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The Sun\",\"The Moon\",\"A spacecraft\",\"An astronaut\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'I am your closest neighbour,\' referring to the Moon.\",\"topic\":\"The Moon\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the Moon move in relation to the Earth?\",\"options\":[\"It stays in one place\",\"It goes round and round the earth\",\"It moves away from the earth\",\"It only moves during the day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Moon says, \'I go round and round the earth.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Moon\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many astronauts have landed on the Moon?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Many\",\"None\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'two astronauts from earth landed on me once.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Moon\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do people on Earth send spacecrafts to the Moon?\",\"options\":[\"To take it away\",\"To live there forever\",\"To study it from close\",\"To hide from the Sun\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'They send spacecrafts to study me from close.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Moon\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the Moon is shown with a smiling face and waving hands. According to the text, who is the Moon greeting?\",\"options\":[\"The Sun\",\"Other planets\",\"People on earth\",\"The stars\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text begins with the Moon saying, \'Hello, people on earth!\'\",\"topic\":\"The Moon\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/083_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What do people on Earth write about the Moon because they love it?\",\"options\":[\"Science textbooks only\",\"Stories and poems\",\"Letters to the Sun\",\"Newspapers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'They write stories and poems about me.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Moon\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the Moon is personified with a face. Based on the text, why might the illustrator have chosen to give the Moon a friendly expression?\",\"options\":[\"Because the Moon is very hot\",\"Because people on earth love the Moon\",\"Because the Moon is very far away\",\"Because the Moon is made of cheese\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'People on earth love me,\' which justifies a friendly, smiling depiction.\",\"topic\":\"The Moon\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/083_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the Moon can people on Earth never see?\",\"options\":[\"The bright side\",\"The front side\",\"The other side or the other half\",\"The top side\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'You never see the other side or the other half of me.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Moon\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the Moon suggest might happen \'some day\'?\",\"options\":[\"The Moon will disappear\",\"The Moon will stop moving\",\"Other people on earth will visit the Moon\",\"The Moon will crash into Earth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Maybe, some day, other people on earth will also come to visit me.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Moon\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If you are looking at the Moon from Earth, what is the maximum amount of its surface you can see at any time according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Both sides\",\"Only one side\",\"The whole Moon\",\"None of it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'From the earth, you always see only one side of me.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Moon\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21667,27,5,'English','en','Guess What!','[\"- **Present tense**: Use for actions happening now or regularly (e.g., *I am reading*).\",\"- **Future tense**: Use for actions that will happen (e.g., *I will read*).\",\"- **Animals make sounds**: Cats purr, lions roar, owls hoot, etc. Remember the correct verb form: *A cat purrs*.\",\"- **Experiment with vinegar and baking soda**: When mixed, they produce carbon dioxide gas that inflates a balloon.\",\"- **Magnet attraction**: Magnets attract iron objects; they can pull metal clips through air, water, or glass.\",\"- **Wind**: A natural force that blows, sings, and can be felt but not seen.\",\"- **Writing sentences**: Use subject + verb + object. Example: *The cat purrs*.\",\"- **Conversation starters**: “Hello”, “May I know who’s calling?”, “Please speak louder”.\",\"- **Listening and repeating**: Good practice for pronunciation and memory.\",\"- **Experiment safety**: Be careful with hot water, sharp objects, and chemicals.\",\"- **Vocabulary**: *experiment, attract, magnet, carbon dioxide, bubble, sound, wind*.\"]','[{\"q\":\"At what time does Ishani get up every day?\",\"options\":[\"7.00\",\"7.30\",\"5.00\",\"6.30\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Ishani says, \'I get up at 7.30 every day.\'\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Completion Table\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What time did Ishani get up \'Today\'?\",\"options\":[\"7.30\",\"5.00\",\"7.00\",\"8.00\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ishani states, \'Today, I got up at 7.00\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Completion Table\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is Ishani\'s plan for \'Some day\' regarding her wake-up time?\",\"options\":[\"To get up at 7.00\",\"To get up at 7.30\",\"To get up at 5.00\",\"To never get up early\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ishani says, \'Some day, I am going to get up at 5.00\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Completion Table\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the table, what did Ishani eat \'Today\'?\",\"options\":[\"Vegetables\",\"A poem\",\"Spinach\",\"Fruit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'ate spinach\' under the \'Today\' column for the food row.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Completion Table\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the table, what does Ishani plan to do \'Some day\' in the second row?\",\"options\":[\"Eat vegetables\",\"Cook\",\"Ate spinach\",\"Read a book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Some day\' column for the second row lists \'cook\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Completion Table\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Ishani \'read books\' every day, what did she do \'Today\'?\",\"options\":[\"Wrote a book\",\"Read a poem\",\"Cooked food\",\"Listened to music\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'read a poem\' in the \'Today\' column for the first row.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Completion Table\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the \'Today\' action for the music row: \'Every day: listen to music; Today: _______\'.\",\"options\":[\"listened to music\",\"learn to sing\",\"cook\",\"walked\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Following the past tense pattern of \'Today\', \'listen\' becomes \'listened to\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Completion Table\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Ishani \'walked to school\' today, how does she usually go \'Every day\'?\",\"options\":[\"Come on a bicycle\",\"Walk to school\",\"Run to school\",\"By bus\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'walk to school\' under the \'Every day\' column for the last row.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Completion Table\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which column in the table represents actions that have already happened or happened specifically on this date?\",\"options\":[\"Every day\",\"Today\",\"Some day\",\"Never\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Today\' column uses past tense verbs like \'got up\', \'read\', \'ate\', and \'walked\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Completion Table\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the future intention for the first row in the \'Some day\' column?\",\"options\":[\"Read books\",\"Read a poem\",\"Write a book\",\"Learn to sing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'write a book\' as the \'Some day\' goal for the first row.\",\"topic\":\"Sentence Completion Table\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, where does the sun always rise?\",\"options\":[\"In the west\",\"In the east\",\"In the north\",\"In the south\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The sun always rises in the east.\'\",\"topic\":\"Always and Never Examples\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text say we should never do?\",\"options\":[\"Speak gently\",\"Finish homework\",\"Shout\",\"Rise in the east\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says, \'We should never shout.\'\",\"topic\":\"Always and Never Examples\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'The sun never rises in the west\', what does the word \'never\' indicate?\",\"options\":[\"It happens every day\",\"It does not happen at any time\",\"It happens sometimes\",\"It happens only in the morning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'never\' is used to show an action that does not occur.\",\"topic\":\"Always and Never Examples\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How should we always speak to others according to the examples?\",\"options\":[\"Loudly\",\"Gently\",\"Quickly\",\"Rudely\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'We should always speak gently.\'\",\"topic\":\"Always and Never Examples\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence based on the text: The sun ____ rises in the west.\",\"options\":[\"always\",\"never\",\"often\",\"sometimes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the example: \'The sun never rises in the west.\'\",\"topic\":\"Always and Never Examples\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the grammar note in the text, which is the correct way to write the sentence about \'She\'?\",\"options\":[\"She always finish her homework.\",\"She always finishes her homework.\",\"She always finishing her homework.\",\"She always to finish her homework.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the specific example: \'She always finishes her homework.\'\",\"topic\":\"Always and Never Examples\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used in the text as the opposite of \'always\'?\",\"options\":[\"Gently\",\"Shout\",\"Never\",\"West\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'always\' actions with \'never\' actions as opposites.\",\"topic\":\"Always and Never Examples\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the sun never rise according to the lesson?\",\"options\":[\"East\",\"West\",\"North\",\"South\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The sun never rises in the west.\'\",\"topic\":\"Always and Never Examples\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If \'speaking gently\' is an action we should always do, what is the opposite action we should never do?\",\"options\":[\"Rising\",\"Finishing\",\"Shouting\",\"Reading\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text contrasts \'speak gently\' with \'shout\'.\",\"topic\":\"Always and Never Examples\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sentences correctly follows the pattern of using a singular subject with \'always\' as shown in the text?\",\"options\":[\"He always shout.\",\"He always shouts.\",\"He always shouting.\",\"He always to shout.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Following the example \'She always finishes\', a singular subject like \'He\' requires the \'s\' form of the verb.\",\"topic\":\"Always and Never Examples\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21668,27,5,'English','en','A Book Speaks','[\"The story is about a little boy who does not want to weed the garden.\",\"His uncle orders him to weed the garden as a form of discipline.\",\"The boy feels sad and unhappy about doing the work.\",\"His mother joins him in weeding the garden.\",\"They work together, chat, laugh, and enjoy the time spent together.\",\"The boy realizes that working with his mother made the task enjoyable.\",\"The story teaches that working together can make hard work feel lighter.\",\"The phrase \'Many hands make light work\' means teamwork reduces effort.\",\"The boy learns that discipline and helping family can lead to happiness.\",\"The garden work includes watering, adding manure, pruning, weeding, and cleaning.\",\"Everyone in the boy’s family helps take care of the garden.\",\"The boy initially thinks weeding is unpleasant but changes his mind after working with his mother.\",\"Emotions like sadness, unhappiness, and later joy are shown in the story.\",\"The mother’s kindness and willingness to help change the boy’s mood.\",\"The story is adapted from ‘Go!’ and ‘Come!’ by Laura E. Richards.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what happens to the book\'s sides when it is dropped on the floor?\",\"options\":[\"They become sore\",\"They become strong\",\"They become clean\",\"They become colorful\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'When you drop me on the floor I get stepped on - my sides are sore\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Book Speaks\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What specific action makes the book \'groan\'?\",\"options\":[\"Reading the book\",\"Torn-out pages\",\"Closing the book\",\"Keeping it on a shelf\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Torn-out pages make me groan\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Book Speaks\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What gives the book pain on its covers?\",\"options\":[\"Every mark and every stain\",\"The title of the book\",\"The weight of the pages\",\"The hands of the reader\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'Every mark and every stain On my covers gives me pain\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Book Speaks\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the book feel if it is \'thrown\'?\",\"options\":[\"Excited\",\"Sleepy\",\"Dizzy\",\"Angry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'I feel dizzy if I\'m thrown\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Book Speaks\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the book say it will do if you bend it?\",\"options\":[\"It will cry loudly\",\"It will not want to talk to you\",\"It will break into pieces\",\"It will become easier to read\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Please don\'t bend me, if you do I don\'t want to talk to you\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Book Speaks\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Under what condition will the book and the reader be \'friends together\'?\",\"options\":[\"If the reader drops the book\",\"If the reader draws on the covers\",\"If the reader protects it from the weather\",\"If the reader throws it in the air\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states they will be friends \'If you protect me from the weather\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Book Speaks\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the book is shown falling. According to the poem, how does the book feel when this action happens?\",\"options\":[\"It feels happy to fly\",\"It feels dizzy\",\"It feels very strong\",\"It feels like singing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'I feel dizzy if I\'m thrown\', which matches the action in the picture.\",\"topic\":\"A Book Speaks\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/085_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants their book to look \'tidy, neat and happy\', what should they do?\",\"options\":[\"Leave it outside in the rain\",\"Keep it clean\",\"Step on it\",\"Tear the pages\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says to \'keep me clean so that I look A tidy, neat and happy book\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Book Speaks\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the book has a pained expression. Based on the poem, which of these is a reason for the book to feel this way?\",\"options\":[\"It is being kept clean\",\"It is being protected from weather\",\"It is being dropped or thrown\",\"It is being read carefully\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem explains that dropping or throwing the book causes it to be sore or dizzy.\",\"topic\":\"A Book Speaks\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/085_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet use words like \'groan\', \'dizzy\', and \'pain\' for the book?\",\"options\":[\"To show that books are made of paper\",\"To show that books have feelings and can be hurt by bad handling\",\"To teach children how to throw things\",\"To explain that books are very heavy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem personifies the book to show how mistreatment affects it negatively.\",\"topic\":\"A Book Speaks\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instruction, what are you asked to present?\",\"options\":[\"A story\",\"A poem\",\"A picture\",\"A song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'Present the poem\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should be used while presenting the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Proper actions\",\"Loud music\",\"Crayons\",\"A notebook\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The instruction states \'with proper actions\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the Marathi word for \'poem\' used in the text?\",\"options\":[\"गाणे\",\"गोष्ट\",\"कविता\",\"धडा\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Marathi translation provided in the text uses the word \'कविता\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the instruction \'Present the poem\', what does the word \'Present\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"To give a gift\",\"To perform or show\",\"To be in class\",\"To write down\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the context of a poem and actions, \'present\' means to perform it.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'proper\' suggest about the actions?\",\"options\":[\"They should be very fast\",\"They should be suitable for the poem\",\"They should be funny\",\"They should be random\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Proper\' means appropriate or suitable for the specific poem being presented.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which Marathi phrase corresponds to \'Present\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"योग्य त्या\",\"हावभावांसह\",\"कविता\",\"सादर करा\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"\'सादर करा\' is the Marathi translation for \'Present\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student uses hand gestures and facial expressions while reciting, they are following which part of the instruction?\",\"options\":[\"Present the poem\",\"Proper actions\",\"योग्य त्या\",\"कविता\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Hand gestures and expressions are examples of \'proper actions\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The instruction is provided in English and which other language?\",\"options\":[\"Hindi\",\"Marathi\",\"Sanskrit\",\"Gujarati\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text \'योग्य त्या हावभावांसह कविता सादर करा\' is in Marathi.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the Marathi text refers specifically to \'gestures\' or \'actions\'?\",\"options\":[\"योग्य\",\"हावभावांसह\",\"कविता\",\"सादर\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'हावभाव\' means gestures or actions.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the Marathi translation \'योग्य त्या हावभावांसह कविता सादर करा\', which word matches the English word \'proper\'?\",\"options\":[\"योग्य\",\"हावभावांसह\",\"कविता\",\"सादर\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'योग्य\' is the Marathi equivalent for \'proper\' or \'suitable\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21669,27,5,'English','en','George Washington Carver','[\"George Washington Carver was born in 1861.\",\"He lost his parents at a young age.\",\"He loved plants from childhood and was called the \'plant doctor\'.\",\"He went from place to place to find a college.\",\"He taught at the Tuskegee Institute in Alabama.\",\"He helped farmers in Alabama improve their soil.\",\"He discovered many uses for peanuts and sweet potatoes.\",\"He died in 1943.\",\"He promoted crop rotation to restore soil fertility.\",\"His work helped poor farmers grow better crops.\",\"He believed in learning from nature.\",\"He was a scientist and inventor.\",\"He did not patent most of his discoveries.\",\"He wanted to help people, not get rich.\",\"He is remembered as a great American scientist.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which place was the man going for a walk when he slipped?\",\"options\":[\"Alabama\",\"Atlanta\",\"Alaska\",\"Arizona\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that a man in Alabama had gone out for a walk.\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the profession of George Washington Carver?\",\"options\":[\"Teacher\",\"Scientist\",\"Doctor\",\"Painter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies George Washington Carver as a \'famous scientist\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was unusual about the stains on the man\'s clothes?\",\"options\":[\"They were brown like mud\",\"They were bright red\",\"They were blue\",\"They disappeared quickly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the man saw the stains were blue.\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does a \'true scientist\' want to study?\",\"options\":[\"Only expensive things\",\"Everything, even mud stains\",\"Only things in books\",\"Only the stars\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'A true scientist wants to study everything - even mud stains!\'\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, what item did the man first use to try and clean his clothes?\",\"options\":[\"A brush\",\"Soap and water\",\"A handkerchief\",\"A piece of paper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says he took out his handkerchief and began to clean his clothes.\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Carver\'s students paint the local church?\",\"options\":[\"Because it was a holiday\",\"Because the church needed paint\",\"Because they wanted to waste the soil\",\"Because they were bored\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'A church in that town needed paint.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What makes Carver\'s discovery of the blue paint remarkable?\",\"options\":[\"It was very expensive to make\",\"It was made from common soil under their feet\",\"It was imported from another country\",\"It only lasted for one day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text highlights that no one could believe the paint was made from the soil under their feet.\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What happened when the man washed the handkerchief?\",\"options\":[\"The blue stains were still there\",\"The handkerchief turned white\",\"The handkerchief was destroyed\",\"The stains turned brown\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'He washed the handkerchief. But the blue stains were still there.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did Carver find out how to make the blue paint?\",\"options\":[\"He bought a recipe\",\"He asked the church\",\"He performed many tests in his lab\",\"He found a book on the road\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'After many tests, he learnt how to make good quality blue paint from the soil.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a scientist wants to follow Carver\'s example to solve a mystery, what should they do first?\",\"options\":[\"Forget about it\",\"Go to a lab and test it\",\"Buy new clothes\",\"Wait for someone else to do it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Carver showed that a scientist rushes to the lab to test and study things.\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what kind of border surrounds the portrait of the man?\",\"options\":[\"A border of stars\",\"A border of flowers\",\"A border of laboratory tools\",\"A border of mud splashes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a portrait of George Washington Carver surrounded by a decorative border of pink flowers.\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/086_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text and the given figure, which famous person is shown in the portrait?\",\"options\":[\"A man who lost his handkerchief\",\"A student from Alabama\",\"George Washington Carver\",\"A church priest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes George Washington Carver as the famous scientist who discovered the blue paint, and the figure shows his portrait.\",\"topic\":\"The Discovery of Blue Paint\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"27\\/086_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In which year was George Washington Carver born?\",\"options\":[\"1851\",\"1861\",\"1871\",\"1881\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that George Washington Carver was born in 1861.\",\"topic\":\"Early Life and the \'Plant Doctor\'\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Carver\'s family work?\",\"options\":[\"In a factory\",\"In a school\",\"On a farm\",\"In a hospital\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that his family worked on a farm in America.\",\"topic\":\"Early Life and the \'Plant Doctor\'\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the status of Carver\'s parents?\",\"options\":[\"They were doctors\",\"They were slaves\",\"They were teachers\",\"They were farm owners\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that his parents were slaves.\",\"topic\":\"Early Life and the \'Plant Doctor\'\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to Carver while he was still a baby?\",\"options\":[\"He moved to a new country\",\"He started working on the farm\",\"He lost both his parents\",\"He became a doctor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says he lost both his parents when he was still a baby.\",\"topic\":\"Early Life and the \'Plant Doctor\'\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Carver care for plants as a child?\",\"options\":[\"He was forced to do so\",\"He wanted to sell them\",\"He loved them\",\"He wanted to be famous\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Carver loved plants even as a child and therefore cared for them.\",\"topic\":\"Early Life and the \'Plant Doctor\'\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What special ability did Carver show regarding plants?\",\"options\":[\"He could make them grow instantly\",\"He understood what they wanted and what was wrong with them\",\"He could talk to animals about plants\",\"He knew how to cook all types of plants\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says he understood what the plants wanted and what was wrong with them.\",\"topic\":\"Early Life and the \'Plant Doctor\'\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a neighbor had a plant that was not growing well, why would they go to young Carver?\",\"options\":[\"Because he was a slave\",\"Because he was the oldest boy on the farm\",\"Because he knew what was wrong with plants\",\"Because he owned the farm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since he understood what was wrong with plants, people sought