 -s at the end\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the beginning of a sentence always starts with a capital letter.\",\"topic\":\"Capital Letters and Plurals\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the group where all words are plurals ending in \'-s\' as per the text examples.\",\"options\":[\"cups, birds\",\"bushes, buses\",\"flies, stories\",\"God, Jaikishan\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'cups\' and \'birds\' as examples of plurals ending in -s.\",\"topic\":\"Capital Letters and Plurals\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following sentences follows the capitalization rule correctly?\",\"options\":[\"but God can see my work.\",\"But god can see my work.\",\"But God can see my work.\",\"but god can see my work.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sentence must start with a capital letter (\'But\') and the name \'God\' should have a capital \'G\'.\",\"topic\":\"Capital Letters and Plurals\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is used to show who something belongs to in English?\",\"options\":[\"Only the letter \'s\'\",\"The symbol \'s\",\"The word \'an\'\",\"The word \'a\'\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'s is used to show \'whose\' something is (possession).\",\"topic\":\"Use of Apostrophe\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct way to show a doll belonging to Meena?\",\"options\":[\"Meenas doll\",\"Meena doll\",\"Meena\'s doll\",\"Meenas\' doll\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Meena\'s doll is the correct example of showing possession.\",\"topic\":\"Use of Apostrophe\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"For plural words ending in -s or -es, what is added to show possession?\",\"options\":[\"Only an apostrophe ( \' )\",\"An apostrophe and s ( \'s )\",\"The word \'an\'\",\"Nothing is added\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that for plural words ending in -s\\/-es, only \' is added at the end.\",\"topic\":\"Use of Apostrophe\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is the correct way to write \'ears of rabbits\'?\",\"options\":[\"Rabbit\'s ears\",\"Rabbits\' ears\",\"Rabbits\'s ears\",\"Rabbits ears\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since \'Rabbits\' is a plural ending in \'s\', only an apostrophe is added at the end.\",\"topic\":\"Use of Apostrophe\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a name ends with the letter \'s\', like Midas, how can we show possession?\",\"options\":[\"Only by using Midas\'\",\"Only by using Midas\'s\",\"By using either Midas\' or Midas\'s\",\"By adding an \'an\' before the name\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that for names ending in \'s\', using either \' or \'s is acceptable.\",\"topic\":\"Use of Apostrophe\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How would you correctly write \'the tail of a tiger\' using an apostrophe?\",\"options\":[\"tiger tail\",\"tigers tail\",\"tiger\'s tail\",\"tigers\' tail\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"For a singular noun like tiger, \'s is added to show possession.\",\"topic\":\"Use of Apostrophe\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Choose the correct phrase for a school meant for many boys.\",\"options\":[\"Boy\'s School\",\"Boys School\",\"Boys\' School\",\"Boys\'s School\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"For the plural word \'Boys\', only an apostrophe is added at the end.\",\"topic\":\"Use of Apostrophe\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the example \'children\'s books\', why is \'s used?\",\"options\":[\"Because children is a singular word\",\"To show the books belong to the children\",\"Because the word ends in \'n\'\",\"To show there is only one book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'s is used to show \'koṇāce kāy\' (who owns what), which is the books belonging to children.\",\"topic\":\"Use of Apostrophe\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these follows the same rule as \'Girls\' Hostel\'?\",\"options\":[\"Midas\'s daughter\",\"Tiger\'s tail\",\"Rabbits\' ears\",\"Meena\'s doll\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Both \'Girls\' Hostel\' and \'Rabbits\' ears\' follow the rule for plural words ending in \'s\'.\",\"topic\":\"Use of Apostrophe\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the correct way to write \'the daughter of Midas\' based on the text.\",\"options\":[\"Midas\'s daughter\",\"Midas\' daughter\",\"Both Midas\' daughter and Midas\'s daughter\",\"Midas daughter\'s\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that both Midas\' daughter and Midas\'s daughter are correct.\",\"topic\":\"Use of Apostrophe\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is correctly paired with \'He\' for regular actions?\",\"options\":[\"He are\",\"He do\",\"He does\",\"He have\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the fixed pair for \'He\' is \'He does\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tenses and Polite Expressions\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What suffix is often added to words to show events that have already happened?\",\"options\":[\"-ing\",\"-s\",\"-d or -ed\",\"-will\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that words showing past events often end in -d or -ed.\",\"topic\":\"Tenses and Polite Expressions\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is mentioned as a polite expression in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Go away\",\"Excuse me\",\"I am late\",\"He is happy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Excuse me\' is listed among the polite expressions like \'Hello\' and \'Thank you\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tenses and Polite Expressions\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How do you change the sentence \'I am late\' into a Yes\\/No question?\",\"options\":[\"I am late?\",\"Am I late?\",\"Late I am?\",\"I late am?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that words are swapped to form questions, giving the example \'Am I late?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Tenses and Polite Expressions\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the word \'I’m\', what does the symbol (’) indicate?\",\"options\":[\"The sentence is ending\",\"The word is a name\",\"Some letters are omitted\",\"The word is plural\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the apostrophe is used to show that letters are omitted (गाळली आहेत).\",\"topic\":\"Tenses and Polite Expressions\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which words should be used when talking about events that will happen in the future?\",\"options\":[\"am or are\",\"did or do\",\"will or going to\",\"was or were\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies using \'will\' or \'going to\' for future events.\",\"topic\":\"Tenses and Polite Expressions\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are talking about an action happening right now, which word ending is correct?\",\"options\":[\"She is play\",\"She is played\",\"She is playing\",\"She is plays\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to use words ending in -ing for actions happening now.\",\"topic\":\"Tenses and Polite Expressions\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following pairs is correct according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"I has\",\"They are\",\"You does\",\"She have\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'They are\' as a fixed pair.\",\"topic\":\"Tenses and Polite Expressions\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which polite expression is most suitable when you want to ask for someone\'s permission or attention?\",\"options\":[\"It’s all right !\",\"I’m going\",\"Do you mind .....\",\"He’s happy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Do you mind\' is listed as a good polite expression to use.\",\"topic\":\"Tenses and Polite Expressions\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the correct pair for the subject \'It\'.\",\"options\":[\"It have\",\"It are\",\"It has\",\"It do\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'It has\' as the correct pair.\",\"topic\":\"Tenses and Polite 