er is 9,99,999.\",\"topic\":\"Solve the following problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In word problems, which word usually indicates that we need to perform addition?\",\"options\":[\"Difference\",\"Left\",\"Altogether\",\"Remaining\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'altogether\' signifies finding the sum or total of quantities.\",\"topic\":\"Solve the following problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In Problem 4, what specific quantities must be added to find the total production?\",\"options\":[\"Metres of cloth produced last year and this year\",\"The number of men and women voters\",\"The cost of computers and TV sets\",\"The cost of a tractor and a thresher\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To find total production, we add the production figures of the two years mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Solve the following problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In an election, 13,47,048 women and 14,29,638 men cast their votes. How many votes were polled altogether?\",\"options\":[\"27,76,686\",\"28,76,686\",\"27,66,686\",\"27,76,586\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"13,47,048 + 14,29,638 = 27,76,686.\",\"topic\":\"Solve the following problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the sum of the smallest and the largest six-digit numbers?\",\"options\":[\"10,00,000\",\"10,99,999\",\"11,99,999\",\"9,99,999\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"1,00,000 + 9,99,999 = 10,99,999.\",\"topic\":\"Solve the following problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Surekhatai bought a tractor for ₹ 8,07,957 and a thresher for ₹ 32,609. How much money did she spend altogether?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 8,30,566\",\"₹ 8,40,556\",\"₹ 8,40,566\",\"₹ 8,39,566\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"₹ 8,07,957 + ₹ 32,609 = ₹ 8,40,566.\",\"topic\":\"Solve the following problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A textile mill produced 17,24,938 metres of cloth last year and 23,47,056 metres this year. What was the total production of the two