on\",\"Division\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The heading of the topic is \'Subtraction : Revision\'.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 10\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To find out \'how many more\' students took an exam this year compared to last year, which operation is used?\",\"options\":[\"Addition\",\"Subtraction\",\"Multiplication\",\"Division\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The example shows that subtraction is used to find the difference between the two years.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 10\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 38,796 from the text, which digit is in the ten-thousands place?\",\"options\":[\"8\",\"7\",\"9\",\"3\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"In 38,796, 3 is in the ten-thousands place.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 10\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Solve the first problem from Problem Set 10: 64,293 - 28,547 = ?\",\"options\":[\"35,746\",\"36,746\",\"35,846\",\"45,746\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Subtracting 28,547 from 64,293 gives 35,746.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 10\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of the second subtraction problem: 37,058 - 23,469?\",\"options\":[\"14,589\",\"13,589\",\"13,689\",\"12,589\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Subtracting 23,469 from 37,058 gives 13,589.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 10\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In Problem 4 (50,432 - 48,647), what is the digit in the units place of the final answer?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"7\",\"5\",\"9\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since 2 is smaller than 7, we borrow to make it 12; 12 - 7 = 5.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 10\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Solve Problem 3: 71,540 - 58,628 = ?\",\"options\":[\"12,912\",\"13,912\",\"12,812\",\"22,912\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Subtracting 58,628 from 71,540 gives 12,912.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 10\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, if we add 10 or 100 to both the numbers before subtracting, what happens to the difference?\",\"options\":[\"The difference increases\",\"The difference decreases\",\"The difference remains the same\",\"The difference becomes zero\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that if we add 10 or 100 to both numbers, the difference remains the same.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'another method\' of subtraction, where do we write the tens added to the lower number?\",\"options\":[\"In the units place\",\"Below it, in the tens place\",\"Above it, in the hundreds place\",\"It is not written down\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that we write the tens added to the lower number below it, in the tens place.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which method should be used to carry out subtractions of numbers with more than five digits?\",\"options\":[\"A completely new method\",\"The same method used for five-digit numbers\",\"Only the \'another method\'\",\"Addition method\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that using the same method as five-digit numbers, we can do subtractions of numbers with more than five digits.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the example 724 - 376, why do we \'untie one tens\' for the upper number?\",\"options\":[\"To make the number smaller\",\"Because we cannot subtract 6 units from 4 units\",\"To add it to the hundreds place\",\"Because 7 is greater than 3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that as we cannot subtract 6 from 4, we untie one tens to get 14 units.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of adding a ten to both the upper and lower numbers in subtraction?\",\"options\":[\"To make the calculation harder\",\"To keep the difference the same while making subtraction possible\",\"To change the final answer\",\"To practice addition\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Adding the same amount to both numbers keeps the difference constant while allowing subtraction of larger digits from smaller ones.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When subtracting 376 from 724 using the \'another method\', what is the total number of tens subtracted from 2 tens after adding the borrowed hundred?\",\"options\":[\"7 tens\",\"1 ten\",\"8 tens\",\"6 tens\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says we cannot subtract (7 + 1) i.e. 8 tens from 2 tens, so we add a hundred to both.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the final result of the subtraction 65,07,843 - 9,25,586?\",\"options\":[\"55,82,257\",\"65,07,843\",\"9,25,586\",\"55,28,257\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The bottom row of the table in the figure shows the result 55,82,257.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/022_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, why is the digit 3 in the units place of the top number replaced by 13?\",\"options\":[\"Because 3 is greater than 6\",\"Because 6 units cannot be subtracted from 3 units\",\"Because we added 10 to the lower number only\",\"It is a printing error\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows borrowing to convert 3 units into 13 units because 6 is larger than 3.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/022_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text suggest about handling borrowed numbers in multi-digit subtraction?\",\"options\":[\"Always write them down in a table\",\"Learn to keep them in your mind without writing them down\",\"Subtract them from the next number first\",\"Ignore them to save time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text advises to learn to subtract by keeping the borrowed numbers in your mind without writing them down.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are subtracting 34,61,058 - 27,04,579, which digit place will require borrowing first?\",\"options\":[\"Units place\",\"Tens place\",\"Lakhs place\",\"Ten lakhs place\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In 34,61,058 - 27,04,579, the units place has 8 - 9, which requires borrowing.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the \'another method\', if we add one hundred to the upper number by untying it, how do we add it to the lower number?\",\"options\":[\"By writing it in the units place\",\"By writing it below in the hundreds place\",\"By subtracting it from the tens place\",\"By multiplying the lower number by 100\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'To add the hundred to the lower number, we write it below, in the hundreds place.\'\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Compare the two methods: borrowing vs. adding to both numbers. What is the common goal when the upper digit is smaller than the lower digit?\",\"options\":[\"To change the lower digit to zero\",\"To increase the value of the upper digit to make subtraction possible\",\"To decrease the value of the lower digit\",\"To avoid subtraction entirely\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both methods aim to adjust the upper digit (either by borrowing or adding 10\\/100) so that the larger lower digit can be subtracted.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction methods\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21739,30,5,'Maths','en','Multiplication and Division','[\"Multiplication is finding the total when one number is added to itself many times.\",\"The number being repeated is the multiplicand; the number of times is the multiplier.\",\"The result of multiplication is called the product.\",\"To multiply a two‑digit number by a three‑digit number, break the three‑digit number into hundreds, tens and units and multiply separately, then add the partial products.\",\"Carry over numbers when the partial product exceeds nine in a column.\",\"Multiplication can be done by repeated addition, but it is faster to use the multiplication method.\",\"The product of 754 and 368 is 277,472.\",\"When multiplying by a zero in any place, the partial product for that place is zero.\",\"The product of a number and 1 is the number itself; the product of a number and 0 is 0.\",\"Division is the reverse of multiplication: it splits a number into equal parts.\",\"The quotient is how many equal parts fit; the remainder is what is left over.\",\"To divide a four‑digit number by a one‑digit number, start from the leftmost digit, bring down the next digit when needed.\",\"When the divisor is larger than the current part of the dividend, write 0 in the quotient for that place.\",\"The same long‑division technique works for dividing by a two‑digit number, using a table of the divisor’s multiples.\",\"Division can be used to find rates, e.g., cost per kilogram by dividing total cost by weight.\",\"Multiplication and division are inverse operations: (a×b)÷b = a and (a÷b)×b = a.\",\"Pairing objects from two groups gives a number of different pairs equal to the product of the group sizes.\",\"The product of the biggest three‑digit number (999) and the biggest four‑digit number (9999) is 9,989,001.\",\"When solving word problems, identify the two numbers to be multiplied or divided and set up the operation accordingly.\",\"Use the ‘carry over’ technique to keep track of numbers that exceed nine in a column.\",\"Always check your answer by multiplying the quotient by the divisor and adding the remainder to see if you get the dividend.\",\"Multiplication tables up to 12 help in quick mental calculations for small numbers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In the multiplication problem 754 × 368 = 2,77,472, what is the number 2,77,472 called?\",\"options\":[\"Multiplicand\",\"Multiplier\",\"Product\",\"Sum\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that 2,77,472 is the product.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the textbook, what should a student make a habit of holding in their mind during multiplication?\",\"options\":[\"The multiplier\",\"The multiplicand\",\"The carried numbers\",\"The final product\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text advises to \'Make a habit of holding the carried numbers in your mind.\'\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is multiplication preferred over adding 368 times 754 to find the total cost of uniforms?\",\"options\":[\"Because addition gives a different answer\",\"Because it takes less time and effort\",\"Because multiplication is harder to do\",\"Because addition is not possible for large numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes that multiplication takes less time and effort than repeated addition.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In Example (1), which number is identified as the \'multiplicand\'?\",\"options\":[\"368\",\"754\",\"2,77,472\",\"8\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'Here, 754 is the multiplicand\'.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If one child\'s uniform costs ₹ 368 and there are 754 students, what is the total cost of the uniforms?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 2,77,472\",\"₹ 19,99,452\",\"₹ 1,73,850\",\"₹ 45,240\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Example (1) calculates the total cost of uniforms for 754 students at ₹ 368 each as ₹ 2,77,472.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of the calculation 3429 × 507 as shown in the text?\",\"options\":[\"17,38,503\",\"19,99,452\",\"2,77,472\",\"24,003\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Example (2) shows the product of 3429 × 507 is 17,38,503.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A shopkeeper bought 78 TV sets for ₹ 25,634 each. Which operation is used to find the total cost?\",\"options\":[\"Subtraction\",\"Division\",\"Multiplication\",\"Addition only\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Example (3) uses multiplication to find the total cost of the TV sets.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the process of multiplying 754 by 368, the multiplier 368 is broken down into which parts for calculation?\",\"options\":[\"3 units, 6 tens, 8 hundreds\",\"8 units, 6 tens, 3 hundreds\",\"36 units and 8 tens\",\"7 units, 5 tens, 4 hundreds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The multiplication steps show multiplying by 8 units, 6 tens, and 3 hundreds.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the result of multiplying 754 by 6 tens?\",\"options\":[\"6032\",\"45240\",\"226200\",\"277472\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The diagram for Example (1) shows that multiplying by 6 tens results in 45240.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/025_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the value obtained in the second row of the addition when multiplying 3429 by 0 tens?\",\"options\":[\"3429\",\"24003\",\"00000\",\"1714500\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The diagram for Example (2) shows that multiplying by 0 tens results in 00000.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/025_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the result of multiplying 25,634 by 8 units?\",\"options\":[\"205072\",\"1794380\",\"1999452\",\"25634\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The diagram for Example (3) shows that 25634 multiplied by 8 units equals 205072.\",\"topic\":\"Multiplying by a three-digit number\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/026_10