and clockwise divisions start from 0.\",\"topic\":\"The protractor\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which instrument is used to measure an angle according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Ruler\",\"Protractor\",\"Compass\",\"Divider\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions using a protractor to measure angles.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring angles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the centre of the protractor be placed while measuring an angle?\",\"options\":[\"On the arm of the angle\",\"On the baseline\",\"On the vertex of the angle\",\"On the zero mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states to put the centre of the protractor on the vertex of the angle.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring angles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the measure of an angle if its arms are extended?\",\"options\":[\"The measure increases\",\"The measure decreases\",\"The measure does not change\",\"The measure becomes zero\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that extending the arms of the angle does not change the measure of the angle.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring angles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If arm BC of ∠ABC is on the right of vertex B, from which side should you start counting the divisions?\",\"options\":[\"Starting from the 90° mark\",\"Starting from the 0 on the left\",\"Starting from the 180° mark\",\"Starting from the 0 on the right\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says if the arm is on the right, count divisions starting from the 0 on the right.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring angles\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When measuring ∠ABC by aligning the baseline with arm BA, where do you find the 0 mark to start counting?\",\"options\":[\"On the side of point A\",\"On the side of point C\",\"At the 90° mark\",\"At the centre point\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states to find the 0 mark on the side of BA and count starting from the 0 on the side of point A.\"