:\"In the figure, the second row contains numbers 7 to 12. The number in column 5 of that row is 11.\",\"topic\":\"One more method to find prime numbers\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/061_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific prime numbers are mentioned as exceptions that appear in columns other than 1 and 5?\",\"options\":[\"1 and 2\",\"2 and 3\",\"5 and 7\",\"11 and 13\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that 2 and 3 are prime numbers found in columns other than 1 and 5.\",\"topic\":\"One more method to find prime numbers\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, looking at the column for 4, all the numbers shown (4, 10, 16, 22, 28, 34) are:\",\"options\":[\"Prime numbers\",\"Composite numbers\",\"Odd numbers\",\"Multiples of 5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that all numbers in the column for 4 are composite numbers.\",\"topic\":\"One more method to find prime numbers\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/061_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific name for prime numbers that have a difference of two?\",\"options\":[\"Even prime numbers\",\"Twin prime numbers\",\"Serial prime numbers\",\"Infinite prime numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that prime numbers with a difference of two are called twin prime numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Something more\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which country did the mathematician Euclid live?\",\"options\":[\"India\",\"Egypt\",\"Greece\",\"Rome\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Euclid the mathematician lived in Greece.\",\"topic\":\"Something more\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many pairs of twin prime numbers are there between 1 and 100?\",\"options\":[\"Five\",\"Seven\",\"Eight\",\"Ten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states there are eight pairs of twin prime numbers between 1 and 100.\",\"topic\":\"Something more\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What did Euclid prove about the list of prime numbers 2, 3, 5, 7, ...?\",\"options\":[\"The list ends at 100\",\"The list will never end\",\"There are only eight prime numbers\",\"The difference is always two\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Euclid proved that the list of prime numbers will never end, meaning they are infinite.\",\"topic\":\"Something more\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a pair of twin prime numbers mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"2 and 3\",\"5 and 7\",\"11 and 12\",\"29 and 30\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"5 and 7 is one of the pairs listed as twin prime numbers in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Something more\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If 4347421 and 4347423 are twin prime numbers, what is the difference between them?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"By definition, twin prime numbers have a difference of two.\",\"topic\":\"Something more\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Around what time did the mathematician Euclid live?\",\"options\":[\"300 AD\",\"100 BC\",\"300 BC\",\"2023 AD\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states Euclid lived in Greece about 300 BC.\",\"topic\":\"Something more\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does it mean when the text says the number of prime numbers is \'infinite\'?\",\"options\":[\"The list of prime numbers has an end\",\"The list of prime numbers never ends\",\"There are no prime numbers after 100\",\"Prime numbers only come in pairs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains \'infinite\' means that the list will never end.\",\"topic\":\"Something more\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why are 71 and 73 considered twin prime numbers?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are both greater than 70\",\"Because they are prime numbers with a difference of two\",\"Because they were discovered by Euclid\",\"Because they are the last pair before 100\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They fit the definition of twin prime numbers: prime numbers with a difference of two.\",\"topic\":\"Something more\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Euclid\'s proof, if we keep writing prime numbers in serial order, what will happen?\",\"options\":[\"We will eventually reach the last prime number\",\"The numbers will stop at 4347423\",\"The list will continue forever\",\"We will only find eight more pairs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Euclid proved the list is infinite, meaning it continues forever and never ends.\",\"topic\":\"Something more\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21744,30,5,'Maths','en','Decimal Fractions','[\"Decimal fractions are numbers whose denominator is a power of 10 (10, 100, 1000, …).\",\"The part to the right of the decimal point is called the fractional part.\",\"The first place after the decimal point is the tenths place (0.1).\",\"The second place is the hundredths place (0.01).\",\"The third place is the thousandths place (0.001).\",\"To read a decimal, say the whole number part, then say “point”, then read each digit in order.\",\"Example: 3.14 is read as “three point one four”.\",\"A decimal can be written from a fraction by dividing the numerator by the denominator.\",\"If the denominator is 10, 100, 1000 … the decimal is obtained by moving the decimal point left as many places as the power of 10.\",\"The value of a digit in a decimal is digit × 10⁻n where n is its position from the decimal point (1 for tenths, 2 for hundredths, etc.).\",\"In money, 1 rupee = 100 paise, so 0.01 rupee = 1 paise.\",\"In length, 1 metre = 100 centimetres, so 0.01 metre = 1 centimetre.\",\"Adding decimals is done column‑wise just like whole numbers; align the decimal points.\",\"When adding, if a column exceeds 9, carry over 1 to the next higher column.\",\"Subtracting decimals also aligns the decimal points; borrow from the next higher column if needed.\",\"Half is 0.5, quarter is 0.25, three‑quarters is 0.75, one and a half is 1.5, one and a quarter is 1.25.\",\"Decimals are useful because they keep all units in the same system (e.g., rupees, metres, litres).\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the full form of \'MRP\' as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Minimum Retail Price\",\"Maximum Retail Price\",\"Market Rate Price\",\"Money Retail Price\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher explains that MRP means maximum retail price.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher, what does the Maximum Retail Price signify?\",\"options\":[\"The price the seller must always charge\",\"The lowest price a seller can offer\",\"The maximum price a seller can charge for the medicine\",\"The price for ten boxes of medicine\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the seller can sell the medicine for a maximum of that price.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the maximum price a seller can charge for this box of eye drops?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 24\",\"₹ 50\",\"₹ 24.50\",\"₹ 2450\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the MRP as ₹ 24.50.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/062_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the price shown in the figure, what does the number \'50\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"The number of eye drops\",\"The amount in paise\",\"The amount in rupees\",\"The expiry date\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher explains that 24.50 means 24 rupees and 50 paise.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/062_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In what form is the number \'24.50\' written?\",\"options\":[\"Fraction form\",\"Word form\",\"Decimal form\",\"Expanded form\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher explicitly states that \'24.50\' has been written in decimal form.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To understand how \'24.50\' means \'twenty-four rupees fifty paise\', what topic does the teacher say needs to be learned?\",\"options\":[\"Multiplication of numbers\",\"Decimal fractions\",\"Addition of rupees\",\"Measurement of weight\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher says you will first have to learn about decimal fractions.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a medicine box has \'MRP ₹ 24.50\' printed on it, how is this amount read in words?\",\"options\":[\"Twenty-four rupees five paise\",\"Two hundred and forty-five rupees\",\"Twenty-four rupees fifty paise\",\"Fifty rupees twenty-four paise\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text clarifies that 24.50 means twenty-four rupees and fifty paise.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a shopkeeper tries to sell the medicine box mentioned in the text for ₹ 26.00, is he following the MRP rule?\",\"options\":[\"Yes, because it is close to the price\",\"No, because it is more than the maximum retail price\",\"Yes, because he can choose any price\",\"No, because he must sell it for exactly 50 rupees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"MRP is the maximum price; charging ₹ 26.00 exceeds the ₹ 24.50 limit.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the decimal form \'24.50\', what is used to separate the rupees from the paise?\",\"options\":[\"A comma\",\"A dash\",\"A dot (decimal point)\",\"A colon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The number 24.50 uses a dot to separate the two parts in decimal form.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who first noticed the price printed on the box of medicine?\",\"options\":[\"Rekha\",\"The Teacher\",\"Soumitra\",\"The Seller\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The dialogue starts with Soumitra saying he saw the MRP printed on a box.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a fraction called when its denominator is 10, 100, or 1000?\",\"options\":[\"Common fraction\",\"Decimal fraction\",\"Proper fraction\",\"Unit fraction\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a fraction whose denominator is 10, 100, 1000 or any ten times multiple of 10 is called a decimal fraction.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the term \'one-tenth\'?\",\"options\":[\"10 units\",\"100 divided by 10\",\"1\\/10\",\"10\\/100\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that 1\\/10 means \'one-tenth\'.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the decimal system, the place value of each place is how many times that of the previous place?\",\"options\":[\"2 times\",\"5 times\",\"10 times\",\"100 times\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the place value of each of these is 10 times that of the previous place.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the \'tenths place\' located in relation to the units place?\",\"options\":[\"To the left of the units place\",\"To the right of the units place\",\"Above the units place\",\"Below the units place\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that for 1\\/10, a place is made to the right of the units place, called the tenths place.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is an example of a decimal fraction as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"5\\/20\",\"68\\/100\",\"1\\/2\",\"3\\/5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides 68\\/100 as an example of a decimal fraction because its denominator is 100.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If we divide one hundred into 10 equal parts, what is each part called?\",\"options\":[\"One unit\",\"One thousand\",\"One ten\",\"One-tenth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, if we divide one hundred into 10 equal parts, each part is one ten.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is another name for the \'tenths place\' mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"First decimal right\",\"Second decimal right\",\"Units place\",\"Tens place\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says the tenths place is also called the \'first decimal right\'.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If one unit is divided into ten equal parts, what does each part become?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/100\",\"10\\/1\",\"1\\/10\",\"10\\/10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'if one unit is divided into ten equal parts, each part becomes 1\\/10\'.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what happens to the place value when we move from the hundreds place to the tens place?\",\"options\":[\"It increases by 10\",\"It is divided into 10 equal parts\",\"It stays the same\",\"It is multiplied by 100\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that if we divide one hundred into 10 equal parts, each part is one ten, and the tens place is to the right of the hundred.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which denominator would NOT make a fraction a \'decimal fraction\' according to the definition?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"100\",\"1000\",\"25\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"A decimal fraction must have a denominator of 10, 100, 1000 or other ten times multiples of 10; 25 is not a multiple of 10 in this sequence.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the usual method of writing numbers, one ten equals how many units?\",\"options\":[\"1 unit\",\"10 units\",\"100 units\",\"1\\/10 units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'one ten equals 10 units\'.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a new place created to the right of the units place?\",\"options\":[\"To write numbers larger than hundreds\",\"To represent parts smaller than one unit, like 1\\/10\",\"To make multiplication easier\",\"To show the tens place\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that to represent 1\\/10 (one unit divided into ten parts), a place is made to the right of the units place.\",\"topic\":\"Decimal fractions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the symbol (.) called when used in writing fractions?\",\"options\":[\"Full stop\",\"Decimal point\",\"Comma\",\"Fraction dot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the symbol (.) is called a decimal point.\",\"topic\":\"The decimal point\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the decimal point written in a number?\",\"options\":[\"Before the first digit of the whole part\",\"After the last digit of the whole part\",\"After the fraction part\",\"Between every digit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a dot is written after the last digit of the whole part of a number.\",\"topic\":\"The decimal point\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the decimal point indicate in a number?\",\"options\":[\"The start of the number\",\"The end of the whole part of a number\",\"The multiplication of two numbers\",\"The end of the decimal part\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the dot is written to indicate the end of the whole part of a number.\",\"topic\":\"The decimal point\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How is the decimal number 8.5 read in words?\",\"options\":[\"Eighty-five\",\"Eight point five\",\"Eight and five\",\"Eight decimal five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that 8.5 is read as \'eight point five\'.\",\"topic\":\"The decimal point\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is the \'usual way\' of writing seven tenths?\",\"options\":[\"0.7\",\"7.10\",\"7\\/10\",\"7.0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'7\\/10\' is the usual way of writing the number.\",\"topic\":\"The decimal point\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a decimal place created in mathematics?\",\"options\":[\"For writing a fraction\",\"For adding whole numbers\",\"For naming large numbers\",\"For drawing symbols\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The very first sentence of the text says the decimal place is created for writing a fraction.\",\"topic\":\"The decimal point\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How would you write 20 3\\/10 in the decimal way?\",\"options\":[\"2.03\",\"203\",\"20.3\",\"0.203\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the example that \'20 3\\/10\' is written as \'20.3\'.\",\"topic\":\"The decimal point\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If \'Seven tenths\' is written as 0.7, how is \'Three tenths\' written in the decimal way?\",\"options\":[\"3.10\",\"0.3\",\"3.0\",\"3\\/10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Following the pattern for 0.7 (seven tenths) shown in the text, three tenths is 0.3.\",\"topic\":\"The decimal point\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 20.3, which part is the whole part of the number?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"0.3\",\"20\",\"20.3\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since the decimal point comes after the last digit of the whole part, 20 is the whole part.\",\"topic\":\"The decimal point\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these represents the \'decimal way\' of writing a number?\",\"options\":[\"7\\/10\",\"8 5\\/10\",\"0.7\",\"Seven tenths\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that \'0.7\' is the decimal way of writing the number.\",\"topic\":\"The decimal point\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If 1\\/10 is divided into 10 equal parts, what is each part called?\",\"options\":[\"One tenth\",\"One hundredth\",\"Ten units\",\"One unit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if 1\\/10 is divided into 10 equal parts, each part becomes 1\\/100 or one hundredth.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the hundredths place created in a decimal fraction?\",\"options\":[\"Before the units place\",\"Next to the tenths place\",\"Before the tens place\",\"After the units place\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that it is possible to create a hundredths place next to the tenths place.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is the decimal fraction 0.14 read according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Zero point fourteen\",\"Zero point one four\",\"Zero point one and four\",\"Zero point forty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that 0.14 is read as \'zero point one four\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When writing 3\\/100 in decimal form, why do we put 0 in the tenths place?\",\"options\":[\"Because there is no number in the tenths place\",\"Because 3 is a big number\",\"Because it is the units place\",\"Because 100 has two zeros\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explains that while writing 3\\/100, we put 0 in the tenths place because there is no number in that place.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the decimal form of the fraction 6 57\\/100?\",\"options\":[\"65.7\",\"0.657\",\"6.57\",\"6.057\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, 6 57\\/100 is written as 6.57.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the decimal form of 50 71\\/100?\",\"options\":[\"5.071\",\"50.71\",\"507.1\",\"0.5071\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that 50 71\\/100 is written as 50.71.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"1 tenth is equal to how many hundredths?\",\"options\":[\"1 hundredth\",\"100 hundredths\",\"10 hundredths\",\"0 hundredths\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that 1 tenth = 10 hundredths.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the decimal fraction 0.14, which digit is written in the hundredths place?\",\"options\":[\"0\",\"1\",\"4\",\"14\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that in 0.14, 1 is in the tenths place and 4 is in the hundredths place.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how is the fraction 82\\/100 written in words?\",\"options\":[\"Eighty-two point zero\",\"Zero point eight two\",\"Eight point two\",\"Zero point eighty-two\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows that 82\\/100 is written in words as \'Zero point eight two\'.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/063_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the table in the given figure, which digit is in the units place for the fraction 7 5\\/10?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"0\",\"7\",\"10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows the digit 7 in the \'Units\' column for the fraction 7 5\\/10.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/063_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is mathematically the same as 0.1 according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"0.01\",\"0.10\",\"1.0\",\"0.11\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that 0.1 = 0.10.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If 14\\/100 = 1\\/10 + 4\\/100, what does the \'1\' represent in the decimal 0.14?\",\"options\":[\"1 unit\",\"1 hundredth\",\"1 tenth\",\"1 ten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that 14\\/100 = 1\\/10 + 4\\/100, meaning 1 is written in the tenths place.\",\"topic\":\"Hundredths\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the place name of the first digit to the right of the decimal point?\",\"options\":[\"Units\",\"Tens\",\"Tenths\",\"Hundredths\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the table in Example (2), the first digit after the decimal point is in the Tenths place.\",\"topic\":\"Place value of the digits\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the decimal fraction 210.86, which digit is in the Hundredths place?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"1\",\"8\",\"6\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table for 210.86 shows that the digit 6 is in the Hundredths place.\",\"topic\":\"Place value of the digits\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The place value of digits in decimal fractions is determined in the same way as in which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"Negative numbers\",\"Whole numbers\",\"Prime numbers\",\"Roman numerals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states we determine the place value of digits in decimal fractions in the same way as in whole numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Place value of the digits\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How is the place value of a digit in the \'Tenths\' place calculated?\",\"options\":[\"Digit × 10\",\"Digit × 1\",\"Digit × 1\\/10\",\"Digit × 1\\/100\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Example (1) shows the place value of 8 in the tenths place is 8 × 1\\/10.\",\"topic\":\"Place value of the digits\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 73.82, what is the place value of the digit 8?\",\"options\":[\"80\",\"8\",\"0.8\",\"0.08\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In Example (1), the place value of 8 is calculated as 8 × 1\\/10 = 0.8.\",\"topic\":\"Place value of the digits\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the place value of the digit 2 in the number 210.86?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"20\",\"200\",\"0.02\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in Example (2) shows the digit 2 is in the Hundreds place, so its value is 2 × 100 = 200.\",\"topic\":\"Place value of the digits\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 210.86, which digit has a place value of 0?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"1\",\"0\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in Example (2) shows the digit 0 is in the Units place and its place value is 0.\",\"topic\":\"Place value of the digits\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the examples, if a digit is in the \'Hundredths\' place, what is it multiplied by to find its place value?\",\"options\":[\"100\",\"1\\/10\",\"1\\/100\",\"1\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Example (1) and (2) both show that digits in the hundredths place are multiplied by 1\\/100.\",\"topic\":\"Place value of the digits\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Comparing 73.82 and 210.86, which digit occupies the \'Tenths\' place in both numbers?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"8\",\"1\",\"6\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In 73.82, 8 is in the tenths place, and in 210.86, 8 is also in the tenths place.\",\"topic\":\"Place value of the digits\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the place value of the digit 1 in the number 210.86?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"10\",\"100\",\"0.1\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in Example (2) shows the digit 1 is in the Tens place, so its value is 1 × 10 = 10.\",\"topic\":\"Place value of the digits\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many paise make one rupee according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"10 paise\",\"50 paise\",\"100 paise\",\"1000 paise\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 100 paise make one rupee.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many millimetres (mm) are equal to 1 centimetre (cm)?\",\"options\":[\"1 mm\",\"10 mm\",\"100 mm\",\"1000 mm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that 10 mm = 1 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, 1 paisa is equal to which fraction of a rupee?\",\"options\":[\"One tenth\",\"One hundredth\",\"One thousandth\",\"One half\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sumit explains that 1 paisa is one hundredth of a rupee.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the decimal form shown for 75 paise?\",\"options\":[\"0.075 rupee\",\"7.5 rupee\",\"0.75 rupee\",\"75.0 rupee\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows 75 paise = 75\\/100 rupee = 0.75 rupee.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/064_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the decimal 0.60 m is shown to be equal to which other decimal form?\",\"options\":[\"0.06 m\",\"0.6 m\",\"6.0 m\",\"0.006 m\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows 60 cm = 60\\/100 m = 0.60 m = 0.6 m.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/064_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"When is it more convenient to write units in decimal form?\",\"options\":[\"Only when dealing with money\",\"When a large unit is divided into 10 or 100 parts\",\"Only when the number is greater than 100\",\"When we want to make the calculation harder\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher explains it is convenient when a large unit is divided into 10 or 100 parts to make smaller units.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If 1 mm = 0.1 cm, what is the decimal form for 3 mm?\",\"options\":[\"0.03 cm\",\"3.0 cm\",\"0.3 cm\",\"0.33 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 3 mm are 0.3 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Convert 75 cm into metres using the decimal form mentioned in the text.\",\"options\":[\"7.5 m\",\"0.075 m\",\"0.75 m\",\"75.0 m\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 100 cm = 1 metre, so 75 cm = 0.75 m.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the patterns in the text, what does 6.3 cm represent in terms of cm and mm?\",\"options\":[\"63 cm and 0 mm\",\"6 cm and 3 mm\",\"60 cm and 3 mm\",\"0 cm and 63 mm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that 6.3 cm are 6 cm and 3 mm.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the table, what is the correct conversion for 14.9 m?\",\"options\":[\"14 m 9 cm\",\"149 m 0 cm\",\"14 m 90 cm\",\"1 m 49 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows 14.9 m = 14 m 90 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct decimal representation for 7 paise as shown in the table?\",\"options\":[\"0.7 rupee\",\"0.07 rupee\",\"7.0 rupee\",\"0.007 rupee\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table lists 0.07 rupee = 7 paise.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many centimetres make 1 metre?\",\"options\":[\"10 cm\",\"100 cm\",\"1000 cm\",\"50 cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that 100 cm = 1 metre.\",\"topic\":\"Use of decimal fractions\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is \'half\' usually written as a fraction?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/4\",\"1\\/2\",\"3\\/4\",\"1\\/10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'half\' is usually written as 1\\/2.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the decimal form of \'three quarters\'?\",\"options\":[\"0.25\",\"0.50\",\"0.75\",\"1.75\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows that Three quarters = 3\\/4 = 75\\/100 = 0.75.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the decimal form of \'a quarter\'?\",\"options\":[\"0.25\",\"0.5\",\"0.75\",\"0.10\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that a quarter = 1\\/4 = 25\\/100 = 0.25.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is \'one and three quarters\' written in decimal form?\",\"options\":[\"1.25\",\"1.50\",\"1.75\",\"17.5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the text lists \'One and three quarters = 1 3\\/4 = 1.75\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why can the denominator of 1\\/4 NOT be made into 10?\",\"options\":[\"Because 10 is not divisible by 4\",\"Because 4 is greater than 1\",\"Because 1\\/4 is a quarter\",\"Because 4 multiplied by 2 is 8\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that 10 is not divisible by 4, so the denominator cannot be made into 10.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To convert 1\\/2 into a decimal form with denominator 10, by what number must we multiply the numerator and denominator?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"4\",\"5\",\"25\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows 1\\/2 = 1x5\\/2x5 = 5\\/10.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these decimal forms represents \'one and a half\'?\",\"options\":[\"1.25\",\"1.5\",\"1.75\",\"17.5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'One and a half = 1 1\\/2 = 1.50 = 1.5\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the fraction representation shown for \'Three quarters\'?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/4\",\"1\\/2\",\"3\\/4\",\"17 1\\/2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows \'Three quarters = 3\\/4\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/066_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If \'half\' is 0.50, how is \'seventeen and a half\' written as a decimal?\",\"options\":[\"1.75\",\"17.25\",\"17.50\",\"17.05\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Seventeen and a half = 17 1\\/2 = 17.50\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the equivalent fraction of 1\\/4 that has 100 as the denominator?\",\"options\":[\"5\\/10\",\"25\\/100\",\"75\\/100\",\"50\\/100\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows 1\\/4 = 1x25\\/4x25 = 25\\/100.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/066_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of the following statements is true about the decimal form of \'half\'?\",\"options\":[\"0.5 is different from 0.50\",\"0.5 is the same as 0.50\",\"0.5 is only written as 5\\/100\",\"0.5 cannot be written with denominator 100\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'half\' is written as \'0.5\' or \'0.50\', showing they are equivalent.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why do we multiply the denominator of 3\\/4 by 25 to convert it to a decimal fraction?\",\"options\":[\"To make the denominator 10\",\"Because 3 multiplied by 25 is 75\",\"To make the denominator 100\",\"Because 4 is not divisible by 10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that since 10 is not divisible by 4, we use 4 x 25 = 100 to get a denominator that is a multiple of 10.\",\"topic\":\"Fractions in decimal form\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the value of 10 tenths?\",\"options\":[\"10 units\",\"1 unit\",\"1 hundredth\",\"0.1 unit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states in the notes that 10 tenths = 1 unit.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the value of 10 hundredths as mentioned in the study notes?\",\"options\":[\"1 unit\",\"10 units\",\"1 tenth\",\"10 tenths\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes state that 10 hundredths = 1 tenth.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When writing down an addition problem with decimals, where should the decimal points be placed?\",\"options\":[\"At the very end of the number\",\"Only in the final answer\",\"One below the other\",\"To the right of the units place only\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sir instructs to remember that decimal points should always be written one below the other.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to Rekha, which place value digits are added first in decimal addition?\",\"options\":[\"Units\",\"Tens\",\"Tenths\",\"Hundreds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rekha states that just as units are added first in whole numbers, tenths are added first here (in the context of the provided example).\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the sum of 3.7 and 12.2 as shown in the first example of the text?\",\"options\":[\"15.7\",\"15.9\",\"16.9\",\"14.9\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the calculation (1) 3.7 + 12.2 = 15.9.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sum 6.8 + 5.5, why is 1 carried over to the units place?\",\"options\":[\"Because 8 + 5 tenths equals 13 tenths, which is 1 unit and 3 tenths\",\"Because 6 + 5 equals 11\",\"Because the decimal point moves one place to the left\",\"Because 10 units make a ten\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Rekha explains that 13 tenths are 10 tenths + 3 tenths, which equals 1 unit + 3 tenths.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How is 167.4 written to make the denominators of the fractions equal when adding it to 45.83?\",\"options\":[\"167.04\",\"167.40\",\"167.43\",\"167.00\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Example 2 explains that 167.4 is written as 167.40 to make the denominators equal.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the sum of 0.5 and 0.5 according to the teacher\'s explanation?\",\"options\":[\"0.10\",\"1.0\",\"0.55\",\"5.5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows 0.5 + 0.5 = 10\\/10 = 1, which is carried over to the units place.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a pencil costs 2.50 rupees and a pen costs 4.50 rupees, what is their total cost?\",\"options\":[\"6.00 rupees\",\"6.50 rupees\",\"7.00 rupees\",\"7.50 rupees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sumit calculates that 2.50 and 4.50 add up to 7 rupees.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the addition 7.09 + 54.93, what is the result of adding the hundredths place?\",\"options\":[\"12 hundredths\",\"10 hundredths\",\"9 hundredths\",\"3 hundredths\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says the 1 from the sum 12 in the hundredths place is carried over.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Sumit observes that there is no carried over number in which of these additions?\",\"options\":[\"6.8 + 5.5\",\"16.9 + 7.5\",\"3.7 + 12.2\",\"7.09 + 54.93\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sumit specifically says, \'There is no carried over number in the first sum\', which is 3.7 + 12.2.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the total of 7.5 cm, 14.2 cm, and 9.6 cm as given in Example 5?\",\"options\":[\"30.3 cm\",\"31.3 cm\",\"31.5 cm\",\"29.3 cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Example 5 in the text states the sum is 31.3 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why can we add decimal fractions in the same way as we add whole numbers?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are always smaller than one\",\"Because we extend the decimal system used for whole numbers to write fractions\",\"Because decimal points do not change the value of digits\",\"Because we only add the numbers after the decimal point\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher explains that because we extend the decimal system to write fractions, we can add them the same way as whole numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In Example 2 (45.83 + 167.40), which digits are added first?\",\"options\":[\"The digits in the hundreds place\",\"The digits in the units place\",\"The digits with the smallest place values\",\"The digits in the tenths place\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'As usual, the digits with the smallest place values are added first\'.\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the addition 48.80 m + 2.57 m = 51.37 m, which digit represents the total hundredths?\",\"options\":[\"0\",\"8\",\"7\",\"3\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In 51.37, 7 is in the hundredths place (0 + 7 = 7).\",\"topic\":\"Adding decimal fractions\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is 1 tenth equal to in terms of hundredths?\",\"options\":[\"1 hundredth\",\"10 hundredths\",\"100 hundredths\",\"0 hundredths\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that 1 tenth is equal to 10 hundredths.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction of decimal fractions\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the subtraction 15.41 - 8.58, why is it necessary to borrow from the tenths place?\",\"options\":[\"Because 8 hundredths cannot be subtracted from 1 hundredth\",\"Because 4 is smaller than 5\",\"Because 15 is greater than 8\",\"Because the decimal point is in the middle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explains that 8 hundredths cannot be subtracted from 1 hundredth, so borrowing is required.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction of decimal fractions\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If 1 tenth is borrowed from 4 tenths to help the hundredths place, how many tenths are left in the tenths place?\",\"options\":[\"4 tenths\",\"5 tenths\",\"3 tenths\",\"10 tenths\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Borrowing 1 from 4 leaves 3 tenths remaining.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction of decimal fractions\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the final digit written in the \'Units\' (U) place of the answer?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"8\",\"6\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The bottom row of the table shows 6 in the Units (U) column.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction of decimal fractions\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/068_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, what does the number in the \'Tenths\' column become after borrowing from the units place to subtract 5?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"13\",\"11\",\"14\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows the number 13 in the Tenths column after borrowing.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction of decimal fractions\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/068_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the result of the subtraction \'11 hundredths minus 8 hundredths\' written?\",\"options\":[\"In the tenths place\",\"In the units place\",\"In the hundredths place under the line\",\"In the tens place\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that 3 hundredths are written in the hundredths place under the line.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction of decimal fractions\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how is the value \'11 hundredths\' obtained?\",\"options\":[\"By adding 10 hundredths to 1 hundredth\",\"By subtracting 1 from 11\",\"By multiplying 10 by 1\",\"By borrowing from the units place\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says the borrowed 10 hundredths and the original one hundredth make 11 hundredths.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction of decimal fractions\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you follow the method in the text to subtract 8 hundredths from 11 hundredths, what is the result?\",\"options\":[\"3 hundredths\",\"19 hundredths\",\"2 hundredths\",\"5 hundredths\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states 11 hundredths minus 8 hundredths are 3 hundredths.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction of decimal fractions\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the subtraction shown in the figure, why is the \'T\' (Tens) place in the final answer \'0\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because 1 ten was borrowed by the units place\",\"Because there was no number in the tens place initially\",\"Because 1 minus 8 is 0\",\"Because the units place did not need to borrow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the 1 in the Tens place crossed out and replaced by 0 because it was borrowed.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction of decimal fractions\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/068_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final result of the subtraction 15.41 - 8.58 as shown in the text?\",\"options\":[\"7.83\",\"6.83\",\"6.93\",\"5.83\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text and image both show the final answer as 6.83.\",\"topic\":\"Subtraction of decimal fractions\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is the basic unit for measuring mass?\",\"options\":[\"Metre\",\"Litre\",\"Gram\",\"Kilometre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, gram is taken as the basic unit for mass.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the English equivalent of the term \'Deca\'?\",\"options\":[\"Hundred\",\"Ten\",\"Thousand\",\"Tenth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table explicitly lists \'Deca\' as meaning \'Ten\'.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"From which languages do the terms \'kilo\', \'hecto\', and \'milli\' originate?\",\"options\":[\"English and French\",\"Greek or Latin\",\"Sanskrit and Hindi\",\"German and Spanish\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the origin of these terms is in the Greek or Latin language.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the decimal unit system, how many times does a unit increase at every step for larger units?\",\"options\":[\"2 times\",\"5 times\",\"10 times\",\"100 times\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that units larger than the basic units increase 10 times at every step.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What fraction of the previous unit does a smaller unit become at each step?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/2\",\"1\\/10\",\"1\\/100\",\"1\\/5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that smaller units become 1\\/10 of the previous unit at each step.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which unit is used to measure volume most of the time?\",\"options\":[\"Kilometre\",\"Gram\",\"Litre\",\"Metre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions litre and millilitre are the units used for volume most of the time.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many metres are equal to 1 hectometre?\",\"options\":[\"10 m\",\"1000 m\",\"100 m\",\"1\\/100 m\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows that 1 hectometre = 100 m.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If 1 decimetre is 1\\/10 m, what is the value of 1 millimetre in metres?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/10 m\",\"1\\/100 m\",\"1\\/1000 m\",\"1000 m\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table defines 1 millimetre as 1\\/1000 m.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following represents 1 centimetre?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/10 m\",\"1\\/100 m\",\"100 m\",\"1\\/1000 m\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table identifies 1 centimetre as 1\\/100 m.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the table, which unit is larger than a decametre?\",\"options\":[\"Decimetre\",\"Centimetre\",\"Hectometre\",\"Millimetre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A decametre is 10m, while a hectometre is 100m, making it larger.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Following the pattern for distance, what would 1 kilogram be equal to in grams?\",\"options\":[\"10 grams\",\"100 grams\",\"1000 grams\",\"1\\/1000 grams\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since kilo means thousand (Th), 1 kilogram equals 1000 grams, similar to 1 kilometre = 1000 m.\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which sequence correctly shows units from the smallest to the largest value relative to the basic unit?\",\"options\":[\"Milli, Centi, Deci\",\"Kilo, Hecto, Deca\",\"Deci, Centi, Milli\",\"Deca, Hecto, Kilo\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Milli (1\\/1000) is smaller than Centi (1\\/100), which is smaller than Deci (1\\/10).\",\"topic\":\"Decimals used for measurement\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21745,30,5,'Maths','en','Measuring Time','[\"- A clock has three hands: hour, minute and second.\",\"- The face of a clock is a circle divided into 60 equal parts.\",\"- One part moved by the second hand equals 1 second.\",\"- When the second hand completes one round (60 parts) it takes 60 seconds – one minute.\",\"- One minute = 60 seconds.\",\"- The minute hand moves one part every minute.\",\"- The hour hand moves one part every 12 hours (one full rotation).\",\"- 12‑hour clock: times are written as AM (ante meridiem) or PM (post meridiem).\",\"- 24‑hour clock: after 12 noon the count continues 13,14,…,24. 00:00 is midnight.\",\"- To convert 12‑hour to 24‑hour: add 12 to PM times (except 12 PM stays 12).\",\"- To convert 24‑hour to 12‑hour: if hour >12 subtract 12; 00 becomes 12 AM; 12 stays 12 PM.\",\"- Time difference can be found by adding or subtracting hours and minutes, borrowing 60 minutes if needed.\",\"- Example: 4 h 30 min + 2 h 45 min = 7 h 15 min.\",\"- Example: 5 h 20 min – 2 h 35 min = 2 h 45 min.\",\"- When a journey starts before midnight and ends after midnight, add the hours before midnight to the hours after midnight.\",\"- A day has 24 hours; 23:59 is one minute before midnight; 00:00 starts a new day.\",\"- In schedules, 24‑hour clock is used to avoid confusion between AM and PM.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the time shown on the clock?\",\"options\":[\"25 minutes past 2\",\"5 minutes past 2\",\"25 minutes past 3\",\"5 minutes past 3\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The hour hand is between 2 and 3, and the minute hand is at 5, which represents 5 × 5 = 25 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/069_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which number is the minute hand pointing to?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"5\",\"12\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The longer hand (minute hand) is pointing directly at the number 5.\",\"topic\":\"Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/069_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the numerical representation of the time \'Quarter past nine\'?\",\"options\":[\"9:45\",\"9:15\",\"9:30\",\"8:45\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Quarter past\' means 15 minutes have passed the hour.\",\"topic\":\"Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the time is \'Quarter to five\', how many minutes are remaining to reach 5 o\'clock?\",\"options\":[\"15 minutes\",\"45 minutes\",\"30 minutes\",\"5 minutes\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Quarter to\' indicates that 15 minutes are left to reach the next hour.\",\"topic\":\"Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A bus leaves Nashik at 5 o’clock in the morning and reaches Pune at ten thirty in the morning. How long does the journey take?\",\"options\":[\"4 hours 30 minutes\",\"5 hours 30 minutes\",\"6 hours 30 minutes\",\"10 hours\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"From 5:00 AM to 10:00 AM is 5 hours, plus 30 minutes makes it 5 hours 30 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A play was scheduled to start at nine fifteen at night. If it was delayed by half an hour, what time did it start?\",\"options\":[\"9:30 PM\",\"9:45 PM\",\"10:15 PM\",\"9:20 PM\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Half an hour is 30 minutes. 9:15 + 30 minutes = 9:45.\",\"topic\":\"Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A train leaves Mumbai at ten fifteen at night and reaches Nagpur at one forty the next afternoon. What is the total duration of the journey?\",\"options\":[\"15 hours 25 minutes\",\"12 hours 25 minutes\",\"13 hours 40 minutes\",\"14 hours 15 minutes\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"10:15 PM to 10:15 AM is 12 hours. 10:15 AM to 1:15 PM is 3 hours. 1:15 PM to 1:40 PM is 25 minutes. Total = 15 hours 25 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the textbook, how many minutes are in \'half an hour\'?\",\"options\":[\"15 minutes\",\"20 minutes\",\"30 minutes\",\"45 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In time measurement, half an hour is equal to 30 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To show the time \'Four thirty\' on a clock, where should the hour hand be placed?\",\"options\":[\"Exactly on 4\",\"Exactly on 6\",\"Between 4 and 5\",\"Between 3 and 4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"At 4:30, the hour hand moves halfway between 4 and 5.\",\"topic\":\"Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a journey starts at 5:00 AM and takes 5 hours and 30 minutes, which of these describes the arrival time?\",\"options\":[\"Quarter past ten\",\"Ten thirty\",\"Quarter to eleven\",\"Five thirty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"5:00 + 5 hours 30 minutes results in 10:30, which is ten thirty.\",\"topic\":\"Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which hand on the clock is described as moving swiftly?\",\"options\":[\"The hour hand\",\"The minute hand\",\"The second hand\",\"The clock face\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the second hand moves swiftly.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Into how many equal parts is the face of a clock divided?\",\"options\":[\"12 parts\",\"24 parts\",\"60 parts\",\"100 parts\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the face of a clock is a circle divided into 60 equal parts.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which unit is used to measure time that is less than a minute?\",\"options\":[\"Hour\",\"Second\",\"Day\",\"Part\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The second is a very small unit used to measure time less than a minute.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, for which of the following are seconds used?\",\"options\":[\"Measuring the length of a room\",\"Measuring the weight of a person\",\"Measuring heartbeats\",\"Measuring the height of a tree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists measuring heartbeats as an occasion where seconds are used.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the minute hand when the second hand completes one full round of the clock face?\",\"options\":[\"It moves one place\",\"It moves 60 places\",\"It stays still\",\"It moves half a round\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that in the time it takes for the second hand to complete one round, the minute hand moves one place.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the second hand moves one part on the clock face, how much time has passed?\",\"options\":[\"One minute\",\"One hour\",\"One second\",\"60 seconds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"When the second hand moves one part, it takes one second.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, how many seconds are equal to 1 minute?\",\"options\":[\"10 seconds\",\"30 seconds\",\"60 seconds\",\"100 seconds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that 1 minute = 60 seconds.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does it take 60 seconds for the second hand to complete one round of the clock face?\",\"options\":[\"Because the clock has 12 numbers\",\"Because the clock face is divided into 60 equal parts\",\"Because the minute hand moves swiftly\",\"Because the second hand is very small\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"One round covers all 60 parts, and each part takes one second, totaling 60 seconds.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a race is timed and it takes exactly 1 minute, how many seconds did the race last?\",\"options\":[\"1 second\",\"60 seconds\",\"15 seconds\",\"40 seconds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since 1 minute is equal to 60 seconds, a 1-minute race lasts 60 seconds.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A clock shows 40 seconds past 10 minutes after 5. How would this be written based on the examples in the text?\",\"options\":[\"10 minutes and 40 seconds past 5\",\"5 minutes and 40 seconds past 10\",\"40 minutes and 10 seconds past 5\",\"10 seconds and 5 minutes past 40\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Following the text\'s format (e.g., 15 minutes and 40 seconds past 10), the correct format is minutes and seconds past the hour.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the second hand has moved across 30 parts of the clock face, how much time has passed?\",\"options\":[\"30 minutes\",\"Half a minute\",\"30 seconds\",\"One round\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since each part represents one second, 30 parts represent 30 seconds.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Compare the movement of the second hand and the minute hand. Which statement is correct according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The minute hand moves 60 parts while the second hand moves one part.\",\"The second hand moves 60 parts while the minute hand moves one place.\",\"The second hand and minute hand move at the same speed.\",\"The minute hand moves swiftly while the second hand moves slowly.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that when the second hand completes one round (60 parts), the minute hand moves one place.\",\"topic\":\"Learning about seconds\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the term \'am\' stand for in the 12-hour clock system?\",\"options\":[\"after morning\",\"ante meridiem\",\"at midday\",\"after meridiem\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the time before 12 noon is stated as ante meridiem or am.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to international agreement, when does one day end and the next day begin?\",\"options\":[\"At 6 o\'clock in the morning\",\"At 12 noon\",\"As the clock strikes 12 midnight\",\"At 8 o\'clock at night\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states it has been internationally agreed that as the clock strikes 12 midnight, one day ends and the next day begins.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the time after 12 noon stated as?\",\"options\":[\"am\",\"ante meridiem\",\"pm\",\"midnight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the time after 12 noon as post meridiem or pm.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the method of measuring time using \'am\' and \'pm\' called?\",\"options\":[\"The 24 hour clock\",\"The International clock\",\"The 12 hour clock\",\"The Shripati method\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that this method of measuring time is called the 12 hour clock.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If Shripati started working at 6 in the morning, how is this time written using the 12-hour clock?\",\"options\":[\"6 pm\",\"6 am\",\"6 midnight\",\"6 noon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Time before 12 noon is stated as am, so 6 in the morning is 6 am.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Shripati finished his work at 8 at night. How should this time be stated?\",\"options\":[\"8 am\",\"8 noon\",\"8 pm\",\"8 midnight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Time after 12 noon is stated as pm, so 8 at night is 8 pm.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the guests initially think Shripati only worked for two hours?\",\"options\":[\"Because he said he worked from 6 to 8 without specifying morning or night\",\"Because he was not actually tired\",\"Because the clock at home was broken\",\"Because he worked from 6 am to 8 am\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The guests misunderstood because Shripati just said \'six o\'clock to eight o\'clock\' without using am or pm.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many hours in total did Shripati spend in the field from 6 am to 8 pm?\",\"options\":[\"2 hours\",\"12 hours\",\"14 hours\",\"8 hours\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that Shripati was in the field from 6 am to 8 pm or for 14 hours.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the 12-hour clock, what time is shown immediately when one hour passes after 12 midnight?\",\"options\":[\"13 o\'clock\",\"1 o\'clock\",\"11 o\'clock\",\"12 noon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when one hour passes after 12 midnight, it is 1 o\'clock.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following describes the sequence of time in a 12-hour clock correctly?\",\"options\":[\"1 to 24 in serial order\",\"1 to 12, then 1 to 12 again in serial order\",\"6 am to 8 pm only\",\"12 midnight to 12 midnight without repeating 1\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that after 12 midnight it goes 1, 2, 3... to 12 noon, and then 1, 2, 3... to 12 again.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary reason for using the \'am\' and \'pm\' system according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To make the day feel longer\",\"To help farmers work in the fields\",\"To avoid mistakes in understanding time\",\"To change the time of midnight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that to avoid such mistakes (like the guests\' misunderstanding), the international agreement on time was made.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is studying at 3 o\'clock in the afternoon, how is this time classified?\",\"options\":[\"3 am\",\"3 pm\",\"3 midnight\",\"3 morning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since afternoon is after 12 noon, the time is stated as pm.\",\"topic\":\"Ante meridiem आणि post meridiem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the 24-hour clock method used in timetables?\",\"options\":[\"To make the clock look digital\",\"To avoid the division of the day into ante meridiem and post meridiem\",\"To make the day longer than 12 hours\",\"To show time only in the form of numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the 24-hour clock is used to avoid dividing the day into am and pm.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which of the following is the 24-hour clock method commonly used?\",\"options\":[\"School wall clocks\",\"Hand-drawn sketches\",\"Long distance boat journeys\",\"Pocket watches with hands\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions this method is used for trains, planes, buses, and long distance boat journeys.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a characteristic of a 24-hour digital watch?\",\"options\":[\"It has three hands\",\"It only shows time in the morning\",\"It does not have hands\",\"It starts again from 1 after 12 noon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that a 24-hour digital watch does not have hands.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What time does a digital clock show at midnight when the day changes?\",\"options\":[\"12:00\",\"24:00\",\"00:00\",\"12:59\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the digital clock will show 00:00 at midnight when the day changes.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is 12 noon shown in a 24-hour clock?\",\"options\":[\"00:00\",\"12:00\",\"24:00\",\"13:00\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the table, 12 noon is shown as 12:00 in the 24-hour clock.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the 24-hour clock method, what number do we continue with after 12 noon instead of starting again from 1?\",\"options\":[\"0\",\"12\",\"13\",\"24\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that instead of starting from 1, 2, 3 after 12 noon, we continue with 13, 14, 15...\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a digital clock shows \'18:20\', what does it represent in the 12-hour clock?\",\"options\":[\"20 minutes past 6 in the morning\",\"20 minutes past 8 in the evening\",\"20 minutes past 6 in the evening\",\"18 minutes past 20\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the example that 20 minutes past 6 in the evening is shown as 18:20.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the time 23:59 signify in a 24-hour clock system?\",\"options\":[\"It is 59 minutes after midnight\",\"It is 59 minutes after 23 and one minute later 24 hours will be complete\",\"It is 23 minutes past 59 in the morning\",\"The day has just started\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines 23:59 as 59 minutes after 23, with one minute remaining to complete 24 hours.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how is \'15 minutes past 10 in the evening\' written in the 24-hour clock format?\",\"options\":[\"10:15\",\"20:15\",\"22:15\",\"00:15\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows that 10:15 pm (15 minutes past 10 in the evening) is 22:15.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/071_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the arrival time of the Mumbai Mail at Nagpur?\",\"options\":[\"13:05\",\"17:20\",\"11:05\",\"13:10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The timetable in the figure shows the arrival time for Mumbai Mail (Train 21028) is 17:20.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/071_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If it is 1:20 pm in the afternoon, how would you write this in a 24-hour clock?\",\"options\":[\"01:20\",\"11:20\",\"13:20\",\"14:20\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To convert pm to 24-hour time, we add 12 to the hour (1 + 12 = 13), so 1:20 pm becomes 13:20.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A clock shows 55 minutes past 6 in the evening. What is the corresponding 24-hour clock time?\",\"options\":[\"06:55\",\"18:55\",\"17:55\",\"19:55\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"6:55 pm in the evening is represented as 18:55 in the 24-hour clock.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How is \'5 minutes past 12 midnight\' written in the 24-hour clock system?\",\"options\":[\"12:05\",\"00:05\",\"24:05\",\"05:00\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows that 0:05 am (5 minutes past 12 midnight) is written as 00:05.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the train timetable, which train departs latest in the day?\",\"options\":[\"Howrah Mail\",\"Shalimar Express\",\"Mumbai Mail\",\"Malda Town Express\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Comparing the departure times (07:45, 09:45, 13:05, 23:10), 23:10 is the latest time in the day.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following times indicates the exact moment a full 24-hour cycle is completed and a new day begins?\",\"options\":[\"12:00\",\"23:59\",\"00:00\",\"01:00\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that at 00:00 at midnight, 24 hours are complete and the day changes.\",\"topic\":\"24‑hour clock\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How is \'30 minutes past 10 in the morning\' written in a 24-hour clock?\",\"options\":[\"10:30\",\"22:30\",\"10:00\",\"00:30\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the 24-hour clock, morning times (am) before 12 noon remain the same numerically.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 44\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When converting \'in the morning\' time to a 24-hour clock, what happens to the hour value?\",\"options\":[\"It stays the same\",\"12 is added to it\",\"12 is subtracted from it\",\"It always becomes 00\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Morning hours (am) are represented by the same numbers in both 12-hour and 24-hour clocks.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 44\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Write \'20 minutes past 1 in the afternoon\' in the 24-hour clock format.\",\"options\":[\"1:20\",\"13:20\",\"2:20\",\"14:20\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"For afternoon times, we add 12 to the hour (1 + 12 = 13) to get the 24-hour clock time.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 44\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the 24-hour clock time for \'40 minutes past 5 in the evening\'?\",\"options\":[\"5:40\",\"15:40\",\"17:40\",\"19:40\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Evening times are converted by adding 12 to the hour (5 + 12 = 17).\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 44\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a 24-hour clock shows 23:10, what is the correct time in the 12-hour clock according to the text examples?\",\"options\":[\"11:10 am\",\"9:10 pm\",\"11:10 pm\",\"10:10 pm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"23:10 is obtained by adding 12 to 11 pm, so 23:10 is 11:10 pm.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 44\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the 24-hour clock representation of \'10 minutes past 8 in the morning\'?\",\"options\":[\"8:10\",\"18:10\",\"20:10\",\"10:08\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Morning time 8:10 am is written as 8:10 in the 24-hour clock.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 44\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which time in the 24-hour clock column matches with 2:10 pm?\",\"options\":[\"23:10\",\"7:25\",\"14:10\",\"17:25\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows 2:10 pm corresponds to 14:10 in the 24-hour clock.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 44\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/072_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the table in the given figure, which 12-hour clock time corresponds to 7:25 in the 24-hour clock?\",\"options\":[\"7:25 am\",\"7:25 pm\",\"5:25 pm\",\"9:10 am\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows that 7:25 am in the 12-hour clock matches 7:25 in the 24-hour clock.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 44\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/072_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"To convert 5:25 pm to the 24-hour clock time of 17:25, what mathematical operation is applied to the hour?\",\"options\":[\"5 + 10\",\"5 + 12\",\"25 + 12\",\"5 + 5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Adding 12 to the 12-hour clock pm hour gives the 24-hour clock hour.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 44\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the 12-hour clock, which term is used to describe the time \'20 minutes past 1\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Morning\",\"Afternoon\",\"Evening\",\"Night\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically uses the term \'afternoon\' for the time 1:20.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 44\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the 24-hour clock, how is 3:30 in the afternoon written?\",\"options\":[\"13:30\",\"14:30\",\"15:30\",\"16:30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that according to the 24-hour clock, 3:30 in the afternoon is 15:30.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Example (1), Abdul worked for 4 hours and 30 minutes. How else is this time described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Four hours\",\"Four and a quarter hours\",\"Four and a half hours\",\"Five hours\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Abdul worked for four hours and thirty minutes, or four and a half hours.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When adding 4 hours 30 min and 2 hours 45 min, what is the total time before converting the minutes?\",\"options\":[\"6 hours 75 min\",\"7 hours 15 min\",\"6 hours 15 min\",\"7 hours 75 min\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Example (2) shows the initial addition result as 6 hours 75 min before it is converted to 7 hours 15 min.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In Example (4), why is 85 minutes converted into 1 hour and 25 minutes?\",\"options\":[\"Because 85 = 60 + 25\",\"Because 85 = 50 + 35\",\"Because 85 = 70 + 15\",\"Because 85 = 40 + 45\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explains that 85 minutes are (60 + 25) minutes, which is 1 hour and 25 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the 24-hour clock mentioned in the text, what is 11 o\'clock in the morning?\",\"options\":[\"23:00\",\"11:00\",\"01:00\",\"12:00\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that according to the 24-hour clock, 11 o\'clock in the morning is 11:00.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Example (2), what is 75 minutes equal to when converted to hours and minutes?\",\"options\":[\"1 hour 5 minutes\",\"1 hour 15 minutes\",\"1 hour 25 minutes\",\"2 hours 15 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Example (2) shows that 75 min = 1 hour 15 min.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, why is 1 hour borrowed from the \'Hr\' column?\",\"options\":[\"Because 5 is a large number\",\"Because 45 minutes cannot be subtracted from 30 minutes\",\"To make the answer 2 hours\",\"Because 30 is bigger than 45\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure text explains that 45 minutes cannot be subtracted from 30 minutes, so we borrow 1 hour.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/072_105.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the total number of minutes in the top row after borrowing 1 hour?\",\"options\":[\"30\",\"60\",\"90\",\"45\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows \'60 + 30\' in the minutes column, which equals 90 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/072_105.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How long did Amruta travel by bus in Example (4)?\",\"options\":[\"1 hour 45 minutes\",\"3 hours 40 minutes\",\"5 hours 25 minutes\",\"4 hours 30 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Amruta travelled by bus for 3 hours 40 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Example (1), Method 1, how much time passes from 12 noon to 3:30 in the afternoon?\",\"options\":[\"1 hour\",\"3 hours 30 minutes\",\"4 hours\",\"4 hours 30 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Method 1 states that from 12 noon to 3:30 in the afternoon, it is 3 hours and 30 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the total time Abdul worked on the computer?\",\"options\":[\"3 hours 30 minutes\",\"4 hours\",\"4 hours 30 minutes\",\"5 hours\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that Abdul worked for a total of 4 hours and 30 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Example (4), what is the final total travel time for Amruta?\",\"options\":[\"4 hours 85 minutes\",\"5 hours 25 minutes\",\"5 hours 15 minutes\",\"4 hours 25 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Amruta travelled for a total of 5 hours and 25 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Examples of time measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the sum of 2 hours 30 minutes and 4 hours 55 minutes?\",\"options\":[\"6 hours 85 minutes\",\"7 hours 25 minutes\",\"7 hours 15 minutes\",\"6 hours 25 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"2h 30m + 4h 55m = 6h 85m; since 60m = 1h, 85m = 1h 25m, making the total 7h 25m.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Add 3 hours 50 minutes and 4 hours 20 minutes.\",\"options\":[\"7 hours 10 minutes\",\"8 hours 20 minutes\",\"8 hours 10 minutes\",\"7 hours 70 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"3h 50m + 4h 20m = 7h 70m, which converts to 8h 10m.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result when 2 hours 40 minutes is subtracted from 3 hours 10 minutes?\",\"options\":[\"1 hour 30 minutes\",\"70 minutes\",\"30 minutes\",\"1 hour 10 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"3h 10m is 2h 70m; 2h 70m - 2h 40m = 30 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A government office opens at 7 in the morning and closes at 3 in the afternoon. How long is it open?\",\"options\":[\"10 hours\",\"8 hours\",\"9 hours\",\"7 hours\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"From 7 am to 12 noon is 5 hours, and from 12 noon to 3 pm is 3 hours. 5 + 3 = 8 hours.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A movie starts at 3:45 pm and lasts for two and a half hours. At what time does it end?\",\"options\":[\"6:15 pm\",\"5:45 pm\",\"6:45 pm\",\"5:15 pm\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"3:45 + 2 hours 30 minutes = 5:75, which is 6:15 pm.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Sakharam ploughed his field from 8 in the morning until 12:30 in the afternoon. How long was he ploughing?\",\"options\":[\"4 hours\",\"5 hours 30 minutes\",\"4 hours 30 minutes\",\"3 hours 30 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"From 8:00 to 12:30 is a duration of 4 hours and 30 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Sakharam left his field at 12:30 and reached home at 1:30. How long did the journey take?\",\"options\":[\"30 minutes\",\"1 hour\",\"2 hours\",\"1 hour 30 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The time elapsed between 12:30 and 1:30 is exactly 1 hour.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Rambhau started a water pump at 10:30 pm and turned it off at a quarter to twelve the same night. How long was it on?\",\"options\":[\"1 hour 15 minutes\",\"1 hour 45 minutes\",\"2 hours 15 minutes\",\"45 minutes\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A quarter to twelve is 11:45. From 10:30 to 11:45 is 1 hour and 15 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Geeta taught for 2 hours 25 minutes in the morning and 1 hour 45 minutes in the afternoon. What was her total teaching time?\",\"options\":[\"3 hours 10 minutes\",\"4 hours 10 minutes\",\"3 hours 70 minutes\",\"4 hours 25 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"2h 25m + 1h 45m = 3h 70m = 4h 10m.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A bank is open from 10 am to 4:30 pm. What is the total duration of business hours?\",\"options\":[\"5 hours 30 minutes\",\"6 hours 30 minutes\",\"7 hours 30 minutes\",\"6 hours\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"From 10:00 to 16:30 (24-hour clock) is 16:30 - 10:00 = 6 hours 30 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a shop is open from 9:30 am to 10 pm, for how many hours is it open?\",\"options\":[\"12 hours 30 minutes\",\"13 hours 30 minutes\",\"11 hours 30 minutes\",\"12 hours\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"9:30 am to 9:30 pm is 12 hours, plus another 30 minutes to reach 10 pm equals 12 hours 30 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The Maharashtra Express leaves Kolhapur at 15:30 and arrives at Gondia at 20:15 the next day. How long is the journey?\",\"options\":[\"4 hours 45 minutes\",\"24 hours 45 minutes\",\"28 hours 45 minutes\",\"29 hours 15 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"15:30 to 15:30 next day is 24 hours. From 15:30 to 20:15 is 4 hours 45 minutes. Total = 28h 45m.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To subtract 2 hours 45 minutes from 6 hours 15 minutes, how should 6 hours 15 minutes be regrouped?\",\"options\":[\"5 hours 15 minutes\",\"6 hours 75 minutes\",\"5 hours 75 minutes\",\"5 hours 60 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Borrow 1 hour (60 mins) from 6 hours and add it to 15 mins to get 5 hours 75 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Calculate the total time: 3 hours 45 minutes + 1 hour 35 minutes.\",\"options\":[\"4 hours 80 minutes\",\"5 hours 20 minutes\",\"5 hours 10 minutes\",\"4 hours 20 minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"3h 45m + 1h 35m = 4h 80m = 5h 20m.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Problem Set 29, which activity takes the longest time?\",\"options\":[\"The bank being open (10 am to 4:30 pm)\",\"The government office being open (7 am to 3 pm)\",\"Sakharam ploughing the field (8 am to 12:30 pm)\",\"The movie duration (2.5 hours)\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Bank = 6.5h, Office = 8h, Ploughing = 4.5h, Movie = 2.5h. The office is open the longest.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 29\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21746,30,5,'Maths','en','Problems on Measurement','[\"- Length is measured in metres (m) and centimetres (cm). 1 metre = 100 centimetres.\",\"- Mass is measured in kilograms (kg) and grams (g). 1 kilogram = 1000 grams.\",\"- Capacity (volume) is measured in litres (l) and millilitres (ml). 1 litre = 1000 millilitres.\",\"- Time is measured in hours (h), minutes (min) and seconds (s).\",\"- For addition and subtraction of length, mass and capacity we write the units in decimal form (e.g., 1.5 m, 2.3 kg).\",\"- When adding or subtracting, align the units of the same type and carry over if the lower unit exceeds 100 (for cm, g, ml).\",\"- Example: 3 m 25 cm + 2 m 80 cm = 6 m 5 cm (because 25 cm + 80 cm = 105 cm → 1 m 5 cm).\",\"- For time, 60 min = 1 h and 60 s = 1 min.  When adding minutes, carry over to hours if minutes ≥ 60.\",\"- Multiplication and division of mixed units is done by converting everything to the lower unit first.\",\"- Speed is distance ÷ time.  Distance = speed × time.\",\"- To find how many pieces of a given length can be made from a wire, divide the total length (in the same unit) by the piece length.\",\"- When converting units, remember: 1 m = 100 cm, 1 kg = 1000 g, 1 l = 1000 ml.\",\"- Always write the answer in the appropriate mixed form (e.g., 4 km 250 m, 3 kg 150 g).\",\"- In word problems, identify the quantity to be found and use the correct operation (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division).\",\"- For “how much is left” problems, subtract the amount used from the amount available.\",\"- For “how many pieces” problems, divide the total length by the piece length and take the integer part.\",\"- For “how far will it travel” problems, multiply speed by time.\",\"- When a problem involves two different units, convert one unit to the other before performing the operation.\",\"- Always check the answer for reasonableness (e.g., a distance of 225 km in 2.5 h at 90 km\\/h is plausible).\",\"- Practice converting between units and solving mixed‑unit problems to build confidence.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which unit is used to measure length every day according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Gram\",\"Litre\",\"Metre\",\"Rupees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that we use the unit metre to measure length.\",\"topic\":\"उदाहरण (1) बेरीज\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which unit is used to measure mass?\",\"options\":[\"Metre\",\"Gram\",\"Litre\",\"Minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that we use the unit gram to measure mass.\",\"topic\":\"उदाहरण (1) बेरीज\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which units are used to measure time?\",\"options\":[\"Metre, gram and litre\",\"Rupees and paise\",\"Days, hours and minutes\",\"Kilometres and metres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions days, hours, and minutes are used to measure time.\",\"topic\":\"उदाहरण (1) बेरीज\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which units are used while shopping for goods?\",\"options\":[\"Hours and minutes\",\"Rupees and paise\",\"Metres and grams\",\"Kilometres and litres\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that while shopping, we use the units rupees and paise.\",\"topic\":\"उदाहरण (1) बेरीज\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the example, what is the result of adding 250 m and 950 m?\",\"options\":[\"1100 m\",\"1200 m\",\"1000 m\",\"1250 m\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The calculation shown in the text is 250 + 950 = 1200.\",\"topic\":\"उदाहरण (1) बेरीज\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How is 1200 m converted into kilometres and metres in the example?\",\"options\":[\"12 km + 0 m\",\"10 km + 200 m\",\"1 km + 200 m\",\"1 km + 20 m\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows 1200 m = 1 km + 200 m.\",\"topic\":\"उदाहरण (1) बेरीज\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the final sum of 37 km 250 m and 15 km 950 m?\",\"options\":[\"52 km 200 m\",\"53 km 200 m\",\"53 km 1200 m\",\"52 km 1200 m\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the final addition result as 53 km 200 m.\",\"topic\":\"उदाहरण (1) बेरीज\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/074_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what does the \'1\' carried over to the km column represent?\",\"options\":[\"100 m from the addition\",\"1 km obtained from 1000 m\",\"10 km obtained from the addition\",\"A placeholder for the next number\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows 1200 m being converted, where 1000 m becomes 1 km and is carried over.\",\"topic\":\"उदाहरण (1) बेरीज\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"30\\/074_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which unit is mentioned in the text for measuring capacity?\",\"options\":[\"Gram\",\"Metre\",\"Litre\",\"Paise\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that we use the unit litre to measure capacity.\",\"topic\":\"उदाहरण (1) बेरीज\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the number in the metre column of the final answer 200 instead of 1200?\",\"options\":[\"Because 1000 m was subtracted and ignored\",\"Because 1000 m was converted to 1 km and added to the km column\",\"Because the metre column can only hold three digits\",\"Because 1200 was a typing mistake\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"1200 m is 1 km and 200 m; the 1 km is carried over to the km column, leaving 200 in the m column.\",\"topic\":\"उदाहरण (1) बेरीज\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many milliliters (ml) are in 1 liter (l)?\",\"options\":[\"100 ml\",\"500 ml\",\"1000 ml\",\"1500 ml\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to \'Convert 1 l into 1000 ml\'.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (1) तांदूळ\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Example (2), why is 1 liter converted into 1000 milliliters?\",\"options\":[\"Because 150 ml is greater than 500 ml\",\"Because we cannot subtract 500 ml from 150 ml\",\"Because the answer must be in liters only\",\"Because 7 l is less than 2 l\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'We cannot subtract 500 ml from 150 ml. Convert 1 l into 1000 ml.\'\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (1) तांदूळ\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of subtracting 2 l 500 ml from 7 l 150 ml?\",\"options\":[\"5 l 350 ml\",\"4 l 650 ml\",\"9 l 650 ml\",\"5 l 650 ml\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Example (2) shows the calculation resulting in 4 l 650 ml.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (1) तांदूळ\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the rice word problem, how much rice did the shopkeeper have initially?\",\"options\":[\"75 kg 750 g\",\"150 kg 500 g\",\"74 kg 750 g\",\"149 kg 1500 g\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Example (1) starts with \'If a shopkeeper has 150 kg 500 g of rice\'.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (1) तांदूळ\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the subtraction table for rice, why is 150 kg changed to 149 kg?\",\"options\":[\"To add 100 g to the grams column\",\"To subtract 75 kg easily\",\"To borrow 1 kg and convert it to 1000 g\",\"Because the shopkeeper sold 1 kg\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To subtract 750 g from 500 g, 1 kg is borrowed from 150 kg, leaving 149 kg.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (1) तांदूळ\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How much rice is left after the shopkeeper sells 75 kg 750 g?\",\"options\":[\"75 kg 250 g\",\"74 kg 750 g\",\"85 kg 500 g\",\"74 kg 500 g\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'74 kg 750 g of rice is left\' after the subtraction.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (1) तांदूळ\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When borrowing 1 kg for the grams column in Example (1), 500 g becomes how many grams?\",\"options\":[\"600 g\",\"1000 g\",\"1500 g\",\"5000 g\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows 1500 g in the grams column after borrowing from the kg column.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (1) तांदूळ\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which unit is used to measure the smaller quantity of rice in Example (1)?\",\"options\":[\"ml\",\"l\",\"g\",\"kg\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table for the rice problem uses \'kg\' and \'g\' (grams).\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (1) तांदूळ\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To find how much rice is \'left\', which mathematical operation is used in the examples?\",\"options\":[\"Addition\",\"Subtraction\",\"Multiplication\",\"Division\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both examples use the subtraction operation to find the remaining amount.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (1) तांदूळ\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If you have 7 liters 150 milliliters of water and you pour out 2 liters 500 milliliters, how much is remaining?\",\"options\":[\"4 l 650 ml\",\"5 l 150 ml\",\"4 l 500 ml\",\"5 l 650 ml\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"This uses the same values as Example (2), which results in 4 l 650 ml.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (1) तांदूळ\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to Example (3), what does a speed of 90 km per hour mean?\",\"options\":[\"The train travels 90 km in two hours\",\"The train travels 90 km in one hour\",\"The train travels 45 km in one hour\",\"The train travels 180 km in one hour\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a speed of 90 kmph means the train travels 90 km in one hour.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (3) वेग व अंतर\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Example (2), what is the total quantity of milk in the two cans altogether?\",\"options\":[\"38 l 250 ml\",\"39 l 800 ml\",\"39 l 250 ml\",\"20 l 450 ml\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states the total quantity of milk is 39 l 250 ml.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (3) वेग व अंतर\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a train travels at 90 kmph, how many kilometers does it travel in the second hour?\",\"options\":[\"45 km\",\"180 km\",\"90 km\",\"225 km\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says it travels 90 more km in the second hour.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (3) वेग व अंतर\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How is the distance for the \'next half an hour\' calculated in Example (3)?\",\"options\":[\"90 + 2\",\"90 - 2\",\"90 × 2\",\"90 ÷ 2\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text shows the calculation for half an hour as 90 ÷ 2 = 45 km.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (3) वेग व अंतर\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In Example (2), which operation is used to find how much milk there is \'altogether\'?\",\"options\":[\"Subtraction\",\"Addition\",\"Multiplication\",\"Division\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows a plus (+) sign, indicating addition is used to find the total quantity.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (3) वेग व अंतर\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Example (3), what is the total distance covered in two and a half hours?\",\"options\":[\"180 km\",\"225 km\",\"270 km\",\"135 km\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text calculates the total distance as 90 + 90 + 45 = 225 km.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (3) वेग व अंतर\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a train travels at 90 kmph, what distance will it cover in exactly 2 hours?\",\"options\":[\"90 km\",\"180 km\",\"225 km\",\"45 km\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since it travels 90 km in the first hour and 90 more in the second, 90 + 90 = 180 km.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (3) वेग व अंतर\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the addition table of Example (2), why does the \'l\' column show 39 instead of 38?\",\"options\":[\"Because 20 + 18 is 39\",\"Because 1 liter was carried over from the ml column (450 + 800 = 1250 ml)\",\"Because the speed was 90 kmph\",\"Because there were three cans of milk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"450 + 800 equals 1250 ml, which is 1 l and 250 ml; the 1 l is carried over to the liter column.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (3) वेग व अंतर\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To find the total distance in Example (3), which three values are added together?\",\"options\":[\"90, 90, and 90\",\"90, 45, and 45\",\"90, 90, and 45\",\"20, 18, and 39\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows the total distance calculation as 90 + 90 + 45.\",\"topic\":\"शब्द समस्या (3) वेग व अंतर\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the speed of the train mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"45 kmph\",\"225 kmph\",\"90 kmph\",\"39 kmph\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'The speed of