:11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which units are NOT written in decimal form?\",\"options\":[\"Length\",\"Mass\",\"Capacity\",\"Time\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that units of measuring time are not in decimal form.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it more difficult to add and subtract time quantities compared to length?\",\"options\":[\"Because time is always changing\",\"Because time units are not in decimal form\",\"Because clocks are hard to read\",\"Because time has no units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes that because time units are not in decimal form, calculations are a little more difficult.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the potato vada activity, how many kilograms of potatoes are you instructed to start with?\",\"options\":[\"5 kg\",\"2 kg\",\"1 kg\",\"10 kg\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The activity starts with the statement \'You have 1 kg of potatoes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Besides the ingredients and their quantities, what else must you find out for the potato vada activity?\",\"options\":[\"The color of the potatoes\",\"The name of the cook\",\"The cost of ingredients and number of vadas made\",\"The weight of the stove\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The activity asks to find out approximately how much each ingredient will cost and how many vadas will be made.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the length of the stick to be fixed in the open field for the shadow activity?\",\"options\":[\"1 cm\",\"1 m\",\"1 km\",\"10 m\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity instructions say to \'Fix a 1 m long stick in an open field\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"At which of these times are you NOT asked to measure the shadow of the stick?\",\"options\":[\"9:00 in the morning\",\"12:00 noon\",\"1:00 in the afternoon\",\"5:00 in the evening\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The specified times are 9:00, 12:00, 3:00, and 5:00; 1:00 is not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main objective of measuring the stick\'s shadow at different times?\",\"options\":[\"To see if the stick grows taller\",\"To observe when the shadow is shortest and longest\",\"To check the quality of the field\",\"To see if the stick falls down\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity asks to observe at which time the shadow is shortest and at what time it is longest.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the third activity, what specific object\'s length are you asked to measure?\",\"options\":[\"A textbook\",\"A pencil box\",\"A pen refill\",\"A school desk\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Measure the length of a pen refill.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which calculation would likely be easier for a student to perform?\",\"options\":[\"Adding 2 hours 15 minutes and 1 hour 50 minutes\",\"Adding 2.5 kg and 1.2 kg of potatoes\",\"Subtracting minutes from hours\",\"Measuring a shadow at night\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states decimal forms (like kg) make addition and subtraction easy, unlike time units.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the potato vada activity, what is the first step to determine the total cost?\",\"options\":[\"Eating the vadas\",\"Counting the potatoes\",\"Finding out approximately how much of each ingredient you need\",\"Fixing a stick in the field\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To find the cost, you must first know which ingredients and how much of each you will need.\",\"topic\":\"Activity\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21747,30,5,'Maths','en','Perimeter and Area','[\"Perimeter is the total length of all sides of a closed figure.\",\"For a rectangle: perimeter = 2 × length + 2 × breadth.\",\"For a square: perimeter = 4 × side length (all sides equal).\",\"The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of its three side lengths.\",\"Area of a rectangle = length × breadth.\",\"Area of a square = side × side (side squared).\",\"Area is measured in square units (sq cm, sq m).\",\"A unit square of 1 cm × 1 cm has an area of 1 sq cm.\",\"To find the area of a shape, count the number of unit squares that fit inside it.\",\"When cutting a shape, the perimeter of the remaining shape can be found by adding the new edges and subtracting removed edges.\",\"Wire needed for a fence equals the perimeter of the plot.\",\"If a fence is triple, multiply the perimeter by 3.\",\"Cost of wire = length of wire × cost per metre.\",\"Cost of labour = area × cost per square unit.\",\"When dividing a shape into equal parts, each part must have the same area and shape.\",\"Use the formulae to solve word problems quickly.\",\"Remember: perimeter is about the boundary, area is about the inside.\",\"For irregular shapes, estimate by drawing a grid and counting squares.\",\"Check units: length in cm or m, area in sq cm or sq m, cost in rupees or dollars.\",\"Practice by writing the perimeter and area of common shapes like rectangles, squares, and triangles.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the sum of the lengths of all the sides of a figure called?\",\"options\":[\"Area\",\"Perimeter\",\"Volume\",\"Length\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the sum of the lengths of all the sides of a figure is called its perimeter.\",\"topic\":\"Perimeter : Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which type of figures have a perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"Open figures\",\"Closed figures\",\"Straight lines\",\"Curved lines\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that \'Closed figures have a perimeter.\'\",\"topic\":\"Perimeter : Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the adjacent sides of a rectangle are 10 cm and 7 cm, what is its perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"17 cm\",\"70 cm\",\"34 cm\",\"27 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Perimeter of a rectangle is the sum of all four sides (10 + 7 + 10 + 7 = 34 cm).\",\"topic\":\"Perimeter : Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the perimeter of square PQRS if the length of one side is 5 cm?\",\"options\":[\"10 cm\",\"15 cm\",\"20 cm\",\"25 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A square has four equal sides, so the perimeter is 5 + 5 + 5 + 5 = 20 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Perimeter : Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In triangle ABC, the lengths of the sides are 4 cm, 8 cm, and 6 cm. What is the perimeter of triangle ABC?\",\"options\":[\"18 cm\",\"12 cm\",\"14 cm\",\"20 cm\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The perimeter is the sum of all sides: 4 + 8 + 6 = 18 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Perimeter : Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To find the perimeter of any figure, what operation must be performed on the lengths of its sides?\",\"options\":[\"Multiplication\",\"Subtraction\",\"Division\",\"Addition\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The term \'sum\' in the definition refers to the operation of addition.\",\"topic\":\"Perimeter : Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the examples provided, which figure has the largest perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"Triangle ABC\",\"Square PQRS\",\"The rectangle with sides 10 cm and 7 cm\",\"All have the same perimeter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Comparing the calculated perimeters: Rectangle (34 cm) > Square (20 cm) > Triangle (18 cm).\",\"topic\":\"Perimeter : Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the square mentioned in the textbook text?\",\"options\":[\"Square ABCD\",\"Square PQRS\",\"Square WXYZ\",\"Square LMNO\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically refers to \'square PQRS\'.\",\"topic\":\"Perimeter : Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are calculating the perimeter of the rectangle mentioned in the text, how many side lengths do you need to add together?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A rectangle has four sides, and perimeter is the sum of all sides.\",\"topic\":\"Perimeter : Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In triangle ABC, which side is the longest based on the measurements given?\",\"options\":[\"Side AB\",\"Side BC\",\"Side CA\",\"All sides are equal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text gives lengths: AB = 4 cm, BC = 8 cm, and CA = 6 cm. 8 cm is the largest value.\",\"topic\":\"Perimeter : Revision\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the basic way to calculate the perimeter of a rectangle?\",\"options\":[\"length + breadth\",\"length + breadth + length + breadth\",\"length × breadth\",\"2 + length + 2 + breadth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Perimeter = length + breadth + length + breadth.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a rectangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which property of a rectangle allows us to simplify the perimeter formula?\",\"options\":[\"All sides are of the same length\",\"It has four corners\",\"Opposite sides are of the same length\",\"It is a closed figure\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that opposite sides of a rectangle are of the same length.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a rectangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the simplified formula for the perimeter of a rectangle?\",\"options\":[\"length + breadth\",\"2 × length + breadth\",\"length + 2 × breadth\",\"2 × length + 2 × breadth\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states: Perimeter of a rectangle = 2 × length + 2 × breadth.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a rectangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'twice the length + twice the breadth\', what does \'twice\' mean mathematically?\",\"options\":[\"Add 2\",\"Divide by 2\",\"2 ×\",\"Square of\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text equates \'twice the length\' to \'2 × length\'.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a rectangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the example provided, what is the length and breadth of rectangle PQRS?\",\"options\":[\"Length 14 cm, Breadth 6 cm\",\"Length 7 cm, Breadth 3 cm\",\"Length 20 cm, Breadth 10 cm\",\"Length 2 cm, Breadth 7 cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the length of the rectangle is 7 cm and its breadth is 3 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a rectangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Using the formula, what is the perimeter of a rectangle with length 7 cm and breadth 3 cm?\",\"options\":[\"10 cm\",\"14 cm\",\"20 cm\",\"21 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Based on the example: 2 × 7 + 2 × 3 = 14 + 6 = 20 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a rectangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a rectangle has a length of 10 cm and a breadth of 5 cm, what is its perimeter using the textbook formula?\",\"options\":[\"15 cm\",\"25 cm\",\"30 cm\",\"50 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Perimeter = 2 × 10 + 2 × 5 = 20 + 10 = 30 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a rectangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the calculation \'2 × 7 + 2 × 3\' used in the example instead of just \'7 + 3\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because a rectangle has four sides, and opposite sides are equal\",\"Because 7 and 3 are prime numbers\",\"Because the perimeter is always double the area\",\"Because the rectangle is named PQRS\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The formula accounts for all four sides (two lengths and two breadths) because opposite sides are equal.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a rectangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the calculation \'14 + 6 = 20\' from the example, what does the number 14 represent?\",\"options\":[\"The total perimeter\",\"Twice the length (2 × 7)\",\"Twice the breadth (2 × 3)\",\"The sum of length and breadth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the step 2 × 7 + 2 × 3 = 14 + 6, 14 is the result of 2 × length.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a rectangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following correctly describes the components of the rectangle\'s perimeter formula?\",\"options\":[\"It only uses the length twice\",\"It only uses the breadth twice\",\"It uses both the length and the breadth twice\",\"It uses the length and breadth only once\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The formula 2 × length + 2 × breadth shows both dimensions are doubled.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a rectangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is a special property of the sides of a square mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only two sides are equal\",\"All sides have different lengths\",\"The lengths of all the sides are equal\",\"The opposite sides are equal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the lengths of all the sides of a square are equal.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a square\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The perimeter of a square is how many times the length of one of its sides?\",\"options\":[\"Two times\",\"Three times\",\"Four times\",\"Six times\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the perimeter of a square is four times the length of one of its sides.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a square\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is the correct formula for the perimeter of a square?\",\"options\":[\"Perimeter = 2 × length of one side\",\"Perimeter = 4 × length of one side\",\"Perimeter = 4 + length of one side\",\"Perimeter = length of one side ÷ 4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the specific formula: Perimeter of a square = 4 × the length of one side.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a square\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the perimeter of a square calculated by multiplying the length of one side by four?\",\"options\":[\"Because squares are large shapes\",\"Because all four sides of a square are equal in length\",\"Because a square has only two sides\",\"Because the length is always 4 cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that because all sides are equal, the perimeter is four times the length of one side.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a square\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the length of one side of a square is 6 cm, what is its perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"10 cm\",\"12 cm\",\"24 cm\",\"36 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Using the formula from the text: 4 × 6 = 24 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a square\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Using the textbook example, if a square has a side of 6 cm, the calculation for perimeter is:\",\"options\":[\"6 + 4\",\"4 × 6\",\"6 × 6\",\"4 + 4 + 4 + 4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The example in the text shows the calculation as 4 × 6 = 24.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a square\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A square has a side of 5 cm. What would be its perimeter based on the rule provided?\",\"options\":[\"9 cm\",\"15 cm\",\"20 cm\",\"25 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Applying the formula 4 × length of one side: 4 × 5 = 20 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a square\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the perimeter of a square is found to be 24 cm, what is the length of one of its sides?\",\"options\":[\"4 cm\",\"6 cm\",\"12 cm\",\"8 cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the example where a 6 cm side results in a 24 cm perimeter, we can analyze that 24 divided by 4 is 6.\",\"topic\":\"Formula for perimeter of a square\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the statement from the text: \'Perimeter of a square = 4 × ________.\'\",\"options\":[