?\",\"options\":[\"Length 100 m, Width 80 m\",\"Length 120 m, Width 70 m\",\"Length 360 m, Width 100 m\",\"Length 80 m, Width 80 m\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states: The length of a rectangular park is 100 m, while its width is 80 m.\",\"topic\":\"Word problems (Perimeter)\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To find the amount of wire needed for a single fence around a plot, what must we calculate?\",\"options\":[\"The area of the plot\",\"The perimeter of the plot\",\"The cost of the wire\",\"The length of one side\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says: To put a single fence around the square plot, we need to find its perimeter.\",\"topic\":\"Word problems (Perimeter)\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a fence is to be a \'triple fence\', how is the total length of wire determined from the perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"By adding 3 to the perimeter\",\"By dividing the perimeter by 3\",\"By tripling the perimeter\",\"By squaring the perimeter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: Since the fence is to be a triple fence, we must triple the perimeter.\",\"topic\":\"Word problems (Perimeter)\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the calculation for the rectangular park, what does the number 160 represent?\",\"options\":[\"The length of the park\",\"The perimeter of the park\",\"Two times the breadth (2 × 80)\",\"Two times the length (2 × 100)\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the formula 2 × 100 + 2 × 80, 160 is the result of 2 × 80 (2 × breadth).\",\"topic\":\"Word problems (Perimeter)\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How is the total cost of the wire calculated in the square plot example?\",\"options\":[\"Perimeter + Rate per metre\",\"Total length of wire × Rate per metre\",\"Side of square × Rate per metre\",\"Perimeter ÷ Rate per metre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows the calculation: 360 (total wire) × 70 (cost per metre) = 25,200.\",\"topic\":\"Word problems (Perimeter)\",\"