2 cm\",\"They double every time\",\"They stay the same\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sequence 2 cm, 4 cm, 6 cm shows a constant increase of 2 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Patterns in floor tiles\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What must you decide about a given number according to the first two questions in the text?\",\"options\":[\"If it is a square or triangular number\",\"If it is a big or small number\",\"If it is a 2 cm or 4 cm number\",\"If it is a tile or a gap\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first two questions ask how you will decide if a number is a square number or a triangular number.\",\"topic\":\"Patterns in floor tiles\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are creating a floor pattern as described in the text, how should the tiles be placed?\",\"options\":[\"With 6 cm gaps between them\",\"One on top of the other\",\"Close together so there is no open ground\",\"Only using triangular numbers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that in specific patterns, there is no gap or open ground between tiles.\",\"topic\":\"Patterns in floor tiles\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a task the text asks the student to perform?\",\"options\":[\"Measure the ground in meters\",\"Make a collection of pictures\",\"Paint the tiles in 2 cm blocks\",\"Calculate the area of the floor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Make a collection of pictures in which you can see square or triangular numbers.\'\",\"topic\":\"Patterns in floor tiles\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what forms a \'specific pattern\' in the pictures?\",\"options\":[\"The gaps between the tiles\",\"The open ground\",\"The tiles in each picture\",\"The 6 cm measurements\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'The tiles in each picture below form a specific pattern.\'\",\"topic\":\"Patterns in floor tiles\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you find a picture of a tiled floor, what should you look for to see if it fits the \'Patterns\' topic mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"Look for square or triangular numbers\",\"Look for the color blue\",\"Look for 10 cm gaps\",\"Look for broken tiles\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text focuses on seeing square or triangular numbers within pictures of patterns.\",\"topic\":\"Patterns in floor tiles\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the significance of the phrase \'no gap or open ground\' in the context of floor tiles?\",\"options\":[\"It means the tiles are missing\",\"It describes a continuous pattern without spaces\",\"It means the tiles are 2 cm apart\",\"It refers to the triangular numbers only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The observation that there is no gap indicates the tiles fit together perfectly to form a pattern.\",\"topic\":\"Patterns in floor tiles\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following measurements is NOT mentioned in the text sequence?\",\"options\":[\"2 cm\",\"4 cm\",\"5 cm\",\"6 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists 2 cm, 4 cm, and 6 cm; 5 cm is not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Patterns in floor tiles\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what material should be used to draw the shapes?\",\"options\":[\"A piece of wood\",\"A large piece of card sheet\",\"A plastic sheet\",\"A metal plate\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions drawing shapes on a large piece of card sheet.\",\"topic\":\"Creating Patterns\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many of the drawn shapes should be coloured?\",\"options\":[\"All of them\",\"None of them\",\"Half of them\",\"One-fourth of them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to \'Colour half of them\' after drawing the shapes.\",\"topic\":\"Creating Patterns\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the next step after cutting out all the shapes?\",\"options\":[\"Glue them together immediately\",\"Separate them\",\"Throw them away\",\"Draw more shapes on top\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Cut them all out and separate them.\'\",\"topic\":\"Creating Patterns\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The text suggests joining shapes in a pattern similar to which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"A brick wall\",\"Floor tiles\",\"A window pane\",\"A staircase\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Join them in a pattern like floor tiles.\'\",\"topic\":\"Creating Patterns\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student draws 12 shapes on the card sheet, how many should they colour according to the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"12 shapes\",\"4 shapes\",\"6 shapes\",\"2 shapes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to colour half; half of 12 is 6.\",\"topic\":\"Creating Patterns\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where can the patterns made from your own shapes be used?\",\"options\":[\"On book covers only\",\"On floor tiles only\",\"For sari and shawl borders\",\"For ceiling fans\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using them to make patterns for sari and shawl borders.\",\"topic\":\"Creating Patterns\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do after joining the shapes and noting the pattern?\",\"options\":[\"Start over\",\"Complete the design\",\"Colour the remaining half\",\"Cut the shapes again\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to \'Note the pattern and complete the design.\'\",\"topic\":\"Creating Patterns\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which sequence of actions is correct based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Cut, Colour, Draw, Separate\",\"Draw, Colour, Cut, Separate\",\"Separate, Cut, Colour, Draw\",\"Colour, Separate, Draw, Cut\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text follows the order: draw shapes, colour half, cut them out, and separate them.\",\"topic\":\"Creating Patterns\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To create a pattern for a shawl border, what is the first step suggested for your own design?\",\"options\":[\"Buy a new shawl\",\"Make your own shapes\",\"Use only the shapes shown alongside\",\"Join floor tiles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Make your own shapes and use them to make patterns for sari and shawl borders\'.\",\"topic\":\"Creating Patterns\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"create\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text ask you to \'Note the pattern\' when joining shapes like floor tiles?\",\"options\":[\"To count how many shapes are there\",\"To ensure the shapes are separated\",\"To help in completing the design\",\"To see if the card sheet is large enough\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Noting the pattern is a step towards completing the overall design.\",\"topic\":\"Creating Patterns\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"From the list 5, 9, 12, 16, 50, 60, 64, 72, 80, 81, which of the following is a square number?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"12\",\"64\",\"72\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the given list, 64 is a square number because 8 x 8 = 64.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 53\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these numbers from the list 3, 6, 8, 9, 12, 15, 16, 20, 21, 42 is a triangular number?\",\"options\":[\"8\",\"15\",\"16\",\"20\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"15 is a triangular number as it can be represented in a triangular pattern (1+2+3+4+5).\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 53\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which number is known to be both a square number and a triangular number?\",\"options\":[\"16\",\"25\",\"36\",\"49\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"36 is both a square number (6 x 6) and a triangular number (1+2+3+4+5+6+7+8).\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 53\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If 4 is considered the first square number, what would be the tenth square number in that sequence?\",\"options\":[\"100\",\"81\",\"121\",\"144\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"If 4 (2 squared) is the 1st, then the 10th is 11 squared, which is 121.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 53\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If 3 is considered the first triangular number, what is the tenth triangular number in that sequence?\",\"options\":[\"55\",\"66\",\"45\",\"78\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"If 3 (the 2nd standard triangular number) is the 1st, then the 10th is the 11th standard triangular number, which is 66.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 53\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these numbers from the list 5, 9, 12, 16, 50, 60, 64, 72, 80, 81 is NOT a square number?\",\"options\":[\"9\",\"16\",\"50\",\"81\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"50 is not a square number because no whole number multiplied by itself equals 50.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 53\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the list 3, 6, 8, 9, 12, 15, 16, 20, 21, 42, which pair consists only of triangular numbers?\",\"options\":[\"3 and 6\",\"8 and 9\",\"12 and 15\",\"16 and 20\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Both 3 and 6 are triangular numbers found in the provided list.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 53\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many square numbers are present in the list: 5, 9, 12, 16, 50, 60, 64, 72, 80, 81?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"There are 4 square numbers: 9, 16, 64, and 81.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 53\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the triangular number from the list 3, 6, 8, 9, 12, 15, 16, 20, 21, 42 that is greater than 20.\",\"options\":[\"21\",\"42\",\"16\",\"20\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"21 is a triangular number (1+2+3+4+5+6) and is greater than 20.\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 53\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If 4 is the first square number, what is the third square number in that specific sequence?\",\"options\":[\"9\",\"16\",\"25\",\"36\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"If 1st is 4 (2^2) and 2nd is 9 (3^2), then the 3rd is 16 (4^2).\",\"topic\":\"Problem Set 53\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21751,30,5,'Maths','en','Preparation for Algebra','[\"Algebra is the use of numbers and letters to state and solve problems.\",\"An expression is a combination of numbers, letters and operations that gives a value.\",\"An equality shows that two expressions have the same value, e.g. (6+6) = (15–3).\",\"An inequality shows that two expressions are not equal, e.g. (7+5) + (7×5).\",\"The symbols < and > mean ‘less than’ and ‘greater than’ respectively.\",\"The symbol = means ‘equal to’ and + (in this book) is used to mean ‘not equal to’.\",\"Addition is commutative: a+b = b+a.\",\"Multiplication is commutative: a×b = b×a.\",\"Multiplying any number by 1 gives the same number: a×1 = a.\",\"Adding zero to any number gives the same number: a+0 = a.\",\"Multiplying any number by 0 gives 0: a×0 = 0.\",\"The value of an expression can be found by performing the operations in the correct order.\",\"Using brackets helps to show which operations are done first.\",\"If two expressions are not equal, one is greater or smaller than the other.\",\"To write an inequality we use <, > or = between the two expressions.\",\"The same number can be written in many different ways using different operations.\",\"When we write (9–5) < (15+3) we are saying 4 is less than 5.\",\"A blank in a question is written as ______.\",\"The book asks students to write equalities and inequalities using pairs of numbers.\",\"Students are also asked to fill in missing numbers or symbols in expressions.\",\"The book uses letters a and b to represent any numbers in properties.\",\"The properties of addition and multiplication are called ‘commutative properties’.\",\"The property that a×1 = a is called the ‘identity property of multiplication’.\",\"The property that a+0 = a is called the ‘identity property of addition’.\",\"The property that a×0 = 0 is called the ‘zero product property’.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does Algebra consist of?\",\"options\":[\"Only addition and subtraction of numbers\",\"The use of numbers and letters to state and solve problems\",\"Only the use of brackets in mathematics\",\"The study of complex geometry shapes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that algebra consists of the use of numbers and letters to state and solve problems.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result when we add, subtract, multiply, or divide two numbers?\",\"options\":[\"A letter\",\"An expression\",\"Another number\",\"An equality\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the answer we get is always another number.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are arrangements like (6 + 6) and (15 - 3) called in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Equalities\",\"Operations\",\"Expressions\",\"Problems\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that arrangements like (6 + 6) and (15 - 3) are called expressions.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is an expression such as (6 + 6) = (15 - 3) called?\",\"options\":[\"A bracket\",\"An equality\",\"A sum\",\"A division\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines an expression such as (6 + 6) = (15 - 3) as an equality.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is \'a number obtained by adding six and six\' expressed using brackets?\",\"options\":[\"6 + 6 = 12\",\"6 + 6\",\"(6 + 6)\",\"12 = (6 + 6)\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says it is easier to express it by using brackets like this: (6 + 6).\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the expression (15 - 3) mean according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A number obtained by adding 15 and 3\",\"A number obtained by subtracting 3 from 15\",\"A number obtained by multiplying 15 by 3\",\"A number obtained by dividing 15 by 3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines (15 - 3) as \'a number obtained by subtracting 3 from 15\'.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the value of two different expressions is the same, what can we say about them?\",\"options\":[\"They are expressions of letters\",\"They are equal to each other\",\"They are addition problems\",\"They are not related\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if the value of expressions is the same, it means all these expressions are equal to each other.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is an example of an equality provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"5 + 3 = 8\",\"(6 + 6)\",\"12 \\/ 4\",\"15 - 3\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists 5 + 3 = 8 as an example of an equality.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the expression (24 ÷ 2) represent?\",\"options\":[\"A number obtained by multiplying 24 by 2\",\"A number obtained by subtracting 2 from 24\",\"A number obtained by dividing 24 by 2\",\"A number obtained by adding 24 and 2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains (24 ÷ 2) means \'a number obtained by dividing 24 by 2\'.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the value of the expression (6 × 2) based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"8\",\"12\",\"7\",\"3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the value of the expression (6 × 2) is 12.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If (6 + 6) = 12 and (24 ÷ 2) = 12, how can we write this as an equality?\",\"options\":[\"(6 + 6) + (24 ÷ 2)\",\"(6 + 6) = (24 ÷ 2)\",\"12 = 12\",\"(6 + 6) - (24 ÷ 2)\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that when two expressions have the same value, we can write them as (6 + 6) = (24 ÷ 2).\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs of numbers results in the number 12 according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"5 + 3\",\"13 - 6\",\"15 - 3\",\"9 × 1\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists (15 - 3) as one of the pairs that results in the number 12.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a correct equality for the number 9 as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"9 × 1 = 9\",\"9 + 1 = 9\",\"9 - 1 = 9\",\"9 ÷ 1 = 9\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifically uses 9 × 1 = 9 as an example of an equality.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why can we write (6 × 2) = (15 – 3)?\",\"options\":[\"Because they both use the same numbers\",\"Because they are both addition problems\",\"Because the value of each expression is 12\",\"Because they both contain brackets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that since the value of each of these expressions is 12, they are equal to each other.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which statement about 13 – 6 = 7 is true?\",\"options\":[\"It is only an expression\",\"It is an equality\",\"It is a letter problem\",\"It is not a mathematical operation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies examples like 5 + 3 = 8 and 9 × 1 = 9 as equalities; 13 - 6 = 7 follows the same structure.\",\"topic\":\"Equality\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the symbol \'≠\' represent in mathematics?\",\"options\":[\"Equal to\",\"Not equal to\",\"Greater than\",\"Less than\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that to represent \'not equal\', the symbol \'≠\' is used.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a representation like (7 + 5) ≠ (7 × 5) called?\",\"options\":[\"An equality\",\"An equation\",\"An inequality\",\"A calculation\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines this kind of representation as an \'inequality\'.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which symbols are used to show that one value is greater or lesser than another?\",\"options\":[\"+ and -\",\"× and ÷\",\"= and ≠\",\"< and >\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"According to the text, to show greater or lesser values, we use the symbols \'<\' and \'>\'.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the value of the expression (7 × 5)?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"35\",\"2\",\"75\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the value of 7 × 5 is 35.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the expression (9 - 5) ≠ (15 ÷ 3) mean?\",\"options\":[\"The expressions are equal\",\"The expressions are not equal\",\"The first expression is greater\",\"The second expression is smaller\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that this means the expressions (9 - 5) and (15 ÷ 3) are not equal.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If two expressions are not equal, what can we conclude about them?\",\"options\":[\"They are both zero\",\"They cannot be compared\",\"One of them is greater or smaller than the other\",\"They must have the same value\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that if two expressions are not equal, one of them is greater or smaller than the other.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How can we write \'(7 + 5) and (7 × 5) are not equal\' in short?\",\"options\":[\"(7 + 5) = (7 × 5)\",\"(7 + 5) < (7 × 5)\",\"(7 + 5) > (7 × 5)\",\"(7 + 5) ≠ (7 × 5)\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says to show they are not equal, we write (7 + 5) ≠ (7 × 5) in short.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why can the relation between (9 - 5) and (15 ÷ 3) be shown as 4 < 5?\",\"options\":[\"Because 9 minus 5 is 4 and 15 divided by 3 is 5\",\"Because 9 minus 5 is 5 and 15 divided by 3 is 4\",\"Because 4 is greater than 5\",\"Because the values are equal\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text calculates the values as 4 and 5 respectively, and since 4 < 5, the relation is shown this way.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the value of one expression is 12 and another is 35, which symbol correctly represents that they are not equal?\",\"options\":[\"=\",\"≠\",\"+\",\"×\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the symbol \'≠\' to represent that values like 12 and 35 are not equal.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, how else can the inequality (9 - 5) < (15 ÷ 3) be written?\",\"options\":[\"(9 - 5) > (15 ÷ 3)\",\"(15 ÷ 3) < (9 - 5)\",\"(15 ÷ 3) > (9 - 5)\",\"(9 - 5) = (15 ÷ 3)\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that (9 - 5) < (15 ÷ 3) can also be shown as (15 ÷ 3) > (9 - 5).\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Analyze the inequality (15 ÷ 3) > (9 - 5). Which comparison of their values justifies this?\",\"options\":[\"4 < 5\",\"5 > 4\",\"12 ≠ 35\",\"5 = 5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The value of (15 ÷ 3) is 5 and (9 - 5) is 4; since 5 > 4, the inequality is justified.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following mathematical statements is an example of an \'inequality\' as defined in the text?\",\"options\":[\"7 + 5 = 12\",\"9 - 5 = 4\",\"7 + 5 ≠ 7 × 5\",\"15 ÷ 3 = 5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines an inequality as a representation showing expressions are not equal, using symbols like ≠.\",\"topic\":\"Inequality\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the value of the expression (9 + 8)?\",\"options\":[\"15\",\"16\",\"17\",\"18\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states 9 + 8 = 17.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Examples\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of the division 30 ÷ 2 as shown in the worked examples?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"15\",\"20\",\"25\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that 30 ÷ 2 = 15.\",\"to