रेल.\",\"बेरीज ८ येईल.\",\"वजाबाकी ८ येईल.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"५ + ४ = ९, जे ८ पेक्षा मोठे आहे, म्हणून विधान बरोबर ठरेल.\",\"topic\":\"पदावल्यांची तुलना व उदाहरणे\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"पदावल्यांच्या तुलनेत \'अनेक उत्तरे\' असणाऱ्या प्रश्नाबाबत मजकुरात काय सुचवले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"सर्व उत्तरे लिहिणे अनिवार्य आहे.\",\"एकच उत्तर लिहिणे पुरेसे असते.\",\"असे प्रश्न सोडवू नयेत.\",\"अशा प्रश्नांची उत्तरे शोधता येत नाहीत.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात म्हटले आहे की, अशा प्रश्नाचे एकच उत्तर लिहिणे पुरेसे असते.\",\"topic\":\"पदावल्यांची तुलना व उदाहरणे\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"गणित विषयाच्या लेखनात चिन्हांचा वापर केल्यामुळे काय फायदा होतो?\",\"options\":[\"लेखन खूप मोठे होते\",\"लेखन अतिशय थोडक्यात करता येते\",\"लेखन करणे कठीण जाते\",\"लेखन चुकीचे होते\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुराप्रमाणे, चिन्हांचा वापर केल्यामुळे लेखन अतिशय थोडक्यात करता येते.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"‘पंचावन्न या संख्येत ५ या संख्येने भागल्यावर भागाकार पाच येतो’ हे वाक्य चिन्हे वापरून कसे लिहाल?\",\"options\":[\"५५ + ५ = ५\",\"५५ - ५ = ५\",\"५५ ÷ ५ = ५\",\"५५ × ५ = ५\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात दिलेल्या उदाहरणाप्रमाणे भागाकारासाठी \'÷\' चिन्हाचा वापर करून हे वाक्य लिहिले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"अक्षरांचा वापर करून गणिती लेखन केल्यावर ते कसे वाटते?\",\"options\":[\"सोपे आणि सुटसुटीत\",\"गुंतागुंतीचे\",\"कंटाळवाणे\",\"अस्पष्ट\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"चिन्हांप्रमाणे अक्षरांचा वापर करूनही लेखन सोपे आणि सुटसुटीत करता येते असे मजकुरात म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"दोन संख्यांची बेरीज आणि त्यांचा क्रम बदलून येणारी बेरीज यांच्याबद्दल कोणता नियम मजकुरात दिला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"क्रम बदलल्यास बेरीज बदलते\",\"क्रम बदलल्यास बेरीज शून्य होते\",\"क्रम बदलून येणारी बेरीज समानच असते\",\"क्रम बदलल्यास बेरीज दुप्पट होते\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"कोणत्याही दोन संख्यांची बेरीज आणि त्यांचा क्रम बदलून येणारी बेरीज समान असते हा गुणधर्म मजकुरात दिला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"जर a आणि b या कोणत्याही दोन संख्या असतील, तर बेरजेचा नियम अक्षरे वापरून कसा लिहाल?\",\"options\":[\"a - b = b - a\",\"a + b = b + a\",\"a × b = b × a\",\"a ÷ b = b ÷ a\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात बेरजेचा नियम (a + b) = (b + a) असा दिला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"कोणत्याही संख्येला १ या संख्येने गुणले असता गुणाकार किती येतो?\",\"options\":[\"१ येतो\",\"शून्य येतो\",\"त्या संख्येएवढाच येतो\",\"संख्येच्या दुप्पट येतो\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"कोणत्याही संख्येला १ ने गुणले असता गुणाकार त्या संख्येएवढाच येतो, हा नियम मजकुरात दिला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"‘कोणत्याही संख्येला १ ने गुणले असता गुणाकार तीच संख्या येते’ हा नियम अक्षरात कसा लिहाल?\",\"options\":[\"a + 1 = a\",\"a - 1 = a\",\"a ÷ 1 = a\",\"a × 1 = a\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात हा नियम a × 1 = a असा थोडक्यात दिला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"भागाकाराच्या संदर्भात (a ÷ b) आणि (b ÷ a) यांच्याबद्दल कोणता निष्कर्ष मजकुरात दिला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"ते नेहमी समान असतात\",\"ते समान नसतात\",\"त्यांचा भागाकार नेहमी १ येतो\",\"त्यांचा भागाकार नेहमी ० येतो\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"दोन वेगवेगळ्या संख्यांचा भागाकार आणि क्रम बदलून केलेला भागाकार समान नसतात, म्हणजेच (a ÷ b) ≠ (b ÷ a).\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"जर a = ४ आणि b = ५ असेल, तर (a + b) = (b + a) या नियमाची पडताळणी केल्यास काय उत्तर येईल?\",\"options\":[\"४ + ५ = ५ + ४\",\"४ + ५ = २०\",\"४ + ५ = १\",\"४ + ५ = ५ - ४\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"अक्षरांच्या जागी दिलेल्या किमती ठेवल्यास ४ + ५ = ५ + ४ हे विधान सत्य ठरते.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"जर a = १० असेल, तर a × 1 = a या नियमानुसार उत्तर काय येईल?\",\"options\":[\"१\",\"०\",\"१०\",\"११\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"नियमानुसार कोणत्याही संख्येला १ ने गुणल्यास तीच संख्या (१०) येते.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"मजकुरातील (a ÷ b) ≠ (b ÷ a) या विधानात \'≠\' या चिन्हाचा अर्थ काय आहे?\",\"options\":[\"समान आहे\",\"समान नाही\",\"अंदाजे समान\",\"मोठे आहे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"गणितात \'≠\' हे चिन्ह \'समान नाही\' (not equal to) दर्शवण्यासाठी वापरले जाते.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"भागाकाराचा क्रम बदलल्यावर काय होते, हे पाहण्यासाठी मजकुरात a आणि b च्या कोणत्या किमती घेऊन पडताळणी करायला सांगितली आहे?\",\"options\":[\"a = १, b = २\",\"a = १०, b = ५\",\"a = ४, b = ५\",\"a = २, b = ३\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मजकुराच्या शेवटी a ची किंमत ४ आणि b ची किंमत ५ घेऊन गुणधर्म पडताळून पाहण्यास सांगितले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"अक्षरांचा उपयोग\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"\'अंश\' या शब्दासाठी कोणता इंग्रजी शब्द सूचीमध्ये दिला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"Denominator\",\"Numerator\",\"Number\",\"Digit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सूचीमधील ६ व्या क्रमांकाच्या शब्दानुसार \'अंश\' म्हणजे \'Numerator\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या आकृतीमधील ७ व्या क्रमांकाच्या शब्दाचा इंग्रजी उच्चार काय आहे?\",\"options\":[\"ग्राफ\",\"पॅटर्न\",\"युनिट\",\"सेंटर\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पहिल्या तक्त्यात ७ व्या क्रमांकावर \'आकृतिबंध\' या शब्दाचा उच्चार \'पॅटर्न\' असा दिला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"31\\/099_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"संख्यांमधील लहान-मोठेपणा ठरवण्यासाठी कोणता शब्द वापरला जातो?\",\"options\":[\"Equality\",\"Inequality\",\"Order relation\",\"Operation\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील २० व्या शब्दानुसार \'क्रमसंबंध\' म्हणजे \'Order relation\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"जर एखादा विद्यार्थी \'Algebra\' हा विषय शिकत असेल, तर तो मराठीत कोणता विषय शिकत आहे?\",\"options\":[\"भूमिती\",\"बीजगणित\",\"अंकगणित\",\"मापन\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील ६१ व्या शब्दानुसार \'Algebra\' म्हणजे \'बीजगणित\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"\'समच्छेद\' आणि \'भिन्नछेद\' या दोन्ही शब्दांत येणाऱ्या \'छेद\' या शब्दाचा इंग्रजी अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"Numerator\",\"Fraction\",\"Denominator\",\"Unit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील ३३ व्या शब्दानुसार \'छेद\' म्हणजे \'Denominator\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"\'त्रिज्या\' या शब्दासाठी कोणता इंग्रजी शब्द सूचीत दिला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"Diameter\",\"Chord\",\"Radius\",\"Arc\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील ३६ व्या शब्दानुसार \'त्रिज्या\' म्हणजे \'Radius\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या आकृतीनुसार, \'वर्तुळ\' या शब्दासाठी कोणता इंग्रजी प्रतिशब्द वापरला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"Square\",\"Triangle\",\"Circle\",\"Rectangle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"दुसऱ्या तक्त्यात ८८ व्या क्रमांकावर \'वर्तुळ\' साठी \'Circle\' हा शब्द दिला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"31\\/102_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"\'मध्यान्हपूर्व\' वेळेसाठी कोणते इंग्रजी संक्षिप्त रूप वापरले जाते?\",\"options\":[\"p.m.\",\"a.m.\",\"m.d.\",\"n.t.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील ७२ व्या शब्दानुसार \'मध्यान्हपूर्व\' म्हणजे \'Ante meridian (a.m.)\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"वर्तुळावरील \'जीवा\' या शब्दासाठी इंग्रजी शब्द कोणता?\",\"options\":[\"Radius\",\"Diameter\",\"Chord\",\"Circumference\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील ३२ व्या शब्दानुसार \'जीवा\' म्हणजे \'Chord\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"त्रिमितीय वस्तूने व्यापलेल्या जागेच्या मापनाशी संबंधित शब्द कोणता?\",\"options\":[\"Area\",\"Perimeter\",\"Volume\",\"Length\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील २७ व्या शब्दानुसार \'घनफळ\' म्हणजे \'Volume\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"\'विभाजक\' या शब्दाचा इंग्रजी अर्थ काय आहे?\",\"options\":[\"Dividend\",\"Divisor\",\"Quotient\",\"Remainder\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील ९१ व्या शब्दानुसार \'विभाजक\' म्हणजे \'Divisor\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"\'दशांश चिन्ह\' या शब्दाचा योग्य इंग्रजी प्रतिशब्द ओळखा.\",\"options\":[\"Decimal fraction\",\"Decimal point\",\"Decimal system\",\"Decimal place\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील ४३ व्या शब्दानुसार \'दशांश चिन्ह\' म्हणजे \'Decimal point\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"दोन राशी समान नसतील, तर सूचीतील कोणता शब्द त्या स्थितीचे वर्णन करतो?\",\"options\":[\"Equality\",\"Inequality\",\"Parallel\",\"Perpendicular\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील ३ ऱ्या शब्दानुसार \'असमानता\' म्हणजे \'Inequality\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"कोन मोजण्यासाठी वापरल्या जाणाऱ्या \'कोनमापक\' या साधनाला इंग्रजीत काय म्हणतात?\",\"options\":[\"Compass\",\"Scale\",\"Protractor\",\"Divider\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील १८ व्या शब्दानुसार \'कोनमापक\' म्हणजे \'Protractor\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"गुणाकाराच्या क्रियेतून मिळणाऱ्या उत्तराला सूचीनुसार काय म्हणतात?\",\"options\":[\"Sum\",\"Product\",\"Quotient\",\"Remainder\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सूचीतील २४ व्या शब्दानुसार \'गुणाकार\' (उत्तर) म्हणजे \'Product\' होय.\",\"topic\":\"पारिभाषिक शब्द सूची\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21768,32,6,'English','en','Monsoon','[\"Monsoon is the rainy season in India, usually from June to September.\",\"It brings heavy rainfall, cool temperatures, and lush green landscapes.\",\"The monsoon is caused by the change in wind direction over the Indian Ocean.\",\"Rainfall during monsoon is essential for agriculture and water supply.\",\"The monsoon can also cause floods and landslides if rainfall is excessive.\",\"The word ‘pit‑pat’ describes the sound of raindrops hitting the ground.\",\"‘Drenched’ means completely wet, while ‘hosed’ refers to rivers flowing strongly.\",\"Repetition is a figure of speech where a word or phrase is repeated for emphasis.\",\"In the poem, words like ‘shimmer’ and ‘streak’ describe light and lightning.\",\"The monsoon season is also called the rainy season or monsoon season.\",\"The monsoon helps recharge groundwater and fill reservoirs.\",\"Monsoon rains are often accompanied by thunder and lightning.\",\"The monsoon is a vital part of India’s climate cycle.\",\"Rainy days are good for planting crops like rice and wheat.\",\"During monsoon, people often use umbrellas and wear waterproof clothing.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what word is used to describe the land when it has dried up due to the hard sun?\",\"options\":[\"Soaked\",\"Parched\",\"Drenched\",\"Cheery\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The land has dried, it’s so parched.\'\",\"topic\":\"1.1 Monsoon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet describe the fields as \'hungry\' and the rivers as \'thirsty\' in the first stanza?\",\"options\":[\"Because they need food\",\"Because they need sunlight\",\"Because they are waiting for rain\",\"Because they are full of water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The fields and rivers are dry and waiting for the rain to come, which is metaphorically described as hunger and thirst.\",\"topic\":\"1.1 Monsoon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which bird is mentioned in the poem as swaying with its feathers spread when the rain is on its way?\",\"options\":[\"The lark\",\"The sparrow\",\"The peacock\",\"The crow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Feathers spread, the peacocks sway.\'\",\"topic\":\"1.1 Monsoon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what activity are the children doing to enjoy the rainy weather?\",\"options\":[\"Planting new trees\",\"Sailing paper boats\",\"Chasing the peacock\",\"Building a mud house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows two children crouched by the water sailing paper boats.\",\"topic\":\"1.1 Monsoon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/011_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which sound word does the poet use to describe the feeling of the first drop of rain?\",\"options\":[\"Dash\",\"Thunder\",\"Pit, pat\",\"Shimmer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem uses the onomatopoeic phrase \'Pit, pat!\' to describe the sound\\/feeling of a drop.\",\"topic\":\"1.1 Monsoon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What do the bolts of lightning do in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Gather and dash\",\"Streak and shimmer\",\"Bathe and hose\",\"Spread and sway\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'Bolts of lightning, streak and shimmer.\'\",\"topic\":\"1.1 Monsoon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the mood of the Earth change after the rain has come, according to the final stanza?\",\"options\":[\"It becomes dark and scary\",\"It becomes dry and parched\",\"It becomes happy, green, and cheery\",\"It becomes hungry and thirsty\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The last stanza states, \'The Earth is happy, green and cheery.\'\",\"topic\":\"1.1 Monsoon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which animal is shown sitting on a rock near the water and the mushrooms?\",\"options\":[\"A peacock\",\"A lark\",\"A frog\",\"A fish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration depicts a frog sitting on a rock in the bottom left corner.\",\"topic\":\"1.1 Monsoon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/011_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"The poet says \'The trees have bathed\'. Which of these situations best explains this line?\",\"options\":[\"The trees are being cut down\",\"The trees are covered in dust\",\"The rain has washed the trees clean\",\"The trees are thirsty for water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rain falling on trees is compared to a bath that cleans and refreshes them.\",\"topic\":\"1.1 Monsoon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'soaked\' as used in the line \'the land is soaked\'?\",\"options\":[\"Extremely dry\",\"Thoroughly wet\",\"Very hot\",\"Very dusty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the context of rain, \'soaked\' means the land has absorbed a lot of water and is completely wet.\",\"topic\":\"1.1 Monsoon\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is \'Repetition\'?\",\"options\":[\"A figure of speech where a word, phrase or line is repeated\",\"A way to describe the sound of rain\",\"A word that means very dry and hot\",\"A type of flash of light\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines Repetition as a figure of speech in which a word, phrase, or a line is repeated.\",\"topic\":\"Figure of Speech: Repetition\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the example \'Fly, fly little bird\', which word shows the use of Repetition?\",\"options\":[\"little\",\"bird\",\"fly\",\"none\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'fly\' is repeated twice in the phrase, making it an example of Repetition.\",\"topic\":\"Figure of Speech: Repetition\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'parched\' mean in the Word Basket?\",\"options\":[\"Completely wet\",\"Very dry and hot\",\"A flash of light\",\"Soft moving light\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket defines \'parched\' as very dry and hot.\",\"topic\":\"Figure of Speech: Repetition\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text describes the sound of tapping raindrops?\",\"options\":[\"streak\",\"shimmer\",\"hosed\",\"pit-pat\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'pit-pat\' as the sound of tapping raindrops.\",\"topic\":\"Figure of Speech: Repetition\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a poet repeats an entire line in a poem, which figure of speech are they using?\",\"options\":[\"Shimmer\",\"Repetition\",\"Drenched\",\"Streak\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The definition states that repeating a line is a figure of speech called Repetition.\",\"topic\":\"Figure of Speech: Repetition\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of \'shimmer\' as per the Word Basket?\",\"options\":[\"To spray water strongly\",\"To be completely wet\",\"To shine with a soft light that seems to be moving\",\"A flash of light\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'shimmer\' as shining with a soft light that seems to be moving.\",\"topic\":\"Figure of Speech: Repetition\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sentences is an example of Repetition based on the definition provided?\",\"options\":[\"The bird is small.\",\"Rain, rain, come again.\",\"The river is flowing.\",\"It is very hot today.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'rain\' is repeated, following the definition of Repetition provided in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Figure of Speech: Repetition\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When the rivers flow strongly as if spraying water, which word describes this action?\",\"options\":[\"hosed\",\"drenched\",\"parched\",\"streak\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'hosed\' as the rivers flowing strongly as if spraying water.\",\"topic\":\"Figure of Speech: Repetition\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definition of \'Repetition\', what can be repeated in this figure of speech?\",\"options\":[\"Only single letters\",\"Only the title of the poem\",\"A word, phrase, or a line\",\"Only the sound of rain\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that a word, phrase, or a line can be repeated.\",\"topic\":\"Figure of Speech: Repetition\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Match the meaning: If a person is \'completely wet\', they are _______.\",\"options\":[\"parched\",\"drenched\",\"shimmered\",\"streaked\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket defines \'drenched\' as completely wet.\",\"topic\":\"Figure of Speech: Repetition\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21769,32,6,'English','en','The Crow and the Snake','[\"- A fable is a short story with animals that act like humans.\",\"- The story is about a family of crows living on a banyan tree.\",\"- A wicked cobra lived in the same tree and ate the crows’ eggs.\",\"- The crows decided to stay away from the tree to protect their eggs.\",\"- A clever crow stole a bracelet from a queen’s lake to trick the cobra.\",\"- The bracelet was dropped in the tree, the cobra was unaware and slept.\",\"- The guards chased the cobra away and the crows stayed safe.\",\"- Moral: One can overcome obstacles with presence of mind.\",\"- Key words: cobra (snake), crows (birds), nest, bracelet, clever, wicked, brave, guard.\",\"- The story shows that smart thinking can solve problems.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did the family of crows live?\",\"options\":[\"On a banyan tree\",\"In a deep forest\",\"Near a palace\",\"In a hollow of a tree\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the family of crows lived on a banyan tree.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who lived in the hollow of the banyan tree?\",\"options\":[\"A family of crows\",\"A wicked cobra\",\"Royal servants\",\"A queen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions a wicked cobra lived in the hollow of that same tree.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why were the crows very happy one day?\",\"options\":[\"They found a precious bracelet\",\"The cobra left the tree\",\"The lady crow had laid eggs\",\"They moved to a new home\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says they were happy because the lady crow had laid eggs.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the cobra do when the crows flew out for food?\",\"options\":[\"He guarded the nest\",\"He ate the little ones of the crows\",\"He stole a bracelet\",\"He slept in the nest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the cobra climbed the tree and ate the little ones while the crows were away.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the crows decide to do the second time the lady crow laid eggs?\",\"options\":[\"Move to another tree immediately\",\"Stay at a short distance to watch their nest\",\"Ask the queen for help\",\"Attack the cobra together\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they decided to stay at a short distance to watch their nest.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the queen go every morning to bathe?\",\"options\":[\"To a river\",\"To a nearby lake\",\"To a royal pool\",\"To the banyan tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the queen came to the lake with her royal servants to bathe.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the clever crow steal from the lake?\",\"options\":[\"A gold coin\",\"A royal crown\",\"A precious bracelet\",\"A silver ring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the crow flew to the lake to steal a precious bracelet.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the crow fly slowly after picking up the bracelet?\",\"options\":[\"The bracelet was too heavy\",\"He wanted the servants to notice him\",\"He was feeling very tired\",\"He was looking for his nest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The crow flew slowly so that the servants would notice and follow him to the cobra\'s hollow.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the crow drop the precious bracelet?\",\"options\":[\"Into the lake\",\"Into the crows\' nest\",\"Into the hollow of the banyan tree\",\"In the middle of the forest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the crow dropped the bracelet into the hollow of the banyan tree.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the guards retrieve the bracelet from the hollow?\",\"options\":[\"They killed the cobra first\",\"They pulled it out tactfully\",\"They waited for the snake to wake up\",\"They cut down the banyan tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the guards pulled out the bracelet tactfully instead of disturbing the cobra.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the snake at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"It was killed by the guards\",\"It ate more crow babies\",\"It was chased away into the deep forest\",\"It stole the bracelet back\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the guards chased away the snake into the deep forest without harming it.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The crow\'s plan to save his family is an example of which quality?\",\"options\":[\"Greed\",\"Presence of mind\",\"Strength\",\"Laziness\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The moral of the story explicitly mentions overcoming obstacles with presence of mind.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the moral of this fable?\",\"options\":[\"Never leave your home alone\",\"One can overcome obstacles with presence of mind\",\"Do not steal from the queen\",\"Always live on a banyan tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes with the moral: One can overcome obstacles with presence of mind.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the lady crow say it had become \'dangerous to stay here\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the tree was falling\",\"Because the lake was drying up\",\"Because the cobra was eating their children\",\"Because the queen was coming to the tree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"She said it was dangerous because the cobra had repeatedly eaten their little ones.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text best describes the cobra?\",\"options\":[\"Clever\",\"Wicked\",\"Tactful\",\"Royal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text repeatedly refers to the cobra as \'wicked\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Crow and the Snake\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'hollow\'?\",\"options\":[\"Filled with heavy stones\",\"With a hole or empty space inside\",\"Made of solid gold\",\"Very large and wide\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'hollow\' as having a hole or empty space inside.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \'of great value\'?\",\"options\":[\"hollow\",\"swiftly\",\"precious\",\"plunged\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, \'precious\' means of great value.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'plunged down\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Jumped suddenly with a force\",\"Walked slowly and carefully\",\"Flew high into the clouds\",\"Sat down to rest\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines \'plunged down\' as jumping suddenly with a force.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If an object is described as \'swiftly\' moving, how is it moving?\",\"options\":[\"Slowly\",\"Quietly\",\"Quickly\",\"Noisily\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'swiftly\' means quickly.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes a \'hollow\' tree trunk?\",\"options\":[\"A trunk filled with wood\",\"A trunk that is very heavy\",\"A trunk with an empty space inside\",\"A trunk that is very expensive\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since \'hollow\' means having an empty space, a hollow trunk would have an empty space inside.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a king has a \'precious\' crown, what can we say about the crown?\",\"options\":[\"It is very light\",\"It is of great value\",\"It is empty inside\",\"It is moving quickly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'precious\' indicates that the crown is of great value.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence: The hawk ____ to catch the snake.\",\"options\":[\"hollowed\",\"precious\",\"swiftly\",\"plunged down\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'plunged down\' fits the action of jumping or diving suddenly with force.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The messenger ran ____ to deliver the urgent news.\",\"options\":[\"hollow\",\"swiftly\",\"precious\",\"plunged\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Swiftly\' is the correct adverb meaning quickly, which fits the context of running.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word would you use to describe a diamond that is worth millions of rupees?\",\"options\":[\"hollow\",\"plunged\",\"precious\",\"swiftly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Something worth a lot of money is described as \'precious\' or of great value.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following describes a physical structure that is the opposite of \'solid\'?\",\"options\":[\"precious\",\"hollow\",\"swiftly\",\"plunged\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A solid object is full, whereas a \'hollow\' object has a hole or empty space inside.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21770,32,6,'English','en','Secret Plan of the Vegetables','[\"- Vegetables are healthy foods that give vitamins and energy.\",\"- Balbir loves chocolates and dislikes vegetables.\",\"- Vegetables feel hurt when Balbir says NO to them.\",\"- Some vegetables plan to make Balbir taste their food differently.\",\"- Salt, chilli, and juice can change the taste of food.\",\"- Healthy food is good for body and mind; packaged food may have extra salt, sugar, or preservatives.\",\"- Simple Present tense is used for habits and general truths (e.g., I play, The Sun rises).\",\"- Adjectives can be changed to adverbs by adding –ly (e.g., slow → slowly).\",\"- Matching taste with food: salty, spicy, sweet, sour, tangy.\",\"- In a sentence, subject, verb, and object must be in correct order.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What was Balbir very fond of, according to the beginning of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Green vegetables\",\"Chocolates\",\"Egg curry\",\"Milk and tea\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Balbir was very fond of chocolates.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which vegetable squeezed its juice onto the egg curry to make it bitter?\",\"options\":[\"Mr. Potato\",\"Miss Bhindi\",\"Mr. Karela\",\"Cauliflower\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Mr. Karela had squeezed his juice on the egg.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the meaning of the word \'growled\'?\",\"options\":[\"Pressed something hard for a particular purpose\",\"Acting in a way that shows a desire for more food\",\"Made a low noise in the throat to show anger\",\"Speaking angrily to someone for doing something wrong\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket in the figure defines growled as making a low noise in the throat to show anger.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/017_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the vegetables feel angry and hurt by Balbir?\",\"options\":[\"Because he ate them too fast\",\"Because he did not like them and refused to eat them\",\"Because he liked egg curry more than paneer\",\"Because he stole chocolates from the fridge\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the vegetables felt angry and hurt because Balbir did not like them.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Balbir\'s parents not believe him when he said the custard was salty?\",\"options\":[\"Because they had tasted it themselves\",\"Because they thought he was just being a grumpy boy about food\",\"Because the cauliflower told them it was sweet\",\"Because they knew he loved salt\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they did not believe him and he got a scolding for being such a grumpy boy.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what does Balbir\'s expression and posture suggest about his dinner?\",\"options\":[\"He is excited to try the new vegetable dish\",\"He is very hungry and ready to eat everything\",\"He is unhappy and unwilling to eat the vegetables on his plate\",\"He is sleepy and wants to go to bed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The drawing shows Balbir looking sad and resting his head on his hand while looking at a plate of vegetables he dislikes.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/016_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"When Balbir greedily put a piece of egg in his mouth, he cried \'Yuk!\' because it tasted:\",\"options\":[\"Salty\",\"Sweet\",\"Bitter\",\"Sour\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Balbir cried \'Yuk! this egg is bitter!\' because of the Karela juice.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Balbir\'s mother says he is \'acting in a way that shows a desire for more food than is actually needed\', which word from the figure is she using?\",\"options\":[\"Growled\",\"Greedily\",\"Squeezed\",\"Scolding\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket defines \'greedily\' as acting in a way that shows a desire for more food than is actually needed.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/017_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What did the vegetables do to the chocolate to make Balbir\'s tongue burn?\",\"options\":[\"They squeezed bitter juice on it\",\"They rubbed chillies on it\",\"They threw a lump of salt on it\",\"They hid it in the back of the fridge\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the vegetables had rubbed chillies on the chocolate.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which vegetable character is shown with a bumpy texture and a vine on its head, talking to the Potato and Bhindi?\",\"options\":[\"Carrot\",\"Cauliflower\",\"Karela\",\"Peas\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Mr. Karela (bitter gourd) in the middle, identified by his characteristic bumpy skin.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/016_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How did Balbir\'s attitude toward gajar halwa change by the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"He liked it even less than before\",\"He realized it was tasty and ate the whole bowl\",\"He only ate it because he was forced by his father\",\"He still refused to look at it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"After trying it, he found it sweet and nice, and ate up all the halwa in the bowl.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the vegetables\' primary goal in ruining the taste of the chocolates and curry?\",\"options\":[\"To make Balbir starve to death\",\"To make him try the vegetable dish (gajar halwa) instead\",\"To make his mother stop cooking for him\",\"To show that they were better than chocolates\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"By making the other foods taste bad, they led him to finally try the vegetable-based halwa.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the outcome of the story, why was the vegetables\' plan considered successful?\",\"options\":[\"Because Balbir\'s mother hugged him\",\"Because Balbir stopped hating vegetables\",\"Because the chocolate was ruined\",\"Because Balbir stayed hungry all night\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The plan worked because Balbir told his mother he doesn\'t hate vegetables anymore.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What specific toppings were on the gajar halwa that Balbir usually refused to look at?\",\"options\":[\"Chillies and salt\",\"Nuts and raisins\",\"Paneer and peas\",\"Chocolate and milk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions gajar halwa topped with nuts and raisins.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Balbir creep to the fridge in the middle of the night?\",\"options\":[\"To check if the vegetables were still there\",\"To help his mother make tea\",\"Because he remained hungry after dinner\",\"To hide the gajar halwa\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says Balbir remained hungry and crept hungrily to the fridge in the middle of the night.\",\"topic\":\"Secret Plan of the Vegetables\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does the word \'growled\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Made a low noise in the throat to show anger\",\"Spoke softly to show kindness\",\"Pressed something hard for a purpose\",\"Shouted loudly to call someone\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'growled\' as making a low noise in the throat to show anger.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What behavior is described as \'greedily\' in the vocabulary section?\",\"options\":[\"Sharing food with others\",\"Acting in a way that shows a desire for more food than needed\",\"Eating very slowly to enjoy the taste\",\"Refusing to eat any food at all\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'greedily\' as acting in a way that shows a desire for more food than is actually needed.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher is \'scolding\' a student, what is the teacher doing according to the definitions?\",\"options\":[\"Praising the student for good work\",\"Whispering a secret to the student\",\"Speaking angrily because the student did something wrong\",\"Asking the student to draw a picture\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'scolding\' as speaking angrily to someone because he\\/she has done something bad or wrong.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the specific task assigned for the green-colored column?\",\"options\":[\"Enlist the disadvantages of packaged food\",\"Enlist the names of different vegetables\",\"Enlist the advantages of healthy food\",\"Enlist the prices of various food items\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table header in the figure explicitly labels the first column as \'Advantages of healthy food\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/017_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which eatable name is already encircled in the very first row of the grid?\",\"options\":[\"PANEER\",\"CARROT\",\"CUSTARD\",\"CHILLI\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The grid in the figure shows the word \'CUSTARD\' encircled in the top row.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/018_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Activity \'e\', which of the following words is classified as a \'Verb\'?\",\"options\":[\"bowl\",\"run\",\"merely\",\"hungry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the classification list, \'run\' is an action word, which is a verb.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the classification list in Activity \'e\' is an \'Adverb\'?\",\"options\":[\"tea\",\"catch\",\"angry\",\"hungrily\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The word \'hungrily\' describes how an action is done, making it an adverb.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In Balbir\'s message, what do vegetables give us besides vitamins?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Energy\",\"Sugar\",\"Sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The message states, \'You give us vitamins and energy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of vegetables according to Balbir’s message?\",\"options\":[\"To make us feel sleepy\",\"To protect us from illness\",\"To make the plate look colorful\",\"To help us win a race\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The message explicitly says, \'You protect us from illness.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list in Activity \'e\' is a \'Noun\'?\",\"options\":[\"merely\",\"catch\",\"bowl\",\"hungry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Bowl\' is a naming word for an object, which makes it a noun.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the vocabulary list, what does \'squeezed\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Pressed something hard for a particular purpose\",\"Pulled something apart gently\",\"Threw something away in anger\",\"Cooked something for a long time\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'squeezed\' as pressing something hard for a particular purpose.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the word grid (Activity d), which vegetable name appears in the sixth row?\",\"options\":[\"PANEER\",\"CHILLI\",\"BHINDI\",\"CARROT\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sixth row of the grid contains the letters B-H-I-N-D-I.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To whom is the message in Activity \'f\' addressed?\",\"options\":[\"To the doctor\",\"To the vegetables\",\"To the farmers\",\"To the students\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The message begins with \'Dear vegetables\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Balbir say \'We must eat you\' in his message?\",\"options\":[\"To stay fit\",\"To finish the food\",\"To grow taller\",\"To please the cook\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The message concludes with \'We must eat you to stay fit.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is an \'Adjective\' according to the classification task?\",\"options\":[\"tea\",\"run\",\"angry\",\"merely\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Angry\' is a word that describes a state or quality, making it an adjective.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the Simple Present Tense used for?\",\"options\":[\"Daily routine and universal truth\",\"Events that happened yesterday\",\"Things that will happen tomorrow\",\"Imaginary stories only\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states we use Simple Present Tense for daily routine, regular actions, habits, and universal truth.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sentences is given as an example of a \'universal truth\'?\",\"options\":[\"I go to school every day.\",\"The Sun rises in the east.\",\"She drinks milk daily.\",\"They read books.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'The Sun rises in the east\' as an example of a universal truth.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the examples provided, which verb form is used with the subject \'She\'?\",\"options\":[\"read\",\"reads\",\"reading\",\"to read\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'She reads\' as an example.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence from the text describes a regular action or daily routine?\",\"options\":[\"I go to school every day.\",\"I play.\",\"You read.\",\"We play.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'I go to school every day\' as an example of daily routine or regular actions.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the verb \'read\' when the subject changes from \'You\' to \'She\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"It stays the same.\",\"It becomes \'reading\'.\",\"An \'s\' is added to the verb.\",\"The verb is removed.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'You read\' but \'She reads\', indicating an \'s\' is added for the third person singular.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the rules in the text, which sentence correctly shows a habit?\",\"options\":[\"She drinks milk daily.\",\"She drink milk daily.\",\"She drinking milk daily.\",\"She drunk milk daily.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'She drinks milk daily\' as an example of a habit in Simple Present Tense.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the subject is \'It\', which verb form is correct according to the text examples?\",\"options\":[\"play\",\"plays\",\"playing\",\"played\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'It plays\' as the correct form for the subject \'It\'.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these sentences follows the subject-verb pattern shown for \'They\'?\",\"options\":[\"They reads books.\",\"They read books.\",\"They reading books.\",\"They to read books.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'They read\' as the correct pattern for the plural subject \'They\'.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Comparing the examples \'I play\' and \'He plays\', what can we conclude about the Simple Present Tense?\",\"options\":[\"The verb never changes.\",\"The verb changes based on the subject.\",\"The verb only changes for \'I\'.\",\"The verb changes for \'You\'.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The examples show that the verb form changes (adding \'s\') when the subject changes from \'I\' to \'He\'.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence is grammatically correct according to the rules of Simple Present Tense in the text?\",\"options\":[\"We watches T.V.\",\"He cut vegetables.\",\"She runs fast.\",\"You reads books.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the rules, \'She\' requires the verb with an \'s\' (runs), while \'We\', \'He\' (in this context), and \'You\' follow different patterns.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which verb form must be selected to make a correct sentence with the subject \'We\'?\",\"options\":[\"watch\",\"watches\",\"watching\",\"watched\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the table, the subject \'We\' corresponds to the verb \'watch\' to make a meaningful sentence.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/019_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the specific \'Object\' associated with the subject \'He\'?\",\"options\":[\"cricket.\",\"books.\",\"T.V.\",\"vegetables\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure aligns the subject \'He\' with the object \'vegetables\'.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Present Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/019_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which letter is silent in the word \'knight\'?\",\"options\":[\"k\",\"n\",\"i\",\"t\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the word \'knight\', the letter \'k\' is not pronounced.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the word \'pneumonia\', which letter is not pronounced?\",\"options\":[\"n\",\"p\",\"e\",\"u\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The letter \'p\' is silent in the word \'pneumonia\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which letter is silent in the word \'limb\'?\",\"options\":[\"l\",\"i\",\"m\",\"b\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The letter \'b\' is silent at the end of the word \'limb\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the word \'knowledge\', which letter is silent at the very beginning?\",\"options\":[\"n\",\"o\",\"k\",\"w\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The letter \'k\' is silent in \'knowledge\', similar to \'knight\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which letter is silent in the word \'school\' according to the exercise list?\",\"options\":[\"s\",\"c\",\"h\",\"l\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the word \'school\', the letter \'h\' is the silent letter.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which letter is silent in the word \'psychology\'?\",\"options\":[\"p\",\"s\",\"y\",\"c\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The letter \'p\' is not pronounced at the start of \'psychology\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the exercise, which letter is silent in both \'honest\' and \'hour\'?\",\"options\":[\"o\",\"n\",\"h\",\"s\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Both \'honest\' and \'hour\' have a silent \'h\' at the beginning.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If \'dumb\' has a silent \'b\', which other word from the list follows the same pattern?\",\"options\":[\"comb\",\"knot\",\"school\",\"hour\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Like \'dumb\', the word \'comb\' also has a silent \'b\' at the end.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these groups of words all contain a silent \'k\'?\",\"options\":[\"knight, knowledge, knot\",\"honest, hour, school\",\"limb, dumb, comb\",\"psychology, pneumonia\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The words \'knight\', \'knowledge\', and \'knot\' all begin with a silent \'k\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the silent letter shared by the words \'limb\', \'dumb\', and \'comb\'.\",\"options\":[\"l\",\"m\",\"b\",\"d\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"All three words—limb, dumb, and comb—end with a silent \'b\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21771,32,6,'English','en','The People Who Protect Nature','[\"Nature is essential for life – forests give fresh air, clean water, food and shelter.\",\"Trees help us breathe and provide oxygen, shade and food.\",\"Animals and birds depend on forests for food and shelter.\",\"People who protect nature are called environmentalists or nature lovers.\",\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata) is a forest guardian from Karnataka who planted over 30,000 saplings.\",\"She was honoured with the Padmashri Award in 2021 for her service to nature.\",\"Rahibai Soma Popere (Seed Mother) is a tribal farmer from Maharashtra who saved many traditional seeds and promoted organic farming.\",\"She received the Padmashri Award in 2020 and was listed in BBC’s 100 Women.\",\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar is a tribal leader who planted 5,000 trees and built check dams to conserve water.\",\"Check dams and trenches store rainwater, raising groundwater levels and helping crops.\",\"Landraces are local crop varieties adapted to specific areas.\",\"Conservation means protecting the natural world from harm.\",\"Sustainable means something that can continue for a long time without depleting resources.\",\"Cultivation is preparing land for growing crops.\",\"Herbs are plants whose leaves or seeds are used in medicine.\",\"Encyclopaedia is a book that contains information on many subjects.\",\"The word ‘mother tree’ refers to the main tree of a species.\",\"Padmashri is a prestigious Indian award for distinguished service.\",\"Forest protection also benefits birds and animals by providing safe homes.\",\"Water conservation helps farmers grow better crops and protects the environment.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what do forests provide us with?\",\"options\":[\"Money and fame\",\"Fresh air, clean water, food and shelter\",\"Buildings and roads\",\"Machines and tools\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that forests give us fresh air, clean water, food and shelter.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who else, besides humans, depends on forests for their survival?\",\"options\":[\"Only insects\",\"Only farm animals\",\"Animals and birds\",\"Only pets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that animals and birds also depend on forests.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many specific people does this lesson tell us about?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'This lesson tells us about three such people\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do trees help us live a healthy life?\",\"options\":[\"They give us money\",\"They help us to breathe\",\"They make the ground hard\",\"They provide fame\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says trees help us to breathe and live a healthy life.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary motivation for the people who work to protect nature?\",\"options\":[\"To become famous\",\"To earn a lot of money\",\"Love and care for nature\",\"To get a government job\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they work with love and care for nature, not for money or fame.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'selflessly\' imply about the people mentioned in the lesson?\",\"options\":[\"They work for their own benefit\",\"They work without expecting anything in return\",\"They work only when they are paid\",\"They work to become popular\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Working selflessly means working for society without seeking money or fame.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person plants trees to help the environment without wanting a reward, which phrase from the text describes their action?\",\"options\":[\"Working for fame\",\"Working for money\",\"Working selflessly\",\"Working for shelter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'selflessly\' to describe people who work for nature without seeking personal gain.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what would be the most likely result if forests were completely destroyed?\",\"options\":[\"People would have more food\",\"Animals and birds would lose their support system\",\"The air would become fresher\",\"Life would become easier\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since animals and birds depend on forests, their destruction would remove their support system.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following best describes the relationship between nature and humans as presented in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Nature is only for animals\",\"Nature is very important for our life\",\"Nature is only for people who want fame\",\"Nature is not necessary for breathing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The very first sentence states that nature is very important for our life.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of including the introduction about these three people?\",\"options\":[\"To show how to earn money from forests\",\"To explain how to become famous\",\"To highlight individuals who protect nature for the good of society\",\"To list different types of trees\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text introduces them as people who loved nature and worked selflessly for society.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the title \'Van Devata\' given to Tulsi Gowda?\",\"options\":[\"Forest Friend\",\"Tree Goddess\",\"Nature Queen\",\"Green Mother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'Van Devata\' means Tree Goddess.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which state of India was Tulsi Gowda born?\",\"options\":[\"Maharashtra\",\"Kerala\",\"Karnataka\",\"Goa\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she was born in a Halakki tribal family in Karnataka.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Tulsi Gowda called the \'Encyclopaedia of the forest\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because she wrote many books about trees\",\"Because she went to a famous school\",\"Because of her great knowledge of trees and plants\",\"Because she worked in a library in the forest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Environmentalists gave her this title due to her deep knowledge of trees, plants, and herbs.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Approximately how many saplings did Tulsi Gowda plant during her life?\",\"options\":[\"More than 3,000\",\"More than 13,000\",\"More than 30,000\",\"More than 3,00,000\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states she planted more than 30,000 saplings in her life.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did Tulsi Gowda gain her knowledge if she never went to school?\",\"options\":[\"By watching television programs\",\"By living close to the forest\",\"By listening to the radio\",\"By attending village meetings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says she learnt many things by living close to the forest.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to follow Tulsi Gowda\'s path, which action would be most appropriate?\",\"options\":[\"Cutting down trees for wood\",\"Studying only from textbooks\",\"Planting and nurturing saplings\",\"Moving away from the forest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tulsi Gowda\'s life work involved planting saplings and taking care of nurseries.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Tulsi Gowda\'s ability to identify the \'mother tree\' of each species indicates that:\",\"options\":[\"She only liked old trees\",\"She had a deep and detailed understanding of forest life\",\"She was looking for wood to cut\",\"She wanted to name the trees after her family\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Identifying mother trees shows a specialized and profound level of ecological knowledge.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which prestigious award did the Government of India give her in 2021?\",\"options\":[\"Bharat Ratna\",\"Padma Bhushan\",\"Padmashri Award\",\"Arjuna Award\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she was honoured with the Padmashri Award in 2021.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was Tulsi Gowda\'s role within the forest department?\",\"options\":[\"She was a security guard\",\"She took care of plant nurseries\",\"She was a school teacher\",\"She was a truck driver\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states she worked with the forest department and took care of plant nurseries.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Tulsi Gowda\'s belief that \'the forest taught her like a teacher\' suggest about her character?\",\"options\":[\"She was a humble learner who respected nature\",\"She did not like human teachers\",\"She was forced to stay in the forest\",\"She wanted to be a school principal\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Viewing nature as a teacher shows her respect and openness to learning from the environment.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, how did Tulsi Gowda treat the trees she planted?\",\"options\":[\"As sources of money\",\"As her own children\",\"As obstacles to her work\",\"As property of the government\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says \'She loved trees as her own children.\'\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following best summarizes Tulsi Gowda\'s contribution to nature?\",\"options\":[\"She wrote an encyclopaedia about Karnataka\",\"She traveled across India to give speeches\",\"She dedicated her life to planting and protecting forest life\",\"She opened a school for tribal children\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Her main contribution, as described, is her lifelong service in planting 30,000+ saplings and nursery care.\",\"topic\":\"Tulsi Gowda (Van Devata)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is Rahibai Soma Popere commonly known as?\",\"options\":[\"Tree Mother\",\"Seed Mother\",\"Nature Queen\",\"Water Mother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that Rahibai Soma Popere is known as the Seed Mother.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which year did Rahibai receive the Padmashri Award?\",\"options\":[\"2018\",\"2019\",\"2020\",\"2021\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, she received the Padmashri Award in 2020.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Rahibai is a tribal farmer from which Indian state?\",\"options\":[\"Gujarat\",\"Madhya Pradesh\",\"Maharashtra\",\"Karnataka\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she is a tribal farmer from Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many landraces are currently under conservation due to Rahibai\'s work?\",\"options\":[\"32\",\"100\",\"122\",\"2020\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that about 122 landraces are under conservation.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Rahibai unable to attend school as a child?\",\"options\":[\"She was not interested in studies\",\"There were no schools in her village\",\"Her family was very poor\",\"She preferred working in the fields\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains she could not attend school because her family was very poor.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did Rahibai learn the art of farming?\",\"options\":[\"By reading books on agriculture\",\"Through daily work and experience\",\"By attending a farming college\",\"From the BBC news reports\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states she learnt farming through daily work and experience.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the main purpose of the seed banks and nurseries started by Rahibai?\",\"options\":[\"To sell seeds for a high price\",\"To protect seeds\",\"To store water for the fields\",\"To grow flowers for decoration\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she started seed banks and nurseries to protect seeds.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Rahibai encourage farmers to grow instead of using only market seeds?\",\"options\":[\"Cash crops\",\"Local crops\",\"Foreign crops\",\"Fruit trees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says she encouraged farmers to grow local crops instead of using only market seeds.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a farmer wants to follow Rahibai\'s teaching, which method should they use for farming?\",\"options\":[\"Using chemical fertilizers\",\"Using only market seeds\",\"Natural methods and organic farming\",\"Modern industrial farming\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she taught people about organic farming and natural methods.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What action did Rahibai take to ensure other farmers could also grow native crops?\",\"options\":[\"She sold seeds at a discount\",\"She shared seeds freely with many farmers\",\"She kept the seeds in a locked bank\",\"She exported the seeds to other countries\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that she shared seeds freely with many farmers.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, Rahibai is being honored with a prestigious award. Based on the text, what is the name of this award?\",\"options\":[\"BBC Award\",\"Kalsubai Samiti Award\",\"Padmashri Award\",\"Seed Mother Award\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she received the Padmashri Award in 2020, which is the national honor shown in the image.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/021_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, Rahibai is shown receiving national recognition. According to the text, her work is considered inspiring for which two things?\",\"options\":[\"Money and fame\",\"Society and nature\",\"Schools and colleges\",\"Markets and cities\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she was included in the BBC list for her inspiring work for society and nature.\",\"topic\":\"Rahibai Soma Popere – Seed Mother\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/021_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In which village did Chaitram Pawar start his social and environmental work?\",\"options\":[\"Dhule\",\"Baripada\",\"Gujarat\",\"Janjati\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that he started his work from his village, Baripada, in Dhule district.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many trees did Chaitram Pawar initially cultivate with his own contribution?\",\"options\":[\"100 trees\",\"500 trees\",\"1000 trees\",\"5000 trees\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"According to the text, he began with the cultivation of 5000 trees with his own contribution.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which year did Chaitram Pawar receive the Padmashri Award?\",\"options\":[\"2015\",\"2020\",\"2025\",\"2030\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that in 2025, he received the Padmashri Award for his valuable work.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which organization assisted Chaitram Pawar in starting his work in Baripada?\",\"options\":[\"Forest Advisory Committee\",\"Janjati Kalyan Ashram\",\"Maharashtra State Board\",\"Gujarat Farmers Union\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states he started work with the help of Janjati Kalyan Ashram.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the result of building check dams and trenches in the villages?\",\"options\":[\"The forests were cut down\",\"The groundwater level increased\",\"The villages were flooded\",\"The birds moved away\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that because of check dams and trenches, the groundwater level increased in many areas.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"As an expert member of the Forest Advisory Committee (2015), what was one of his main goals?\",\"options\":[\"To build large factories in forests\",\"To promote self-reliant development and empower tribal communities\",\"To move tribal people to cities\",\"To stop farming in Maharashtra\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He helped protect forests, empower tribal communities, and promote self-reliant development.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did Chaitram Pawar\'s work specifically benefit the farmers?\",\"options\":[\"He gave them free seeds\",\"He provided them with more water for farming, which improved their crops\",\"He taught them how to build houses\",\"He moved their farms to Gujarat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that farmers got more water for farming and their crops improved due to increased groundwater.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a village wanted to store rainwater effectively using Chaitram Pawar\'s methods, what should they build?\",\"options\":[\"Large wooden fences\",\"Check dams and trenches\",\"New roads\",\"Factory buildings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he helped villages by building check dams and trenches to store rainwater.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which states have benefited from Chaitram Pawar\'s community development work according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only Maharashtra\",\"Maharashtra and Madhya Pradesh only\",\"Maharashtra, Gujarat, and Madhya Pradesh\",\"Maharashtra and Delhi\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions his work extended to villages in Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, and Gujarat.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the link between forest protection and the lives of birds and animals in this text?\",\"options\":[\"Forest protection made animals leave the area\",\"Forest protection provided birds and animals with safe homes\",\"Forest protection was only for the benefit of farmers\",\"Forest protection led to fewer trees for birds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states his work helped birds and animals to get safe homes and saved many forests.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is Chaitram Pawar described as a \'tribal social and environmental leader\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because he has over 30 years of experience in conservation and community development\",\"Because he only works in his own village\",\"Because he received an award in 2015\",\"Because he is a member of a city council\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"His leadership is defined by his 30 years of experience in leading conservation and community development.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what was the primary sequence of Chaitram Pawar\'s water conservation impact?\",\"options\":[\"Building dams -> Increased groundwater -> Improved crops\",\"Improved crops -> Building dams -> Increased groundwater\",\"Increased groundwater -> Building dams -> Improved crops\",\"Building dams -> Improved crops -> Increased groundwater\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text describes building check dams first, which increased groundwater, which then improved crops.\",\"topic\":\"Chaitram Deochand Pawar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What are plants called when their leaves and seeds are used in medicine?\",\"options\":[\"herbs\",\"landraces\",\"trenches\",\"crops\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the text, herbs are plants whose leaves and seeds are used in medicine.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which book gives information about many subjects arranged in alphabetical order?\",\"options\":[\"Dictionary\",\"Encyclopaedia\",\"Storybook\",\"Notebook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"An encyclopaedia is a book or set of books that gives information about many subjects arranged from A to Z.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'increased\'?\",\"options\":[\"became smaller\",\"stayed the same\",\"became something larger\",\"disappeared\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'increased\' as becoming something larger.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'conservation\' mean in the context of nature?\",\"options\":[\"The destruction of forests\",\"The protection of the natural world\",\"The use of chemicals on land\",\"The digging of deep holes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Conservation is defined as the protection of the natural world.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a process is described as \'sustainable\', it means it:\",\"options\":[\"can continue for a long time\",\"will end very quickly\",\"is only for medicinal use\",\"is arranged from A to Z\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Sustainable means that which can continue for a long time.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary purpose of \'cultivation\'?\",\"options\":[\"To protect the natural world\",\"To prepare and use land for growing crops\",\"To arrange books in alphabetical order\",\"To make something larger\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Cultivation is the preparation and the use of the land for growing crops.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A farmer digs a long narrow hole in the ground so that water can flow along it. What has he created?\",\"options\":[\"A herb\",\"A trench\",\"A landrace\",\"An encyclopaedia\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A trench is a long narrow hole dug in the ground for water to flow along.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A farmer in a specific village grows a variety of rice that is perfectly suited to his local climate. This variety is called a:\",\"options\":[\"Sustainable crop\",\"Landrace\",\"Trench\",\"Medicinal herb\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Landraces are varieties of crops that suit the conditions of a particular local area.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How is the information in an encyclopaedia organized?\",\"options\":[\"By the size of the book\",\"By the date of the information\",\"In the order of the alphabet\",\"By the type of crop\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that information in an encyclopaedia is arranged in the order of the alphabet (from A to Z).\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these activities is most directly related to preparing land for farming?\",\"options\":[\"Conservation\",\"Cultivation\",\"Alphabetizing\",\"Increasing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Cultivation involves the preparation and use of land specifically for growing crops.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the chart, which pronoun is used for the word \'father\'?\",\"options\":[\"She\",\"It\",\"He\",\"They\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The chart explicitly lists \'father\' under the Masculine gender which uses the pronoun \'He\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of Feminine gender in the provided chart?\",\"options\":[\"King\",\"Queen\",\"Father\",\"Boy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The chart lists \'queen\' as an example of the Feminine gender.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'This is a tree. It is green\', what does the pronoun \'It\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"The boy\",\"The girl\",\"The tree\",\"The color\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the example sentences, \'It\' is used to refer back to the tree.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which gender category does the word \'city\' belong to according to the chart?\",\"options\":[\"Masculine\",\"Feminine\",\"Neuter\",\"Common\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The chart lists \'city\' as an example under the Neuter gender category.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'He\' is used for a boy, which pronoun is used for a girl according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"It\",\"She\",\"Him\",\"Her\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows \'She\' is the pronoun used for a girl.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence using the correct pronoun from the chart: \'This is a book. ___ is new.\'\",\"options\":[\"He\",\"She\",\"It\",\"They\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The chart classifies \'book\' as Neuter gender, which uses the pronoun \'It\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which pronoun would you use for a \'king\' based on the Masculine gender category?\",\"options\":[\"She\",\"It\",\"He\",\"Her\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The chart lists \'king\' under Masculine gender, which corresponds to the pronoun \'He\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the group where all words belong to the Neuter gender according to the text.\",\"options\":[\"Boy, father, king\",\"Girl, mother, queen\",\"Book, table, city\",\"King, queen, fruit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The chart lists book, table, and city all under the Neuter category.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following pairs correctly matches the word with its gender as per the chart?\",\"options\":[\"Mother - Masculine\",\"Fruit - Neuter\",\"King - Feminine\",\"Boy - Neuter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The chart correctly identifies \'fruit\' as Neuter gender.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If \'father\' is Masculine, what is the gender of \'mother\' according to the chart?\",\"options\":[\"Neuter\",\"Masculine\",\"Feminine\",\"Pronoun\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The chart lists \'mother\' as an example of the Feminine gender.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21772,32,6,'English','en','One Thing that I Wonder','[\"- The chapter is about *wonder* – a feeling of curiosity and asking questions.\",\"- *Wonder* means to want to know something or to be amazed.\",\"- The poem shows many things the speaker wonders about: the roundness of the world, why trees grow up, why the sky is blue, why spiders have eight legs, why bunnies burrow, why whales sleep in the sea, etc.\",\"- A *list of wonders* can be made: e.g., Great Wall of China, Taj Mahal, Statue of Liberty, etc.\",\"- *Alliteration* is the repetition of the same consonant sound at the start of words in a sentence (e.g., “Busy bees buzz”).\",\"- *Pun* is a joke that uses a word with two meanings or sounds similar to another word (e.g., “two tired” for “too tired”).\",\"- *Minimal pairs* are two words that differ in only one sound, like “sleep” vs “slip” or “bat” vs “cat.”\",\"- Short vowel sounds: \\/æ\\/ (a in cat), \\/e\\/ (e in bed), \\/ɪ\\/ (i in sit), \\/ɒ\\/ (o in hot), \\/ʌ\\/ (u in cup), \\/ʊ\\/ (oo in book).\",\"- Short vowels usually appear in closed syllables (ending with a consonant).\",\"- In short vowel words, the vowel does not sound like the name of the letter (e.g., \\/æ\\/ in cat is not “A”).\",\"- Practice by underlining the short vowels in words like “apple,” “pen,” “dog.”\",\"- Break words into syllables and identify which syllable contains the short vowel.\",\"- The chapter encourages making lists, writing poems, and creating puns and minimal pairs.\",\"- Students should read aloud to hear sounds and practice pronunciation.\",\"- The teacher can ask students to find examples of alliteration and puns in everyday sentences.\",\"- The chapter also introduces the concept of *schwa* \\/ə\\/ which sounds like a very short “uh” sound in words like “teacher.”\",\"- Understanding these phonetic concepts helps improve reading and speaking skills.\",\"- The exercises include fill‑in‑the‑blank, true\\/false, matching, and short answer questions.\",\"- Remember to write the answers clearly and check for correct spelling.\",\"- Practice makes the sounds and concepts stick!\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the author of the poem \'One Thing that I Wonder\'?\",\"options\":[\"Robert Frost\",\"Charles Ghigna\",\"William Wordsworth\",\"Rudyard Kipling\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem is attributed to Charles Ghigna at the end of the text.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, how many legs do spiders have?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Four\",\"Six\",\"Eight\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'And why spiders all have eight legs\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where do whales sleep according to the speaker?\",\"options\":[\"In a tree\",\"Underground\",\"In the sea\",\"In laps\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions \'While whales sleep in the sea\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where do bunnies burrow according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"In the sky\",\"Underground\",\"In a tree\",\"In the sea\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'That bunnies burrow underground\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What shape of the world does the speaker wonder about?\",\"options\":[\"Square\",\"Flat\",\"Round\",\"Oval\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The speaker asks \'why the world is round\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In which direction do trees grow according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Toward the sky\",\"Upside down\",\"Underground\",\"Into the sea\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions trees grow \'toward the sky instead of upside down\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What color is the sky according to the speaker\'s wonderings?\",\"options\":[\"Green\",\"Blue\",\"White\",\"Grey\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speaker wonders \'why the sky is blue\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many legs do \'we\' (humans) have?\",\"options\":[\"Eight\",\"Four\",\"Two\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'While we have only two\' in comparison to spiders.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is described as being \'quick to sit in laps\'?\",\"options\":[\"Bunnies\",\"Birds\",\"Whales\",\"Cats\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem states \'That cats are quick to sit in laps\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a bird lives in a tree, where does the poem say a bunny lives?\",\"options\":[\"In the sea\",\"Underground\",\"In a lap\",\"Toward the sky\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem contrasts bunnies burrowing underground with birds living in trees.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final thing the speaker wonders about in the last stanza?\",\"options\":[\"Why the sky is blue\",\"Why spiders have eight legs\",\"Why we wonder why\",\"Why trees grow up\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The last stanza begins with \'One thing that I wonder Is why we wonder why\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the final lines, where are the \'wonders of the earth\' found?\",\"options\":[\"Only in the sea\",\"Only in the sky\",\"In the sea and sky\",\"Underground\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem concludes by mentioning wonders \'That fill the sea and sky\'.\",\"topic\":\"One Thing that I Wonder\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does the word \'wonder\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"To want to know something\",\"To go for a long walk\",\"To sleep for a long time\",\"To dig a hole in the ground\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'wonder\' as \'to want to know something\'.\",\"topic\":\"Alliteration\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are \'whales\' as described in the glossary section?\",\"options\":[\"Small insects in the garden\",\"Very large animals that live in the sea\",\"Rabbits that live in holes\",\"Flowers that bloom in spring\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'whales\' as \'very large animals that live in the sea\'.\",\"topic\":\"Alliteration\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'burrow\'?\",\"options\":[\"To fly in the sky\",\"To swim in the sea\",\"To dig a hole in the ground or shelter by rabbits\",\"To make a buzzing sound\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'burrow\' as \'to dig a hole in the ground or shelter by rabbits\'.\",\"topic\":\"Alliteration\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the definition of \'Alliteration\' provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The repetition of vowel sounds at the end of words\",\"The repetition of consonant sounds at the beginning of words\",\"A type of flower that blooms in spring\",\"A sound made by busy bees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Alliteration is a repetition of consonant sounds at the beginning of words.\'\",\"topic\":\"Alliteration\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'Busy bees buzz in the garden\', which sound is repeated to create alliteration?\",\"options\":[\"The \'s\' sound\",\"The \'z\' sound\",\"The \'b\' sound\",\"The \'g\' sound\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that the words Busy, bees and buzz begin with the same sound \'b\'.\",\"topic\":\"Alliteration\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, when does Alliteration occur?\",\"options\":[\"When two or more words together begin with the same sound\",\"When a sentence has only one word\",\"When words end with the same letter\",\"When animals live in the sea\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'When two or more words together begin with the same sound, it is called Alliteration.\'\",\"topic\":\"Alliteration\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the repeated sound in the example: \'Pretty pink flowers bloom in spring.\'\",\"options\":[\"The \'f\' sound\",\"The \'s\' sound\",\"The \'p\' sound\",\"The \'l\' sound\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that in this line, the \'P\' sound is repeated.\",\"topic\":\"Alliteration\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definition of Alliteration, which of these new examples follows the same rule?\",\"options\":[\"Cats like milk\",\"Seven silly seals\",\"Dogs bark at night\",\"Birds fly away\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Seven silly seals\' repeats the \'s\' sound at the beginning of the words, matching the definition.\",\"topic\":\"Alliteration\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where must the repeated sounds be located in words for it to be considered Alliteration?\",\"options\":[\"At the end of the words\",\"In the middle of the words\",\"At the beginning of the words\",\"Only in the longest word\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines alliteration as the repetition of sounds \'at the beginning of words\'.\",\"topic\":\"Alliteration\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which type of sounds are specifically mentioned as being repeated in Alliteration?\",\"options\":[\"Vowel sounds\",\"Consonant sounds\",\"Animal sounds\",\"Silent sounds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines Alliteration as a repetition of \'consonant sounds\'.\",\"topic\":\"Alliteration\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What are word pairs called when they differ in only one sound and have different meanings?\",\"options\":[\"Maximum pairs\",\"Minimal pairs\",\"Dual pairs\",\"Sound pairs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines word pairs that differ in only one sound and meaning as Minimal pairs.\",\"topic\":\"Pun\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a humorous sentence with a dual meaning called?\",\"options\":[\"Poem\",\"Minimal pair\",\"Pun\",\"Prose\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a humorous sentence with dual meaning, intentionally used, is called a Pun.\",\"topic\":\"Pun\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is an example of a minimal pair mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"bat - cat\",\"maths - book\",\"two - tired\",\"doctor - virus\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'bat - cat\' as an example of a minimal pair.\",\"topic\":\"Pun\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the joke about the Maths book, why is the book \'sad\'?\",\"options\":[\"It is very old\",\"It has many problems\",\"It has no pages\",\"It is too heavy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The student says the Maths book is sad because it has many problems, creating a pun on mathematical sums and life troubles.\",\"topic\":\"Pun\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The pun in the bicycle joke plays on which two similar-sounding phrases?\",\"options\":[\"two-tires and too tired\",\"stand and own\",\"bicycle and cycle\",\"tired and retired\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text notes that the joke plays on \'two-tires\' vs \'too tired\'.\",\"topic\":\"Pun\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the computer go to the doctor in the example provided?\",\"options\":[\"It was broken\",\"It had a virus\",\"It was too old\",\"It needed a battery\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the dual meaning of \'virus\' (medical vs computer) to create a joke.\",\"topic\":\"Pun\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the minimal pair \'sip - ship\', how many sounds are different?\",\"options\":[\"Two sounds\",\"All sounds\",\"Only one sound\",\"No sounds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Minimal pairs are defined as words that differ in only one sound.\",\"topic\":\"Pun\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the definition, a pun is used __________.\",\"options\":[\"Accidentally\",\"Intentionally\",\"Sadly\",\"Quietly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a pun as a humorous sentence with dual meaning used intentionally.\",\"topic\":\"Pun\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the sentence \'Because it is two tired\' creates the humorous dual meaning?\",\"options\":[\"Because\",\"It\",\"Stand\",\"Two tired\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'two tired\' creates the pun by sounding like \'too tired\' while referring to the bicycle\'s tires.\",\"topic\":\"Pun\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary purpose of using a Pun according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To make a sentence humorous\",\"To teach new vocabulary\",\"To explain math problems\",\"To describe a doctor\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text describes a pun as a \'humorous sentence\' with dual meaning.\",\"topic\":\"Pun\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, short vowels are usually found in which type of syllables?\",\"options\":[\"Open syllables\",\"Closed syllables\",\"Long syllables\",\"Silent syllables\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Quick tip\' states that short vowels are usually found in closed syllables ending with a consonant.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the IPA symbol for the short vowel sound found in the word \'cat\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/e\\/\",\"\\/ɪ\\/\",\"\\/æ\\/\",\"\\/ɒ\\/\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table lists \\/æ\\/ as the IPA sound for the word \'cat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which IPA sound is represented by the common letters \'oo\' and \'u\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/ʌ\\/\",\"\\/ʊ\\/\",\"\\/ɒ\\/\",\"\\/ə\\/\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows that the sound \\/ʊ\\/ uses common letters \'oo\' and \'u\' as in book and put.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/027_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How do short vowels differ from long vowels according to the \'Quick tip\'?\",\"options\":[\"They always sound like the name of the letter.\",\"They are only found at the start of words.\",\"They don’t sound like the name of the letter.\",\"They are always followed by two consonants.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that short vowels don\'t sound like the name of the letter, unlike long vowels.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the examples provided, which word shares the same short vowel sound as \'gym\'?\",\"options\":[\"bed\",\"sit\",\"hot\",\"sun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both \'sit\' and \'gym\' are listed under the \\/ɪ\\/ sound category.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which IPA sound is associated with the words \'teacher\' and \'doctor\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/e\\/\",\"\\/ʌ\\/\",\"\\/ʊ\\/\",\"\\/ə\\/ (schwa)\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'teacher\' and \'doctor\' as examples for the \\/ə\\/ (schwa) sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/027_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words contains the \\/ʌ\\/ sound as shown in the textbook table?\",\"options\":[\"luck\",\"book\",\"box\",\"pen\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'luck\' is listed as an example for the \\/ʌ\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the word \'cat\' has a short vowel sound \\/æ\\/ because it is in a closed syllable, which of these is the reason?\",\"options\":[\"It starts with a consonant.\",\"It ends with a consonant.\",\"It has only three letters.\",\"It sounds like the letter \'A\'.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A closed syllable is defined in the text as one ending with a consonant.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Compare the words \'cat\' and \'cake\' based on the \'Quick tip\'. Why is \'cat\' considered to have a short vowel?\",\"options\":[\"Because it sounds like the letter \'A\'.\",\"Because it does not sound like the name of the letter \'A\'.\",\"Because it has more consonants than \'cake\'.\",\"Because it is a longer word.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The tip explains that cat (\\/æ\\/) doesn’t sound like the letter \'A\', making it a short vowel.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which common letter is used to represent the \\/ɒ\\/ sound in the words \'hot\', \'dog\', and \'box\'?\",\"options\":[\"a\",\"u\",\"o\",\"e\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows the letter \'o\' is the common letter for the \\/ɒ\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21773,32,6,'English','en','The Brother','[\"The poem is about a brother, showing love and support.\",\"A brother is a close friend who stands beside you in joy and sorrow.\",\"Simile: a comparison using ‘like’ or ‘as’ (e.g., ‘The moon is like a silver ball’).\",\"Metaphor: a comparison without ‘like’ or ‘as’ (e.g., ‘He is a lion’).\",\"Rhyming words in the poem: moon & sun, pain & gain, smile & worthwhile, flow & sea, dark & long, break & break.\",\"The poem’s message: a brother’s love is strong, unbreakable and always there.\",\"The poem’s title is ‘The Brother’ and the poet is Amanjeet Singh.\",\"The poem uses similes to describe the brother’s qualities.\",\"A brother’s qualities: loyalty, support, love, strength, and companionship.\",\"The poem shows how a brother helps you in good times and bad.\",\"The poem’s structure: stanzas of four lines with rhyme scheme AABB.\",\"Similes in the poem: ‘You are my moon and sun’, ‘Your strength and hope keep me strong’.\",\"Metaphors in the poem: ‘You stand beside through loss and gain’ (implied).\",\"A brother can be a friend, a guide, and a protector.\",\"The poem encourages gratitude and appreciation for siblings.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the poet of the poem \'The Brother\'?\",\"options\":[\"Rabindranath Tagore\",\"Amanjeet Singh\",\"Sarojini Naidu\",\"Robert Frost\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem is signed by Amanjeet Singh at the end of the text.\",\"topic\":\"The Brother\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what can the brother\'s eyes see?\",\"options\":[\"The bright sun\",\"The flowing river\",\"Hidden pain\",\"The deep sea\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The second stanza mentions, \'With eyes that see my hidden pain\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Brother\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The brother is compared to which two celestial bodies in the first stanza?\",\"options\":[\"Stars and Moon\",\"Sun and Stars\",\"Moon and Sun\",\"Earth and Moon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'You, my brother, my moon and sun.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Brother\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'Through storm and sun\' most likely represent?\",\"options\":[\"Different types of weather\",\"Good times and difficult times\",\"Day and night cycles\",\"Traveling to different countries\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In poetry, storm and sun often symbolize the challenges and joys shared in a relationship.\",\"topic\":\"The Brother\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To what does the poet compare the strength of their togetherness?\",\"options\":[\"A mountain standing tall\",\"Rivers flowing to the sea\",\"A tree in a storm\",\"The heat of the sun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Like rivers flow to the sea, together strong, you and me.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Brother\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What makes everything \'worthwhile\' for the speaker?\",\"options\":[\"Winning a game\",\"The brother\'s presence\",\"Seeing the moon\",\"Traveling through space\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Your presence makes it all worthwhile.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Brother\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the speaker is facing a very difficult time (\'dark days\'), what does the brother provide?\",\"options\":[\"Money and gifts\",\"Food and water\",\"Strength and hope\",\"Laughter and jokes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The third stanza says, \'Your strength and hope keep me strong\' when days are dark.\",\"topic\":\"The Brother\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem, how does the brother act during times of \'loss and gain\'?\",\"options\":[\"He leaves the speaker alone\",\"He stands beside the speaker\",\"He only celebrates the gain\",\"He hides his own feelings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'You stand beside through loss and gain.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Brother\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the central theme of the poem \'The Brother\'?\",\"options\":[\"The beauty of nature and rivers\",\"The cycle of day and night\",\"The unbreakable bond of love between siblings\",\"The importance of physical strength\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem focuses on the deep, enduring, and unbreakable bond shared with a brother.\",\"topic\":\"The Brother\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet imply by saying the bond cannot be broken by \'time and space\'?\",\"options\":[\"The brother is a time traveler\",\"The relationship is temporary\",\"Distance and years do not change their love\",\"They live in a place without time\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase suggests that no matter how much time passes or how far apart they are, the bond remains.\",\"topic\":\"The Brother\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is a \'Simile\'?\",\"options\":[\"A comparison between two different things using \'like\' or \'as\'\",\"A word that means the same as another word\",\"A sentence that does not use any comparison\",\"A type of drum used for beating fast\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines Simile as a comparison between two different things using the words \'like\' or \'as\'.\",\"topic\":\"Simile\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words are used to identify a Simile in a sentence?\",\"options\":[\"and, but\",\"like, as\",\"is, are\",\"very, too\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that a Simile uses the words \'like\' or \'as\'.\",\"topic\":\"Simile\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'worthwhile\' mean as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"Advantage in something\",\"Shining bright\",\"Enjoyable or useful\",\"Beating fast\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'worthwhile\' as \'enjoyable or useful\'.\",\"topic\":\"Simile\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the example \'The moon is like a silver ball\', what is the moon compared with?\",\"options\":[\"A happy drum\",\"A silver ball\",\"The bright sun\",\"A shining star\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'The moon is like a silver ball. -> Moon is compared with silver ball.\'\",\"topic\":\"Simile\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the heart compared with in the second example?\",\"options\":[\"Fun\",\"Fast beating\",\"A happy drum\",\"A silver ball\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows \'My heart is like a happy drum\' and points out that the heart is compared with a happy drum.\",\"topic\":\"Simile\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/029_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'gain\' according to the provided text?\",\"options\":[\"To lose something\",\"Advantage in something\",\"To be useful\",\"To beat fast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'gain\' as \'advantage in something\'.\",\"topic\":\"Simile\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student writes \'He is as brave as a lion\', which figure of speech from the text are they using?\",\"options\":[\"Rhyme\",\"Simile\",\"Noun\",\"Verb\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sentence uses \'as\' to compare a person to a lion, which fits the definition of a Simile.\",\"topic\":\"Simile\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following sentences is an example of a Simile based on the rules in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The sun is very hot today.\",\"She runs very fast.\",\"Her smile is like sunshine.\",\"The drum is beating loudly.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sentence \'Her smile is like sunshine\' uses \'like\' to compare two different things, making it a Simile.\",\"topic\":\"Simile\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, look at the definition in the green box. A Simile must involve a comparison between how many things?\",\"options\":[\"Only one thing\",\"Two different things\",\"Three similar things\",\"No things at all\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The green box in the figure states: \'When there is a comparison between two different things...\'\",\"topic\":\"Simile\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/029_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the sentence \'My heart is like a happy drum\' considered a Simile?\",\"options\":[\"Because it compares the heart to a drum using the word \'like\'\",\"Because it describes how a heart beats\",\"Because the words \'heart\' and \'drum\' rhyme\",\"Because it is a very long sentence\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"It is a Simile because it compares two different things (heart and drum) using the word \'like\' as per the textbook rule.\",\"topic\":\"Simile\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is a \'Metaphor\'?\",\"options\":[\"A comparison using the word \'like\'\",\"A comparison using the word \'as\'\",\"A comparison between two different things without using \'like\' or \'as\'\",\"A description of a single object without any comparison\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a metaphor as a comparison between two different things without using the words \'like\' or \'as\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is provided as an example of a metaphor in the text?\",\"options\":[\"He is as brave as a lion\",\"My classroom was a zoo\",\"She shines like a star\",\"Time flies like an arrow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Example 3 in the text explicitly states \'My classroom was a zoo\' as a metaphor.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What words must NOT be used when forming a metaphor?\",\"options\":[\"is, was\",\"he, she\",\"like, as\",\"a, the\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that metaphors are comparisons made without using the words \'like\' or \'as\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the example \'Time is money\', what is the text illustrating?\",\"options\":[\"A simile\",\"A metaphor\",\"A literal fact\",\"A funny emoji\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Time is money\' as example number 4 of a metaphor.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are the learners asked to use along with words to form sentences?\",\"options\":[\"Dictionaries\",\"Funny emojis\",\"Drawing tools\",\"Textbooks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The facilitator instructions suggest providing words and funny emojis to learners for sentence formation.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the facilitator expected to explain regarding similes and metaphors?\",\"options\":[\"The similarities only\",\"The history of the words\",\"The differences between them\",\"How to spell the words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs the facilitator to \'Explain the differences\' between simile and metaphor.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definition in the text, which of the following is a metaphor?\",\"options\":[\"The snow is like a white blanket\",\"The snow is as white as a blanket\",\"The snow is a white blanket\",\"The snow looks white\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A metaphor compares two things directly without \'like\' or \'as\', making \'The snow is a white blanket\' the correct choice.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a facilitator provides the word \'Cloud\' and a \'Cotton\' emoji, which sentence follows the metaphor pattern from the text?\",\"options\":[\"The cloud is cotton\",\"The cloud is like cotton\",\"The cloud is as soft as cotton\",\"The cloud looks like cotton\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Following the text\'s examples (e.g., \'He is a lion\'), a metaphor directly equates the two things.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'She is a shining star\' classified as a metaphor in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Because it uses the word \'is\' to compare a person to a star without using \'like\'\",\"Because it describes a girl who is literally a star in space\",\"Because it uses the word \'shining\' to describe her\",\"Because it is a very short sentence\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"It fits the definition of comparing two different things (a person and a star) without using \'like\' or \'as\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the facilitator providing \'other examples of simile\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To show that similes and metaphors are exactly the same\",\"To help learners understand the differences between the two figures of speech\",\"To replace metaphors with similes\",\"To make the lesson longer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests giving examples of both to explain their differences.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21774,32,6,'English','en','Stories on Strings','[\"Puppets are figures that can be moved by pulling strings or using fingers.\",\"They are used to tell stories, teach values and entertain people.\",\"India has many puppet traditions: Kathputli in Rajasthan, Bommalattam in Karnataka and Tamil Nadu, Tholu Bommalata in Andhra Pradesh, and tiny rod puppets in Odisha and Bengal.\",\"Tholu Bommalata creates shadow pictures on a white screen and is used to tell sacred stories like the Ramayana.\",\"Bommalattam puppets are large, carved, and used in temple festivals and village gatherings.\",\"Puppets can be made from various materials: leather, wood, paper, ice‑cream sticks, or even fingers.\",\"Making finger puppets involves drawing a face on a thumb or finger and adding clothes and names.\",\"Ice‑cream stick puppets are made by gluing a V‑shaped stick to paper shapes of body and face, then colouring them.\",\"Puppets help children learn good behaviour, kindness, bravery and truth through stories.\",\"They also bring blessings, joy, and harmony to the community.\",\"Puppets can be simple or elaborate; even a small puppet can create a big story.\",\"Puppets are a living tradition that continues to entertain children and adults.\",\"Puppets can be used in classroom activities to develop creativity and language skills.\",\"Puppets can be used to introduce new words and practice pronunciation.\",\"Puppets can be used to practice listening and speaking through dialogues.\",\"Puppets can be used to teach moral lessons in a fun way.\",\"Puppets can be used to show how stories are told in different regions of India.\",\"Puppets can be used to show the importance of tradition and culture.\",\"Puppets can be used to show how art and craft are connected.\",\"Puppets can be used to show the role of music and movement in storytelling.\",\"Puppets can be used to show how stories can be adapted to modern times.\",\"Puppets can be used to show how imagination can bring stories to life.\",\"Puppets can be used to show how stories can be shared with others.\",\"Puppets can be used to show how stories can be remembered for generations.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which parts of India are puppet traditions found according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only in the North and South\",\"Only in Rajasthan\",\"In every corner of the country\",\"Only in the West\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that puppet traditions are found in every corner of our country - North, South, East, and West.\",\"topic\":\"India\'s Puppet Traditions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is unique about each region\'s puppets?\",\"options\":[\"They all look exactly the same\",\"Each region has its own special style\",\"They all tell the same story\",\"They are all made by the same person\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that each region has its own special style of puppets that tells wonderful stories.\",\"topic\":\"India\'s Puppet Traditions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific state in the North is mentioned for its bright and dancing puppets?\",\"options\":[\"Maharashtra\",\"Rajasthan\",\"Gujarat\",\"Punjab\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions Rajasthan in the North for its Kathputli puppets.\",\"topic\":\"India\'s Puppet Traditions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the puppets found in Rajasthan?\",\"options\":[\"Kathputli\",\"Gombe\",\"Putul\",\"Bommalattam\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the puppets in Rajasthan as Kathputli puppets.\",\"topic\":\"India\'s Puppet Traditions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of characters are featured in the Kathputli puppet tales?\",\"options\":[\"Brave kings and clever queens\",\"Talking animals and birds\",\"Space explorers and aliens\",\"Modern doctors and engineers\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that Kathputli puppets perform tales of brave kings and clever queens.\",\"topic\":\"India\'s Puppet Traditions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the game described in the text, what must a learner do when the music stops while they are holding the ball?\",\"options\":[\"Start dancing like a puppet\",\"Pass the ball to the next person quickly\",\"Speak a funny dialogue as if the puppet is talking\",\"Sit down and stop playing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The activity instructions state the learner must speak any funny dialogue\\/sentence as if the puppet is talking.\",\"topic\":\"India\'s Puppet Traditions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text mention \'North, South, East and West\'?\",\"options\":[\"To show that puppets are only found in four cities\",\"To emphasize that puppet traditions are widespread across India\",\"To explain the directions for the ball game\",\"To describe the movement of the Kathputli puppets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The directions are mentioned to show that puppet traditions are found in every corner of the country.\",\"topic\":\"India\'s Puppet Traditions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which adjective is used in the text to describe the Kathputli puppets?\",\"options\":[\"Silent\",\"Heavy\",\"Dancing\",\"Ancient\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes them as \'bright and dancing Kathputli puppets\'.\",\"topic\":\"India\'s Puppet Traditions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is attached to the puppets to help the performer move them?\",\"options\":[\"Wooden sticks\",\"Thin strings\",\"Metal rods\",\"Thick ropes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration clearly shows thin white strings attached to the puppets\' hands and heads for manipulation.\",\"topic\":\"India\'s Puppet Traditions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/031_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, how many puppets are shown standing together in the row?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"By counting the distinct puppet figures in the illustration, there are five puppets shown.\",\"topic\":\"India\'s Puppet Traditions\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/031_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which states are traditionally famous for the Bommalattam style of puppetry?\",\"options\":[\"Andhra Pradesh and Kerala\",\"Karnataka and Tamil Nadu\",\"Maharashtra and Gujarat\",\"Odisha and West Bengal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that South states like Karnataka and Tamil Nadu are famous for Bommalattam puppets.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What material is used to make the Tholu Bommalata puppets of Andhra Pradesh?\",\"options\":[\"Carved wood\",\"Coloured cloth\",\"Shining leather\",\"Baked clay\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that in Andhra Pradesh, the puppets are made of shining leather.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why were Bommalattam puppets particularly effective for teaching moral values?\",\"options\":[\"Because they were very large in size\",\"Because they were only shown in temples\",\"Because they could move their hands, head, and eyes smoothly\",\"Because they were made by very famous artists\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that because the puppets could move their parts smoothly, they were used to teach moral values.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How are Tholu Bommalata puppets presented to the audience?\",\"options\":[\"As three-dimensional dolls on a wooden stage\",\"As magical shadow pictures on a white screen\",\"As puppets controlled by visible strings from above\",\"As giant statues carried through the village\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes Tholu Bommalata puppets as creating magical shadow pictures on a white screen.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a puppet show is being organized in a village in Karnataka to tell a story from the Mahabharata, which puppet type is most likely being used?\",\"options\":[\"Tholu Bommalata\",\"Bommalattam\",\"Leather shadow puppets\",\"Glove puppets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Karnataka is famous for Bommalattam, which is used to tell stories from the Mahabharata.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A community in Andhra Pradesh wants to organize a show to please village deities. According to the text, which puppet style would they choose?\",\"options\":[\"Bommalattam\",\"Wooden carved puppets\",\"Tholu Bommalata\",\"Local legend puppets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that shadow puppets (Tholu Bommalata) were believed to please village deities in Andhra Pradesh.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is a major difference between Bommalattam and Tholu Bommalata puppets?\",\"options\":[\"One is used for entertainment, the other is not\",\"One uses carved figures, while the other uses leather shadows\",\"One tells stories of the Ramayana, the other does not\",\"One is used in festivals, the other is used in schools\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Bommalattam puppets are described as carved, while Tholu Bommalata are leather shadow puppets.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What common purpose do both Bommalattam and Tholu Bommalata serve for their communities?\",\"options\":[\"They are used to sell leather and wood products\",\"They are used to teach important life lessons and values\",\"They are used to train people in classical dance\",\"They are used to celebrate modern historical events\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both styles are mentioned as tools to teach moral values, good behaviour, kindness, and truth.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text suggest that these puppet shows were considered more than just entertainment?\",\"options\":[\"Because they were very expensive to produce\",\"Because they were believed to bring blessings, joy, and harmony\",\"Because the performers were treated like kings\",\"Because the puppets were kept in museums after the show\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes beliefs that they brought blessings, joy, and harmony to the community.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which of these is NOT a lesson taught through Tholu Bommalata?\",\"options\":[\"Bravery\",\"Kindness\",\"Modern Science\",\"Good behaviour\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists good behaviour, kindness, bravery, and truth, but does not mention modern science.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the puppets represent characters from sacred stories. Based on the text, which state\'s tradition does this leather puppet style belong to?\",\"options\":[\"Tamil Nadu\",\"Karnataka\",\"Andhra Pradesh\",\"Maharashtra\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows leather puppets, which the text identifies as Tholu Bommalata from Andhra Pradesh.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/032_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what physical feature of the puppets allows for the \'expressive movements\' mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The bright colors used on the bodies\",\"The joints at the shoulders and elbows\",\"The large size of the puppet heads\",\"The bows held by the characters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows visible joints in the limbs, which allow the puppets to move expressively as described in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Puppets of the South\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/032_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In which states of India are these tiny rod puppets found?\",\"options\":[\"Maharashtra and Goa\",\"Odisha and Bengal\",\"Kerala and Tamil Nadu\",\"Punjab and Haryana\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions Odisha and Bengal as the locations for these rod puppets.\",\"topic\":\"Rod Puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the text describe the size of the rod puppets?\",\"options\":[\"Huge\",\"Giant\",\"Tiny\",\"Heavy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses the word \'tiny\' to describe the rod puppets.\",\"topic\":\"Rod Puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT an action performed by the rod puppets as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Slide\",\"Jump\",\"Fly\",\"Twist\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists slide, jump, and twist, but does not mention flying.\",\"topic\":\"Rod Puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of stories do these puppets teach the audience?\",\"options\":[\"Modern science stories\",\"Stories from India\'s rich culture\",\"Stories about space travel\",\"Stories from other countries\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states they teach us beautiful stories from India’s rich culture.\",\"topic\":\"Rod Puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to see a puppet show that feels like a \'fairytale come alive\', which puppets should they watch?\",\"options\":[\"Glove puppets\",\"Shadow puppets\",\"Rod puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"String puppets of Rajasthan\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says watching these specific rod puppets feels like seeing a fairytale come alive.\",\"topic\":\"Rod Puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, in what manner do the puppets move?\",\"options\":[\"In a scary way\",\"In funny ways\",\"In a very slow way\",\"In a boring way\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the puppets slide, jump, and twist in \'funny ways\'.\",\"topic\":\"Rod Puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Besides singing and dancing, what other two things do these puppets do?\",\"options\":[\"Sleep and eat\",\"Act and teach\",\"Run and hide\",\"Paint and draw\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says these puppets \'sing, dance, act and even teach us\'.\",\"topic\":\"Rod Puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main educational purpose of these puppets according to the passage?\",\"options\":[\"To scare children\",\"To sell toys\",\"To teach beautiful stories\",\"To win a race\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text highlights that the puppets \'teach us beautiful stories\'.\",\"topic\":\"Rod Puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A teacher uses a puppet to tell a story about Indian traditions. Based on the text, which puppet matches this description?\",\"options\":[\"A tiny rod puppet\",\"A large robot\",\"A movie character\",\"A plastic doll\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text describes tiny rod puppets that teach stories from India\'s culture.\",\"topic\":\"Rod Puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the author describe these puppets as \'wonderful\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are made of gold\",\"Because they can talk like humans\",\"Because they perform many actions and teach culture\",\"Because they are very expensive\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The author calls them wonderful because they sing, dance, act, and teach stories.\",\"topic\":\"Rod Puppets of Odisha and Bengal\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21775,32,6,'English','en','All About News','[\"News is a report of recent events that is published in newspapers, magazines or online.\",\"Rumour is an unverified piece of information that may or may not be true.\",\"News is usually written in a factual and objective style, while rumours are often unverified and may be exaggerated.\",\"Information can be spread through newspapers, television, radio, the internet and social media.\",\"A newspaper contains different sections such as local news, national news, sports, entertainment, and classifieds.\",\"A news article has a headline, a lead paragraph, body paragraphs and a dateline (date and place).\",\"The headline is written in bold letters to grab the reader’s attention and give a quick idea of the story.\",\"The lead paragraph gives the most important facts: who, what, when, where, why and how.\",\"Body paragraphs provide details, background and quotes from people involved.\",\"The dateline states the place and date of the news report.\",\"Simple past tense is used for actions that finished at a specific time in the past (e.g., yesterday, last week).\",\"In simple past tense we add –ed to regular verbs (play → played) and use irregular forms for irregular verbs (go → went).\",\"Past time words include yesterday, last night, last week, ago, etc.\",\"When writing a news article, start with a clear headline, then the lead, followed by body and conclusion.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where is Kanya Shala located according to the news report?\",\"options\":[\"Mumbai\",\"Chalisgaon\",\"Pune\",\"Nagpur\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'Kanya Shala Chalisgaon\' at the beginning of the report.\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"On which day of the week was Maharashtra Din celebrated at the school?\",\"options\":[\"Monday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Wednesday\",\"Friday\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the celebration was held \'on Wednesday to mark the formation of the state\'.\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What activity marked the beginning of the celebration?\",\"options\":[\"A speech by the Principal\",\"A pledge by the learners\",\"Singing of the Maharashtra Rajyageet\",\"Distribution of prizes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The celebration began with the singing of the Maharashtra Rajyageet.\'\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the celebration held on May 1st?\",\"options\":[\"It was the school\'s foundation day\",\"To mark the formation of the state of Maharashtra\",\"To celebrate the start of summer vacation\",\"To honor the senior teacher Mrs. Patil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the event was held \'to mark the formation of the state of Maharashtra\'.\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the teachers talk about during the programme?\",\"options\":[\"The importance of news reporting\",\"The history and culture of Maharashtra\",\"The rules of the school\",\"How to dress for functions\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that teachers \'spoke about the history and culture of Maharashtra in simple words\'.\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what made the programme look \'colourful and lively\'?\",\"options\":[\"The bright decorations in the hall\",\"The learners dressed in traditional Maharashtrian attire\",\"The use of colourful posters and charts\",\"The flowers brought by the Principal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that learners in traditional attire \'made the programme colourful and lively\'.\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to follow the Principal\'s advice, what should they aim to become?\",\"options\":[\"A famous singer\",\"A senior teacher\",\"A responsible citizen\",\"A news reporter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Principal \'motivated the learners to become responsible citizens\'.\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the report, which of these would be a part of the \'short speeches\' presented by learners?\",\"options\":[\"A talk on the history of Chalisgaon city\",\"A talk on Maharashtra and its great leaders\",\"A talk on how to write a newspaper\",\"A talk on the importance of sports\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says learners presented \'short speeches and poems on Maharashtra and its great leaders\'.\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which specific word is printed in bold to describe the way the school celebrated the day?\",\"options\":[\"Active\",\"Enthusiasm\",\"Formation\",\"Simple\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the image, the word \'enthusiasm\' is clearly printed in bold text in the first paragraph.\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/035_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the word \'attire\' is highlighted in bold. Based on the text around it, what does \'attire\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"The way students speak\",\"The songs students sing\",\"The clothes students wear\",\"The prizes students win\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'dressed in traditional Maharashtrian attire\', indicating it refers to clothing.\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/035_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What was the main purpose of the pledge taken at the end of the programme?\",\"options\":[\"To promise to respect Maharashtra\'s values and work for its development\",\"To promise to attend school every day on time\",\"To thank Mrs. Patil for her guidance\",\"To celebrate the formation of the state\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying the pledge was \'to respect Maharashtra\'s values and work sincerely for its development\'.\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who was responsible for guiding and encouraging the learners to participate confidently?\",\"options\":[\"The Principal\",\"Mrs. Patil\",\"The local citizens\",\"The news reporter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Mrs. Patil a senior teacher guided the learners and encouraged them to participate confidently.\'\",\"topic\":\"KANYA SHALA CELEBRATES MAHARASHTRA DIN\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'attire\' as given in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Food items\",\"Clothes\",\"School bags\",\"Books\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'attire\' as clothes.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, a person who can be trusted to behave well and sensibly is called:\",\"options\":[\"Enthusiastic\",\"Responsible\",\"Attired\",\"Learner\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'responsible\' as a person that you can trust to behave well and in a sensible way.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'enthusiasm\' mean according to the vocabulary list?\",\"options\":[\"A strong feeling of excitement or interest\",\"A type of school uniform\",\"A way of reporting news\",\"A person who behaves well\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines enthusiasm as a strong feeling of excitement or interest in something.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a specific element to be found in a news item according to activity \'c\'?\",\"options\":[\"Name of the printer\",\"Price of the paper\",\"Place of reporting\",\"Number of pages\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Activity \'c\' asks to find the Headline, Date, and Place of reporting from the news item.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the sequence of events, what did the teachers do during the celebration?\",\"options\":[\"They took a pledge\",\"They presented poems\",\"They explained the importance of the day\",\"They wrote the headline\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sequence of events mentions \'Teachers explained the importance of the day\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific day was celebrated according to the sentences provided for rearrangement?\",\"options\":[\"Independence Day\",\"Republic Day\",\"Maharashtra Din\",\"Children\'s Day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Maharashtra Din was celebrated\' in the list of sentences.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the learners do during the celebration according to the sequence list?\",\"options\":[\"They organized the whole programme\",\"They presented speeches and poems\",\"They interviewed the Principal\",\"They wrote the news report\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Learners presented speeches and poems\' as one of the activities.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'Maharashtra Din was celebrated\', which word is a Proper Noun?\",\"options\":[\"Was\",\"Celebrated\",\"Maharashtra\",\"Day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Activity \'g\' asks to find Proper Nouns; \'Maharashtra\' is a specific name of a state, making it a proper noun.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the action word (verb) from the following options based on the sequence of events in the text.\",\"options\":[\"Pledge\",\"Addressed\",\"Learners\",\"Speeches\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Activity \'g\' asks for action words; \'addressed\' is the action performed by the Principal.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a headline usually written in bold letters in a news report?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is the longest sentence\",\"To make it stand out and grab attention\",\"Because it is written by the Principal\",\"To save space on the paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Activity \'f\' asks to think about why headlines are bold; the standard reason is to draw the reader\'s attention.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If you were to arrange the events, which of these would likely happen after the Principal addresses the learners?\",\"options\":[\"The news is printed\",\"Learners present speeches and poems\",\"The date is decided\",\"The headline is chosen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the provided sequence, learners presenting speeches and poems is listed alongside the Principal\'s address as part of the celebration activities.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of an \'Adjective\' that could be found in the text\'s vocabulary definitions?\",\"options\":[\"Attire\",\"Responsible\",\"Pledge\",\"Organised\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Activity \'g\' asks for adjectives; \'responsible\' is a word describing a person, which is an adjective.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which tense is used for an action that ended at a specific time in the past?\",\"options\":[\"Simple Present Tense\",\"Simple Past Tense\",\"Future Tense\",\"Continuing Tense\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that we use simple past tense for action that ended at a specific time in the past.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT listed as a \'past word\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"yesterday\",\"last night\",\"tomorrow\",\"ago\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists yesterday, last night, last week, and ago as past words; tomorrow is not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first part of the news format mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Dateline\",\"Lead paragraph\",\"Headline\",\"Concluding paragraph\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Headline\' as the first item in the format of news.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, when do we use the Simple Past Tense?\",\"options\":[\"To talk about something happening today\",\"To talk about a completed action\",\"To talk about future plans\",\"To talk about things that never end\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states we use Simple Past Tense to talk about a completed action.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a sentence describes something that happened \'last week\', which tense should be used according to the rules provided?\",\"options\":[\"Simple Present Tense\",\"Simple Past Tense\",\"Future Tense\",\"Present Continuous Tense\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'last week\' as a past word used with the Simple Past Tense.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the news format, which paragraph comes immediately after the \'Lead paragraph\'?\",\"options\":[\"Headline\",\"Dateline\",\"Concluding paragraph\",\"Continuing paragraph\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The sequence provided is Headline, Dateline, Lead paragraph, then Continuing paragraph.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the Simple Present Tense is \'I play\', what is the Simple Past Tense form according to the examples?\",\"options\":[\"I playing\",\"I plays\",\"I played\",\"I will play\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'I play\' in Today (Present) becomes \'I played\' in Yesterday (Past).\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Change the sentence \'Sai studies\' into Simple Past Tense using the pattern in the text.\",\"options\":[\"Sai study\",\"Sai studied\",\"Sai studying\",\"Sai studies yesterday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'Sai studies\' as present and \'Sai studied\' as the corresponding past tense.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the examples of \'go\' and \'went\', what can be concluded about Simple Past Tense verbs?\",\"options\":[\"All verbs must end in -ed\",\"Verbs never change their spelling\",\"Some verbs change completely (like go to went)\",\"Verbs only change if the subject is \'I\'\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The example \'It goes\' becoming \'It went\' shows that not all past tense verbs simply add -ed.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following correctly pairs a \'Today\' action with its \'Yesterday\' action as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"We play - We goes\",\"He looks - He looked\",\"They go - They goed\",\"She looks - She look\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'He looks\' under Today and \'He looked\' under Yesterday.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the underlined past tense word used for the subject \'She\'?\",\"options\":[\"looks\",\"looked\",\"goes\",\"went\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the \'Yesterday\' column of the table, the word next to \'She\' is \'looked\'.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/037_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word from the \'Today\' column changes to \'went\' in the \'Yesterday\' column?\",\"options\":[\"play\",\"looks\",\"go\",\"studies\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'It goes\' and \'They go\' in the Today column correspond to \'went\' in the Yesterday column.\",\"topic\":\"Simple Past Tense\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/037_101.jpg\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21776,32,6,'English','en','Healthy Dessert : Millet Kheer of Kalahandi Tribals','[\"Millets are small, round grains used by many tribes for food.\",\"Suan Kheer is a sweet dessert made from foxtail millet (Suan Chaula).\",\"The recipe uses 0.5 kg millet, 2 L water, 100 g peanuts, 50 g fennel seeds, 0.5 kg jaggery, 100 g desiccated coconut.\",\"Jaggery is dissolved in water to make a sweet syrup before adding to millet.\",\"The mixture is simmered gently to keep it from boiling too hard.\",\"Adding ghee and a pinch of salt can improve taste.\",\"Millets are healthy because they are rich in fibre, protein and minerals.\",\"The word ‘boggles’ means something that is hard to understand or imagine.\",\"‘Repertoire’ means a collection of skills or items a person can do or use.\",\"‘Craving’ is a strong desire for something, especially food.\",\"‘Simmering’ is cooking in liquid that is almost boiling.\",\"‘Syrupy’ means thick and sticky like syrup.\",\"‘Sumptuous’ means very rich, luxurious or impressive.\",\"The recipe is an example of how traditional food can be both tasty and healthy.\",\"The book also talks about different types of sentences: assertive, imperative, interrogative, exclamatory, and descriptive.\",\"Students can practice by identifying sentence types and arranging cooking steps in order.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the name of the famous sweet dish prepared by the Kalahandi tribals?\",\"options\":[\"Suan Kheer\",\"Rice Kheer\",\"Millet Porridge\",\"Sugar Kheer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions the famous \'Suan Kheer\' as the sweet dish of the Kalahandi tribals.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'have a sweet tooth\' mean in the context of the passage?\",\"options\":[\"Having a tooth made of sugar\",\"Liking to eat sweet food\",\"Having a pain in the tooth\",\"Having white teeth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In English, \'having a sweet tooth\' is a common idiom meaning a person enjoys eating sweets.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of people adds to India\'s amazing repertoire of sweet dishes with \'Suan Kheer\'?\",\"options\":[\"Urban chefs\",\"Kalahandi tribals\",\"Foreign tourists\",\"School children\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Kalahandi tribals add to the country\'s repertoire with their famous dish.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what \'boggles the mind\' regarding Indian desserts?\",\"options\":[\"The high price of sweets\",\"The lack of healthy options\",\"The sheer variety across communities\",\"The difficulty in making them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the \'sheer variety of desserts across communities boggles the mind\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is looking for a \'healthy option\' for a dessert, which dish mentioned in the text would be suitable?\",\"options\":[\"Any Indian sweet\",\"Suan Kheer\",\"A sugar-free candy\",\"A plain fruit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically describes Suan Kheer as a \'healthy option\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text state that Suan Kheer has \'twin benefits\'?\",\"options\":[\"It is cheap and easy to cook\",\"It is served both hot and cold\",\"It satisfies sweet cravings and is healthy\",\"It uses two types of millets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains the twin benefits are satisfying cravings for a post-meal sweet and being a healthy option.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"When is Suan Kheer typically desired, according to the text\'s mention of cravings?\",\"options\":[\"Before breakfast\",\"During lunch\",\"Post-meal\",\"Early morning\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions it satisfies cravings for a \'post-meal sweet\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'amazing repertoire of sweet dishes\', what does the word \'repertoire\' most likely mean?\",\"options\":[\"A secret recipe\",\"A collection or range\",\"A type of cooking pot\",\"A specific tribe\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Repertoire refers to the wide range or collection of dishes available in the country.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A nutritionist wants to recommend a traditional dessert that isn\'t just \'empty calories\'. Based on the text, why would they choose Suan Kheer?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is famous in Kalahandi\",\"Because it is a healthy option while being sweet\",\"Because it is made by tribals\",\"Because it boggles the mind\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text highlights that it is a healthy option, making it suitable for nutritional recommendations.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the introduction, how do the Kalahandi tribals compare to other Indian communities regarding sweets?\",\"options\":[\"They do not like sweets at all\",\"They only eat healthy food and no sweets\",\"They are \'no different\' and also enjoy a variety of sweets\",\"They only eat Suan Kheer and nothing else\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Kalahandi tribals are no different\' from most Indians who have a sweet tooth.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific Indian term used for millets in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Chota anaaj\",\"Mota anaaj\",\"Meetha anaaj\",\"Safed anaaj\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the focus in India is on the \'mota anaaj\'.\",\"topic\":\"Millets and Tribal Cuisine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two specific tribes are mentioned as having learned the Suan Kheer recipe?\",\"options\":[\"Bhil and Warli\",\"Gonds and Kondhs\",\"Santhal and Munda\",\"Naga and Kuki\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions Gonds, Kondhs and some other tribes.\",\"topic\":\"Millets and Tribal Cuisine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is Suan Kheer a good example of?\",\"options\":[\"A bitter medicinal drink\",\"A modern fast food item\",\"Eating healthy that also tastes well\",\"A spicy main course dish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states Suan Kheer serves as one good example of eating healthy that also tastes well.\",\"topic\":\"Millets and Tribal Cuisine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the headquarters of the Kalahandi district located?\",\"options\":[\"Bhubaneswar\",\"Bhawanipatna\",\"DAPTA\",\"Gond\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies Bhawanipatna as the Kalahandi district headquarters.\",\"topic\":\"Millets and Tribal Cuisine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the acronym DAPTA stand for in the context of the text?\",\"options\":[\"Department of Agriculture and Tribal Affairs\",\"Development Agency for Poor and Tribal Awakening\",\"District Association for People and Tribal Arts\",\"Division of Ancient Plants and Tribal Agriculture\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines DAPTA as the Development Agency for Poor and Tribal Awakening.\",\"topic\":\"Millets and Tribal Cuisine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to study tribal food habits, which group should they look at according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Urban populations\",\"International chefs\",\"Tribal communities like Gonds and Kondhs\",\"Modern food scientists\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that millets have always been a part of tribal cuisine and food habits.\",\"topic\":\"Millets and Tribal Cuisine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the recipe for Suan Kheer being highlighted currently?\",\"options\":[\"Because the world is celebrating the International Year of Millets\",\"Because it is the only dessert in India\",\"Because it was recently invented by scientists\",\"Because it is a very expensive dish\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text links the focus on these recipes to the celebration of the International Year of Millets.\",\"topic\":\"Millets and Tribal Cuisine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Millets have \'always been a part of\' which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"Only modern restaurants\",\"Tribal cuisine and food habits\",\"Western breakfast cereals\",\"Chemical food processing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The opening sentence states millets have always been a part of tribal cuisine and food habits.\",\"topic\":\"Millets and Tribal Cuisine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, if you are visiting the DAPTA office, in which district would you be?\",\"options\":[\"Gond district\",\"Kondh district\",\"Kalahandi district\",\"Mota district\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions DAPTA is at Bhawanipatna, the Kalahandi district headquarters.\",\"topic\":\"Millets and Tribal Cuisine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What role did DAPTA play for the Gonds and Kondhs according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"It sold them expensive seeds\",\"It provided programs to teach them recipes like Suan Kheer\",\"It prohibited them from eating \'mota anaaj\'\",\"It moved them to the district headquarters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the tribes learned the recipe from programmes run by DAPTA.\",\"topic\":\"Millets and Tribal Cuisine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the English name for \'Suan Chaula\' as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Pearl millet\",\"Finger millet\",\"Foxtail millet\",\"Barnyard millet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'Suan Chaula (foxtail millet)\'.\",\"topic\":\"Recipe for Suan Kheer\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How much water is required to boil half a kilo of Suan Chaula?\",\"options\":[\"1 litre\",\"2 litres\",\"3 litres\",\"500 ml\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The recipe states that half a kilo of Suan Chaula is boiled in 2 litres of water.\",\"topic\":\"Recipe for Suan Kheer\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it important to stir the millet continuously while boiling?\",\"options\":[\"To make it sweet\",\"To change its color\",\"To avoid lumps\",\"To increase the quantity\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'stirring continuously to avoid lumps\'.\",\"topic\":\"Recipe for Suan Kheer\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you use 100 gm of powdered peanuts (moongfali), how much saunf (fennel seeds) should you add?\",\"options\":[\"100 gm\",\"200 gm\",\"50 gm\",\"25 gm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states to use \'half that amount\' of saunf compared to 100 gm of peanuts.\",\"topic\":\"Recipe for Suan Kheer\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What must be done to the gur (jaggery) before it is added to the boiling millet?\",\"options\":[\"It should be roasted\",\"It should be dissolved in water and filtered\",\"It should be powdered and kept dry\",\"It should be mixed with peanuts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'Half a kilo of gur (jaggery) is dissolved in about a liter of water and then filtered.\'\",\"topic\":\"Recipe for Suan Kheer\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which ingredient is added to the kheer just before it is left to simmer?\",\"options\":[\"Desiccated coconut\",\"Fennel seeds\",\"Raw millet\",\"Cold water\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions adding 100 gm of desiccated coconut and then leaving the kheer to simmer.\",\"topic\":\"Recipe for Suan Kheer\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the recipe, in what order should the ingredients be added to the boiling millet?\",\"options\":[\"Coconut first, then jaggery\",\"Peanut mixture first, then jaggery\",\"Jaggery first, then the peanut mixture\",\"Salt first, then the millet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'The jaggery is slowly added to the boiling millet and then the peanut mixture.\'\",\"topic\":\"Recipe for Suan Kheer\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final texture and quality of the Suan Kheer described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Dry and crunchy\",\"Syrupy and sumptuous\",\"Thick and salty\",\"Thin and watery\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the result as a \'syrupy, sumptuous dessert\'.\",\"topic\":\"Recipe for Suan Kheer\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which two ingredients are mentioned as optional additions to enhance the taste?\",\"options\":[\"Sugar and milk\",\"Oil and pepper\",\"Ghee and salt\",\"Honey and ginger\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Many people like to add some ghee and salt to the sweet dish to enhance the taste.\'\",\"topic\":\"Recipe for Suan Kheer\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which ingredient serves as the primary sweetener in this tribal recipe?\",\"options\":[\"Saunf\",\"Gur\",\"Moongfali\",\"Coconut\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Gur (jaggery) is the ingredient used to provide the sweet taste in the kheer.\",\"topic\":\"Recipe for Suan Kheer\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Word Basket, what are \'millets\'?\",\"options\":[\"Grains used as food for people or birds\",\"A type of thick and sticky syrup\",\"Expensive and impressive feasts\",\"Dried fruits used in cooking\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines millets as grains used as food for people or birds.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'craving\'?\",\"options\":[\"A feeling of being full\",\"A strong desire for something\",\"A way of cooking gently\",\"A complex situation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines craving as a strong desire for something.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The term \'repertoire\' refers to:\",\"options\":[\"A type of grain\",\"All the things a person is able to do\",\"A very expensive feast\",\"A liquid that is almost boiling\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Repertoire is defined as all the things that a person is able to do.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a situation \'boggles the mind\', it is:\",\"options\":[\"Very easy to explain\",\"Hard to imagine or understand\",\"A simple daily routine\",\"A type of dried food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes \'boggles the mind\' as an unusual or complex situation that is hard to imagine or understand.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does it mean when food is \'desiccated\'?\",\"options\":[\"It is cooked in a thick syrup\",\"It is dried in order to keep it for a long time\",\"It is served at a lavish feast\",\"It is boiling rapidly on a stove\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Desiccated means food dried in order to keep it for a long time.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes cooking gently in a liquid that is almost boiling?\",\"options\":[\"Sumptuous\",\"Simmering\",\"Syrupy\",\"Desiccated\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Simmering is defined as cooking gently in a liquid that is almost boiling.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a tribal feast is described as \'sumptuous\', it is:\",\"options\":[\"Very expensive and impressive\",\"Small and simple\",\"Hard to understand\",\"Dried for long storage\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Sumptuous means very expensive and impressive, lavish, or a feast.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word would you use to describe a liquid that is thick and sticky?\",\"options\":[\"Simmering\",\"Desiccated\",\"Syrupy\",\"Millet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Syrupy is defined as something thick and sticky like syrup.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definition of \'desiccated\', what is the primary purpose of drying the food?\",\"options\":[\"To make it syrupy\",\"To keep it for a long time\",\"To make it simmer faster\",\"To make it boggle the mind\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The definition 