u happy?\",\"Don\'t shout.\",\"Today is Monday.\",\"What a lovely flower!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Don\'t shout\' is listed as an example of an order\\/request under Imperative Sentences.\",\"topic\":\"Types of Sentences\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does an Exclamatory Sentence show?\",\"options\":[\"A request\",\"Information\",\"Strong feeling\",\"A question\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that Exclamatory Sentences show strong feeling.\",\"topic\":\"Types of Sentences\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you say \'Please, help me\', which category does it fall into?\",\"options\":[\"Imperative Sentences\",\"Assertive Sentences\",\"Interrogative Sentences\",\"Exclamatory Sentences\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Requests like \'Please, help me\' are categorized as Imperative Sentences in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Types of Sentences\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following sentences is an Interrogative Sentence?\",\"options\":[\"Open your book.\",\"How tall the building is!\",\"Where do you live?\",\"This is not my classroom.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Where do you live?\' is an example of asking something, which is an Interrogative Sentence.\",\"topic\":\"Types of Sentences\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the examples provided, how many total types of sentences are described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by stating, \'These are four types of sentences.\'\",\"topic\":\"Types of Sentences\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'Wow! It is raining!\' classified as an Exclamatory Sentence in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Because it gives information about the weather.\",\"Because it shows a strong feeling.\",\"Because it asks about the rain.\",\"Because it gives an order to the rain.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text classifies such sentences as Exclamatory because they show strong feeling.\",\"topic\":\"Types of Sentences\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first thing the facilitator is asked to collect for the learners?\",\"options\":[\"Different types of recipes\",\"A variety of millets\",\"Pictures of Kalahandi tribals\",\"Samples of kheer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly tells the facilitator to \'Collect a variety of millets.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these features are learners asked to write about after seeing the millets?\",\"options\":[\"Price and weight\",\"Taste and smell\",\"Colour and size\",\"Origin and history\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that learners should write about their colour, size, appearance, and importance.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how should learners write about the importance of millets?\",\"options\":[\"In great detail\",\"Briefly\",\"Using diagrams\",\"In a long essay\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that learners should write about the importance \'briefly\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides colour and size, what other physical characteristic should learners describe?\",\"options\":[\"Appearance\",\"Hardness\",\"Nutritional value\",\"Moisture content\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'appearance\' as one of the things learners should write about.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the facilitator\'s role regarding grammar in this topic?\",\"options\":[\"To teach the history of languages\",\"To motivate learners to find examples of sentence types\",\"To correct spelling mistakes in recipes\",\"To explain the meaning of tribal words\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'Motivate learners to find more examples of types of sentences.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is observing the physical look of a millet grain, which category from the text are they fulfilling?\",\"options\":[\"Importance\",\"Appearance\",\"Sentence types\",\"Facilitation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Observing the physical look corresponds to describing the \'appearance\' mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A teacher shows learners Ragi, Bajra, and Jowar. What should the learners do next according to the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Cook a dessert\",\"Find sentence types in the textbook\",\"Write about their features and importance\",\"Interview the Kalahandi tribals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions state that after showing millets, learners should write about their colour, size, appearance, and importance.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity mentioned in the text focuses on language skills rather than observation?\",\"options\":[\"Collecting millets\",\"Describing the size of grains\",\"Finding examples of types of sentences\",\"Writing about the colour of millets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Finding examples of types of sentences is a linguistic activity, while the others are observational.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT a specific point learners are asked to write about millets?\",\"options\":[\"Colour\",\"Size\",\"Cooking method\",\"Importance\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists colour, size, appearance, and importance, but does not mention the cooking method.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To follow the facilitator\'s instructions, what should a student look for in their reading material?\",\"options\":[\"Different types of sentences\",\"Pictures of millets\",\"Names of tribal leaders\",\"Prices of grains\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to find more examples of types of sentences.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21777,32,6,'English','en','The Plight of the Shy','[\"- A son‑in‑law is the husband of your sister or brother.\",\"- A daughter‑in‑law is the wife of your sister or brother.\",\"- The mother‑in‑law is your spouse’s mother.\",\"- The father‑in‑law is your spouse’s father.\",\"- A shy son‑in‑law may feel nervous around his in‑laws.\",\"- In the story the son‑in‑law was shy and did not want to eat the dish at dinner.\",\"- He tried to hide the sticky liquid by covering himself with cotton and hiding among sheep.\",\"- The thief thought the son‑in‑law was a sheep and lifted him, but the son‑in‑law asked to be put down gently and escaped.\",\"- Past tense of verbs: serve‑served, try‑tried, carry‑carried, steal‑stole, refuse‑refused, smear‑smudged, creep‑crept, stick‑stuck.\",\"- Long vowels: \\/iː\\/ in “see”, \\/ɑː\\/ in “car”, \\/ɔː\\/ in “saw”, \\/uː\\/ in “moon”, \\/ɜː\\/ in “bird”.\",\"- Opposites: light‑dark, loudly‑softly, bold‑timid, few‑many, low‑high, reject‑accept, yes‑no, come‑go, over‑under.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the introductory section, what is the relation of \'my sister\'s son\' to me?\",\"options\":[\"Nephew\",\"Niece\",\"Cousin\",\"Uncle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In family relations, a sister\'s son is referred to as a nephew.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why had the man gone to his parents-in-law\'s home?\",\"options\":[\"To attend a festival\",\"To bring his wife back from her short visit\",\"To learn how to cook a new dish\",\"To meet his sister\'s husband\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the man went to bring his wife from her parents\' home where she had gone for a short visit.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the two men doing?\",\"options\":[\"They are cooking a meal together.\",\"They are serving food to guests.\",\"They are sitting on a mat and having a meal.\",\"They are cleaning the floor after dinner.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows two men sitting cross-legged on a mat with plates of food in front of them.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/041_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What gesture did the man make to suggest he did not want the meal served by his mother-in-law?\",\"options\":[\"He shook his head \'no\'.\",\"He put his hand over his plate.\",\"He stood up and left the room.\",\"He told her he was not hungry.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the man felt shy and put his hand over his plate to suggest he did not want the food.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the man realize that the dish was actually very tasty?\",\"options\":[\"His wife told him it was delicious.\",\"He smelled the aroma from the kitchen.\",\"He accidentally licked drops that fell on his hand.\",\"He watched his father-in-law enjoy the meal.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says a few drops fell on his hand, he licked them away, and found the dish tasty.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a woman is the wife of your brother, she is your:\",\"options\":[\"Sister-in-law\",\"Daughter-in-law\",\"Niece\",\"Cousin\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Based on the relationship definitions in the text, a brother\'s wife is a sister-in-law.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the dish not brought in front of the man a second time?\",\"options\":[\"The pot was empty.\",\"His mother-in-law forgot about him.\",\"He had refused it the first time.\",\"The dish was too hot to serve again.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that since he had refused it the first time, it was not brought back to him.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where is the man reaching for the pot?\",\"options\":[\"Inside a low kitchen cabinet\",\"On top of a table in the hall\",\"In the attic or a high storage area\",\"Underneath a wooden bed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The image shows the man reaching for a pot placed high up, which corresponds to the \'attic\' mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/041_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how did men in \'olden days\' compare to women regarding their in-laws?\",\"options\":[\"Men were much bolder than women.\",\"Men were as shy of their parents-in-law as women were.\",\"Men never visited their parents-in-law.\",\"Men were responsible for serving the meals.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that in olden days, men were as shy of their parents-in-law as women were of their in-laws.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text refers to a space or room just below the roof of a house, often used for storing things?\",\"options\":[\"Dinner\",\"Attic\",\"Pot\",\"Visit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The wife tells the man to go to the \'attic\' where the pot is kept.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the main conflict the man faced during the dinner?\",\"options\":[\"He did not like the food his mother-in-law cooked.\",\"He was too shy to ask for food he actually wanted.\",\"He had a fight with his wife at the table.\",\"He forgot to bring a gift for his in-laws.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The man\'s \'plight\' is that his shyness prevented him from accepting or asking for the tasty food he desired.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What can be inferred about the man\'s behavior at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"He decided to stay hungry all night.\",\"He overcame his shyness to talk to his wife about his desire.\",\"He asked his mother-in-law for the recipe.\",\"He left the house immediately without his wife.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that although he was shy at dinner, he eventually told his wife about his desire to eat the dish at night.\",\"topic\":\"The Plight of the Shy Son-In-Law\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"At what time did the man creep up to the attic?\",\"options\":[\"At noon\",\"At midnight\",\"In the early morning\",\"At sunset\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the man crept up to the attic at midnight.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the man find the heap of cotton?\",\"options\":[\"In the kitchen\",\"Outside the house\",\"Nearby in the attic\",\"In his bedroom\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he suddenly saw a heap of cotton nearby while he was in the attic.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'in a fix\' mean as used in the passage?\",\"options\":[\"To repair a broken pot\",\"In a difficult situation\",\"Standing in a fixed spot\",\"Feeling very happy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, being \'in a fix\' describes the man\'s trouble after the liquid spilled on him.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the man try to use the cotton initially?\",\"options\":[\"To make a new shirt\",\"To hide the broken pieces of the pot\",\"To wipe off the sticky liquid\",\"To keep himself warm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The man thought he could wipe off the liquid with the cotton.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is happening to the liquid in the pot?\",\"options\":[\"It is being poured carefully into a glass\",\"It is spilling all over the man\'s head and clothes\",\"It is being stored safely on a shelf\",\"It is being mixed with cotton\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the pot slipping and the liquid falling onto the man.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/042_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, what is the man\'s immediate reaction as the pot slips?\",\"options\":[\"He is laughing at the mess\",\"He is sleeping soundly\",\"He is reaching out his hand as the pot falls\",\"He is already washing his clothes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the man with his hand raised and eyes squinted as the accident occurs.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/042_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What happened when the man tried to wipe the liquid with the cotton?\",\"options\":[\"The liquid was cleaned perfectly\",\"The cotton turned into liquid\",\"All the cotton stuck to his clothes\",\"The cotton caught fire\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says when he tried to wipe it, all the cotton stuck to his clothes because the liquid was sticky.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the liquid had not been sticky, how would the man\'s plan to use the cotton have changed?\",\"options\":[\"The cotton would have still stuck to him\",\"He would have been able to wipe the liquid off successfully\",\"He would have needed more cotton\",\"The pot would not have broken\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The cotton stuck because the liquid was sticky; if it wasn\'t, the cotton would have functioned as a normal wiper.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the man\'s main concern when he decided he needed a bath?\",\"options\":[\"Finding enough soap\",\"Doing it without anyone noticing him\",\"Finding a bigger pot\",\"Cleaning the attic floor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks \'But how could he do so with no one noticing?\', showing his concern for secrecy.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the man stick cotton all over his body and head?\",\"options\":[\"To stay warm during the night\",\"To look like a woolly creature as a disguise\",\"To dry the liquid faster\",\"Because he ran out of clothes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He did this so he looked like a woolly creature to move out of the house unnoticed.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the liquid in the pot based on the events?\",\"options\":[\"Watery\",\"Sticky\",\"Dry\",\"Invisible\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly describes the liquid as \'sticky\' because it made the cotton stick to his clothes.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the man\'s actions, what can we conclude about his character in this incident?\",\"options\":[\"He is very brave and loud\",\"He is trying to be secretive and clever\",\"He is a professional cleaner\",\"He does not care if people see him\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"His actions of creeping at midnight and disguising himself show he is trying to be secretive.\",\"topic\":\"The Incident in the Attic\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the son-in-law hide himself?\",\"options\":[\"In a river\",\"Amongst a herd of sheep\",\"In his in-laws\' house\",\"Behind a large tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states he went to the pen and hid himself amongst the sheep.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"At what time did the son-in-law usually go to the river for a bath?\",\"options\":[\"At midnight\",\"Just before day-break\",\"After sunset\",\"In the afternoon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he would go to the river just before day-break.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the thief\'s specific goal when he entered the pen?\",\"options\":[\"To count the sheep\",\"To steal the smallest sheep\",\"To steal the heaviest sheep\",\"To find the son-in-law\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the thief naturally wanted the heaviest one.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the thief try to identify the heaviest sheep?\",\"options\":[\"By looking at their size\",\"By feeding them\",\"By lifting each sheep one by one\",\"By asking the son-in-law\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states he lifted each sheep one by one to find the heaviest.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the thief carry the son-in-law away?\",\"options\":[\"He knew it was a human\",\"He thought the son-in-law was a sheep\",\"He wanted to kidnap him\",\"The son-in-law asked for a ride\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains the thief lifted the son-in-law, \'who he thought was a sheep\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What caused the thief to get tired?\",\"options\":[\"Lifting all the sheep\",\"Running away from the pen\",\"Walking some distance while carrying the weight\",\"Having a bath in the river\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says after walking some distance, the thief got tired.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the son-in-law speak to the thief?\",\"options\":[\"To scare the thief away\",\"Because he thought the thief would throw him down\",\"To ask for directions\",\"To tell the thief he was not a sheep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Thinking that the thief would throw him down, the son-in-law said...\'\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the thief do immediately after the son-in-law spoke?\",\"options\":[\"He apologized to the man\",\"He put him down gently\",\"He threw him down and ran away\",\"He carried him back to the pen\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the thief got so scared that he threw him down and ran away.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the text refers to the enclosed area where the sheep were kept?\",\"options\":[\"Herd\",\"Pen\",\"Ground\",\"River\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he went to the \'pen\' to hide amongst the sheep.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, why was the thief\'s plan unsuccessful?\",\"options\":[\"He was not strong enough to carry a sheep\",\"He was frightened by the unexpected voice of his \'prey\'\",\"The in-laws caught him in the pen\",\"The sheep were too light for him\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The thief ran away because he got scared when the person he thought was a sheep spoke.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What can be inferred about the setting when the thief arrived?\",\"options\":[\"It was broad daylight\",\"It was dark or nighttime\",\"It was raining heavily\",\"It was early afternoon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'on that particular night\' and \'just before day-break\', implying it was dark.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes the thief\'s reaction at the end of the passage?\",\"options\":[\"Greedy\",\"Brave\",\"Terrified\",\"Angry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the thief \'got so scared\' that he ran away.\",\"topic\":\"The Thief and the Sheep\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'smeared\' as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"Spread a sticky substance across something\",\"A small living thing\",\"To have or own something\",\"Doing things in a quiet, careful way\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'smeared\' as spreading a sticky substance across something.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is a \'creature\'?\",\"options\":[\"A sticky substance\",\"Any small living thing\",\"A way of owning things\",\"A type of long vowel\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'creature\' as any small living thing.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why are long vowels often referred to as \'alphabet sounds\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are the first letters of the alphabet\",\"Because they sound like the name of the letter itself\",\"Because they are only used in long words\",\"Because they are written in capital letters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Quick tip\' states long vowels are called alphabet sounds because they sound like the name of the letter.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'Quick tip\', which letter does the sound in the word \'home\' (\\/əʊ\\/) sound like?\",\"options\":[\"Letter A\",\"Letter E\",\"Letter O\",\"Letter U\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that home (\\/əʊ\\/) sounds like the letter O.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which IPA sound is associated with the example words \'moon\', \'flute\', \'new\', and \'blue\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/i:\\/\",\"\\/u:\\/\",\"\\/a:\\/\",\"\\/ɜ:\\/\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows that \'moon\', \'flute\', \'new\', and \'blue\' are examples of the \\/u:\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/045_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the table, which word is an example of the \\/a:\\/ sound?\",\"options\":[\"Field\",\"Calm\",\"Door\",\"Learn\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'calm\' as an example for the \\/a:\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these letter combinations is commonly used to produce the \\/ɜ:\\/ sound?\",\"options\":[\"ee, ea, ie\",\"aw, au, oor\",\"ir, ur, er\",\"oo, ew, ue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows that \'ir, ur, er, ear\' are common letters for the \\/ɜ:\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a word contains the letters \'ee\' or \'ie\' as in \'see\' or \'field\', what is its IPA sound sound according to the table?\",\"options\":[\"\\/i:\\/\",\"\\/a:\\/\",\"\\/ɔ:\\/\",\"\\/u:\\/\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'ee\' and \'ie\' under the \\/i:\\/ sound category.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many syllables is the word \'appreciatively\' broken into?\",\"options\":[\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\",\"Seven\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows \'ap\\/pre\\/ci\\/a\\/tive\\/ly\', which consists of six syllables.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/045_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which sound is represented by the common letters \'aw\', \'au\', \'oor\', and \'ore\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/a:\\/\",\"\\/ɔ:\\/\",\"\\/u:\\/\",\"\\/ɜ:\\/\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table identifies \\/ɔ:\\/ as the sound for letters like aw, au, oor, and ore.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the patterns in the table, which word would most likely contain the \\/ɜ:\\/ sound?\",\"options\":[\"Father\",\"Bird\",\"Eat\",\"More\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'bird\' as an example of the \\/ɜ:\\/ sound due to the \'ir\' letters.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the syllable divisions in the text, which word is divided into the most parts?\",\"options\":[\"in\\/di\\/vid\\/u\\/al\\/i\\/za\\/tion\",\"re\\/or\\/gan\\/i\\/za\\/tion\\/al\",\"ap\\/pre\\/ci\\/a\\/tive\\/ly\",\"u\\/ni\\/ver\\/si\\/ty\\/ed\\/u\\/ca\\/tion\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Comparing the divisions, \'u\\/ni\\/ver\\/si\\/ty\\/ed\\/u\\/ca\\/tion\' has 9 syllables, which is more than the others listed in the options.\",\"topic\":\"Phonetics Awareness\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21778,32,6,'English','en','The World of Geometry','[\"- Geometry is the study of shapes and space.\",\"- A line is straight and has no thickness.\",\"- Two lines that meet form an angle.\",\"- Three lines that meet at a point form a triangle.\",\"- A triangle has three equal sides and three equal angles in this chapter.\",\"- A square has four equal sides and four right angles.\",\"- A pentagon has five equal sides and five angles.\",\"- A hexagon has six equal sides and six angles.\",\"- A heptagon has seven equal sides and seven angles.\",\"- An octagon has eight equal sides and eight angles.\",\"- A nonagon has nine equal sides and nine angles.\",\"- A decagon has ten equal sides and ten angles.\",\"- Symmetry means parts of a shape match each other when folded or reflected.\",\"- Adding one more line to a shape can change it into a new shape.\",\"- The poem shows how lines join to create different polygons.\",\"- Geometry helps us see patterns in everyday objects.\",\"- Shapes can be drawn with sticks, paper, or by using a ruler.\",\"- Understanding shapes helps in building and designing things.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the poet of the poem \'The World of Geometry\'?\",\"options\":[\"Ruhee Parlekar\",\"Rabindranath Tagore\",\"Sarojini Naidu\",\"R. K. Narayan\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The name of the poet, Ruhee Parlekar, is mentioned at the end of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what is formed when two lines join together after going out to dine?\",\"options\":[\"A square\",\"A triangle\",\"An angle\",\"A circle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'And when they were back, They formed an angle.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many lines in total are needed to form a triangle according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Two lines\",\"Three lines\",\"Four lines\",\"Five lines\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says the lines of the angle called a \'third one\' to form a triangle.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When a fourth line joins the triangle, which shape is created?\",\"options\":[\"A rectangle\",\"A pentagon\",\"A hexagon\",\"A square\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'A fourth line came in... And when it joined over, It was a square!\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a hexagon invites one more line to join it, what will the new shape be called based on the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Heptagon\",\"Octagon\",\"Nonagon\",\"Decagon\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem lists the shapes born as more lines are added, starting with Heptagon after Hexagon.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the progression of shapes in the poem, how many lines would a \'decagon\' have?\",\"options\":[\"8 lines\",\"9 lines\",\"10 lines\",\"12 lines\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem follows a numerical progression of sides; a decagon is the final shape in the sequence (10 sides).\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned in the last stanza as a component of the poetry on Geometry?\",\"options\":[\"Lines\",\"Shapes\",\"Symmetry\",\"Colors\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The last stanza mentions lines, shapes, and symmetry, but not colors.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How did the first line feel at the very beginning of the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Perfectly fine\",\"Very lonely\",\"Extremely sad\",\"Quite angry\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first stanza says, \'There was once a line, Who was perfectly fine.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which shape from the poem is depicted?\",\"options\":[\"A square\",\"A pentagon\",\"A hexagon\",\"A triangle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a five-sided shape, which the poem identifies as a pentagon.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/047_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many lines have joined together to form this specific shape?\",\"options\":[\"4 lines\",\"5 lines\",\"6 lines\",\"7 lines\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"By counting the sides of the shape in the image, we find there are 5 lines.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/047_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the lines of the angle decide to call a third line?\",\"options\":[\"Because they wanted to grow\",\"Because they were hungry\",\"Because they wanted to walk\",\"Because they were tired\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'We want to grow, Said the lines of the angle, Let\'s call a third one.\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which shape is mentioned immediately after the \'octagon\' in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Heptagon\",\"Nonagon\",\"Decagon\",\"Hexagon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem lists them as \'Heptagon, octagon, nonagon, And finally a decagon!\'\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many straight and equal sides does a pentagon have according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\",\"Seven\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a pentagon as a shape that has five straight and equal sides.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a flat shape with six straight sides called?\",\"options\":[\"Pentagon\",\"Hexagon\",\"Heptagon\",\"Octagon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A hexagon is defined in the text as a flat shape with six straight sides.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which shape is described as having seven sides?\",\"options\":[\"Hexagon\",\"Heptagon\",\"Octagon\",\"Nonagon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a heptagon is a flat shape with seven sides.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the term \'symmetry\' mean in geometry?\",\"options\":[\"Having ten straight sides\",\"Having parts that match each other\",\"Having only straight lines\",\"A shape with five angles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Symmetry is defined as the quality of having parts that match each other.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a shape is a decagon, how many straight sides does it have?\",\"options\":[\"Eight\",\"Nine\",\"Ten\",\"Seven\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a decagon is a flat shape with ten straight sides.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definitions provided, which shape has the highest number of sides?\",\"options\":[\"Octagon\",\"Nonagon\",\"Decagon\",\"Heptagon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A decagon has 10 sides, which is more than the octagon (8), nonagon (9), or heptagon (7).\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you draw a flat shape with exactly nine straight sides, what should you name it?\",\"options\":[\"Octagon\",\"Nonagon\",\"Decagon\",\"Hexagon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A nonagon is defined as a flat shape with nine straight sides.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student cuts a paper shape and finds that the left half matches the right half perfectly. Which word describes this quality?\",\"options\":[\"Pentagon\",\"Symmetry\",\"Octagon\",\"Decagon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Symmetry is the quality of having parts that match each other.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these shapes has exactly two more sides than a hexagon?\",\"options\":[\"Heptagon\",\"Octagon\",\"Nonagon\",\"Decagon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A hexagon has 6 sides and an octagon has 8 sides; 8 is two more than 6.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does a pentagon differ from a hexagon according to their definitions?\",\"options\":[\"A pentagon has one more side than a hexagon\",\"A pentagon has one less side than a hexagon\",\"A pentagon has two more sides than a hexagon\",\"A pentagon has no straight sides\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A pentagon has 5 sides and a hexagon has 6 sides, so a pentagon has one less side.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these materials is NOT mentioned in the text for making a wall-hanging?\",\"options\":[\"Coloured papers\",\"Glitter pens\",\"Scissors\",\"Glue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists coloured papers, scissors, glue, and thread as the materials needed.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step in the process of preparing a wall-hanging?\",\"options\":[\"Cut the shapes carefully\",\"Draw different geometrical shapes\",\"Take coloured papers\",\"Decorate the shapes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 1 in the text is \'Take coloured papers\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'Fun with shapes\' activity, how many triangles should be formed by moving the sticks?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'move any three sticks and make five triangles\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Rangoli activity, which of these can be used along with shapes like squares and triangles?\",\"options\":[\"Straight and curved lines\",\"Only straight lines\",\"3D models\",\"Paint brushes\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions using triangles, rectangles, squares, straight lines, and curved lines for the Rangoli.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should be done immediately after cutting the geometrical shapes?\",\"options\":[\"Tie the thread at the top\",\"Decorate the shapes as per your imagination\",\"Paste the shapes in a vertical line\",\"Draw the shapes on paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 4 follows step 3 (cutting) and states \'Decorate the shapes as per your imagination\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the thread be tied in the wall-hanging project?\",\"options\":[\"At the bottom\",\"In the middle\",\"At the top\",\"To the scissors\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 7 states to \'Tie the thread at the top\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final purpose of the wall-hanging as mentioned in the steps?\",\"options\":[\"To sell it in the market\",\"To decorate your classroom\",\"To give it as a gift\",\"To keep it in a bag\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 8 states \'Decorate your classroom using wall hanging\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which traditional art form is suggested for identifying shapes in the warm-up section?\",\"options\":[\"Madhubani Paintings\",\"Warli Paintings\",\"Mural Paintings\",\"Oil Paintings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The warm-up activity (a) asks to look at Warli Paintings and identify shapes.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many sticks need to be moved in the \'Fun with shapes\' stick puzzle?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Five\",\"None\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructions say to \'Move any three sticks\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When arranging the shapes for the wall-hanging, how should they be attached to the thread?\",\"options\":[\"In a horizontal line\",\"In a circular pattern\",\"In a vertical line\",\"In a zig-zag way\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 6 states \'Paste\\/attach the shapes with thread in a vertical line\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which geometrical shape is used as the main frame from which all the threads hang?\",\"options\":[\"A square\",\"A triangle\",\"A circle or ring\",\"A rectangle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the threads hanging from a circular ring held by the boy.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/049_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure and the text, what is the boy doing with the shapes?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing them on a wall\",\"Cutting them with scissors\",\"Arranging them creatively in a design\",\"Painting a Rangoli\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the boy holding a finished wall-hanging, which corresponds to step 5: \'Arrange the shapes creatively to design a wall hanging\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/049_101.jpg\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21779,32,6,'English','en','She Knew No Fear','[\"- The story is about a girl named Nirmala who was jealous of her friend Sayal and later learns a lesson about courage and friendship.\",\"- Nirmala dislikes Sayal because she is more beautiful and more intelligent.\",\"- Sayal helps Nirmala when a python attacks them; she uses her strength and calmness to free Nirmala.\",\"- After the incident, Nirmala becomes happier and learns that jealousy can be overcome.\",\"- Key vocabulary: ignored (paid no attention), coiled (made a round shape), shrieked (made a loud noise), squirmed (moved restlessly).\",\"- Base verbs: threw – throw, kicked – kick, disliked – dislike, stuck – stick.\",\"- Opposite of “intelligent” can be “stupid”.\",\"- Opposite of “ignored” can be “appreciated” or “paid no attention”.\",\"- Contractions: I am → I’m, he is → he’s, we are → we’re, you are → you’re, she has → she’s, they have → they’ve, you will → you’ll, she would → she’d.\",\"- Contractions for negatives: is not → isn’t, are not → aren’t, have not → haven’t, has not → hasn’t, had not → hadn’t, do not → don’t, did not → didn’t, does not → doesn’t.\",\"- Vocabulary practice: Antakshari – think of words that start with the last letter of the previous word.\",\"- Crossword clues: “I grow on your head” → hair, “I smell with it” → nose, “It is above the neck” → head, “Even the chair has these” → legs, “I hear with my” → ears, “I see with my” → eyes.\",\"- The story teaches that courage and friendship can overcome fear and jealousy.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Why did Nirmala dislike Sayal at the beginning of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Sayal was mean to her\",\"Sayal was more beautiful and intelligent\",\"Sayal stole her grazing ground\",\"Sayal refused to talk to her\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Nirmala disliked Sayal because she was more beautiful and intelligent.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Nirmala and Sayal meet on that \'fine day\'?\",\"options\":[\"At the village school\",\"At the Republic Day parade\",\"At the village grazing ground\",\"Near the President\'s house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the two met at the village grazing ground.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the snake doing as Nirmala stands in the grass?\",\"options\":[\"It is sleeping in the sun\",\"It is coiling itself around her feet\",\"It is chasing a bird\",\"It is hiding in a hole\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the snake coiling around Nirmala\'s feet\\/legs as she looks back.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/050_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'her blood froze\' indicate about Nirmala\'s state of mind?\",\"options\":[\"She was feeling very cold\",\"She was extremely terrified\",\"She was feeling sick\",\"She was very angry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The phrase is used to show extreme fear when she saw the monster snake.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how long was the snake that attacked Nirmala?\",\"options\":[\"Five feet long\",\"Ten feet long\",\"Twelve feet long\",\"Twenty feet long\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly describes the snake as a \'twelve feet long monster\'.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what action is Sayal taking to help Nirmala?\",\"options\":[\"She is running away to get help\",\"She is hitting the snake with a stick\",\"She is grabbing the snake\'s jaws with her hands\",\"She is calling the village people\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure and text show Sayal grabbing the snake\'s jaws to force them open.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/050_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What scientific fact did Sayal use to calm Nirmala\'s fear of being poisoned?\",\"options\":[\"All snakes are friendly\",\"Pythons are not poisonous\",\"The snake was too small to have poison\",\"She had medicine for the poison\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sayal assured Nirmala by saying, \'Pythons are not poisonous.\'\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What did Sayal do when she realized the stick was not enough to control the python?\",\"options\":[\"She climbed a tree\",\"She threw the stick away and used her hands\",\"She started screaming for help\",\"She used a stone to hit the snake\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says she threw the stick away and grabbed the snake’s jaws with her hands.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the two girls doing after escaping the snake?\",\"options\":[\"They are looking for the snake\'s eggs\",\"They are walking slowly back to the village\",\"They are running away without looking back\",\"They are playing in the grazing ground\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the girls running away from the snake which is left behind in the grass.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/051_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What command did Sayal give to Nirmala to help her get out of the snake\'s grip?\",\"options\":[\"Run!\",\"Pull!\",\"Kick!\",\"Shout!\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sayal commanded, \'Kick! Nirmala. Free yourself.\'\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did the village people react when they heard the story of the girls?\",\"options\":[\"They were angry at the girls for going there\",\"They were scared of the snake\",\"They were proud of Sayal’s bravery\",\"They did not believe the story\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the village people were proud of Sayal\'s bravery.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who honored Sayal for her courage and bravery?\",\"options\":[\"The Village Headman\",\"The Indian President\",\"Nirmala\'s parents\",\"The School Principal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she was honoured by the Indian President on Republic Day.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was Sayal riding during the Republic Day procession?\",\"options\":[\"A horse\",\"A tractor\",\"A decorated elephant\",\"A flower-covered jeep\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Nirmala saw Sayal ride a decorated elephant in the Republic Day procession.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the ending, what was the most important change in Nirmala\'s character?\",\"options\":[\"She became afraid of all animals\",\"She decided to become a snake catcher\",\"She overcame her jealousy and became happier\",\"She moved to a different village\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that Nirmala realized she was a happier person once she overcame jealousy.\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of Sayal\'s traits most likely helped her know that pythons are not poisonous?\",\"options\":[\"Her physical strength\",\"Her intelligence and knowledge of things around her\",\"Her ability to run fast\",\"Her beauty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Sayal was intelligent and \'seemed to know a lot about things around her.\'\",\"topic\":\"3.2 She Knew No Fear\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is a contraction according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A long form of a word\",\"A shortened or contracted form of a word\",\"A word with the opposite meaning\",\"A word that sounds like another word\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a contraction as a shortened\\/contracted form of a word.\",\"topic\":\"Contracted forms\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which punctuation mark is used to replace omitted letters in a contraction?\",\"options\":[\"Comma\",\"Full stop\",\"Apostrophe\",\"Hyphen\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that omitted letters are replaced with an apostrophe.\",\"topic\":\"Contracted forms\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is a contraction created based on the explanation provided?\",\"options\":[\"By adding extra letters to a word\",\"By splitting one word into two\",\"By combining words and omitting some letters\",\"By changing the spelling of the first word only\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A contraction is created by combining two or more words and omitting some letters.\",\"topic\":\"Contracted forms\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'They are playing hockey\', what is the contracted form of \'They are\'?\",\"options\":[\"They\'is\",\"They\'re\",\"They\'am\",\"They\'r\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'They\'re playing hockey\' as the contracted version of \'They are playing hockey\'.\",\"topic\":\"Contracted forms\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'he will\' becomes \'he\'ll\', what is the correct contracted form for \'you will\'?\",\"options\":[\"you\'ill\",\"you\'l\",\"you\'will\",\"you\'ll\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Following the pattern of \'he\'ll\', the table lists \'you\'ll\' as the contraction for \'you will\'.\",\"topic\":\"Contracted forms\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct contracted form of the words \'does not\'?\",\"options\":[\"does\'nt\",\"doesn\'t\",\"do\'not\",\"doesnot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the text lists \'doesn\'t\' as the contracted form of \'does not\'.\",\"topic\":\"Contracted forms\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the contracted form shown for the words \'They have\'?\",\"options\":[\"They\'ve\",\"They\'h\",\"They\'s\",\"They\'are\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure explicitly pairs \'They have\' with \'They\'ve\'.\",\"topic\":\"Contracted forms\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/052_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which full form corresponds to the contraction \'hadn\'t\'?\",\"options\":[\"has not\",\"have not\",\"had not\",\"did not\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows \'had not\' as the full form for