Rules for children\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the \'Golden Rules\', what does the text imply about interrupting others?\",\"options\":[\"It is allowed if you say \'Excuse me\'\",\"It should be avoided by letting others finish talking\",\"It is part of \'Smile Power\'\",\"It is necessary when you have heavy bags\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Listen First\' rule implies that you should not interrupt by stating one should let others finish talking first.\",\"topic\":\"Golden Rules for children\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, where do good manners start?\",\"options\":[\"Only at school\",\"Only when guests arrive\",\"At home\",\"At the playground\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'They start at home!\'\",\"topic\":\"Manners at Home\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Cleaning your own mess is a sign of being a ________ person.\",\"options\":[\"Responsible\",\"Strict\",\"Quiet\",\"Fast\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Cleaning your own mess is a sign of a responsible person.\'\",\"topic\":\"Manners at Home\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why should you always knock on a closed door before entering?\",\"options\":[\"To see if the door is locked\",\"To show respect for the other person’s privacy\",\"To wake up the person inside\",\"To check if the room is clean\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that knocking shows you respect the other person’s privacy.\",\"topic\":\"Manners at Home\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text suggest we should do during family dinner instead of watching TV?\",\"options\":[\"Eat as fast as possible\",\"Read a storybook\",\"Talk to each other\",\"Play with toys\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text advises to \'Talk to each other instead!\' during dinner.\",\"topic\":\"Manners at Home\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message regarding how we should treat our family members?\",\"options\":[\"We only need to be polite to guests\",\"Family deserves our best behavior too\",\"We should only speak when spoken to\",\"We should save our manners for school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Your family deserves your best behavior too.\'\",\"topic\":\"Manners at Home\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which specific instruction from the text is the boy following by interacting with the elderly lady?\",\"options\":[\"Keep it Tidy\",\"Knock-Knock!\",\"Respect your Elders\",\"Phone Manners at Home\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a boy speaking politely to an elder (Aaji), which falls under \'Respect your Elders\'.\",\"topic\":\"Manners at Home\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/059_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you have just finished playing with your building blocks, what should you do according to the \'Keep it Tidy\' rule?\",\"options\":[\"Leave them on the floor for later\",\"Put them back in their places\",\"Ask your parents to clean them\",\"Hide them under the bed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to put toys or books back in their places after playing.\",\"topic\":\"Manners at Home\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, what is a polite question the boy might be asking the lady to make her happy?\",\"options\":[\"Where is my toy?\",\"When is dinner ready?\",\"How was your day, Aaji?\",\"Can I watch TV now?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the example \'How was your day, Aaji?\' as a way to make a grandmother happy.\",\"topic\":\"Manners at Home\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/059_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these actions would be considered a violation of \'Phone Manners at Home\'?\",\"options\":[\"Using a phone in the bedroom\",\"Checking a phone while the family eats dinner\",\"Calling a friend in the afternoon\",\"Charging a phone 