a fridge\",\"He is putting waste into a dustbin\",\"He is whispering to a friend\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a boy putting waste into a green bin, which the text describes as a manner towards Mother Earth.\",\"topic\":\"Manners in Public Places\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/059_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the proper behavior while waiting for a school bus?\",\"options\":[\"Push others to get in first\",\"Jump the line to save time\",\"Wait for your turn in a queue\",\"Run to the front of the bus\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that in a queue for a school bus, one should wait for their turn and not push or jump the line.\",\"topic\":\"Manners in Public Places\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should you say when you are leaving a friend\'s house after a visit?\",\"options\":[\"\\\"I am going now.\\\"\",\"\\\"Thank you for having me over.\\\"\",\"\\\"See you at school.\\\"\",\"\\\"I liked your sofa.\\\"\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that when leaving a friend\'s house, you should always say, \'Thank you for having me over.\'\",\"topic\":\"Manners in Public Places\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are at a friend\'s house and feel thirsty, what is the correct manner to follow?\",\"options\":[\"Open their fridge immediately\",\"Ask before opening their fridge\",\"Jump on the sofa until they give you water\",\"Wait until you leave the house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text advises not to open a friend\'s fridge without asking.\",\"topic\":\"Manners in Public Places\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure and the text, why is the boy\'s action important for the environment?\",\"options\":[\"It helps him represent his school\",\"It shows he is waiting for his turn\",\"It prevents waste from being thrown on the road\",\"It helps him focus in the library\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that looking for a dustbin instead of throwing waste on the road is a manner towards Mother Earth.\",\"topic\":\"Manners in Public Places\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/059_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these actions is specifically mentioned as a way to show respect to a friend\'s parents?\",\"options\":[\"Opening their fridge\",\"Jumping on their sofa\",\"Greeting them when you visit\",\"Whispering in their house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says that when you visit a friend, you should greet their parents.\",\"topic\":\"Manners in Public Places\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following behaviors would be considered \'jumping the line\'?\",\"options\":[\"Waiting for your turn at the ticket counter\",\"Moving to the front of the bus queue before others\",\"Greeting parents at a friend\'s house\",\"Whispering in a library\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Jumping the line means not waiting for your turn and moving ahead of others who were there first.\",\"topic\":\"Manners in Public Places\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what speaks even when your mouth is closed?\",\"options\":[\"Your thoughts\",\"Your body\",\"Your magic words\",\"Your heart\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'Your body speaks!\' even when the mouth is closed.\",\"topic\":\"Body Language - The Silent Manners\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does standing straight indicate about a person?\",\"options\":[\"They are lazy\",\"They are listening\",\"They are active\",\"They are friendly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Standing straight shows you are active.\'\",\"topic\":\"Body Language - The Silent Manners\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the club mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Silent Manners Club\",\"Body Language Club\",\"Universal Language Club\",\"Magic Words Club\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the \'Magic Words Club\' in the concluding sentence.\",\"topic\":\"Body Language - The Silent Manners\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is eye contact important when talking to someone?\",\"options\":[\"It shows you are friendly\",\"It shows you are confident and listening\",\"It shows you are standing straight\",\"It shows you are using magic words\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says eye contact \'shows you are confident and listening.\'\",\"topic\":\"Body Language - The Silent Manners\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a smile described as a \'universal language\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is used in every club\",\"Because it shows you are active\",\"Because it says \'I am friendly\' without using words\",\"Because it helps you stand straight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains a smile says \'I am friendly\' without using any words, making it universal.\",\"topic\":\"Body Language - The Silent Manners\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text suggest about slumping or leaning too much?\",\"options\":[\"It makes you look active\",\"It shows you are listening\",\"It can look lazy\",\"It is a universal language\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Slumping or leaning too much can look lazy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Body Language - The Silent Manners\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Rohan wants to show his teacher that he is paying attention and is sure of himself, what should he do?\",\"options\":[\"He should slump against the desk\",\"He should keep his mouth closed\",\"He should maintain eye contact\",\"He should lean towards the door\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says eye contact shows you are confident and listening.\",\"topic\":\"Body Language - The Silent Manners\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is standing straight during an assembly, how are they presenting themselves according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"As a lazy person\",\"As an active person\",\"As a person who is not listening\",\"As a person who is speaking with their mouth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Standing straight is identified in the text as showing that you are active.\",\"topic\":\"Body Language - The Silent Manners\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned as a form of body language in the provided text?\",\"options\":[\"Posture\",\"Eye Contact\",\"Hand Gestures\",\"A Smile\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text discusses eye contact, posture, and smiles, but does not mention hand gestures.\",\"topic\":\"Body Language - The Silent Manners\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final advice given to the members of the \'Magic Words Club\' regarding these manners?\",\"options\":[\"Keep them in your heart and use them every day\",\"Only use them when your mouth is closed\",\"Use them only when you are in the club\",\"Learn them but do not use them\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying \'keep them in your heart and remember to use them every day!\'\",\"topic\":\"Body Language - The Silent Manners\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'mysterious\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A thing that is very easy to explain\",\"A thing you don\'t understand or can explain easily\",\"A thing that everyone in the world knows\",\"A way of behaving towards other people\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines mysterious as a thing you don’t understand or can explain easily.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes the way someone behaves towards other people?\",\"options\":[\"Posture\",\"Leaning\",\"Manners\",\"Universal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines manners as the way that someone behaves towards other people.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the term \'posture\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"The way a person sits, stands, walks etc.\",\"A position that is not straight or upright\",\"Something that affects everyone in the world\",\"A thing you cannot understand easily\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines posture as the way that a person sits, stands, walks etc.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If something is described as \'universal\', who does it affect?\",\"options\":[\"Only people in one country\",\"Only the person who is leaning\",\"Everyone in the world\",\"People with good manners\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines universal as affecting everyone in the world.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does it mean to be \'leaning\'?\",\"options\":[\"To stand perfectly straight\",\"To behave well towards others\",\"To be in a position that is not straight or upright\",\"To explain something very easily\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines leaning as being in a position that is not straight or upright.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word would you use for a situation that you cannot explain easily?\",\"options\":[\"Manners\",\"Universal\",\"Posture\",\"Mysterious\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"A thing you cannot explain easily is defined as mysterious.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is sitting in a way that is not upright, which word describes their position?\",\"options\":[\"Universal\",\"Leaning\",\"Manners\",\"Mysterious\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Leaning is defined as being in a position that is not straight or upright.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When a teacher observes how a student walks and stands, the teacher is looking at the student\'s:\",\"options\":[\"Posture\",\"Universal\",\"Mysterious\",\"Leaning\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Posture is defined as the way a person sits, stands, or walks.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words specifically relates to social interaction between people?\",\"options\":[\"Posture\",\"Manners\",\"Leaning\",\"Universal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Manners refers to behavior towards other people, which is a social interaction.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a new law is described as \'universal\', how does its reach compare to a \'mysterious\' law?\",\"options\":[\"The universal law is not straight, while the mysterious one is.\",\"The universal law affects everyone, while the mysterious one is hard to understand.\",\"The universal law is about walking, while the mysterious one is about sitting.\",\"The universal law is about manners, while the mysterious one is about posture.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Universal means affecting everyone, while mysterious means hard to understand or explain.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21782,32,6,'English','en','Joy of Letter Writing','[\"Letter writing is a way to send messages to people far away.\",\"There are two types: informal (to friends, family) and formal (to authority).\",\"Informal letters are friendly, simple and use a casual tone.\",\"Formal letters are polite, use a respectful tone and follow a strict format.\",\"An informal letter has: sender’s address, date, salutation, body, closing, and signature.\",\"The salutation in an informal letter is usually “Dear + name” or “Hi + name”.\",\"The body of the letter contains the main message and is written in paragraphs.\",\"The closing (subscription) is a short phrase like “Yours affectionately” or “Yours lovingly”.\",\"The signature line is the writer’s name written at the end of the letter.\",\"When writing a letter, think about the purpose, the reader, and the message you want to convey.\",\"Use simple sentences and correct spelling and punctuation.\",\"Practice writing letters by filling in blanks or writing from scratch.\",\"Remember to keep the tone appropriate: friendly for informal, respectful for formal.\",\"Check your letter for spelling, punctuation and neatness before sending it.\",\"Letter writing helps you express feelings, share news and keep in touch with friends and family.\",\"Writing letters is also a good exercise for improving writing skills and vocabulary.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In the poem \'A-Tisket A-Tasket\', what are the colors of the basket?\",\"options\":[\"Red and blue\",\"Green and yellow\",\"Pink and white\",\"Black and white\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions \'A green and yellow basket\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and understand\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who did the speaker in the poem write a letter to?\",\"options\":[\"Their father\",\"Their teacher\",\"Their mother\",\"Their brother\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'I wrote a letter to my mother\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and understand\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the letter on the way?\",\"options\":[\"It got wet\",\"It was posted\",\"It was dropped\",\"It was torn\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'And on the way I dropped it\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and understand\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which grade does Shantanu study?\",\"options\":[\"6th grade\",\"1st grade\",\"5th grade\",\"3rd grade\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text identifies Shantanu as a brother who studies in 3rd grade.\",\"topic\":\"Read and understand\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Harshita, what is the meaning of letter writing?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing pictures for friends\",\"Writing a message to someone far away\",\"Reading a book aloud\",\"Talking on a mobile phone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Harshita defines it as \'writing a message to someone who is far away from us\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and understand\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is Mrs. Patil?\",\"options\":[\"Shantanu\'s friend\",\"Harshita\'s mother\",\"The English teacher\",\"A relative\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Harshita mentions, \'Today our English teacher, Mrs. Patil, taught us letter writing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and understand\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What were letters used for before mobile phones and technology existed?\",\"options\":[\"To play games\",\"To share feelings, news, and experiences\",\"To complete school exams only\",\"To buy groceries\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Harshita explains that people wrote letters to share feelings, news, and experiences.\",\"topic\":\"Read and understand\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Shantanu wants to write a letter to his cousin, what type of letter would it be?\",\"options\":[\"Formal letter\",\"Informal letter\",\"Business letter\",\"Official letter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Informal letters are written to friends, parents, cousins, or relatives.\",\"topic\":\"Read and understand\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student needs to write a letter to a person in authority. Which type should they choose?\",\"options\":[\"Informal letter\",\"Friendly letter\",\"Formal letter\",\"Simple letter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states formal letter writing is written to a person in authority.\",\"topic\":\"Read and understand\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the dialogue, how is letter writing similar to WhatsApp?\",\"options\":[\"Both require a basket\",\"Both are used to send messages\",\"Both are only for 6th grade students\",\"Both are written on paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Harshita agrees with Shantanu that letter writing is like sending messages on WhatsApp.\",\"topic\":\"Read and understand\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes the style of an informal letter according to Harshita?\",\"options\":[\"Strict and difficult\",\"Friendl