absence.\'\",\"topic\":\"Jumbled Sentences Activity\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of sentences would be most appropriate for a letter of apology for missing a party?\",\"options\":[\"Sentences 5, 8, and 11\",\"Sentences 7, 10, and 4\",\"Sentences 1, 6, and 9\",\"Sentences 2, 12, and 13\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sentences 1, 6, and 9 all deal with regretting, explaining, and excusing absence.\",\"topic\":\"Jumbled Sentences Activity\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence is best suited to conclude the body of the letter by showing appreciation for the recipient\'s patience?\",\"options\":[\"Sentence 3\",\"Sentence 5\",\"Sentence 10\",\"Sentence 14\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Sentence 3 (\'Thanking you for your understanding\') is a typical way to conclude after explaining a problem.\",\"topic\":\"Jumbled Sentences Activity\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main theme of sentences 5 and 8?\",\"options\":[\"Expressing gratitude\",\"Congratulating someone\",\"Asking for help\",\"Saying goodbye\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both sentences 5 and 8 use the word \'congratulate\' or \'congratulations\'.\",\"topic\":\"Jumbled Sentences Activity\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are diphthongs according to the \'Quick tip\'?\",\"options\":[\"Consonant sounds that repeat\",\"Vowel sounds that glide from one to another\",\"Silent letters in a word\",\"Sounds that only happen at the end of a word\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines diphthongs as vowel sounds that glide from one vowel to another within the same syllable.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Diphthongs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the word \'coin\', the sound moves from \\/ɔ\\/ to which other sound?\",\"options\":[\"\\/e\\/\",\"\\/a\\/\",\"\\/ɪ\\/\",\"\\/ʊ\\/\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The \'Quick tip\' specifically states that in coin (\\/ɔɪ\\/), the sound moves from \\/ɔ\\/ to \\/ɪ\\/.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Diphthongs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of the \\/aʊ\\/ sound?\",\"options\":[\"Cake\",\"Boat\",\"House\",\"Time\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'house\' and \'cow\' as examples for the \\/aʊ\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Diphthongs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, a diphthong glide happens within how many syllables?\",\"options\":[\"Two different syllables\",\"The same syllable\",\"Every syllable in a word\",\"Only the first syllable\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Quick tip\' states the glide happens within the same syllable.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Diphthongs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which common letters are used to represent the \\/ɔɪ\\/ sound?\",\"options\":[\"ai, ay\",\"ou, ow\",\"oi, oy\",\"ie, y\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows that the sound \\/ɔɪ\\/ is represented by the letters \'oi\' and \'oy\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Diphthongs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which sound is shared by the words \'hear\' and \'deer\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/ɪə\\/\",\"\\/eə\\/\",\"\\/ʊə\\/\",\"\\/əʊ\\/\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'hear\' and \'deer\' as examples for the \\/ɪə\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Diphthongs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to write a word with the \\/eɪ\\/ sound using the \'ai\' letters, which word from the text should you use?\",\"options\":[\"Cake\",\"Rain\",\"Day\",\"Time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'rain\' as an example of the \\/eɪ\\/ sound using the \'ai\' letters.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Diphthongs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words uses the \'ow\' letters to produce the \\/əʊ\\/ sound?\",\"options\":[\"Cow\",\"Snow\",\"Now\",\"How\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'snow\' as an example for the 