ry in a few words.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Make a Bird-feeder\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these materials is NOT listed as needed to make a bird-feeder?\",\"options\":[\"A small stick\",\"Bird-seeds\",\"Glue or tape\",\"Scissors\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The materials list includes a bottle, seeds, stick, string\\/thread, and scissors, but does not mention glue or tape.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Make a Bird-feeder\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the first item you need to take to start the activity?\",\"options\":[\"A glass jar\",\"An empty plastic bottle\",\"A bag of seeds\",\"A wooden stick\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure and the first instruction both indicate taking an empty plastic bottle.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Make a Bird-feeder\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/070_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure and instructions, what must be the state of the bottle before you begin?\",\"options\":[\"It must be full of water\",\"It must be empty\",\"It must be cut in half\",\"It must be painted green\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Instruction 1 and the figure caption specify taking an \'empty\' plastic bottle.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Make a Bird-feeder\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/070_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"After making two small holes in the bottle, what is the next step you should perform?\",\"options\":[\"Fill the bottle with seeds\",\"Hang the bottle on a tree\",\"Put a stick through the holes\",\"Tie a string to the bottle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Instruction 3 follows the hole-making step and says to \'Put a stick through the holes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Make a Bird-feeder\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you do not have a string to hang the bottle, what other material does the text suggest you can use?\",\"options\":[\"A metal wire\",\"A piece of thread\",\"A rubber band\",\"A plastic strip\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The materials list mentions \'string or thread\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Make a Bird-feeder\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final step in making the bird-feeder?\",\"options\":[\"Filling it with seeds\",\"Tying a string\",\"Making small holes\",\"Hanging it on a tree\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The 6th and final instruction is to \'Hang the bottle on a tree\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Make a Bird-feeder\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why are \'scissors\' included in the list of materials?\",\"options\":[\"To stir the bird seeds\",\"To help make the holes or cut the string\",\"To decorate the plastic bottle\",\"To repair the broken stick\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Scissors are necessary to perform tasks like making holes or cutting the string\\/thread mentioned in the instructions.\",\"topic\":\"Activity: Make a Bird-feeder\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which author is mentioned in the text for learners to be introduced to?\",\"options\":[\"Sarojini Naidu\",\"Mahadevi Verma\",\"Rabindranath Tagore\",\"Ruskin Bond\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions providing an introduction about Mahadevi Verma.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific name for a poem that does not have a rhyme scheme?\",\"options\":[\"Blank verse\",\"Free verse\",\"Short story\",\"Prose\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a poem without a rhyme scheme as \'free verse.\'\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instructions, where should students share the bird stories they collect?\",\"options\":[\"In the classroom\",\"In the school assembly\",\"In the library\",\"At home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests sharing the collected bird stories in the school assembly.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text state about rhyme schemes in poetry?\",\"options\":[\"Every poem must have a rhyme scheme.\",\"Rhyme schemes are only for bird poems.\",\"Every poem does not have a rhyme scheme.\",\"Rhyme schemes are found in free verse.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text clarifies that every poem does not necessarily have a rhyme scheme.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should learners be encouraged to do regarding Mahadevi Verma\'s literature?\",\"options\":[\"Memorize her biography\",\"Read her other works\",\"Translate her poems\",\"Write stories about her\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to read other works by Mahadevi Verma.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student finds a poem that lacks a regular pattern of rhyming sounds, how should they categorize it based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"As a story\",\"As an assembly speech\",\"As free verse\",\"As a rhyme scheme\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A poem without a rhyme scheme is categorized as free verse according to the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A teacher asks a student to prepare for the school assembly based on this topic. What should the student collect?\",\"options\":[\"Rhyme schemes\",\"Definitions of free verse\",\"Different stories about birds\",\"Biographies of all poets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to collect different stories about birds for the assembly.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are reading a book by Mahadevi Verma as suggested by the text, what are you doing?\",\"options\":[\"Collecting bird stories\",\"Reading her other works\",\"Creating a rhyme scheme\",\"Practicing for the assembly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Reading books by the mentioned author aligns with the instruction to read her other works.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What can be inferred about the structure of poetry from the mention of \'free verse\'?\",\"options\":[\"Poetry must always be complex.\",\"Poetry has diverse structures, including those without rhyme.\",\"Only Mahadevi Verma writes free verse.\",\"Bird stories cannot be written in free verse.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The existence of free verse shows that poetry does not always require a rhyme scheme.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text likely suggest sharing bird stories in the school assembly?\",\"options\":[\"To teach students how to fly\",\"To provide a platform for sharing collected information\",\"To ensure every poem has a rhyme scheme\",\"To introduce Mahadevi Verma to the parents\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sharing in the assembly is a way to present the stories students were asked to collect.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21784,32,6,'English','en','Aim High Like Sheetal','[\"- Sheetal Devi is a Paralympic archery champion from India.\",\"- She won a gold medal in the Paralympics.\",\"- She had a disability but used her legs to shoot arrows.\",\"- She practiced every day, rain or shine, showing dedication and perseverance.\",\"- Key qualities: determination, focus, hard work, courage, resilience.\",\"- Important words: archery, Paralympics, gold medal, dedication, perseverance, disability, courage, focus, goal.\",\"- Opposite pairs: high – low; strong – weak; easy – difficult; wrong – right; unbelievable – believable; courage – fear.\",\"- In sentences, use verbs like aim, focus, aim for a goal, concentrate, give attention.\",\"- Positive statements: “I do not watch TV at night” is negative; “I love animals” is affirmative.\",\"- Palindromes are words that read the same backward and forward: eye, noon, madam, radar, kayak, wow, mom, dad.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which sport did Sheetal Devi win a gold medal for India?\",\"options\":[\"Shot put\",\"Paralympic Archery\",\"High jump\",\"Discus throw\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Sheetal Devi won a gold medal in Paralympic Archery for India.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Sheetal Devi use to perform archery since she did not have hands?\",\"options\":[\"A special machine\",\"Her teeth\",\"Her legs\",\"Help from others\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Swarup mentions that Sheetal Devi made her legs work like hands.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the skit, how often did Sheetal Devi practice?\",\"options\":[\"Only on sunny days\",\"Once a week\",\"Every single day, rain or shine\",\"Only before competitions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sakshi mentions that Sheetal Devi practiced every single day, rain or shine.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the meaning of the word \'amazing\'?\",\"options\":[\"To give attention\",\"Very surprising and difficult to believe\",\"A sports competition\",\"A final goal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket in the figure defines amazing as \'very surprising and difficult to believe, incredible\'.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/072_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word is defined as a \'goal\'?\",\"options\":[\"Focus\",\"Amazing\",\"Aim\",\"Paralympics\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket in the figure clearly defines \'aim\' as \'goal\'.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/072_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main lesson Shailesh wants everyone to learn from Sheetal Devi\'s story?\",\"options\":[\"Archery is the best sport\",\"Never give up, even if you fail many times\",\"Only people without hands can be brave\",\"Winning gold is the only goal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Shailesh explicitly states the lesson is to never give up, even if you fail many times.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the quote \'Your disability is not your inability\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Physical challenges do not stop a person from being capable\",\"People with disabilities cannot play sports\",\"Inability is better than disability\",\"Only athletes have disabilities\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The quote implies that having a physical disability does not mean a person lacks the ability to achieve great things.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does Sakshi plan to apply Sheetal Devi\'s inspiration in her own life?\",\"options\":[\"By joining an archery club\",\"By working harder on her homework\",\"By traveling to the Paralympics\",\"By stopping her sports practice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sakshi says, \'I feel like working harder on my homework now!\' after hearing the story.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Manasvi wants to be like Sheetal Devi while facing challenges, what quality does she need to have?\",\"options\":[\"Fear\",\"Bravery\",\"Laziness\",\"Doubt\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Manasvi says she will try to be brave like Sheetal Devi while facing challenges.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the Word Basket, what does a student need to do to \'focus\' during a lecture?\",\"options\":[\"Talk to friends\",\"Concentrate and give attention\",\"Look out of the window\",\"Sleep in class\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket defines focus as \'to concentrate, to give attention\'.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Swarup say Sheetal Devi \'proved them wrong\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because she lost the competition\",\"Because she showed she could do archery despite having no hands\",\"Because she stopped practicing\",\"Because she chose a different sport\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She proved wrong the people who said archery was too difficult for her because she had no hands.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Word Basket, who participates in the \'Paralympics\'?\",\"options\":[\"Only professional archers\",\"Athletes who have physical or mental disability\",\"Only students from local schools\",\"Athletes who have no interest in sports\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines Paralympics as a sports competition for athletes who have disability (physical or mental).\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which character mentions that Sheetal Devi \'started small too\'?\",\"options\":[\"Sakshi\",\"Varsha\",\"Sai\",\"Shivam\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Varsha tells Manasvi not to worry because Sheetal started small too and kept trying.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'rain or shine\' tell us about Sheetal Devi\'s character?\",\"options\":[\"She liked the weather\",\"She was very dedicated and consistent\",\"She only practiced when it rained\",\"She was afraid of the sun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Practicing \'rain or shine\' indicates that she was dedicated and did not let external conditions stop her.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final collective message given by the characters at the end of the skit?\",\"options\":[\"To stop playing games\",\"To aim high like Sheetal Devi\",\"To only focus on homework\",\"To complain about difficulties\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The skit ends with Swarup saying \'Let\'s aim high, just like Sheetal Devi!\' and everyone cheering.\",\"topic\":\"Aim High like Sheetal Devi\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'aim\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Goal\",\"Surprise\",\"Disability\",\"Attention\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'aim\' as a \'goal\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is defined as \'very surprising and difficult to believe\'?\",\"options\":[\"Focus\",\"Paralympics\",\"Amazing\",\"Aim\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The definition for \'amazing\' is provided as \'very surprising and difficult to believe\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The \'paralympics\' is a sports competition specifically for athletes who have:\",\"options\":[\"No experience\",\"Disability (physical or mental)\",\"Incredible speed\",\"Surprising goals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines paralympics as a competition for athletes with physical or mental disabilities.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, to \'focus\' means to:\",\"options\":[\"Act in a skit\",\"Give attention\",\"Win a competition\",\"Believe in something\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'focus\' as \'to concentrate, to give attention\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What role should the facilitator play while learners are performing the skit?\",\"options\":[\"Write the script\",\"Guide the learners\",\"Judge the competition\",\"Watch in silence\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The facilitator instructions state to \'Guide learners while they enact the skit\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides guiding the skit, what specific concept should the facilitator make learners aware of?\",\"options\":[\"Spelling\",\"Intonation\",\"Grammar\",\"Vocabulary\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions making learners aware about \'intonation and its importance\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is trying to \'concentrate\' on their studies, which word from the text describes their action?\",\"options\":[\"Aim\",\"Focus\",\"Amazing\",\"Paralympics\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Focus is defined as \'to concentrate\', so it applies to this scenario.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student is preparing to perform a play in class. Based on the facilitator\'s instructions, what should the teacher help them with?\",\"options\":[\"Finding a sports goal\",\"Enacting the skit\",\"Defining incredible words\",\"Entering the Paralympics\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The facilitator is instructed to guide learners while they enact the skit.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definition of \'paralympics\', which of these athletes would qualify for the event?\",\"options\":[\"An athlete with a physical disability\",\"An athlete who is very surprising\",\"An athlete who has no focus\",\"An athlete who only plays for fun\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The definition specifies athletes who have disability (physical or mental).\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the facilitator need to focus on \'intonation\' during the skit enactment?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is surprising\",\"Because it is important\",\"Because it is a goal\",\"Because it is incredible\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the facilitator should make them aware of intonation and its \'importance\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21785,32,6,'English','en','How to Salute the Sun','[\"Surya Namaskar is a yoga exercise that salutes the sun and improves overall health.\",\"It has 12 distinct steps that work the whole body.\",\"A complete set of 12 steps takes about 15 minutes.\",\"It can be done by people aged 8 to 80, including children and the elderly.\",\"It strengthens both large (sthul) and small (sukshm) muscles.\",\"It benefits sensory, respiratory, digestive, circulatory, muscular and nervous systems.\",\"It improves concentration, memory, emotional control and alertness.\",\"It should be practiced under guidance and in the correct order.\",\"Avoid exercising after a meal, when weak or ill, or with jerky movements.\",\"Drink water before or after, not during the exercise.\",\"Use the correct breathing: inhale and exhale with each movement.\",\"The sun is called Surya, the world nourisher.\",\"The prayer of the sun’s names is called Beej Mantra.\",\"The body is a machine that needs proper diet, exercise, rest and relaxation.\",\"Yoga includes asanas, pranayama and meditation to regulate the body‑mind complex.\",\"The benefits of Surya Namaskar are balanced physical growth and efficient body function.\",\"It is a universal exercise, irrespective of caste, creed, religion, gender or nationality.\",\"The steps of Surya Namaskar are performed in a flowing sequence.\",\"Use the correct article: a, an, the, when speaking about objects or places.\",\"The present continuous tense uses am\\/is\\/are + verb+ing for actions happening now.\",\"The bee is flying around the flower – example of present continuous.\",\"The bee fly becomes the bee is flying when using the correct helping verb.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the shastras, for how many years can the human body work efficiently?\",\"options\":[\"50 years\",\"80 years\",\"100 years\",\"150 years\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the human body is a perfect machine to work efficiently for a hundred years as per our shastras.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who said the words, \'Shariramadyam Khalu Dharm Sadhanam\'?\",\"options\":[\"Valmiki\",\"Kalidas\",\"Patanjali\",\"Vyas\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly attributes the quote \'Shariramadyam Khalu Dharm Sadhanam\' to Kalidas.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the human body described as in the opening of the text?\",\"options\":[\"A simple tool\",\"Nature\'s most marvellous creation\",\"A temporary vessel\",\"A biological accident\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins by stating the human body is one of nature\'s most marvellous creations.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned as a component of Yog in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Asan\",\"Pranayam\",\"Meditation\",\"Weightlifting\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists asan, pranayam, and meditation as parts of Yog, but does not mention weightlifting.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is considered our \'foremost duty\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To earn money\",\"To keep the body fit\",\"To study shastras\",\"To travel the world\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'It is our foremost duty to keep this body fit.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text say Yog strengthens, regulates, and enhances?\",\"options\":[\"The digestive system only\",\"The Body-Mind Complex\",\"The skeletal structure\",\"The respiratory system\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Yog strengthens, regulates, and enhances the efficiency of the Body-Mind Complex.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To maintain the \'machine\' of the body properly, which four things are required?\",\"options\":[\"Proper diet, exercise, rest, and relaxation\",\"Proper sleep, water, sunlight, and air\",\"Proper medicine, vitamins, surgery, and rest\",\"Proper reading, writing, thinking, and speaking\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that we must maintain the body with proper diet, exercise, rest, and relaxation.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to Kalidas, what is the \'best instrument\' to reach the goal of life?\",\"options\":[\"A sharp mind\",\"The human body\",\"Wealth and power\",\"Religious books\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Kalidas says the body is the best instrument to reach the goal of life.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to improve their overall \'Body-Mind Complex\' efficiency, what should they practice based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only Sthool Vyayam\",\"Only Sukshm Vyayam\",\"Sthool Vyayam, Sukshm Vyayam, and Yog\",\"Only meditation\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text groups Sthool Vyayam, Sukshm Vyayam, and Yog together as ways to enhance the Body-Mind Complex.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How should one treat the human body to ensure it functions like a \'perfect machine\'?\",\"options\":[\"By ignoring it until it breaks\",\"By maintaining it with proper diet and exercise\",\"By using it only for physical work\",\"By avoiding all forms of relaxation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says it is our duty to maintain this machine properly with diet, exercise, rest, and relaxation.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text refer to the body as a \'Body-Mind Complex\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the body is complicated to understand\",\"Because physical exercises and Yog affect both the body and the mind\",\"Because the mind is more important than the body\",\"Because the body is made of many different organs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links exercises like Yog and meditation to the efficiency of the \'Body-Mind Complex\', implying they are interconnected.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the relationship between \'Shariramadyam Khalu Dharm Sadhanam\' and the \'goal of life\' mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"They are unrelated concepts\",\"The body is the primary means to achieve life\'s goals\",\"The goal of life is to avoid physical exercise\",\"Only shastras can help reach the goal of life\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The quote translates to the body being the first instrument of dharma\\/duty, which the text links to reaching the goal of life.\",\"topic\":\"The Human Body\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Surya Namaskar is a gift of which heritage to humankind?\",\"options\":[\"Western heritage\",\"Indian heritage\",\"Global heritage\",\"Modern heritage\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that Surya Namaskar is a gift of Indian heritage to humankind.\",\"topic\":\"Benefits of Surya Namaskar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the recommended age range for an able-bodied person to perform Surya Namaskar?\",\"options\":[\"5 years to 50 years\",\"10 years to 60 years\",\"8 years to 80 years\",\"12 years to 70 years\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that any able-bodied person from 8 years to 80 years can perform this exercise.\",\"topic\":\"Benefits of Surya Namaskar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two types of Vyayam benefits does Surya Namaskar provide?\",\"options\":[\"Sthul and Sukshm\",\"Physical and Mental\",\"Internal and External\",\"Active and Passive\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states it gives the benefits of Sthul as well as Sukshm Vyayam.\",\"topic\":\"Benefits of Surya Namaskar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which systems of glands have their functioning corrected by the vibrations generated during Namaskaras?\",\"options\":[\"Sensory and Respiratory\",\"Digestive and Circulatory\",\"Exocrine and Endocrine\",\"Muscular and Nervous\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that vibrations correct the functioning of exocrine and endocrine systems of glands.\",\"topic\":\"Benefits of Surya Namaskar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text mean by saying Surya Namaskar is \'universal in application\'?\",\"options\":[\"It can only be done in India\",\"It is only for people of a specific religion\",\"It applies to everyone regardless of caste, creed, or nationality\",\"It is only for professional athletes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Universal application means it is for everyone irrespective of caste, creed, religion, gender, and nationality.\",\"topic\":\"Benefits of Surya Namaskar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does Surya Namaskar specifically help children in their growing age?\",\"options\":[\"It helps them sleep longer\",\"It enables balanced physical growth and a healthy body\",\"It makes them experts in Indian history\",\"It teaches them how to chant perfectly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions it enables children to achieve balanced physical growth and a healthy, efficient body.\",\"topic\":\"Benefits of Surya Namaskar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what generates the minute vibrations in the body?\",\"options\":[\"The stretching of muscles\",\"The fast movement of limbs\",\"The utterances chanted while performing\",\"The heavy breathing during exercise\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the utterances chanted while performing the Namaskaras generate minute vibrations.\",\"topic\":\"Benefits of Surya Namaskar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a mental benefit of Surya Namaskar mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Improved eyesight\",\"Enhanced work efficiency through concentration\",\"Stronger muscular system\",\"Faster running speed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Concentration is listed as a factor that enhances work efficiency through Surya Namaskar.\",\"topic\":\"Benefits of Surya Namaskar\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student wants to improve thei