' section clearly states: \'Don\'t exercise after eating food\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Amit has just finished a heavy lunch. Based on the instructions, what should he do?\",\"options\":[\"Begin his exercises immediately\",\"Drink water while exercising\",\"Avoid exercising at this time\",\"Stretch very hard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Don\'t exercise after eating food\', so Amit should avoid it.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Sita is feeling very weak and has a fever. What is the correct advice for her according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"She should keep practicing\",\"She should not exercise when ill\",\"She should do jerky movements\",\"She should follow the right order\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Don\'ts\' section states: \'Don\'t exercise when you are weak or ill\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is listed as a \'Don\'t\' in the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Follow the right order\",\"Begin under guidance\",\"Drink water while exercise\",\"Keep practicing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Drinking water while exercising is listed under the \'Don\'ts\' section.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which movement is specifically prohibited in the \'Don\'ts\' list?\",\"options\":[\"Natural flow\",\"Jerky movements\",\"Gentle stretching\",\"Guided exercise\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says \'Don\'t do jerky movements\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is another name for the Present Continuous Tense as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Past Continuous Tense\",\"Present Progressive Tense\",\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"Simple Present Tense\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Present Continuous Tense is also called Present Progressive Tense.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When is the Present Continuous Tense used according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"When the action happened yesterday\",\"When the action will happen tomorrow\",\"When the action is happening now\",\"When the action never happens\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains we use this tense when the action is happening now.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct structure for the Present Continuous Tense?\",\"options\":[\"am\\/is\\/are + verb + ed\",\"was\\/were + verb + ing\",\"am\\/is\\/are + verb + ing\",\"will + verb + ing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the structure as am\\/is\\/are + verb + ing.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which helping verb is used with the subject \'I\' in the example sentences?\",\"options\":[\"is\",\"are\",\"am\",\"was\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the examples \'I am writing\' and \'I am eating a banana\', \'am\' is used with \'I\'.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'He is walking\', which word is the main verb in the -ing form?\",\"options\":[\"He\",\"is\",\"walking\",\"walk\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the structure verb + ing, \'walking\' is the main verb form used here.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the sentence that is in the Present Continuous Tense from the text.\",\"options\":[\"Seeta read a novel.\",\"Seeta is reading a novel.\",\"Seeta will read a novel.\",\"Seeta reads a novel.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Seeta is reading a novel\' as an example of Present Continuous Tense.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the \'ing\' form of the verb \'sing\'?\",\"options\":[\"singed\",\"sings\",\"singing\",\"sang\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to change the verb into the -ing form, which for \'sing\' is \'singing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which helping verb should be used for the subject \'Children\'?\",\"options\":[\"am\",\"is\",\"are\",\"was\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the table, \'Children\' is a plural subject, so the correct helping verb is \'are\'.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/079_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the rules in the text, what is the correct sentence for the subject \'Mother\' and main verb \'cook\'?\",\"options\":[\"Mother am cooking dinner.\",\"Mother are cooking dinner.\",\"Mother is cooking dinner.\",\"Mother cook dinner.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Following the rule am\\/is\\/are + verb + ing, \'Mother is cooking dinner\' is correct.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the complete sentence formed for the subject \'I\'?\",\"options\":[\"I is drawing a picture.\",\"I are drawing a picture.\",\"I am drawing a picture.\",\"I drawing a picture.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Using the table data, the subject \'I\' takes \'am\' and the verb \'draw\' becomes \'drawing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/079_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Analyze the sentence \'Students are completing their home work\'. Why is \'are\' used instead of \'is\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the action is in the past\",\"Because \'Students\' is a plural subject\",\"Because \'Students\' is a singular subject\",\"Because \'home work\' is the object\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In English grammar, \'are\' is used with plural subjects like \'Students\'.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the Present Continuous formula \'am\\/is\\/are + verb + ing\' specifically shows that the action is continuous?\",\"options\":[\"The subject\",\"The helping verb\",\"The \'ing\' suffix on the verb\",\"The object\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The addition of \'ing\' to the main verb indicates the continuous nature of the action.\",\"topic\":\"Present Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21786,32,6,'English','en','The Naughty Keyboard','[\"The naughty keyboard is a device that can make mistakes when typing.\",\"A keyboard can change words in an email without the user knowing.\",\"Bezzil is a wizard who lives in an enchanted house.\",\"The wizard can ask his kitchen, television, and other objects to do things.\",\"The story shows that computers can be helpful but also can cause problems.\",\"A keyboard can be bored and act mischievous.\",\"When the keyboard changed the word ‘table’ to ‘Antarctica’, it caused a misunderstanding.\",\"Bezzil fixed the mistake and the table was shipped correctly.\",\"The story teaches that we should check our messages before sending.\",\"A wizard is a person believed to have magic power.\",\"Enchanted means affected by magic powers.\",\"Packers and movers are professionals who help move things from one place to another.\",\"Mischievous means behaving badly or annoying people.\",\"A keyboard can feel emotions like boredom, fear, or sadness in the story.\",\"The story uses simple sentences to explain how a keyboard can be naughty.\",\"The chapter includes a word basket to learn new words.\",\"It also has a crossword puzzle to practice spelling.\",\"Students are asked to identify feelings of characters using emojis.\",\"The chapter encourages writing letters to friends about new gadgets.\",\"It also lists uses of common household appliances like washing machines and fridges.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did Bezzil the wizard live?\",\"options\":[\"In a modern apartment\",\"In an enchanted house\",\"In a computer shop\",\"In Antarctica\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Bezzil, the wizard, lived in an enchanted house.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To whom did Bezzil want to transport a table?\",\"options\":[\"To his sister\",\"To the packers and movers\",\"To his brother\",\"To the wizard\'s kitchen\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he wanted to transport a table to his brother.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the table supposed to be shipped?\",\"options\":[\"America\",\"Antarctica\",\"Australia\",\"The enchanted house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies the destination was Antarctica.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the keyboard replace the table\'s name with in the email?\",\"options\":[\"Bezzil\",\"The television\",\"Its own name\",\"Antarctica\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the keyboard replaced the table\'s name with its own.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'had a mind of its own\' mean regarding the items in Bezzil\'s house?\",\"options\":[\"The items were broken\",\"The items were very expensive\",\"The items could think and act independently\",\"The items were controlled by a remote\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the context of the enchanted house, it means the objects were sentient and could act on their own.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the keyboard decide to be naughty and change the email?\",\"options\":[\"It was angry with Bezzil\",\"It was bored\",\"It wanted to visit Antarctica\",\"It was broken\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'The keyboard was bored and decided to be naughty.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the television respond when Bezzil wanted to cheer up?\",\"options\":[\"It played loud music\",\"It turned itself off\",\"It switched to his favourite comedy show\",\"It showed him the news\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the television would switch to his favourite comedy show to cheer him up.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened when Bezzil asked the kitchen to cook food?\",\"options\":[\"Bezzil had to cook it himself\",\"The keyboard ordered food online\",\"Everything came together to fix a delicious meal\",\"The movers brought him food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes that everything in the kitchen would come together to fix a meal.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Bezzil needs to move a heavy object to another country, which service does he use according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The enchanted kitchen\",\"The television network\",\"Packers and movers\",\"The naughty keyboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Bezzil typed a mail to the \'packers and movers\' to transport the table.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text best describes the keyboard\'s personality?\",\"options\":[\"Helpful\",\"Mischievous\",\"Delicious\",\"Boring\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the words \'naughty\' and \'mischievous\' to describe the keyboard.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the movers ignore the keyboard\'s cries that there had been a mistake?\",\"options\":[\"They couldn\'t hear the keyboard\",\"They were following the written instructions in Bezzil\'s email\",\"They wanted to play a trick on Bezzil\",\"They were in a hurry to get to Antarctica\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The movers said, \'Bezzil\'s email said to ship you off to Antarctica,\' showing they relied on the written proof.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the consequence of the keyboard\'s prank?\",\"options\":[\"It successfully went on a trip to Antarctica\",\"It was thrown away by Bezzil\",\"It got scared and learned to be less naughty\",\"It made Bezzil lose his table forever\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the keyboard learned its lesson and tried to be less mischievous after the scare.\",\"topic\":\"The Naughty Keyboard\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the word basket, what is a \'wizard\'?\",\"options\":[\"A person believed to have magic power\",\"A person who moves furniture\",\"A person who behaves badly\",\"A person who carries goods\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines a wizard as a person who is believed to have magic power.\",\"topic\":\"Word basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'mess\' mean in the given text?\",\"options\":[\"A cry of pain\",\"The state of being untidy\",\"A professional service\",\"A magic spell\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines mess as the state of being untidy.\",\"topic\":\"Word basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is \'enchanted\', what has happened to them?\",\"options\":[\"They are moving to a new house\",\"They are feeling very annoyed\",\"They are affected by magic powers\",\"They are crying out in pain\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Enchanted is defined as being affected by magic powers.\",\"topic\":\"Word basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the phrase \'paid no heed\'?\",\"options\":[\"Paid for the transport\",\"Paid no attention\",\"Paid the movers\",\"Paid for magic powers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that \'paid no heed\' means \'paid no attention\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes a sudden short cry of pain?\",\"options\":[\"Mischievous\",\"Transport\",\"Yelped\",\"Enchanted\"]