eycomb, a house with thousands of six‑sided cells.\",\"Each cell is made of beeswax, produced by the bee itself.\",\"The bee feeds and protects larvae (baby bees) inside the comb.\",\"It fans its wings to keep the comb cool and to thicken nectar into honey.\",\"Nectar is a thin sweet liquid collected from flowers; pollen is yellow powdery pollen.\",\"The bee turns nectar into thick honey by evaporating water.\",\"Bees work together without fighting; teamwork builds perfect houses.\",\"The bee’s job changes with age: young bees guard larvae, older bees collect nectar and pollen.\",\"A bee’s routine: find a flower, sip nectar, fly back, store honey in a cell.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What name does the bee prefer to be called because of its hard work?\",\"options\":[\"A lazy bee\",\"A busy bee\",\"A honey bee\",\"A flower bee\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The bee explicitly states it is called a \'busy bee\' because it is hard at work.\",\"topic\":\"A Honey Bee Speaks: A Monologue\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main difference between what people think the bee does and what it actually does?\",\"options\":[\"People think it works; it actually plays\",\"People think it plays; it actually works\",\"People think it sleeps; it actually flies\",\"People think it is big; it actually is small\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The bee clarifies that flitting among flowers is hard work, not just having fun.\",\"topic\":\"A Honey Bee Speaks: A Monologue\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific rule for \'The Challenge\' mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Draw a flower\",\"Do not lift your pencil\",\"Draw a bee\",\"Use only one color\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the challenge as not lifting the pencil off the paper until the drawing is finished.\",\"topic\":\"A Honey Bee Speaks: A Monologue\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the bee offer to show the reader?\",\"options\":[\"The flowers\",\"Its house\",\"The honey\",\"The pencil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The bee says, \'Come, I\'ll show you my house\'.\",\"topic\":\"A Honey Bee Speaks: A Monologue\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following \'The Challenge\' to draw a honeycomb, what must you avoid doing?\",\"options\":[\"Using a pencil\",\"Lifting the pencil\",\"Drawing hexagons\",\"Looking at the paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states the pencil must not be lifted until the drawing is finished.\",\"topic\":\"A Honey Bee Speaks: A Monologue\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text would you use to describe a butterfly moving quickly from plant to plant?\",\"options\":[\"Simply\",\"Flitting\",\"Correct\",\"Busy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Flitting is the specific verb used in the text for moving lightly and quickly between flowers.\",\"topic\":\"A Honey Bee Speaks: A Monologue\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the bee start its monologue with \'Hmmmm... Hmmmm... ..What! Me, a lazy bee?\'\",\"options\":[\"To show it is angry\",\"To respond to a common misunderstanding\",\"To sing a song\",\"To introduce its name\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The bee is reacting to the common perception that it is lazy rather than hardworking.\",\"topic\":\"A Honey Bee Speaks: A Monologue\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes the bee\'s message to the reader?\",\"options\":[\"Work is fun\",\"Bees are lazy\",\"Bees are hard workers\",\"Flowers are beautiful\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The bee\'s monologue aims to prove that bees are industrious and work all their lives.\",\"topic\":\"A Honey Bee Speaks: A Monologue\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the bee flitting among?\",\"options\":[\"Trees\",\"Flowers\",\"Clouds\",\"Honeycombs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows the bee flying above several white flowers.\",\"topic\":\"A Honey Bee Speaks: A Monologue\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/083_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the bee is shown flying over flowers. According to the text, what is the purpose of this action?\",\"options\":[\"To show off its wings\",\"To perform hard work\",\"To take a rest\",\"To play with the petals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that while it looks like fun, the bee is actually working hard when flitting over flowers.\",\"topic\":\"A Honey Bee Speaks: A Monologue\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/083_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the honey bee\'s house mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A hive\",\"A honeycomb\",\"A nest\",\"A shelter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'My house is called a honeycomb.\'\",\"topic\":\"Work of a Young Bee\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many sides does each room or cell in the honeycomb have?\",\"options\":[\"Four equal sides\",\"Five equal sides\",\"Six equal sides\",\"Eight equal sides\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'Each room has six equal sides.\'\",\"topic\":\"Work of a Young Bee\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What material do the bees produce to build their comb?\",\"options\":[\"Honey\",\"Nectar\",\"Beeswax\",\"Mud\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the material they produce for building is called beeswax.\",\"topic\":\"Work of a Young Bee\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what are \'larvae\'?\",\"options\":[\"The rooms in the honeycomb\",\"The material used for building\",\"The babies that grow into bees\",\"The enemies of the bee\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines larvae as \'the babies that would grow into bees.\'\",\"topic\":\"Work of a Young Bee\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the young bee\'s primary responsibility while staying at home?\",\"options\":[\"To collect nectar from flowers\",\"To look after, feed, and protect the larvae\",\"To clean the outside of the honeycomb\",\"To produce honey for the queen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the young bee had to look after, feed, and protect the larvae.\",\"topic\":\"Work of a Young Bee\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the bee refer to itself as a \'soldier\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it builds strong walls\",\"Because it travels long distances\",\"Because it is ready to use its sting to protect the comb\",\"Because it works in a large group\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The bee says it is a soldier because it is ready with its sting if anyone disturbs the comb.\",\"topic\":\"Work of a Young Bee\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a predator approaches the honeycomb, what action would the young bee take based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"It would hide inside a cell\",\"It would fly away to find help\",\"It would use its sting to protect the comb\",\"It would start building more rooms\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'If anyone came near our comb to disturb it, I was ready with my sting!\'\",\"topic\":\"Work of a Young Bee\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which role does the young bee NOT perform according to the passage?\",\"options\":[\"Builder of the comb\",\"Feeder of the larvae\",\"Soldier protecting the house\",\"Gatherer of nectar from far away\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text focuses on the young bee staying at home; gathering nectar is not mentioned as a duty for the young bee here.\",\"topic\":\"Work of a Young Bee\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What can we conclude about the nature of a young bee\'s life from the text?\",\"options\":[\"It is very easy and involves only resting\",\"It involves a lot of work even when staying at home\",\"It is spent entirely outside the honeycomb\",\"It involves only building and no other duties\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The bee says, \'when I was very young... even then I had to do a lot of work.\'\",\"topic\":\"Work of a Young Bee\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the bee say \'Beware, don\'t trouble me!\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is too busy to talk\",\"Because it is warning others of its ability to sting as a soldier\",\"Because it is afraid of strangers\",\"Because it wants to keep the beeswax a secret\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The warning follows the bee\'s description of being a soldier ready with a sting.\",\"topic\":\"Work of a Young Bee\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does the honey bee keep the comb cool?\",\"options\":[\"By fanning it with its wings\",\"By bringing water from flowers\",\"By moving to a shady place\",\"By building thicker walls\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states the bee had to keep the comb cool by fanning it with its wings.\",\"topic\":\"Keeping the house in order\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the bee do to keep the house in order?\",\"options\":[\"Cleans the floor of the comb\",\"Puts away the honey and food brought by other bees\",\"Chases away other insects\",\"Decorates the entrance of the hive\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions keeping the house in order involves putting away all the honey and food.\",\"topic\":\"Keeping the house in order\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many bees work together?\",\"options\":[\"Only two or three\",\"A dozen bees\",\"Hundreds of other bees\",\"Thousands of different insects\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The bee mentions having hundreds of other bees working with it.\",\"topic\":\"Keeping the house in order\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main reason bees can build perfect and beautiful houses?\",\"options\":[\"They use special mud from flowers\",\"They work together without ever fighting\",\"They are very old and wise\",\"They work only during the day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says working together without fighting is one reason they can build perfect houses.\",\"topic\":\"Keeping the house in order\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why do the bees keep building more and more rooms?\",\"options\":[\"To make the house look bigger than others\",\"To hide from the wind and rain\",\"For the babies and for the food and honey they gather\",\"To allow every bee to have a separate bedroom\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states rooms are built for the babies and for all the food and honey gathered.\",\"topic\":\"Keeping the house in order\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a bee is \'fanning\', which part of its body is it actively using?\",\"options\":[\"Its legs\",\"Its sting\",\"Its wings\",\"Its antennae\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions fanning with \'wings\'.\",\"topic\":\"Keeping the house in order\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what do other bees bring from the flowers?\",\"options\":[\"Only nectar\",\"Honey and food\",\"Wax and sticks\",\"Water and leaves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'honey and food that other bees brought from the flowers\'.\",\"topic\":\"Keeping the house in order\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the way bees work together according to the passage?\",\"options\":[\"Selfish\",\"Peaceful\",\"Slow\",\"Noisy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they work together \'without ever fighting\', which implies a peaceful cooperation.\",\"topic\":\"Keeping the house in order\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If a group of bees started fighting, what would be the likely result according to the text\'s logic?\",\"options\":[\"They would build houses faster\",\"They would not be able to build perfect houses\",\"They would find more honey\",\"The babies would grow faster\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links the lack of fighting to the ability to build perfect and beautiful houses.\",\"topic\":\"Keeping the house in order\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the \'house\' referred to in the phrase \'building more and more rooms in our house\'?\",\"options\":[\"A garden\",\"A flower\",\"A comb\",\"A tree hole\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The passage begins by referring \'back to the comb\' as the place they are building and cooling.\",\"topic\":\"Keeping the house in order\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is nectar according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The yellow powdery stuff on flowers\",\"The sweet juice in flowers\",\"A thin type of honey\",\"The wax used to build combs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines nectar as the sweet juice in flowers.\",\"topic\":\"Gathering Nectar and Making Honey\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the \'yellow powdery stuff\' seen on flowers called?\",\"options\":[\"Nectar\",\"Honey\",\"Pollen\",\"Juice\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that pollen is the yellow powdery stuff you see on flowers.\",\"topic\":\"Gathering Nectar and Making Honey\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the yellow center of the flower where the bee is sitting contains:\",\"options\":[\"Nectar and pollen\",\"Only honey\",\"Water for the bee\",\"The bee\'s home\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text and figure show that bees visit flowers to gather nectar and pollen from them.\",\"topic\":\"Gathering Nectar and Making Honey\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/084_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how do bees change nectar to make honey?\",\"options\":[\"They make it thinner\",\"They turn it into yellow powder\",\"They turn the thin nectar into sweet thick honey\",\"They mix it with water from the comb\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that bees turn thin nectar into sweet thick honey.\",\"topic\":\"Gathering Nectar and Making Honey\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When does a honey bee start flying out of the comb to gather nectar?\",\"options\":[\"As soon as it is born\",\"When it becomes older\",\"Only when it is called lazy\",\"When the nectar becomes thick\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The bee mentions, \'When I became older, I began to fly out of the comb...\'\",\"topic\":\"Gathering Nectar and Making Honey\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the bee doing while sitting on the flower?\",\"options\":[\"Taking a rest because it is lazy\",\"Gathering nectar and pollen to carry back\",\"Waiting for the juice to become thick\",\"Playing with the yellow powdery stuff\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that bees visit flowers to gather nectar and pollen and carry them back to the comb.\",\"topic\":\"Gathering Nectar and Making Honey\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/084_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a honey bee visits hundreds of flowers and makes several trips daily, which word best describes its behavior?\",\"options\":[\"Lazy\",\"Slow\",\"Hardworking\",\"Careless\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The bee\'s description of visiting hundreds of flowers without wasting a moment shows it is hardworking.\",\"topic\":\"Gathering Nectar and Making Honey\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What would happen if a bee \'wasted a single moment\' while working?\",\"options\":[\"It would make more honey\",\"It would not be able to visit hundreds of flowers\",\"The nectar would turn thick instantly\",\"It would stay younger for longer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The bee emphasizes not wasting a moment to complete its heavy workload of visiting hundreds of flowers.\",\"topic\":\"Gathering Nectar and Making Honey\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the bee stop its work to talk to the listener?\",\"options\":[\"It wanted to take a long break\",\"It was tired of flying to flowers\",\"It wanted to explain it wasn\'t lazy\",\"It had finished making all the honey\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The bee says it only stopped because the listener called it a \'lazy bee\'.\",\"topic\":\"Gathering Nectar and Making Honey\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phrases from the text shows that the bee is very busy?\",\"options\":[\"\'I became older\'\",\"\'Sweet juice in flowers\'\",\"\'I have not a moment to lose\'\",\"\'Yellow powdery stuff\'\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'not a moment to lose\' indicates that the bee has a lot of work and no time to waste.\",\"topic\":\"Gathering Nectar and Making Honey\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is another name for the Past Continuous Tense according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Past Simple Tense\",\"Past Progressive Tense\",\"Past Perfect Tense\",\"Future Continuous Tense\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the Past Continuous Tense is also called the Past Progressive Tense.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When do we use the Past Continuous Tense?\",\"options\":[\"When actions are going to happen in the future\",\"When actions are finished long ago\",\"When actions were ongoing at a specific time in the past\",\"When actions happen every day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines this tense as being used when actions were ongoing at a specific time in the past.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct structure for the Past Continuous Tense?\",\"options\":[\"is\\/am\\/are + verb + ing\",\"was\\/were + verb + ing\",\"was\\/were + verb + ed\",\"has\\/have + verb + ing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the formula: was\\/were + verb + ing.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the vocabulary list, what is a \'monologue\'?\",\"options\":[\"A conversation between two people\",\"A short poem about bees\",\"A long speech by one person\",\"A song sung by a group\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines monologue as a long speech by one person.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'We were playing cricket\', which word is the helping verb?\",\"options\":[\"We\",\"were\",\"playing\",\"cricket\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the structure \'was\\/were + verb + ing\', \'were\' acts as the helping verb.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the correct sentence for Sr. No. 2?\",\"options\":[\"Children was singing a song.\",\"Children were sing a song.\",\"Children were singing a song.\",\"Children singing a song.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since \'Children\' is plural, the helping verb is \'were\', and the verb \'sing\' becomes \'singing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/085_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which helping verb and verb form should be used for Sr. No. 4?\",\"options\":[\"were, drawing\",\"was, draw\",\"was, drawing\",\"were, draw\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"For the subject \'I\', the helping verb is \'was\', and the verb \'draw\' changes to \'drawing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/085_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the sentence that is in the Past Continuous Tense.\",\"options\":[\"The bee flies to the flower.\",\"The bee will fly to the flower.\",\"The bee was flying around the flower.\",\"The bee has flown to the flower.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'was flying\' follows the was\\/were + verb + ing rule mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the subject is \'Mother\' as shown in the table, which sentence is grammatically correct according to the Past Continuous rules?\",\"options\":[\"Mother was cooking dinner.\",\"Mother were cooking dinner.\",\"Mother was cook dinner.\",\"Mother cooking dinner.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Mother\' is a singular subject, so \'was\' is the correct helping verb followed by \'cooking\'.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'were\' used in the sentence \'Students were practicing yoga\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the action is happening now\",\"Because \'Students\' is a plural subject\",\"Because \'yoga\' is a singular object\",\"Because the sentence is a monologue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In English grammar, \'were\' is used with plural subjects like \'Students\'.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the \'sweet liquid that bees collect from the flower\' called?\",\"options\":[\"Larvae\",\"Honey\",\"Nectar\",\"Flitting\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines nectar as the sweet liquid bees collect to make honey.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the sentence \'Seeta was reading a novel last night\' indicates the action was ongoing in the past?\",\"options\":[\"Seeta\",\"a novel\",\"was reading\",\"last night\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The verb phrase \'was reading\' (was + verb + ing) indicates the Past Continuous Tense.\",\"topic\":\"Past Continuous tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the sound symbol for the letter \'b\' as in the word \'bat\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/p\\/\",\"\\/d\\/\",\"\\/b\\/\",\"\\/v\\/\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the table, the letter \'b\' represents the sound \\/b\\/.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two sets of letters are listed in the text as representing the sound \\/f\\/?\",\"options\":[\"f and v\",\"f and ph\",\"p and ph\",\"f and p\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'f, ph\' as the letters for the sound \\/f\\/.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, the letter \'c\' is pronounced as \\/s\\/ when it is followed by which letters?\",\"options\":[\"a, o, or u\",\"b, d, or f\",\"e, i, or y\",\"k, l, or m\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'c\' is pronounced as \\/s\\/ when followed by e (cy, ci, ce).\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which sound symbol represents the \'ch\' sound found in the words \'chair\' and \'child\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/ʃ\\/\",\"\\/tʃ\\/\",\"\\/dʒ\\/\",\"\\/h\\/\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows the letters \'ch\' correspond to the sound \\/tʃ\\/.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words has the same consonant sound as the \'ph\' in \'phone\'?\",\"options\":[\"van\",\"fish\",\"pen\",\"bag\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both \'fish\' (f) and \'phone\' (ph) represent the \\/f\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the examples provided in the text contains the sound \\/ŋ\\/?\",\"options\":[\"man\",\"net\",\"sing\",\"red\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'sing\' as an example for the sound \\/ŋ\\/.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The words \'think\' and \'this\' both start with \'th\'. According to the table, which sound symbol belongs specifically to the word \'think\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/θ\\/\",\"\\/ð\\/\",\"\\/t\\/\",\"\\/h\\/\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table distinguishes \'think\' with the symbol \\/θ\\/ and \'this\' with \\/ð\\/.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the examples in the text, in which word is the letter \'g\' pronounced as \\/dʒ\\/?\",\"options\":[\"go\",\"girl\",\"bag\",\"giant\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'giant\' as an example where \'g\' makes the \\/dʒ\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which sound symbol is used for the letter \'y\' in the word \'yes\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/y\\/\",\"\\/j\\/\",\"\\/w\\/\",\"\\/i\\/\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows the sound symbol \\/j\\/ for the letter \'y\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/086_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word is provided as an example for the sound \\/ʃ\\/?\",\"options\":[\"sun\",\"ship\",\"chair\",\"think\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure lists \'ship\' as the first example for the \\/ʃ\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/086_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the letter \'c\' is followed by \'o\' as in the word \'cook\', which sound does it make according to the rules in the text?\",\"options\":[\"\\/s\\/\",\"\\/k\\/\",\"\\/ch\\/\",\"\\/g\\/\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'c\' is pronounced as \\/k\\/ when followed by a\\/o\\/u.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the table\'s examples ends with the sound \\/d\\/?\",\"options\":[\"dog\",\"door\",\"bed\",\"red\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the word \'bed\', the \\/d\\/ sound comes at the end, whereas in \'dog\' and \'door\' it is at the start.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Consonant sounds\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21788,32,6,'English','en','Homework Machine','[\"Homework Machine is a fun idea that shows how machines can do work quickly.\",\"The poem says the machine takes about ten seconds to finish homework.\",\"It needs a dime (a small coin) to start the machine.\",\"The machine gives wrong answers sometimes, e.g., it says 9+4=3.\",\"Machines can work only as programmed and can make mistakes but cannot feel emotions.\",\"Humans can think, feel, learn, and need food, water, rest; machines need power and do not feel.\",\"Repetition, personification, and alliteration are figure‑of‑speech examples in the poem.\",\"Repetition: “Your homework comes out, quick and clean as can be.”\",\"Personification: “quick and clean” gives human quality to the homework.\",\"Alliteration: “The Homework Machine, Oh, the Homework Machine.”\",\"Machines are useful but should not replace human thinking.\",\"Using phones in exams is banned because they can help students cheat.\",\"The poem invites us to think about the limits of machines and the value of human effort.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the author of the poem \'The Homework Machine\'?\",\"options\":[\"Shel Silverstein\",\"Balbharati\",\"William Wordsworth\",\"Robert Frost\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions Shel Silverstein at the end of the poem.\",\"topic\":\"Homework Machine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How much time does the machine take to process the homework?\",\"options\":[\"Ten minutes\",\"Ten seconds\",\"One hour\",\"Five seconds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'and in ten second\'s time. Your homework comes out\'.\",\"topic\":\"Homework Machine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What must be dropped into the machine to make it work?\",\"options\":[\"A penny\",\"A nickel\",\"A dime\",\"A switch\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says to \'drop in a dime\' after putting in the homework.\",\"topic\":\"Homework Machine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the poem, what does the word \'contraption\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"A type of homework\",\"A machine or device\",\"A ten-second timer\",\"A math problem\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The speaker calls the Homework Machine a \'perfect contraption\', meaning a mechanical device.\",\"topic\":\"Homework Machine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does the homework appear when it comes out of the machine?\",\"options\":[\"Messy and wrong\",\"Quick and clean\",\"Slow and dirty\",\"Torn and wet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem describes the output as \'quick and clean as can be\'.\",\"topic\":\"Homework Machine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the speaker say \'Oh me . . .\' at the end of the poem?\",\"options\":[\"He is happy with the result\",\"He is tired of waiting\",\"He is disappointed or worried by the error\",\"He forgot to drop in a dime\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The speaker realizes the machine gave a wrong answer (\'three\' for \'nine plus four\') and expresses doubt.\",\"topic\":\"Homework Machine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the specific word written on the yellow and pink machine?\",\"options\":[\"Robot\",\"Printer\",\"Homework\",\"School\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the word \'Homework\' clearly printed on the front of the machine.\",\"topic\":\"Homework Machine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/087_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the boy holding in his hand as he looks at the machine?\",\"options\":[\"A dime\",\"A piece of paper\",\"A school bag\",\"A mobile phone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the boy holding a white sheet of paper, presumably his homework.\",\"topic\":\"Homework Machine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/087_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"The machine calculates \'nine plus four\' as \'three\'. What is the correct mathematical answer?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"13\",\"14\",\"15\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem shows the machine\'s error; the actual sum of 9 + 4 is 13.\",\"topic\":\"Homework Machine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem\'s ending, why is the machine \'not as perfect\' as the speaker first thought?\",\"options\":[\"It takes too much money\",\"It is too noisy\",\"It gives incorrect answers to simple problems\",\"It is too big for the room\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The speaker concludes it\'s not perfect because it incorrectly calculated 9+4 as 3.\",\"topic\":\"Homework Machine\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is a \'contraption\'?\",\"options\":[\"A simple wooden tool\",\"A strange piece of equipment or device\",\"A type of American coin\",\"A button for an electric circuit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a contraption as a strange piece of equipment or device.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the value of a \'dime\' as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Five cents\",\"One dollar\",\"Ten cents\",\"Twenty cents\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that a dime is an American coin worth ten cents.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'ever\' mean in the context of the vocabulary list?\",\"options\":[\"Never at any time\",\"Only in the future\",\"At any time upto now\",\"Every single day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The definition provided for \'ever\' is \'at any time upto now\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which device is used for opening or closing an electric circuit?\",\"options\":[\"A dime\",\"A contraption\",\"A switch\",\"A snap\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a switch as a button or device for opening or closing an electric circuit.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to start the Homework Machine, they would need to \'____\' it.\",\"options\":[\"dime\",\"snap on\",\"ever\",\"circuit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'snap on\' as \'to switch on\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a boy has two \'dimes\' in his pocket, how many cents does he have in total?\",\"options\":[\"Five cents\",\"Ten cents\",\"Twenty cents\",\"Fifty cents\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since one dime is ten cents, two dimes equal twenty cents.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is described specifically as an \'American coin\'?\",\"options\":[\"Switch\",\"Dime\",\"Contraption\",\"Snap\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the dime as an American coin.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How would you describe a machine that looks very unusual and strange based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"A circuit\",\"A switch\",\"A contraption\",\"A dime\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A strange piece of equipment is called a contraption.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the relationship between \'snap on\' and a \'switch\'?\",\"options\":[\"A switch is used to snap on a device\",\"They are both types of coins\",\"Snap on is a type of strange equipment\",\"A switch is worth ten cents\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A switch is a device for circuits, and \'snap on\' means to switch something on.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which term refers to the action of activating an electric circuit?\",\"options\":[\"Dime\",\"Ever\",\"Snap on\",\"Contraption\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Snap on means to switch on, which activates the circuit via the switch.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21789,32,6,'English','en','The Lifeline of Godavari River','[\"Godavari River is the lifeline of Maharashtra because it supplies drinking water, irrigation and supports many crops like rice, sugarcane, cotton and wheat.\",\"It originates at Trimbakeshwar in the Western Ghats near Nashik and flows 1,465 km through Maharashtra, Telangana and Andhra Pradesh before emptying into the Bay of Bengal.\",\"The river is sacred; the Kumbh Mela, a major pilgrimage, is held on its banks in Nashik every twelve years.\",\"It is the second longest river in India after the Ganges and supports millions of people socially, culturally and economically.\",\"Rivers are called lifelines because they provide water for drinking, agriculture, industry, transport and are essential for life.\",\"Godavari faces challenges such as industrial waste, sewage, plastic pollution and other pollution that threaten its health.\",\"Protecting the river requires joint effort from citizens, government and environmental groups; schools can educate people about river conservation.\",\"The river’s tributaries are small rivers that flow into it; they also support local communities.\",\"The Godavari’s wide expanse of land, water and sky is called the expanse; it is a large open area.\",\"The river’s importance is not only geographical but also cultural and religious.\",\"Water from the Godavari is stored in dams and reservoirs for use during dry seasons.\",\"The river supports a variety of plants, fish, birds and animals.\",\"The Godavari has influenced Maharashtra’s culture and traditions for centuries.\",\"World River Day is celebrated on the 4th Sunday of September to raise awareness about rivers.\",\"The river’s health is vital for the well‑being of all who depend on it.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the rank of the Godavari river in terms of length in India?\",\"options\":[\"First longest\",\"Second longest\",\"Third longest\",\"Fourth longest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Godavari is the second longest river in India after the Ganges.\",\"topic\":\"The Lifeline of Maharashtra\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which specific location does the Godavari river originate?\",\"options\":[\"Mahabaleshwar\",\"Trimbakeshwar\",\"Gangotri\",\"Niphad\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the Godavari originates in Trimbakeshwar, near the city of Nashik.\",\"topic\":\"The Lifeline of Maharashtra\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the Godavari river referred to as the \'lifeline of Maharashtra\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is the only river in India\",\"Because it flows into the Ganges\",\"Because it supports drinking water, agriculture, and economic activities\",\"Because it is located in the Western Ghats\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains it is the lifeline because it supports drinking water supply, agriculture, culture, and economic activities.\",\"topic\":\"The Lifeline of Maharashtra\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How frequently is the famous pilgrimage \'Kumbh Mela\' held in Nashik?\",\"options\":[\"Every six years\",\"Every ten years\",\"Every twelve years\",\"Every year\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the Kumbh Mela is held in Nashik after every twelve years.\",\"topic\":\"The Lifeline of Maharashtra\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is NOT mentioned as a sector supported by the Godavari river?\",\"options\":[\"Agriculture\",\"Space Exploration\",\"Culture\",\"Economic activities\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions drinking water, agriculture, culture, and economic activities, but not space exploration.\",\"topic\":\"The Lifeline of Maharashtra\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a farmer in Maharashtra uses water from the Godavari to grow his crops, which role of the river is he utilizing?\",\"options\":[\"Pilgrimage\",\"Agriculture\",\"Mountain Range\",\"Western Ghats\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using water for crops is part of agriculture, which the text says the river supports.\",\"topic\":\"The Lifeline of Maharashtra\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which lake is located on the Godavari river just to the west of Nashik city?\",\"options\":[\"Darna Lake\",\"Gangapur Lake\",\"Nandur Madhameshwar\",\"Anjaneri Lake\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The map shows Gangapur Lake situated on the Godavari river upstream (west) of Nashik.\",\"topic\":\"The Lifeline of Maharashtra\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/089_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the direction indicator in the given figure, in which general direction does the Godavari flow from Nashik towards Niphad?\",\"options\":[\"West\",\"South\",\"East\",\"North\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the compass rose and the river path, the flow from Nashik to Niphad is towards the East.\",\"topic\":\"The Lifeline of Maharashtra\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/089_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"The text describes the Godavari as a \'sacred\' river. This description is most closely linked to which activity?\",\"options\":[\"Drinking water supply\",\"Economic activities\",\"The Kumbh Mela pilgrimage\",\"Industrial growth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sacred nature of the river is linked to religious pilgrimages like the Kumbh Mela.\",\"topic\":\"The Lifeline of Maharashtra\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A travel agency planning a tour for devotees to visit the origin of the Godavari would send them to which mountain range mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Himalayas\",\"Western Ghats\",\"Eastern Ghats\",\"Satpura Range\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the river originates in Trimbakeshwar in the Western Ghats.\",\"topic\":\"The Lifeline of Maharashtra\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the Godavari river begin its journey?\",\"options\":[\"Bay of Bengal\",\"Trimbakeshwar\",\"Telangana\",\"Andhra Pradesh\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Godavari begins its journey from Trimbakeshwar.\",\"topic\":\"Journey of the River\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the total length of the Godavari river?\",\"options\":[\"1,265 kilometres\",\"1,465 kilometres\",\"1,645 kilometres\",\"1,500 kilometres\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the total length of the river is about 1,465 kilometres.\",\"topic\":\"Journey of the River\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Into which water body does the Godavari river finally empty?\",\"options\":[\"Arabian Sea\",\"Indian Ocean\",\"Bay of Bengal\",\"Dead Sea\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the river flows through several states before finally emptying into the Bay of Bengal.\",\"topic\":\"Journey of the River\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Across which large landform does the Godavari flow after starting at Trimbakeshwar?\",\"options\":[\"The Himalayan Range\",\"The Thar Desert\",\"The Deccan Plateau\",\"The Coastal Plains\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that the river begins its journey across the wide expanse of the Deccan Plateau.\",\"topic\":\"Journey of the River\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In which state does the majority or \'bulk\' of the Godavari river flow?\",\"options\":[\"Telangana\",\"Andhra Pradesh\",\"Maharashtra\",\"Karnataka\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the bulk of Godavari passes through Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"Journey of the River\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, the Godavari is vital from which points of view besides geographical?\",\"options\":[\"Industrial and technological\",\"Social, cultural and religious\",\"Political and military\",\"Scientific and space-related\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions it is vital from a social, cultural and religious point of view.\",\"topic\":\"Journey of the River\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a traveler follows the river from its source to its end, which sequence of states would they pass through?\",\"options\":[\"Maharashtra, Telangana, and Andhra Pradesh\",\"Andhra Pradesh, Telangana, and Maharashtra\",\"Maharashtra, Karnataka, and Kerala\",\"Telangana, Andhra Pradesh, and Maharashtra\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text describes the flow starting in Maharashtra (Trimbakeshwar), then through Telangana and Andhra Pradesh.\",\"topic\":\"Journey of the River\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does the Godavari river support the people living near its banks?\",\"options\":[\"By providing a path for high-speed trains\",\"By nourishing the land and sustaining communities\",\"By acting as a border between countries\",\"By cooling the temperature of the entire continent\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the river nourishes the land and sustains communities that stay around it.\",\"topic\":\"Journey of the River\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the Godavari described as more than just a \'geographical\' feature in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is the only river in India\",\"Because it flows in a straight line\",\"Because it has deep social, cultural, and religious importance to people\",\"Because it is exactly 1,465 kilometres long\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text highlights its impact on communities and its social, cultural, and religious significance.\",\"topic\":\"Journey of the River\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these statements best summarizes the journey of the Godavari based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"It is a short river that stays within the Deccan Plateau.\",\"It is a long river that sustains life and culture across multiple states.\",\"It is a religious river that does not have any geographical importance.\",\"It is a river that starts in the Bay of Bengal and flows to Trimbakeshwar.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes its long path, the states it crosses, and its role in sustaining land and culture.\",\"topic\":\"Journey of the River\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these crops is mentioned in the text as being nurtured by the Godavari river?\",\"options\":[\"Maize\",\"Sugarcane\",\"Jowar\",\"Bajra\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions rice, sugarcane, cotton, and wheat as crops nurtured by the river.\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and Ecology\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the water from the Godavari stored to be used during dry seasons?\",\"options\":[\"In large wells\",\"In underground pipes\",\"In dams and reservoirs\",\"In plastic tanks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that water is stored in dams and reservoirs for use during dry seasons.\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and Ecology\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'Word Basket\' in the given figure, what is the meaning of the word \'tributaries\'?\",\"options\":[\"Large rivers that flow into the sea\",\"Small rivers that flow into a large river\",\"The waste matter from a city\",\"A large open area of land\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure defines tributaries as \'small rivers that flow into large river\'.\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and Ecology\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/090_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why do farmers consider the Godavari and its tributaries a \'big blessing\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the water is very cold\",\"Because it helps in growing crops like rice and cotton\",\"Because it is the longest river in the world\",\"Because it flows only during the rainy season\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says farmers consider it a blessing because it nurtures crops such as rice, sugarcane, cotton, and wheat.\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and Ecology\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which word from the \'Word Basket\' means \'to need someone or something\'?\",\"options\":[\"originates\",\"sacred\",\"rely on\",\"expanse\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure defines \'rely on\' as \'to need someone or something\'.\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and Ecology\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/090_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text imply when it says the river is a \'home\' to plants and animals?\",\"options\":[\"Animals build houses on the river banks\",\"The river is a natural habitat for various species\",\"People keep their pets in the river\",\"Plants are grown in pots inside the river\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Being a \'home\' to plants, fish, birds, and animals means the river provides a natural environment for them to live.\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and Ecology\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a new settlement is built along the banks of the Godavari, what will they most likely use the river for daily, based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"For generating electricity only\",\"For swimming competitions\",\"For their daily water supply\",\"For washing their cars\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that many settlements along the banks rely on the river for daily water supply.\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and Ecology\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A farmer wants to grow wheat during a period when there is no rain. Based on the text, how does the Godavari help?\",\"options\":[\"By providing water stored in dams and reservoirs\",\"By making the air very humid\",\"By changing the direction of the wind\",\"By providing sacred sand for the fields\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states water is stored in dams and reservoirs for use during dry seasons.\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and Ecology\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of the following best describes the ecological role of the Godavari?\",\"options\":[\"It is only a source of income for the government\",\"It is a life-supporting system for both humans and wildlife\",\"It is primarily a place for waste disposal\",\"It is only useful for growing sugarcane\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows the river supports human settlements (drinking water\\/crops) and wildlife (home to plants, fish, birds, and animals).\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and Ecology\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement best summarizes why the Godavari is important for the region\'s economy and nature?\",\"options\":[\"It is a sacred river that people visit for respect\",\"It provides waste matter called sewage for the land\",\"It supports agriculture, provides drinking water, and acts as a habitat for wildlife\",\"It originates in a particular place and flows into the sea\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text covers its importance for farmers (crops), settlements (drinking water), and ecology (home to plants and animals).\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and Ecology\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is mentioned as a specific challenge threatening the Godavari river?\",\"options\":[\"Excessive rainfall\",\"Industrial waste\",\"Lack of fish\",\"High water speed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists industrial waste, sewage, and plastic as challenges that threaten the river.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"For how long has the Godavari influenced the culture and traditions of Maharashtra?\",\"options\":[\"For a few decades\",\"For many years\",\"For centuries\",\"Since last year\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Godavari has influenced the culture and traditions of the people of Maharashtra for centuries.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which groups can play a major role in educating people about rivers?\",\"options\":[\"Factories and industries\",\"Only government officials\",\"Schools, colleges, and communities\",\"International tourists\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that schools, colleges, and other communities of our society can play a major role in education.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What will happen to us if the Godavari is affected by waste?\",\"options\":[\"We will not be affected at all\",\"We will find a new river\",\"We who depend on her will also be affected\",\"Only the fish will be affected\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that if the river is affected by waste, then those who depend on her will also be affected.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is essential to preserve the Godavari river?\",\"options\":[\"Citizens, government, and organizations working jointly\",\"Building more factories near the river\",\"Stopping all use of the river water\",\"Letting only the government handle it\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text emphasizes that it is essential for citizens, governmental bodies, and environmental organizations to work jointly.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the term \'lifeline\' suggest about the Godavari in this context?\",\"options\":[\"It is a line drawn on a map\",\"It is a source of life and support for the people\",\"It is a dangerous place to swim\",\"It is a boundary between states\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The context of being \'depended on\' and influencing \'culture\' shows it is a vital source of life.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to help the Godavari based on the text, what is the best action for their school to take?\",\"options\":[\"Organizing a trip to a factory\",\"Educating people about the value of rivers\",\"Building a new bridge over the river\",\"Moving the school away from the river\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests schools play a role in educating people about the value and responsibility towards rivers.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which action demonstrates using the river\'s resources \'with wisdom\'?\",\"options\":[\"Dumping plastic only in small amounts\",\"Using the water carefully and keeping it clean\",\"Allowing sewage to flow into the river\",\"Ignoring the challenges the river faces\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using resources with wisdom implies caring for the river and avoiding the waste mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the joint effort of citizens and government necessary for the Godavari?\",\"options\":[\"Because the river is too long to clean\",\"Because the river\'s existence is threatened by waste\",\"Because the river has no beauty left\",\"Because schools are not allowed to help\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links the threat to the river\'s existence to the need for joint preservation efforts.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the relationship between the river and the people of Maharashtra?\",\"options\":[\"The river is only used for industrial waste\",\"The people have no responsibility towards the river\",\"The river is a cultural lifeline that people depend on\",\"The river is a new discovery for the people\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the river as a lifeline that has influenced culture and traditions for centuries.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary condition mentioned for the Godavari to \'continue to be our lifeline\'?\",\"options\":[\"If we build more schools near it\",\"If we care for her and use resources with wisdom\",\"If we stop all industrial activities in Maharashtra\",\"If we only use plastic in the river\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The final sentence states it will continue to be a lifeline if we care for her and use resources with wisdom.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best summarizes the author\'s message regarding the Godavari?\",\"options\":[\"The river is beautiful and needs no help\",\"Only the government is responsible for the river\",\"Collective responsibility and education are key to saving the river\",\"Industrial waste is the only problem the river faces\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text highlights the need for joint work, education, and wise resource use to preserve the river.\",\"topic\":\"Challenges and Conservation\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'originates\'?\",\"options\":[\"To end at a specific location\",\"To appear for the first time in a particular place\",\"To flow into a larger body of water\",\"To become dirty with waste matter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, originates means to appear for the first time in a particular place.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If something is described as \'sacred\', how is it considered?\",\"options\":[\"As a large open area\",\"As something to be ignored\",\"As holy and deserving respect\",\"As a small part of a river\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines sacred as being considered holy and deserving respect.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are \'tributaries\'?\",\"options\":[\"Large oceans that connect to land\",\"The waste matter found in rivers\",\"Small rivers that flow into a large river\",\"The starting points of all rivers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tributaries are defined as small rivers that flow into a large river.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes a large open area of land, water, and sky?\",\"options\":[\"Expanse\",\"Sewage\",\"Sacred\",\"Originates\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"An expanse is defined as a large open area of land, water, and sky.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the term \'sewage\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"Fresh rainwater\",\"Small flowing streams\",\"The waste matter\",\"Holy water from a river\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines sewage simply as the waste matter.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a village must have water from the Godavari river to survive, we can say the villagers _____ the river.\",\"options\":[\"originate\",\"rely on\",\"sewage\",\"tributary\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"To \'rely on\' means to need someone or something, which fits the context of needing water.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A scientist finds a spot where a new stream first appears on a mountain. This spot is where the stream _____.\",\"options\":[\"tributaries\",\"sewage\",\"originates\",\"expanses\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Originates means to appear for the first time in a particular place.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these best describes the relationship between a small stream and a large river it joins?\",\"options\":[\"The small stream is an expanse of the river.\",\"The small stream is a tributary of the large river.\",\"The small stream is the sewage of the large river.\",\"The small stream is the sacred part of the river.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since the small stream flows into the large river, it meets the definition of a tributary.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the definition of \'expanse\', which of the following would be an example?\",\"options\":[\"A small bottle of water\",\"A single drop of rain\",\"A vast, wide desert under the open sky\",\"A pipe carrying waste matter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A vast desert under the sky fits the definition of a large open area of land and sky.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a river is treated with great respect and people perform prayers there, which word from the text best explains why?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is sewage\",\"Because it is an expanse\",\"Because it is sacred\",\"Because it has tributaries\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sacred means considered to be holy and deserving respect.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21790,32,6,'English','en','Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup','[\"Nasreddin Hodja is a wise judge who listens carefully before deciding.\",\"He is known for his clever, humorous solutions to problems.\",\"In the story, he pays the beggar for the smell of soup, showing fairness.\",\"The beggar wanted only the smell of soup, not the food.\",\"The innkeeper demanded payment for the smell, which is unfair.\",\"Hodja teaches the innkeeper that paying for a smell is absurd.\",\"The story shows that justice can be achieved through wit.\",\"Key vocabulary: stare, savoury, cauldrons, stammered, beckoned, dragged off, protest, terrified, beckoned.\",\"Stare means to look at something for a long time.\",\"Savoury means a salty, not sweet, taste.\",\"Cauldrons are large pots used for cooking over fire.\",\"Stammered means speaking with difficulty, often repeating sounds.\",\"Beckoned means to invite someone closer with a gesture.\",\"Dragged off means pulled someone forcefully away from a place.\",\"Protest means to say you do not agree with something.\",\"Terrified means feeling very afraid.\",\"Future continuous tense is used for planned future actions (e.g. ‘will be playing’).\",\"In future continuous, use ‘will\\/shall + be + verb+ing’.\",\"The beggar’s action changes from present to past to future continuous tense.\",\"The story encourages reading more humorous tales of Nasreddin Hodja, Tenali Raman, Akbar, and Birbal.\",\"It also encourages sharing stories in class as speaking activities.\",\"The lesson shows that fairness and humor can solve disputes.\",\"The story uses simple language suitable for Standard‑6 students.\",\"It helps students practice new vocabulary and grammar points.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did the beggar have to eat at the beginning of the story?\",\"options\":[\"A bowl of savoury soup\",\"A small piece of dry, old bread\",\"A fresh loaf of bread from the market\",\"A portion of food from the restaurant\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the beggar had a small piece of bread, dry and old, and that was all he had to eat that day.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who did the innkeeper take the beggar to for judgment?\",\"options\":[\"The King\",\"The rich people in the inn\",\"Nasreddin Hodja\",\"The market police\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the innkeeper dragged him off to Nasreddin Hodja, the judge.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the innkeeper angry with the beggar?\",\"options\":[\"The beggar stole a bowl of soup\",\"The beggar entered the inn without permission\",\"The beggar was enjoying the smell of the soup without paying\",\"The beggar broke a cauldron\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The innkeeper insisted the beggar must pay for the smell of the soup he was enjoying.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'stammered\' suggest about the beggar\'s state of mind?\",\"options\":[\"He was very angry\",\"He was confused and terrified\",\"He was feeling very hungry\",\"He was trying to be funny\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the beggar as \'confused\' and \'terrified\' while he stammered.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'He drew some coins out of his pocket and beckoned the innkeeper closer\', what does \'beckoned\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Shouted at someone\",\"Signaled someone to come nearer\",\"Pushed someone away\",\"Gave money to someone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Beckoned means to make a gesture with the hand or head to encourage someone to come nearer.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Hodja shake the coins near the innkeeper\'s ear instead of giving them to him?\",\"options\":[\"He wanted to tease the innkeeper\",\"He didn\'t have enough money to pay\",\"To provide the \'sound\' of money as payment for the \'smell\' of soup\",\"He was checking if the coins were real\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Hodja explained that the sound of the money was the fair payment for the smell of the soup.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes Nasreddin Hodja\'s way of solving the problem?\",\"options\":[\"Cruel\",\"Wise\",\"Careless\",\"Greedy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Hodja uses wit and wisdom to ensure a fair outcome for the poor beggar, which is a trait of a wise judge.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What did Hodja do to the coins to make them ring together?\",\"options\":[\"He dropped them on the floor\",\"He threw them at the innkeeper\",\"He shook his hand gently\",\"He hit them with a spoon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says he \'shook his hand gently so the coins rang together\'.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text mean by \'savour its good smell\'?\",\"options\":[\"To ignore the smell\",\"To enjoy the smell completely\",\"To cook something that smells good\",\"To complain about the smell\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"To savour means to enjoy or appreciate something completely, in this case, the smell of the soup.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the innkeeper feel after Hodja told him he had been paid?\",\"options\":[\"Happy\",\"Satisfied\",\"Angry\",\"Terrified\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The innkeeper said angrily, \\\"but my payment...\\\"\'.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If the soup was being cooked in \'cauldrons\', what were they using?\",\"options\":[\"Small frying pans\",\"Large deep pots for boiling\",\"Flat plates\",\"Wooden bowls\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A cauldron is a large metal pot with a lid and handle, used for cooking over an open fire.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the beggar when he was \'ordered out empty-handed\'?\",\"options\":[\"The market road\",\"Nasreddin Hodja\'s house\",\"A nearby restaurant\\/inn\",\"A bakery\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says he went to a nearby restaurant to beg for food but was ordered out of the inn.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the man in the blue robe doing with the large pot?\",\"options\":[\"Cleaning the pot\",\"Lifting the lid to check the soup\",\"Adding water to the fire\",\"Eating directly from the pot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the innkeeper lifting a lid from a large cauldron over a fire, letting steam escape.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/092_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the man with the headband doing as the yellow steam reaches him?\",\"options\":[\"He is sneezing\",\"He is closing his eyes and enjoying the smell\",\"He is crying because of the smoke\",\"He is trying to blow the steam away\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the beggar with his eyes closed and a peaceful expression, inhaling the steam\\/smell.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/092_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, who is the person on the far left watching the scene with his arms crossed?\",\"options\":[\"The Beggar\",\"The Innkeeper\",\"Nasreddin Hodja\",\"A rich customer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Hodja (the judge) observing the beggar and the innkeeper.\",\"topic\":\"Nasreddin Hodja and the Smell of Soup\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/093_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'stare\' mean according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To look at something for a short time\",\"To look at somebody or something for a long time\",\"To close one\'s eyes tightly\",\"To look away quickly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'stare\' as looking at somebody or something for a long time.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes a taste that is salty but not sweet?\",\"options\":[\"Bitter\",\"Sour\",\"Savoury\",\"Spicy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, \'savoury\' is a taste that is not sweet but salty.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are \'cauldrons\' used for?\",\"options\":[\"Serving cold drinks\",\"Storing dry grains\",\"Cooking over fire\",\"Washing clothes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'cauldrons\' as large deep metal pots used for cooking over fire.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why might a person \'stammer\' while speaking?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are very happy\",\"Because of fear or nervousness\",\"Because they are eating savoury food\",\"Because they are staring at something\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that stammering happens because of fear or nervousness.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'protest\'?\",\"options\":[\"To agree with someone\'s idea\",\"To remain silent and listen\",\"To say or show that you don\'t agree with something\",\"To pull someone forcefully away\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'protest\' as saying or showing that you don\'t agree with something.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is \'terrified\', how are they feeling?\",\"options\":[\"Very afraid\",\"Very excited\",\"Very hungry\",\"Very sleepy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'terrified\' as being made to feel frightened or very afraid.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a king uses a hand gesture to tell a servant to come closer, he has ____ the servant.\",\"options\":[\"Protested\",\"Beckoned\",\"Stammered\",\"Dragged off\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'beckoned\' as directing someone to come closer by using a gesture.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A guard takes a prisoner by the arm and pulls him forcefully away from the room. Which term describes this?\",\"options\":[\"Stared\",\"Savoury\",\"Dragged off\",\"Beckoned\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'dragged off\' as pulling someone forcefully away from a specific location.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a characteristic of a \'cauldron\' as described in the Word Basket?\",\"options\":[\"It is a small wooden bowl\",\"It is a flat plastic plate\",\"It is a large deep metal pot\",\"It is a sweet-tasting dish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes cauldrons specifically as large deep metal pots.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the text, how does \'stammered\' differ from normal speaking?\",\"options\":[\"It involves speaking very loudly\",\"It involves repeating sounds or words with difficulty\",\"It involves speaking without any fear\",\"It involves using gestures to come closer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that \'stammered\' means speaking with difficulty, often repeating sounds or words.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"When is World River Day celebrated every year?\",\"options\":[\"1st Sunday of September\",\"2nd Sunday of September\",\"3rd Sunday of September\",\"4th Sunday of September\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states that World River Day is celebrated every year on the 4th Sunday of September.\",\"topic\":\"Swimming Instructions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which year was World River Day first celebrated?\",\"options\":[\"2000\",\"2005\",\"2010\",\"2015\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the note, World River Day was first celebrated in 2005.\",\"topic\":\"Swimming Instructions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary reason for celebrating World River Day?\",\"options\":[\"To promote swimming competitions\",\"To build new bridges over rivers\",\"To raise awareness about protecting rivers\",\"To celebrate the start of the monsoon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions it was started to raise awareness about the importance of rivers and the need to protect them.\",\"topic\":\"Swimming Instructions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should a swimmer do immediately if the weather becomes bad?\",\"options\":[\"Swim faster\",\"Dive deeper\",\"Exit the water\",\"Wait for the rain\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to \'Exit immediately during bad weather\'.\",\"topic\":\"Swimming Instructions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a safe practice to follow before entering the water?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore warning signs\",\"Check depth and bottom\",\"Enter floodwaters\",\"Swim alone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Checking the depth and bottom is listed as a safe instruction (Do).\",\"topic\":\"Swimming Instructions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a child is going for a swim, which instruction ensures they are not alone?\",\"options\":[\"Wear a life jacket\",\"Dive or jump in\",\"Have adult supervision\",\"Check depth and bottom\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Adult supervision ensures the child is not swimming alone and is being watched for safety.\",\"topic\":\"Swimming Instructions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which instruction is categorized as a \'Don\'t\' because it involves ignoring safety indicators?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore warning signs\",\"Wear a life jacket\",\"Check depth and bottom\",\"Dive or jump in\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Ignoring warning signs is a dangerous action and is listed among the \'Don\'ts\'.\",\"topic\":\"Swimming Instructions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'Play near fast-moving water\' listed as a \'Don\'t\' in the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is a rule for World River Day\",\"Because fast-moving water is a hazard for swimmers\",\"Because it is only allowed for adults\",\"Because it is a way to protect rivers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Fast-moving water is dangerous and categorized under things one should not do while swimming.\",\"topic\":\"Swimming Instructions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the heading of the second column used for listing unsafe activities?\",\"options\":[\"Do\'s\",\"Don\'ts\",\"Safety\",\"Rules\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The image shows two columns, the second one is titled \'Don\'ts\'.\",\"topic\":\"Swimming Instructions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, in which column should the instruction \'Enter floodwaters\' be written?\",\"options\":[\"Do\'s\",\"Don\'ts\",\"Both columns\",\"Neither column\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Entering floodwaters is dangerous and must be placed in the \'Don\'ts\' column of the table.\",\"topic\":\"Swimming Instructions\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which river name is found in the seventh row of the grid?\",\"options\":[\"KOYNA\",\"KRISHNA\",\"GODAVARI\",\"WARDHA\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The seventh row contains the letters K-R-I-S-H-N-A.\",\"topic\":\"Find the Names of Rivers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which river name is found in the third column of the grid?\",\"options\":[\"TAPI\",\"BHIMA\",\"WARDHA\",\"YAMUNA\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The third column contains the letters W-A-R-D-H-A.\",\"topic\":\"Find the Names of Rivers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many letters make up the river name \'TAPI\' found in the last column?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"4\",\"5\",\"6\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The river TAPI is spelled with 4 letters (T-A-P-I) at the bottom of the last column.\",\"topic\":\"Find the Names of Rivers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the grid, in which column is the river \'YAMUNA\' located?\",\"options\":[\"First column\",\"Last column\",\"Eighth column\",\"Fifth column\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The letters Y-A-M-U-N-A are found vertically in the eighth column.\",\"topic\":\"Find the Names of Rivers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which river name is spelled vertically in the second column?\",\"options\":[\"KOYNA\",\"KRISHNA\",\"NARMADA\",\"SINDHU\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The second column contains the letters K-O-Y-N-A.\",\"topic\":\"Find the Names of Rivers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What type of geographical features are the names hidden in the grid?\",\"options\":[\"Mountains\",\"Cities\",\"Rivers\",\"Forests\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions for the grid specify finding the names of rivers in India.\",\"topic\":\"Find the Names of Rivers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you read the first column from the bottom to the top, which river name do you find?\",\"options\":[\"SINDHU\",\"KOYNA\",\"TAPI\",\"BHIMA\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Reading the first column from bottom to top gives the letters S-I-N-D-H-U.\",\"topic\":\"Find the Names of Rivers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which river name is spelled out horizontally from left to right in the seventh row?\",\"options\":[\"NARMADA\",\"KRISHNA\",\"GODAVARI\",\"WARDHA\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The seventh row of the grid clearly spells KRISHNA from left to right.\",\"topic\":\"Find the Names of Rivers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/091_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which river name is hidden in the last row when read from right to left starting from the eighth letter?\",\"options\":[\"NARMADA\",\"KRISHNA\",\"YAMUNA\",\"KOYNA\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Reading the last row from right to left (starting from N) spells N-A-R-M-A-D-A.\",\"topic\":\"Find the Names of Rivers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/091_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which river name found in the grid has the highest number of letters?\",\"options\":[\"KRISHNA\",\"GODAVARI\",\"NARMADA\",\"WARDHA\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"GODAVARI has 8 letters, while KRISHNA and NARMADA have 7, and WARDHA has 6.\",\"topic\":\"Find the Names of Rivers\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is another name for the Future Continuous Tense according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Future Simple Tense\",\"Future Progressive Tense\",\"Future Perfect Tense\",\"Future Past Tense\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that Future Continuous Tense is also called Future Progressive Tense.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct formula for the Future Continuous Tense?\",\"options\":[\"subject + was\\/were + verb + ing + object\",\"subject + am\\/is\\/are + verb + ing + object\",\"subject + shall\\/will + be + verb + ing + object\",\"subject + shall\\/will + verb + object\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the formula: subject + shall\\/will + be + verb + ing + object.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, when do we use the Future Continuous Tense?\",\"options\":[\"If the action was completed in the past\",\"If the action is in progress in the future\",\"If the action happens every day\",\"If the action happened a long time ago\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'If the action is in progress in the future, we use Future Continuous Tense.\'\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence is an example of the Future Continuous Tense?\",\"options\":[\"The beggar is walking along the road.\",\"The beggar was walking along the road.\",\"The beggar will be walking along the road.\",\"The beggar walks along the road.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'The beggar will be walking along the road\' as an example of the change to future continuous.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The Future Continuous Tense can be used to ask politely about what?\",\"options\":[\"Someone\'s past mistakes\",\"Someone\'s current feelings\",\"Someone\'s future plans\",\"Someone\'s name\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions it can be used to ask politely about someone\'s future plans.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If \'I am enjoying the smell\' is Present Continuous, what is the Future Continuous form?\",\"options\":[\"I was enjoying the smell.\",\"I shall be enjoying the smell.\",\"I enjoyed the smell.\",\"I enjoy the smell.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows the change from \'I am enjoying\' to \'I shall be enjoying\' for the future.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence in Future Continuous Tense: \'The students ____ (study) for the exam.\'\",\"options\":[\"will be studying\",\"was studying\",\"are studying\",\"studied\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Following the formula \'will + be + verb-ing\', \'will be studying\' is the correct form.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'I shall be enjoying the smell\', which part represents the \'verb + ing\'?\",\"options\":[\"shall\",\"be\",\"enjoying\",\"smell\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the formula, \'enjoying\' is the verb \'enjoy\' with the \'ing\' suffix.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following describes a use of the Future Progressive Tense?\",\"options\":[\"To show an action that happened yesterday\",\"To show an action that will be happening at a certain time in the future\",\"To show an action that is happening right now\",\"To show an action that never happens\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states it is used to show an action that will be happening at a certain time in the future.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which sentence structure is used for \'planned or fixed future activities\'?\",\"options\":[\"Past Continuous\",\"Present Continuous\",\"Future Continuous\",\"Simple Present\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'planned or fixed future activities\' as a use for the Future Continuous Tense.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Choose the correct Future Continuous form for the verb \'play\' with the subject \'He\'.\",\"options\":[\"He will playing\",\"He will be playing\",\"He shall playing\",\"He be playing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Applying the formula \'subject + will + be + verb-ing\', we get \'He will be playing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the error in this sentence if it aims to be Future Continuous: \'They will being eating lunch.\'\",\"options\":[\"The subject is wrong\",\"\'being\' should be \'be\'\",\"\'eating\' should be \'eat\'\",\"The word \'will\' should be \'was\'\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the formula \'shall\\/will + be + verb + ing\', the word should be \'be\', not \'being\'.\",\"topic\":\"Future Continuous Tense\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the dialogue, how old does Nasreddin Hodja claim to be?\",\"options\":[\"Thirty-eight\",\"Forty\",\"Forty-two\",\"Fifty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the text, Nasreddin explicitly states he is \'Forty\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Nasreddin give the same age he gave two years ago?\",\"options\":[\"He forgot his real age\",\"He wants to stay young forever\",\"He always stands by what he says\",\"He is bad at doing math\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Nasreddin justifies his answer by saying, \'Yes, I always stand by what I say.\'\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What activity should the facilitator conduct to explain water conservation practically?\",\"options\":[\"Write an essay on water\",\"Conduct water conservation activities in school\",\"Draw a picture of a tap\",\"Read a story about rain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests conducting water conservation activities in school to explain their importance practically.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Besides Nasreddin Hodja, which other humorous characters are mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Mulla Do-Piyaza and Vikram\",\"Tenali Raman, Akbar and Birbal\",\"Panchatantra and Jataka\",\"Aesop and Grimm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions reading stories of characters like Tenali Raman, Akbar and Birbal.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary purpose of arranging a tour to a nearby river according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To go for a picnic and swim\",\"To catch fish for the school\",\"To understand the status of the river and ways to protect it\",\"To learn how to build a dam\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the visit is to guide learners to understand the status of the river and ways to protect it.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Where are learners encouraged to go to read more humorous stories?\",\"options\":[\"The playground\",\"The science lab\",\"The library\",\"The river bank\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text encourages learners to visit the library to read more humorous stories.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How should students share the stories they have read in the class?\",\"options\":[\"By writing them in their notebooks only\",\"As part of speaking activities or play presentation\",\"By keeping them a secret from others\",\"By drawing the characters on the blackboard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests sharing stories as part of speaking activities or play presentation.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does Nasreddin\'s logic about his age imply in the context of the joke?\",\"options\":[\"He is very honest about time passing\",\"He interprets \'standing by one\'s word\' in a humorous, literal way\",\"He is confused about how many years have passed\",\"He is trying to trick the man into giving him money\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The humor comes from Nasreddin being consistently \'wrong\' to show he is \'consistent\' with his word.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the facilitator\'s role regarding humorous stories?\",\"options\":[\"To discourage students from reading them\",\"To encourage learners to visit the library and share stories\",\"To test students on the dates these characters lived\",\"To write new stories for the students\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists encouraging library visits and story sharing as tasks for the facilitator.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'stand by what I say\', what does Nasreddin mean?\",\"options\":[\"He stands up when he speaks\",\"He remains firm on his previous statement\",\"He likes to talk while standing near a wall\",\"He only speaks when he is standing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, it means he refuses to change the information he gave previously.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21791,32,6,'English','en','Festival of Kites','[\"- Kites are light, flat structures that fly in the wind.\",\"- The Festival of Kites is celebrated on Makar‑Sankranti, usually 14th or 15th January.\",\"- Makar‑Sankranti marks the sun moving from south to north and the start of longer days.\",\"- The festival is also called Uttarayan, Khichdi Parv, Pongal, Suggi Habba, or Makaravilakku in different states.\",\"- Flying kites helps people enjoy the sun, learn patience and teamwork, and boost immunity.\",\"- Common kite shapes: Box kite, Diamond‑shaped kite, Parafoil, Delta, Rokkaku.\",\"- Children and adults make their own kites and compete in kite‑flying contests.\",\"- The International Kite Festival in Gujarat attracts kite flyers from many countries.\",\"- The festival spreads messages of friendship, peace, and unity.\",\"- Kite flying is a fun way to celebrate the end of winter and the beginning of spring.\",\"- The word “diversity” means a wide variety of things.\",\"- “Immunity” is the body’s ability to fight diseases.\",\"- “Tradition” is a custom followed for a long time.\",\"- “Exposure” to the sun during kite flying helps increase immunity.\",\"- “Solar calendar” is based on the movement of the sun.\"]','[{\"q\":\"On which dates is the festival of Makar-Sankranti usually celebrated every year?\",\"options\":[\"January 1 or 2\",\"January 14 or 15\",\"March 14 or 15\",\"December 24 or 25\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the festival is celebrated on January 14 or 15 every year based on the solar calendar.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the festival of Makar-Sankranti called in the state of Tamil Nadu?\",\"options\":[\"Khichdi Parv\",\"Suggi Habba\",\"Pongal\",\"Makaravilakku\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Makar-Sankranti is known as Pongal in Tamil Nadu.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Dadaji, why is the festival also known as \'Uttarayan\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is the festival of kites\",\"Because people eat tilgul laddoos\",\"Because the sun starts moving from south to north\",\"Because it is celebrated in North India\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states it is known as Uttarayan because the sun starts moving from south to north from this day.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the duration of the sky (daylight) from the day of Makar-Sankranti onwards?\",\"options\":[\"It starts decreasing\",\"It remains the same\",\"It starts increasing\",\"It becomes dark earlier\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Dadaji explains that from this day onwards, the duration of the sky starts increasing.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what specific observation does Riya make that Rahul initially thinks is normal?\",\"options\":[\"Kites are colorful\",\"Kites are diamond-shaped\",\"More kites are flying in the sky today\",\"Dadaji is carrying a bag\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the first figure, Riya clarifies her observation by saying \'more kites are flying in the sky today\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/096_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what happens to our body when the weather changes?\",\"options\":[\"Immunity increases\",\"Immunity reduces\",\"We feel more energetic\",\"We stop eating laddoos\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Dadaji explains that when the weather changes, our body\'s immunity reduces.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what two things does Dadaji mention to help increase immunity?\",\"options\":[\"Flying kites and running\",\"Buying new clothes and sweets\",\"Staying in the sun and eating tilgul laddoos\",\"Returning from the market and talking\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text in the second figure explicitly mentions staying in the sun and eating tilgul laddoos to increase immunity.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/097_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a student moves from Maharashtra to Karnataka, what name would they hear for Makar-Sankranti?\",\"options\":[\"Khichdi Parv\",\"Suggi Habba\",\"Pongal\",\"Uttarayan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the festival is known as Suggi Habba in Karnataka.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the scientific reason provided for the tradition of kite flying on this day?\",\"options\":[\"To compete with neighbors\",\"To show off different kite shapes\",\"For exposure to the sun\",\"To mark the end of the solar calendar\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Kite flying is done on this day for exposure to the sun.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is mentioned as a \'commonly seen\' kite shape in the introductory list?\",\"options\":[\"Box kites\",\"Rokkaku\",\"Diamond-shaped kite\",\"Parafoil\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The list in section a(ii) asks to choose the commonly seen one, which is the Diamond-shaped kite.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Makar-Sankranti marks the transition between which two seasons?\",\"options\":[\"End of summer and beginning of monsoon\",\"End of winter and beginning of spring\",\"End of spring and beginning of summer\",\"End of monsoon and beginning of winter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes it as the \'end of the winter season and the beginning of the spring season\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Dadaji mean by the phrase \'unity in diversity\' in the context of this festival?\",\"options\":[\"Everyone flies the same type of kite\",\"The festival has different names but is celebrated across the country\",\"Only people in Uttar Pradesh celebrate it\",\"Diversity means only eating laddoos\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Dadaji refers to the different names for the same festival across India as a specialty of unity in diversity.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which name is used for Makar-Sankranti in Kerala?\",\"options\":[\"Pongal\",\"Suggi Habba\",\"Makaravilakku\",\"Khichdi Parv\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists Makaravilakku as the name for the festival in Kerala.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why does Riya say \'soon we will get rid of the winter season\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because she is tired of flying kites\",\"Because the sun is moving south\",\"Because Makar-Sankranti marks the beginning of spring\",\"Because she finished all the laddoos\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Riya says this after Dadaji explains that the festival marks the beginning of the spring season.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The festival of Makar-Sankranti is based on which type of calendar?\",\"options\":[\"Lunar calendar\",\"Solar calendar\",\"Gregorian calendar\",\"Weekly calendar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the festival \'depends on the solar calendar\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Tradition of Makar-Sankranti\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which month is the International Kite Festival celebrated every year?\",\"options\":[\"December\",\"January\",\"March\",\"August\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the festival is celebrated every year in January during Makar Sankranti.\",\"topic\":\"International Kite Festival Gujarat\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where do the main celebrations of the International Kite Festival take place?\",\"options\":[\"Mumbai\",\"Delhi\",\"Ahmedabad\",\"Kolkata\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the main celebrations take place in Ahmedabad.\",\"topic\":\"International Kite Festival Gujarat\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Along which specific riverfront are the kite festival celebrations held?\",\"options\":[\"Ganga Riverfront\",\"Sabarmati Riverfront\",\"Yamuna Riverfront\",\"Narmada Riverfront\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the celebrations happen along the Sabarmati Riverfront.\",\"topic\":\"International Kite Festival Gujarat\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the kite festival in Gujarat described as \'International\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is only for local people\",\"Because kite flyers from many countries participate\",\"Because it is celebrated at night\",\"Because the kites are made of plastic\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that kite flyers from many countries like Japan, China, and USA come to Gujarat, making it global.\",\"topic\":\"International Kite Festival Gujarat\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the sky during Makar Sankranti in Gujarat?\",\"options\":[\"It becomes dark and cloudy\",\"It fills with thousands of bright and beautiful kites\",\"It stays empty and blue\",\"It fills with birds from other countries\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the sky fills with thousands of bright and beautiful kites during the festival.\",\"topic\":\"International Kite Festival Gujarat\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What do international kite flyers bring to the festival to make it exciting?\",\"options\":[\"Food and clothes\",\"Unique and creative kites\",\"Only paper and string\",\"Books about kites\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that flyers bring unique and creative kites, making the festival exciting.\",\"topic\":\"International Kite Festival Gujarat\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a kite flyer travels from Australia to Gujarat for this festival, which description from the text applies to them?\",\"options\":[\"They are a local flyer\",\"They are an international flyer\",\"They are a riverfront worker\",\"They are a Makar Sankranti priest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Australia is listed as one of the countries from which international flyers come.\",\"topic\":\"International Kite Festival Gujarat\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student wants to see the most colorful kite festival in Ahmedabad. When should they plan their visit?\",\"options\":[\"During the monsoon season\",\"During Makar Sankranti in January\",\"During the summer holidays in May\",\"During the Diwali festival\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The festival occurs in January during Makar Sankranti.\",\"topic\":\"International Kite Festival Gujarat\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the list of countries mentioned (Japan, China, USA, France, Brazil, Australia, Indonesia), what can be concluded about the festival?\",\"options\":[\"Only Asian countries participate\",\"Only English-speaking countries participate\",\"People from different continents around the world participate\",\"Only neighboring countries of India participate\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The list includes countries from Asia, North America, Europe, South America, and Oceania, showing global participation.\",\"topic\":\"International Kite Festival Gujarat\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does the presence of flyers from many different countries affect the festival\'s atmosphere?\",\"options\":[\"It makes the festival global and exciting\",\"It makes the festival very quiet\",\"It makes the festival local to Gujarat only\",\"It makes the festival difficult to celebrate\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that flyers from many countries make the festival global and exciting.\",\"topic\":\"International Kite Festival Gujarat\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of workshops are organized specifically for children during the festival?\",\"options\":[\"Music workshops\",\"Kite-making workshops\",\"Dance workshops\",\"Cooking workshops\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'Kite-making workshops for children\' as a fun activity.\",\"topic\":\"Fun Activities and Special Kites\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is mentioned as a \'yummy snack\' available at the food stalls?\",\"options\":[\"Samosa\",\"Dhokla\",\"Undhiyu\",\"Gulab Jamun\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists jalebi, fafda, and undhiyu as yummy snacks at the food stalls.\",\"topic\":\"Fun Activities and Special Kites\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how big can \'Giant kites\' be?\",\"options\":[\"As big as a car\",\"As big as a tree\",\"As big as a bird\",\"As big as buildings\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text describes giant kites as being \'as big as buildings\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun Activities and Special Kites\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the special feature of \'Night kites\'?\",\"options\":[\"They are shaped like superheroes\",\"They glow with lights\",\"They have long ribbons\",\"They are as big as buildings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that night kites \'glow with lights\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun Activities and Special Kites\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child wants to see a kite shaped like a \'cartoon character\', which category should they look for?\",\"options\":[\"Giant kites\",\"3D kites\",\"Long ribbon kites\",\"Night kites\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"3D kites are described as being shaped like animals, cartoon characters, birds, and superheroes.\",\"topic\":\"Fun Activities and Special Kites\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which kites are described as \'dancing in the wind\'?\",\"options\":[\"Long ribbon kites\",\"3D kites\",\"Giant kites\",\"Night kites\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Long ribbon kites that dance in the wind\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fun Activities and Special Kites\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Apart from kite flying and food, what other entertainment is provided at the festival?\",\"options\":[\"Storytelling sessions\",\"Music and dance programmes\",\"Magic shows\",\"Puppet shows\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Music and dance programmes\' as one of the fun activities.\",\"topic\":\"Fun Activities and Special Kites\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A visitor wants to try traditional snacks like fafda and jalebi. Where should they go?\",\"options\":[\"To the kite-making workshop\",\"To the music programme\",\"To the food stalls\",\"To the kite flying competition\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that snacks like jalebi and fafda are found at the food stalls.\",\"topic\":\"Fun Activities and Special Kites\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a shape for 3D kites?\",\"options\":[\"Animals\",\"Birds\",\"Superheroes\",\"Buildings\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Buildings are used to describe the size of Giant kites, not the shape of 3D kites.\",\"topic\":\"Fun Activities and Special Kites\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the descriptions, which kite would be most visible in the dark?\",\"options\":[\"3D kites\",\"Night kites\",\"Long ribbon kites\",\"Giant kites\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Night kites are specifically mentioned to glow with lights, making them visible in the dark.\",\"topic\":\"Fun Activities and Special Kites\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What special message does the festival of kites spread among people?\",\"options\":[\"Friendship, peace, and unity\",\"Competition and winning\",\"Health and immunity\",\"Diversity and variety\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the festival spreads the message of friendship, peace, and unity.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific cry heard early in the morning to start the festival?\",\"options\":[\"Happy Festival!\",\"Kai Po Che!\",\"Unity and Peace!\",\"Look at the Sky!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the festival begins with the cry \'Kai Po Che!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does the sky look like during the festival?\",\"options\":[\"A dark cloud\",\"A blue ocean\",\"A rainbow made of kites\",\"A field of flowers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the sky as looking like a rainbow made of kites.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the definition of \'diversity\' as provided in the Word Basket?\",\"options\":[\"The ability to avoid disease\",\"The wide variety of something\",\"Working together in a team\",\"Celebrating under one sky\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines diversity as the wide variety of something.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a group of children works together to fly a large kite, which skill from the text are they practicing?\",\"options\":[\"Teamwork\",\"Immunity\",\"Diversity\",\"Peace\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists teamwork as one of the things children learn from the festival.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A child waits calmly for the wind to pick up before launching a kite. Which quality mentioned in the text does this show?\",\"options\":[\"Immunity\",\"Patience\",\"Diversity\",\"Unity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Patience is one of the three specific values children learn according to the text.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'immunity\' mean in the context of the Word Basket?\",\"options\":[\"The ability to fly kites high\",\"The ability to avoid disease\",\"The ability to make friends\",\"The ability to work in a team\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines immunity as the ability to avoid disease.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text mention that people from different countries celebrate \'under one sky\'?\",\"options\":[\"To show that the sky is very large\",\"To highlight the message of unity and coming together\",\"To explain why kites are colorful\",\"To show that everyone is afraid of disease\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Celebrating under one sky illustrates the message of unity and people coming together.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a skill children learn from the festival according to the \'Did You Know?\' section?\",\"options\":[\"Teamwork\",\"Patience\",\"Creativity\",\"Immunity\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says children learn teamwork, patience, and creativity; immunity is a vocabulary word, not a skill learned from flying kites.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does the text connect the idea of \'creativity\' to the festival?\",\"options\":[\"It is one of the things children learn through the festival\",\"It is the ability to avoid disease\",\"It is the cry heard in the morning\",\"It is the reason people from different countries meet\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that children learn creativity during the festival.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21792,32,6,'English','en','The Magic of Flute','[\"The flute is a musical instrument that makes sound when air is blown through it.\",\"A melody is a sequence of notes that sounds pleasant.\",\"When a sound is very attractive and holds your attention, we call it mesmerising.\",\"A reward is a prize given for a good deed or achievement.\",\"A trance is a state where you are deeply absorbed in something, like music.\",\"In the story, Princess Mohini was very ill and could not speak or eat.\",\"The king promised rewards to anyone who could make her smile again.\",\"A boy named Chandu played the flute and his music made the princess recover.\",\"The king then made Chandu a tutor and later an advisor.\",\"The word ‘flute’ is a noun; ‘flutist’ is a person who plays it.\",\"The story shows how music can heal and bring joy.\",\"The word ‘trance’ comes from the Latin ‘transeo’ meaning ‘to pass through’.\",\"A prefix is added before a word to change its meaning; a suffix is added after a word.\",\"Examples: ‘unhappy’ (prefix ‘un-’), ‘happiness’ (suffix ‘-ness’).\",\"The digraph ‘sh’ makes the \\/ʃ\\/ sound as in ‘ship’.\",\"The digraph ‘ch’ makes the \\/tʃ\\/ sound as in ‘chair’.\",\"The digraph ‘th’ can be \\/θ\\/ as in ‘thin’ or \\/ð\\/ as in ‘this’.\",\"The digraph ‘ph’ makes the \\/f\\/ sound as in ‘phone’.\",\"The digraph ‘wh’ can be \\/w\\/ as in ‘when’ or \\/hw\\/ as in ‘whale’.\",\"The digraph ‘ck’ makes the \\/k\\/ sound as in ‘duck’.\",\"The digraph ‘ng’ makes the \\/ŋ\\/ sound as in ‘sing’.\",\"The digraph ‘qu’ makes the \\/kw\\/ sound as in ‘queen’.\",\"The word ‘antakshari’ is a game where each sentence starts with the last letter of the previous sentence.\",\"The story encourages making a simple flute from a straw to learn about sound.\",\"The story also teaches about prefixes, suffixes, and digraphs.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who was the ruler of Mohanpur according to the story?\",\"options\":[\"King Chandu\",\"King Madho Singh\",\"The Royal Physician\",\"A mysterious boy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Mohanpur was ruled by King Madho Singh.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the name of the King\'s daughter?\",\"options\":[\"Mohini\",\"Madhuri\",\"Malini\",\"Meena\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the King had a daughter named Mohini.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the boy drop when he saw the King and his soldiers?\",\"options\":[\"A bag of gold\",\"His books\",\"His flute\",\"A piece of fruit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The flute fell off his hands\' when he saw the King and soldiers.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the King and his soldiers find the boy playing the flute?\",\"options\":[\"In the palace garden\",\"In the middle of the market\",\"Under a tree far away from the palace\",\"Inside the Princess\'s chamber\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states they found a boy sitting under a tree far away from the palace.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the boy\'s name?\",\"options\":[\"Madho\",\"Mohan\",\"Chandu\",\"Singh\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The boy identifies himself by saying, \'My name is Chandu.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase describes Mohini\'s physical condition during her illness?\",\"options\":[\"She was active and playful\",\"She would lie like a skeleton\",\"She was eating too much\",\"She was constantly talking\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes her weakness by saying she would just lie like a skeleton.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the King\'s announcement, what would begin the process of Mohini\'s recovery?\",\"options\":[\"A new medicine from the physician\",\"A smile back on her face\",\"A trip to the forest\",\"Eating a special meal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says it was said that the smile would begin the process of her recovery.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the King and Queen rush to Mohini\'s chamber?\",\"options\":[\"Because she had stopped breathing\",\"Because they heard the flute music there\",\"Because they heard the news of Mohini speaking again\",\"Because the physician called them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The news of Mohini speaking again brought the King and Queen to her chamber.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the wild creatures when the boy played his flute?\",\"options\":[\"They ran away in fear\",\"They attacked the soldiers\",\"They were frozen in a trance\",\"They started dancing loudly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions wild creatures were around him frozen in the trance of his music.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What two things did Chandu ask for when the King offered a reward?\",\"options\":[\"Gold and a house\",\"A job and to study\",\"A new flute and a horse\",\"To become the new King\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Chandu said, \'I need some job and want to study.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the Princess react the moment she heard the flute music?\",\"options\":[\"She started dancing immediately\",\"She opened her eyes and spoke after months\",\"She asked the soldiers to stop the noise\",\"She fell into a deeper sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says Mohini opened her eyes and spoke after months, asking \'Who\'s playing that?\'\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did the King ensure Chandu got the education he wanted?\",\"options\":[\"He sent him to a far away school\",\"He taught him personally\",\"He arranged tutors for Chandu\'s education\",\"He gave him books to read alone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the King arranged tutors for Chandu’s education.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text best describes music that is so beautiful it captures complete attention?\",\"options\":[\"Mysterious\",\"Mesmerising\",\"Faint\",\"Interrupted\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'mesmerising\' to describe the tune that filled the air.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Mohini object to the soldiers bringing the flute player to the palace immediately?\",\"options\":[\"She was afraid of the player\",\"She didn\'t want the music to be interrupted\",\"She wanted to go to the forest herself\",\"She did not like the soldiers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Mohini objected to it. She didn’t want the music to be interrupted.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the long-term outcome for Chandu after he received his education?\",\"options\":[\"He became a famous physician\",\"He became a professional soldier\",\"He became an advisor to the King\",\"He returned to the forest to live with animals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying he later became an advisor to the King.\",\"topic\":\"The Magic of Flute\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'wafted\' as given in the Word Basket?\",\"options\":[\"Carried gently through the air\",\"Blown away by a strong wind\",\"Dropped suddenly on the floor\",\"Moving very fast in a circle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket defines \'wafted\' as carried gently through the air.\",\"topic\":\"Make a flute with straw\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text means \'slowly\'?\",\"options\":[\"Wafted\",\"Gradually\",\"Interrupted\",\"Trance\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'gradually\' as \'slowly\'.\",\"topic\":\"Make a flute with straw\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a performance is \'mesmerising\', what does it do?\",\"options\":[\"It makes the audience feel sleepy\",\"It holds attention completely\",\"It is very loud and disturbing\",\"It ends very quickly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the Word Basket, \'mesmerising\' means holding attention completely.\",\"topic\":\"Make a flute with straw\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when something is \'interrupted\'?\",\"options\":[\"It becomes much faster\",\"It stays the same forever\",\"Its continuity is broken\",\"It starts from the beginning\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'interrupted\' as \'broke the continuity\'.\",\"topic\":\"Make a flute with straw\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is a \'trance\' according to the Word Basket?\",\"options\":[\"A state of being very angry\",\"A state of being very happy\",\"A mental state where you don\'t understand what is going on around you\",\"A physical exercise to stay fit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket defines \'trance\' as a mental state in which you don’t understand what is going on around you.\",\"topic\":\"Make a flute with straw\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step in making a flute with a straw?\",\"options\":[\"Cut the straw into two halves\",\"Press one end with your finger\",\"Blow into the straw immediately\",\"Trim the tip of the straw\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to first take a straw and press one end with your finger.\",\"topic\":\"Make a flute with straw\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Into which shape should you cut the pressed end of the straw?\",\"options\":[\"A square shape\",\"A circular shape\",\"A triangular shape\",\"A star shape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to cut the pressed end into a triangular shape.\",\"topic\":\"Make a flute with straw\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why should you trim the tip of the triangular end slightly?\",\"options\":[\"To make it look beautiful\",\"To make a small opening\",\"To make the straw shorter\",\"To change the color of the straw\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to trim the tip slightly to make a small opening.\",\"topic\":\"Make a flute with straw\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How can you create different sounds using this straw flute?\",\"options\":[\"By blowing as hard as possible\",\"By closing your eyes while blowing\",\"By cutting the straw little by little\",\"By pressing the middle of the straw\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to cut the straw little by little to create different sounds.\",\"topic\":\"Make a flute with straw\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where should you place the pointed end of the straw to play it?\",\"options\":[\"Against your teeth\",\"In your mouth\",\"Near your ear\",\"Between your palms\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to put the pointed end in your mouth and blow gently.\",\"topic\":\"Make a flute with straw\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the term for a combination of two letters that represent a single, unique sound?\",\"options\":[\"Blend\",\"Digraph\",\"Vowel\",\"Syllable\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a digraph as a combination of two letters that represent a single, unique sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the IPA sound for the digraph \'ph\'?\",\"options\":[\"\\/p\\/\",\"\\/h\\/\",\"\\/f\\/\",\"\\/v\\/\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table lists the sound (IPA) for \'ph\' as \\/f\\/.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which digraph represents the sound \\/k\\/ as seen in the word \'clock\'?\",\"options\":[\"ch\",\"ck\",\"qu\",\"ng\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'ck\' with the sound \\/k\\/ and provides \'clock\' as an example.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does a digraph differ from a blend according to the \'Quick tip\'?\",\"options\":[\"In a blend, only one sound is heard.\",\"In a digraph, both sounds are heard.\",\"In a digraph, two letters make a single sound.\",\"Blends and digraphs are the same thing.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The \'Quick tip\' states that in a digraph, two letters combine to make a single sound, whereas in a blend, both sounds are heard.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the word \'mother\', what type of sound does the digraph \'th\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"Voiceless\",\"Voiced\",\"Silent\",\"Double\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text categorizes \'th\' in the word \'mother\' as \\/ð\\/ (voiced).\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the text contains a digraph that makes the \\/ʃ\\/ sound?\",\"options\":[\"chair\",\"thin\",\"shoe\",\"phone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'shoe\' as an example for the digraph \'sh\', which has the sound \\/ʃ\\/.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence with the correct digraph: \'The __ ip sailed across the ocean.\'\",\"options\":[\"ch\",\"th\",\"sh\",\"ph\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Based on the exercise in the text, the word is \'ship\', which uses the \'sh\' digraph.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which digraph should be used to complete the word \'ele__ant\'?\",\"options\":[\"ph\",\"th\",\"sh\",\"wh\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'elephant\' as an example for the digraph \'ph\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To complete the word \'ri__\' in the sentence \'The bell will ri__ at noon\', which digraph is needed?\",\"options\":[\"ck\",\"ng\",\"ch\",\"qu\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word is \'ring\', which uses the \'ng\' digraph as shown in the text\'s examples.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the word \'blue\', the letters \'bl\' form a blend. Why is \'sh\' in \'ship\' considered a digraph instead?\",\"options\":[\"Because \'sh\' consists of two consonants.\",\"Because \'sh\' makes a single unique sound \\/ʃ\\/.\",\"Because \'sh\' is at the beginning of the word.\",\"Because \'sh\' is easier to pronounce.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that in a digraph like \'sh\', the two letters combine to make a single sound, unlike a blend where both sounds are heard.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following words uses the voiceless \\/θ\\/ sound of the \'th\' digraph?\",\"options\":[\"this\",\"that\",\"mother\",\"both\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'both\' as an example of the voiceless \\/θ\\/ sound for the digraph \'th\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the IPA sound for the digraph \'qu\' as listed in the text?\",\"options\":[\"\\/q\\/\",\"\\/kw\\/\",\"\\/k\\/\",\"\\/w\\/\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the text shows the sound (IPA) for \'qu\' is \\/kw\\/.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which digraph is shown to have two different types of sounds (voiced and voiceless)?\",\"options\":[\"ch\",\"sh\",\"th\",\"wh\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows two entries for \'th\', one labeled \'voiceless\' and one labeled \'voiced\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/103_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the examples provided in the given figure, which word uses the \\/tʃ\\/ sound?\",\"options\":[\"cheese\",\"shoe\",\"thin\",\"phone\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure lists \'cheese\' as an example for the digraph \'ch\', which represents the \\/tʃ\\/ sound.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/103_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you are completing the word \'du__\' to describe a bird in a pond, which digraph from the text is the correct choice?\",\"options\":[\"ng\",\"ck\",\"ch\",\"th\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The exercise in the text uses \'duck\' (du + ck) as the correct word for the pond bird.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Digraphs\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21793,32,6,'English','en','The World is With You','[\"- The world is with you means that the world supports and helps you in every step.\",\"- Discipline is the ability to control yourself and follow rules.\",\"- A poem can teach lessons about discipline and friendship.\",\"- Repetition of words like ‘later’ or ‘you’ helps emphasize the message.\",\"- A letter should have a greeting, body, and closing in order.\",\"- When you write, use polite language and clear sentences.\",\"- Listening carefully and raising your hand shows respect and discipline.\",\"- A warm‑up activity helps students think about the poem’s main idea.\",\"- Reciting a poem with different tunes makes it more interesting.\",\"- Collecting poems from different sources expands your knowledge of literature.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the author of the poem \'World is with you\'?\",\"options\":[\"Shrunkhal Khemraj\",\"Balbharati\",\"The Class Teacher\",\"Anonymous\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem is signed by Shrunkhal Khemraj at the end of the text.\",\"topic\":\"World is with you\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instructions in section (a), when should a student raise their hand?\",\"options\":[\"When they want to go home\",\"If they agree with a statement\",\"When they are hungry\",\"If they want to sing a song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'Raise your hand if you agree.\'\",\"topic\":\"World is with you\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, where is the world going?\",\"options\":[\"To the playground\",\"At the bottom\",\"At the top\",\"To the school\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'The world is going at the top\'.\",\"topic\":\"World is with you\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the list of actions, which activity is specifically mentioned to be done before recess?\",\"options\":[\"Studying hard\",\"Washing clothes\",\"Attending school\",\"Eating tiffin\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the action: \'I eat my tiffin before recess.\'\",\"topic\":\"World is with you\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student follows the instruction \'I respect elders\', which of these behaviors would they show?\",\"options\":[\"Ignoring their parents\",\"Speaking rudely to teachers\",\"Helping an old person cross the road\",\"Running away from the classroom\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Respecting elders involves being helpful and polite to older people.\",\"topic\":\"World is with you\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet say is \'getting clean\' with you?\",\"options\":[\"Your clothes\",\"Your discipline\",\"The playground\",\"The flowers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Your discipline it getting clean With you.\'\",\"topic\":\"World is with you\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet mean by the question \'Is least you realized?\'\",\"options\":[\"You have realized everything\",\"You have not fully understood or noticed how you live\",\"You are very smart\",\"You are always on time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The question suggests a lack of awareness about one\'s own way of living.\",\"topic\":\"World is with you\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these actions is NOT listed in the student\'s agreement list in section (a)?\",\"options\":[\"I study hard\",\"I wash my clothes\",\"I watch television\",\"I attend school everyday\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Watching television is not mentioned in the list of six actions provided in the text.\",\"topic\":\"World is with you\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the boy in the middle using to move around?\",\"options\":[\"A bicycle\",\"A wheelchair\",\"A skateboard\",\"A pair of crutches\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a boy sitting and moving in a green wheelchair.\",\"topic\":\"World is with you\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/104_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which elements of nature are shown accompanying the children?\",\"options\":[\"A bird, butterflies, and flowers\",\"A dog and a cat\",\"Rain and clouds\",\"Trees and a river\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The picture shows a yellow bird, yellow butterflies, and white flowers near the children.\",\"topic\":\"World is with you\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/104_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'discipline\' as per the World Basket?\",\"options\":[\"The ability to control your behaviour\",\"The ability to run very fast\",\"The ability to speak many languages\",\"The ability to draw beautiful pictures\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines discipline as the ability to control your behaviour.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is defined as \'always, for all time\'?\",\"options\":[\"Realize\",\"Forever\",\"Top\",\"Discipline\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines forever as always, for all time.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the World Basket, what is the \'top\' of something?\",\"options\":[\"The lowest part\",\"The middle section\",\"The highest part or point\",\"The hidden part\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines top as the highest part or point of something.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does it mean when a student \'realizes\' a concept?\",\"options\":[\"They have forgotten it\",\"They know and understand it\",\"They are ignoring it\",\"They are drawing it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Realize is defined in the text as to know and understand.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific role of the leader appointed by the facilitator?\",\"options\":[\"To write new poems\",\"To read statements in the warm-up activity\",\"To grade the students\' letters\",\"To collect information from the internet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The facilitator instructions state to appoint a leader to read statements given in the warm-up activity.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should the facilitator help students use to collect information?\",\"options\":[\"Only one textbook\",\"Various sources\",\"Only the leader\'s notes\",\"Only the warm-up statements\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions helping students use various sources to collect information.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is writing a letter to a friend about their favorite hobby, which facilitator instruction are they following?\",\"options\":[\"Reading about Indian poets\",\"Writing informal letters\",\"Appointing a leader\",\"Defining discipline\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Writing to a friend is an informal letter, which the facilitator is encouraged to motivate.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student decides to read a biography of the Indian writer Premchand. This action aligns with which facilitator goal?\",\"options\":[\"Presenting the central idea\",\"Reading about Indian poets and writers\",\"Adding statements to the warm-up\",\"Controlling behaviour\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The facilitator is encouraged to motivate students to read about Indian poets and writers.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the facilitator expected to do regarding the statements in the warm-up activity?\",\"options\":[\"Remove the existing statements\",\"Add more statements to the activity\",\"Only use the statements provided\",\"Ask students to memorize the statements\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions explicitly say to \'Add more statements in it\' regarding the warm-up activity.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the facilitator\'s responsibility regarding the poem\'s \'central idea\'?\",\"options\":[\"To tell the students to ignore it\",\"To guide students to present it\",\"To write the central idea for them\",\"To change the central idea of the poem\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the facilitator should \'Guide them to present the central idea of the poem\'.\",\"topic\":\"For the Facilitator\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21794,32,6,'English','en','The Day Dreamer','[\"- A day dreamer is someone who imagines a better future.\",\"- In the story, a poor couple in Bengal dreams of owning a cow.\",\"- The wife wants to sell milk, ghee, butter and cheese to become rich.\",\"- She buys five pots: one for milk, one for buttermilk, one for ghee, one for cheese, and one extra for her sister’s milk.\",\"- The husband is angry because he thinks the extra pot is wasteful.\",\"- The neighbour Chenna gets angry when the husband thinks he has a cow and starts eating his vegetables.\",\"- The couple’s quarrel shows how misunderstandings can cause fights.\",\"- The story teaches that dreams should be realistic and that sharing can be good.\",\"- Vocabulary: miserable, extravagance, hesitantly, furious, smashed, screaming, commotion, folly.\",\"- The story also includes activities like matching professions with tools and role‑play.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which part of India did the poor couple live according to the story?\",\"options\":[\"Maharashtra\",\"Bengal\",\"Punjab\",\"Kerala\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the couple lived in a tiny village of Bengal.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the table in the given figure, what is the meaning of the word \'extravagance\'?\",\"options\":[\"The habit of spending more money than necessary\",\"A very sad and unhappy life\",\"Crying out loudly in a high voice\",\"An act that is not sensible\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure defines extravagance as the habit of spending more money than necessary.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/107_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How many pots did the wife buy from the potter?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that she went to the potter and bought five pots.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the husband angry with his wife for buying the pots?\",\"options\":[\"He did not like the color of the pots\",\"He thought she spent too much money unnecessarily\",\"He wanted to buy a vegetable garden instead\",\"He wanted to buy a cow first\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The husband was angry because he considered buying so many pots an \'extravagance\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the couple most likely doing based on their facial expressions and the story title?\",\"options\":[\"Fighting about their neighbor\",\"Looking for their lost cow\",\"Daydreaming about getting rich\",\"Buying pots from the market\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the couple looking upwards thoughtfully, which represents their habit of daydreaming mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/106_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which milk product was the fourth pot intended for?\",\"options\":[\"Ghee\",\"Buttermilk\",\"Butter\",\"Cheese\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The wife explained that the fourth pot was for storing cheese.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the wife plan to do with the fifth pot?\",\"options\":[\"Store extra butter in it\",\"Give it to the potter\",\"Send extra milk to her sister\",\"Use it for the vegetable garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The wife hesitantly said she wanted to send the extra milk to her sister in the fifth pot.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what does the presence of the cow and the many pots illustrate?\",\"options\":[\"A real dairy farm owned by the couple\",\"The wife\'s visit to the potter\'s shop\",\"The husband\'s dream of owning a cow and the wife\'s plan for the pots\",\"The neighbor\'s vegetable garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration visualizes the couple\'s daydream about having a cow and multiple pots for milk products.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/106_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the wife needs one pot for each specific product mentioned (milk, buttermilk, ghee, cheese) and one for her sister, how many pots does she need in total?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"6\",\"3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She needs 4 pots for the products and 1 for the sister, totaling 5 pots as mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What action did the husband take in a rage during the argument?\",\"options\":[\"He bought a cow\",\"He smashed all the pots\",\"He went to the sister\'s house\",\"He started a vegetable garden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says he smashed all the pots in a rage.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Chenna start hitting his neighbor with a stick?\",\"options\":[\"Because the neighbor\'s real cow ate his plants\",\"To teach the neighbor a lesson about his imaginary cow\",\"Because he wanted to steal the pots\",\"Because he was a very mean person\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Chenna used the stick to pretend his garden was ruined by a \'silly cow\' to show the husband the folly of fighting over things that don\'t exist.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What specific plants did Chenna claim the \'silly cow\' ate?\",\"options\":[\"Tomato and potato\",\"Cucumber and bean saplings\",\"Wheat and rice\",\"Grapes and mangoes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Chenna claimed the cow ate his cucumber and bean saplings.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the neighbor\'s reaction, what was the \'folly\' that the husband finally realized?\",\"options\":[\"That he should have bought more pots\",\"That his wife was right about her sister\",\"That they were fighting over a cow they didn\'t even own yet\",\"That Chenna was a bad gardener\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The folly was daydreaming and fighting over imaginary things, as they didn\'t actually have a cow or a garden.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the \'World Basket\' describes the \'great noise\' that Chenna heard?\",\"options\":[\"Miserable\",\"Commotion\",\"Folly\",\"Extravagance\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the vocabulary list, \'commotion\' means a great noise.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/107_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What was the husband\'s reaction when Chenna said he was hitting him because the cow ate his saplings?\",\"options\":[\"He apologized to Chenna\",\"He pointed out that Chenna doesn\'t have any saplings\",\"He offered to pay for the damage\",\"He smashed Chenna\'s stick\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The husband stated, \'Your cucumber and bean saplings? But you don’t have any,\' which led to him realizing his own mistake.\",\"topic\":\"The Day Dreamer\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the meaning of the word \'miserable\'?\",\"options\":[\"Very happy\",\"Very sad and unhappy\",\"Very angry\",\"Very loud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines miserable as very sad, very unhappy.\",\"topic\":\"World Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes the habit of spending more money than is necessary?\",\"options\":[\"Commotion\",\"Folly\",\"Extravagance\",\"Hesitantly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Extravagance is defined as the habit of spending more money than necessary.\",\"topic\":\"World Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a person acts \'uncertainly\' or \'reluctantly\', which word are they demonstrating?\",\"options\":[\"Furious\",\"Hesitantly\",\"Smashed\",\"Yelled\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Hesitantly means uncertainly or reluctantly.\",\"topic\":\"World Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'smashed\' imply happened to an object?\",\"options\":[\"It was polished\",\"It was lost\",\"It was broken violently\",\"It was bought cheaply\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Smashed means broke something violently.\",\"topic\":\"World Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is \'very angry\' because they lost their pen, which word from the list best describes them?\",\"options\":[\"Miserable\",\"Furious\",\"Extravagant\",\"Hesitant\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Furious is defined in the text as very angry.\",\"topic\":\"World Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word should be used to describe a \'great noise\' happening in a classroom?\",\"options\":[\"Commotion\",\"Folly\",\"Extravagance\",\"Smashed\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Commotion is defined as a great noise.\",\"topic\":\"World Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific difference between \'yelled\' and \'screaming\' according to the definitions?\",\"options\":[\"Yelled is quiet, while screaming is loud\",\"Yelled is shouting loudly, while screaming is crying out in a high voice\",\"Yelled is being sad, while screaming is being angry\",\"Yelled is a sensible act, while screaming is a folly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines yelled as shouted very loudly and screaming as crying out loudly in a high voice.\",\"topic\":\"World Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"An act that is not sensible and may result in something bad is called a:\",\"options\":[\"Commotion\",\"Folly\",\"Extravagance\",\"Hesitation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Folly is defined as an act that is not sensible and may have a bad result.\",\"topic\":\"World Basket\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definitions, which word describes a physical action of destruction?\",\"options\":[\"Miserable\",\"Smashed\",\"Folly\",\"Extravagance\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Smashed involves the physical action of breaking something violently.\",\"topic\":\"World Basket\",\"p