sted in the text, how many simple dialogues should be used?\",\"options\":[\"1-2\",\"4-5\",\"10-12\",\"Exactly 8\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs students to \'prepare a short role play using 4-5 simple dialogues\'.\",\"topic\":\"Read and learn\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the joke, what did the sign say that caused the student to be late?\",\"options\":[\"Stop and look\",\"School ahead, go slow!\",\"No entry for students\",\"Fasten your seatbelts\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions the student saw a sign saying, \'School ahead, go slow!\'\",\"topic\":\"Just read and enjoy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did one wall say it would meet the other wall?\",\"options\":[\"In the middle\",\"At the door\",\"At the corner\",\"On the roof\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The joke in the text states, \'I will meet you at the corner.\'\",\"topic\":\"Just read and enjoy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the Maths book feel sad according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"It was very old\",\"It had too many problems\",\"No one liked to read it\",\"It was lost in the school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the Maths book was sad because it had \'too many problems.\'\",\"topic\":\"Just read and enjoy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the grammar table, which is the correct sentence for \'She\'?\",\"options\":[\"She write a diary.\",\"She writes a diary.\",\"She wrote a diary.\",\"She shall write a diary.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'She\' corresponds with \'writes\' in the example provided.\",\"topic\":\"Just read and enjoy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the table, what is the past tense form used for \'They\'?\",\"options\":[\"write\",\"writes\",\"wrote\",\"writing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'They\' followed by \'wrote\' in the past tense column.\",\"topic\":\"Just read and enjoy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The text asks you to find other examples of a \'Pun\'. What is a \'Pun\' as used in the Maths book joke?\",\"options\":[\"A word that rhymes with another\",\"A word used in a way that suggests two meanings\",\"A sentence that is very long\",\"A question that has no answer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The joke uses \'problems\' to mean both mathematical exercises and troubles, which is wordplay (a pun).\",\"topic\":\"Just read and enjoy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Using the table, how would you describe the future action of the children in the annual function?\",\"options\":[\"Children danced\",\"Children dances\",\"Children shall\\/will dance\",\"Children dance\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'Children\' paired with \'shall\\/will dance\' for future action.\",\"topic\":\"Just read and enjoy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you follow the pattern for \'Sakshi\' in the table, which sentence describes her current action?\",\"options\":[\"Sakshi dance in annual function.\",\"Sakshi dances in annual function.\",\"Sakshi danced in annual function.\",\"Sakshi will dance in annual function.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table provides \'Sakshi\' and \'dance\\/dances\', where \'dances\' is the correct singular present form.\",\"topic\":\"Just read and enjoy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the student\'s joke, why is the excuse \'go slow\' funny?\",\"options\":[\"Because the student was walking too fast\",\"Because the student misinterpreted a traffic warning as a personal instruction\",\"Because the sign was actually for the teacher\",\"Because there was no school that day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The humor comes from the student taking the \'go slow\' traffic safety sign literally to justify being late.\",\"topic\":\"Just read and enjoy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the jokes relies on a double meaning to create humor?\",\"options\":[\"Corner\",\"Slow\",\"Problems\",\"Ahead\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'problems\' refers to both math sums and life difficulties, creating the pun.\",\"topic\":\"Just read and enjoy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21795,32,6,'English','en','The Space Women','[\"- Women scientists in India have played key roles in ISRO’s Mars Orbiter Mission.\",\"- Ritu Karidhal, Nandini Harinath and Anuradha TK are senior women scientists at ISRO.\",\"- ISRO’s Mars mission launched in 2012 and reached Mars in 2014.\",\"- The mission was completed in 18 months, a very short time window.\",\"- Women scientists work alongside engineers, often brainstorming and solving problems on weekends.\",\"- ISRO’s workforce now has 20‑25% women out of 16,000 employees.\",\"- The word *orbit* means a curved path taken by a planet around another body.\",\"- *Gorgeous* means extremely pleasant or attractive.\",\"- *Ecstatic* means extremely happy.\",\"- *Stereotype* is a fixed idea about a type of person that is often not true.\",\"- *Heritage* refers to traditions and culture that have existed for a long time.\",\"- *Interplanetary* means between planets.\",\"- ISRO’s acronyms: ISRO – Indian Space Research Organisation, VSSC – Vikram Sarabhai Space Centre, PSLV – Polar Satellite Launch Vehicle, INSAT – Indian National Satellite.\",\"- NASA – National Aeronautics and Space Administration.\",\"- A mission’s *window* is the short period of time available to complete it.\",\"- Women scientists at ISRO are treated equally, with recruitment based on knowledge and contribution.\",\"- The success of the Mars mission shows teamwork and innovation.\",\"- Celebrations of women scientists challenge stereotypes that rocket science is only for men.\",\"- ISRO’s achievements inspire girls to pursue science careers.\",\"- The journey to space involves many stages: launch, orbit insertion, data collection, and return (if applicable).\",\"- Learning about space scientists helps students understand real-world science careers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where is the Indian Space Research Organization (ISRO) located according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Mumbai\",\"Bengaluru\",\"Delhi\",\"Chennai\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions ISRO is in the Southern city of Bengaluru.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who travelled to Bengaluru to meet the women who took India into space for a BBC report?\",\"options\":[\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"Geeta Pandey\",\"Sunita Williams\",\"Kalpana Chawla\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the BBC\'s Geeta Pandey recently travelled to Bengaluru to meet the women.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'male preserve\' mean in the context of rocket science in India?\",\"options\":[\"A place where only men live\",\"A field dominated or controlled by men\",\"A special forest for men\",\"A museum for men\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, it refers to the stereotype that the field was only for men.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what did the viral photograph of women celebrating challenge?\",\"options\":[\"The use of saris in offices\",\"The location of ISRO\",\"The stereotype that rocket science is only for men\",\"The success of the Mars mission\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the photograph challenged the stereotype that rocket science in India was a male preserve.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to find information about the organization that put a satellite into orbit around Mars, which one should they research?\",\"options\":[\"BBC\",\"ISRO\",\"NASA\",\"Mars Orbiter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies ISRO as the organization that successfully put a satellite into orbit around Mars.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did ISRO clarify the identity of the women in the viral photograph?\",\"options\":[\"To say there were no women scientists at all\",\"To explain that the women shown were administrative staff while scientists were in the control room\",\"To stop people from wearing saris to work\",\"To move the office from Bengaluru to another city\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"ISRO clarified that while the women in the photo were administrative staff, women scientists were indeed in the control room.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, what is the name of the scientist shown?\",\"options\":[\"Geeta Pandey\",\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"Sunita Williams\",\"Kalpana Chawla\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The caption in the figure identifies the person as Ritu Karidhal.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/110_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the caption in the given figure, what was the specific role of the person shown in the Mars Orbiter Mission?\",\"options\":[\"Administrative Staff\",\"Deputy Operations Director\",\"BBC Reporter\",\"Satellite Designer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure caption lists her title as Deputy Operations Director, Mars Orbiter Mission.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/110_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Where were the women scientists at the time of the satellite launch, according to ISRO\'s clarification?\",\"options\":[\"In the garden\",\"In the control room\",\"In the administrative office\",\"At the BBC office\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"ISRO added that several women scientists were in the control room at the time of the launch.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what would be a suitable title for the viral photograph described?\",\"options\":[\"Men in Space\",\"Women Celebrating Success at ISRO\",\"The History of Bengaluru\",\"BBC News Report\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes a photograph of women celebrating at ISRO after the Mars mission success.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text suggest about the diversity of roles held by women at ISRO?\",\"options\":[\"Women only worked as reporters\",\"Women were not involved in the mission\",\"Women held both administrative and scientific roles\",\"Women only worked in the control room\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions both administrative staff (in the photo) and scientists (in the control room).\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement best describes the impact of the viral photograph mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"It made people dislike rocket science\",\"It showed that women have no place in science\",\"It changed public perception about who can work in rocket science\",\"It proved that saris are not good for work\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the photograph challenged the stereotype that rocket science was a male preserve.\",\"topic\":\"The Space Women Scientists in India\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What was Ritu Karidhal\'s specific role in the Mars Orbiter Mission?\",\"options\":[\"Chief Engineer\",\"Deputy Operations Director\",\"Head of NASA\",\"Newspaper Editor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states Ritu Karidhal was the Deputy Operations Director for the Mars Orbiter Mission.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two subjects did Ritu Karidhal love as a student of science?\",\"options\":[\"Biology and Chemistry\",\"History and Geography\",\"Physics and Maths\",\"English and Art\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that as a student of science, Ms. Karidhal loved physics and maths.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did Ritu Karidhal collect information about space science when she was a student?\",\"options\":[\"By watching television all day\",\"By scouring daily newspapers for news clippings\",\"By visiting NASA every weekend\",\"By writing letters to ISRO scientists\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says she scoured daily newspapers for information and collected news clippings.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, when did the Mars Orbiter Mission begin?\",\"options\":[\"April 2010\",\"August 2015\",\"April 2012\",\"January 2018\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the mission began in April 2012.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the \'big challenge\' faced by the scientists during the mission?\",\"options\":[\"Finding enough scientists to work\",\"Realizing the project within a very small window of 18 months\",\"Collecting enough newspapers for research\",\"Learning how to speak different languages\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the big challenge was to realize the project in the short time of 18 months.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student today wants to follow Ritu Karidhal’s early habits to become a scientist, what should they do?\",\"options\":[\"Only play video games about space\",\"Wait for a job offer without studying\",\"Read every little detail about space science and stay informed\",\"Avoid reading newspapers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ms. Karidhal\'s habit was reading every little detail about space science to prepare herself.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'no heritage of interplanetary missions\' suggest about the team\'s situation?\",\"options\":[\"They had many old maps to use\",\"They did not have previous experience or past records of such missions\",\"They inherited the project from their parents\",\"The mission was very easy to complete\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"No heritage implies they were doing something new without a past history of similar missions to guide them.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the team manage to complete the work in such a short period?\",\"options\":[\"They worked only on weekdays\",\"They brainstormed with engineers and worked even on weekends\",\"They asked NASA to do the work for them\",\"They extended the deadline to 5 years\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they brainstormed with engineers and worked even on weekends to meet the challenge.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Ms. Karidhal’s statement, what was the primary reason for the mission\'s success?\",\"options\":[\"Individual effort\",\"Teamwork\",\"Reading newspapers\",\"Having a postgraduate degree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Ms. Karidhal says the mission\'s success was due to teamwork.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the 18-month period described as a \'small window\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the spacecraft had small windows\",\"Because it was a very short amount of time for such a complex mission\",\"Because they only worked during the day\",\"Because the office windows were small\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, a \'small window\' refers to the limited time available to achieve the goal.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what emotion is being expressed by the women scientists?\",\"options\":[\"Sadness and failure\",\"Anger and frustration\",\"Joy and celebration of success\",\"Boredom and tiredness\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The image shows the women scientists hugging and smiling, which indicates joy and celebration.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/111_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the caption in the given figure, who is the Deputy Operations Director shown celebrating with her team?\",\"options\":[\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"Nandini Harinath\",\"A student of science\",\"An unnamed engineer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The caption in the figure identifies the person as Nandini Harinath, Deputy Operations Director.\",\"topic\":\"Ritu Karidhal\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/111_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is Nandini Harinath\'s official role in the Mars Orbiter Mission?\",\"options\":[\"Chief Engineer\",\"Deputy Operations Director\",\"Maths Teacher\",\"Science Fiction Writer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states she is the Deputy Operations Director for the Mars Orbiter Mission.\",\"topic\":\"Nandini Harinath\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was Nandini Harinath\'s first exposure to science?\",\"options\":[\"Reading textbooks\",\"Watching Star Trek on television\",\"Visiting ISRO\",\"Doing experiments at home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions her first exposure to science was through Star Trek on television.\",\"topic\":\"Nandini Harinath\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"For how many years has Nandini Harinath been working at ISRO?\",\"options\":[\"10 years\",\"15 years\",\"20 years\",\"25 years\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states she has been working there for 20 years.\",\"topic\":\"Nandini Harinath\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the professions of Nandini Harinath\'s parents?\",\"options\":[\"Both are space scientists\",\"A doctor and a nurse\",\"A maths teacher and an engineer\",\"A pilot and a physicist\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions her mother is a maths teacher and her father is an engineer.\",\"topic\":\"Nandini Harinath\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'ISRO just happened\' suggest about Nandini Harinath\'s career path?\",\"options\":[\"She planned to join ISRO since childhood.\",\"It was an accidental discovery of a building.\",\"She didn\'t originally plan to be a space scientist, but got the first job she applied for.\",\"She was forced to join by her parents.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says she never thought of becoming a space scientist and it was simply the first job she applied for.\",\"topic\":\"Nandini Harinath\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the scientists handle problems in the mission design during the launch period?\",\"options\":[\"They waited for instructions from other countries.\",\"They used quick solutions and innovation.\",\"They ignored the problems and continued the launch.\",\"They went home to think about the solutions.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states they solved problems through quick solutions and innovation during sleepless nights.\",\"topic\":\"Nandini Harinath\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the expression \'no looking back\' mean in the context of her 20-year career?\",\"options\":[\"She never returned to her home town.\",\"She continued to progress and stay committed to her work.\",\"She forgot everything she learned in the past.\",\"She was too busy to look behind her while walking.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It implies she has been steadily and successfully working at ISRO without regret or stopping.\",\"topic\":\"Nandini Harinath\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which action shows how Nandini Harinath balanced her professional responsibilities with her family duties?\",\"options\":[\"She took her daughter to the ISRO launch site.\",\"She quit her job during her daughter\'s exams.\",\"She woke up at 4 a.m. to support her daughter\'s studies despite working