s of the Mars mission?\",\"options\":[\"Celebrating the achievement for a long time.\",\"Building more televisions for science fiction.\",\"Exploring more of the universe.\",\"Finding more \'women from Mars\'.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states she believes the focus should now be on exploring more of the universe.\",\"topic\":\"Nandini Harinath\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How many years has Ms. Anuradha worked with ISRO according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"25 years\",\"34 years\",\"19 years\",\"40 years\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states she has worked with ISRO for 34 years.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which year did Ms. Anuradha join ISRO?\",\"options\":[\"1972\",\"1982\",\"1992\",\"2002\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions she joined ISRO in 1982.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is Ms. Anuradha\'s specific area of work at ISRO?\",\"options\":[\"Building rockets for moon missions\",\"Training astronauts for space travel\",\"Sending communication satellites into space\",\"Studying the atmosphere of Mars\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says she specialises in sending communication satellites into space.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to Ms. Anuradha, why is science suitable for everyone?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is logical\",\"Because it is easy to learn\",\"Because it involves traveling\",\"Because it is only for engineers\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"She believes science is logical and therefore suitable for everyone.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If ISRO has over 16,000 employees today, approximately how many are women based on the percentage given in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Less than 500\",\"Exactly 1,000\",\"More than 3,200\",\"Exactly 16,000\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"20% of 16,000 is 3,200; the text says more than 20-25% are women.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Ms. Anuradha wrote a poem about a man landing on the moon. In which language did she write it?\",\"options\":[\"English\",\"Hindi\",\"Kannada\",\"Marathi\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies she wrote a poem in Kannada.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Ms. Anuradha was inspired by an event that happened when she was nine years old. Which event was it?\",\"options\":[\"The launch of the first satellite\",\"Neil Armstrong\'s moon landing\",\"The founding of ISRO\",\"Her first science fair\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She became interested in space after hearing about Neil Armstrong\'s moon landing.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does the number of women at ISRO today compare to when Ms. Anuradha first joined in 1982?\",\"options\":[\"The number of women has decreased\",\"The number of women has stayed the same\",\"The percentage of women has grown significantly\",\"There are no longer any women engineers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"She started with only 5-6 women in her batch, but now women make up over 20-25% of the staff.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the main reason gender is not considered an \'issue\' at ISRO?\",\"options\":[\"Because only women are allowed to work there\",\"Because promotions are based on knowledge and contribution\",\"Because women get special treatment over men\",\"Because there are no male engineers at ISRO\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states recruitment and promotions depend on knowledge and contribution, not gender.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Communication satellites are sent into space at what distance from Earth?\",\"options\":[\"3,600 km\",\"16,000 km\",\"36,000 km\",\"82,000 km\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions sending communication satellites about 36,000 km from Earth.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The woman shown in the given figure is the senior-most woman officer at ISRO. What is her name?\",\"options\":[\"Ms. Kalpana Chawla\",\"Ms. Anuradha TK\",\"Ms. Sunita Williams\",\"Ms. Tessy Thomas\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Ms. Anuradha, who is described in the text as the senior-most woman officer at ISRO.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/112_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text and the given figure, what is one way this scientist motivates other girls?\",\"options\":[\"By giving them free books\",\"By showing that women can achieve success in the space programme\",\"By teaching them how to write poems in Kannada\",\"By recruiting them personally at the age of nine\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says seeing women in the space programme motivates other girls to think they can achieve the same.\",\"topic\":\"Anuradha TK\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/112_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is an \'orbit\'?\",\"options\":[\"A straight line between two planets\",\"A curved path taken by a planet around another planet or star\",\"A fixed idea about a particular person\",\"The tradition and culture of a country\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines orbit as a curved path taken by a planet as it moves around another planet or star.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the \'Word Basket\' means \'extremely pleasant or attractive\'?\",\"options\":[\"Ecstatic\",\"Heritage\",\"Gorgeous\",\"Interplanetary\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines gorgeous as extremely pleasant or attractive.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is feeling \'ecstatic\', how are they feeling?\",\"options\":[\"Extremely happy\",\"Extremely sad\",\"Very confused\",\"Very tired\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines ecstatic as extremely happy.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'interplanetary\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"Inside a single planet\",\"Between planets\",\"Outside the solar system\",\"A path around a star\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines interplanetary as \'between planets\'.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which term describes traditions and culture that have existed for a long time in a country?\",\"options\":[\"Stereotype\",\"Orbit\",\"Heritage\",\"Ecstatic\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Heritage is defined as tradition, qualities and culture of a country that existed for a long time.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A \'stereotype\' is a fixed idea about a person or thing that is often:\",\"options\":[\"Always true\",\"Not true\",\"Extremely pleasant\",\"Between planets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a stereotype is a fixed idea which is often not true.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a mission is traveling from Earth to Mars, it is best described as an ________ mission.\",\"options\":[\"Ecstatic\",\"Interplanetary\",\"Orbit\",\"Heritage\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since the mission is between planets, the term interplanetary applies.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When the astronauts successfully landed, they were \'ecstatic\'. This means they were:\",\"options\":[\"Moving in a curved path\",\"Following a tradition\",\"Extremely happy\",\"Attractive\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ecstatic is applied here to mean the astronauts were extremely happy.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definitions provided, what is the main difference between \'heritage\' and \'stereotype\'?\",\"options\":[\"Heritage is about planets, while stereotype is about people.\",\"Heritage is about long-existing culture, while stereotype is a fixed, often false idea.\",\"Heritage is always true, while stereotype is always pleasant.\",\"Heritage is a curved path, while stereotype is a straight line.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines heritage as long-existing culture and stereotype as a fixed, often untrue idea.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words would you use to describe a view that is \'extremely attractive\'?\",\"options\":[\"Orbit\",\"Interplanetary\",\"Gorgeous\",\"Stereotype\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Gorgeous is the specific word defined as extremely pleasant or attractive.\",\"topic\":\"Word Basket\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21796,32,6,'English','en','My Books','[\"Books are a source of joy and knowledge.\",\"A poem can describe books as friends and boats.\",\"Reading books gives new ideas and adventures.\",\"Books can be compared to boats that sail the sea of knowledge.\",\"The poet says books are friends because they give happiness and help learn.\",\"A mystery is something not easily understood.\",\"Sail means to travel on water.\",\"True\\/False: Books give joy to the poet – True.\",\"True\\/False: The poet reads the same books every time – False.\",\"True\\/False: Books are compared to boats – True.\",\"True\\/False: Books do not have knowledge – False.\",\"Opposites: start–stop, fresh–stale, far–near, short–long, small–large, dirty–clean, black–white, soft–hard, dark–light, cold–warm.\",\"A library visit can help make a list of favourite books.\",\"Taking care of books means handling them gently and keeping them clean.\",\"Reading poetry helps understand rhythm and rhyme.\",\"Figures of speech in the poem include metaphor (books are boats).\",\"Writing about books helps develop writing skills.\",\"Using a word basket helps remember meanings of words.\",\"Books can be a friend that never leaves you.\",\"Reading expands imagination and knowledge.\",\"Books can be a safe place for ideas and dreams.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the author of the poem \'My Books\'?\",\"options\":[\"Rabindranath Tagore\",\"Harindranath Chattopadhyay\",\"Sarojini Naidu\",\"Ruskin Bond\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem is attributed to Harindranath Chattopadhyay at the end of the text.\",\"topic\":\"My Books\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet compare his books to in the first line?\",\"options\":[\"Teachers\",\"Toys\",\"Friends\",\"Boats\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poet explicitly states, \'I love my books, they are my friends\'.\",\"topic\":\"My Books\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what kind of skies do books take the poet to?\",\"options\":[\"Cloudy skies\",\"Dark skies\",\"Clear skies\",\"Rainy skies\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'To forests deep or skies so clear\'.\",\"topic\":\"My Books\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens every time the poet reads a book?\",\"options\":[\"He gets tired\",\"He finds something new\",\"He forgets the story\",\"He finishes it quickly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poet says, \'Each time I read, I find something new\'.\",\"topic\":\"My Books\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet mean by \'joy that never ends\'?\",\"options\":[\"Books are very long\",\"The happiness from books is continuous\",\"Books are hard to finish\",\"Reading takes a lot of time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It refers to the lasting pleasure and happiness books provide to the reader.\",\"topic\":\"My Books\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the poem, books are described as boats that sail the sea of:\",\"options\":[\"Water and salt\",\"Fish and whales\",\"Knowledge, fun and mystery\",\"Storms and wind\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The last two lines state books sail the sea \'Of knowledge, fun and mystery\'.\",\"topic\":\"My Books\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to experience a \'dream come true\' through reading, what might they find in a book according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only facts\",\"A story or a picture\",\"A map of the school\",\"Homework instructions\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'A story, a picture or a dream come true\'.\",\"topic\":\"My Books\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these places can a reader visit through books based on the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Only their own house\",\"Only the city market\",\"Deep forests and clear skies\",\"Only the school playground\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions books take the reader to \'forests deep or skies so clear\'.\",\"topic\":\"My Books\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet use the metaphor of \'boats\' for books?\",\"options\":[\"Because books are made of wood\",\"Because books carry the reader on a journey of discovery\",\"Because books can float on water\",\"Because books are shaped like ships\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The metaphor suggests that books are a means of travel to different worlds of knowledge and fun.\",\"topic\":\"My Books\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the overall message of the poet regarding books?\",\"options\":[\"Books are only for studying\",\"Books are difficult to understand\",\"Books are valuable companions that offer endless discovery\",\"Books should only be read in forests\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem highlights the love, friendship, joy, and adventure found in reading.\",\"topic\":\"My Books\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Word Basket, what does it mean to \'sail\'?\",\"options\":[\"To fly in the air in a plane\",\"To travel on water in a boat or ship\",\"To walk on a long path\",\"To drive a car on the road\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines sail as traveling on water in a boat or ship.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the definition of \'mystery\' provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A type of large ship\",\"A way to travel on water\",\"The things that you can\'t understand or explain\",\"A basket used for words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines mystery as things that you can\'t understand or explain.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are using a boat to travel across a lake, which word from the text describes your action?\",\"options\":[\"Mystery\",\"Explain\",\"Sail\",\"Understand\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Traveling in a boat on water is defined as sailing.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used for things that are difficult to explain?\",\"options\":[\"Sail\",\"Mystery\",\"Boat\",\"Ship\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A mystery refers to things that cannot be explained or understood.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A detective is looking into a case that no one can understand. This case is a ________.\",\"options\":[\"Sail\",\"Boat\",\"Mystery\",\"Ship\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since the case cannot be understood, it fits the definition of a mystery.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Rohan is going to travel across the sea in a ship. What is he going to do?\",\"options\":[\"Sail\",\"Explain\",\"Mystery\",\"Understand\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Traveling on water in a ship is the definition of sailing.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the Word Basket, what is the relationship between a boat and a ship?\",\"options\":[\"They are both used to explain mysteries\",\"They are both used for sailing on water\",\"They are both things that cannot be understood\",\"They are both types of baskets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links both boats and ships to the action of sailing on water.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when you encounter a \'mystery\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"You travel on water\",\"You use a boat or ship\",\"You find things you cannot explain\",\"You go to a Word Basket\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A mystery involves things that you cannot understand or explain.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these scenarios correctly demonstrates the word \'sail\'?\",\"options\":[\"A bird flying over the ocean\",\"A man driving a truck on a bridge\",\"A girl traveling in a boat on a river\",\"A boy solving a difficult puzzle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sailing requires traveling on water in a boat or ship.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'Word Basket\', which word is specifically associated with a \'boat or ship\'?\",\"options\":[\"Mystery\",\"Sail\",\"Explain\",\"Understand\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The definition of sail mentions a boat or ship.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21797,32,6,'English','en','Playing Detective','[\"- Detective: a person who investigates crimes or mysteries.\",\"- Detective work involves observing, collecting clues, and solving problems.\",\"- Raju, the innkeeper’s son, liked to play detective by keeping tabs on guests.\",\"- Tabs = small notes or records kept about people.\",\"- Raju followed a tourist who turned out to be an architect, not a thief.\",\"- A good detective stays calm, watches carefully, and does not jump to conclusions.\",\"- Words related to detective: spy, investigate, clue, suspect, evidence, mystery, sleuth.\",\"- Homophones are words that sound the same but have different meanings and spellings (e.g., see\\/sea, here\\/hear).\",\"- Simple future tense: will + base verb (e.g., He will work).\",\"- Future progressive tense: will be + present participle (e.g., He will be working).\",\"- Prepositions show location or direction (e.g., on, at, to).\",\"- Moral of the story: Not all quiet people are suspicious; don’t judge by appearance.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who was Raju in the story?\",\"options\":[\"A famous detective\",\"The innkeeper\'s son\",\"A tourist\",\"An architect\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Raju was the innkeeper\'s son.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the tourist\'s actual profession?\",\"options\":[\"A policeman\",\"A photographer\",\"An architect\",\"A detective\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Raju learned that the tourist was actually an architect.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the tourist go when Raju shadowed him?\",\"options\":[\"To the village square\",\"To the school competition\",\"To the police station\",\"To another inn\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says Raju shadowed the man all the way to the village square.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Raju decide to follow the tourist?\",\"options\":[\"The tourist asked for directions\",\"The tourist was loud and noisy\",\"The tourist was quiet and serious-looking\",\"The tourist was a famous criminal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Raju targeted him because he was quiet, serious-looking, and minded his own business.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'keep tabs on\' mean in the context of the story?\",\"options\":[\"To give money to someone\",\"To monitor or watch someone closely\",\"To play games with someone\",\"To help someone with their bags\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the story, Raju \'kept tabs\' on guests to play detective, meaning he watched them.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to Raju while he was keeping an eye on the man at the village square?\",\"options\":[\"He caught the man stealing\",\"He took pictures of the man\",\"He fell fast asleep\",\"He ran back to the inn\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Raju\'s eyelids grew heavy and he fell fast asleep.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Raju\'s habit, what would he most likely think of a guest who wears dark glasses and speaks very little?\",\"options\":[\"The guest is a friendly person\",\"The guest is likely a criminal\",\"The guest is a famous actor\",\"The guest is very tired\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The story says if guests were even vaguely suspicious, Raju was convinced they were criminals.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the boy in the foreground doing while sitting on the bench?\",\"options\":[\"He is reading a detective novel\",\"He is sleeping soundly\",\"He is keeping an eye on the man sitting behind him\",\"He is talking to the tourist\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Raju sitting on a bench, looking back to watch the man as part of his detective play.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/118_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what can be inferred about the boy\'s activity compared to the man\'s activity?\",\"options\":[\"The boy is playing while the man is working\",\"The boy is spying while the man is relaxing\\/looking around\",\"Both are waiting for a bus together\",\"The boy is hiding from the man\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure illustrates Raju \'shadowing\' the man who is just sitting and looking around.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/118_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What did Raju realize at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Detectives should never sleep on duty\",\"Architects are very dangerous people\",\"Not all quiet people are fishy\",\"Village buildings do not need remodeling\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The final sentence of the story states Raju realized that not all quiet people are fishy.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the tourist taking pictures in the village?\",\"options\":[\"He was a professional spy\",\"He wanted to sell them to Raju\",\"He was hired to remodel the village buildings\",\"He was a detective looking for clues\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"As an architect, he was hired to remodel buildings, which explains why he was looking around and taking pictures.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text describes a person who is \'vaguely suspicious\'?\",\"options\":[\"Serious\",\"Fishy\",\"Quiet\",\"Target\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'fishy\' to describe people who seem suspicious.\",\"topic\":\"Read and enjoy the story\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the definition of homophones according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Words with the same spelling and same meaning\",\"Words with different pronunciation but same spelling\",\"Words with the same pronunciation but different meanings and spellings\",\"Words that mean the opposite of each other\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines homophones as words having the same pronunciation or similar sounds but different meanings and spellings.\",\"topic\":\"Homophone\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'vaguely\' mean in the \'Word Basket\'?\",\"options\":[\"In a very clear way\",\"In a way that is not clear\",\"To design a building\",\"Something suspicious\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket defines \'vaguely\' as \'in a way that is not clear\'.\",\"topic\":\"Homophone\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, who is an architect?\",\"options\":[\"A person who catches fish\",\"A person who investigates crimes\",\"A person whose job is to design buildings\",\"A person who writes stories\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines an architect as a person whose job is to design buildings.\",\"topic\":\"Homophone\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs is listed as a homophone pair in the text?\",\"options\":[\"tell - talk\",\"ship - sheep\",\"fish - fishy\",\"clear - vague\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'ship - sheep\' as pair number 5 in the homophone section.\",\"topic\":\"Homophone\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a situation seems \'fishy\', what does it mean?\",\"options\":[\"It smells like the sea\",\"It involves an architect\",\"It seems suspicious or dishonest\",\"It is very clear to understand\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Word Basket defines \'fishy\' as \'seeming suspicious or dishonest\'.\",\"topic\":\"Homophone\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is common between the words \'new\' and \'knew\'?\",\"options\":[\"They have the same spelling\",\"They have the same meaning\",\"They have the same pronunciation\",\"They are both related to buildings\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"As homophones, \'new\' and \'knew\' have the same pronunciation but different spellings and meanings.\",\"topic\":\"Homophone\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text would you use to describe a large body of salt water?\",\"options\":[\"see\",\"sea\",\"ship\",\"sheep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the homophone pair \'see-sea\', \'sea\' refers to the body of water.\",\"topic\":\"Homophone\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to say you have information about something, which word from the homophone pairs should you use?\",\"options\":[\"no\",\"new\",\"know\",\"knew\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'know\' (from the pair no-know) refers to having knowledge or information.\",\"topic\":\"Homophone\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the pairs \'two-to\' and \'here-hear\', what is the main reason they are called homophones?\",\"options\":[\"They are spelled exactly the same way\",\"They sound the same but have different meanings\",\"They both describe the job of an architect\",\"They are both found in the \'Word Basket\'\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Homophones are defined by having the same pronunciation (sound) but different meanings.\",\"topic\":\"Homophone\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is TRUE about the homophone pairs \'ear-year\' and \'ship-sheep\' as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"They have the same spelling\",\"They have the same meaning\",\"They have similar sounds but different spellings\",\"They are not homophones\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states homophones can have the same pronunciation or \'similar sounds\' with different spellings.\",\"topic\":\"Homophone\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the examples \'write\' and \'right\', what are words that sound the same but have different meanings called?\",\"options\":[\"Synonyms\",\"Antonyms\",\"Homophones\",\"Adjectives\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text introduces words like write\\/right and blue\\/blew as homophones.\",\"topic\":\"Homophones\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'The blue bird blew away\', which word is the homophone for the color \'blue\'?\",\"options\":[\"bird\",\"blew\",\"away\",\"wind\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'blue\' and \'blew\' as a pair of underlined homophones.\",\"topic\":\"Homophones\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text sounds like \'write\' but refers to a direction or being correct?\",\"options\":[\"rite\",\"right\",\"wrote\",\"light\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the example \'I will write a letter with my right hand.\'\",\"topic\":\"Homophones\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word correctly completes the sentence: \'I can _____ a bird in the sky\'?\",\"options\":[\"sea\",\"see\",\"saw\",\"seen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks to choose between \'see\' and \'sea\' for observing a bird.\",\"topic\":\"Homophones\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of \'Meena has long _____\', which homophone is appropriate?\",\"options\":[\"hair\",\"hare\",\"here\",\"heir\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'hair\\/hare\' as options for Meena\'s long hair.\",\"topic\":\"Homophones\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word should be used to describe sending a letter in the past tense?\",\"options\":[\"scent\",\"cent\",\"send\",\"sent\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text uses the homophone pair \'sent\\/scent\' for the sentence \'I sent a letter yesterday.\'\",\"topic\":\"Homophones\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are describing the path you traveled on, which word is correct: \'We travelled by _____\'?\",\"options\":[\"rowed\",\"rode\",\"road\",\"rod\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text offers \'road\\/rode\' as options for the path of travel.\",\"topic\":\"Homophones\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Complete the sentence using the correct homophone: \'I went _____ the market.\'\",\"options\":[\"too\",\"two\",\"to\",\"toe\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'to\\/too\' as choices for indicating direction toward the market.\",\"topic\":\"Homophones\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the paragraph provided, the sentence \'I wanted too by a pear of shoes\' contains errors. What is the correct homophone for \'pear\' in this context?\",\"options\":[\"pare\",\"pair\",\"payer\",\"pier\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the paragraph correction exercise, \'pear\' (a fruit) must be changed to \'pair\' (two of a kind).\",\"topic\":\"Homophones\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The paragraph mentions a \'grate deal\'. Which homophone correctly describes a large or excellent deal?\",\"options\":[\"great\",\"greet\",\"grate\",\"gate\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text requires rewriting the paragraph using the proper homophone \'great\' instead of \'grate\'.\",\"topic\":\"Homophones\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is a blend?\",\"options\":[\"A combination of vowels and consonants\",\"A combination of two or three consonants where each sound is heard\",\"A single consonant sound that is very loud\",\"A word that has no rhyming partner\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a blend as a combination of two\\/three consonants where each individual sound is still heard.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of an initial blend mentioned in the table?\",\"options\":[\"-nd\",\"-st\",\"bl\",\"-nk\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the table, \'bl\' is listed under the \'Final initial\' (Initial) column, while the others are final blends.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used as an example for the \'squ\' blend in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Scream\",\"Splash\",\"Square\",\"Stringy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table explicitly lists \'square\' as the example for the \'squ\' blend.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the individual sounds in a consonant blend?\",\"options\":[\"Only the first sound is heard\",\"Only the last sound is heard\",\"Each individual sound is still heard\",\"The sounds combine to make a completely new sound\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The definition states that in a blend, each individual sound is still heard.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the word \'bench\', which part is the final blend according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"be\",\"en\",\"ch\",\"nch\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'-nch\' as the final blend for the example word \'bench\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words contains a blend made of three consonants?\",\"options\":[\"Truck\",\"Spring\",\"Brown\",\"Skip\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'spring\' uses the \'spr\' blend, which consists of three consonants (s, p, r).\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the rhyming word provided for the word \'blue\'?\",\"options\":[\"True\",\"Glue\",\"Clue\",\"New\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the example \'bl -> blue -> true\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/122_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the \'Blend Rhyme Time\' activity for the blend \'cl\', which sequence is correct?\",\"options\":[\"cl -> clap -> flag\",\"cl -> cloud -> proud\",\"cl -> clock -> back\",\"cl -> clean -> green\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity requires saying a word with the blend, then a rhyming word; \'cloud\' starts with \'cl\' and rhymes with \'proud\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the table in the given figure, which word is an example of a \'Final blend\'?\",\"options\":[\"Glow\",\"Craft\",\"Smile\",\"Scan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the table, \'craft\' is listed under the \'example\' column for the \'Final blend\' -ft.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"32\\/122_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these blends from the text has the same number of consonants as the blend in \'scream\'?\",\"options\":[\"st\",\"str\",\"pr\",\"sc\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\'Scream\' has the \'scr\' blend (3 consonants), which matches \'str\' (3 consonants).\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word correctly matches its blend type as shown in the textbook table?\",\"options\":[\"Block - Final blend\",\"Jump - Initial blend\",\"Pink - Final blend\",\"Frog - Final blend\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'pink\' as an example of the final blend \'-nk\'.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the word that uses a three-consonant initial blend from the list below.\",\"options\":[\"Splash\",\"Stove\",\"Snail\",\"Spot\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'Splash\' uses the \'spl\' blend, which contains three consonants.\",\"topic\":\"Phonics Awareness : Blends\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what should you do if you feel uneasy about someone touching you inappropriately?\",\"options\":[\"Keep quiet and ignore it\",\"Blame yourself for the situation\",\"Tell someone whom you trust\",\"Wait for it to happen again\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that you must tell someone whom you trust if you feel uneasy about an inappropriate touch.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Awareness\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the electronic tool mentioned for informing the National Commission for Protection of Child Rights?\",\"options\":[\"Safety e-box\",\"POCSO e-box\",\"Child-help e-box\",\"NCPCR e-mail\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that you can inform the commission through the POCSO e-box.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Awareness\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text say you need not feel \'bad\' when you get an unsafe touch?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is a common mistake\",\"Because it is not your fault\",\"Because you are a child\",\"Because you can forget it easily\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text clearly states, \'You need not feel \\\"bad\\\" because it\'s not your fault.\'\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Awareness\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these feelings is NOT mentioned in the text as a reaction to an unsafe touch?\",\"options\":[\"Confused\",\"Helpless\",\"Bad\",\"Excited\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions feeling bad, confused, and helpless, but does not mention feeling excited.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Awareness\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is afraid to talk to their parents about an unsafe touch, what alternative action does the text suggest?\",\"options\":[\"Inform the National Commission for Protection of Child Rights\",\"Write a letter to a friend\",\"Search for the person on the internet\",\"Keep the secret to themselves\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text suggests informing the National Commission for Protection of Child Rights through the POCSO e-box.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Awareness\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A child feels guilty after an uncomfortable incident. Which instruction from the text should they follow first?\",\"options\":[\"Press the button\",\"Not blame yourself\",\"Send an email\",\"Keep quiet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first point listed in the text is \'Not blame yourself\'.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Awareness\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary message the author wants to convey to children regarding safety?\",\"options\":[\"Children should solve their own problems\",\"Children should speak up and seek help against unsafe touch\",\"Children should learn to use e-mail for school work\",\"Children should never talk to strangers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text encourages children not to keep quiet and to tell trusted people or use the e-box for help.\",\"topic\":\"Child Safety Awareness\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the POCSO e-box a significant resource according to the information provided?\",\"options\":[