wn that passes through all three\",\"Because they are on a cable\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states Afroz\'s points are non-collinear because no line can be drawn through all three.\",\"topic\":\"Collinear and Non-collinear points\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the discussion, how many lines can pass through both point A and point B simultaneously?\",\"options\":[\"Zero\",\"Only one\",\"Two\",\"Infinite\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that only one line can be drawn passing through both points when two points are taken.\",\"topic\":\"Collinear and Non-collinear points\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the text, who drew points that were collinear?\",\"options\":[\"Afroz\",\"Sarita\",\"Both Sarita and Afroz\",\"Neither\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states only one line can be drawn through all three points drawn by Sarita, making them collinear.\",\"topic\":\"Collinear and Non-collinear points\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a flat surface that is infinite on all sides called in geometry?\",\"options\":[\"A line segment\",\"A ray\",\"A plane\",\"A point\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a flat surface that is infinite on all sides as a plane.\",\"topic\":\"Segment and Ray\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following are considered basic concepts in geometry according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Ray, segment and angle\",\"Point, line and plane\",\"Route, path and paper\",\"Sun, torch and laser\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that point, line and plane are basic concepts in geometry.\",\"topic\":\"Segment and Ray\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The point from which a ray starts is specifically called the ______.\",\"options\":[\"Endpoint\",\"Midpoint\",\"Starting point\",\"Infinite point\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the point from which the ray starts