ions\":[\"The starting points of two rays\",\"The arrows of a plane\",\"The endpoints of the segment\",\"The infinite directions of a line\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the points at the ends of a line segment are called its endpoints.\",\"topic\":\"Segment and Ray\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it incorrect to name a ray starting at point A and passing through point B as \'ray BA\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because a ray must be read from its starting point\",\"Because B is further away than A\",\"Because rays cannot be named with two letters\",\"Because BA is a line segment, not a ray\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that a ray is read and written from its starting point.\",\"topic\":\"Segment and Ray\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definitions provided, what is the primary difference between a line segment and a ray?\",\"options\":[\"A segment is infinite, while a ray is finite\",\"A segment has two endpoints, while a ray extends indefinitely in one direction\",\"A segment is a flat surface, while a ray is a point\",\"A segment is named with capital letters, but a ray is not\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a segment by its two endpoints and a ray as extending indefinitely in one direction from a starting point.\",\"topic\":\"Segment and Ray\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a diagram shows a flat surface labeled with a capital letter \'H\' and arrows on the sides, what does it represent?\",\"options\":[\"Ray H\",\"Segment H\",\"Plane H\",\"Point H\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that a plane is a flat surface, its boundlessness is shown by arrows, and it is named by a capital letter.\",\"topic\":\"Segment and Ray\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the common starting point of two rays that form an angle called?\",\"options\":[\"Arm of the angle\",\"Vertex of the angle\",\"Side of the angle\",\"Segment of the angle\"],\"answer