,{\"q\":\"An obtuse angle is defined as an angle with a measure ______.\",\"options\":[\"Greater than 0° and less than 90°\",\"Exactly 90°\",\"Greater than 90° and less than 180°\",\"Exactly 180°\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The fan diagram text describes an obtuse angle as greater than 90° and less than 180°.\",\"topic\":\"Types of angles\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the hands of a clock show the time 02:00, what type of angle is formed between them?\",\"options\":[\"Zero angle\",\"Acute angle\",\"Obtuse angle\",\"Right angle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"At 2 o\'clock, the measure is less than 90°, making it an acute angle.\",\"topic\":\"Types of angles\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which points are located \'on the angle\'?\",\"options\":[\"Point P, M, N\",\"Point Q, R\",\"Point A, B, C, D\",\"Point O, X, Y\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that point A, point B, point C and point D are points on the angle.\",\"topic\":\"Types of angles\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/028_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"When a paper fan is completely closed, what type of angle is formed between its two edges?\",\"options\":[\"Straight angle\",\"Complete angle\",\"Zero angle\",\"Right angle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that when a paper fan is closed, a zero angle is formed.\",\"topic\":\"Types of angles\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific name for an angle that measures exactly 90°?\",\"options\":[\"Acute angle\",\"Obtuse angle\",\"Right angle\",\"Straight angle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the measure of a right angle is 90°.\",\"topic\":\"Types of angles\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the basic concept in geometry that defines a location in a plane?\",\"options\":[\"Line\",\"Point\",\"Ray\",\"Angle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a point defines a location in a plane.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is a point represented in English geometry notation?\",\"options\":[\"By a small letter\",\"By a number\",\"By a capital letter\",\"By a symbol like @ or #\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states a point is represented by a capital letter in English.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which geometric figure is described as being infinite in both sides?\",\"options\":[\"Line segment\",\"Ray\",\"Line\",\"Vertex\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a line as being infinite in both sides.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the common starting point of two rays forming an angle called?\",\"options\":[\"Arm\",\"Side\",\"Plane\",\"Vertex\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The common starting point of the rays forming an angle is called the vertex.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A surface that is infinite in all directions is known as a:\",\"options\":[\"Plane\",\"Line\",\"Ray\",\"Angle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A plane is defined as a surface that is infinite in all directions.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following describes a ray?\",\"options\":[\"It is infinite in both sides\",\"It is a part of a line segment\",\"It starts from a point and extends indefinitely in one direction\",\"It is a surface infinite in all directions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states a ray starts from a starting point and extends indefinitely in one direction.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If an angle measures exactly 180°, what type of angle is it?\",\"options\":[\"Right angle\",\"Obtuse angle\",\"Straight angle\",\"Reflex angle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A straight angle is defined in the text as having a measure of 180°.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"An angle measures 210°. Into which category does it fall?\",\"options\":[\"Obtuse angle\",\"Reflex angle\",\"Complete angle\",\"Straight angle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A reflex angle is greater than 180° and less than 360°.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the mathematical puzzle, if the measure is 20°, what type of angle is formed when it is multiplied by 5?\",\"options\":[\"Acute angle\",\"Right angle\",\"Obtuse angle\",\"Straight angle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"20° multiplied by 5 is 100°, which is greater than 90° and less than 180° (obtuse).\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which measure satisfies the puzzle: 2x, 3x, and 4x are acute, but 5x is obtuse?\",\"options\":[\"10°\",\"20°\",\"25°\",\"40°\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"At 20°: 40, 60, 80 are acute; 100 is obtuse. At 25°, 4x (100) is already obtuse.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"During a drill, if you move your arm from a starting position to a full circle back to the start, what angle have you formed?\",\"options\":[\"Zero angle\",\"Straight angle\",\"Reflex angle\",\"Complete angle\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"A full circle measure is 360°, which is a complete angle.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the difference between an acute angle and an obtuse angle based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Acute is 90°, Obtuse is 180°\",\"Acute is less than 90°, Obtuse is greater than 90° but less than 180°\",\"Acute is 0°, Obtuse is 360°\",\"Acute is greater than 90°, Obtuse is less than 90°\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines acute as 0-90° and obtuse as 90-180°.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical puzzle and At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21820,34,6,'Maths','en','In the World of Numbers','[\"Natural numbers are 1, 2, 3, … and are used for counting.\",\"Whole numbers include zero: 0, 1, 2, 3, …\",\"Integers are all whole numbers plus the negative numbers: …, –3, –2, –1, 0, 1, 2, 3, …\",\"Zero represents nothing and is the only number that is neither positive nor negative.\",\"The largest natural number does not exist – the set is infinite.\",\"The smallest whole number is 0.\",\"Opposite numbers have the same magnitude but opposite signs, e.g. +4 and –4; their sum is 0.\",\"Adding integers with the same sign: add the magnitudes and keep the sign.\",\"Adding integers with different signs: subtract the smaller magnitude from the larger one and keep the sign of the larger magnitude.\",\"Subtracting a number is the same as adding its opposite.\",\"On a number line, positive numbers are to the right of 0 and negative numbers to the left.\",\"The largest whole number is not defined – the set is infinite.\",\"The largest integer is also not defined – the set is infinite.\",\"The smallest integer is –∞ – not defined.\",\"The Kaprekar constant for four‑digit numbers is 6174 – any four‑digit number (with at least two different digits) will reach 6174 after repeated rearrangement and subtraction.\",\"A Harshad number is divisible by the sum of its digits.\",\"A Demlo number is a number that can be expressed as the sum of two squares in two different ways.\",\"The number 0 is called the void, cipher, or zero in English.\",\"The decimal system has ten digits: 0–9; the word ‘deca’ comes from the word for ten.\",\"The sum of opposite numbers is always zero.\",\"The difference of two integers with the same sign is found by subtracting the smaller magnitude from the larger magnitude and keeping the sign of the larger.\",\"The difference of two integers with different signs is found by adding the magnitudes and keeping the sign of the larger magnitude.\",\"The number line is a useful tool for visualising addition, subtraction, and comparison of integers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is another name for counting numbers according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Whole numbers\",\"Natural numbers\",\"Decimal numbers\",\"Infinite numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that counting numbers are also called natural numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is the smallest natural number?\",\"options\":[\"0\",\"1\",\"9\",\"10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the smallest natural number is 1.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which country was the digit zero born?\",\"options\":[\"England\",\"America\",\"India\",\"Greece\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'I born in India\' referring to the digit zero.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which name was transformed into the English word \'Zero\'?\",\"options\":[\"Void\",\"Cipher\",\"Zipra\",\"Zephyro\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Zephyro has been transformed into Zero in English.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the symbol used to show \'nothing\'?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"9\",\"0\",\"10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'I am used to show nothing. \'0\' is my symbol.\'\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text say about the quantity of natural numbers?\",\"options\":[\"They end at 29761\",\"They are finite\",\"They are infinite\",\"They end at 9 digits\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Natural numbers are infinite.\'\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When zero is included in the set of natural numbers, what is the new set called?\",\"options\":[\"Counting numbers\",\"Whole numbers\",\"Infinite numbers\",\"Decimal numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the set of whole numbers as the set of natural numbers including zero.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the value of a number when a zero is placed after it?\",\"options\":[\"It stays the same\",\"It increases five times\",\"It increases ten times\",\"It decreases ten times\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that once zero is after a number, the value of that number increases ten times.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the decimal system use the word \'deca\' in its name?\",\"options\":[\"Because it was born in India\",\"Because it uses ten digits including zero\",\"Because natural numbers are infinite\",\"Because zero means nothing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links \'deca\' to the presence of the tenth digit, which is zero.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a name for zero used outside India?\",\"options\":[\"Deca\",\"Natural\",\"Cipher\",\"Infinite\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists Void, Cipher, Zephyro, and Zipra as names used outside India.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are counting objects in a group, which set of numbers are you using?\",\"options\":[\"Only zero\",\"Natural numbers\",\"Negative numbers\",\"Void numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states we use natural numbers to count objects in a group.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the number 5 is a natural number, what is the result of 5 - 5 according to the text\'s discussion?\",\"options\":[\"A natural number\",\"A counting number\",\"Zero, which is not a natural number\",\"A number larger than 5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks \'Is 5-5 = 0 a natural number?\' and later explains zero is added to natural numbers to form whole numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following numbers belongs to the set of whole numbers but NOT to the set of natural numbers?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"951\",\"0\",\"2374333\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Zero is the only number in the whole number set (0, 1, 2...) that is not in the natural number set (1, 2, 3...).\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main difference between the sequence 1, 2, 3... and 0, 1, 2, 3...?\",\"options\":[\"The first is whole numbers, the second is natural\",\"The first is natural numbers, the second is whole numbers\",\"The first is finite, the second is infinite\",\"There is no difference\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines natural numbers starting from 1 and whole numbers as including zero.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why is it impossible to name the \'largest\' natural number?\",\"options\":[\"Because zero was born in India\",\"Because natural numbers are infinite\",\"Because the decimal system only has ten digits\",\"Because the population of cities is too large\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since natural numbers are infinite, there is no final or largest number.\",\"topic\":\"Natural and Whole Numbers\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the revision section, what is the smallest whole number?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"10\",\"0\",\"None\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the smallest whole number is 0.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the altitude of Mount Everest (Sagarmatha) as mentioned in the table?\",\"options\":[\"8611 meters\",\"8849 meters\",\"8586 meters\",\"8485 meters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table lists the altitude of Mount Everest (Sagarmatha) as 8849 meters.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which name is used for Mount Everest in the provided table?\",\"options\":[\"Lao Tse\",\"Makalu\",\"Kanchanjunga\",\"Sagarmatha\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table lists \'Mount Everest (Sagarmatha)\' as the name of the peak.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"From where is the altitude (height) of the peaks measured, according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"From the mountain base\",\"From the ground level\",\"Above sea level\",\"From the clouds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the altitudes are given in \'meters above sea level\'.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the altitude recorded for the peak Kanchanjunga?\",\"options\":[\"8516\",\"8611\",\"8586\",\"8485\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Looking at the table in the figure, Kanchanjunga has an altitude of 8586 meters.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/033_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which peak has an altitude of 8516 meters?\",\"options\":[\"K-2\",\"Lao Tse\",\"Makalu\",\"Kanchanjunga\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows that Lao Tse corresponds to the altitude 8516 meters.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/033_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the table, which peak is the shortest among the five listed?\",\"options\":[\"Lao Tse\",\"Makalu\",\"Kanchanjunga\",\"K-2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Comparing the altitudes, Makalu (8485 m) is the smallest number.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many meters higher is Mount Everest than Makalu?\",\"options\":[\"364 meters\",\"238 meters\",\"464 meters\",\"354 meters\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Calculation: 8849 (Everest) - 8485 (Makalu) = 364 meters.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the Mathematical Discussion, what operation would Asawari primarily use to find the total approximate amount needed for both a laptop and a mobile phone?\",\"options\":[\"Subtraction\",\"Multiplication\",\"Division\",\"Addition\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"To find the total amount for two items, addition is the required operation.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following shows the peaks Lao Tse, K-2, and Kanchanjunga in descending order of their height?\",\"options\":[\"Lao Tse, Kanchanjunga, K-2\",\"K-2, Kanchanjunga, Lao Tse\",\"Kanchanjunga, K-2, Lao Tse\",\"K-2, Lao Tse, Kanchanjunga\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Descending order means largest to smallest: K-2 (8611), Kanchanjunga (8586), Lao Tse (8516).\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The text asks, \'Can you tell the largest whole number?\'. Based on mathematical principles of whole numbers, what is the correct answer?\",\"options\":[\"9,99,99,999\",\"1,00,00,000\",\"It cannot be told because numbers are infinite\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"There is no largest whole number as you can always add 1 to any number.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If we arrange the peaks in ascending order of their height, which peak would come first?\",\"options\":[\"Mount Everest\",\"K-2\",\"Makalu\",\"Lao Tse\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ascending order starts with the smallest value, and Makalu (8485) is the smallest altitude listed.\",\"topic\":\"Altitude of Peaks and Revision\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How is the number 2,37,50,145 written in words according to the practice set?\",\"options\":[\"Twenty-three lakh seventy-five thousand one hundred forty-five\",\"Two crore thirty-seven lakh fifty thousand one hundred forty-five\",\"Two crore thirty-seven thousand fifty one hundred forty-five\",\"Two crore thirty-seven lakh fifty thousand one hundred fifty-four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The number 2,37,50,145 is read as Two crore thirty-seven lakh fifty thousand one hundred forty-five.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which symbol correctly fits in the box: 59,21,492 [ ] 64,79,426?\",\"options\":[\"<\",\">\",\"=\",\"+\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"59,21,492 is less than 64,79,426 because 59 lakh is smaller than 64 lakh.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of the subtraction: 95,754 - 38,254?\",\"options\":[\"57,500\",\"67,500\",\"57,000\",\"58,500\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Subtracting 38,254 from 95,754 gives 57,500, but checking the units: 4-4=0, 5-5=0, 7-2=5, 15-8=7, 8-3=5; the result is 57,500.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the comparison exercise, which statement is true regarding 7,579 and 0?\",\"options\":[\"7,579 < 0\",\"7,579 = 0\",\"7,579 > 0\",\"0 > 7,579\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Any positive number like 7,579 is greater than zero.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the sum of 85,39,652 and 53,27,541?\",\"options\":[\"1,38,67,193\",\"1,39,67,193\",\"1,38,57,193\",\"1,38,67,293\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Adding the two numbers: 85,39,652 + 53,27,541 = 1,38,67,193.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the school nutrition expenditure was ₹ 87,000 in June and ₹ 1,69,000 in July, what was the total expenditure for both months?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 2,46,000\",\"₹ 2,56,000\",\"₹ 82,000\",\"₹ 2,55,000\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Total expenditure is the sum of June and July: 87,000 + 1,69,000 = 2,56,000.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How much more was the expenditure in July (₹ 1,69,000) than in June (₹ 87,000)?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 72,000\",\"₹ 92,000\",\"₹ 2,56,000\",\"₹ 82,000\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"To find how much more, subtract June expenditure from July: 1,69,000 - 87,000 = 82,000.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the word form of the number 49,38,67,521?\",\"options\":[\"Forty-nine crore thirty-eight lakh sixty-seven thousand five hundred twenty-one\",\"Four crore ninety-three lakh eighty-six thousand seven hundred twenty-one\",\"Forty-nine lakh thirty-eight thousand six hundred seventy-five\",\"Forty-nine crore thirty-eight lakh sixty-seven thousand five hundred twelve\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The number 49,38,67,521 is written as Forty-nine crore thirty-eight lakh sixty-seven thousand five hundred twenty-one.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which symbol correctly completes the expression 48,579 [ ] 48,579?\",\"options\":[\"<\",\">\",\"=\",\"-\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since both numbers are identical, the equals symbol (=) is used.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"An organization deposited ₹ 9,25,498 in February and ₹ 11,49,505 in March. What was the total income tax deposited?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 20,75,003\",\"₹ 20,74,003\",\"₹ 19,75,003\",\"₹ 20,75,103\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Total tax is the sum of both months: 9,25,498 + 11,49,505 = 20,75,003.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the number 6,79,81,049, which digit is in the units place?\",\"options\":[\"6\",\"4\",\"9\",\"0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the number 6,79,81,049, the last digit on the right (9) is in the units place.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the practice set, which is the correct relation between 0 and 700?\",\"options\":[\"0 < 700\",\"0 > 700\",\"0 = 700\",\"700 < 0\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Zero is less than any positive number like 700.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 3.1\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the set of zero, all positive numbers, and all negative numbers called?\",\"options\":[\"Natural numbers\",\"Whole numbers\",\"Integers\",\"Negative numbers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the set of zero, all positive numbers, and all negative numbers as integers.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which sign is mandatory to write when representing negative numbers?\",\"options\":[\"The (+) sign\",\"The (–) sign\",\"The (x) sign\",\"No sign is needed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states there is a need to write a (–) sign for negative numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When subtracting a number from a given number on the number line, in which direction does the given number move?\",\"options\":[\"To the right\",\"To the left\",\"Upwards\",\"It stays at zero\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, while subtracting, the given number moves to the left on the number line.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the elevator example, what does the button marked (-2) represent?\",\"options\":[\"Two floors above the ground floor\",\"The second floor\",\"Two floors below the ground floor\",\"The ground floor itself\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that to go two floors below the ground floor, the button (-2) is pressed.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where are negative numbers located on the number line relative to zero?\",\"options\":[\"To the right of zero\",\"To the left of zero\",\"Directly on zero\",\"Above zero\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that numbers written to the left of zero are negative numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the number 2 written without a sign in the example \'4 - 2 = 2\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is a negative number\",\"Because it is zero\",\"Because there is no need to write a (+) sign for positive numbers\",\"Because signs are only for fractions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states there is no need to write a (+) sign when writing positive numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the temperature in Siachen fell to 40 degrees Celsius below zero, how is it represented numerically?\",\"options\":[\"40\",\"+40\",\"0\",\"-40\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text uses -40 degrees Celsius to describe the temperature falling below zero in Siachen.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the number line rules provided, what is the result of the calculation 2 - 4?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"-2\",\"6\",\"-6\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly calculates 2 - 4 = -2 using the number line movement rule.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a car is parked 3 floors below the ground floor, which integer would represent this level?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"-3\",\"0\",\"+3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Following the elevator example in the text, levels below ground are represented by negative integers.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following statements is true regarding the position of numbers on a number line?\",\"options\":[\"A number on the left is always greater than a number on the right.\",\"A number on the right is always greater than a number on the left.\",\"Zero is greater than all positive numbers.\",\"Negative numbers are greater than positive numbers.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that on the number line, a number on the right is always greater than a number on the left.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the comparison rules in the text, which of these is correct?\",\"options\":[\"(-3) > (-2)\",\"(-1) < (-2)\",\"(-2) < (-1)\",\"0 < (-1)\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows the relationship (-3) < (-2) < (-1) < 0.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which sequence correctly shows the numbers in increasing order (from smallest to largest)?\",\"options\":[\"0, -1, -2, -3\",\"-1, -2, -3, 0\",\"-3, -2, -1, 0\",\"3, 2, 1, 0\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text illustrates the order as (-3) < (-2) < (-1) < 0, which is an increasing sequence.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Integers\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What value is assigned to the general condition water level in the well example?\",\"options\":[\"+2\",\"0\",\"-3\",\"6\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the general submerged level is considered as zero.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Integers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many steps of the well are generally submerged in water?\",\"options\":[\"Two steps\",\"Three steps\",\"Six steps\",\"Zero steps\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that generally six steps of that well are always submerged.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Integers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the well, what does a positive number like (+2) represent?\",\"options\":[\"A decrease in water level\",\"A rise in water level\",\"The general water level\",\"The summer water level\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the rise in water means (+2).\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Integers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"under