The table shows \'Today\'s Attendance\' for the Sixth class is 48.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides attendance, what other topic is mentioned for mathematical discussion?\",\"options\":[\"School uniform\",\"Sports day\",\"Balanced diet\",\"Classroom cleaning\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Mathematical Discussion section mentions learning about a balanced diet.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To determine which class hoists the flag, what must be calculated first?\",\"options\":[\"The total number of students in the school\",\"The percentage attendance of each class\",\"The number of teachers present\",\"The height of the flag pole\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity instructions require calculating the percentage attendance of each class to compare them.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the attendance flag hoisted each day?\",\"options\":[\"In the principal\'s office\",\"On the school roof\",\"In front of the classroom\",\"At the school gate\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the flag is hoisted in front of their classroom.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which class has the highest total strength according to the provided data?\",\"options\":[\"Fifth\",\"Sixth\",\"Seventh\",\"Eighth\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Comparing the total strength column: Fifth (50), Sixth (60), Seventh (60), Eighth (70).\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'Today\'s Attendance\' represent in the table?\",\"options\":[\"The number of students enrolled\",\"The number of students present today\",\"The number of students absent today\",\"The number of students who hoisted the flag\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the context of calculating proportions for a flag, attendance refers to those present.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the percentage attendance of the Fifth class (45 present out of 50)?\",\"options\":[\"45%\",\"50%\",\"90%\",\"85%\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"(45\\/50) * 100 = 90%.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the percentage attendance of the Seventh class (42 present out of 60)?\",\"options\":[\"42%\",\"60%\",\"70%\",\"75%\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"(42\\/60) * 100 = 70%.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the table calculations, which class will hoist the attendance flag today?\",\"options\":[\"Fifth\",\"Sixth\",\"Seventh\",\"Eighth\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Class 5 (90%) is higher than Class 6 (80%), Class 7 (70%), and Class 8 (80%).\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which two classes have the exact same percentage attendance today?\",\"options\":[\"Fifth and Sixth\",\"Sixth and Eighth\",\"Seventh and Eighth\",\"Fifth and Seventh\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Class 6 is 48\\/60 (80%) and Class 8 is 56\\/70 (80%).\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"A percentage is a fraction whose denominator is ____.\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"100\",\"1000\",\"1\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a percentage is a fraction whose denominator is 100.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which symbol is used to represent \'percent\'?\",\"options\":[\"‰\",\"$\",\"%\",\"#\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'percent\' is represented by the symbol \'%\'.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is the symbol \'%\' read according to the textbook?\",\"options\":[\"Per thousand\",\"Percentage\",\"Percent\",\"Ratio\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that \'%\' is read as \'percent\'.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a ratio that represents a percentage, what is the value of the second term?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"50\",\"100\",\"1000\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A percentage is defined as a ratio whose second term is 100.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is another way to write \'percentage\'?\",\"options\":[\"Per cent\",\"Per thousand\",\"Per ten\",\"Per unit\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Percentage\' is also called \'percent\' or \'per cent\'.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the term \'Per hundred\' signify in the context of the symbol \'%\'?\",\"options\":[\"A fraction with denominator 10\",\"The meaning of the percent symbol\",\"A ratio with second term 1000\",\"The grant received\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'Per hundred – %\' as a concept to remember.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a transaction where percentages are used, as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Measuring distance\",\"Counting objects\",\"Interest rates\",\"Telling time\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists interest rates as one of the transactions where percentages are used.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a value is described as \'Per thousand\', which symbol should be used?\",\"options\":[\"%\",\"‰\",\"1\\/100\",\"100\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes \'Per thousand – ‰\' in the \'Remember\' section.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is NOT listed as a use for percentages?\",\"options\":[\"Profit and loss\",\"Analysis of student scores\",\"Inflation rates\",\"Measuring the weight of a stone\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Weight measurement is not mentioned in the text\'s list of uses for percentages.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a ratio has a second term of 100, it is a percentage. If it has a second term of 1000, it is \'Per thousand\'. What is the primary difference between % and ‰ based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"The symbol name\",\"The base value (hundred vs thousand)\",\"The type of transaction\",\"The numerator\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text distinguishes between \'Per hundred (%)\' and \'Per thousand (‰)\'.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21831,34,6,'Maths','en','Geometrical Constructions','[\"• A compass is used to draw circles and arcs.\",\"• The centre of a circle is the point from which all points on the circle are equidistant.\",\"• The radius is the distance from the centre to any point on the circle.\",\"• The diameter is a straight line through the centre that passes through two points on the circle; its length is twice the radius.\",\"• A ruler (scale) is used to measure straight line segments and to draw straight lines.\",\"• A protractor measures angles; the centre of the protractor is placed at the vertex of the angle.\",\"• A 30° angle can be drawn by marking the 30° mark on a protractor and drawing a ray through that mark.\",\"• A 45° angle can be drawn without a protractor by using a set square (right‑angle tool).\",\"• A 90° angle is a right angle; it is drawn by using a set square or a protractor at the 90° mark.\",\"• Two lines are perpendicular when they form a right angle; this is written as Line PQ | Line RS.\",\"• A perpendicular line through a point on a given line can be drawn with a set square, a protractor, or a compass and ruler.\",\"• A perpendicular line from a point outside a given line can be drawn by folding paper or by using a set square or a compass and ruler.\",\"• The bisector of an angle divides the angle into two equal parts; it can be constructed by folding paper or by using a compass and ruler.\",\"• To bisect an angle with a compass: draw equal arcs from the vertex on both sides of the angle, then draw arcs from the intersection points to meet at the bisector.\",\"• A rectangle has four right angles and opposite sides equal; a square has all sides equal and all angles right.\",\"• A circle can be drawn by keeping the compass width fixed and rotating the pencil around the centre.\",\"• A ruler can be used to check the length of a drawn line segment by comparing it with a known length.\",\"• Estimating lengths or angles and then measuring them is a useful practice exercise.\",\"• Drawing angles of 70°, 105°, 140°, 110°, 30°, 45°, 90° and bisecting them helps build confidence with construction tools.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which tool from the compass box is used to rotate a pencil to draw a circle?\",\"options\":[\"Ruler\",\"Compass\",\"Protractor\",\"Set square\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that we can draw a circle by placing the tip of the compass at a point and rotating the pencil.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing a Circle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the activity described, what is the fixed point H called?\",\"options\":[\"Radius\",\"Diameter\",\"Centre\",\"Chord\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, \'Point H is called the centre of the circle.\'\",\"topic\":\"Drawing a Circle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What shape is obtained by rotating a pencil at a fixed distance from a point?\",\"options\":[\"A square\",\"A triangle\",\"A circle\",\"A rectangle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks \'What shape do you get?\' and answers \'A circle!\'.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing a Circle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the distance kept in the compass called when drawing a circle?\",\"options\":[\"Centre\",\"Radius\",\"Diameter\",\"Point\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'And the distance taken is called the radius.\'\",\"topic\":\"Drawing a Circle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a distance of 4 cm is kept in the compass to draw a circle, what is the radius of that circle?\",\"options\":[\"2 cm\",\"8 cm\",\"4 cm\",\"1 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions keeping a distance of 4 cm in the compass, which is defined as the radius.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing a Circle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To draw a circle around point H, where should the tip of the compass be placed?\",\"options\":[\"On the ruler\",\"At point H\",\"On the pencil\",\"Anywhere on the paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions say to \'place the tip of the compass at point H\'.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing a Circle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which tool is used to measure the 4 cm distance before setting it in the compass?\",\"options\":[\"Ruler\",\"Pencil\",\"Point H\",\"Paper\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'with the help of a ruler... keep a distance 4 cm in the compass\'.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing a Circle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What can be said about the distance of every point on the circle from the centre H?\",\"options\":[\"It is different for every point\",\"It is always 8 cm\",\"It is the same as the radius (4 cm)\",\"It is half of the radius\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The distance of each point on the circle from point H is 4 cm.\'\",\"topic\":\"Drawing a Circle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are asked to show the parts of the circle drawn in the activity, which three must you identify?\",\"options\":[\"Point, Line, Angle\",\"Centre, Radius, Diameter\",\"Ruler, Compass, Pencil\",\"Paper, H, 4 cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying, \'Show the centre, radius and diameter of this circle.\'\",\"topic\":\"Drawing a Circle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it difficult to show all points 4 cm away from H using only a ruler?\",\"options\":[\"Because there are no such points\",\"Because the ruler is too short\",\"Because there are infinitely many points forming a circle\",\"Because the pencil cannot rotate on a ruler\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text implies that a ruler alone cannot easily show \'all\' points, leading to the use of a compass to form a continuous circle.\",\"topic\":\"Drawing a Circle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What tool can you use to measure the exact length of a given line segment?\",\"options\":[\"Compass\",\"Ruler\",\"Protractor\",\"Set square\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that you can measure the length of the given line segment using a ruler.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Line Segments\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how is the length of line segment AB written if it is 8 cm?\",\"options\":[\"AB = 8\",\"Length AB = 8\",\"l(AB) = 8 cm\",\"Seg(AB) = 8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that the length is written as l(AB) = 8 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Line Segments\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the name of the tool shown?\",\"options\":[\"Compass\",\"Divider\",\"Scale\",\"Pointer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text in the figure identifies the tool as a divider.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Line Segments\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/112_104.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text accompanying the tool in the figure, what is its specific use?\",\"options\":[\"To draw circles\",\"To measure the distance between two points\",\"To draw straight lines\",\"To measure angles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure text states that the divider is used to measure the distance between two points.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Line Segments\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/112_104.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"To measure the distance between two points using a divider, which other tool must also be used?\",\"options\":[\"A compass\",\"A measuring scale\",\"A protractor\",\"An eraser\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that for measuring the distance with a divider, a measuring scale is also used.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Line Segments\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the \'l\' in the notation \'l(AB) = 8 cm\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"Line\",\"Level\",\"Length\",\"Long\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the context of measuring line segments, \'l\' stands for length.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Line Segments\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student needs to find the length of a segment PQ, how should they write the result if it measures 5 cm?\",\"options\":[\"l(PQ) = 5 cm\",\"PQ = 5 cm\",\"Length(PQ) = 5\",\"m(PQ) = 5 cm\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Following the example l(AB) = 8 cm, the correct notation is l(PQ) = 5 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Line Segments\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student wants to check the length of line segment AB using a divider. What is the correct procedure based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Use only the divider to get the final answer in cm.\",\"Use the divider to mark the points and then use a measuring scale.\",\"Use a ruler first and then a compass.\",\"Use a protractor to check the distance.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to measure and check the length using a divider and a measuring scale.\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Line Segments\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a measuring scale necessary when using a divider to find the length of a segment?\",\"options\":[\"The divider itself does not have numerical markings for measurement.\",\"The divider is only used for drawing circles.\",\"The scale is used to sharpen the divider points.\",\"The divider is used to hold the scale in place.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The divider measures the distance between points, but the scale provides the numerical value (cm).\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Line Segments\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which combination of tools is suggested to \'measure and check\' the length of segment AB?\",\"options\":[\"Ruler and Compass\",\"Divider and Measuring Scale\",\"Scale and Protractor\",\"Divider and Compass\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically instructs to \'Measure and check the length of line segment AB using a divider and a measuring scale.\'\",\"topic\":\"Measuring Line Segments\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which tool is mentioned in the text to try drawing a 45° angle without using a protractor?\",\"options\":[\"Compass\",\"Set square\",\"Ruler\",\"Divider\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks if a set square can be used to draw a 45° angle without a protractor.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Discussion\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To draw ∠TLN, at which point should the centre of the protractor be placed according to the construction steps?\",\"options\":[\"Point T\",\"Point L\",\"Point N\",\"Any point on ray LN\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 2 of the construction states to place the centre of the protractor at L.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Discussion\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the construction of ∠TLN, what is the very first step mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Draw ray LT\",\"Draw ray LN\",\"Place the protractor\",\"Mark point T\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first step in the example is \'Draw the ray LN\'.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Discussion\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what part of the protractor must lie on ray LN when drawing the angle?\",\"options\":[\"The 90° mark\",\"The curved edge\",\"The bottom line\",\"The 180° mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Step 2 states that the protractor should be placed so that the bottom line lies on LN.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Discussion\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the letter \'m\' represent in the statement \'m∠TLN = 30°\'?\",\"options\":[\"Method\",\"Middle\",\"Measure\",\"Mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In geometry, \'m\' stands for the measure of the angle.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Discussion\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, why is the measurement m∠TXE = 95° in the first picture considered incorrect?\",\"options\":[\"The center is not at X\",\"The ray XT is actually at the 85° mark from E\",\"The ray XE is not straight\",\"The protractor is upside down\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Looking at the inner scale starting from 0 at E, the ray XT passes through 85, not 95.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Discussion\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/113_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the second picture of the given figure, what is the main error in the way the angle m∠TXE = 87° is being measured?\",\"options\":[\"The ray XT is missing\",\"The center is not at X\",\"The bottom line of the protractor does not lie on ray XE\",\"The scale is read from the wrong side\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the protractor is tilted and its bottom line is not aligned with the base ray XE.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Discussion\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/113_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"When drawing ∠TLN = 30°, at what specific mark should point T be taken?\",\"options\":[\"0° mark\",\"30° mark\",\"90° mark\",\"180° mark\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Step 2 says to \'take point T at 30° mark\'.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Discussion\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct mathematical way to write the measure of angle TLN as shown in the text?\",\"options\":[\"angle TLN = 30\",\"m∠TLN = 30°\",\"TLN = 30 degrees\",\"∠TLN is 30\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the notation \'m∠TLN = 30°\' to denote the measure of the angle.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Discussion\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the \'Mathematical Discussion\' section, what is the purpose of checking the two pictures of angle TXE?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to draw rays\",\"To find what is wrong with the measurements\",\"To calculate the sum of the angles\",\"To name the vertices\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly asks to \'Find what is wrong with them\' regarding the two pictures.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Discussion\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the notation \'l(BC)\', what does \'l\' stand for?\",\"options\":[\"Line\",\"Length\",\"Level\",\"Long\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The notation l(BC) is used to denote the length of line segment BC.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 14.1\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is the correct way to write the measure of an angle according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"l∠ABC\",\"seg ABC\",\"m∠ABC\",\"cm∠ABC\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'m∠\' followed by the angle name to denote the measure of an angle.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 14.1\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are asked to draw \'Seg AR = 6 cm\', what does \'Seg\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"Sequence\",\"Sector\",\"Segment\",\"Section\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In geometrical constructions, \'Seg\' is the short form for a line segment.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 14.1\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the unit of measurement used for the length of line segments in Practice Set 14.1?\",\"options\":[\"Degrees\",\"Millimetres\",\"Centimetres (cm)\",\"Metres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly uses \'cm\' for measurements like 6 cm, 4 cm, and 9 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 14.1\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the measurement m∠XYZ = 105°, what does the symbol \'°\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"Centimetre\",\"Degree\",\"Length\",\"Angle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The degree symbol (°) is used to measure the magnitude of angles.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 14.1\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To draw Seg DS = 9 cm, which geometric tool is most appropriate for measuring the length?\",\"options\":[\"Protractor\",\"Ruler (Scale)\",\"Set-square\",\"Compass only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A ruler or scale is used to measure and draw line segments of specific lengths in centimetres.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 14.1\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which instrument must a student use to draw m∠BRT = 70° accurately?\",\"options\":[\"Ruler\",\"Compass\",\"Protractor\",\"Divider\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A protractor is the standard tool used to measure and draw angles of specific degrees.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 14.1\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the measurements provided in the text, which of these line segments is the longest?\",\"options\":[\"Seg AR = 6 cm\",\"Seg BT = 4 cm\",\"Seg DS = 9 cm\",\"Seg BC\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Comparing 6 cm, 4 cm, and 9 cm, the segment DS with 9 cm is the longest.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 14.1\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If m∠ABC = 140°, what kind of angle are you drawing?\",\"options\":[\"Acute angle\",\"Right angle\",\"Obtuse angle\",\"Straight angle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"An angle measuring 140° is greater than 90° and less than 180°, making it an obtuse angle.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 14.1\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you draw Seg AR (6 cm) and Seg BT (4 cm) end-to-end in a straight line, what would be the total length?\",\"options\":[\"2 cm\",\"10 cm\",\"24 cm\",\"12 cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Adding the lengths 6 cm and 4 cm results in a total length of 10 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Practice Set 14.1\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the mathematical game described, what is the first thing you should do after your friend measures a line segment?\",\"options\":[\"Measure it with a ruler\",\"Estimate its length\",\"Draw a new segment\",\"Give your friend a point\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that after a friend measures a segment, you should estimate its length.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Game\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many points does a player receive if their estimated length is very close to the actual length?\",\"options\":[\"0 points\",\"1 point\",\"2 points\",\"5 points\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, if your answer is very close to the actual length, you get 1 point.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Game\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the value recorded under the \'Actual length\' column for the first segment?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"2.1\",\"1\",\"0\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows \'2.1\' in the \'Actual length\' column for the first row.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Game\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/114_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a student estimates a length as 5 units and the actual length is found to be 5.1 units, how many marks should they get based on the example in the text?\",\"options\":[\"0 marks\",\"1 mark\",\"5 marks\",\"2 marks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The example shows that an estimate of 2 for an actual length of 2.1 earns 1 mark because it is very close.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Game\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Besides line segments, what else can be estimated when playing this game in two groups?\",\"options\":[\"The weight of the paper\",\"The area of the classroom\",\"The angle measure\",\"The number of students\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the game can be played by estimating the angle measure.\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Game\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is declared the winner of this mathematical game?\",\"options\":[\"The one who draws the straightest line\",\"The one who finishes first\",\"The one with the more points\",\"The one who uses the longest ruler\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'The one with the more points wins.\'\",\"topic\":\"Mathematical Game\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":