 parallel\",\"The lines are of equal length\",\"The lines intersect at a right angle\",\"The lines do not touch each other\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The square symbol at the intersection N represents a right angle, indicating the lines are perpendicular.\",\"topic\":\"Perpendicular Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/115_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"How is the expression \'Line PQ ⊥ Line RS\' read?\",\"options\":[\"Line PQ Parallel Line RS\",\"Line PQ Plus Line RS\",\"Line PQ Perpendicular Line RS\",\"Line PQ Intersect Line RS\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that \'Line PQ ⊥ Line RS\' is read as \'Line PQ Perpendicular Line RS\'.\",\"topic\":\"Perpendicular Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If line PQ is perpendicular to line RS, what is the measure of each angle formed at their point of intersection?\",\"options\":[\"45°\",\"90°\",\"180°\",\"60°\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Perpendicular lines intersect at right angles, and a right angle measures 90°.\",\"topic\":\"Perpendicular Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What characteristic is shared by the musical pillars in the Vitthal Temple?\",\"options\":[\"They are of different lengths\",\"They are of uniform length\",\"They are made of wood\",\"They are not perpendicular\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the pillars as being of uniform length.\",\"topic\":\"Perpendicular Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are told that two line segments are perpendicular, what must be true about the angle where they meet?\",\"options\":[\"It must be an acute angle\",\"It must be an obtuse angle\",\"It must be a right angle\",\"It must be a straight angle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The definition of perpendicularity provided is that the intersection occurs at right angles.\",\"topic\":\"Perpendicular Line\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the Vitthal Temple located?\",\"options\":[\"Maharashtra\",\"Ka