'Take a trace paper\' for the activity.\",\"topic\":\"Bisector using trace paper\",\"part\":26,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To create a bisector by folding, the paper must be folded through which part of the angle?\",\"options\":[\"The vertex\",\"The end of the arms\",\"Any point on the ray\",\"Outside the angle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states to \'Fold the paper through the vertex of the angle\'.\",\"topic\":\"Bisector using trace paper\",\"part\":26,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When folding the trace paper to find the bisector, what must happen to the two arms of the angle?\",\"options\":[\"They must stay apart\",\"They must cross each other\",\"They must coincide with each other\",\"They must be cut off\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says to fold the paper \'so that two arms of the angle coincides with each other\'.\",\"topic\":\"Bisector using trace paper\",\"part\":26,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which ray is the bisector of the angle?\",\"options\":[\"Ray QP\",\"Ray QR\",\"Ray QT\",\"Ray PR\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'In the figure, ray QT is the bisector of ∠PQR\'.\",\"topic\":\"Bisector using trace paper\",\"part\":26,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/119_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if ray QT is the bisector of ∠PQR, what is the relationship between the two smaller angles formed?\",\"options\":[\"∠PQT is larger than ∠TQR\",\"∠PQT is smaller than ∠TQR\",\"∠PQT and ∠TQR are equal in measure\",\"∠PQT is double the size of ∠TQR\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A bisector divides an angle into two equal parts, so the resulting angles are equal.\",\"topic\":\"Bisector using trace paper\",\"part\":26,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/119_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you draw an angle of 80° on trace paper and fold it to create a bisector, what will be the measure of each of the two new parts?\",\"options\":[\"80°\",\"40°\",\"20°\",\"160°\"],