,\"kilometer\",\"sq.m.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows that if the unit of side is \'meter\', the unit of area is \'square meter\'.\",\"topic\":\"Unit of area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the correct pair of Region and its Unit of Area from the text.\",\"options\":[\"Taluka - square meter\",\"Floor - square kilometer\",\"Open space around the house - square meter\",\"Notebook - square kilometer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text pairs \'open space around the house\' with \'square meter\'.\",\"topic\":\"Unit of area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the area of a District measured in square kilometers rather than square centimeters?\",\"options\":[\"Because a District is a plane figure\",\"Because square centimeter is only for books\",\"Because kilometer is the standard unit of side for large regions like a District\",\"Because square kilometer is the only standard unit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text indicates that for large regions like a District, the unit of side is kilometer, making the area unit square kilometer.\",\"topic\":\"Unit of area\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the formula for the area of a rectangle?\",\"options\":[\"Area = length + breadth\",\"Area = length × breadth\",\"Area = side × side\",\"Area = length - breadth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states: Area of rectangle = length × breadth.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the formula for the area of a square as mentioned in the topic?\",\"options\":[\"Area = length × breadth\",\"Area = side + side\",\"Area = side × side\",\"Area = 4 × side\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: Area of a square = side × side.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a rectangle contains 8 squares of size 1 sq.cm, what is its area?\",\"options\":[\"4 sq.cm\",\"2 sq.cm\",\"8 sq.cm\",\"16 sq.cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that if a rectangle contains 8 squares of 1 sq.cm, its area is 8 sq.cm.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the area of a square calculated as \'side × side\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it has four corners\",\"Because all four sides are equal\",\"Because it is a type of rectangle\",\"Because it is measured in cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'Since all four sides of a square are equal, it is clear that area of a square = side × side.\'\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Find the area of a rectangle whose length is 8 cm and breadth is 7 cm.\",\"options\":[\"15 sq.cm\",\"56 sq.cm\",\"30 sq.cm\",\"49 sq.cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using the formula: Area = length × breadth = 8 × 7 = 56 sq.cm.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Find the area of a square with a side of 6 cm.\",\"options\":[\"12 sq.cm\",\"24 sq.cm\",\"36 sq.cm\",\"48 sq.cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Using the formula: Area = side × side = 6 × 6 = 36 sq.cm.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A rectangular region has a length of 6 cm and a breadth of 4 cm. How many squares of size 1 sq.cm does it contain?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"24\",\"12\",\"20\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the text shows that for a rectangle with length 6 cm and breadth 4 cm, the number of squares is 24.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a square has a side of 4 cm, what calculation is used to find its area based on the \'Square Region\' table?\",\"options\":[\"4 × 2\",\"4 + 4\",\"4 × 4\",\"4 - 4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"For a square with side 4, the \'Side × Side\' column would be 4 × 4.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which two measurements are specifically listed in the table to be taken for finding the area of objects?\",\"options\":[\"Side and Side\",\"Length and Breadth\",\"Length and Side\",\"Breadth and Side\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The \'Do it\' table columns are Figure\\/Object, Length, Breadth, and Area.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the text, for a rectangle with length 9 cm, the area calculation is represented as:\",\"options\":[\"9 + breadth\",\"9 × breadth\",\"9 × 9\",\"9 + 9\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'Area = length × breadth\', so for length 9, it is 9 × breadth.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which of the following is an object listed for measurement?\",\"options\":[\"Classroom door\",\"Classroom floor\",\"School bag\",\"Playground\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure lists \'Classroom floor\' as the first object.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/129_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which two columns must be filled to calculate the \'Area\' of the \'Classroom Window\'?\",\"options\":[\"Figure \\/ Object and Length\",\"Length and Breadth\",\"Length and Area\",\"Breadth and Area\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"To find the area in the last column, one must first measure and fill the Length and Breadth columns.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a rectangle and square\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/129_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the formula for the area of a triangle?\",\"options\":[\"base × height\",\"(base × height) \\/ 2\",\"2 × (base + height)\",\"base + height\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the Area of a triangle = (base × height) \\/ 2.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a right-angled triangle, if one side forming the right angle is the base, what is the other side forming the right angle considered as?\",\"options\":[\"Diagonal\",\"Hypotenuse\",\"Height\",\"Perimeter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that if one of the two sides forming the right angle is the base, then the other side is the height.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When a rectangular sheet is cut on one of its diagonals, it forms two matching right triangles. What can be said about their areas?\",\"options\":[\"The areas are different\",\"The areas are equal\",\"One area is double the other\",\"The areas cannot be determined\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since the two right triangles match exactly, the text concludes that the areas of both triangles are equal.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if the rectangle has length \'b\' and breadth \'a\', what is the area of one of the right-angled triangles formed by the diagonal?\",\"options\":[\"a × b\",\"2 × (a × b)\",\"(a × b) \\/ 2\",\"a + b\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a rectangle of sides a and b divided into two triangles; the text derives the area as (a × b) \\/ 2.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/129_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, for triangle PQR, which segment is identified as the height when QR is the base?\",\"options\":[\"PQ\",\"PR\",\"PS\",\"SR\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure explicitly lists \'PS\' as the height for triangle PQR with base \'QR\'.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/130_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If the sides of a right-angled triangle forming the right angle are 10 cm and 8 cm, what is its area?\",\"options\":[\"80 sq.cm\",\"18 sq.cm\",\"40 sq.cm\",\"20 sq.cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Area = (Product of sides forming right angle) \\/ 2 = (10 × 8) \\/ 2 = 40 sq.cm.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the height of any triangle ABC when a side is taken as the base?\",\"options\":[\"The length of the side itself\",\"The length of the diagonal\",\"The length of the perpendicular from the opposite vertex to the base\",\"The sum of the other two sides\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines height as the length of the perpendicular drawn from the vertex opposite to the base to the base.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the area of a right-angled triangle is 25 sq.cm, what would be the area of the rectangle from which it was formed by cutting along a diagonal?\",\"options\":[\"12.5 sq.cm\",\"50 sq.cm\",\"100 sq.cm\",\"25 sq.cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states 2 × Area of a right angled triangle = Area of a rectangle. So, 2 × 25 = 50 sq.cm.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"A triangle has a base of 12 cm and a height of 5 cm. Calculate its area.\",\"options\":[\"60 sq.cm\",\"30 sq.cm\",\"17 sq.cm\",\"15 sq.cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Area = (base × height) \\/ 2 = (12 × 5) \\/ 2 = 60 \\/ 2 = 30 sq.cm.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why is the area of a right-angled triangle calculated as (a × b) \\/ 2?\",\"options\":[\"Because a triangle has three sides\",\"Because it is half the area of a rectangle with sides a and b\",\"Because the diagonal is twice the length\",\"Because the base and height are always equal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that the area of the rectangle (a × b) is the sum of two equal right triangles, so one triangle is half the rectangle.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the product of the base and height of a triangle is 36, what is the area of that triangle?\",\"options\":[\"36 sq.units\",\"72 sq.units\",\"18 sq.units\",\"9 sq.units\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Area = (base × height) \\/ 2. If base × height = 36, then Area = 36 \\/ 2 = 18.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In triangle LMC shown in the figure table, if CM is the base, the height LD is drawn to which line?\",\"options\":[\"The vertex M\",\"The side LC\",\"The extension of the base CM\",\"The vertex C\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the height LD is a perpendicular drawn to the line containing the base CM (extended to D).\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/130_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is required to find the area of a non-right-angled triangle?\",\"options\":[\"Only the lengths of all three sides\",\"The length of the diagonal\",\"The base and the corresponding height\",\"The perimeter and one side\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states Area of a triangle = (base × height) \\/ 2 for any triangle.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If we change the side chosen as the base of a triangle, what must also change to calculate the area correctly?\",\"options\":[\"The name of the triangle\",\"The corresponding height (perpendicular from the opposite vertex)\",\"The number of vertices\",\"The area of the triangle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The height is defined relative to the specific side taken as the base (perpendicular from the opposite vertex).\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the relationship between the area of a rectangle and the right-angled triangles formed by its diagonal?\",\"options\":[\"Area of rectangle = Area of one triangle\",\"Area of rectangle = 2 × Area of one triangle\",\"Area of rectangle = Area of triangle \\/ 2\",\"Area of rectangle = 4 × Area of one triangle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: 2 × Area of a right angled triangle = Area of a rectangle.\",\"topic\":\"Area of a triangle\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the formula for the area of a rectangle as used in the hall example?\",\"options\":[\"Length × Breadth\",\"Side × Side\",\"Length + Breadth\",\"2 × (Length + Breadth)\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states Area of the hall = Length × Breadth.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the formula for the area of a square carpet?\",\"options\":[\"Length × Breadth\",\"Side × Side\",\"4 × Side\",\"Side + Side\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Area of the square carpet = Side × Side.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the first example, what is the total area of the hall floor?\",\"options\":[\"9 sq.m.\",\"11 sq.m.\",\"20 sq.m.\",\"25 sq.m.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text calculates the area of the hall as 5 × 4 = 20 sq.m.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the area of the square carpet mentioned in the first example?\",\"options\":[\"9 sq.m.\",\"12 sq.m.\",\"16 sq.m.\",\"20 sq.m.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text calculates the area of the square carpet as 3 × 3 = 9 sq.m.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a hall has an area of 20 sq.m and a carpet covers 9 sq.m, how much area is not covered?\",\"options\":[\"29 sq.m.\",\"15 sq.m.\",\"12 sq.m.\",\"11 sq.m.\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text shows the calculation: 20 – 9 = 11 sq.m.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In Sunitabai\'s land, what is the side length of each square flower bed?\",\"options\":[\"12 meters\",\"4 meters\",\"10 meters\",\"16 meters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Sunitabai planted flower plants in square flower beds of side 4 meters each.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what do the four green square regions in the corners represent?\",\"options\":[\"The entire land\",\"The area without flowers\",\"The flower beds\",\"The carpet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes Sunitabai planting flower beds in the four corners of the land.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/132_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the length and breadth of the total land?\",\"options\":[\"12 m and 10 m\",\"4 m and 4 m\",\"120 m and 64 m\",\"5 m and 4 m\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure labels the sides as 12 m and 10 m, which the text confirms as length and breadth.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/132_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If one square flower bed has an area of 16 sq. m., what is the total area of four such beds?\",\"options\":[\"32 sq. m.\",\"64 sq. m.\",\"120 sq. m.\",\"56 sq. m.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text calculates the area of four flower beds as 4 × 16 sq.m = 64 sq. m.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How is the \'Area of land without flower beds\' determined in the second example?\",\"options\":[\"By adding the area of land and flower beds\",\"By multiplying length and breadth of the beds\",\"By subtracting the area of four flower beds from the total area of land\",\"By dividing the total area by four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: Area of land without flower beds = Area of land – Area of four flower beds.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the total area of the land that is 12 meters long and 10 meters wide?\",\"options\":[\"22 sq. m.\",\"44 sq. m.\",\"100 sq. m.\",\"120 sq. m.\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text calculates Area of land = 12 × 10 = 120 sq. m.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the calculations for Sunitabai\'s land, what is the final area left without flower beds?\",\"options\":[\"56 sq. m.\",\"64 sq. m.\",\"120 sq. m.\",\"16 sq. m.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that the area of land without flower beds is 120 – 64 = 56 sq. m.\",\"topic\":\"Illustrative Examples on Area\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the textbook tables, what is the unit used to measure the area of the figures?\",\"options\":[\"cm\",\"sq. cm.\",\"m\",\"sq. m.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The tables in the text explicitly use \'sq. cm.\' as the unit for Area.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the unit used to measure the perimeter in the provided tables?\",\"options\":[\"sq. cm.\",\"cm\",\"cm²\",\"m\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The tables list \'Perimeter (cm)\' as the standard unit for perimeter.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"From the table of squares, what happens to the area when the perimeter of a square is increased?\",\"options\":[\"The area decreases\",\"The area remains the same\",\"The area increases\",\"The area becomes zero\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'From the table above, it can be seen that if the perimeter of a square is increased, the area increases.\'\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What can be observed about rectangles that have the same perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"They must have the same area\",\"They can have different areas\",\"Their areas are always doubled\",\"They always have the same side lengths\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes: \'rectangles with the same perimeter can have different areas.\'\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the rectangle table, Rectangle 2 and Rectangle 3 both have a perimeter of 20 cm. What does this demonstrate?\",\"options\":[\"Rectangles with the same perimeter always have the same area\",\"Rectangles with the same perimeter can have different areas\",\"The area is always half of the perimeter\",\"The length and breadth must be equal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows that even with the same perimeter (20 cm), the areas differ (16 sq. cm. vs 24 sq. cm.).\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a square has a side of 3 cm, its perimeter is 12 cm. If the side increases to 4 cm, what happens to the perimeter according to the table?\",\"options\":[\"It increases to 16 cm\",\"It decreases to 9 cm\",\"It stays at 12 cm\",\"It increases to 20 cm\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table shows that for Side 3, Perimeter is 12, and for Side 4, Perimeter is 16.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the rectangle table, if Rectangle 3 has a length of 6 cm and a breadth of 4 cm, what is its perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"10 cm\",\"24 cm\",\"20 cm\",\"18 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Perimeter = 2 * (length + breadth) = 2 * (6 + 4) = 20 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the square table, when the side of a square is 5 cm, what is its perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"10 cm\",\"15 cm\",\"20 cm\",\"25 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Perimeter of a square = 4 * side = 4 * 5 = 20 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Using the data for Rectangle 4 (Length 9 cm, Breadth 1 cm), calculate its area.\",\"options\":[\"10 sq. cm.\",\"20 sq. cm.\",\"9 sq. cm.\",\"18 sq. cm.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Area of a rectangle = length * breadth = 9 * 1 = 9 sq. cm.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Calculate the area of Square 3 in the table where the side is 5 cm.\",\"options\":[\"20 sq. cm.\",\"25 sq. cm.\",\"10 sq. cm.\",\"15 sq. cm.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Area of a square = side * side = 5 * 5 = 25 sq. cm.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Compare Rectangle 2 (L=8, B=2) and Rectangle 4 (L=9, B=1). Both have a perimeter of 20 cm. Which one has a smaller area?\",\"options\":[\"Rectangle 2\",\"Rectangle 4\",\"Both have the same area\",\"Rectangle 3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Rectangle 2 area = 16 sq. cm.; Rectangle 4 area = 9 sq. cm. Therefore, Rectangle 4 is smaller.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"For Square 4 in the table, the side is 6 cm. What are its Perimeter and Area respectively?\",\"options\":[\"24 cm and 36 sq. cm.\",\"36 cm and 24 sq. cm.\",\"12 cm and 36 sq. cm.\",\"24 cm and 24 sq. cm.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Perimeter = 4 * 6 = 24 cm; Area = 6 * 6 = 36 sq. cm.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of Perimeter and Area\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the perimeter of a closed figure?\",\"options\":[\"The measurement of the space occupied by the figure\",\"The sum of the length of all the sides of the figure\",\"The product of the base and the height\",\"The length of the longest side only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines perimeter as the sum of the length of all the sides of a closed figure.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the side of a triangle is measured in centimeters (cm), what will be the unit of its perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"sq cm\",\"cm\",\"m\",\"cubic cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the unit of the perimeter of any figure is the same as the unit of its side.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the measurement of the space occupied by a figure on a flat surface represent?\",\"options\":[\"Perimeter\",\"Height\",\"Area\",\"Length\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the area of a figure is the measurement of the space occupied by that figure on a flat surface.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which formula is used to calculate the area of a triangle?\",\"options\":[\"(base + height) \\/ 2\",\"base × height\",\"(base × height) \\/ 2\",\"base + height + side\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly provides the formula: Area of a triangle = (base × height) \\/ 2.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How is the area of a right angled triangle calculated?\",\"options\":[\"(Sum of the sides) \\/ 2\",\"(Product of the length of the sides forming the right angle) \\/ 2\",\"Product of all three sides \\/ 2\",\"Base × Height × 2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the area of a right angled triangle is (Product of the length of the sides forming the right angle) \\/ 2.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A triangle has a base of 8 cm and a height of 4 cm. What is its area?\",\"options\":[\"32 sq cm\",\"12 sq cm\",\"16 sq cm\",\"24 sq cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Using the formula (base × height) \\/ 2: (8 × 4) \\/ 2 = 32 \\/ 2 = 16.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In a right angled triangle, the two sides forming the right angle are 6 cm and 10 cm. What is its area?\",\"options\":[\"60 sq cm\",\"30 sq cm\",\"16 sq cm\",\"20 sq cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using the formula (Product of sides forming right angle) \\/ 2: (6 × 10) \\/ 2 = 60 \\/ 2 = 30.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the perimeter of a closed figure is 40 meters, what can we conclude about the units of its sides?\",\"options\":[\"The sides are measured in square meters\",\"The sides are measured in meters\",\"The sides are measured in centimeters\",\"The sides have no units\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the unit of perimeter is the same as the unit of its side; thus, if perimeter is in meters, sides are in meters.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following describes the relationship between a figure\'s sides and its perimeter?\",\"options\":[\"Perimeter is the space inside the sides\",\"Perimeter is the product of all sides\",\"Perimeter is the total length of all sides\",\"Perimeter is half the sum of the sides\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines perimeter as the sum of the length of all the sides.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To calculate the area of a right angled triangle, which information is essential based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"The length of the perimeter\",\"The length of all three sides\",\"The lengths of the sides that form the right angle\",\"The measurement of the space outside the figure\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The formula for a right angled triangle specifically requires the product of the lengths of the sides forming the right angle.\",\"topic\":\"At a glance\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21833,34,6,'Maths','en','Baudhayana-Pythagoras Theorem','[\"Right‑angled triangle has one 90° angle.\",\"The side opposite the 90° angle is called the hypotenuse.\",\"Other two sides are called legs or catheti.\",\"In a right‑angled triangle, the square of the hypotenuse equals the sum of the squares of the legs.\",\"Formula: c² = a² + b² (c = hypotenuse).\",\"If a,b,c satisfy c² = a² + b², the triangle is right‑angled.\",\"Triples like (3,4,5), (7,24,25) are Baudhayana‑Pythagorean triples.\",\"For any right‑angled triangle, the hypotenuse is the longest side.\",\"To find a missing side, rearrange the formula: a = √(c² – b²).\",\"In a right‑angled triangle, the area of the square on the hypotenuse equals the combined area of squares on the legs.\",\"The theorem was known to the Indian sage Baudhayana before Pythagoras.\",\"A ladder leaning against a wall forms a right‑angled triangle with the ground.\",\"When two legs are known, the distance from the base to the top of the ladder is √(ladder² – horizontal²).\",\"If the sides of a triangle form a Pythagorean triple, the triangle is right‑angled.\",\"When given a set of three numbers, check if the largest squared equals the sum of the other two squared to decide if it is a triple.\",\"The Pythagorean theorem is used to find missing lengths in many everyday problems.\",\"In a triangle with sides 11,12,15 the largest side squared (225) is less than the sum of the other two squares (265), so it is not right‑angled.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is a triangle called if one of its angles is a right angle?\",\"options\":[\"Acute angled triangle\",\"Right angled triangle\",\"Obtuse angled triangle\",\"Equilateral triangle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a right angled triangle as a triangle in which one angle is a right angle.\",\"topic\":\"Right angled triangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a right angled triangle, what is the name of the side opposite the right angle?\",\"options\":[\"Base\",\"Height\",\"Hypotenuse\",\"Median\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the side opposite the right angle is called the hypotenuse.\",\"topic\":\"Right angled triangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, triangles are classified into types based on which two criteria?\",\"options\":[\"Angles and sides\",\"Area and perimeter\",\"Color and size\",\"Height and weight\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions types of triangles based on angles and types of triangles based on sides.\",\"topic\":\"Right angled triangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the triangle ΔPQR mentioned in the text, if side PR is the hypotenuse, which sides form the right angle?\",\"options\":[\"Side PQ and Side PR\",\"Side PR and Side QR\",\"Side PQ and Side QR\",\"Side PQ and Side PQ\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that in ΔPQR, side PQ and side QR are the sides that form the right angle.\",\"topic\":\"Right angled triangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If side PR is the hypotenuse of ΔPQR, which of the following statements is true?\",\"options\":[\"∠PQR is a right angle\",\"∠QPR is a right angle\",\"∠PRQ is a right angle\",\"Side PQ is the hypotenuse\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Since side PR is opposite the right angle, the right angle must be at vertex Q, making ∠PQR the right angle.\",\"topic\":\"Right angled triangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In a right angled triangle, if the right angle is ∠LMN, which sides form the right angle?\",\"options\":[\"Side LM and Side LN\",\"Side MN and Side LN\",\"Side LM and Side MN\",\"Side LN and Side LM\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sides meeting at the vertex of the right angle (M) are the sides that form the right angle.\",\"topic\":\"Right angled triangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a right angled triangle has a right angle at vertex Y, which side is the hypotenuse?\",\"options\":[\"Side XY\",\"Side YZ\",\"Side XZ\",\"Side YX\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The hypotenuse is the side opposite the right angle; for a right angle at Y, the opposite side is XZ.\",\"topic\":\"Right angled triangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In a right angled triangle, if side AB and side BC form the right angle, where is the right angle located?\",\"options\":[\"At vertex A\",\"At vertex B\",\"At vertex C\",\"Opposite side AC\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The common vertex of the two sides that form the right angle is where the right angle is located.\",\"topic\":\"Right angled triangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, look at the triangle in Sr. No. 2. Which side is the hypotenuse?\",\"options\":[\"Side DE\",\"Side DF\",\"Side EF\",\"Side D\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In triangle DEF, the right angle is at vertex D, so the opposite side EF is the hypotenuse.\",\"topic\":\"Right angled triangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/136_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, look at the triangle in Sr. No. 3. Which angle is the right angle?\",\"options\":[\"∠GHI\",\"∠HGI\",\"∠HIG\",\"∠GIH\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The square symbol indicating the right angle is at vertex G, which is ∠HGI.\",\"topic\":\"Right angled triangle\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/136_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the side length of each square piece used in the activity?\",\"options\":[\"One unit\",\"Two units\",\"Three units\",\"Four units\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states to cut several square pieces with side one unit each.\",\"topic\":\"Do it.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the right-angled triangle formed in the activity, what is the name of side AC?\",\"options\":[\"Base\",\"Perpendicular\",\"Hypotenuse\",\"Adjacent side\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text refers to side AC as the hypotenuse.\",\"topic\":\"Do it.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many square pieces are placed in a straight line to form the segment AB?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"4\",\"5\",\"9\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to place 4 pieces in a straight line and name their end points A and B.\",\"topic\":\"Do it.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the total number of square pieces used to form the square on the hypotenuse AC?\",\"options\":[\"9\",\"16\",\"25\",\"7\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that total 25 pieces were used to form the square on hypotenuse AC.\",\"topic\":\"Do it.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the activity, the area of the square drawn on the hypotenuse is equal to which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"The difference of the areas of the squares on the other two sides\",\"The sum of the areas of the squares drawn on the other two sides\",\"The product of the areas of the squares on the other two sides\",\"The length of the other two sides added together\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that the area of the square on the hypotenuse is equal to the sum of the areas of the squares on the other two sides.\",\"topic\":\"Do it.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the square on side BC uses 9 pieces and the square on side AB uses 16 pieces, what is the sum of the pieces on both sides forming the right angle?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"12\",\"25\",\"144\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows the calculation: Total square pieces on both sides forming the right angle = 9 + 16 = 25.\",\"topic\":\"Do it.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which mathematical statement correctly represents the relationship found in the activity?\",\"options\":[\"Square of 3 + Square of 4 = Square of 5\",\"Square of 3 + Square of 4 = Square of 7\",\"3 + 4 = 5\",\"9 + 16 = 7\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states: Square of 3 + Square of 4 = Square of 5.\",\"topic\":\"Do it.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the formula provided in the text, if the area of the square on side BC is 9 and the area of the square on side AB is 16, what is [(AC)]²?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"25\",\"144\",\"5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using the formula [(BC)]² + [(AB)]² = [(AC)]², we get 9 + 16 = 25.\",\"topic\":\"Do it.\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If we use the pieces from the squares on sides AB and BC to cover the square on side AC, how many square units will the area of the square on AC be?\",\"options\":[\"16 square units\",\"9 square units\",\"25 square units\",\"7 square un