ons based on them.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of collecting graphs from newspapers according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To see various information\",\"To learn how to print\",\"To check the weather\",\"To practice cutting paper\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text notes that these graphs show various information.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the instructions, which of these is a necessary step before drawing a bar graph of garden plants?\",\"options\":[\"Buying a new ruler\",\"Collecting information\",\"Planting new seeds\",\"Asking the teacher for a graph\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text implies that you must collect information about the plants before you can draw the graph.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final goal of the activity involving the school garden?\",\"options\":[\"To become a gardener\",\"To represent collected data as a bar graph\",\"To identify different species of flowers\",\"To clean the garden area\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ultimate goal stated is to try to draw a bar graph from the information collected.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21836,34,6,'Maths','en','Magical Mathematics - 2','[\"Ramanujan\'s birthday is 22 December 1887 and is celebrated as National Mathematics Day.\",\"In Ramanujan\'s square, the sum of numbers in each row, column, and diagonal is 139.\",\"Tower of Hanoi with n discs requires minimum 2^n - 1 moves to transfer all discs.\",\"For 3 discs in Tower of Hanoi, minimum moves = 7; for 4 discs, 15; for 5 discs, 31.\",\"To find a lighter object among 9 identical objects using a pan balance, minimum 2 weighings are needed.\",\"Area of square = side × side; perimeter of square = 4 × side.\",\"If two squares are joined along a side, the area of the resulting shape equals sum of individual areas.\",\"In a right-angled triangle, square of hypotenuse = sum of squares of other two sides (Pythagoras theorem).\",\"Twin primes are pairs of primes differing by 2, e.g., (3,5), (11,13), (17,19).\",\"Profit = Selling Price - Cost Price; Loss = Cost Price - Selling Price.\",\"Percentage profit or loss is calculated on cost price.\",\"To convert percentage to fraction, divide by 100 and simplify.\",\"To find simple interest: SI = (P × R × T) \\/ 100, where P = principal, R = rate, T = time.\",\"Area of rectangle = length × breadth; perimeter = 2 × (length + breadth).\",\"Volume of cube = side³; volume of cuboid = length × breadth × height.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which place was the world-renowned mathematician Srinivas Ramanujan born?\",\"options\":[\"Erode\",\"Madras City\",\"Mumbai\",\"Delhi\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that Srinivas Ramanujan was born in Erode.\",\"topic\":\"Sir Srinivas Ramanujan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which date is celebrated as \'National Mathematics Day\' in India?\",\"options\":[\"December 22\",\"December 25\",\"January 22\",\"April 26\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the text, December 22 is celebrated as \'National Mathematics Day\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sir Srinivas Ramanujan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Approximately how many theorems did Ramanujan prove to become world-famous?\",\"options\":[\"4000\",\"1000\",\"2000\",\"8000\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he became world-famous for proving approximately 4000 theorems.\",\"topic\":\"Sir Srinivas Ramanujan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which province was Erode located during the time of Ramanujan\'s birth?\",\"options\":[\"Madras province\",\"Bombay province\",\"Bengal province\",\"Punjab province\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifies he was born in Erode, then in the Madras province.\",\"topic\":\"Sir Srinivas Ramanujan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":