ions\":[\"Your date of birth\",\"Your roll number\",\"Your favorite numbers\",\"Your age in years\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text suggests making a square like this with \'your date of birth\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sir Srinivas Ramanujan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the total sum of the four numbers in the first horizontal row (22, 12, 18, 87)?\",\"options\":[\"139\",\"129\",\"149\",\"138\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Adding the numbers in the first row: 22 + 12 + 18 + 87 = 139.\",\"topic\":\"Sir Srinivas Ramanujan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"34\\/160_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the properties of the Ramanujan Square, if the first row sums to 139, what must be the sum of the first vertical column (22, 88, 10, 19)?\",\"options\":[\"139\",\"140\",\"119\",\"200\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In a Ramanujan Square, the horizontal and vertical sums are the same.\",\"topic\":\"Sir Srinivas Ramanujan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How are the numbers in the first row of the Ramanujan Square (22, 12, 18, 87) organized?\",\"options\":[\"They represent the day, month, and year of his birth\",\"They are the first four prime numbers he discovered\",\"They represent the number of theorems he proved each year\",\"They are random numbers with no specific meaning\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The first row (22, 12, 18, 87) corresponds to his birth date: 22-12-1887.\",\"topic\":\"Sir Srinivas Ramanujan\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many wooden sticks are required to arrange the discs for the Brahma Tower game as per the instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Two sticks\",\"Three sticks\",\"Four sticks\",\"Five sticks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states to arrange three wooden sticks (bamboo sticks or empty sketch pens).\",\"topic\":\"Brahma Tower (Tower of Hanoi)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Rule 1 of the game, how many discs can be picked up from a stick at a time?\",\"options\":[\"Only one disc\",\"Two discs\",\"All discs at once\",\"Any number of discs\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Rule 1 explicitly states that only one disc can be picked up from any 1 stick at a time.\",\"topic\":\"Brahma Tower (Tower of Hanoi)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the Brahma Tower game, how are the coloured wooden discs initially arranged on the stick?\",\"options\":[\"In descending order of size\",\"In random order of size\",\"In ascending order of size\",\"By colour only\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions arranging discs of different sizes in ascending order.\",\"topic\":\"Brahma Tower (Tower of Hanoi)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the condition for the game to end?\",\"options\":[\"When all discs are moved to stick-2\",\"When all discs are moved to stick-3 in the original order\",\"When the discs are arranged in descending order\",\"When the player makes 10 moves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Rule 3 states the game ends when all the discs on stick-1 are moved to stick-3 in the original order.\",\"topic\":\"Brahma Tower (Tower of Hanoi)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following actions is strictly forbidden by Rule 2?\",\"options\":[\"Placing a smaller disc on a larger disc\",\"Moving a disc to an empty stick\",\"Placing a larger disc on a smaller disc\",\"Picking up a disc from stick-2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rule 2 states that a larger disk cannot be placed on a smaller disk.\",\"topic\":\"Brahma Tower (Tower of Hanoi)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the table provided for recording moves, what does the letter \'t\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"Total time taken\",\"Number of discs\",\"Number of moves\",\"Thickness of discs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the table columns, \'t\' is used as the symbol for the \'Number of moves\'.\",\"topic\":\"Brahma Tower (Tower of Hanoi)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If