ense of danger from an animal\",\"Changes in temperature\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The girl is covering her eyes in a sunny outdoor setting, indicating bright light is the stimulus.\",\"topic\":\"Response to Stimuli\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/017_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how quickly do animals respond to different stimuli?\",\"options\":[\"Slowly over many days\",\"Only after the sun sets\",\"Instantly\",\"Only when they are hungry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Animals respond to different stimuli instantly.\'\",\"topic\":\"Response to Stimuli\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the process of removal of waste materials from the body called?\",\"options\":[\"Respiration\",\"Excretion\",\"Reproduction\",\"Germination\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the removal of waste materials from the body as \'Excretion\'.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following waste materials is released by animals while breathing out?\",\"options\":[\"Urine\",\"Sweat\",\"Water vapour\",\"Tannins\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, animals release water vapour and carbon dioxide while breathing out.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where do plants store waste materials like calcium oxalate crystals?\",\"options\":[\"In the seeds\",\"In the flowers\",\"In the bark or old leaves\",\"In the new buds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that plants store waste in their bark or in old leaves.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the process called when a living organism produces another living organism like itself?\",\"options\":[\"Germination\",\"Excretion\",\"Reproduction\",\"Sprouting\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'Reproduction\' as the process where every living organism produces another living organism like itself.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the first part that grows out of the seed into the soil?\",\"options\":[\"Leaves\",\"Flowers\",\"Roots\",\"Stem\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the roots emerging and growing downwards into the soil first.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/018_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why do some plants release a sticky liquid from their stems?\",\"options\":[\"To attract insects\",\"Due to man-made or natural injury\",\"To store food for the winter\",\"To help the seeds grow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that plants release a sticky liquid (gum) due to some man-made or natural injury.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where does a seedling get its food from during the initial stages of growth?\",\"options\":[\"From the air\",\"From the sunlight\",\"Stored inside the seed\",\"From the soil minerals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the food for the seedling to grow is stored inside the seed.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these are considered the main characteristics to distinguish living organisms from non-living organisms?\",\"options\":[\"Breathing and walking\",\"Growth and reproduction\",\"Eating and sleeping\",\"Barking and running\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that growth and reproduction are the main characteristics used to distinguish living from non-living organisms.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student observes a plant shedding its old leaves. Which life process is primarily being demonstrated?\",\"options\":[\"Reproduction\",\"Excretion\",\"Germination\",\"Respiration\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\