ng sweat\\/CO2 and plants storing waste in bark\\/leaves or releasing gum.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a similarity between beans and grains like wheat regarding their seeds?\",\"options\":[\"They both lay eggs.\",\"They both contain stored food for the growing seed.\",\"They both produce gum from their stems.\",\"They both excrete through sweat.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes that both beans (two halves) and grains like wheat contain stored food for the growing seed.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement best describes the relationship between germination and growth?\",\"options\":[\"Germination happens after a plant is fully grown.\",\"Germination is the process of waste removal.\",\"Germination is the beginning stage of a plant\'s growth from a seed.\",\"Germination only occurs in animals that lay eggs.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that sprouting and germination are the beginning stages of a plant\'s growth.\",\"topic\":\"Excretion and Reproduction\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In which months do sea turtles usually lay their eggs on the beaches of the Konkan region?\",\"options\":[\"June to August\",\"September to November\",\"December to March\",\"April to May\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, sea turtles lay their eggs in the sand during December to March in the Konkan region.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know? (Sea Turtles)\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which species of sea turtle is mentioned as becoming rare nowadays?\",\"options\":[\"Green Sea Turtle\",\"Olive Ridley\",\"Leatherback Turtle\",\"Hawksbill Turtle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions that the Olive Ridley species of sea turtles is becoming rare.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know? (Sea Turtles)\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the female Olive Ridley turtle lay her eggs?\",\"options\":[\"In the seawater\",\"In a hole dug in the sand on the beach\",\"Under the rocks near the shore\",\"On the leaves of sea plants\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The female turtle digs a hole in the sand on the beach and lays her eggs there.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know? (Sea Turtles)\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, in which specific areas are the eggs usually laid?\",\"options\":[\"In deep shaded areas\",\"Where the rays of the rising sun fall\",\"Far away from the shoreline\",\"Inside the seawater\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that these eggs are usually laid in areas where the rays of the rising sun fall.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know? (Sea Turtles)\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens immediately after the hatchlings emerge from their eggs at dawn?\",\"options\":[\"They start digging deeper into the sand\",\"They wait for the villagers to pick them up\",\"They move towards the bright light of the sea\",\"They hide under the electric lamps\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Hatchlings immediately start moving towards the bright light on the surface of the sea to enter the water.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know? (Sea Turtles)\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it vital for the turtle hatchlings to reach the seawater quickly?\",\"options\":[\"To find food immediately\",\"To avoid getting a sunburn\",\"Because they may not survive otherwise\",\"To meet the other adult turtles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions it is vital for them to reach seawater quickly because if they do not, they may not survive.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know? (Sea Turtles)\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What color does the eastern sky turn just before sunrise during the hatching season?\",\"options\":[\"Bright blue\",\"Dark purple\",\"Reddish hue\",\"Pale yellow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes that just before sunrise, the eastern sky