y describes the relationship between breathing and respiration?\",\"options\":[\"Breathing and respiration are the same process\",\"Breathing is a part of movement\",\"Breathing and respiration are two different processes\",\"Plants breathe but do not respire\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that breathing and respiration are two different processes.\",\"topic\":\"Respiration and Movement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why do animals show movements such as walking, jumping, or swimming?\",\"options\":[\"To produce carbon dioxide\",\"To obtain food, protection, and shelter\",\"To help plants grow towards sunlight\",\"To turn food into oxygen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Animals move to obtain food, protection, shelter, and as a response to stimuli.\",\"topic\":\"Respiration and Movement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a plant is placed in a room where sunlight comes only from a window on the left, what movement will the branches show?\",\"options\":[\"They will grow away from the window\",\"They will stop growing\",\"They will grow in the direction of the sunlight\",\"They will fold their leaves immediately\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that if sunlight comes from one side, the branches grow in that direction.\",\"topic\":\"Respiration and Movement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the growth of roots towards moisture demonstrate about plants?\",\"options\":[\"Plants can move from one place to another\",\"Plants are aware of their surroundings\",\"Plants do not need oxygen\",\"Plants are looking for shelter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Roots growing towards moisture shows that plants are aware of their surroundings.\",\"topic\":\"Respiration and Movement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the leaves of certain trees when the sun sets and it gets dark?\",\"options\":[\"They fall off the branches\",\"They change their color\",\"They fold together like