a dark corner\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that healing and growth occur because new cells are constantly being formed.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which of these parts has a different cell structure compared to the others?\",\"options\":[\"Bones\",\"Water tanks\",\"Wooden objects\",\"Earthen pots\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions differences in the structure of cells in parts such as bones, muscles, and skin.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the experiment with seeds, how often should you maintain the record of observations?\",\"options\":[\"Every day\",\"Every second day\",\"Every third day\",\"Once a week\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to maintain the record after every third day.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to a piece of a wooden object if it breaks off?\",\"options\":[\"It grows new shoots\",\"It heals over time\",\"It does not return to its original shape\",\"It forms new cells\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text implies that non-living objects like wooden objects do not return to their original shape after breaking.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student plants bean seeds, which of the following can they observe over a long time?\",\"options\":[\"The growth of mosquito larvae\",\"The vine, its leaves, and pods\",\"The transformation of soil into sand\",\"The healing of wooden objects\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states you can observe the growing vine, its leaves, and pods by planting bean seeds.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the organisms shown in the magnified circular views?\",\"options\":[\"Small fish\",\"Mosquito larvae\",\"Bean seeds\",\"Plant cells\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text and figure describe small larvae of mosquitoes found in stagnant water like puddles or tanks.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/021_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, where is the most likely place to find these larvae in a home environment?\",\"options\":[\"In a dry earthen pot\",\"On a new shoot of a tree\",\"In an uncovered container of water in a dark corner\",\"Inside a bag of bean seeds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that mosquito larvae can be seen in containers of water left uncovered in dark corners.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/021_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the movement of mosquito larvae described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Moving from the edges to the center only\",\"Moving up and down from the bottom to the top\",\"Staying still at the bottom\",\"Crawling on the soil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that larvae can be seen moving up and down from the bottom to the top of the water.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A student observes a tree trunk and a broken glass pot. What is the fundamental difference in their ability to \'repair\' themselves?\",\"options\":[\"The glass pot needs more water to grow\",\"The tree trunk forms new cells while the glass pot cannot\",\"The glass pot is kept in the sun while the tree is in the dark\",\"The tree trunk has no nutrients\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Growth and healing in living things (like trees) happen because new cells are formed, which non-living things (like glass) lack.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following seeds is NOT mentioned in the \'Try this\' activity for germination?\",\"options\":[\"Brinjal\",\"Mango\",\"Tomato\",\"Corn\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists red chili, brinjal, beans, tomato, and corn, but not mango.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What will happen to the small larvae in a water tank if they are observed over several days?\",\"options\":[\"They will turn into seeds\",\"They will transform into mosquitoes\",\"They will become new cells of the tank\",\"They will disappear into the soil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that within a few days, these small larvae transform into mosquitoes.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text suggest that there are many mosquitoes near the edges of a pond?\",\"options\":[\"Because the water is cleaned regularly\",\"Because the mosquitoes eat the sand\",\"Because larvae in the water transform into mosquitoes there\",\"Because the pond is made of cells\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links the presence of larvae in stagnant water to the transformation into mosquitoes.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If you are recording the germination of a seed, which specific features does the text tell you to record?\",\"options\":[\"The amount of sand and soil used\",\"The size, number, and shape of the leaves\",\"The depth of the water tank\",\"The structure of the bone cells\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks to keep a record of time for germination, and the size, number, and shape of the leaves.\",\"topic\":\"Cells and Growth\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What do the clusters of frog eggs look like when observed near a pond?\",\"options\":[\"Small black stones\",\"White foam\",\"Green leaves\",\"Yellow jelly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that clusters of frog eggs look like white foam.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific term used for the stages of change from a larva to an adult frog?\",\"options\":[\"Respiration\",\"Reproduction\",\"Metamorphosis\",\"Circulation\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the stages of change as the Life Cycle or Metamorphosis.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Through which organ does a tadpole breathe during its different stages?\",\"options\":[\"Lungs\",\"Skin\",\"Gills\",\"Nose\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that during the different stages, the tadpole breathes through gills.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where should the branch with frog eggs be placed when setting up an observation jar?\",\"options\":[\"Completely submerged in water\",\"Slightly above the water\",\"Outside the jar\",\"At the bottom of the jar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to make sure that the branch stays slightly above the water.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these animals has young ones that look very similar to their parents?\",\"options\":[\"Frog\",\"Butterfly\",\"Elephant\",\"Mosquito\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the young ones of cows or elephants have features very similar to their parents.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first thing that hatches from a frog\'s egg?\",\"options\":[\"A small frog\",\"A larva\",\"A kitten\",\"A pupa\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the larva hatches from the egg.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which body parts develop in a tadpole before it transforms into an adult frog?\",\"options\":[\"Wings and a beak\",\"Two hind legs and a tail\",\"Four legs and scales\",\"Fins and a blowhole\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the tadpole develops two hind legs and a tail.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are collecting water for a jar to observe frog eggs, which source is recommended by the text?\",\"options\":[\"Tap water\",\"Distilled water\",\"Water from the pond itself\",\"Boiled water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using water from the pond itself if possible.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it difficult to identify which animal a frog larva belongs to just by looking at it?\",\"options\":[\"It is too small to see\",\"It does not look like a frog at all\",\"It stays hidden under the branch\",\"It changes color every hour\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the larva does not look like a frog at all, creating a great difference from the parent.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What should a student do to track the changes in the frog\'s life cycle accurately over a week?\",\"options\":[\"Observe once a week\",\"Draw pictures and write down dates\",\"Only look at the eggs\",\"Keep the jar in the dark\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text advises to write down the date and draw pictures of observations each day.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the text, how does the growth of a kitten differ from the growth of a frog larva?\",\"options\":[\"A kitten undergoes metamorphosis, a frog does not\",\"A kitten looks like its parent from birth, while a frog larva does not\",\"A kitten breathes through gills, a frog larva does not\",\"A kitten hatches from an egg, a frog does not\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes kittens are identified as young cats immediately, whereas frog larvae look nothing like frogs.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of comparing your records with your friends\' records during the experiment?\",\"options\":[\"To see who drew the best picture\",\"To check if the developmental time is the same or different\",\"To see who found the most eggs\",\"To decide which pond water is better\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks students to compare the time required for changes to see if it is the same or different.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the instructions, what should be placed inside the jar for the developing larvae?\",\"options\":[\"Fish food\",\"A leaf\",\"Sand\",\"Small stones\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says \'Put a leaf in the jar for them.\'\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a characteristic of the \'Life Cycle\' described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The body structure never changes\",\"The young ones always look like parents\",\"It involves several stages of transformation\",\"It only happens in animals that give birth to live young\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the life cycle as going through several stages and transformation.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What can we conclude about animal reproduction from the examples of cows and frogs in the text?\",\"options\":[\"All animals are born from eggs\",\"All animals give birth to young ones\",\"Some animals are born from eggs, while others are born from their mothers\",\"Young ones always look different from their parents\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states some animals are born from eggs, while in some, the mother gives birth to young ones.\",\"topic\":\"Life Cycle of a Frog\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the process of a new plant growing from a seed called?\",\"options\":[\"Respiration\",\"Germination\",\"Excretion\",\"Nutrition\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the growth of a new plant from a seed is called germination.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following are identified as the main characteristics of living organisms?\",\"options\":[\"Movement and Excretion\",\"Growth and Reproduction\",\"Respiration and Nutrition\",\"Stimulus and Response\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that among all characteristics, growth and reproduction are the main ones.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do all living things need food?\",\"options\":[\"To change their location\",\"For energy and growth\",\"To sense the surroundings\",\"To produce seeds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that every living thing needs food for energy and growth.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does the movement of plants differ from that of animals?\",\"options\":[\"Plants can change their location like animals\",\"Plants do not show any kind of movement\",\"Plants cannot change their place on their own\",\"Animals cannot change their location\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that animals can change location, but plants cannot change their place on their own.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a living organism is so small that it cannot be seen with the naked eye, it is classified as:\",\"options\":[\"Macroscopic\",\"Microscopic\",\"A seed\",\"A response\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes organisms that cannot be seen with the naked eye as microscopic.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A plant bends towards a source of light. In this scenario, the light is the ________ and the bending is the ________.\",\"options\":[\"Response, Stimulus\",\"Stimulus, Response\",\"Growth, Germination\",\"Nutrition, Energy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ability to sense surroundings is the stimulus, and the resulting action is the response.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the term for the ability of a living being to sense its surroundings?\",\"options\":[\"Reaction\",\"Stimulus\",\"Respiration\",\"Excretion\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the ability to sense surroundings as a stimulus.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do \'life stages\' or a \'life cycle\' refer to in living organisms?\",\"options\":[\"The ability to move from place to place\",\"The process of taking in food for energy\",\"Significant changes in body structure during growth\",\"The process of removing waste from the body\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines life stages or life cycles as significant changes that occur in body structure during growth.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which process is directly responsible for nutrition occurring in living organisms?\",\"options\":[\"Respiration\",\"Movement\",\"The intake of food\",\"Germination\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that nutrition in living organisms occurs because of the food.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the list provided in the text, which of these is NOT mentioned as a characteristic of living organisms?\",\"options\":[\"Respiration\",\"Excretion\",\"Digestion\",\"Reproduction\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists growth, response to stimuli, excretion, respiration, reproduction, and movement, but does not list digestion.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is there diversity in the nutrition of living organisms?\",\"options\":[\"Because all organisms eat the same food\",\"Because different organisms have different types of food\",\"Because only animals require energy for growth\",\"Because plants do not require nutrition\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes that diversity in food leads to diversity in nutrition among different organisms.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement best describes the diversity of living organisms mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"All living organisms are macroscopic\",\"All living organisms are microscopic\",\"Living organisms range from microscopic to macroscopic\",\"Living organisms only exist as seeds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states there is a great diversity ranging from microscopic to macroscopic organisms.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21857,36,6,'Science','en','Measurement','[\"Measurement is the act of finding the size, amount or degree of something using a suitable instrument.\",\"Standard units give the same result for everyone; non‑standard units (finger‑width, hand span) vary with the person measuring.\",\"The SI (International System of Units) is the modern standard system used worldwide.\",\"Length is measured in metres (m). 1 metre = 100 centimetres (cm) = 1000 millimetres (mm).\",\"Kilometre (km) = 1000 metres – used for long distances between cities.\",\"Mass is measured in kilograms (kg).\",\"Time is measured in seconds (s).\",\"A ruler is used for straight lengths; a flexible measuring tape is used for curved surfaces or large objects.\",\"The starting point of a ruler or tape is called the reference point; the measurement is read from this point.\",\"A thermometer measures temperature; the most common units are Celsius (°C), Fahrenheit (°F) and Kelvin (K).\",\"The normal human body temperature is about 37 °C (98.6 °F).\",\"Digital thermometers give a numerical reading; infrared thermometers measure temperature from a distance without touching.\",\"A laboratory thermometer uses mercury or coloured alcohol in a glass tube; the liquid level indicates temperature on a scale.\",\"When measuring, keep the instrument straight, vertical and the bulb in contact with the object.\",\"Accuracy matters: a few millimetres may be acceptable for a playground but not for machine parts.\",\"Temperature cannot be known exactly by touch; a thermometer is required.\",\"The SI unit of temperature is Kelvin, but Celsius is used for everyday measurements.\",\"A ruler’s smallest readable length is usually 1 mm in a standard 15 cm ruler.\",\"The order of length units from largest to smallest is kilometre > metre > centimetre > millimetre.\",\"Standard measurement tools ensure consistency in trade, science and everyday life.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In ancient Egypt, what was the unit of length measured from a person\'s elbow to the tip of the middle finger called?\",\"options\":[\"Hand span\",\"Cubit\",\"Footstep\",\"Angul\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that in ancient Egypt, the distance from the elbow to the tip of the middle finger was called a Cubit.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the Roman unit \'mille passus\'?\",\"options\":[\"One hundred steps\",\"One thousand paces\",\"Twelve inches\",\"Two feet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that \'mille passus\' means one thousand paces.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Roman system, how many inches make up one foot?\",\"options\":[\"Ten\",\"Two\",\"Twelve\",\"One thousand\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Romans divided each foot into twelve equal parts called inches.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why are units like \'hand span\' and \'finger-width\' called non-standard measurements?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are very old units\",\"Because they are difficult to calculate\",\"Because measurements vary based on age and body size\",\"Because they are only used for measuring furniture\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that because age and body sizes vary, measurements taken by different people also vary, which is why they are called non-standard.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main characteristic of a \'Standard measurement\' system?\",\"options\":[\"It uses body parts for measuring\",\"The measurement remains the same regardless of who measures it\",\"It was only used by Kings in the past\",\"It changes according to the size of the object\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines standard measurement as a system where a fixed unit is used so the measurement remains the same for everyone.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In ancient Egypt, why was the \'Royal Cubit\' established?\",\"options\":[\"To measure the height of the King\",\"Because the standard cubit varied from person to person\",\"To measure long distances like miles\",\"Because it was divided into twelve inches\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says that since the cubit varied from person to person, the King’s cubit was established as the Royal Cubit for consistency.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you buy one metre of cloth from a shop and your grandfather measures it again at home with a metre scale, what will be the result?\",\"options\":[\"The measurement will be different because of age\",\"The measurement will be different because of body size\",\"The measurement will be the same\",\"The measurement will change depending on the shop\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since a metre scale is a standard measurement, the measurement remains the same regardless of who measures it.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if both the man and the girl measure the length of the same table using their hand spans, what is the most likely outcome?\",\"options\":[\"Both will get the exact same number of hand spans\",\"The man will count more hand spans than the girl\",\"The girl will count more hand spans than the man\",\"Hand spans cannot be used to measure tables\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Because the girl\'s hand is smaller than the man\'s, she will need to use more hand spans to cover the same distance.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/025_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, why is the method of measurement shown considered unreliable for official trade?\",\"options\":[\"Because hand spans are too difficult to count\",\"Because the size of a hand span differs between the man and the girl\",\"Because tables should only be measured in inches\",\"Because the table is too long for hand spans\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes that measurements vary because body sizes vary, making hand spans a non-standard and unreliable method.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/025_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Comparing the ancient Roman \'mille passus\' to the modern \'mile\', which statement is correct according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"They are exactly the same distance\",\"The mille passus is longer than the mile\",\"The mile is slightly more than the mille passus\",\"The mile is exactly two thousand paces\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the distance we call a mile today is slightly more than the mille passus.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these units from the past was specifically used to measure long distances?\",\"options\":[\"Mushti\",\"Angul\",\"Mille passus\",\"Hasta\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that for long distances, the Romans used a unit called mille passus.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following describes the relationship between a Roman cubit and a Roman foot?\",\"options\":[\"A cubit was divided into two feet\",\"A foot was divided into two cubits\",\"A cubit was equal to twelve feet\",\"A foot was equal to one thousand cubits\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Romans had their own version of the cubit, divided into two feet.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and History\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the International System of Units also known as?\",\"options\":[\"Regional System\",\"Standard System\",\"Local System\",\"Common System\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the uniform system of measuring instruments and units is known as the Standard System or the International System of Units (SI Units).\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the SI system, which unit is used for measuring Mass?\",\"options\":[\"Metre\",\"Second\",\"Gram\",\"Kilogram\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table in the text lists Kilogram (kg) as the unit for Mass.\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was a uniform system of measurement established globally?\",\"options\":[\"To make rulers look the same\",\"To solve difficulties in trade and daily tasks\",\"To increase the number of units\",\"To make measuring distance harder\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that different regional units caused significant difficulties in trade, leading to the establishment of a uniform system.\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many centimetres (cm) make up one metre (m)?\",\"options\":[\"10\",\"1000\",\"100\",\"15\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that 1 metre = 100 centimetres.\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a millimetre (mm) in relation to a centimetre (cm)?\",\"options\":[\"It is the tenth part of a centimetre\",\"It is ten times larger than a centimetre\",\"It is the hundredth part of a centimetre\",\"It is equal to one centimetre\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines a millimetre as the tenth part of a centimetre (1cm = 10 millimetre).\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which unit is most suitable for measuring the distance between two cities?\",\"options\":[\"Metre\",\"Centimetre\",\"Kilometre\",\"Millimetre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that for measuring the distance between two cities, a larger unit called the kilometre (km) is used.\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a line segment measures 4 centimetres, how many millimetres long is it?\",\"options\":[\"400 mm\",\"40 mm\",\"0.4 mm\",\"4000 mm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since 1 cm = 10 mm, 4 cm equals 4 x 10 = 40 mm.\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct symbol for the SI unit of Time?\",\"options\":[\"T\",\"sec\",\"m\",\"s\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table in the text shows that the symbol for the unit \'Second\' is \'s\'.\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A playground needs to be measured. According to the text, which unit is more suitable than a centimetre for this task?\",\"options\":[\"Millimetre\",\"Metre\",\"Kilogram\",\"Second\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that for measuring the length and breadth of a playground, the metre is a more suitable unit.\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the distance between two points is 2000 metres, what is this distance in kilometres?\",\"options\":[\"20 km\",\"200 km\",\"2 km\",\"0.2 km\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since 1 km = 1000 metres, 2000 metres equals 2 kilometres.\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"On a standard 15 cm ruler, what does the distance between two big markings represent?\",\"options\":[\"1 millimetre\",\"1 metre\",\"10 centimetres\",\"1 centimetre\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states that on the 15 cm ruler, the distance between two big markings is 1 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a piece of cloth is 3 metres long, how many centimetres is its length?\",\"options\":[\"30 cm\",\"300 cm\",\"3000 cm\",\"3.0 cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Using the conversion 1 metre = 100 centimetres, 3 metres equals 300 centimetres.\",\"topic\":\"Standard System of Units (SI Units)\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is necessary to measure the distance between any two points?\",\"options\":[\"A weighing scale\",\"A ruler\",\"A thermometer\",\"A stopwatch\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a ruler is necessary to measure the distance between any two points.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific instrument is mentioned as being perfect for measuring the length of a piece of chalk?\",\"options\":[\"A metre scale\",\"A surveyor\'s tape\",\"A 15 cm ruler\",\"A tailor\'s tape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that a ruler of 15 cm is perfect for measuring a piece of chalk.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do different types of measuring tapes have different markings?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are made by different companies\",\"Because they have convenient markings based on their requirements\",\"Because the units of measurement change every year\",\"Because markings are only for decoration\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that measuring tapes have convenient markings based on the requirements of the users like carpenters or surveyors.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you need to measure the height of a classroom door, which tool should you choose according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A 15 cm ruler\",\"A metre scale\",\"A piece of string\",\"A compass\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that to measure the height of a door, a metre scale or a measuring tape will be required.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which instrument is essential for measuring the circumference of objects with curved surfaces?\",\"options\":[\"A rigid wooden ruler\",\"A metal scale\",\"A flexible measuring tape\",\"A surveyor\'s chain\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that for curved surfaces, we must use the flexible measuring tape (tailor\'s tape).\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a 15 cm ruler not suitable for measuring the height of a door?\",\"options\":[\"It is too flexible for the door\",\"It is not appropriate for the size of the requirement\",\"It cannot measure straight lines\",\"It is only used for curved surfaces\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text implies we must use appropriate tools; a 15 cm ruler is for small items like chalk, while a door requires a metre scale.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Flexible measuring tape is also known as ______.\",\"options\":[\"Carpenter\'s tape\",\"Surveyor\'s tape\",\"Tailor\'s tape\",\"Merchant\'s tape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses the term \'tailor\'s tape\' as a synonym for flexible measuring tape.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which professional would likely use a measuring tape with markings specific to their work?\",\"options\":[\"A Chef\",\"A Carpenter\",\"A Doctor\",\"A Musician\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions carpenters, cloth merchants, and surveyors as users of measuring tapes.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student needs to measure the round edge of a circular table. Which tool from the text is best for this task?\",\"options\":[\"A 15 cm ruler\",\"A rigid metre scale\",\"A tailor\'s tape\",\"A surveyor\'s metal tape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A circular table has a curved surface, and the text says flexible (tailor\'s) tape is used for curved surfaces.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the most important factor when choosing a measuring tape according to the topic?\",\"options\":[\"The color of the tape\",\"The material of the tape\",\"The needs of the specific measurement task\",\"The price of the tape\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states it is essential to use the appropriate type of tape according to our needs.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, several types of measuring instruments are shown. Which of these is most likely the \'flexible measuring tape\' mentioned for curved surfaces?\",\"options\":[\"The rigid metal ruler at the bottom\",\"The long, thin white and orange ribbons at the top\",\"The yellow tape in the middle\",\"The small metal retractable tape\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The white and orange tapes shown are flexible (tailor\'s tapes), unlike the rigid ruler at the bottom.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/026_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the variety of tools shown supports which statement from the text?\",\"options\":[\"All measuring tapes are exactly the same.\",\"Only rulers are used for measurement.\",\"Measuring tapes have convenient markings based on their requirements.\",\"Curved surfaces cannot be measured.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows different designs and markings, illustrating that tapes are designed for specific requirements.\",\"topic\":\"Accurate Measurement of Length\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/026_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"For accurate measurement, where should the object be placed in relation to the ruler?\",\"options\":[\"Slightly above the ruler\",\"In direct contact with the ruler\",\"A few centimeters away from the ruler\",\"At an angle to the ruler\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the object whose length is to be measured must be in direct contact with the ruler.\",\"topic\":\"Correct Position of the Ruler\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which mark on the ruler should be aligned with the beginning edge of the object?\",\"options\":[\"The 1 cm mark\",\"The middle mark\",\"The 0 mark\",\"The 10 cm mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The ruler should be held such that its starting point (the 0 mark) aligns with the beginning edge of the object.\",\"topic\":\"Correct Position of the Ruler\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do if the zero mark of your ruler is broken or not clear?\",\"options\":[\"Discard the ruler and do not measure\",\"Guess the distance from the broken edge\",\"Start measuring from the next clearly visible number\",\"Always add 1 cm to the final reading\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"If the zero mark is not clear or broken, the text advises starting measurement from the next clearly visible number.\",\"topic\":\"Correct Position of the Ruler\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you start measuring an object from the 2 cm mark and the reading at the other end is 9 cm, what is the exact length of the object?\",\"options\":[\"9 cm\",\"11 cm\",\"7 cm\",\"2 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"By subtracting the initial number (2) from the final reading (9), we get the exact length: 9 - 2 = 7 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Correct Position of the Ruler\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},