s broken. The final reading is 15 cm. What is the length of the ribbon?\",\"options\":[\"15 cm\",\"20 cm\",\"10 cm\",\"5 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Subtract the initial number from the final reading: 15 - 5 = 10 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Correct Position of the Ruler\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a thread preferred over a ruler to measure the circumference of a ball?\",\"options\":[\"Because a thread is longer than a ruler\",\"Because a ruler cannot bend along the curved surface\",\"Because a thread has centimeter marks on it\",\"Because a ball is too soft for a ruler\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text implies that for curved surfaces, a thread is used because a straight ruler cannot measure the curve directly.\",\"topic\":\"Correct Position of the Ruler\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of subtracting the initial number from the final reading when the zero mark is not used?\",\"options\":[\"The total length of the ruler\",\"The error in measurement\",\"The exact length of the object\",\"The distance to the zero mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that by subtracting the initial number from the final reading, you can obtain the exact length of the object.\",\"topic\":\"Correct Position of the Ruler\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the instructions for \'Correct Position of the Ruler\', which of these is a requirement for accuracy?\",\"options\":[\"The ruler must be longer than the object\",\"The reading must be taken from a side view\",\"The starting point must align with the beginning edge\",\"The object must be kept away from the ruler marks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"One of the important points is that the ruler\'s starting point must align with the beginning edge of the object.\",\"topic\":\"Correct Position of the Ruler\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific point or fixed object from which a distance is measured called?\",\"options\":[\"Starting line\",\"Reference Point\",\"Boundary mark\",\"Metre tape\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a \'Reference Point\' as the fixed object or specific point from which a distance is measured.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which tool does a sports teacher use to mark the boundaries for sports as shown in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A wooden ruler\",\"A piece of string\",\"A metre tape\",\"A milestone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that the sports teacher uses a metre tape to mark boundaries.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the game of Kho-Kho, what serves as the reference point for the second pole?\",\"options\":[\"The boundary line\",\"The metre tape\",\"The first fixed pole\",\"The milestone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that while marking the Kho-Kho field, the first fixed pole serves as the reference point for the second pole.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is indicated by the boards or stones (milestones) found on highways connecting major cities?\",\"options\":[\"The name of the sports teacher\",\"The distance to the next big town\",\"The length of the highway\",\"The speed limit of the town\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, milestones indicate the distance to the next big town.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why must a reference point be a \'fixed\' object or point?\",\"options\":[\"So it can be moved easily\",\"To ensure the distance measured remains consistent\",\"Because metre tapes only work with fixed objects\",\"To make the playground look better\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A reference point must be fixed so that the measurement taken from it is reliable and specific.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does every sports field have?\",\"options\":[\"Specific length and breadth\",\"Only one pole\",\"Milestones at every corner\",\"A highway connection\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that each sports field has specific length and breadth.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is asked to mark a boundary 10 metres away from a wall, what does the wall represent in this measurement?\",\"options\":[\"The metre tape\",\"The breadth\",\"The Reference Point\",\"The milestone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since the measurement starts from the wall, the wall acts as the fixed object or reference point.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When marking a playground for a competition, what is the first step the teacher must take before using the metre tape?\",\"options\":[\"Find the next big town\",\"Identify a fixed starting point or reference point\",\"Change the length and breadth of the field\",\"Remove all the poles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Measurement always requires a starting fixed point, which is the reference point.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A milestone shows \'Pune 50 km\'. In this context, what is the milestone acting as?\",\"options\":[\"A boundary line\",\"A reference point for the distance to the town\",\"A metre tape\",\"A sports field\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The milestone serves as a specific point to indicate how far the town is, functioning as a reference point.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What would happen to the distance between two Kho-Kho poles if the first pole was not fixed?\",\"options\":[\"The distance would always stay the same\",\"The reference point would be lost, making the measurement unreliable\",\"The metre tape would break\",\"The second pole would become the first pole\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"If the reference point is not fixed, the measurement between the two points cannot be accurately maintained.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Compare the use of a pole in Kho-Kho and a milestone on a highway. What is the common scientific purpose they both serve?\",\"options\":[\"They both mark the end of a town\",\"They both act as fixed reference points for measuring distance\",\"They are both used to mark sports boundaries\",\"They are both measured using the same metre tape\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Both the pole and the milestone serve as fixed points from which specific distances are determined.\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is the most essential requirement for measuring the length of a sports field accurately?\",\"options\":[\"Having a very long highway\",\"Using a milestone instead of a tape\",\"Establishing a fixed reference point\",\"Measuring from a moving object\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text emphasizes that whenever a distance is measured, it must be from a fixed object or specific point (Reference Point).\",\"topic\":\"Reference Point\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a special instrument mentioned in the text for precise measurements?\",\"options\":[\"Measuring tape\",\"Screw Gauge\",\"Metre scale\",\"Handspan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions the Screw Gauge as a special instrument used for precise measurements in industries.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"For which of the following is a measurement difference of one or two millimetres considered acceptable?\",\"options\":[\"Manufacturing machine parts\",\"Measuring the length of a shirt\",\"Fitting engine components\",\"Measuring thickness of a pencil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a difference of one or two millimetres is acceptable when measuring the length of a shirt or a playground.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why must machine parts be measured with extreme accuracy?\",\"options\":[\"To make them look shiny\",\"To ensure they match and fit together perfectly\",\"To increase their weight\",\"To make them easier to carry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that parts must match accurately so they can fit together perfectly.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In which setting are instruments like the Vernier Caliper mainly used?\",\"options\":[\"Tailoring shops\",\"Playgrounds\",\"Industries\",\"Classrooms\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that such precise instruments are mainly used in industries and factories that produce machinery.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To manufacture a machine part that fits perfectly, one must be able to measure accurately up to what range?\",\"options\":[\"Exactly one metre\",\"Much smaller than a millimetre\",\"Exactly one centimetre\",\"At least one decimetre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that for machine parts, one must make accurate measurements up to a much smaller range than a millimetre.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the \'Think\' section, which instrument would be most suitable to measure the thickness of a pencil?\",\"options\":[\"A measuring tape\",\"A long rope\",\"A Vernier Caliper\",\"A playground scale\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists the Vernier Caliper as a special instrument for measuring thickness and small ranges where precision is needed.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which unit would be most appropriate for measuring the length of a playground as discussed in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Millimetre\",\"Metre\",\"Milligram\",\"Litre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"While the text mentions millimetre differences are acceptable, the standard unit for large areas like playgrounds is the metre.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a factory produces machine parts using a standard ruler that only measures in whole millimetres, what is the most likely problem?\",\"options\":[\"The parts will be too colourful\",\"The parts may not fit together perfectly\",\"The parts will become too long for the factory\",\"The parts will be easier to sell\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text implies that without sub-millimetre accuracy, machine parts will not match and fit together as required.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the instrument shown in the given figure.\",\"options\":[\"Vernier Caliper\",\"Screw Gauge\",\"Thermometer\",\"Barometer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure is explicitly labeled as a \'Screw Gauge\' in the textbook diagram.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/028_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is being measured by the instrument?\",\"options\":[\"The length of a playground\",\"The thickness\\/diameter of a small sphere\",\"The weight of a red ball\",\"The temperature of a metal part\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a small red spherical object placed between the spindle and anvil to measure its thickness or diameter.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/028_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Compare the measurement of a saree and a machine part. Which statement is true based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Both require sub-millimetre precision.\",\"A saree needs more precision than a machine part.\",\"A machine part requires much higher precision than a saree.\",\"Neither requires accurate measurement.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that machine parts need accuracy smaller than a millimetre, whereas items like cloth (saree\\/shirt) allow for small differences.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these objects from the \'Think\' section would require the most precise instrument to measure its thickness?\",\"options\":[\"A classroom\",\"A playground\",\"A newspaper\",\"A saree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A newspaper sheet is very thin, requiring a precise instrument like a Screw Gauge to measure its thickness accurately.\",\"topic\":\"Precision in Measurement\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21858,36,6,'Science','en','Let\'s Separate the Components','[\"- A mixture is a combination of two or more substances that are not chemically bonded.\",\"- The parts that make up a mixture are called components.\",\"- Some mixtures can be separated easily by hand; others need special techniques.\",\"- Handpicking: pick out items by sight and touch (e.g., stones in wheat).\",\"- Winnowing: use wind or fan to separate light debris from heavy grains.\",\"- Sieving: use a mesh to separate particles of different sizes.\",\"- Filtration: use a strainer or filter paper to separate a solid from a liquid.\",\"- Sedimentation: heavy solid particles settle at the bottom of a liquid when left still.\",\"- Decantation: carefully pour the liquid off the settled solids.\",\"- Evaporation: a liquid turns into vapor when heated; leaves solids behind (e.g., salt from seawater).\",\"- Magnetic separation: a magnet attracts magnetic metals like iron, cobalt, nickel.\",\"- The choice of method depends on the physical differences (size, weight, magnetism, solubility).\",\"- Oil and water do not mix because they have different densities and are immiscible; oil floats on water.\",\"- When separating oil and water, the top layer is oil and the bottom layer is water.\",\"- In a mixture of solid and liquid, the solid can be removed by filtration; the liquid can be separated by evaporation or decantation if the solid is insoluble.\",\"- In a mixture of two liquids, the heavier liquid can be separated by decantation after sedimentation if one is denser.\",\"- Magnetic separation is useful for recycling metal waste from garbage.\",\"- Evaporation uses solar energy to produce salt from seawater without extra fuel.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did Saina unknowingly mix into the oil bottle while she was in a hurry?\",\"options\":[\"Milk\",\"Juice\",\"Water\",\"Kerosene\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Saina unknowingly mixed water into the oil bottle.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Saina\'s mother say that the oil and water must be separated?\",\"options\":[\"Because the bottle was full\",\"Because we must not waste that oil\",\"Because the water was dirty\",\"Because Saina needed the bottle for school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Her mother specifically mentioned, \'We must not waste that oil,\' as the reason for separation.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When did Saina plan to separate the oil from the water?\",\"options\":[\"Before leaving for school\",\"During her school hours\",\"After she returned from school\",\"The next morning\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Saina replied, \'I’ll do it after I return from the school\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is Saina observing in the glass container?\",\"options\":[\"A uniform yellow liquid\",\"Two separate layers of liquids\",\"Bubbles forming at the top\",\"The bottle breaking into two\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Saina looking at a container where two distinct layers (oil and water) are visible.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/035_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'Try this\' activity, how much oil should you take in a bottle or glass?\",\"options\":[\"One full cup\",\"Half a cup\",\"Two cups\",\"A few drops\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to \'Take half a cup of oil in a bottle or a glass\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the visible state of the mixture when Saina returned from school?\",\"options\":[\"The oil had disappeared\",\"The water had turned yellow\",\"Two separate layers were visible\",\"The oil and water had turned into ice\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that \'two separate layers were visible in the bottle\' upon her return.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many distinct components are being separated in the bottle?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure and text describe the mixture of two components: oil and water.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/035_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do after trying to separate the oil and water using your own method?\",\"options\":[\"Throw the mixture away immediately\",\"Note down what happened while separating\",\"Mix them again to see what happens\",\"Stop doing science experiments\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests to \'Note down what happened while separating the oil and water\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which action by Saina\'s mother shows she values resource conservation?\",\"options\":[\"Stopping Saina from going to school\",\"Insisting that the oil must not be wasted\",\"Asking Saina to hurry up\",\"Filling the water bottle herself\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Her mother\'s concern about not wasting the oil shows she values the resource.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What was Saina doing immediately before she made the mistake of mixing water into the oil?\",\"options\":[\"Eating her breakfast\",\"Filling her own bottle with water\",\"Talking to her friends\",\"Cleaning the kitchen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'She filled her own bottle with water... Unknowingly you mixed water into the oil bottle!\'\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What can be concluded about the mixture of oil and water after it is left undisturbed for some time?\",\"options\":[\"They dissolve into each other completely\",\"They form two separate layers\",\"The water evaporates leaving only oil\",\"The oil sinks to the bottom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that after Saina returned from school, two separate layers were visible.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final step suggested in the \'Try this\' activity after noting down your observations?\",\"options\":[\"Show the bottle to your teacher\",\"Talk to your friends about it\",\"Pour the oil back into the original bottle\",\"Draw a picture of the layers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Talk to your friends about it afterwards.\'\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When oil and water are mixed in a bottle, what is observed after some time?\",\"options\":[\"They mix completely to form one liquid\",\"Two different layers of liquids appear\",\"The oil disappears into the water\",\"The water turns into oil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that two different layers of liquids appear in the bottle when oil and water are mixed.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a mixture of oil and water, which liquid forms the top layer?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Oil\",\"Both liquids mix equally\",\"Neither liquid stays on top\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The experiment involves pouring the liquid from the top layer to separate the oil, indicating oil is on top.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which tool can be used to try and separate all the oil from the mixture?\",\"options\":[\"A filter paper\",\"A magnet\",\"A needleless syringe\",\"A spoon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text suggests trying to separate the oil using a plastic tube or a needleless syringe.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it difficult to separate all the oil by simply pouring the top layer into another container?\",\"options\":[\"The oil evaporates too fast\",\"The oil layer is at the bottom\",\"Some water may get mixed while pouring the top layer\",\"The bottle is too heavy to lift\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks if it is possible to separate all oil this way, implying difficulties in achieving complete separation by simple pouring.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what method are the students using to separate the components of the mixture?\",\"options\":[\"Filtering through a cloth\",\"Pouring the liquid from the top layer\",\"Using a magnet to attract oil\",\"Boiling the mixture\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows students slowly pouring the top layer from one container to another as described in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/035_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what specific tool is the student using to extract a liquid layer?\",\"options\":[\"A glass dropper\",\"A needleless syringe\",\"A drinking straw\",\"A test tube\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure illustrates the text\'s suggestion to use a needleless syringe for separation.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/035_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which liquid is flowing out of the hole into the bottom container?\",\"options\":[\"Oil\",\"Water\",\"Milk\",\"Fruit juice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since water forms the bottom layer in an oil-water mixture, it flows out of the bottom hole first.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/036_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is used to make a hole at the bottom of the transparent plastic bottle in the second experiment?\",\"options\":[\"A pair of scissors\",\"A nail\",\"A hot rod\",\"A knife\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions state to make a hole at its bottom using a nail.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When using the bottle with a hole at the bottom, which liquid starts flowing out first?\",\"options\":[\"The liquid in the top layer\",\"The liquid in the bottom layer\",\"Both layers flow out together\",\"Only the oil flows out\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The liquid at the bottom (water) is directly above the hole and will flow out first.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When should you quickly place your finger back over the hole to stop the liquid from coming out?\",\"options\":[\"As soon as the water starts flowing\",\"When the bottom container is full\",\"Just as the top layer (oil) reaches the hole\",\"After all the oil has flowed out\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To separate the two, you must stop the flow once the first liquid (water) has finished draining and the second (oil) reaches the hole.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"After the experiment with the hole is completed successfully, where will the oil be located?\",\"options\":[\"In the bottom container\",\"In the top container\",\"It will have disappeared\",\"It will be mixed with the water in the bottom container\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The water drains into the bottom container, leaving the oil in the top container.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Why do the oil and water remain as \'separate and distinct\' layers in the bottle?\",\"options\":[\"Because they have different colors\",\"Because they do not mix with each other\",\"Because the bottle is transparent\",\"Because a nail was used to make a hole\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The distinct layers form because oil and water are immiscible and do not mix.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is formed when two or more substances are mixed together?\",\"options\":[\"A compound\",\"A mixture\",\"An element\",\"A pure substance\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when two or more substances are mixed together, it is called a mixture.\",\"topic\":\"Mixtures and Separation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the individual substances that make up a mixture called?\",\"options\":[\"Elements\",\"Particles\",\"Components\",\"Reactants\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the substances that are mixed are called the components of the mixture.\",\"topic\":\"Mixtures and Separation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following mixtures allows components to be easily picked out and separated?\",\"options\":[\"Saltwater\",\"Air\",\"Chivda\",\"Milk\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions chivda, farsan, and bhel as examples where components can be easily picked out.\",\"topic\":\"Mixtures and Separation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why can components of bhel be separated easily compared to other mixtures?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are liquid\",\"Because they can be easily picked out\",\"Because they are chemically bonded\",\"Because they have the same color\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that in mixtures like bhel, components can be easily picked out and separated.\",\"topic\":\"Mixtures and Separation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is necessary to separate components that cannot be easily picked out by hand?\",\"options\":[\"Adding more substances\",\"Heating the mixture only\",\"Using certain techniques\",\"Shaking the mixture\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that for mixtures that cannot be separated easily, certain techniques must be used.\",\"topic\":\"Mixtures and Separation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the basis for planning a specific method of separation?\",\"options\":[\"The total weight of the mixture\",\"The cost of the components\",\"The differences between the mixed substances\",\"The time taken to mix them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A method is planned by identifying the differences between the mixed substances and utilizing those differences.\",\"topic\":\"Mixtures and Separation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student separates peanuts from a bowl of farsan, which concept from the text are they applying?\",\"options\":[\"Creating a new mixture\",\"Separating components by picking them out\",\"Using a chemical reaction\",\"Identifying invisible differences\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Picking out peanuts from farsan is an application of separating components that can be easily picked out.\",\"topic\":\"Mixtures and Separation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A scientist needs to separate two liquids that look identical. Based on the text, what should be their first step?\",\"options\":[\"Mix them with farsan\",\"Identify the differences between the two substances\",\"Pick them out by hand\",\"Assume they cannot be separated\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests identifying the differences between mixed substances to plan a separation method.\",\"topic\":\"Mixtures and Separation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text distinguish between bhel and \'many other mixtures\'?\",\"options\":[\"To show that all mixtures are easy to separate\",\"To explain that some mixtures require special techniques while others do not\",\"To prove that bhel is not a mixture\",\"To show that components are only found in food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text contrasts easy-to-separate mixtures like bhel with others that require specific techniques.\",\"topic\":\"Mixtures and Separation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the relationship between \'differences between substances\' and \'methods of separation\'?\",\"options\":[\"Methods of separation create differences between substances\",\"Differences between substances are used to plan separation methods\",\"There is no relationship between them\",\"Methods of separation only work if substances have no differences\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that methods of separation are planned by utilizing the differences between the mixed substances.\",\"topic\":\"Mixtures and Separation\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the method of separating heavy and light substances with the help of wind called?\",\"options\":[\"Sifting\",\"Winnowing\",\"Threshing\",\"Filtering\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'Winnowing\' as the method of separating heavy and light substances with the help of wind.\",\"topic\":\"Winnowing\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is chaff carried away by the wind during the process of winnowing?\",\"options\":[\"It is heavier than the grain\",\"It is lighter in weight\",\"It is the same weight as the grain\",\"It is sticky in nature\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, chaff and other light trash are carried away by the wind because they are lighter in weight.\",\"topic\":\"Winnowing\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you rub roasted peanuts on your palm and blow on them, what will remain in your hand?\",\"options\":[\"Only the skins\",\"The mixture of skins and peanuts\",\"Clean peanuts\",\"Only the dust\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that when you blow on rubbed peanuts, clean peanuts will remain in your hand.\",\"topic\":\"Winnowing\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the process of winnowing, what happens to the heavy grains when they are dropped from a height?\",\"options\":[\"They are carried away by the wind\",\"They fall straight down\",\"They float in the air\",\"They turn into chaff\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if a mixture is dropped from a height, the heavy grains fall straight down.\",\"topic\":\"Winnowing\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What can be used to create a strong flow of air for winnowing if there is no natural wind?\",\"options\":[\"A small sieve\",\"A large fan of a machine\",\"A water pump\",\"A magnet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that a strong flow of air can be created using a large fan of a machine.\",\"topic\":\"Winnowing\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Winnowing is used by farmers to separate grains from a mixture of which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"Stones and mud\",\"Water and salt\",\"Dried leaves and chaff\",\"Iron filings and sand\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions farmers use this method to separate grains from a mixture of dried leaves, chaff, and grains.\",\"topic\":\"Winnowing\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the primary purpose of dropping the mixture from a height?\",\"options\":[\"To keep the grain away from birds\",\"To allow the wind to carry away the lighter chaff\",\"To dry the grain in the sun\",\"To prevent the grain from touching the ground\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows manual winnowing where height is used so that wind can separate the light chaff from the falling grain.\",\"topic\":\"Winnowing\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/036_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the main advantage of using the device shown in the given figure compared to manual winnowing?\",\"options\":[\"It makes the grain heavier\",\"It requires more natural wind\",\"It can do the same task in less time\",\"It uses water to clean the grain\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that using a machine can do the task in less time by creating a strong flow of air.\",\"topic\":\"Winnowing\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/036_104.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which property of the components is primarily used to separate them in the winnowing process?\",\"options\":[\"Difference in color\",\"Difference in weight\",\"Difference in shape\",\"Difference in hardness\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Winnowing relies on the difference between heavy substances (grains) and light substances (chaff).\",\"topic\":\"Winnowing\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Besides peanuts, which other roasted food item is mentioned in the text as an example for this separation method?\",\"options\":[\"Roasted corn\",\"Roasted chickpeas\",\"Roasted almonds\",\"Roasted cashews\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions taking roasted peanuts or roasted chickpeas on your palm.\",\"topic\":\"Winnowing\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the method of separating small stones from grain by observing their shape and colour called?\",\"options\":[\"Sieving\",\"Handpicking\",\"Grinding\",\"Mixing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines handpicking as picking out small stones or trash from grains by hand after observing their shape and colour.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these are the coarse particles found in flour that need to be separated using a fine mesh?\",\"options\":[\"Sand\",\"Stones\",\"Bran\",\"Chilies\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that a sieve with fine mesh is used to separate coarse particles called bran from the flour.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When is the method of handpicking considered an easy task to perform?\",\"options\":[\"When the components to be removed are many in number\",\"When the components to be removed are few in number\",\"When the components are in liquid form\",\"When the components are very small in size\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that handpicking is easy if the components to be removed from the grain are few in number.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the process of sieving, which particles remain on the sieve mesh?\",\"options\":[\"Particles smaller than the holes\",\"Particles larger than the holes\",\"Liquid particles\",\"All particles in the mixture\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, particles larger than the holes remain on the sieve mesh while smaller ones fall through.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you find chilies in your vegetable dish during school break, which method mentioned in the text will you use to remove them?\",\"options\":[\"Sieving\",\"Grinding\",\"Handpicking\",\"Filtering\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text gives the example of picking out chilies from vegetables in a tiffin as an application of handpicking.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How can a mixture of coarse sand and fine sand be separated from each other at a construction site?\",\"options\":[\"By handpicking\",\"By using a sieve\",\"By grinding them\",\"By washing them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests that sieving is used to separate solid substances that differ in size, such as sand and gravel at construction sites.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a \'finer mesh\' sieve used for flour compared to the one used for cleaning stones from grains?\",\"options\":[\"Because flour particles are larger than stones\",\"Because bran is smaller than stones\",\"Because flour particles are very small and can pass through fine holes\",\"Because grains are smaller than flour particles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A finer mesh is needed for flour because flour particles are smaller than the holes of a standard grain sieve.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The method of sieving is used when the components of a mixture of two solid substances differ in ______.\",\"options\":[\"Colour\",\"Shape\",\"Size\",\"Weight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that sieving is used when the components of a mixture of two solid substances differ in size.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the flour particles that are smaller than the holes of the sieve during the cleaning process?\",\"options\":[\"They stay on the mesh\",\"They fall through the holes\",\"They change their colour\",\"They become coarse particles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that particles smaller than the holes of the sieve fall through.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which method of separation is being demonstrated by the woman?\",\"options\":[\"Sieving\",\"Handpicking\",\"Grinding\",\"Winnowing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a woman picking out small stones or trash from a tray of grain by hand, which is handpicking.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/037_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the woman is separating components based on which physical characteristics?\",\"options\":[\"Weight and density\",\"Taste and smell\",\"Shape and colour\",\"Solubility in water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text associated with the figure explains that handpicking is done by observing the shape and colour of the components.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/037_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the correct sequence of steps to get bran-free flour from grain containing small stones?\",\"options\":[\"Grinding, then sieving stones\",\"Sieving stones, then grinding, then sieving bran\",\"Handpicking, then grinding, then mixing\",\"Sieving bran, then grinding, then sieving stones\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes sieving stones from grain first, then grinding the grain, then using a finer sieve to remove bran.\",\"topic\":\"Handpicking and Sieving\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What tool is used to separate two solid substances when their particles differ in size?\",\"options\":[\"A magnet\",\"An appropriate sieve\",\"A glass rod\",\"A thermometer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when a mixture consists of two solid substances and their particles differ in size, they are separated using an appropriate sieve.\",\"topic\":\"Filtration\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which type of solid can be separated from a liquid using a strainer or a fine mesh sieve?\",\"options\":[\"Soluble solid\",\"Insoluble solid\",\"Dissolved solid\",\"Liquid solid\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, mixtures consisting of a liquid and an insoluble solid can be separated using a strainer or sieve.\",\"topic\":\"Filtration\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What specific feature must a sieve or strainer have to separate a liquid from an insoluble solid?\",\"options\":[\"A very fine mesh\",\"A wooden frame\",\"Large openings\",\"A long handle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that for liquid and insoluble solid mixtures, a strainer or sieve with a very fine mesh is used.\",\"topic\":\"Filtration\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When filtering a mixture of tea leaves and liquid tea, what is the physical state of the substance that remains on the strainer?\",\"options\":[\"Liquid\",\"Gas\",\"Solid\",\"Vapour\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The tea leaves are insoluble solids that are caught by the strainer, while the liquid tea passes through.\",\"topic\":\"Filtration\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Besides a tea strainer