opic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which world-famous organization gave Dr. Bharali an award in the ‘Technology of the Future’ competition?\",\"options\":[\"ISRO\",\"UNESCO\",\"NASA\",\"WHO\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he received an international award from NASA.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides agriculture and industry, for which other group of people has Dr. Bharali created useful tools?\",\"options\":[\"Foreign tourists\",\"Persons with disabilities\",\"School teachers\",\"Plastic bag manufacturers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states he created tools for agriculture, industry, and persons with disabilities.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a factory needs to process large quantities of pomegranates, which of Dr. Bharali\'s inventions would be most appropriate to use?\",\"options\":[\"Plastic bag making machine\",\"Tea gardening tools\",\"Pomegranate seed extraction tools\",\"NASA research tools\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text highlights tools that extract pomegranate seeds as important for large factories.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the primary motivation for Dr. Bharali to develop his first machine in 1988?\",\"options\":[\"To win a NASA award\",\"To avoid the high cost of a foreign machine\",\"To move his factory to another country\",\"To research tea leaves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He developed it himself because the foreign machine was worth 5.5 lakh rupees, which was very expensive.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the person shown is a renowned inventor. According to the text, which award did he receive for his work in technology?\",\"options\":[\"Nobel Prize\",\"Technology of the Future award from NASA\",\