bitat\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/049_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the plants in the given figure, which part of the plant are we primarily observing as the edible storage organ?\",\"options\":[\"The stem\",\"The root\",\"The bud\",\"The leaf\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows carrots, radishes, and beets, which the text identifies as specific plants where roots store food.\",\"topic\":\"Functions of Roots and Habitat\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/049_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Sprouts that grow from the buds on a potato are considered to be parts of which organ?\",\"options\":[\"The root\",\"The stem\",\"The flower\",\"The root hair\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that sprouts growing from buds on potatoes are parts of the stem.\",\"topic\":\"Functions of Roots and Habitat\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT listed in the text as a factor that influences a habitat?\",\"options\":[\"Soil type\",\"Temperature\",\"Total duration of sunlight\",\"The depth of the river\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists soil type, temperature, sunlight duration, and other organisms, but does not mention river depth as a general factor.\",\"topic\":\"Functions of Roots and Habitat\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A gardener wants to plant a Cactus. Based on the text, which environment would be most suitable?\",\"options\":[\"A pond or lake\",\"A snowy mountain top\",\"A dry, arid region\",\"A dark room with no sunlight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the habitat for plants like cactus is arid.\",\"topic\":\"Functions of Roots and Habitat\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these plants is specifically mentioned as having an aquatic habitat?\",\"options\":[\"Acacia\",\"Cactus\",\"Lotus\",\"Potato\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the habitat of the lotus plant is aquatic (water).\",\"topic\":\"Functions of Roots and Habitat\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the textbook, which are the two major groups of living organisms?\",\"options\":[\"Insects and Birds\",\"Animals and Plants\",\"Microbes and Reptiles\",\"Four-legged and Two-legged\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Animals\' and \'Plants\' are the two major groups of living organisms.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the students laugh when Ramesh included a \'Crow\' in his list of animals?\",\"options\":[\"Because a crow has only two legs\",\"Because they thought a crow is a bird, not an animal\",\"Because crows are not found in their environment\",\"Because Ramesh spelled the word incorrectly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that someone said, \'Hey, a crow is a bird! Why is it in the list of animals?\' implying they didn\'t realize birds are animals.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the habitat for camels?\",\"options\":[\"Snowy regions\",\"Large water bodies\",\"The desert\",\"Local forests\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'The desert is the habitat for camels\'.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What defines the \'habitat\' of an animal according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The number of legs an animal has\",\"The place where an animal is kept by humans\",\"The environment where an animal can live comfortably\",\"A list of names written on a blackboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines habitat as \'The environment where an animal can live comfortably\'.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a bear from the snowy Himalayan region is moved to a local forest, why would it be difficult for it to survive?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is not a four-legged animal\",\"Because it cannot adapt to the different local conditions and food\",\"Because there are no other bears in the forest\",\"Because it is a microbe and needs water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states bears live in the Himalayas by adapting to local conditions, food, and cold; it would be difficult for them to survive elsewhere.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following groups contains only organisms that are considered \'animals\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Cows, Trees, and Grass\",\"Mosquitoes, Birds, and Microbes\",\"Rocks, Water, and Insects\",\"Plants, Giraffes, and Termites\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text clarifies that microbes, insects, and birds are all animals.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where are crocodiles and alligators typically found?\",\"options\":[\"In the snowy Himalayan regions\",\"In the middle of the desert\",\"Near large water bodies\",\"Only in local forests\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'areas near large water bodies are the habitat for crocodiles and alligators\'.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What determines the specific region where an animal is found?\",\"options\":[\"The number of students who know its name\",\"Its ability to adapt to the surrounding environment\",\"Whether it has more than four legs\",\"Whether it is written on the blackboard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Only the animals that can adapt to the surrounding environment are found in a particular region.\'\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these animals is NOT found everywhere?\",\"options\":[\"Crow\",\"Mosquito\",\"Kangaroo\",\"Dog\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions giraffes, kangaroos, and ostriches as animals that are not found everywhere.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is a cockroach often missing from a student\'s list of animals?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is not a living organism\",\"Because it does not have any legs\",\"Because people often only think of four-legged creatures as animals\",\"Because it only lives in snowy regions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that when people think of animals, they usually think of four-legged ones, so names like cockroach are rarely seen.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these factors does an animal\'s habitat depend on?\",\"options\":[\"The length of the animal\'s name\",\"The number of people who laugh at it\",\"Local temperature and available food\",\"The number of legs it has\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states habitats depend on \'local temperature, available food and other animals in that area.\'\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the \'Try this\' game, what is the purpose of writing unique names on the blackboard?\",\"options\":[\"To show that only four-legged animals exist\",\"To prepare a comprehensive list of different animals\",\"To prove that insects are not animals\",\"To count how many students have pens\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes preparing a \'comprehensive list\' on the blackboard to look for answers about animal diversity.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these organisms found in river water is classified as an animal in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Plants\",\"Microbes\",\"Rocks\",\"Sand\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Microbes in river or lake water... are all animals.\'\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A student lists a \'Termite\'. Based on the text, this student is:\",\"options\":[\"Correct, because a termite is an animal\",\"Incorrect, because a termite is a plant\",\"Incorrect, because only four-legged creatures are animals\",\"Correct, because termites live in the snowy Himalayas\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that termites are actually animals.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main similarity between a tiny insect and a large elephant according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"They both have four legs\",\"They both live in the desert\",\"They both belong to the group called \'Animals\'\",\"They both live in snowy regions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that while there are differences, insects, birds, and large mammals are all part of the \'Animals\' group.\",\"topic\":\"Diversity in Animals\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the term used for animals that live their entire lives on land?\",\"options\":[\"Aquatic\",\"Amphibian\",\"Terrestrial\",\"Aerial\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that all animals that live on land are called terrestrial (Bhuchar).\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the Marathi word \'Bhuchar\', what does the part \'Char\' signify?\",\"options\":[\"Land\",\"One who moves\",\"Water\",\"One who flies\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that in Marathi, \'Char\' means one who moves.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How do fish obtain the oxygen they need to survive?\",\"options\":[\"By taking oxygen directly from the air\",\"Through their skin while swimming\",\"By taking oxygen dissolved in the water through gills\",\"By poking their noses out of the water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Fish take oxygen dissolved in the water through their gills and cannot take it from the air directly.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which characteristic defines an \'Amphibian\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"They spend their entire life in water.\",\"They live only on land but breathe through gills.\",\"They spend one stage in water and later live on both land and water.\",\"They spend most of their time flying in the sky.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Amphibians spend one stage of life in water and later can live both on land and in water.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In which ancient script did Maharshi Charak describe the classification of animals?\",\"options\":[\"Sushruta Samhita\",\"Charak Samhita\",\"Bhuchar Samhita\",\"Varishaya Samhita\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Maharshi Charak gave a classification system in his script called Charak Samhita.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to Maharshi Charak\'s classification, what are animals living in caves called?\",\"options\":[\"Bilashaya\",\"Guhashaya\",\"Shakhad\",\"Dhanvachara\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Guhashaya\' refers to animals living in caves.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a bird like a swan is observed floating on the surface of water, how would it be classified in the Charak Samhita?\",\"options\":[\"Varishaya\",\"Aanup\",\"Varichara\",\"Shakhad\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'Varichara\' as birds like swans floating on the surface of water.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary reason desert camels have long legs?\",\"options\":[\"To help them run faster on sand\",\"To prevent their bellies from getting burnt by the hot sand\",\"To help them see predators from a distance\",\"To allow them to walk through deep snow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Long legs keep their bodies high above the hot sand, preventing their bellies from getting burnt.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how does the physical structure of the animal\'s legs help it survive in this specific environment?\",\"options\":[\"Short legs help it stay warm near the ground.\",\"Broad feet help it walk through the sand.\",\"Long legs keep the body high above the hot sand.\",\"Thick hair on the legs prevents snow accumulation.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a camel in the desert; the text says long legs keep their bodies high above hot sand.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/051_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, which feature is an adaptation specifically for the snowy environment shown?\",\"options\":[\"Long, thin legs for heat dissipation\",\"Broad feet to walk easily through snow\",\"A transparent membrane over the eyes\",\"The ability to breathe through gills\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a camel in Ladakh; the text states their feet are broader to walk easily through snow.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/051_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the function of the nictitating membrane in fish?\",\"options\":[\"To help the fish breathe underwater\",\"To detect dissolved oxygen in the water\",\"To prevent soil and dried leaves from entering their eyes\",\"To help the fish swim faster in rivers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Fish have a transparent nictitating membrane to prevent soil particles and dried leaves from entering their eyes.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these animals is mentioned in the text as living in burrows?\",\"options\":[\"Fox\",\"Wolf\",\"Bandicoot\",\"Tiger\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists mice, bandicoots, shrews, and rabbits as animals that live in burrows.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why are birds classified as \'Aerial\' animals?\",\"options\":[\"Because they live in burrows\",\"Because they spend much of their time on trees or flying in the sky\",\"Because they can live both on land and in water\",\"Because they have a nictitating membrane\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Birds are called aerial because they spend much of their time on trees or flying in the sky.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Compare the camels of the desert and Ladakh. Which feature is unique to the Ladakh camel for cold protection?\",\"options\":[\"Long legs\",\"Nictitating membrane\",\"Thick hair on their necks and bodies\",\"Living in burrows\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions thick hair on the necks and bodies of Ladakh camels keeps them warm.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why can a fish not survive on land?\",\"options\":[\"It cannot move its fins on land.\",\"It cannot take oxygen from the air directly.\",\"Its nictitating membrane only works in water.\",\"It is a bhuchar animal.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that fish cannot take oxygen from the air directly.\",\"topic\":\"Animal Habitats and Classification\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is listed in the text as one of the various parts of a plant?\",\"options\":[\"Fruit\",\"Bark\",\"Flowers\",\"Thorns\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions roots, stems, leaves, and flowers as the various parts of a plant.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the term used for the favorable environment where specific plants and animals are found?\",\"options\":[\"Surroundings\",\"Habitat\",\"Ecosystem\",\"Locality\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines habitats as the favorable environments where different animals and plants are found.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Trees, shrubs, herbs, climbers, and creepers are groups of plants classified based on which characteristic?\",\"options\":[\"The shape of their leaves\",\"The type of their roots\",\"The types of their stems\",\"The number of seeds they produce\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, these groups are based on the types of their stems.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the number of cotyledons in their seeds, plants are divided into how many types?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that based on the number of cotyledons, plants are of two types: monocotyledonous and dicotyledonous.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a plant has \'net-like\' venation on its leaves, what is the technical term for this type of venation?\",\"options\":[\"Parallel\",\"Circular\",\"Reticulate\",\"Linear\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines reticulate venation as being net-like.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two features are used to identify whether a plant is a monocot or a dicot?\",\"options\":[\"Height and stem nature\",\"Leaf shape and flower presence\",\"Leaf venation and root type\",\"Number of flowers and stem type\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states a plant can be identified as a monocot or a dicot based on its leaf venation and its root type.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student finds a plant with parallel venation. According to the text, this observation helps in determining:\",\"options\":[\"If the plant is a tree or a shrub\",\"If the plant is a monocot or a dicot\",\"The height of the plant\",\"The habitat of the plant\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Leaf venation is one of the two criteria mentioned to identify a plant as a monocot or a dicot.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned as a characteristic for classifying plants in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Nature of the stem\",\"Color of the flowers\",\"Number of cotyledons\",\"Presence or absence of flowers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists height, stem nature, leaf shape, cotyledons, flowers (presence\\/absence), and roots, but not flower color.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a plant is classified as \'dicotyledonous\', this classification is specifically based on its:\",\"options\":[\"Roots\",\"Leaves\",\"Seeds\",\"Stem\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that monocotyledonous and dicotyledonous types are based on the number of cotyledons in the seeds.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following groups would a plant with a very weak stem that grows along the ground likely belong to?\",\"options\":[\"Trees\",\"Shrubs\",\"Creepers\",\"Herbs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists creepers as a group based on the type of stem (implied by the category name in the context of stem types).\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What can be inferred about the relationship between a plant and its habitat from the text?\",\"options\":[\"Plants can grow in any environment regardless of conditions\",\"Plants are only found in environments that are favorable to them\",\"Habitats are determined only by the type of soil\",\"All plants share the same habitat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that different plants are found in environments that are favorable to them, which are called their habitats.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which characteristic is used to group plants into categories like \'herbs\' and \'shrubs\'?\",\"options\":[\"The type of root system\",\"The number of cotyledons\",\"The nature of the stem\",\"The type of leaf venation\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that trees, shrubs, herbs, climbers, and creepers are groups based on the types of their stems.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21860,36,6,'Science','en','Disaster Management','[\"Disaster – a sudden, critical event that causes loss of life and property.\",\"Natural disasters happen because of nature (earthquakes, floods, storms, forest fires).\",\"Man‑made disasters are caused by human actions (accidents, war, cyber crimes).\",\"Disaster Management is planning, preparation and action to reduce damage.\",\"Earthquake – movement of underground rocks; energy released at the epicenter.\",\"Epicenter – the point on the surface directly above the earthquake source.\",\"Seismometer – device that records earthquake intensity.\",\"Richter Scale – measures earthquake intensity; 9 is very strong.\",\"If epicenter is on the ocean floor, a tsunami can form.\",\"Tsunami – huge waves that travel fast and destroy coastal areas.\",\"Storm – rapid wind caused by low pressure; cyclone is a strong storm.\",\"Cloudburst – sudden heavy rain that can flood villages quickly.\",\"River flood – river overflows due to heavy rain or snow melt.\",\"Forest fire – dry branches ignite and spread rapidly.\",\"Accident – sudden event caused by human error (vehicle, factory, etc.).\",\"War – conflict between countries; can cause bomb blasts, fires, pollution.\",\"Cyber crime – illegal acts using computers (phishing, ransomware).\",\"First aid – immediate help for injuries before hospital treatment.\",\"External bleeding – large amount of blood loss; control by pressure.\",\"Sunstroke – overheating of body; treat by cooling and rest.\",\"Burns – do not burst blisters; roll on ground to stop flames.\",\"Snake bite – keep victim calm, wash wound, seek medical help.\",\"Dog bite – wash wound, get rabies vaccine.\",\"When to call emergency – keep phone numbers handy.\",\"Avoid crowds at accident sites – safety and to allow rescue.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In which district of Maharashtra is the village \'Killari\' located?\",\"options\":[\"Bhopal\",\"Latur\",\"Pune\",\"Mumbai\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that an earthquake struck at a small village ‘Killari’ in Latur district.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and Disaster Management\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How much poisonous gas leaked into the air during the first two hours of the Bhopal tragedy?\",\"options\":[\"10 tonnes\",\"20 tonnes\",\"40 tonnes\",\"10,000 tonnes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that in the first 2 hours, 40 tonnes of poisonous gas got mixed up in the air.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and Disaster Management\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the definition of a \'Disaster\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A planned event in nature\",\"A sudden calamity causing large-scale damage to life and property\",\"A slow movement of rocks deep underground\",\"A weather event that only affects animals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a disaster as a sudden calamity that causes large-scale damage to life and property.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and Disaster Management\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"On which date did a massive Tsunami hit the coasts of 14 countries?\",\"options\":[\"September 30, 1993\",\"December 3, 1984\",\"December 26, 2004\",\"August 15, 1947\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that on December 26, 2004, an earthquake triggered a massive Tsunami hitting 14 countries.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and Disaster Management\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the primary cause of the earthquake in Killari in 1993?\",\"options\":[\"A cloudburst in the sky\",\"Movement of rocks deep underground\",\"A poisonous gas leak from a factory\",\"Giant waves from the ocean\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains the earthquake occurred due to movement of rocks deep underground.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and Disaster Management\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase does the text use to describe the intensity of a cloudburst?\",\"options\":[\"A movement of rocks\",\"A sudden leak in a tank\",\"A dam in the sky has burst\",\"A shaking of the Earth\'s surface\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes a cloudburst as an event where it rains so heavily it feels like a dam in the sky has burst.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and Disaster Management\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What are disasters that occur due to events happening in nature called?\",\"options\":[\"Man-made disasters\",\"Natural disasters\",\"Advance arrangements\",\"Chemical disasters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that disasters occurring due to events happening in nature are called ‘Natural disasters’.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and Disaster Management\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'Disaster Management\' involve when a disaster cannot be avoided?\",\"options\":[\"Stopping the earthquake from happening\",\"Moving the village to another country\",\"Planning, preparation, and ensuring help reaches on time\",\"Ignoring the calamity until it passes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines disaster management as the planning, preparation, and actions taken to face disasters and ensure help reaches on time.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction and Disaster Management\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, a specific type of disaster is shown. How does the text classify this event?\",\"options\":[\"A natural disaster\",\"A sudden calamity\",\"A cloudburst\",\"A movement of rocks\