d the public.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the general belief about the Earth 1500 years ago?\",\"options\":[\"The Earth was moving around the Sun\",\"The Earth was stationary\",\"The Earth was 15 lakh km away from space\",\"The Earth was a falling meteor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that 1500 years ago, everyone believed the Earth was stationary.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student sees a shooting star and believes it will bring them good luck, what would the textbook categorize this belief as?\",\"options\":[\"Scientific fact\",\"Mathematical proof\",\"Blind belief\",\"Natural observation\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists seeing a falling meteor (shooting star) as bringing good luck under \'blind beliefs\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did Aryabhatta manage to calculate the Earth\'s rotation time accurately without modern instruments?\",\"options\":[\"By using a spectrometer made at home\",\"By using only observation and mathematics\",\"By visiting the Hanle observatory\",\"By reading the James Webb telescope data\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states he calculated the time using only observation and mathematics.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which scientific facility is shown that is located near Khodad village in Junnar Taluka?\",\"options\":[\"Jantarmantar\",\"IUCAA Pune\",\"Giant Metrewave Radio Telescope (GMRT)\",\"Ladakh Observatory\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The caption for the third figure identifies it as the GMRT located near Khodad village in Junnar.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/089_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure and the text, the scientist shown discovered a comet that returns once in how many years?\",\"options\":[\"300 years\",\"1500 years\",\"1949 years\",\"Sixty thousand years\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Vainu Bappu, and the text says he proved mathematically that his comet comes once in sixty thousand years.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/088_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, identify the world-famous astronomer who regularly answered science questions for curious students.\",\"options\":[\"Dr. Vainu Bappu\",\"Dr. Jayant Narlikar\",\"Aryabhatta\",\"Bhaskaracharya\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Dr. Jayant Narlikar, who the text says regularly answered science questions asked by curious students.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/088_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Comparing the different observatories mentioned, which one is located furthest from the Earth\'s surface?\",\"options\":[\"Jantarmantar\",\"Hanle India\",\"James Webb space telescope\",\"GMRT Khodad\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the James Webb space telescope is 15 lakh km away from the Earth in Space.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the space around the earth as far as the atmosphere exists called?\",\"options\":[\"The universe\",\"The sky\",\"The galaxy\",\"The solar system\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the sky as the space around the earth as far as the atmosphere exists.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the empty region beyond the sky called?\",\"options\":[\"Atmosphere\",\"Cloud layer\",\"Space\",\"Nakshatra\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The empty region beyond the sky is specifically defined as space in the text.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these phenomena is seen in the sky rather than