 part of a huge and vast galaxy\",\"It contains billions of galaxies\",\"It is the same size as the entire universe\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that our Solar system is a very small part of a huge and vast galaxy.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What comprises the universe according to the textbook text?\",\"options\":[\"Only our solar system\",\"Just the sky and the atmosphere\",\"Billions of galaxies\",\"Only stars and the moon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the universe is made up of billions of galaxies.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which organization is mentioned as conducting various missions for space research?\",\"options\":[\"NASA\",\"ISRO\",\"The Atmosphere Board\",\"Celestial Observers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions ISRO as conducting various missions for space research.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why are aeroplanes and stars categorized differently?\",\"options\":[\"Aeroplanes are in the sky, while stars are far beyond in space\",\"Aeroplanes are made of ice, while stars are made of dust\",\"Stars are in the atmosphere, while aeroplanes are in space\",\"Aeroplanes have a fixed arrangement, but stars do not\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text distinguishes between things in the sky (aeroplanes) and things far beyond in space (stars).\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"A scientist observes a celestial object orbiting the sun that eventually moves far away into space. What is this object?\",\"options\":[\"A Nakshatra\",\"A galaxy\",\"A comet\",\"The atmosphere\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes comets as objects that orbit the sun and then go far away in space.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21864,36,6,'Science','en','From Diet to Health','[\"- Food gives energy and nutrients to the body.\",\"- A diet is the food we eat regularly.\",\"- A balanced diet contains all essential nutrients: carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals, water and fibre.\",\"- Carbohydrates give energy and are found in rice, wheat, millets and pulses.\",\"- Proteins help growth and repair and are found in pulses, milk, eggs and meat.\",\"- Fats give energy and help absorb vitamins; they are in oil, ghee and butter.\",\"- Vitamins (A, C, D, B‑group) boost immunity and help vision, bone growth and skin health.\",\"- Minerals like iron and calcium strengthen blood and bones.\",\"- Water removes waste, regulates temperature and keeps skin fresh.\",\"- Fibre aids digestion and keeps stools smooth.\",\"- Seasonal foods and regional diets give variety and meet local needs.\",\"- Cooking methods (boiling, roasting, frying) change taste but can preserve nutrients if done properly.\",\"- Deficiency diseases: goitre (iodine), rickets (vitamin D), scurvy (vitamin C), night blindness (vitamin A).\",\"- Use iodised salt, sunlight, citrus fruits, and vegetables rich in vitamins to prevent these diseases.\",\"- Millets are small cereals rich in protein, fibre, iron and magnesium and should be part of every diet.\",\"- Proper food handling: wash vegetables, cook without excess water, avoid over‑cooking to retain nutrients.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What do elderly people say when a person eats regularly but remains weak and tired?\",\"options\":[\"The person is eating too much\",\"The food does not nourish his body\",\"The person needs more rest\",\"The food is very tasty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that if a person looks weak and tired despite eating, elderly people say the food does not nourish the body.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is necessary to perform activities, movements, and play games?\",\"options\":[\"Sleep\",\"Medicines\",\"Energy\",\"Water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that energy is necessary to perform different activities, movements, and playing games.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a function of food mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"It makes us sleep better\",\"It helps the body recover from wear and tear\",\"It changes the climate of a region\",\"It helps in farming crops\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that food helps the body recover from wear and tear, supports growth, and provides immunity.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the term used for food items prepared from crops available in surrounding regions?\",\"options\":[\"International Diet\",\"Festival Food\",\"Regional Diet\",\"Nutritious Diet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'Regional Diet\' as food items prepared from the crops available in surrounding regions.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why are wheat-based food items used more in North India?\",\"options\":[\"Because rice is too expensive there\",\"Because wheat is grown in that particular region\",\"Because they do not like rice\",\"Because it is a festival tradition\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that crops grown in a particular region are used more, so wheat is used in North India.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which factors contribute to the diversity of crops in different places?\",\"options\":[\"Population and height of people\",\"Number of festivals and holidays\",\"Climate, rainfall, and types of soil\",\"Cooking styles and types of utensils\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that diversity in climate, amount of rainfall, and types of soil causes crops to vary by region.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is healthy, strong, and rarely falls sick, what can we conclude about their food?\",\"options\":[\"The food nourishes their body\",\"They are eating only festival food\",\"They are not eating enough\",\"They only eat wheat and butter\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says that for a healthy, strong, and active individual, we say \'The food nourishes his body!\'\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these food items is NOT mentioned as a major part of food in South India?\",\"options\":[\"Idli\",\"Dosa\",\"Sambar\",\"Pithala\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Pithala is mentioned as part of a regular meal (implied Maharashtra context), while idli, dosa, and sambar are listed for the South.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A student lives in a region where rice farming is very common. Based on the text, what is likely to be a part of their main food?\",\"options\":[\"Wheat roti and butter\",\"Jowar bhakari\",\"Masala rice and idli\",\"Potato and ghee\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that in regions where rice farming is common (like South India), rice items like masala rice and idli are included in the main food.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the text say about the cultivation of jowar and wheat in South India?\",\"options\":[\"They are the main crops\",\"They are not cultivated there\",\"They are grown only during festivals\",\"They are grown in large quantities\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions that in South India, jowar and wheat are not cultivated.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which food items are used more in North India according to the passage?\",\"options\":[\"Jowar and Pithala\",\"Idli and Sambar\",\"Wheat, butter, and potato\",\"Lemon rice and Pulav\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'Wheat, butter, ghee and potato are used more in the north.\'\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a person eats meals regularly but lacks enthusiasm for playing, what is their body likely failing to get from the food?\",\"options\":[\"Taste\",\"Variety\",\"Nourishment\",\"Soil\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links the lack of enthusiasm and energy to the food not nourishing the body.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does food help the body when we are injured or growing?\",\"options\":[\"It changes the soil type\",\"It recovers wear and tear and supports growth\",\"It increases the rainfall\",\"It makes the climate better\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states food helps the body recover from wear and tear and supports growth.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why would a person in Kashmir likely have a different diet than a person in South India?\",\"options\":[\"Because they have the same soil\",\"Because the climate and crops grown are different\",\"Because they both eat the same regional diet\",\"Because festivals are the same everywhere\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that crops vary by region due to climate and soil, leading to different regional diets.\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a requirement for a diet to \'nourish\' the body?\",\"options\":[\"It must contain only festival items\",\"It must be from North India\",\"It must fulfill all the needs of the body\",\"It must contain only rice\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'If our diet can fulfill all these needs, then the food we take can nourish our body.\'\",\"topic\":\"From Diet to Health & Regional Diet\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What are all the food items that we eat together called?\",\"options\":[\"Ingredients\",\"Diet\",\"Variety\",\"Nutrition\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'Diet\' as all the food items that we eat together.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned in the text as a cooking method that creates variety in food?\",\"options\":[\"Roasting\",\"Frying\",\"Steaming\",\"Cooking\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions roasting, cooking, and frying as methods used for preparation.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it recommended to drink buttermilk, lemon juice, and coconut water during summer?\",\"options\":[\"To increase immunity\",\"To speed up digestion\",\"To reduce the risk of dehydration\",\"To provide energy for the cold\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that in summer, these drinks reduce the risk of dehydration.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the human body\'s digestion process during the monsoon season?\",\"options\":[\"It speeds up\",\"It stops completely\",\"It slows down\",\"It remains the same as summer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, digestion slows down in the monsoon.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which type of food is best suited for the winter season to help the body stay warm and energetic?\",\"options\":[\"Light and boiled food\",\"Energy rich food like ghee and bajra\",\"Cold drinks like panhe and ambil\",\"Only seasonal fruits like jamun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests energy-rich foods like bajra bhakari, tilgul, and ghee for winter.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person wants to increase their immunity and stay healthy, what should they include in their diet?\",\"options\":[\"Only grains and pulses\",\"Tea and coffee every day\",\"Seasonal fruits and vegetables\",\"Fried food items\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that including seasonal fruits and vegetables increases immunity and keeps us healthy.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why do we not eat grains and pulses exactly as they are obtained from the farm?\",\"options\":[\"They have no taste\",\"Various processes are carried out to prepare different food items\",\"They are not part of a diet\",\"They can only be eaten in winter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that various processes are carried out on grains and pulses to prepare different food items.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the given figure, which of these is a seasonal fruit specifically listed for the winter season?\",\"options\":[\"Jackfruit\",\"Custard apple\",\"Guava\",\"Banana\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure lists orange, guava, sweet lime, and chickoo under the Winter column.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/093_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which food item is listed as being part of the diet in all three seasons (Winter, Summer, and Monsoon)?\",\"options\":[\"Varan bhat\",\"Bhakari\",\"Dink ladoo\",\"Khichadi\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table shows \'bhakari\' listed in the Winter, Summer, and Monsoon columns.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/093_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs of food items are mentioned as not being available throughout the year?\",\"options\":[\"Banana and Chickoo\",\"Mangoes and Amala\",\"Jaggery and Sesame\",\"Carrot and Beet root\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that mangoes and amala are not available throughout the year.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"A student is planning a menu for a rainy monsoon day. Based on the text, which would be the most suitable choice?\",\"options\":[\"Cold lemon water and salad\",\"Hot khichadi and boiled vegetables\",\"Tilgul and bajra bhakari\",\"Mango and coconut water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text recommends easy to digest, hot food, boiled vegetables, and khichadi for the monsoon.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary reason for the variety seen in food items according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Different cooking methods, spices, and seasonal availability\",\"The need to eat the same food every day\",\"Because grains cannot be processed\",\"Only because of climate change\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text attributes variety to different food items, spices available in seasons, and various cooking methods.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a summer drink mentioned in the text that is made from raw mangoes?\",\"options\":[\"Ambil\",\"Panhe\",\"Sherbet\",\"Buttermilk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Panhe is listed as a summer drink (traditionally made from mango, though the text just lists it as a summer item).\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text suggest that our diet needs to change with the seasons?\",\"options\":[\"Because we get bored of the same taste\",\"Because farmers only grow one crop\",\"Because the needs of the body change as the climate changes\",\"Because spices are only available in winter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that climate changes in every season and the needs of the body about the diet change accordingly.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these fruits would you most likely find in the market during the monsoon season according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Orange\",\"Mango\",\"Jamun\",\"Bor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists jamun and custard apple as seasonal fruits for the monsoon.\",\"topic\":\"Variety in Food and Seasonal Diet\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What are the useful components necessary for our body obtained from food items called?\",\"options\":[\"Spices\",\"Nutrients\",\"Pathogens\",\"Culinary art\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'Nutrients\' as the useful components necessary for our body obtained from food items.\",\"topic\":\"Balanced Diet and Nutrients\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which term refers to the food items that fulfill all the needs of our body together?\",\"options\":[\"Raw food\",\"Roasted food\",\"Balanced diet\",\"Regional dishes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A balanced diet is defined as food items that fulfill all the needs of our body.\",\"topic\":\"Balanced Diet and Nutrients\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is a specific need of the body related to food?\",\"options\":[\"Making the hair long\",\"Fighting against pathogens\",\"Increasing the height of teeth\",\"Learning new recipes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Fighting against pathogens is listed as one of the food-related needs of the body.\",\"topic\":\"Balanced Diet and Nutrients\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In earlier times, before humans learned to use fire, how did they eat their food?\",\"options\":[\"In raw form\",\"Using steam\",\"By frying\",\"Using a microwave\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states 