ting roasted food\",\"They stopped eating fruits\",\"They began using microwave ovens\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"After learning to make fire, humans started eating roasted food.\",\"topic\":\"Balanced Diet and Nutrients\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A chef makes a dish that is very tasty but destroys all the nutrients during frying. Does this chef demonstrate \'Cooking skill\' as defined in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Yes, because the food is tasty\",\"Yes, because frying is a cooking method\",\"No, because cooking skill requires no loss of nutrients\",\"No, because spices were not mentioned\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Cooking skill is specifically defined as preparing food with taste *without* any loss of nutrients.\",\"topic\":\"Balanced Diet and Nutrients\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which sequence correctly shows the progression of cooking methods over time as per the text?\",\"options\":[\"Microwave -> Frying -> Raw\",\"Raw -> Roasting -> Steam\\/Frying\",\"Frying -> Raw -> Roasting\",\"Steam -> Raw -> Microwave\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the progression from raw food to roasting, then to methods like steam and frying.\",\"topic\":\"Balanced Diet and Nutrients\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why has there been progress in \'culinary art\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Because people stopped using spices\",\"Because humans returned to eating raw food\",\"Due to experiments and efforts to make new recipes\",\"Because pathogens have been eliminated\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that experiments and efforts to make new recipes lead to progress in culinary art.\",\"topic\":\"Balanced Diet and Nutrients\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you move to a new region and start cooking dishes from that area, what are you contributing to?\",\"options\":[\"The loss of nutrients\",\"The variety in your everyday diet\",\"The growth of pathogens\",\"The use of raw food only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that information about dishes from other regions leads to cooking new dishes, adding to variety.\",\"topic\":\"Balanced Diet and Nutrients\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT listed as a body need fulfilled by a balanced diet?\",\"options\":[\"Giving energy to the body\",\"Helping the body to grow\",\"Keeping the body fit\",\"Learning how to make fire\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Learning to make fire is a historical event, not a biological need fulfilled by a balanced diet.\",\"topic\":\"Balanced Diet and Nutrients\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the relationship between \'foodstuff\' and \'nutrients\' based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Foodstuff is made from nutrients\",\"Nutrients are the useful components obtained from food items\",\"Foodstuff and nutrients are the same thing\",\"Nutrients are only found in raw foodstuff\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that useful components (nutrients) are obtained from food items made from foodstuff.\",\"topic\":\"Balanced Diet and Nutrients\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the collective term for the daily diet, festival food, and food-related habits of local people?\",\"options\":[\"Food processing\",\"Food culture\",\"Food storage\",\"Food science\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'Food culture\' as the daily diet, festival food, and food-related habits of a place.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In earlier times, what type of grains and ingredients were primarily used to cook food?\",\"options\":[\"Imported grains\",\"Processed ingredients\",\"Local grains\",\"Artificial ingredients\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that since earlier times, using local grains and ingredients has been our food culture.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was a characteristic of food prepared for weddings and festivals in the past?\",\"options\":[\"It was ordered from outside\",\"It was different for different people\",\"It was homemade and the same for all\",\"It was always low in nutrition\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that food prepared for festivals or weddings was homemade and same for all.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is ordering food from outside for feasts considered a concern today?\",\"options\":[\"It is always cheaper than homemade food\",\"We lack information about its preparation and ingredient quality\",\"It is always served in very small quantities\",\"It contains only local grains and ingredients\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states we usually do not have information about where, by whom, and how the food is prepared or if ingredients are of good quality.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is mentioned as a low-nutrition food that children often start liking?\",\"options\":[\"Basundi\",\"Local grains\",\"Pizza\",\"Milk\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists pizza and burgers as examples of low-nutrition foods children start liking.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a physical consequence of consuming low-nutrition foods from an early age?\",\"options\":[\"Improved immunity\",\"Weight gain and improper body growth\",\"Faster height growth\",\"Better digestion\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that because of low-nutrition foods, weight gain and other diseases start early and the body does not grow properly.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why are harmful artificial colors and chemicals added to food nowadays?\",\"options\":[\"To increase the nutritional value\",\"To make the food look more attractive\",\"To reduce the cost of the food\",\"To make the food digest faster\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that harmful artificial colors and chemicals are added unnecessarily to make food look more attractive.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which combination of food items is specifically mentioned as causing discomfort?\",\"options\":[\"Milk and fish\",\"Pizza and burgers\",\"Local grains and vegetables\",\"Basundi and ice cream\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that eating foods like milk and fish together can cause discomfort.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is a major disadvantage of serving many items like panipuri, chaat, and ice cream together at feasts?\",\"options\":[\"It saves a lot of time\",\"It reduces the cost of the feast\",\"It leads to a lot of food wastage\",\"It ensures everyone gets enough nutrition\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that arranging many items like panipuri and chaat leads to a lot of food wastage and higher costs.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the \'incompatible\' food combination often served in modern wedding meals according to the text.\",\"options\":[\"Pizza and burgers\",\"Basundi and panipuri\",\"Milk and local grains\",\"Chaat and ice cream\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text gives the example of basundi and panipuri being served together as a risk of consuming incompatible food items.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How has the habit of eating together as a family changed from the past?\",\"options\":[\"It was a part of food culture in the past but is often ignored now\",\"It is a new habit developed in modern times\",\"It was avoided in the past to prevent wastage\",\"It is only done during festivals in modern times\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says enjoying meals together as a family was our food culture since earlier times, but many ignore these good habits nowadays.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child frequently consumes various sauces and burgers, what is likely to happen based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"They will grow taller than others\",\"They will avoid all diseases\",\"They may face weight gain from an early age\",\"They will develop a taste for local grains\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links the consumption of sauces, pizza, and burgers to weight gain starting from an early age.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these practices was strictly followed in the past to maintain health?\",\"options\":[\"Ordering food from outside\",\"Avoiding incompatible food combinations\",\"Adding artificial colors to festival food\",\"Eating only what one likes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that in earlier times, care was taken to avoid eating incompatible foods like milk and fish together.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of the modern practice where \'everyone should eat what they like\' at programs?\",\"options\":[\"Better health for all guests\",\"Lower expenses for the host\",\"Increased food wastage and higher costs\",\"Promotion of local food culture\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that thinking everyone should eat what they like leads to many items being arranged, resulting in wastage and higher costs.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is an example of an incompatible food combination involving fruit?\",\"options\":[\"Milk and sour fruits\",\"Pizza and burgers\",\"Basundi and panipuri\",\"Local grains and sour fruits\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that eating milk and sour fruits together can cause discomfort.\",\"topic\":\"Food culture in the past and present\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What are the starchy substances present in grains like jowar and wheat called?\",\"options\":[\"Proteins\",\"Carbohydrates\",\"Vitamins\",\"Fats\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that starchy substances present in grains are called carbohydrates.\",\"topic\":\"Components of Food\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these minerals are specifically mentioned as being necessary for making bones and teeth strong?\",\"options\":[\"Magnesium and Potassium\",\"Iodine and Sodium\",\"Iron and Calcium\",\"Zinc and Phosphorus\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, minerals of iron and calcium make bones and teeth strong.\",\"topic\":\"Components of Food\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary role of proteins in the human body?\",\"options\":[\"To provide instant energy\",\"To increase immunity against diseases\",\"To remove harmful substances from the body\",\"For growth and recovery from wear and tear\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions proteins are essential for recovery from wear and tear and growth of the body.\",\"topic\":\"Components of Food\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which component of food helps the body increase its immunity against diseases?\",\"options\":[\"Vitamins\",\"Fats\",\"Carbohydrates\",\"Water\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Vitamins help in increasing immunity of the body against diseases.\",\"topic\":\"Components of Food\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A person is having difficulty with the smooth passage of stools. Which food component should they increase in their diet?\",\"options\":[\"Fats\",\"Fibres\",\"Proteins\",\"Starch\"]