:1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the script called \'Rigveda\' was written 3,500 years ago.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who wrote the ancient scripts known as the Vedas?\",\"options\":[\"Ancient kings\",\"Indian sages\",\"Foreign travelers\",\"Modern scientists\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the Vedas were written by Indian sages in ancient times.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the basis of the information written in the Vedas?\",\"options\":[\"Imaginary stories\",\"Careful observations and reasoning\",\"Only religious rituals\",\"War strategies\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The information is based on careful observations of nature, events in life, reasoning, and conclusions.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a factor that changes with the seasons?\",\"options\":[\"Intensity of sunlight\",\"Content of water vapour\",\"Duration of daylight\",\"Speed of the earth\'s rotation\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists temperature, water vapour, sunlight intensity, and daylight duration as changing factors.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How long does the transition period from the end of one season to the beginning of another usually take?\",\"options\":[\"Seven days\",\"Fifteen days\",\"Thirty days\",\"Two months\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the change from one season to another takes place in fifteen days.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the skin during the seasonal transition period?\",\"options\":[\"It becomes oily\",\"It gets dry\",\"It becomes thicker\",\"It changes color\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that during the transition period, effects like the skin getting dry are seen.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What effect does the seasonal change have on a person\'s immunity?\",\"options\":[\"Immunity increases\",\"Immunity stays the same\",\"Immunity decreases\",\"Immunity disappears completely\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the immunity of the body decreases during the transition period.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the relation between changes in nature, diet, and daily routine called?\",\"options\":[\"Seasonal cycle\",\"Natural balance\",\"Environmental health\",\"Biological clock\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'Natural balance\' as the relation between changes in nature, diet, and daily routine.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"During which festival is the traditional oil bath known as \'abhyangsnan\' performed?\",\"options\":[\"Sankranti\",\"Gudhi Padwa\",\"Diwali\",\"Holi\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text refers to the importance of abhyangsnan (oil bath) during Diwali.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which food item is traditionally made during Sankranti for health benefits?\",\"options\":[\"Neem leaves\",\"Tilgul\",\"Puran poli\",\"Modak\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions finding information about tilgul made during Sankranti.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What natural resource is used on Gudhi Padwa for good health according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Mango leaves\",\"Neem leaves and flowers\",\"Rose petals\",\"Tulsi leaves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the use of neem leaves and flowers on the day of Gudhi Padwa for good health.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the Rigveda suggest making changes to our diet during seasonal transitions?\",\"options\":[\"To enjoy different tastes\",\"To adapt with the changes in nature\",\"To increase body weight\",\"To save food for winter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says diet changes are mentioned in order to adapt with the changes occurring in nature.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to digestion during the fifteen-day period between seasons?\",\"options\":[\"It becomes faster\",\"It stops completely\",\"It becomes slow\",\"It remains unaffected\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that during this period, effects like digestion becoming slow are seen.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does the text describe the speed of change from one season to another?\",\"options\":[\"It happens suddenly\",\"It happens slowly\",\"It happens overnight\",\"It happens in a single day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the change from the end of one season to the beginning of another happens slowly.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a daily routine practice mentioned in the Rigveda to help the body?\",\"options\":[\"Sleeping during the day\",\"Applying oil to the body before a bath\",\"Drinking only cold water\",\"Exercising only in summer\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the importance of applying oil to the body before taking a bath as stated in the Rigveda.\",\"topic\":\"Seasonal change and diet\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What are the diseases caused due to insufficient food or eating inappropriate food items called?\",\"options\":[\"Infectious diseases\",\"Deficiency diseases\",\"Chronic diseases\",\"Genetic diseases\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines diseases caused by a lack of certain nutrients as \'Deficiency diseases\'.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which mineral is present in small quantities in the salt obtained from seawater?\",\"options\":[\"Calcium\",\"Iron\",\"Iodine\",\"Phosphorus\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that iodine is present in small quantities in salt obtained from seawater.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do tribal people living in mountains often suffer from Goitre?\",\"options\":[\"They eat too much seafood\",\"They use rock salt which lacks iodine\",\"They do not get enough sunlight\",\"They eat too many green vegetables\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that rock salt used by tribal people lacks iodine, leading to Goitre.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child shows symptoms of rickets, what did elders in the past advise to improve the condition of the limbs?\",\"options\":[\"Eating more rock salt\",\"Taking expensive medicines\",\"Exposure to morning sunlight\",\"Avoiding dairy products\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that elders advised keeping the child in morning sunlight to improve rickets.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In which part of the body is Vitamin D prepared when exposed to morning sunlight?\",\"options\":[\"Inside the bones\",\"In the stomach\",\"Under the skin in the lower layer\",\"In the thyroid gland\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states Vitamin D is prepared in our body under the skin in the lower layer upon exposure to sunlight.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a symptom of scurvy caused by Vitamin C deficiency?\",\"options\":[\"Poor vision in dim light\",\"Bleeding of gums\",\"Frequent breaking of bones\",\"Increase in size of thyroid gland\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists bleeding of gums as a symptom of scurvy.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A student finds it difficult to see clearly in dim light. Which food items should be included in their diet to help reduce this condition?\",\"options\":[\"Dates and grapes\",\"Salt and water\",\"Carrots and papaya\",\"Meat and peas\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Night blindness (poor vision in dim light) is treated by eating foods rich in Vitamin A like carrots and papaya.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A person feels restless, looks pale, and gets tired very quickly. Which nutrient is most likely deficient in their diet?\",\"options\":[\"Vitamin D\",\"Iodine\",\"Iron\",\"Calcium\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tiredness, pale look, and restlessness are symptoms of Anaemia, caused by iron deficiency.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary symptom of the disease Beriberi?\",\"options\":[\"Deformity of bones\",\"Fatigue or tiredness and weakness\",\"Dry skin\",\"Poor vision\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the table, the symptoms of Beriberi are fatigue, tiredness, and weakness.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text and table, which of these food items is a source for both Vitamin A and Vitamin C?\",\"options\":[\"Milk\",\"Tomato\",\"Spinach\",\"Egg yolk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tomato is listed as a source for both Vitamin A (in the text) and Vitamin C (in the table).\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person suffers from frequent bone fractures, which two nutrients should they increase in their diet?\",\"options\":[\"Iron and Iodine\",\"Vitamin A and Vitamin B\",\"Calcium and Phosphorus\",\"Vitamin C and Iron\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Frequent breaking of bones is caused by a deficiency of calcium and phosphorus.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which fruit is mentioned as containing Vitamin C in large proportions?\",\"options\":[\"Banana\",\"Mango\",\"Amla\",\"Papaya\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states Vitamin C is present in amla in large proportions.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which disease is correctly matched with the symptom \'Weakening of bones\'?\",\"options\":[\"Scurvy\",\"Rickets\",\"Beriberi\",\"Anaemia\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows that Rickets is caused by Vitamin D deficiency and results in weakening of bones.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/098_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"The activity shown in the given figure produces a substance that can prevent which disease if it contains iodine?\",\"options\":[\"Night blindness\",\"Anaemia\",\"Goitre\",\"Scurvy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a salt pan; salt containing iodine is the remedy for Goitre.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/097_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the visible swelling in the neck is caused by the enlargement of which specific gland?\",\"options\":[\"Salivary gland\",\"Thyroid gland\",\"Skin gland\",\"Bone gland\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Goitre, which the table describes as an increase in the size of the thyroid gland.\",\"topic\":\"Deficiency Diseases\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"36\\/097_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which indicator is used to identify the presence of starch in food samples?\",\"options\":[\"Sodium hydroxide\",\"Copper sulphate\",\"Iodine indicator\",\"Oil\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that adding two drops of iodine indicator is a test to identify starch.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What color appears on a food sample if starch is present after adding the indicator?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Blue\",\"Purple\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, if starch is present, the sample will show a blue colour.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a paper used to wrap \'Shev\' shows an oily stain, which component is present in the food?\",\"options\":[\"Proteins\",\"Starch\",\"Fats\",\"Iodine\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that oily stains on paper are because of fats present in the food.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the test for proteins, what color change indicates a positive result?\",\"options\":[\"Light green\",\"Dark purple or blue\",\"Bright orange\",\"Translucent white\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when proteins are present, you will see a dark purple or blue colour in the mixture.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student wants to test a piece of bhakari for starch. What should they do first?\",\"options\":[\"Wrap it in paper and press it\",\"Make a paste and add copper sulphate\",\"Add two drops of iodine indicator on it\",\"Dry it in a saucer for some time\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the starch test as adding two drops of iodine indicator on the sample.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a test tube is unavailable, which of these can be used to perform the protein test?\",\"options\":[\"A piece of paper\",\"A plastic vessel\",\"A wooden block\",\"A cotton cloth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using a saucer or a plastic vessel if a test tube is not available.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text suggest letting the paper dry if it appears wet during the fat test?\",\"options\":[\"To make the iodine react faster\",\"To distinguish between water and oily stains\",\"To allow the protein paste to settle\",\"To change the color to blue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to let the paper dry to see if an oily or translucent stain remains, differentiating it from simple wetness.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the concentration of the sodium hydroxide solution used in the protein test?\",\"options\":[\"1%\",\"5%\",\"10%\",\"100%\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions using 10% sodium hydroxide solution.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these food items is specifically mentioned as a sample for the starch test?\",\"options\":[\"Fritters\",\"Shev\",\"Chickpeas\",\"Sodium hydroxide\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Chickpeas are listed among the samples for the starch test (potato, chapati, bhakari, chickpeas, etc.).\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A food sample is mixed with sodium hydroxide and copper sulphate, but the color does not change. What does this mean?\",\"options\":[\"The food contains starch\",\"The food contains fats\",\"There are no proteins in the foodstuff\",\"The food is a liquid\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that if the colour does not change during this specific test, there are no proteins.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following describes the correct order of adding chemicals for the protein test?\",\"options\":[\"Add iodine then copper sulphate\",\"Add sodium hydroxide then copper sulphate\",\"Add copper sulphate then iodine\",\"Add iodine then sodium hydroxide\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to add 10% sodium hydroxide first and then 1% copper sulphate.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What percentage of copper sulphate solution is required for the protein test?\",\"options\":[\"1%\",\"2%\",\"10%\",\"20%\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifies the use of 1% copper sulphate solution.\",\"topic\":\"Testing Food Components\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is recognized as the \'Father of Indian Nutrition Science\'?\",\"options\":[\"Dr. Kamala Sohonie\",\"Dr. Coluthur Gopalan\",\"Dr. Homi Bhabha\",\"Dr. Vikram Sarabhai\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that Dr. Coluthur Gopalan is the father of Indian Nutrition Science.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which prestigious Indian award was conferred upon Dr. Coluthur Gopalan?\",\"options\":[\"Bharat Ratna\",\"Padmabhushan\",\"Padma Shri\",\"Arjuna Award\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Dr. Coluthur Gopalan received the Padmabhushan and many international awards.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which institution was established by Dr. Coluthur Gopalan?\",\"options\":[\"Hafkins Laboratory\",\"Institute of Science, Mumbai\",\"National Institute of Nutrition\",\"Cambridge University\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Dr. Coluthur Gopalan established the \'National Institute of Nutrition\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Dr. Coluthur Gopalan\'s research work had a significant influence on which national program?\",\"options\":[\"Pulse Polio Program\",\"Clean India Mission\",\"Mid-Day Meal Program\",\"Digital India Program\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that his work influenced the Mid-Day Meal Program in India.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction to Scientists\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the primary focus of Dr. Coluthur Gopalan\'s fundamental research?\",\"options\":[\"Space exploration and rockets\",\"Malnutrition and vitamin deficiency\",\"Plant diseases and pesticides\",\"Water purific