e Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A diet based on the crops available and the climate of a particular region is called a:\",\"options\":[\"Healthy diet\",\"Balanced diet\",\"Regional diet\",\"Seasonal diet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a diet based on regional crops and climate as a Regional diet.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why are nutrients essential for our body?\",\"options\":[\"Only for making food tasty\",\"For growth, energy production, and maintaining good health\",\"Only for working and playing\",\"To change the climate of the region\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Nutrients are essential for growth, energy production, and maintaining good health as per the text.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What leads to the development of \'deficiency diseases\'?\",\"options\":[\"Eating too many citrus fruits\",\"Insufficient food or eating inappropriate food items\",\"Sitting in the sunlight for too long\",\"Using too many ingredients in cooking\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Deficiency diseases are caused by insufficient food or eating inappropriate food items.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why should millets be an essential part of our diet?\",\"options\":[\"They are only eaten during festivals\",\"They are used for energy production only\",\"They are rich in all nutrients\",\"They are the only source of water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that millets are rich in all nutrients and should be an essential part of our diet.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is suffering from Night Blindness, which of these should they include in their diet?\",\"options\":[\"Iodized salt\",\"Citrus fruits\",\"Morning sunlight\",\"Carrot and spinach\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text suggests including carrot, spinach, tomato, cabbage, and papaya to remedy Night Blindness.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To prevent Scurvy, which of the following food items would be most effective to add to a meal?\",\"options\":[\"Millets\",\"Lemons and Oranges (Citrus fruits)\",\"Iodized salt\",\"Bread and Butter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Scurvy is caused by Vitamin C deficiency, and the remedy is using citrus fruits in the diet.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following best describes the \'art of cooking\' based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Finding new nutrients in the soil\",\"Preparing tasty dishes using available ingredients and various methods\",\"Growing crops according to the climate\",\"Studying the deficiency of vitamins\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines cooking as the art of preparing tasty dishes using available ingredients through various methods.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which factor contributes to the variety in our daily diet according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"The number of vitamins in the air\",\"The distance from the sun\",\"Methods of preparation and use of foodstuff\",\"The amount of energy used while sleeping\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Variety is brought by ingredients, seasons, needs, foodstuff use, and methods of preparation.\",\"topic\":\"What We Have Learnt?\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21865,36,6,'Science','en','Into the Magical World of Magnets','[\"Magnets are objects that attract iron, nickel and cobalt.\",\"A magnet has two poles – north and south.\",\"Like poles repel each other; unlike poles attract.\",\"A freely suspended magnet always aligns itself north‑south.\",\"The end of a bar magnet that points north is called the north pole.\",\"The magnetic field is the region around a magnet where its force acts.\",\"Natural magnets are made of magnetite found in the earth’s crust.\",\"Artificial magnets are made from iron, steel, aluminium, nickel and cobalt (e.g., alnico, ceramic).\",\"Magnetic discs stick to iron surfaces because of a black iron piece on the back.\",\"Magnets are used in electric generators, motors, compasses, MRI machines and many appliances.\",\"A magnetic compass has a needle that can rotate freely and points north.\",\"The magnetic strip on an ATM card stores account information magnetically.\",\"Iron filings gather near the poles of a magnet, showing the field lines.\",\"The strength of a magnet is concentrated at its poles, especially the ends.\",\"Magnetic force decreases with distance from the magnet.\",\"Magnetic materials are called magnetic substances; others are non‑magnetic.\",\"Magnetic poles cannot be separated; they always exist in pairs.\",\"The Earth itself behaves like a giant magnet with a north and south pole.\",\"Magnetic attraction is used to separate metal from waste in recycling.\",\"A magnet can be identified by touching it to iron objects – the ones that stick are attracted.\",\"The colour dot on a laboratory magnet indicates the north pole.\",\"Magnetism is used to produce sound in loudspeakers and headphones.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did Nilu see the funny experiments that she was thinking about while going home?\",\"options\":[\"At a science exhibition\",\"At a school playground\",\"At a local market\",\"At a toy shop\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that Nilu was thinking about experiments seen after visiting a science exhibition.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What material was the monkey in the experiment made of?\",\"options\":[\"Plastic\",\"Wood\",\"Cotton\",\"Metal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'One monkey made of cotton was kept on it\'.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the swing when 