ain\":\"The text states that information about the stone was given in Chinese scripts 2500 years ago.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the iron ore that is found in many places and acts as a natural magnet?\",\"options\":[\"Magnesia\",\"Turkistan\",\"Magnetite\",\"Iron cap\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies the iron ore called magnetite as being found in many places.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which region did the shepherd boy notice stones sticking to his stick?\",\"options\":[\"China\",\"Magnesia, Turkistan\",\"India\",\"Egypt\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The story mentions that some stones from Magnesia, Turkistan stuck to the iron cap of the shepherd\'s stick.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the shepherd fit an iron cap at the end of his stick?\",\"options\":[\"To attract magnetic stones\",\"To make the stick heavier\",\"To prevent the pointed tip from wearing out easily\",\"To help him climb mountains\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the iron cap was fitted to prevent the pointed tip of his stick from wearing out easily.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When a long magnetic stone is hung in the air, in which direction does it remain aligned?\",\"options\":[\"East-West\",\"North-South\",\"Up-Down\",\"Left-Right\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that when a long stone is hung, it remains aligned in the north-south direction.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is a characteristic property of natural magnets mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"They have very strong magnetic properties\",\"They are only found in Chinese scripts\",\"Their magnetic properties are weak\",\"They are made by humans in factories\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the magnetic properties are weak in such stones (natural magnets).\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a traveler 3500 years ago needed to find their way, what would they have used according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A map made of iron filings\",\"A well-polished, long strip-like stone\",\"A shepherd\'s stick with an iron cap\",\"A piece of lightning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Historians found that 3500 years ago, well-polished, long strip-like stones were used to find out directions.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you perform the experiment with iron filings and a bar magnet, what will you observe about the magnetic force?\",\"options\":[\"It is spread evenly across the whole magnet\",\"It is concentrated in specific parts of the magnet\",\"It only exists in the middle of the magnet\",\"It disappears when the magnet is lifted\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The experiment asks to observe which part attracts objects more strongly, implying the force is concentrated in specific parts.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to scientists, what natural event caused iron ore to be converted into magnets in the soil?\",\"options\":[\"Heavy rainfall\",\"Extreme heat from the sun\",\"Reactions due to lightning\",\"Pressure from the mountains\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states scientists think reactions occurred due to lightning converted this ore into magnet.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What can be inferred about the discovery of magnets from the text?\",\"options\":[\"It was discovered exactly 2500 years ago in China\",\"The exact person and time of discovery are unknown\",\"The shepherd boy was the first to record it in scripts\",\"It was discovered by scientists studying lightning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text begins by stating \'Nobody knows when and who discovered a magnet.\'\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story of the shepherd, why did the stones stick to his stick but not to his wooden staff?\",\"options\":[\"The stones only attract wood\",\"The stones attract the iron cap fitted at the end of the stick\",\"The stones were sticky like glue\",\"The shepherd used a special magnet to pick them up\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains the stones stick to the \'iron cap\' fitted at the end of the stick.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How many years ago were well-polished stones used for finding directions?\",\"options\":[\"2500 years ago\",\"3500 years ago\",\"1000 years ago\",\"500 years ago\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that 3500 years ago, those stones were used to find out directions.\",\"topic\":\"Do You Know?\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the term used for magnets that are manmade?\",\"options\":[\"Natural magnets\",\"Artificial magnets\",\"Soil magnets\",\"Metal magnets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that manmade magnets are called artificial magnets.\",\"topic\":\"Artificial Magnets\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following metals is NOT part of the mixture used to make Alnico magnets?\",\"options\":[\"Aluminium\",\"Nickel\",\"Cobalt\",\"Copper\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Alnico magnets are made from a mixture of aluminium, nickel, and cobalt.\",\"topic\":\"Artificial Magnets\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Ceramic magnets are made using a mixture of fine metal powder and which other material?\",\"options\":[\"Special soil used for cups and saucers\",\"Pure aluminium\",\"Liquid cobalt\",\"Steel wool\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions ceramic magnets are made from a mixture of special soil and fine metal powder.\",\"topic\":\"Artificial Magnets\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why were new techniqu