agnets\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How do ceramic magnets differ from alnico magnets based on the materials mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"Ceramic magnets use soil, while alnico uses a mixture of specific metals.\",\"Ceramic magnets are more powerful than alnico magnets.\",\"Alnico magnets are manmade, but ceramic magnets are natural.\",\"Alnico magnets are used for toys, while ceramic magnets are not.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text describes alnico as a metal mixture and ceramic as a mixture involving special soil.\",\"topic\":\"Artificial Magnets\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which characteristic of ceramic magnets allows them to be used for a variety of decorative items?\",\"options\":[\"They are only made of iron\",\"They are available in different shapes\",\"They are the most expensive magnets\",\"They are made without metal powder\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states ceramic magnets are available in different shapes and are low cost, making them suitable for decorations.\",\"topic\":\"Artificial Magnets\",\"part\":9,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is another name for a magnetic compass as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Desert compass\",\"Mariner\'s compass\",\"Sea needle\",\"Rotating magnet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that a magnetic compass is also called a mariner\'s compass.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic Compass\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"For how long have magnets been used to find directions while travelling?\",\"options\":[\"Hundreds of years\",\"Decades\",\"Thousands of years\",\"Millions of years\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that magnets were used for thousands of years to find directions.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic Compass\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the name of the central part that is free to rotate?\",\"options\":[\"Magnetic needle\",\"Iron box\",\"Plastic support\",\"Direction scale\"],\