िया\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"इंडोनेशियात आजही कोणत्या भारतीय महाकाव्यांवर आधारित नृत्य-नाट्ये लोकप्रिय आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"रामायण आणि महाभारत\",\"रघुवंश आणि मेघदूत\",\"वेदांत आणि उपनिषदे\",\"बुद्धचरित आणि त्रिपिटक\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"इंडोनेशियात आजही रामायण आणि महाभारत यातील कथांवर आधारित नृत्य-नाट्ये लोकप्रिय आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"आग्नेय आशिया\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"आग्नेय आशियातील कोणत्या देशांमध्ये प्राचीन काळात बौद्ध धर्म पोहोचला होता?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ म्यानमार\",\"म्यानमार, थायलंड, इंडोनेशिया\",\"केवळ व्हिएतनाम\",\"चीन आणि जपान\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"प्राचीन कालखंडात बौद्ध धर्म म्यानमार, थायलंड, इंडोनेशिया इत्यादी देशांत पोहोचला होता.\",\"topic\":\"आग्नेय आशिया\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"इत्सिंगने चिनी भिक्षूंना भारतात जाण्यापूर्वी कोणता सल्ला दिला होता?\",\"options\":[\"थेट भारतात जावे\",\"पर्शियन जहाजातून प्रवास करू नये\",\"श्रीविजय राज्यात १-२ वर्षे संस्कृत शिकावे\",\"केवळ बौद्ध धर्माचा अभ्यास करावा\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"श्रीविजय राज्यात १-२ वर्षे संस्कृत शिकण्यासाठी राहून मगच भारतात जाण्याचा सल्ला इत्सिंगने दिला होता.\",\"topic\":\"आग्नेय आशिया\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"आग्नेय आशियातील कला आणि सांस्कृतिक जीवनावर भारतीय संस्कृतीचा प्रभाव कशामुळे पडला?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ व्यापारामुळे\",\"भारतातून गेलेल्या लोकांनी तेथे राज्ये स्थापन केल्यामुळे\",\"चिनी प्रवाशांच्या आक्रमणामुळे\",\"पर्शियन जहाजांच्या वाहतुकीमुळे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"भारतातून गेलेल्या काहींनी तेथे राज्ये स्थापन केली, ज्यामुळे भारतीय संस्कृतीचा प्रसार झाला.\",\"topic\":\"आग्नेय आशिया\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रातील \'अंकोरवट\' हे प्रसिद्ध मंदिर कोणत्या देशात आहे?\",\"options\":[\"इंडोनेशिया\",\"थायलंड\",\"कंबोडिया\",\"म्यानमार\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"पाठ्यपुस्तकातील मजकूर आणि चित्राच्या संदर्भावरून अंकोरवट हे मंदिर कंबोडियामध्ये आहे.\",\"topic\":\"आग्नेय आशिया\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"40\\/094_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रातील वास्तुकलेवरून आग्नेय आशियावर कोणत्या संस्कृतीचा ठसा उमटलेला दिसतो?\",\"options\":[\"ग्रीक संस्कृती\",\"भारतीय संस्कृती\",\"पर्शियन संस्कृती\",\"रोमन संस्कृती\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"चित्रातील मंदिर आणि मजकुरावरून स्पष्ट होते की आग्नेय आशियातील कलेवर भारतीय संस्कृतीचा ठसा आहे.\",\"topic\":\"आग्नेय आशिया\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"40\\/094_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"नंतरच्या काळात आग्नेय आशियात कोणत्या देवतांच्या मंदिरांची निर्मिती झाली?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ गणपती\",\"शिव आणि विष्णू\",\"इंद्र आणि वरुण\",\"केवळ सूर्य\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"बौद्ध धर्माच्या प्रसारानंतरच्या काळात तेथे शिव आणि विष्णू यांच्या मंदिरांची निर्मिती झाली.\",\"topic\":\"आग्नेय आशिया\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"प्राचीन इतिहास शिकल्यामुळे विविध देशांतील संबंधांबाबत काय साध्य होते?\",\"options\":[\"सांस्कृतिक संबंध दृढ होतात\",\"केवळ व्यापार वाढतो\",\"युद्धे कमी होतात\",\"केवळ भाषा बदलतात\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"प्राचीन इतिहास शिकल्यामुळे विविध देशांतील सांस्कृतिक संबंध कसे दृढ होतात हे समजते.\",\"topic\":\"आग्नेय आशिया\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21892,41,7,'English','en','1.1 It’s a small world','[\"It’s a small world is a popular song and poem by Richard and Robert Sherman.\",\"The poem shows that people around the world are similar and connected.\",\"Key idea: ‘It’s a small world’ is used to express surprise when meeting someone familiar in a new place.\",\"The poem repeats the line ‘It’s a small world after all’ to emphasize the theme.\",\"Rhyming words in the poem: laughter\\/tear, hopes\\/fears, moon\\/sun, smile\\/friendship (not exact rhyme but close).\",\"The poem talks about laughter, tears, hopes, fears, moon, sun, smile, friendship.\",\"A smile is a universal sign of friendship in many cultures.\",\"Some gestures have different meanings in different regions (e.g., thumbs‑up).\",\"The poem encourages using your mother tongue to discuss implied meaning.\",\"Activities: sing the song, find rhyming pairs, add new rhymes, discuss lines, create conversations using expressions from the poem.\",\"The lesson also includes writing down conversations and sharing them in class.\",\"The song is played in Disneyland’s ‘It’s a small world’ ride.\",\"The poem is used to teach vocabulary, listening, speaking, and cultural awareness.\",\"Students can note down pairs of rhyming words and add one more rhyming word to each pair.\",\"The poem’s lines can be used to guess meanings and discuss feelings.\",\"The expressions in the poem can be used to prepare simple conversations for the first day of school.\",\"Students should write three conversations they prepared or heard.\",\"The lesson focuses on listening, speaking, and cultural understanding.\",\"The poem is a good resource for teaching rhyming and rhythm.\",\"The poem is also useful for teaching how gestures convey meaning across cultures.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who are the authors of the poem \'It\'s a small world\'?\",\"options\":[\"Richard M. Sherman and Robert B. Sherman\",\"William Wordsworth and Robert Frost\",\"Ruskin Bond and R.K. Narayan\",\"J.K. Rowling and Enid Blyton\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions Richard M. Sherman and Robert B. Sherman as the authors at the end.\",\"topic\":\"A smile means Friendship\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what does a smile mean to every one?\",\"options\":[\"Happiness\",\"Friendship\",\"Laughter\",\"Kindness\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'And a smile means Friendship to every one.\'\",\"topic\":\"A smile means Friendship\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many golden suns are mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Many\",\"One\",\"None\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'There is just one moon And one golden sun\'.\",\"topic\":\"A smile means Friendship\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'a world of tears\' most likely refer to in the context of the poem?\",\"options\":[\"A world full of water\",\"A world of sadness and sorrow\",\"A world where it always rains\",\"A world of oceans\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the poem, \'tears\' is used as a contrast to \'laughter\', representing the sad aspects of life.\",\"topic\":\"A smile means Friendship\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet say it is time for us to be aware of?\",\"options\":[\"That the world is very large\",\"That there is so much we share\",\"That mountains are hard to climb\",\"That the sun is golden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'There\'s so much that we share That it\'s time we\'re aware\'.\",\"topic\":\"A smile means Friendship\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which two geographical features are mentioned as things that divide or are wide?\",\"options\":[\"Rivers and Valleys\",\"Deserts and Forests\",\"Mountains and Oceans\",\"Islands and Continents\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'Though the mountains divide And the oceans are wide\'.\",\"topic\":\"A smile means Friendship\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student from another country meets you, which action from the poem would best show friendship?\",\"options\":[\"Talking about the moon\",\"Sharing a smile\",\"Measuring the ocean\",\"Climbing a mountain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem applies the concept that a smile means friendship to everyone, regardless of distance.\",\"topic\":\"A smile means Friendship\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs from the poem represents contrasting human emotions?\",\"options\":[\"Sun and Moon\",\"Mountains and Oceans\",\"Laughter and Tears\",\"Small and Wide\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Laughter and tears represent the opposite emotions of joy and sadness shared by people.\",\"topic\":\"A smile means Friendship\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet repeat the phrase \'It\'s a small world after all\' multiple times?\",\"options\":[\"To show that the Earth is physically shrinking\",\"To emphasize the idea of global unity and connection\",\"To describe the size of the moon\",\"To explain why mountains are so high\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Repetition is used to emphasize the central theme that despite differences, we are all connected in a small world.\",\"topic\":\"A smile means Friendship\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the significance of the line \'There is just one moon and one golden sun\'?\",\"options\":[\"It highlights that we all live under the same sky and are connected\",\"It provides a scientific fact about the solar system\",\"It explains why the world is so bright\",\"It suggests that we should only look at the sky\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The mention of a single sun and moon for everyone reinforces the theme of unity in a \'small world\'.\",\"topic\":\"A smile means Friendship\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the title of the popular song mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"It\'s a big world\",\"It\'s a small world\",\"Welcome to Disneyland\",\"Human Beings are Alike\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'It\'s a small world\' is a very popular song.\",\"topic\":\"About the Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the ride with the title \'It\'s a small world\' located?\",\"options\":[\"In a local park\",\"In a school\",\"In Disneyland\",\"In a movie theater\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions this song is played on a ride of the same title in Disneyland.\",\"topic\":\"About the Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Into how many languages has the song \'It\'s a small world\' been translated?\",\"options\":[\"Only one language\",\"Two languages\",\"Many languages\",\"No other languages\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the song is \'translated into many languages\'.\",\"topic\":\"About the Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In this poem, what do the words \'It\'s a small world\' tell us about human beings?\",\"options\":[\"That humans are very short\",\"That all human beings are alike\",\"That humans live in small cities\",\"That humans do not know each other\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the words are used to tell us that all human beings are alike.\",\"topic\":\"About the Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What emotion is expressed by using the phrase \'It\'s a small world\' when meeting someone unexpectedly?\",\"options\":[\"Anger\",\"Sadness\",\"Surprise\",\"Fear\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the words are used to show your surprise on such an occasion.\",\"topic\":\"About the Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, when might you use the phrase \'It\'s a small world\'?\",\"options\":[\"When you are traveling to a large country\",\"When you meet the same people in an unexpected place\",\"When you are learning a new language\",\"When you are visiting a ride for the first time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains the phrase is used when meeting people in unexpected places or finding common connections.\",\"topic\":\"About the Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are on a vacation in a far-off city and suddenly see your school teacher, which phrase from the text would you most likely say?\",\"options\":[\"It\'s a big world\",\"It\'s a small world\",\"Welcome to the ride\",\"Human beings are different\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the phrase is used to show surprise when meeting the same people in an unexpected place.\",\"topic\":\"About the Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"You find out that your new friend in a different town knows your cousin. Based on the text, this is an example of:\",\"options\":[\"A ride in Disneyland\",\"A translation of a song\",\"Finding out people are connected to those you know\",\"A poem about the Earth\'s size\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'It\'s a small world\' as finding out people are connected to people you know.\",\"topic\":\"About the Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the connection between the song and the ride mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"They share the same title\",\"They are in different languages\",\"They have different meanings\",\"They are not related at all\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says the song is played on a ride \'of the same title\'.\",\"topic\":\"About the Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the song \'It\'s a small world\' likely translated into many languages?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is only played in Disneyland\",\"Because it is a very popular song with a universal message\",\"Because it is a very short poem\",\"Because people keep meeting in unexpected places\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text links its popularity and its message about all humans being alike to its widespread use.\",\"topic\":\"About the Poem\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem\'s workshop, what does a \'smile\' mean to everyone?\",\"options\":[\"Happiness\",\"Friendship\",\"Laughter\",\"Kindness\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'The poem says And a smile means friendship to everyone.\'\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the line \'A world of tears\', what does the word \'tears\' most likely imply?\",\"options\":[\"Rainy weather\",\"Sorrow or sadness\",\"Ocean water\",\"Joyful crying\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the context of \'laughter\' and \'hopes\', \'tears\' implies the opposite emotion, which is sadness.\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a pair of rhyming words found in the workshop text?\",\"options\":[\"Laughter - Hopes\",\"Tears - Fears\",\"Smile - Friendship\",\"School - Vacation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tears and fears rhyme as they have the same ending sound.\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which gesture is specifically mentioned as having a meaning only in certain regions?\",\"options\":[\"A smile\",\"Waving hello\",\"Thumbs up sign\",\"Shaking hands\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the \'Thumbs up\' sign as an example of a gesture with a specific meaning in certain regions.\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where were the expressions like \'It\'s nice to be back in school\' heard?\",\"options\":[\"At a summer camp\",\"In a school on the first day\",\"During a family vacation\",\"At a graduation ceremony\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'The following sentences were heard in a school on the first day.\'\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are students permitted to use when discussing the implied meaning of the lines?\",\"options\":[\"Only English\",\"Their mother tongue\",\"A dictionary\",\"Written notes only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text in the figure says: \'Allow the students to use their mother tongue if necessary...\'\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/012_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If you meet a new student, which expression from the given figure would be most appropriate to introduce yourself?\",\"options\":[\"How was your journey to...?\",\"I\'m new here. My name\'s .... what\'s yours?\",\"We had so much fun together!\",\"It\'s nice to be back in school.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The expression \'I\'m new here. My name\'s .... what\'s yours?\' is specifically for introductions.\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/012_104.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first activity students are asked to do in the English Workshop?\",\"options\":[\"Note down rhyming words\",\"Sing the song\",\"Discuss the meaning\",\"Prepare conversations\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first point in the workshop is \'1. Sing the song.\'\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the workshop instructions, what should students do after noting down pairs of rhyming words?\",\"options\":[\"Draw a picture\",\"Add one more rhyming word to each pair\",\"Translate them to their mother tongue\",\"Write a new poem\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Task 2 says: \'Note down pairs of rhyming words from the poem. Add one more rhyming word to each pair.\'\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which expression would you use to ask a friend about their time away from school?\",\"options\":[\"How was your holiday?\",\"Meet my friends\",\"I am so glad to see you all!\",\"Hi!\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Asking \'How was your holiday?\' is the standard way to inquire about their time away.\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The workshop asks for examples of gestures that mean the same in \'all parts of the world\'. What is the contrast to this?\",\"options\":[\"Gestures that mean nothing\",\"Gestures that have a specific meaning only in certain regions\",\"Gestures that are only used by teachers\",\"Gestures that are used only in songs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks for examples of universal gestures and then contrasts them with gestures having specific meanings in certain regions.\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final task mentioned in the provided workshop text?\",\"options\":[\"Sing the song again\",\"Discuss the meaning of laughter\",\"Write down three of the conversations prepared\",\"Give examples of gestures\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The last instruction is: \'* Write down three of the conversations you have prepared \\/ presented \\/ heard.\'\",\"topic\":\"ENGLISH WORKSHOP\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21893,41,7,'English','en','1.2 Warm up with Tara and Friends','[\"1. Warm‑up activities help students recall letters, words and phrases.\",\"2. Step One: Think of the alphabet from A to Z until partner stops; write the letter you get.\",\"3. Step Two: Each partner writes three words that start with that letter.\",\"4. Step Three: Exchange words and use them to make meaningful phrases.\",\"5. Game 1: Speed reading of common words – read as many as possible in 15 seconds.\",\"6. Game 2: Fill a table with words of at least 3 letters; avoid plurals, -ing, -ed, -en endings.\",\"7. Scoring: 3‑letter words = 1 mark, 4‑letter = 2 marks, 5‑letter = 3 marks, 6‑letter = 4 marks, 7‑letter = 5 marks, 8+ letters = 1 mark each.\",\"8. Extra 5 marks for writing 25 words in 2 minutes.\",\"9. Game 3: Word Art – create attractive labels or bookmarks using letters of your name or textbook title.\",\"10. Game 4: Scene‑out‑of‑the‑hat – write scene titles on slips, draw lots, enact the scene, speak 2‑3 times each.\",\"11. Game 5: Adding ‘‑s’ to verbs – write wrong sentences and correct them, focusing on subject‑verb agreement.\",\"12. Game 6: Questions Race – write one meaningful question starting with each given word (Who, Are, What, etc.).\",\"13. Game 7: Mirror activity – write sentences and demonstrate them in a mirror.\",\"14. Parts of Speech: Noun, Pronoun, Adjective, Verb, Adverb, Preposition, Conjunction, Interjection – each has a specific role.\",\"15. Noun: a name of a person, place or thing.\",\"16. Pronoun: replaces a noun (he, she, it, they).\",\"17. Adjective: describes a noun (color, size).\",\"18. Verb: shows action or state (run, is).\",\"19. Adverb: describes how an action is done (quickly, well).\",\"20. Preposition: shows relation (in, at, on).\",\"21. Conjunction: joins words or clauses (and, but, or).\",\"22. Interjection: expresses emotion (hurray, oh).\"]','[{\"q\":\"Tara greets Biscu, Paddy, and which other character at the beginning of the text?\",\"options\":[\"Mia\",\"Kuku\",\"Toto\",\"Moti\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text starts with \'Hi Biscu! Hi Paddy! Hi Kuku!\'\",\"topic\":\"Warm up with Tara and Friends\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does one character exclaim \'Oh, no!\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they lost a game\",\"Because they are hungry\",\"Because the holidays are over\",\"Because they missed the bus\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text links the exclamation \'Oh, no!\' directly to the statement \'Holidays are over!\'\",\"topic\":\"Warm up with Tara and Friends\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where will there be \'more play\' according to the dialogue?\",\"options\":[\"In the classroom\",\"At home\",\"On the school ground\",\"In the garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'More play on the school ground.\'\",\"topic\":\"Warm up with Tara and Friends\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Besides starting studies, what is another reason a character is excited to return to school?\",\"options\":[\"To get new books\",\"To see friends\",\"To eat lunch\",\"To meet the teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"One character says, \'I\'m excited too! I\'ll see my friends.\'\",\"topic\":\"Warm up with Tara and Friends\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which character is specifically mentioned as being missed by a friend?\",\"options\":[\"Tara\",\"Mia\",\"Paddy\",\"Kuku\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'I\'m sad without Paddy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Warm up with Tara and Friends\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do the animals (like Mia) consider themselves \'lucky\'?\",\"options\":[\"They have new toys\",\"They don\'t have school\",\"They are going on holiday\",\"They found a biscuit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'We are lucky! 