an to rejoice for the holiday\",\"A big crowd gathered and a fight began\",\"They helped Akulka clean her dress\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the men running out, a crowd gathering, and a fight beginning.\",\"topic\":\"The Quarrel\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what emotion is most clearly shown on the faces of the women in the foreground?\",\"options\":[\"Happiness\",\"Anger\",\"Sadness\",\"Sleepiness\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the women with aggressive facial expressions and gestures, indicating they are quarreling in anger.\",\"topic\":\"The Quarrel\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/023_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If Akulka\'s dress is described as \'bespattered\', what has most likely happened to it?\",\"options\":[\"It has been torn by a dog\",\"It has been splashed with liquid or mud\",\"It has been ironed neatly\",\"It has been lost in the street\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Bespattered means to be splashed with something, which fits the context of Malasha splashing water on Akulka.\",\"topic\":\"The Quarrel\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which term from the text correctly identifies the group of village people involved in the conflict?\",\"options\":[\"Soldiers\",\"Peasants\",\"Merchants\",\"Sailors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the grandmother \'stepped in the midst of the peasants.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Quarrel\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why was it impossible for the people in the crowd to hear their neighbors?\",\"options\":[\"Because it was a very windy day\",\"Because everyone was crying (shouting) at once\",\"Because the grandmother was speaking too loudly\",\"Because the men were too far away\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'All were crying, and nobody could hear his neighbour.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Quarrel\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the men 