orm of \'country\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/032_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the table in the given figure, which of these is an example of an uncountable noun?\",\"options\":[\"Mile\",\"Sky\",\"Road\",\"Word\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure lists \'sky\' under the category of Uncountable nouns.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/032_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is true about uncountable nouns according to the Language Study section?\",\"options\":[\"They have a plural form\",\"They stand for something that cannot be counted\",\"They are always animals\",\"They are the same as countable nouns\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines uncountable nouns as those that stand for something that cannot be counted.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct plural form of \'story\' as shown in the examples?\",\"options\":[\"storys\",\"storyes\",\"stories\",\"storyies\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table provided in the text lists \'stories\' as the plural form of \'story\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'mountain\' is a countable noun, what is its plural form according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"mountaines\",\"mountains\",\"mountain\'s\",\"mountanes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'mountains\' as the plural form of \'mountain\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following expressions is correct to use for an uncountable noun like \'water\'?\",\"options\":[\"Three waters\",\"Two glasses of water\",\"Many waters\",\"A water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes that we use expressions like \'two glasses of water\' because we do not say \'waters\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it incorrect to say \'funs\' or \'hairs\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Because they are countable nouns\",\"Because they are uncountable nouns\",\"Because they are always singular\",\"Because they are not common nouns\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that for uncountable nouns like hair and fun, we do not use plural forms like hairs or funs.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following words from the text would be misplaced if put in the \'Countable nouns\' list?\",\"options\":[\"Road\",\"Desert\",\"Fire\",\"Mile\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Fire is listed under \'Uncountable nouns\' in the text, while the others are countable.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":14,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is listed as a countable noun in the text?\",\"options\":[\"water\",\"sky\",\"mountain\",\"fun\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'mountain\' under the plural form \'mountains\', identifying it as a countable noun.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct plural form of \'country\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"countrys\",\"countries\",\"countryes\",\"countris\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'countries\' as the plural form of \'country\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is categorized as an uncountable noun?\",\"options\":[\"mile\",\"road\",\"fire\",\"desert\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'fire\' alongside hair, sky, water, and fun as uncountable nouns.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which of these words should NOT be used in a plural form like \'funs\' or \'waters\'?\",\"options\":[\"roads\",\"stories\",\"hair\",\"miles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that for uncountable nouns like hair, we do not say \'hairs\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the plural form of the word \'story\' as shown in the text?\",\"options\":[\"storys\",\"stories\",\"storyes\",\"story\'s\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'stories\' as the plural form for the singular word \'story\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which expression should be used to describe a quantity of water according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"two waters\",\"two glasses of water\",\"two water\",\"two waterses\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using expressions like \'two glasses of water\' instead of saying \'waters\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to talk about individual pieces of hair, which expression does the text recommend?\",\"options\":[\"hairs\",\"hair strands\",\"hair bits\",\"hair pieces\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'hair strands\' as the correct expression to use for hair.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which group contains only countable nouns based on the provided list?\",\"options\":[\"word, water, sky\",\"country, mile, road\",\"fire, fun, desert\",\"mountain, story, hair\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Country, mile, and road are all listed in the singular\\/plural countable nouns table.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the grammar rules in the text, which of the following sentences is correct?\",\"options\":[\"We had a bit of funs at the party.\",\"We had a bit of fun at the party.\",\"We had many funs at the party.\",\"We had a fun at the party.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies the expression \'a bit of fun\' and states we do not say \'funs\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these nouns follows the same pluralization pattern (changing \'y\' to \'ies\') as \'country\' and \'story\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"miles\",\"deserts\",\"roads\",\"None of these\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"In the provided text, only \'country\' and \'story\' show the \'ies\' plural ending; the others listed use \'s\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21896,41,7,'English','en','1.5 Children are going to school','[\"Children go to school in the early morning when the sky is still dark and the air is cool.\",\"The poem describes the morning with soft light, gentle breezes, and singing birds.\",\"The sun is described as wearing a golden muslin turban and smiling on the road.\",\"Natural elements like the sky, sun, breezes, flowers, and trees are personified to show their actions.\",\"The sky bows its head in respect, the sun waits and smiles, breezes sing, flowers awaken the roads, and the peepal waves its hands.\",\"Every particle of the earth throbs like a mother’s heart, showing the earth’s joy.\",\"Time is described as sitting on an old roof and flying pigeons, symbolising the passing of time.\",\"The whole world feels happy because children are going to school, indicating the importance of education.\",\"The poem uses capital letters for natural elements to give them a human-like importance.\",\"The poem’s language is simple and vivid, using sensory words like bright sunlight, cool breeze, and fragrant flowers.\",\"The poem encourages children to observe nature and feel the atmosphere of early morning.\",\"It shows that nature celebrates the start of a school day, reflecting harmony between humans and nature.\",\"The poem invites readers to imagine colours and sounds of the morning scene.\",\"It uses verbs ending in ‘-s’ to give a rhythmic flow, e.g., ‘waves’, ‘smiles’, ‘sings’.\",\"The poem is a celebration of learning and the joy it brings to the world.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what does the Sky do in respect for the children?\",\"options\":[\"Sings a song of blessings\",\"Bows his head\",\"Wears a golden turban\",\"Waves his hands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Once again, the Sky bows his head in respect, For children are going to school.\'\",\"topic\":\"Nature\'s Melodies\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the Peepal tree stand as the children go to school?\",\"options\":[\"In the middle of the river\",\"On the green-topped branches\",\"At the corner of the lane\",\"Under the morning light\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions the Peepal tree is \'At the corner of the lane\'.\",\"topic\":\"Nature\'s Melodies\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of turban is the Sun described as wearing?\",\"options\":[\"Silver silk turban\",\"Green leaf turban\",\"Golden muslin turban\",\"Fragrant flower turban\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the Sun as \'dressed up in his golden muslin turban\'.\",\"topic\":\"Nature\'s Melodies\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the Sun do after taking his morning dip in the river?\",\"options\":[\"He sleeps on the road\",\"He bows his head in respect\",\"He waits and smiles on one side of the road\",\"He awakens the sleepy roads\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says the Sun \'waits and smiles on one side of the road\' after his dip.\",\"topic\":\"Nature\'s Melodies\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How do the breezes contribute to the morning atmosphere?\",\"options\":[\"They wave their hands to the children\",\"They sing songs of blessings through branches\",\"They dress up in muslin turbans\",\"They bow their heads in respect\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Breezes sing their songs of blessings\' through the branches.\",\"topic\":\"Nature\'s Melodies\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What specific action do the Fragrant Flowers take?\",\"options\":[\"They take a dip in the river\",\"They wave their hands from the lane\",\"They awaken the sleepy roads with melodies\",\"They spread morning light over the earth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'Fragrant Flowers awaken the sleepy roads with their melodies.\'\",\"topic\":\"Nature\'s Melodies\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which natural element is described as having \'lush deep foliage\'?\",\"options\":[\"The Sun\",\"The Peepal\",\"The Breezes\",\"The Sky\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to \'the Peepal in his lush deep foliage\'.\",\"topic\":\"Nature\'s Melodies\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the Sun is \'smiling\' and \'waiting\', what does this suggest about his attitude toward the children?\",\"options\":[\"He is angry that they are awake\",\"He is indifferent to their presence\",\"He is welcoming and happy to see them\",\"He is trying to hide from the Sky\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Smiling and waiting on the road suggests a welcoming and positive attitude toward the children going to school.\",\"topic\":\"Nature\'s Melodies\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'awaken the sleepy roads\', what does the word \'sleepy\' imply about the time of day?\",\"options\":[\"It is late at night\",\"It is early morning when things are just starting\",\"It is the middle of a hot afternoon\",\"It is sunset when everyone is tired\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The mention of \'Morning light\' and \'awaken\' indicates it is early morning.\",\"topic\":\"Nature\'s Melodies\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, how does nature collectively react to children going to school?\",\"options\":[\"Nature ignores the children to focus on the sun\",\"Nature becomes quiet and dark to let them pass\",\"Nature shows respect, joy, and provides blessings\",\"Nature tries to stop them by blocking the roads\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Sky bows, the Sun smiles, breezes bless, and flowers sing, showing a collective positive reaction.\",\"topic\":\"Nature\'s Melodies\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'muslin\' as per the glossary?\",\"options\":[\"A kind of soft cotton fabric\",\"A type of shiny metal\",\"A green leafy cover\",\"A hard wooden surface\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines muslin as a kind of soft cotton fabric.\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the text means \'shining brightly\'?\",\"options\":[\"Foliage\",\"A-gleam\",\"Muslin\",\"Throb\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary explicitly defines \'a-gleam\' as shining brightly.\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the term \'foliage\' refer to in the glossary?\",\"options\":[\"Soft cotton clothes\",\"Brightly lit roads\",\"Greenery or leafy cover\",\"Pigeons in the sky\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines foliage as greenery or leafy cover.\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what does every particle of the Earth throb like?\",\"options\":[\"A ticking clock\",\"A mother\'s heart\",\"A flying pigeon\",\"A shining road\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'every particle of the Earth throbs like a mother’s heart.\'\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the translator of the poem \'Bachche school ja rahe hain\'?\",\"options\":[\"Balbharati\",\"Angels of Light\",\"Nida Fazli\",\"A school teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the poem is translated from \'Bachche school ja rahe hain\' by Nida Fazli.\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where is \'Time\' sitting in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"On a green leaf\",\"On an old roof\",\"In a school classroom\",\"On the gleaming road\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem describes \'Time, sitting on an old roof\'.\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is wearing a shirt made of \'muslin\', what kind of material is it?\",\"options\":[\"Rough wool\",\"Soft cotton\",\"Heavy leather\",\"Shiny plastic\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since muslin is a soft cotton fabric, a shirt made of it would be soft cotton.\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a photographer describes a landscape as having \'dense foliage\', what would you expect to see?\",\"options\":[\"Many pigeons flying\",\"Brightly lit city roads\",\"Lots of greenery and leaves\",\"Old roofs and buildings\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Foliage means greenery or leafy cover, so dense foliage implies lots of leaves.\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What activity is \'Time\' performing while sitting on the roof?\",\"options\":[\"Making the roads gleam\",\"Flying pigeons in the sky\",\"Setting out light\",\"Covering the earth with muslin\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says \'Time... flies pigeons in the sky.\'\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the central reason for the Earth throbbing and the roads gleaming in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Because the sun has just risen\",\"Because pigeons are flying high\",\"Because children are going to school\",\"Because the foliage is very green\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem concludes that these events happen \'For children are going to school.\'\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21897,41,7,'English','en','1.6 In a Class of their own !','[\"- A good teacher gives ready‑made answers but also challenges students to think.\",\"- A good teacher is friendly, humorous and encourages work.\",\"- A good friend keeps secrets, supports you and shows you answers when needed.\",\"- A good student is punctual, participates, learns on his own and remembers answers.\",\"- Unity in a class means staying together, working together and avoiding quarrels.\",\"- Collective nouns refer to groups (e.g., class, herd, flock).\",\"- Regular plurals add -s, -es or -ies; irregular plurals change internally (e.g., child‑children).\",\"- Concrete nouns are things you can touch; abstract nouns are ideas or feelings.\",\"- The idiom “in a class of one’s own” means unique or better than others.\",\"- A plan of action (PoA) is a set of steps to achieve a goal.\",\"- Study guards and searchlights are classmates who help others study.\",\"- “On cloud nine” means very happy.\",\"- “Take a test” means to sit for an exam; “give a test” means to conduct an exam.\",\"- Adverbs like always, regularly, sometimes, never modify verbs.\",\"- Pronouns: myself, yourself, himself, herself, ourselves, yourselves, itself.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many friends should you talk to for your opinion poll?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Five\",\"Ten\",\"The whole class\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to \'talk to any five of your friends\' for the opinion poll.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are the three types of responses you should note down during the poll?\",\"options\":[\"Yes - No - Maybe\",\"True - False - Not Given\",\"Agree - Disagree - Not sure\",\"Good - Bad - Average\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists the responses as \'Agree - Disagree - Not sure\'.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is responsible for putting together the findings and making the presentation?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher\",\"Every member of the group\",\"A group leader\",\"The five friends polled\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says each group should select a group leader to put together findings and make a presentation.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which characteristic of a good friend involves being honest even when it is difficult?\",\"options\":[\"Shows you the answer sheets at the time of exam\",\"Points it out when you are doing something wrong\",\"Sides with you in all fights and quarrels\",\"Tells you all the gossip\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Pointing out when a friend is doing something wrong is a sign of honest guidance.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/036_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which characteristic describes a student who is always on time?\",\"options\":[\"Learns all answers by heart\",\"Keeps quiet in the classroom\",\"Is punctual and regular\",\"Often brings gifts for the teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Punctuality refers to being on time.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/036_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what object is used to represent the \'Warming up!\' activity?\",\"options\":[\"A book\",\"A pencil\",\"An eraser\",\"A ruler\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows a personified pencil running.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/036_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What should the class discuss after the group presentations are finished?\",\"options\":[\"The marks obtained in the exam\",\"The most important characteristic of a friend, student, and teacher\",\"Which group leader was the best speaker\",\"How to write better answer sheets\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'Follow the presentations with a discussion on the most important characteristic...\'\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a characteristic of a \'good student\' mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Provides readymade answers\",\"Sides with you in all fights\",\"Takes efforts to learn something on his\\/her own\",\"Brings in a lot of fun and humour\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Taking efforts to learn independently is listed under the \'Good student\' characteristics table.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'Good Teacher\' characteristics, what kind of tasks should a teacher give?\",\"options\":[\"Easy tasks\",\"Challenging tasks\",\"No tasks at all\",\"Gossip-related tasks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions a good teacher \'gives challenging tasks and makes the students work on them\'.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student \'participates in all classroom activities\', which table does this characteristic belong to?\",\"options\":[\"What makes a good friend\",\"What makes a good student\",\"What makes a good teacher\",\"What makes a good leader\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Participating in activities is listed in the \'What makes a good student\' table.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text mention that you may consider characteristics \'not mentioned in the tables\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the tables are incorrect\",\"To encourage students to think of more qualities beyond the examples\",\"Because the teacher forgot to write them\",\"To make the poll shorter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It allows for a broader discussion and personal input from the students\' own experiences.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which characteristic of a good teacher focuses on their emotional connection with students?\",\"options\":[\"Provides readymade answers\",\"Understands students\' problems\",\"Learns all answers by heart\",\"Keeps a secret\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Understanding problems is an empathetic quality listed for teachers.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step in carrying out this opinion poll activity?\",\"options\":[\"Select a group leader\",\"Make a presentation\",\"Pick one of the given topics\",\"Discuss findings in a group\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text starts with \'Use any one of the topics given below to carry out a quick opinion poll\'.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these friend characteristics might be considered unhelpful for actual learning?\",\"options\":[\"Keeps a secret\",\"Points out when you are wrong\",\"Shows you the answer sheets at the time of exam\",\"Sides with you in fights\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Showing answer sheets during an exam is a form of cheating, not helpful for genuine learning.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How many total topics are provided for the opinion poll?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides three topics: a good friend, a good student, and a good teacher.\",\"topic\":\"An Opinion Poll\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many students are there in the class described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Fifty girls and boys\",\"Sixty girls and boys\",\"Sixty girls only\",\"Forty boys and girls\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'We are a class of sixty girls and boys\'.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the new Class Teacher?\",\"options\":[\"Mrs. Patil\",\"Mrs. Joshi\",\"Mrs. Desai\",\"Mrs. Sharma\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'And so was our new Class Teacher, Mrs Desai.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which specific punishment is mentioned in the text regarding writing?\",\"options\":[\"Writing a thousand words\",\"Copying a hundred lines from the book\",\"Writing a letter of apology\",\"Copying the entire chapter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'copy a hundred lines from the book as a punishment\'.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'we do not tell tales\' imply about the students?\",\"options\":[\"They do not like reading stories.\",\"They do not complain about each other to the teachers.\",\"They do not speak to each other during class.\",\"They do not know how to narrate events.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'telling tales\' means reporting someone\'s misdeeds to an authority figure.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the students feel about the previous teachers shouting at them?\",\"options\":[\"They felt very sad and cried.\",\"They were scared of the teachers.\",\"It made no difference to them.\",\"They decided to study harder.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'But we didn’t mind it. It made no difference to us.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to Mrs. Desai, what is the \'very important quality\' that the class possesses?\",\"options\":[\"Intelligence\",\"Punctuality\",\"Unity\",\"Cleanliness\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mrs. Desai says, \'Unity is a very important quality and you must always maintain it.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a teacher punishes the class by making them run around the ground, how does this class react?\",\"options\":[\"They blame the student who made the mistake.\",\"They take the punishment together as a class.\",\"They argue with the teacher to cancel it.\",\"Only the naughty students do the running.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'We take the punishment as a class.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these addresses would Mrs. Desai NOT use for her students?\",\"options\":[\"Young lady\",\"Young man\",\"Children\",\"My dear\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically notes, \'It’s never ‘children’.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What can be analyzed about the class\'s internal relationship from the text?\",\"options\":[\"They are always perfect and never fight.\",\"They are divided into camps and have quarrels, but stay united against outsiders.\",\"They hate each other and only talk when the teacher is present.\",\"They are all best friends who never have arguments.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they have camps and quarrels, but \'when it comes to facing others... we are all one.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why do the students feel \'nice\' when Mrs. Desai addresses them?\",\"options\":[\"Because she gives them rewards.\",\"Because she treats them with respect and dignity.\",\"Because she speaks very softly.\",\"Because she lets them do whatever they want.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Addressing them as \'young lady\' or \'young man\' shows respect, making them feel good.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, evaluate why Mrs. Desai is different from the previous teachers.\",\"options\":[\"She is stricter than the previous teachers.\",\"She focuses on their positive quality of unity rather than just their faults.\",\"She does not give any punishments.\",\"She only teaches the girls in the class.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"While others shouted for poor marks, she expressed pride in their unity.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following was NOT a reason mentioned for teachers shouting at the class?\",\"options\":[\"Shabby work\",\"Incomplete homework\",\"Poor marks\",\"Talking in the library\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists poor marks, shabby work, incomplete homework, and irregular attendance, but not library behavior.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part I\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the definition of \'camps\'?\",\"options\":[\"A place where students go for holidays\",\"A group of people who think alike\",\"A type of school building\",\"A collection of textbooks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'camps\' as a group of people who think alike.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'shabby\' mean in the vocabulary list?\",\"options\":[\"Very clean\",\"Expensive\",\"Untidy\",\"Colorful\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'shabby\' means untidy.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does it mean to \'tell tales\'?\",\"options\":[\"To read a storybook aloud\",\"To write a long essay\",\"To talk to others about someone\'s faults or secrets\",\"To lie about one\'s homework\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'tell tales\' as talking to other people about someone’s faults, mistakes, or secrets.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase describes meeting people when you are likely to be scolded or punished?\",\"options\":[\"Facing others\",\"Unity\",\"In a class of one\'s own\",\"Telling tales\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'facing others\' as talking to or meeting others when scolding or punishment is likely.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of \'unity\' among a group of people according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"They get higher marks in exams\",\"They stay and work together without fights\",\"They all wear the same uniform\",\"They become famous in the school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that unity means people stay together and work together without fights or quarrels.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the idiom \'In a class of one\'s own\'?\",\"options\":[\"Being the only student in a room\",\"Studying alone for a test\",\"Unique and better than all others\",\"Belonging to a specific grade\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines this idiom as meaning unique or better than all others.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a group of students decides to help each other with a project without any arguments, which quality are they showing?\",\"options\":[\"Shabbiness\",\"Unity\",\"Facing others\",\"Telling tales\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Working together without fights is the definition of unity provided in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student is called to the Principal\'s office for breaking a window. Which vocabulary term best describes this situation?\",\"options\":[\"Telling tales\",\"Unity\",\"Facing others\",\"Camps\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Meeting someone when you are likely to be punished is described as \'facing others\'.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student\'s notebook has torn pages and ink stains everywhere, which word from the text best describes it?\",\"options\":[\"Unique\",\"Shabby\",\"Unity\",\"Camp\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The word \'shabby\' means untidy, which fits the description of a messy notebook.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the discussion section, what is the purpose of printing certain words in \'bold type\'?\",\"options\":[\"To make the page look colorful\",\"To show they are less important\",\"To draw attention to specific terms for discussion\",\"To indicate the end of a chapter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks to discuss why words are in bold, implying they are key terms or points of focus.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following behaviors would NOT be considered part of \'unity\' as defined in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Staying together during a crisis\",\"Working together on a task\",\"Starting a quarrel with a teammate\",\"Avoiding fights within the group\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines unity as being \'without fights or quarrels\', so starting a quarrel is the opposite.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If someone says a class is \'unique\', which idiom from the text are they most likely referring to?\",\"options\":[\"Facing others\",\"Tell tales\",\"In a class of its own\",\"Thinking alike\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that \'In a class of its own\' means unique.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What did the students usually expect to receive after a unit test?\",\"options\":[\"Praise and rewards\",\"Scolding and punishments\",\"Gifts and sweets\",\"Extra holidays\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that after the test, they all got ready to receive their usual share of scolding and punishments.\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who brought the progress report cards to the class?\",\"options\":[\"The Principal\",\"Sushmita\",\"Mrs. Desai\",\"Asmita\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Mrs. Desai came with the progress report cards.\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did Mrs. Desai\'s eyes look when she entered the class with the report cards?\",\"options\":[\"They looked angry\",\"They looked very happy\",\"They didn\'t look happy\",\"They were closed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says she smiled as usual, but her eyes didn’t look happy.\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the result for \'many\' of the students in the class?\",\"options\":[\"They had failed in one subject or the other\",\"They had topped the whole school\",\"They had all scored full marks\",\"They had lost their report cards\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the text, \'Many of us had failed in one subject or the other.\'\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Mrs. Desai do when her eyes filled with tears?\",\"options\":[\"She started crying loudly\",\"She shouted at the students\",\"She blinked them away and turned to the blackboard\",\"She left the classroom immediately\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states she didn\'t let the tears fall; she just blinked them away and turned to the blackboard.\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what are the students doing after school hours?\",\"options\":[\"They are playing a game of football\",\"They are waiting and talking about the teacher\'s reaction\",\"They are cleaning the classroom floor\",\"They are writing their homework quietly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text and image show the students gathered together, and the text says \'We waited after school and talked about this.\'\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/038_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what does the facial expression of the students suggest about their conversation?\",\"options\":[\"They are celebrating a victory\",\"They are serious and concerned about their performance\",\"They are bored and falling asleep\",\"They are laughing at a joke\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The students\' expressions in the drawing are somber and serious, reflecting their concern over the test results and their teacher\'s sadness.\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/038_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Who noticed the specific difference between \'I am proud\' and \'I will always want to be proud\'?\",\"options\":[\"Snehal\",\"Mrs. Desai\",\"The Principal\",\"The boys in the back\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Snehal asked Asmita if she noticed that the teacher said \'I will always want to be proud of you\' instead of \'I am proud of you.\'\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what category do students who did not take the test fall into?\",\"options\":[\"Failed in all subjects\",\"Had not appeared for the test\",\"Got good marks\",\"Done well in all subjects\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'Some had not appeared for the test.\'\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the narrator say, \'How do you expect her to be proud of us?\'\",\"options\":[\"Because the teacher is never happy\",\"Because the class was too noisy\",\"Because many failed or missed the test\",\"Because they didn\'t bring their books\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The narrator points out that since many failed or missed the test, they cannot expect the teacher to be proud.\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"When Mrs. Desai says \'Take out your books,\' what is she asking the students to do?\",\"options\":[\"Pack their bags to go home\",\"Go back to their studies\",\"Give the books to Sushmita\",\"Throw the books away\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She says, \'Come on, now, let us go back to our studies. Take out your books.\'\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the teacher\'s statement \'I will always want to be proud of you\' imply about her current feelings?\",\"options\":[\"She is currently very proud of them\",\"She has stopped caring about the class\",\"She is not proud of them right now due to the results\",\"She is angry and wants to punish everyone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The students analyze that she didn\'t say she *is* proud, implying the current results don\'t give her a reason to be proud yet.\",\"topic\":\"The First Unit Test\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what are nouns that stand for groups of things or people called?\",\"options\":[\"Proper nouns\",\"Collective nouns\",\"Abstract nouns\",\"Common nouns\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines nouns that stand for groups of things or people as collective nouns.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Collective Nouns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the correct collective noun for \'players\' mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A herd of players\",\"A flock of players\",\"A team of players\",\"A set of players\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly provides \'a team of players\' as an example of a collective noun.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Collective Nouns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does a collective noun represent?\",\"options\":[\"A single specific person\'s name\",\"A group of things or people\",\"An action or a feeling\",\"A quality of a person\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that collective nouns stand for groups of things or people.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Collective Nouns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which example from the text refers to a group of birds?\",\"options\":[\"A herd of birds\",\"A flock of birds\",\"A set of birds\",\"A class of birds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'a flock of birds\' as one of the examples of collective nouns.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Collective Nouns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If one group is called a \'herd\', what is the plural form of this collective noun according to the grammar rule in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Herdes\",\"Herds\",\"Herdies\",\"Herding\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes that collective nouns have plural forms and gives \'herd - herds\' as an example.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Collective Nouns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the examples in the text, which collective noun would you use for \'cards\'?\",\"options\":[\"A list of cards\",\"A team of cards\",\"A set of cards\",\"A flock of cards\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'a set of cards\' as a specific example of a collective noun.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Collective Nouns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'a class of sixty girls and boys\', which word is the collective noun?\",\"options\":[\"Sixty\",\"Girls\",\"Boys\",\"Class\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text identifies \'class\' as a collective noun standing for a group of girls and boys.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Collective Nouns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following statements about collective nouns is true based on the \'Note\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"They only have singular forms.\",\"They only have plural forms.\",\"They have both singular and plural forms.\",\"They do not have any plural forms.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states: \'Note that collective nouns also have singular and plural forms.\'\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Collective Nouns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What collective noun is used for \'cattle\' in the provided text?\",\"options\":[\"Flock\",\"Herd\",\"Team\",\"Set\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'a herd of cattle\' as an example of a collective noun.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Collective Nouns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the example \'lists of names\', which word represents the plural form of the collective noun?\",\"options\":[\"Names\",\"Lists\",\"Of\",\"List\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'lists of names\' where \'lists\' is the plural form of the collective noun \'list\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Collective Nouns\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is described as the \'maths genius\' in the class?\",\"options\":[\"Akash\",\"Niyati\",\"Sunil\",\"Nilesh\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'Niyati. She is the maths genius in our class.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the abbreviation \'PoA\' stand for in the context of the students\' discussion?\",\"options\":[\"Point of Agreement\",\"Practice of Arithmetic\",\"Plan of Action\",\"Program of Achievement\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the class sat together to discuss the \'Plan of Action\'.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what was the specific role of the \'Searchlights\'?\",\"options\":[\"To help students solve difficult math problems\",\"To visit students at home and ensure they study\",\"To report naughty students to Mrs. Desai\",\"To prepare the report cards for the class\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Soli suggests that Searchlights will \'visit us at home, talk to us every day to see that we study.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the students decide to keep their \'Plan of Action\' a secret from the teachers?\",\"options\":[\"They were afraid of being punished\",\"They wanted to give Mrs. Desai a surprise\",\"They did not want to follow the school rules\",\"They were not sure if the plan would work\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'We wanted to give Mrs. Desai a surprise.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following was a change Mrs. Desai spotted in the class within a week?\",\"options\":[\"Everyone was getting perfect marks\",\"The classroom was much cleaner\",\"No one was ever absent\",\"The students were bringing gifts for her\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mrs. Desai notes, \'No one is ever absent. Everyone pays attention during lessons.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is described as being \'way behind\' in class, what does it mean?\",\"options\":[\"They are physically sitting at the back of the room\",\"They are not making as much progress as other students\",\"They are late to school every day\",\"They are very good at sports but not studies\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'way behind\' as an informal way of saying not making progress as other students.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What did Akash mean when he said the class should not be a \'class of copycats\'?\",\"options\":[\"Students should not dress like each other\",\"Students should not repeat what the teacher says\",\"Students should not just copy answers without understanding\",\"Students should not keep cats as pets\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Akash tells Nilesh that they must study till they understand rather than just getting answers to copy.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How did the students feel when Mrs. Desai said there was no other class like theirs?\",\"options\":[\"They felt confused\",\"They were on cloud nine\",\"They felt crushed\",\"They were worried about the test\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'We felt so happy we were on cloud nine!\' after her praise.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who suggested the idea of having \'Searchlights\'?\",\"options\":[\"Niyati\",\"Akash\",\"Soli\",\"Sunil\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'“I have an idea,” said Soli. “Let some of the students work as our ‘Searchlights’.”\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the role of \'Study Guards\' (SGs)?\",\"options\":[\"To stand at the door and check uniforms\",\"To help classmates out of their difficulties in subjects\",\"To make sure no one talks during the test\",\"To collect the report cards from the teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Nilesh suggests \'Study Guards\' who will \'help us out of our difficulties.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the question asks why the teacher appreciated Naina. According to the text, what was the reason for this appreciation?\",\"options\":[\"Naina had topped the class in Science\",\"Naina had stopped crying and started studying\",\"Naina showed a \'leap\' in progress by improving her marks from 2 to 16\",\"Naina was the only one who followed the PoA\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mrs. Desai points out that Naina went from 2 marks to 16 marks, calling it a \'leap\' in the right direction.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/042_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text and the question in the given figure, which subject did Naina show improvement in?\",\"options\":[\"Maths\",\"English\",\"Science\",\"History\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mrs. Desai specifically mentions Naina\'s marks in Science (from two to sixteen).\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/042_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the students feel \'crushed\' after the second test results were announced?\",\"options\":[\"Because Mrs. Desai was angry with them\",\"Because the PoA was a complete failure\",\"Because some students still got poor marks or failed despite their efforts\",\"Because they didn\'t want to take any more tests\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains they felt crushed because \'there were still some who got poor marks, and some had even failed.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What quality did the students demonstrate by creating SLs and SGs and working together secretly?\",\"options\":[\"Selfishness\",\"Determination and unity\",\"Laziness\",\"Dishonesty\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Mrs. Desai praises them for their \'wonderful ideas\' and \'determination\'.\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'on cloud nine\' mean in the sentence \'We felt so happy we were on cloud nine!\'?\",\"options\":[\"Feeling very sleepy\",\"Feeling extremely happy\",\"Feeling scared of heights\",\"Feeling confused by nine different things\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text provides the meaning: \'When you are ‘on cloud nine’, you feel great happiness.\'\",\"topic\":\"In a Class of Their Own! Part II\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, the word \'live\' in the phrase \'Live English\' rhymes with which word?\",\"options\":[\"give\",\"sieve\",\"five\",\"leave\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that in the phrase \'Live English\', the word \'live\' rhymes with \'five\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In what format should the student write their name on the library membership form?\",\"options\":[\"In cursive writing\",\"In block letters\",\"In small letters\",\"Only the first name\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The form specifies \'Name (in block letters)\' for the applicant.\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where can a student find the Library Rules mentioned in the application form?\",\"options\":[\"On the school notice board\",\"In the English textbook\",\"On the back of the form\",\"At the Librarian\'s desk\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The form contains a note: \'Please read the Library Rules carefully on the back of the form.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary reason given in the text for learning \'Live English\'?\",\"options\":[\"To pass the English examination\",\"To use English for day-to-day purposes like filling forms\",\"To learn how to speak like a teacher\",\"To memorize poems and prose\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states we use English for many purposes in day-to-day life, such as filling in forms and applications.\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does a student agree to by signing the library application form?\",\"options\":[\"To pay the fees every month\",\"To donate books to the library\",\"To follow the Library Rules carefully\",\"To become the Librarian\'s assistant\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text above the signature line says, \'I have read the Library Rules carefully and I will follow them.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the application form should be left blank by the student?\",\"options\":[\"Membership Fees section\",\"Date of birth section\",\"For Office Use only section\",\"Guardian details section\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The section labeled \'For Office Use only\' is meant for the library staff, not the applicant.\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if a student is a \'New Member\' and wants a \'Yearly\' membership, how much fee must they pay?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 50\",\"₹ 35\",\"₹ 70\",\"₹ 100\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The fee table in the figure shows that for New Members, the Yearly fee is ₹ 100.\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/043_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is renewing their membership for a \'Half yearly\' period, which fee should they select?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 50\",\"₹ 35\",\"₹ 100\",\"₹ 70\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the Membership Fees table, Renewals for Half yearly cost ₹ 35.\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which two pieces of information are recorded under the \'For Office Use only\' section?\",\"options\":[\"Student\'s Signature and Date\",\"User ID and Card issued on date\",\"Class and Division\",\"Phone and email\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The box for \'For Office Use only\' contains fields for \'User ID\' and \'Card issued on\'.\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/043_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final activity suggested for the class to perform after discussing in the class?\",\"options\":[\"Fill the form for the teacher\",\"Frame rules for the School Library\",\"Calculate the total fees collected\",\"Write a letter to the Librarian\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes with the activity: \'Frame rules for the School Library after discussing them in the class.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"create\"},{\"q\":\"What is the yearly fee for \'Renewals\' as per the membership table?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 100\",\"₹ 70\",\"₹ 50\",\"₹ 35\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The table lists the Yearly fee for Renewals as ₹ 70.\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do the letters \'DD MM YYYY\' represent in the Date of birth section?\",\"options\":[\"District, Month, Year\",\"Date, Month, Yearly\",\"Day, Month, Year\",\"Division, Marks, Year\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In date formats, DD stands for Day, MM for Month, and YYYY for Year.\",\"topic\":\"Activity : Live English!\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what are concrete nouns?\",\"options\":[\"Things that represent ideas and feelings\",\"Things that you can actually touch or see\",\"Words that always end in -s or -es\",\"Words that only stand for actions\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines concrete nouns as things you can actually touch or see.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is an example of an abstract noun mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Butterflies\",\"Cards\",\"Happiness\",\"Child\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Happiness is listed in the text as an example of an abstract noun representing a feeling.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How are regular plural forms of nouns typically formed?\",\"options\":[\"By changing the middle vowels\",\"By adding -s, -es or -ies at the end\",\"By changing the entire word\",\"By adding -en at the end\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that plural forms of nouns usually have -s, -es or -ies at the end.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of an irregular plural provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Butterflies\",\"Cards\",\"Mice\",\"Teachers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mice is listed as the irregular plural form of mouse.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Abstract nouns can stand for which of the following categories?\",\"options\":[\"Physical objects and animals\",\"People and places you can visit\",\"Ideas, qualities, feelings, and actions\",\"Things you can touch and see\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that abstract nouns stand for ideas, qualities, feelings, actions, etc.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the word \'mathematics\' classified as an abstract noun in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is a physical object\",\"Because it stands for a field of study or idea rather than a touchable object\",\"Because it ends with the letter \'s\'\",\"Because it is a plural form of a concrete noun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Mathematics is listed under abstract nouns because it represents an idea or subject, not a physical object.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What makes the plural form \'children\' different from regular plurals?\",\"options\":[\"It ends in -ies\",\"It does not end in -s, -es, or -ies\",\"It is a concrete noun\",\"It represents a feeling\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Irregular plurals like \'children\' are formed differently than the standard -s, -es, or -ies endings.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the category of abstract nouns, \'movement\' is an example of which type?\",\"options\":[\"A quality\",\"A feeling\",\"An action\",\"A physical object\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'movement\' as an example of an abstract noun standing for an action.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'leaf\' follows the irregular plural rule mentioned in the text, what is its plural form?\",\"options\":[\"Leafs\",\"Leafes\",\"Leaves\",\"Leafies\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'leaf - leaves\' as an example of an irregular plural.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify an abstract noun from the following sentence in the text: \'We wanted to give Mrs Desai a surprise.\'\",\"options\":[\"Mrs Desai\",\"Give\",\"Surprise\",\"We\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Surprise is an abstract noun found in the paragraph provided for analysis.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which group contains only irregular plurals as listed in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Men, feet, leaves\",\"Cards, butterflies, teachers\",\"Home, school, child\",\"Life, time, unity\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Men, feet, and leaves are all listed in the text\'s section on irregular plurals.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text\'s classification, how does \'childhood\' differ from \'child\'?\",\"options\":[\"Childhood is a regular plural, while child is singular\",\"Childhood is an abstract noun, while child is a concrete noun\",\"Childhood is a concrete noun, while child is an abstract noun\",\"Childhood is an irregular plural, while child is a regular plural\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'child\' as a concrete noun and \'childhood\' as an abstract noun.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study - Noun Types\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the full form of \'TOW\' according to the exercise instructions?\",\"options\":[\"Tell Only Words\",\"Tell Other Words\",\"Tell as many Words as possible\",\"Time Of Words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines TOW as \'Tell as many words as possible\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How much time is allotted to complete the TOW activity for a word?\",\"options\":[\"One minute\",\"Two minutes\",\"Five minutes\",\"Ten minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the activity should be done \'within two minutes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT one of the five target words provided for the activity?\",\"options\":[\"earth\",\"turban\",\"pigeons\",\"bright\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Bright is listed as an example for \'light\', not as a main target word like earth, turban, and pigeons.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the example provided, which word is related to \'light\'?\",\"options\":[\"earth\",\"bulb\",\"turban\",\"sleepy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The example list for light includes \'bright, star, day, bulb\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which target word in the list refers to a living creature?\",\"options\":[\"earth\",\"turban\",\"pigeons\",\"sleepy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Pigeons are birds, which are living creatures.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the example \'light – bright, star, day, bulb\', how many related words are listed?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The words listed are 1. bright, 2. star, 3. day, and 4. bulb.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If you were performing the TOW activity for \'earth\', which word would be the most relevant to list?\",\"options\":[\"soil\",\"bulb\",\"turban\",\"sleepy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Soil is directly related to the physical composition of the earth.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the list describes a physical item of clothing or headwear?\",\"options\":[\"light\",\"earth\",\"turban\",\"sleepy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A turban is a type of headwear mentioned in the target word list.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following words is a target word that describes a state of being?\",\"options\":[\"pigeons\",\"sleepy\",\"earth\",\"turban\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sleepy describes a state of being or a feeling.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the example for \'light\', which category of words is being requested?\",\"options\":[\"Opposites\",\"Rhyming words\",\"Associated or related words\",\"Words starting with the same letter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The example shows words like \'star\' and \'bulb\' which are associated with \'light\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21898,41,7,'English','en','2.1 We shall overcome','[\"- ‘We Shall Overcome’ is a protest song used in the Civil Rights movement in the USA.\",\"- The song expresses unity, determination to fight injustice, and hope for a better future.\",\"- It encourages people to stand together and not give up.\",\"- The phrase ‘We shall’ shows firm resolve to do something.\",\"- The song is often sung with emphasis using ‘do’ (e.g., ‘I do believe’).\",\"- The lyrics repeat the line ‘We shall overcome’ to reinforce hope.\",\"- The song has many versions and has inspired other movements worldwide.\",\"- In Hindi, a popular inspirational song is based on ‘We shall overcome’.\",\"- The Civil Rights movement aimed to end racial segregation and discrimination.\",\"- Songs like ‘We Shall Overcome’ helped people feel united and motivated to fight for equality.\",\"- The song’s simple, repetitive structure makes it easy to remember and sing in groups.\",\"- Singing together can strengthen community bonds and create a sense of solidarity.\",\"- The phrase ‘We shall overcome’ can be used in everyday language to show determination.\",\"- The song’s message is still relevant for any struggle against injustice.\",\"- Understanding the song helps students appreciate the power of music in social change.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does the speaker believe \'deep in my heart\'?\",\"options\":[\"We shall lose\",\"We shall overcome some day\",\"We are afraid today\",\"We will walk alone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Oh! Deep in my heart I do believe, we shall overcome some day.\'\",\"topic\":\"We are not afraid\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, when are the people \'not afraid\'?\",\"options\":[\"Some day\",\"Yesterday\",\"Today\",\"Tomorrow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem explicitly says, \'We are not afraid today.\'\",\"topic\":\"We are not afraid\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How do the people plan to walk \'some day\'?\",\"options\":[\"Separately\",\"Hand in hand\",\"In a hurry\",\"Quietly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'We’ll walk hand in hand some day.\'\",\"topic\":\"We are not afraid\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'Deep in my heart\' signify in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"A physical feeling in the chest\",\"A strong, sincere inner belief\",\"A secret that no one knows\",\"A feeling of sadness\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, it expresses the depth and sincerity of the speaker\'s conviction.\",\"topic\":\"We are not afraid\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is facing a difficult exam and says \'We shall overcome\', which sentiment from the text are they applying?\",\"options\":[\"Fear of the future\",\"Hope and determination to succeed\",\"Walking away from the problem\",\"Believing in today only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'We shall overcome\' is an expression of hope and the will to succeed eventually.\",\"topic\":\"We are not afraid\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The repetition of the line \'We shall overcome\' throughout the text serves to:\",\"options\":[\"Show that the speaker is confused\",\"Emphasize the speaker\'s firm determination\",\"Make the poem longer\",\"Show that they have already succeeded\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Repetition in this poem emphasizes the strength of the belief and determination.\",\"topic\":\"We are not afraid\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the text indicates that the victory or \'overcoming\' might not happen immediately?\",\"options\":[\"Today\",\"Heart\",\"Some day\",\"Afraid\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'some day\' suggests a future time, not necessarily the present moment.\",\"topic\":\"We are not afraid\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message of the stanza starting with \'We are not afraid\'?\",\"options\":[\"Current courage and fearlessness\",\"Future worries\",\"Walking together\",\"Believing in others\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The stanza focuses on the state of not being afraid \'today\'.\",\"topic\":\"We are not afraid\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which action mentioned in the text best represents the idea of unity and togetherness?\",\"options\":[\"Believing deep in the heart\",\"Walking hand in hand\",\"Not being afraid\",\"Overcoming some day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Walking \'hand in hand\' is a physical representation of unity and cooperation.\",\"topic\":\"We are not afraid\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the difference between the timing of \'overcoming\' and \'not being afraid\'?\",\"options\":[\"Overcoming is for today, fearlessness is for some day\",\"Both are happening right now\",\"Overcoming is for some day, while fearlessness is for today\",\"Both will only happen in the future\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'we shall overcome some day\' (future) but \'we are not afraid today\' (present).\",\"topic\":\"We are not afraid\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In which country was the song \'We shall overcome\' used during the Civil Rights movement?\",\"options\":[\"United Kingdom\",\"India\",\"USA\",\"South Africa\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states the song was used as a protest song in the Civil Rights movement in the USA.\",\"topic\":\"About the song\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which Hindi inspirational song is based on \'We shall overcome\'?\",\"options\":[\"होंगे कामयाब\",\"सारे जहाँ से अच्छा\",\"वन्दे मातरम्\",\"जन गण मन\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the well-known Hindi inspirational song ‘होंगे कामयाब’ was based on ‘We shall overcome’.\",\"topic\":\"About the song\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the song, what will eventually make us free?\",\"options\":[\"Peace\",\"The truth\",\"Unity\",\"Determination\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The lyrics state, \'The truth shall make us free... someday\'.\",\"topic\":\"About the song\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What three qualities does the song \'We shall overcome\' express?\",\"options\":[\"Anger, revenge, and victory\",\"Unity, determination to fight injustice, and hope\",\"Fear, sadness, and loneliness\",\"Silence, patience, and truth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the song expresses unity, determination to fight injustice, and hope.\",\"topic\":\"About the song\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a group of people in India sings \'होंगे कामयाब\' during a rally, which original song are they indirectly referencing?\",\"options\":[\"We shall live in peace\",\"We shall overcome\",\"The truth shall make us free\",\"Deep in my heart\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since \'होंगे कामयाब\' is based on \'We shall overcome\', singing it references the original song.\",\"topic\":\"About the song\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The text mentions the song has \'many versions\'. What does this suggest about the song?\",\"options\":[\"The original lyrics were lost\",\"The song is difficult to remember\",\"The song has been adapted by different cultures and languages\",\"The song is only meant for one movement\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Having many versions, like the Hindi one, indicates it has been adapted across different contexts.\",\"topic\":\"About the song\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the primary purpose of the song \'We shall overcome\' in the USA?\",\"options\":[\"A lullaby for children\",\"A celebration song for festivals\",\"A protest song in the Civil Rights movement\",\"A national anthem\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies it as a protest song used in the Civil Rights movement.\",\"topic\":\"About the song\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the singer\'s attitude toward the future in the line \'We shall live in peace some day\'?\",\"options\":[\"Doubtful\",\"Indifferent\",\"Hopeful\",\"Fearful\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song expresses \'hope\' for a future where people live in peace.\",\"topic\":\"About the song\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The phrase \'Deep in my heart I do believe\' implies that the singer\'s conviction is:\",\"options\":[\"A temporary feeling\",\"A superficial thought\",\"A profound and sincere belief\",\"A forced opinion\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The use of \'deep in my heart\' signifies a strong, sincere internal belief.\",\"topic\":\"About the song\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"A student wants to show how music can connect different countries. Which fact from the text best supports this?\",\"options\":[\"The song mentions \'the truth\'\",\"An American protest song inspired a popular Hindi song\",\"The song has many verses\",\"The song mentions living in peace\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The connection between the USA\'s \'We shall overcome\' and India\'s \'होंगे कामयाब\' shows musical connection between countries.\",\"topic\":\"About the song\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21899,41,7,'English','en','2.2 Two Fables','[\"A fable is a very short story, usually with animal characters or inanimate things that speak, ending with a moral or message.\",\"The two fables in this chapter are Aesop’s “Town Mouse and Country Mouse” and the story of two friends and a bear.\",\"Key vocabulary: fable, moral, rustic, turn up his long nose, put up with, set off, refreshment, mastiff, only, better…than…\",\"The moral of “Town Mouse and Country Mouse” is that simple, peaceful life is better than fancy, frightening life.\",\"In the bear story, the moral is: Never trust a friend who deserts you at a pinch.\",\"Verbs have different tenses: past (‑ed, ‑d, ‑ied), present (‑s, ‑es, ‑ies for third person), future (will\\/shall).\",\"Use “will” for future actions, e.g., “I will write novels.”\",\"The phrase “better … than …” compares two situations, e.g., “Better beans and bread in peace than cakes and jellies in fear.”\",\"In “Town Mouse and Country Mouse”, the country mouse says “only!” meaning “just!” or “simply!”\",\"The story has two parts: part one – the mice visit the town; part two – they return to the country and are chased by dogs.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is a fable?\",\"options\":[\"A long novel about history\",\"A very short story with a moral\",\"A news report about animals\",\"A poem without any characters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a fable as a very short story that usually ends with a message or a moral.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Aesop, the famous story-teller mentioned in the text, belonged to which country?\",\"options\":[\"England\",\"India\",\"Greece\",\"France\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that these two fables come from Aesop, the famous Greek story-teller.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a unique feature of inanimate things in a fable?\",\"options\":[\"They remain silent\",\"They are always the villains\",\"They can speak\",\"They are never used as characters\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that fables have animal characters or even inanimate things that speak.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the primary purpose of a fable mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"To teach about the ways of the world and behavior in society\",\"To provide scientific facts about animals\",\"To list the names of famous Greek kings\",\"To teach students how to draw characters\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text in the figure states that a fable tells you about the ways of the world and how one should behave in society.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/047_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the instructions in the given figure, what should students do if their favorite stories are not in English?\",\"options\":[\"They should not list those stories\",\"They should translate the titles into English\",\"They should write the stories in their original script\",\"They should only tell the stories orally\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure instructs to encourage students to translate their titles in English if the stories are in other languages.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/047_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Why were Aesop\'s stories retold in many different ways across various countries?\",\"options\":[\"Because the original stories were lost\",\"To make them longer and more complex\",\"To suit the local conditions of each country\",\"Because the characters were not liked by people\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says his stories were retold in many countries according to their own local conditions.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific style used for the retelling of the town mouse and country mouse story in this chapter?\",\"options\":[\"Greek style\",\"English style\",\"Ancient style\",\"Scientific style\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the story of the town mouse and country mouse is retold in the English style.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to categorize a story about a detective solving a mystery, which type from the provided list should they use?\",\"options\":[\"Mythology\",\"Fairy tale\",\"Detective story\",\"Satire\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Detective story is one of the specific story types listed in the textbook for describing stories.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A story that is meant to make people laugh would best be described by which term from the text?\",\"options\":[\"Tragedy\",\"Horror story\",\"Comedy\",\"Science fiction\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Comedy is the term used in the list for stories intended to be humorous.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you are asked to do the \'Two minutes of Oral Work\' for the word \'forest\', which set of words is most relevant?\",\"options\":[\"Buildings, traffic, elevators\",\"Trees, wildlife, bushes\",\"Tractors, farms, wells\",\"Classroom, blackboard, chalk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The oral work requires telling words related to the forest; trees, wildlife, and bushes are directly related.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What can we infer about the \'local conditions\' mentioned in the text regarding Aesop\'s stories?\",\"options\":[\"Stories remain exactly the same everywhere\",\"Cultural settings influence how a story is presented\",\"Only Greek people can understand the stories\",\"The moral of the story changes every time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Retelling stories according to local conditions implies that the cultural or geographical setting changes to make it relatable.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following best justifies why \'Parable\' and \'Fable\' are listed as separate story types?\",\"options\":[\"They are exactly the same thing\",\"They have different lengths and character types\",\"One is only for adults and the other for children\",\"One is always written in Greek and the other in English\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists them separately to show they are distinct types of stories with their own special features.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Where were the two friends travelling when they encountered the bear?\",\"options\":[\"Through a desert\",\"Through a wood\",\"Along a river\",\"Over a mountain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the friends were travelling together through a wood.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the bear do as soon as it saw the travellers?\",\"options\":[\"It ran away in fear\",\"It climbed a nearby tree\",\"It rushed out upon them\",\"It hid behind the leaves\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the bear saw the travellers and rushed out upon them.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the first traveller climb the tree so quickly?\",\"options\":[\"He wanted to get a better view\",\"He was good at climbing trees\",\"He wanted to pull his friend up\",\"He was looking for fruit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says one traveller was good at climbing trees and did so without waiting for his friend.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What belief led the second traveller to lie flat on the ground?\",\"options\":[\"Bears are afraid of humans\",\"Bears only attack people who run\",\"Bears do not bother with dead animals\",\"Bears cannot see things on the ground\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The traveller had heard that bears do not bother with dead animals, so he threw himself down.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, where is the first traveller positioned while the bear is on the ground?\",\"options\":[\"He is hiding behind the bear\",\"He is lying next to his friend\",\"He is sitting on a branch of a tree\",\"He is running away into the distance\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows one man safely up in the tree while the bear sniffs the other on the ground.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/048_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What did the bear do when it put its muzzle close to the man\'s ear?\",\"options\":[\"It bit the man\'s ear\",\"It whispered a secret\",\"It sniffed and sniffed\",\"It started to eat him\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the bear put its muzzle close to his ear and sniffed and sniffed.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the man on the ground doing to protect himself?\",\"options\":[\"He is fighting the bear with his hands\",\"He is lying perfectly still with his face down\",\"He is trying to crawl away slowly\",\"He is calling out for help from his friend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the man lying flat on his stomach with his face down, imitating a dead body.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/048_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'slouched\' suggest about how the bear left?\",\"options\":[\"It ran away very fast\",\"It walked away in a lazy or heavy manner\",\"It jumped into the trees\",\"It attacked the other friend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Slouched off indicates a heavy, slow, or drooping way of walking away.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What name did the friend in the tree use to refer to the bear?\",\"options\":[\"Master Bruin\",\"Sir Grizzly\",\"Mr. Wood\",\"Comrade Bear\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The friend in the tree jokingly asks what \'Master Bruin\' whispered.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the story, what does the phrase \'at a pinch\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"In a small space\",\"In a time of trouble or emergency\",\"When someone hurts you\",\"During a fun game\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'at a pinch\' refers to a difficult situation where help is needed.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the friend in the tree laughing when he came down?\",\"options\":[\"He thought the bear was funny\",\"He was happy he found some fruit\",\"He was making fun of his friend\'s scary situation\",\"He was glad the bear died\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"He asked mockingly what the bear whispered, showing he was not taking his friend\'s danger seriously.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the moral lesson the second traveller teaches his friend?\",\"options\":[\"Always learn how to climb trees\",\"Bears are very friendly animals\",\"Never trust a friend who leaves you when you are in trouble\",\"It is better to travel alone in the woods\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The man says, \'Never trust a friend who deserts you at a pinch,\' which is the moral of the fable.\",\"topic\":\"THE TWO FRIENDS AND THE BEAR\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'slouched\' as used in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Ran away quickly in fear\",\"Walked away with shoulders bent forward\",\"Jumped over a large obstacle\",\"Stood still and hid behind a tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'slouched\' as walking away with its shoulders bent forward.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Bear)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is a synonym for \'comrade\'?\",\"options\":[\"Enemy\",\"Stranger\",\"Companion\",\"Master\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'comrade\' as a friend or companion.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Bear)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who is referred to as \'Master Bruin\' in the story?\",\"options\":[\"The Traveller\",\"Mr Bear\",\"The Friend\",\"The Master\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Master Bruin\' refers to Mr Bear.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Bear)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'at a pinch\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"In an emergency\",\"To hurt someone\",\"Very quickly\",\"In a small space\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'at a pinch\' as \'in an emergency\'.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Bear)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does it mean to \'desert\' someone according to the vocabulary list?\",\"options\":[\"To give them a sweet treat\",\"To leave them behind\",\"To travel to a dry land\",\"To walk with bent shoulders\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'desert\' as \'leave behind\'.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Bear)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the grammar note in the text, how should we write \'its\' in the phrase \'its head\'?\",\"options\":[\"it\'s\",\"its\'\",\"its\",\"i\'ts\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that we do not use the apostrophe in \'its\' in phrases like \'its head\'.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Bear)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence uses the phrase \'at a pinch\' correctly based on its meaning in the text?\",\"options\":[\"He gave me a small at a pinch on my arm.\",\"I can use my umbrella as a walking stick at a pinch.\",\"The bear was at a pinch in the forest.\",\"They slouched at a pinch towards the house.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since \'at a pinch\' means \'in an emergency\' or necessity, using an umbrella as a stick in such a situation is the correct application.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Bear)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following sentences follows the grammar rule mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The dog wagged it\'s tail happily.\",\"The bird cleaned its\' feathers.\",\"The bear moved its heavy body slowly.\",\"The tree lost it\'s leaves in autumn.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that \'its\' should not have an apostrophe when used to show possession (like \'its head\').\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Bear)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the discussion questions, where did the traveler lie when the bear approached?\",\"options\":[\"Up in the branches of a tree\",\"Behind a large rock\",\"With his face in the dust\",\"Inside a dark cave\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The discussion prompt asks \'Why did the other traveller lie with his face in the dust?\', indicating that is where he was.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Bear)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a person \'deserts\' a \'comrade\' \'at a pinch\', what are they doing?\",\"options\":[\"Helping a friend during a difficult time\",\"Walking away from a friend with bent shoulders\",\"Leaving a friend behind during an emergency\",\"Whispering a secret to a companion\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Combining the definitions: \'desert\' (leave behind), \'comrade\' (friend), and \'at a pinch\' (emergency).\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Bear)\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What simple fare did the Country Mouse offer to his town friend?\",\"options\":[\"Jellies and cakes\",\"Beans, cheese and bread\",\"Fine feast remains\",\"Meat and wine\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the Country Mouse had beans, cheese, and bread to offer.\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the Town Mouse live in the big house?\",\"options\":[\"In a grand dining room\",\"In a kitchen cupboard\",\"In a hole\",\"In the garden\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the Town Mouse lived in a hole in the big house.\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the mice find in the grand dining room when they arrived?\",\"options\":[\"Two huge mastiffs\",\"A fresh hot meal\",\"The remains of a fine feast\",\"Only beans and bread\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they found the remains of a fine feast in the grand dining room.\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What sounds did the mice hear suddenly while eating jellies and cakes?\",\"options\":[\"Music and singing\",\"Growling and barking\",\"Whistling and shouting\",\"Purring and meowing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they suddenly heard growling and barking.\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who entered the room when the door flew open?\",\"options\":[\"The Country Mouse\'s cousin\",\"A group of servants\",\"Two huge mastiffs\",\"A cat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that two huge mastiffs came in when the door flew open.\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'turned up his long nose\' imply about the Town Mouse?\",\"options\":[\"He had a physical deformity\",\"He was smelling the food carefully\",\"He looked down upon the simple food\",\"He was sneezing because of the country air\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase indicates that the Town Mouse felt the country food was inferior or not good enough for him.\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the Town Mouse invite the Country Mouse to the town?\",\"options\":[\"Because he was lonely in the big house\",\"To show him how to live and see town life\",\"To help him escape from the dogs\",\"To ask for more beans and bread\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Town Mouse said, \'Come with me and I will show you how to live. When you see town life, you will wonder how you could ever live in the country.\'\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When the Country Mouse says, \'I do not like that music at my dinner\', what is he referring to?\",\"options\":[\"The sound of the mastiffs barking\",\"The noise of the mice eating\",\"Actual music playing in the dining room\",\"The sound of the door opening\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He uses \'music\' sarcastically to refer to the frightening sound of the dogs barking.\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text describes the Country Mouse as a person belonging to the countryside?\",\"options\":[\"Polite\",\"Rustic\",\"Grand\",\"Huge\"],\"answer\":1,