e\'s behavior\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"His final words, \'Better beans and bread in peace than cakes and jellies in fear\', explain his decision.\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"How does the setting of the town house contrast with the country home in this story?\",\"options\":[\"The town is quieter than the country\",\"The town offers luxury but comes with danger\",\"The country has better food but no friends\",\"The town house is safer than the country hole\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The town has \'fine feasts\' but also \'huge mastiffs\' that cause the mice to run in fear.\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following best summarizes the moral of the fable?\",\"options\":[\"Town life is always better than country life\",\"It is better to be poor and safe than rich and in danger\",\"Always visit your cousins during the holidays\",\"Dogs are the enemies of all mice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The story concludes that peace and security are more valuable than fine food accompanied by fear.\",\"topic\":\"THE TOWN MOUSE AND THE COUNTRY MOUSE\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the meaning of the word \'rustic\'?\",\"options\":[\"Living in a city\",\"Living in a village\",\"Living in a palace\",\"Living in a forest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'rustic\' as rural or living in a village.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Mouse)\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'fare\' refer to in the context of the vocabulary list?\",\"options\":[\"The cost of a bus ticket\",\"A type of clothing\",\"Food\",\"A long journey\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'fare\' as food.\",\"topic\":\"Vocabulary and Discussion (Mouse)\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are \'mastiffs\' as described in the text?\",\"opti