 expensive telescope\",\"A degree from the Royal Society\",\"A laboratory in the middle of the ocean\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says it needed a questioning mind with a scientific outlook to find the reason.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Philosophy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student has no money for a lab but works hard and thinks independently, how would Raman view their potential?\",\"options\":[\"They cannot succeed without equipment\",\"They possess the true essence of science\",\"They should wait until they have 200 rupees\",\"They should give up on science\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Raman believed the essence of science is independent thinking and hard work, not equipment.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Philosophy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement best summarizes Raman\'s view on laboratories?\",\"options\":[\"Laboratories are the only place for science\",\"Scientists should not be confined to laboratories\",\"Laboratories must have equipment worth 2000 rupees\",\"Nature is not as important as a laboratory\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Raman strongly felt that scientists should not be confined to laboratories to solve problems.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Philosophy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'measly\' in the phrase \'measly two hundred rupees\' suggest about the cost?\",\"options\":[\"It was a very large amount\",\"It was a very small, insignificant amount\",\"It was a fair price\",\"It was too expensive for a scientist\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'measly\' emphasizes how small the amount was compared to the importance of the discovery.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Philosophy\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In which year did C.V. Raman win the Nobel Prize for Physics?\",\"options\":[\"1928\",\"1930\",\"1935\",\"1947\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Raman won the Nobel prize for physics in 1930.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which date is celebrated as National Science Day according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"28 January\",\"28 February\",\"15 August\",\"26 January\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks why 28 February was declared as National Science Day.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the \'Think and Answer\' section, what is a characteristic of great scientific minds?\",\"options\":[\"They are always calm\",\"They are restless\",\"They are forgetful\",\"They are satisfied\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks \'Why are great scientific minds restless?\' indicating this is a key trait.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the scientific discovery associated with C.V. Raman mentioned in the activities?\",\"options\":[\"The Einstein Effect\",\"The Physics Effect\",\"The Raman Effect\",\"The Questioning Effect\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The \'Things to do\' section specifically mentions finding out more about the \'Raman Effect.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which field of science did Raman receive his Nobel Prize?\",\"options\":[\"Chemistry\",\"Biology\",\"Physics\",\"Astronomy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions the \'Nobel prize for physics.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you want to follow the \'Things to do\' advice, what should you do with questions that come to your mind?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore them\",\"Note them down and discuss them\",\"Keep them to yourself\",\"Wait for a teacher to ask\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests to \'Note them down and discuss them with others.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Apart from C.V. Raman, which other scientist are students encouraged to find information about?\",\"options\":[\"Newton\",\"Einstein\",\"Galileo\",\"Pasteur\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Find more information about Einstein.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the \'Listen and answer\' section, what determines if someone is a \'good scientist\'?\",\"options\":[\"Their age\",\"Their wealth\",\"Their qualities\",\"Their nationality\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text asks about the \'qualities of a good scientist.\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary purpose of the \'Think and Answer\' section regarding scientific theories?\",\"options\":[\"To memorize theories\",\"To find out how to prove a theory scientifically\",\"To ignore old theories\",\"To write new theories without proof\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks to \'Find out : What does one have to do to prove a theory scientifically?\'\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text link C.V. Raman\'s Nobel Prize to National Science Day questions?\",\"options\":[\"To show he was a politician\",\"To highlight his contribution to science and its national recognition\",\"To explain why he liked arts\",\"To show that he was restless\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The grouping of the Nobel Prize and National Science Day questions evaluates the significance of his scientific achievement.\",\"topic\":\"Activities\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is a group of words that expresses a complete idea called?\",\"options\":[\"A phrase\",\"A sentence\",\"A predicate\",\"A subject\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a sentence is a group of words that expresses a complete idea.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Into how many components is a sentence divided?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Three\",\"Two\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that a sentence has two components – subject and predicate.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of a sentence names the person or thing that we speak about?\",\"options\":[\"The predicate\",\"The verb\",\"The subject\",\"The object\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the subject as the part which names the person, thing, etc. that we speak about.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the function of the predicate in a sentence?\",\"options\":[\"To name the person we speak about\",\"To express a complete idea\",\"To tell us more about the subject\",\"To act as a group of words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the predicate is the part that tells us more about the subject.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'The sky is blue\', which part is the subject?\",\"options\":[\"is blue\",\"The sky\",\"sky is\",\"blue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the provided table, \'The sky\' is listed under the Subject column.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'Great scientific minds are restless with question\', identify the predicate.\",\"options\":[\"Great scientific minds\",\"are restless\",\"are restless with question\",\"scientific minds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the table, \'are restless with question\' is the predicate for the subject \'Great scientific minds\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what determines the form of the verb in a sentence?\",\"options\":[\"The length of the sentence\",\"The predicate\",\"The subject\",\"The complete idea\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that the verb form in each sentence depends on the subject.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the sentence \'She goes to school every day\' use \'goes\' instead of \'go\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because the subject is \'She\'\",\"Because it happens every day\",\"Because \'goes\' is part of the predicate\",\"Because the sentence is a complete idea\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states the verb form depends on the subject; \'She\' requires the form \'goes\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the subject in the sentence: \'They go home in the evening.\'\",\"options\":[\"go home\",\"in the evening\",\"They\",\"home\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the table, \'They\' is categorized as the subject.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'The remaining part of the sentence tells us more about the subject\', which of these is that part in \'They go home in the evening\'?\",\"options\":[\"They\",\"go home in the evening\",\"evening\",\"They go\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The predicate is the remaining part after the subject, which is \'go home in the evening\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21904,41,7,'English','en','3.1 Sleep, Baby, Sleep !','[\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep! is a lullaby that helps a child fall asleep.\",\"A lullaby is a short, soothing song that lulls a child to sleep.\",\"The poem uses gentle threats, pleasant images, and promises to calm the child.\",\"Key words: sleep, trees, bright, be, dog, go, herds, thee, heavens, bleat, rogue.\",\"The poem’s stanzas show loving threats, pleasant pictures, safety, night description, and a promised gift.\",\"Lullabies often rhyme and use simple, repetitive language.\",\"The poem mentions a shepherd, sheep, stars, moon, and a golden bell as comforting symbols.\",\"Teachers can ask students to sing the song, find rhyming words, and identify ideas in each stanza.\",\"Students can also list and label their favourite songs or poems using categories like lullaby, folk song, etc.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the father\'s activity while the baby sleeps?\",\"options\":[\"Shaking a little tree\",\"Herding his sheep\",\"Watching the stars\",\"Chasing a black dog\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Your father herds his sheep\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, what falls from the little tree when the mother shakes it?\",\"options\":[\"Leaves\",\"Apples\",\"Pretty dreams\",\"Golden bells\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'Your mother shakes the little tree From which fall pretty dreams on thee\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What color is the dog mentioned in the final stanza?\",\"options\":[\"White\",\"Golden\",\"Brown\",\"Black\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem refers to the dog as \'you barking black dog\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the second stanza, what are the \'lambs\' that make the heavens white?\",\"options\":[\"Clouds\",\"Stars\",\"The moon\",\"Dreams\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem clarifies, \'For they are lambs - those stars so bright\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Who is referred to as the \'shepherd of the night\'?\",\"options\":[\"The father\",\"The baby\",\"The moon\",\"The dog\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'And the moon\'s shepherd of the night\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What gift does the speaker promise to give the baby?\",\"options\":[\"A little tree\",\"A golden bell\",\"A sheep\",\"A bright star\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The speaker says, \'And I\'ll give thee a sheep\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What will be attached to the sheep that the baby receives as a play-fellow?\",\"options\":[\"A silver ribbon\",\"A golden bell\",\"A black leash\",\"A white star\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sheep will have a \'golden bell\' to be a play-fellow for the baby.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the baby warned not to \'bleat like a sheep\'?\",\"options\":[\"So the father won\'t get confused\",\"To prevent the shepherd\'s dog from biting\",\"To keep the stars bright\",\"To help the mother shake the tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem warns, \'Or else the shepherd\'s angry dog Will come and bite my naughty rogue\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the line \'The heavens are white with sheep\', what does the word \'heavens\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"A grassy field\",\"The sky\",\"A dream world\",\"The baby\'s room\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, \'heavens\' refers to the night sky where the stars (lambs) are located.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What term does the speaker use to describe the baby when warning about the dog?\",\"options\":[\"Little lamb\",\"Pretty dream\",\"Naughty rogue\",\"Barking dog\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The speaker uses the phrase \'my naughty rogue\' when mentioning the dog might bite.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary purpose of the speaker in this poem?\",\"options\":[\"To teach the baby how to herd sheep\",\"To describe the beauty of the stars\",\"To soothe the baby into falling asleep\",\"To warn the baby about dangerous dogs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The repeated refrain \'Sleep, baby, sleep!\' indicates the poem is a lullaby intended to induce sleep.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the second stanza rhymes with \'night\'?\",\"options\":[\"Sheep\",\"Bright\",\"Bell\",\"Rogue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the second stanza, \'bright\' and \'night\' are the rhyming words.\",\"topic\":\"Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What type of song is \'Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\'?\",\"options\":[\"A fast dance song\",\"A traditional lullaby\",\"A loud marching song\",\"A modern pop song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Sleep, Baby, Sleep!\' is a traditional lullaby.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the purpose of a lullaby?\",\"options\":[\"To teach children how to sing\",\"To wake up a child in the morning\",\"To lull a child to sleep\",\"To help a child learn new words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A lullaby is defined as a song used to \'lull\' a child to sleep.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'thee\' as used in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Them\",\"They\",\"You\",\"Me\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The vocabulary list explicitly defines \'thee\' as \'you\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of this lullaby, what does the word \'heavens\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"The clouds\",\"The sky\",\"The stars\",\"The moon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'heavens\' as the \'sky\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person \'herds\', what are they doing?\",\"options\":[\"Feeding the birds\",\"Looking after the sheep\",\"Shearing the wool\",\"Counting the cows\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'herds\' as \'looks after the sheep\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes the whining sound made by a sheep?\",\"options\":[\"Bark\",\"Roar\",\"Bleat\",\"Moo\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'bleat\' as making a whining sound.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a child refuses to do what they are asked, which word from the text describes them?\",\"options\":[\"Rogue\",\"Herds\",\"Bleat\",\"Lull\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'rogue\' as a child who does not do what is asked.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which two adjectives are used in the text to describe a lullaby?\",\"options\":[\"Slow and boring\",\"Quick and soothing\",\"Loud and energetic\",\"Quiet and sad\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes a lullaby as a \'quick, soothing song\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a mother is singing a song to make her baby fall asleep, she is trying to ______ the child.\",\"options\":[\"Bleat\",\"Rogue\",\"Lull\",\"Heavens\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that a lullaby is used to \'lull\' a child to sleep.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the best definition of a \'bleat\' based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"A loud shout\",\"A happy song\",\"A whining sound\",\"A deep growl\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'bleat\' specifically as making a whining sound.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21905,41,7,'English','en','3.2 The Welcome','[\"The Welcome is a one‑act play by Rabindranath Tagore.\",\"Chaturbhuj Babu has just passed his MA exams and returns to his village.\",\"He brings a plump Afghan cat with him.\",\"The villagers, Nilratan, Zamindar, Uncle Satu, Mother, Aunt, Sadhucharan and Paran react mainly to the cat, not to Chaturbhuj’s achievement.\",\"Chaturbhuj is annoyed because people ignore his academic success.\",\"The play shows how people focus on trivial things and ignore real accomplishments.\",\"Key vocabulary: plump (fat), confound (to surprise or anger), stunner (very beautiful), delighted (very happy).\",\"The play uses simple dialogues and humor to convey its message.\",\"The ending shows the cat dead and the villagers teasing Chaturbhuj, highlighting his frustration.\",\"The play encourages listening and understanding others’ perspectives.\",\"The play is adapted from Tagore’s original Bengali work.\",\"The play is used to teach listening skills, empathy and response types.\",\"The play also includes activities like guessing games, role play and listening exercises.\",\"The play is suitable for Standard 7 English learners.\",\"It helps students practice speaking, listening and comprehension.\",\"It also introduces some basic grammar concepts like progressive and perfect tenses.\",\"Students can learn to identify main ideas and supporting details.\",\"They can also practice summarizing dialogues.\",\"They can learn to ask and answer questions about a text.\",\"They can practice using descriptive language.\",\"They can learn to differentiate between enthusiastic, sarcastic, attentive, neutral, indifferent responses.\",\"They can learn to identify character relationships.\",\"They can learn to identify the setting and plot points.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the author of the play \'The Welcome\'?\",\"options\":[\"Rabindranath Tagore\",\"Mahatma Gandhi\",\"R. K. Narayan\",\"Premchand\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that Gurudev Rabindranath Tagore is the writer of \'The Welcome\'.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What type of literary work is \'The Welcome\'?\",\"options\":[\"A long novel\",\"A funny one-act play\",\"A collection of songs\",\"A scientific essay\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes \'The Welcome\' as a funny one-act play.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the play \'The Welcome\', what big achievement does the young man want to share with his village?\",\"options\":[\"He bought a new cat.\",\"He won a cricket match.\",\"He has passed his M.A.\",\"He found a lost wallet.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the young man wants to tell the people he has passed M.A.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What do the villagers talk to the young man about, instead of his academic success?\",\"options\":[\"His uncle\",\"His cat\",\"His wallet\",\"His exams\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'everybody talks to him about his cat!\' instead of his M.A. results.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student says \'So what?\' in response to news, what type of response is it according to Activity A?\",\"options\":[\"Enthusiastic\",\"Attentive\",\"Indifferent\",\"Neutral\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In Activity A, \'So what?\' is listed as an Indifferent response.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an enthusiastic response to the news \'Our team has won the match!\'?\",\"options\":[\"I see. Congrats!\",\"Wow! Great news! We are so proud of you!\",\"Your uncle was the umpire, right?\",\"So what?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Wow! Great news! We are so proud of you!\' as the Enthusiastic response for Activity A.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what three aspects should students use to rate the responses in the activity table?\",\"options\":[\"Words, Gestures, and Tone\",\"Speed, Volume, and Pitch\",\"Height, Weight, and Age\",\"Writing, Reading, and Speaking\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table in the text lists \'Words\', \'Gestures\', and \'Tone\' as the criteria for rating.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the situation in \'The Welcome\' considered funny?\",\"options\":[\"Because the young man forgot he had a cat.\",\"Because the villagers are trying to help him study.\",\"Because a significant achievement is ignored in favor of trivial talk about a cat.\",\"Because the young man failed his M.A. exam.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The humor arises from the contrast between the man\'s desire to share his M.A. success and the villagers\' obsession with his cat.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which response is categorized as \'Indifferent\' to the statement about Raju losing his wallet?\",\"options\":[\"Oh, really! How sad!\",\"Such things happen.\",\"Oh, I see.\",\"Can we help?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the diagram, the orange circle labeled \'Indifferent\' contains the text \'Such things happen.\'\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/072_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many specific types of responses are listed in the top row for students to rate?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"4\",\"5\",\"6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table header lists five types: Enthusiastic, Attentive, Neutral, Indifferent, and Sarcastic.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/072_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What does the sarcastic response \'I know! Your uncle was the umpire, right?\' imply about the team\'s win?\",\"options\":[\"The win was fair and square.\",\"The win was only possible because of unfair help or favoritism.\",\"The speaker is happy for the uncle.\",\"The speaker wants to become an umpire.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sarcasm here suggests the win wasn\'t genuine but due to the uncle being the umpire.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Besides being a writer, which other roles is Rabindranath Tagore known for in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Scientist and Doctor\",\"Musician and Thinker\",\"Umpire and Athlete\",\"Actor and Director\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first sentence of the text states he was a \'great writer, musician and thinker\'.\",\"topic\":\"Warming up!\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where does Scene I of the play take place?\",\"options\":[\"A village road\",\"A house in Calcutta\",\"The Zamindar\'s palace\",\"A school classroom\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The opening stage direction explicitly states the setting is \'A village road\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which examination has Chaturbhuj Babu passed before returning to the village?\",\"options\":[\"BA\",\"MA\",\"SSC\",\"Primary School\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Chaturbhuj Babu has come back after passing his MA examinations.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the man on the right (Chaturbhuj) carrying?\",\"options\":[\"A bag of books\",\"A plump cat\",\"A certificate\",\"A walking stick\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows Chaturbhuj holding a cat, which matches the text describing him with a plump Afghan cat.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/073_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how does Chaturbhuj\'s facial expression compare to Nilratan\'s?\",\"options\":[\"Chaturbhuj looks happy while Nilratan looks sad\",\"Both men are laughing loudly\",\"Chaturbhuj looks annoyed or unhappy while Nilratan looks cheerful\",\"Chaturbhuj is sleeping while Nilratan is talking\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The drawing shows Nilratan smiling and gesturing, while Chaturbhuj has a frown and looks displeased.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/073_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What kind of cat does Chaturbhuj have with him?\",\"options\":[\"A thin local cat\",\"A wild jungle cat\",\"A plump Afghan cat\",\"A small kitten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes the cat as a \'plump Afghan cat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'make a great fuss over him\' mean in the context of the story?\",\"options\":[\"To ignore someone completely\",\"To give someone a lot of respect, praise, and attention\",\"To argue with someone loudly\",\"To ask someone to leave the village\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary in the text defines this phrase as giving a lot of respect, praise, and attention.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is Chaturbhuj annoyed with Nilratan?\",\"options\":[\"Nilratan stole his cat\",\"Nilratan is only interested in the cat and not Chaturbhuj\'s MA degree\",\"Nilratan refused to help him carry his bags\",\"Nilratan did not recognize him\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Chaturbhuj says to himself, \'Confound him, he can\'t talk about anything but the cat! It doesn\'t seem to matter that I\'ve just passed my MA!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Zamindar, who are the people who would be \'delighted\' to see the cat?\",\"options\":[\"The village elders\",\"The teachers in Calcutta\",\"The boys at his place\",\"The other cats in the village\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Zamindar says, \'The boys would be delighted\' when suggesting Chaturbhuj drop by with the cat.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the Zamindar suggest if Chaturbhuj himself cannot come to his house?\",\"options\":[\"To sell the cat to him\",\"To leave the cat on the road\",\"To send Beni round with the cat\",\"To come back after a year\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Zamindar says, \'even if you can\'t come yourself, send Beni round with the cat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When Chaturbhuj says he is going home \'furiously\', how is he feeling?\",\"options\":[\"Very happy and excited\",\"Very tired and sleepy\",\"Very angry\",\"Very hungry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines \'furiously\' as \'angrily\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'stunner\' as used by the Zamindar to describe the cat?\",\"options\":[\"Very ugly\",\"Very beautiful\",\"Very dangerous\",\"Very loud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines \'stunner\' as \'very beautiful\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does Satu believe is \'ruining these young people\'?\",\"options\":[\"The Afghan cat\",\"Village life\",\"Education\",\"Walking too much\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Satu says, \'It\'s education that\'s ruining these young people.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does Chaturbhuj do when Satu tries to ask another \'civil question\' about the cat?\",\"options\":[\"He sits down to talk\",\"He gives the cat to Satu\",\"He strides away without another word\",\"He starts crying\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The stage direction states, \'(Chaturbhuj strides away without another word.)\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'stuffed full of conceit\' imply about the young people according to Satu?\",\"options\":[\"They are very knowledgeable\",\"They are very very proud of themselves\",\"They are very helpful to elders\",\"They are very healthy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines \'stuffed full of conceit\' as \'very very proud of oneself\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the dialogue, what is the main conflict Chaturbhuj faces in this scene?\",\"options\":[\"He lost his cat on the way to the village\",\"He failed his MA examinations\",\"He wants recognition for his education, but everyone only notices his cat\",\"He does not want to go home to his family\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Throughout the scene, Chaturbhuj tries to talk about his exams, but Nilratan, the Zamindar, and Satu only talk about the cat, leading to his frustration.\",\"topic\":\"Scene I\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who is referred to as \'Dada Babu\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Uncle Hari\",\"The Little Boy\",\"Chaturbhuj\",\"The Maid\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Maid informs the Mother that \'Dada Babu\' has come home, and immediately after, Chaturbhuj enters.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the phrase \'in a blazing temper\' as used in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Feeling very cold\",\"Very angry\",\"Extremely happy\",\"Feeling very tired\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'in a blazing temper\' as being very angry.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Chaturbhuj slap the little boy?\",\"options\":[\"The boy stole his money\",\"The boy asked for the cat\",\"The boy broke a vase\",\"The boy was being too loud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"When the little boy asks \'Dada, can I have this cat?\', Chaturbhuj slaps him out of frustration.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what food does the mother intend to give the cat?\",\"options\":[\"Fish and water\",\"Bread and butter\",\"Rice and milk\",\"Meat and soup\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Mother says, \'I\'ll give it some rice and milk that I\'ve put by.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a character is speaking \'plaintively\', how are they expressing themselves?\",\"options\":[\"In a loud, joyful voice\",\"In a sad, complaining way\",\"In a very quiet whisper\",\"In a fast and excited manner\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'plaintively\' as speaking in a sad, complaining way.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does Chaturbhuj mean when he says people don\'t care for \'men of worth\'?\",\"options\":[\"People don\'t like rich men\",\"People don\'t care for great, valuable men\",\"People only care about money\",\"People don\'t like men who work hard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'men of worth\' as great, valuable men.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Chaturbhuj refuse to stay for his meal?\",\"options\":[\"He is not hungry\",\"He has another meeting\",\"He feels the family cares more about the cat than him\",\"He does not like the food his mother cooked\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Chaturbhuj complains that everyone is crazy about cats and no one cares for men of worth, leading him to leave furiously.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"When the Aunt says \'you\'re all heart\', what quality is she describing?\",\"options\":[\"Being very brave\",\"Being very kind\",\"Being very healthy\",\"Being very intelligent\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'you\'re all heart\' as being very kind.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Who does the little girl call to come and see the cat\'s \'big fat tail\'?\",\"options\":[\"Chaturbhuj\",\"The Maid\",\"Uncle Hari\",\"The Little Boy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The little girl says, \'Come and see, Uncle Hari - what a big fat tail!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the dialogue, how does Chaturbhuj feel about the cat?\",\"options\":[\"He loves it and wants to feed it\",\"He is indifferent and ignores it\",\"He is resentful and annoyed by the attention it gets\",\"He is afraid of it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Chaturbhuj slaps a boy for asking about it, kicks out at it, and complains that people care more for the cat than for him.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the woman in the center (the Mother) holding in her arms?\",\"options\":[\"A bundle of clothes\",\"A large white cat\",\"A small baby\",\"A bag of rice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration shows the mother holding the white cat that is the subject of the scene\'s conflict.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/075_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which character is depicted on the far left with an angry expression, walking away?\",\"options\":[\"Uncle Hari\",\"The Little Boy\",\"Chaturbhuj\",\"The Maid\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Chaturbhuj with a scowl, matching the text\'s description of him being in a \'blazing temper\' and leaving.\",\"topic\":\"Scene II\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/075_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Where does Scene III of the play take place?\",\"options\":[\"In Chaturbhuj\'s house\",\"On the road\",\"At the village market\",\"Inside a temple\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The stage direction at the beginning of the scene states \'(On the road)\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is Chaturbhuj carrying in his hand when he enters the scene?\",\"options\":[\"A cat\",\"A book\",\"A bag\",\"A rope\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'Enter Chaturbhuj, bag in hand, without the cat.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What reason does Chaturbhuj give Sadhucharan for the cat\'s absence?\",\"options\":[\"It ran away\",\"It is dead\",\"He sold it\",\"He left it at home\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Chaturbhuj explicitly tells Sadhucharan, \'It\'s dead.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does Chaturbhuj respond when Sadhucharan asks how the cat died?\",\"options\":[\"He explains the illness\",\"He cries loudly\",\"He says he doesn\'t know irritably\",\"He ignores him completely\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says Chaturbhuj responds \'(irritably) I don\'t know!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the vocabulary notes, what does the word \'urchins\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Small animals\",\"Street kids\",\"Village elders\",\"Angry cats\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'urchins\' as \'kids in the street.\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When Paran asks how the cat died, what rude comparison does Chaturbhuj make?\",\"options\":[\"It died like a dog\",\"It died like a king\",\"It died the same way they all will die\",\"It died of old age\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Chaturbhuj says, \'The same way all of you\'ll die - by swinging at the end of a rope!\'\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'positively\' as used by Paran?\",\"options\":[\"Happily\",\"Very\",\"Surely\",\"Slowly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The vocabulary note in the text defines \'positively\' as \'very\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What action do the urchins take as they follow Chaturbhuj?\",\"options\":[\"They help him carry his bag\",\"They ask him about his studies\",\"They clap and tease him with cries of \'Pussy cat\'\",\"They offer him food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text describes a swarm of urchins \'clapping and teasing him with cries of Pussy cat, Pussy cat\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is used in the text to describe the group of urchins?\",\"options\":[\"Crowd\",\"Swarm\",\"Army\",\"Pack\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the phrase \'A swarm of urchins\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is Chaturbhuj likely so angry throughout this scene?\",\"options\":[\"He lost his bag on the road\",\"He is tired of everyone asking about the cat instead of his achievements\",\"He is sad because his cat actually died\",\"He is afraid of the urchins\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The context of the play shows Chaturbhuj is frustrated that people only care about the cat, not his return or education.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does Paran\'s reaction \'Good God, he\'s positively furious!\' tell us about Chaturbhuj\'s behavior?\",\"options\":[\"Chaturbhuj is acting very calm\",\"Chaturbhuj\'s anger is extreme and noticeable\",\"Chaturbhuj is joking with them\",\"Chaturbhuj is feeling sick\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Paran uses the word \'furious\' to describe Chaturbhuj\'s intense anger.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"This play is adapted from a translation of a work by which famous author?\",\"options\":[\"R. K. Narayan\",\"Premchand\",\"Rabindranath Tagore\",\"Sarojini Naidu\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Adapted from the translation of a play by Rabindranath Tagore\'.\",\"topic\":\"Scene III\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the construction \'Be + main verb (v + -ing)\' indicate about an action?\",\"options\":[\"The action is complete\",\"The action is not complete and goes on\",\"The action happened in the distant past\",\"The action will happen in the future\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Be + main verb (v + -ing)\' shows that the action is\\/was not complete; it goes on.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The progressive tense is also known by which other name?\",\"options\":[\"Perfect tense\",\"Past tense\",\"Continuous tense\",\"Future tense\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the progressive tense is also known as the continuous tense.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which auxiliary verb is used to show that an action is or was complete?\",\"options\":[\"Be\",\"Do\",\"Have\",\"Go\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that the auxiliary verb \'Have\' shows that the action is or was complete.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific name for the tense that shows an action is or was complete?\",\"options\":[\"Progressive tense\",\"Perfect tense\",\"Continuous tense\",\"Present tense\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when an action is\\/was complete, it is known as the perfect tense.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of the Present Perfect tense?\",\"options\":[\"I am writing.\",\"They were playing.\",\"He has passed the examination.\",\"She was singing.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the text, \'He has passed the examination\' is listed under the Present Perfect column.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the past form of \'see\' is \'saw\', what is the past form of \'sing\' based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Singed\",\"Sung\",\"Sings\",\"Sang\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table in the text lists \'sang\' as the past form of the verb \'sing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'They were playing\', which tense is being used?\",\"options\":[\"Present Progressive\",\"Past Progressive\",\"Present Perfect\",\"Past Perfect\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text categorizes \'They were playing\' as Past Progressive.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To form the perfect tense, what is added to the auxiliary verb \'have\'?\",\"options\":[\"Main verb (v + -ing)\",\"Main verb (v + -ed \\/ -en)\",\"Only the main verb in present form\",\"The word \'not\'\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the perfect tense structure as \'Have + main verb (v + -ed \\/-en)\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which form of the verb \'write\' is used for the perfect tense according to the provided table?\",\"options\":[\"Wrote\",\"Writing\",\"Written\",\"Writes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table shows that the perfect form of \'write\' is \'written\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which sentence is an example of Past Progressive?\",\"options\":[\"I am writing.\",\"You were reading.\",\"They are playing.\",\"She is singing.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In the figure, \'You were reading\' is listed under the Past Progressive column.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/078_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which auxiliary verb is used specifically for the \'Past Perfect\' tense?\",\"options\":[\"have\",\"has\",\"had\",\"was\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows that \'had + main verb\' is the formula for Past Perfect.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/078_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the \'Perfect\' form of the verb \'do\'?\",\"options\":[\"did\",\"doing\",\"does\",\"done\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows \'done\' as the perfect form of the verb \'do\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/078_104.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the first instruction, what is the time limit for thinking of words ending in \'-ing\'?\",\"options\":[\"One minute\",\"Two minutes\",\"Five minutes\",\"Ten minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states to think of as many words as possible within two minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Two minutes of Oral Work\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many words ending in \'-ing\' must be selected for the second part of the activity?\",\"options\":[\"Five words\",\"As many as possible\",\"Ten words\",\"Two words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says to \'Select any ten of the words ending in -ing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Two minutes of Oral Work\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What suffix must all the words in this activity have?\",\"options\":[\"\'-ed\'\",\"\'-ly\'\",\"\'-ing\'\",\"\'-tion\'\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The activity focuses specifically on words ending in \'-ing\'.\",\"topic\":\"Two minutes of Oral Work\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final step mentioned in the instructions for the sentence-making task?\",\"options\":[\"Speak the sentences aloud\",\"Write down the sentences\",\"Count the words again\",\"Draw a picture for each sentence\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes the second instruction with \'Write down the sentences.\'\",\"topic\":\"Two minutes of Oral Work\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the requirement for the sentences created using the selected words?\",\"options\":[\"They must be meaningful\",\"They must be very long\",\"They must be about the school\",\"They must rhyme\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to \'Try to make a meaningful sentence using one or more of them\'.\",\"topic\":\"Two minutes of Oral Work\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student selects the word \'playing\', how should they use it according to the task?\",\"options\":[\"Write it ten times\",\"Find a word that rhymes with it\",\"Use it in a meaningful sentence\",\"Change it to \'played\'\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The task requires making meaningful sentences using the selected \'-ing\' words.\",\"topic\":\"Two minutes of Oral Work\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the instructions, how much total time is allocated for both thinking of words and making sentences?\",\"options\":[\"Two minutes total\",\"Four minutes total\",\"Six minutes total\",\"Eight minutes total\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Each of the two tasks has a two-minute limit, totaling four minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Two minutes of Oral Work\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is allowed when making sentences with the ten selected words?\",\"options\":[\"Using only one word per sentence\",\"Using more than one selected word in a single sentence\",\"Using words that do not end in \'-ing\'\",\"Taking ten minutes to write them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to use \'one or more of them\' in a sentence until all ten are used.\",\"topic\":\"Two minutes of Oral Work\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student has finished selecting ten words, what is their next time-bound goal?\",\"options\":[\"Think of ten more words in two minutes\",\"Make sentences for all ten words within two minutes\",\"Write the words in alphabetical order in two minutes\",\"Read the words to the teacher in two minutes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The second task requires making sentences for all ten words within two minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Two minutes of Oral Work\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary objective of the second task in this \'Oral Work\'?\",\"options\":[\"To test spelling of \'-ing\' words\",\"To see how fast a student can write\",\"To use all ten selected words in meaningful sentences quickly\",\"To list as many verbs as possible\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The task evaluates the ability to construct meaningful sentences using specific words within a time limit.\",\"topic\":\"Two minutes of Oral Work\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21906,41,7,'English','en','3.3 News Analysis','[\"News can be good or bad depending on how it makes us feel.\",\"A news item is reliable if it cites trustworthy sources like authorities or witnesses.\",\"Phrases such as ‘according to our sources’ or ‘authorities say’ are used to show reliability.\",\"Adjectives for news: breaking, shocking, urgent, exclusive, sensational, positive, negative, reliable, unreliable.\",\"Good news is news that makes us happy; bad news makes us sad or angry.\",\"Reliable news is based on facts and evidence; unreliable news may be rumours or false claims.\",\"When reading news, think critically: check facts, compare with other sources, and keep an open mind.\",\"News items often have a headline, body, and sometimes a picture or map.\",\"Different types of news: local, national, international, sports, entertainment, science, business, weather.\",\"News is published to inform people, influence opinions, and sometimes to sell products or ideas.\",\"In a newspaper, besides news stories there are editorials, letters to the editor, classifieds, and advertisements.\",\"When a news item is doubtful, look for corroborating evidence or statements from experts.\",\"A news headline may use a question mark to show uncertainty or to attract attention.\",\"When you read a news story, identify the who, what, when, where, why, and how – the 5Ws and 1H.\",\"A news article that claims a miracle cure should be treated with caution unless proven by science.\",\"The word ‘breaking’ means the news is new and important.\",\"The word ‘shocking’ means the news is surprising or upsetting.\",\"The word ‘exclusive’ means only this outlet has the information.\",\"The word ‘reliable’ means trustworthy; ‘unreliable’ means doubtful.\",\"The word ‘good’ means positive; ‘bad’ means negative.\",\"The word ‘interesting’ means engaging; ‘boring’ means dull.\",\"The word ‘important’ means significant; ‘unimportant’ means not significant.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, what do many people believe about information printed on paper?\",\"options\":[\"It is always boring\",\"It must be true and reliable\",\"It is usually written by eye witnesses\",\"It is only for elders to read\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that many people believe all that is printed on paper must be true and reliable.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do before forming an opinion about the news you read or hear?\",\"options\":[\"Discuss it only with authorities\",\"Believe it immediately if it is printed\",\"Think well and carefully with an open mind\",\"Ignore it if it doesn\'t match your ideas\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text advises to think well and carefully before forming an opinion, doing so with an open mind.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'authorities\' as used in the news analysis context?\",\"options\":[\"People who write the news\",\"People who are in control\",\"People who read the news daily\",\"People who see an event happen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'authorities\' as people who are in control.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a person sees an event happen with their own eyes, they are called a\\/an:\",\"options\":[\"Authority\",\"Reporter\",\"Eye witness\",\"Source\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"An eye witness is defined as someone who has seen something with his or her own eyes.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When people discuss news \'with feeling\', how are they behaving?\",\"options\":[\"They are reading silently\",\"They are showing emotions like anger or happiness\",\"They are ignoring the facts\",\"They are looking for eye witnesses\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains \'with feeling\' as showing how they feel about it—angry, happy, etc.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a synonym for the word \'account\' as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Calculation\",\"Bank balance\",\"Report or story\",\"Adjective\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the meaning of \'account\' as a report or story.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which adjective would you use for a piece of news that makes you feel sad?\",\"options\":[\"Reliable news\",\"Good news\",\"Bad news\",\"Breaking news\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that if news makes you angry or sad, you will say it is bad news.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why do reporters use phrases like \'according to our sources\' or \'authorities say that\'?\",\"options\":[\"To make the news item longer\",\"To confuse the readers\",\"To convince readers that the news is reliable\",\"To show that the news is boring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions these phrases are used to convince readers or viewers that the news is reliable.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which object represents the primary medium of printed news discussed in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The pens\",\"The spectacles\",\"The newspaper\",\"The wooden block\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows a newspaper, which is the main subject of the text regarding printed information.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/079_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the spectacles (glasses) placed on the newspaper most likely symbolize which action mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Reading with an open mind\",\"Thinking well and carefully about what we read\",\"Becoming an eye witness\",\"Listening to news bulletins\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Spectacles are tools for seeing clearly, symbolizing the \'careful thinking\' and \'analysis\' required when reading news.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"41\\/079_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase does a reporter use when information has recently become known?\",\"options\":[\"It is boring that...\",\"It has come to light that...\",\"It is unreliable that...\",\"With feeling that...\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'It has come to light that...\' as a phrase reporters use to present information.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What should a reader consider to decide if a news item is \'reliable\' or \'unreliable\'?\",\"options\":[\"If it is printed on colorful paper\",\"If it matches facts, experiences, and ideas\",\"If it is only about happy things\",\"If it is read by elders\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests comparing news with facts, experiences, and ideas to see if they tally.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Besides \'breaking\' and \'shocking\', which of the following is an adjective used for news in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Reliable\",\"Tally\",\"Bulletin\",\"Opinion\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'reliable\' and \'unreliable\' as ways to consider or describe news.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a news item does not \'tally\' with facts, it means the news:\",\"options\":[\"Is very interesting\",\"Does not match the truth\",\"Is written by an eye witness\",\"Is breaking news\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'tally\' to mean \'match\', so not tallying means it does not match the facts.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the \'Warming up!\' section in this text?\",\"options\":[\"To teach how to write a newspaper\",\"To encourage students to question and analyze the news they consume\",\"To prove that all printed news is false\",\"To list the names of famous reporters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The section asks questions about how we read, feel, and think about news, encouraging analysis.\",\"topic\":\"News Analysis Introduction\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the Shivam Institute of Innovative Technology located?\",\"options\":[\"Mumbai\",\"Bengaluru\",\"Delhi\",\"Pune\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions \'Bengaluru : Shivam Institute of Innovative Technology\'.\",\"topic\":\"CLOSED SHOES NOT ALLOWED\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What has the institute recently issued for the candidates taking the Entrance Test?\",\"options\":[\"A list of textbooks\",\"A list of DO’s and DON’Ts\",\"A list of exam results\",\"A list of scholarship winners\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the institute \'has recently issued a list of DO’s and DON’Ts for candidates\'.\",\"topic\":\"CLOSED SHOES NOT ALLOWED\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, who will provide pens to the candidates in the examination hall?\",\"options\":[\"The parents\",\"The candidates themselves\",\"The invigilators\",\"The security guards\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'The pens should be provided in the hall by the invigilators.\'\",\"topic\":\"CLOSED SHOES NOT ALLOWED\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following footwear is specifically mentioned as NOT allowed in the hall?\",\"options\":[\"Open sandals\",\"Flip-flops\",\"Closed shoes\",\"Rubber slippers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions that \'candidates will not be allowed to enter the examination hall wearing closed shoes\'.\",\"topic\":\"CLOSED SHOES NOT ALLOWED\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a candidate arrives at the hall wearing socks, what will happen according to the rules?\",\"options\":[\"They will be given a new pair of socks\",\"They will not be allowed to enter the hall\",\"They will be allowed if the socks are white\",\"They must pay a fine to wear them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says candidates will not be allowed to enter wearing \'even socks\'.\",\"topic\":\"CLOSED SHOES NOT ALLOWED\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the news, which of these electronic gadgets is prohibited inside the hall?\",\"options\":[\"Digital watches\",\"Microphones\",\"Laptops\",\"Electric fans\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'microphones\' as one of the items not allowed inside.\",\"topic\":\"CLOSED SHOES NOT ALLOWED\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the context of the text, what is the most likely meaning of the word \'invigilators\'?\",\"options\":[\"People who clean the hall\",\"People who supervise the examination\",\"Students taking the test\",\"People who sell pens\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Invigi