 Smell of Man\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What do humans do to pangolin holes or nests according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"They protect them from rain\",\"They search for them and dig them up\",\"They build new ones for the pangolins\",\"They fill them with food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that humans \'search for our holes\\/nests and dig them up.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Smell of Man\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why do humans sell pangolin scales for \'loads and loads of money\'?\",\"options\":[\"Humans think the scales are medicinal\",\"The scales are used to make clothes\",\"The scales are made of gold\",\"The scales are used as toys\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'Humans think our scales are medicinal.\'\",\"topic\":\"The Smell of Man\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When Mama Pangolin \'uncurled herself very very cautiously\', what does this tell us about her behavior?\",\"options\":[\"She was feeling very sleepy\",\"She was acting with great care to ensure safety\",\"She was in a hurry to find food\",\"She was angry at the baby\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Uncurling \'cautiously\' indicates she was being careful because she was still alert to potential danger.\",\"topic\":\"The Smell of Man\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If a human is described as \'wicked beyond measure\', how would you describe their wickedness?\",\"options\":[\"Small and limited\",\"Without limit or extremely wicked\",\"Easy to measure\",\"Not wicked at all\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'beyond measure\' as \'without limit\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Smell of Man\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what is the primary reason humans kill pangolins?\",\"options\":[\"To keep them as pets\",\"To eat their flesh and sell their scales\",\"To help them move to new homes\",\"To study their behavior\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'They kill us, eat our flesh and sell our scales...\'\",\"topic\":\"The Smell of Man\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which physical action did Mama Pangolin take to protect her belly?\",\"options\":[\"She stood on her hind legs\",\"She pulled her body into a tight ball\",\"She lay flat on her back\",\"She ran into a deep hole\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"By pulling her long body into a tight ball, she protects her soft belly and holds the baby close.\",\"topic\":\"The Smell of Man\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who were the only people who knew about pangolins long ago?\",\"options\":[\"International smugglers\",\"Tribal people living in jungles\",\"Modern scientists\",\"Greedy hunters\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that long ago, only tribal people living in the jungles knew about them.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How do greedy people spot pangolins during their nighttime wandering?\",\"options\":[\"By using trap cameras\",\"By following their tracks\",\"By flashing harsh torch lights\",\"By listening to their sounds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that greedy people flash harsh torch lights to spot pangolins at night.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why did tribal people kill animals in the past?\",\"options\":[\"For greed\",\"For international smuggling\",\"For sport and fun\",\"Not for greed (for need)\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that tribal people killed animals but \'not for greed\'.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In what way are pangolins \'helpers\' to humans?\",\"options\":[\"They help clear the jungles\",\"They remove millions of ants and termites\",\"They guide people through the forest\",\"They help in farming\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The mother pangolin explains that they remove millions of ants and termites for humans.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which organization is specifically mentioned as working in Maharashtra to protect pangolins?\",\"options\":[\"World Wildlife Fund\",\"Sahyadri Nisarg Mitra\",\"Forest Department of India\",\"Global Pangolin Rescue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Sahyadri Nisarg Mitra and other organizations in Maharashtra.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is there no room left for pangolins to build their homes?\",\"options\":[\"Because of too many ants and termites\",\"Because tribal people have moved away\",\"Because wicked people destroyed habitats and cleared jungles\",\"Because trap cameras are taking up space\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that wicked people have destroyed habitats and cleared away jungles, leaving no room for homes.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What modern technology is used to get photographs and study pangolins?\",\"options\":[\"Satellite imaging\",\"Mobile phone cameras\",\"Modern trap cameras\",\"Flashlights and guns\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that organizations set up modern trap cameras to get photographs and study them.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What do organizations do in villages to help protect pangolins?\",\"options\":[\"They build homes for pangolins\",\"They hold meetings and urge people to protect them\",\"They sell pamphlets to the villagers\",\"They clear the jungles for the villagers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they hold meetings in villages and urge people to protect pangolins.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What irony does the mother pangolin point out regarding humans and insects?\",\"options\":[\"Humans love ants but hate termites\",\"Humans spend huge amounts to remove ants but kill the pangolins who do it for free\",\"Humans use pangolins to find ants\",\"Humans protect ants but destroy pangolin habitats\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes humans spend huge amounts to remove ants\\/termites themselves but will not spare the pangolins who help.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Besides posters and meetings, what else do organizations use to spread awareness?\",\"options\":[\"Radio advertisements\",\"Television shows\",\"Pamphlets\",\"School textbooks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they put up posters and hand out pamphlets.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a pangolin family is out at night, when must they return home to stay safe?\",\"options\":[\"When the moon is high\",\"Before the day breaks\",\"After the greedy people sleep\",\"When they are full of termites\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The mother says, \'Now we must reach home before the day breaks.\'\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what does the mother pangolin hope will happen to their \'kith and kin\'?\",\"options\":[\"They will move to the city\",\"They will flourish\",\"They will learn to use cameras\",\"They will stop eating termites\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The mother hopes that with the help of good people, their \'kith and kin will flourish\'.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the mother pangolin call certain people \'wicked\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they study them with cameras\",\"Because they live in the jungle\",\"Because they destroy habitats and kill for greed\",\"Because they spend money on termite removal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text labels those who destroy habitats and kill for greed as \'wicked\'.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What specific illegal activity are organizations trying to stop?\",\"options\":[\"Tribal hunting\",\"International smuggling\",\"Village meetings\",\"Nighttime wandering\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states they \'try hard to put a stop to international smuggling\'.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary purpose of the awareness campaigns mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"To teach pangolins how to hide\",\"To help people understand the importance of pangolins in food chains\",\"To collect money for the Forest Department\",\"To encourage people to clear more jungle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says good people know their importance in food chains and run awareness campaigns to help them.\",\"topic\":\"Protecting Pangolins\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which protein are the scales of a pangolin made of?\",\"options\":[\"Calcium\",\"Keratin\",\"Collagen\",\"Iron\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the scales are made of a protein called Keratin.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Indian Wild Life Protection Act 1972, pangolins receive the same protection as which animal?\",\"options\":[\"Lions\",\"Rhinos\",\"Tigers\",\"Elephants\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that being in Schedule I means they enjoy the same protection that tigers do.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Approximately how many ants or termites does one pangolin eat in a single year?\",\"options\":[\"7 lakh\",\"70 thousand\",\"7 crore\",\"7 billion\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that one pangolin eats as many as 7 crore ants\\/termites in a year.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What percentage of a pangolin\'s total body weight is contributed by its scales?\",\"options\":[\"10%\",\"20%\",\"50%\",\"75%\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that scales comprise as much as 20% of its total body weight.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is there a high international demand for pangolin scales?\",\"options\":[\"To make jewelry\",\"For use in Chinese medicine\",\"To produce keratin for hair\",\"For building houses\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that pangolin scales are used in Chinese medicine and are in great demand.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following describes the sensory abilities of a pangolin?\",\"options\":[\"Strong eyesight and weak smell\",\"Strong eyesight and strong smell\",\"Weak eyesight and weak smell\",\"Weak eyesight and strong smell\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states that pangolins have a weak eyesight but a strong sense of smell.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a specific Indian pangolin weighs 10 kg, how many kilograms of that weight are its scales?\",\"options\":[\"1 kg\",\"2 kg\",\"5 kg\",\"8 kg\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since scales are 20% of the body weight, 20% of 10 kg is 2 kg.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A pangolin needs to reach a high branch on a tree. Which body parts will it use to climb?\",\"options\":[\"Scales and nose\",\"Strong claws and tail\",\"Teeth and claws\",\"Back and scales\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that a pangolin uses its strong claws and tail to climb up a tree.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these would also contain the same protein found in pangolin scales?\",\"options\":[\"Tiger skin\",\"Ant hills\",\"Human hair\",\"Tree bark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that our nails, hair, and rhino horns all consist of Keratin, just like pangolin scales.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the contradiction mentioned in the text regarding pangolin scales and medicine?\",\"options\":[\"They are expensive but easy to find\",\"They are in demand for medicine but have no medicinal properties\",\"They are used for medicine but only in India\",\"They are made of protein but cannot be eaten\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes they are in demand for Chinese medicine, yet research proves Keratin has no medicinal properties.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement correctly compares male and female Indian pangolins?\",\"options\":[\"Females are larger than males\",\"Males and females are the same size\",\"Females are smaller than males\",\"Males are twice the length of females\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'Females are smaller than the males.\'\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the curling behavior of a pangolin effective against predators like lions?\",\"options\":[\"It makes the pangolin look like a rock\",\"It hides the pangolin\'s scent\",\"It creates a hard ball that is difficult to crack\",\"It allows the pangolin to roll away quickly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says tigers and lions find it difficult to crack\\/eat a pangolin that has curled itself into a tight ball.\",\"topic\":\"Pangolin Fact Sheet\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(21911,41,7,'English','en','4.3 Chasing the Sea Monster','[\"- Jules Verne is called the ‘Father of Science Fiction’.\",\"- The story is from his novel *Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea*.\",\"- The narrator is Professor Pierre Aronnax.\",\"- The ship is the frigate *Abraham Lincoln*.\",\"- The event takes place at 12:53 am, with later actions until about 10:50 pm.\",\"- Key nautical terms: yard, mast, bow, deck, forecastle, starboard, stern, afterdeck, 