ys \'the Hail stopped dancing... and the North Wind ceased roaring\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Return of Spring\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What relationship does the text suggest between the children and the seasons?\",\"options\":[\"The children only come when it is winter\",\"The presence of children brings Spring to the trees\",\"The children are afraid of the Spring blossoms\",\"The children prefer the North Wind and Hail\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that where children sat, trees blossomed (Spring), but where the child couldn\'t reach, it remained winter.\",\"topic\":\"The Return of Spring\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does the author personify the trees in this passage?\",\"options\":[\"By saying they were lying awake in bed\",\"By saying they were waving their arms gently\",\"By saying they were singing like musicians\",\"By saying they were creeping through holes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the trees \'waving their arms gently,\' giving them human-like characteristics.\",\"topic\":\"The Return of Spring\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What can be inferred about the little boy\'s situation compared to the other children?\",\"options\":[\"He was the only one who didn\'t like the garden\",\"He was excluded by the other children\",\"His physical size prevented him from experiencing Spring like the others\",\"He was the only child who entered through the gate\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Because he was \'too tiny\' to reach the branches, his specific tree remained in winter while others enjoyed Spring.\",\"topic\":\"The Return of Spring\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What tool did the giant use to knock down the wall of his garden?\",\"options\":[\"A large hammer\",\"A great axe\",\"A heavy shovel\",\"An iron crowbar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the giant \'took a great axe and knocked down the wall\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Giant\'s Change of Heart\",\"