acks air, sound cannot be heard.\",\"topic\":\"Temperature and Sound\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\",\"figure_image\":\"46\\/029_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following best describes the process of temperature regulation mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Sun -> Heat reflection -> Absorption by air -> Warm surface\",\"Sun -> Sound reflection -> Density increase -> Cold surface\",\"Air removal -> Heat absorption -> Suitable for life\",\"Winter -> Density decrease -> Clear sound transmission\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text describes energy from the sun being reflected as heat, absorbed by air constituents, keeping the surface warm.\",\"topic\":\"Temperature and Sound\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Under ordinary conditions, in which state is water found?\",\"options\":[\"Solid state\",\"Liquid state\",\"Gaseous state\",\"Plasma state\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that water occurs in liquid state under ordinary conditions.\",\"topic\":\"Properties of water\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a characteristic property of water as a fluid?\",\"options\":[\"It has its own definite shape.\",\"It cannot pass through small holes.\",\"It does not have its own shape, but has a volume.\",\"It does not seep through cracks.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, water is a fluid that does not have its own shape but has a volume.\",\"topic\":\"Properties of water\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to water when it is poured into an oil-cladded dish?\",\"options\":[\"It spreads evenly across the dish.\",\"It forms small round drops.\",\"It dissolves the oil immediately.\",\"It changes into a solid state.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that on an oil-cladded dish, water does not spread but forms small round drops.\",\"topic\":\"Properties of water\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a plastic bottle more than half full of water 