:[\"Because distance and displacement are both measured in the same unit (metres).\",\"Because time period is measured in different units for each.\",\"Because speed and velocity are the same physical quantity.\",\"Because the text says the units are always ignored.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Since both distance and displacement use the unit of length (metres) and both are divided by time (seconds), the resulting unit is the same.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s find the unit\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the total actual distance traversed by Ranjit from his home to school?\",\"options\":[\"1000 m\",\"1500 m\",\"500 m\",\"800 m\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the actual distance is AB + BC + CD = 500 m + 700 m + 300 m = 1500 m.\",\"topic\":\"Ranjit\'s velocity and speed\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How much total time did Ranjit take to reach the school from his home?\",\"options\":[\"15 minutes\",\"20 minutes\",\"25 minutes\",\"30 minutes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Total time is calculated as 8 minutes + 11 minutes + 6 minutes = 25 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Ranjit\'s velocity and speed\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the magnitude of Ranjit\'s displacement (AD) from home to school?\",\"options\":[\"1500 metres\",\"700 metres\",\"1000 metres\",\"500 metres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that Ranjit\'s displacement AD = 1000 metres.\",\"topic\":\"Ranjit\'s velocity and speed\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, which formula is used to calculate Ranjit\'s velocity?\",\"options\":[\"Velocity = Distance traversed \\/ Total time\",\"Velocity = Displacement \\/ Total time\",\"Velocity = Total time \\/ Displacement\",\"Velocity = Distance + Displacement \\/ Time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines Velocity as Displacement divided by Total time.\",\"topic\":\"Ranjit\'s velocity and speed\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\