swer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows average velocity is 40 km \\/ 1 hour, which is displacement divided by time.\",\"topic\":\"Average and instantaneous velocity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the truck traverses a 10 km distance (BC) in 20 minutes, what is its velocity for that segment in km\\/hr?\",\"options\":[\"20 km\\/hr\",\"30 km\\/hr\",\"40 km\\/hr\",\"50 km\\/hr\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"10 km in 20 minutes means 30 km in 60 minutes (10\\/20 * 60 = 30).\",\"topic\":\"Average and instantaneous velocity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the truck traverses a 20 km distance (CD) in 30 minutes, what is its velocity for that segment in km\\/hr?\",\"options\":[\"20 km\\/hr\",\"30 km\\/hr\",\"40 km\\/hr\",\"60 km\\/hr\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"20 km in 30 minutes means 40 km in 60 minutes (20\\/30 * 60 = 40).\",\"topic\":\"Average and instantaneous velocity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"The text calculates the velocity for AB as 60 km\\/hr because the truck covers 10 km in 10 minutes. How many minutes are used to standardize this to one hour?\",\"options\":[\"10 minutes\",\"30 minutes\",\"40 minutes\",\"60 minutes\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The calculation shown is 10 km \\/ 10 minutes = 60 km \\/ 60 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Average and instantaneous velocity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Comparing the segments AB (60 km\\/hr), BC (30 km\\/hr), and CD (40 km\\/hr), in which segment is the velocity highest?\",\"options\":[\"Segment AB\",\"Segment BC\",\"Segment CD\",\"The velocity is the same in all\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Based on the calculations, AB is 60 km\\/hr, which is higher than 30 and 40.\",\"topic\":\"Average and instantaneous velocity\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the velocity in segment AB (60 km\\/hr) different from the average velocity of the whole trip (40 km\\/hr)?\",\"options\":[\"Because the truck stopped at point B\",\"Because average velocity conside