he largest muscle of the human body located?\",\"options\":[\"In the back\",\"In the arm\",\"In the thigh\",\"In the chest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the largest muscle of our body is in the thigh.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is considered the basic property of muscles?\",\"options\":[\"Expansion\",\"Contraction\",\"Vibration\",\"Rigidity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that contraction is the basic property of muscles.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the primary benefit of getting regular exercise for the muscular system?\",\"options\":[\"It makes the muscles strong\",\"It changes the structure of vertebrae\",\"It makes the muscles smaller\",\"It reduces the need for proteins\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that regular exercise makes the muscles strong.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the breathing process during physical exercise?\",\"options\":[\"Breathing becomes slower\",\"Breathing stops for a while\",\"Breathing becomes faster\",\"Breathing remains unchanged\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that during exercise, breathing becomes faster to ensure oxygen supply.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the consequence of sitting with a hunched or bent back over a long period?\",\"options\":[\"The muscles become more efficient\",\"Changes occur in the structure of the vertebrae\",\"The heart muscles become slower\",\"The thigh muscles become larger\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text warns that sitting with a hunched back leads to changes in the structure of the vertebrae.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student wants to ensure their muscles are repaired quickly after a sports injury. Based on the text, what should they prioritize in their diet?\",\"options\":[\"Only fats\",\"Proteins and carbohydrates\",\"Only water\",\"Vitamins and minerals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that proteins and carbohydrates are required for the repair of muscles.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is experiencing pain in their shoulder and back, which habit mentioned in the text might be the cause?\",\"options\":[\"Eating too many carbohydrates\",\"Exercising too much\",\"Sitting with a bent back\",\"Studying myology\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that sitting with a bent back causes muscles in the shoulder and back to hurt.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why do the heart muscles move more rapidly and breathing become faster during exercise?\",\"options\":[\"To make the stapes bone stronger\",\"To change the structure of the thigh muscle\",\"To ensure a sufficient supply of oxygen and nutrients\",\"To prevent the contraction of muscles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states these changes ensure a sufficient supply of oxygen and nutrients to various parts of the body.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following describes the location of the smallest muscle in the human body?\",\"options\":[\"Attached to a bone in the ear\",\"Inside the vertebral column\",\"Attached to the thigh bone\",\"Inside the heart\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states the smallest muscle is attached to a bone in the ear called the stapes.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is a direct result of maintaining a straight back while sitting?\",\"options\":[\"Increasing the heart rate\",\"Preventing disorders of the vertebral column\",\"Increasing the size of the stapes\",\"Improving the study of myology\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text implies that not sitting straight leads to vertebral disorders; therefore, sitting straight prevents them.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the process of converting food into a soluble form and its absorption into the blood called?\",\"options\":[\"Respiration\",\"Digestion\",\"Circulation\",\"Excretion\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines digestion as the conversion of food into a soluble form and its absorption into the blood.\",\"topic\":\"The Digestive System\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the approximate total length of the alimentary canal in a human being?\",\"options\":[\"5 metres\",\"7 metres\",\"9 metres\",\"12 metres\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the total length of the alimentary canal is about 9 metres.\",\"topic\":\"The Digestive System\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a digestive gland connected to the alimentary canal?\",\"options\":[\"Stomach\",\"Small intestine\",\"Pancreas\",\"Rectum\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions salivary glands, liver, and pancreas as the digestive glands connected to the alimentary canal.\",\"topic\":\"The Digestive System\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The digestive system is primarily composed of which two components?\",\"options\":[\"The heart and blood vessels\",\"The alimentary canal and digestive glands\",\"The lungs and the pharynx\",\"The muscles and the stomach\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the digestive system consists of the alimentary canal and digestive glands.\",\"topic\":\"The Digestive System\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which organ follows the pharynx in the path of the alimentary canal?\",\"options\":[\"Stomach\",\"Oesophagus\",\"Small intestine\",\"Large intestine\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists the parts in order: mouth, pharynx, oesophagus, stomach, etc.\",\"topic\":\"The Digestive System\",\"part\":8