",\"It pushes the particles away from the centre\",\"It pushes the particles upwards\",\"It pulls the particles in a circular path only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that a force is generated which pushes the particles away from the centre.\",\"topic\":\"Centrifugation\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How does the behavior of soil particles in turbid water differ from milk particles when both are kept undisturbed?\",\"options\":[\"Soil particles settle slowly while milk particles do not settle\",\"Milk particles settle quickly while soil particles do not settle\",\"Both soil and milk particles settle at the same speed\",\"Neither soil nor milk particles settle at all\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text notes that soil particles in turbid water slowly settle, but particles of milk do not settle even when left undisturbed.\",\"topic\":\"Centrifugation\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the method of filtration ineffective for separating particles from a mixture like ink?\",\"options\":[\"Because the particles are too large for the filter\",\"Because the particles are very tiny and evenly distributed\",\"Because ink is a pure substance, not a mixture\",\"Because the liquid in ink evaporates too quickly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states these tiny, light, and evenly distributed particles cannot be separated by filtration.\",\"topic\":\"Centrifugation\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how is a test tube positioned on the disc of the centrifuge machine?\",\"options\":[\"Vertically\",\"Horizontally\",\"At a 45-degree angle\",\"Upside down\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that a test tube is kept horizontally on the disc.\",\"topic\":\"Centrifugation\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what specific type of laboratory equipment is shown?\",\"options\":[\"Manual centrifuge\",\"Electrical centrifuge\",\"Microscope\",\