stic beads\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The 19th century includes the year 1850, and the text says soap-based toothpaste came into use in the 19th century.\",\"topic\":\"History of Toothpaste\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A museum displays a toothpaste container dated 1873. Which significant event in toothpaste history does this represent?\",\"options\":[\"The discovery of bone powder\",\"The first use of soap in toothpaste\",\"The first commercial production of toothpaste\",\"The invention of chalk-based toothpaste\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The year 1873 marks when the first commercial toothpaste was made by the Colgate company.\",\"topic\":\"History of Toothpaste\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following shows the correct chronological order of materials used in toothpaste according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Soap -> Chalk-like material -> Bone powder\",\"Bone powder -> Soap -> Chalk-like material\",\"Chalk-like material -> Soap -> Bone powder\",\"Bone powder -> Chalk-like material -> Soap\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Bone powder was used prior to 500 BC, soap in the 19th century, and chalk-like material later.\",\"topic\":\"History of Toothpaste\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, how did the availability of toothpaste change in 1873?\",\"options\":[\"It became a homemade product only\",\"It was no longer made of soap\",\"It became a commercial product\",\"It was banned in New York City\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text highlights 1873 as the year the first \'commercial\' toothpaste was made.\",\"topic\":\"History of Toothpaste\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"From which language is the word \'detergent\' derived?\",\"options\":[\"Greek\",\"Latin\",\"Sanskrit\",\"French\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the word \'detergent\' is derived from the Latin word \'detergere\'.\",\"topic\":\"Detergents\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the lit