ain metals from ores?\",\"options\":[\"Because ores contain very little metal\",\"Because ores are found only on the surface\",\"Because the high proportion of metal makes extraction worthwhile\",\"Because ores do not contain any gangue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Ores contain a high proportion of metal, making it cost-effective (economical) to extract the metal.\",\"topic\":\"Minerals and ores\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"A student finds a mineral and rubs it on a tile to see the color of the powder left behind. Which property is the student testing?\",\"options\":[\"Cleavage\",\"Hardness\",\"Streak\",\"Lustre\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Streak is the characteristic property of a mineral related to the color of its powder.\",\"topic\":\"Minerals and ores\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a metal is found in nature as a \'compound\', what does this imply compared to a \'free state\' metal?\",\"options\":[\"It is mixed with other elements rather than being pure\",\"It is always found as a liquid\",\"It cannot be mined\",\"It does not contain any gangue\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Metals in the free state occur alone, while a majority occur as compounds (combined with other elements).\",\"topic\":\"Minerals and ores\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What two processes must be performed to obtain pure metals from their ores?\",\"options\":[\"Mining and Digging\",\"Extraction and Purification\",\"Fracture and Cleavage\",\"Hardness and Lustre\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that metals are obtained from their ore by extraction and purification.\",\"topic\":\"Minerals and ores\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following best explains why all minerals are not considered ores?\",\"options\":[\"Some minerals are not found in rocks\",\"Some minerals do not have a characteristic colour\",\"Some minerals may not have a high enough proportion of metal to be economical\",\"Some minerals are o