hich of the following could it be?\",\"options\":[\"Potash\",\"Bauxite\",\"Natural gas\",\"Tungsten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the classification, energy minerals include coal, mineral oil, and natural gas.\",\"topic\":\"How are minerals formed?\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"A student finds a piece of Mica. Based on the classification of minerals, what type of mineral is it?\",\"options\":[\"Non-metal mineral\",\"Metal mineral\",\"Energy mineral\",\"Inorganic organism mineral\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Mica is listed under the category of non-metal minerals.\",\"topic\":\"How are minerals formed?\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is an example of an inorganic mineral produced by a living organism?\",\"options\":[\"Feldspar\",\"Conches\",\"Tin\",\"Magnetite\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies conches and shells as inorganic minerals produced by living organisms.\",\"topic\":\"How are minerals formed?\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these minerals is formed from magma in the earth\'s crust?\",\"options\":[\"Magnetite\",\"Halite\",\"Graphite\",\"Sulphur\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists Magnetite as an example of a mineral formed from magma in the earth\'s crust.\",\"topic\":\"How are minerals formed?\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which group of minerals consists only of metals?\",\"options\":[\"Mica, Sulphur, Gypsum\",\"Iron, Gold, Silver\",\"Coal, Mineral oil, Natural gas\",\"Diamond, Graphite, Feldspar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Iron, gold, and silver are all listed under the \'Metal minerals\' category.\",\"topic\":\"How are minerals formed?\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does the formation of Magnetite differ from the formation of Halite?\",\"options\":[\"Magnetite forms by evaporation, while Halite forms from magma.\",\"Magnetite forms from living organisms, while Halite forms from lava.\",\"Magnetite forms from cooling magma, while Halite forms by evaporation.\",\"Magnetite forms under high pressure, while Halite forms by cooling lava.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Magnetite is formed from magma\\/lava cooling, whereas Halite is formed when crystals remain after evaporation.\",\"topic\":\"How are minerals formed?\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which mineral is illustrated as a result of transformation from one form to another due to temperature and pressure?\",\"options\":[\"Mica\",\"Halite\",\"Diamond\",\"Shell\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows Diamond in the column describing transformation due to changes in temperature and pressure.\",\"topic\":\"How are minerals formed?\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"46\\/115_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which category includes minerals like Platinum and Tungsten?\",\"options\":[\"Non-metal minerals\",\"Metal minerals\",\"Energy minerals\",\"Inorganic minerals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The classification table shows Platinum and Tungsten under the \'Metal minerals\' column.\",\"topic\":\"How are minerals formed?\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"46\\/115_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific name given to the deposits of common salt found in the earth?\",\"options\":[\"Sea salt\",\"Rock salt\",\"Table salt\",\"Crystal salt\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that deposits of common salt found in the earth are called rock salt.\",\"topic\":\"Gems and gemlike minerals\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which year was the Indian School of Mines, Dhanbad founded?\",\"options\":[\"1920\",\"1926\",\"1936\",\"1947\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the Indian School of Mines, Dhanbad, was founded in 1926.\",\"topic\":\"Gems and gemlike minerals\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which institute was originally founded to impart education in mining at Dhanbad?\",\"options\":[\"Indian I