\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When a vibrating object is touched by hand, what happens to the sound?\",\"options\":[\"The sound becomes louder\",\"The sound changes its pitch\",\"We no longer hear the sound\",\"The sound continues for a long time\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that when we touch the vibrating object, the vibrations stop and we no longer hear the sound.\",\"topic\":\"Generation of Sound\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the motion called when it is repeated again and again at fixed intervals of time?\",\"options\":[\"Linear motion\",\"Random motion\",\"Periodic motion\",\"Circular motion\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines motion repeated again and again at fixed intervals of time as periodic motion.\",\"topic\":\"Generation of Sound\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When the string of a tanpura is plucked, which part of the string remains still?\",\"options\":[\"The middle part\",\"The two ends\",\"The entire string\",\"The right side only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that while the string vibrates, the two ends of the vibrating string are still.\",\"topic\":\"Generation of Sound\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student strikes a metal bell and then immediately holds it tightly, why does the sound stop?\",\"options\":[\"The bell becomes too hot\",\"The vibrations are stopped by the hand\",\"The bell loses its shape\",\"The air around the bell disappears\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Touching a vibrating object stops the vibrations, which in turn stops the generation of sound.\",\"topic\":\"Generation of Sound\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why are we sometimes unable to see the vibrations of an object that is producing sound?\",\"options\":[\"Because sound is invisible\",\"Because the vibrations are too minute\",\"Because the object is not actually vibrating\",\"Because the sound travels too fast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains 