a\\/sitar being tuned, which the text uses as an example of a stringed instrument producing sound through vibration.\",\"topic\":\"Generation of Sound\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"46\\/129_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the musicians are \'tuning\' their instruments. According to the text, what physical process must occur in these instruments to produce sound?\",\"options\":[\"Chemical reaction\",\"Rhythmic vibration\",\"Heating of the surface\",\"Cooling of the air\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that sound is generated by the rhythmic vibration of an object, which applies to all musical instruments shown.\",\"topic\":\"Generation of Sound\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"46\\/129_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the position of a swing at rest called in the given experiment?\",\"options\":[\"Starting point\",\"End position\",\"Central position\",\"Side position\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the position of the swing at rest marked on the ground is the central position.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A swing that moves back and forth is specifically referred to as an ____.\",\"options\":[\"Accelerator\",\"Oscillator\",\"Indicator\",\"Insulator\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, a swing that moves back and forth like this is an oscillator.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When is a swing said to have completed one oscillation?\",\"options\":[\"When it reaches the central position once\",\"When it moves from one end to the other and returns to its starting point\",\"When it is pulled to one side and let go\",\"When it stays at the central position\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines one oscillation as moving from one end to the other and returning to the starting point.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the back and forth motion of an oscillator on either side of a central position called?\",\"options\":[\"Linear motion\",\"Circular motion\",\"Oscillatory motion\",\"Random motion\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the back and forth motion of an oscillator on either side of a central position as oscillatory motion.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If you are observing a child on a swing, which part of the movement represents the oscillatory motion?\",\"options\":[\"The swing staying still at the center\",\"The swing being pulled to one side before release\",\"The back and forth movement on either side of the center\",\"The act of marking the ground below the swing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Oscillatory motion is the back and forth movement on either side of the central position.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"While swinging, which point does the swing cross again and again?\",\"options\":[\"The starting point only\",\"The central position\",\"The ground mark at the far end\",\"The highest point only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the swing will be seen to cross the central position again and again.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To observe the motion of a swing correctly, what is the first step mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Pull the swing to one side\",\"Let the swing go\",\"Mark the central position while the swing is at rest\",\"Count the number of oscillations\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to go to a swing at rest and mark its position on the ground first.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A student pulls a swing to the left and releases it. It goes to the right and comes back to the left. What has occurred?\",\"options\":[\"Half an oscillation\",\"One oscillation\",\"Two oscillations\",\"No oscillation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Moving from one end to the other and returning to the starting point constitutes one oscillation.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which of these is a requirement for a motion to be \'oscillatory\'?\",\"options\":[\"It must move in a straight line forever\",\"It must move back and forth on either side of a central position\",\"It must only move to one side of the central position\",\"It must stop immediately after one movement\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The definition specifies back and forth motion on either side of a central position.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the swing\'s position relative to the mark on the ground as it oscillates?\",\"options\":[\"It stays exactly above the mark at all times\",\"It moves further away from the mark and never returns\",\"It moves to either side of the mark, crossing it repeatedly\",\"It moves in a circle around the mark\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says the swing crosses the central position (the mark) again and again as it moves from one end to the other.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the \'oscillator\' in the example provided in the text.\",\"options\":[\"The ground\",\"The mark made on the ground\",\"The swing\",\"The child\'s hand\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'A swing that moves back and forth like this, is an oscillator.\'\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a swing is pulled to one side and released, but it stops exactly at the central position without moving to the other side, can we call this a complete oscillation?\",\"options\":[\"Yes, because it reached the center\",\"No, because it must move to the other end and return to the start\",\"Yes, because it moved from its starting point\",\"No, because it did not cross the ground\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"One oscillation requires the object to move to the other end and return to its starting point.\",\"topic\":\"Oscillator and Oscillatory Motion\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the maximum distance between the original position A and the position B on stretching a rubber band called?\",\"options\":[\"Frequency\",\"Amplitude of vibration\",\"Oscillation\",\"Pitch\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the maximum distance between the original position A and the stretched position B as the amplitude of vibration.\",\"topic\":\"Amplitude of vibration\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to a rubber band when it is stretched and released?\",\"options\":[\"It stops moving\",\"It changes color\",\"It vibrates\",\"It breaks immediately\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, when the rubber band is stretched and released, it vibrates.\",\"topic\":\"Amplitude of vibration\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the experiment described, which letter represents the original position of the rubber band before it is stretched?\",\"options\":[\"Position B\",\"Position C\",\"Position A\",\"Position D\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the rubber is stretched from the original position A.\",\"topic\":\"Amplitude of vibration\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When a greater force is applied to the rubber band, what happens to the amplitude?\",\"options\":[\"The amplitude decreases\",\"The amplitude increases\",\"The amplitude remains the same\",\"The amplitude becomes zero\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that when a greater force is applied, the rubber is stretched further, meaning the amplitude increases.\",\"topic\":\"Amplitude of vibration\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},