all piece of cardboard in the experiment?\",\"options\":[\"Glue\",\"Sticking tape\",\"Thread\",\"Wax\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states to stick the needle to a small piece of cardboard by means of a sticking tape.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic needle\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the experiment described, what is the purpose of marking directions on the square cardboard?\",\"options\":[\"To decorate the pot\",\"To help identify the direction in which the needle points\",\"To keep the water level steady\",\"To prevent the cardboard from sinking\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Marking directions allows the observer to find out in which direction the magnetized needle points.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic needle\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are following the instructions in the text, where should you place the pot filled with water?\",\"options\":[\"On the edge of the cardboard\",\"Under the square cardboard\",\"In the centre of the cardboard\",\"Outside the square cardboard\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly instructs to \'Place a pot filled with water in the centre of the cardboard\'.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic needle\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, based on the labels \'W\', \'E\', and \'S\', which direction is the purple arrow indicating?\",\"options\":[\"North\",\"South\",\"East\",\"West\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the diagram, \'S\' is at the bottom, \'W\' is on the left, and \'E\' is on the right; therefore, the arrow pointing towards the top indicates North.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic needle\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"46\\/137_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, a magnetic needle of a compass does not settle ______ to the ground.\",\"options\":[\"Perpendicular\",\"Parallel\",\"Vertical\",\"Opposite\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text asks why the needle does \'not settle parallel to the ground but at an angle to it\'.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic needle\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the expected behavior of the magnetized needle when it is placed on the surface of water?\",\"options\":[\"It will spin continuously\",\"It will sink to the bottom\",\"It will point in a specific direction\",\"It will dissolve in the water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The experiment is designed to find out in which direction the magnetized needle points.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic needle\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Before placing the magnetized needle on the surface of the water, what step must be taken to ensure it floats?\",\"options\":[\"Magnetize the water\",\"Stick it to a small piece of cardboard\",\"Mark directions on it\",\"Place it in a square pot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to stick the needle to a small piece of cardboard before placing it on the surface of the water.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic needle\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the purpose of placing the needle on a small piece of cardboard floating in water?\",\"options\":[\"To allow the needle to move freely and align itself\",\"To keep the needle dry so it doesn\'t lose magnetism\",\"To make the needle point towards the bottom of the pot\",\"To stop the needle from pointing North\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Floating the needle on water allows it to rotate freely to show its magnetic alignment.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic needle\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"46\\/137_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the \'Use your brain power\' section, what can be inferred about the position of a compass needle at any place?\",\"options\":[\"It always stays perfectly flat\",\"It settles at an angle to the ground\",\"It points towards the geographic South pole\",\"It only works when placed in water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the needle does not settle parallel to the ground but at an angle to it.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic needle\",\"part\":4,\