m\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, where do the magnetic lines of force go?\",\"options\":[\"From the center of the magnet to the edges\",\"From one end of the bar magnet to the other\",\"Only around the North pole\",\"In circles around the cardboard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions lines going from one end of the bar magnet to the other.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic field\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the experiment with iron filings, what action helps the filings arrange themselves into a pattern?\",\"options\":[\"Heating the cardboard\",\"Wetting the cardboard\",\"Tapping the cardboard gently\",\"Blowing air on the filings\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The procedure instructs to \'Tap the cardboard gently\' to observe the iron filings.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic field\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How is the intensity of the magnetic field at a place gauged?\",\"options\":[\"By the weight of the bar magnet\",\"By the number of lines of force passing through a unit area perpendicular to it\",\"By the size of the cardboard used\",\"By the distance between the two poles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states intensity is gauged by the number of lines of force passing through a unit area, perpendicular to that area.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic field\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If the magnetic lines of force in a certain region are \'concentrated\', what does it indicate about the magnetic field?\",\"options\":[\"The intensity is low\",\"The intensity is high\",\"There is no magnetic force\",\"The magnet is losing power\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the intensity is high where the lines of force are concentrated.\",\"topic\":\"Magnetic field\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the intensity of the magnetic field where the lines of force are \'sparse\'?\",\"options\":[\"High\",\"Low\",\"Zero\",\"Infinite\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that 