hape of a hunter, you have found a ________.\",\"options\":[\"Nebula\",\"Galaxy\",\"Constellation\",\"Planetary nebula\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Stars making a particular figure are known as a constellation.\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the lifecycle figure, which type of star will eventually result in a \'White dwarf\'?\",\"options\":[\"Ordinary star\",\"Massive star\",\"Neutron star\",\"Black hole\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the path from Ordinary star leads to a White dwarf, while the Massive star path does not.\",\"topic\":\"Observe and discuss\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"46\\/141_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the line called where the sky seems to meet the ground when looking into the distance?\",\"options\":[\"Celestial equator\",\"Horizon\",\"Meridian\",\"Ecliptic\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the horizon as the line at which the sky seems to touch the ground.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The virtual sphere on which stars and planets appear to move is known as the __________.\",\"options\":[\"Atmosphere\",\"Solar system\",\"Celestial sphere\",\"Global sphere\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the virtual sphere on which stars and planets appear to move is called the celestial sphere.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which point on the celestial sphere is located exactly above the observer\'s head?\",\"options\":[\"Nadir\",\"Celestial North Pole\",\"Zenith\",\"Ecliptic\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The point on the celestial sphere exactly above our head is called the zenith.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the point on the celestial sphere exactly below the observer\'s feet called?\",\"options\":[\"Nadir\",\"Zenith\",\"Horizon\",\"Celestial South Pole\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The point on the celestial sphere exactly below our feet is called the nadir.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The celestial sphere is divided into two halves by which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"The celestial equator\",\"The meridian\",\"The circular horizon\",\"The ecliptic\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that the circular horizon divides the celestial sphere into two halves.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you turn around yourself in an open space, what shape does the horizon appear to form?\",\"options\":[\"A square\",\"A circle\",\"A triangle\",\"A straight line\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"While turning around oneself, the horizon will be seen to form a circle.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The celestial equator is located in the same plane as which part of the Earth?\",\"options\":[\"Earth\'s axis\",\"Earth\'s North Pole\",\"Earth\'s equator\",\"Earth\'s meridian\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The celestial equator is in the same plane as the earth\'s equator.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the \'ecliptic\' in astronomy?\",\"options\":[\"The actual path of the moon around the earth\",\"The apparent motion of the sun around the earth\",\"The line where the sky meets the ground\",\"The point exactly above the observer\'s head\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ecliptic is the circle describing the apparent motion of the sun around the earth.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the Earth\'s axis of rotation is extended towards the North, where does it penetrate the celestial sphere?\",\"options\":[\"At the Zenith\",\"At the Celestial North Pole\",\"At the Celestial equator\",\"At the Meridian\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Extending the axis of rotation in the north direction penetrates the celestial sphere at the celestial North Pole.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"An astronomer wants to draw a \'Meridian\' on a star map. Which points must this circle pass through?\",\"options\":[\"Only the Zenith and Nadir\",\"Only the North and South celestial poles\",\"Both celestial poles, the Zenith, and the Nadir\",\"The celestial equator and the horizon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A meridian is a great circle passing through both celestial poles and the observer\'s zenith and nadir.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a student stands in a field and looks at the point directly beneath their feet, they are looking towards the:\",\"options\":[\"Horizon\",\"Zenith\",\"Nadir\",\"Ecliptic\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The point exactly below our feet on the celestial sphere is the nadir.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the sun appear to move along the ecliptic circle even though the sun is at the center of the solar system?\",\"options\":[\"Because the sun rotates on its own axis\",\"Because the earth moves around the sun\",\"Because the celestial sphere is spinning\",\"Because the zenith and nadir are moving\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the earth moves around the sun, but seen from earth, the sun appears to move along the ecliptic.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is described as a \'virtual sphere\' rather than a physical object in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The Earth\",\"The Sun\",\"The Celestial sphere\",\"The Ground\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly refers to the celestial sphere as a \'virtual sphere\'.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definitions provided, which two points are always exactly opposite to each other on the celestial sphere relative to the observer?\",\"options\":[\"Horizon and Ecliptic\",\"Zenith and Nadir\",\"Celestial North Pole and Zenith\",\"Celestial Equator and Horizon\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Zenith is exactly above the head and Nadir is exactly below the feet, making them opposite points.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If the Earth\'s equator were to expand uniformly in all directions, what would it form on the celestial sphere?\",\"options\":[\"The Horizon\",\"The Meridian\",\"The Celestial equator\",\"The Ecliptic\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that uniformly expanding the earth\'s equator results in the celestial equator.\",\"topic\":\"Sky watching\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the portion of the earth\'s atmosphere and the portion beyond that which can be seen in the form of a roof called?\",\"options\":[\"Space\",\"Sky\",\"Horizon\",\"Galaxy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines the sky as the portion of the atmosphere and beyond seen as a roof from the earth.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the continuous, empty space between planets and stars in the sky called?\",\"options\":[\"Atmosphere\",\"Sky\",\"Space\",\"Orbit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Space is defined as the continuous, empty space between spheres like planets and stars.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In which direction does the Earth rotate?\",\"options\":[\"East to West\",\"North to South\",\"West to East\",\"South to North\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the earth rotates from the west to the east.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do the sun, the moon, and the stars appear to rise in the east and set in the west?\",\"options\":[\"Because the sun moves around the earth\",\"Because the earth rotates from west to east\",\"Because the stars move from east to west\",\"Because of the earth\'s motion around the sun\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The apparent rising in the east and setting in the west is due to the earth\'s rotation from west to east.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following may be contained within space?\",\"options\":[\"Only solid planets\",\"Gas and dust particles\",\"Only liquid water\",\"A solid roof\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that space may contain gas and dust particles.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a star rises at 8:00 pm tonight, at what time will it rise tomorrow?\",\"options\":[\"8:04 pm\",\"8:00 pm\",\"7:56 pm\",\"7:50 pm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Stars rise and set 4 minutes earlier every day; 8:00 pm minus 4 minutes is 7:56 pm.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Against the background of stars, in which direction do the sun and the moon appear to move?\",\"options\":[\"East to West\",\"North to South\",\"West to East\",\"South to North\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that against the background of stars, the sun and moon appear to move from west to east.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many degrees does the sun appear to move every day against the background of stars?\",\"options\":[\"One degree\",\"Four degrees\",\"Twelve degrees\",\"Thirteen degrees\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states the sun moves through one degree every day.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the sun moves one degree per day, how many degrees will it appear to have moved after 5 days?\",\"options\":[\"1 degree\",\"5 degrees\",\"12 degrees\",\"20 degrees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since the sun moves one degree every day, in 5 days it moves 5 degrees.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What causes the moon to appear to move 12 to 13 degrees against the background of stars?\",\"options\":[\"The rotation of the earth on its axis\",\"The motion of the sun around the earth\",\"The motion of the moon around the earth\",\"The motion of the stars around the moon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The movement of the moon against the stars happens due to the motion of the moon around the earth.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"A star rises at 10:00 pm on Monday. At what time will it rise on Wednesday (two days later)?\",\"options\":[\"10:08 pm\",\"9:56 pm\",\"9:52 pm\",\"9:48 pm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The star rises 4 minutes earlier each day. In two days, it rises 8 minutes earlier (10:00 pm - 8 mins = 9:52 pm).\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which statement best evaluates the difference between the motion of the sun and the moon against the stars?\",\"options\":[\"The sun moves faster than the moon\",\"The moon moves much faster than the sun\",\"Both move at the exact same rate\",\"The sun moves 12 degrees while the moon moves 1 degree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sun moves 1 degree daily while the moon moves 12 to 13 degrees, meaning the moon\'s apparent motion is faster.\",\"topic\":\"Sky and space\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is a group of stars occupying a small portion of the celestial sphere called?\",\"options\":[\"A constellation\",\"A planet\",\"A galaxy\",\"A solar system\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines a constellation as a group of stars occupying a small portion of the celestial sphere.\",\"topic\":\"Constellations\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How many constellations have western observers divided the celestial sphere into?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"27\",\"88\",\"360\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that western observers have divided the celestial sphere into 88 constellations.\",\"topic\":\"Constellations\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the brightest star in a nakshatra called?\