:\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the moon takes approximately 27.3 days for one revolution, how many nakshatras did Indian astronomers suggest?\",\"options\":[\"27\",\"12\",\"88\",\"360\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text links the moon\'s revolution of ~27 days to the 27 nakshatras suggested by Indian astronomers.\",\"topic\":\"Constellations\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Calculate the approximate angular measure of one nakshatra if the 360 degrees of the celestial sphere is divided into 27 equal parts.\",\"options\":[\"30 degrees\",\"88 degrees\",\"1 degree\",\"13 degrees and 20 minutes\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text calculates that 360 degrees divided into 27 parts results in about 13 degrees and 20 minutes.\",\"topic\":\"Constellations\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why were constellations named after animals, humans, or objects?\",\"options\":[\"Because they contain exactly 88 stars each\",\"Because the moon passes through them every day\",\"Based on the figures they appear to form and ancient beliefs\",\"To match the 12 equal parts of the ecliptic\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says figures are named after events or beliefs of the times when the constellations were identified based on the shapes they appear to form.\",\"topic\":\"Constellations\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is specifically listed as a zodiac sign in the provided text?\",\"options\":[\"Yogatara\",\"Libra\",\"Nakshatra\",\"Celestial sphere\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Libra is explicitly listed in the text as one of the 12 zodiac signs.\",\"topic\":\"Constellations\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why is the angular measurement of a nakshatra (13° 20\') smaller than that of a zodiac sign (30°)?\",\"options\":[\"Because the celestial sphere is divided into 27 nakshatras but only 12 zodiac signs\",\"Because the moon moves faster than the sun\",\"Because there are 88 constellations in total\",\"