 remember - Sky watching\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student wants to observe stars that will disappear from view first during the night, which direction should they look?\",\"options\":[\"North\",\"South\",\"East\",\"West\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Stars in the west set early, so they are the first to disappear from view.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember - Sky watching\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how are the directions East and West positioned on a sky map compared to a geographical map?\",\"options\":[\"They are shown to the right and left, just like in geographical maps\",\"They are swapped compared to geographical maps\",\"They are shown at the top and bottom\",\"They are not shown on a sky map at all\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Point 5 states that as in geographical maps, east and west are shown to the right and left respectively.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember - Sky watching\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"On a sky map, which direction is shown towards the top of the map?\",\"options\":[\"North\",\"South\",\"East\",\"West\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Point 6 states that on a sky map, the south is towards the top of the map.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember - Sky watching\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why are the North and South directions placed at the bottom and top of a sky map?\",\"options\":[\"Because the stars move from North to South\",\"Because the map is designed to be held overhead\",\"Because the Pole Star is at the top of the sky\",\"Because geographical maps also place North at the bottom\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains this orientation is used because the sky map is intended to be held overhead.\",\"topic\":\"Always remember - Sky watching\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are facing North while sky watching, how should you hold the sky map?\",\"options\":[\"With the South side at the bottom\",\"With the East side at the 