साठी मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वे या दोन्हीची गरज असते.\",\"topic\":\"मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वे आणि मूलभूत हक्क\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"भारतीय संविधानात मूलभूत कर्तव्यांचा समावेश कोणत्या वर्षी करण्यात आला?\",\"options\":[\"१९५०\",\"१९६६\",\"१९७६\",\"१९८६\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"पाठ्यपुस्तकानुसार, ४२ व्या घटनादुरुस्तीने १९७६ साली मूलभूत कर्तव्ये संविधानात समाविष्ट करण्यात आली.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"कोणत्या घटनादुरुस्तीनुसार भारतीय नागरिकांच्या मूलभूत कर्तव्यांचा संविधानात समावेश झाला?\",\"options\":[\"४० वी घटनादुरुस्ती\",\"४२ वी घटनादुरुस्ती\",\"४४ वी घटनादुरुस्ती\",\"५२ वी घटनादुरुस्ती\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"संविधानातील मूलभूत कर्तव्ये ४२ व्या घटनादुरुस्तीने समाविष्ट केली गेली आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"लोकशाहीत नागरिकांवर असणारी \'दुहेरी जबाबदारी\' म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"निवडणूक लढवणे आणि मतदान करणे\",\"कर भरणे आणि समाजसेवा करणे\",\"हक्कांबाबत जागरूक राहणे आणि कर्तव्ये पार पाडणे\",\"शिक्षण घेणे आणि नोकरी करणे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"लोकशाहीत नागरिकांना हक्कांबाबत जागरूक राहावे लागते आणि कर्तव्येही पार पाडावी लागतात, हीच दुहेरी जबाबदारी होय.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"शासनाने केलेल्या सुधारणांचे लाभ सर्वांना मिळण्यासाठी नागरिकांनी काय करणे आवश्यक आहे?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ हक्कांची मागणी करणे\",\"शासकीय योजनांवर टीका करणे\",\"आपली मूलभूत कर्तव्ये पार पाडणे\",\"परदेशात जाऊन शिक्षण घेणे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"नागरिक जोपर्यंत आपली मूलभूत कर्तव्ये पार पाडत नाहीत, तोपर्यंत सुधारणांचे लाभ सर्वांना मिळत नाहीत.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"\'स्वच्छ भारत\' अभियानाचे उदाहरण देऊन पाठ्यपुस्तकात लोकांच्या कोणत्या सवयीत बदल होणे गरजेचे असल्याचे म्हटले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"कमी पाणी वापरण्याची सवय\",\"सार्वजनिक ठिकाणी अस्वच्छता करण्याची सवय\",\"झाडे लावण्याची सवय\",\"व्यायाम न करण्याची सवय\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"स्वच्छ भारत अभियानासाठी लोकांनी सार्वजनिक ठिकाणी अस्वच्छता निर्माण करण्याच्या सवयी बदलल्या पाहिजेत.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"संविधानानुसार नागरिकांनी राष्ट्रध्वज आणि राष्ट्रगीतासोबतच आणखी कशाचा आदर करणे बंधनकारक आहे?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ राजकीय नेत्यांचा\",\"संविधानातील आदर्शांचा\",\"केवळ स्वतःच्या धर्माचा\",\"परकीय संस्कृतीचा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"प्रत्येक नागरिकाने संविधानाचे पालन करावे आणि त्यातील आदर्शांचा आदर करावा असे कर्तव्यात नमूद आहे.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"स्त्रियांच्या सन्मानासाठी नागरिकांनी कोणते कर्तव्य पार पाडणे अपेक्षित आहे?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ स्त्रियांना शिक्षण देणे\",\"स्त्रियांच्या प्रतिष्ठेला कमीपणा आणणाऱ्या प्रथांचा त्याग करणे\",\"स्त्रियांना केवळ घरकाम सांगणे\",\"स्त्रियांना मतदानाचा हक्क नाकारणे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"स्त्रियांच्या प्रतिष्ठेला बाधा आणणाऱ्या प्रथांचा त्याग करणे हे भारतीय नागरिकांचे मूलभूत कर्तव्य आहे.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"एखाद्या जखमी प्राण्याला मदत करणे, हे कोणत्या मूलभूत कर्तव्याशी संबंधित आहे?\",\"options\":[\"वैज्ञानिक दृष्टी बाळगणे\",\"देशाचे रक्षण करणे\",\"सजीव प्राण्यांबद्दल दयाबुद्धी बाळगणे\",\"सार्वजनिक मालमत्तेचे जतन करणे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"नैसर्गिक पर्यावरणाचे जतन आणि सजीव प्राण्यांबद्दल दयाबुद्धी बाळगणे हे एक मूलभूत कर्तव्य आहे.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"नागरिकांनी \'वैज्ञानिक दृष्टी\' आणि \'मानवतावाद\' अंगी बाळगावा, असे का म्हटले असावे?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ परीक्षेत पास होण्यासाठी\",\"अंधश्रद्धा दूर करून प्रगतीशील समाज घडवण्यासाठी\",\"परदेशात नोकरी मिळवण्यासाठी\",\"केवळ यंत्रांचा वापर वाढवण्यासाठी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"वैज्ञानिक दृष्टी, मानवतावाद आणि जिज्ञासूवृत्ती अंगी बाळगणे हे देशाच्या प्रगतीसाठी आवश्यक कर्तव्य आहे.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"देशाचे सार्वभौमत्व, एकता व अखंडत्व सुरक्षित ठेवण्यासाठी नागरिकांनी कसे असावे?\",\"options\":[\"उदासीन असावे\",\"प्रयत्नशील असावे\",\"केवळ टीकाकार असावे\",\"स्वार्थी असावे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"देशाचे सार्वभौमत्व, एकता व अखंडत्व टिकवणे हे नागरिकांचे कर्तव्य असून त्यासाठी त्यांनी प्रयत्नशील राहणे गरजेचे आहे.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"सार्वजनिक मालमत्तेचे जतन करण्यासोबतच नागरिकांनी कशाचा त्याग करणे आवश्यक आहे?\",\"options\":[\"अहिंसेचा\",\"हिंसेचा\",\"शांततेचा\",\"सहकार्याचा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्यानुसार नागरिकांनी सार्वजनिक मालमत्तेचे जतन करावे आणि हिंसेचा त्याग करावा.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"देशाची उत्तरोत्तर प्रगती होण्यासाठी नागरिकांनी कोणत्या कार्यात उच्चत्त्वाची पातळी गाठण्याचा प्रयत्न करावा?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ स्वतःच्या फायद्याच्या कार्यात\",\"केवळ करमणुकीच्या कार्यात\",\"व्यक्तिगत व सामूहिक कार्यात\",\"केवळ परदेशी व्यापारात\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"देशाच्या प्रगतीसाठी व्यक्तिगत व सामूहिक अशा दोन्ही कार्यात उच्चत्त्वाची पातळी गाठणे हे कर्तव्य आहे.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"स्वातंत्र्याच्या चळवळीला प्रेरणा देणाऱ्या आदर्शांचे पालन करणे हे कर्तव्य का महत्त्वाचे आहे?\",\"options\":[\"कारण ते केवळ इतिहासात दिले आहे\",\"कारण त्यामुळे देशाप्रती निष्ठा आणि राष्ट्रप्रेम टिकून राहते\",\"कारण ते पाळणे सक्तीचे नाही\",\"कारण त्यामुळे केवळ मनोरंजन होते\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"स्वातंत्र्य चळवळीचे आदर्श आपल्याला लोकशाही आणि राष्ट्रवादाची प्रेरणा देतात, म्हणून त्यांचे पालन करणे आवश्यक आहे.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात मुलगा ऐतिहासिक वास्तूवर नाव कोरत आहे, ही कृती कोणत्या कर्तव्याच्या विरोधात आहे?\",\"options\":[\"वैज्ञानिक दृष्टी बाळगणे\",\"देशाची सेवा करणे\",\"संमिश्र संस्कृतीच्या वारशाचे जतन करणे\",\"बंधुत्वाची भावना जोपासणे\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"ऐतिहासिक वास्तू हा आपल्या संस्कृतीचा वारसा आहे, त्यावर नाव कोरणे हे वारसा जतन करण्याच्या कर्तव्याचे उल्लंघन आहे.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"51\\/095_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रातील मुलाची कृती थांबवण्यासाठी तुम्ही त्याला कोणत्या जबाबदारीची जाणीव करून द्याल?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ स्वतःच्या घराची स्वच्छता ठेवण्याची\",\"सार्वजनिक मालमत्तेचे व ऐतिहासिक वारशाचे जतन करण्याची\",\"केवळ शाळेचा अभ्यास करण्याची\",\"चित्रे काढण्याची कला जोपासण्याची\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"ऐतिहासिक वास्तूंचे विद्रुपीकरण करणे चुकीचे असून त्यांचे जतन करणे ही प्रत्येक नागरिकाची जबाबदारी आहे.\",\"topic\":\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"51\\/095_101.jpg\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(22055,51,7,'History & Civics','mr','नागरिकशास्त्र : मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वे व मूलभूत कर्तव्ये','[\"नागरिक म्हणजे देशाचा सदस्य, ज्याला हक्के व कर्तव्ये मिळतात.\",\"भारतीय संविधानातील मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वे राज्याच्या कार्यसूचनेचे दिशानिर्देश देतात.\",\"मूलभूत कर्तव्ये नागरिकांचे देशाबद्दलचे कर्तव्य आहेत, जे संविधानाच्या भाग IV-A मध्ये आहेत.\",\"शिक्षण हा ६ ते १४ वयाचा मूलभूत हक्क आहे, जे राज्याने पुरवावा लागतो.\",\"सर्व नागरिकांना समानता, स्वातंत्र्य, भाईचारा यांचे मूल्य पाळणे आवश्यक आहे.\",\"सार्वजनिक संपत्तीचा संरक्षण व योग्य वापर प्रत्येक नागरिकाचा कर्तव्य आहे.\",\"पर्यावरणाचे संरक्षण करणे व प्रदूषण टाळणे नागरिकांचा कर्तव्य आहे.\",\"राष्ट्रध्वज, राष्ट्रगीत यांचे आदर करणे व त्यांचे अपमान न करणे कर्तव्य आहे.\",\"वृद्धांसाठी पेंशन योजना, आरोग्यसेवा योजना सारखे मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वे राज्याने लागू केली जातात.\",\"सर्व धर्मांचे सन्मान व त्यांचे सण-उत्सवात सहभागी होणे नागरिकत्वाचा भाग आहे.\",\"लिंगभेद आधारित वेतन भेदभाव करणे संविधानात प्रतिबंधित आहे.\",\"नागरिकांना कर देणे, कायदे पालन करणे, राष्ट्रीय सेवा देणे यांचा पालन करावा.\",\"शिक्षण हा हक्क असल्याने पण तेथे सुविधा नसलेली शाळा जाणे असेल तर त्याची जबाबदारी नागरिकांची आहे.\",\"संविधानातील मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वे न्याय्य सामाजिक आर्थिक राज्य स्थापित करण्यासाठी आहेत.\",\"नागरिकांचे मूलभूत कर्तव्ये त्यांचे हक्कांचे संतुलन ठेवतात.\"]','[{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात मुलगा नदीतील कोणत्या प्रकारच्या कचऱ्याबद्दल बोलत आहे?\",\"options\":[\"काचेचा कचरा\",\"प्लास्टिकचा कचरा\",\"कागदी कचरा\",\"लोखंडी कचरा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"चित्रातील मजकुरानुसार, मुलगा नदीतील प्लास्टिकच्या कचऱ्याबद्दल बोलत आहे.\",\"topic\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"51\\/096_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या चित्रात मुलगी कोणत्या समस्येकडे लक्ष वेधत आहे?\",\"options\":[\"पाण्याचे प्रदूषण\",\"वायू प्रदूषण\",\"कानठळ्या बसवणारे आवाज\",\"रस्त्यावरील गर्दी\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"चित्रात मुलगी \'कानठळ्या बसवणाऱ्या त्या आवाजांचे काय करायचे?\' असा प्रश्न विचारत आहे.\",\"topic\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"51\\/096_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"मुला-मुलींना कोठे जाण्यासाठी सांगणे ही आपली जबाबदारी आहे असे पाठात म्हटले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"बागेत\",\"शाळेत\",\"बाजारात\",\"कचेरीत\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पाठातील निश्चयानुसार, मुला-मुलींना शाळेत जाण्यासाठी सांगणे ही आपली जबाबदारी आहे.\",\"topic\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"सार्वजनिक सुविधांचा वापर आपण कसा केला पाहिजे?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ स्वतःच्या फायद्यासाठी\",\"जबाबदारीने आणि योग्य प्रकारे\",\"कसाही केला तरी चालेल\",\"वापर करणे टाळले पाहिजे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सार्वजनिक सुविधांचा योग्य वापर व काळजी घेणे ही नागरिकाची जबाबदारी आहे.\",\"topic\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"हाती घेतलेली सर्व कामे कोणत्या पद्धतीने करणे अपेक्षित आहे?\",\"options\":[\"कमी वेळात आणि घाईने\",\"दुसऱ्याच्या मदतीने\",\"प्रामाणिकपणे आणि उत्तम रीतीने\",\"केवळ पैशांसाठी\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"पाठात नमूद केल्याप्रमाणे हाती घेतलेली कामे प्रामाणिकपणे आणि उत्तम रीतीने करावीत.\",\"topic\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"पर्यावरण दूषित न करता सण साजरे करणे म्हणजे नेमके काय?\",\"options\":[\"सण साजरे करणे बंद करणे\",\"फटाके आणि आवाजाचे प्रदूषण टाळणे\",\"केवळ स्वतःच्या धर्माचे सण साजरे करणे\",\"नदीत कचरा टाकून सण साजरे करणे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पर्यावरण दूषित न करता सण साजरे करणे म्हणजे प्रदूषणाला आळा घालणे होय.\",\"topic\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"जर तुमच्या शाळेतील बाके (Desks) कोणीतरी खराब करत असेल, तर तुम्ही कोणत्या जबाबदारीचे पालन कराल?\",\"options\":[\"शाळेतील सुविधांचा जबाबदारीने वापर करणे\",\"पर्यावरण रक्षण करणे\",\"केवळ स्वतःचा अभ्यास करणे\",\"देशाविषयी अभिमान बाळगणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"शाळेतील सुविधांची काळजी घेणे ही एक महत्त्वाची नागरी जबाबदारी आहे.\",\"topic\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"दिवाळीत फटाके न वाजवण्याचा निर्णय घेणे, हे खालीलपैकी कोणत्या निश्चयाशी संबंधित आहे?\",\"options\":[\"शाळेत जाणे\",\"सार्वजनिक सुविधांचा वापर\",\"पर्यावरण दूषित न करता सण साजरे करणे\",\"कामात प्रामाणिकपणा\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"फटाके न वाजवणे हे पर्यावरण पूरक सण साजरा करण्याच्या निश्चयाचा भाग आहे.\",\"topic\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"पाठातील संवादावरून लोकांच्या कोणत्या वृत्तीबद्दल खेद व्यक्त केला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"लोक खूप काम करतात\",\"लोकांना जबाबदाऱ्यांचे भान राहत नाही\",\"लोक खूप शिकलेले आहेत\",\"लोक नेहमी मदत करतात\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"उलटच सारे करतात याचे भानच राहत नाही लोकांना, या वाक्यातून लोकांच्या बेजबाबदारपणाबद्दल सांगितले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या पार पाडण्यासाठी पाठात कोणता मार्ग सुचवला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"दुसऱ्यांनी सुरुवात करण्याची वाट पाहणे\",\"स्वतःपासून हळूहळू सुरुवात करून निश्चय करणे\",\"केवळ तक्रारी करत राहणे\",\"नदीत कचरा टाकणाऱ्यांना शिक्षा करणे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"आपण हळूहळू सुरुवात तर करूया... काही निश्चय करूया, असे पाठात सुचवले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"नागरिक म्हणून आपल्या जबाबदाऱ्या\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"६ ते १४ वर्षे वयोगटांतील मुला-मुलींना कोणता अधिकार मिळाला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"उच्च शिक्षणाचा अधिकार\",\"प्राथमिक शिक्षणाचा अधिकार\",\"नोकरी करण्याचा अधिकार\",\"मतदानाचा अधिकार\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुराप्रमाणे ६ ते १४ वर्षे वयोगटांतील मुलांना प्राथमिक शिक्षणाचा अधिकार मिळाला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"तुम्हांला काय वाटते?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"मजकुरामध्ये हक्क आणि कशाचा संबंध विचारला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"नफा\",\"कर्तव्ये\",\"खेळ\",\"इतिहास\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुरात \'हक्क आणि कर्तव्ये यांचा काही संबंध असतो का?\' असा प्रश्न विचारला आहे.\",\"topic\":\"तुम्हांला काय वाटते?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"काही मुले-मुली शाळेत का जाऊ शकत नाहीत?\",\"options\":[\"त्यांना खेळायला आवडते म्हणून\",\"शाळा खूप लांब आहे म्हणून\",\"आई-वडिलांना आर्थिक मदत करण्यासाठी काम करावे लागते म्हणून\",\"त्यांना सुट्टी हवी असते म्हणून\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"आई-वडिलांना आर्थिक मदत करण्यासाठी काम करावे लागत असल्याने काही मुले शाळेत जाऊ शकत नाहीत.\",\"topic\":\"तुम्हांला काय वाटते?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"६ ते १४ वर्षे वयोगटांतील मुलांच्या बाबतीत काय आवश्यक आहे?\",\"options\":[\"त्यांनी कारखान्यात काम करणे\",\"सर्व मुले-मुली शाळेत असणे\",\"त्यांनी फक्त घरी राहणे\",\"त्यांनी प्रवास करणे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मजकुराप्रमाणे या वयोगटांतील सर्व मुले-मुली शाळेत असणे आवश्यक आहे.\",\"topic\":\"तुम्हांला काय वाटते?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"कर्तव्यांचे पालन केल्याने काय होते, या प्रश्नातून कोणता बोध होतो?\",\"options\":[\"कर्तव्यांचे महत्त्व समजते\",\"केवळ हक्क महत्त्वाचे आहेत\",\"शाळेत जाणे गरजेचे नाही\",\"आर्थिक मदत करणे हेच एकमेव कर्तव्य आहे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कर्तव्यांचे पालन केल्याने होणाऱ्या परिणामांवर विचार केल्यास कर्तव्यांचे महत्त्व समजते.\",\"topic\":\"तुम्हांला काय वाटते?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"एखादा १० वर्षांचा मुलगा हॉटेलमध्ये काम करत असेल, तर त्याच्या कोणत्या अधिकाराचे उल्लंघन होत आहे?\",\"options\":[\"खेळण्याचा अधिकार\",\"प्राथमिक शिक्षणाचा अधिकार\",\"फिरण्याचा अधिकार\",\"जेवणाचा अधिकार\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"६ ते १४ वयोगटातील मुलाला प्राथमिक शिक्षणाचा अधिकार असल्याने काम करणे हे त्या अधिकाराचे उल्लंघन आहे.\",\"topic\":\"तुम्हांला काय वाटते?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"मुलांना शाळेत आणण्याचा आग्रह धरणे अन्यायकारक आहे का, हा प्रश्न काय दर्शवतो?\",\"options\":[\"शिक्षणापेक्षा काम महत्त्वाचे आहे\",\"मुलांच्या परिस्थितीचा आणि कर्तव्यांचा विचार करण्याची गरज\",\"शाळेत जाणे बंधनकारक नाही\",\"पालकांचे उत्पन्न वाढवणे हेच ध्येय आहे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"हा प्रश्न मुलांची परिस्थिती आणि शिक्षणाचे कर्तव्य यातील संघर्षावर विचार करण्यास प्रवृत्त करतो.\",\"topic\":\"तुम्हांला काय वाटते?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"जर हक्क आणि कर्तव्ये एकाच नाण्याच्या दोन बाजू असतील, तर शिक्षण हा हक्क असल्यास शाळेत जाणे हे काय असेल?\",\"options\":[\"केवळ एक छंद\",\"एक कर्तव्य\",\"एक ओझे\",\"एक खेळ\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"हक्क आणि कर्तव्ये संबंधित असल्याने, शिक्षण हा हक्क असल्यास शाळेत जाणे हे मुलांचे आणि पालकांचे कर्तव्य ठरते.\",\"topic\":\"तुम्हांला काय वाटते?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"मजकुरातील \'आर्थिक मदत\' या शब्दाचा संबंध कशाशी आहे?\",\"options\":[\"मुलांचे खेळणे\",\"मुलांचे काम करणे\",\"शाळेची फी\",\"पुस्तकांचा खर्च\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"आई-वडिलांना आर्थिक मदत करण्यासाठी मुलांना काम करावे लागते, असे मजकुरात म्हटले आहे.\",\"topic\":\"तुम्हांला काय वाटते?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"शाळेत न जाणाऱ्या मुलांना शाळेत आणण्याचा आग्रह धरणे, या कृतीचे मूल्यमापन करताना कोणता मुद्दा महत्त्वाचा ठरेल?\",\"options\":[\"मुलांचे वय आणि शिक्षणाचा अधिकार\",\"मुलांना मिळणारा पगार\",\"मुलांच्या कामाचे स्वरूप\",\"शाळेची सुट्टी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मुलांचे वय (६-१४) आणि त्यांचा शिक्षणाचा अधिकार हे या कृतीचे मूल्यमापन करण्यासाठी महत्त्वाचे आहेत.\",\"topic\":\"तुम्हांला काय वाटते?\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"८ व्या शतकात सिंधवर कोणी स्वारी केली होती?\",\"options\":[\"मुहम्मद घोरी\",\"मुहम्मद बिन कासिम\",\"तैमूरलंग\",\"बाबर\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पाठ्यपुस्तकातील कालपटानुसार, ८ व्या शतकात मुहम्मद बिन कासिमची सिंधवर स्वारी झाली होती.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"मुघल राजवटीची सुरुवात कोणत्या शतकात झाली?\",\"options\":[\"१४ वे शतक\",\"१५ वे शतक\",\"१६ वे शतक\",\"१७ वे शतक\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"१६ व्या शतकात दिल्लीवरील सुलतानशाही संपुष्टात येऊन मुघल राजवट सुरू झाली.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"१३ व्या शतकात दिल्लीचा सुलतान म्हणून कोणाची कारकीर्द सुरू झाली?\",\"options\":[\"कुतुबुद्दीन ऐबक\",\"अकबर\",\"औरंगजेब\",\"पहिला बाजीराव\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"१३ व्या शतकात कुतुबुद्दीन ऐबक दिल्लीचा सुलतान झाला.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"१४ व्या शतकात राजधानी दिल्लीहून कोठे हलवण्यात आली होती?\",\"options\":[\"पुणे\",\"सिंध\",\"देवगिरी\",\"पैठण\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"१४ व्या शतकात तुघलक सत्तेच्या काळात राजधानी दिल्लीहून देवगिरीला व परत दिल्लीला नेण्यात आली.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"१५ व्या शतकात महाराष्ट्रात कोणत्या पंथांचा उल्लेख कालपटात आढळतो?\",\"options\":[\"भक्ती पंथ व सूफी पंथ\",\"वारकरी पंथ व महानुभाव पंथ\",\"नाथ पंथ व दत्त पंथ\",\"शिख पंथ व जैन पंथ\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"१५ व्या शतकाच्या नोंदीमध्ये वारकरी पंथ आणि महानुभाव पंथ यांचा उल्लेख आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"छत्रपती शिवाजी महाराजांचा राज्याभिषेक कोणत्या शतकात झाला?\",\"options\":[\"१६ वे शतक\",\"१७ वे शतक\",\"१८ वे शतक\",\"१९ वे शतक\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"१७ व्या शतकात स्वराज्यस्थापना आणि महाराजांचा राज्याभिषेक या महत्त्वाच्या घटना घडल्या.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"१८ व्या शतकात मराठ्यांनी कोणाचा पराभव केला होता?\",\"options\":[\"मुघलांचा\",\"इंग्रजांचा\",\"पोर्तुगिजांचा\",\"तुर्कांचा\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"१८ व्या शतकात मराठ्यांकडून पोर्तुगिजांचा पराभव झाला, अशी नोंद कालपटात आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या कालपटात ८ व्या शतकाच्या रकान्यात \'मुहम्मद बिन कासिमची स्वारी\' सोबत कोणत्या घराण्याचा उल्लेख आहे?\",\"options\":[\"चोळ घराणे\",\"पाल घराणे\",\"यादव घराणे\",\"होयसळ घराणे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"आकृतीमधील ८ व्या शतकाच्या रकान्यात पाल घराण्याचा उल्लेख स्पष्टपणे दिसतो.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"51\\/098_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"दिलेल्या कालपटाचे निरीक्षण केल्यास, \'पानिपतची लढाई\' कोणत्या शतकात झाल्याचे समजते?\",\"options\":[\"१६ व्या\",\"१७ व्या\",\"१८ व्या\",\"१९ व्या\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"आकृतीमधील १८ व्या शतकाच्या घटनांच्या यादीत पानिपत लढाईचा समावेश आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"51\\/098_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"सम्राट अकबराचा संघर्ष खालीलपैकी कोणाशी झाला नाही?\",\"options\":[\"महाराणा प्रताप\",\"चांदबिबी\",\"राणी दुर्गावती\",\"सुलतान रझिया\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"सुलतान रझिया १३ व्या शतकात होती, तर अकबराचा संघर्ष महाराणा प्रताप, चांदबिबी आणि राणी दुर्गावती यांच्याशी झाला.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"१९ व्या शतकातील भारताच्या राजकीय स्थितीबाबत कोणता महत्त्वाचा बदल कालपटात नोंदवला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"मुघल सत्तेचा उदय\",\"इंग्रजांकडून मराठ्यांचा पराभव\",\"विजयनगरची स्थापना\",\"स्वराज्य स्थापना\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"१९ व्या शतकात दुसरा बाजीराव पेशवे यांची कारकीर्द आणि इंग्रजांकडून मराठ्यांचा पराभव या घटना घडल्या.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"११ व्या शतकात भारतावर कोणाची स्वारी झाली होती?\",\"options\":[\"गझनीचा महमूद\",\"मुहम्मद घोरी\",\"तैमूरलंग\",\"बाबर\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कालपटातील ११ व्या शतकाच्या नोंदीनुसार गझनीच्या महमूदाची भारतावर स्वारी झाली होती.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"जर तुम्हाला विजयनगर आणि बहमनी राज्याच्या स्थापनेचा इतिहास अभ्यासायचा असेल, तर तुम्ही कोणत्या शतकातील माहिती पाहाल?\",\"options\":[\"१२ वे शतक\",\"१३ वे शतक\",\"१४ वे शतक\",\"१५ वे शतक\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"विजयनगर आणि बहमनी राज्याची स्थापना १४ व्या शतकात झाली आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"कालपटातील घटनांच्या क्रमानुसार, मुघल-शीख संघर्ष कोणत्या शतकात झाला?\",\"options\":[\"१५ वे शतक\",\"१६ वे शतक\",\"१७ वे शतक\",\"१८ वे शतक\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"१७ व्या शतकात छत्रपती शिवाजी महाराजांच्या कारकीर्दीसोबतच मुघल-शीख संघर्षाचा उल्लेख आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"कालपटावरून असे समजते की, १२ व्या शतकात कोणत्या घराण्याची राजवट संपुष्टात आली?\",\"options\":[\"पाल घराणे\",\"राष्ट्रकूट घराणे\",\"यादव घराणे\",\"गुर्जर-प्रतिहार\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"१२ व्या शतकाच्या रकान्यात \'यादव घराणे संपुष्टात\' अशी नोंद दिलेली आहे.\",\"topic\":\"कालपट - ८ वे शतक ते १९ वे शतक\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(22056,52,8,'English','en','1.1 Be the Best','[\"Be the best means doing your best in whatever role you have, not just the most important one.\",\"A pine tree is tall and at the top of a hill; a scrub is a small plant that grows in the valley.\",\"A rill is a small stream; a lake is a large body of water.\",\"A muskie (muskellunge) and a bass are types of fish; a bass can also mean a low voice.\",\"A highway is a main road; a trail is a narrow path beside it.\",\"A captain is the leader of a ship; crew are the sailors who work on the ship.\",\"The poem says success is not about size or position but about being the best you can be.\",\"The moral: use your strengths and be proud of your role.\",\"In the word sets, arrange from smallest to largest: seed‑sapling‑plant‑tree, baby‑child‑youth‑adult, stone‑rock‑hill‑mountain, river‑stream‑sea‑ocean.\",\"In the story of the Lion and the Mouse, the mouse helps the lion by chewing the net so the lion can escape.\"]','[{\"q\":\"In the \'Chit-Chat\' section, which of the following is asked regarding success and failure?\",\"options\":[\"We should only accept success.\",\"We should accept success as well as failure.\",\"Failure is not important.\",\"Success is the only goal.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Question 4 of the Chit-Chat section asks if we should accept success as well as failure.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct increasing order of size for the water bodies mentioned in set (a)?\",\"options\":[\"Ocean, sea, river, stream\",\"Sea, ocean, stream, river\",\"Stream, river, sea, ocean\",\"River, stream, ocean, sea\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In increasing order of size, a stream is smallest, followed by a river, then a sea, and finally an ocean.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word represents the smallest unit in the set: hill, stone, mountain, rock?\",\"options\":[\"Hill\",\"Stone\",\"Mountain\",\"Rock\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A stone is the smallest geological feature among the options provided in set (b).\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Arrange the following in the correct order of biological growth: plant, sapling, tree, seed.\",\"options\":[\"Seed, sapling, plant, tree\",\"Tree, plant, sapling, seed\",\"Sapling, seed, tree, plant\",\"Plant, tree, seed, sapling\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Growth starts from a seed, becomes a sapling, then a plant, and finally a tree.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the human growth set (d), which stage comes immediately after \'child\' when arranged in increasing order?\",\"options\":[\"Baby\",\"Adult\",\"Youth\",\"Infant\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Following the sequence of growth: baby -> child -> youth -> adult.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The Chit-Chat section asks for your reaction if you are not selected in a _____.\",\"options\":[\"Competition\",\"Team\",\"Class\",\"Race\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Question 5 specifically mentions the reaction to not being selected in a team.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from set (b) is larger than a \'rock\' but smaller than a \'mountain\'?\",\"options\":[\"Stone\",\"Pebble\",\"Hill\",\"Boulder\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the increasing order of size for set (b), a hill is larger than a rock and smaller than a mountain.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the common theme for the words: child, adult, baby, youth?\",\"options\":[\"Types of professions\",\"Stages of human growth\",\"Family members\",\"School grades\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"These words represent the different stages a human goes through during growth.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instructions in 1.B, how should the sets of words be rearranged?\",\"options\":[\"Alphabetical order\",\"Decreasing order of importance\",\"Increasing order of size\\/growth\",\"Random order\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Instruction 1.B explicitly asks to rearrange the words according to the increasing order of their size\\/growth.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If \'ocean\' is the largest in its set, which word is the largest in the set containing \'sapling\'?\",\"options\":[\"Seed\",\"Plant\",\"Tree\",\"Forest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the set (c) provided in the text, \'tree\' is the final stage of growth and the largest.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the lion sleeping at the beginning of the story?\",\"options\":[\"In a cave\",\"In a forest\",\"Under a bush\",\"In a cage\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the lion was sleeping in a forest.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the mouse do that caused the lion to wake up?\",\"options\":[\"It bit the lion\'s tail\",\"It squeaked loudly\",\"It started playing on him\",\"It stole the lion\'s food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the mouse started playing on the lion, causing him to get up.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the lion feel when he caught the mouse?\",\"options\":[\"He was amused\",\"He was angry\",\"He was frightened\",\"He was confused\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the lion got up \'angrily\' after the mouse played on him.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did the mouse promise the lion so that he would let it go?\",\"options\":[\"It would bring the lion food\",\"It would never play again\",\"It would help the lion someday\",\"It would lead the lion to the hunters\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The mouse begged to be left alone and said it would help the lion someday.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the lion\'s immediate reaction to the mouse\'s promise of help?\",\"options\":[\"He roared in anger\",\"He laughed\",\"He ignored the mouse\",\"He thanked the mouse\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the gap-fill words, the lion \'laughed\' and let the mouse go.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did the lion get trapped later in the story?\",\"options\":[\"He fell into a deep pit\",\"He was caught in a net\",\"He was locked in a wooden cage\",\"He was tied to a tree with ropes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the lion was caught in a net set up by hunters.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the lion do while he was trying to escape the hunters\' net?\",\"options\":[\"He cried for help\",\"He stayed very quiet\",\"He roared loudly\",\"He bit the net\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says he \'roared loudly\' as he tried to escape.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the mouse know the lion was in trouble?\",\"options\":[\"It saw the hunters\",\"It heard the lion\'s roar\",\"The lion called its name\",\"Another animal told the mouse\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text indicates the mouse \'heard\' the lion and came to help.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which physical feature of the mouse was used to free the lion?\",\"options\":[\"Its long tail\",\"Its small size\",\"Its sharp teeth\",\"Its fast legs\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies the mouse chewed the net with its \'sharp teeth\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was the final outcome for the lion after the mouse arrived?\",\"options\":[\"He was caught by hunters\",\"He was set free\",\"He ate the mouse\",\"He ran away to another forest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that the mouse set the lion \'free\'.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text describes the action of the mouse on the net?\",\"options\":[\"Pulled\",\"Cut\",\"Chewed\",\"Broke\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The word \'chewed\' is provided in the box to describe how the mouse handled the net.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the events of the story, which moral is most appropriate?\",\"options\":[\"Might is right\",\"A friend in need is a friend indeed\",\"Look before you leap\",\"Unity is strength\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The story demonstrates that even a small friend (the mouse) can be a great help to a large friend (the lion) in times of trouble.\",\"topic\":\"The Lion and the Mouse\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the author of the poem \'Be The Best\'?\",\"options\":[\"Douglas Malloch\",\"Robert Frost\",\"Walt Whitman\",\"William Wordsworth\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The name \'Douglas Malloch\' is mentioned at the end of the poem as the author.\",\"topic\":\"Be The Best\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, if you cannot be a pine on the top of the hill, what should you be?\",\"options\":[\"A tall tree\",\"A scrub in the valley\",\"A captain of a ship\",\"A muskie in the lake\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first stanza states, \'If you can\'t be a pine on the top of the hill, Be a scrub in the valley\'.\",\"topic\":\"Be The Best\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the poem suggest the \'best little scrub\' should be located?\",\"options\":[\"On the highway\",\"In the middle of the lake\",\"By the side of the rill\",\"On the top of the hill\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions being the \'best little scrub by the side of the rill\'.\",\"topic\":\"Be The Best\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a person cannot be a \'muskie\', what kind of \'bass\' does the poet encourage them to be?\",\"options\":[\"The largest bass\",\"The quietest bass\",\"The liveliest bass\",\"The oldest bass\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The second stanza says, \'If you can\'t be a muskie then just be a bass – But the liveliest bass in the lake!\'\",\"topic\":\"Be The Best\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In a team setting, if everyone cannot be a \'captain\', what must they be according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Leaders\",\"Crew\",\"Stars\",\"Muskies\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The third stanza states, \'We can\'t all be captains, we\'ve got to be crew\'.\",\"topic\":\"Be The Best\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet mean by the line \'It isn\'t by size that you win or you fail\'?\",\"options\":[\"Only big things are successful\",\"Success depends on your effort and quality, not your position or size\",\"Small things always fail in life\",\"Size is the only way to measure winning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem emphasizes being the \'best\' of whatever you are, regardless of how big or small the role is.\",\"topic\":\"Be The Best\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the central message or theme of the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Always try to change who you are\",\"Only big tasks are worth doing\",\"Be the best version of yourself in whatever role you have\",\"Winning is only possible if you are the sun\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The final line \'Be the best of whatever you are!\' summarizes the theme of performing every role to its best potential.\",\"topic\":\"Be The Best\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"If you cannot be a highway, what does the poet suggest you be?\",\"options\":[\"A star\",\"A trail\",\"A bush\",\"A tree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The fourth stanza says, \'If you can\'t be a highway then just be a trail\'.\",\"topic\":\"Be The Best\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what specific flowers are illustrated at the bottom of the page?\",\"options\":[\"Sunflowers\",\"Red roses\",\"White lilies\",\"Lotus flowers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The illustration at the bottom of the figure clearly shows red roses with green leaves.\",\"topic\":\"Be The Best\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/013_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text in the given figure, which word is used to describe the type of work that is the opposite of \'big\'?\",\"options\":[\"Small\",\"Tiny\",\"Lesser\",\"Near\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text in the figure says, \'There\'s big work to do, and there\'s lesser, to do\'.\",\"topic\":\"Be The Best\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/013_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the definition of a \'rill\' according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"A narrow path\",\"A stream\",\"A type of fish\",\"A low plant\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines a \'rill\' as a stream.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What are \'muskie\' and \'bass\'?\",\"options\":[\"Types of sailors\",\"Names of plants\",\"Names of fish\",\"Types of paths\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that muskie and bass are names of fish.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does the word \'lesser\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Important\",\"Smaller\",\"Unimportant\",\"Faster\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The vocabulary list defines \'lesser\' as \'unimportant\'.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the text describe a \'scrub\'?\",\"options\":[\"A tall pine tree found on mountains\",\"An area covered with small, low plants\",\"A group of sailors working together\",\"A narrow path for walking\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines scrub as an area covered with small, low plants.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific role of a \'crew\' as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"People who plant trees\",\"People who walk on trails\",\"Sailors who work on a ship\",\"People who live along the highway\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'crew\' as sailors who work on a ship.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are walking on a \'trail\', what are you walking on?\",\"options\":[\"A wide highway\",\"A flowing stream\",\"A narrow path\",\"A large ship\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a \'trail\' as a narrow path.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person is described as a member of a \'crew\', where are they most likely working?\",\"options\":[\"In a scrub area\",\"On a highway\",\"On a ship\",\"Along a rill\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since a crew consists of sailors, they would be working on a ship.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a gardener wants to plant a \'scrub\', what should they look for?\",\"options\":[\"Tall pine seeds\",\"Small, low plants\",\"A narrow walking path\",\"A stream of water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A scrub is characterized by small, low plants according to the text.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the definitions, what is the main physical difference between a pine tree and a scrub?\",\"options\":[\"One is a fish and the other is a plant\",\"One is a sailor and the other is a path\",\"One is tall\\/large while the other consists of small\\/low plants\",\"One is found in a rill and the other on a highway\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text contrasts the two, implying the pine is the larger counterpart to the small, low scrub.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of the question \'What do people like to see along the highway?\' in the context of the poem\'s message?\",\"options\":[\"To teach traffic rules\",\"To encourage people to look for beauty in different roles\",\"To explain how to build a trail\",\"To identify different types of fish\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The question prompts the reader to consider the value and visibility of different elements in life.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(22057,52,8,'English','en','1.2 Androcles and the Lion','[\"- Androcles was a kind slave who escaped from a cruel master.\",\"- He found a wounded lion in the forest and helped it by removing a thorn from its paw.\",\"- The lion showed gratitude by licking Androcles’ arm and later by following him and sharing food.\",\"- Soldiers captured both Androcles and the lion and put them in a cage in the city.\",\"- In the emperor’s circus, the lion stopped attacking Androcles and instead petted him, showing friendship.\",\"- The emperor was moved by this act and freed both Androcles and the lion.\",\"- Lions are called the king of the jungle, belong to the cat family, are carnivorous, have a mane only on males, live in groups called a pride, and attack only when hungry.\",\"- Key vocabulary: courteous, bound by law, clutches, coward, flee, piteously, moaned, cautiously, whimpered, distress, summoning up courage, intention.\",\"- The story teaches that kindness and bravery can change hearts and earn freedom.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which hand did Androcles use to take the lion\'s paw?\",\"options\":[\"His right hand\",\"His left hand\",\"Both his hands\",\"He did not use his hands\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Androcles took the paw in his left hand.\'\",\"topic\":\"Life in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'deftly\' as used in the passage?\",\"options\":[\"Slowly and carefully\",\"Roughly and quickly\",\"Skilfully and quickly\",\"Fearfully and silently\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides the definition of deftly as \'skilfully and quickly\'.\",\"topic\":\"Life in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did Androcles use to bind the lion\'s injured paw?\",\"options\":[\"A piece of dry grass\",\"A bandage from his bag\",\"Large leaves from the forest\",\"A piece of his own clothing\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Androcles \'tearing a piece of his own clothing\' to bind the paw.\",\"topic\":\"Life in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the lion lick Androcles\' arm?\",\"options\":[\"Because it was hungry\",\"To show its gratitude\",\"To clean Androcles\' arm\",\"Because it was in pain\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the lion licked his arm \'as if to show gratitude\'.\",\"topic\":\"Life in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did Androcles provide food for the \'helpless beast\'?\",\"options\":[\"He gathered fruits from the trees\",\"He would hunt in the forest and share his food\",\"The lion hunted for both of them\",\"He brought food from the nearby village\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The passage states, \'He would hunt in the forest and share his food with the helpless beast.\'\",\"topic\":\"Life in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How often did Androcles clean and dress the lion’s wound?\",\"options\":[\"Once a week\",\"Every day\",\"Only when the lion cried\",\"Twice a day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies, \'Every day, he would clean and dress the lion’s wound.\'\",\"topic\":\"Life in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happened once the lion was able to move about again?\",\"options\":[\"It ran away into the deep forest\",\"It attacked other animals for Androcles\",\"It followed Androcles wherever he went\",\"It stayed in the cave all day\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Many times, it followed Androcles, wherever he went.\'\",\"topic\":\"Life in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the cause of the lion\'s injury?\",\"options\":[\"A sharp stone\",\"A hunter\'s arrow\",\"A thorn\",\"A bite from another animal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Androcles \'pulled out the thorn\' from the lion\'s paw.\",\"topic\":\"Life in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the actions described, which word best describes Androcles?\",\"options\":[\"Brave\",\"Kind\",\"Fearful\",\"Selfish\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly refers to him as \'the kind man\' when he bound the paw.\",\"topic\":\"Life in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"For how long did Androcles remain with the lion?\",\"options\":[\"Until the wound stopped bleeding\",\"Until the lion could walk again\",\"For a few hours only\",\"Until he ran out of clothing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Androcles remained with the lion till it could walk again.\'\",\"topic\":\"Life in the Forest\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who complained to the authorities about Androcles running away?\",\"options\":[\"The forest guards\",\"The soldiers\",\"Androcles\' master\",\"The lion\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Androcles’ master had complained to the authorities that his slave had run away.\",\"topic\":\"Capture and Imprisonment\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the soldiers search for Androcles?\",\"options\":[\"Only in the city\",\"In all directions\",\"Only near the cave\",\"Inside the master\'s house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, soldiers were sent in all directions to capture Androcles.\",\"topic\":\"Capture and Imprisonment\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'searched for him high and low\' imply in the context of the passage?\",\"options\":[\"They looked on mountains and in valleys\",\"They searched everywhere thoroughly\",\"They looked at the sky and the ground\",\"They only searched in tall buildings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The idiom \'high and low\' means searching everywhere, which describes the soldiers\' extensive search.\",\"topic\":\"Capture and Imprisonment\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why were the soldiers specifically looking for Androcles?\",\"options\":[\"He was a brave soldier\",\"He had stolen a lion\",\"He was a runaway slave\",\"He was a famous hunter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The master complained because his slave Androcles had run away, making him a fugitive.\",\"topic\":\"Capture and Imprisonment\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a soldier was following the master\'s complaint, what was his primary objective?\",\"options\":[\"To kill the lion in the forest\",\"To find a new cave for the master\",\"To capture Androcles and bring him back\",\"To protect the forest animals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The soldiers were sent specifically to capture Androcles following the master\'s complaint.\",\"topic\":\"Capture and Imprisonment\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What happened because Androcles went out alone on the day the soldiers arrived?\",\"options\":[\"He managed to hide from the soldiers\",\"He and the lion were both captured\",\"He found a new place to live\",\"He escaped to the city safely\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that because he was out and the lion was resting, both fell into the hands of the soldiers.\",\"topic\":\"Capture and Imprisonment\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Where was the lion when Androcles was captured?\",\"options\":[\"Hunting for food in the forest\",\"Resting near the cave\",\"Attacking the soldiers\",\"Hiding inside the prison\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'the lion rested near the cave\' while Androcles had gone out alone.\",\"topic\":\"Capture and Imprisonment\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the soldiers\' treatment of Androcles differ from their treatment of the lion after capture?\",\"options\":[\"Androcles was caged and the lion was chained\",\"Both were put in the same prison cell\",\"Androcles was put in chains in a prison while the lion was caged\",\"The lion was set free while Androcles was taken to the city\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that they put Androcles in chains in a prison and the lion was caged.\",\"topic\":\"Capture and Imprisonment\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the master\'s attitude towards his runaway slave based on his actions?\",\"options\":[\"Forgiving\",\"Persistent\",\"Indifferent\",\"Kind\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The master\'s action of complaining to authorities and having soldiers sent in all directions shows he was persistent in finding Androcles.\",\"topic\":\"Capture and Imprisonment\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the soldiers take Androcles and the lion after capturing them in the forest?\",\"options\":[\"To the master\'s house\",\"To a different forest\",\"Back to the city\",\"To the authorities\' office\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states, \'The soldiers took them back to the city.\'\",\"topic\":\"Capture and Imprisonment\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was considered a very serious crime in the days of Androcles?\",\"options\":[\"Stealing food from the market\",\"Running away from one’s master\",\"Refusing to watch the circus\",\"Hunting wild beasts in the forest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that running away from one’s master was a very serious crime at that time.\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the definition of an \'arena\'?\",\"options\":[\"A cage for wild animals\",\"A palace for the emperor\",\"A ground surrounded by seats for sports and public events\",\"A large gate used to release lions\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines an arena as a ground surrounded by seats on all sides for sports and other public events.\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the lion kept hungry before being released into the arena?\",\"options\":[\"Because there was a shortage of food\",\"To make it more ferocious\",\"To make it move slower\",\"To punish the lion for being wild\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the lion had been kept hungry to make it more ferocious.\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did Androcles feel when he was brought into the arena?\",\"options\":[\"Excited and hopeful\",\"Angry and aggressive\",\"Weak and dismayed\",\"Calm and relaxed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that Androcles felt weak and dismayed upon entering the arena.\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to Androcles\' chains once he was in the arena?\",\"options\":[\"They were tightened\",\"They were unbound\",\"They were attached to the lion\",\"They were replaced with heavier ones\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'His chains were unbound\' after he was brought into the arena.\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a person was found guilty of a serious crime in that era, what was the standard punishment?\",\"options\":[\"They were made to serve the emperor\",\"They were forced to become trumpeters\",\"They were fed to wild beasts\",\"They were banned from the circus\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says people found guilty of a serious crime were fed to wild beasts as punishment.\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'put up a brave front\' mean in the context of Androcles\' situation?\",\"options\":[\"He wore a mask to hide his face\",\"He stood at the front of the arena\",\"He showed that he was not afraid despite being filled with fear\",\"He prepared to fight the lion with his bare hands\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The vocabulary note defines \'put up a brave front\' as showing that one is not afraid.\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who arrived at the circus to take his place before the event began?\",\"options\":[\"The master\",\"The lion\",\"The emperor\",\"The trumpeters\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'On the appointed day, the emperor arrived at the circus and took his place.\'\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Androcles certain that it was the last day of his life?\",\"options\":[\"He was very ill\",\"A ferocious, hungry lion was released to attack him\",\"The emperor had already announced his death\",\"The crowd was cheering for his execution\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The presence of a ferocious, hungry lion in the arena led Androcles to believe he would not survive.\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What action by the trumpeters signaled Androcles\' entry into the arena?\",\"options\":[\"They stopped playing music\",\"They cheered loudly\",\"They blew the trumpet\",\"They opened the gate\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says, \'The trumpeters blew the trumpet and Androcles was brought into the arena.\'\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the description of the \'circus\' in the text, what was its primary function in this story?\",\"options\":[\"A place for animal tricks and clowns\",\"A venue for public punishments and spectacles\",\"A training ground for soldiers\",\"A place where slaves were sold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the circus as the place where the emperor watches the punishment of criminals being fed to beasts.\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text best describes the nature of the lion released into the arena?\",\"options\":[\"Dismayed\",\"Ferocious\",\"Unbound\",\"Serious\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text repeatedly uses the word \'ferocious\' to describe the wild and dangerous lion.\",\"topic\":\"In the Arena\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What was the lion\'s initial reaction when it first saw Androcles?\",\"options\":[\"It stopped and turned back\",\"It rushed towards him, bounding and roaring\",\"It lay down and slept\",\"It began to purr immediately\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the lion rushed towards him, bounding and roaring, before stopping.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Reunion\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the lion\'s rage as it moved slowly towards Androcles?\",\"options\":[\"It seemed to have melted\",\"It became even stronger\",\"It turned into hunger\",\"It stayed the same\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that \'All its rage seemed to have melted.\'\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Reunion\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did the lion show affection when it finally reached Androcles?\",\"options\":[\"It licked his feet\",\"It roared loudly at the crowd\",\"It began to purr and rub its nose against him\",\"It jumped over his head\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the lion began to purr and rub its nose against him.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Reunion\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the reaction of the people watching this event?\",\"options\":[\"They were angry\",\"They were amazed\",\"They were terrified\",\"They were disappointed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'To everyone\'s amazement\', indicating the crowd\'s reaction.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Reunion\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Androcles do when the lion reached him?\",\"options\":[\"He ran away in fear\",\"He attacked the lion\",\"He hugged the lion\",\"He shouted for help\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text clearly says \'Androcles hugged the lion.\'\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Reunion\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the lion stop in its tracks after initially rushing forward?\",\"options\":[\"It was too tired to run\",\"It recognized Androcles as its friend\",\"It saw the guards approaching\",\"It was scared of the crowd\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text notes that \'Each friend recognized the other,\' explaining the change in behavior.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Reunion\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which two emotions did Androcles feel during the reunion?\",\"options\":[\"Fear and anger\",\"Relief and joy\",\"Sadness and guilt\",\"Hunger and thirst\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions he \'wept with relief and joy.\'\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Reunion\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the lion\'s behavior, which sound indicated it was no longer a threat?\",\"options\":[\"Roaring\",\"Bounding\",\"Purring\",\"Melting\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Purring is a sound of contentment, contrasting with the initial roaring.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Reunion\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'stopped in its tracks\' imply about the lion\'s movement?\",\"options\":[\"It followed a specific path\",\"It stopped very suddenly\",\"It tripped over something\",\"It slowed down gradually\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In this context, stopping in one\'s tracks means a sudden, complete halt.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Reunion\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary reason the lion\'s behavior changed from \'roaring\' to \'purring\'?\",\"options\":[\"It was no longer hungry\",\"It was intimidated by Androcles\",\"It recognized a past friendship\",\"It was confused by the crowd\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text highlights the recognition between the \'two friends\' as the cause for the change.\",\"topic\":\"Recognition and Reunion\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the reaction of the audience and the emperor to the sight of Androcles and the lion?\",\"options\":[\"They were filled with fear\",\"They watched in great wonder\",\"They were angry at the lion\",\"They ignored the scene\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the audience and emperor watched the tender sight in \'great wonder\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the people do when they began to cheer Androcles?\",\"options\":[\"Asked for his execution\",\"Asked for his release\",\"Asked for more lions\",\"Asked for the emperor to leave\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, people cheered Androcles and asked for his release.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was Androcles\' status before the emperor ordered him to be set free?\",\"options\":[\"A soldier\",\"A king\",\"A slave\",\"A hunter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that after being set free, he would \'no longer be a slave\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What did the emperor ask Androcles to explain?\",\"options\":[\"How he escaped the forest\",\"The lion\'s strange behaviour\",\"Why he was a slave\",\"Where he found the lion\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The emperor asked Androcles to explain the lion\'s strange behaviour in the arena.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does the phrase \'moved by\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"To change location\",\"To be physically pushed\",\"To have strong feelings\",\"To walk away\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'moved by\' as \'have strong feelings\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What specific qualities between the man and the beast moved the emperor?\",\"options\":[\"Their strength and power\",\"Their fear and anger\",\"Their gratitude and friendship\",\"Their speed and agility\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the emperor was moved by the \'gratitude and friendship between man and beast\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"When the emperor offered a reward, what did Androcles request for himself?\",\"options\":[\"A bag of gold\",\"His own house\",\"Nothing for himself\",\"A position in the army\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Androcles replied that he \'did not want anything for himself\'.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did Androcles demonstrate his friendship toward the lion at the end of the story?\",\"options\":[\"By taking the lion to his home\",\"By asking for the lion to be set free too\",\"By leaving the lion in the arena\",\"By asking the emperor to kill the lion\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Androcles requested that the lion be set free as his reward.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why was the lion\'s behaviour described as \'strange\' by the emperor?\",\"options\":[\"Because the lion ran away\",\"Because the lion attacked the audience\",\"Because the lion showed affection instead of attacking\",\"Because the lion slept in the arena\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The \'strange behaviour\' refers to the \'tender sight\' of friendship instead of the expected violence.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the final destination for the two friends?\",\"options\":[\"The emperor\'s palace\",\"The city streets\",\"The forest\",\"A new cage\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying the two friends went back to the forest.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what changed the emperor\'s mind about Androcles\' punishment?\",\"options\":[\"The cheering of the crowd only\",\"Hearing the whole story of gratitude and friendship\",\"The lion\'s roar\",\"Androcles\' plea for gold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says when he heard the whole story, he was moved and ordered the release.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the central theme of the \'Reward\' given to Androcles and the lion?\",\"options\":[\"Wealth and riches\",\"Power and control\",\"Freedom and companionship\",\"Victory in battle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text focuses on them being set free and living a \'free life\' together as friends.\",\"topic\":\"Reward and Freedom\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What is the other name for Auxiliary verbs as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Action verbs\",\"Helping verbs\",\"Main verbs\",\"Object verbs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that Auxiliary verbs are also called helping verbs.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these are the three most common Primary Auxiliary verbs?\",\"options\":[\"can, may, will\",\"shall, should, must\",\"be, do, have\",\"am, is, are\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text identifies \'be\', \'do\', and \'have\' as the three most common Primary Auxiliaries.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the purpose of Auxiliary verbs?\",\"options\":[\"To replace the main verb in a sentence\",\"To help form tenses, moods, and voices\",\"To describe the quality of a noun\",\"To connect two different sentences\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines Auxiliary verbs as verbs that help to form tenses, moods, and voices.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is a unique characteristic of Primary Auxiliaries compared to Modals?\",\"options\":[\"They can stand alone in a sentence\",\"They always require a main verb\",\"They only show the future tense\",\"They cannot be used in the past tense\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that Primary Auxiliaries can stand alone in a sentence, unlike Modals.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'She is a student of Class 8\', which form of \'Be\' is used?\",\"options\":[\"am\",\"are\",\"is\",\"was\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The example provided in the text uses \'is\' as a form of \'be\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the Modal Auxiliary verb in the sentence: \'He must work hard.\'\",\"options\":[\"He\",\"must\",\"work\",\"hard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'must\' as a Modal Auxiliary verb.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT a form of the Primary Auxiliary \'Do\'?\",\"options\":[\"do\",\"does\",\"did\",\"done\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'do\', \'does\', and \'did\' as forms of \'Do\'; \'done\' is not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is listed as a form of the Primary Auxiliary \'Have\'?\",\"options\":[\"having\",\"had\",\"have been\",\"has to\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'have\', \'has\', and \'had\' as forms of \'Have\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What must a Modal Auxiliary verb always accompany in a sentence?\",\"options\":[\"An Adjective\",\"A Main (Action) verb\",\"A Primary Auxiliary\",\"A Noun phrase\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that Modal Auxiliaries accompany Main (Action) verbs.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'I have a cold\', how is the verb \'have\' categorized?\",\"options\":[\"Modal Auxiliary\",\"Main Action Verb\",\"Primary Auxiliary\",\"Future Tense Verb\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text uses this sentence as an example of a Primary Auxiliary standing alone.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a form of \'Be\' used for the future tense in the text?\",\"options\":[\"was\",\"were\",\"will \\/ shall be\",\"am\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'will \\/ shall be\' under the forms of \'Be\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which group contains only Modal Auxiliary verbs according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"am, is, are\",\"do, does, did\",\"can, could, shall\",\"have, has, had\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'can, could, shall\' as Modal Auxiliaries, while the others are Primary Auxiliaries.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study: Auxiliary Verbs\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(22058,52,8,'English','en','1.3 Trees are the Kindest Things I Know','[\"Trees are the kindest things we know – they never hurt anyone.\",\"They give shade, fruit, wood and firewood for cooking.\",\"They help birds and animals by providing food, shelter and nesting places.\",\"At sunrise the tree’s leaves catch the first rays of light.\",\"At sunset the tree’s branches hold the last light of the day.\",\"Trees are called harmless because they only grow and never attack.\",\"During Halloween in the West it is autumn – leaves are burned to keep the forest clean and to celebrate the harvest.\",\"People use trees for building houses, making paper, and as food sources.\",\"Trees absorb carbon dioxide and release oxygen – they clean the air.\",\"They also prevent soil erosion by holding the ground with their roots.\",\"The poem “Trees are the kindest things I know” shows trees as gentle and caring.\",\"The poem uses personification – trees are described as humming and singing lullabies.\",\"The poem mentions trees giving fruit, wood, shade, and firewood for Halloween.\",\"Trees are the first to greet the morning sun and the last to keep the evening light.\",\"They are a symbol of patience, strength and kindness in many cultures.\",\"The poem’s rhyme scheme is simple and easy to remember for children.\",\"The poem teaches us to respect and protect trees for future generations.\",\"Trees are a living part of the environment that supports many life forms.\",\"They are also a source of medicine, food, and shelter for humans and animals.\",\"The poem encourages us to think about how trees help us in everyday life.\",\"Trees are a natural resource that should be preserved and not cut down without reason.\",\"They provide a quiet place for children to play and learn from nature.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the poet of the poem \'Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\'?\",\"options\":[\"Robert Frost\",\"Harry Behn\",\"William Wordsworth\",\"Rabindranath Tagore\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem is attributed to Harry Behn at the end of the text.\",\"topic\":\"Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, for whom do the trees spread a shade?\",\"options\":[\"Sleepy cows\",\"Small children\",\"Tired travelers\",\"Gathering birds\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'And spread a shade for sleepy cows\'.\",\"topic\":\"Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet consider trees to be the kindest things?\",\"options\":[\"Because they grow very tall\",\"Because they do not harm and simply grow\",\"Because they change colors in autumn\",\"Because they stay awake all night\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'They do not harm, they simply grow,\' explaining their kindness.\",\"topic\":\"Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What specific growth do trees show during the Spring season according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Falling brown leaves\",\"Wood for houses\",\"New buds of green\",\"Morning sun beams\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions, \'And in the Spring new buds of green\'.\",\"topic\":\"Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a person needs to construct a house, which part of the tree mentioned in the poem would be used?\",\"options\":[\"The green buds\",\"The fruit\",\"The boughs\",\"The wood\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem states trees give us \'wood to make our houses of\'.\",\"topic\":\"Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How does the poet describe the tree\'s interaction with the sun at the beginning of the day?\",\"options\":[\"They hide the sun behind their leaves\",\"They are the first to touch the beams of the morning sun\",\"They hum a lullaby to the sun\",\"They hold the light until it turns into night\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says, \'They are the first when day’s begun \\/ To touch the beams of morning sun.\'\",\"topic\":\"Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Under what condition do the trees hum a \'drowsy lullaby\'?\",\"options\":[\"When the sun is at its peak\",\"When the birds start singing in the boughs\",\"When a moon floats on the sky\",\"When the new buds appear in Spring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'And when a moon floats on the sky \\/ They hum a drowsy lullaby\'.\",\"topic\":\"Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"On which specific occasion are tree leaves used for burning according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Christmas\",\"Hallowe’en\",\"Spring Equinox\",\"New Year\'s Eve\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'And leaves to burn on Hallowe’en\'.\",\"topic\":\"Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, birds are seen flying near the trees. Which line from the poem best describes the relationship between the birds and the trees?\",\"options\":[\"They do not harm, they simply grow\",\"And gather birds among their boughs\",\"They are the last to hold the light\",\"They hum a drowsy lullaby\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows birds near the tree branches (boughs), matching the line \'And gather birds among their boughs\'.\",\"topic\":\"Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/023_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"The given figure shows small orange shapes among the green leaves. Based on the poem, what do these most likely represent?\",\"options\":[\"Leaves to burn on Hallowe\'en\",\"Morning sun beams\",\"Fruit in leaves above\",\"New buds of green\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions trees \'give us fruit, in leaves above\', which corresponds to the orange shapes shown in the foliage in the figure.\",\"topic\":\"Trees are the Kindest Things I Know\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/023_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the simple form of an adjective called according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Positive Degree\",\"Comparative Degree\",\"Superlative Degree\",\"Simple Degree\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the adjective in its simple form is called the Positive Degree.\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'boughs\' mean in the context of trees?\",\"options\":[\"Roots\",\"Flowers\",\"Branches\",\"Seeds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'boughs\' as \'branches\'.\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which suffix is added to a basic adjective to form the Comparative Degree?\",\"options\":[\"-est\",\"-ly\",\"-er\",\"-ing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that \'-er\' is added to the basic adjective for the Comparative Degree.\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When is the Comparative Degree of an adjective used?\",\"options\":[\"When there is no comparison\",\"When there is a comparison of two nouns\",\"When there is a comparison of more than two nouns\",\"When describing a single noun\'s highest quality\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines Comparative Degree as referring to a higher degree when there is a comparison of two nouns.\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is a \'lullaby\' as described in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A loud morning song\",\"A festival in Autumn\",\"A soft, slow song to put children to sleep\",\"The first rays of the sun\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a lullaby as a soft, slow song to put children to sleep.\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which degree of comparison refers to the \'highest degree\' involving more than two nouns?\",\"options\":[\"Positive Degree\",\"Comparative Degree\",\"Superlative Degree\",\"Basic Degree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the Superlative Degree refers to the highest degree of comparison of one with more than two nouns.\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'kind\' is the basic adjective, what would be its Superlative form based on the rules provided?\",\"options\":[\"Kinder\",\"Kindest\",\"More kind\",\"Most kind\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the rule, \'-est\' is added to the basic adjective to form the Superlative Degree.\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the sentence \'The tree is taller than the bush\', which degree of comparison is used?\",\"options\":[\"Positive\",\"Comparative\",\"Superlative\",\"Simple\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The use of \'-er\' in \'taller\' to compare two nouns indicates the Comparative Degree.\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'strongest\' used in the sentence \'Pravin is the strongest of all\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is the simple form of the adjective\",\"Because only two people are being compared\",\"Because one person is being compared with more than two nouns\",\"Because it is a festival name\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that the Superlative Degree (-est) is used for comparison of one with more than two nouns.\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the word \'stronger\' identifies it as a Comparative Degree adjective?\",\"options\":[\"The root word \'strong\'\",\"The suffix \'-er\'\",\"The prefix \'str-\'\",\"The whole word\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that \'-er\' is added to the basic adjective to create the Comparative Degree.\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the rules, which of these sequences correctly follows the order: Positive, Comparative, Superlative?\",\"options\":[\"Strong, strongest, stronger\",\"Stronger, strong, strongest\",\"Strong, stronger, strongest\",\"Strongest, stronger, strong\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists the degrees in the order of simple (Positive), higher (Comparative), and highest (Superlative).\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence correctly applies the rule for the Superlative Degree?\",\"options\":[\"He is the stronger boy in class.\",\"He is the strongest boy in class.\",\"He is strong than his brother.\",\"He is strong boy.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Superlative Degree uses \'-est\' and compares one to many (the whole class).\",\"topic\":\"Degrees of Comparison: Rules\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what figure of speech is used when human characteristics are given to non-human things?\",\"options\":[\"Alliteration\",\"Personification\",\"Metaphor\",\"Simile\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that when human characteristics are given to something non-human, the Figure of Speech is Personification.\",\"topic\":\"Personification\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of Personification mentioned in the textbook text?\",\"options\":[\"Tall trees\",\"Green grass\",\"Humming trees\",\"Big mountains\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'humming trees\' as an example of Personification.\",\"topic\":\"Personification\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'smiling flowers\', what is the human characteristic being given?\",\"options\":[\"Growing\",\"Smiling\",\"Blooming\",\"Fragrance\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Smiling is a human characteristic given to the non-human flowers in this example.\",\"topic\":\"Personification\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Personification is used when human characteristics are given to which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"Only other humans\",\"Something non-human\",\"Adjectives with two syllables\",\"Superlative degrees\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The definition states human characteristics are given to \'something non human\'.\",\"topic\":\"Personification\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which human characteristic is attributed to a river in the textbook examples?\",\"options\":[\"Walking\",\"Talking\",\"Running\",\"Sleeping\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'running river\' as an example of Personification.\",\"topic\":\"Personification\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'humming trees\' considered Personification according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Because trees are tall\",\"Because humming is a human characteristic given to a non-human tree\",\"Because it uses more than two syllables\",\"Because it is a superlative degree\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It fits the definition of giving a human characteristic (humming) to a non-human thing (trees).\",\"topic\":\"Personification\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a poet writes about \'dancing leaves\', which figure of speech are they using based on the provided definition?\",\"options\":[\"Comparative degree\",\"Positive degree\",\"Personification\",\"Syllable count\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Giving the human action of \'dancing\' to \'leaves\' (non-human) follows the rule for Personification.\",\"topic\":\"Personification\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text\'s logic, which of these would be an example of Personification?\",\"options\":[\"A fast car\",\"A blue sky\",\"A thirsty soil\",\"A large house\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Thirst is a human\\/living feeling given to the non-human soil, similar to the text\'s examples.\",\"topic\":\"Personification\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the figure of speech described, what does \'non-human\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"Objects, plants, or elements of nature\",\"Only people in a poem\",\"Adjectives like \'successful\'\",\"Comparative degrees of words\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The examples (trees, river, flowers) show that non-human refers to things in nature or objects.\",\"topic\":\"Personification\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which requirement must be met for a line to contain Personification according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"It must have more than two syllables\",\"It must use the words \'more\' or \'most\'\",\"A human characteristic must be given to a non-human thing\",\"It must be in the Superlative degree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines Personification by the act of giving human traits to non-human things.\",\"topic\":\"Personification\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(22059,52,8,'English','en','1.4 Miss Slippery','[\"Miss Slippery is a story about a girl named Sayali who is teased by classmates and faces difficulties at home.\",\"She often forgets things and gets nervous, which makes her feel like she is always ‘slipping’ even when she is careful.\",\"The teacher gives her responsibilities to help her feel useful and to build confidence.\",\"Key words: all‑devouring look (frightening look), went blank (could not remember), vociferous (noisy), inevitable (certain), stern (strict).\",\"Compound words are formed by joining two words, e.g., homework, kind‑hearted.\",\"Irregular verbs do not follow the regular -ed pattern, e.g., go – went – gone, break – broke – broken.\",\"Continuous tense shows an action in progress (was coming). Perfect tense shows a completed action (has asked).\",\"Polite requests use modal verbs: Could I…, Would you mind…, May I…\",\"Anagrams are words formed by rearranging letters, e.g., state – taste.\",\"Traffic signs give instructions; students should learn them for safety.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the survey in the text, which of these is an option for how you handle teasing?\",\"options\":[\"Fight back\",\"Cry\",\"Run away\",\"Laugh it off\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'Cry\', \'Ignore\', and \'Complain to teacher\' as options for handling teasing.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the punctuation exercise, which city is mentioned in the question \'why did you go to...\'?\",\"options\":[\"Mumbai\",\"Nagpur\",\"New Delhi\",\"Pune\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifically mentions \'nagpur\' in the second punctuation exercise sentence.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which branch of science is NOT mentioned in the punctuation exercise list?\",\"options\":[\"Physics\",\"Chemistry\",\"Biology\",\"Zoology\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists physics, chemistry, zoology, and botany; biology is not mentioned.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the survey ask you to decide when you are punished in class?\",\"options\":[\"To leave the school\",\"To argue with the teacher\",\"To decide to change\",\"To ignore the punishment\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"One of the options provided for handling oneself when punished is \'Decide to change\'.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the Chit-Chat section, what is the focus of the question regarding \'dear ones\'?\",\"options\":[\"Their academic performance\",\"Forgiving or punishing them for mistakes\",\"Their favorite hobbies\",\"How much money they spend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Question 4 of Chit-Chat asks if we forgive or punish our dear ones for their mistakes.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of the survey question \'Do you with your friends, also tease, trouble or give names to any of your classmates?\'\",\"options\":[\"To see if you are a victim of bullying\",\"To check if you participate in bullying others\",\"To find out who your best friend is\",\"To learn how to name new students\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The question asks about your own behavior toward others, specifically regarding teasing or giving names.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which punctuation mark is most appropriate for the end of the sentence: \'what a loud explosion that was\'?\",\"options\":[\"Question mark (?)\",\"Full stop (.)\",\"Exclamation mark (!)\",\"Comma (,)\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sentence is an exclamatory sentence expressing strong emotion about an explosion.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many words should be capitalized in the sentence: \'the president of india lives at rashtrapati bhavan in new delhi\'?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"5\",\"7\",\"4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The (start of sentence), President (title), India (country), Rashtrapati Bhavan (building), New Delhi (city) all require capitals.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the correct way to rewrite: \'amar said i could not complete my geography homework\'\",\"options\":[\"Amar said, I could not complete my geography homework.\",\"Amar said, \\\"I could not complete my geography homework.\\\"\",\"amar said \\\"i could not complete my geography homework\\\"\",\"Amar said: i could not complete my geography homework!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Proper punctuation for reported speech requires a capital for the name, a comma, and quotation marks.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the survey options, which reaction to others troubling you is categorized alongside \'Take revenge\' and \'Ignore them totally\'?\",\"options\":[\"Become depressed\",\"Fight them\",\"Tell your parents\",\"Laugh at them\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The survey lists \'Take revenge\', \'Ignore them totally\', and \'Become depressed\' as reaction options.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The \'Chit-Chat\' section primarily encourages the student to reflect on which aspect of their life?\",\"options\":[\"Scientific knowledge\",\"Geographical locations\",\"Social interactions and emotions\",\"Grammar and punctuation\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The questions focus on arguments, quarrels, and feelings toward friends and dear ones.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following best describes the task in section (3) of the text?\",\"options\":[\"A multiple-choice question about science\",\"A punctuation correction exercise\",\"A creative writing task about helping a friend improve\",\"A survey about classroom punishment\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Section (3) asks students to write in their own words how to get rid of a negative quality in a friend.\",\"topic\":\"WARMING UP !\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What subject did the class teacher teach in the first period?\",\"options\":[\"History\",\"Mathematics\",\"English\",\"Science\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the class teacher, who taught English, told the students to take out their composition notebooks.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which notebook did Sayali accidentally take out during the first period?\",\"options\":[\"History notebook\",\"Mathematics notebook\",\"English composition notebook\",\"Science notebook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, Sayali took out the mathematics notebook by mistake instead of the composition notebook.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'all-devouring look\' mean as used in the story?\",\"options\":[\"A look of great hunger\",\"A look of deep confusion\",\"A frightening look\",\"A look of pride\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The glossary provided in the text defines \'all-devouring look\' as a frightening look.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the English teacher believe Sayali dropped the notebook on purpose?\",\"options\":[\"Because Sayali was laughing at her\",\"Because the notebook fell on the teacher\'s feet\",\"Because Sayali refused to come to her chair\",\"Because Sayali was talking to other girls\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that when Sayali reached the chair, the notebook fell on the teacher\'s feet, leading the teacher to think it was intentional.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what was the specific topic Sayali had to memorize for the History class?\",\"options\":[\"The causes and effects of the Battle of Panipat\",\"The life of the English teacher\",\"The composition of English notebooks\",\"The history of school punishments\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states the teacher asked them to memorize the causes and effects of the Battle of Panipat.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to Sayali when it was her turn to answer in the History class?\",\"options\":[\"She answered all questions correctly\",\"She started a vociferous quarrel\",\"She went blank and could not remember anything\",\"She dropped her History notebook\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'When my turn came I went blank\', which the glossary defines as \'could not remember anything\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does the text describe the arguments between Sayali\'s Mama and Papa?\",\"options\":[\"Occasional and quiet\",\"Never-ending tiffs\",\"Friendly discussions\",\"Short and meaningful\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly describes their arguments as \'never-ending tiffs\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If Sayali hears a raised voice in a quiet place, how does she react based on her experiences at home?\",\"options\":[\"She feels happy and safe\",\"She feels as if her parents are quarrelling\",\"She starts to memorize History\",\"She laughs loudly with other girls\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that whenever and wherever she heard raised voices, she felt as if Mama and Papa were quarrelling.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'vociferous\' imply about Mama\'s role in the quarrels?\",\"options\":[\"She was quiet and calm\",\"She was noisy and forceful in expressing feelings\",\"She was always forgiving\",\"She was afraid to speak\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines \'vociferous\' as noisy and forceful in expressing one\'s feelings.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the description of Sayali\'s home life, why does she struggle to perform well in school?\",\"options\":[\"She is naturally lazy and does not study\",\"She is upset and unnerved due to problems at home\",\"She wants to be punished by her teachers\",\"She does not like the subjects English and History\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The introductory paragraph explains she is unable to do any task well because she is upset and unnerved due to problems at home.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what visual element represents the text\'s description that Sayali\'s \'legs quivered\'?\",\"options\":[\"The blue color of her dress\",\"The wavy lines drawn around her legs\",\"The way her hair is tied in braids\",\"The brown color of her socks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The wavy lines near the legs in the illustration visually represent the trembling or quivering mentioned in the text.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/028_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the girl\'s facial expression and posture best illustrate which state mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Being well-prepared for History\",\"Being vociferous during a quarrel\",\"Being upset and unnerved\",\"Expressing annoyance like Papa\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The girl\'s wide eyes and worried expression in the figure match the text\'s description of her being \'upset and unnerved\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/028_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What was the result of the \'third one\' (Sayali) being affected by the parents\' quarrels?\",\"options\":[\"She became very brave\",\"Punishment inevitably descended on her at school\",\"She stopped going to school\",\"She started teaching English\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the punishment inevitably descended on the third one, which is Sayali at school.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which word from the text is a synonym for \'strict\'?\",\"options\":[\"Stern\",\"Vociferous\",\"Inevitably\",\"Annoyance\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The glossary explicitly defines \'stern\' as \'strict\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Sayali stand \'stiff, still, with my head hanging down in shame\' during the History class?\",\"options\":[\"She was acting out a scene from the Battle of Panipat\",\"She was waiting for the bell to ring\",\"She was embarrassed because she could not remember the answers\",\"She was trying to hide from the English teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sayali stood that way because she \'went blank\' despite being well-prepared, causing her to feel shame under the teacher\'s stare.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: Sayali\'s Troubles\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many steps did Sayali tumble down when she fell?\",\"options\":[\"Five steps\",\"Seven steps\",\"Ten steps\",\"Twelve steps\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states she fell and came tumbling down about seven steps.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of Sayali\'s new frock was torn?\",\"options\":[\"The sleeves\",\"The collar\",\"The seams\",\"The hem\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions her new frock was torn at the seams.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'extravagant\' mean in the context of Mama\'s complaint?\",\"options\":[\"Very cheap\",\"Very expensive\",\"Unnecessary\",\"Frequent\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines extravagant as \'very expensive\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Sayali yearn for from her mother after the fall?\",\"options\":[\"A new frock\",\"Antiseptic lotion\",\"To be held and consoled\",\"To be left alone\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says within her lingered the yearning that her mother would hold her and console her.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What did Mama apply to Sayali\'s elbows and knees?\",\"options\":[\"Cold water\",\"A bandage\",\"Antiseptic lotion\",\"Soap and water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states Mama fetched an antiseptic lotion and applied it to her elbow and knees.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Sayali start crying again when her younger brother sat beside her?\",\"options\":[\"Because he hit her\",\"Because he was teasing her\",\"Because he showed kindness and asked if she was in pain\",\"Because she was afraid of him\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sayali hugged him and cried again after he placed his hand on her arm and whispered kindly.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the class monitress, how is Sayali different from other people who slip?\",\"options\":[\"She slips on ice\",\"She slips even on dry land\",\"She never slips on wet ground\",\"She only slips on the stairs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The monitress said, \'Others slip on wet ground. Sayali manages to slip even on dry land.\'\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which word in the text describes the \'hurting\' sensation in Sayali\'s limbs?\",\"options\":[\"Soothing\",\"Smarting\",\"Lingering\",\"Frantic\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines \'smarting\' as hurting.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What \'new scope for fun\' did the girls in the class find?\",\"options\":[\"Playing games on the stairs\",\"Teasing Sayali with the title \'Slippery\'\",\"Writing stories about the school\",\"Helping Sayali walk cautiously\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the nickname provided the other girls new scope for fun by teasing her every day.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the verse composed by the girls, what does \'muck\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"Dry land\",\"Wet mud or dirt\",\"A type of shoe\",\"The school stairs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines \'muck\' as wet mud or dirt.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the rhyme, what happens if you ask Sayali the simplest question?\",\"options\":[\"She gives a long answer\",\"She starts crying\",\"She gives no answer\",\"She runs away\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The rhyme says: \'Ask her the simplest question \\/ No answer is your luck!\'\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was Sayali\'s state of mind regarding the people around her?\",\"options\":[\"She was very happy\",\"She lived in perpetual fear\",\"She was angry at everyone\",\"She was indifferent\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states: \'I lived in perpetual fear of everyone\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'muster the courage\' mean as used in the text?\",\"options\":[\"To lose hope\",\"To gather courage\",\"To speak loudly\",\"To hide away\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines \'muster courage\' as gather courage.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did Sayali behave when she was inside the classroom?\",\"options\":[\"She talked to everyone\",\"She dared not move out\",\"She played with her friends\",\"She studied hard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says: \'When I was in class, I dared not move out\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes Sayali\'s walking style despite her frequent stumbles?\",\"options\":[\"Carelessly\",\"Cautiously\",\"Quickly\",\"Frantically\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'I used to walk quite cautiously, yet I would often stumble.\'\",\"topic\":\"Part - 1: The Nickname \'Slippery\'\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the teacher ask Sayali to meet her after the class?\",\"options\":[\"In the playground\",\"In the principal\'s office\",\"In the teachers’ room\",\"At the school gate\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the teacher told Sayali to see her in the teachers’ room after the class.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the teacher\'s facial expression when Sayali first sought permission to enter the classroom?\",\"options\":[\"She was smiling broadly\",\"She wore a frown on her face\",\"She looked very angry\",\"She was crying\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the teacher wore a frown on her face when Sayali reached the school.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did Sayali feel as she walked toward the teachers\' room?\",\"options\":[\"Confident and bold\",\"Nervous and hesitant\",\"Angry and annoyed\",\"Excited and happy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions an unknown fear made her nervous and she reached the room with hesitant steps.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'confide\' mean as used in the teacher\'s request to Sayali?\",\"options\":[\"To hide a mistake\",\"To share a secret or trouble\",\"To shout loudly\",\"To ignore someone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The vocabulary notes define \'confide\' as sharing a secret.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the teacher, what is the meaning of the word \'didi\'?\",\"options\":[\"Mother\",\"Friend\",\"Elder sister\",\"Teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher explicitly asks, \'Do you know the meaning of didi? It means elder sister.\'\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the teacher advise Sayali to ignore the girls who tease her?\",\"options\":[\"Because the girls are her friends\",\"Because crying will make them pester her more\",\"Because the teacher is scared of the girls\",\"Because the girls are just joking\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher says, \'If you cry like this, they will pester you all the more. So ignore them.\'\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What physical gesture did the teacher use to comfort Sayali while she was crying in the teachers\' room?\",\"options\":[\"She shook her hand\",\"She patted her on the head\",\"She gave her a pen\",\"She pointed at the door\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text describes the teacher \'patting me on the head\' while asking why she was crying.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two specific relationships did the teacher offer to Sayali?\",\"options\":[\"Mother and Teacher\",\"Sister and Friend\",\"Principal and Guide\",\"Classmate and Sister\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher refers to herself as a \'sister\' (didi) and later says \'Now you are a friend too.\'\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If Sayali decides to tell the teacher about her problems, which word from the text best describes this action?\",\"options\":[\"Reassuring\",\"Pestering\",\"Confiding\",\"Frowning\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"To share one\'s troubles or secrets with someone trusted is to \'confide\' in them.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What quality did the teacher specifically say she likes her friends to have?\",\"options\":[\"To be quiet\",\"To be brave\",\"To be smart\",\"To be fast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher says, \'But I like my friends to be brave. You’ve got to try to be brave.\'\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'stand by you\' mean in the teacher\'s closing remarks?\",\"options\":[\"To stand next to someone in a line\",\"To support someone\",\"To watch someone from a distance\",\"To wait for someone at the gate\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The vocabulary notes define \'to stand by someone\' as \'to support someone\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How did Sayali\'s reaction change when the teacher spoke to her in a tender tone?\",\"options\":[\"She stopped crying immediately\",\"Her sighs turned into sobs\",\"She ran out of the room\",\"She started laughing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'Her tender tone turned my sighs into sobs.\'\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"The teacher calls Sayali her \'little pal\'. What is the meaning of \'pal\'?\",\"options\":[\"Student\",\"Enemy\",\"Friend\",\"Sister\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The vocabulary notes define \'pal\' as \'friend\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did a \'rare thrill\' run through Sayali\'s entire frame?\",\"options\":[\"Because she was scared of being punished\",\"Because the teacher offered to be like a sister to her\",\"Because the bell for the next class rang\",\"Because she was happy to leave the room\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The thrill occurred right after the teacher asked Sayali to confide in her as a sister.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the teacher\'s final words, what was the teacher\'s main goal in talking to Sayali?\",\"options\":[\"To scold her for being late\",\"To encourage her to be brave and offer support\",\"To tell her to find new friends among the girls\",\"To explain the school rules\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher encourages bravery and promises to \'always stand by you\', showing a goal of support.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: The Teacher\'s Support\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what did the teacher spontaneously accept Sayali as?\",\"options\":[\"A student and a helper\",\"A sister and a friend\",\"A daughter and a student\",\"A leader and a monitor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the teacher had spontaneously accepted Sayali as a sister and a friend.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the \'prime pastime\' of the girls in Sayali\'s class?\",\"options\":[\"Studying hard\",\"Playing games\",\"Teasing Sayali\",\"Helping the teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the class was full of wild girls whose prime pastime was teasing Sayali.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'lavished\' mean as used in the context of the teacher\'s love?\",\"options\":[\"Hidden away\",\"Poured in great quantity\",\"Given strictly\",\"Forgotten quickly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines \'lavished\' as poured in great quantity.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Sayali feel like she was on \'winged feet\' when running to her class?\",\"options\":[\"Because she was wearing new shoes\",\"Because she was late for the lecture\",\"Because she was filled with extreme joy and excitement\",\"Because she was trying to escape from Maya\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Her excitement and joy from the teacher\'s affection made her feel light and fast, described as \'winged feet\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to Sayali during the break that caused the other girls to laugh?\",\"options\":[\"She tripped over a bag\",\"Her water bottle fell and drenched her\",\"She forgot her notebooks\",\"She failed a surprise test\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says the water bottle she was drinking from fell on her and she got fully drenched.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How did Sayali react to Maya and Chanda\'s teasing this time?\",\"options\":[\"She started crying hysterically\",\"She complained to the teacher immediately\",\"She turned her back and ignored them completely\",\"She shouted back at them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Remembering the teacher\'s words, Sayali chose to ignore the bullies by turning her back to them.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'non-plussed\' describe about the girls who teased Sayali?\",\"options\":[\"They were very happy\",\"They were confused and unable to react\",\"They were angry and aggressive\",\"They were bored and tired\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary defines \'non-plussed\' as confused and unable to react.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following was NOT a responsibility given to Sayali by the teacher?\",\"options\":[\"Bringing the register every morning\",\"Bringing chalk and duster\",\"Cleaning the teacher\'s table\",\"Carrying notebooks to the teacher\'s room\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher asked her to bring the register, chalk, duster, and carry notebooks, but did not mention cleaning the table.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Sayali completed the assigned job \'in a jiffy\', how long did it take her?\",\"options\":[\"A very long time\",\"Until the end of the day\",\"Within no time\",\"Exactly one hour\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'in a jiffy\' means within no time or very quickly.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What instruction did the teacher give Sayali regarding the notebooks?\",\"options\":[\"Give them to the peon\",\"Count them and keep them in the drawer\",\"Distribute them to the class\",\"Correct the mistakes in them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The teacher specifically told Sayali to \'Count them and keep them in my drawer.\'\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the \'miraculous strength\' in Sayali\'s legs symbolize?\",\"options\":[\"A physical recovery from an injury\",\"The effect of drinking plenty of water\",\"A newfound confidence and psychological boost\",\"The result of running fast to class\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The strength represents her emotional transformation and confidence gained from the teacher\'s trust.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How did Sayali\'s internal feeling change regarding her wet frock by the end of the day?\",\"options\":[\"She felt very cold and sick\",\"She felt ashamed and hid from others\",\"She found no awkwardness in moving about in it\",\"She was annoyed that it hadn\'t dried\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states she found no awkwardness in moving about in her still-wet frock due to her new pride.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the ultimate \'victory\' Sayali sensed?\",\"options\":[\"Winning a sports race\",\"Getting the highest marks in class\",\"Overcoming her fear and the impact of bullying\",\"Becoming the teacher\'s favorite student\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Her victory was emotional; she felt empowered by ignoring the bullies and not letting them affect her.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the girl carrying that relates to the task assigned by the teacher?\",\"options\":[\"A water bottle\",\"A stack of notebooks\",\"A school bag\",\"A register and chalk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows the girl carrying a stack of notebooks, which matches the teacher\'s instruction to carry them to the room.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/031_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the girl\'s upright posture and smile indicate that her heart is...\",\"options\":[\"Filled with fear\",\"Inflated with pride\",\"Feeling very tired\",\"Full of sorrow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text and the figure together show Sayali\'s transformation into a confident girl whose heart is \'inflated with pride\'.\",\"topic\":\"Part - 2: Sayali\'s Transformation\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/031_101.jpg\"}]','vertex/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(22060,52,8,'English','en','2.1 Try Again','[\"Try again is a poem about perseverance and courage.\",\"Key idea: keep trying even if you fail at first.\",\"Courage means the willingness to keep going.\",\"Persevere means to keep trying until you succeed.\",\"Patience is the ability to wait without losing hope.\",\"If you fail, try again – do not give up.\",\"If you lose a race, do not feel ashamed; keep trying.\",\"When others succeed, you can too if you are patient.\",\"Success is more valuable when earned after hard work.\",\"A proverb is a simple truth that is widely accepted.\",\"The poem can be used as a poster or a web activity.\",\"Anagrams in the poem help remember words like ‘rainy tag’ = ‘try again’.\",\"The poem’s lines can be matched with meanings: ‘heed’ = pay attention, ‘strive’ = try hard, etc.\",\"Opposite words: succeed ↔ fail, punishment ↔ reward, courage ↔ fear, stop\\/quit ↔ continue, lose ↔ win.\",\"The lesson: never give up; keep trying and you will win.\",\"Use the poem to create a poster or a web diagram of ‘Trying again leads to success’.\",\"Remember: Try again, keep courage, stay patient, and you will conquer.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the primary lesson that the poet says one should \'heed\'?\",\"options\":[\"Try again\",\"Give up\",\"Fear failure\",\"Run the race\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The very first stanza introduces \'Try again\' as the lesson to be heeded.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the first stanza, what should appear if you do not succeed at first?\",\"options\":[\"Fear\",\"Courage\",\"Disgrace\",\"Reward\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Then your courage should appear\' if you don\'t succeed at first.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is working on a difficult project and finds the \'task is hard\', what does the poem advise?\",\"options\":[\"Change the task\",\"Try again\",\"Ask other folk\",\"Wait for luck\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem advises to try again specifically when a task is perceived as hard in the third stanza.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet state that \'striving\' is not a disgrace?\",\"options\":[\"Because we already won\",\"Because we failed twice\",\"Because the act of trying is not shameful\",\"Because time is short\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poet explains that even if we don\'t win a race, the act of striving (trying) is not a cause for shame.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the third stanza, what will bring you your reward?\",\"options\":[\"Luck\",\"Other folk\",\"Time\",\"Disgrace\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that \'Time will bring you, your reward\'.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which quality is mentioned as necessary to do what \'other folk\' can do?\",\"options\":[\"Courage\",\"Patience\",\"Fear\",\"Disgrace\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poet asks why we cannot do what others do if we use patience.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How many times might you fail before you \'prevail\', according to the second stanza?\",\"options\":[\"Once or twice\",\"Never\",\"Always\",\"A hundred times\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem acknowledges that failure might happen \'once or twice\' before success.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the ultimate outcome promised to those who \'never fear\' and \'persevere\'?\",\"options\":[\"They will fail\",\"They will be disgraced\",\"They will lose the race\",\"They will conquer\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem promises that perseverance leads to conquering one\'s fears and tasks.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the darts that have missed the target represent which phrase from the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Conquer, never fear\",\"Time will bring reward\",\"If at first you don\'t succeed\",\"Keep this rule in view\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The darts on the ground represent attempts that did not succeed at first.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/038_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Looking at the darts in the given figure, what \'rule\' from the poem should the player keep in view?\",\"options\":[\"Try again\",\"Win the race\",\"Task is hard\",\"Time is reward\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem\'s central message and \'rule\' is to keep trying regardless of initial failure.\",\"topic\":\"कविता\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/038_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word \'heed\' as given in the vocabulary list?\",\"options\":[\"To ignore completely\",\"To pay attention to\",\"To run away from\",\"To speak loudly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines \'heed\' as \'pay attention to\'.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does it mean to \'strive\'?\",\"options\":[\"To give up easily\",\"To wait for others\",\"To try very hard or struggle\",\"To sleep peacefully\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'strive\' as \'try very hard\\/struggle\'.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How does the text define \'patience\'?\",\"options\":[\"The ability to finish work quickly\",\"The capacity to accept delay without losing hope\",\"The act of complaining about problems\",\"The speed at which one climbs a wall\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'patience\' as the \'capacity to accept delay, without losing hope\'.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is the shortened form of \'It is\' as mentioned in the poem\'s notes?\",\"options\":[\"\'Twas\",\"\'Tis\",\"Its\",\"It\'s\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'\'Tis\' is the shortened form of \'It is\'.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the spider story activity, what happens immediately after the spider begins to climb the wall?\",\"options\":[\"It reached the top\",\"It fell down again\",\"It slipped and fell down\",\"It gave up the effort\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the logical sequence of the spider story, after beginning to climb (4), it slips and falls (3).\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final outcome for the spider in the sequencing activity?\",\"options\":[\"It reached the top\",\"It stopped trying\",\"It stayed on the ground\",\"It waited for help\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Line 5 of the spider activity states \'Finally, it reached the top\'.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the spider\'s actions in the activity, which moral best fits the story?\",\"options\":[\"Slow and steady wins the race\",\"Try and try until you succeed\",\"Look before you leap\",\"Honesty is the best policy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The spider\'s repeated attempts despite falling illustrate the theme of \'Try Again\'.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the group activity (1)(A), what specific type of experience are students asked to share?\",\"options\":[\"A time they won a prize without trying\",\"A situation where they failed first but succeeded after continuous efforts\",\"A story about a spider they saw on a wall\",\"A poem they wrote for their teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The instructions specify sharing an experience of failure followed by success through continuous effort.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the instructions for the group activity, how many members should be in each group?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Four\",\"Six\",\"Ten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text says \'Form groups of six each\'.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'persevere\' imply in the context of the \'Warming Up\' activities?\",\"options\":[\"Achieving success on the very first try\",\"Keeping on trying until one achieves their goal\",\"Asking others to do the work for you\",\"Paying attention to the teacher\'s poem\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines \'persevere\' as \'keep trying till one achieves\'.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, how many boxes are provided to outline the steps taken for success?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Counting the boxes in the flow chart F1 shows there are exactly five boxes.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/037_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the direction of the flow after the third box in the sequence?\",\"options\":[\"It goes upward\",\"It goes to the left\",\"It goes downward\",\"It stops completely\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The arrow from the third box (top right) points vertically down to the fourth box.\",\"topic\":\"Warming Up\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/037_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem \'Try Again\', what is the first thing you should do when you fail?\",\"options\":[\"Feel ashamed\",\"Give up the task\",\"Try again\",\"Wait for others to help\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem explicitly states that if at first you don\'t succeed, you should try again.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the central theme of the exercise questions provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The importance of winning\",\"The value of persistence and effort\",\"The history of the poem\",\"The rules of classroom behavior\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The questions focus on handling failure and the rules of persistence, which points to the theme of perseverance.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student fails to solve a math problem on the first attempt, which action best follows the lesson\'s advice?\",\"options\":[\"Closing the book and doing something else\",\"Feeling disgraced by the mistake\",\"Attempting to solve it again with more effort\",\"Asking the teacher to provide the answer immediately\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The core rule of the lesson is to \'Try Again\' when faced with failure or difficulty.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem\'s context, why is \'striving\' not considered a disgrace?\",\"options\":[\"Because it guarantees immediate success\",\"Because making an effort is honorable even if you don\'t win\",\"Because everyone else is doing it\",\"Because it is a simple task\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem suggests that even if we don\'t \'win the race\', the act of striving (trying hard) is not a shame.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What specific \'rule\' does the text mention must be always kept in mind?\",\"options\":[\"Always win the race\",\"Never feel ashamed\",\"Try again\",\"Work only when it is easy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem concludes by stating that the rule to \'Try again\' should always be kept in view.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet imply will happen if you find your task is hard?\",\"options\":[\"You should find an easier task\",\"You should try again because time brings a reward\",\"You should feel ashamed of your struggle\",\"You should stop trying immediately\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests that if a task is hard, you must persist because time will eventually bring success.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What quality is mentioned as necessary to achieve what \'other folks\' can do?\",\"options\":[\"Luck\",\"Strength\",\"Patience\",\"Wealth\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem asks why you shouldn\'t succeed with patience, just as other people do.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the poem\'s logic, when is the only time a person should truly feel \'disgraced\' by failure?\",\"options\":[\"When they lose a competition\",\"When they find the task too hard\",\"When they stop striving and give up\",\"When they take too much time to succeed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem argues that striving is no disgrace; therefore, the only real failure is the refusal to try again.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What will \'Time\' bring to those who keep trying?\",\"options\":[\"More work\",\"A reward\",\"Disgrace\",\"Failure\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem states, \'Time will bring you your reward,\' emphasizing the result of persistence.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the question \'When do we generally feel ashamed?\', which word from the poem is a synonym for \'shame\'?\",\"options\":[\"Strive\",\"Patience\",\"Disgrace\",\"Reward\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the poem, \'disgrace\' is used to describe the feeling of shame associated with failure.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(22061,52,8,'English','en','2.2 The House builder','[\"Architect designs the building structure.\",\"Engineer finalises details and ensures safety.\",\"Building contractor hires workers and supervises construction.\",\"Mason builds walls, floors and ensures quality of stone and bricks.\",\"Carpenter makes wooden framework for doors and windows.\",\"Tiler lays tiles on floors and walls.\",\"Interior decorator beautifies the inside of a home.\",\"A syllable is a single sound containing a vowel.\",\"Words with one vowel sound are one‑syllable words.\",\"Two‑syllable words have two vowel sounds, e.g. father, mason, builder.\",\"Three‑syllable words have three vowel sounds, e.g. engineer, carpenter, construction.\",\"Retirement is leaving a job after a long career.\",\"People retire when they reach a certain age or after many years of work.\",\"Reasons for retirement include age, health, or desire for rest.\",\"After retirement people may spend time with family or hobbies.\",\"A mason’s dedication, diligence and persistence made him highly sought after.\",\"A contractor rewards good work with a good salary and appreciation.\",\"A legal ownership document is given when a house is handed over.\",\"Homophones are words that sound the same but have different meanings.\",\"Examples: hair – hare, waist – waste, knew – new.\",\"Understanding syllables helps in pronunciation and spelling.\"]','[{\"q\":\"According to the text, which professional is responsible for planning and designing a structure?\",\"options\":[\"Engineer\",\"Architect\",\"Building contractor\",\"Mason\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text matches the Architect with the work of planning and designing the structure.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary responsibility of an Engineer in construction?\",\"options\":[\"To build walls and roofs\",\"To make wooden frameworks\",\"To ensure the structure is strong and stable\",\"To do the flooring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that an Engineer ensures the structure will be strong and stable.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which professional is tasked with making the wooden framework of doors and windows?\",\"options\":[\"Mason\",\"Tiler\",\"Carpenter\",\"Interior decorator\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a Carpenter as one who makes wooden frameworks of doors, windows, etc.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does a Tiler do in the process of house building?\",\"options\":[\"Builds the roof\",\"Does the flooring\",\"Plasters the walls\",\"Employs workers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the matching exercise in the text, a Tiler does the flooring.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A person who builds walls and roofs and also does the plastering is called a:\",\"options\":[\"Mason\",\"Carpenter\",\"Engineer\",\"Architect\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text describes a Mason as someone who builds walls, roof, etc., and plasters.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which professional supervises the construction and employs the workers?\",\"options\":[\"Interior decorator\",\"Architect\",\"Building contractor\",\"Engineer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Building contractor supervises construction and employs workers and professionals.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific role of an Interior decorator as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Designing the building\'s exterior\",\"Making wooden doors\",\"Beautifying the inside of a home\",\"Ensuring the structure is stable\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text matches the Interior decorator with the work of beautifying the inside of a home.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a homeowner wants to ensure their new house won\'t collapse during a storm, which professional\'s expertise is most critical for this specific need?\",\"options\":[\"Tiler\",\"Engineer\",\"Interior decorator\",\"Carpenter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Engineer ensures the structure will be strong and stable.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If you need to hire a team of workers and manage the daily progress of a construction site, whom should you contact?\",\"options\":[\"Architect\",\"Mason\",\"Building contractor\",\"Tiler\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Building contractor supervises construction and employs workers.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the roles described, which two professionals work most closely on the physical \'shell\' (walls and frame) of the house?\",\"options\":[\"Interior decorator and Tiler\",\"Architect and Building contractor\",\"Mason and Carpenter\",\"Engineer and Interior decorator\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Masons build walls and roofs, while Carpenters make the wooden frameworks.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which professional\'s work is primarily focused on the aesthetic appeal of the home\'s interior rather than its structural strength?\",\"options\":[\"Engineer\",\"Interior decorator\",\"Mason\",\"Building contractor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Interior decorator beautifies the inside, whereas the others focus on structure or management.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the context of the Chit-Chat section, \'retirement from occupation\' most likely refers to:\",\"options\":[\"Starting a new construction project\",\"Leaving one\'s professional work permanently\",\"Hiring a building contractor\",\"Designing a house plan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The discussion questions about \'when do people retire\' and \'reasons to retire\' imply leaving one\'s occupation.\",\"topic\":\"Professionals in Construction\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is each unit of pronunciation having one vowel sound called?\",\"options\":[\"A consonant\",\"A syllable\",\"A beat\",\"A letter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines each unit of pronunciation having one vowel sound as a syllable.\",\"topic\":\"Understanding Syllables\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Syllables are sometimes referred to as the ______ of spoken language.\",\"options\":[\"rhythms\",\"notes\",\"beats\",\"tunes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that syllables are sometimes referred to as the \'beats\' of spoken language.\",\"topic\":\"Understanding Syllables\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A syllable is described as a single, ______ sound of a spoken or written word.\",\"options\":[\"unbroken\",\"divided\",\"complex\",\"silent\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines a syllable as a single, unbroken sound.\",\"topic\":\"Understanding Syllables\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what must a syllable always contain?\",\"options\":[\"Two consonants\",\"One vowel sound\",\"At least five letters\",\"A hyphen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines a syllable as a unit of pronunciation having one vowel sound.\",\"topic\":\"Understanding Syllables\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following describes the structure of a syllable?\",\"options\":[\"Only consonant sounds\",\"Only vowel sounds without consonants\",\"One vowel sound with or without consonant sounds around it\",\"Multiple vowel sounds in one unit\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states a syllable has one vowel sound with or without consonant sounds around it.\",\"topic\":\"Understanding Syllables\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the examples provided, how many syllables does the word \'mason\' have?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'ma-son\' as an example of a word with two syllables.\",\"topic\":\"Understanding Syllables\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words from the text is an example of a three-syllable word?\",\"options\":[\"builder\",\"father\",\"construction\",\"will\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text categorizes \'cons-truc-tion\' as having three syllables.\",\"topic\":\"Understanding Syllables\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How is the word \'carpenter\' correctly broken into syllables according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"car-penter\",\"carp-enter\",\"c-a-r-p-e-n-t-e-r\",\"car-pen-ter\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text provides the breakdown \'car-pen-ter\' for the word carpenter.\",\"topic\":\"Understanding Syllables\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the word that has only one syllable according to the text.\",\"options\":[\"see\",\"father\",\"mason\",\"engineer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists \'see\' as an example of a word with just one syllable.\",\"topic\":\"Understanding Syllables\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student breaks a word into units based on \'beats\' of language, what are they identifying?\",\"options\":[\"The number of letters\",\"The number of syllables\",\"The number of consonants\",\"The meaning of the word\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that \'beats\' is another way to refer to syllables.\",\"topic\":\"Understanding Syllables\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Who did the mason work for in the story?\",\"options\":[\"A famous architect\",\"A building contractor\",\"A civil engineer\",\"The house owner\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the mason worked for a building contractor.\",\"topic\":\"The Dedicated Mason\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is the definition of a \'mason\'?\",\"options\":[\"One who designs the house layout\",\"One who finalizes engineering details\",\"One who builds with stone, bricks, cement etc.\",\"One who provides construction materials\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines a mason as someone who builds with stone, bricks, cement, etc.\",\"topic\":\"The Dedicated Mason\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who finalizes the details of the house before the contractor sends for the mason?\",\"options\":[\"The architect\",\"The owner\",\"The mason\",\"The engineer\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions details are finalized by the engineer before the mason starts.\",\"topic\":\"The Dedicated Mason\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What was the mason\'s attitude towards his work?\",\"options\":[\"He worked only for the money\",\"He strove to do his work to perfection\",\"He preferred to work slowly and waste time\",\"He ignored the engineer\'s details\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states the mason always strove to do his work to perfection.\",\"topic\":\"The Dedicated Mason\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these qualities made the mason a very good workman?\",\"options\":[\"He used the cheapest materials available\",\"He finished the work before the architect designed it\",\"He took great interest and worked with full dedication\",\"He only built walls and ignored doorways\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text highlights his interest and full dedication as reasons for his quality work.\",\"topic\":\"The Dedicated Mason\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the meaning of the word \'zeal\'?\",\"options\":[\"Constant careful efforts\",\"Great enthusiasm and energy in one\'s efforts\",\"Money given for work done\",\"Feeling disappointed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The glossary in the figure defines zeal as great enthusiasm and energy.\",\"topic\":\"The Dedicated Mason\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/041