 text mentions Mrs. Darling \'helped them to get the boat out.\'\",\"topic\":\"Setting Off for the Rescue\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What was Mrs. Darling\'s main concern regarding the storm?\",\"options\":[\"That the boat would get lost\",\"That her family would be drowned\",\"That the people were already dead\",\"That the wind would break the window\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She asks, \'How will it help those poor people if you are drowned?\'\",\"topic\":\"Setting Off for the Rescue\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, what was Mrs. Darling doing as they \'set off\'?\",\"options\":[\"She was shouting for them to come back\",\"She was watching and praying\",\"She was rowing with them\",\"She was calling for neighbors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text concludes by saying \'She watched and prayed as they set off.\'\",\"topic\":\"Setting Off for the Rescue\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does Mrs. Darling\'s statement \'God will help them, perhaps, but we cannot!\' imply?\",\"options\":[\"She believes the situation is too dangerous for humans to intervene\",\"She does not want to help the people\",\"She thinks God is rowing the boat\",\"She believes the storm is not real\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"It implies that she feels the storm is so severe that only a miracle can help, as human effort seems impossible to her.\",\"topic\":\"Setting Off for the Rescue\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What were the waves at sea compared to in the text?\",\"options\":[\"High walls\",\"Hills\",\"Mountains\",\"Giant buildings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the boat went up and down over waves as high as hills.\",\"topic\":\"Reaching the Rocks\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what does the word \'clinging\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"To save someone\",\"To begin a journey\",\"To attach oneself to\",\"To row a boat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The voc