s, and 3 women, totaling 7 people.\",\"topic\":\"The Rescue Operation\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"How many total survivors were rescued from the rocks across both trips?\",\"options\":[\"Five\",\"Seven\",\"Nine\",\"Eleven\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The first trip rescued 5 (2 sailors + 3 women) and the second trip rescued 4 men, totaling 9.\",\"topic\":\"The Rescue Operation\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did William Darling and the two sailors have to row back across the sea?\",\"options\":[\"To find the wrecked ship\",\"To rescue four men still on the rock\",\"To get more supplies from the lighthouse\",\"To look for Grace\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they rowed back to rescue the four men still on the rock.\",\"topic\":\"The Rescue Operation\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \'dangerous sea\' suggest about the rescue operation?\",\"options\":[\"The water was very shallow\",\"The journey was easy and quick\",\"The conditions were risky and required courage\",\"The sea was full of rocks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The term \'dangerous\' implies that the rescue was a high-risk and difficult task.\",\"topic\":\"The Rescue Operation\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the survivors stay after being rescued from the rocks?\",\"options\":[\"On the wrecked ship\",\"On the rocks\",\"At the lighthouse\",\"In the boat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions they journeyed back to the lighthouse where Grace and the women got out.\",\"topic\":\"The Rescue Operation\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Who remained at the lighthouse while the second rescue trip took place?\",\"options\":[\"William Darling and the sailors\",\"Grace and the three women\",\"The four men from the rock\",\"Only the two sailors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says Grace and the three women got out at the lighthouse before the men rowed back.\",\"topic\":\"The Rescue Operation\",\"part\":12,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was Grace Darling busy doing all day after the rescue?\",\"options\":[\"Resting in her room\",\"Helping her mother warm and feed the passengers\",\"Writing the story for the newspapers\",\"Sailing back to the wreck\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states Grace was busy helping her mother to warm and feed the rescued passengers.\",\"topic\":\"Fame and Recognition\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Where did the rescued passengers return to after several days?\",\"options\":[\"Scotland\",\"Ireland\",\"England\",\"Wales\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions the passengers were able to return to their homes in England.\",\"topic\":\"Fame and Recognition\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To whom did the passengers first tell the story of the brave girl and her father?\",\"options\":[\"To the newspaper reporters\",\"To their families and friends\",\"To other lighthouse keepers\",\"To the government officials\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says they told the story to their families and friends.\",\"topic\":\"Fame and Recognition\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How did the story of Grace and her father\'s heroism reach a wider audience?\",\"options\":[\"Through radio broadcasts\",\"Through stories told in newspapers\",\"Through letters written by Grace\",\"Through a book written by the father\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the story of their heroism was told in the newspapers.\",\"topic\":\"Fame and Recognition\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What was the immediate result of the passengers sharing their experience?\",\"options\":[\"Grace and her father became famous suddenly\",\"Grace decided to leave the lighthouse\",\"The passengers stayed at the lighthouse forever\",\"The lighthouse was closed down\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that suddenly Grace Darling and her father were famous after the story was told.\",\"topic\":\"Fame and Recognition\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"How does the text describe the lives of lighthouse keepers?\",\"options\":[\"Exciting and social\",\"Dangerous and lonely\",\"Safe and comfortable\",\"Boring and easy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly describes their lives as \'dangerous, lonely lives\'.\",\"topic\":\"Fame and Recognition\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a charity wanted to use the fame of Grace Darling to help others, who would be the beneficiaries according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Only the rescued passengers\",\"All lighthouse keepers\",\"Newspaper publishers\",\"Grace\'s mother only\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions money was raised to help all the lighthouse keepers.\",\"topic\":\"Fame and Recognition\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Grace not have any time to rest after the rescue?\",\"options\":[\"She had to go back to sea immediately\",\"She was occupied with caring for the survivors\",\"She was busy talking to the famous people\",\"She had to travel to England\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text indicates she was busy helping her mother with the rescued passengers, leaving no time for rest.\",\"topic\":\"Fame and Recognition\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What can be inferred about the spread of Grace\'s fame?\",\"options\":[\"It was a slow process over many years\",\"It happened rapidly through word of mouth and media\",\"It only stayed within the local village\",\"It was kept secret by the passengers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The use of the word \'suddenly\' and the mention of newspapers suggest the fame spread quickly.\",\"topic\":\"Fame and Recognition\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What was the primary purpose of raising money following the news of the rescue?\",\"options\":[\"To pay the passengers for their story\",\"To support lighthouse keepers in their difficult profession\",\"To build a new home for Grace in England\",\"To fund the local newspaper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says money was raised to help lighthouse keepers in their dangerous, lonely lives.\",\"topic\":\"Fame and Recognition\",\"part\":13,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"At what age did Grace die according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Twenty five\",\"Twenty seven\",\"Thirty\",\"Seventeen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'She died at the age of twenty seven.\'\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What were Grace and her father given for their heroism?\",\"options\":[\"A gold medal\",\"A new boat\",\"A special reward\",\"A large sum of money\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions, \'Grace and her father were given a special reward for their heroism.\'\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the Language Study section, why are tag questions often used?\",\"options\":[\"To start a new conversation\",\"To confirm information we think is true\",\"To express extreme anger\",\"To give a direct command\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines tag questions as being \'often used to confirm information that we think, we know is true.\'\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the rule provided, if the main clause is negative, what must the question tag be?\",\"options\":[\"Negative\",\"Exclamatory\",\"Affirmative\",\"Imperative\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states, \'if the main clause is negative question tag is affirmative.\'\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What action of Grace shows her \'unselfish courage\' as mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"She lived for twenty seven years\",\"She rested after the rescue\",\"She risked her own life for others\",\"She received a special reward\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains her courage by saying, \'She risked her own life for others.\'\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Choose the correct Question Tag for the sentence: \'She risked her own life, _______?\'\",\"options\":[\"did she?\",\"didn\'t she?\",\"was she?\",\"wasn\'t she?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to section (A)(iii) of the text, the correct tag is \'didn\'t she?\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which modal correctly completes the sentence: \'They _______ hear anything else.\'?\",\"options\":[\"does not\",\"have not\",\"could not\",\"should\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Section (B)(i) of the text uses \'could not\' to complete this sentence.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the proper modal used in the text to express necessity in the sentence \'We _______ do something.\'\",\"options\":[\"must\",\"would\",\"need\",\"may\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Section (B)(iv) of the text uses the modal \'must\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is an example of an Interrogative sentence from the text?\",\"options\":[\"Do not try.\",\"Will you ever sleep again?\",\"She risked her own life.\",\"No, no!\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In section (C), \'Will you ever sleep again?\' is matched with the \'Interrogative\' type.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How is the sentence \'\\\"No\\\", no! She exclaimed\' classified in the Language Study section?\",\"options\":[\"Assertive\",\"Imperative\",\"Exclamatory\",\"Interrogative\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Section (C) matches this sentence with the \'Exclamatory\' type.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which sentence type is correctly matched with the sentence \'Do not try.\'?\",\"options\":[\"Exclamatory\",\"Assertive (Statement)\",\"Interrogative\",\"Imperative\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure matches \'(a) Do not try\' with \'(iv) Imperative\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/061_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which sentence is categorized as an \'Assertive (Statement)\'?\",\"options\":[\"Do not try.\",\"Will you ever sleep again?\",\"Grace did not have any time to rest now.\",\"\\\"No\\\", no! She exclaimed.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure matches sentence (c) with \'(ii) Assertive (Statement)\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Study\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"52\\/061_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the rules of a Word Ladder, what must be true about the starting and ending words?\",\"options\":[\"They must start with the same letter\",\"They must be of the same length\",\"They must be synonyms\",\"They must be proper nouns\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that starting and ending words in a Word Ladder must be of the same length.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a Word Chain, which letter does the next word begin with?\",\"options\":[\"The first letter of the previous word\",\"The middle letter of the previous word\",\"The letter that the previous word ended with\",\"Any vowel from the previous word\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A Word Chain begins with the letter that the previous word ended with.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is a Tongue Twister defined as in the text?\",\"options\":[\"A sequence of words difficult to pronounce quickly\",\"A list of words that rhyme perfectly\",\"A ladder of words with the same length\",\"A chain of nouns and adjectives\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines a Tongue Twister as a sequence of words or sounds difficult to pronounce quickly and correctly.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is strictly forbidden as an intermediate step in a Word Ladder?\",\"options\":[\"Verbs\",\"Adjectives\",\"Proper nouns\",\"Three-letter words\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The rules for Word Ladder explicitly state \'no proper nouns allowed!\'.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'HARD to EASY\' word ladder example, which word follows \'hard\'?\",\"options\":[\"care\",\"hare\",\"east\",\"cast\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The example chain provided is: hard - hare - care - cart - cast - east - easy.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a Word Chain follows the theme \'Nouns\' and starts with \'Teacher\', what is the next required step?\",\"options\":[\"A word starting with \'T\'\",\"A word starting with \'R\'\",\"An adjective starting with \'R\'\",\"A verb starting with \'E\'\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since \'Teacher\' ends in \'r\', the next word in the chain must start with \'R\'.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is an example of a Tongue Twister provided in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Hard to Easy\",\"Pig to Sty\",\"Saina leads, Sayali needs\",\"Teacher to R\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Saina leads, Sayali needs\' is listed under the Tongue Twister examples.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you are playing a Word Chain with the theme \'Noun\' and the current word is \'Player\', which word would be a valid next step?\",\"options\":[\"Run\",\"Red\",\"Rabbit\",\"Rarely\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"\'Rabbit\' is a noun starting with \'r\', which is the last letter of \'Player\'.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In a Word Ladder from \'CAT\' to \'DOG\', which of these would be a valid first step by changing only one letter?\",\"options\":[\"COT\",\"DIG\",\"CAR\",\"DOT\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\'COT\' changes only the middle letter \'A\' to \'O\', moving closer to the \'O\' in \'DOG\'.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the ladder \'Pig - wig - wag - way - say - sty\', how many letters are changed at each individual step?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Two\",\"Three\",\"None\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The Word Ladder rule states players can change one letter at a time.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why is \'Peter piper picked a pack of pickled peper\' considered a tongue twister?\",\"options\":[\"Because it uses a word ladder\",\"Because it is a sequence of similar sounds difficult to say fast\",\"Because it follows a noun-verb-noun chain\",\"Because it uses only proper nouns\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tongue twisters use sequences of words or sounds that are difficult to pronounce quickly and correctly.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If a player used the word \'India\' in a Word Ladder, why would it be considered an invalid move?\",\"options\":[\"It is too long\",\"It is a proper noun\",\"It has too many vowels\",\"It is not a valid English word\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that in a Word Ladder, \'no proper nouns allowed!\'.\",\"topic\":\"WORD PLAY\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, where can you find a new word for the \'Just one new word a day\' activity?\",\"options\":[\"Only in your English textbook\",\"Only on the radio or TV\",\"Anywhere like newspapers, boards, or hoardings\",\"Only by asking your teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions you may find a new word anywhere, including textbooks, newspapers, boards, TV, or radio.\",\"topic\":\"Language Learning Activities\",\"part\":19,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first thing you should do after finding a new word?\",\"options\":[\"Translate it into your mother tongue\",\"Write it down on a card\",\"Put it in a dictionary\",\"Find a word that sounds the same\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first step listed under the activity is to write down the new word on a card.\",\"topic\":\"Language Learning Activities\",\"part\":19,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How should the word cards in your collection be arranged?\",\"options\":[\"In the order you found them\",\"By the length of the words\",\"In alphabetical order\",\"By the date they were written\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states to make sure word cards are always arranged in alphabetical order.\",\"topic\":\"Language Learning Activities\",\"part\":19,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If you have cards for \'Boat\' and \'Ship\', where should you insert the new word card \'Ocean\'?\",\"options\":[\"Before \'Boat\'\",\"Between \'Boat\' and \'Ship\'\",\"After \'Ship\'\",\"At the very beginning of the stack\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In alphabetical order, \'O\' comes after \'B\' and before \'S\'.\",\"topic\":\"Language Learning Activities\",\"part\":19,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the \'Question a day\' activity, what is required besides framing a simple question?\",\"options\":[\"Knowing the appropriate answer to it\",\"Translating it into three languages\",\"Finding a word that sounds like the question\",\"Writing it on a hoarding\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states you should also know the appropriate answer to the question you frame.\",\"topic\":\"Language Learning Activities\",\"part\":19,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"How often should you use a new question according to the \'Question a day\' activity?\",\"options\":[\"Once a week\",\"Every day\",\"Only during exams\",\"Whenever you find a new word\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity instructions specify that you must use a new question every day.\",\"topic\":\"Language Learning Activities\",\"part\":19,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct process for the \'A sentence a day\' activity?\",\"options\":[\"Find a sentence in a newspaper and copy it\",\"Frame a sentence in English and translate it to your mother tongue\",\"Frame a sentence in your mother tongue and translate it into English\",\"Look up a sentence in the dictionary\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text instructs to frame a sentence in the mother tongue first, then translate it into English.\",\"topic\":\"Language Learning Activities\",\"part\":19,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"The words \'right\' and \'write\' are examples of words that:\",\"options\":[\"Sound the same but have a different meaning\",\"Have the same spelling but different pronunciation\",\"Look the same and sound the same\",\"Are written in the mother tongue\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'right\' and \'write\' as examples of words that sound the same but have different meanings.\",\"topic\":\"Language Learning Activities\",\"part\":19,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is an example of a word with the same spelling but different pronunciations?\",\"options\":[\"Light\",\"Right\",\"Read\",\"Write\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides \'read\' (pronounced as reed and red) as an example of same spelling but different pronunciation.\",\"topic\":\"Language Learning Activities\",\"part\":19,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word \'light\' represent in the \'Better your work\' section?\",\"options\":[\"A word that sounds like \'write\'\",\"A word that looks and sounds the same but has different meanings\",\"A word that is only found in newspapers\",\"A word that cannot be translated\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'light\' to illustrate words that look and sound the same but have different meanings (not heavy vs lamp light).\",\"topic\":\"Language Learning Activities\",\"part\":19,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To \'Better your work\', what should you do when you find a word like \'read\'?\",\"options\":[\"Check if it has different pronunciations like \'reed\' and \'red\'\",\"Translate it into your mother tongue immediately\",