\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the phrase \'profoundly moved\', what does \'profoundly\' indicate?\",\"options\":[\"That the movement was small\",\"That the movement was caused by a virus\",\"That the feeling was great or deep\",\"That the person is a zoo keeper\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Profoundly is defined as greatly or deeply.\",\"topic\":\"Glossary\",\"part\":3,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the poem, why is it difficult to be a successful vet?\",\"options\":[\"Because animals cannot speak to describe their pain\",\"Because the vet must know the needs of many different animals\",\"Because medicine for animals is very expensive\",\"Because animals are often aggressive towards doctors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The vet must have incredibly wide knowledge because each animal species has a different anatomy and set of problems.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What specific problem is mentioned regarding ducks and chickens in the exercise?\",\"options\":[\"They are refusing to eat their grain\",\"They are losing their feathers\",\"They are failing to lay eggs\",\"They are unable to swim or fly\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions that ducks and chickens are failing to lay as one of the many problems a vet faces.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the lion has caught a chill, what is the \'opposite\' illness affecting the Arctic fox?\",\"options\":[\"It has a broken leg\",\"It is feeling too hot\",\"It has lost its appetite\",\"It is unable to sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem contrasts the lion\'s chill with the Arctic fox being too hot (suffering from heat).\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What physical ailment do the giraffes suffer from according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Sore throats\",\"Broken legs\",\"Stiff necks\",\"Blurred vision\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text specifically asks why the giraffes have got stiff necks.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poet mean by calling the vet \'omniscient\'?\",\"options\":[\"The vet is very wealthy\",\"The vet is all-knowing about animal health\",\"The vet is very old and experienced\",\"The vet is able to talk to animals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Omniscient means all-knowing; the poet uses it to highlight the vast knowledge a vet must possess.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the poet\'s final advice to the reader regarding career choice?\",\"options\":[\"Study hard to become a great vet\",\"Earn a living by treating humans instead\",\"Open a zoo to look after animals\",\"Become a scientist to study animal behavior\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poet advises the reader to be a doctor for humans because it is much easier than being a vet.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the poet use the word \'omniscient\' to describe the vet?\",\"options\":[\"To mock the vet\'s lack of knowledge\",\"To emphasize the incredible variety of knowledge required\",\"To show that the vet is a magical being\",\"To explain why vets are paid more than human doctors\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The term emphasizes that the vet must know everything about every different kind of animal.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, which animal\'s illness is directly related to its natural cold habitat?\",\"options\":[\"The Lion\",\"The Giraffe\",\"The Arctic Fox\",\"The Chicken\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Arctic fox is mentioned in the context of having an illness opposite to a chill, implying it is too hot for its nature.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When the poet asks if the reader thinks he \'means\' his advice, what is he implying?\",\"options\":[\"He is being serious and hates animals\",\"He is being light-hearted or 