 what is the relationship between a pair of numbers regarding their position?\",\"options\":[\"The number to the left is smaller than the other.\",\"The number to the right is smaller than the other.\",\"The number to the left is larger than the other.\",\"Both numbers are always equal regardless of position.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that for any pair of numbers on a number line, the number to the left is smaller.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of rational numbers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the value of a rational number if both its numerator and denominator are multiplied by the same non-zero number?\",\"options\":[\"The value increases.\",\"The value decreases.\",\"The value remains the same.\",\"The value becomes zero.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the value of a rational number does not change if multiplied by a non-zero number.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of rational numbers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the property $\\\\frac{a}{b} = \\\\frac{ka}{kb}$, what is the essential condition for the multiplier $k$?\",\"options\":[\"$k$ must be equal to 0\",\"$k$ must be a non-zero number ($k \\\\ne 0$)\",\"$k$ must be greater than 1\",\"$k$ must be a negative number\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies the condition ($k \\\\ne 0$) for the value to remain the same.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of rational numbers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a number $x$ is located to the left of number $y$ on a number line, which mathematical statement is correct?\",\"options\":[\"$x > y$\",\"$x = y$\",\"$x < y$\",\"$x + y = 0$\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states the number to the left is smaller, which is represented by the symbol \'<\'.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of rational numbers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is $\\\\frac{2}{3}$ equal to $\\\\frac{10}{15}$ based on the provided text?\",\"options\":[\"Because 10 and 15 are larger than 2 and 3.\",\"Because the numerator and denominator were multiplied by the non-zero number 5.\",\"Because they are both positive numbers.\",\"Because they are on the same side of the number line.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that $\\\\frac{a}{b} = \\\\frac{ka}{kb}$; here $k=5$, so the value remains the same.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of rational numbers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the number line rule, how do we compare two rational numbers?\",\"options\":[\"By checking which one has a larger numerator.\",\"By checking which one is further from zero.\",\"By determining their relative positions; the one on the left is smaller.\",\"By adding them together.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines comparison based on the left-right position on the number line.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of rational numbers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If $\\\\frac{a}{b} = \\\\frac{5}{7}$ and we choose $k = 3$, what is the resulting equivalent fraction $\\\\frac{ka}{kb}$?\",\"options\":[\"$\\\\frac{15}{21}$\",\"$\\\\frac{8}{10}$\",\"$\\\\frac{15}{7}$\",\"$\\\\frac{5}{21}$\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Using $\\\\frac{ka}{kb}$, we multiply $5 \\\\times 3 = 15$ and $7 \\\\times 3 = 21$.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of rational numbers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If number $P$ is at $-8$ and number $Q$ is at $-3$ on a number line, which statement is true according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"$Q$ is smaller than $P$.\",\"$P$ is smaller than $Q$ because $P$ is to the left of $Q$.\",\"$P$ and $Q$ are equal.\",\"$-8$ is larger than $-3$.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"On a number line, $-8$ is to the left of $-3$, making it the smaller number.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of rational numbers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following represents the property that rational numbers maintain their value through multiplication?\",\"options\":[\"$\\\\frac{a}{b} = \\\\frac{a+k}{b+k}$\",\"$\\\\frac{a}{b} = \\\\frac{ka}{kb}$\",\"$\\\\frac{a}{b} = \\\\frac{a-k}{b-k}$\",\"$\\\\frac{a}{b} = k \\\\times (a+b)$\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly provides the formula $\\\\frac{a}{b} = \\\\frac{ka}{kb}$ to show the value remains the same.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of rational numbers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the text specify that $k$ must be a \'non zero\' number in the formula $\\\\frac{ka}{kb}$?\",\"options\":[\"Because multiplying by zero would make the denominator zero, which is not allowed.\",\"Because zero is not a rational number.\",\"Because zero is always on the left of the number line.\",\"Because multiplying by zero increases the value.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the fraction $\\\\frac{ka}{kb}$, if $k=0$, the denominator $kb$ becomes zero, which is undefined in rational numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Comparison of rational numbers\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, a negative number is always ______ than a positive number.\",\"options\":[\"greater\",\"less\",\"equal\",\"double\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that a negative number is always less than a positive number.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example 2\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If $a$ and $b$ are positive numbers such that $a < b$, then which of the following is true according to the rule for negative numbers?\",\"options\":[\"$-a < -b$\",\"$-a = -b$\",\"$-a > -b$\",\"$-a$ is positive\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that if $a < b$, then $-a > -b$.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example 2\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What method does the text suggest to verify the comparisons of negative numbers?\",\"options\":[\"Using a calculator\",\"Using a number line\",\"Using multiplication\",\"Using addition\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says to \'Verify the comparisons using a number line.\'\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example 2\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the com