 the number $\\\\sqrt{2}$?\",\"options\":[\"It is a rational number\",\"It is an irrational number\",\"It is a terminating decimal\",\"It is a recurring decimal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that $\\\\sqrt{2}$ is an irrational number.\",\"topic\":\"Showing $\\\\sqrt{2}$ on a number line\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the construction to show $\\\\sqrt{2}$ on a number line, which number does point A represent?\",\"options\":[\"0\",\"2\",\"1\",\"$\\\\sqrt{2}$\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that on a number line, the point A shows the number 1.\",\"topic\":\"Showing $\\\\sqrt{2}$ on a number line\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the characteristic of the decimal form of an irrational number?\",\"options\":[\"Terminating and recurring\",\"Non-terminating and recurring\",\"Terminating and non-recurring\",\"Non-terminating and non-recurring\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states that the decimal form of an irrational number is non-terminating and non-recurring.\",\"topic\":\"Showing $\\\\sqrt{2}$ on a number line\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Numbers on the number line that are not rational numbers are called:\",\"options\":[\"Natural numbers\",\"Irrational numbers\",\"Integers\",\"Whole numbers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines numbers that are not rational as irrational numbers.\",\"topic\":\"Showing $\\\\sqrt{2}$ on a number line\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Using Pythagoras theorem for $\\\\triangle$ OAP, if OA = 1 and AP = 1, what is the value of OP²?\",\"options\":[\"1\",\"2\",\"4\",\"$\\\\sqrt{2}$\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"By Pythagoras theorem, OP² = OA² + AP² = 1² + 1² = 1 + 1 = 2.\",\"topic\":\"Showing $\\\\sqrt{2}$ on a number line\",\"part\":11,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"To show $-\\\\sqrt{2}$ on the number line, where should point R be marked relative to the origin O?\",\"options\":[\"To the right of O\",\"Above point O\",\