entage bar graph defined as in the textbook?\",\"options\":[\"A simple bar graph with large numbers\",\"A subdivided bar graph drawn by converting data into percentages\",\"A graph that only shows the total number of items\",\"A line graph used for town planning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a subdivided bar graph which is drawn by converting the data into percentages is called a percentage bar graph.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a percentage bar graph, what is the height of all the bars?\",\"options\":[\"Variable based on the total number\",\"50 units\",\"100 units\",\"75 units\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that in a percentage bar graph, all bars are in height 100 units.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A percentage bar graph is a specific type of which other graph?\",\"options\":[\"Joint bar graph\",\"Subdivided bar graph\",\"Line graph\",\"Pictograph\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that a percentage bar graph is a specific type of subdivided bar graph.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it necessary to find the percentage of survived plants to compare towns instead of just using the number of trees?\",\"options\":[\"Because the total number of trees planted in each town is different\",\"Because percentages are easier to add\",\"Because the number of trees is always 100\",\"Because the towns are in different districts\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explains that to know which town\'s plantation is more successful, only numbers are not sufficient because the total planted varies (60, 75, 90).\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In each bar of a percentage bar graph, if one part shows the percentage of survived trees, what does the remaining part show?\",\"options\":[\"The total number of trees\",\"The percentage of trees that did not survive\",\"The percentage of trees in the next town\",\"The height of the graph\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the remaining part shows the percentage of trees which did not survive.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to the town data provided, which town had the most successful plantation based on survival percentage?\",\"options\":[\"Morshi\",\"Barshi\",\"Arvi\",\"All were equal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that Arvi has 70%, Morshi 60%, and Barshi 50%, making Arvi the most successful.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the town Arvi, 42 trees out of 60 survived. What is the correct calculation for the percentage of survived trees?\",\"options\":[\"60\\/42 × 100\",\"42\\/100 × 60\",\"42\\/60 × 100\",\"42 + 60 \\/ 100\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text shows the calculation for Arvi as 42\\/60 × 100 = 70.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If 45 trees out of 90 survived in Barshi, what percentage will be shown for survived trees in the bar graph?\",\"options\":[\"45%\",\"90%\",\"50%\",\"55%\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The calculation provided in the text for Barshi is 45\\/90 × 100 = 50.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In Morshi, if the percentage of survived trees is 60%, what is the percentage of trees that did not survive?\",\"options\":[\"40%\",\"60%\",\"15%\",\"75%\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Since the total height is 100 units, 100 - 60 = 40% represents the unsurvived trees.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the scale used on the Y-axis?\",\"options\":[\"1 cm = 10 trees\",\"1 cm = 10 %\",\"1 cm = 1 unit\",\"1 cm = 100 %\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The scale mentioned in the top right corner of the graph image is \'Scale: On Y axis 1 cm = 10 %\'.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/083_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, which town has the highest percentage of \'Trees unsurvived\'?\",\"options\":[\"Arvi\",\"Morshi\",\"Barshi\",\"They are all the same\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the graph, the white part (unsurvived) is largest for Barshi (from 50 to 100, which is 50%).\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/083_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what is the specific calculation shown to find the percentage for town Morshi?\",\"options\":[\"42\\/60 × 100 = 70\",\"45\\/90 × 100 = 50\",\"45\\/75 × 100 = 60\",\"75\\/45 × 100 = 166\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows the calculation for Morshi as 45\\/75 × 100 = 60.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/083_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If we were to draw a percentage bar graph for a new town where 20 out of 25 trees survived, what would be the height of the \'survived\' section?\",\"options\":[\"20 units\",\"25 units\",\"80 units\",\"100 units\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Calculation: 20\\/25 × 100 = 80. In a percentage bar graph, the section height corresponds to the percentage.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Compare the data for Morshi and Barshi. Even though both towns have 45 survived trees, why is Morshi\'s plantation considered more successful?\",\"options\":[\"Because it has a higher total number of trees\",\"Because its percentage of survival (60%) is higher than Barshi\'s (50%)\",\"Because the bar for Morshi is taller than Barshi\",\"Because Morshi is mentioned first in the table\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Success is determined by the percentage of survival; Morshi\'s 60% is greater than Barshi\'s 50%.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step mentioned in the text for drawing a percentage bar graph?\",\"options\":[\"Draw the X and Y axes\",\"Prepare a table with total numbers and percentages\",\"Color the bars blue\",\"Mark 100 units on the graph paper\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'First of all we prepare a table as follows\' before showing the data calculation.\",\"topic\":\"Percentage bar graph\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which two types of bar diagrams are mentioned in the activity for comparison and discussion?\",\"options\":[\"Simple bar diagram and Joint bar diagram\",\"Percentage bar diagram and Subdivided bar diagram\",\"Line graph and Pictograph\",\"Frequency polygon and Histogram\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions comparing and discussing a percentage bar diagram and a subdivided bar diagram.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the activity, what should students do with the two types of bar diagrams?\",\"options\":[\"Only draw them in the notebook\",\"Memorize their definitions\",\"Compare and discuss them\",\"Calculate the mean of the data\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The activity specifically instructs to \'Compare and discuss\' the two types of diagrams.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In which subjects does the text suggest using these bar diagrams to learn graphs?\",\"options\":[\"History and Civics\",\"English and Marathi\",\"Science and Geography\",\"Art and Physical Education\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions using these diagrams to learn graphs in subjects like Science and Geography.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a student is studying a graph in a Geography textbook, which mathematical tool from this activity would be most relevant?\",\"options\":[\"Percentage bar diagram\",\"Pythagoras theorem\",\"Expansion formulae\",\"Square root table\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using percentage and subdivided bar diagrams to learn graphs in Geography.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the primary purpose of the activity mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"To learn how to draw a circle\",\"To use mathematical diagrams to understand graphs in other subjects\",\"To solve algebraic equations\",\"To measure the length of a bar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity aims to use the comparison of bar diagrams to learn graphs in subjects like Science and Geography.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the activity, which of the following is a key action to perform during the learning process?\",\"options\":[\"Discussion\",\"Subtraction\",\"Multiplication\",\"Division\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly lists \'discuss\' as one of the actions to be performed in the activity.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A student wants to apply their knowledge of Statistics to a Science project. Which diagram type mentioned in the text should they consider?\",\"options\":[\"Subdivided bar diagram\",\"Frequency curve\",\"Tally mark table\",\"Number line\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A subdivided bar diagram is one of the two types mentioned to be used in subjects like Science.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What does the activity imply about the relationship between Mathematics and subjects like Science and Geography?\",\"options\":[\"They are completely unrelated\",\"Mathematical diagrams help in understanding concepts in other subjects\",\"Only Science uses graphs, not Geography\",\"Geography does not require mathematical tools\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text suggests using mathematical bar diagrams to learn graphs in Science and Geography, showing inter-subject utility.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"When comparing a percentage bar diagram and a subdivided bar diagram, what is a student likely to observe about their structure?\",\"options\":[\"Both represent data using bars divided into parts\",\"One uses bars and the other uses only dots\",\"One is used for Science and the other only for Geography\",\"They cannot be compared\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Both are types of bar diagrams that show components, which is the basis for their comparison in the activity.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the activity suggest \'comparing\' these two specific diagrams?\",\"options\":[\"To identify similarities and differences in how they represent data\",\"To prove that one is always better than the other\",\"To avoid using them in Science\",\"To make the Geography syllabus longer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Comparison in a mathematical context is used to understand the distinct characteristics and applications of different data representation methods.\",\"topic\":\"Exercise\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29');
INSERT INTO `ep_topic_packs` VALUES (22125,55,8,'Maths','en','Equations in one variable','[\"- An equation is a statement that two expressions are equal.\",\"- The value of the variable that makes the equation true is called the solution.\",\"- Solving an equation means finding its solution.\",\"- Operations performed on both sides of an equation do not change its solution.\",\"- Allowed operations: add the same number, subtract the same number, multiply by the same non‑zero number, divide by the same non‑zero number.\",\"- When an equation contains parentheses, first simplify inside the parentheses before applying operations.\",\"- If a variable appears on both sides, bring all variable terms to one side and constants to the other.\",\"- After simplifying, isolate the variable by dividing or multiplying.\",\"- Check the solution by substituting it back into the original equation.\",\"- For equations of the form \\\\\\/(a\\/x) = b, multiply both sides by the denominator to clear fractions.\",\"- In word problems, translate the given information into an algebraic expression using a variable.\",\"- When a variable represents a quantity, use the same letter consistently.\",\"- For linear equations, the solution is unique unless the equation is an identity or inconsistent.\",\"- In a system of equations, solve one equation for a variable and substitute into the other.\",\"- Practice: write the equation, perform operations step by step, and verify the answer.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the value of the variable which satisfies a given equation called?\",\"options\":[\"The constant\",\"The solution\",\"The expression\",\"The operation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the value of the variable which satisfies the given equation is called the solution of the equation.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'solving an equation\' mean according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To change the variable\",\"To find the solution of the equation\",\"To add numbers to the variable\",\"To remove the equality sign\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly defines solving an equation as finding the solution of the equation.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the same operation is performed on both sides of an equation, what happens to its solution?\",\"options\":[\"The solution changes\",\"The solution becomes zero\",\"The solution does not change\",\"The solution becomes double\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the equation obtained by performing the same operation on its both sides does not change its solution.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why do we use the property of performing the same operation on both sides of an equation?\",\"options\":[\"To make the equation longer\",\"To eliminate the variable entirely\",\"To obtain new but simpler equations\",\"To change the value of the variable\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, using this property helps obtain new but simpler equations to solve the given equation.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a valid operation to perform on both sides of an equation to keep the solution unchanged?\",\"options\":[\"Add the same number to both sides\",\"Add different numbers to both sides\",\"Multiply only the left side by a number\",\"Divide only the right side by a number\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text lists adding the same number to both sides as one of the valid operations.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To solve the equation \'x - 7 = 10\', which operation should be performed on both sides based on the text?\",\"options\":[\"Subtract 7 from both sides\",\"Divide both sides by 7\",\"Add 7 to both sides\",\"Multiply both sides by 10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Adding the same number (7) to both sides is a valid operation mentioned in the text to simplify and solve the equation.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"When dividing both sides of an equation by a number, what is the specific condition mentioned in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The number must be a variable\",\"The number must be a non-zero number\",\"The number must be positive\",\"The number must be greater than one\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text specifies that we can divide both sides by the same \'non zero\' number.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the equation \'5x = 20\', which operation helps in finding the solution?\",\"options\":[\"Subtracting 5 from both sides\",\"Adding 5 to both sides\",\"Dividing both sides by 5\",\"Multiplying both sides by 20\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Dividing both sides by the same non-zero number (5) is a valid operation to isolate the variable and find the solution.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these operations is NOT listed in the text as a way to obtain a simpler equation?\",\"options\":[\"Subtracting the same number from both sides\",\"Multiplying both sides by the same number\",\"Squaring both sides of the equation\",\"Adding the same number to both sides\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text only lists addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division by non-zero numbers as operations.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If a student divides both sides of an equation by zero, why is this incorrect according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Because the text says to divide by a non-zero number\",\"Because zero is not a number\",\"Because the solution must change\",\"Because addition is preferred over division\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text specifically states that division must be by a \'non zero\' number.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall.\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the equation $x + 4 = 9$, what number must be subtracted from both sides to solve for $x$?\",\"options\":[\"9\",\"5\",\"4\",\"13\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to Ex. (1), to solve $x + 4 = 9$, we subtract 4 from both sides: $x + 4 - 4 = 9 - 4$.\",\"topic\":\"Fill in the boxes\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the equation $x - 2 = 7$, what number should be filled in the boxes: $x - 2 + \\\\square = 7 + \\\\square$?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"2\",\"9\",\"5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to Ex. (2), we add 2 to both sides to isolate $x$.\",\"topic\":\"Fill in the boxes\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To solve the equation $\\\\frac{x}{3} = 4$, by what number should both sides be multiplied?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"12\",\"1\",\"3\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Ex. (3) shows that we multiply both sides by 3: $\\\\frac{x}{3} \\\\times 3 = 4 \\\\times 3$.\",\"topic\":\"Fill in the boxes\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the equation $4x = 24$, which number is used as the divisor in the step $\\\\frac{4x}{\\\\square} = \\\\frac{24}{\\\\square}$?\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"24\",\"6\",\"1\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Ex. (4) shows that we divide both sides by 4 to solve for $x$.\",\"topic\":\"Fill in the boxes\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final value of $x$ in the equation $x + 4 = 9$?\",\"options\":[\"x = 13\",\"x = 5\",\"x = 4\",\"x = 9\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"From Ex. (1), $x = 9 - 4$, which equals 5.\",\"topic\":\"Fill in the boxes\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final value of $x$ in the equation $x - 2 = 7$?\",\"options\":[\"x = 5\",\"x = 7\",\"x = 9\",\"x = 2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"From Ex. (2), $x = 7 + 2$, which equals 9.\",\"topic\":\"Fill in the boxes\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Ex. (3), if $\\\\frac{x}{3} = 4$, then $x = \\\\square$. What is the value of $x$?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"7\",\"1\",\"4\\/3\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"By multiplying both sides by 3, we get $x = 4 \\\\times 3 = 12$.\",\"topic\":\"Fill in the boxes\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on Ex. (4), if $4x = 24$, then $x = \\\\square$. What is the value of $x$?\",\"options\":[\"20\",\"28\",\"96\",\"6\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"By dividing both sides by 4, we get $x = 24 \\/ 4 = 6$.\",\"topic\":\"Fill in the boxes\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the step $\\\\frac{4x}{4} = \\\\frac{24}{4}$, why is the number 4 chosen to be in the denominator?\",\"options\":[\"Because 4 is the result of $24 - 20$\",\"Because 4 is the coefficient of $x$ that needs to be removed\",\"Because 4 is the smallest number in the equation\",\"Because 24 is a multiple of 4\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"To isolate $x$ in $4x = 24$, we must divide by the coefficient 4.\",\"topic\":\"Fill in the boxes\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the equation $\\\\frac{x}{3} = 4$, the operation $\\\\frac{x}{3} \\\\times 3$ is performed to:\",\"options\":[\"Make the denominator larger\",\"Multiply the variable by itself\",\"Isolate $x$ by canceling the division by 3\",\"Change the value of $x$\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Multiplying by 3 cancels out the division by 3, leaving $x$ by itself.\",\"topic\":\"Fill in the boxes\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first operation performed on the equation in the given example?\",\"options\":[\"Adding 30 to both sides\",\"Multiplying both sides by 5\",\"Subtracting 3x from both sides\",\"Dividing both sides by 7\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Multiplying both sides by 5\' as the first step in the solution.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the final value of x obtained in the worked example?\",\"options\":[\"x = 42\",\"x = 7\",\"x = 6\",\"x = 30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The final step of the solution shows x = 6.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which number is added to both sides of the equation 10x - 30 = 3x + 12?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"12\",\"3\",\"30\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly says \'Adding 30 to both sides\' after the expansion step.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why are both sides of the equation multiplied by 5 in the first step?\",\"options\":[\"To increase the value of x\",\"To eliminate the denominator 5\",\"To subtract 3x from both sides\",\"To add 30 to both sides\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Multiplying by 5 is done to clear the fraction where the denominator is 5.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the step \'10x - 30 = 3x + 12\', what is the purpose of adding 30 to both sides?\",\"options\":[\"To isolate the term with x on the right side\",\"To remove the constant -30 from the left side\",\"To divide the equation by 7\",\"To multiply the equation by 5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Adding 30 cancels out the -30 on the left side, helping to isolate the variable terms.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What operation is used to transform 7x = 42 into x = 6?\",\"options\":[\"Subtracting 7 from both sides\",\"Multiplying both sides by 7\",\"Dividing both sides by 7\",\"Adding 7 to both sides\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Dividing both sides by 7\' to reach the final solution.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the example, what is the result of the calculation 10x - 3x?\",\"options\":[\"13x\",\"7x\",\"30x\",\"7\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows that 10x - 3x results in 7x.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the result of the expression 3x + 12 + 30 as shown in the solution steps?\",\"options\":[\"3x + 42\",\"3x + 18\",\"45x\",\"3x - 18\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text shows that 3x + 12 + 30 simplifies to 3x + 42.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following correctly shows the expansion of 10(x - 3) as used in the text?\",\"options\":[\"10x - 3\",\"10x - 30\",\"x - 30\",\"10x + 30\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text shows 10(x - 3) becomes 10x - 30 in the second line of the solution.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Analyze the step: 10x - 3x = 3x + 42 - 3x. What is the main objective of this specific step?\",\"options\":[\"To multiply the equation by 3\",\"To remove the variable term 3x from the right side\",\"To add 30 to both sides\",\"To find the final value of x\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Subtracting 3x from both sides removes the variable from the right side so all x terms are on the left.\",\"topic\":\"Worked Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is used to convert the information given in a word problem into an algebraic expression?\",\"options\":[\"A variable\",\"A constant only\",\"A diagram only\",\"A ruler\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that information in word problems can be converted into an algebraic expression using a variable.\",\"topic\":\"Converting Word Problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the solution for the equation 9x - 4 = 6x + 29, what is the first step performed on both sides?\",\"options\":[\"Subtracting 4\",\"Adding 4\",\"Dividing by 9\",\"Subtracting 29\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The solution text explicitly states \'Adding 4 to both sides\' as the first step.\",\"topic\":\"Converting Word Problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the textbook solution for 9x - 4 = 6x + 29, what is the final value of x?\",\"options\":[\"33\",\"3\",\"11\",\"4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The final line of the provided solution is \'x = 11\'.\",\"topic\":\"Converting Word Problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, if \'My age is x year\', how is the sister\'s age expressed in years?\",\"options\":[\"x + 4\",\"4x\",\"x - 4\",\"x \\/ 4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure states sister\'s age is 4 less than my age, which is (x - 4).\",\"topic\":\"Converting Word Problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/087_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which expression represents the friend\'s age?\",\"options\":[\"x + 5\",\"x \\/ 2 + 5\",\"2x + 5\",\"5x + 1\\/2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The figure shows friend\'s age is 5 more than half of my age, which is x\\/2 + 5.\",\"topic\":\"Converting Word Problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/087_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"According to the solution steps, what operation is used to transition from 3x = 33 to x = 11?\",\"options\":[\"Subtracting 3 from both sides\",\"Adding 3 to both sides\",\"Multiplying both sides by 3\",\"Dividing both sides by 3\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Dividing both sides by 3\' to get the final value of x.\",\"topic\":\"Converting Word Problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If \'My age is x year\', how is the mother\'s age represented according to the diagram?\",\"options\":[\"x + 3\",\"3x\",\"x - 3\",\"x \\/ 3\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The diagram states mother\'s age is 3 times my age, which is 3x.\",\"topic\":\"Converting Word Problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/087_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the diagram, the grandmother\'s age is given as (4x + 10) years. What is the word description for this?\",\"options\":[\"4 more than 10 times my age\",\"10 more than 4 times my age\",\"10 less than 4 times my age\",\"4 times the sum of my age and 10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text in the box says \'My grandmother\'s age is 10 more than 4 times my age\'.\",\"topic\":\"Converting Word Problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/087_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"To solve the equation 9x = 6x + 33, what step is taken to move the variable term to one side?\",\"options\":[\"Adding 6x to both sides\",\"Subtracting 6x from both sides\",\"Dividing both sides by 6x\",\"Subtracting 33 from both sides\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The solution shows \'Subtracting 6x from both sides\' to simplify the equation to 3x = 33.\",\"topic\":\"Converting Word Problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If my age is x, and my father\'s age is \'32 years more than my age\', what is the algebraic expression for his age?\",\"options\":[\"32x\",\"x - 32\",\"x + 32\",\"x \\/ 32\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase \'32 years more than\' indicates addition to the variable x.\",\"topic\":\"Converting Word Problems\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/087_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the expression for \'My grandmother\'s age\' if it is 10 more than 4 times my age (x)?\",\"options\":[\"10x + 4\",\"4x + 10\",\"4(x + 10)\",\"x\\/4 + 10\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states grandmother\'s age is (4x + 10) yrs.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If \'My age\' is represented by x, how is \'My sister\'s age\' expressed in the text?\",\"options\":[\"x + 4\",\"4 - x\",\"x - 4\",\"x \\/ 4\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states sister\'s age is 4 less than my age, which is x - 4.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which expression represents \'My friend\'s age\' being 5 more than half of my age?\",\"options\":[\"x\\/2 + 5\",\"2x + 5\",\"(x + 5) \\/ 2\",\"5x + 1\\/2\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines friend\'s age as x\\/2 + 5.\",\"topic\":\"Introduction\",\"part\":10,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If \'My age\' is x, what is the expression for \'My father\'s age\' which is 32 years more than mine?\",\"options\":[\"32x\",\"x - 32\",\"x + 32\",\"x \\/ 32\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"32 years more than x is written as x + 