it number problem, what is the sum when the original number is added to the number obtained by interchanging digits?\",\"options\":[\"45\",\"54\",\"66\",\"700\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the sum of the original number and the interchanged number is 66.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Digits and Tickets\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If \'x\' is the smallest of three consecutive natural numbers, how is the greatest number represented?\",\"options\":[\"x + 1\",\"x + 2\",\"x + 3\",\"2x\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Consecutive natural numbers increase by 1, so the three numbers are x, x+1, and x+2.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Numbers and Profit\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"According to Problem 7, which equation correctly represents \'five times the smallest number is 9 more than four times the greatest number\'?\",\"options\":[\"5x + 9 = 4(x + 2)\",\"5(x + 2) = 4x + 9\",\"5x = 4(x + 2) + 9\",\"5x = 4x + 2 + 9\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The smallest is x and the greatest is x+2; \'9 more than\' means adding 9 to the four times the greatest.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Numbers and Profit\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What is the definition of consecutive natural numbers based on the context of Problem 7?\",\"options\":[\"Numbers that differ by 2\",\"Numbers that follow each other in order, differing by 1\",\"Numbers that are all even\",\"Numbers that are all prime\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Natural numbers like x, x+1, x+2 are consecutive because they follow each other by a difference of 1.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Numbers and Profit\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Problem 8, Amit sold the bicycle for ₹ 1134 with \'no loss and no profit\'. What does this imply about Amit\'s total cost price?\",\"options\":[\"His total cost price was less than ₹ 1134\",\"His total cost price was more than ₹ 1134\",\"His total cost price was exactly ₹ 1134\",\"His total cost price was ₹ 54\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"No loss and no profit means the Selling Price is equal to the total Cost Price.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Numbers and Profit\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Amit spent ₹ 54 on repairs and his total cost price was ₹ 1134. At what price did he buy the bicycle from Raju?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 1188\",\"₹ 1080\",\"₹ 1000\",\"₹ 1100\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Amit\'s purchase price = Total cost - Repair cost = 1134 - 54 = 1080.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Numbers and Profit\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If Raju\'s cost price is \'x\' and he sold it to Amit at 8% profit, which expression represents the selling price for Raju?\",\"options\":[\"x + (8\\/100)x\",\"x - (8\\/100)x\",\"x + 8\",\"8x\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Profit is added to the cost price; 8% profit on x is (8\\/100)x.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Numbers and Profit\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In Problem 7, solving the equation 5x = 4(x + 2) + 9 results in which value for the smallest number?\",\"options\":[\"x = 15\",\"x = 17\",\"x = 19\",\"x = 9\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"5x = 4x + 8 + 9; 5x - 4x = 17; therefore x = 17.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Numbers and Profit\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, who is the person who originally purchased the bicycle before selling it at a profit?\",\"options\":[\"Amit\",\"Nikhil\",\"Raju\",\"The repairman\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states \'Raju sold a bicycle to Amit\', making Raju the original purchaser in this context.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Numbers and Profit\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If the smallest number in Problem 7 is found to be 17, what are the three consecutive natural numbers?\",\"options\":[\"17, 18, 19\",\"16, 17, 18\",\"17, 19, 21\",\"15, 16, 17\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Consecutive natural numbers starting from 17 are 17, 17+1, and 17+2.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Numbers and Profit\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"What was the specific amount Amit spent on repairing the bicycle?\",\"options\":[\"₹ 1134\",\"₹ 8\",\"₹ 54\",\"₹ 1080\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states \'Amit repaired it spending ₹ 54\'.\",\"topic\":\"Problems on Numbers and Profit\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"}]','gemini/gemini-3-flash-preview','2026-10-03 16:25:29'),(22126,55,8,'Maths','en','Congruence of triangles','[\"Congruent figures are exactly the same shape and size.\",\"Two segments of equal length are congruent.\",\"Two angles of equal measure are congruent.\",\"If all corresponding parts of two triangles are congruent, the triangles are congruent.\",\"One‑to‑one correspondence means each vertex of one triangle matches exactly one vertex of the other.\",\"The order of vertices in the notation AABC = A PQR shows the correspondence A↔P, B↔Q, C↔R.\",\"Six pairs of corresponding parts are congruent: three sides and three angles.\",\"SAS test: two sides and the included angle are congruent → triangles are congruent.\",\"SSS test: all three sides are congruent → triangles are congruent.\",\"ASA test: two angles and the included side are congruent → triangles are congruent.\",\"AAS (or SAA) test: two angles and a non‑included side are congruent → triangles are congruent.\",\"Hypotenuse‑side test: in right‑angled triangles, if the hypotenuse and one other side are congruent, the triangles are congruent.\",\"If two sides and an angle not included by them are congruent, the triangles need not be congruent.\",\"When writing a congruence, the order of vertices must follow the one‑to‑one correspondence.\",\"If a congruence is written incorrectly, it may imply wrong equalities between parts.\",\"Identical marks on a figure indicate congruent parts.\",\"The side opposite an angle is the side not touching that angle.\",\"The side included by two angles is the side that lies between them.\",\"The side included by two sides is the side that connects the two vertices of those sides.\",\"The angles adjacent to a side are the two angles that share that side.\",\"When two triangles are copied on tracing paper, overlapping parts show congruence.\",\"If two triangles are not placed with correct correspondence, they will not coincide.\",\"The notation AABC = A PQR is read as “Triangle AABC is congruent to triangle A PQR”.\",\"Congruence is a geometric equality, not just similarity.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What are figures that exactly coincide with each other called?\",\"options\":[\"Similar figures\",\"Congruent figures\",\"Equal figures\",\"Parallel figures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that figures which exactly coincide with each other are called congruent figures.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Under what condition are two segments considered congruent?\",\"options\":[\"When they are parallel\",\"When they intersect at a point\",\"When they have equal lengths\",\"When they are part of the same line\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, segments of equal lengths are congruent.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When are two angles said to be congruent?\",\"options\":[\"When they have equal measures\",\"When they are both acute\",\"When they share a common vertex\",\"When they are supplementary\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text defines congruent angles as those having equal measures.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In triangle DEF, which angle is opposite to the side DE?\",\"options\":[\"∠D\",\"∠E\",\"∠F\",\"∠EDF\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In triangle DEF, the vertex not contained in side DE is F, so ∠F is the opposite angle.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In triangle DEF, which side is opposite to ∠E?\",\"options\":[\"Side DE\",\"Side DF\",\"Side EF\",\"Side ED\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The side that does not contain the vertex E is side DF.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which angle is included by side DE and side DF in triangle DEF?\",\"options\":[\"∠E\",\"∠F\",\"∠D\",\"∠EFD\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The vertex common to both side DE and side DF is D, so ∠D is the included angle.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If segment AB measures 7 cm and segment XY measures 7 cm, what is the relationship between them?\",\"options\":[\"They are parallel\",\"They are congruent\",\"They are perpendicular\",\"They are unequal\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since their lengths are equal, the segments are congruent based on the definition provided.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If ∠P = 60° and ∠Q = 60°, what can be concluded about these two angles?\",\"options\":[\"They are congruent\",\"They are complementary\",\"They are right angles\",\"They are adjacent\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Angles with equal measures are congruent.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In triangle DEF, which side is included by ∠E and ∠F?\",\"options\":[\"Side DE\",\"Side DF\",\"Side EF\",\"Side D\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The side connecting the vertices of ∠E and ∠F is side EF.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following pairs represents the angles adjacent to side DE in triangle DEF?\",\"options\":[\"∠D and ∠F\",\"∠E and ∠F\",\"∠D and ∠E\",\"∠F and ∠D\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The angles at the endpoints of side DE are ∠D and ∠E.\",\"topic\":\"Let\'s recall\",\"part\":1,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which symbol is used to denote the one-to-one correspondence between two vertices?\",\"options\":[\"≅\",\"↔\",\"=\",\"Δ\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'Point A corresponds to point P is denoted as A ↔ P\'.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When two triangles are congruent in a specific correspondence, how many total congruences (pairs of equal parts) are obtained?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that when two triangles are congruent, \'we get six congruences\', which include three angles and three sides.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What does it mean when two triangles \'coincide exactly\' with each other?\",\"options\":[\"They have the same name\",\"They are congruent\",\"They are of different sizes\",\"They have only one vertex in common\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that if triangles coincide exactly when placed on each other, \'they are congruent\'.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If △ ABC ≅ △ PQR, which vertex corresponds to point B according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Point P\",\"Point Q\",\"Point R\",\"Point A\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The correspondence ABC ↔ PQR implies A ↔ P, B ↔ Q, and C ↔ R.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the correspondence A ↔ P, B ↔ Q, C ↔ R, which segment is congruent to seg BC?\",\"options\":[\"seg PQ\",\"seg QR\",\"seg RP\",\"seg AB\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the six congruences listed in the text for this correspondence, seg BC ≅ seg QR.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If △ ABC ≅ △ PQR, which angle is congruent to ∠C?\",\"options\":[\"∠P\",\"∠Q\",\"∠R\",\"∠A\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that △ ABC ≅ △ PQR implies ∠C ≅ ∠R.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If placing point A on point Q, B on R, and C on P does not make the triangles coincide, what can be concluded?\",\"options\":[\"The triangles are not congruent in that specific correspondence\",\"The triangles are not congruent in any correspondence\",\"The vertices are not points\",\"The tracing paper is incorrect\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that if placed differently, they will not coincide, meaning the vertices must be matched in a specific way.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How is the statement \'△ ABC and △ PQR are congruent\' written symbolically?\",\"options\":[\"△ ABC = △ PQR\",\"△ ABC ↔ △ PQR\",\"△ ABC ≅ △ PQR\",\"△ ABC ≈ △ PQR\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that the congruence is written as △ ABC ≅ △ PQR.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the order of vertices important when writing the congruence of two triangles?\",\"options\":[\"To make the names shorter\",\"To observe the one-to-one correspondence ascertaining congruence\",\"To distinguish between sides and angles\",\"To show the triangles are of different shapes\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says we must take care of the order to observe the one-to-one correspondence that ascertains congruence.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If △ XYZ ≅ △ LMN, which of the following is the correct implied correspondence?\",\"options\":[\"X ↔ L, Y ↔ M, Z ↔ N\",\"X ↔ N, Y ↔ M, Z ↔ L\",\"X ↔ M, Y ↔ L, Z ↔ N\",\"X ↔ L, Y ↔ N, Z ↔ M\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Following the pattern of △ ABC ≅ △ PQR, the vertices match in the order they are written.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If △ ABC ≅ △ PQR under the correspondence ABC ↔ PQR, which of these is NOT one of the six congruences mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"∠A ≅ ∠P\",\"seg AB ≅ seg PQ\",\"seg BC ≅ seg RP\",\"∠B ≅ ∠Q\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"According to the text, seg BC ≅ seg QR, not seg RP.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the activity, what is the essential requirement for two triangles to be congruent?\",\"options\":[\"They must be drawn on tracing paper\",\"They must have the same name\",\"The vertices must be matched in a specific one-to-one correspondence\",\"They must be placed on top of each other in any random way\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text emphasizes that \'the vertices must be matched in a specific way\' for the triangles to coincide and be congruent.\",\"topic\":\"Congruence of triangles\",\"part\":2,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"In the discussion between Anil, Rehana, and Surjit, who wrote the correct congruence statement for the triangles?\",\"options\":[\"Anil\",\"Rehana\",\"Surjit\",\"None of them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that Surjit wrote △ ABC ≅ △ PQR, which is the correct statement based on identical marks.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the convention mentioned in Example 2, how is a common side indicated in a figure?\",\"options\":[\"By a specific symbol\",\"By a dotted line\",\"By a bold line\",\"By an arrow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text notes that it is a convention to indicate a common side by a specific symbol.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Example 1, if the congruence is written as △ XYZ ≅ △ STU, which side would side ST be congruent to?\",\"options\":[\"Side YZ\",\"Side XZ\",\"Side XY\",\"Side ZY\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text explains that writing △ XYZ ≅ △ STU implies side ST ≅ side XY.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is side AD congruent to itself in Example 2?\",\"options\":[\"Because it is the longest side\",\"Because every segment is congruent to itself\",\"Because it is a vertical line\",\"Because it bisects the triangle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The solution in Example 2 states that every segment is congruent to itself.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In Example 1, which vertex corresponds to vertex U in the correspondence STU ↔ XZY?\",\"options\":[\"Vertex X\",\"Vertex Z\",\"Vertex Y\",\"Vertex S\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the correspondence STU ↔ XZY, the third vertex U corresponds to the third vertex Y.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In Example 1, which vertex corresponds to vertex S in the correspondence STU ↔ XZY?\",\"options\":[\"Vertex X\",\"Vertex Z\",\"Vertex Y\",\"Vertex T\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"In the correspondence STU ↔ XZY, the first vertex S corresponds to the first vertex X.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the statement △ XYZ ≅ △ STU considered wrong in Example 1?\",\"options\":[\"The triangles are not congruent at all\",\"The correspondence of vertices is incorrect\",\"The identical marks are missing\",\"The names of the triangles must be in alphabetical order\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the statement is wrong because it implies an incorrect side congruence (ST ≅ XY).\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In Example 2, which side is identified as the common side between △ ABD and △ ACD?\",\"options\":[\"Side AB\",\"Side AC\",\"Side BD\",\"Side AD\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that in △ ABD and △ ACD, side AD is common.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct one-to-one correspondence for the triangles in Example 2?\",\"options\":[\"A ↔ A, B ↔ D, D ↔ C\",\"A ↔ A, B ↔ C, D ↔ D\",\"A ↔ B, B ↔ C, D ↔ A\",\"A ↔ D, B ↔ B, D ↔ C\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The solution for Example 2 lists the correspondence as A ↔ A, B ↔ C, D ↔ D.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If △ STU ≅ △ XZY, which of the following is another correct way to write the congruence?\",\"options\":[\"△ UST ≅ △ YXZ\",\"△ TUS ≅ △ XZY\",\"△ SUT ≅ △ ZXY\",\"△ TSU ≅ △ YZX\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text identifies △ UST ≅ △ YXZ as another correct way to write the congruence.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, how many mistakes must be pointed out to show that a congruence statement is wrong?\",\"options\":[\"All possible mistakes\",\"At least two mistakes\",\"It is sufficient to point out one mistake\",\"Three mistakes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text notes that to show an answer is wrong, it is sufficient to point out one mistake.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In Example 1, if the triangles are congruent in the correspondence STU ↔ XZY, which side is congruent to side TU?\",\"options\":[\"Side XZ\",\"Side ZY\",\"Side XY\",\"Side ST\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the correspondence STU ↔ XZY, the pair TU corresponds to ZY.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following statements about Example 2 is correct?\",\"options\":[\"△ ABD ≅ △ ACD\",\"△ ABD ≅ △ ADC\",\"△ ADB ≅ △ ACD\",\"△ BAD ≅ △ CAD\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text concludes that △ ABD ≅ △ ACD based on the identified correspondence.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Example 1, if we change the order of vertices to △ TUS, what must be the order for the second triangle to remain correct?\",\"options\":[\"△ ZYX\",\"△ ZXY\",\"△ YZX\",\"△ XZY\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Using the correspondence S↔X, T↔Z, U↔Y; TUS corresponds to ZYX.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"What can be inferred if a congruence statement like △ XYZ ≅ △ STU is labeled \'wrong\' in the text?\",\"options\":[\"The triangles have different shapes\",\"The vertices do not match in the specified order\",\"The triangles have different areas\",\"The triangles are not in the same plane\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text demonstrates that the statement is wrong because the implied side congruences do not match the actual identical marks.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Example\",\"part\":4,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"How many total corresponding parts are there in a pair of triangles?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Six\",\"Eight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A triangle has three sides and three angles, making a total of six parts.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"To show that a pair of triangles is congruent, what is the minimum number of specific corresponding parts required?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Five\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states it is sufficient if three specific parts of one triangle are congruent with the corresponding parts of the other.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If three specific parts of one triangle are congruent with the corresponding parts of another, what happens to the remaining three parts?\",\"options\":[\"They are also congruent with each other\",\"They are never congruent\",\"They are always double in size\",\"They remain unknown and cannot be compared\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"According to the text, if the test is satisfied, the remaining three corresponding parts are also congruent.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the SAS test for congruence, what does the \'A\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"Any angle of the triangle\",\"The largest angle\",\"The angle included between the two sides\",\"The angle opposite to the first side\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"SAS stands for two sides and the included angle.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which test is applied when three sides of one triangle are congruent to the three corresponding sides of another triangle?\",\"options\":[\"SAS test\",\"SSS test\",\"ASA test\",\"AAS test\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The SSS test (Side-Side-Side) involves three corresponding sides.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which side of triangle LMN corresponds to side BC of triangle ABC based on the markings?\",\"options\":[\"Side LM\",\"Side MN\",\"Side LN\",\"Side AB\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The markings (triple hatch marks) on side BC match the markings on side MN.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/093_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which test of congruence is demonstrated by the markings on the triangles?\",\"options\":[\"SSS test\",\"ASA test\",\"SAS test\",\"AAA test\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure shows two sides and the angle included between them as congruent, which is the SAS test.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/093_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"If in ΔPQR and ΔXYZ, l(PQ) = l(XY), l(QR) = l(YZ), and l(RP) = l(ZX), which correspondence makes the triangles congruent?\",\"options\":[\"P ↔ Y, Q ↔ X, R ↔ Z\",\"P ↔ X, Q ↔ Y, R ↔ Z\",\"P ↔ Z, Q ↔ Y, R ↔ X\",\"P ↔ X, Q ↔ Z, R ↔ Y\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Based on the side lengths given, the vertices must match as P to X, Q to Y, and R to Z.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In the ASA test, which part must be congruent along with two angles?\",\"options\":[\"Any side of the triangle\",\"The side opposite the larger angle\",\"The side included by the two angles\",\"The hypotenuse\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"ASA stands for two angles and their included side.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If ΔXYZ and ΔDEF are congruent such that l(XZ) = l(DF), ∠X ≅ ∠D and ∠Z ≅ ∠F, which test is being used?\",\"options\":[\"SAS test\",\"SSS test\",\"ASA test\",\"SSA test\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Two angles and the side between them (XZ and DF) are congruent, indicating the ASA test.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it said that specific three parts \'ascertain the test of congruence\'?\",\"options\":[\"Because they define a unique triangle\",\"Because triangles only have three parts\",\"Because angles are more important than sides\",\"Because tracing paper only works for three parts\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the three specific parts define a unique triangle, which decides the test.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Suppose you have two triangles where two sides are congruent to two sides of the other, but the congruent angles are NOT the included angles. Can you definitely use the SAS test?\",\"options\":[\"Yes, any angle works\",\"No, the angle must be included between the sides\",\"Yes, if the triangles are right-angled\",\"No, because only the SSS test would work then\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The SAS test specifically requires the \'included angle\' to be congruent.\",\"topic\":\"Tests for Congruence\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the sum of the measures of angles in a triangle according to the AAS test explanation?\",\"options\":[\"90°\",\"180°\",\"270°\",\"360°\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that the sum of the measures of angles in a triangle is 180°.\",\"topic\":\"AAS and Hypotenuse-side test\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is another name for the AAS test?\",\"options\":[\"SAS test\",\"SSS test\",\"SAA test\",\"ASA test\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'(4) AAS (or SAA) test\'.\",\"topic\":\"AAS and Hypotenuse-side test\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"The Hypotenuse-side test is specifically used for which type of triangles?\",\"options\":[\"Acute angled triangles\",\"Obtuse angled triangles\",\"Right angled triangles\",\"Equilateral triangles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text refers to the \'Hypotenuse side test for right angled triangles\'.\",\"topic\":\"AAS and Hypotenuse-side test\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, there is a ______ right angled triangle of a given side and hypotenuse.\",\"options\":[\"Unique\",\"Similar\",\"Congruent\",\"Different\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'There is a unique right angled triangle of a given side and hypotenuse.\'\",\"topic\":\"AAS and Hypotenuse-side test\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If two corresponding pairs of angles in two triangles are congruent, what is true about the remaining pair of angles?\",\"options\":[\"They are supplementary\",\"They are complementary\",\"They are also congruent\",\"They are unequal\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'if two corresponding pairs of angles in two triangles are congruent, then the remaining pair of angles is also congruent.\'\",\"topic\":\"AAS and Hypotenuse-side test\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the AAS test lead to the conclusion that triangles are congruent?\",\"options\":[\"Because it fulfills the condition for the SSS test\",\"Because it fulfills the condition for the ASA test\",\"Because it fulfills the condition for the SAS test\",\"Because all angles are 60°\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says: \'the condition for ASA test is fulfilled. So the triangles are congruent.\'\",\"topic\":\"AAS and Hypotenuse-side test\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the AAS test, the congruent side must be ______ to one of the congruent angles.\",\"options\":[\"Opposite\",\"Adjacent\",\"Hypotenuse\",\"Parallel\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states: \'if two angles and a side adjacent to one of them are congruent...\'\",\"topic\":\"AAS and Hypotenuse-side test\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To prove two right-angled triangles are congruent using the Hypotenuse-side test, which parts must be congruent?\",\"options\