e property leads to ASA condition\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses the 180° sum property to show that AAS fulfills the ASA test condition.\",\"topic\":\"AAS and Hypotenuse-side test\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, what is indicated by identical marks on the parts of triangles?\",\"options\":[\"The parts are of different lengths\",\"The parts are congruent\",\"The parts are parallel\",\"The parts are perpendicular\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that parts of triangles bearing identical marks are congruent.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Ex. (1), which test is used to show that the triangles in the correspondence PQR ↔ UTS are congruent?\",\"options\":[\"SAS test\",\"ASA test\",\"SSS test\",\"Hypotenuse - side test\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The solution for Ex. (1)(i) explicitly states \'By SSS test, in the correspondence PQR ↔ UTS\'.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, the square symbols at vertices M and D indicate that the triangles are of what type?\",\"options\":[\"Equilateral triangles\",\"Obtuse angled triangles\",\"Right angled triangles\",\"Isosceles triangles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The square symbol at a vertex denotes a right angle, making them right angled triangles.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/095_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which segment is identified as the common side for both triangles?\",\"options\":[\"Side AB\",\"Side BC\",\"Side CD\",\"Side CA\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The solution for Ex. (2)(ii) states that \'The side CA of the two triangles is common\'.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/095_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, what additional information is necessary to show that the triangles are congruent by the Hypotenuse - side test?\",\"options\":[\"hypotenuse LN ≅ hypotenuse EF\",\"side MN ≅ side DF\",\"side LM ≅ side ED\",\"∠ L ≅ ∠ E\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states the additional information necessary is hypotenuse LN ≅ hypotenuse EF.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/095_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure (iii), which congruence test is most appropriate based on the identical marks shown on all three pairs of sides?\",\"options\":[\"ASA test\",\"SAS test\",\"SSS test\",\"Hypotenuse - side test\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Figure (iii) shows three pairs of sides with identical marks, which corresponds to the SSS test.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"55\\/095_103.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In Ex. (2)(i), what is the correct one to one correspondence in which the triangles will be congruent?\",\"options\":[\"LMN ↔ FED\",\"LMN ↔ DEF\",\"LMN ↔ EDF\",\"LMN ↔ EFD\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The solution for Ex. (2)(i) states the triangles will be congruent in the correspondence LMN ↔ EDF.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Ex. (2)(ii), to satisfy the ASA test, which specific angle must be congruent to ∠ BAC?\",\"options\":[\"∠ DAC\",\"∠ BCA\",\"∠ DCA\",\"∠ ADC\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The solution for Ex. (2)(ii) states the additional necessary information is ∠ DCA ≅ ∠ BAC.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In Ex. (1)(ii), which test is applied to the correspondence DBA ↔ DBC?\",\"options\":[\"SSS test\",\"ASA test\",\"SAS test\",\"Hypotenuse - side test\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The solution for Ex. (1)(ii) states \'By ASA test, in the correspondence DBA ↔ DBC\'.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the solution for Ex. (2)(i), which segment is the hypotenuse of triangle EDF?\",\"options\":[\"Side ED\",\"Side DF\",\"Side EF\",\"Sid