,\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the requirement for the side in the A-S-A test?\",\"options\":[\"It must be the longest side\",\"It must be the side included by the two angles\",\"It must be the side opposite the first angle\",\"It can be any side of the triangle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The A-S-A test requires two angles and a side included by them to be congruent.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If two angles and a side NOT included by them are congruent with the corresponding parts of another triangle, which test is applied?\",\"options\":[\"A-S-A test\",\"S-A-S test\",\"A-A-S test\",\"S-S-S test\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The A-A-S test applies when two angles and a side not included by them are congruent.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To prove two triangles are congruent using the Hypotenuse-side test, what must be congruent besides the hypotenuse?\",\"options\":[\"One corresponding side\",\"Two corresponding angles\",\"The included angle\",\"All three sides\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The test requires the hypotenuse and a side of a right-angled triangle to be congruent with the corresponding parts.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main difference between the A-S-A test and the A-A-S test?\",\"options\":[\"The number of angles required\",\"The number of sides required\",\"Whether the side is included between the angles or not\",\"One is only for right-angled triangles\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A-S-A requires the included side, while A-A-S involves a side not included by the angles.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In triangle XYZ and triangle LMN, if XY = LM, YZ = MN, and angle Y = angle M, which test proves their congruence?\",\"options\":[\"S-S-S test\",\"S-A-S test\",\"A-S-A test\",\"Hypotenuse-side test\"],\"answer\":1,\"expla