 square root for triangle LMN, which product results in 1728?\",\"options\":[\"12 × 9 × 48\",\"12 × 3 × 48\",\"108 × 12\",\"48 × 48\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states A(triangle LMN) = 12 × 3 × 48 = 1728.\",\"topic\":\"Area of Triangle LNO and Plot\",\"part\":17,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the formula to calculate the area of a parallelogram?\",\"options\":[\"base + height\",\"base × height\",\"1\\/2 × base × height\",\"2 × (base + height)\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the text, the area of a parallelogram is calculated as base × height.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which formula is used to find the area of a rhombus?\",\"options\":[\"base × height\",\"1\\/2 × sum of lengths of diagonals\",\"1\\/2 × product of lengths of diagonals\",\"product of lengths of diagonals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that the area of a rhombus is 1\\/2 × product of lengths of diagonals.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Heron\'s formula, what does \'s\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"s = a + b + c\",\"s = (a + b + c) \\/ 2\",\"s = a × b × c\",\"s = √(a + b + c)\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text defines s as (a + b + c) \\/ 2 in the context of Heron\'s formula.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the area of a trapezium based on the provided formula?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/2 × product of parallel sides × height\",\"sum of the lengths of parallel sides × height\",\"1\\/2 × sum of the lengths of parallel sides × height\",\"1\\/2 × sum of the lengths of parallel sides + height\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines the area of a trapezium as 1\\/2 × sum of the lengths of parallel sides × height.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If sides of △ ABC are a, b, and c, which expression represents Heron\'s formula for the area?\",\"options\":[\"√(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)\",\"s√(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)\",\"√[s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)]\",\"1\\/2 × √[s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)]\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text provides Heron\'s formula as √[s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)].\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"To calculate the area of a rhombus, which specific measurement of the diagonals is required?\",\"options\":[\"The sum of their lengths\",\"The difference of their lengths\",\"The product of their lengths\",\"The square of their lengths\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The formula for the area of a rhombus specifically uses the product of the lengths of the diagonals.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A parallelogram has a base of 10 cm and a height of 6 cm. What is its area?\",\"options\":[\"16 sq cm\",\"30 sq cm\",\"60 sq cm\",\"120 sq cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Using the formula base × height: 10 × 6 = 60 sq cm.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If the sides of a triangle are a = 3, b = 4, and c = 5, what is the value of \'s\' for Heron\'s formula?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"6\",\"7\",\"3.5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"s = (a+b+c)\\/2 = (3+4+5)\\/2 = 12\\/2 = 6.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a trapezium has parallel sides of lengths \'x\' and \'y\' and a height \'h\', which expression correctly represents its area?\",\"options\":[\"1\\/2 × x × y × h\",\"1\\/2 × (x + y) × h\",\"(x + y) × h\",\"1\\/2 + (x + y) × h\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Substituting \'x\' and \'y\' for the parallel sides in the trapezium formula gives 1\\/2 × (x + y) × h.\",\"topic\":\"Now I know\",\"part\":18,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a necessary step before applying Heron\'s formula √[s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)]?\",\"options\":[\"Finding the height of the triangle\",\"Calculating the product of the sides\",\"Calculating the value of s using the lengths of the sides\",\"Ensuring the triangle is a right-angled triangle\"],\"answer\