culated areas (65, 136, 405, 265), the trapezium AQRE has the largest area at 405 sq m.\",\"topic\":\"Ex. Area of a polygon\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"To find the area of polygon ABCDE, which combination of shapes was summed?\",\"options\":[\"Two triangles and two trapeziums\",\"Three triangles and one trapezium\",\"Four triangles\",\"One triangle and three trapeziums\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The area is the sum of A(Δ AQB), A(☐ AQRE), A(Δ ERD), and A(Δ BCD), which are three triangles and one trapezium.\",\"topic\":\"Ex. Area of a polygon\",\"part\":22,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"What is the formula for the area of a circle as given in the text?\",\"options\":[\"Area = 2πr\",\"Area = πr²\",\"Area = πd\",\"Area = 2πr²\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states the formula for the area of a circle is πr².\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":24,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In Example (1), what is the unit used for the area of the circle?\",\"options\":[\"cm\",\"sq m\",\"sq cm\",\"m\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The solution in Example (1) concludes with the unit \'sq cm\'.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":24,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What value of π is used in the calculations in the provided examples?\",\"options\":[\"3.14\",\"7\\/22\",\"22\\/7\",\"21\\/7\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Both examples show the substitution of π as 22\\/7.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":24,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In the formula Area = πr², what does the letter \'r\' represent?\",\"options\":[\"Ratio\",\"Radius\",\"Round\",\"Region\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text uses \'r\' to represent the radius of the circle.\",\"topic\":\"Solved Examples\",\"part\":24,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If the radius of a circle is 21 cm, what is its area according to Example (1)?\",\"options\":[\"1386 sq cm\",\"66 sq cm\",\"441 sq cm\",\"3850 sq cm\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Example (1) calculates the area 