es that these two arcs are called corresponding arcs of chord AB.\",\"topic\":\"Arcs corresponding to the chord\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If P is the point where the perpendicular from the centre meets chord AB, how is l(AB) related to l(PB)?\",\"options\":[\"l(AB) = l(PB)\",\"l(AB) = 2 × l(PB)\",\"l(AB) = 1\\/2 × l(PB)\",\"l(AB) = l(PB) + 2\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"According to the calculation shown, l(AB) = 2 × l(PB) because the perpendicular bisects the chord.\",\"topic\":\"Arcs corresponding to the chord\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"If l(PB) = 8 cm and P is the foot of the perpendicular from the centre to chord AB, what is the length of chord AB?\",\"options\":[\"4 cm\",\"8 cm\",\"16 cm\",\"32 cm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"As per the example, l(AB) = 2 × 8 = 16 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Arcs corresponding to the chord\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"In a circle with centre O and chord AB, if arc AXB is the minor arc, what is arc AYB?\",\"options\":[\"A central arc\",\"A major arc\",\"A diameter arc\",\"A chord arc\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies arc AXB as the minor arc and arc AYB as the major arc.\",\"topic\":\"Arcs corresponding to the chord\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Chord AB is described as the \'corresponding chord\' for which of the following?\",\"options\":[\"Only arc AXB\",\"Only arc AYB\",\"Both arc AXB and arc AYB\",\"Only the centre O\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states chord AB is called the corresponding chord of arc AXB and arc AYB.\",\"topic\":\"Arcs corresponding to the chord\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"If the length of a chord AB is 20 cm, what would be the length of the segment PB if P bisects the chord?\",\"options\":[\"5 cm\",\"10 cm\",\"20 cm\",\"40 cm\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since l(AB) = 2 × l(PB), then l(PB) = l(AB) \\/ 2 = 20 \\/ 2 = 10 cm.\",\"topic\":\"Arcs corresponding to the chord\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which point is designated as the centre of the circle in the \'Let\'s learn\' figure description?\",\"options\":[\"Point A\",\"Point B\",\"Point O\",\"Point X\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions \'a circle with centre O\'.\",\"topic\":\"Arcs corresponding to the chord\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the relationship between a chord and its corresponding arcs?\",\"options\":[\"The chord is the corresponding chord of the arcs\",\"The chord is always longer than the arcs\",\"The chord bisects the arcs\",\"The chord is perpendicular to the arcs\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that the chord is called the corresponding chord of the minor and major arcs.\",\"topic\":\"Arcs corresponding to the chord\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the property of the perpendicular from the centre, if l(AP) = l(PB), what can be concluded about point P?\",\"options\":[\"P is the centre of the circle\",\"P is the foot of the perpendicular from the centre to the chord\",\"P is a point on the major arc\",\"P is the endpoint of the chord\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text implies that the perpendicular from the centre bisects the chord, meaning P would be the midpoint where the perpendicular meets the chord.\",\"topic\":\"Arcs corresponding to the chord\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, when are two arcs of a circle said to be congruent?\",\"options\":[\"If their lengths are different\",\"If the measures of the two arcs are same\",\"If they are in different circles\",\"If they have different centers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly states that if the measures of two arcs of a circle are same, then the two arcs are congruent.\",\"topic\":\"Congruent arcs\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In a circle with centre O, if $m \\\\angle AOB = m \\\\angle COD$, what can be concluded about the measures of their corresponding arcs?\",\"options\":[\"$m(arc 