emember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the text, why has the proportion of CO₂ increased over the last 100 years?\",\"options\":[\"Due to agricultural yield\",\"Due to industrialization\",\"Due to melting glaciers\",\"Due to distribution of wild animals\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explicitly mentions that the proportion of CO2 has increased due to industrialization over the last 100 years.\",\"topic\":\"Green House Effect and Global Warming\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following gases is NOT listed as a \'green house gas\' in the provided text?\",\"options\":[\"Nitrous oxide\",\"Methane\",\"CFC\",\"Hydrogen\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text identifies CO2, nitrous oxide, methane, and CFC as greenhouse gases.\",\"topic\":\"Green House Effect and Global Warming\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which specific type of radiation is shown being emitted from the Earth and trapped by the atmosphere?\",\"options\":[\"Ultraviolet radiation\",\"Infrared radiation\",\"Solar heat\",\"Visible light\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The diagram labels the orange arrows reflecting back from the atmosphere as \'Infrared radiation\'.\",\"topic\":\"Green House Effect and Global Warming\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"57\\/067_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the given figure, where is the energy emitted by the Sun absorbed?\",\"options\":[\"Only in the atmosphere\",\"Only by the earth surface\",\"In both the atmosphere and by the earth surface\",\"It is not absorbed at all\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The figure contains two labels: \'Energy emitted by Sun is absorbed in atmosphere\' and \'Energy emitted by Sun is absorbed by earth surface\'.\",\"topic\":\"Green House Effect and Global Warming\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"analyze\",\"figure_image\":\"57\\/067_101.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"What is the definition of the \'green house effect\' as per the textbook text?\",\"options\":[\"The melting of icebergs