nts themselves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text explains that heavy metals are absorbed up by plants and thereby enter the food chain indirectly.\",\"topic\":\"Acid Rain\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the effects listed, which statement best evaluates the impact of acid rain on infrastructure?\",\"options\":[\"It only affects buildings made of wood\",\"It causes erosion of metal idols, bridges, and monuments\",\"It helps in the preservation of historical busts\",\"It prevents the rusting of wire fences\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text identifies erosion of buildings, busts, monuments, bridges, and metal idols as effects of acid rain.\",\"topic\":\"Acid Rain\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"evaluate\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following machinery should be used to control harmful particles emerging from factory smoke?\",\"options\":[\"Arresters and filters\",\"Atomic testers\",\"CFC burners\",\"Chemical weapon sensors\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text states that pollution controlling machinery like arresters and filters should be used for factory smoke.\",\"topic\":\"Prevention of Air Pollution\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What action is recommended for stinking waste generated in cities to prevent air pollution?\",\"options\":[\"Burning it in open squares\",\"Proper disposal\",\"Mixing it with CFCs\",\"Using it in atomic tests\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions proper disposal of stinking waste generated in cities as a preventive measure.\",\"topic\":\"Prevention of Air Pollution\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a preventive measure for air pollution related to modern weaponry and energy testing?\",\"options\":[\"Increasing the production of CFCs\",\"Using filters in busy squares\",\"Control on atomic tests and chemical weapons\",\"Measuring ozone levels in factories\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text lists control on atomic tests and chemical weapons as a preventive measu