frequency is measured in Hertz.\",\"topic\":\"Frequency of Sound Waves\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"If a tuning fork has a frequency of 512 Hz, how many times does it vibrate in one second?\",\"options\":[\"256 times\",\"512 times\",\"1024 times\",\"1 time\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A frequency of 512 Hz means that the fork vibrates 512 times per second.\",\"topic\":\"Frequency of Sound Waves\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What determines the number of cycles formed in the air in one second?\",\"options\":[\"The distance the sound travels\",\"The number of vibrations of the vibrating body in one second\",\"The volume of the air around the object\",\"The temperature of the medium\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states the number of cycles is decided by the number of times the vibrating body vibrates back and forth in one second.\",\"topic\":\"Frequency of Sound Waves\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"A frequency is said to be 1 Hz if:\",\"options\":[\"One cycle is completed in one minute\",\"One vibration occurs in ten seconds\",\"One cycle is completed in one second\",\"Ten cycles are completed in one second\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text defines 1 Hz as one cycle completed in one second.\",\"topic\":\"Frequency of Sound Waves\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"A vibrating object completes 256 cycles of compression and rarefaction in one second. What is the frequency of the sound generated?\",\"options\":[\"128 Hz\",\"256 Hz\",\"512 Hz\",\"256 cycles\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Since frequency is cycles per second, 256 cycles in one second equals 256 Hz.\",\"topic\":\"Frequency of Sound Waves\",\"part\":5,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"If a tuning fork produces 100 compressions and 100 rarefactions in one second, what is its frequency?\",\"options\":[\"50 Hz\",\"100 Hz\",\"200 Hz\",\"1 Hz\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"One compression and one rarefaction make one cycle; therefore, 100 of ea