 instrument created by arranging glass cups with different water levels called?\",\"options\":[\"Sitar\",\"Jaltarang\",\"Tabla\",\"Flute\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text refers to the experiment of striking glass cups with varying water levels as a simple \'Jal-tarang\'.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the experiment, what object is used to strike the glass cups sequentially?\",\"options\":[\"A metal spoon\",\"A glass rod\",\"A pencil\",\"A wooden stick\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The instructions explicitly state to \'Take a pencil and strike the cups sequentially\'.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"When a cup in the Jaltarang is struck, where are the sound waves primarily set up?\",\"options\":[\"In the pencil used for striking\",\"In the water itself\",\"In the air column above the water level\",\"In the table holding the glasses\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that \'waves are set up in the air column above the water level in the cup\'.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"What specific property of the generated sound wave depends on the height of the air column?\",\"options\":[\"Loudness\",\"Frequency\",\"Amplitude\",\"Speed\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that \'The frequency of the generated wave depends on the height of the air column\'.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Why is the sound generated by each cup in the experiment different?\",\"options\":[\"Because the glasses are made of different materials\",\"Because the pencil strikes at different angles\",\"Because the height of the air column in each glass is different\",\"Because the thickness of the glass cups varies\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Since the water level is different, the air column height is different, leading to different frequencies.\",\"topic\":\"Try this\",\"part\":6,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},