\"Decomposers like Aspergillus\",\"Abiotic factors like soil and water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Secondary consumers feed on primary consumers; therefore, a decrease in ants\\/butterflies directly affects snakes\\/lizards.\",\"topic\":\"Evergreen forests\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which sanctuary is listed at serial number 6?\",\"options\":[\"Sunderban\",\"Melghat\",\"Periyar\",\"Kaziranga\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table in the figure shows \'Sunderban\' at serial number 6.\",\"topic\":\"Evergreen forests\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"remember\",\"figure_image\":\"57\\/135_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"In the given figure, which sanctuary is listed immediately before Kaziranga?\",\"options\":[\"Dachigam\",\"Ranthambore\",\"Dajipur\",\"Geer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"In the table, Dajipur is number 4 and Kaziranga is number 5.\",\"topic\":\"Evergreen forests\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"understand\",\"figure_image\":\"57\\/135_102.jpg\"},{\"q\":\"A wildlife photographer wants to capture images of two-thirds of the world\'s total population of single-horned rhinos. Which state should they visit?\",\"options\":[\"Gujrat\",\"Asam\",\"Maharashtra\",\"Rajasthan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that two-thirds of the world\'s single-horned rhinos are found at Kaziranga in Asam.\",\"topic\":\"Evergreen forests\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"apply\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following correctly matches a consumer with its category as per the forest ecosystem table?\",\"options\":[\"Spider - Primary consumer\",\"Snake - Tertiary consumer\",\"Tiger - Secondary consumer\",\"Ant - Decomposer\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The table lists Spider under Primary consumers, Snake under Secondary, and Tiger under Tertiary.\",\"topic\":\"Evergreen forests\",\"part\":7,\"bloom\":\"analyze\"},{\"q\":\"Based on the text, why is the Bharatpur sanctuary categorized differently from Ranthambore?\",\"options\":[\"Bharatpur is for tigers, while Ranthambo