tom\",\"Inside the bodies of large fish\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text states that decomposers are at the bottom of water reservoirs.\",\"topic\":\"18.5 Aquatic ecosystem\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these organisms is listed as a producer in a fresh water ecosystem?\",\"options\":[\"Azolla\",\"Snail\",\"Frog\",\"Heron\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Azolla is listed under the \'Producers\' column in the fresh water ecosystem chart.\",\"topic\":\"18.5 Aquatic ecosystem\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"According to the fresh water ecosystem chart, to which category do \'Annelids\' belong?\",\"options\":[\"Producers\",\"Primary Consumers\",\"Secondary Consumers\",\"Decomposers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Annelids are listed under the \'Primary Consumers\' column in the textbook chart.\",\"topic\":\"18.5 Aquatic ecosystem\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"remember\"},{\"q\":\"What is the specific role of decomposers like bacteria and fungi in the aquatic ecosystem?\",\"options\":[\"They provide food for small fishes\",\"They convert dead bodies into abiotic factors\",\"They produce oxygen for aquatic plants\",\"They help in the flow of water currents\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text states that decomposers decompose dead bodies of plants and animals and convert them into abiotic factors.\",\"topic\":\"18.5 Aquatic ecosystem\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"In a marine ecosystem, which organisms are found in shallow water feeding on algae?\",\"options\":[\"Crocodiles and Herons\",\"Large fishes and sharks\",\"Small fishes and prawns\",\"Bacteria and fungi\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text mentions that shallow water contains small fishes and prawns feeding on algae.\",\"topic\":\"18.5 Aquatic ecosystem\",\"part\":8,\"bloom\":\"understand\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the sea is described as having a \'less number of aquatic living organisms\'?\",\"options\":[\"The shore\",\"The central part\",\"The bottom\",\"T